(comment highlyRelevantMt "A #$CycInferenceHeuristicRelevancePredicate. (#$highlyRelevantMt MT) means that all assertions in the #$Microtheory MT should be heuristically considered highly relevant to inferences done in the #$Microtheory MT-1 in which (#$highlyRelevantMt MT) is asserted (where MT-1 and MT need not be the same).  As a consequence, note that when (#$highlyRelevantMt MT) is asserted in a #$Microtheory MT-1, each of the assertions in MT will be a #$highlyRelevantAssertion (q.v.) for inferences done in MT-1.")
(comment highlyRelevantPredAssertion "(#$highlyRelevantPredAssertion PREDICATE ASSERTION) states that the given ASSERTION should be heuristically considered highly relevant to inferences concluding uses of the given PREDICATE in the current mt.  See also other instances #$CycInferenceHeuristicRelevancePredicate.")
(comment Persecution "A specialization of #$HostileSocialAction.  Each instance of #$Persecution is a hostile event in which a person or group of persons is subject to oppression or harassment in virtue of their  race, religion, gender, sexual orientation, or beliefs.")
(comment transportees-Type "(#$transportees-Type TRANSEVENT STUFF) means that STUFF is transported in the #$Conveying-Generic TRANSEVENT.")
(comment PersuadingToAct "A specialization of #$Convincing-CommunicationAct and #$InfluencingAnAgent. Each instance of this collection is a #$CommunicationAct-Single in which the performer successfully induces the recipient to perform (or not perform) an action.  This does not cover cases where situations, rather than agents, persuade: e.g., \"Polling results persuaded the candidate to withdraw.\" Notable specializations of this collection include #$RecruitingActivity and #$CoercingAnAgent.")
(comment Person "A specialization of #$SocialBeing and #$IndividualAgent: the collection of all persons. Personhood is a vague, emotionally loaded yet extremely salient concept with respect to common-sense reasoning. Something is an instance of #$Person if it is an individual #$IntelligentAgent with perceptual sensibility, capable of complex social relationships, and possessing a certain moral sophistication and an intrinsic moral value, or -- if it lacks certain of these characteristics -- is a member of a distinct type of #$SocialBeing (usually a species) which generally possesses such characteristics and is therefore acknowledged by other members of that type as a person within their social systems. Most currently known instances of #$Person are instances of #$HomoSapiens but there is no reason why all need be (consider #$Hobbits in the fictional world of #$LordOfTheRings-Trilogy). They need not even be instances of #$BiologicalLivingObject (consider the possibility of a person-like AI). Also note that #$Person excludes non-human \"legal persons\", who are, however, included in the collection #$LegalAgent.")
(comment Blackmail "The collection of activities in which one agent extorts another by threatening to reveal information that would harm the victim.")
(comment BiologicalTaxon "A collection of collections and a specialization of #$OrganismClassificationType (q.v.).  Instances of  #$BiologicalTaxon correspond to ranked categories  accepted by biologists for the classification of  organisms according to their suspected evolutionary  relationships.  Such categories change as biologists learn more about the organisms involved and determine that existing classifications are more or less useful.  They include all levels of taxons.   Specializations of #$BiologicalTaxon include  #$BiologicalOrder and #$BiologicalSpecies; instances include #$Marsupial and #$Ape.  See also  #$BiologicalTaxonType.")
(comment MilitaryWeapon "A specialization of #$Weapon.  Each specialization of #$MilitaryWeapon is a type of weapon typically used only by military organizations.  Specializations of #$MilitaryWeapon include #$SilkwormMissile, #$NuclearWeapon, and #$Mine-Weapon.")
(comment Bomb "A specialization of #$ExplosiveDevice and #$MilitaryWeapon.  Each instance of #$Bomb is a weapon designed to explode, thereby damaging people or property. Some instances of #$Bomb are meant to explode on impact. Some are dropped from a #$BomberPlane and can sometimes be remotely guided to change their fall towards the target. Other #$Bombs are meant to be hidden somewhere and explode after a certain time, e.g. #$Mine-Weapon are prime examples.  The detonation can be triggered in many ways: by applying pressure to the bomb, or controlling it with a #$Clock or remote control.  The important property of a #$Bomb is that the explosion is the primary means of destruction. Thus a #$ProjectileSlug-Bullet is not a #$Bomb even if it explodes on impact, because it is intended to penetrate the victim. ")
(comment spectators "A #$BinaryPredicate used to relate an event to its spectators, and a specialization of #$observers. (#$spectators EVENT AGENT) means that in the #$Event-Localized EVENT, AGENT (who is an instance of both #$IntelligentAgent and #$PerceptualAgent) is perceiving EVENT and is not acting in it in any other way.  AGENT may observe all or part of EVENT.")
(comment observers "A #$BinaryPredicate used to relate an event to its observers, and a specialization of #$awareOf and #$temporallyIntersects. (#$observers EVENT AGENT) means that the #$IntelligentAgent AGENT observes the #$Event EVENT in part or whole. AGENT may be an individual or a group or organization -- such as a UN delegation. The observations in question may be  individual or collective, direct or mediated (observation of the event may be mediated by artificial means, including spy satellites). For cases where AGENT is not acting in EVENT in any way, and is also perceiving it directly (and thus EVENT is an instance of #$Event-Localized), see the more specialized #$spectators.")
(comment Gunpowder "#$Gunpowder is a specialization of #$LowExplosive and an instance of #$TangibleStuffCompositionType.  Each instance of #$Gunpowder is a low explosive powdery mixture comprised of 75% #$PotassiumNitrate (KNO3), 15% #$Carbon, and 10% #$Sulfur.")
(comment ExplosiveMaterial "A specialization of #$DangerousTangibleThing.  Each instance of #$ExplosiveMaterial is a chemical substance that under certain circumstances (usually upon the application of heat or shock) will decompose or rearrange very quickly, yielding large amounts of gas and heat.  Explosive material  can either deflagrate (see #$LowExplosive) or detonate (see #$HighExplosive).")
(comment ruralRouteNumber "Gives the rural route number in an address. E.g. in R.R. 2A, Box 75, #$Sparta, KY the entry on this slot would be the string ``2A''.")
(comment HourOfDayType "A specialization of #$TimeOfDayType (q.v.) and a collection of collections of calendar-hours.  There are exactly twenty-four instances of #$HourOfDayType, each of which is a clock-synchronized subcollection of #$CalendarHour; e.g. #$TimeOfDay-8AM.  See also #$TimeOfDay.")
(comment agentOwesAgentAmount "The agent ARG1 owes to the agent ARG2 the money (amount) ARG3.")
(comment WinterSeason "A specialization of #$ColdSeason.  In the #$TemperateClimateCycle, generally a time of cold and dormancy.  #$WinterSeason represents the climatic aspects of Winter; for its purely temporal aspects, see #$CalendarWinter.")
(comment (FruitFn BreadfruitTree) "The collection of individual Breadfruits.")
(disjointWith Translation-NoLocationChange Translation-LocationChange)
(comment MailOrderSale "A subset of #$SaleWithDelivery. In an instance of #$MailOrderSale, the object purchased is delivered to the buyer via some shipping organization, such as a postal service. Note that payment for the object can be made via mail, via phone, or electronically, but is usually not made directly to the seller.")
(comment RequestForBid "A request issued by a potential customer to a potential vendor, for a bid on some product(s)/service(s).  Usually the first step of sales contract negotiation.  This is not that same as #$RequestingToMakeAPurchase because it involves no obligation on the part of the requestor to buy.")
(comment GymParallelBars "The piece of gymnastic equipment used during a paralell bar routine, with two long, thin, horizontal bars in paralell.")
(comment RegisteredPharmacistCredential "The abreviation is RPH. you can't legally fill out prescriptions without one of these.  You must have a B.S. in Pharm and then pass an exam to have this credential, however, practically everyone having this degree passes.")
(comment freightAirTrafficRate "This measures the rate at which freight is shipped by air

in some region. The most common rate measure for this is in

terms of billion net ton-kilometers per year.")
(comment MarkingTemplate "Instances are objects that can be used, intentionally or not, to produce visual marks that all share more or less the same informational content.  Rubber stamps are MarkingTemplates.  Finger pads are MarkingTemplates.  Lithographic plates are MarkingTemplates.")
(comment HealthMaintenanceOrganization "A business which provides health-care for a fixed, regular fee rather than on a per-use basis.  This organization typically has a network of doctors, hospitals, pharmacies which participate.  Other health-care-providers' fees are not included in the premiums.")
(disjointWith CalendarMinute TimePoint)
(comment kleeneStarOf "(#$kleeneStarOf SUPER SUB) means that (SUPER A B) means that zero or more applications of (SUB U V) will transform A to B.  SUPER is thus necessarily reflexive.  If at least one iteration of SUB is needed, use #$kleenePlusOf.")
(comment OrganizationWithIndividualCustomers "A specialization of #$OrganizationWithIndividualClients.  Each instance of #$OrganizationWithIndividualCustomers sells goods and/or services to customers, most of whom are individual #$Persons, rather than businesses or other #$Organizations.")
(comment FanLetter " The collection of letter that fans of a certain famous person address to the person .")
(comment ReproductiveEndocrinologist "A reproductive endocrinologist is a doctor who specializes in diagnosing and treating disorders of the endoctrine system which interfere with reproductive capabilities.")
(comment signalState "The type of logic value this node is.")
(disjointWith EMailAddress PhoneNumber)
(comment SaladCourse "The collection of events defined as subevents within formal dining in which one eats salad.")
(comment FirstSecretary-HeadOfPoliticalParty "The #$FirstSecretary-HeadOfPoliticalParty of a country that is usually ruled by Communists.")
(comment War "A specialization of #$MilitaryConflictEvent and #$ViolentAction. Each instance of this collection is a state of open, armed, often prolonged conflict carried on between nations, states, or parties. It usually ends only with one of the parties #$Surrendering.")
(comment superlativeAdverb "The relationship between an #$EnglishWord and its superlative adverbial form.  Example: 'best'.")
(comment eventSubdivisionType "#$eventSubdivisionType(E ET NUM) means that temporal thing [#$TemporalThing] E is subdivided into a sequence of exactly NUM temporal things of type ET.  Each temporal thing in the sequence is contiguousBefore the next one in the sequence.  The first in the sequence starts E and the last one finishes E.")
(disjointWith Doctor-Medical NonPhysicianMedicalCareProfessional)
(comment Glyph-Abstract "largely pictorial characters used in ancient writing systems, esp. Mayan and Aztec")
(comment ConfusingOpponent "Confusing an opponent.")
(comment Massaging "The collection of events in which someone is massaged.")
(comment Flippancy "Emotion shown by irresponsibly gay or indifferent behavior, when seriousness is expected. Empty conduct")
(disjointWith PersonTypeByActivity PharmacyProductType)
(comment HundredDollarBill-US "The US 100 dollar bill -- with Benjamin Franklin on it")
(comment Boil-Infection "A skin infection characterized by inflamed, swollen hair follicles filled with pus.")
(comment Scar "The markings left over from cuts.")
(comment ShootingAGun-Portable "The firing of a small, portable gun, like a pistol.")
(comment LightweightGRWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of GRWrestlingSportsEvent")
(comment CycLAssertionDirection "The collection of possible inference \"directions\" that a #$CycLAssertion
can have.  A given CycL assertion's direction (see #$assertionDirection) 
indicates something about how and when the assertion can be used in inferences
by the Cyc system.  More precisely: #$Backward-AssertionDirection indicates
that the assertion can only be used in inferences carried out when a query
is asked; #$Forward-AssertionDirection indicates that the assertion can be used 
in inferences carried out at the time the assertion is added to the Knowledge 
Base as well as those carried out at ask-time; and #$Code-AssertionDirection
indicates that the assertion itself cannot be used in either backward 
(ask-time) or forward (assert-time) inferences, but is instead implemented 
in the underlying code of the Cyc system.  Each CycL assertion has exactly 
one of the above three directions; the default direction is Forward for 
ground atomic assertions (see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence) and Backward for 
rule assertions.  Note that a CycL sentence is given a direction at the time 
of its assertion to the system, and this fact _need_not_ be reflected in 
another, #$assertionDirection assertion's being added to the system (as
that would of course lead to an infinite regress).")
(comment poBoxNumber "Gives the number of the P.O. Box of an address.  E.g., in P.O. Box 1677-B, New York, NY, the entry on this slot would be the string ``1677-B''.")
(comment LegalHoliday-UnitedStates "The set of standard #$LegalHolidays officially celebrated throughout the United States of America.  Schools, banks, Federal and State offices are closed.  Many businesses are closed on these holidays; service businesses tend to have reduced business hours.  Some of these are #$ReligiousHolidays, and some are #$Mondays immediately following a #$ReligiousHoliday, and some commemorate some historically important (to the USA) #$Event or #$Person.")
(comment LongTime "This is a qualifier to be used as an optional argument to temporal relations.")
(comment (FruitFn FigTree) "The collection of individual Figs.")
(comment Translation-NoLocationChange "A collection of translational motion events; hence a subcollection of #$Movement-TranslationEvent.  In any instance of #$Translation-NoLocationChange, the #$objectMoving undergoes translational motion but ends up where it started --- i.e., there is no NET movement; i.e., its #$fromLocation and #$toLocation are the same.  Between the beginning and the end of a #$Translation-NoLocationChange, the #$objectMoving may visit the #$toLocation and the #$fromLocation any number of times.   E.g., consider the motion of a person who is born in, and 80 years later dies in, the very same hospital, and has been there a few times in between for operations, visiting patients, etc.  A less dramatic example is the motion of your car on a particular day, as it gets moved around, crosses its own path a few times, etc., but ends the day in the same place it started.   Instances of #$Translation-NoLocationChange may be periodic or nonperiodic movements.  An important subcollection of #$Translation-NoLocationChange is #$Translation-RoundTrip.")
(comment SaleByCheck "A specialization of #$Buying. Each instance of #$SaleByCheck is a buying event in which the payment tendered (see the predicate #$objectTendered) is an instance of #$Check-TenderObject (q.v.).")
(comment agreeingBuyer "Agreeing agents that have the buying role in a sales contract")
(comment GymRings "The piece of gymnastic equipment used during a rings routine, with two rings hanging from ropes.")
(comment NursingDegree-RN "The set of degrees that registered nurses have.")
(comment Intangible "The collection of things that are not physical -- are not made of, or encoded in, matter.  Every #$Collection is an #$Intangible (even if its instances are tangible), and so are some #$Individuals.  Caution: do not confuse `tangibility' with `perceivability' -- humans can perceive light even though it's intangible--at least in a sense.  For more on this issue, see the relevant #$cyclistNotes.")
(comment interArgFormat5-3 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat5-3 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the third argument-place of PRED when PRED's fifth argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ... ARGN) in which ARG5 is an instance of COL, 
PRED's arg3 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG3' 
in the preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its 
instances for further explanation.")
(comment policyHolder "The agreeing Agent that receives the insurance.")
(comment availableForEvent "(#$availableForEvent AGENT OBJECT EVENT) means that AGENT has available OBJECT for the event EVENT.  That is, if AGENT is capable of using OBJECT in EVENT, nothing prevents AGENT from choosing to use OBJECT in EVENT.  Note that if OBJECT is #$availableForEvent to AGENT in EVENT, AGENT may still, for other reasons, be incapable of using OBJECT in EVENT.")
(comment HurdleSportsEvent "The collection of races with hurdles.")
(comment DermatoPathologist "A dernatopathologist is a doctor who specializes in diagnosis and treatment of diseases of the skin.")
(comment SlidingConnection "The sliding connection")
(comment DitransitiveNP-ThatClauseFrame "This frame is used for words that take exactly two complements,

          the first of which is an NP and the second a that-clause.

          In HPSG terms: [COMPS  <NP, S[that]>] Example: 'I assure you that this car is new'.")
(comment specialEventFor "The event ARG1 has some special (sacred, memorable, emotionally-charged) significance for the agent ARG2.")
(comment SaladCourse "The salad course, if it happens during a given #$HavingAMeal, happens after the appetizer and/or soup courses if they occur.  It happens before the main and dessert courses.  For a given meal, there is no more than one salad course.")
(comment HeadOfMilitaryCouncil "The head of militaryCouncil of a nation")
(comment Fellow-FACN "This title is given to fellows of the American College of Nurses.")
(comment Doctor-Medical "An instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation, and a specialization of #$PersonWithOccupation. Each instance of #$Doctor-Medical is a person with a certain type of education in the field of medicine (usually such a person has obtained an MD degree) who is professionally licensed to practice medicine.")
(comment RomanLetter "The collection of all Roman (English) alphabet letters.  This includes our familiar alphabet of 26 letters, including upper and lower case letters.  They may also be used without regard to case (see #$UncasedLetter), as in spelling.  These letters are abstract characters (instances of #$Character-Abstract) from a character set, rather than physical printed or displayed letters (see #$CharacterToken).")
(comment LeaningForwardDuringFlight "During the flying part of the ski jump, leaning body forward.")
(comment Caressing "The collection of events in which someone is caressed.")
(comment Doubt "Feeling of unsureness; lack of certitude or conviction about someone or about the result of something. Skepticism. Carries no evil suspicion, as Mistrust does")
(comment JobInterview "The collection of events in which one or more agents interviews one or more other agents to determine if they are suitable candidates for a job/task/employment.")
(disjointWith MicrotheoryType PersonTypeByActivity)
(comment FilingPapers "The collection of all events in which an agent (person) files papers in a filing cabinet (the default), or in some other hardcopy-file storage device.")
(comment ThrowingTheFirstPitch "The opening ceremony of the baseball season in which the president throws the first pitch.")
(comment IntrauterineDevice "The collection of all IUDs.  An IUD is a birth-control device made from plastic and copper which fits inside a woman's uterus.")
(comment QuadScullsRowingSportsEvent "The rowing sports events in which sculls are propelled by four rowers with two oars each.")
(comment HumanSchoolageChild "Kids that are of the age to go to school and are younger than teenagers (between the ages of 5 and 12).")
(comment Forward-AssertionDirection "An instance of #$CycLAssertionDirection (q.v.).  A CycL assertion that
has the #$Forward-AssertionDirection can be used in inferences carried 
out at the time the assertion is added to the Knowlege Base as well as 
those carried out at when a query is asked.  This is the default direction 
for ground atomic assertions (see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence).  Contrast 
with #$Backward-AssertionDirection and #$Code-AssertionDirection.  Also 
see #$assertionDirection.")
(comment ist-Information "An instance of #$MicrotheoryDesignatingPredicate (q.v.) and a specialization of #$ist (q.v.).  (#$ist-Information PIT SENT) means that the #$Proposition (q.v.) expressed by SENT is part of the explicitly-stated (as opposed to the merely inferred) informational content of the #$PropositionalInformationThing PIT.  This does _not_ entail that SENT itself is asserted either in PIT (cf. #$ist-Asserted) or in some more general microtheory PIT-GENL whose content PIT inherits (via the inverse of #$genlMt); but it does entail that either (i) a sentence SENT-PRIME that has the same informational content (i.e. expresses the same proposition) as SENT is asserted in PIT or in some PIT-GENL or (ii) SENT is a conjunction each conjunct CONJi of which is such that there is some sentence with the same informational content as CONJi asserted either in PIT or in some PIT-GENL.")
(disjointWith Sleeping QualitativeTimeOfDay)
(comment ShortTime "This is a qualifier to be used as an optional argument to temporal relations.")
(comment VisualInformationBearingThing "A specialization of both #$Artifact-Generic and #$InformationBearingThing.  Each instance of this collection is an artifact from which information is extracted by viewing it (note that a viewer may need to be familiar with an appropriate set of interpretive conventions in order to do this).  Examples of #$VisualInformationBearingThing include handwritten letters, newspapers, sculptures, television sets, and neon signs.  (Thus, the information content of #$VisualInformationBearingThings may or may not be propositional in nature.)  In the proper conditions, instances of #$VisualInformationBearingThing produce instances of #$VisualImage (which, unlike instances of #$VisualInformationBearingThing, are instances of #$Event).  For example, if one shines light on a photograph, a characteristic #$VisualImage is produced.  Likewise, if one electrifies a neon sign, a #$VisualImage is produced. A notable specialization of this collection is #$StillImageSource -- sources of #$VisualImage that do not move (which thus includes all the examples of #$VisualInformationBearingThing given above except for the television set). See also the predicate #$visuallyDepicts.")
(comment (FruitFn Legume-ThePlant) "The kind of fruit borne by members of the legume order - the classic pea pod, which splits into two halves when dry.")
(comment LogicalTable "The collection of all contexts (mts) in which the actual content of a database table is represented. The schema (defining information) for a #$LogicalTable will be represented in an instance of #$LogicalTableSchema. An instance of #$LogicalTable will be related to an instance of #$LogicalTableSchema with the predicate #$usesSchema.")
(comment SwimmingTheLengthOfOlympicPool "Swimming one lap in a 50 M pool. A lap is swimming the length of the pool once, NOT down and back.")
(comment BidOnSale "A proposal formulated by a potential seller, communicated to a potential buyer.  If accepted by both, may turn into a contract.")
(comment DoctorOfEducationDegree "An advanced degree in Education.  Different than a PhD in Education according to the UT School of Education.")
(comment TransitiveInfinitivePhraseFrame "This frame is used for transitive words (usually verbs or adjectives) that take exactly one

          complement which is an infinitive phrase. In HPSG terms:

          [COMPS  <CP[infinitive]>] Example: 'I decided to leave'.")
(comment insuranceFundedBy "The agent that pays for an insurance policy - not necessarily the #$insuredAgent or the #$policyHolder (esp. the employer).")
(disjointWith Obligation Proposal)
(comment MexicanImmigrantToUSA "Folks who have come from #$Mexico to the USA to work")
(comment Hugging "Two people wrap their arms around one another to show their affection for each other.")
(comment RadiationOncologist "An radiation oncologist is a doctor who specializes using radiation in the diagnosis and treatment of tumors.")
(comment nationalBudgetRevenues "(#$nationalBudgetRevenues NATION MONEY) means that MONEY is the total revenue in the budget of NATION.  The vast majority of such revenues are usually mostly in the form of taxes or revenues from nationally owned industries. However, included in such revenues could also be in money gained from NATION selling arms or presumably from receiving certain kinds of monetary aid.")
(comment SelectingSomething "A collection of events.  Each instance of #$SelectingSomething is an event, perhaps an extended activity, during which something is selected.  Selecting may be relatively simple or prolonged and complex; e.g., selecting an apple from a grocery store's produce counter, or choosing a general contractor to build a new courthouse.  An instance of #$SelectingSomething may have sub-events (see the predicate #$subEvents) which are instances of #$Research or #$Evaluating, in which an agent gathers information about the options.  The selecting ends with a choice being made.")
(comment AppetizerCourse "The appetizer course, if it happens during a given #$HavingAMeal, happens first.  For a given meal there is no more than one appetizer course.")
(comment Sultan-HeadOfGovernment "The #$Sultan-HeadOfGovernment of a country.")
(comment AirFrontEvent "The collection of all #$WeatherEvents in which one large atmospheric air mass moves into a region of different temperature with a well defined boundry.  The edge of the moving air mass is the locus of the #$AirFrontEvent.")
(comment Fellow-FACG "This title is given to fellows of the American College of Gastroenterology.")
(comment IndividualAgent "An instance of #$ExistingObjectType and a specialization of #$Agent-Generic.  Each instance of #$IndividualAgent is an instance of #$Agent-Generic that is not itself a group composed of other instances of #$Agent-Generic.  Notable specializations of #$IndividualAgent include #$Person and #$Animal. Note that #$Organization is not a specialization of #$IndividualAgent, since instances of #$Organization are groups composed of other instances of #$Agent-Generic.")
(disjointWith BlueCollarWorker Doctor-Medical)
(comment Quasi-AlphabeticWriting "so very nearly an alphabet")
(comment ObstructingATeamMember "Getting in the way of a fellow teammember.")
(comment Pinching "The collection of events in which something is pinched.")
(comment Misery "Feeling of unhappiness and wretched condition attending distress and suffering")
(comment Interviewing "The collection of events in which one or more agents interviews one or more other agents for the purpose of gathering information (usually about the interviewees, or about something in which they have a vested interest).")
(comment TenDollarBill-US "The US 10 dollar bill -- with Alexander Hamilton on it")
(comment HumanYoungAdult "Adults between 18 and 35 years of age.")
(comment SpeechPart "The collection of all parts of speech -- a specialization of #$LinguisticObjectType. Instances of #$SpeechPart include #$Preposition, #$Adverb, #$CountNoun, #$Determiner, #$QuantifyingIndexical, #$Punctuation-SP, #$Pronoun).  To link a specific word with the parts of speech for which it has forms, see #$posForms; e.g., #$You-TheWord has a #$Pronoun form, #$And-TheWord has a #$CoordinatingConjunction form, #$Hit-TheWord has both #$CountNoun and #$Verb forms.")
(comment Shopping "Events in which the performer pursues the purchase of something, whether or not there is a purchase.  Shoppings may involve #$LookingForSomething, GatheringInformation, Evaluating that information, and Buying.  This is the overarching event, under which a Buying may occur.")
(comment AFewCenturiesDuration "Duration of 2 to 10 centuries")
(comment MogulsSportsEvent "The alpine sports event in which competitors are judged on their negotiation of a mogul field")
(comment Backward-AssertionDirection "An instance of #$CycLAssertionDirection (q.v.).  A CycL assertion that
has the #$Backward-AssertionDirection can only be used in inferences that 
are carried out when a query is asked. This is the default direction for 
rule assertions.  Contrast with #$Forward-AssertionDirection and #$Code-AssertionDirection.  Also see #$assertionDirection.")
(comment ist-Obligation "This is a form of #$ist that applies to the specified details of an obligation; #$ist itself is used for other conditions that are true but not part of the obligation.  For example, the fact that Joe is obligated to sweep the floor is #$ist-Obligation; this requires Joe to be an agent, which is an #$ist type of condition.")
(comment imperviousToStuffTypes "Any spatially continuous instance of StuffType U will not let any instance of StuffType V pass through it.")
(comment June "A specialization of #$CalendarMonth.  Each instance of #$June is the sixth month of a particular year in the #$GregorianCalendar (q.v.).")
(comment LocomotionAccident "A specialization of #$Accident and #$CompositePhysicalAndMentalEvent. Each instance of this collection is an accident had by an #$Animal while locomoting (i.e. moving under its own power, c.f. #$LocomotionEvent-Animal). Thus this collection includes instances of falling, bumping into things, slipping, and drowning.....A notable specialization of this collection is #$Tripping.")
(comment (FruitFn LemonTree) "The collection of individual Lemons.")
(comment keysOfTable "The keys for tables using the #$LogicalTableSchema ARG1 are the logical fields represented by the terms in the #$TermSet ARG2.")
(comment SportsRecord "The collection of records for sports events.")
(comment SalesContractNegotiation "A specialization of #$ContractNegotiation and #$CommercialActivity. Each instance of this collection is a negotiation intended to result in an agreement (cf. #$SalesAgreement) which is a sales contract.")
(comment SkiJumpSportsEvent "Ski jump sports events, both normal and large hills")
(comment BillingLocation "A  specialization of #$MailingLocation.  Each instance of #$BillingLocation is a location to which invoices are sent.  For most private individuals, their billing location is their home address.")
(comment SubLObject "The collection of computational (i.e., abstract, intangible, syntactically structured) objects which make up Cyc's CycL-based system.")
(comment DitransitiveNP-ADJPFrame "This frame is used for words that take exactly two complements,

          the first of which is an NP and the second an AdjP. 

          In HPSG terms: [COMPS  <NP, AdjP>] Examples: 'They consider Kim stupid' and 'Chris ate the fish raw'.")
(comment thingSpecified "The class of things this specification concerns.  This slot does  not always have a value for every specification.   For example, in the buying domain, a buyer may have a specification for the item or items he is trying to obtain.  That sort of specification would not be the type that is intended to apply to a class of things. ")
(comment interArgFormat4-2 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat4-2 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the second argument-place of PRED when PRED's fourth argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ... ARGN) in which ARG4 is an instance of COL, 
PRED's arg2 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG2' 
in the preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its 
instances for further explanation.")
(comment Market "Markets can be thought of as all sales satisfying some criterion - for example, sales in the US of home furnishings, or worldwide sales to teenagers of Billy Idol records.")
(comment clients "This predicate relates two agents.  (#$clients AGENT1 AGENT2) means that AGENT1 provides goods and/or services to AGENT2.  AGENT2 may or may not pay AGENT1 for the goods/services received.  The predicate #$clients can indicate either a one-time or a more long-term relationship.  See also #$suppliers and #$customers.")
(comment PerformSimultaneouslyFn "This is a variadic function. (#$PerformSimultaneouslyFn script-type1 script-type2 ...) denotes the class of events where a person simultaneously performs script-type1, script-type2 ... A script-type may be repeated many times in the argument list of #$PerformSimultaneouslyFn and indicates performing that many of that kind of script-type simultaneously. The order of arguments does not matter.")
(comment intends "This predicate can be used to state some particular thing that a given intelligent agent intends or has in mind as a purpose, represented as a propositional attitude. (#$intends AGENT SENT) means that AGENT intends the proposition PROP expressed by SENT to become (or remain) true. This implies that AGENT believes s/he has at least some degree of influence or control over bringing about (or maintaining) the truth of PROP.  While this predicate is obviously similar to #$goals (q.v.), AGENT's intending PROP is likely to be more short-term and event-centered (\"I did it because I intended that...\") and more mechanically satisfied (\"I intend to turn off the lamp\") than any of AGENT's goals. You may intend to turn off the lamp, but it would be odd to call that one of your goals.  For a similar predicate that represents intending in relation to types of temporal situations, see #$intends-SitType.")
(comment HeadAndNeckSurgeon "A head and neck surgeon is a doctor who specializes in performing surgical procedures on the head and neck.")
(disjointWith SelectingSomething ApplyingAForce)
(comment mtImageBackground "ARG2 is the background region of the image space described by assertions made in ARG1.")
(comment SoupMealCourse "The soup course, if it happens during a given #$HavingAMeal, happens after the #$AppetizerCourse, if there is one.  For a given meal, there is no more than one soup meal course.")
(comment ReligiousHeadOfCountry "The religious head of country of a nation")
(comment GeriatricPsychiatrist " A geriatric psychiatrist is a doctor who specializes in diagnosing and treating mental problems of the elderly.")
(disjointWith DeadLanguage LivingLanguage)
(comment MinimizingWindResistance "The streamlining of an object such that wind resistance is minimized.")
(comment Rubbing "A collection of events.  An instance of #$Rubbing is an event in which the #$objectActedOn is rubbed.")
(comment Pleasure-Feeling "Agreeable feeling of gratification or satisfaction")
(comment SportsOfficial "People who enforce the rules of sports, such as Referee, Umpire, Linesmen, etc.")
(comment FiveDollarBill-US "The US 5 dollar bill -- with Abraham Lincoln on it")
(comment Modal-Contracted "The collection of all contracted modal forms. The only modals which can contract are 'would' and 'will'. Example: -ll from 'will'.")
(comment Verb "The collection of all verbs. Verbs usually denote events, states, or processes. Verbs can be conjugated. Example: `eat'.")
(comment Spoiling "A collection of events.  In a #$Spoiling event, an object deteriorates to the point that it is no longer suitable for its intended purpose (whether that purpose is natural or imposed).  For example, spoiled food is food which has become inedible (either too unhealthy and/or too unappetizing to eat).  Note that spoiled food might still be quite suitable for compost; being `spoiled' is always relative to some intended use.")
(comment AFewYearsDuration "Duration of 2 to 10 years")
(comment FoilFencingSportsEvent "Competitive events of foil fencing for sport, a kind of sword play.")
(comment President-CorporateOfficer "A collection of people.  An instance of #$President-CorporateOfficer is designated as `President' on the official records of the company or corporation for which s/he works.  Every company has a President.  A company president is often also the Chief Executive Officer (CEO), and there is no superior authority in the company other than the Board of Directors and its Chairperson.")
(comment schemeForBilling "A slot indicating the way #$basicPrice is calculated in a Buying.  See the instances of BillingScheme for more info.")
(disjointWith Heartbeating QualitativeTimeOfDay)
(comment December "A specialization of #$CalendarMonth.  Each instance of #$December is the twelth and final month of a particular year in the #$GregorianCalendar (q.v.).")
(comment queryNL "ARG2 is a string which more or less expresses the meaning of the CycL query expression ARG1.")
(disjointWith CashAndCarrySale SaleWithDelivery)
(comment agreeingSeller "Agreeing agents that have the selling role in a sales contract.")
(comment scaleUsedInJudgement "(#$scaleUsedInJudgement STYPE CRITERION SCALE) states that when evaluating scripts of type STYPE for performance of a CRITERION, the values of the scoring metric are all instances of SCALE.  For example, when judging figure skating for technical merit, the 0-10 scale is used.")
(comment YesOrNoField "RF's whose entries are truth values, i.e., YES or NO.")
(comment EnergyQuantity "Energy, or work, is force times distance; it is measured in Joules in the MKS system.")
(comment Preposition-Directional "The collection of all prepositions which express a directional, dynamic spatial relation. Example: 'into', as in 'the man walked into the room'.")
(comment documentsDifference "(#$documentsDifference OBJ1 OBJ2 ASPECT EXP) says that the difference in some ASPECT between OBJ1 and OBJ2 is described somehow by the expression EXP")
(comment claimedAmount "ARG2 is the amount of money that the insurance claim ARG1 states is due to the #$policyHolder.")
(comment MedicaidPatient "A person who is eligible for Medicaid coverage.")
(comment MoneyTransaction "A specialization of both #$CommercialActivity and #$MoneyTransfer.  Each instance of #$MoneyTransaction is an event in which a transfer of money occurs, and the transfer is done in exchange for something else, according to some (implicit or explicit) agreement.  Thus, buying something, investing, making a donation, executing a bequest, and exchanging currency are all examples of money transactions.")
(comment operatingCost "The cost to operate ARG1. This includes the cost of using it (e.g. the cost of gas in using a car) and the cost of maintaining it.")
(comment depthOfObject "Depth of an object, usually used to measure things that go down, like valleys and lakes and wells")
(comment AIResearchDepartment "Department that does research in artificial intelligence.")
(comment PediatricCardiologist "A pediatric cardiologist is a doctor who specializes in the study and care of the heart in children.")
(comment SeasonsDuration "The length of a season is a quarter-year")
(disjointWith SelectingSomething SportsCompetition)
(comment degreeIn "Gives the field of study associated with a particular degree.")
(comment DessertCourse "The dessert course, if it happens during a given #$HavingAMeal, happens after the main course.")
(comment MarineBiologist "A Scientist whose major research emphasis is MarineBiology.")
(disjointWith CalendarCoveringType ClimateCycleType)
(comment superlativeDegree "The relationship between an #$EnglishWord and its superlative adjectival form. This is often formed by suffixing 'est' to the regular form. Example: 'strongest'.")
(comment UnitOfAcceleration "A specialization of #$UnitOfRate. Each instance of #$UnitOfAcceleration is a function which returns an instance of #$Acceleration (q.v.) when applied to a real number (see the collection #$SubLRealNumber) or a sequence of two real numbers. For instance, (#$MetersPerSecondPerSecond 32) is an acceleration of 32 meters per second per second.")
(comment DermatoImmunologist " A dermatoimmunologist is a doctor who specializes in immunological disorders the skin.")
(comment MusicalNotation-General "The class of notations which give instruction to the musician as to what to play or sing.  An example would be the notation used most commonly in western music traditions, where marks or notes are written, on or between lines that designate different musical notes (e.g. A,B,C,D,E,F,G in various octaves); each mark corresponds to such a note that is to be played or sung.")
(comment Rebounding "In basketball, taking possession of the ball after a failed shot.")
(comment ReadingAloud "A collection of actions; each of which is the action of

reading textual material aloud.")
(comment Gloominess "Low spirits; Depression. Without cheerfulness or optimism")
(comment BasketballTeam "An organization of athletes that play basketball.")
(comment PubliclyHeldCorporation "A specialization of both #$Business and #$LegalCorporation.  Each instance of #$PubliclyHeldCorporation is an incorporated business whose stock (see the collection #$Stock) is traded publicly on some stock exchange or other public securities market.  Businesses that are not traded publicly are instances of #$PrivatelyHeldCorporation (q.v.).")
(comment DeskWorker "A subcollection of #$PersonWithOccupation.  #$DeskWorker is a very broad category, consisting of those people who do a significant amount of their work sitting at desks (as opposed, e.g., to those who do physically demanding or outdoor work).  While the sorts of work performed at desks make up too heterogeneous a class for #$DeskWorker itself to be considered an #$PersonTypeByOccupation (q.v.), some of its subcollections do correspond to types of occupations, e.g. #$Administrator, #$ComputerOperator, and #$Secretary.")
(comment target "This predicate relates any sort of \"transfer\" event to the \"place\" where the thing being transferred is intended, by the agent who performs or directs the transfer, to end up.  More precisely, (#$target TRANSFER TARGET) means that an agent playing either the  #$performedBy or #$directingAgent role in the #$GeneralizedTransfer TRANSFER intends that some tangible thing playing the #$transferredThing role in TRANSFER be at TARGET upon the completion of TRANSFER.  Obviously, this does not entail that the transferred thing actually end up at TARGET.  For example, if I throw a dart the target is likely to be a dartboard (or, if I'm really good, the bullseye), and when I drive my car immediately after work the target is likely to be my house.")
(comment soldAt "The agent that sells this individual item (could be a good or service). ")
(disjointWith Employee SelfEmployedWorker)
(comment CuttingNails "The event in which fingernails or toenails are cut. A nail cutter is held throughout.")
(comment M1000SpeedSkateSportsEvent "The 1000M speed skating competition")
(comment Stabilizing "The situation in which something is stabilized in equilibrium, such that changes to its position or orientation are resisted.")
(comment UnskilledWorker "A subcollection of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each instance of #$UnskilledWorker is a person who holds a job that requires little skill or training.  Although such jobs are too various in kind for this collection to constitute an instance of OccupationType (q.v.) in its own right, certain specializations of #$UnskilledWorker are occupation-types.")
(disjointWith Breathing QualitativeTimeOfDay)
(comment keepsObjectOut "U keeps out objects v1, v2, ....")
(comment September "A specialization of #$CalendarMonth.  Each instance of #$September is the ninth month of a particular year in the #$GregorianCalendar (q.v.).")
(comment WeddingAnniversaryCelebration "Celebrations held on or near the anniversary of a wedding to commemorate the marriage.  Attendees might include only the couple, but could include others as well -- but that's more common for 'important' anniversaries like the 20th, 50th, etc.")
(comment Slimy "Slimy.")
(comment MovingInACircle "Elements of #$MovingInACircle are events in which any #$objectMoving moves along a #$motionPathway-Complete which is roughly circular and does so periodically.  For example, a spacecraft in orbit is an #$objectMoving in such an event.")
(comment Convention-Meeting "A large gathering of people with a common interest meeting together to discuss and present relevant information")
(comment interArgFormat2-1 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat2-1 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the first argument-place of PRED when PRED's second argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ... ARGN) in which ARG2 is an instance of COL, PRED's arg1
position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG1' in the 
preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its instances 
for further explanation.")
(comment insuringAgent "The agreeingAgent that provides the insurance.")
(comment SocialBeing "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent.  Each instance of #$SocialBeing is an intelligent agent whose status as an agent is acknowledged within some social system, and who is capable of playing certain social roles within that system.  Note that in many (but not all) cases, a #$SocialBeing will have certain rights and responsibilities associated with his/her/its status within the relevant social system.  For agents who are granted rights and responsibilities under some legal system, see the specialization #$LegalAgent.  Other  notable specializations of #$SocialBeing are #$Person and #$Organization.")
(comment DistributedFlowRate "the rate at which stuff piles up.")
(comment RoleReferentTheTerm "The Terms which may denote roles in some situation or specification. For example, ThePowerSource is a role that may be present in various dynamic situations.")
(comment ServiceEstablishment "A specialization of both #$CommercialServiceOrganization and #$SingleSiteLocalOrganizationWithClients.  Each instance of #$ServiceEstablishment is a local, commercial service organization with a single physical location.  Notable specializations of #$ServiceEstablishment include #$Restaurant-Organization and #$ShoeRepairShop.")
(comment CensusGroupOfUSNativeAmericans-Generic "The collection of persons identified on US census forms as having origins within ethnic groups of Native Americans.")
(comment AMAGroupPracticeID "An 8-character code used by the American Medical Association to identify group practices.")
(comment Barrel-UnitOfVolume "A function which returns an element of #$Volume.  One barrel -- (#$Barrel-UnitOfVolume 1) -- is about 158.97 #$Liters.")
(comment hasVisibleSurfacePatternType "ARG1 (the surface or visible parts of ARG1) has a visual pattern of type ARG2.")
(comment MedicineRelatedFieldAttribute "Field attributes for fields likely to be found in a hospital data base.")
(comment Mathematician "Scientist engaged in the study, development and understanding of Mathematics and its applications")
(disjointWith WeatherEvent Music)
(comment chairpersonOfEvent "(#$chairpersonOfEvent EVENT CHAIR) means that the #$Person CHAIR is the chairperson of EVENT.  The #$arg1Isa, #$SocialGathering may be generalized but in the meantime keeping it possibly overspecific will help prevent divergence (i.e. will help prevent people from asserting #$chairpersonOfEvent facts about new terms that should have #$SocialGathering as their genl.")
(comment PediatricPathologist " A pediatric pathologist is a doctor who specializes in diagnosis and treatment of diseases in children.")
(comment Comma-TheSymbol "The comma symbol ',', as a #$Character-Abstract.")
(comment MakingATriplePlay "Getting three members of the opposing team out, in the same play.")
(comment developedProductType "The agent who designed or developed the stated product type.")
(comment Security-Emotion "Freedom from danger, fear or anxiety")
(comment BaseballTeam "An organization of athletes that play baseball.")
(disjointWith RetailChainStore PubliclyHeldCorporation)
(comment tenderValue "A predicate which relates instances of #$TenderObject (such as dollar bills, foodstamps, vouchers, etc), to the amount of money they explicitly represent. (#$tenderValue TENDER VALUE) means that the #$TenderObject TENDER represents the #$MonetaryValue VALUE. In rare cases, (#$monetaryValueOfThing TENDER VALUE) will not be true, as in the case of rare coins or stamps which may be worth much more than their value as legal tender. However, usually TENDER's #$tenderValue is its value simpliciter.")
(comment SelfEmployedWorker "A subcollection of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each instance of #$SelfEmployedWorker is a worker who earns a living from funds paid directly to him/her by customers, or who is paid by a company s/he owns.   Self-employed workers have no boss or supervisor.")
(comment Receivable "The financial obligation for a specific sale of goods or services.")
(comment StandingInLine "You stand, you take a step forward, you stand some more, you take a step forward...The process of standing in a line, waiting in an orderly fashion till it's your turn to perform some action")
(comment HairCuttingEvent "The collection of hair cutting events.  This refers to the whole (composite) event of getting/giving a haircut, not to cutting individual strands of hair.  The latter are #$subEvents of #$HairCuttingEvent.")
(comment RythmicGymnasticsSportsEvent "The collection of rythmic gymnastic events.")
(comment negligibleWRT "#$negligibleWRT(OOM1 OOM2) states that order of magnitude quantity OOM1 is negligible compared to order of magnitude quantity OOM2.  Therefore, any quantity Q1 subsumed by OOM1 is negligible compared to any quantity Q2 subsumed by OOM2.")
(disjointWith InvoluntaryBodyMovement QualitativeTimeOfDay)
(comment March "A specialization of #$CalendarMonth. Each instance of #$March is the third month of a particular year in the #$GregorianCalendar (q.v.).")
(comment (FruitFn FlaxPlant) "The fruit of the flax plant; a capsule containing about 10 flax seeds, or linseeds.")
(comment CreditSale "A collection of events.  In an instance of #$CreditSale, the customer buys something using credit --- the seller extends that credit to the customer.  
Note: #$CreditSale events differ from instances of #$SaleByCreditCard, because in credit card sales, the seller is paid in full by the credit card company.  The credit used by a credit-card customer is not extended by the seller.")
(comment judicialActionType "After an agent performs an event of type arg1, the agent performs an event of type arg3 which is a penalty assessed by the judicial agent in arg1 of type arg2.")
(comment Housepainter "Someone who paints houses as a job.")
(comment Baptism "The collection of events in which someone--usually, but not exclusively, a baby--is admitted into a religion--typically a Christian church--by being sprinkled with, or immersed in, water.")
(comment RunningATutorial "Going through the exercies of a tutorial in order to become acquainted with the features of something.")
(comment costOfLicense "If you buy a program, you must pay the costOfLicense value.  Even in a store like K-mart when you are buying for your PC.")
(comment absorbencyOfSubstInSubst "(#$absorbencyOfSubstInSubst SUBST ABSORBER-TYPE ATTRIB) indicates that the particular #$TangibleThing SUBST is absorbed by stuff of the #$ExistingStuffType ABSORBER-TYPE with the #$Absorbency ATTRIB.")
(comment BankOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations that are in the banking business, whether in the private or public sector.  An instance of #$BankOrganization may be as large and as multinational in character as #$BankOfAmerica or as small and local as the branch of the UT Federal Credit Union located on Guadalupe Street.")
(comment plaintiffs "(#$plaintiffs ARG1 ARG2) means that the agent ARG2 is the complaining party (the party bringing an accusation of wrong-doing) in the lawsuit ARG1.")
(comment Dexamethasone "The chemical compound which is a cortico-steroid. It helps reduce inflammatory tissue.")
(disjointWith TameAnimal WildAnimal)
(comment EmploymentRelatedFieldAttribute "A field that is likely to be found in a personnel data base.")
(comment Physicist "Scientist engaged in the development and application of Physics")
(comment DentalDegree-BDS "A bachelor's degree in dentistry.")
(comment PediatricCriticalCareSpecialist " A pediatric critical care specialist is a doctor who specializes in treating children who are in intensive care situations.")
(comment QuestionMark-TheSymbol "The question mark symbol '?', most often used used at the end of a sentence to indicate doubt or ask a question.  This is the abstract character (see #$Character-Abstract), not any physical instantiation.")
(comment FallingBackwards "Falling so as to land on one's posterior or back.")
(comment awardingAgent "The body who authorizes this award to be given out, not the individual who physically hands the award to the recipient.")
(comment Patience "Feeling of a person that endures trials, pains, provocation or waiting  calmly or without complaint")
(comment SportsLeague "A collection of organizations.  An element of #$SportsLeague is an organization of sports team organizations, specialized by sport.  Important types of #$SportsLeague are #$MajorLeague, #$MinorLeague, and college sports league.  In many cases, sports leagues are further specialized by region (continent, country, or region).  Examples: #$NationalFootballLeague, #$NationalHockeyLeague, #$CentralDivision-NBA, #$NationalLeagueEast-Baseball.")
(comment HalfDollarCoin-US "The US half dollar -- 50 cents, silvery, with JFK on it")
(comment MarinePersonnel "A specialization of #$MilitaryPerson.  Each instance of #$MarinePersonnel is a person who is a member of some instance of #$MarineCorps (q.v.).")
(comment Adverb "The collection of all adverbs. Adverbs are words which can modify adverbs, verbs, or adjectives. Many adverbs are morphologically derived from adjectives. Example: `slowly'.")
(comment mobifiedEntries "arg3 is the set of entries on arg1's arg2 slot, considered as a mob.")
(comment DitransitiveNP-BareInfinitiveFrame "This frame is used for words that take exactly two complements,

          the first of which is an NP and the second a bare infinitive 

          (a bse VP, in HPSG). 

          In HPSG terms: [COMPS  <NP, VP[bse]>] Example: 'He watched them leave'.")
(comment Bullfight "The collection of sports events in which a bull is ritually exercised, and usually killed, by a matador and assistants known as banderilleros and picadores.  (Note this represents the Spanish style of bullfighting.)")
(comment ShavingBody "The collection of all events of shaving hairs from part of a body.  This is distinct from #$ShavingSomething, in which thin slices (\"shavings\") of the object being shaved are removed.")
(comment FigureSkatingSportsEvent "The collection of figure skating competitions")
(disjointWith PublishedMaterial Place)
(comment Oncologist "A doctor who specializes in the treatment of tumors.")
(comment keepsObjectIn "U keeps in objects v1, v2, ....")
(comment RainySeason "A specialization of #$SeasonOfYear.  Each instance of #$RainySeason is the wettest season of the year during an annual climate cycle (in terms of having the most intense preciptation) in a particular region.  Note that #$RainySeason is _not_ a specialization of #$CalendarSeason.")
(comment EatingAMorsel "A specialization of #$Ingesting and #$PhysicalDestructionEvent.  Each instance of #$EatingAMorsel is an event that starts with holding food, is followed by then chewing the food (if necessary), then swallowing it.  When #$HomoSapiens eat a morsel, the first thing they must do is hold the food somehow.  If it is with a #$Tool, then the #$deviceUsed should be a #$SilverwarePiece or pair of #$ChopSticks. If one is grabbing the food by hand then #$GrabbingOntoWithHand is used. Next #$Chewing happens (unless the food is a liquid). #$Swallowing ends after #$Chewing ends.")
(comment (FruitFn NutmegTree) "The fruit of the nutmeg tree, containing one nutmeg (the seed) and its associated mace-the spice (the aril of the seed).")
(disjointWith AreaCode Address-PhysicalLocationDesignator)
(comment PingPongTable "the table on which ping-pong is played.")
(comment SeasonFn "An instance of #$DateDenotingFunction.  When applied to an instance of #$CalendarSeasonType and #$CalendarYear, #$SeasonFn returns an instance of #$CalendarSeason.  (#$SeasonFn SEASON YEAR) denotes SEASON during  YEAR.  For example, (#$SeasonFn #$CalendarSpring (#$YearFn 1966)) denotes spring of 1966.")
(comment CubicMile "A unit of measure for Volume.")
(comment Distance "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity. Each instance of #$Distance is the length of a path in space extending from one point to another. In some contexts, for example in the argument 2 position of #$altitudeAboveSeaLevel, an instance of #$Distance will include directional information.  In these contexts, instances can take on positive or negative values.  In other contexts, directional information will not matter, and instances of #$Distance will only take on non-negative values.  See the specialization #$Distance-Absolute for measures of distance that necessarily do not include directional information, and thus are always non-negative.  An instance of #$Distance may be either a fixed interval, such as the height of the #$WashingtonMonumentInWashingtonDC or the altitude of the #$DeadSea, or a range, such as #$WithinAudibleDistance (see #$ScalarInterval for more explanation). See #$UnitOfDistance for the units used by Cyc to measure distances.")
(comment CableSocket " The socket that enables a connection with Cable TV to occur.")
(comment Rough "The attribute of feeling rough in texture")
(comment FinancialOrganization "#$FinancialOrganization is a specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$FinancialOrganization is primarily or significantly engaged in the #$FinancialIndustry or whose activities focus on that industry.  Instances of both #$CommercialServiceOrganizations (e.g., banks and brokerage houses) and #$NonProfitOrganizations (e.g., #$InternationalMonetaryFund) may be instances of #$FinancialOrganization.  Specializations of #$FinancialOrganization include #$BankOrganization, #$FinancialExchange, and #$InvestmentOrganization.")
(comment MillionBarrels "A function which returns an element of #$Volume.  One million barrels -- (#$MillionBarrels 1) or (#$Barrel-UnitOfVolume 1000000) -- is about 158.97 million #$Liters.")
(comment Precision "The collection of attributes that represent levels of precision needed to perform some activity accurately, i.e., within a narrow tolerance, whether those bounds be spatial (as for physical movements), perceptual, or intellectual.")
(comment InsuranceRelatedFieldAttribute "Field attributes for fields related to insurance.")
(comment ComputerScientist "A scientist knowledgeable in Computer Science, its theory, uses and applications")
(comment verbSemTrans "(#$verbSemTrans VERB NUM FRAME TRANS) means that the translation of word sense number NUM of VERB, appearing with subcategorization frame FRAME, is TRANS.")
(comment NursingDegree-DNS "A Doctoral degree in Nursing Science.")
(comment August "The collection of all Augusts,

 the eighth month of the year in the #$GregorianCalendar.")
(comment PediatricEmergencyMedicineSpecialist " A pediatric emergency medicine specialist is a doctor who specializes in the emergency medical treatment of children.")
(comment Semicolon-TheSymbol "The semicolon symbol ';', as a #$Character-Abstract.")
(comment InterceptingAPass "Catching a pass intended for a player on the opposing team.")
(comment Innocence "Feeling of freedom from guilt or sin")
(comment SportsEvent "A specialization of both #$GameEvent and #$SportsCompetition.  Each instance of #$SportsEvent is an entire sports competition at the end of which either a winner is declared or a draw is declared.  For instance, an entire sandlot baseball game would be a #$SportsEvent, but the first inning of that game would not, since the first inning is a proper part of the game, and since neither a winner nor a draw is declared at the end of the first inning.  Note that several #$SportsEvents can be organized into a #$SportsFormalCompetition (q.v.); for example, the 2001 World Series was a #$SportsFormalCompetition consisting of seven #$SportsEvents.  Specializations of #$SportsEvent include #$BaseballGame, #$TennisMatch, and #$FootballGame-American.")
(comment TwoDollarBill-US "The US 2 dollar bill -- with Thomas Jefferson on it")
(comment NonProfitEmployee "The collection of all instances of #$PersonWithOccupation (q.v.) who are employed by some non-profit organization, such as a college, museum, or charity foundation.")
(comment LegalAgreement "An instance of #$ObjectType, and a specialization of #$Agreement.  Each instance of #$LegalAgreement is an agreement which has a legal status; that is, it is recognized as a valid agreement by some government.  Notable specializations of #$LegalAgreement include #$SalesContract, #$Visa-Permit, and #$Account.")
(comment Preposition "The collection of all prepositions. Prepositions are function words which usually take a noun phrase complement. They usually express temporal, spatial, or other relations. Example: `at'.")
(comment Laugh "Laughs -- utterances caused by humor.")
(comment AFewMonthsDuration "A few months 2-10")
(comment LightHeavyweightFSWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of FSWrestlingSportsEvent")
(comment negligibleFluentWRT "#$negligibleFluentWRT(OBJ F(X) G(X)) states that the order of magnitude of F(OBJ) is #$negligibleWRT the order of magnitude of G(OBJ).  Another way of thinking of it is that F(OBJ) is negligible compared to G(OBJ).")
(comment MedicalCareProvider "A specialization of #$SocialBeing
instances of which are agents -- either individuals or organizations
-- who provide medical care in a professional capacity.  Specializations 
of #$MedicalCareProvider include #$MedicalCareProfessional and 
#$MedicalCareOrganization.")
(comment containerMaintainsCondition "The container (ARG1) maintains the value of some slot (ARG3) for the RegionType (ARG2).")
(comment SpringSeason "A specialization of#$SeasonOfYear.  Each instance of #$SpringSeason is, in a temperate climate cycle (see #$TemperateClimateCycle), the time ice from the preceding Winter melts, the average temperature starts to increase, the days get longer, plants begin to put forth buds, etc.  Note that #$SpringSeason represents the climatic aspects of spring; it is _not_ a specialization of #$CalendarSpring.  For the collection of the purely temporal  aspects of spring, see #$CalendarSpring.")
(comment groom "(#$groom WED GROOM) means that GROOM plays the part of the groom -- the male partner in the upcoming or recent marriage -- in WED.")
(comment (FruitFn SesamePlant) "The fruits of the sesame plant; seeds inside are sesame seeds; fruits are dry when mature and dehisce [open up], releasing the seeds.")
(comment SchemaPF "RESULT is a #$PhysicalField in the #$PhysicalTableSchema ARG1, which represents the physical database field named ARG2.")
(disjointWith PhoneNumber Address-PhysicalLocationDesignator)
(comment evaluationsReceived "(#$evaluationsReceived EVENT JUDGE CRITERIA VAL) states that the JUDGE gave the performer of EVENT an evaluation of VAL for how the EVENT satisfied a particular judging CRITERIA.")
(comment Trader "Instances are agents who trade goods and services for a living, or who facilitate such trades for a living.")
(comment claimedEvent "ARG1 is an insurance claim which is made for the expenses incurred in Event ARG2.")
(comment ComputerEngineer "They design computers.  Usually EEs, but not necessarily. They know low level software, too.")
(disjointWith WasteWaterPipe CleanWaterPipe)
(comment Insulin "A protein pancreatic hormone secreted by the islets of Langerhans that is essential for the metabolism of carbohydrates, and is used in the treatment and control of diabetes.")
(comment Creativity "Performing an activity creatively.")
(comment BillingRelatedFieldAttribute "A field likely to be found on a bill.")
(comment Chemist "A scientist trained in Chemistry")
(comment NursingDegree-CNS "This credential is given to clinical nurse specialists.")
(comment July "The collection of all Julys,

 the seventh month of the year in the #$GregorianCalendar.")
(comment UrologicalSurgeon " A urological surgeon is a doctor who specializes in performing surgerical procesdures on the urinary tract.")
(comment CloseParen-TheSymbol "The close-parenthesis character ')', usually used with an open-parenthesis character #$OpenParen-TheSymbol to delimit the en  a parenthetic clause in text.  It is also used in mathematics and logic to group other symbols together.  This refers to the abstract character (see #$Character-Abstract) rather than any physical instantiation.")
(comment BreakingOpponentsServe "In tennis, winning a game served by the opponent.")
(comment pagerNumberText "This string is the pager number of this object.")
(comment Belligerence "Hostility. Aggressive and unfriendly attitude or disposition. Enmity. Ill will; positive hatred")
(comment BaseballSwing "The collection of events in which a #$BaseballPlayer standing at #$HomePlate tries to make #$BaseballContact. The player uses a #$BaseballBat to try and #$Hitting-ProjectilePropelling the #$Baseball-Ball moving in a #$BaseballPitch.")
(comment DollarCoin-US "The US dollar coin")
(comment Scientist "An instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation, and a specialization of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each instance of #$Scientist is a person who is educated and employed in one (or more) of the natural, social, or abstract sciences.  Specializations of #$Scientist include the collections #$Astronomer, #$Chemist, #$Linguist, #$Mathematician, #$Geneticist, and #$CulturalAnthropologist.")
(comment DragRacing "Racing cars a very short distance (i.e. usually less than 1 mile) in a straight line towards a finish line.")
(comment Account-LegalAgreement "An instance of #$ObjectType and a specialization of #$LegalAgreement. Each instance of #$Account is a recorded obligation (of some particular type) between specified parties, consisting of \"funds\" (not necessarily monetary funds) which typically can be added to and drawn upon. Positive examples include instances of #$RetirementAccount, #$TravelExpenseAccount, and of the many types of #$FinancialAccount. Note that the contents of an account need not be monetary; for example, the contents may be amounts of time, as in the specializations #$VacationAccount and #$SickLeaveAccount. #$Account does not include debt obligations of fixed face value that cannot be increased or reduced (such as instances of #$Bond-Agreement).")
(comment Modal "The collection of all modal auxiliary verbs. Modals have only tensed forms, do not inflect for person and number, and can take contracted negation. Example: `should'.")
(comment moneyTransferMode "(#$moneyTransferMode TRANSACTION

TYPE) means that in some particular money transfer TRANSACTION,

the #$MoneyTenderType used in that transaction was TYPE, e.g.,

#$CreditCard, #$Check-TenderObject, etc.")
(comment LiftingOntoShoulders "When a person moves an object up to his/her shoulders and rests it there.")
(comment GoingToUniversity "The collection of attending a university events.")
(comment SlalomSportsEvent "The downhill slalom competition")
(comment widowOf "(#$widowOf DECEASED WIDOW) means that WIDOW is alive and was married to DECEASED at the time when DECEASED died.  Despite the name, WIDOW may be either a widow or a widower (female or male).  In cultures in which one may only have a single spouse, there may be only one widow(er) for any deceased.")
(comment BorderCheckpoint-LandTraffic "The collection of Border checkpoints whose primary purpose is to handle land-based traffic, e.g. people and goods travelling by car, truck, or foot.  Usually located on a road and at the border.")
(comment orderOfMagnitude "#$orderOfMagnitude(Q OOM) states that quantity Q is of the order of magnitude OOM")
(comment PhysicalCheckUp "The regular exam that doctors perform on their patients, as a matter of routine health care, rather than as a focus on a particular ailment.")
(comment insulatingAbility "U's relative ability as a thermal insulator is v1")
(comment FallSeason "A specialization of #$SeasonOfYear.  Each instance of #$FallSeason is the season during a temperate climate cycle (see #$TemperateClimateCycle) during which the bulk of harvesting occurs and many plants cease growth in order to enter a dormant period for the coming Winter. Thus instances of #$FallSeason also typically have harvest celebrations as sub-events.  Note that #$FallSeason represents the climatic aspects of Fall; it is _not_ a specialization of #$CalendarSeason.  For the collection of temporal extents of fall seasons, see #$CalendarAutumn.")
(comment (FruitFn AppleTree) "The collection of individual apples.")
(comment fieldDependentCodedValues "The value ARG2 is a candidate interpretation of ARG1 when ARG3 has the value ARG4.")
(comment winningScore "A specialized termination criterion.  The first agent in the competition to reach this winning score as the value of the #$metricOfEvaluation of the competition wins the competition.")
(comment QuartersDuration "A #$UnitOfTime function that takes one or two real numbers as arguments and returns, as its value, a comparable #$Time-Quantity attribute measured in quarter-years.  More precisely, an expression of the form (#$QuartersDuration NUM) denotes the (\"point-value\") #$Time-Quantity of being exactly NUM quarter-years in duration, and an expression of the form (#$QuartersDuration MIN MAX) denotes the (properly interval-like) #$Time-Quantity of being at least MIN quarter-years and at most MAX quarter-years in duration.")
(comment Rejecting-CommunicationAct "An acknowledgement in which the performer denies what was communicated to them in a prior communication.")
(comment numberOfUnitsSoldDuring "The number of units of product ARG1 sold during time interval ARG2 is ARG3")
(comment interArgFormat3-1 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat3-1 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the first argument-place of PRED when PRED's third argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3... ARGN) in which ARG3 is an instance of COL, PRED's arg1
position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG1' in the 
preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its instances 
for further explanation.")
(comment ExperimentalMedicalProcedure "The collection of medical procedures which are experimental at the time/place that they are performed.")
(comment Chef "This apparently means anyone who cooks as a job, as opposed to only the high-social-status 'chef'.")
(comment Pharmacist "The collection of professionals who are trained and licensed to prepare and distribute legal drugs.")
(comment nonDeliberateActors "(#$nonDeliberateActors ACT ACTOR) means that ACTOR plays some role in the #$Event ACT, but is not acting deliberately.  For example, #$JohnKennedy was a #$nonDeliberateActors in his assassination, a person is a #$nonDeliberateActors in his/her own autonomic bodily functioning, and Mount #$Vesuvius-Volcano was a #$nonDeliberateActors in the event of its eruption that destroyed Pompeii.  #$nonDeliberateActors is a negative specification of the role an actor has in an event; the role of particular #$nonDeliberateActors might be further specified positively, for example, with #$bodilyActedOn or #$bodilyDoer.")
(comment LiabilitySuit "The collection of law suits in which an agent or group of agents sues another agent or group of agents, ususally to win compensation for damages or injury suffered due to the real or presumed defects of a product, and/or the negligence of the parties judged responsible.  The parties judged to be guilty are held responsible (liable) for the damages suffered due to negligence or supplying/selling a defective product or service.")
(comment SystemOfMeasure "Basic systems of measure, FPS, MKS etc.")
(comment LevelOfHeatSensation "The type of internal sensation or feeling of heat. This unit is for describing how hot somebody feels internally.")
(comment objectIdentified "The object which this ID document identifies")
(comment FieldCluster "If two fields are members of the same #$FieldCluster, they are more likely to be found next to each other in a spreadsheet.")
(comment MechanicalEngineer "Engineers dealing with the mechanical aspects of matter: thermodynamics, kinetics, mechanics, etc., including micro and macroscopic interactions")
(comment gunCaliber "(#$gunCaliber GUN CALIBER) means that the 
particular gun GUN has a cylindrical bore of diameter CALIBER.")
(comment MedicalDegree-DPH "This degree is given to doctors who specialize in public health issues.")
(comment April "The collection of all Aprils, 

the fourth month of the year in the #$GregorianCalendar.")
(comment MusculoskeletalSpecialist " A musculoskeletal specialist is similar to an orthopaedic doctor except that a musculoskeletal specialist also dignosis and treats muscle-related problems.")
(comment OpenParen-TheSymbol "The open-parenthesis character '(', usually used with a closing parenthesis character #$CloseParen-TheSymbol to delimit a parenthetic clause in text.  It is also used in mathematics and logic to group other symbols together.  This refers to the abstract character (see #$Character-Abstract) rather than any physical instantiation.")
(comment ScoringATouch "Scoring in fencing.")
(comment Modesty "Feeling free from brashness, boldness or assertiveness. Has no connotation of inferiority; see Humility")
(comment OneDollarBill-US "The US dollar bill -- with George Washington on it")
(comment LegalConflict "This is the collection of conflicts that take place within the rules of a legal system.")
(comment Punctuation-SP "The collection of all punctuation marks. Example: '?' or ','.")
(comment PayingByPhone "A collection of events; a subset of #$Paying.  In an instance of #$PayingByPhone, the agent doing the paying (i.e., the #$fromPossessor of the money paid) uses a telephone connection to make the payment to the payee (the #$toPossessor) or the payee's agent.  An instance of #$PayingByPhone could involve electronically transferring funds (such as funds in a checking account) to the payee or verbally giving the payee authorization to charge the payer's credit card.")
(comment FungalInfection "An instance of #$InfectionTypeByPathogenType, and a specialization of #$Infection. Each instance of #$FungalInfection is an infection caused by fungi (see the constant #$Fungus).  Specializations of #$FungalInfection include #$Histoplasmosis and #$AthletesFoot.")
(comment Booing "What you do when you don't like a performance.")
(comment GoingToPreSchool "Attending a pre-school.")
(comment IceDancingSportsEvent "The ice dancing competition")
(comment divorcedFrom "Entries are the person(s) from whom U is divorced.")
(comment BorderCheckpointFacility "The collection of all Border checkpoint stations, that is, places through which people and goods must pass when entering a country.  Includes checkpoints on roads, at airports, and at seaports.  Not necessarily located at a border.")
(comment allNegligibleWRT "The Kleene plus of #$negligibleWRT.  See #$negligibleWRT for details")
(comment GraduateFn "Results in the collection of people who have successfully completed a course of education offered by an organization of type ARG1 - e.g. HighSchoolGraduate.")
(comment paymentModeForPurchase "A predicate relating types of things that people pay to use or buy and common payment methods for using or buying them. (#$paymentModeForPurchase THINGTYPE PAYMENTTYPE) means that PAYMENTTYPE is a common way to purchase or pay to use an instance of THINGTYPE.")
(comment subTexts "(#$subTexts WHOLE_TEXT PARTIAL_TEXT) means that PARTIAL_TEXT is a text that is included in WHOLE_TEXT.  This allows one to assert, for example, that a certain passage is part of the whole text of a certain article.")
(comment fieldDependentCodedValues "The value ARG4 for the #$LogicalField ARG3 depends on the value ARG2 for the #$LogicalField ARG1.")
(disjointWith TelephoneCountryCode Address-PhysicalLocationDesignator)
(comment scoreInAction "(#$scoreInAction AGENT ACT VAL) states that AGENT achieved a score of VAL in the action ACT.")
(comment amountOfSalesDuring "The value of all the units of product ARG1 sold during time interval ARG2 is ARG3")
(comment FilingAnInsuranceClaim "The action of filing a claim against an insurance company for having been involved in a covered event.")
(comment FlightAttendant "The collection of persons who take care of passengers on commercial airliners")
(comment perpendicularVectors "A specialization of #$disjointDirections.  (#$perpendicularVectors VECTOR1 VECTOR2) means that VECTOR1 is perpendicular 
(i.e. at a 90-degree angle) to VECTOR2.  For example, 
(#$perpendicularVectors #$East-Directly #$North-Directly) holds.")
(comment playsRole "The predicate #$playsRole is used to indicate the way that something participates in a particular situation.  (#$playsRole SIT THING ROLE) means that in the #$Situation SIT, the item THING plays the #$Role ROLE.  E.g., instances of #$HangGlider play the role of #$vehicle in instances of #$RecreationalActivity.")
(comment ContinuingEducationCOS "A course of study intended for people who already have degrees, who may be out in the workplace and not normally in an academic setting.")
(comment RetirementAccount "An account for the money that employee receives for when he/she retires.")
(comment subordinates "(#$subordinates SUPER SUB) means that SUB is a subordinate of SUPER in some organization.  This does not necessarily mean that SUB has SUPER for a boss.  But SUPER somehow outranks SUB or has authority over SUB.  Note that if two people both have two jobs in two separate organizations, say a restaurant and a mini-market, the subordinate in the restaurant might be the assistant manager in the mini-market.")
(comment TeacherFn "(#$TeacherFn FIELDOFSTUDY) denotes the collection of all #$Teachers of the #$FieldOfStudy, FIELDOFSTUDY. In the #$AcademicLifeMt, the use of this function denotes a subcollection of #$AcademicProfessional. Use #$ProfessionalTeacherOfActivityFn to denote professional teachers of an activity of a certain type, and #$TeacherOfSkillFn to denote non-professional teachers of an activity or skill.")
(comment ElectricalEngineer "An engineer knowledgeable in Electrical Engineering, that is, physical transformations of systems involving electricity and its related effects, such as electromagnetics, computer engineering, computer science, power systems, etc.")
(comment DentalDegree-DDS "A Doctoral degree in Dental Science/Surgery.")
(comment NurseAnesthetist " A nurse anesthetist is a registered nurse who is qualified to administer anesthesia.")
(comment ExclamationPoint-TheSymbol "The exclamation-point character '!'.  This is as an abstract character (see #$Character-Abstract), not as a physical instantiation of it.  Traditionally used in texts to indicate emphasis, exclamation or loudness.  Used in mathematics for the factorial operator.")
(comment HoldingAPosition-Skillfully "Holding steady in a position or posture, e.g. in gymnastics.")
(comment PhDThesis "A written dissertation submitted for a PhDDegree.")
(comment Humility "Insignificance, Inferiority: feeling of absence of pride in oneself and in one's achievement, with the connotation of undue self-deprecation, humilliation or abjectness")
(comment Currency-US "all forms of tangible United States currency")
(comment PersonWithOccupation "The collection of persons who have a (skilled or unskilled) occupation.  Most (but not all) instances of #$PersonWithOccupation spend a significant part of their waking hours doing activities that are characteristic of their occupations.  Typically their actions are performed for pay (but not always: consider a \"starving artist\" who is unable to sell any of her works).  Note that a #$PersonWithOccupation need not be working over the entire duration of when s/he has an occupation; e.g. college professors on summer break and the temporarily unemployed still have occupations.  Most reified specializations of #$PersonWithOccupation classify workers according to their job titles, the kinds of work they perform, or the skills involved; while a few exploit other (usually quite broad) features of their working lives (e.g. #$SelfEmployedWorker and #$DeskWorker).  But note that many collections corresponding to what are colloquially considered professions or occupations (e.g. #$Lifeguard, #$StockBroker, #$Housekeeper, and many others) are _not_ specializations of #$PersonWithOccupation, as those collections include people for whom the work in question is not their occupation.")
(comment PayingByMail "The collection of #$Paying events in which the agent doing the paying (i.e., the #$fromPossessor of the money paid) uses a (physical) mailing service to make the payment.  That could mean sending currency to the payee (the #$toPossessor) -- or the payee's agent -- but more likely means sending a check, money order, or credit card authorization.")
(comment BungeeJumping "The activity where participants attach themselves to an elastic cord (bungee cord) and jump from a height (such as a bridge, hot air balloon, or crane) for sport.")
(comment SportsAction "A purposeful action in sports, commonly used and practiced.")
(comment EdibleFruit "The collection of individual edible fruits, often eaten whole by people or used in cooking. Note that this is the common-sense notion of fruit, so tomatoes, olives, legumes are NOT #$EdibleFruit.  See also #$Fruit.")
(comment HalfMiddleJudoSportsEvent "Judo matches for sport, in the HalfMiddle weight class.")
(comment comparableFluents "(#$comparableFluents OBJ F(X) G(X)) states that the order of magnitude of F(OBJ) is also the order of magnitude of G(OBJ).  Another way of thinking of it is that F(OBJ) and G(OBJ) are of comparable orders of magnitude, and neither one is negligible with respect to the other.")
(comment VeterinaryCareEvent "A medical care event done by a veterinarian, with a patient that is a non-human animal.")
(comment WrappingSomething "The collection of events in which a wrapper is wrapped around an object")
(comment BabyShower "The collection of all parties [#$Party-Celebration] to bestow gifts upon a woman shortly before she gives birth [#$BirthEvent].  The gifts are to be used for the forthcoming child.")
(comment (FruitFn LimeTree) "The collection of individual limes.")
(comment overlappingAgents "The agent denoted by ARG1 shares some possibly significant attribute with the agent denoted by ARG2. In the extreme case, ARG1 might denote the same entity as ARG2.")
(comment WithoutHair "An attribute for describing a body part that has no hair covering it.")
(comment AquaticSportsEvent "A sports event (usually) involving a swimming pool (as opposed to a lake, as with Rowing).  Includes swimming races, diving events and water polo games, but not rowing or yachting.")
(disjointWith TimePoint CalendarQuarter)
(disjointWith MultiDirectionalCommunication CommunicationAct-Single)
(comment arg4Format "An instance of #$ArgFormatPredicate (q.v.) used to place a particular #$Format (q.v.) constraint on the fourth (or \"arg4\") argument-place of a given predicate.  (#$arg4Format PRED FORMAT) means that PRED's arg4 is constrained to FORMAT.  See the reified instances #$Format for

further details.")
(comment situationQualifiesForCoverage "ARG1 is the insurance policy which will pay the policyholder for the costs associated with Event ARG2.  (Associated costs are spelled out in the policy itself.  We should have rules which describe the standard costs that are included for various classes of insurance).")
(comment Mover "The collection of people who work for a moving company as the heavy laborers, the people who actually do the moving of objects.")
(comment PassingThroughPortal "A collection of movement events.  In an instance of #$PassingThroughPortal, an object goes from one spatial region to another by passing through a #$Portal between the regions.  Examples: a portion of food passing from the stomach to the small intestine; a person walking through a door from the outdoors into a house.")
(comment WHDeterminer "The collection of all wh-words which can act as determiners. Example: 'which'.")
(comment presenter "(#$presenter GATHERING PERSON) means that PERSON speaks to a group of audience members who have a role in GATHERING.")
(comment ForceAffectingAnObjectsMovement "The collection of events in which some kind of force acts on an object so as to affect its movement in some way.  The force might cause the object to move, prevent it from moving, or influence the manner in which it moves.")
(comment SISPhysicalSchema "Descriptions of mappings from a Structured Information System (SIS) to a physical representation of it.")
(comment materialsSuppliers "See the inverse.")
(comment uniformTypeComponentType "(#$uniformTypeComponentType UNIFORM-TYPE CLOTHING-TYPE) means that elements of UNIFORM-TYPE have elements of CLOTHING-TYPE as #$groupMembers.")
(comment ChemicalEngineer "Engineer involved in the design, understanding and optimization of chemical process, chemical reactions and products obtained with the help of Chemistry and Chemical Engineering")
(disjointWith Shotgun Rifle)
(comment Acetate "Acetate is a substance formed from instances of #$AceticAcid; it is a salt or an               #$Ester.")
(comment DentalDegree-DMD "A Doctoral degree in Dental Medicine.")
(comment PulmonaryDiseaseSpecialist "A pulmonary disease specialist is a doctor who specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of lung disease.")
(comment WritingSystem "A specialization of #$CommunicationConvention.  Each instance of #$WritingSystem is a system of physical markings used to record pieces of a language.  Writing systems are typically associated with particular languages, although some may be common to many languages.  Instances of #$WritingSystem include #$JapaneseKatakanaWriting, #$WesternEuropeanWriting, and #$MusicalWriting.")
(comment AdvancingOnSportsOpponent "In a sport such as fencing, gaining ground on an opponent.")
(comment Patent "The legal rights to a specification for the design of a tangible device which an agent controls for a certain period of time. Any product which conforms to the specification which was made without the patent's owner's consent is illegal.  Patent rights can be sold.")
(comment Enthusiasm "Support and excitement towards a thing that is considered worthwhile")
(comment NickelCoin-US "The US nickel -- five cents, silvery, with Jefferson on it")
(comment LegalProfessional "An instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation, and a specialization of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each instance of #$LegalProfessional is a person working in the field of law. Notable specializations of #$LegalProfessional include #$Lawyer, #$Judge, and #$Paralegal.")
(comment Couple-Heterosexual "The heterosexual pair of people that consists of one man and one woman.")
(comment PPTStrengthFn "USes are collections of drug products of type ARG1 and of strength ARG2.  Strengths can either be measured as quantity per dose (usually mass), as some sort of concentration, or ... ")
(comment TernaryPredicate "A specialization of both #$TernaryRelation and #$Predicate.  #$TernaryPredicate is the collection of all predicates whose arity (see #$arity) is 3.")
(comment Complementizer "The collection of all complementizers. In English, this is only the word 'that'. Complementizers introduce a tensed clauses.")
(comment DitransitiveNP-GerundPhraseFrame "This frame is used for words that take exactly two complements,

          the first of which is an NP and the second a gerund phrase.

          In HPSG terms: [COMPS  <NP, VP[gerund]>] Example: 'He heard them laughing'.")
(disjointWith TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure SportsAction)
(comment HousePlant-Potted "A plant that one may keep at home, inside or out, including pot and soil, as furnishing.")
(comment EuropeSportsEvent "A class of YachtingSportsEvent")
(comment developmentalStages "The developmental stages of living objects.")
(comment addressText "The predicate #$addressText relates an instance of #$ContactLocation to an instance of #$Address-LocationDesignator. (#$addressText LOC ADDRESS) means that the #$ContactLocation LOC has the  #$Address-LocationDesignator ADDRESS.")
(comment DentalExam "An activity typically performed once or twice a year, in which the patient's teeth are cleaned and examined by a dentist and/or dental hygienist.")
(comment SchoolSuppliesMarketCategory "The items marketed to children and adolescents to use at school.  Overlaps with stationary and office supplies, but includes things like teenage mutant ninja turtle pencil sharpeners seldom found elsewhere.")
(comment SeasonOfYear "A specialization of #$PhysicalEvent.  Each instance of #$SeasonOfYear is an event characterized by specific meteorological or climatic conditions that occurs during an annual climate cycle (see #$AnnualClimateCycle).  Notable specializations are #$WinterSeason, #$SpringSeason, #$SummerSeason, and #$FallSeason.")
(comment (FruitFn OrangeTree) "The collection of individual oranges.")
(comment fieldCodes "(#$fieldCodes FIELD VALUE MEANING) indicates that if the value of the logical or physical field FIELD is VALUE, it should be interpreted to mean MEANING.")
(comment ShippingAddress "A specialization of #$MailingAddress. Each instance of #$ShippingAddress is a mailing address which does not include a P.O. Box number.  Typically then, a shipping addresses includes a street name and number and often an apartment or suite number. For example: `3721 Executive Center Drive, Suite 100, Austin, TX 78731', the shipping address of Cycorp.")
(comment FreeWeight "A weight used in a WeightliftingSportsEvent")
(disjointWith TimeOfDay CalendarQuarter)
(comment Conversation "Every #$Conversation includes at least two #$CommunicationAct-Single as #$subEvents, with the #$senderOfInfo in one being the #$recipientOfInfo in the other.")
(comment interArgFormat4-3 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat4-3 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the third argument-place of PRED when PRED's fourth argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ... ARGN) in which ARG4 is an instance of COL, PRED's
arg3 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG3' in the 
preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its instances 
for further explanation.")
(comment insuredAgent "The agents that are covered by the insurance, although they are not necessarily the one that pays for it.")
(comment ShortOrderCook "The collection of cooks who specialize in a variety of quick, inexpensive dishes (pancakes, hamburgers, grilled cheese sandwiches).  Does not include fast-food cooks (see FastFoodCook).")
(comment FirstYearCOS "The first year of a larger course of study.  Students newly admitted start with this.")
(comment AtheisticBeliefSystem "All the #$BeliefSystems which deny the existence of divine beings.  Examples of this include #$Marxism-Leninism, etc., and the most general example of all which is #$Atheism.")
(comment stuffUsed "The predicate #$stuffUsed relates an event to some tangible substance which facilitates that event.  (#$stuffUsed EVENT STUFF) means that STUFF is a portion of an instance of #$ExistingStuffType which plays an instrumental role in EVENT.  STUFF may or may not be consumed in the course of EVENT.  Examples: portions of #$Water are #$stuffUsed in instances of #$WashingDishes, #$WashingHair, #$WashingClothesInAMachine, etc.; portions of #$EdibleOil are #$stuffUsed in some instances of #$Frying food and #$BakingBread.")
(comment PagerNumber "The string representing the pager number.")
(comment Courtyard "A courtyard a a region of flat ground with no roof, usually surrounded by building(s).")
(comment Biologist "#$Scientist that studies, advances and exploits #$Biology")
(comment PediatricNeuroSurgeon " A pediatric neurosurgeon is a doctor who specializes in surgery of the neurological system in children.")
(comment TakingABeating "Taking a physical beating in some event.  Usually qualified by endurance so that the athlete is standing up to the beating.")
(comment SportsCompetition "The collection of #$Competitions consisting primarily of one or more #$SportsEvents.  See its specializations #$SportsFormalCompetition and #$SportsEvent also.")
(comment Coin-US "US coins of all amounts")
(comment Technician "A collection of persons; a subset of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each element of #$Technician is a worker whose occupation involves the execution of detailed procedures, typically using some kind of laboratory equipment or mechanical instruments.  Special training and sometimes certification is required of members of these occupations.  Elements of the collection #$Technician include members of its subsets #$MedicalLabTechnician, #$EmergencyMedicalTechnician, #$DentalHygienist, #$MediaTechnician, and others.")
(comment QuaternaryPredicate "A specialization of both #$QuaternaryRelation and #$Predicate.   #$QuaternaryPredicate is the collection of all predicates whose arity (see #$arity) is 4.")
(comment RegulatingFluidFlow "Controlling the flow of a fluid by using a tap to either open or close a portal in the container which holds that fluid.")
(comment keepsIn "The container U keeps in the stuff types v1, v2,... This means that if there is an instance of one of the stuff types in the container, it can't get out without passing through a portal.")
(comment Babysitting "A non-parent temporarily caring for an infant.  This definition could be changed if we want to consider situations where a parent cares for his/her own child to be babysitting.")
(disjointWith Cleaning SportsAction)
(comment DailyRoutine "Your everyday life routine")
(comment RingsSportsEvent "The collection of gymnastic events on the rings.")
(disjointWith Dawn Dusk)
(comment Epicotyl "Part of an angiosperm shoot system; in embryos it is the apical end of the axis of the embryo above the cotyledon(s), which gives rise to the stem and associated organs.  The epicotyl is there through the entire life of the plant, although it may not be identifiable if the cotyledons have been removed.")
(comment BorderPoliceOrganization "A collection of law enforcement organizations.  An element of #$BorderPoliceOrganization is a sub-organization of the government of a #$Country which has responsibility for policing that country's borders.  Their patrol area includes the border of the #$Country by which they are employed.  Examples: #$USCustomsService, #$USBorderPatrol.")
(comment placeOfWork "The predicate #$placeOfWork is used to indicate the physical location where a person works.  (#$placeOfWork PERSON PLACE) means that the #$Person PERSON works in the physical location PLACE.")
(comment LaundrySuppliesMarketCategory "Detergent, Bleach, and all the other products that are commonly sold with them.  Generally things which are consumed in the process of doing laundry.")
(comment DrySeason "A specialization of #$SeasonOfYear.  Each instance of #$DrySeason is the driest season of the year in a particular region during an annual climate cycle (see #$AnnualClimateCycle). Note that #$DrySeason is _not_ a specialization of #$CalendarSeason.")
(comment dependentMapping "The #$ReifiedMapping ARG4 will be used to interpret the #$PhysicalField ARG3 when the #$PhysicalField ARG1 has the value ARG2.")
(comment Prof "The prefix ``Prof.'' or ``Professor'' that may attach to a person's name.")
(comment SubstringFn "A ternary function.  When applied to an instance of #$SubLString, an instance of #$NonNegativeInteger, and an instance of #$PositiveInteger, #$SubstringFn returns an instance of #$SubLString.  (#$SubstringFn STRING START END) denotes the string that begins at position START of STRING and ends before position END.  The first character of a string is at position 0. Thus, for example, (#$SubstringFn \"cycorp\" 0 2) denotes the string \"cy\".")
(comment canPassThroughPortal "U can pass through the portal V, if it is open.")
(comment CalendarQuarter "An instance of #$CalendarCoveringType, and a specialization of #$Date.  Each instance of #$CalendarQuarter is a quarter of a year on a particular calendar, and thus will be either the first, second, third, or fourth quarter of some year (see the collection #$CalendarYear) on that calendar. Example instances of #$CalendarQuarter include (#$QuarterFn 1 (#$YearFn 1996)) and (#$QuarterFn 4 (#$YearFn 1929)).")
(comment BackgroundFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction for denoting the background of the image associated with the mt ARG1.")
(comment FootballUniform "include pants, jersey, FootballHemlet, mouth protectors, and protective pads.")
(comment amountPurchased "The amount, in dollars, of arg2 purchased in arg1.")
(comment MalpracticeSuit "The collection of law suits in which an agent or group of agents sues another agent or group of agents for real or presumed shortcomings in the provision of some service.  Usually the service is a professional one (medical, psychological counselling, etc.")
(disjointWith StationeryMarketCategory ShelterConstruction)
(comment agreementID "The id assigned to this agreement (e.g., account numbers, liscense numbers, ...)")
(comment decodingDeviceType "This predicate is used to specify the type of device needed for decoding information contained in a particular kind of encoding scheme.  (#$decodingDeviceType SCHEME DEV-TYP) means that DEV-TYP is the type of device required to decode the information encoded with encoding scheme SCHEME.  For example, a telephone is the kind of device needed to decode audio information sent over telephone lines.  A cable TV box is the device type needed to decode cable TV signals.  And so on.  See also #$EncodingSchemeType.")
(comment Stadium-Indoor "A huge roofed building which houses a stadium astroturf fields, etc.")
(comment MusicalInstrumentPlayer "One who plays an instrument")
(comment WinterSolsticeDay "A collection of #$CalendarDays and an instance of #$AnnualTemporalObjectType.  Each instance of #$WinterSolsticeDay is a calendar-day during which the sun is farthest from the equator away from the local hemisphere (north or south), making the daytime (see #$DaytimeHours). The winter solstice occurs around December 21 or 22 each year in the northern hemisphere [#$NorthernHemisphere-Region] and about June 21 in the southern hemisphere [#$SouthernHemisphere-Region] and marks the end of #$CalendarAutumn and the beginning of the #$CalendarWinter.")
(comment (HighAmountFn LevelOfFitness) "The physical fitness level of a very active person (or animal).")
(comment Bar-Object "The collection of all bars.  A bar is a solid object that is longer than it is wide.")
(comment Pulmonologist "A doctor specializing in the care of the lungs.")
(comment TrickingOpponent "Tricking an opponent.")
(comment Many-Quant "The fuzzy quantity of many of something.")
(comment CraftWorker "The collection of persons who practice some craft, which typically involves producing some kind of hand-made goods.  Professional craft worker earn money from practicing their crafts, usually by selling the goods they produces.  Craft workers have specialized skills, often gained through some sort of practical training or apprenticeship.  Craft work frequently involves some artistry.  Craft occupations may be considered archaic or quaint, in cultures where the kinds of products once made only by skilled handwork are currently mass-produced by machines or assembly lines.  Examples of #$CraftWorkers include potters, florists, blacksmiths, watchmakers, and goldsmiths.")
(disjointWith AcademicSemester AcademicYear)
(comment DBSchemaSlot "The maximum cardinality for a DB Schema slot [there should be no more than this number of entries on the slot]")
(comment QuintaryPredicate "A specialization of #$Predicate and #$QuintaryRelation.  #$QuintaryPredicate is the collection of all predicates whose arity (see #$arity) is 5.")
(comment AgentiveNoun "A specialization of #$DeVerbalNoun.  Each instance of #$AgentiveNoun is a noun in the agentive form.  Agentive nouns usually denote the `doer' or `performer' of some action, and often end in `-er' or `-or'. Example: `runner'.")
(comment keepsOut "The container U keeps out the stuff types v1, v2, ... This means that if there is an instance of one of the stuff types outside the container, it can't get in without passing through a portal.")
(comment FourShellWithoutCoxRowingSportsEvent "The rowing sports events in which shells are propelled by four rowers with one oar each (two row port, two starboard), with no coxswain.")
(disjointWith Night Sunrise)
(comment imperviousToStuffTypes "The types of TangibleStuff that this piece of TangibleStuff is impervious to.")
(comment phoneNumberText "The predicate #$phoneNumberText is used to relate a telephone number to a contact location.  (#$phoneNumberText LOC NUM) means NUM is a string denoting (one of) the phone number(s) of the #$ContactLocation LOC.")
(comment StationeryMarketCategory "The group of products commonly sold along with pens, pencils, writing paper, desktop supplies, letter envelopes.  Sort of office supplies for home use")
(comment bride "(#$bride WED BRIDE) means that in the wedding-related event WED, BRIDE plays the role of the bride - the female partner in the upcoming or recent marriage.")
(comment Free-MonetaryCost "#$Free-MonetaryCost is the zero #$cost of something that is basically free, that is, something bought, or available, for nothing  - without payment of money.  See also the function #$FreeThingOfTypeFn.")
(comment compositeFieldFormat "This predicate is used to express how to either a) derive the value of a #$compositeFields by combining the values for two or more explicit fields, or b) derive the values of #$containedFields by extracting them from one explicitField.  (#$compositeFieldFormat FIELD METHOD LIST-O-FIELDS) means that the value of the #$LogicalField FIELD is composed of the values of the fields in LIST-O-FIELDS, according the the #$FieldCombiningMethod METHOD.")
(comment NonCommercialSale "A collection of events; a subset of #$Buying.  In an instance of #$NonCommercialSale, the #$buyer is a `non-commercial' agent -- that is, is a person rather than a business or other organization.")
(comment rankInCompetition "(#$rankInCompetition AGENT COMP RANK) states that AGENT came in RANK place in competition COMP.")
(disjointWith FiscalYear CalendarQuarter)
(disjointWith ExchangeOfUserRights CommunicationAct-Single)
(comment SettingUpAComputerProgram "Configuring and installing a piece of software so it will run correctly.")
(comment interArgFormat1-3 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat1-3 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the third argument-place of PRED when PRED's first argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ... ARGN) in which ARG1 is an instance of COL, PRED's arg2
position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG3' in the 
preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its instances 
for further explanation.")
(comment LawCommonToMostModernWesternLegalCodes "Instances are #$Laws which are part of the legal codes in most modern western countries.  Examples: laws against murder, stealing, tax evasion, bribery, etc.")
(comment AstronomicalBody "A specialization of #$AstronomicalObject (q.v.).  Each instance of 
#$AstronomicalBody is an astronomical object that is an individual 
body, as opposed to a group or system of such bodies.  Specializations
include #$Planet and #$Star.  Note that this collection includes only 
natural bodies; artificially-made objects such as spaceships and 
communications satellites are excluded.")
(comment Fellow-FACP "This title is given to fellows of the American College of Physicians.")
(comment CompositeTangibleAndIntangibleObject "The collection of individuals that have both a tangible and an intangible component.  Instances include people (who have bodies and minds), information bearing objects (which consist of intangible information encoded in a tangible object, such as the music on a CD or the text in a book), and many other things.  Each instance of #$CompositeTangibleAndIntangibleObject, being partially tangible, exists in time (see #$TemporalThing).  Although occasionally it can be useful to reify separately the tangible and intangible components of a composite object (e.g. to state certain things about Lenin's body as opposed to his mind), in most cases it is sufficient simply to reify the composite.")
(comment sitConstraints "The predicate #$sitConstraints is used to relate the constraints on a particular situation to the type of consequences that will occur if those constraints are NOT met.  In `(#$sitConstraints SIT CONSTR RESULT)', CONSTR is a proposition, expressed as a #$ELSentence-Assertible, which describes a constraint for the #$Situation SIT.  If CONSTR is NOT true in the situation SIT, the outcome is RESULT.  For example, if a car engine is running (the situation), and there is no oil in it (the constraint), the result is a #$DamageOutcome.  Depending on the particular #$OutcomeType indicated by RESULT, additional inferences may be made about how SIT will develop if CONSTR is not satisfied.  Possible values for RESULT include, e.g., #$InjuryOutcome, #$DamageOutcome, #$FailureOutcome; see also #$OutcomeType.")
(comment minContractAmount "Arg3 is the smallest dollar amount of arg2 that may be purchased under the terms of the agreement arg1.  Any smaller purchase is not governed by the terms of arg1. ")
(comment PattingOnTheBack "The collection of actions in which a person pats another person on the back, as a gesture of approval, encouragement, congratulations, or consolation.")
(comment Weekly "Used to indicate that something happens regularly on a weekly basis. This differs from PerWeek only in how it is used, and perhaps some would combine them.")
(comment ScenarioTestingMicrotheory "The collection of mts used for demonstrating Cyc NL-to-CycL  scenario entry and querying capabilities.")
(comment agreementID "The account number assigned to this account by the account administrator")
(comment PowerEngineer "An engineer knowledgeable in Power Engineering, that is, physical transformations of systems involving electricity and its related effects, such as electromagnetics, computer engineering, computer science, power systems, etc.")
(comment SummerSolsticeDay "A collection of #$CalendarDays and an instance of #$AnnualTemporalObjectType.  Each instance of #$SummerSolsticeDay is a calendar-day during which the sun is farthest into the hemisphere of reference, e.g. being furthest north of the equator when considered in the #$NorthernHemisphere-Region, making the daytime (see #$DaytimeHours) the longest of the year in that #$GeographicalHemisphere and the shortest of the year in the opposite one. The summer solstice occurs around June 21 or 22 each year in the #$NorthernHemisphere-Region and marks the end of the #$CalendarSpring and beginning of the #$CalendarSummer.  See #$JuneSolsticeDay and #$DecemberSolsticeDay for reference to the day of year that has the same meaning throughout the time zone.")
(comment PhDDegreeInFn "A NAT to denote collections of PhD Degrees in different fields.")
(comment tertiaryMedicalSpecialty "A medical specialty this person practices occasionally.")
(comment AddictionMedicineSpecialist " An addiction medicine specialist is a doctor who specializes in the treatment of patients who are suffering from drug addiction.")
(comment MakingABaseballOut "In baseball, causing an out.")
(comment Prototyping "A special kind of making in which the first of a class is made.  Often this is part of a #$DevelopingAProduct action.")
(disjointWith DeviceRunning SportsCompetition)
(comment Millions-Quant "The fuzzy quantity of millions of something")
(comment AcademicProfessional "A subcollection of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each instance of #$AcademicProfessional is a person whose job is to educate and/or  perform research as an affiliate of an academic institution.  This includes members of the teaching and/or research staffs of schools, colleges, universities, and research institutes.")
(comment Auditor "An accountant who checks a company's books for accuracy.  This person could work for the company, be hired as a contractor, or work for the IRS, or some other organization which has a legal right to check the company's records.")
(comment SexualBehavior "Any sexual behavior by animals. Copulation (the specific intercourse act) is a spec.")
(comment BinaryPredicate "A specialization of both #$BinaryRelation and #$Predicate.  #$BinaryPredicate is the collection of all predicates whose arity (see #$arity) is 2.")
(comment StripedPattern "The collection of all instances of striped patterns (typically on the surfaces of things, such as clothing, tigers, or zebras.")
(comment TimeOfDay-NoonHour "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at noon.")
(comment WavingAFlag "The set of actions in which a performer holds a flag that s/he waves back and forth, usually in a crowd of people.  Not the destruction or denigration of the flag, for which a different collection of actions is required.")
(comment TakingANightsSleep "The collection of events in which someone has a night's sleep")
(comment LightweightFSWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of FSWrestlingSportsEvent")
(disjointWith Evening Sunrise)
(comment costRateForType "Instances of ARG1, when sold by ARG2, are sold at the cost rate of ARG3.  So if HEB sells Bananas for $0.49 per pound, (costRateForType Banana-TheFruit HEB (DollarsPerPound 0.49)).  Entries on the instance-level slot #$costRate can be inferred from costRateForType entries.")
(comment HomeElectronicsMarketCategory "Machines which are commonly sold together which are used around the house, are of small to moderate size, often used for entertainment.  Includes stereos, tvs, microwaves, telephones")
(comment WarOrPeaceCommemoration "The collection of commemorations of war victories and of a peace settlements.")
(comment prohibitedSubstances "Substance which it is prohibited to ingest or otherwise take in for a certain sports competition.")
(disjointWith CalendarCentury CalendarQuarter)
(comment WritingSymbolCharacterSet "A collection of collections.

Each instance of #$WritingSymbolCharacterSet is the collection of 

characters (i.e. the specialization of #$WritingSymbolCharacter) used as 

symbols in some particular system of writing.  Instances include 

#$GaelicLetter, #$BengaliCharacter, #$RomanLetter, #$ChineseCharacter, 

and #$CuneiformCharacter.")
(disjointWith CommunicationAct-Single Travel-TripEvent)
(disjointWith StoneStuff VegetableMatter)
(disjointWith Law LegalCode)
(comment GeographicalDirection "A specialization of #$TerrestrialDirection 
(q.v.).  The #$GeographicalDirections derive from the \"intrinsic\" directional 
axes of a terrestrial frame of reference: North-South and East-West.  Like all 
#$VectorIntervals, geographical directions can be specified precisely (e.g. 
#$North-Directly) or as proper intervals (e.g. #$North-Generally); see the specializations #$GeographicalDirection-Direct and #$GeographicalDirection-General.")
(comment Fellow-FCCP "This title is given to fellows of the American College of Chest Physicians.")
(comment compositeParts "This predicate relates a given composite-tangible-and-intangible object to any other such objects that are parts of the first.  (#$compositeParts WHOLE PART) means that WHOLE and PART are both #$CompositeTangibleAndIntangibleObjects such that PART is a part of WHOLE.")
(comment NonPhysicianPrescriber "Non-physicians who have prescribing ability.")
(comment PolevaultArea "The collection of areas where #$PoleVaultSportsEvent typically occur.")
(comment HavingDinner "The collection of 

 events of having a dinner meal.")
(comment frequencyOfServiceToSameRecipient "How often is the same activity done for the same recipient (like lawn mowing is weekly)?")
(comment objectID "(#$objectID ?OBJ ?MAP ?ID) states that ?OBJ  has the associated ?ID according to the mapping ?MAP. Example: (#$objectID #$Goolsbey US-SSN-Mapping '444-88-9999')")
(comment SoccerGoal-ScoringRegion "Every #$SoccerGoal-ScoringRegion is a region of space enclosed by some #$SoccerGoal.  If a team kicks or heads the ball in play such that it the opposing team's #$SoccerGoal-ScoringRegion #$spatiallySubsumes that ball, then the team scores a point.")
(comment HighSchoolStudent "The collection of high school students.")
(comment LiquidAsset "A specialization of #$SomethingExisting.  Each instance of #$LiquidAsset is either an instance of #$Currency or some asset that is readily convertible to currency by selling or borrowing against it.  Examples of #$LiquidAssets include stocks, bonds, and money market accounts.")
(comment Cytopathologist " A cytopathologist is a doctor who specializes in diagnosis and treatment of disease and its affect on cells.")
(comment SymmetricAnatomicalPartType "A collection of collections.  Instances are types of #$anatomicalParts of bilaterally symmetrical organisms (#$Organism-Whole) which occur in bilaterally symmetric pairs.  This is not intended to include broader categories like #$Tooth, #$Rib-AnimalBodyPart, or #$Finger, but the specific parts of which the organism only has two (EyeTooth, FifthRib, or #$RingFinger).")
(comment Spiking-Volleyball "In volleyball, leaping into the air while close to the net and smashing the ball into the opponents' court.")
(comment Abhorrence "Extreme repugnance felt towards a person or thing, typically resulting in strenuous efforts to avoid it.")
(disjointWith SportsCompetition HeatingProcess)
(comment Few-Quant "This is used to capture the fuzzy quantity of a few.")
(comment NavyPersonnel "A specialization of #$MilitaryPerson. Each instance of #$NavyPersonnel is a person who is a member of some instance of #$Navy.")
(comment AnimalBodyRegion "A specialization of #$AnimalBLO. Each instance of #$AnimalBodyRegion is a significant spatial subdivision of the body of some animal, where the subdivision in question is usually contiguous, and has some more or less clear boundary. Instances of this collection include anatomical parts (see the specialization #$AnimalBodyPart) , such as a person's head, beard, or right arm. In addition, this collection includes     body regions that are not anatomical parts, such as a blister, a puncture wound, or a bruise.")
(disjointWith CalendarDay FiscalYear)
(comment MusicalDrama "Shows like Brigadoon, Sweeney Todd, etc - the actors do lots of singing.")
(comment SpottedPattern "The collection of all instances of spotted patterns (typically on the surfaces of objects such as dalmatian dogs, textiles, etc.")
(comment TimeOfDay-1PM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 1PM.")
(comment MiddleweightGRWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of GRWrestlingSportsEvent")
(comment BorderCheckpoint-AirTraffic "The collection of border checkpoints whose primary purpose is to handle air-based traffic, e.g. people and goods travelling by airplane. Usually located at an airport.")
(comment serviceBasicPrice "The price of a service which is being sold.  The #$cost of that service would be the total cost including tax, etc.  See objectBasicPrice for analogous info about objects being sold.")
(comment ElectronicCommerce "A specialization of #$CommercialActivity. Instances of this collection are commercial activities where communication and often even money transfer are done electronically, via #$ComputerNetworks.")
(comment FurnitureMarketCategory "The kinds of furniture which you expect to buy in furniture stores or the furniture departments of department stores.  Something like a wastebasket is marketed as furniture (among other catagories) even though one might not think of it as furniture per se.")
(comment DinnerParty "A party at which the focal event is sharing a dinner meal.")
(comment dateOfInvention "The date or year of invention.  Only intangibles can be invented.  It is the design of the transistor that can be invented, for instance.  Actual transistors are merely created.")
(comment WarrantyProduct "Products which typically come with a warranty when sold new. Almost any product may be held to have an implicit warranty, but this collection is intended to denote those which explicitly provide one, such as cars, refrigerators, computers, etc.")
(comment SalesAgreement "A specialization of #$Agreement. Each instance of #$SalesAgreement is an agreement which governs aspects of some #$Buying activity. This includes bidding activities as well as instances of #$SalesContract.")
(disjointWith CalendarDay CalendarQuarter)
(comment informationAccordingTo "Allows represention of facts such as `According to Columbus, the Earth is round' without necessitating the baggage of explicitly reifying some #$IBOCreation.  See also the similar predicate #$providesInformationAbout.--Siegel, Aug. 19, 1997")
(comment LifetimesDuration "Duration of a human lifetime.")
(comment ForegroundFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction for denoting the foreground of the image associated with the mt ARG1.")
(comment BaseballCap "The set of all baseball caps.")
(comment developerOfIBTType "An #$IntangibleObjectPredicate that relates a given content-specific type of information bearing thing to its creator(s).  (#$developerOfIBTType IBTTYPE AGENT) means that AGENT is one of the people, corporations, publishers, or other agents responsible for the invention or bringing into being of the #$IBTContentType and specialization of #$InformationBearingThing IBTTYPE -- which might be a book, a computer program, a type of currency, a flag, etc.  For example, (#$developerOfIBTType #$CycTheCollection #$Lenat) holds.  In many cases, IBTTYPE will be an instance of #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType (q.v.).  Note, however, that this predicate has been largely supplanted by the now much more widely-used #$creatorOfCW (q.v.).")
(comment FellowCredential "This title is given to people who are a member of a collegiate foundation which provides money and direction for research.")
(comment WHPronoun "The collection of all wh-words which can stand in for nouns. Example: 'whatever'.")
(comment HighJumpArea "The collection of areas where HighJumpSportsEvents occur.")
(comment HavingBreakfast "The collection of events in which someone has breakfast.")
(comment TakingAFoodOrder "What a waitperson does when waiting on a table.  The provider of service is the waitperson.  The recipient is the customer.")
(comment IDString "A specialization of #$CharacterString.  Each instance of #$IDString is a character string which is used to denote a specific object in some identification mapping.  Notable specializations of #$IDString include #$IPAddress, #$PhoneNumber, #$ProperNameString, and #$ContactInfoString.")
(comment CulturalAnthropologist "Researcher engaged in the study of similarity and diversity in the ways people(s) think and live, everywhere")
(comment BachelorsDegreeInFn "A NAT to denote collections of Bachelors Degrees in different fields.")
(comment PublishedMaterial "A specialization of #$InformationStore.  Each instance of #$PublishedMaterial is either a conceptual work (an instance of #$ConceptualWork) with instantiations which have been produced for distribution, or an information-bearing thing (an instance of #$InformationBearingThing) which has been produced for distribution.  Note that \"published\" here does not mean \"printed and physically distributed\", since intangible information-bearing things can be published using the #$WorldWideWeb-Concrete, or broadcast on the airwaves.  Notable specializations of #$PublishedMaterial include #$Book-CW, #$RecordedVideoProduct, and #$RecordedSoundProduct.")
(comment VascularRadiologist " A vascular radiologist is a doctor who uses radiation to diagnose and treat diseases of the blood vessels.")
(comment theTermConstraints "#$theTermConstraints defines a set of constraints on the `TheTerms' used in a specified context.  The first argument is the context and the second is the constraint (stated in the syntax of an IfThenAxiom left-hand-side).")
(comment MediaAgent "These are agents of the media who dispense, collect, and analyze information.")
(comment NeutronAbsorptionByNucleusEvent "What happens when a neutron is absorbed by an atomic nucleus to form a larger, and usually unstable, nucleus. Typically, the first event in a nuclear fission event.")
(disjointWith StoringSomething SportsCompetition)
(comment Sportscaster "a person who reads and/or reports the sports on a television or radio program")
(comment AirForcePersonnel "A specialization of #$MilitaryPerson. Each instance of  #$AirForcePersonnel is a person who is a member of some instance of #$AirForce.")
(comment operatesOnMachines "(#$operatesOnMachines PROGRAM COMPUTER) means that #$programCopies of some versions (#$genlPrograms) of PROGRAM are capable of running on the individual #$Computer COMPUTER.  If you want to state that a program is actively running on a computer, use #$programRunningOn instead.  Also see #$runsUnderOS and #$runsOS.")
(disjointWith CalendarMonth FiscalYear)
(comment partitionedInto "(#$partitionedInto SETORCOL PART) means that the mathematical set or collection PART is a partition of the mathematical set or collection SETORCOL; that is, the elements of PART are themselves mathematical sets or collections, and every element of SETORCOL is an element of exactly one element of PART, and every element of PART is a subset of SETORCOL.  In other words, PART is a set or collection of pairwise disjoint sets or collections whose union is co-extensional with SETORCOL.  Typically, the #$DisjointSetOrCollectionType that plays the role of PART in an assertion about partitioning will be a set specified by enumerating its elements, using the function #$ThePartition.")
(comment CheckPattern "The collection of all instances of checked patterns (typically on the surfaces of things, such as clothing, draperies, textiles, the playing surface of a checker board or chess board, etc.)")
(comment TimeOfDay-2PM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 2PM.")
(comment DaycareTeacher "Daycare teachers - teachers who work with preschool children at daycare facilities.")
(comment representsAgentToAgent "(#$representsAgentToAgent AGENT1 AGENT2 AGENT3) means that in in dealings with AGENT3,  AGENT1 represents AGENT2.  For example, if Joe Terwilliger is a salesman working for IBM, and is their sales rep to NASA, then we could represent that by asserting to Cyc  (#$representsAgentToAgent JoeTerwilliger IBM #$NASA).")
(comment PerformanceTesting "This is the collection of testing done in order to find out whether or how well a person, object, or procedure fulfills its primary function or functions.")
(comment ST500MeterSpeedSkateSportsEvent "The short track 500M speed skating competition")
(comment Coxswain-Racing "Person who steers a racing shell and gives directions to its crew.")
(comment BorderCheckpoint-WaterTraffic "The collection of customs checkpoints whose primary purpose is to handle water-based traffic, e.g. people and goods travelling by boat.  Usual ly located at a seaport.")
(comment AttackOnTangible "#$AttackOnTangible is the collection of actions             intentionally #$performedBy an actor (or actors)              who have the #$purposeInEvent that the action             #$damages the #$objectAttacked.")
(comment GamesAndPuzzlesMarketCategory "Includes BoardGames, JigsawPuzzles, etc.  Often found together near books, or for some bizzare reason, near luggage in fancy department stores.")
(comment MicroscopicScaleObject "A specialization of #$PartiallyTangible.  Each instance of #$MicroscopicScaleObject is a partially tangible object which is so small that human beings cannot perceive it, except (perhaps) with the use of special devices such as #$Microscopes or #$ElectronMicroscopes.  Specializations of #$MicroscopicScaleObject include #$Molecule, #$Atom, #$SubAtomicParticle, #$Chloroplast, and #$Mitochondrion.")
(comment Inauguration "The subcollection of #$InitiationCeremony in which an official in some organization is formally inducted into office.")
(comment EvaluatingAnAction "The collection of actions taken to determine how well something or someone (the #$thingEvaluated) is performing the #$evaluatedAction.  Some of the rules depend on the requirement that only one action may be evaluated in an instance of #$EvaluatingAnAction.  This is enforced by a #$SingleEntry constraint on #$evaluatedAction.  Nonetheless, a performer can evaluate many people or things performing an action.  So if we want to say that a performer is evaluating many actions we would assert that it is performing many evaluating's, each mapping to a unique action.")
(comment TravelAgent "People who arrange (and sell) travel-trips for a living.")
(comment ReceivingAYellowWarningCard "The receiving of a yellow card as a warning in a sports contest.  The receiver is a player/contestant, the giver is a referee.")
(disjointWith CalendarMonth CalendarQuarter)
(comment contiguousAfter "(#$contiguousAfter AFTER BEFORE) means that the #$TemporalThing AFTER starts immediately following the #$TemporalThing BEFORE.  AFTER and BEFORE have no time points in common, but there is also no time point between the ending of BEFORE and the starting of AFTER.")
(comment TextMicrotheory "The collection of Microtheories each of which contains assertions that convey the information content of a particular text.  The propositional content of a text is a #$PropositionalInformationThing, and it forms a #$TextMicrotheory.")
(disjointWith AreaCode PhoneNumber)
(comment ViewerFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction denoting the viewer of the image associated with the mt ARG1.")
(comment Coat "The set of all coats.")
(comment coversEmployees "This is the relation between an insurance provider and an agency which has contracted for its service.")
(comment LFAttribute-Function "Instances of #$LFAttribute-Function are functions which return instances of #$LogicalFieldAttribute.")
(comment meetsSpecification "Actually, the name should be shouldMeetSpecification, but that's too long.  In other words, #$meetsSpecification won't go away if there is a discrepancy between the thing and what its specification says.  If (#$meetsSpecification O S R), it is usually consistent for O to fill in as R in S.")
(comment LongJumpTrack "The collection of tracks designed for LongJumpSportsEvents.")
(comment MakingAnAppointment "A collection of events.  In each #$MakingAnAppointment, two or more people agree to meet at a particular time and place, generally for some agreed-upon purpose.  Sometimes, the appointment is made between a person and an institution (such as a medical clinic) rather than another person.  Less commonly, one might even make an appointment with oneself, to reserve a set time to do some activity.")
(comment AnsweringATelephone "The collection of all events in which a telephone signals that someone is making a call, and some other actor answers the telephone, usually via an instance of #$PickingUpATelephoneReceiver if the doer is a human agent *in situ*. We do, however, accept the convention that an instance of #$AnsweringMachine can be the #$deviceUsed in an instance of #$AnsweringATelephone, together with the #$Telephone itself.")
(comment FileFn "Returns the #$ComputerFile-Abstract with this filename.")
(comment CivilEngineer "An engineer knowledgeable in Civil Engineering, who deals with designing structures.  Civil engineers might specialize in the design of dams, streets, bridges, buildings.")
(comment secondaryMedicalSpecialty "A medical specialty this person practices, though not as their primary specialty.")
(comment CriticalCareSurgeon " A critical care surgeon is a doctor who specializes in treating critical-care patients through surgery.")
(comment ChangingLanesInSportsEvent "Moving from one lane to another, as in speed skating.")
(disjointWith SportsCompetition MaintenanceEvent)
(comment Weathercaster "a person who reads and/or reports the weather on a television or radio program")
(comment fieldsOfFormalEducation "(#$fieldsOfFormalEducation PERSON FIELD) means that the #$Person PERSON has had formal academic or tutorial education in the #$FieldOfStudy FIELD.")
(disjointWith TimePoint FiscalYear)
(comment interestInType "ARG1 is interested in having the relationship ARG3 to some instance of the class of things, ARG2.")
(comment Music "A specialization of both #$SoundInformationBearingThing and #$Artifact-Intangible.  Each instance of #$Music is a particular sound produced by actions such as singing, whistling, playing an instrument, playing recorded music, and so on.  Music has certain features that distinguish it from random noise (though recognizing them may depend upon a specific cultural background); such features usually include variations of pitch over time (i.e., melody), multiple (somehow) related pitches sounding at one time (i.e., some kind of harmony), and/or some regular temporal pattern to the component sounds (i.e., rhythm).  Instances of #$Music include the debut performance of Beethoven's Fifth Symphony, Leonard Bernstein's rendition of the Ninth Symphony with the BPO in Berlin in 1989, a particular playing of a particular CD of Bernstein's 1989 Ninth in Berlin, and the Messiah sing-in in Austin, TX, in 1995. This collection is not to be confused with #$MusicalText or #$MusicalTextCopy (qq.v.), which refer to the represented instructions which musicians often follow in order to create #$Music.")
(comment BlotchyPattern "The collection of all instances of blotchy or mottled patterns (typically on the surfaces of objects such as houses or cars with peeling paint, organisms with skin maladies, etc.")
(comment TimeOfDay-3PM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 3PM.")
(comment PlantingACrop "The collection of events in which a crop is planted.")
(comment TensOfMinutesDuration "Things that take some tens of minutes, i.e. from 10 to 90 minutes")
(comment ST3000MeterSpeedSkateSportsEvent "The short track 3000M speed skating competition")
(comment PanelDiscussion "A type of public speaking event in which a small group of speakers exchanges information or opinions about a common topic, in front of an audience.  Typically, there is someone who acts as a moderator for the panel.  Often, audience members may ask questions of the panel.")
(comment LargeApplianceMarketCategory "The large, durable machines for use in the home which are sold together in some department stores, appliance stores.  Refrigerators, Washers, Stoves, etc.")
(comment Halloween "Each of these is a one-day-long annual #$Holiday celebrating the supernatural spirit world.  Although derived from Pagan and  Christian religious tradition, it is essentially a purely secular holiday as practiced in the United States of America.")
(comment MakingCoffee-TheBeverage "Brewing coffee - doesn't include instant coffee.")
(comment fieldDataType "(#$fieldDataType P-FIELD TYPE) means that the physical field P-FIELD can accurately represent any value representable by the data type TYPE.  It is possible for a person to update this predicate at table-description time, but it is usually preferable to update this automatically by examining the database directly.
Note that an assertion of, say, (#$fieldDataType P-FIELD #$StringObject) means that *any* string can be stored in a P-FIELD, and thus specifically P-FIELD is unbounded.")
(comment FreePointPenalizing "A penalty in which the opposing team is given a free point.")
(comment SalesBidOrContractItem "Instances are like line items of a sales contract.  They are agreements concerning the sale of individual product types.")
(comment scaleUsedInCompetition "(#$scaleUsedInCompetition COMP SCALE) states the type of the entries for the #$metricOfEvaluation for competiton COMP is SCALE.  For example, (#$scaleUsedInCompetition SuperBowlXXVI #$NonNegativeInteger)")
(disjointWith CalendarSecond CalendarQuarter)
(comment MilitaryExercise "A collection of events. In each element of this collection, a group of military personal acts as if it were in a warfare situation for training purposes.  However, often it does not involve real weapons.")
(disjointWith PhoneNumber TelephoneCountryCode)
(comment defnNecessary "A #$CycInferenceDescriptorPredicate.  
(#$defnNecessary COL TEST) means that TEST is the name of a piece 
of code in the SubL implementation of Cyc that specifies, and tests 
for, a necessary condition for a CycL term's denoting an instance of 
(see #$isa) the collection COL.  Only if TEST returns `T' (for 
`True') when applied to a particular term can that term's 
denotatum be considered an instance of COL; all terms that denote 
instances of COL must fulfill TEST's requirements, although there 
may be additional requirements for denoting an instance of COL as 
well.  See also #$defnSufficient and #$defnIff.")
(comment laws "The predicate #$laws is used to relate a geopolitical region (country, state, city, etc.) to a law or entire legal code which applies there.  (#$laws GEOPOL CODE) means that the #$GeopoliticalEntity GEOPOL officially has the law (or set of laws) CODE.  See also #$GovernmentCOC for the representation of a #$Law or a #$LegalCode as a #$Microtheory.")
(comment GeneralMicrotheory "A specialization of #$DeclarativeContext.  Instances of #$GeneralMicrotheory contain general axioms useful for multiple purposes.  This excludes microtheories that deal with specific situations,  such as instances of #$ProblemSolvingCntxt, microtheories that represent the information content of one specific #$InformationBearingObject such as the US Declaration of Independence, and those that are purely lexical microtheories.  Instances of this collection include #$HumanSocialLifeMt, #$BuyingMt, and #$NaiveAnimalsMt.  Non-instances include #$GeneralLexiconMt (purely lexical)  and #$PeopleDataMt (no general axioms).")
(comment CertifiedPublicAccountantCredential "This credential is given to accountants who meet a given state's requirements.  Usually this is evaluated by a state-administered test.")
(comment FieldLengthsFn "Results in a #$FieldCombiningMethod which constructs the larger field out of component fields of the fixed lengths given as arguments.  Takes one or more arguments.  When used with #$compositeFieldFormat, the number of arguments should be the same as the number of fields in the list that is #$compositeFieldFormat's arg4, and the total of the arguments should be the same as the number of positions the larger field occupies, but there is no check on this in code. ")
(comment TripleJumpArea "The collection of areas where TripleJumpSportsEvents typically occur.")
(comment HavingLunch "A collection of events.  Each instance of #$HavingLunch is an eating of the midday meal")
(comment CubicFoot "A function which returns an element of #$Volume.  One cubic foot (#$CubicFoot 1) equals about .028 cubic meters.")
(comment ParkingPlace "place where a single car is parked.")
(comment MusicalComposer "A musician who composes music.")
(comment BachelorsDegree "The educational degrees normally issued after passing four years of college.")
(comment MoneyTenderType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$MoneyTenderType is a collection of objects of a type commonly offered in payment for goods, services, fees, wage-work, and so on.  Notable instances of #$MoneyTenderType include #$Currency, #$CreditCard, and #$Check-TenderObject.")
(comment PediatricNephrologist "A pediatric nephrologist is a doctor who specializes in diagnosing and treating kidney problems in children.")
(comment VisualRepresentationMicrotheory "A specialization of #$PropositionalInformationThing.  Each instance of #$VisualRepresentationMicrotheory is a context containing the propositional content of a particular visual representation, where visual representations include, among other things, paintings, photographs, digitized images, moving pictures, and statues.")
(comment SlidingIntoBase "Sliding, in baseball.")
(disjointWith MaterialHandling SportsCompetition)
(comment BusinessPerson "A subcollection of #$PersonWithOccupation. Each instance of #$BusinessPerson is someone whose occupation primarily consists in the ownership or operation of a #$Business.")
(comment PrivateSectorEmployee "A specialization of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each instance of #$PrivateSectorEmployee is a worker who is not paid a salary or wage by any governmental organization.  For example, employees of publicly traded corporations are instances of #$PrivateSectorEmployee.")
(comment SolitaryGameType "a collection of subcollections of events.  Each element of each element is an event in which an individual plays a game designed to be played by one person.")
(comment VehicleTransmissionType "Elements are types of vehicle transmissions, specialized by mechanism of action and number of speeds.  Elements are sibling-disjoint (see #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType). ")
(comment PlaidPattern "The collection of all instances of plaid patterns (typically on the surfaces of things, such as clothing, draperies, textiles, a decorative garbage can, etc.)")
(comment TimeOfDay-10AM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 10AM.")
(comment courseOfStudyLevel "Gives the educational level, or grade level, of this course of study.")
(comment longerDurationThan "(#$longerDurationThan TIME-INT1 TIME-INT2) means that the time interval TIME-INT1 lasts longer than the time interval TIME-INT2.")
(comment TornadoSportsEvent "A class of YachtingSportsEvent")
(disjointWith FuelPoweredDevice NuclearPoweredDevice)
(comment TrapDevice "A class of devices whose main use is to capture animals, alive or dead.")
(comment WholesaleBuying "A collection of events; a subset of #$BuyingAnObject.  An instance of #$WholesaleBuying is a purchase in which, typically, (1) the #$buyer pays significantly less than the usual #$retailCost; (2) a large quantity of the merchandise is purchased at one time; (3) the #$seller is a business that manufactures or distributes the merchandise, rather than a #$RetailOrganization; and (4) the merchandise is bought to be resold or to be used as input to some commercial manufacturing or other commercial activity.")
(comment SmallApplianceMarketCategory "The products which typically use electricity, are used around the house but not in the workshop, and are sold together in department stores.  Toasters, Blenders, Hair Dryers, Vacuum Cleaners")
(comment SummerSeason "A specialization of #$SeasonOfYear. Each instance of #$SummerSeason is the time of greatest warmth during a temperate climate cycle (see #$TemperateClimateCycle).  Instances of #$SummerSeason are characterized solely by climatic conditions; consequently, #$SummerSeason is _not_ a specialization of #$CalendarSeason.  For the collection of summers defined by dates on a calendar, see #$CalendarSummer.")
(comment FathersDay "Each of these is a one-day-long annual #$Holiday celebrating fathers and fatherhood.  In the United States it falls in #$June, while in Finland it falls in #$November.")
(comment GreatWealth "The approximate amount of wealth that one would consider a very rich and perhaps famous person (like a millionaire) to own.")
(comment OrganizationStructureInformation "The collection of pieces of information about the structure (composition, suborganizations, members, ...) of an organization.")
(comment GymUnevenBars "The piece of gymnastic equipment used during an uneven bars gymnastic routine, with two long, thin, parallel bars at different heights from the ground.")
(comment Progesterone "A sex hormone predominating in females, which is used to regulate the periods of fertility.")
(comment SewingSuppliesMarketCategory "The items one uses either as materials (fabrics, threads, buttons, zippers, rubber bands) or as tools (needles, pins, scissors, garment patterns, sewing machines, etc) during sewing.")
(comment AssociatesDegreeInFn "A NAT to denote collections of #$AssociatesDegrees in different fields.")
(comment LearningFromInformationSource "Learning by communicating with someone, reading a book, watching a film or video, etc.")
(comment Pharmacist-Institutional "An institutional pharmacist is a person who makes and dispenses drugs at a hospital or other health institution.")
(comment JumpingHurdles "This is in #$AnimalActivitiesMt because it is used in the #$CycCourseExercisesMt which is limited in the microtheories which it sees.  It belongs in #$SportsMt.")
(comment WritingByHand "Writing is the formation of characters or symbols on a suitable surface for transmitting information.")
(comment UnitOfAngularDistance "The collection of functions which return elements of #$AngularDistance.  E.g., (#$Radian 5) denotes 5 radians.")
(comment Surrendering "A specialization of both #$HumanActivity and #$PurposefulAction.  Each instance of #$Surrendering is an event in which one agent voluntarily gives himself/herself/itself up into the power of another agent.")
(comment conflictOfInterest "#$conflictOfInterest(X Y Z) means that agent X affects whether some proposition P will be true, X has a vested interest in both agents Y and Z, and Y and Z want different (conflicting) truth values for P.")
(comment boardMembers "The predicate #$boardMembers relates a particular organization to the persons who serve on its board of directors.  (#$boardMembers ORG PERSON) means PERSON belongs to that instance of #$BoardOfDirectors which is responsible for oversight of the #$Organization ORG.  A member of the Board of Directors of an organization may or may not be an executive of the organization.")
(comment ApprenticeCertifForFn "A NAT for certificates of apprenticeship for different professions.")
(comment InterActorSlot "A specialization of #$BinaryPredicate.  Each instance of #$InterActorSlot is a binary predicate that relates two individuals who are participants in some particular event.  For example, #$authorOfPublication-IBT is an instance of #$InterActorSlot, since (#$authorOfPublication-IBT X Y) implies the existence of a #$Writing event in which X is the author and Y is the book written.  Other examples of #$InterActorSlot are #$agreeingAgents, #$artisticWorksCreated, #$spouse, and #$wornOn.")
(comment NeonatalPerinatalSpecialist "These are doctors specializing in the care of the #$HumanInfant and the #$mother,  especially during the five months prior and the first month after the #$BirthEvent.")
(comment MissingAHandOver "Missing a hand over in a relay, by either dropping the baton or failing to transfer it within the marked zone. Also, missing the hike in football.")
(comment arbitratingAgents "What person or organization is the arbiter of this competition?  For some types of competition, there won't be one (economic competition, e.g.).")
(comment remotelyConnectedTo "means that u is connected to the v1 remotely")
(comment MensSportsCompetition "Sports competitions where the participants are limited to male persons.  The competitors may be organizations in the case of team competition, but the players must be male persons.")
(comment Newscaster "a person who reads and/or reports the news on a television or radio program")
(comment PrimeMinister-HeadOfGovernment "A specialization of #$HeadOfGovernment.  Each instance of #$PrimeMinister-HeadOfGovernment is a person who holds the political office of Prime Minister in some instance of #$Country.")
(disjointWith CalendarCentury FiscalYear)
(comment Translation-RoundTrip "A specialization of #$Translation-NoLocationChange.  Each instance of #$Translation-RoundTrip represents one round trip event.  That is, an instance of #$Translation-RoundTrip is a complete translational movement that begins and ends in the same place (thus, the #$fromLocation and #$toLocation of the round trip are identical).  However, a round trip is usually a discontinuous motion (cf. #$Movement-TranslationProcess).  In the simplest case, it has exactly one #$outboundLegOfRoundTrip and exactly one #$inboundLegOfRoundTrip (qq.v.), and the trip breaks at the #$destination-RoundTrip, which is the place that the traveller visits in between the two legs of the journey.  Thus, in addition to a #$fromLocation and #$toLocation, an instance of #$Translation-RoundTrip also has an #$origin-RoundTrip and #$destination-RoundTrip.  The #$origin-RoundTrip is just the same as the #$fromLocation and #$toLocation.  Note: to describe a multi-stop `round trip',  instead of using #$Translation-RoundTrip one can represent it as a circuit composed of a series of one-way legs.")
(comment VisualPattern "The collection of visually perceivable patterns, such as the pattern of colors and shapes on a polka-dotted dress, the spots on a leopard, the stripes on a zebra, or the playing surface of a checkerboard.")
(comment TimeOfDay-4PM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 4PM.")
(comment TechUserOfSimpleFueledDevices "Members are persons who use simple fueled devices, e.g., charcoal stoves, and not including (or implying) internal combustion engines.")
(comment HalfHeavyJudoSportsEvent "Judo matches for sport, in the HalfHeavy weight class.")
(disjointWith KineticEnergyPoweredDevice NuclearPoweredDevice)
(comment QuarterCoin-US "The US quarter -- 25 cents, silvery, and, if minted after 1931, depicting with George Washington.")
(comment SalesActivity "A collection of actions and a specialization of #$BusinessEvent and #$CommercialActivity. Each instance of #$SalesActivity is an action performed in an effort to achieve a sale to a second agent. Examples of #$SalesActivity include #$Advertising, telemarketing, showing samples and/or actual products to customers in a show room or a store. Instances of #$SalesActivity which are successful lead to corresponding instances of #$Buying. Note: #$SalesActivity does NOT include manufacturing, accounting, and other such ancillary business activities.")
(comment ToysMarketCategory "Products sold for children to play with. Sold in toy stores and toy departments.  Anything can be a toy, but this is the collection whose members are commonly sold together for this purpose.")
(comment MothersDay "Each of these is a one-day-long annual #$Holiday celebrating mothers and motherhood.")
(comment Memorizing "Commiting things like plays, musical text, phone numbers to memory.")
(comment VerbParticle "The collection of all particles which can combine with verbs. Verb particles may appear before the object noun phrase, or may appear after it, as in 'I put down the phone' and 'I put the phone down'. Verb particles are usually prepositions, although they may be adverbials.")
(comment IceSkate "The collection of all skates used for ice skating")
(comment AFewWeeksDuration "Duration of 2 to 10 weeks")
(comment Estrogen "A class of sex hormones predominating in females, which are used to regulate the periods of fertility.  These hormones are also administered to women after menopause to prevent osteoporosis and coronary problems.")
(comment HairBarrette "Barrettes worn in hair.")
(comment Socket "Sockets are objects, often parts of other things, which are intended to serve as the site for stuffs to enter the thing.")
(comment Pharmacist-Retail "A retail pharmacist is a person who makes and dispenses drugs at a retail pharmacy.")
(comment Target-Device "A piece of equipment at which competitors aim a projectile.  Usually marked with some scoring/grading system (like the archetypal 'bulls-eye' pattern).")
(comment BaseballDelivery "Part of playing baseball - throwing the ball to the batter, in a way such that he/she has a chance to hit it with the bat.")
(comment Milliradian "This is a unit of length derived by dividing a radian by 1000")
(comment opinions "(#$opinions AGENT PROP) implies that (i) AGENT believes PROP is true, but (ii) the evidence AGENT has for PROP falls short of justifying his/her belief in PROP.  Since (#$opinions AGENT PROP) implies that AGENT's belief in PROP is not fully justified, #$opinions is a #$negationPreds of #$knows (q.v.).  Note that (#$opinions AGENT PROP), unlike (#$knows AGENT PROP), does not imply that PROP is true, although it also does not imply that PROP is false (since an agent can have a true belief, even if the evidence available to that agent does not justify that belief).")
(comment shareholders "The predicate #$shareholders identifies particular agents as owners of shares in a particular organization.  (#$shareholders ORG AGENT) means AGENT owns one or more shares of #$Stock in the company ORG and hence is an owner of the company and may receive dividends from the company.  #$shareholders indicates owners of a company's stock generically, whether they hold common or preferred shares.  Voting shareholders may vote (one vote per share) for the Board of Directors.  Shareholders do not normally participate in the operation of a company, and they are not personally liable for the debts of the company.")
(comment Linguist "A person trained in the scientific study of human languages")
(comment primaryMedicalSpecialty "The main medical specialty this person practices. See also #$secondaryMedicalSpecialty and #$tertiaryMedicalSpecialty.")
(comment Rhinologist " A rhinologist is a doctor who specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of problems with the nose.")
(disjointWith HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject HardcopyInformationBearingObject)
(comment TakingABall "In baseball, not swinging at a ball pitched outside the strike zone.")
(comment BookkeepingPredicateForAnyThing "This is the set of bookkeeping slots that apply to all units in CYC.")
(comment WeightClassSportsCompetition "Sports competitions where the participants are limited to persons whose weight is in some range.  The competitors may be organizations in the case of team competition, but the players must meet the weight restrictions.")
(comment overlooks "(#$overlooks OBJ1 OBJ2) means OBJ1 is generally over OBJ2 and OBJ1 faces OBJ2.")
(comment ArmyPersonnel "A specialization of #$MilitaryPerson. Each instance of #$ArmyPersonnel is a person who is a member of some instance of #$Army-BranchOfService.")
(comment requiresPeripherals "This predicate specifies the kinds of peripheral devices a computer running a certain program should have.")
(disjointWith CalendarSecond FiscalYear)
(comment StandupComedy "An instance involves one person telling jokes as        a performance.")
(comment hasVisibleSurfacePattern "ARG1 (the surface or visible parts of ARG1) has the pattern ARG2.")
(comment TimeOfDay-11AM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 11AM.")
(comment TechUserOfNuclearDevices "Members are persons who use nuclear-powered devices.  Implies the use of electronic devices.")
(comment endsRelativeToStartOf " (#$endsRelativeToStartOf e1 d e2) means that the e1 ended d units of time after e2 started")
(comment SuperHeavyweightGRWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of GRWrestlingSportsEvent")
(comment HumanPreSchoolageChild "Kids who aren't old enough to start school yet (under 5 years of age).")
(comment sellingAgent "A selling agent acts on behalf of a would be seller to bring about a buying event involving his/her/its client as the seller. ")
(comment ArtSuppliesMarketCategory "Items marketed to artists for use in creating instances of WorkOfArt.  Such items include oil and water based paints, canvasses, clay, etc.")
(comment EasterHoliday "Each of these is an annual #$ChristianHoliday which commemorates the Resurrection of Christ after his Crucifixion.")
(comment PlayScript "A narrative structured around scenes, actors speaking parts, direction, scene descriptions etc.  Something actors memorize and use while rehearsing.")
(comment DischargeWithPrejudice "The collection of events in which employees are fired as a result of perceived incompetence or having a defective personality.")
(disjointWith CalendarWeek CalendarQuarter)
(comment Earring-Jewelry "The collection of earrings.")
(comment CoordinatingConjunction "The collection of all coordinating conjunctions. Typically, coordinating conjunctions can appear in phrases with any number of conjuncts. Coordinating conjunctions can link terms of any functional category. Example: 'and'.")
(comment PhysicalPartPredicate "A collection of predicates that are used to relate a partially tangible thing to its distinct, identifiable, non-diffuse, partially tangible parts.  Each instance of #$PhysicalPartPredicate has an #$arity of 2, and both argument places are constrained (see #$argIsa) to instances of #$PartiallyTangible, or some subcollection thereof.  Each instance of #$PhysicalPartPredicate is a specialization of the predicate #$physicalParts (q.v.); consequently, for each instance PRED of #$PhysicalPartPredicate, either (#$genlPreds PRED #$physicalParts) or (#$genlInverse PRED #$physicalParts) holds.")
(comment Coupler "Couplers are things which play a role such that they may form a connection to another thing, for the purpose of transmitting force, stuffs, ...")
(disjointWith MedicalCareInstitution Pharmacy)
(comment Radian "This is the basic unit of angular measure.  2*pi radians make a complete circle.")
(comment TimeOfDay-MidnightHour "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at midnight.")
(comment SportsMedicineSpecialist " A sports medicine specialist is a doctor who specializes in the treatment and prevention of sports-related injuries and conditions.")
(comment HardcopyInformationBearingObject "The \"collection-intersection\"  (and thus a common specialization) of #$Artifact, #$StillImageSource and  #$HumanAccessibleIBO (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$HardcopyInformationBearingObject is an human-created #$InformationBearingObject (IBO) in a \"hard\" format (e.g.  written on paper, on wood, on palm leaves, engraved in metal, or carved on stone) that humans can obtain information from by viewing (if there is sufficient light)  without using a computer or electronic device.  In many cases the information is  encoded in visual symbols, whose #$CommunicationConvention must be understood by  anyone who would access the information.  For example, the information may be  stored as English text.  Examples of #$HardcopyInformationBearingObject include:  a billboard, a greeting card, a restaurant check, a magazine, an engraving by  Rembrandt, a Picasso painting, and a hardcopy of a map with no text on it.  Note  that this collection does _not_ include IBOs embodied in magnetic media such as  tape or disk (as the information they bear is not directly accessible to someone  viewing them) or Braille books (as they are not instances of #$StillImageSource,  whose information content must be accessed visually).")
(comment PerformingADifficultManeuver "Performing a maneuver: a jump, dive or figure (in skating) that is considered of above-average difficulty for the competition. (These often receive higher rankings in terms of points.)")
(comment Cheering "The oral noises that people in a crowd make, to express their approval.")
(comment WhaleSized "ABout how big whales are")
(comment TipSide "the tip side of an object that has an intrinsic pointing axis, like an arrow or a fish or a gun")
(comment HealthProfessional "An instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation, and a specialization of #$Professional-Adult. Each instance of #$HealthProfessional is a person employed in some health-related field. Specializations of #$HealthProfessional include #$MedicalCareProfessional and #$HealthInspector")
(comment PolkaDotPattern "The collection of all instances of `polka-dot' patterns (typically on the surfaces of textiles, toys, etc.")
(comment TimeOfDay-8AM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 8AM.")
(comment TechUserOfHandmadeArtifacts "Members are persons who use handcrafted items in everyday tasks.")
(comment Weathering "A collection of events.  In a #$Weathering event, the physical state of an object is altered due to the action of weather, typically over some extended period of time such as years or decades or centuries or millenia.  To undergo a #$Weathering process, the #$objectOfStateChange must be outdoors (or at least exposed to the outdoor weather).  The specific processes involved in a particular #$Weathering event depend upon (1) the climate in which the process occurs, and (2) the type of material that the #$objectOfStateChange is made of.  One typical effect of a #$Weathering is the removal of paint (and other coatings) from the object, through the action of sun, rain, freezing, and wind.")
(comment SuperHeavyweightWeightliftingSportsEvent "A weight class of WeightliftingSportsEvent")
(comment BuyingActivity "A specialization of #$SelectingSomething and #$CommercialActivity.  #$BuyingActivity is a collection of events that are very generally related to purchasing goods or services.  Each instance of #$BuyingActivity is an event that is either (i) a common prelude to buying (i.e., the kinds of activities that contribute to their doers becoming buyers), or (ii) an instance of #$Buying itself.  Examples of #$BuyingActivity include shopping for, or ordering, something very specific, and also general expressions of interest in purchasing something, such as placing an `Item Wanted' ad in a newspaper.")
(comment Trademark-String "#$Trademark-String is the collection of all (abstract) character strings that are used by some agent as the trademark of some goods or service.  It is a kind of #$ProperNameString.")
(comment Toxicity "How toxic a substance is")
(comment AutomobileElectronicsMC "Machines which are commonly sold together which are used in Automobiles.  Includes CarAlarm, CarStereo, RadarDetector")
(comment MLKHoliday "The holiday observed in some States of the U.S., commemorating the birthday of Martin Luther King, Jr.")
(comment MusicalText "The collection of all (abstract) text representing a piece of music or a part of such.  A written #$InformationBearingThing instantiating a #$MusicalText [#$MusicalTextCopy] can be read by a musician as instructions as to how to perform some #$Music.")
(comment STIB "An instance of #$IndividualDenotingFunction.  When applied to an instance THING of #$TemporalThing, #$STIB returns the `Short Time Interval Before' THING.  (#$STIB THING) does not include the time point (#$StartFn THING), but does include every time point in between (#$StartFn THING) and (#$StartFn (#$STIB THING)).  The function #$STIB is used to state axioms which assert propositions about the world just before some #$TemporalThing.  E.g., just before some event begins, or just before some tangible object comes into being.  Whether the propositions hold beyond the bounds of the short interval specified depends the nature of the proposition.  Consider the axiom `before launching, the Space Shuttle's fuel tanks are full'. The fuel tanks are only known to be full immediately before the launching event, and for some (measurable but potentially short) time interval before that launch, and so we use #$STIB to specify the time interval in which the assertion of fullness will hold.  Before or after that time, additional axioms are required to conclude whether the tanks are full or not.  Also see:  #$STIF.")
(comment DrugStore "The collection of #$RetailStores that sell prescription and non-prescription drugs and other sundry items - like the Eckerds down the street.  These organizations always have a #$Pharmacy as a department.  Note the constant #$DrugStoreChain should be used to refer to #$Organizations with multiple outlets.")
(comment Scull "The boat in which you perform the sport of Rowing.")
(comment MarketingActivity "A specialization of #$CommercialActivity and #$BusinessEvent. Instances of this collection include events such as market research, #$Advertising, product design and pricing and of course, sales (cf. #$SalesActivity).")
(comment argsGenl "A binary #$ArgGenlPredicate (q.v.) that is used to put a specified #$genls based argument-type constraint on all of a given relation's argument-places at once.  (#$argsGenl RELN COL) means that semantic well-formedness requires that each argument to which RELN is applied (regardless of argument-place) be an subcollection of COL.  For example, `(#$argsGenl #$PerformSimultaneouslyFn #$Event)' means that the function #$PerformSimultaneouslyFn must only be applied to types of events.  #$argsGenl is particularly useful for constraining (any and all of) the arguments to a #$VariableArityRelation (the preceding example being a case in point); though #$argsGenl may be applied to fixed-arity relations as well.  For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its immediate specializations.  See also #$argsIsa.")
(comment ImageCatalogue "A collection for keeping straight which visual images belong to which image catalogue.")
(comment HairAccessory "Decorative and/or functional gee-gaws worn in the hair.  Barrettes, bows, etc.")
(comment MedicarePatient "A person who is eligible for Medicare coverage.")
(comment SubordinatingConjunction "The collection of all conjunctions which can introduce a subordinate clause. Example: 'after'.")
(comment LearningByDoing "Learning by experimentation, by trial and error.")
(disjointWith MedicalCareInstitution ManagedCareOrganization)
(comment penaltyForInfraction "(#$penaltyForInfraction GAME INFRACT PENALTY) states that during sports events of type GAME, if a competitor commits an infraction of the type INFRACT, then the agents enforcing the sporting event make that competitor perform a penalty of type PENALTY.")
(comment LispHacker "People who hack Lisp code")
(comment AngularDistance "#$AngularDistance is a measure of the separation between the rays defined by two points and a fixed center.")
(comment hasProtagonists "See the inverse.")
(comment AccountsPayableWorker "accounting dept employees who handle co's bills to others")
(comment TimeOfDay-8PM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 8PM.")
(comment languageSpoken "(#$languageSpoken AGENT NATLANG) means that the #$IntelligentAgent AGENT speaks the natural human language NATLANG at least somewhat fluently.  The language must be speakable by humans, as are English, Latin, or Japanese, but not LISP, C or LINCOS.  See also #$NaturalLanguage.")
(comment PediatricGastroenterologist " A pediatric gastroenterologist is a doctor who specializes in diagnosis and treatment of stomach and intestinal disorders in children.")
(disjointWith SubmachineGun Handgun)
(comment PuttingBallOutOfPlay "Hitting, throwing, carrying or otherwise placing the ball, puck, birdie, etc. out of bounds and thereby out of play.")
(comment Cheering "Expressing approval loudly and enthusiastically by shouting expressions such as 'Hooray' or other approving words; esp. by audiences at performance events.")
(comment spans-Bridgelike "(#$spans-Bridgelike ?OBJ1 ?OBJ2) states that ?OBJ1 crosses over from one side of ?OBJ2 to the other.  ?OBJ1 does not extend far beyond the spanned region of ?OBJ2 (i.e. the length of the region not directly over ?OBJ2 is less than or equal to the length of the region directly over ?OBJ2).  Because of this restriction, ?OBJ1 can not be long enough to wrap around and be spanned by ?OBJ2.  Thus #$spans-Bridgelike can be an instance of #$AsymmetricBinaryPredicate.")
(comment Administrator "A specialization of #$AdministrativeStaffPerson.  Each instance of #$Administrator is an employee of an organization who is responsible for managing its organizational affairs.  Instances of #$Administrator may or may not also be required to manage people.  If so, then they are also #$Managers (q.v.).")
(comment SmogCertificate "The collection of information bearing objects which certify that an identified vehicle is within the pollution standards set for an administrative area.")
(comment TenderObject "An instance of #$ExistingObjectType, and a specialization of #$LiquidAsset.  Each instance of #$TenderObject is an object widely accepted as a means of payment for goods and services, and can thus play the role of #$objectTendered in instances of #$MoneyTransfer.  Important specializations of #$TenderObject include #$Currency, #$CreditCard, and #$Check-TenderObject.")
(comment SolidColorPattern "The collection of all instances of a uniform (solid) color pattern.  The could be thought of a the ABSSENCE of pattern, except for (some) pure color.")
(comment TimeOfDay-9AM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 9AM.")
(comment Late20thCenturyDevelopedCountryMiddleClassPerson "Postmodern persons of intermediate socioeconomic status living in developed countries in the late 20th century.")
(comment FeatherweightWeightliftingSportsEvent "A weight class of WeightliftingSportsEvent")
(comment LawnAndGardenMarketCategory "The category of lawn and garden supplies.  This includes items like garden hoses and lawn furniture, and may also include stuff such as garden fertilizer, seeds, and plants")
(comment ThanksgivingHoliday-US "The American holiday which falls on the fourth Thursday of November, traditionally celebrated with a big turkey feast.")
(comment TendingAPlant "The collection of events in which plants are purposely tended and cared for")
(comment informStatement "A #$MicrotheoryDesignatingPredicate and a                        specialization of #$ist (q.v.) that relates a given information                    context, or \"PIT\" (see #$PropositionalInformationThing), to any sentence                     that is true in that context.  (#$informStatement PIT SENT) means that SENT                    is true in PIT: SENT is asserted either in PIT itself or in some more general                  microtheory MT such that (#$genlMt PIT MT) holds.")
(comment relativeVarietyOn "For the things on ARG1's ARG2 slot, the number of different entries on their ARG3 slot is ARG4 when compared to other instance of ARG5.  For example, we might say (#$relativeVarietyOn SevenEleven001 #$sellsProductType #$insMarketedAs Medium #$RetailStore) to say that SevenEleven001 sells products that fall into a medium-large number of market categories, when compared with other RetailStores")
(comment CommunicationsOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations that are primarily or significantly engaged in the communications industry (including both the #$TelecommunicationsIndustry and the publishing industry) or whose activities focus on that industry.")
(disjointWith PurposefulAction Accident)
(comment (NoAmountFn Flammability) "This attribute characterizes materials that will not burn.
This corresponds to a National Fire Protection Association rating of 0, which indicates any
material that will not burn in air when exposed to a temperature of 1500 degrees Fahrenheit for 5 minutes.")
(comment interArgFormat4-1 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat4-1 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the first argument-place of PRED when PRED's fourth argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ... ARGN) in which ARG4 is an instance of COL, PRED's
arg1 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG1' in the 
preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its instances 
for further explanation.")
(comment HairPin "Pins worn in hair.")
(comment AssociatesDegree "The educational degrees normally issued after passing two years of community college or correspondence courses.")
(disjointWith UnitOfPower UnitOfAngularAcceleration)
(disjointWith MedicalCareInstitution VeterinaryHospital)
(comment IntervalAfterFn "(#$IntervalAfterFn T-OBJ DUR) denotes the #$TimeInterval which immediately follows T-OBJ, lasting for duration DUR.")
(comment commerciallyUsefulParts "The #$commerciallyUsefulParts of a plant, etc.")
(comment UnitOfAngularSpeed "The collection of functions which return elements of #$RateOfRotation.  E.g., (#$RadiansPerSecond 5) denotes a change of 5 radians in angular distance per second.")
(comment accountants "The people who perform the accounting functions for this organization")
(comment ReservationsManager "Manager of the reservations dept of a co.")
(comment TimeOfDay-5PM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 5PM.")
(comment titleOfPerson-String "(#$titleOfPerson-String PERSON STRING) relates the #$Person PERSON to a #$CharacterString, STRING, which is a word for a title (such as ``Dr.'') PERSON has.  A person may have more than one title, even cotemporally.")
(comment TelephoneConversation "The collection of all exchanges of information between two or more agents where the information transfer is mediated in whole or in part by a telephone transmission.  Included are cases where two or more human agents converse over the telephone conversing parties are organizations and the information exchange is an automated exchange of electronic data also count as borderline cases.  Instances of this collection only include the actual series of information exchanges for as long as it persists--they do *not* include the procedures by which the phone connection itself are established are ended.  Thus, every instance of (#$CommunicatingByMeansOfFn #$Telephone) will incorporate an instance of #$TelephoneConversation as a subevent.  Most instances of #$TelephoneConversation will incorporate multiple instances of #$SendingInformationByTelephone and #$ReceivingInformationByTelephone, and if one or more human users are involved in the exchange, these will generally be instances of #$SpeakingOnATelephone and #$ListeningOnATelephone, respectively.")
(comment Acing "A score made by a serve that one's opponent fails to touch.")
(comment FallingDown "The action in which an animal loses control of its balance and falls towards the ground.")
(comment rangeOfDistribution "The range of a distribution. This should be a list containing 2 numbers: the lowest value of the range and the highest. ")
(comment Billions-Quant "The fuzzy quantity of billions of something")
(comment Gang "The collection of all gangs.  Gangs are informal groups of (usually fairly young) adults or teens who engage in particular activities together.  #$Gangs are usually local (even confined to particular neighborhoods), but there are instances of #$Gang that are national in scope (e.g., the Guardian Angels).")
(comment directionBetweenObjects "(#$directionBetweenObjects OBJ1 OBJ2 UVI) means that UVI, an instance of #$UnitVectorInterval , is a vector or set of vectors which point(s) from a point (or set of points) in OBJ1 to a point (or set of points) in OBJ2. See also #$VectorFromToFn which is roughly interchangeable with #$directionBetweenObjects. #$directionBetweenObjects has the advantage that an arbitrarily precise direction may be specified. #$VectorFromToFn saves the user from doing the labor involved with reifying and from having to know the direction between OBJ1 and OBJ2.")
(comment DistinctivelyUnitedStatesCuisine "Not a good name -- a slippery concept.  What some Americans (white? black? Anglo? Hispanic? Jewish?) think of as distinctively `American' food.  Probably best thought of as a nationalist mass-media generalization, perhaps appropriate in the 1940s or 1950s, but hopelessly misleading now")
(comment M10000SpeedSkateSportsEvent "The 10000M speed skating competition")
(comment objectBasicPrice "An object being sold has an #$objectBasicPrice.  It also has a #$cost, which is the #$objectBasicPrice plus tax, shipping, handling, etc.  See #$serviceBasicPrice for the analogous information about services being sold.")
(comment writtenString "#$writtenString is a predicate relating a physical written sequence of characters (in an #$InformationBearingObject) to a formal character string in some character-based representation.  The written physical characters each have a corresponding formal #$Character-Abstract taken from some #$characterSetForWritingSystem.")
(comment inPatients "ARG2 is an in-patient at the medical facility ARG1.")
(comment LawnAndGardenStore "The collection of stores that sell lawn&garden supplies, such as Aus-Tex Garden Supply")
(comment adminRouteOfType "For a type of pharmacy product, gives the kind of administration script normally used to give the drug to a patient.")
(comment ChristmasHoliday "Each of these is a #$ChristianHoliday which commemorates the birth of Christ, but which is also widely observed as a secular winter #$Holiday in countries with significant Christian segments of their population.")
(comment WateringAPlant "The collection of events in which a plant is watered")
(comment JobApplicationForm "A form with which one applies for a job.")
(comment averageYearlyIncome "The average annual income of the residents of this geographical region.")
(disjointWith PurposefulAction Dying)
(comment DosageFormType "Drug products organized according to their form when they are given as doses.")
(comment NewspaperCopy "Publication containing ephemeral (daily or weekly) accounts of news events since the last publication.")
(comment (LowAmountFn Flammability) "This attribute characterizes materials that must be preheated before ignition will occur. This corresponds to a National Fire Protection Association rating of 1, which indicates any material that has a #$flashPoint above 200 degrees Fahrenheit; or that will burn in air when exposed to a temperature of 1500 degrees Fahrenheit for 5 minutes or less. Most ordinary combustible materials fall into this class.")
(comment recipientOfService "(#$recipientOfService EVENT AGENT) means that AGENT is a recipient of the #$ServiceEvent EVENT.  Thus, the service in question is done for or performed on AGENT, and AGENT is correspondingly affected by it.")
(disjointWith UnitOfPower UnitOfAcceleration)
(comment criticalToBehavior "(crit PART DEV SIT ROLE) This component (PART) is critical to a particular behavior (SIT and ROLE) of the device (DEV) of which it is a physical part.")
(disjointWith MedicalCareInstitution HomeNursingServiceOrganization)
(disjointWith Food Drink)
(comment MetersPerSecondPerSecond "The basic measure of acceleration")
(comment numericFluentGT "(#$numericFluentGT OBJ F(X) G(X)) states that F(OBJ) > G(OBJ)")
(comment mtImageTimeOfDay "ARG2 is the time of day type of the images described by assertions in the mt ARG1.")
(comment BarelyVisibleSized "A volume ranging from a size just able to be seen by the naked eye up to about 5 millimeters in diameter.")
(comment ReservationsClerk "clerical worker in the reservations dept of a co.")
(comment TimeOfDay-10PM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 10PM.")
(comment UnderseaMedicineSpecialist "An instance of #$UnderseaMedicineSpecialist is a #$Doctor-Medical who specializes           in that branch of medicine (Underseas Medicine) concerning some of the effects of being           underwater or in other highly pressurized environments.  For more information           see http://www.mmslists.com/s1_phy_spec_def.html, a website of the           American Medical Association.")
(comment BlockingAScore "Preventing the opponent from scoring.")
(comment MakingAnObsceneGesture "The set of actions in which a person makes an obscene or objectionable sign, usually with fingers, hands, or arms; an expression of contempt or hostile provocation.")
(comment PositionVector "The coordinate position of the reference point of an object.")
(comment MeasuredSportsEvent "games where there is some measurement of performance; each competitor attempts to perform the game, without interference. the competitor achieving the best measurement wins. Diving, running, rowing, but not tennis or basketball.")
(comment Congregation "A group of people attending a #$CommunalWorshipService")
(comment EducationalDegree "A specialization of #$Credential.  Each instance of #$EducationalDegree is a credential conferred by some instance of #$EducationalOrganization on a student who has successfully completed a prescribed course of study there.  #$EducationalDegree includes as instances high school, associate, baccalaureate, licensate, magisterial, professional, and doctoral degrees.")
(comment Estate-LegalEntity "An estate is a collection of property managed by an executor, a #$LegalAgent.")
(comment protectsFromAction "ARG1 protects ARG2 from #$TemporalObjectType ARG3")
(comment Upset "Competitions in which an upset occurred, i.e. someone who was not a contender won")
(comment TechUserOfElectronicDevices "Members are persons who use electronic devices; e.g., calculators, TVs, computers.  Implies the use of electrical devices.")
(comment M5000SpeedSkateSportsEvent "The 5000M speed skating competition")
(comment occurrencesPerPeriod "(#$occurrencesPerPeriod SUB-TYPE SUPER-TYPE N) means that N instances of #$TemporalObjectType SUB-TYPE occur during each instance of #$TemporalObjectType SUPER-TYPE.  For example, (#$occurrencesPerPeriod #$CalendarDay #$CalendarWeek 7) means that there are seven calendar days in each calendar week.")
(disjointWith Reading Hearing)
(comment CommercialBuying "Buying events involving commercial organizations. Typically, this involves one business buying goods or services from another business. Typically, a purchase order is sent from the buyer, and the seller extends credit terms to the buyer for the transaction.")
(comment BeastOfBurden "The collection of all animals used as providers of motive force, for animal power (plowing, pulling, etc.) or for carrying.  This collection probably should not have any specs, at least not in the #$BaseKB.")
(comment booleanResult "ARG2 is the boolean value returned by the TrueOrFalse test ARG1.  Although it does not necessarily reflect reality, in general we will assume that test results are accurate.")
(comment MusicalInstrumentMarketCategory "Products sold as musical instruments.")
(comment ValentinesDay "Each of these is an annual #$Holiday celebrating romance and love.  Although derived from the celebration of the Christian Saint Valentine, it is essentially a purely secular holiday as practiced in the United States of America.")
(comment FertilizingAPlant "The collection of events in which a plant is fertilized")
(comment PersonnelRecord "The collection of documents held by an employer about individual employees, generally containing information about the work agreement and the employee's performance.")
(comment SwimmingPoolLaneDivider "The collection of floating dividers that stretch across the lengths of swimming pools, dividing them into lanes.")
(comment CarWashShop "The collection of all #$Organizations that provide car washing services.  This collection includes school groups who offer to wash cars on the side of the road in order to raise money for school trips (or whatever).")
(comment PurposefulAction "A specialization of both #$Action and #$AtLeastPartiallyMentalEvent.  Each instance of #$PurposefulAction is an action consciously, volitionally, and purposefully done by (see #$performedBy) at least one actor.")
(comment VersionSuffix "A string appended to the end of names of computer files, contracts, software releases etc in order to indicate which version of the object it is.")
(comment IntangibleExistingThing "A specialization of both #$IntangibleIndividual and #$SomethingExisting.  Instances of #$IntangibleExistingThing exist stably in time (unlike instances of #$Event), but lack any material parts (unlike instances of #$PartiallyTangible). Notable specializations of #$IntangibleExistingThing include #$DevisedPracticeOrWork and #$Agreement.")
(comment (MediumAmountFn Flammability) "This attribute characterizes materials that must be  moderately heated before ignition will occur. This corresponds to a National Fire Protection Association rating of 2, which indicates any liquid that has a #$flashPoint between 100 and 200 degrees Fahrenheit; or solids which readily give off flammable vapors.")
(comment PerceivingSlot "A collection of predicates. Each instance of #$PerceivingSlot is a binary predicate relating a perceiver and an object or event (not a sense-datum) that s/he perceives in the mode specified by the predicate; e.g., sees, hears, smells, tactuallyPerceives, tastes. Assertions that use a predicate belonging to #$PerceivingSlot imply that some perception event occurs during the time that the assertion holds. See also #$Perceiving and its subcollections.")
(comment interArgFormat2-4 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat2-4 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the fourth argument-place of PRED when PRED's second argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ... ARGN) in which ARG2 is an instance of COL, PRED's
arg4 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG4' in the 
preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its instances 
for further explanation.")
(comment ActOfDissent "A collection of events.  Each element of #$ActOfDissent is an event in which some agent (or agents) publicly disapproves of, protests against, or exhibits resistance to another agent's exercise of power.  Typically the dissenting agent is in some way subject to the authority or power of the agent s/he acts against.  An act of dissent is inherently a social occurrence.  For example, writing a petition calling for Tibetan independence is an act of dissent in China, even if the petition is written in solitude and circulated by others.  An act of dissent may or may not involve violence; an act of terrorism may or may not express dissent.  An act of dissent may or may not involve explicit communication; for example, a bombing or assassination, or a Buddhist monk's self-immolation, might occur without an accompanying verbal message, but its dissenting intent might be understood (or surmised) from context.  See also #$PublicProtesting (for dissent which involves explicit communication) and its subsets.")
(comment BuyingAService "A specialization of #$Buying. In each instance of #$BuyingAService, an agent exchanges money for some service (cf. #$ServiceEvent). This collection includes events in which an agent buys both a good and a service (for instance, when an agent buys a sit-down meal in a restaurant), as well as events in which an agent pays for a service, but does not buy any goods (for instance, when a parent pays a babysitter to watch his or her child).")
(comment percentOfClientsWithEmployer "This expresses the percentage of HMO clients who are employees of a certain employer.")
(disjointWith UnitOfAngularSpeed UnitOfPower)
(comment InventingSomething "Inventing something.")
(disjointWith DentistsOffice MedicalCareInstitution)
(comment DeclaringWar "The communicating of the intent to wage war on another army.")
(comment RadiansPerSecond "The basic measure of #$RateOfRotation.")
(comment Story "The collection of microtheories each of which contains the assertional content of a story -- a #$Narrative describing a particular sequence of events which occur to one or more characters in the story.  The story is at least partially fictional as opposed to \"true stories\".")
(comment mtImageMonth "ARG2 is the type of calendar month of the images described by assertions in the mt ARG1.")
(comment Family-Nuclear "The conventional human nuclear family consisting of a father, a mother and their children.")
(comment FrontOfficeManager "Manager of the front office, sometimes called guest services department")
(comment TimeOfDay-11PM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 11PM.")
(comment IV-NameSuffix "The numeral ''IV'' is used as a suffix on a person's name to represent the fourth generation to use the same full name.")
(comment ComputationalObject "A specialization of both #$MathematicalOrComputationalThing and #$IntangibleIndividual.  Each instance of #$ComputationalObject is a syntactically structured form, such as a Cyc system expression, a Lisp string, a C variable name, or an equation in a particular canonical form format.")
(disjointWith Perceiving BodilyFunctionEvent-Involuntary)
(comment VolleyballMatch "The collection of volleyball matches. The team to win the best of 5 sets wins the match.")
(comment UsingProfanity "Using vulgar language.  Need not be spoken.")
(comment InformationTransferEvent "A specialization of #$GeneralizedTransfer.  Each instance of #$InformationTransferEvent is an event in which information is transferred from a source (#$informationOrigin) to one or more destinations (#$informationDestination), where the source and the various destinations are either intelligent agents or #$InformationBearingThings (IBTs).  Examples include reading a book (transfer of information from the book to the reader), saying something to someone (transfer of information from the speaker to the listener), machine translation (transfer of information from an encoded IBT in the source language to an encoded IBT in the target language), OCR scanning (transfer of information from a visual information source to another IBT in a different format), carving initials in a tree (transfer of information from an agent to an IBT),  and making a speech (transfer of information from an agent to other agents).  See also the specialization #$InformationTransferPhysicalEvent.")
(comment MatchSportsEvent "games where competitors play against each other - typically, only two competitors play each other at a time. Actions are taken by each competitor to achieve a goal and to prevent the other agent from obtaining the goal.")
(comment Thousands-Quant "The fuzzy quantity of thousands of something")
(comment Director-Movie "An instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation. Each instance of #$Director-Movie is a person responsible for the development of the production of a film.")
(comment Kneading "Working semi-solid stuff (e.g. dough or clay) by pressing, squeezing, folding and stretching it.  Can be done by hand or machine.")
(comment DecadesDuration "A #$UnitOfTime function that takes one or two real numbers as arguments and returns, as its value, a comparable #$Time-Quantity attribute measured in decades. More precisely, an expression of the form (#$DecadesDuration NUM) denotes the (\"point-value\") #$Time-Quantity of being exactly NUM decades in duration, and an expression of the form (#$DecadesDuration MIN MAX) denotes the (properly interval-like) #$Time-Quantity of being at least MIN decades and at most MAX decades in duration.")
(comment roleExpectedBy "agent arg4 expects agent arg1 to satisfy the role of arg3 in the mt arg2.")
(comment Sturdy "The attribute of being durable, the opposite of fragile")
(comment WearAndTear "The process of wear and tear that occur as a result of usage")
(comment GiantSlalomSportsEvent "The downhill giant slalom competition")
(comment scheduledIntervals "arg2 is a termporal interval over which the schedule that is arg1 applies")
(comment LevelOfTicklingSensation "The type of internal sensation or feeling of being tickled.")
(comment BusinessSuit "The collection of all business suits, a kind of clothing usually consisting (for men) of trousers and a matching jacket worn over a shirt with a necktie; and (for women) a skirt or slacks with a matching jacket worn over a blouse")
(comment Holiday "A specialization of #$HumanActivity.  Each instance of #$Holiday is an event featuring social celebrations and/or rituals.  Instances of #$Holiday typically last for one day (see the constant #$DaysDuration) and typically coincide with some day of the year (see the constant #$CalendarDay).  However, some instances of #$Holiday (such as the instances of #$ChanukkahHoliday or #$Oktoberfest-Holiday) last for several days.  While instances of #$Holiday are often annual events, they may also be one-time events or scheduled in some other manner.  They are also contextual, as different nationalities and ethnic groups celebrate different ones.")
(comment Practicing-Preparing "Doing some action repetitively in order to learn it.  It will someday have assertions like the following:  Performer of practice does action X repetitively.  Goal is to make performance of X better (#$wantsToRelnChange).  Practice makes performance of activity better (for humans).  During practice, stakes are not high, there is no audience or boss or teacher (exception: coaching).  This unit allows us to say things like (doesInsAsJobWIthRElnType Musician24601 performer Practicing #$subEvents #$PlayingAMusicalInstrument) to say 'Musician24601 plays a musical instrument while practicing.'  This way we don't have to make a silly unit like PracticingAMusicalInstrument.  For more examples see specs of PerformerArtsEntertainment.--Siegel, May 17, 1996")
(comment Invitation-IBT "The IBT bearing a message to some agent that asks the individual to attend a particular event.")
(comment Torch "A flammable torch, such as the one passed by runners in the Olympics.")
(comment LongTermMedicalCareProvidingOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations that provide long-term medical care for patients.")
(comment PerformanceReviewDocument "The collection of documents that describe an agent's job-related performance (usually of specific tasks).")
(comment Rotation-NonPeriodic "The collection of all rotational movements in which rotation occurs in a nonperiodic fashion; e.g., the turning of a knob on a kitchen appliance or a radio dial, or movements of a trackball.  See also #$Rotation-Periodic for the context-sensitive nature of this dichotomy.")
(comment PotencyFn "Returns a type of stuff of the given potency, which is a spec of ARG2.")
(comment (HighAmountFn Flammability) "This attribute characterizes materials that can be ignited under almost all ambient temperature conditions. This corresponds to a National Fire Protection Association rating of 3, which indicates any liquid that has a #$flashPoint between 73 and 100 degrees Fahrenheit; and solids which burn with extreme rapidity or are in fibrous or dust form.")
(comment NumericQuantifier "Numeric quantifiers denote a numeric value which is the result of applying the function specified in the second argument to all of the elements of the set expression denoted by the first argument.")
(comment Negotiator "One who engages in discussions, working toward agreements between the organization they represent and some other organization or individual.")
(comment subjectToCOC "This predicate is used to state that a given agent is subject to a given code of conduct, that is, that agent is obliged to abide by that code of conduct.")
(comment NursingDegree-CCRN "This credential is given to registered nurses who, through additional study, are qualified to give cardiac or critical care.")
(disjointWith UnitOfMonetaryRate UnitOfPower)
(comment genlRoles "The predicate #$genlRoles relates two Cyc constants representing #$Roles.  (#$genlRoles SP-ROLE GEN-ROLE) indicates that the role GEN-ROLE is a general characterization of another role SP-ROLE. If an object plays the more specific role SP-ROLE in a situation, it thus also fills the more general role GEN-ROLE. For example, in a #$Microtheory representing the use of a dishwasher, a #$genlRoles of #$TheDishes is #$TheObjectActedOn, and a #$genlRoles of #$TheWashCycle is #$TheSubEventRole.")
(disjointWith DoctorsOffice MedicalCareInstitution)
(comment IntervalBeforeFn "An instance of #$IndividualDenotingFunction.  When applied to an instance THING of #$TemporalThing and an instance DURATION of #$Time-Quantity, #$IntervalBeforeFn returns the interval of time (an instance of #$TimeInterval) of duration DURATION (see the predicate #$duration) immediately preceding the start of THING (so that (#$contiguousAfter THING (#$IntervalBeforeFn THING DURATION)) holds).")
(comment DeclaringCeaseFire "A collection of events.  In each #$DeclaringCeaseFire event, some parties are #$MakingAnAgreement to halt their armed conflict.")
(comment RateOfRotation "A collection of scalar rates of rotation.")
(comment GeneralPayrollClerk "accounting dept employees who disburse salary checks, refunds, etc.")
(comment TimeOfDay-9PM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 9PM.")
(comment constituentPercentByMass "(#$constituentPercentByMass ?obj ?stuff-type ?percent) means ?obj has  ?percent amount of ?stuff-type as a #$constituents.  In other words,  the mass of the #$constituents of ?obj which are instances of ?stuff-type  constitute ?percent amount of the total mass of ?obj.")
(comment PreventiveMedicineSpecialist " A preventive medicine specialist is a doctor who specializes in preventing disease and making other disorders less severe.")
(comment WringingHands "The set of actions in which a person repeatedly clasps, rubs, or grasps his/her own hands; an expression of nervousness or worry.")
(comment endsAfterEndingOf "(#$endsAfterEndingOf LATER EARLY) means that LATER ceases to exists or occur after EARLY ceases to exist or occur.  That is, the #$endingPoint of LATER is later than the #$endingPoint of EARLY, or, equivalently, (#$after (#$EndFn LATER) (#$EndFn EARLY).    This implies nothing about whether, or by how much, LATER and EARLY overlap, except that they can't be fully #$cotemporal.")
(comment MajorSalesActivity "These sales events have a duration that extends beyond the actual buying and also involve a major financial transaction.")
(comment Tens-Quant "The fuzzy quantity of tens of something")
(comment Philosopher "A specialization of #$Person; in the context of #$HumanActivitiesMt this collection is an instance of #$PersonTypeByActivity, in the context of #$JobMt it is an instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation.  Each instance of #$Philosopher is a person who habitually thinks about philosophical matters such as what is or might be, what we can know, how we can know anything, etc. In the contemporary era most philosophers are academics or professionals, but a significant number (now and historically) don't fit this profile.")
(comment ComputerUserInteraction "Communication between human user and computer.")
(comment HumanNameSuffix "Basically, the collection of jr., III, esq., Ph.D., Ed.D., M.A., and other such suffixes to names.")
(comment coreRelatives "In this microtheory, (#$coreRelatives PERSON1 PERSON2) means, specifically, that PERSON2 is a child, grandchild, sibling, spouse, parent, or grandparent of PERSON1.  In other words, this predicate relates a person to her/his (i) siblings, (ii) lineal relatives that are one or two generations \"above\" or \"below\" her, and (iii) closest affine (spouse).")
(comment MillisecondsDuration "A #$UnitOfTime function that takes one or two real numbers as arguments and returns, as its value, a comparable #$Time-Quantity attribute measured in milliseconds. More precisely, an expression of the form (#$MilliSecondsDuration NUM) denotes the (\"point-value\") #$Time-Quantity of being exactly NUM milliseconds in duration, and an expression of the form (#$MilliSecondsDuration MIN MAX) denotes the (properly interval-like) #$Time-Quantity of being at least MIN milliseconds and at most MAX milliseconds in duration.")
(comment authorityCapableOf "The predicate #$authorityCapableOf is used to assert that a particular agent has the authority to participate in a certain kind of situation in the capacity of a particular role, because of said agent's intrinsic properties.  (#$authorityCapableOf AGENT SITTYPE ROLE) means that AGENT is authorized by the appropriate agency of authorization to play the role ROLE in situations of type SITTYPE. For example, it is true in Orange County that (#$authorityCapableOf LanceIto #$Trial-Criminal #$judicialAgents). Note that even though an agent may be #$authorityCapableOf playing a certain role in a certain kind of situation, this does not necessarily imply that the agent will be physically or mentally capable of playing that role in every instance of the situation type, or even that the agent is physically or mentally capable in general of playing that role in situations of that type.")
(comment Wall-GenericBarrier "The collection of all walls, those of construction artifacts as well as of other artifacts, e.g., container products, and of non-artifacts such as caves.")
(comment VictoryLap "The set of actions in which the performer does a lap around a track to express celebration or triumph after a victory.")
(comment TechUserOfICEngines "Members are persons who use devices driven by internal-combustion engines.  Implies the use of simple fueled devices.")
(comment Scuffing "Scuffing happens to certain materials (e.g: leather) as a result of processes involving physical contact and is a special case of wear & tear")
(comment AirPistolShootingSportsEvent "A marksmanship sports event in which air pistols are used.")
(disjointWith ClimateCycleType WeeklyTemporalObjectType)
(comment ActiveSalesActivity "Sales activities in which the performer entices specific (potential) customers to make purchases (contrast with #$PassiveSalesActivity).")
(comment Pound-UnitOfForce "The force that the earth's gravity exerts on a mass of one pound at sea level.  The distinction between #$Pound-UnitOfMass and #$Pound-UnitOfForce is very often blurred because of the implicit 1g assumption.")
(comment MedicalLabTechnician "The people who actually perform the medical tests your doctor is always taking samples for.")
(comment SleepWear "Clothes you wear when you're ready to sleep at night, or after you wake up in the morning -- clothes that are worn during sleep, and during the transition period between sleep and wakeful activity and vice versa")
(comment activeIngredientsOfType "This predicate gives the kinds of active ingredient(s) in a type of pharmacy product.")
(comment Vector-Precise "A specialization of #$VectorInterval.  An instance VECTOR of #$VectorInterval is also an instance of #$Vector-Precise just in case both the direction and magnitude of VECTOR are single values, rather than ranges of values.  One example of a #$Vector-Precise is `5 feet due West'.  An important specialization of #$Vector-Precise is #$UnitVector-Precise.")
(disjointWith SeparationEvent Holiday)
(comment Acting "Being someone you aren't.  Taking on a character role.  Someday this may be partially related to lying.  What actors do during plays.  What comedians might do as part of a joke.  Something children do for fun.")
(comment MedalPlatform "The platform that medal winners stand on during the olympic medal awards ceremony.")
(comment Vineyard "The collection of agricultural organizations that are running viticultural activities, a specialization of #$CropFarm. Instances of #$Vineyard are farms that are growing grapes [see #$GrapeVine]. Some instances of this collection, but not all, are also producing wine [see #$Wine] and are instances of #$Winery. A domain operated by a vineyard is an instance of #$ViticulturalDomain.")
(comment CrossCountrySkiingSportsEvent "The NordicSkiingSportsEvents that are cross country ski races")
(comment Rotation-Periodic "A specialization of both #$Movement-Rotation and #$Movement-Periodic.  Each instance of #$Rotation-Periodic is a series of partial or full rotations occurring periodically.  Examples of #$Rotation-Periodic include the swinging of a clock pendulum and the rotation of the Earth on its axis.")
(comment (VeryHighAmountFn Flammability) "This attribute characterizes materials that will rapidly or completely vaporize at atmospheric pressure and normal ambient temperature. This corresponds to a National Fire Protection Association rating of 4, which indicates any liquid that has a #$flashPoint below 73 degrees Fahrenheit; flammable gases; and materials that can form explosive mixtures with air.")
(disjointWith NumericQuantifier SetDenotingFunction)
(comment interArgFormat1-5 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat1-5 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the fifth argument-place of PRED when PRED's first argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ... ARGN) in which ARG1 is an instance of COL, 
PRED's arg5 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG5' in 
the preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its 
instances for further explanation.")
(comment Tendon "A #$Tendon is a white inflexible cord of #$ConnectiveTissue connecting a #$MuscleTissue to another body part.")
(comment GovernmentCOC-ModernWestern "Meant to include the #$GovernmentCOCs of most modern western governments, which largely share notions of what's legal and what's not.  Should include, for example, the COCs of modern-day United States, Britain, #$France, #$Germany, #$Japan, #$Canada, etc.  Includes both #$Laws and #$LegalCodes so long as they are modern western ones.")
(comment NursingDegree-NA "This credential is given to registered nurses who, through additional study, are qualified to administer anesthesia.")
(disjointWith UnitOfFlowRate UnitOfPower)
(comment allGenlRoles "Kleene star of #$genlRoles.  If one role is the allGenlRole of another in a situation, then if an object plays the more specific role, they also play the more general one.")
(disjointWith MedicalCareInstitution CardiacCatheterizationUnit)
(comment JobHunting "Instances are complicated actions in which the performer looks for a job.  This can involve reading job advertisements, sending out resumes, going for interviews, and general schmoozing ('networking').")
(disjointWith Breathing TakingABreath)
(comment CubicFootPerSecond "The amount of material moving by; used, e.g., for flow rates")
(comment prefersOnSlot "Agent ARG1 prefers that ARG4 fill ARG2's ARG3 slot over having ARG5 fill it. ")
(comment AccountingClerk "accounting dept clerical worker")
(comment TimeOfDay-1AM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 1AM.")
(comment Jr-NameSuffix "''Jr.'' is used as a suffix on a person's name to represent the second generation to use the same full name.  It is often used to distinguish two consecutive generations who use the same name.  ''Jr.'' is less formal than ''II'' .")
(comment PediatricDiagnosticLabImmunologist " A pediatric diagnostic lab immunologist is a doctor whose speciality is diagnosing problems with a child's immune system through laboratory tests.")
(comment Bill-PaymentRequest-PIT "A collection of abstract (informational) objects; a subset of #$TextMicrotheory.  Each element of #$Bill-PaymentRequest-PIT is a formal request for payment (for products or services); the informational content of a #$Bill-PaymentRequest.  Typically, this information includes the name and address of the billing agent; the name, address, account number (if there is one) of the debtor; the amount owed and where/how/when to remit it.")
(comment AdvancingToTheNextRound "Completing an event successfully enough to place high enough to qualify for further competition.")
(comment ClenchingFists "The collection of actions in which a performer closes one or both hands to make a fist or fists, either intentionally or semi-reflexively.")
(comment Chlorophyll "A piece of chlorophyll - a piece of substance made of chlorophyll molecules which exists within a plant.")
(comment Anchorperson "a person who anchors a news program on television or radio")
(comment BankTeller "A clerical worker in a bank's front office (transaction processing office) who enters debit/credit transactions.")
(comment computationalResourcesSpent "(#$computationalResourcesSpent PROBLEM-SOLVING TIME) means that the total amount of TIME (from one or more #$ComputationalSystems) is used to solve the problem addressed during PROBLEM-SOLVING.")
(comment salutation "(#$salutation PRSN TITLE) means the #$Person PRSN's name may have the #$CourtesyTitle TITLE attached to it, such as: Mr., Ms., Mrs., Miss, Dr., etc., when that person is addressed.")
(comment TribalOrganization "A governmental organization formed by members of a single tribe or sets of tribes.")
(comment WeeksDuration "A #$UnitOfTime function that takes one or two real numbers as arguments and returns, as its value, a comparable #$Time-Quantity attribute measured in weeks. More precisely, an expression of the form (#$WeeksDuration NUM) denotes the (\"point-value\") #$Time-Quantity of being exactly NUM weeks in duration, and an expression of the form (#$WeeksDuration MIN MAX) denotes the (properly interval-like) #$Time-Quantity of being at least MIN weeks and at most MAX weeks in duration.")
(comment legallyCapableOf "The predicate #$legallyCapableOf indicates that an agent is legally able to take a certain role in a certain type of action.  (#$legallyCapableOf AGENT SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that the individual AGENT is legally qualified and/or entitled to act in this ROLE in #$Situations of the type SIT-TYPE.  For example, a person over 35 years of age is #$legallyCapableOf becoming #$UnitedStatesPresident.  This notion of legal capability should not be confused with the legality or illegality of an action.")
(comment BackWall "The collection of back walls of objects")
(comment AuthorizedAgreement "A specialization of #$Agreement.  Each instance of #$Agreement is a generic agreement that is authorized by one of the agreeing parties (typically by the issuer of the document embodying the agreement).  #$AuthorizedAgreements are generic in the sense that their authorizing agents are party to many similar agreements; for that reason, an #$AuthorizedAgreement is typically given a unique identification number.  Notable positive examples include bank accounts, driver's licenses, and stock certificates.")
(comment TechUserOfElectricalDevices "Members are persons who use electrical devices (but not necessarily electronic ones).")
(comment Stirring "A collection of actions in which a liquid or other substance is agitated with a continuous or repetitive motion.  Stirring is usually performed with an implement such as a spoon.")
(comment HalfLightJudoSportsEvent "Judo matches for sport, in the HalfLight weight class.")
(comment WeeklyTemporalObjectType "A specialization of #$TemporalObjectType.  Each instance of #$WeeklyTemporalObjectType is a collection of temporal things, all of which are synchronized with some calendar, with exactly one of those things occuring each calendar week.  For example, one instance of #$WeeklyTemporalObjectType is #$Wednesday, since there is exactly one instance of #$Wednesday each calendar week.")
(comment thingAttachedTo "arg2 is the thing to which the attached thing is connected, in the Attachment configuration ARG1.")
(comment PassiveBuyingActivity "Activities which are intended to lead to a Buying, and in which the performer interacts with potential providers of desired goods or services as a class, rather than as individual agents.  Perhaps `FocussedBuyingActivity' would be a better name.  Advertising a desire to purchase something would be a #$PassiveBuyingActivity, but looking through a catalog, which is put out by a particular vendor, would not.  Contrast with #$ActiveBuyingActivity.")
(comment Pharaoh-HeadOfState "A ruler of ancient #$Egypt.")
(comment TrueOrFalseTest "The collection of tests which return a boolean value.")
(comment T-Shirt "The sets of T-shirts")
(comment StorageOfSomething "This unit represents the static situation of something in storage.  Also see #$StoringSomething.")
(comment Letter-PIT "The collection of all mts which represent the content of letters (personal letters, business letters, etc.).")
(comment ReleasingFromConfinement "Releasing an object from a container, such as an animal from a cage, a prisoner from a cell, or air from a tire.")
(comment Winery "A collection of organization, a specialization of #$FoodProcessingEstablishment. Instances of #$Winery are producing wine [#$Wine]. These are not necessarily, but may, also be instances of #$Vineyard.")
(comment RelayRaceSportsEvent "A race in which a team of athletes competes, taking turns performing, and their combined times are used to determine the team's standing.")
(comment MarketingPerson "Someone who works in marketing.")
(comment QuarterFn "An instance of #$DateDenotingFunction.  When applied to an integer in the range 1 through 4 and an instance of #$CalendarYear, #$QuarterFn returns an instance of #$CalendarQuarter. (#$QuarterFn N YEAR) is the Nth quarter of YEAR. For example, (#$QuarterFn 2 (#$YearFn 1966)) is the second quarter of 1966.")
(comment RotationTransmissionProcess "the transmission of rotation")
(comment ProductStandard "A specialization of #$Specification.  Each instance of #$ProductStandard is a precise description applied to the instances of a particular instance of #$ProductType.  Manufacturers of that product type agree explicitly or in practice, or they may obey a government requirement, to make product designs following the specifications stated in the standard, so that products within the type will all have certain features in common.  For example, telephones and television sets fulfil certain product standards.  The resultant interchangeability allows compatibility with other devices and products, with public utilities, commercial trading expectations, and government purchasing requirements.")
(comment salesRate "the rate in dollars per unit time at which this product is sold, worldwide.")
(comment FatPhysicalBuild "An attribute for describing an animal that is overweight.  Orthogonal to whether or not the animal's intrinsic physical build is slight, average, or stocky.")
(comment SulfuricAcid "The collection of samples of H2SO4.")
(comment (LowAmountFn LevelOfFitness) "The physical fitness (or unfitness) level of couch potatoes.")
(comment AssociateInArtsDegree "An associate in arts degree is normally issued after passing two years of college-level liberal arts classes at an accredited college which issues such degrees.")
(disjointWith UnitOfAngularSpeed UnitOfAngularAcceleration)
(comment MedicalCareInstitution "#$MedicalCareInstitution is a specialization of #$OrganizationWithIndividualClients and #$MedicalCareOrganization.  Each instance of #$MedicalCareInstitution is a large organization that provides medical or psychiatric care and has facilities for human patients to stay at least overnight.")
(comment AlumniOrganization "A collection of organizations.  An element of #$AlumniOrganization is a social organization that offers membership to persons who have attended a particular #$EducationalOrganization, usually a college or university or professional school.  Social events for alumni, including reunion gatherings, are organized by a school's #$AlumniOrganization.  Another function of an #$AlumniOrganization is to raise money for the alma mater that sponsors it.")
(comment ElectricalEvent "The class of electrical events.")
(comment likesSensorially "(#$likesSensorially AGT SENSUM) means that the #$PerceptualAgent AGT derives some physical pleasure from the sensory experience of SENSUM (a taste, odor, or other #$SensoryAttribute).")
(comment BellCaptain "guest services dept employee, supervisor of bellmen")
(comment Verb-Contracted "The collection of all contracted verbal endings. The only main verbs which can contract are 'have' and 'be'. Example: -ve, from 'have'.")
(comment TimeOfDay-7PM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 7PM.")
(comment CollectionDenotingFunction "The subcollection of #$Function-Denotational whose instances return instances of #$Collection.  Examples include #$SwimmingEventFn, #$GroupFn, and #$MoleculeFn.  For example, (#$MoleculeFn #$Oxygen) denotes the collection of all oxygen molecules.  See also the collections #$IndividualDenotingFunction and #$SetDenotingFunction.")
(comment SurprisingOpponent "Taking advantage of an opponent's inattention or expectations to surprise him.")
(comment RaisingArmsInVictory "The set of actions in which the performer raises one or both arms upward to express celebration or triumph.")
(disjointWith MensSportsCompetition WomensSportsCompetition)
(comment TailSide "the tail side of an object that has an intrinsic pointing axis, like an arrow or a fish or a gun")
(comment artisticWorksCreated "A binary predicate that relates instances of #$Artist to instances of #$ArtObject.  (#$artisticWorksCreated AGT ART) means that AGT created ART.")
(comment computationalResourcesAvailable "(#$computationalResourcesAvailable PROBLEM-SOLVING TIME) means that the total amount of TIME (from one or more #$ComputationalSystems) is available to be to solve the problem addressed in PROBLEM-SOLVING.")
(comment CourtesyTitle "The collection of #$Titles, such as  Mr., Ms., Mrs., Miss, Dr., etc., which precede names in Anglo-American addressing custom.")
(comment LimitedPartnership "An organization which includes at least one partner with unlimited liability.  The other partners, instances of #$LimitedPartner, are liable only for the capital that they contributed to the organization.")
(comment CenturiesDuration "A #$UnitOfTime function that takes one or two real numbers as arguments and returns, as its value, a comparable #$Time-Quantity attribute measured in centuries. More precisely, an expression of the form (#$CenturiesDuration NUM) denotes the (\"point-value\") #$Time-Quantity of being exactly NUM centuries in duration, and an expression of the form (#$CenturiesDuration MIN MAX) denotes the (properly interval-like) #$Time-Quantity of being at least MIN centuries and at most MAX centuries in duration.")
(comment Base-Support "The collection of bases of tangible objects, typically the bottommost surfaces that are in contact with the ground or the floor.")
(comment Late20thCenturyPerson "Persons living during the latter half of the 20th century.")
(comment ReallyDirty "#$ReallyDirty")
(comment ST5000MeterSpeedSkateSportsEvent "The short track 5000M speed skating competition")
(comment PassiveSalesActivity "Sales activities in which the performer interacts with a class of potential customers and waits to be contacted by the actual customers (e.g., advertising; contrast with #$ActiveSalesActivity).")
(comment PhysicalPartOfObject "The collection of things that are best thought of as parts of other things, and about which we might have something useful to say.  Think of table legs, sleeves of garments, etc.  This is just to make it easier to search through all this part stuff when someone needs to do so.  None of us (#$Guha, Karen, Nick ...) are very happy with this collection ...")
(comment WomensHosiery "The collection of all stockings")
(comment ImageMicrotheory "A collection of microtheories; a subset of #$VisualRepresentationMicrotheory.  Each element of #$ImageMicrotheory is a context in which to state the propositional content of a particular two-dimensional visual image.  That includes both still images and moving pictures.  Images which are approximately two-dimensional (such as friezes) may also be described with an image microtheory.")
(comment MailingLocation "A specialization of #$ContactLocation.  Each instance of #$MailingLocation is a location at which an agent can be contacted by mail.")
(comment RequestingMoney "The performer is requesting that money be transferred to their possession")
(disjointWith ChainOrganization IndependentOrganization)
(comment TurnTakingSportsEvent "A sports event in which only one competitor competes at a time, with no overlap.")
(comment NewPrescriptionSales "instances are groups of sales of new prescriptions, in some region over some time.  Given the same region and time, an instance of #$NewPrescriptionSales will be included in an instance of #$TotalPrescriptionSales. ")
(comment promiseStatement "A specSlot of #$ist such that entries were explicitly communicated in the form of a promise.")
(comment interArgFormat3-5 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat3-5 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the fifth argument-place of PRED when PRED's third argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ... ARGN) in which ARG3 is an instance of COL, 
PRED's arg5 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG5' in 
the preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its 
instances for further explanation.")
(comment SlightPhysicalBuild "An attribute for describing an animal with an intrinsically slight, `small-boned' physical build.  Orthogonal to height, and to whether or not the animal happens to be fat (overweight).")
(comment AssociateInScienceDegree "An associate in science degree is normally issued after passing two years of college-level science classes at an accredited college which issues such degrees.")
(disjointWith UnitOfMonetaryRate UnitOfAngularAcceleration)
(comment CollegeFraternalGreekOrganization "College Frats and Sororities")
(comment Puree "Food which has been put through a blender for a while")
(comment NuclearEvent "A nuclear event")
(comment dislikesSensorially "(#$dislikesSensorially AGT SENSUM) means that the #$PerceptualAgent AGT feels some physical discomfort from the sensory experience of SENSUM (a taste, an odor, a particular level of pain, etc. --- see #$SensoryAttribute).
Note: this is a stronger statement than (#$not (#$likesSensorially AGT SENSUM)), as there may be many #$SensoryAttributes which one neither particularly likes nor dislikes.")
(comment mtImageForeground "ARG2 is the foreground region of the image space described by assertions made in ARG1.")
(comment GuestServiceRep "employee of #$Guest Services dept who deals with unhappy guests")
(comment TimeOfDay-4AM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 4AM.")
(comment EarNoseAndThroatCareEvent "The treatment or prevention of ear, nose and throat problems.")
(comment WinningAGamePortion "Winning one portion of a game that is divided up into smaller games, bouts, or sets. For example, winning a set of tennis or a bout in fencing.")
(comment PointingAFinger "The set of actions in which the performer points an index finger at someone or something s/he finds remarkable or objectionable.")
(comment ComputerInterfaceConvention "the collection of computer interfaces")
(comment WomensSportsCompetition "Sports competitions where the participants are limited to female persons.  The competitors may be organizations in the case of team competition, but the players must be female persons.")
(comment Hundreds-Quant "The quantity range of hundreds of something.")
(comment Artist-Visual "A specialization of #$Artist. Each instance of this collection is a person who creates #$ArtObjects which are appreciated by looking at them (e.g. sculpture, paintings and so forth).")
(comment ComputerBulletinBoard "An electronic forum which contains ongoing discussions about a particular topic.  It consists of postings made by subscribers to the board about the topic.")
(comment Buffer "A  temporary store of things,  often used to smooth out differences in flow of inputs and flow of outputs.")
(comment SocialAidOrganization "A collection of organizations.  Instances of SocialAidOrganization are groups whose main goal is to provide aid to those in need.  For a group to be an instance of this collection it must provide a tangible benefit to those it aims to serve, whether by directly providing goods and/or services to those in need or by assisting other organizations in such endeavors.  Examples include #$InternationalRedCrossAndRedCrescentMovement, #$SaveTheChildren, #$DoctorsWithoutBorders. Note that social welfare departments that supply government-subsidized aid are classified not under this constant but in #$HumanServicesOrganization.")
(comment MicroSecondsDuration "A #$UnitOfTime function that takes one or two real numbers as arguments and returns, as its value, a comparable #$Time-Quantity attribute measured in microseconds. More precisely, an expression of the form (#$MicroSecondsDuration NUM) denotes the (\"point-value\") #$Time-Quantity of being exactly NUM microseconds in duration, and an expression of the form (#$MicroSecondsDuration MIN MAX) denotes the (properly interval-like) #$Time-Quantity of being at least MIN microseconds and at most MAX microseconds in duration.")
(comment hasIDOfType "arg1 has an authorized agreement of type arg2 that has id agr3 (e.g., (#$hasIDOfType Fred #$DriverLicense 15142515)).")
(comment endsRelativeToEndOf " (#$endsRelativeToEndOf e1 d e2) means that the e1 ended d units of time after e2 ended")
(comment HeavyweightGRWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of GRWrestlingSportsEvent")
(disjointWith EmittingAnObject Sliding-Generic)
(comment Siren "A device which is used to make loud warning sounds (non-verbal), such as an air-raid siren or an ambulance siren.")
(comment Underwear "The collection of all undergarments")
(comment packagingOfType "For a type of pharmacy product package, gives the type and size of package it is in.")
(comment covering "A #$TaxonomicSlot that relates a #$SetOrCollection (q.v.)  to a #$SetOrCollectionType (q.v.) that \"covers\" it, i.e. the union of all of the latter's elements (which are themselves sets or collections) includes all of the former's elements.  (#$covering SETORCOL COVER) means that COVER is a covering of SETORCOL: the elements of COVER are themselves mathematical sets or collections, and every element of SETORCOL is an element of at least one of the elements of COVER.  For example, the Linnaean taxonomy of types of living things (Dog, Mammal, Chordate, Fungus, etc.) is a covering of the set of all animals alive today, as every animal alive today is a member of one or more of the Linnaean categories.  Note that COVER may contain \"extra\" elements that are not members of SETORCOL.  For example, the union of all the Linnaean categories (see #$OrganismClassificationType) is actually much larger than the set of animals alive today, encompassing as it does plants, extinct animal species, etc.  In order to express an assertion about covering, one need not create a new constant from scratch to play the role of COVER if such a constant doesn't already exist.  Instead, using the function #$TheCovering (q.v.), one can specify a covering by enumerating its elements.  (#$TheCovering is a special #$ReifiableFunction whose principal reason-for-being is to facilitate the inference heuristics associated with assertions about covering.)")
(comment InitiationCeremony "The collection of events in which someone is admitted into some group, organization, or social status.")
(comment DivorceDecreeDocument "A divorce decree - the document, not the event.")
(comment OlympicTorch-Large "The large torch they light at the Olympics.")
(comment AsynchronousSportsEvent "A sports event in which competitors do not start competing at the same time, although their efforts may overlap.")
(comment Prescriber "An instance of #$PersonTypeByActivity, and a specialization of #$MedicalCareProfessional.  Each instance of #$Prescriber is a person who can prescribe medication. Instances include doctors, as well as non-physician prescribers.")
(comment offerStatement "A specSlot of #$ist such that entries were explicitly communicated in the form of a offer.")
(comment JointVentureActivity "A collection of events.  Each instance of #$JointVentureActivity is a business activity in which two or more independent companies cooperate to work on a business project mutually beneficial to all.  During the venture, each participant is a partner to the others (see #$businessPartners).  Joint ventures are always governed by at least one explicit #$Agreement.")
(comment VisualPerception "A specialization of #$Perceiving.  Each instance of   #$VisualPerception is an event in which an agent (an instance of #$PerceptualAgent (q.v.)) sees something by means of an #$ElectroMagneticRadiationSensor (usually, the agent's own #$Eyes) detecting wavelengths of visible light.")
(comment ProblemSolvingCntxt "A specialization of #$Microtheory.
#$ProblemSolvingCntxts are microtheories that are used to reason about 
particular situations.  Queries posed in #$ProblemSolvingCntxts are
expected to draw -- via the #$genlMt relation -- on a large number
of other microtheories.  A #$ProblemSolvingCntxt is usually created 
for temporary use with a problem at hand, and is discarded after the 
problem is dealt with.  In contrast, a #$GeneralMicrotheory (q.v.), e.g., 
is created for lasting use.  Specializations of #$ProblemSolvingCntxt 
include #$ParsingContext and #$ScenarioTestingMicrotheory.")
(comment BachelorOfFineArtsDegree "A bachelor of fine arts degree is normally issued after passing four to five years of appropriate fine arts classes (such as painting) at an accredited university.")
(disjointWith UnitOfFlowRate UnitOfAngularAcceleration)
(comment InternationalSportsCompetition "International sports competitions, including the Olympics, Wimbledon, World Figure Skating competitions, etc.")
(comment MusicalCommunicatingFromPerformerToListener "The communication of a musical idea from a performer to a listener.")
(comment UnitOfAngularAcceleration "The collection of functions which return elements of #$AngularAccelerationRate (i.e., the rate of change in the #$RateOfRotation).")
(comment LogicalTableSchema "Instances represent the propositions that define the schema (not the actual content) of a database table, or other information sources that can be considered as abstract tables.  They are often referred to as 'logical tables'. The axioms for interpreting a database table are expressed as assertions involving instances of #$LogicalField, which serve as prototypes for the values in the fields of the table.  The actual content of a database table, to the extent that this content is ever imported into the Cyc KB, is represented in some instance of #$LogicalTable.")
(comment mtImageYear "ARG2 is the calendar year of the images described by assertions in the mt ARG1.")
(comment TimeOfDay-2AM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 2AM.")
(comment OsteopathicCareEvent "The osteopathic treatment or prevention of disease.")
(comment Memory "A specialization of #$MentalInformation.  Each instance of #$Memory is the propositional content of a mental state in which a person recalls past events.  Most commonly those memories concern first-person experiences, but they may include recollections of anything that the person has learned in the past.")
(comment Turning "The act of changing the direction of movement or orientation.")
(comment SportsFormalCompetition "A #$SportsFormalCompetition is something like the 1992 Olympic 100M Sprint. Individual races or games (like the finals) are #$SportsEvent and not #$SportsFormalCompetition. Also, there are prizes, officiating bodies, etc., unlike a #$SportsEvent.  You can be first in a #$SportsEvent but you can win a gold only in a #$SportsFormalCompetition.")
(comment MediaProfessional "A collection of persons; a subset of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each element of #$MediaProfessional is a person whose job is gathering, organizing, or disseminating information or entertainment for distribution through TV, radio, or newspaper.  This collection includes journalists, sports announcers, news anchors, weathercasters, and all technical support staff such as camera operators, editors, etc.")
(comment HumanCyclist "A specialization of #$Cyclist and #$Person.  Each instance of  #$HumanCyclist is a person who is entitled to inspect and modify the Cyc knowledge base.")
(comment programsIn "A binary predicate relating instances of #$ComputerProgrammer to instances of #$ComputerLanguage. (#$programsIn PROG LANG) means that #$ComputerLanguage LANG is a programming language understood and used by #$ComputerProgrammer PROG. PROG is typically an instance of #$Person but need not be (see the comment on #$ComputerUser, which #$ComputerProgrammer is a specialization of).")
(comment Dr "The prefix ``Dr.'' that may attach to a person's name.")
(comment InvestmentOrganization "An organization who trades commodities on stock exchanges for profit.")
(comment FrontWall "The collection of front walls of objects")
(comment TechUserOfAnimalPoweredDevices "Members are persons who use animal-powered devices in everyday tasks.  Implies the use of handcrafted devices.")
(comment ALittleDirty "#$ALittleDirty")
(comment RespiratoryAilment "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$RespiratoryAilment is a state of sickness that impacts the respiratory system more severely than it impacts any other system.  This collection includes chronic diseases such as #$Emphysema and (#$CancerFn #$Lung), as well as #$CommonCold.")
(comment LightHeavyweightGRWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of GRWrestlingSportsEvent")
(comment hasAttachedIBO "This refers to an #$InformationBearingObject physically attached to something.  Can be anything from a clothing label to a traffic sign on a highway (assuming the sign is attached to the roadside), but does have markings, either diagrams or words, imparting info.")
(comment Diaper "The collection of diapers, a loose-fitting undergarment, typically fastened with safety pins and worn by babies")
(comment HangingClothes "Hanging clothes, typically using a hanger, a clothespin, or a coat-hook.")
(comment usesMapping "(#$usesMapping P-FIELD MAP) indicates that the physical field P-FIELD should be interpreted with the set of mappings MAP.")
(comment RequestingPayment "The performer is requesting money in payment (e.g., for merchandise or services).")
(comment ruleSystemUsed "This slot specifies the systems of rules that are used to judge/control/monitor this action")
(disjointWith Perceiving DirectedTranslation)
(comment TotalPrescriptionSales "instances are groups of sales of all prescriptions, in some region over some time. Includes both refills and new prescriptions.")
(comment queryStatement "A specSlot of #$ist such that entries were explicitly communicated in the form of a query.")
(comment interArgFormat2-5 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat2-5 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the fifth argument-place of PRED when PRED's second argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ... ARGN) in which ARG2 is an instance of COL, 
PRED's arg5 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG5' in 
the preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its 
instances for further explanation.")
(comment BusinessRelationshipActivity "A specialization of #$BusinessEvent.  Each instance of #$BusinessRelationshipActivity is a (usually long-term, and often complex) social activity whose participants are in some type of business relationship.  An instance of #$BusinessRelationshipActivity is typically carried out over multiple social occasions, and may consist of many sub-events. The social events constituting an instance of #$BusinessRelationshipActivity further, either directly or indirectly, the (usually mutual) business interests of the participants.")
(disjointWith Water Oil)
(comment Doctor-MD "A collection of persons; a subset of #$Doctor-Medical. Each element of #$Doctor-MD is a doctor who has completed the education and training required to be awarded an M.D. degree. Cf. #$Doctor-Osteopathic.")
(disjointWith UnitOfAngularSpeed UnitOfAcceleration)
(comment SimpleRepairing "The collection of events in which something gets fixed.")
(comment Dieting "This is the purposeful directing of one's food intake for a particular purpose, not necessarily weight loss.  Dieting could include eating in order to reduce salt intake, or increase muscle, not necessarily to reduce calories or fat.")
(comment MusicalCommunicatingFromComposerToListener "The communication of a musical idea from a composer to a listener.")
(comment MicroPhysicalEvent "Every #$MicroPhysicalEvent involves some types of forces acting on some objects, changing their position, velocity, exchanging energy with each other, etc.")
(comment marketingRepresentatives "Entries are the persons who perform the marketing for the organization")
(comment RetirementEvent "The actual event of retiring from work.")
(comment TimeOfDay-6AM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 6AM.")
(comment EyeCareEvent "The treatment or prevention of eye problems.")
(comment TennisSet "The collection of tennis sets. The first player to win six games wins the set, unless each player has won five sets, in which case play continues until one side is two games ahead.")
(comment MakingAVictoryGesture "The set of actions in which a person raises two fingers (index and middle) to form a ''V,'' signifying victory.")
(comment interviewForJobType "The job interview ARG1 is to find a candidate to perform a job of type ARG2.")
(comment Dozens-Quant "The fuzzy quantity of dozens of something")
(comment Engineer "A specialization of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each instance of #$Engineer is a professional who works in some branch of engineering (see the constant #$EngineeringField).  Notable specializations of #$Engineer include #$ElectricalEngineer, #$ChemicalEngineer, #$CivilEngineer, and #$MechanicalEngineer.")
(comment programDomain "A predicate which relates a given #$ComputerProgram-CW to the set of things that the variables in the program denote, or to what the input and output is.  So for #$MSWord, this would be documents, for a web-page editor it would be web-pages, etc.")
(comment firstName "An instance of #$ProperNamePredicate-Strict and a specialization of
#$nameString.  (#$firstName AGENT NAMESTRING) means that AGENT is 
known by NAMESTRING as his or her first name.  Note that a person 
rarely has more than one first name, though s/he may have one or 
more nicknames that acquaintances use interchangeably with, or 
instead of, her/his actual first name.  For example, a person whose 
first name is `Robert' might have the nicknames `Bob' and `Bobby'.  
See #$nicknames and #$commonNickname.")
(comment MutualInsuranceAssociation "The collection of all #$InsuranceProviders which operate as insurance cooperatives.  The members of an instance of #$MutualInsuranceAssociation contribute an amount of money to the association; the sum of all those funds, and the interest that accrues on those funds, form the pool of funds from which insurance claims made by the members are paid.")
(comment HostileSocialAction "A specialization of both #$PurposefulAction and #$SocialOccurrence.  Each instance of #$HostileSocialAction is a hostile or pugnacious event, adverse to some agent(s), in which multiple agents, at least one of whom is acting deliberately, take part.  Specializations of this collection include #$PhysicallyAttackingAnAgent and #$PoliticalDispute.")
(comment minimalCrossSection "The minimal cross section of an object")
(comment SouthernStyleCuisine "Southern US style food")
(comment Swim-200MeterBackstroke "Swimming race - 200 meter backstroke.")
(comment MaintainingSomething "The collection of events in which an object is maintained (maintenance is performed on an object).  This is more specific than #$TakingCareOfSomething.  Our intuition is that an object being `maintained' is somehow being kept in a steady state (of repair, condition, etc.).")
(comment Bra "The collection of bras.")
(comment pptOfPackage "For a type of pharmacy product package, gives the kind of pharmacy product contained. ")
(comment Mob "A specialization of #$Group.  Each instance of #$Mob is a group that contains a large number of objects or events of the same type.  Mobs typically have more members than would be feasible to enumerate or reify.  One rarely refers to particular members of a given mob; and when one does, it is usually only to relatively few of them.  Examples: the #$Andes-Mountains is a mob of mountains; each instance of #$Galaxy is a mob of stars; a cupful of sand is a mob of grains of sand; and making popcorn involves a mob of corn kernel bursting events. See also #$MobFn.")
(comment NationalHeroCelebration "A celebration of a national hero, most commonly on his/her observed birthday.  May include parades, speeches, TV specials, etc.")
(comment TopWall "A collection of top walls, not the same as #$TopSurface which is the outer surface.")
(comment fieldDataFormat "(#$fieldDataFormat P-FIELD FORMAT) indicates that the data in the physical field P-FIELD has the data format FORMAT.")
(comment idStringOfType "ARG1 has ARG3 for its ARG2.  For example, Karen's computer has 'A3000' for its #$ModelNumber.")
(comment SkatingSportsEvent "The collection of ice skating events, including ice hockey, figure skating, and speed skating")
(comment GraduateProgram "The collection of courses of study which are intended (primarily) for students who have already completed an undergraduate degree.")
(comment MechanicalConnection "This is the parent unit for all the mecchanical connection units.")
(comment manyToOneReln "ARG1 is a group of things, and ARG2 is an #$Individual, such that there is a many-to-one relationship between ARG1 and ARG2.  The relationship is that the members of the group ARG1 are each the first arg in an assertion using the #$BinaryPredicate ARG3; in each of these assertions, ARG2 is the second argument.  See also #$oneToManyReln, #$everyToEveryReln.")
(disjointWith BiologicalProcess BusinessRelationshipActivity)
(comment DiningRoom "The room in a home or in a restaurant where people dine.  This doesn't include kitchens right now.")
(comment FormularyType "Instances are collections of formularies, grouped according to  how restrictive they are: with an open formulary, the formulary is just a  suggestion but the doctors can make their own decisions about what to  prescribe. A closed formulary is the most restrictive, and prescribing must adhere to it (or there are penalties -- the patient has to pay out of pocket, or...) Restricted is an intermediate type in which, under certain conditions, the doctor can prescribe off the formulary.")
(disjointWith UnitOfMonetaryRate UnitOfAcceleration)
(comment InfinitiveComp "The collection of all infinitive complementizers. In English, this is only the word 'to'. Infinitive complementizers introduce non-tensed clauses.")
(disjointWith InformationTransferEvent Dieting)
(comment MusicalCommunicatingFromComposerToPerformer "The communication of a musical idea from a composer to a performer.")
(comment angularAcceleration "The rate at which the angle to an object is accelerating")
(comment hasNegativeInterestIn "This is sort of a specialization of #$negativeVestedInterest.  The agent ARG1 has a negative vested interest in the value of the slot ARG3 on the thing ARG2.  For example, (#$hasNegativeInterestIn #$AmericanAirlines #$UnitedAirlines #$financialState) means that the corporate entity #$AmericanAirlines cares about (has a negative vested interest in) the financial health of #$UnitedAirlines.  But #$AmericanAirlines probably doesn't care what color United paints their planes, etc.")
(comment donors "see the inverse.")
(comment TimeOfDay-3AM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 3AM.")
(comment likesRoleInEventType "This predicate relates agents to the kinds of things they like to do.  (#$likesRoleInEventType AGENT ROLE EVENTTYPE) means that AGENT enjoys playing ROLE in events of the type EVENTTYPE.  This entails that AGENT actually _has_ played -- and enjoyed playing -- ROLE in one or more instances of EVENTTYPE, and that on most (if not all) such occasions she enjoyed herself.  Typically, AGENT  will have played ROLE in a number of instances of EVENTTYPE.  For example, (#$likesRoleInEventType Joe #$performedBy #$Running) means that Joe likes to run.  Cf. #$dislikesRoleInEventType.")
(comment Sr-NameSuffix "''Sr.'' is used as a suffix on a person's name to represent the first of two or moregenerations who use the same full name.  It is often used to distinguish two consecutive generations who use the same name. ")
(comment DroppingGameObject "Dropping a ball or baton -- the wand-like object passed from runner to runner during a relay race.")
(comment BlowingAKiss "The set of actions in which a person kisses his/her hand and blows on it, as if blowing the kiss toward the recipient(s); generally, something done by a performer in front of a crowd of fans.")
(comment Sermon "The speaking that a church leader does in front of the church members during a church service.")
(comment objectTendered "'A binary predicate which relates instances of #$ExchangeOfUserRights to instances of #$PartiallyTangible. '(#$objectTendered EXCHANGE OBJECT)' means that OBJECT is a #$PartiallyTangible offered in payment during the #$ExchangeOfUserRights EXCHANGE.  Just about any object may be offered in exchange for goods or services; for instance, a farmer offering a doctor a watermelon in exchange for medical treatment.  Of course, purely intangible objects cannot be exchanged; for instance, one cannot buy a car with the number pi or the Equator.  For a narrower interpretation of #$objectTendered in terms of conventional media of exchange, see #$FinancialTransactionMt.")
(comment lastName "An instance of #$ProperNamePredicate-Strict and a specialization of #$nameString.  (#$lastName AGENT NAMESTRING) means that AGENT is known by NAMESTRING as his or her last name.  Note that a person rarely has more than one last name at any one time.  Note also that last names may change as a result of certain actions, such as marriages, deaths, etc., in various cultures.  In Western cultures a #$lastName is generally a surname (see #$familyName), while in Eastern cultures a #$lastName is generally a given name (see #$givenNames).")
(disjointWith BeliefSystem Dream)
(comment SideWall "The collection of side walls of objects")
(comment TrackTeam "An organization of athletes that run track events, usually both in individual events and in relay events.")
(comment Weeding "Events in which a person pulls weeds from the ground.")
(comment TidinessLevel "Tidiness is a personality trait that corresponds to a person's desire for order.  Real slobs let entropy take over while very tidy people desire their surroundings to be well-ordered, clean, etc.")
(comment Swim-4By100MeterFreestyleRelay "Swimming race - 100 meter freestyle relay.")
(comment CalculatingSalesTaxOnAnItem "The event in which tax is mentally computed by multiplying the tax rate times the price of the item purchased.  This figure is used in computing total sales tax. (See #$CalculatingTotalSalesTaxAtCheckOut).")
(disjointWith Communicating MaintainingSomething)
(comment PatientMedicalRecord-Hardcopy "The file associated with each patient of a medical care provider containing the information pertinent to that patient's health and history, and the provider's care/recommendations given to that patient.")
(comment Slip "The collection of slips.")
(comment after "A #$PrimitiveTemporalPredicate that relates two points in time.  (#$after LATER EARLIER) means #$TimePoint LATER is after (occurs later in time than) #$TimePoint EARLIER.")
(comment Rightward-Directly "From the perspective of a specified observer, A is directly rightward of B if from the observer's perspective A is located further toward the positive end of the Cartesian x axis than is B, and A and B are in the same position on the Cartesian y axis.")
(comment CookingGrid "A framework of metal bars or wires for broiling.")
(comment NDCPlusCheckDigit "This is an eleven-digit unique identifier used by Glaxo. An NDC-plus-check-digit string consists of a ten-digit National Drug Code string, plus a final digit added by Glaxo for internal use.")
(comment CertifiedPublicAccountant "A collection of persons; a subset of #$Accountant.  Each element of #$CertifiedPublicAccountant is an accountant who has met the necessary requirements of education, experience, and examination to become a credentialed accountant.")
(comment ParksAndNatureManagementOrganization "The collection of all organizations, government or not, concerned with overseeing and managing parks, wildlife, nature, and the environment.  This would include organizations such as the #$SierraClub and the #$UnitedStatesForestService.")
(comment SynchronousSportsEvent "A sports event in which competitors start competing at the same time.")
(comment EmployeeHiring "A specialization of both #$MakingAnAgreement and #$OrganizationalTransferIn.  Each instance of #$EmployeeHiring is an event in which some agent -- either an organization or a person -- hires a person to work as its employee.  Note that a hiring event is viewed as occurring at the time the prospective employee accepts an offer of a job, rather than the (possibly later) time s/he first begins that job.  See also #$employees and #$WorkAgreement.")
(comment chosenFor "The thing ARG2 is chosen in the event ARG1, for the  expression ARG3 to hold.  It is possible that ARG3 never becomes  true, but it is the intent of the chooser(s)")
(comment oneToManyReln "ARG1 is an #$Individual, and ARG2 is a group of things, such that there is a one-to-many relationship between ARG1 and ARG2.  The relationship is that ARG1 is the first arg in a number of assertions using the #$BinaryPredicate ARG3; in each of these assertions, one of the members of the group ARG2 is the second argument.  See also #$everyToEveryReln and #$oneToOneReln.")
(comment interArgFormat1-4 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat1-4 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the fourth argument-place of PRED when PRED's first argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ... ARGN) in which ARG1 is an instance of COL, PRED's
arg4 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG4' in the 
preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its instances 
for further explanation.")
(disjointWith SingleDoerAction BusinessRelationshipActivity)
(comment Garage-Household "Garages in Modern Houses")
(disjointWith UnitOfFlowRate UnitOfAcceleration)
(comment Safeness "#$Safeness is the #$ScriptPerformanceAttributeType for describing actions in which the performer acts without endangering itself or others.")
(comment PossessivePronoun-Post "The collection of all possessive pronouns which occur as predicative complements. Example: 'mine', as in 'This book is mine'.")
(disjointWith Dieting MovementEvent)
(comment GenerationOrConversionEvent "A collection of events involving the generation or conversion of force, energy, or motion.")
(comment hasPositiveInterestIn "This is sort of a specialization of #$positiveVestedInterest.  The agent ARG1 has a positive vested interest in the value of the slot ARG3 on the thing ARG2.  For example, #$hasPositiveInterestIn(#$Guha GuhasBank #$financialState) means that #$Guha cares about (has a positive vested interest in) the financial health of his bank.  He probably doesn't care how old it is or what its name is.")
(comment Family-SingleParent "A human family consisting of a single parent or guardian and their children.")
(comment Receptionist "employees who take care of incoming and leaving clients, phone calls, etc.")
(comment TimeOfDay-5AM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 5AM.")
(comment II-NameSuffix "The numeral ''II'' is used as a suffix on a person's name to represent the second generation to use the same full name.  It is often used to distinguish two consecutive generations who use the same name.  ''II'' is more formal than ''Jr.'' .")
(comment WinningAVie "Gaining possession of the ball or puck when it's placed up for grabs by the ref. i.e., winning a face off in hockey, a jump ball in basketball, or a scrum in rugby.")
(comment PointingThumbsUp "The set of actions in which a performer points his/her thumb upward to signify approval, pride, or triumph.")
(comment MajorBuyingActivity " The  events that a buyer would consider major because they involve a major financial transaction .")
(disjointWith ElectricalDevice MusicalInstrument-Acoustic)
(comment Electrician "A person who works on electrical systems of buildings.")
(comment Mr "The prefix ``Mr.'' that may attach to a person's name.")
(disjointWith BeliefSystem SystemOfMeasure)
(comment AAAIConference "Conference held yearly, organized by the American Association for Artificial Intelligence.")
(comment AboutADaysDuration "Duration of 10 hours up to almost 2 days")
(comment SportsPistolShootingSportsEvent "A marksmanship sports event in which a sports pistol is used.")
(comment BillSubtotaling "The step in #$CheckingOutPurchases when the the price of all the items is added up.  Does not include tax computation.")
(disjointWith MaintainingSomething PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment PracticalNurse "A collection of persons.  Each element of #$PracticalNurse is a nurse who has completed the education (viz., a #$NursingDegree-LPN) and training required for certification as a Licensed Practical Nurse.")
(comment BowTie "The collection of bow ties, a type of clothing accessory attached under the shirt collar and worn at the front of the neck for decoration")
(comment StoveTop " The part of a #$CookingRange (cf) that has the burners and is used for frying & boiling in pots & pans. Often called 'Stove' in english..")
(comment CityCouncil "A collection of local government organizations.  An element of #$CityCouncil is a governing board which manages an element of #$City.  In democratic countries, the members of a city council are elected.  A city council may govern a city either directly, through a #$Mayor, or through a City Manager. ")
(comment PoetrySystem "A system of written materials that formulates a concentrated imaginative awareness of experience in language chosen and arranged to create a specific emotional response through meaning, sound, and rhythm.")
(comment oneToOneReln "ARG1 is a group of things, and ARG2 is a group of things, such that there is a one-to-one relationship between ARG1 and ARG2.  The relationship is that each of the things in the group ARG1 is the first arg to the #$BinaryPredicate ARG3 where exactly one of the members of the group ARG2 is the second argument.  The groups ARG1 and ARG2 must have the same number of members.  See also #$oneToManyReln and #$everyToEveryReln.")
(comment PatentFiling "The action of submitting a formal request to a patenting agency that the submitter be recognized as the owner to rights to produce tangibles meeting the specification included in the request.")
(comment Stairwell "A vertical shaft or opening with entrances on each (or most) levels that contains a stairway.")
(comment Surgery "A specialization of #$MedicalCareEvent.  Each instance of #$Surgery is a medical care event in which a medical professional cuts a part of a living body, either to examine what's inside (a diagnostic, exploratory surgery) or to treat an ailment (an instance of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent).  Instances of #$Surgery which are also instances of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent include: removal of some object - such as a cancer or an organ that's causing trouble - from the body; insertion of a medical device (e.g, a pacemaker) into the body; repair of some internal structure.")
(disjointWith UnitOfMonetaryRate UnitOfAngularSpeed)
(disjointWith KineticEnergyPoweredDevice SelfPoweredDevice)
(comment AgentDenotingFieldAttribute "Fields attributes that, when used as the ARG2 to #$SchemaLF, result in #$LogicalField s that denote people, organizations and other agents.")
(comment EmployeeLayoff "Actions in which a person's job ends due to the employer no longer affording to pay the person's salary or wages.")
(comment occupants "This predicate relates a building or other structure intended for human occupation to a being that is presently inside it.  (#$occupants CONSTRUCT OCCUPANT) means that OCCUPANT is in CONSTRUCT.  See also #$residesInDwelling.")
(comment ConstrainingEvent "Constrainment events involve the constrainment (blocking, containing, guiding, etc.) of one body (solid or fluid) by another.")
(comment easierThan "#$easierThan(AGENT Y_ACTIONS Z_ACTIONS) means that it is (mentally, physically) easier for AGENT to perform an action of type Y_ACTIONS than to perform an action of type Z_ACTIONS.  This is different from moreConvenientThan.  In performing any event, there are often other things that need to be done - getting the tools, cleaning up the place, travelling.... Convenience seems to be a measure of the ease of these other subsidiary actions.  The concept of ease is more general and applies to the whole event. So, for most people, eating spaghetti is easier than solving quadratics, but solving quadratics might be more convenient (if you are given a piece of paper and a pencil, but have to go buy the spaghetti, etc.).")
(disjointWith Family-Nuclear Family-SingleParent)
(comment Psychologist "A scientist knowledgeable in Psychology, its theory, uses and applications.")
(comment SpaceShuttleControlWorkStation "The area in which an astronaut who is flying a space shuttle works. Especially includes the control panel.")
(comment III-NameSuffix "The numeral ''III'' is used as a suffix on a person's name to represent the third generation to use the same full name.")
(comment News "A specialization of #$PropositionalInformationThing.  Each instance of #$News consists of some factual information about recent events in the world (or #$geographicalSubRegions thereof).  News is commonly embodied in newspapers and communicated through radio and television news broadcasts. Note that #$News does not include as instances any instance of #$NewsArticle (q.v.). Rather, an instance of #$News might be the content of a #$NewsArticle, and could be the content of distinct #$NewsArticles")
(comment OvertakingACompetitor "In a race, passing another racer. More generally, switching places in the competition hierarchy such that the change indicates a better score for you and a worse one for the competitor.")
(comment CollapsingLegs "The collection of events in which a performer loses control of his/her leg muscles while in a standing posture and abruptly falls unless supported by arms or by others.")
(comment YachtingSportsEvent "The collection of all sailing competitions")
(comment EnlistedPerson "A specialization of #$MilitaryPerson. Each instance of #$EnlistedPerson is a person in some branch of the military who holds a rank below that of a commissioned officer (see the collection #$CommissionedOfficer).")
(comment Miss "The prefix ``Miss'' that may attach to a person's name.")
(comment GeneralPartner "The collection of all #$PartnershipPartners that are general partners of #$Partnerships.  Instances of #$GeneralPartner are jointly and severally liable for the debts and other liabilities of the #$Partnership.")
(comment costPerPackage "Packages of objects of type ARG1 contain ARG2 individuals and cost ARG3 (amount of money).")
(comment Exercising "The collection of events in which humans move their bodies for the purpose of general physical conditioning and/or strengthening muscles.")
(comment Swim-800MeterFreestyle "Swimming race - 800 meter freestyle.")
(comment ShippingLocation "A specialization of #$MailingLocation.  Each instance of #$ShippingLocation is a location to which merchandise can be physically delivered, e.g., a house, an office, a corporate mailroom, a post office box.")
(comment Movement-Periodic "A specialization of #$MovementEvent.  Each instance of #$Movement-Periodic is a movement event in which the moving object (see the predicate #$objectMoving) returns repeatedly to a certain location or orientation at more or less regular time intervals.  Examples of #$Movement-Periodic include the motion of a seesaw one afternoon, the dribbling of a basketball in place by Magic Johnson, and the motion of a slinky going down a staircase as it periodically changes its orientation through a fixed, repetive series of orientations.")
(comment CalculatingTotalSalesTaxAtCheckOut "The event that occurs after the sub total for purchases being checked out has occurred.  Total sales tax is the sum of the tax on all items purchased.")
(disjointWith DecompositionProcess MaintainingSomething)
(comment Perinatologist "The collection of doctors (#$Doctor-Medical) who specialize in the area of medicine concerned with the care of the fetus and newborn, and the study of diseases of infancy and of sudden infant death syndrome.")
(comment Glove "The collection of gloves, a kind of paired clothing accessory worn on the hands for decoration and/or to protect the hands from damage due to harsh environmental conditions")
(comment dosageFormOfType "For a type of pharmacy product, gives the form it is usually in when it is administered.")
(comment lastEventOfType "(#$lastEventOfType EVENT EVENTTYPE ROLE ACTOR BEFORE) means that EVENT was the last time ACTOR filled the actor slot ROLE in an instance of event type EVENTTYPE. (Prior to BEFORE.) For example : 'The last time Liz sneezed was at 9 a.m.' (#$lastEventOfType LizSneezingAt9am Sneezing #$bodilyDoer Liz #$Now). Also, 'Before the 1992 summer Olympics, the last time a Bulgarian won an Olympic gold medal was in 1980.' (#$lastEventOfType OlympicEvent1980 #$OlympicCompetition winner #$Bulgaria SummerOlympicsOfTheYear1992).")
(comment PerformanceReview "The collection of events in which an agent evaluates another agent's performance at a job or task (or series of tasks).")
(comment PointOfServicePlan "The collection of all plans where the insured person  has the option of getting medical care from a provider other  than those contracted by the plan (at a higher co-pay amount).")
(comment interArgFormat2-3 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat2-3 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the third argument-place of PRED when PRED's second argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ... ARGN) in which ARG2 is an instance of COL, PRED's arg3
position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG3' in the 
preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its instances 
for further explanation.")
(comment CustomerServicePeriod "A business activity in which a service provider agrees to provide service to the customer for some period of time, under certain conditions.  Such activities can be sold as products or included with an item sold, and are always governed by some #$ServiceContractDocument.")
(comment BarRegionInARoom "the area in a room which has a bar, alcohol, glasses, etc, where drinks are prepared.")
(comment Presentation "A lot like lecturing except the audience members may be skeptical and are more likely to be peers of the speaker rather than students.  Also the topic is likely to be business or technically related.")
(comment UnitOfTime "A collection of functions and an instance of #$UnitOfMeasureTypeByTypeMeasured. Each function in this collection is used to denote instances of #$Time-Quantity. For example, (#$YearsDuration 100) returns a time period equal to a century, (#$MilliSecondsDuration 24) returns 24 thousandths of a second.")
(disjointWith Surgery PreparingFoodOrDrink)
(disjointWith UnitOfFlowRate UnitOfAngularSpeed)
(disjointWith Device-UserPowered SolarPoweredDevice)
(comment WHAdverb "The collection of all wh-words which can act as adverbs. Example: 'when'.")
(comment Undressing "When you take your clothes off.  See also subevent #$TakingOffAClothingItem.")
(comment reverseEvent "(#$reverseEvent X Y) means that Y is the event that reverses the changes that occurred during X.  Therefore Y must happen after X.")
(comment LexicalWord "A subcollection of #$LexicalItem.  #$LexicalWord is the collection of all natural language words.  A lexical word is a \"free\" morpheme: it can appear in a phrase without being \"bound to\" (i.e. concatenated with) another lexical item.  (Cf. #$LexicalAffix.)  Note that different inflectional forms of a given word do not constitute distinct lexical words.  Instances of #$LexicalWord include #$Aluminum-TheWord, #$Confetti-TheWord, #$To-TheWord, #$Hang-Glide-MWW.")
(comment mtImageSeason "ARG2 is the season of year type of the images described by assertions in the mt ARG1.")
(comment LevelOfRenown "Level of awareness about something.  Higher values indicate knowing more and more about various aspects of it.")
(comment CognitivePsychologist "A scientist knowledgeable in Cognitive Psychology, its theory, uses and applications.")
(comment DeliCounterWorker "Collection of people who work in a deli")
(comment dislikesRoleInEventType "This predicate relates agents to the kinds of things they dislike doing.  (#$dislikesRoleInEventType AGENT ROLE EVENTTYPE) means that AGENT dislikes playing ROLE in events of the type EVENTTYPE.  This entails that AGENT actually _has_ played -- and disliked playing -- ROLE in one or more instances of EVENTTYPE, and that s/he found most (if not all) such occasions unpleasant.  Typically, AGENT  will have played ROLE in a number of instances of EVENTTYPE.  For example, (#$dislikesRoleInEventType Joe #$performedBy #$Running) means that Joe dislikes running.  Cf. #$likesRoleInEventType.")
(comment ParryingAThrust "Deflecting a thrust made by an opponent in, e.g. fencing.")
(comment BodySuit "The collection of bodysuits, including #$JumpSuits, #$WeightLiftingSuits, and the clothing worn by skiers and divers, etc.")
(comment SwimmingRaceEvent "Swimming races (not syncronized swimming or water polo).")
(comment TopographicMap "The collection of all maps of geographical regions which show the contours and elevations (usually above sea level) of depicted features")
(comment Dentist "A specialization of #$MedicalCareProfessional.  Each instance of #$Dentist is a medical care professional who has been trained to diagnose and treat diseases of, and injuries to, the gums and teeth.")
(comment LimitedPartner "The collection of all limited partners in an instance of #$LimitedPartnership.  Instances of #$LimitedPartner are not jointly and severally liable for the debts and other liabilities of the #$LimitedPartnership -  rather, their liability is limited as set forth in the applicable limited partnership agreement.")
(comment File-FolderOfPapers "The collection of files. A file consists of one or more sheets of writing paper contained in a file folder")
(comment GeographicDirectionFunction "Functions which map from a geographic region to another geographic region which is a subregion of the first and whose location is indicated by the direction.")
(comment ShootingAGun "The collection of all instances of #$ShootingAProjectileWeapon in which the #$deviceUsed is an instance of #$Gun.")
(comment BoardsailingSportsEvent "A class of YachtingSportsEvent")
(comment estimateFor "U is a cost Estimate for the transaction V.  This should reflect the actual amount of money paid in the transaction.")
(comment OrthopedicSurgeon "OrthopaedicSurgeons deal with surgical treatment for fractures, bone grafting, joint and limb replacement, and the fitting of braces or other appliances.")
(comment Camisole "The collection of camisoles -- a women's undergarment similar to a loose-fitting sleeveless t-shirt")
(comment strengthOfType "For a type of pharmacy product, gives the strength of the product.  The strength may be how concentrated the product is or may be the size of a dose in mass, volume, or some other measurement.")
(comment TimesFn "A #$VariableArityRelation that represents multiplication in #$CycL. (#$TimesFn MULT1 MULT2 ...) yields a quantity which is the result of multiplying MULT1 MULT2 (...) together. All arguments to #$TimesFn must be instances of #$ScalarInterval, as is its result. Thus (#$TimesFn 2 3 4) returns 24; (#$TimesFn #$Pi-Number #$E-LogarithmBase) returns pi times e. For division see #$QuotientFn.")
(comment DentistsOffice "A local (one site) organization that provides dental care to patients/customers for a fee.")
(comment Run-100Meter "The collection of 100 meter dashes.")
(comment MakingConstructionArtifact "A collection of events.  In each #$MakingConstructionArtifact event, some instance of #$ConstructionArtifact (bridges, houses, stadiums, airports, fences, etc.) is created.")
(comment Reservation "An agreement between a person or group of people and a restaurant hotel etc. to have a table, room, etc ready for the person(s) use at a specific time.")
(comment SystemOfWrittenMaterials "The basic divisions that comprise all written materials. These can't be strictly defined by any 'test', but are subjectively sensed - e.g. what connotates poetry is undefinable, yet poetry is distinguishable from prose.  This is the manifestation of a way written material is communicated; SystemsOfWrittenMaterials is the highest level of several substrata, determining if something is drama, prose, poetry, etc.")
(comment RequestingToMakeASale "Communicating, in some medium, a request to sell goods or services; specifies which items the potential buyer is interested in purchasing. This implies an obligation on the part of the performer/requestor to participate in the buying as specified by the (possibly implicit) terms of the request if these terms are accepted by the recipient of the request (ergo this is a kind of offering).")
(comment Urea "A chemical compound that is one of the constituents of urine.  It can be synthesized from ammonia and carbon dioxide.  Urea is used in many products, including fertilizer and beauty products.")
(comment particleConcentrationPerVol "the piece of space, arg1, has a number of particles present of type arg2, at a concentration arg3.")
(disjointWith SociabilityBasedAction Surgery)
(disjointWith UnitOfMonetaryRate UnitOfFlowRate)
(comment MicrotheoryType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$MicrotheoryType is a specialization of #$Microtheory.  Instances of #$MicrotheoryType include the collections #$HypotheticalContext and #$GeneralMicrotheory.")
(comment PostQuant-SP "The collection of all quantifiers which can appear post-nominally. Example: 'all'.")
(comment mealComponents "The parts of this meal - includes foods and beverages that make it up.")
(comment hasRepeatedEvents "ARG1 contains a mob of instances of ARG2 as repeated #$subEvents occurring in sequence.  None of them temporally overlap.")
(comment NonlexicalLinguisticObject "The collection of linguistic objects which are not morphemes, but which nonetheless make up part of a language system; e.g., the parts of speech.")
(disjointWith Motion-SolidAgainstSolid Flying)
(comment CommercialPassengerAirplane "The collection of all commercially owned or operated airplanes designed or used to carry passengers.")
(comment TwiceMonthly "Used to indicate that something happens regularly twice a month")
(comment infoRemoved "(#$infoRemoved CHANGE INFO) means that in the #$InformationUpdating action, CHANGE, INFO was removed from the IBO (#$InformationBearingObject) acted on.")
(comment correspondingSlot "The predicate #$correspondingSlot relates two types of Cyc constants.  (#$correspondingSlot ROLE PRED) means that the #$RoleReferentTheTerm ROLE corresponds to the #$Predicate PRED.  Examples: (#$correspondingSlot #$TheDeviceRole #$deviceUsed); (#$correspondingSlot #$TheBodyPartUsed #$actorPartsInvolved).")
(comment ObtainingUpperPosition "In wrestling, moving from the underneath position to the uppermost position. Gaining control.")
(comment PentathlonSportsEvent "The collection of pentathlon events.")
(comment BathymetricMap "The collection of all maps of bodies of water which show the depth of the body at various locations")
(disjointWith Dentist DentalHygienist)
(comment Ms "The prefix ``Ms.'' that may attach to a person's name.")
(disjointWith GeographicDirectionFunction MathematicalFunctionOnScalars)
(comment CompetitionEventTypeFn "#$CompetitionEventTypeFn takes as argument any spec of #$Event and returns the collection of all such events which are also instances of #$Competition.  For example, (#$CompetitionEventTypeFn #$Bodybuilding) returns the collection of all bodybuilding competitions.")
(comment Yachting470SportsEvent "A class of YachtingSportsEvent")
(comment nieces "Entries are U's nieces")
(comment CommissionAgreement "A #$CommissionAgreement is an agreement that specifies payments to one party if they serve as a #$sellingAgent or #$buyingAgent in certain Buying events where the other party is the seller")
(comment ThoracicSurgeon "ThoracicSurgeons are concerned with the area of the throrax.  In mammals that is the area between the neck and the abdomen.")
(comment Apron "The collection of all aprons, an item typically worn to protect the front of the body while working in the kitchen")
(comment MammographyProvider "The collection of all #$Organizations that perform mammographies, i.e., x-rays on female patients that may detect breast cancer.")
(comment apparentlyBetween "From the perspective of ARG1, ARG2 is apparently between (colinear with) ARG3 and ARG4.")
(comment StreetAddress "A specialization of #$ContactInfoString. Each instance of #$StreetAddress is a string (an instance of #$CharacterString (q.v.)) that includes a street number and street name.  For example: `3721 Executive Center Drive', the street address of #$Cycorp.  Each #$ShippingAddress (q.v.) includes a street address as a substring.")
(comment DoctorsOffice "Local (one site) organizations composed of one or more physicians and support personnel that provide (usually routine to only moderately serious) medical care to patients/clients for a fee.")
(comment SocialGathering "A specialization of #$SocialOccurrence.  Each instance of #$SocialGathering is an intentional social gathering of people who have the same or similar purposes in attending, and in which there is communication between the participants.  Specializations include #$BabyShower, #$Carnival, and #$Rally.  Note that a group of people waiting to board an elevator is not typically a #$SocialGathering, even though they share a common purpose, since they are not expected to talk to each other.")
(comment UnemployedPerson "A collection of persons.  Each instance of #$UnemployedPerson is a worker who is unemployed.  An unemployed worker is someone who either has worked previously and could still do so (if s/he had a job), or someone who is qualified to work (e.g., a recent graduate) but has not yet worked.")
(comment WritingTechniqueUsedInWrittenMaterials "These are the techniques used in written materials that make them more effective.  This encompasses the techniques of prose writers, such as stream of consciousness, as well as the more technical techniques of poetry writien, techniques used in journalism to best present a sotry, etc.")
(comment numericFluentReln "(#$numericFluentReln OBJ1 F1(X) RELN OBJ2 F2(X)) states that F1(OBJ1) RELN F2(OBJ2) is true.  Thus, we can say (#$numericFluentReln UT-ESB-Building #$lengthOfObject GreaterThan UT-Tower #$heightOfObject) to state that the UT engineering science building is longer thatn the tower is tall.")
(comment interArgFormat3-2 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat3-2 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the second argument-place of PRED when PRED's third argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ... ARGN) in which ARG3 is an instance of COL, PRED's arg2
position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG2' in the 
preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its instances 
for further explanation.")
(comment expertAgents "(#$expertAgents TERM AGENT) indicates that AGENT is an expert regarding TERM.  See also #$technicalSupporters.")
(disjointWith OrganismClassificationType MicrotheoryType)
(comment EventDenotingFieldAttribute "Field attributes that, when used as arg2 to #$SchemaLF, produce instances of #$LogicalField  that denote events.")
(comment DoingAerobics "Performing aerobics as a form of exercise.")
(comment spanOfUsability "This predicate relates an object to the length of time it is useful.  Note that this is not the same as shelf life.  #$spanOfUsability assumes that the object is being used, and it indicates how long the object (e.g., a device or a store of consumable stuff) will last under typical conditions of use.")
(comment defaultImplicitTime "All propositions in microtheory ARG1 implicitly weakened by a #$holdsIn ARG2.")
(comment bodyPartState "describes the state of a body part, internal to the part.  To express the realtive position of a body part to what it's part of, use relativePosition.  This slot is generally meant to be used to talk about the state of body parts which have skeletal and muscular elements, not body parts like hair and organs. ")
(disjointWith ContactLocationType PersonTypeByCulture)
(comment CommercialTransportation "A collection of events.  An instance of #$CommercialTransportation is a transportation event in which someone or something is transported for commercial purposes (i.e., a business shipping its products, a taxi or ferry some carrying paying passengers, etc.)  A borderline non-example would be a passengerless taxi cruising around looking for fares.  A borderline example would be a Goodwill truck carrying charitably donated furniture to one of their warehouses (for free), or a junkyard towing away a wrecked car at no charge (to be later sold for parts), or a city towing away a parking violator's car.")
(comment Steadiness "Performing an activity with physical steadiness.")
(comment knowsValue "(#$knowsValue AGENT X PRED) means that, if (PRED X VAL) is true, then the #$IntelligentAgent AGENT knows that (PRED X VAL); i.e., (#$knows AGENT (PRED X VAL)).")
(comment Entree "Food dishes which might be served for the main part of the meal.")
(comment MissingAReception "Failing to gain control of the game object after it has been passed to you by another team member.")
(comment DodgingSomething "The act of moving quickly out of the way of some object which would otherwise have hit you.")
(comment temporaryParts "ARG2 is a temporary part of the object ARG1.  The part ARG2 is naturally shed before the end of ARG1's lifetime. Examples: deciduous teeth (milk teeth, baby teeth); deciduous leaves of maple trees.")
(comment Manager "A specialization of #$AdministrativeStaffPerson.  Each instance of #$Manager is a person whose primary job is to manage other people, directing their work activity in an #$Organization or for a #$Project.  A #$Manager tells his or her subordinate workers what to do.")
(comment titleOfPerson "Predicate indicating the title(s) of a person; i.e., their position in some hierarchy.  For example, President, Manager, Director, etc.")
(comment TemporaryAssociation "An temporary legally-binding association between two or more legal agents.")
(comment IDNumber "A specialization of #$IDString.  Each instance of #$IDNumber is a string consisting of only numeric characters and which is used to identify a specific object.")
(comment WordSense "Word Sense --- a particular use of a word. So, for the word `bear' we have at least 2 senses - as in the animal and as in the action of bearing something")
(comment SingScullsRowingSportsEvent "The rowing sports events in which a single rower with two oars propels each scull.")
(comment excludedTypesOfInsurance "(#$excludedTypesOfInsurance ?insurance-plan ?script-type) means that any #$isa ?script-type is not covered under ?insurance-plan (i.e. (#$not (insuredEvents ?insurance-plan ?script-type)))")
(comment ProductDistributionEvent "A specialization of #$DistributionEvent. Each instance of this collection is an event in which #$Products are distributed from a source (e.g., wholesaler or manufacturer) to various destinations (e.g., retailers) via some distribution network.")
(comment PlasticSurgeon "PlasticSurgeons are concerned with surgical repair of congenital or acquired deformities and the restoration of contour to improve the apprearance of tissue defects.  They also use PlasticSurgery to restore vital movement and function of destroyed tissues.")
(comment SwimSuit "The collection of all swim suits- male and female")
(comment MammographyProvider "A mammography facility is a place which has the facilities to perform x-rays on female patiens to help diagnose the possibility of breast cancer.")
(comment ImageViewpoint "The collection of locations from which the spaces depicted in visual images are viewed.")
(comment MedicalGroupPractice "A business partnership among 2 or more physicians.  Doctors in a group practice pool resources, share staff and equipment, just as any other business partnership.")
(comment JournalismSystem "A system of written materials characterized by a direct presentation of facts or description of events without an attempt at interpretation.")
(comment Marching "The collection of all marching events, in which an animal locomotes by lifting its legs higher than usual and stepping in a stylized, rhythmic fashion.")
(disjointWith Grass-Plant GrassTurf)
(disjointWith GaseousTangibleThing Particle)
(comment CorporateOfficer "A subcollection of #$Administrator.  Each instance of #$CorporateOfficer is a person who is officially recognized as an officer of a corporation.  Common types of #$CorporateOfficer include #$President-CorporateOfficer, #$VicePresident-CorporateOfficer, and #$ChiefFinancialOfficer.")
(disjointWith Washing Surgery)
(comment UnitOfDistance "A specialization of #$UnitOfMeasure.  Each instance of #$UnitOfDistance is a function which, when applied to a number or pair of numbers, returns an instance of #$Distance as its value.  Instances of #$UnitOfDistance include #$Inch and #$Meter.")
(disjointWith ClimateCycleType MicrotheoryType)
(comment DryingBody "Events in which the body or part of the body are dried.")
(disjointWith Field-Mathematical Product)
(comment MedicalCareEvent "A collection of events.  Each instance of #$MedicalCareEvent is an event in which a medical care professional provides a medical service to some human or animal patient(s). Notable specializations of #$MedicalCareEvent include #$MedicalTesting, #$HospitalCareEvent, and #$Surgery.")
(comment AccessingScriptType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$AccessingScriptType is a type (i.e., a collection) of actions by which an agent may come to possess, or gain user rights to, some tangible thing.  Instances of #$AccessingScriptType include the collections #$Buying, #$Renting, and #$BorrowingSomething.")
(comment ChoosingABuildingLevel "Events in which a person (in an elevator) selects the building level they want to go to.")
(comment Strength "#$Strength is the #$ScriptPerformanceAttributeType for describing actions performed by exerting nontrival force at the times it is necessary.")
(comment CourseOfStudyType "This is not simply the collection of things which have #$CourseOfStudy as a genls.  This is the collection of courses of particular topics that can be given many times.  So, #$GoingToUniversity is not a #$CourseOfStudyType, but Math101AtUT is.")
(comment BlockingASpike "Blocking a spike.")
(comment Rioting "The collection of events in which many agents go on a rampage, willfully destroying property, looting, and possibly endangering lives.")
(comment PingPongBall "The ball manipulated in a game of ping-pong (table-tennis).")
(comment Amusement-Feeling "The emotion experienced when one finds something funny.  Usually people laugh when they are amused.")
(comment GovernmentEmployee "A specialization of #$PublicSectorEmployee.  Each instance of #$GovernmentEmployee is a person employed by some government.  The government in question may be the government of any instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity, including a city, county, province, or nation-state.")
(comment maidenName "Predicate indicating the maiden name of a person.")
(comment JointVentureOrganization "An legal association between two or more agents with the purpose of completing a single project- for example, building a hotel.  During the project, each agent is a #$GeneralPartner, although each can act only on his/her own behalf.  The association ends when the project is complete.")
(comment IDStringType "A collection of collections and a specialization of #$ObjectType.  Each instance of #$IDStringType is a collection of character strings which is a specialization of #$IDString (q.v.).  A few notable instances of #$IDStringType are #$ProductName, #$ProductVersion, #$EMailAddress, #$PhoneNumber, #$PostalCode.")
(comment Athlete "A collection of persons.  Each instance of #$Athlete is a person who trains to compete in contests involving physical agility, stamina, or strength.  Note that in the #$JobMt, #$Athlete is a subcollection of #$PersonWithOccupation (q.v.), and hence in that microtheory represents the collection of professional athletes.")
(disjointWith Intangible PartiallyTangible)
(comment Swim-1500MeterFreestyle "Swimming race - 1500 meter freestyle.")
(comment PrescriptionDrugType "Instances are drug products which require a prescription for dispensing.")
(comment PurchasingManager "The person who manages a team of PurchasingAgents.  Although this person might also function as a #$PurchasingAgent, they have additional responsibilities, such as approving large purchases, setting employee schedules and quotas, enforcing company policies on the sales force.")
(comment NeuroSurgeon "NeuroSurgeons are concerned with surgery of the neurological system.")
(comment Scarf "The collection of scarfs, an item of clothing used to protect the wearer's face and neck from the cold, or to hold the wearer's hair in place, or simply for decoration")
(comment DialysisUnit "The collection of organizations (may just be suborgs of some other, more formal organization) with the equipment and expertise to perform #$BloodDialysis.")
(comment ImageViewpoint "Instances are the spatial regions (places) from which the depicted spaces of images are viewed.")
(comment ElectricToothbrush "The collection of electric tooth brushes.")
(disjointWith MedicalGroupPractice IndependentPracticeAssociation)
(comment Ceremony "An activity which has certain recognizable portions, prescribed by rituals or conventions.  A ceremony may  have one or more rituals performed as #$subEvents.")
(comment TeleconferenceSiteMeeting "The collection of meetings that are part of Teleconferences, such that the participants are all at the same site.  These participants are also participants in the Teleconference that is a superevent.")
(comment ProseSystem "A system of written materials that is distinguished by its greater irregularity and variety of rhythm and its closer correspondence to the patterns of everyday speech.  Prose is less constrained than other literary systems such as journalism, and therefore is the more common system for works of fiction.")
(disjointWith MotorOil EdibleOil)
(comment interArgFormat4-5 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat4-5 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the fifth argument-place of PRED when PRED's fourth argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ... ARGN) in which ARG4 is an instance of COL, 
PRED's arg5 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG5' in 
the preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its 
instances for further explanation.")
(comment ParticleFn "argument is a kind of tangible stuff, value is the collection of particles of that stuff.")
(comment PreferredProviderOrganization "A health care provider organization that gives higher benefits to clients getting medical care from a list of preferred doctors.")
(disjointWith IDStringType MicrotheoryType)
(comment MtOfIBOTFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction for referring to an mt associated with all the instances (copies) of some #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType, such as Book or #$VideoClip.")
(comment Pajamas "The collection of instances of #$SleepWear consisting of a loose, soft top and pants.  These were first worn in Western cultures in the early 20th century.  The style is thought to have originated in India.")
(disjointWith Android BiologicalLivingObject)
(comment researchers "The people who perform research for this organization")
(comment OpeningPresents "The highly ritualized act of opening presents that have been given.")
(comment Photographer "The people who take photographs, not necessarily as professionals")
(comment TimesAll "Computes the product of the function values over all elements in the Set.")
(comment TaxonomicSlotForCollections "A subcollection of #$TaxonomicSlot. Each instance of #$TaxonomicSlotForCollections is a binary predicate used to define the taxonomy of #$Collections by specifying relations between various collections; hence at least one of its argument-places is constrained to instances (see #$argIsa) of #$Collection (and nothing more specific than that).  Examples include #$genls, #$coExtensional, and #$disjointWith.")
(comment CheckingOpponent "In hockey, colliding with an opponent so as to make them lose control of the puck.")
(comment LiftingWeights "The lifting of free weights for the purpose of increasing or maintaining muscle.")
(comment TennisBall "The ball manipulated in a tennis game.")
(comment PublicSectorEmployee "A specialization of #$Professional-Adult and #$Employee.  Each instance of #$PublicSectorEmployee is a person employed by a local, state (or provincial), or national government.  This collection includes those who are employed directly in government administration (for example, elected and appointed officials, tax officers, and police and military personnel) as well as those who are employed in support services wholly funded by the government (for example, postal employees, public school teachers, firefighters, and unionized government workers).  Although numerous subcollections of #$PublicSectorEmployee constitute instances of #$PersonTypeByOccupation (q.v.), work in the public sector displays too much variation for #$PublicSectorEmployee to be considered an occupation-type in its own right.")
(comment Trust-LegalEntity "The collection of all #$Organizations that exist in the form of a trust.  Although most trusts, in the legal sense, are collections of property or assets, some trusts do exist, apart from the assets they own or manage, as a group of #$IntelligentAgents acting together for a common purpose (e.g., a trust agreement that names two trustees to manage a group of assets).  Some instances of #$Trust-LegalEntity are also instances of #$SpeciallyCharteredInstitution (e.g. Real Estate Investment Trusts).")
(disjointWith IntangibleExistingThing PairOfObjects)
(disjointWith IDStringType TemporalStuffType)
(comment PayingForServices "A collection of events; a subset of #$Paying.  In an instance of #$PayingForServices, a customer pays for services rendered.  Payment for services may occur before or after the service is performed, depending on the provider's policies; e.g., typically commerical lodging is paid for beforehand, but dry cleaning is paid for on pickup.")
(comment EightShellRowingSportsEvent "The rowing sports events in which shells are propelled by eight rowers with one oar each (four row port, four starboard), directed by a coxswain.")
(comment odorSmelledByAgent "(#$odorSmelledByAgent ODOR THING AGENT) means that the odor ODOR from the object or event THING is smelled by the #$PerceptualAgent AGENT.")
(comment RetailDepartmentManager "A manager of a particular department in a department store.  Typically doesn't perform direct sales activities, but might do so sometimes.  Responsible for the smooth running of the department, including assuring that sufficient inventory is available, setting employee schedules, and approving checks for customers.")
(comment RadiationTherapy "Medical treatments in which parts of the body are irradiated.  The common place this occurs is in the treatment of cancer.")
(comment TieTack "The collection of tie tacks, a kind of decorative fastening device used to connect a tie to a shirt and so keep it from flopping around or getting out of place")
(disjointWith DialysisUnit MedicalCareInstitution)
(comment volumeContained "A predicate used to indicate the total volume enclosed by a given container.  (#$volumeContained CONT VOL) means that the total available volume of the #$PartiallyTangible CONT is VOL.")
(comment apparentlyOnLine "From the perspective of the viewpoint ARG1, ARG2 is on (intersects) the line ARG3.")
(comment (RepairingFn ComputerHardwareItem) "A collection of events.  Each (#$RepairingFn #$ComputerHardwareItem) event is a #$SimpleRepairing in which a computer is repaired, typically by reseating or replacing (or, more rarely these days, repairing) some of its components.")
(disjointWith Hospital MedicalGroupPractice)
(comment expects "(#$expects AGT PROP) means that AGT believes it highly likely that PROP will be true at some time in the future.")
(comment BoltedConnection "A connection which necessarily has a nut and a bolt. May or may not join to other objects.")
(disjointWith CordlessTelephone CellularTelephone)
(comment FieldConcerningFn "(#$FieldConcerningFn THING) returns a field of study that centers THING.  If CollectionA is a spec of CollectionB, then (#$FieldConcerningFn CollectionA) is a subField of (#$FieldConcerningFn CollectionB).")
(comment DoctorGroup "A group of doctors which practices together; not necessarily a  #$MedicalGroupPractice because they may not be a partnership and have at least   3 members and share expenses, etc.")
(comment Rehabilitation-Medical "A collection of events.  Each #$Rehabilitation-Medical event is likely to have numerous #$subEvents.  Taken together, the #$Rehabilitation-Medical event is intended and expected to restore, perhaps over an extended period of time, personal capabilities removed by injury, disease, addiction, etc.  A physical rehabilitation event, such as a regime of treatment for someone who was in a badcar crash, typically involves repeated physical therapy and exercise #$subEvents.  A mental rehabilitation event, such as a regime of psychotherapy for a recovering cocaine addict, typically involves repeated psychological counseling and/or behavioral modification techniques as #$subEvents.")
(comment PositiveInteger "A specialization of #$Integer.  An instance INT of #$Integer is an instance of #$PositiveInteger just in case INT is an integer greater than 0.")
(disjointWith ContactLocationType MicrotheoryType)
(comment QuantifyingIndexical "The collection of all inherently quantified indexicals. Example: 'everything'.")
(comment PreparingABeverage "Making a batch of something drinkable.")
(disjointWith OrganicMaterial InorganicMaterial)
(disjointWith ShootingAProjectileWeapon MedicalCareEvent)
(comment PublicSpeaking "Relatively formal public speaking. Usually a podium or lecture is involved. A group of people are in the audience.  The stuff spoken is usually non-fiction prose.  Theatrical performances are not in this category (else rules like sender is stationary would be wrong).")
(comment UnitVector-Precise "A specialization of both #$Vector-Precise and #$UnitVectorInterval.  Each instance of #$UnitVector-Precise is a vector interval with a magnitude of 1 and a precisely specified direction (e.g., due North, straight down).  Thus, one precise unit vector differs from another only in direction, since each vector consists of a magnitude and a direction (in a space of n > 1 dimensions).  So instances of #$UnitVector-Precise in effect indicate different directions such as `straight up' or `due East'.")
(comment GainingTheServe "In court and net games where the server is the only one who scores, becoming the server.")
(comment Diving "Jumping in such a way as to have the uppermost end of your body be leading in the direction of motion.")
(comment SoccerBall "The ball manipulated in a soccer game.")
(comment TemporaryWorker "An instance of #$EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus and a specialization of #$Employee. Each instance of #$TemporaryWorker is an employee hired with the expectation, by his employer, that his employment will be temporary.")
(comment PairOfObjects "The collection of pairs of objects.  The members of a given pair of objects are usually thought of as belonging together as a unit, sometimes by virtue of human bilateral symmetry (e.g. pairs of gloves or shoes), and sometimes for other reasons (e.g. pairs of dice or chopsticks).")
(comment UniqueID "A specialization of #$IDObject.  Each instance of #$UniqueID is an object that can be used as unique identification for a distinct entity.  Instances of this collection are typically strings or numbers.  Notable specializations of this collection are #$SocialSecurityNumber, #$IPAddress, and #$MedicareNumber.")
(comment exposedToInEvent "(#$exposedTo ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4) means that ARG1 is aware of/has been exposed to the individual object ARG2 at least in the way and/or to the degree specified by ARG3, and that the exposure occured in the event ARG4.")
(comment lifeSpanType "(#$lifeSpanType s col1 col2 ti) means that if we have (s x y) where (allIO x col1) and (allIO y col2), then, as a default, the temporal projection time of (s x y) is ti")
(comment FinnSportsEvent "A class of YachtingSportsEvent")
(comment formularyDrugs "(#$formularyDrugs ?formulary ?drug) means that ?drug is covered under the insurance plan associated with ?formulary.")
(comment InventoryBuyingAgent "An employee who purchases inventory of a company. ** ")
(comment BloodTransfusionProcess "The process of transfusing blood through a pipelike conduit from a container into the circulatory system of an organism.")
(comment Cufflink "The collection of cufflinks, a kind of decorative fastening device used to bind the cuffs of a shirt in a formal setting")
(comment CardiovascularTestingFacility "The collection of organizations that have the equipment and expertise to test the functions of the cardiovascular system.")
(comment temporallyCoterminal "A #$ComplexTemporalPredicate that
relates temporal things that terminate (i.e. cease to exist or end) 
at the same time.  (#$temporallyCoterminal TEMP1 TEMP2) means that 
the time point at which TEMP1 ends (see #$endingPoint) is the same
as that at which TEMP2 ends.  It thus entails that 
(#$simultaneousWith (#$EndFn TEMP1) (#$EndFn TEMP2)) holds.  See
also #$temporallyCooriginating.")
(comment RollingOver "Events in which an object (often animate) turns approximately 180 degrees about its #$HorizontalDirection major axis while remaining in contact with a supporting surface.  An animate object can roll itself over, while both animate and inanimate objects can be rolled over by another actor.  Rolling over makes right-side-up objects upside-down, prone objects supine, and vice versa.")
(comment (RepairingFn ElectricalHouseholdAppliance) "A collection of events.  Each (#$RepairingFn #$ElectricalHouseholdAppliance) event is a #$SimpleRepairing in which an appliance is repaired.")
(comment F1WorkVisa "A kind of limited U.S. work visa.")
(comment minPurchaseAmount "Any sale which is governed by the agreement ARG1 must have a sales value of at least ARG2, or else a service charge of ARG3 is added to the total cost.")
(comment DramaSystem "A system of written materials that is organized within specific structural bounds. Drama is intended to portray life or character or to tell a story through action and dialogue and designed for a theatrical performance, although a performance of written material is not the criterion for labelling it drama, nor vice versa.")
(comment FallingEvent "The collection of occurrences in which the center of gravity of the #$objectMoving moves to a lower altitude.  Includes both #$Falling-Freefall and #$FallingDown.")
(disjointWith MusicalInstrument GameBoard)
(comment interArgFormat3-4 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat3-4 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the fourth argument-place of PRED when PRED's third argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ... ARGN) in which ARG3 is an instance of COL, PRED's
arg4 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG4' in the 
preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its instances 
for further explanation.")
(disjointWith Sunset Sunrise)
(comment Quantifier-SP "The collection of all quantifying words. Quantifiers can modify nouns. Example: 'most'.")
(comment TrippingSomeone "The collection of events in which one agent trips another.")
(comment ProducingAnAlcoholicBeverage "Making a batch of some alcoholic beverage such as beer, wine, etc.")
(disjointWith SubLString TruthValue)
(disjointWith SportsAction MedicalCareEvent)
(comment technicalSupporters "The people who provide technical support for this agent. See also #$expertAgents.")
(comment averageAmbientHumidity "The relative humidity of a region averaged over a year's time, with irregularities averaged out.")
(comment Average "Computes the average of the function values over all elements in the Set.")
(comment represents "(#$represents REPRESENTATIVE AGENT) means that REPRESENTATIVE represents the interests of AGENT.")
(comment BroadMicrotheory "The collection of those microtheories that contain so many assertions that they are not useful for `relevance' focusing during inference.  (A #$BroadMicrotheory is not used internally in Cyc's indexing scheme during inference.)  Examples: #$BaseKB and #$EnglishMt.")
(comment SubLAtomWithValue "A specialization of #$SubLAtom.  Each instance of #$SubLAtomWithValue is an atomic SubL expression that has a value (e.g., 2) associated with it.")
(comment HighSchoolDiploma "The collection of all credentials certifying someone to have reached the level of education of someone who has successfully graduated from a high school. A #$HighSchoolDiploma may be granted to someone who has actually completed a high school curriculum, or - as in the case of a #$GeneralEducationalDevelopmentCredential - to someone who otherwise demonstrates a similar level of academic acheivement.")
(comment Feinting "In boxing, tricking an opponent into thinking you're about to hit him.")
(comment HittingAnObject "The striking of an object, with your hand or a tool manipulated by your hand (a tennis racket, a hammer, etc.).")
(comment GymnasticsSportsEvent "The collection of gymnastic events.")
(comment directingPerformsFor "arg1 is both the performer and #$directingAgent of the instances of arg3 in which arg2 is the recipient.  For example, we may say (#$directingPerformsFor SeniorSecretary001 JuniorSecretary001 AdministrativeSupervision). This implies that arg1 has some authority over arg2 particularly when arg1 is performing instances of arg3 where arg2 is the recipient.")
(disjointWith BranchOrganization IndependentOrganization)
(comment obscuresFrom "(#$obscuresFrom OBJ1 OBJ2 AGENT) means that the #$PartiallyTangible OBJ1 visually blocks the #$PerceptualAgent AGENT's view of the #$PartiallyTangible OBJ2.")
(comment LevelOfQuality "A measure of how well a particular instance of #$Artifact performs its intended function.  It is assessed according to different standards based on the kind of #$Artifact involved.  Standards may be formal and objective, or the product of subjective judgement.  Also, for certain kinds of #$Artifact, #$Quality may vary over time, so the user should give serious consideration to temporally qualifying assertions involving attributions of #$Quality.")
(comment lengthOfStringType "elements of arg1 are strings of length arg2")
(comment personalWealthOwned "the wealth of a person.")
(comment lifeSpanType-1 "(#$lifeSpanType-1 s col o ti) means that as a default, if an instance of col is on the slot s of the object o, the temporal projection time of this proposition is ti")
(comment SkeetShootingSportsEvent "A marksmanship sports event in which the targets are clay pidgeons tossed into the air at different angles and positions.")
(comment InpatientDrugTherapy "#$DrugTherapy that occurs while one is an inpatient.")
(comment SalesManager "The person who manages a team of SalesPersons.  Although this person might also function as a #$SalesPerson, they have additional responsibilities, such as customer check verification, setting employee schedules and quotas, enforcing company policies on the sales force.")
(comment Abortion-Intentional "An intentional ending of a pregnancy.")
(comment Belt-Clothing "The collection of all belts, the article of clothing used to hold up pants and skirts, and for decoration")
(disjointWith CardiovascularTestingFacility MedicalCareInstitution)
(comment FeedingEvent "A collection of events.  In an instance of #$FeedingEvent, an agent intentionally supplies food to an organism.  In this sense, feeding is not the same as eating.  Rather, a feeding event is a prelude to some #$EatingEvent which is expected to follow the feeding.  The food may be placed into the intended recipient's mouth or where it can be reached easily by the recipient.   Feeding may be done by one agent for another, but an organism may also feed itself.  Feeding is part of the care of captive animals, as well as of caring by a parent for its offspring (in most species).")
(comment CateringFoodEvent "The collecton of food catering events.")
(comment H1WorkVisa "A kind of limited U.S. work visa.")
(comment LeftObject "An instance of #$TangibleObjectTypeBySide.
#$LeftObject is the collection of tangible objects that are meant for, 
or are found on and distinctively structured for, the left side of some 
larger object or ensemble of parts.  Examples include left hands, left 
shoes, and automobile left-turn.  A given #$LeftObject will typically 
be one of a pair whose other member is a #$RightObject.")
(comment Pronoun "The collection of all pronouns. Pronouns are indexicals which can replace nouns. Example: `she'.")
(comment preSituation "(#$preSituation EVENT SIT) means that the #$StaticSituation SIT holds just prior to the start of the #$Event EVENT, and SIT is directly related to EVENT in some salient way.  The required `salience' of the two arguments to each other is difficult to formalize but usually intuitively clearcut.  Commonly, SIT and EVENT share many of the same objects involved in various roles, and there is often a causal connection as well.   For instance, if SIT is an instance of #$Configuration (q.v.), then SIT might be somehow `taken apart' by EVENT or might `trigger' EVENT.")
(disjointWith PierAndBeamFoundation SlabFoundation)
(comment SchemaOfIBOFn "(#$SchemaOfIBOFn ?INFO) denotes the #$SISLogicalSchema of the #$InformationSource ?INFO.")
(comment percentOfPatientsInsuredByType "ARG3 percent of ARG1's patients are covered by a provider of type ARG2.")
(comment SubLList "A collection of list-denoting expressions that are not represented in CycL (i.e. they are not #$CycLConstants or #$CycLNonAtomicTerms) but are represented in SubL, the underlying implementation language of the Cyc system.  Each instance of #$SubLList is a sequence of #$SubLListOrAtoms (q.v.) enclosed in parentheses.  SubL lists are those things that pass the #$defnIff LISTP. Note that this collection is \"quoted\" (see #$quotedCollection).")
(comment DoctorOfOsteopathyDegree "Credential held by osteopathic medicine doctors.")
(comment DietingForMuscleGain "A subset of #$Dieting in which a #$Person controls their intake of food for the purpose of gaining weight in the form of muscle.")
(disjointWith Dancing-Human PerformingADanceMotion)
(disjointWith BiologicalLivingObject InanimateObject)
(disjointWith LawEnforcementActivity MedicalCareEvent)
(comment Pensiveness "A feeling of deep thoughtfulness, reflection, or introspection, and sometimes melancholia.  This is a #$Collection --- for an explanation of that, see #$Happiness.")
(comment Cashier "A cashier in a commercial enterprise, such as a grocery store, a clothing store, etc.")
(disjointWith Student HumanToddler)
(comment ScoringAGoal "Scoring in a ball and goal game.")
(comment Splashing "The striking or pushing of a liquid in such a way as to make parts of it airborn.")
(comment Sword "The weapon used for hand-to-hand fighting.")
(comment bossIn "ARG1 is the boss of ARG2 concerning instances of ARG3.  That is, ARG1 supervises, evaluates, and monitors ARG2 doing the ARG3.  For related slots see #$directingPerformsFor and #$bossIn.")
(disjointWith Subsidiary IndependentOrganization)
(comment ImageSpace "Instances are the spatial regions (usually 3d) depicted or displayed in a visual image.")
(comment costPerQuantity "The predicate #$costPerQuantity gives the price for a measured amount of some type of stuff.  (#$costPerQuantity STUFF UNITS QUANTITY PRICE) means that this kind of STUFF costs PRICE for each QUANTITY of UNITS.  For example, #$Milk, as measured by volume (i.e., by the predicate #$volumeOfObject), costs about US $3 per gallon.")
(comment exposedTo "(#$exposedTo ARG1 ARG2 ARG3) means that ARG1 is aware of/has been exposed to the individual object ARG2 at least in the way and/or to the degree specified by ARG3.")
(comment UnevenBarsSportsEvent "The collection of gymnastic events on the UnevenBars.")
(comment providerAMCNumber "The number given to this medical care provider by the American Medical Census organization.  ARG1 is an organization, and is an HMO or other medical insurer.")
(comment RetailSalesClerk "People who help you if you ask them. RetailSalesClerks usually do not work on commission.")
(comment MouthToMouthResuscitation "An emergency treatment for someone who has stopped breathing, which involves another person regularly blowing air into their lungs.")
(comment Anklet "The collection of anklets, a kind of jewelry (typically ringlike in shape) intended to be worn on the ankle")
(comment ElectrocardiologyFacility "An organization which has the personnel and equipment to diagnose patients through use of electrocardiograms.")
(comment HumanMaleFirstName "People with these given names can be assumed to be male.")
(comment streetAddressText "The predicate #$streetAddressText maps from a particular place to a string representing its street address.  (#$streetAddressText LOC STREET) means that LOC is found at the number and street given in the string STREET.  See also #$ContactLocation.")
(comment CardiacCatheterizationUnit "A suborganization of a hospital that treats heart patients.")
(disjointWith RightObject LeftObject)
(comment TransitiveNPFrame "This frame is used for transitive words that take exactly one complement which is an NP. In HPSG terms: [COMPS  <NP>] Example: 'I ate a sandwich'.")
(comment startingTimeRelativeTo "the event to which the starting time of event u is given. NOTE: The starting time of u is relative to the ending time of v.")
(comment arg5Format "An instance of #$ArgFormatPredicate (q.v.) used to place a particular #$Format (q.v.) constraint on the fifth (or \"arg5\") argument-place of a given predicate.  (#$arg5Format PRED FORMAT) means that PRED's arg5 is constrained to FORMAT.  See the reified instances #$Format for further details.")
(comment Cuteness-EmotionalResponse "Attractive or pretty in a delicate way")
(comment BloodDialysis "The treatment undergone by patients with kidney problems, in which the blood is circulated from the patient's body, through a machine which removes the body's waste, and back into the patient's body.")
(comment ReciprocalPronoun "The collection of all reciprocal pronouns. Reciprocal pronouns are indexicals which are used in reciprocal contexts. Example: 'each other'.")
(comment Doctor-Osteopathic "A collection of persons; a subset of #$Doctor-Medical. Each element of #$Doctor-Osteopathic is a doctor who has completed the education and training required to be awarded a #$DoctorOfOsteopathyDegree.  Cf. #$Doctor-MD.")
(comment OlympicTeam "This is a team which represents some country at an instance of OlympicGames.  It competes in some way as a team - i.e. we wouldn't talk about a USTrack&FieldTeam (since there is no overall track&field competition), but we could talk about a USWomensGymnasticsTeam or USMens100DashRelayTeam or USHockeyTeam.")
(comment PedalingABicycle "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$PedalingABicycle, one person pushes on the pedals of a bicycle, moving the crankshaft around.  Every instance of #$PedalingABicycle has at least one instance of #$Pedaling among its #$subEvents.  #$PedalingABicycle may be done on a stationary bike, such as an #$ExerciseBike, or on a more conventional #$Bicycle which one could ride from place to place.")
(disjointWith TimeInterval Product)
(comment WatchingAStageProduction "Watching a performance where the actors are on a stage.  Some examples include a play, opera, musical, etc...")
(comment DayCareCenter "A place where children are looked after and taken care of while their parents or guardian works.")
(comment PortfolioManager "These folk detect trends in the financial situation of a business. Woe is them.")
(comment SolvingAMathematicalEquation "Taking an equation and determining the value of a variable in terms of constants and other variables within the rules of algebra.  The catalyst to creating this unit was skills required effort.")
(comment SensoryInformation "A specialization of #$MentalInformation.  Each instance of #$SensoryInformation is the propositional content of a mental state in which an animal or other sentient being perceives something.")
(comment LiftingOpponent "In judo, lifting one's opponent, esp. from the mat to shoulder height.")
(comment TreadingWater "The act of moving your body in such a way as to keep an upright position in the water, but not to travel at all.")
(comment FencingFoil "The weapon used for hand-to-hand fighting.")
(comment nicknames "(#$nicknames THING NAME) means that the  #$ProperNameString NAME is a nickname for THING.   THING could also be, among  other things, a non-person agent (such as the #$BostonRedSox), a neighborhood  (such as #$SpanishHarlem), or even a type of object  (such as #$FlagOf-UnitedStatesOfAmerica).")
(comment conceals "(#$conceals OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 blocks OBJ2 entirely from view.  View should probably be a function of context.  Therefore, in a still image (e.g. photograph) microtheory a wall could conceal what was behind it.  However in a microtheory in which the viewpoint could change (e.g. a `hide and go seek sort of context') only objects that were completely surrounded could be concealed.  Defining it this way allows us to make #$conceals an instance of #$AsymmetricBinaryPredicate.")
(comment AudioTapeDeckMechanism "Tape deck mechanism;  can record and/or play audio cassette tapes.  See also StereoSystemTapeDeck")
(comment LightFlyweightFSWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of FSWrestlingSportsEvent")
(comment iDSuffix "(#$iDSuffix ?id ?suffix) means that ?suffix appended to ?id is an identifier for some thing.  It does not mean ?suffix is a tailing substring of ?id.")
(comment hasFamilyMembers "Entries are the members of FamilyCohabitationUnit U.")
(comment AssistantManager "A person whose immediate boss is a manager and who has secondary power to act in that manager's absence.  Having this role is common practice in operations where the manager is not present for significant amounts of time.")
(comment BloodTest "Blood is tested to determine the presence and amount of certain substances.")
(comment Necklace "The collection of necklaces, a kind of jewelry (usually circular in shape) intended to be worn around the neck")
(comment AudiologyOrganization "An organization which has the personnel and equipment to test hearing and to treat and diagnose patients with impaired hearing.")
(comment CalendarSecond "A subcollection of #$Date (q.v.) and an instance of #$CalendarCoveringType (q.v.).  #$CalendarSecond is the collection of seconds that make up the calendar.  Each #$CalendarMinute (q.v.) is divided into sixty contiguous calendar-seconds.  Note that (as with any instance of an instance of  calendar-covering-type) a given calendar-second is a temporally-continuous individual that occurs only _once_; e.g. it is not something that recurs each hour or each year.")
(comment HandRail "A rail that one holds onto for support.")
(comment J1WorkVisa "A kind of limited U.S. work visa.")
(comment BurnCareUnit "A suborganization of a hospital that treats burn victims.")
(comment RightObject "An instance of #$TangibleObjectTypeBySide.
#$RightObject is the collection of tangible objects that are meant for, 
or are found on and distinctively structured for, the right side of some 
larger object or ensemble of parts.  Examples include right hands, right 
shoes, automobile right-turn indicators.  A given #$RightObject will 
typically be one of a pair whose other member is a #$LeftObject.")
(comment rateOfRotationOfObject "#$rateOfRotationOfObject relates an instance of #$PartiallyTangible to the rate of change of its physical component's angular separation from a reference vector as measured from a point of origin.")
(comment interArgFormat5-4 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat5-4 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the fifth argument-place of PRED when PRED's fifth argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ... ARGN) in which ARG5 is an instance of COL, 
PRED's arg4 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG4' in 
the preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its 
instances for further explanation.")
(disjointWith ProkaryoticCell EukaryoticCell)
(comment AgreementLineItem "A single point of an agreement.  In the case of sales agreements  or other kinds of contracts, the line items often have their own id numbers and so on. ")
(comment Direction "A specialization of #$UnitVectorInterval (q.v.).  Each instance of #$Direction is a vector representing a direction, typically between two objects or locations.  Specializations include #$GeographicalDirection, #$TerrestrialDirection, and #$AnatomicalDirection.  Note that, since a given vector can represent a particular direction only in relation to some frame of reference, a frame of reference must be (explicitly or implicitly) specified for assertions about particular directions, either by the context (i.e. #$Microtheory) of the assertion or by the type of #$Direction in question (e.g. #$GeographicalDirections are intrinsically tied to a particular terrestrial frame of reference).")
(comment IntensiveCareEvent "The collection of hospital intensive care treatment events.")
(comment CalendarMonth "An instance of #$CalendarCoveringType, and a specialization of #$Date.  Each instance of #$CalendarMonth is a month in a particular calendar.  An example sub-collection of #$CalendarMonth is #$February , the collection of all months of February.  One instance of the collection #$February (and thus one instance of the collection #$CalendarMonth) is (#$MonthFn #$February (#$YearFn 1992)), February of 1992.")
(comment NursingDegree-LPN "The amount of training that a person needs in order to become a licensed practical nurse (LPN).  The formal training usually lasts around a year.  A LPN may practice the duties of a nurse under the supervision of a registered nurse.  LPNs are sometimes called Licensed Vocational Nurses (LVNs).")
(comment Painting-Activity "The action of painting on a surface")
(disjointWith MicroscopicScaleObject HumanScaleObject)
(disjointWith LegalProceeding MedicalCareEvent)
(comment ChurchService "A ceremony that is held in a Christian church.")
(comment OptionsTrader "Buys and sells options")
(comment PaymentObligation "The class of contexts arising from an agent agreeing to render payment for goods/services.")
(comment AccessingAnIBT "A specialization of both #$InformationTransferEvent and #$PurposefulAction.  Each instance of #$AccessingAnIBT is an action by which an agent accesses the content of some instance(s) of #$InformationBearingThing.  Examples include (getting information from) reading a newspaper, watching a film, listening to a musical performance, decoding an encrypted message, seeing a traffic police officer wave one on, or hearing one's roommate ask one to take out the trash.")
(comment ThrowingJudoOpponent "In judo, picking up an opponent and throwing him.")
(comment AquaticBodyMovement "The collection of movements typical of animals when the animal's body is immersed (partially or wholly) in water. Includes movements for locomotion or maintaining position.")
(comment FencingEpee "The weapon used for hand-to-hand fighting.")
(comment MilitaryTrainingCourse "Training for the skills needed to serve in the military.  Usually includes training in combat and the use of firearms, and often includes other specialized sorts of training.")
(comment Partnership "#$Partnership is a specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$Partnership is an organization that has been formally organized as a partnership pursuant to partnership agreements.  In the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, most instances of #$Partnership are organized pursuant to specific statutes.  #$GeneralPartners of a #$Partnership are jointly and severally liable for the debts and other liabilities of the #$Partnership.  The liability of #$LimitedPartners is limited in accordance with the governing partnership agreement.  The #$PartnershipPartners of an instance of #$Partnership may be individuals or entities.  For example, an instance of #$LimitedPartnership may have an instance of #$LegalCorporation as its #$GeneralPartner and individuals as its #$LimitedPartners.")
(comment StartFn "An instance of #$IndividualDenotingFunction.  When applied to an instance THING of #$TemporalThing, #$StartFn  returns the #$TimePoint at which THING began.")
(comment ImageBackground "The collection of backgrounds of visual images.  The background is a more or less distinct region of space displayed or depicted in an image.  The background is the region apparently `further from' the viewer of the image.  Every ImageBackground is part of the DepictedSpace of an image.")
(comment TrashCompacting "The process where the size of an amount of trash is reduced by crushing")
(comment HelpingSomeoneGetAbout "The action of assisting someone to walk or move.")
(comment Alkaloid "Instances are pieces of organic compounds composed of carbon, hydrogen, nitrogen, and usually oxygen, and are often derived from plants.  Though poisons, many alkaloids have physiological effects that render them useful as medicines or interesting as narcotics.  Some popular and notable alkaloids are curare, altropine, morphine, codeine, cocaine, caffeine, LSD, quinine, serotonin, strychnine, and nicotine.")
(comment RapidPistolShootingSportsEvent "A marksmanship sports event in which rapid fire pistols are used.")
(comment HomosexualHuman "The collection of persons whose sexual preference is predominantly for other persons of the same sex.")
(comment CommercialSalesRepresentative "The person who sells to companies (not individuals).  CommericalSalesReps frequently have PurchasingAgents or InventoryBuyers as contactPoints.  CommericalSalesReps might receive QuoteRequestDocuments from their contactPoints, and CommericalSalesReps might send FormalEstimateDocuments to their contactPoints.")
(comment GenDoingFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction for denoting an event type that involves generally doing something, even though the doer may not be actively or continuously engaged in one type of activity.  Example, (#$GenDoingFn #$SnowSkiing) denotes the collection of events in which the doer is generally involved in snow skiing, even though at any given time x, the doer may just be standing around rather than sliding down a ski slope.")
(comment MammographyExam "The collection of events in which an Xray picture is taken of a breast, frequently used to screen for cancer.")
(comment Jewelry "The collection of all kinds of jewelry -- items made of precious stones and/or metals, or fake analogs of these, intended to be worn on the body/clothing for decoration")
(comment OptometricServicesProvider "The collection of all #$Organizations that provide optometric services, i.e., testing and fitting services for eyeglasses and contact lenses.")
(comment Movement-TranslationEvent "A specialization of #$Translocation.  Each instance of #$Movement-TranslationEvent is an event in which an object (an instance of #$SomethingExisting) moves some distance (so that at some point in the event, the object's center of mass changes location with respect to the relevant frame of reference).  The moving object need not move completely out of its original spatial extent; for example, a building moving one foot to the left undergoes a #$Movement-TranslationEvent.  Instances of #$Movement-TranslationEvent include events in which the movement ends in the same place it started from (e.g. one lap of a race car around the Indianapolis race track, or a trip to the grocery store and back).  In such cases (all of which are instances of the specialization #$Translation-NoLocationChange), the to and from locations of the movement (see the predicates #$toLocation and #$fromLocation) are identical.  In other cases of #$Movement-TranslationEvent (e.g. the movement of the baseball during a home run hit by Roger Maris), the to and from locations are different; in these cases, the movement events are also instances of #$Translation-LocationChange (q.v.).")
(comment HumanFemaleFirstName "People with these given names can be assumed to be female.")
(comment GreenCard "A U.S. work visa premitting any kind of employment and acknowledging permanent residence.")
(disjointWith Pharmacy ManagedCareOrganization)
(comment RoadRoller "The collection of vehicles, generally with a relatively high ratio of weight per square inch of wheel surface, used for leveling and packing down road and other construction surfaces.")
(comment SubcategorizationFrame "The collection of subcategorization frames found in natural languages.")
(comment hasProductFeatures "The features that this product has.  See ProductFeature for more details.")
(comment Wonder-Admiration "The attribute-type associated with the feeling of amazed admiration toward something. (For the rationale behind treating feelings as types -- i.e. collections -- of attributes, see the comment on #$Happiness.)")
(comment expenseDuringPeriodForType "During the time interval ARG4, the amount of money specified in ARG3 is paid out of an account owned/controlled by ARG1 to cover the expense incurred in an instance of action type ARG2.")
(comment South-Directly "An instance of #$GeographicalDirection-Direct (q.v.).
#$South-Directly is due South (from a given point of reference).")
(comment DoctorVisit "Scripts in which a person sees a doctor or other medical care professional for medical care.  There is usually at least one #$MedicalCareEvent as a subevent, but perhaps more.  The person may go to the doctor's office, or the doctor may see the patient at a hospital or clinic or at their home.")
(comment RegisteredTechnologistCredential "The American Registry of Radiologic Technology gives the registered technologist (RT) title to people who are qualified to act as x-ray technologists.")
(comment Drawing-Depicting "The making of designs on a surface using a writing implement.")
(comment NonPhysicalPartPredicate "A collection of predicates. Instances of #$NonPhysicalPartPredicate are used to describe the relationship between a #$PartiallyIntangible and its non-physical parts.")
(disjointWith RecreationalActivity MedicalCareEvent)
(comment Carnival "Rides, games, food -- a carnival")
(comment infoContributed "The predicate #$infoContributed is used to identify which agent said what in a particular complex communication activity.  (#$infoContributed MULTICOM AGENT INFO) means that in the #$MultiDirectionalCommunication event MULTICOM, AGENT does something that expresses INFO.  Note that speaking, writing, or otherwise signalling are all viable methods of `saying'.  The (unspecified) thing that AGENT does in MULTICOM generates the message, and INFO is a propositional item expressing the content of AGENT's message.  See also #$PropositionalInformationThing and #$IBTGeneration.")
(comment MarketingCommunication "The collection of communication events where the purpose of the communication is to promote some sales activity.")
(comment BringingSportsOpponentToGround "In boxing or wrestling, forcing an opponent to the ground.")
(comment StretchingBody "Getting into particular body positions in order to 'stretch out' and 'warm up' muscles and increase flexibility in the body.  Could be either intensive stretching (a gymnast before a routine), or just casual stretching (a person getting out of bed in the morning).")
(comment FencingSabre "The weapon used for hand-to-hand fighting.")
(disjointWith OldHuman YoungHuman)
(comment evaluatedAction "(#$evaluatedAction EVAL EVT) means that in the #$EvaluatingAnAction event EVAL, an evaluation is made of the action, event, or occurrence EVT.  For example, in the evaluation of an employee, the #$evaluatedAction will be one of the job activities being #$performedBy the worker who is being evaluated.")
(disjointWith Partnership GeopoliticalEntity)
(comment (SolidFn Salt-NaCl) "Solid, crystalline sodium chloride.")
(comment ImageBackground "The collection of backgrounds of visual images.  The background is a more or less distinct region of space displayed or depicted in an image.  The background is the region apparently `further from' the viewer of the image.  Every #$ImageBackground is part of the DepictedSpace of an image.")
(comment mentalActivityLevel "The predicate #$mentalActivityLevel relates a particular action to the specific #$LevelOfMentalActivity that its agent has while doing it.  (#$mentalActivityLevel ACT LEVEL) means that the agent who does the #$AnimalActivity ACT uses the #$LevelOfMentalActivity LEVEL in doing ACT.  Default rules may be used to infer that in general an agent has the specific #$LevelOfMentalActivity characteristic of those who perform some type of activity; e.g., instances of #$Memorizing require #$ConcentratingMentalActivityLevel.")
(comment spatialExtent "The default spatial region associated with/occupied by an event")
(comment DoublesTennisMatch "Games of Doubles Tennis.")
(comment tableOfDB "(#$tableOfDB TABLE DB) means that the physical table TABLE is part of the physical database DB.  A physical table may be part of only one database, but a database may have many tables.")
(comment InventoryBuyingManager "The person who manages a team of InventoryBuyingAgents.  Although this person might also function as a #$InventoryBuyingAgent, they have additional responsibilities, such as approving large purchases, setting employee schedules and quotas, enforcing company policies on the sales force.")
(comment ArrangingForSomething "A specialization of #$PurposefulAction.  Each instance of #$ArrangingForSomething is an event in which some action or set of actions is arranged or facilitated.  Note that events in which objects are arranged (e.g., instances of #$FlowerArranging) _not_ usually instances of #$ArrangingForSomething.")
(comment TakingABloodSample "The collection of events in which blood is removed from an animal's body, usually in order to be tested.")
(comment Ring-Jewelry "The collection of rings, a kind of jewelry (circular in shape) intended to be worn on the fingers")
(comment AllergyTestingOrganization "An organization (may just be suborg of some other, more formal organization) which has the equipment and expertise to test a person for allergies.")
(comment USWorkVisaType "The types of work visas given in the U.S.")
(comment IndependentPracticeAssociation "The collection of all IPAs, associations of independent physicians who contract with IPA-model hmos.  Also called `individual practice associations'.")
(comment PairFn "A unary collection denoting function that takes an object-type as argument and returns the collection of all instances of #$PairOfObjects consisting of two objects of that type.  (#$PairFn OBJTYPE) denotes the collection of all and only pairs of OBJTYPEs.  Note, however, that not every two-member #$Group of OBJTYPEs necessarily constitutes a #$PairOfObjects.  For example, the fact that a child has donned an unmatched \"pair\" of its father's shoes for play does not make those shoes members of the same instance of (#$PairFn #$Shoe), even though they might be seen as constituting a two-member group.  As with #$Groups generally, pairs of #$PartiallyTangibles are themselves #$PartiallyTangibles.")
(comment TeacherOfSkillFn "(#$TeacherOfSkillFn SKILL) denotes the collection of #$Teachers who teach the skilled activity, SKILL. For example, (#$TeacherOfSkillFn #$Juggling) denotes the collection of juggling instructors. If an assertion using this function is made in the #$AcademicLifeMt, the collection denoted by using this function will also be a spec of #$AcademicProfessional.  Use #$TeacherFn to denote teachers of #$FieldOfStudys.")
(comment standardConcerns "(standardConcerns STAND SCRIPT ASLOT) states that the standard STAND concerns the things which show up on the ASLOT of instances of SCRIPT")
(comment interArgFormat5-2 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat5-2 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the second argument-place of PRED when PRED's fifth argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ... ARGN) in which ARG5 is an instance of COL, 
PRED's arg2 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG2' 
in the preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its 
instances for further explanation.")
(comment MedicalInsuranceClaimForm "Insurance claim forms for health insurance claims.")
(comment revenueFromType "During the time interval ARG3, the amount of money specified by ARG4 accrues to ARG1 as a result of actions of type ARG2.")
(comment North-Directly "An instance of #$GeographicalDirection-Direct (q.v.).  #$North-Directly is due North (from a given point of reference).")
(comment CalendarDay "An instance of #$CalendarCoveringType, and a specialization of #$Date.  Each instance of #$CalendarDay is a day on some particular calendar.  Instances of #$CalendarDay include (#$DayFn 1 (#$MonthFn #$July (#$YearFn 1646))) and (#$DayFn 8 (#$MonthFn #$November (#$YearFn 1848))).")
(comment VeterinarianDegree-DVM "Doctor of Veterinary Medicine")
(comment DryingLaundry "The event in which water evaporates from wet clothes, towels, sheets, etc., and they become dry.  In the #$HumanActivitiesMt, #$DryingLaundry involves a person transporting the objects involved to some device (either a #$ClothesDryer or a clothes line, and handling that device.")
(comment Cavity "The collection of all cavities, including instances of #$Crevice, deep concavities or holes, and cavities of containers (for example,  the interior of a box).  Instances of #$Cavity can include walls as parts, in which case they are instances of #$CavityWithWalls.  Instances of #$Cavity, unlike instances of #$Container, do not have well defined outside walls.")
(disjointWith Travel-TripEvent MedicalCareEvent)
(comment LegalConflict "Conflicts that are juridified by a legal system.")
(comment ChristianHoliday "The subset of #$ReligiousHolidays specified as part of the religion #$Christianity.")
(disjointWith SeatingDevice Tool)
(comment FunctionalRelation "A specialization of #$Relation each instance of which is either a function (see #$Function-Denotational) or a predicate that is \"functional\" in at least one argument-place (see #$FunctionalPredicate and #$functionalInArgs).  Examples include #$IntervalMaxFn, #$ElectricalPotentialDifferenceFn, #$revenueFromType, #$costRateForType, and #$biologicalMother.  See also the specialization #$StrictlyFunctionalRelation.")
(comment FallingForwards "Falling so as to land on one's hands, stomach, face, etc.")
(comment TrainingForFn "#$TrainingForFn takes as argument any type of learned activity and returns the collection of all instances of #$Training in which that activity is (a signficant part of) what is taught. For example, (#$TrainingForFn #$WebDesign) returns the collection of all instances of training in web design.")
(comment HockeyPuck "The little disk moved about by the players in a Hockey game.")
(disjointWith MiddleAgedHuman YoungHuman)
(comment MaintenanceAgreement "An agreement between a manufacturer and purchaser of an object/service, of the form 'If something goes wrong in a given period of time, we'll fix it and charge you nothing.'  The difference between this and a warranty is that the customer must pay extra for this arrangement.")
(disjointWith LegalCorporation TerroristGroup)
(disjointWith HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject (LiquidFn Water))
(comment circularBetween "ARG3 is a circular layer, or barrier, between ARG1 and ARG2.")
(comment LevelOfPhysicalActivity "A collection of attributes.  Instances of #$LevelOfPhysicalActivity denote the various intensities of physical effort with which agents perform activities.   #$LevelOfPhysicalActivity includes levels of exertion represented by non-atomic terms (NATs) such as (#$HighAmountFn #$LevelOfPhysicalActivity), as well as instances such as #$ExtremePhysicalActivityLevel.  All of those intensities are treated as ordered intervals and must be related appropriately; see #$ScalarInterval for more detail.  See also #$GenericValueFunction, #$physicalActivityLevel.")
(comment ParallelBarsSportsEvent "The collection of gymnastic events on the ParallelBars.")
(comment tableName "(#$tableName TABLE STRING) means that STRING is a string used as the name for the physical database table TABLE.")
(comment Traffic "The event made up of many driving #$subEvents in a given place over a given time period.")
(comment ThroatCultureTest "A sample from someone's throat is cultured and tested to determine the presence and amount of certain substances.")
(comment Jacket "The set of all jackets.")
(comment PulmonaryTestingFacility "The collection of organizations with the personnel and equipment to test lung capacity and function.")
(comment BusTrip "A bus trip.  See mts for different perspectives.")
(comment physicallyDisadvantagedIn "ARG1 has a physical handicap while attempting to succeed at ARG2.")
(disjointWith Hospital IndependentPracticeAssociation)
(comment WinterCoat "The collection of #$Coats worn as #$OuterGarments.  One of the main functions of the #$WinterCoat is to protect its wearer against the cold.")
(comment Down-Partially "The direction #$Down-Partially is a unit vector interval which includes in its range all unit vectors that have a less than zero upward component.  Different #$Down-Partially assertions in different #$FrameOfReference microtheories should not be considered equivalent by default.  A rock in freefall as well as an airplane on a very gradual descent move in the #$Down-Partially direction. See #$Down-Generally and #$Down-Directly for more directionally constrained versions of `down'.")
(comment DeFactoProductStandard "The standard of some standardized product which evolved to become the de facto standard for products in its market.  The prototypical example is the IBM-PC-AT-Standard")
(comment netValue "The total value of all assets owned by the agent minus the total value of all liabilities owed.")
(comment East-Directly "An instance of #$GeographicalDirection-Direct (q.v.).  #$East-Directly is due East (from a given point of reference).")
(comment objectOfStateChange "The predicate #$objectOfStateChange is used to identify an object undergoing a change of state in an instance of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent.  (#$objectOfStateChange EVENT OBJECT) means that the #$PartiallyTangible OBJECT undergoes some kind of intrinsic change of state (such as a change in one of its physical properties) in the #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent EVENT.  OBJECT exists before EVENT, is directly involved in EVENT, and persists after EVENT (accordingly, this predicate has as #$genlPreds both #$preActors and #$postActors).  The change which OBJECT undergoes is internal or intrinsic; this predicate is not used for extrinsic changes, such as changes in location, orientation, ownership, or status.  Note that if OBJECT were destroyed by EVENT and went out of existence in the course of EVENT, then the right predicate to use would be #$inputsDestroyed, rather than #$objectOfStateChange.")
(disjointWith PhysicallyAttackingAnAgent SociabilityBasedAction)
(comment VideoCassetteRecording "Recording video images onto a #$VideoCassette tape")
(comment WritingSymbolCharacter "The specialization of #$Character-Abstract whose instances are characters used as writing symbols in some writing system or other.  Specializations of #$WritingSymbolCharacter include #$Letter-Alphabetic, #$Numeral, #$RomanLetter, #$ChineseCharacter, and many others.  Instances of #$WritingSymbolCharacter include the Roman letter 'a', the Arabic numeral '1', and #$PercentSign-TheSymbol.  (See also #$WritingSymbolCharacterSet.)")
(disjointWith MedicalCareEvent DoingMath)
(comment MolecularStuff "A collection of tangible stuff.  Every instance of #$MolecularStuff is a portion of stuff composed of covalently-bonded molecules.  Thus, #$Water and #$DNAStuff are subcollections of #$MolecularStuff; each of their instances consists of covalently bonded molecules.  But instances of #$Salt-NaCl are not examples of #$MolecularStuff.  Also, #$Oxygen is not a subcollection of #$MolecularStuff, since #$Oxygen denotes anything composed of that element, not just O2 (molecular oxygen) and O3 (ozone). ")
(comment actorSlotOfMt "ARG3 is the #$ActorSlot which provides the perspective of the #$PerspectiveMicrotheory, ARG1 on the domain of the Microtheory ARG2.")
(comment KnockingDown-Boxing "In boxing, knocking down an opponent.")
(comment Agility "#$Agility is the #$ScriptPerformanceAttributeType for describing actions in which the performer's whole body moves precisely and in a well-coordinated fashion.")
(comment HockeyStick "The stick with which the puck is manipulated in a Hockey game.")
(comment IndoorActivity "The collection of activities which happen indoors.")
(comment PoliticalDispute "A specialization of both #$PoliticalEvent and #$DisputeEvent: the collection of all political disputes, including serious political controversies and skirmishes between individuals, organizations or countries. Such disputes involve some question of public policy, as opposed to purely personal or commercial issues.")
(comment SupervisingFn "The performer of (#$SupervisingFn ARG1) directs, evaluates, and oversees instances of ARG1.")
(disjointWith LegalCorporation SoleProprietorship)
(comment BirthControlEvent "The collection of events in which the actor tries to prevent conception from occurring.")
(disjointWith ImageBackground ImageForeground)
(comment LevelOfMentalActivity "A collection of attributes.  Instances of #$LevelOfMentalActivity denote the various intensities of mental effort with which agents perform activities.  #$LevelOfMentalActivity may include levels of exertion represented by non-atomic terms (NATs) such as (#$HighAmountFn #$LevelOfMentalActivity), as well as #$ConcentratingMentalActivityLevel and #$AlertMentalActivityLevel.  All of those intensities are treated as ordered intervals and must be related appropriately; see #$ScalarInterval for more detail.  See also #$GenericValueFunction, #$mentalActivityLevel.")
(comment PreparingFoodOrDrink "A specialization of both #$PurposefulPhysicalAction and #$HumanActivity. Each instance of #$PreparingFoodOrDrink is an event in which an instance of #$FoodOrDrink is created.  An instance of #$PreparingFoodOrDrink may be an event in which preparation is done `from scratch', using raw ingredients, or it may be an event in which semi-prepared or `convenience' products (such as cake mixes, margarita mixes, or frozen foods) are used. Typical sub-events (see the predicate #$subEvents) in instances of #$PreparingFoodOrDrink include activities commonly performed by cooks and/or bartenders, including instances of #$ChoppingSomething, #$CookingFood, #$BakingFood, or #$MixingAlcoholicDrinks. Each instance of #$PreparingFoodOrDrink ends when the item prepared is ready to eat.  Notable specializations of #$PreparingFoodOrDrink include #$GrillingFood, #$SteamingFood, and #$PreparingABeverage.")
(comment SabreFencingSportsEvent "Competitive events of sabre fencing for sport, a kind of sword play.")
(comment physicalLogicalSchemaMap "(#$physicalLogicalSchemaMap PHYSICAL LOGICAL) indicates that PHYSICAL is a physical table corresponding to the logical table LOGICAL.")
(comment CommissionedWorker "An instance of #$EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus and specialization of #$Employee. The collection of all instances of #$Employee that are paid on a commission basis for work done.  See also #$HourlyWorker and #$SalariedWorker.")
(comment CharOfHexFn "(#$CharOfHexFn HEX) returns the ascii character corresponding to HEX, where HEX is a hexadecimal number between 0 and 255, represented as a string of length 2 containing the digits 1 through F. Note that many characters in that range are non-printing or may be interpreted as control characters when displayed by some programs. This function is useful in dealing with database tables which use such characters (actually, binary values masquerading as character fields) to encode other content.")
(comment TakingAUrineSample "The collection of events in which urine is removed from an animal's body, usually in order to be tested.")
(comment JumpSuit "The collection of jump suits, a kind of one-piece garment with long sleeves and legs, usually with a zipper in the front")
(comment RadiologyFacility "An organization which has the facilities to treat and diagnose patients through use of X-rays, radioisotopes and non-ionizing radiation.  The organization may be as informal as a suborganization of some more formal organization, including the qualified medical care professionals and equipment necessary to properly use radiation in the treatment of patients.")
(comment Bread-Slice "A slice of #$Bread.")
(comment disadvantagedIn "ARG1 has some disadvantage or handicap while attempting to succeed at ARG2.")
(comment HomeNursingServiceOrganization "An organization which provides nurses on a temporary basis for home care.")
(comment bannedFromBy "The agent ARG1 is banned from the event/action ARG2 by the agent ARG3.")
(comment contractPrice "The sales contract (item) Arg 1 stipulates the price Arg 3 for the type of product Arg 2.")
(disjointWith Stairway PathForWheeledVehicles)
(comment IBOAboutEvent "The collection of IBOs which are event-centered.")
(comment paymentOutForType "ARG1 makes payments for events of type ARG2 during time ARG3 of total ARG4.")
(comment Northwest-Directly "An instance of #$GeographicalDirection-Direct (q.v.).  #$Northwest-Directly is directly Northwest (from a given point of reference).")
(comment CalendarHour "An instance of #$CalendarCoveringType, and a specialization of #$Date.  Each instance of #$CalendarHour is an hour in some particular calendar.  Instances of #$CalendarHour include (#$HourFn 12 (#$DayFn 20 (#$MonthFn #$January (#$YearFn 1965)))) and (#$HourFn 13 (#$DayFn 13 (#$MonthFn #$July (#$YearFn 2000)))).")
(disjointWith PublishedMaterial NonPublishedText)
(comment MechanicalPositionConnection "A unit which is there to represent the relation between 2  entities which cannot be expressed thro a single slot.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentEvent MedicalCareEvent)
(comment AbsoluteValueFn "#$AbsoluteValueFn is the unary mathematical function that returns the absolute value of its argument; e.g., (#$AbsoluteValueFn -2) returns 2, and (#$AbsoluteValueFn 2) returns 2.")
(comment paidForIn "A binary predicate which connects a #$MoneyTransfer event to the event in which the debt was incurred. (#$paidForIn BUYING PAYING) means that the #$MoneyTransfer PAYING settled the debt incurred in the #$Event BUYING.")
(comment PharmacyProductType-Level2 "The collection of types of drug products that may be specified as to administration route, dosage form, and type of preparation (the drug product(s) contained), but are not specified as to strength or packaging.")
(comment Flexibility "The flexibility level of an animal.")
(comment TennisRacket "The hand-held racket used to hit the ball in tennis.")
(comment WorkAgreement "A specialization of both #$Agreement and #$Obligation.  Each instance of #$WorkAgreement is an agreement between an employer and an employee, regarding the duties and remuneration which pertain to that employee's job for that employer.  Instances of #$WorkAgreement consist of various #$subAgreements, typically including instances of #$JobDescription, #$CompensationPackage, and some #$CodeOfConduct. See also #$employedAgent, which relates instances of #$WorkAgreement to instances of #$Employee, and #$jobAgreement, which relates instances of #$WorkAgreement to instances of #$HasPositionRelationship.")
(comment Waitperson "A #$Person who serves as a waiter or waitress.")
(comment Miscarriage "A natural ending of a pregnancy, which is not a #$BirthEvent.")
(comment ImageForeground "The collection of foregrounds of visual images.  The foreground is a more or less distinct region of space displayed or depicted in an image.  The foreground is the region apparently `closer to' the viewer of the image.  Every #$ImageForeground is part of the DepictedSpace of an image.")
(comment physicalActivityLevel "The predicate #$physicalActivityLevel relates a particular action to the specific #$LevelOfPhysicalActivity that its agent has while doing it.  (#$physicalActivityLevel ACT LEVEL) means that the agent who does the #$AnimalActivity ACT uses the #$LevelOfPhysicalActivity LEVEL in doing ACT.  Default rules may be used to infer that in general an agent has the specific #$LevelOfPhysicalActivity characteristic of those who perform some type of activity; e.g., instances of #$BoxingCompetition require #$ExtremePhysicalActivityLevel.")
(comment MotorcyclingSportsEvent "the collection of all #$SportsEvents in which participants ride on #$Motorcycles.  This includes motorcyle races as well as events in which contestants jump their bikes over things.")
(comment taxIDNumber "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates instances of #$Person to instances of #$IDString. (#$taxIDNumber PER NUM) means that PER's uniquely identifying number for tax purposes is NUM.")
(comment MobOfFeathers "Group of feathers")
(comment BalanceBeamSportsEvent "The collection of gymnastic events on the BalanceBeam.")
(comment databaseAccessIdentifier "(#$databaseAccessIdentifier A B) indicates that B is an access identifier used for the physical database ARG1.")
(comment Liter "The measurement function used in Cyc to represent the standard unit of capacity in the Metric system (and also in Cyc). See also #$UnitOfVolume, #$MKSUnitOfMeasure, #$UnitOfMeasure.")
(comment MammographicBreastCancerScreening "The entire event in which a mammogram is performed and potentially follow-up testing, such as a biopsy")
(comment Vest "The set of all vests.")
(disjointWith MedicalCareInstitution RadiologyFacility)
(comment ImageTypeCollectionType "The collection of all types of visual image types.  Instances are collections of collections.")
(comment Touched-Feeling "The feeling of being emotionally touched. Something that is stirring, touching or moving.")
(comment IntensiveCareUnit "A subOrg of a hospital in which critical patients are treated - there is a higher staffing level, there is more emergency equipment there than in other wards.")
(comment SocialRitual "A specialization of both #$SocialGathering and #$Ritual.  Each instance of #$SocialRitual is a ritual performed by two or more people.  Specializations of #$SocialRitual include #$GraduationCeremony, #$AwardsCeremony, #$Parade, and #$Funeral.")
(comment contractProductType "Sales governed by ARG1 involve the purchase of instances of ARG2.")
(comment NarrativeStyle "One of the ways a body of written material is presented. Narrative style implies that someone is telling the story as if they were physically telling (or narrating) it to the audience, without striving for an objective opinion, or attempting to present other points of view unless they (the narrator) feel like it.")
(disjointWith Tap-FlowControlDevice PathForWheeledVehicles)
(comment prescribedDrugType "ARG1 is a doctor's prescription which authorizes (and recommends) the named patient to purchase and use a specified substance ARG2 (although not a particular instance of that substance).")
(comment paymentIn "Agent ARG1 is paid (for a debt incurred in event ARG2) at time ARG3 the amount of money ARG4.")
(comment Southwest-Directly "An instance of #$GeographicalDirection-Direct (q.v.).  #$Southwest-Directly is directly Southwest (from a given point of reference).")
(comment OutpatientDepartment "The collection of outpatient units in hospitals -- suborganizations of the hospital that provide outpatient care.")
(comment CalendarWeek "An instance of #$CalendarCoveringType and a specialization of #$Date.  Each instance of #$CalendarWeek is a particular week on some particular calendar.  Instances of #$CalendarWeek include the first week (i.e. the initial seven-day-long #$TimeInterval) of December, 2001.")
(comment HumanTypeByLifeStageType "A collection of collections.  #$HumanTypeByLifeStageType is the collection of specializations of #$HomoSapiens that are each collections of humans of a single age group.  This collection exists to make it easier to refer specifically to that dimension or facet of a human being's behavior, attitudes, and beliefs (culture) which derives from, or is influenced by, its life stage.")
(comment Moral-AesopKind "Moral of a story or fable.  This piece of information is the lesson or the 'greater truth' which is a part of the larger InformationThing (usually some sort of Narrative --like a fable, a story, or a parable.")
(comment AdjectiveModifyingFrame "This frame is used for adverbs which modify adjectives. Example: 'very', as in 'He is very happy'.")
(comment Celebration "The collection of acts of celebrating. For example, jumping for joy.")
(comment VideoGamePlaying "The process of Playing a video game")
(disjointWith TimeInterval SomethingExisting)
(disjointWith YardWork MedicalCareEvent)
(comment Face-MainSurface "The main or most important surface of certain object.  Cliffs and watches for example have these kinds of faces.  Probably the faces of a cube are not this kind of a face.  Should #$FaceOfAnimal be a spec of this?  I guess so.  This units existence and meaning is driven by NL utility.  It was created for face of a cliff.")
(disjointWith MovieShowingAtATheater LiveEntertainment)
(comment SubLVariable "The subcollection of #$SubLSymbol whose instances are variables in SubL.  Every #$ELVariable is also a #$SubLVariable.  Note that this collection is \"quoted\" (see #$quotedCollection).")
(comment PharmacyProductType-Level3 "The collection of types of drug products that may be specified as to strength, administration route, dosage form, and type of preparation (the drug compounds(s) contained), but are not specified as to packaging. ")
(comment LowlandsAltitude "The span of altitude from sea level to the point where most people begin to feel the thinness of the air.")
(comment SenseOfBalance "The sense of balance of an animal.")
(comment SententialConstituent "A sentential constituent is a possible part of a natural language sentence, such as a noun phrase or verb phrase.")
(comment BobsledSportsEvent "The collection of bobsled competitions")
(comment Navigating "The collection of all events in which the performer determines the location of an object in some frame of reference, and determines the direction the object should travel to reach some destination.  Navigating usually involves using some devices (compass, clock, etc.) as aids")
(disjointWith MakingAnAgreement EntertainmentEvent)
(comment scheduleFor "Schedules can be for SomethingExistings (including people and businesses) or SomethingOccurrings.  Usually for a Schedule unit, the slot #$scheduleFor will contain actions that are supposed to adhere to the schedule, and objects that are supposed to be actors in those actions.  Just because some object is an actor in an event that adheres to a schedule is not reason enough for the schedule to be #$scheduleFor that actor.  For example, AirlineFlight007 is scheduledIn Schedule007.  I take along a magazine, which is a transportee in that flight.  The magazine is not scheduledIn Schedule007.")
(comment MainVerb "The collection of verbs, excluding auxiliary verbs and modals (but including participles).")
(disjointWith HumanAdult Embryo)
(comment maxAbstinenceTime "ARG4 is the amount of time which ARG1 usually goes without playing the role ARG3 in a situation of type ARG2.")
(comment legRelayerOrder "Which leg a certain runner runs in a relay race")
(comment TownSized "Smaller than a city, larger than a stadium")
(comment SmallRifle3PosShootingSportsEvent "A marksmanship sports event in which small bore rifles are used in three different positions.")
(comment MedicalPlanTypeByAdministration "Instances of #$MedicalPlanTypeByAdministration are types of medical plans characterized by how they are administered.")
(comment amountOfPrecipitation "This is one attribute of an object (often the object is actually a place and time) that indicates the amount of Precipitation associated with it.")
(comment requestStatement "#$requestStatement is a specialization of #$ist-Information.  (#$requestStatement INFO WANTED) means that the #$ELSentence-Assertible WANTED represents some or all of what an agent asks for in the content (INFO) of a request that the agent is making.  See also #$Requesting-CommunicationAct.")
(comment CheckingOutPurchases "What a cashier does as a job: reads price tags, totals the prices of all purchases on a cash register, and receives payment for the purchases.")
(comment Bib "The collection of all bibs, an item of clothing typically worn by babies while eating")
(comment OrthoticEquipmentProvider "An organization which has the euqipment and knowhow to fit patients for and prepare orthotic devidces.")
(disjointWith CarRacing HarvestingAPlant)
(comment Rocking "Repetitive tipping back and forth (or side to side) along a (normally vertical) plane with a somewhat regular rhythm.  The motion is constrained by the surface of the object being rocked.  Each unidirectional rock is equivalent to a time slice of a #$SurfaceConstrainedRotation event.  The motion of a #$RockingChair, rocking horse, or a #$Watercraft being rocked by the waves are examples of #$Rocking.  For rocking on a solid surface there is no #$Slipping betwen the rocking object and the surface.  The somewhat similar motion in a #$Chair-PieceOfFurniture whose seat pivots on an #$IntrinsicAxisOfObject, but whose legs remain firmly on the supporting surface is technically not #$Rocking, but #$Swinging (about the pivot).  #$Rocking is normally limited in angular extent by the shape of the object.  The limit being exceeded will normally cause #$TippingOver or a #$CapsizingEvent, not #$SurfaceConstrainedRotation.")
(comment rootsFor "ARG1 roots for ARG3 in the event ARG2. Use instead of #$positiveVestedInterest where appropriate.")
(comment MedicalClinic "A medical organization composed of several doctors and support staff, but where the doctors are not the sole administrators.")
(comment Loyalty "Combination of Respect and Faithfulness to something or someone .")
(comment SalesContractItem "Often a part of some larger #$SalesContract; each #$SalesContractItem is an agreement about the sale of some particular type of product.")
(comment paymentOut "Agent ARG1 pays (for a debt incurred in event ARG2) at time ARG3 the amount of money ARG4.")
(comment West-Directly "An instance of #$GeographicalDirection-Direct (q.v.).  #$West-Directly is due West (from a given point of reference).")
(comment PharmaceuticsAndTherapeuticsCommittee "The collection of all committees that set treatment and formulary policy for an HMO or other medical care organization.")
(comment Fable "A short allegorical story intended to convey a moral")
(comment AdverbModifyingFrame "This frame is used for adverbs which modify other adverbs. Example: 'very', as in 'He ran very slowly'.")
(comment SoccerTeam "The collection of organizations of athletes who play soccer.")
(comment Tuxedo "The collection of all tuxedos, a kind of attire for very formal or very frivolous occasions")
(disjointWith ImportExportEvent MedicalCareEvent)
(disjointWith CommercialActivity PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment Footprint "A collection of visual marks.  Each element of #$Footprint is an impression made by a foot of an animal.  Footprints may be made in soft earth, clay, concrete, or on paper with paint or ink.  Footprints may be made accidentally or on purpose.")
(comment MovieShowingAtATheater "See mts for different perspectives of this event.")
(disjointWith PoundingDrivingSomething Sewing)
(comment FallingOffAConveyance "Falling out of a transportation vehicle, e.g. a luge, a bobsled, or a horse.")
(comment RasterArray "Arrays used for storing rasters, mon.")
(comment RowingSportsEvent "Rowing sports events, of the kind in the Olympic Games.  In the Olympics, all the men's events are on a 2000-meter course and all the women's events are on a 1000-meter course.")
(comment Swastika "Originally (and still) a Hindu symbol of auspiciousness/good luck, believed to have come originally from the pictogram denoting a flock of geese in flight.  In the 20th century, it is appropriated by Nazi theorists as a symbol of Aryan supremacy.  Because of Nazi beliefs and atrocities, the swastika is now a symbol of right-wing German nationalism and anti-semitism, etc.")
(disjointWith MovieShowingAtATheater Meeting-SocialGathering)
(comment WorkNeed "A collection whose instances contain bundles of propositions about needs of an agent related to their work. Some of the assertions in #$WorkNeed instances will come from baseMts which are work-related obligations.  Work-related obligations are obligations either: 1) arising from the commands of superiors, 2) arising from accepting the requests of superiors, or 3) arising from the work agreement itself.")
(comment AuxVerb "The collection of auxiliary verbs, including 'have', 'be', and 'do', as well as the modal verbs.  All of these can be inverted in questions, and have other distributional peculiarities.")
(comment TimeOfDay "A specialization of #$TimeInterval.  Each instance of #$TimeOfDay is a temporal interval marking a particular time of the day.  Notable specializations of #$TimeOfDay include #$CalendarHour, #$DaytimeWorkingHours, #$TimeOfDay-AM, and #$TimeOfDay-PM.")
(comment AlertMentalActivityLevel "An attribute; an element of the collection #$LevelOfMentalActivity.  #$AlertMentalActivityLevel represents the level of mental activity which is required to perform voluntary physical actions, such as handling a fork, and basic mental-and-physical activities, such as talking.")
(comment Nickname "Names used for individuals that do not fall into a category of common given names like Betty or Liz.  They often are based on some notable characteristic of the referent ('Red' for a red-headed person, 'The Refrigerator' for a very large person).")
(comment perceivedPropositions "(#$propositionsPerceived PERCEIVING PROP) means that in the #$Perceiving event PERCEIVING, the perceiver mentally grasps the proposition(s) PROP.  E.g., ten people witness a particular car crash, and yet each one gets their own particular set of propositions which they later can relate to the police; there are ten separate #$Perceivings in this case, and each one has its own unique set of #$propositionsPerceived.")
(comment CommonCold "A specialization of #$RespiratoryAilment and #$ViralInfection. Each instance of #$CommonCold is an ailment condition whose conditions may include sneezing, sore throat, stuffed-up or runny nose, possibly coughing.")
(comment LightweightWeightliftingSportsEvent "A weight class of WeightliftingSportsEvent")
(disjointWith TimePoint CalendarHalfCentury)
(comment componentIF "The predicate #$componentIF is used to indicate that portion of the content of a communication which represents the illocutionary force of the communication--that is, how the speaker wants the listener to understand, and respond to, the situation described in the communication.  (#$componentIF PIT IF) means that the #$PropositionalInformationThing PIT, which represents the entire content of a communication, includes the #$IllocutionaryForce IF.  For example, a PIT with the content `Jerry does the dishes' might be presented with an IF that belongs to any one of the following subsets of #$IllocutionaryForce: (1) #$Query (`Is Jerry doing the dishes?'), (2) #$Request (`Jerry, will you do the dishes?'), (3) #$Offer (Jerry: `I'll do the dishes if you want'), (4) #$Promise (Jerry: `I will do the dishes'), etc.")
(comment mentionsTT "The Microtheory ARG1 mentions, or actually 'constrains' might be a better description, the #$RoleReferentTheTerm ARG2.")
(comment MedicalPatient "A specialization of #$Animal and #$SocialBeing. Each instance of this collection is an animal undergoing some form of medical care  (cf. #$MedicalCareEvent). This includes routine examinations (cf. #$MedicalTesting) as well as treatment for injuries or illnesses. Two important specializations of this collection are #$Inpatient and #$Outpatient.")
(comment Sweater "The collection of all sweaters")
(disjointWith MedicalCareInstitution OrthoticEquipmentProvider)
(comment UnaryFunction "A specialization of both #$FixedArityFunction and #$UnaryRelation (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$UnaryFunction is a function that always takes a single argument, i.e. has an arity (see #$arity) of 1.")
(comment TighteningAConnection "A collection of events.  In each #$TighteningAConnection event, a connection between two (or more) objects (or parts of one object) is made more rigid or secure by increasing the tension in some aspect of the connection.  E.g., tightening the connection between two pipes by screwing them together more firmly; pulling a knot tighter; fitting a cork more securely into a wine bottle.")
(comment rootsAgainst "(#$rootsAgainst PERSON WHEN AGENT) means that PERSON (an instance of #$IntelligentAgent) roots against AGENT during WHEN (which can be a #$TimeInterval or #$Event). Use instead of #$negativeVestedInterest where appropriate.")
(comment InvestmentFirm "A service organization with the main function of making investments for, and providing investment advice to, customers/clients.")
(comment WavingSomething "The set of actions in which a performer holds something (e.g., a flag) that s/he waves back and forth, esp. in a crowd of people.")
(comment FirstPersonNarrative "A narrative style which indicates that there is one person speaking, as if they were telling a story (or plot), versus a speaker/narrator who is also a part of a story.")
(disjointWith GutterOnARoof PathForWheeledVehicles)
(comment consultants "Entries consult for the Organization ARG1.")
(comment EventOfIBOFn "This NAT results in the central event which an #$IBOAboutEvent concerns.")
(comment cashAssetsOfAgent "The total value of all money immediately available to the agent.")
(comment Northeast-Directly "An instance of #$GeographicalDirection-Direct (q.v.).  #$Northeast-Directly is directly Northeast (from a given point of reference).")
(comment AOANumber "The collection of all AOA numbers, an identifying number assigned to a physician by the American Osteopathy Association.")
(comment HoursDuration "A #$UnitOfTime function that takes one or two real numbers as argument(s) and returns, as its value, a comparable #$Time-Quantity attribute measured in hours.  More precisely: an expression of the form (#$HoursDuration NUM) denotes a (\"point-like\") #$Time-Quantity of being exactly NUM hours in duration; an expression of the form (#$HoursDuration MIN MAX) denotes a (properly interval-like) #$Time-Quantity of being at least MIN hours and most MAX hours in duration.")
(comment Logo "An image which is used to denote an organization, product type, etc. It is often copyrighted, and is used on product packaging, stationery, advertising, etc. Examples include the NBC 'peacock' mark and the five interlocking rings that symbolize the Olympic Games.")
(comment ClauseModifyingFrame "This frame is used for adverbs which modify clauses. Example: 'fortunately', as in 'Fortunately, they arrived on time'.")
(comment AudioTapeRecording "Recording audio sounds onto an #$AudioCassette tape")
(comment Prince-HeadOfState "The collection of all sovereign #$Princes of countries, which are usually monarchies and always Principalities.")
(comment StagePerformer "The professional person who performs on stage and is usually watched by an audience.  The performer might be an actor, singer, musician, etc...")
(comment ProductionArea "The space in a building where manufacturing (the transformation operations mentioned in ProductionLine) occurs.  Typically enclosed (walls and a roof) with loading docks, and with all necessary tools and workstations supplied for the workers.")
(comment InformationRemoving "A specialization of #$InformationUpdating.  Each instance of #$InformationRemoving is an event in which information is removed from some information-bearing object (see the collection #$InformationBearingObject), so that after the event the remaining information content of the information-bearing object is only a proper part of what it started out to be.  Notable specializations of #$InformationRemoving include #$DeletingAFile and #$EliminatingAComputerVirus.")
(comment NounPremodifierFrame "This frame is for adjectives which can take a nominal premodifier. Example: 'He is six feet tall.'")
(comment SportsJudge "The collection of official reviewers who produce the scores in JudgedSportsEvents, following complex rules and making aesthetic judgments about the quality of sports performances in those events.")
(comment IncurringEquipmentDamage "The collection of events in which some piece of equipment gets damaged or broken.")
(comment FencingSportsEvent "Competitive events of fencing for sport, a kind of sword play.")
(comment CatholicPriest "The collection of all Roman Catholic priests")
(disjointWith PhysicalTransformationEvent MovieShowingAtATheater)
(comment MaintenanceSchedule "Instances contain axioms describing maintenance events which are supposed to be performed on a particular device.  MaintenanceSchedules describe not only what is done in these events but their timing, etc.")
(comment TransitiveForNPInfinitivePhraseFrame "This frame is used for verbs and adjectives which can be used with a 'for-NP-infinitival' phrase. Examples: 'I would hate for him to leave' and 'I would be happy for you to join us'.")
(disjointWith TimeOfDay CalendarMonth)
(comment ConcentratingMentalActivityLevel "An attribute; an element of the collection #$LevelOfMentalActivity.  #$ConcentratingMentalActivityLevel represents the level of mental activity required for understanding, analyzing, and conceptualizing, as in instances of #$PlayingChess, #$DebuggingAComputerProgram, #$Surgery, #$MusicalPerformance, and (one would hope) (#$RepairingFn #$Automobile).")
(comment SportsCategoryType "The Collection whose instances are sports catagories. This is a narrower concept than SportsEventType. A SportsCategoryType is a collection of sports events that all involve the same types of activities are and intrinsically similar. Thus Run-800Meter is too narrow to be a SportsCategoryType, QuickBurstSport is too broad, and TrackSportsEvent is just right.")
(comment DownhillSkiingSportsEvent "An alpine skiing event with a long steep hill and very few gates")
(disjointWith TimeOfDay CalendarHalfCentury)
(comment commandStatement "#$commandStatement is a specialization of #$ist-Information.  (#$commandStatement INFO COMMANDED) means that the #$ELSentence-Assertible COMMANDED represents some or all of what the agent orders to be done in the content (INFO) of a command that the agent is making.  See also #$Ordering-CommunicationAct.")
(comment incomeToAccount "This is a predicate for indicating regular payments to an Agent's (ARG1) account: ARG4 is added to ARG1's ARG2 at ARG3 intervals. The mt in which this assertion is made will indicate which agent is paying into the account.  For example to say that JaneDoe gets $1000 in salary twice a month:  (#$incomeToAccount JaneDoe #$SalaryAccount #$TwiceMonthly (#$Dollar-UnitedStates 1000))")
(comment Advertising "A specialization of #$CommunicationAct-Single. Each instance of this collection consists of some communication to potential clients of an #$Organization, the desire of the organization that they be its clients. The organization may be a #$Business wanting people to do business with it (cf. the more specific #$Advertising-Business). Or it may be, for example, a #$PoliticalParty (cf. the more specific #$Advertising-Political). See also #$AdvertisingCampaign.")
(comment Suspenders "The collection of all suspenders, an article of clothing used to hold up pants and sometime -- decoratively -- skirts")
(comment RehabilitationFacility "An organization (may just be part of some other, more formal organization) which has the expertise and equipment to provide rehabilitation and physical therapy services.")
(comment Irony "The feeling or tone of something that points to something that is the opposite of what is expected or considered appropriate.")
(comment AutoRentalCompany "Organizations (usually national or statewide) with local offices that allow customers/clients to rent (the use of) automobiles or other road vehicles.  (examples:  Hertz, Budget, Avis)")
(comment WavingAHand-Gesture "The set of actions in which the performer moves a hand (or both hands) back and forth as a friendly greeting to an individual or to a crowd of people.")
(comment MicroPhysicalProcess "Every MechanicalProcess involves some types of forces acting on some objects, changing their position, velocity, exchanging energy with each other, etc.")
(comment DitransitiveNP-InfinitivePhraseFrame "This frame is used for words that take exactly two complements, the first of which is an NP and the second an infinitive phrase. In HPSG terms: [COMPS  <NP, VP[infinitive]>] Example: 'I told him to make a sandwich'.")
(disjointWith ElectricalDevice Bicycle)
(comment collaborators "(#$collaborators AGENT1 AGENT2) means that AGENT2 collaborates with AGENT1, and vice versa.")
(comment paymentInForType "Payments are made to ARG1 for events of type ARG2 during time ARG3 of total ARG4.")
(comment Southeast-Directly "An instance of #$GeographicalDirection-Direct (q.v.).  #$Southeast-Directly is directly Southeast (from a given point of reference).")
(comment basicPriceForType "This is a type-level predicate corresponding to #$basicPrice. Many billing schemes are defined at the type level. The price of fuel in the US, for example, is measured in dollars per gallon, which means that any particular gallon of fuel will cost a certain amount of dollars. Formally this is (#$basicPriceForType #$GasolineFuel (#$PerFn #$Dollar-UnitedStates #$Gallon-US)). ")
(comment summarizes "Denotes the information things which this information thing is actually just a summary of")
(comment VerbPhraseModifyingFrame "This frame is used for adverbs which can modify verb phrases by either right-attaching them or left-attaching them. Example: 'slowly', as in 'He ate slowly'.")
(comment TrackRelayRace "The collection of relay races whose PlayingOfs #$eventOccursAt a #$RunningTrack.")
(comment PlayingAMusicalInstrument "The set of events in which a single person uses a single #$MusicalInstrument as the #$deviceUsed to produce #$Music (or at least an #$AudibleSound).  Thus an #$Orchestra playing is not an instance of this.  But the first violinist's playing, a #$subEvents of the whole orchestra's playing is a #$PlayingAMusicalInstrument.  Two people playing a piano duet is a music making event which has two #$PlayingAMusicalInstrument #$subEvents.  Note: see also #$InstrumentPlayingFn which is used to denote e.g. the collection of all tuba playing events as (#$InstrumentPlayingFn #$Tuba)")
(comment IntelligenceLevel "How intelligent an agent is")
(comment PrimaryCareEvent "Mostly defined by being disjoint from all the specialized kinds of medical care, such as #$HospitalCareEvent, #$EmergencyMedicalTreatment, etc.")
(disjointWith HumanInfant PunkRocker)
(comment StageProduction "#$StageProduction is the collection of instances of #$EntertainmentPerformance which occur on a stage.")
(disjointWith InformationAdding InformationRemoving)
(comment Curiosity "The collection of feelings of intellectual interest, desire to know (more), to understand (more about) a thing.")
(comment BoycottingAnEvent "The collection of events in which an agent who is eligible to participate in some event chooses not to participate for reasons of protest.  The protest often involves a disagreement with the organization running or sanctioning the event.")
(comment ActingSafely "Being safe in your actions.")
(comment TableTennisPaddle "The flat hand-held paddle used to hit the ball in ping-pong.")
(comment ClassMeeting "a group of students meet with their teacher, and learn.")
(disjointWith SeparationEvent MovieShowingAtATheater)
(comment Warranty "A specialization of #$AuthorizedAgreement.  Each instance of #$Warranty is an agreement between the seller (and/or manufacturer) and the purchaser of some object or service.  In a warranty, the seller/manufacturer promises that the object or service will be satisfactory in some indicated way (e.g., free of defects).  Usually a warranty specifies what compensation an unsatisfied purchaser is entitled to (e.g., free repairs, a refund), and how s/he can claim it.")
(comment PrivatelyHeldCorporation "#$PrivatelyHeldCorporation is a specialization of #$PrivatelyHeldOrganization and #$LegalCorporation.  Each instance of #$PrivatelyHeldCorporation is an incorporated business whose stock, if it exists, is not traded publicly on any stock exchange. Businesses that are traded publicly are instances of #$PubliclyHeldCorporation.")
(comment Dew "The water residue that one finds coating things outdoors in the morning.")
(disjointWith TimeOfDay CalendarYear)
(comment InattentiveMentalActivityLevel "An attribute; an element of the collection #$LevelOfMentalActivity.  #$InattentiveMentalActivityLevel represents the level of mental activity which takes place during physiological processes and other activities in which the agent is absentmindedly engaged, as in instances of #$Yawning, #$Sleeping, all #$InvoluntaryBodyMovements, #$HoldingHands, etc.")
(comment Insignia "A collection of symbolic objects.  Each element of #$Insignia is a visual configuration conventionally associated with some organization, person, or other agent.  Elements of #$Insignia include monograms, company logos, devices of heraldry, totems, the official seals of universities, etc.")
(comment InterCityDistance "A collection of distances.  Each element of #$InterCityDistance is a distance between between two cities.")
(comment MiddleHeavyweightWeightliftingSportsEvent "A weight class of WeightliftingSportsEvent")
(comment subGoals "(#$subGoals G SUB) means that SUB is a subordinate goal of G.  In other words, SUB is an intermediate objective or milestone to be accomplished in the course of pursuing the overall #$Goal G.")
(disjointWith FiscalYear CalendarHalfCentury)
(comment overlapFraction "#$overlapFraction(COLL SETEXP N) states that the fraction of the instances of collection COLL which are also elements of the set SETEXP is N.  Thus, you can state things like 52% of people are female as (#$overlapFraction Person (#$FemalePerson allInstances) 0.52)")
(comment NeckTie "The collection of neck ties, a type of clothing worn around the neck under the shirt collar, and hanging down the front of the wearer's shirt for decoration")
(comment OpticalShop "The collection of organizations which grind lenses, usually for glasses.  Every #$OpticalRetailer may not be an #$OpticalShop, but some might. ")
(comment coExtensional "A #$TaxonomicSlotForCollections (q.v.) that holds between collections whose extents (see #$extent) are exactly the same. (#$coExtensional COL1 COL2) means that COL1 and COL2 have all their elements in common: every instance of (see #$isa) one is an instance of the other.  Note that since collections (see #$Collection), unlike mathematical sets (see #$Set-Mathematical), are \"intensionally defined\", two collections can be coextensional without thereby being identical (see #$equals).  See also 
#$coextensionalSetOrCollections.")
(comment Streptococcus "A collection of #$Bacterium forming a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These are #$Bacterium-Immotile, #$CoccusBacterium, and #$NonSporeFormingBacterium and metabolize fermentatively.  They are also catalase negative and not acid-fast.  This genus includes several species pathogenic for humans.")
(comment USWorkVisa "A U.S. work visa, permission form the U.S. government for a non-citizen to work in the country.")
(comment IceCreamShop "The collection of local establishments that sell exclusively ice cream, usually in small quantities that can be eaten on or near the premises.")
(comment Disappointment "The attribute-type associated with feeling defeated in expectation or hope. (For the rationale behind treating feelings as types -- i.e. collections -- of attributes, see the comment on #$Happiness.)")
(comment Hematologist "A hematologist is a doctor who wpecializes in the diagnosis and treatment of blood disorders.")
(comment NuclearCollisionEvent "The impinging of a particle on an atomic nucleus. Can result in an absorption, excitation or elastic collision.")
(comment dbAbbreviationString "The table ARG1 contains a tuple indicating that the character string ARG2 is an abbreviation for the character string ARG3.")
(disjointWith PierAndBeamFoundation PartOfRoomInAConstruction)
(comment PharmacyMedicineLabel "The collection of labels which are attached to medicine containers and tell the name and amount of the drug contained, the instructions for its use, the patient, the doctor, and the pharmacy.")
(comment DeliveryObligation "The class of contexts arising from an agent agreeing to deliver goods/services.")
(comment SpatialThing "A specialization of #$Individual.  The collection of all things that have a spatial extent or location relative to some other #$SpatialThing or in some embedding space.  Note that to say that an entity is a member of this collection is to remain agnostic about two issues.  First, a #$SpatialThing may be #$PartiallyTangible (e.g. #$Texas-State) or wholly #$Intangible (e.g. #$ArcticCircle or a line mentioned in a geometric theorem).  Second, although we do insist on location relative to another spatial thing or in some embedding space, a #$SpatialThing might or might not be located in the actual physical universe.  It is far from clear that all #$SpatialThings are so located: an ideal platonic circle or a trajectory through the phase space of some physical system (e.g.) might not be.  If the intent is to imply location in the empirically observable cosmos, the user should employ this collection's specialization, #$SpatialThing-Localized.")
(comment OrthopedicCare "The treatment or prevention of skeletal problems or deformities.")
(comment amountMoving "The amount (mass, volume, amount of money, whatever) moving in a MovingProcess.")
(comment CrowdMobbingSomeone "The collection of events in which a crowd of people (usually fans) flocks around one or more agents -- a rock group, a winning sports team, an outnumbered group of police officers in a riot situation, etc.")
(comment OftenWhileAwake "The frequency with which things such as walking occur")
(comment DilationAndCurettage "The medical procedure in which a patient's cervix is dilated and the uterus is scraped with a curette.")
(comment HoleMakingProcess "A processes which creates a hole (or #$Cavity) in the #$objectActedOn")
(comment HolidaySeason "Instances of #$HolidaySeason are events which encompass the activities around a #$Holiday (or group of #$Holidays).  The clearest example is #$ChristmasSeason.  While the exact boundaries of a #$HolidaySeason may be vague, it is nonethless a useful concept; in fact, much of the usefulness comes from that very fuzziness: it is hard to define exactly, but there are many things worth saying about it.")
(comment PunkRocker "punkers -- devotees of punk rock music.  Punkers typically wear outlandish clothes and have bizarre hair and jewelry")
(comment StoryTelling "This is the collection of acts of orally communicating a story, as opposed to writing one down.")
(comment ShapingTool "A tool used to shape things to a finer degree than simple straight cuts produced by a CuttingImplement.  Routers, chisels, sandpaper, jigsaws would all be examples.")
(comment InformationAdding "A specialization of #$InformationUpdating.  Each instance of #$InformationAdding is an event in which information is added to the information content of an instance of #$InformationBearingObject (q.v.).  After the action, the instance of #$InformationBearingObject (which is related to the action by #$informationDestination)`has' the new information.  The resulting information content of that instance of #$InformationBearingObject includes both its content immediately prior to the addition, plus the newly added information.  Examples of #$InformationAdding include recording a check in the check register of one's checkbook; taking the next photograph on a roll of film; adding new information to a database.")
(comment NobelPrize "#$NobelPrize is the collection of prizes awarded annually to the person or persons whom Swedish learned societies determine to have done the most significant recent work in physics, chemistry, physiology or medicine, and literature, and to the person who is determined by the Norwegian Parliament to have rendered the greatest service to the cause of peace. They were established by the will of #$AlfredNobel, and are traditionally awarded on December 10th, the anniversary of his death.  A #$NobelPrize for economic sciences was added in 1969, financed by the Swedish National Bank.")
(comment subjectOfWrittenMaterial "This predicate relates a piece of textual material to any of the objects, events, or other #$TemporalThings that it is generally \"about\".  (#$subjectOfWrittenMaterial TEXT SUBJECT) means that SUBJECT is one of the subjects or topics of TEXT.  See also the other specializations of #$containsInformationAbout-Focally.")
(comment TableTennisGame "Games of Table-Tennis, or PingPong.")
(comment Saluting "A gesture indicating respect.  In the US Military, placing the index finger side of the flattened right hand to the brow is the salute used.")
(disjointWith YardWork EntertainmentEvent)
(comment EmotionalNeed "A need that an agent has related to its emotional state.")
(disjointWith TimeOfDay CalendarDecade)
(comment PrideOfMembership "The feeling of pride in belonging to an organization or group.")
(comment TameAnimal "A specialization of #$NonPersonAnimal.  Each instance of #$TameAnimal is a non-human animal that is generally not afraid of humans (so that it will generally not flee when humans approach it), and which will generally not attack humans.  An important specialization of #$TameAnimal is #$DomesticatedAnimal.")
(comment inPreparationFor "(#$inPreparationFor ACT EVENT) means that the #$Action ACT is done in conscious preparation for the #$Event EVENT. ACT starts before EVENT.  ACT may continue after EVENT begins, but it doesn't continue past EVENT.  ACT may be a necessary precondition for EVENT, such as booking a hall or caterers for a wedding reception, but it may also be something incidental, such as dressing up for the reception.  Cf. #$preconditionFor-Events.")
(comment FeatherweightFSWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of FSWrestlingSportsEvent")
(comment FeeForServiceReimbursementPlan "A type of medical insurance plan under which the plan holder pays for services out of his/her pocket, but then is reimbursed by the plan provider (insurer).")
(comment CalendarHalfCentury "An instance of #$CalendarCoveringType, and a specialization of #$Date.  Each instance of #$CalendarHalfCentury is a  half-century on a particular calendar, and thus will be either the first half or the second half of some century (see the constant #$CalendarCentury) on that calendar.  Instances of #$CalendarHalfCentury include #$FirstHalfOf20thCenturyCE and #$LastHalfOf20thCenturyCE.")
(comment AutoAccessoriesMarketCategory "Enhancements for automobiles which are commonly sold together.  Includes stuff like wheel covers, various chrome parts, etc.")
(comment PurchasingAgent "An employee of a company, who gathers product information from vendors, usually through CommercialSalesRepresentatives.  PurchasingAgents might receive PurchaseRequisitionDocuments from within the company and send #$QuoteRequestDocument to vendors.  They then might receive FormalEstimateDocuments from the vendors")
(comment RadioCommercial-IBT "Radio programming which is an advertisement.")
(comment Pantyhose "The collection of all PantyHose")
(comment DirectorOfOrganization "A collection of people.  An instance of #$DirectorOfOrganization is a person who is among the highest leaders of some organization.  Directors are typically charged with responsibility for the financial, administrative, and/or inspirational direction of the #$Organizations which they lead.")
(comment overridingMts "satisfying a role in arg1 takes priority over satsifying the same role in arg2.")
(comment HandlingFn "this function can be used to denote the set of events in which a device of a certain type is handled - in the sense of controlling it.")
(comment ControversialAction "An action that is controversial in the sense that it is opposed and complained about.")
(comment BakeryStore "A retail store which includes a bakery.  It is often also allIO restaurant - there is some place to eat pastries and have coffee.")
(comment Otorhinolaryngologist "An ear, nose and thoat specialist is a doctor who specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of problems with the ears, nose, or throat.")
(disjointWith PartOfRoomInAConstruction SlabFoundation)
(comment pitEnglishCaption "ARG1 is a #$PropositionalInformationThing which contains assertions describing the `content' of a (set of) #$InformationBearingObject(s).  ARG2 is a list of strings which can be or have been parsed to generate the CycL content assertions in ARG1.")
(comment authorizationFor "ARG1 authorizes the owner (bearer?) to perform the restricted activity ARG2.")
(comment MedicalCareProfessional "A specialization of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each instance of #$MedicalCareProfessional is a person whose occupation principally involves medical care of patients, including surgery, psychological care, physical therapy, practical nursing, and dispensing drugs.  Notable specializations of #$MedicalCareProfessional include #$Doctor-Medical, #$Dentist, and #$Pharmacist.")
(comment amountSold "Like #$quantitySold, but for elements of #$ExistingStuffType rather than #$ExistingObjectType.")
(comment ObligatoryReflexiveObjectFrame "This frame is used for transitive words that take exactly one complement which is a reflexive pronominal. In HPSG terms:
  [COMPS  <NP [CONT  reflexive]>] Example: 'He perjured himself'.")
(disjointWith Canoe ElectricalDevice)
(comment SensoryReactionType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$SensoryReactionType is a type of sensation (e.g., pain, pressure, pleasure, or warmth) that may be felt by instances of #$PerceptualAgent (q.v.).  Instances of #$SensoryReactionType include #$LevelOfPain, #$LevelOfDiscomfort, and #$LevelOfRelaxationFeeling.")
(disjointWith InformationTransferEvent HolidaySeason)
(comment Rally "A large gathering of people to show and generate support of a specific cause")
(comment HairStylist "Any professional that cuts human hair for profession.")
(comment WoodworkingTool "Tools used to shape, join, and cut wood, where the wood itself is or forms the desired object.  Includes both chisels and the hammers used to drive the chisels; power routers, sanders, saws, etc.  Does not include nail guns or other carpentry tools  where the wood is simply an included part of a larger structure.  These tools/devices are capable of being used and are designed to be used on wood, but this doesn't preclude their use on other types of materials (having similar textures, properties, etc.) for which they might be suited.")
(comment Frequency "A specialization of #$Rate.  Each instance of #$Frequency is the number of times something happens during some time interval.  Instances of #$Frequency may be either single values (see the collection #$ScalarPointValue), such as 103 kiloHertz, or a range of values, such as #$Rarely.  Note that instances of #$Frequency are important in the characterization of types of #$WavePropagation.")
(disjointWith SelectingSomething IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(comment Picketing "Marching in front of something holding signs in order to persuade others not to support it.")
(comment MicroscopicSized "Something of the size that it cannot be seen with the human eye.")
(comment thresholdOfPain-Pressure "ARG1 feels discomfort or pain in body part(s) of type ARG2 when pressures equal to or greater than ARG3 are applied for an extended period.")
(comment DateRape "Moniker given to cases of rape where the attacker and the victim are acquaintances.")
(disjointWith MovieShowingAtATheater BodyMovementEvent)
(comment WHWord "The collection of all wh-words.  These words generally appear at the beginning of a clause and have an interrogative or relative function.")
(comment RadioactiveStuff "instances are radioactive substances")
(disjointWith TimeOfDay CalendarWeek)
(comment Bar-DrinkingEstablishment "A localized (i.e., at one particular site) organization that serves alcoholic drinks, and possibly food.")
(comment GymnasticsApparatus "A piece of gymnastic equipment used during a routine, where the gymnast's weight is supported by the device, for however short a time.  Does not include the rings and ribbons that are twirled by rhythmic gymnasts.")
(comment Pig-Domesticated "A specialization of #$DomesticatedAnimal and #$Pig.  Each instance of #$Pig-Domesticated is a pig kept on a farm or as a pet.")
(comment HumanResidence "A specialization of #$HumanShelterConstruction.  Each instance of #$HumanResidence is a humanly constructed shelter (or a part of one) in which humans reside.  The collection #$HumanResidence includes residential huts, igloos, longhouses, hotels, barracks, palaces, houseboats, and mobile homes, as well as apartments, duplexes, and detached houses.  A person's residence is typically the place where she/he usually sleeps and keeps most personal effects.")
(comment SideHorseVaultSportsEvent "The collection of gymnastic vaulting events on the side-horse.")
(comment Kilometer "The measurement function used in Cyc to represent the 1000-meter unit used within the Metric system to measure distance.  Modern countries using the metric system measure their roads - and their road races - in kilometers. See also #$MKSUnitOfMeasure, #$UnitOfMeasure.")
(comment HospitalRoomStay "The collection of events in which a person checks into a hospital, stays in a hospital room, and then (usually) checks out again.  Each of these is a subEvent of a #$HospitalCareEvent, which might have other #$subEvents such as Surgery, administration of medicines, etc.")
(comment Garter "The collection of garters, an item of clothing used to hold up some kinds of women's stockings")
(comment SkinContactWithFn "this function can be used to denote the set of events in which a person's skin touches a certain type of thing (given by arg1).")
(comment ControversialAction-Social "An action that is socially controversial.")
(disjointWith IndependentOrganization LocalChainOrganization)
(comment Disqualification "A penalty of automatically losing the game, or not being allowed to compete.")
(comment FamilyPractitioner "A family practitioner is a general practitioner whose patients are of all ages.")
(comment LispHacking "This is a cyclic process.  Study it carefully. - This is not the way we want things done.")
(disjointWith TransportationDevice PlumbingFixture)
(comment MedicalTestResultReport "Documents which convey the results of one or more medical tests.")
(disjointWith Herbivore Carnivore)
(comment assets "Assets are economic resources (things of value) owned by an agent which are expected to benefit future operations.")
(comment DoAux "The auxiliary verb 'do'. It has unique syntactic functions, for example, do-support in yes/no questions, so it is treated as a separate part of speech.")
(comment imports "(#$imports REGION PRODUCT-TYPE) means that the region  REGION regularly imports substantial amounts of the goods or services PRODUCT-TYPE from other regions. ")
(comment ThrillsDrive "Driving a motor vehicle for entertainment.")
(comment Gargling "Swishing a liquid around in your mouth, leaning your head back and keeping the liquid in your throat while exhaling, and then spitting it out.")
(comment IndividualIntelligence "The intelligence aspect of an individual entity")
(comment determinerAgreement "(#$determinerAgreement DET POS-PRED) means that the determiner DET requires that the part of speech of the N-bar it is a specifier of be a spec-pred of POS-PRED.")
(comment Wall-Vertical "A planar object or surface that is by definition vertical.  May have one or two sides;  Two sides walls include  stone walls; Great Wall of China.  One sides walls include cliffs, `the walls in my office'.  Why talk about the latter as one-sided when such walls have two sides? Well, identifying a unique surface facilitates identifying which surface we are talking about when we say, 'the wall of my office is convex').")
(comment HoleMakingTool "Tools used to punch or bore holes in something (typically, an awl).")
(comment LogicalConnective "A collection of mathematical objects, including the basic logical connectives.  Each instance of #$LogicalConnective is a #$Relation which takes one or more truth-valued expressions (sentences) as arguments and returns a truth-valued sentence.  The instances of #$LogicalConnective include #$and, #$or, #$not, and #$implies.")
(comment RunningSportsEvent "A specialization of #$RacingSportsEvent and #$TrackSportsEvent.  Each instance of #$RunningSportsEvent is ann event in which the winning competitor is the individual or team who traverses a certain distance in a specific amount of time.")
(disjointWith SportsPenalizing IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(comment OutdoorSportsEvent "A sport normally held outdoors, although most could possibly be held indoors (most of the boating sports being obvious exceptions).")
(comment highestPossibleScore "The highest possible value that the metricOfEvaluation on this unit could ever return.  For example, allInstances of GymnasticsSportsEvent will have a value of 10 on this slot.")
(comment TooHotToTouch "A temperature that would be #$TooHotToTouch, not WarmToTheTouch and not RoomTemperature.  For humans this is set to 150 degrees Fahrenheit or hotter.")
(comment M3000SpeedSkateSportsEvent "The 3000M speed skating competition")
(comment Rape "A collection of events.  Each element of #$Rape is a violent action in which the performer forces another person to undergo an act of sexual intercourse.  The rape is #$performedBy the #$perpetrator, while the #$victim is #$bodilyActedOn.  (Cf. instances of #$SexualCopulation, in which all participants are #$deliberateActors; i.e., the role relations between actors are completely different.)")
(comment PhysicalNeed "A collection whose instances are mts containing statements that are needs that a particular thing has related to its physical extent.  For example `People need to eat food.'`Gas engines need gasoline.'")
(comment ambientWindDirection "(#$ambientWindDirection X DIR) means that in the vicinity of X the wind is blowing from the direction DIR.")
(disjointWith TimeOfDay CalendarCentury)
(comment Monthly "Used to indicate that something happens regularly about once a month")
(comment AnchorRelayLeg "The last leg of a relay.")
(comment HornPlayer "The collection of people who play a #$BrassInstrument.  Examples include trumpeters, trombonists, tuba-players, etc.")
(comment SoccerField "The large open field where soccer is played.")
(disjointWith CalendarHalfCentury CalendarQuarter)
(disjointWith Communicating HospitalCareEvent)
(comment TVCommercial-IBT "Television programming which is an advertisement.")
(comment RainCoat "The collection of all rain coats")
(comment HumanScaleObject "A specialization of #$PartiallyTangible.  Each instance of #$HumanScaleObject is an object that can be perceived and manipulated by human beings.  Instances of this collection range roughly from objects the size of pinheads to objects the size of aircraft carriers.")
(comment DietingForWeightLoss " Dieting is an activity that spans days, weeks, or months, in which the type of food and drink consumed is healthier and/or the amount is smaller. Disciplined form of eating in which the eater carefully controls what is eaten")
(comment ControversialAction-Political "An action that is politically controversial.")
(comment LocalChainOrganization "A collection of organizations.  An element of #$LocalChainOrganization is an organization which is among the #$subOrganizations of a larger #$ChainOrganization with wider geographic scope.  A local chain organization may be a corporation in its own right while still being a sub-organization of the larger organization whose franchising agreements control or constrain the business operations of the local organization.  Note that a #$LocalChainOrganization need not be a #$SingleSiteOrganization.")
(comment BaseKBPredicate "These predicates should only be asserted in the #$BaseKB.")
(disjointWith SeatingDevice Clock)
(comment Solitude "The state of being alone or remote from society")
(disjointWith Invertebrate Vertebrate)
(comment serviceSold "The service performed for money.")
(comment BeAux "The auxiliary verb 'be'. It has unique syntactic functions, for example, in forming compound tenses, so it is treated as a separate part of speech.")
(comment Pepper-TheSpice "Black granular spice usually in a shaker like salt.")
(disjointWith HavingAMeal DisasterEvent)
(comment PedestrianSportsEvent "Sports events played on foot, not in the water, or on horse-back, or in a boat, etc.")
(comment WithinGraspableDistance "The proximity where the actor is close enough to touch the object in question")
(comment MachineIntelligence "The intelligence aspect of a machine")
(comment urgeSatisfied "(#$urgeSatisfied EVT URGETYPE) means that the sensory event EVT satisfies an instance of a physical urge of type URGETYPE.   Use the predicate, #$urgeTypeSatisfied, to stateg rules about what sorts of actions relieve what sorts of urges.  E.g., scratching relieves an #$UrgeToScratch.")
(comment eventOccursNear "The predicate #$eventOccursNear relates an event to its approximate location.  (#$eventOccursNear EVENT LOC) means that EVENT occurs at or near (see #$near) LOC.  #$eventOccursNear is useful when the more exact location is unknown, hard to specify, or not worth reifying; otherwise use
#$eventOccursAt.  For example, #$eventOccursNear could be used to CycLify
\"Bob was cycling by the dam\", \"We played checkers near the TV\", and \"He is standing by the horse's hind legs\".  See the #$cyclistNotes for ideas on how to formalize this.")
(comment ReligiousCeremony "Generalized religious service, like with a priest or rabbi and congregation.  Not a religious obligation or solitary activity like praying or fasting.")
(comment MassManufacturing "A collection of events.  In a typical #$MassManufacturing event, a mob of the same kind of product is produced in one `production cycle'.  [A `mob' is `a large number.']")
(comment InformationUpdating "A specialization of #$InformationTransferPhysicalEvent.  Each instance of #$InformationUpdating is an event in which the information content of an information bearing object (see the collection #$InformationBearingObject) is altered, either by removing or by adding information.  Important specializations of #$InformationUpdating are #$InformationRemoving and #$InformationAdding.")
(disjointWith Cleaning AdministeringADrug)
(disjointWith SocialGathering IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(comment Vandalism "The intentional damaging or destruction of property which you have no right to damage or destroy.")
(comment WavingArmsInAir "The set of actions in which the performer waves one or both arms.")
(comment HardAsARock "Something that feels hard and unyielding, e.g., #$HardAsARock.")
(comment WelterweightGRWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of GRWrestlingSportsEvent")
(disjointWith TimePoint CalendarWeekend)
(comment StoringFn "The function which returns collections of events in which instances of ARG1 are stored.")
(disjointWith MaintenanceEvent EntertainmentEvent)
(disjointWith TimeOfDay FiscalYear)
(comment ActuallyTouching "This is the proximiity where the actor is so close to an object that he is actually touching it.")
(comment SportsAttempt "In some sports events, a player gets several attempts to perform some action. E.g. in the shot put the best of 3 attempts is taken.")
(disjointWith Massaging PolishingSomething)
(comment EpeeFencingSportsEvent "Competitive events of epee fencing for sport, a kind of sword play.")
(disjointWith CalendarWeek CalendarHalfCentury)
(comment ResaleOrganization "Organizations that purchase (rather than manufacture) their merchandise.")
(comment MovingImageWithSound "The collection of all #$InformationBearingWavePropagations that are artifacts (i.e., instances of #$Artifact-Intangible) and have #$subEvents of #$MovingImages. By default, they have #$SoundInformationBearingThing #$subEvents as well, but there are some exceptions, such as silent movies. This collection includes the visual and audio aspects of movies, tv shows, TV commercials, multimedia presentations, computer games, etc. Some instances are #$MediaProducts, while others are amateur.")
(comment Briefs "The collection of briefs -- short-pant-like undergarments for the lower part of the body")
(comment StomachAcid "#$Acid found in the stomach used in digestion")
(comment BirthControlClinic "A medical clinic which primarily provides birth control to women, but also provides rudimentary gynecological care.")
(disjointWith Fishing ContactSportsEvent)
(comment NeuroPathologist "A neurological pathologist is a doctor who specializes in diagnosing and treating nervous system pathologies.")
(comment Indivisible "The collection of discrete entities without distinguishable parts, portions, entries, subsets, elements,...  A couple examples are:  the #$False truth-value; any single #$MathematicalPoint.")
(comment objectSelected "(#$objectSelected SEL OBJ) means that OBJ, an instance of #$SomethingExisting, is the object chosen in the event SEL, an instance of #$SelectingSomething.")
(comment InsuranceClaimForm "The forms that holders of insurance policies must fill out whenever they make a claim against that insurance.")
(disjointWith Omnivore Herbivore)
(comment HaveAux "The auxiliary verb 'have'. It has unique syntactic functions, for example, in forming compound tenses, so it is treated as a separate part of speech.")
(comment Sweetener "Substances used to sweeten other #$EdibleStuffs.")
(comment generalizedFlow "The Rate at which any #$MovementProcess occurs.")
(comment Bronchitis "A specialization of #$UpperRespiratoryInfection. #$Bronchitis is an inflammation of the lining of the bronchial tubes.  It causes less air to be able to flow to and from the lungs and a heavy mucus or phlegm is coughed up.")
(comment MarksmanshipSportsEvent "A sports event involving marksmanship, the hitting of a target with a projectile weapon, such as archery or target shooting.")
(comment Whistling-Human "The whistling that humans do as opposed to birds, or whistles (the physical device)")
(comment Animal-Intelligence "The intelligence aspect of an animal")
(comment Toughness "Describes how well a material can withstand impact forces.")
(comment Fisherman "one who fishes.")
(comment Packing "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$Packing, some object(s) is/are put into a package.  

Note: Although #$Packing is a type of event, not a type of process, nevertheless one sometimes `packs an item' for shipment by partially disassembling it and then `packing it' in several packages, and that is seen as one single instance of #$Packing, even though each of the individual packages being packed is also seen as a #$Packing.  For a related concept, see #$PackagingEvent.")
(disjointWith IBTGeneration-Original IBTGeneration-Replication)
(comment (VeryHighAmountFn LevelOfFitness) "The physical fitness level of professional athletes or dedicated amateurs (e.g., marathoners), or, among animals, of racehorses or healthy draft animals.")
(comment InferenceRelatedBookkeepingPredicate "A collection of predicates.  Each instance of #$InferenceRelatedBookkeepingPredicate is a predicate involved in assertions used by the Cyc application to direct inferencing.  Examples: #$defnIff, #$defnSufficient, #$termOfUnit, #$afterAdding.")
(comment PoliticalProtesting "A specialization of #$Objecting-CommunicationAct.  In each instance of #$PoliticalProtesting, some individual or group protests some political action by an individual or group.  May include spontaneous acts, such as publicly humming the National Anthem in one's occupied country, as well as formal actions, such as banning South Africa from the Olympics.")
(comment SoftAsAPillow "Something that feels soft and yielding, e.g., #$SoftAsAPillow.")
(comment HockeyField "The large open field where field hockey is played.")
(disjointWith TimeOfDay CalendarWeekend)
(comment DistributionEvent "A specialization of both #$PurposefulPhysicalAction and #$TransferOut.  Each instance of #$DistributionEvent is an event in which tangible objects are distributed from a source to various destinations via some distribution network.")
(comment WithinAudibleDistance "This is the proximity where the actor is close enough in order to properly hear the necessary object.  The actual distance can vary depending upon each individual case.")
(comment transactionID "ARG1 was assigned a unique id ARG2 by ARG3 for transactions of type ARG4 where (ARG5 ARG1 ARG3).  ARG5 is an actor slot.  For example, (#$transactionID DexterOrderingSocksFromLandsEnd 1234 LandsEnd #$RequestingToMakeAPurchase recipient) means that LandsEnd assigned the event DexterOrderingSocksFromLandsEnd an id, 1234, which is unique for the instances of #$RequestingToMakeAPurchase in which LandsEnd is the recipient")
(comment GoingToTheBathroom "The collection of all scripts in which a person uses a facility designed to accept excreta by excreting into the facility.  Other #$subEvents might include opening and closing a lid of the facility and using #$ToiletPaper.")
(comment Swim-100MeterBackstroke "Swimming race - 100 meter backstroke.")
(comment StaffModelHMOPlan "The collection of medical insurance plans offered by staff model HMOs.")
(comment DryingOut "Events in which the water contained in the pores of an object is removed.")
(comment faxNumberText "The predicate #$faxNumberText relates a particular location to the fax number at that location.  (#$faxNumberText LOC NUM) means that NUM is a string denoting (one of) the fax number(s) of the #$ContactLocation LOC.")
(comment Commercial-IBT "Advertisements which are either sound-based or sound-and-pictures-based - the sorts of advertisements aired on radio and television broadcasts.")
(comment BoxerShorts "The collection of boxer shorts.  No, they're not just for men anymore.")
(comment TooGeneral-CycTermStatus "when used to describe an assertion on a unit, indicates the assertion has been made at too general a level.")
(comment WorldPeace "This type of situation is a situation in which the different countries of the world are not in a state of war with each other and, presumably, in which all countries are free of civil war, in other words, situations in which the world is inhabited by agents and free from war. Note that this is a situation type suggesting that those aiming for world peace are seeking to create an *instance* of #$WorldPeace.")
(comment Hospital-Private "A hospital that is not owned or operated by a government entity.  May include non-profit and for-profit hospitals.")
(comment Gasping "Suddenly catching the breath.")
(comment InfectiousDiseaseSpecialist "An infectious disease specialist is a doctor who specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of patients with particularly infectious diseases.")
(comment europeanDiscoveryBy "the first European or group of Europeans to find something")
(comment Poaching "Action in which someone traps or kills a #$NonPersonAnimal without the right permits.")
(comment enablesEventOfType "If agent ARG1 uses the item ARG2, then the agent is capable (all other capabilities allowing) of performing instances of the collection ARG3.")
(comment Agriculture "An activity consisting of a variety of more specific activities involving the husbandry of animals, the planting and harvesting of crops, etc.")
(disjointWith Omnivore Carnivore)
(comment DBQueryInfoType "Instances of this #$Collection are used to organize queries for applications and prototypes that use the predicate #$profileDBQueries (q.v.).")
(comment closerTo "(#$closerTo OBJ NEAR FAR) iff OBJ is closer to NEAR than to FAR.  For example, (#$closerTo #$Sun #$PlanetMercury #$PlanetVenus).")
(comment Singing-Human "The collection of acts of producing #$Music sounds with the human vocal cords.")
(comment MicrosporeGroup "A group of Microspores; ususally inside the anther.")
(comment PublicProtesting "A specialization of #$PoliticalEvent in which one or more participants engage in instances of #$Objecting-CommunicationAct.  Each instance of #$PublicProtesting is a public objection, by an individual or group, to some action or state of affairs.")
(comment hero "Arg2 is a hero in Arg1. Arg2 is a hero according to the residents of Arg1")
(comment HeavyweightWeightliftingSportsEvent "A weight class of WeightliftingSportsEvent")
(comment employedAgent "A binary predicate which relates instances of #$WorkAgreement to instances of #$Employee, and identifies the particular employee who is covered by a particular work agreement.  (#$employedAgent AGREE WORKER) means that AGREE covers the employee WORKER. See also #$jobAgreement, which relates instances of #$WorkAgreement to instances of #$HasPositionRelationship, #$employingAgent and #$employees (which relates employees to their employers).")
(disjointWith Mixture PureSubstance)
(comment ShootingAProjectileWeapon "A specialization of both #$EmittingAnObject and #$DirectedTranslation. In each instance of #$ShootingAProjectileWeapon, a #$ProjectileLauncher (such as a #$Gun) is used to emit and propell a #$ProjectileWeapon (such as a #$BulletAssembly). To indicate the type of #$ProjectileLauncher used in a #$ShootingAProjectileWeapon see #$launcherTypeInShooting. To indicate the type of projectile used, see #$projectileTypeInShooting. To define specializations of #$ShootingAProjectileWeapon by launcher type and by projectile type, see #$ShootingByLauncherTypeFn and #$ShootingByProjectileTypeFn, respectively.")
(comment FlyweightGRWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of GRWrestlingSportsEvent")
(comment FieldCombiningMethod "Instances of #$FieldCombiningMethod are methods for combining component #$LogicalField instances into their composite fields.")
(comment phoneNumberAreaCode "ARG2 is the area code (character string), also known in some countries as the `city code', of the #$ContactLocation ARG1.")
(comment IntensiveCareUnitRoomStay "The collection of events in which a person checks into a hospital, stays in a room in the intensive care ward, and then (usually) checks out again.  Each of these is a subEvent of a #$HospitalCareEvent, which might have other #$subEvents such as Surgery, administration of medicines, etc.")
(comment Brooch "The collection of brooches, a kind of decorative pin often used to attach a scarf")
(comment DayOfWeekType "A collection of collections and a specialization of #$WeeklyTemporalObjectType.
Each instance of #$DayOfWeekType is a collection of #$CalendarDays, all of
whose instances correspond to the same particular \"day of the week\" in 
the respective weeks in which they occur.  For example, #$Monday -- the 
collection of all mondays -- is an instance of #$DayOfWeekType.")
(comment TooSpecific-CycTermStatus "when used to describe an assertion on a unit, indicates the assertion is too specific and should be generalized.")
(comment Condenser "The thing attached to your spark plug wires in a car engine.")
(comment Hospital-Public "A hospital that is owned or operated by a government entity.")
(comment ArcheryRange "Where one typically holds an archery competition.  See #$ArcherySportsEvent.")
(comment VascularSurgeon "A vascular surgeon is a doctor who specializes in correcting blood-vessel-disorders  through surgery.")
(comment exploredBy "(#$exploredBy REGION EXPLORER) means that REGION (an instance of #$GeographicalRegion) has been explored by EXPLORER.")
(comment Quarterly "This refers to a frequency of 4 times a year - every 3 months.")
(comment easeOfPerformanceWith "If agent ARG1 uses the item ARG2, then the ease with which that agent can perform instances of ARG3 becomes ARG4.")
(comment Tourist "People who visit a location (e.g., city) and go sight seeing, shopping for souvenirs, visit the tourist attractions, ride the camels, ...")
(disjointWith FemaleAnimal MaleAnimal)
(comment GuidanceProcess "A specialization of #$ConstrainingEvent.  Each instance of #$GuidanceProcess is an event in which one body (solid or fluid) is guided by another.")
(comment GraduatingEvent "The act of graduating from an educational institution.  Not the same as the ceremony -- participating in the ceremony requires that you graduate, but graduation doesn't require participation in the ceremony.")
(comment objectTypeMoving "The type of object(s) or stuff moving in a MovingProcess.")
(comment Preposition-Temporal "The collection of all prepositions which express temporal relations. Example: 'on', as in 'we arrived on Tuesday'.")
(comment OutOfControlCrowdEvent "The collection of events in which a crowd of people is passing the normal bounds of social control.")
(comment TakingABath "The collection of all taking-a-bath events")
(comment PartialRotationalConnection "The rotational connection - one object may rotate with respect to another in the direction || to the axis of connection. the freedom of rotation is 180 degrees")
(comment PayingACommission "A sales agent is paid for acting as the directingAgent in a completed Buying event; typically the payment is made by the seller in the Buying event.")
(comment orgWithPosition "(#$orgWithPosition REL ORG) means that the #$Organization ORG is the employer in a #$HasPositionRelationship. See also #$JobPosition, #$orgWithJobPosition and #$versionOfJobPosition.")
(comment teammates "'(#$teammates MATE1 MATE2)' means that MATE1 and MATE2 are people on a #$Team together.")
(comment PassingAGameBall "Passing an object (successfully) through the air, along the ground, etc. to a teammate. This includes both the throwing AND the catching. 'Successfully' means that the thrower intends the catcher to be the one who catches the object.")
(comment FlyweightWeightliftingSportsEvent "A weight class of WeightliftingSportsEvent")
(disjointWith CalendarSecond CalendarWeekend)
(comment Journalist "The collection of persons who write for periodicals")
(comment Collecting "A specialization of #$TransferIn.  Each instance of #$Collecting is an event in which tangible or intangible objects are collected together at a single \"place\".  The objects might come from various sources, and might be gathered via some collection network. Notable specializations of this collection include #$GroupingObjects and #$CollectingInformation.")
(comment Shipping "Shipping of objects from one physical location to another. Shipping from the perspective of being done as a dedicated service, such as what UPS, the US Postal Service, or Dominoes Pizza Delivery might do.")
(comment Firework-Display "A specialization of #$PyrotechnicEvent.  Each instance of #$Firework-Display is a colorful, short-lived aftermath of a fireworks explosion.")
(comment SuperGiantSlalomSportsEvent "The downhill super giant slalom competition")
(comment numberOfSpeakersCurrently "A rough guess at the number of native speakers of the language. Can be computed by adding up the groups who speak the language.")
(comment ReleaseOfSupport "The class of actions in which an object is released from support, either by an agent or not.  Before the action the object is supported by something , but afterwards it is not.")
(comment voiceMailNumberText "The entire voice mail number of a contact location represented as a string in a format which phone numbers are typically stated, such as ''(512) 555-3634''")
(comment OfficeVisit "A single visit to a professional in their office.  This may be the only such visit in a consultation, or one of several - which case there will also be an overarching #$ConsultingAnExpert event which this is a #$subEvents of.")
(comment Overalls "The collection of overalls, a kind of one-piece sleeveless garment with long legs and suspenders.  A typical kind of clothing on farms in the midwest (still), and among handymen/women")
(comment SquareCentimeter "A unit of measure for area equivalent to a square with each side of length one centimeter.")
(comment Monday "A collection of #$CalendarDays and an 
instance of #$DayOfWeekType.  #$Monday is the collection of all 
(and only) mondays.")
(comment LevelOfStress "The type of internal feeling or sensation of being stressed out.")
(comment InWrongMicrotheory "when used to describe an assertion on a unit, indicates the assertion has been put in the wrong microtheory.  See also #$repatriateToMt.")
(comment BoxingRing "Where a #$BoxingSportsEvent occurs.")
(comment MedicalResidencyProgramOrganization "Educational programs that are part of some hospital, and that provide advanced training to doctors in various medical specialties.")
(comment discoveredByEuropeansWhen "The date or year of discovery by Europeans.")
(comment competitionExpr "An expression to describe what all the #$competingAgents in this Competition are trying to be the value of.  For example, if this expression were (income ?COMPETITOR (Maximum (C001 #$competingAgents) income)), then each of the agents is competing to have the highest income among the competitors.  Note the use of the special variable ?COMPETITOR - it's used to denote the competingAgent that actually wins the competition.")
(disjointWith Cyclist NonPersonAnimal)
(comment MovementEvent "A specialization of #$GeneralizedTransfer and #$MovementOrShapeChangeEvent (qq.v.).  This is the most general collection of physical movements.  Each instance of #$MovementEvent is an event in which at least one object (see #$objectMoving) either translates some distance or moves from one rotational orientation to another, relative to a frame of reference that is not part of the translating/rotating object.  The movement in question might be periodic or not, continuous or not.  Notable specializations of #$MovementEvent include #$Translocation, #$Movement-Rotation, #$Movement-Periodic, and #$MovementProcess.")
(comment schoolGraduated "The graduation in Arg1 is from the school Arg2.")
(comment SetOrCollection "A specialization of #$MathematicalThing.  Something is an instance of #$SetOrCollection just in case it is a collection (i.e. an instance of #$Collection) or a mathematical set (i.e. an instance of #$Set-Mathematical).  Instances of #$Set-Mathematical and instances of #$Collection (and thus instances of #$SetOrCollection) share some basic common features.  All instances of #$Collection and all instances of #$Set-Mathematical (and thus all instances of #$SetOrCollection) are abstract entities, lacking spatial and temporal properties.  Nearly all instances of #$Collection (except \"empty\" collections) and nearly all instances of #$Set-Mathematical (except the empty set; see #$TheEmptySet) have \"elements\" (i.e. instances or members; see #$elementOf); hence set-or-collections may stand to one another in generalized set-theoretic relations such as #$subsetOf and #$disjointWith (qq.v.).  (It is this shared feature of having elements that provides the basic rationale for reifying the collection #$SetOrCollection.)  Nevertheless, sets and collections differ in two important ways.  First, each collection is intrinsically associated with an intensional criterion for membership -- a more or less natural property (or group of properties) possessed by all of (and only) its elements.  Collections are thus akin to kinds.  In contrast, the elements of a set are not required to be homogeneous in any respect: any things whatsoever may together constitute the elements of a set.  The second major difference between sets and collections is that no two distinct sets can be coextensional (i.e. have exactly the same elements; see #$coExtensional).  Sets can thus be identified purely on the basis of their extensions (see #$extent).  Collections, on the other hand, are individuated by their intensional criteria for membership.  So collections that have exactly the same elements might nevertheless be distinct, differing in their respective membership criteria.  (Note that the general relationship between collections and their \"intensional criteria for membership\" in the above sense is not something that is currently represented explicitly in the Knowledge Base (though this seems a worthwhile area for future work); still the #$comment and other \"definitional\" assertions on a given collection should ideally convey a reasonably clear and precise idea of its associated membership criterion.)")
(comment PossessivePronoun "The collection of all possessive pronouns. Possessive pronouns can replace possessive nouns. Example: 'my'.")
(comment EquestrianSportsArea "The collection of areas where EquestrianSportsEvents typically occur.")
(comment YardWork "All the various horticulture actions which are done to maintain the grounds of a #$HumanOccupationConstruct")
(comment RotationalConnection "The rotational connection - one object may rotate with respect to another in the direction || to the axis of connection")
(comment majorAccomplishments "The things that ARG1 has accomplished and is proud of.  ARG2 is usually successful and finished.")
(disjointWith Stealing MakingSomething)
(comment CatalogDistribution "Events in which a company distributes copies of their catalogue to customers or prospective customers.")
(comment InterAgentSituation-TwoAgent "The class of reified relationships between two agents.  Such relationships exist in time and change over time, so #$SomethingExisting is an allgenls.")
(comment AutomotiveLocatorService "The collection of all events in which someone receives help from a professional service in finding a used #$Automobile to buy.")
(comment AudioBeep "An audible `beep' sound.")
(comment HeavyweightFSWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of FSWrestlingSportsEvent")
(comment ZonedHeatDwelling "Dwelling has central heat, but different zones are controlled by different furnaces.")
(comment nounPrep "This predicate expresses the relationship between nouns, prepositions with which they co-occur, and the semantic interpretation of the noun and preposition together. Example: 'investment in IBM'")
(comment WithinVisibleDistance "This is the proximity where the actor is close enough in order to properly view the necessary object.  The actual distance can vary depending upon each individual case.")
(comment SpecialOrderPurchase "A subset of #$BuyingAnObject. In each instance of #$SpecialOrderPurchase, a buyer purchases an item from a seller, where the item in question is something not kept in stock by the seller. The buyer places an order for the item with the seller, and the seller then ensures that the item is made available to the buyer (either by shipping the item directly to the buyer, or to a store or factory where it can be picked up by the buyer).")
(comment AffixingSignature "#$AffixingSignature is a collection of events in which an agent affixes his or her signature to a document.")
(comment PommelHorseSportsEvent "The collection of gymnastic events on the PommelHorse.")
(disjointWith InpatientMedicalProcedure OutpatientMedicalCareEvent)
(comment TruthValue "#$TruthValue is a collection of mathematical objects; it contains the abstract, logical objects #$True and #$False.")
(comment DroppingAnObject-Purposeful "The collection of physical actions in which an agent purposefully releases an object so that it falls and collides with something below (like the floor or the ground).  Before the release, the object might be supported by part of the agent's body, or by some device the agent controls.")
(comment faxNumberPrefix "The prefix of the #$faxNumber of this Contact Location.  Up through 2002 fax numbers have been telephone numbers and therefore #$faxNumberPrefix has merely been the #$phoneNumberExchange.")
(comment expenseToAccount "This is a predicate for indicating regular payments  (i.e. expenses) from an Agent's (ARG1) account: ARG4 is added to ARG1's ARG2 at ARG3 intervals. For example to say that XYZCompany pays $20000 a week in personal expenses: (#$expenseToAccount XYZCompany #$PersonnelExpenseAccount Weekly (#$Dollar-UnitedStates 20000))")
(comment RootCanalSurgery "Surgery performed when the root canal of a tooth has been eroded away by an infection.")
(comment Bracelet "The collection of bracelets, a kind of jewelry (typically ringlike in shape) intended to be worn on the wrist")
(comment InternationalUnit "A unit of measure typically used for vitamins.")
(comment Tuesday "A collection of #$CalendarDays and an 
instance of #$DayOfWeekType.  #$Tuesday is the collection of all 
(and only) tuesdays.")
(comment SupportSurface "Surfaces to place or stack things on, possibly shelves. Most TopSurfaces are also SupportSurfaces.")
(comment OlympicCyclingTrack "A track designed for Olympic bicycle races.")
(comment HandSurgeon "A hand surgeon is a doctor who specializes in performing surgical procedures on the hands.")
(comment fanout "The number of destinations to which a signal source is connected.")
(comment Competition "A specialization of #$ConflictEvent.  An instance of #$Competition is a conflict
event that typically involves one or more agents who are each striving to attain 
a certain goal uniquely or to outdo the other competitors with respect to some 
game or task.  Examples include arm wrestling contests, football games, fighting 
for prey, competitive courting, racing events, and spelling bees.  Note that it 
is possible for the competitors in a competition to be unaware that a competition has been going on until after it is over (e.g. the first year a \"Best Restaurant in Town\" award is given out in a particular city).  See also #$competingAgents.")
(disjointWith Person NonPersonAnimal)
(comment AnimalBodyPartType "A collection of specializations of #$AnimalBodyRegion.  Each instance of #$AnimalBodyPartType is a collection of body parts, where the parts in question are differentiated from other body parts according to structure or function.  Instances of #$AnimalBodyPartType include #$SpinalColumn, #$Eyelash, #$NervousSystem, #$Urethra, #$Wing-AnimalBodyPart, and #$HeelOfPalm.")
(comment Preposition-Of "The preposition 'of'. It has unique syntactic functions, for example, occurring after quantifiers, so it is treated as a separate part of speech.")
(comment TakingOutTheGarbage "Taking out the garbage by means of some sort of garbage bag, and depositing it in a #$TrashContainer located outside.  First one lifts the garbage container, then carries it to the garage, driveway, or street, where it is put in another usually larger trash container.")
(comment Real0-100 "A number between 0 and 100 used to denote the real0-100age of what ever.")
(comment Bartender "A person who knows about and mixes alcoholic and other beverages")
(comment BoltingTo "Connecting solid objects together with a Bolt, often with a nut.")
(comment Mass "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity.  Instances of #$Mass may be either a fixed interval, such as two kilograms, or a range, such as a legal load for a certain type of trailer.  The more mass an object has, the greater is the force required to accelerate it.")
(comment CrossTraining "The collection of all events in which a person participates in more than one type of exercise during a workout.")
(comment SyntheticSound "Synthesized sound output.")
(comment FSWrestlingSportsEvent "Freestyle wrestling")
(comment LicenseType "Elements are different classes of rights to #$InformationBearingObjects.  If something #$isa #$LicenseType, its elements are all agreements that give the same _kinds_ of rights, but to various #$InformationBearingObjects.  A class including all the various kinds of licenses to War and Peace, for example, would not be #$isa #$LicenseType.")
(disjointWith CalendarSeason CalendarWeekend)
(disjointWith OneStoryBuilding Skyscraper)
(comment Writer "Not the same as Author.  A writer is someone who writes as an occupation (for a living); an author may or may not be a writer")
(comment fieldName "(#$fieldName ARG1 ARG2) means that ARG2 is the name (name string) of the #$PhysicalField represented by ARG1")
(comment Gecko "A group of lizard species that are best known for their sticky foot pads which allow them to cling to smooth surfaces. Most species are tropical, nocturnal insectivores.")
(comment retailCost "The default price paid to a dealer by a purchaser. This is usually the max amount.")
(comment Divorce "The event which causes a marriage to end (when neither of the spouses' lives do).")
(comment Swim-100MeterFreestyle "Swimming race - 100 meter freestyle.")
(comment DatabaseDataFormat "Instances of #$DatabaseDataFormat are data formats for physical database fields.  Examples include things such as the various possible formattings of a social security number: as a 9-digit integer, a 9-char string, or an 11-char string with two dashes, etc.")
(comment Poacher "A dastardly fellow committed to the illegal capture and murder of helpless wild animals.")
(comment BiologicalProductFn "(#$BiologicalProductFn ARG1 ARG2) denotes the collection of objects of type ARG2 that were biologically produced by the body of ARG1.  ARG2 is typically either a type of secretion or a kind of body part.  The instances may be either still part of the BLO or separate.")
(comment NDCCompanyNumber "The unique number assigned to each company which manufactures, labels, or sells drugs in the US.  This number is the first part of a drug's #$NationalDrugCode (NDC).")
(comment Wednesday "A collection of #$CalendarDays and an 
instance of #$DayOfWeekType.  #$Wednesday is the collection of all 
(and only) wednesdays.")
(comment WorkSurface "This stands for the surface on a #$WorkStation.")
(comment RetailPharmacyNetwork "The collection of networks of retail pharmacies.  The members of a pharmacy network may contract with one or more managed health care providers or insurers to provide reduced-costs services to customers.")
(comment radius "The radius of an object with a circular shape.")
(comment UnitOfPower "The collection of functions which return elements of #$Power.  E.g., (#$Watt 5) denotes 5 watts.")
(comment Freedom-Emotion "Pleasant emotion associated with situations where the person believes themself to be relatively unconstrained in their behavior, not controlled by others.")
(comment MaleBondingActivity "An activity is a male bonding activity if the performers include two or more guys and one of the purposes or at least results of the activity is that the dudes involved develop stronger friendships or deeper understanding of their mutual guyhood.  Usually, recreational activities performed by a smallish group of guys are MaleBondingActivities.")
(disjointWith DeadAnimal HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject)
(comment PITOfIBTFn "An instance of both #$IndividualDenotingFunction and #$ReifiableFunction.  Given as its argument a particular instance of #$InformationBearingThing (q.v.), #$PITOfIBTFn returns the information content of that thing.  The object returned is an instance of #$PropositionalInformationThing (q.v.).  Thus, (#$PITOfIBTFn IBT) is the abstract, propositional chunk of information that is represented in IBT.  For example: if IBT is MyCopyOfPsalm23 (a particular printed copy of Psalm 23), then (#$PITOfIBTFn MyCopyOfPsalm23) is the propositional content of Psalm 23.")
(comment Preposition-Spatial "The collection of all prepositions which express spatial relations. This includes locative and directional prepositions. Example: 'under', as in 'the dog is under the table'.")
(comment dividesEvenly "(#$dividesEvenly NUMBER MULTIPLE) means there is integer N such that N times NUMBER is MULTIPLE.  NUMBER and MULTIPLE are restricted to being instances of #$Integer.")
(comment PaintingAPicture "The collection of actions in which paint is applied to a surface to produce an image considered (at least by the performer) to be an #$ArtObject.")
(comment percentWaterByWeight "The weight of the total water in a living object given as a percentage of the entire weight of the object. ")
(comment MakingWrittenMaterial "The collection of events in which an #$InformationBearingObject containing written material is created.  Includes #$Writing, and the reproduction of #$TextualMaterial.")
(comment PhysEdTeacher "Physical Education Teachers.")
(comment ChemicalProcessing "Transforming something by chemical means.")
(comment customers "This predicate relates an agent to another agent to whom the former sells goods or services.  (#$customers SELLER CUSTOMER) means SELLER sells goods and/or services to CUSTOMER.  CUSTOMER must actually buy something from SELLER in order to be one of SELLER's #$customers.  (Thus, #$customers has a narrower meaning than `customer' in colloquial English, which includes potential buyers.)  See also #$clients.  Cf. #$buyingAgent (in a particular sales event). ")
(comment SupplierRelationship "The class of relationships in which one agent supplies merchandise or materials to the other.")
(comment Area "A specialization of #$ScalarInterval.  Each instance of #$Area is an amount of two-dimensional space.  Instances of #$Area may be either a fixed interval, such as the area of a rectangle 5 cm x 10 cm, or a range, such as the area of a city lot.")
(comment PhysicalAttackOnOpponent "Physically attacking opponent outside of attacks allowed by the rules of the game (such as those in combat sports).")
(comment Soaping "The #$subEvents of a washing where the surfactant is applied to the object washed.  This is not just applying the soap, but lathering it into the object washed.  A wash cycle on a washing machine is considered a soaping event.")
(comment WelterweightFSWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of FSWrestlingSportsEvent")
(comment RoadConstructing "A collection of events.  In each #$RoadConstructing event, a new #$PathForWheeledVehicles is made or incrementally added to.")
(comment Saint "An individual especially recognized within a religion for his/her         holiness, intuitive religious understanding, visions, good works         (including miracles, in Roman Catholicism), martyrdom or other         evidence of close relation to God. 

Interestingly, one is often not recognized as a saint until after one dies.")
(disjointWith OneDiningRoomDwelling TwoDiningRoomDwelling)
(comment Preposition-Locative "The collection of all prepositions which express a locative, static spatial relation. Example: 'beside', as in 'the desk is beside the bookcase'.")
(comment ReversibleProcess "Instances are processes that have a #$reverseProcessType, i.e. they can be undone.")
(comment Reading "A specialization of #$Perceiving-Voluntary and #$AccessingAnIBT.  Each instance of #$Reading is an act of reading an instance of #$TextualMaterial.  Acts of #$Reading may be performed for any of a number of purposes: e.g., in order to extract some sort of information from a text, for entertainment, to impart the content of the text to others (if an instance of #$ReadingAloud (q.v.)), or to test reading skills.  A person can read visually (see #$Reading-Visual) or by touch (e.g. reading Braille; see #$Reading-Tactile).")
(comment dealerCost "The default price paid by a dealer to the manufacturer.")
(comment ApplyingSoapToBody "Events in which soap is applied to the body or part of the body.")
(comment Swim-200MeterButterfly "Swimming race - 200 meter butterfly stroke, not a huge insect.")
(comment referredServiceProvider "(#$referredServiceProvider SERVICE PROVIDER) means that PROVIDER performs or provides SERVICE (see the predicate #$providerOfService), and that PROVIDER was referred to the agent benefitting from SERVICE (see the predicate #$recipientOfService) by another agent.")
(comment UniversalConstant "Measurable physical, chemical, etc. constants of the universe, e.g., 1.42")
(comment lightVerb-TransitiveSemTrans "This predicate expresses the relationship between a light verb, the word which co-occurs with the light verb to make an expression, and the semantic interpretation of that phrase.")
(comment ExtractCountryCodeFn "This function returns the country code of a phone number represented as a string.  For example, (#$ExtractCountryCodeFn ''011-512-338-3634'') will return 011.  If the country code is not present in the phone number, the function returns NIL")
(disjointWith SomethingExisting FocusMicrotheory)
(comment OrthodonticCareEvent "The long event in which teeth are straightened using braces, retainer, etc.")
(comment Robe-Sleepwear "The collection of robes, a loose-fitting article of clothing typically worn before and after sleeping and bathing.")
(comment IntransitiveVerbFrame "This frame is used for words which can be used intransitively, that is, without any complements at all. In HPSG terms: [COMPS  < >]   Example: 'I dance'.")
(comment February "The collection of all Februaries,  the second month of the year in the #$GregorianCalendar.")
(comment violators "(violators x y z) denotes agent x violated role z in mt y.")
(comment VehicleDriveTrainType "Types of drive trains, such as front wheel drive, four wheel drive, etc.")
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization Pharmacy)
(comment Parade "A collection of (often festive) events in which the participants march together along a designated route.  Often includes musical participants as well as other performers, celebrities, and animals.")
(comment Thin "Thin")
(comment WashingHair "The collection of hair-washing events.")
(disjointWith UrbanArea NaturalRegion)
(comment Neurologist "Neurologists are doctors who are skilled in the diagnosis and treatment of injuries and disease of the nervous system.")
(comment bookValue "The historical cost of an asset; the original amount paid.  For depreciable assets, bV equals cost minus accumulated depreciation. For current value, see #$monetaryValueOfThing and its specializations.")
(comment credentialIssueDate "The credential Arg1 was issued on the date Arg2.")
(comment LanguageFamilyType "Related groups of languages.")
(comment Movement-NonPeriodic "A specialization of #$MovementEvent.  Each instance of #$Movement-NonPeriodic is a movement event in which the moving object (see the predicate #$objectMoving) does not return to a previous location or orientation, or returns to a previous location or orientation only in a non-regular manner.  An example of a #$Movement-NonPeriodic would be the motion of a basketball being dribbled by a basketball player as she runs downcourt.  For contrast, see #$Movement-Periodic.")
(comment PlayingABoardGame "Playing a game such as Monopoly, Chess, Checkers, etc...")
(comment RipeFruit "The stage of a fruit when it is ripe.  SOme ripe fruits are fleshy and have a high sugar, starch, or oil content; some are dry and may be ready to break apart to release the seeds contained within.")
(disjointWith Fishing MakingWrittenMaterial)
(comment Welding "Fusing two pieces of metal by melting together adjoining areas of the two pieces.")
(comment relatedAgents "The agents that are related in this relationship.  Doesn't distinguish among the various roles they play; look at my ''specslots'' for predicates that do.")
(comment Goose-Bird "The animal known as a Goose")
(comment RudeAction "The collection of behaviors that go against the social conventions of politeness.  This will be a different set of behaviors in different circumstances (contexts).  In an office, e.g., it might be rude to make a loud noise, but at a football game it might be rude to not do so.")
(comment BreakfastFood "The collection of foods and beverages normally eaten by instances of #$Person as part of #$HavingBreakfast.")
(comment Swim-200MeterFreestyle "Swimming race - 200 meter freestyle.")
(comment LiberalArtsFieldOfStudy "A collection of microtheories; a subset of #$FieldOfStudy.  Each element of #$LiberalArtsFieldOfStudy is one of those fields of study affiliated with the liberal arts, which includes fields expected to be known to some degree by all educated people, but excluding most specialized knowledge taught in professional schools.  Examples: #$History-FieldOfStudy, #$ArtHistory, #$PhilosophyModern, #$Mathematics.")
(disjointWith TownHouse DetachedHouse)
(disjointWith FoodGroup OutdoorLocationTypeByWeather)
(comment TimesPerMinute "Times per minute -- unit of frequency")
(comment SinglesTableTennisGame "Games of Singles Table-Tennis, or PingPong.")
(comment agentReferred "In the referral event ARG1, the sender recommends the agent ARG2 to the recipient.")
(comment Consultant "A specialization of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each instance of #$Consultant is a person who works with some business in a consulting capacity.  Consultants can be self employed, or they can work for a consulting company.")
(comment faxNumberCountryCode "The country code of the #$faxNumber of this Contact Location")
(comment FocusMicrotheory "Mts which focus on a particular thing or type of thing.")
(comment IntravenousFeeding "The collection of events in which nutrients are introduced directly into someone's bloodstream using IV equipment.")
(disjointWith ThermalEnergy PartiallyTangible)
(comment participatesInAlternation "A relation between a verb sense and the type of transitivity alternations in which it participates.")
(comment punishmentFor "(#$punishmentFor x y z) denotes agent x is punished as described in punishment y because proposition z is true.")
(comment ProductName "For example, a car with the Brand VW, the ProductModel Jetta, and the #$ProductVersion GTI.")
(comment GreekOrthodoxOrganization "The collection of all explicitly Greek Orthodox religious organizations")
(comment Triumph " The feeling of pride, joy and exculatation after a success or victory .")
(comment PediatricHemoOncologist "A pediatric hematologist/oncologist is a doctor who specializes in the treatment of cancers, including leukemia, in children.")
(comment Deep "Deep")
(comment Stockbroker "A specialization of both #$PersonWithOccupation and #$Broker.  Each instance of #$StockBroker is a professional broker whose job consists in trading corporate stock on behalf of one or more clients.")
(disjointWith TransportationCompany TouristAttraction)
(comment Ophthalmologist "Ophthalmologists are doctors who specialize in the structure, functions, and diseases of the eye.")
(comment Surprise "The attribute-type associated with the feeling of  surprise at the occurrence of something unexpected, unanticipated, or startling.  A specialization of #$Surprise is #$Wonder-Admiration.  (For  the rationale behind treating feelings as types -- i.e. collections -- of attributes, see the comment on #$Happiness.)")
(comment PartiallyIntangible "The collection of things that either are wholly intangible (see #$Intangible) or have at least one intangible (i.e. immaterial) part (see #$intangibleParts).  This includes intangible individuals, such as instances of #$Number-General or #$Agreement, as well as non-individuals (all of which are intangible), i.e. instances of #$SetOrCollection.  It also includes things that have both tangible and intangible components (see #$CompositeTangibleAndIntangibleObject), such as a printed copy of a newspaper (as its information content is intangible) or a person (as her mental states are intangible).")
(comment CuttingDownATree "The process of chopping down trees, either in a forest or one's yard")
(comment LegalProceeding "A legal event")
(disjointWith MakingWrittenMaterial MedicalCareEvent)
(comment joinDependency "(#$joinDependency ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4) indicates that ARG1 equals ARG2 when ARG3 equals ARG4; all arguments are instances of #$LogicalField. ARG1 and ARG3 are fields in one #$LogicalTableSchema, while ARG2 and ARG4 are fields in another.")
(comment personWithPosition "(#$personWithPosition REL PERSON) means that the #$Person filling the job position in a #$HasPositionRelationship REL is PERSON.  See also #$JobPosition,  #$personWithJobPosition and #$versionOfJobPosition.")
(comment HighAltitude "Altitudes starting at where the thiness of air is first noticable, up to (but not including) where it is impossible for most people to function normally (without special equiptment).")
(comment DownhillSkiing "The #$SnowSkiing where one skis down a snowy slope. Gravity provides the motive force.")
(comment M1500SpeedSkateSportsEvent "The 1500M speed skating competition")
(comment AppliedDesignFieldOfStudy "A collection of fields of study.  Each element of #$AppliedDesignFieldOfStudy is a specialized body of knowledge about the design of useful objects or structures.  Examples: #$ArchitecturalDesign, commercial art studies, industrial design.")
(disjointWith TownHouse ApartmentUnit)
(comment ticketHolder "If a ticket issued to be used by a particular person, this predicate gives their identity.  ARG1 is a ticket that has been issued to be used by the person ARG2.")
(comment DollarsPerMile "The cost of something (in U.S.Dollars) per linear mile.  I suppose this could be used to measure both the cost of building a highway and the cost of using (or renting) a car, although the meaning is different in these two cases.")
(comment CustomerSupport "The action of assisting a customer in the use of a product.  Typically, this assistance is rendered by an employee of the organization that produced the product.")
(comment WillPermeate "has greater than #$NoAmountFn Permeability")
(comment TaxonomicSlotForAnyThing "A subcollection of #$TaxonomicSlot (q.v.). Each instance of #$TaxonomicSlotForAnyThing is a taxonomic slot that can in principle be used to help specify the location of anything whatsoever within some taxonomy; hence at least one of its argument-places must be constrained to instances (see #$argIsa) of #$Thing (and to nothing more specific than #$Thing). Examples include #$isa and #$generalizations.")
(comment serviceCharge "A service charge of the amount ARG2 is included in the total cost of the transaction ARG1.")
(comment HeavyJudoSportsEvent "Judo matches for sport, in the Heavy weight class.")
(comment AdministrativeStaffPerson "A specialization of #$DeskWorker.  Each instance of #$AdministrativeStaffPerson is a worker whose primary job responsibilities are administrative and/or managerial tasks.  Such jobs can be at any level in an organization's hierarchy, from receptionist/secretary to executive assistant to manager.")
(comment faxNumberAreaCode "The area code of the #$faxNumber of this Contact Location")
(comment CommoditiesTrader "#$CommoditiesTrader buys and sells commodities.")
(comment IntravenousHydration "The collection of events in which liquids (primarily water) are introduced directly into someone's bloodstream using IV equipment.")
(comment acronymString "(#$acronymString THING STRING) means that THING may be referred to by the acronym STRING.  For example, because the Medical College Admission Test is sometimes referred to as MCAT or M.C.A.T. we assert (#$acronymString #$MedicalCollegeAdmissionTest ``MCAT'').  STRING is case-insensitive. See also #$initialismString and the #$abbreviation* predicates, as acronyms, abbreviations, and initialisms are technically distinct.")
(comment Friday "A collection of #$CalendarDays and an 
instance of #$DayOfWeekType.  #$Friday is the collection of all 
(and only) fridays.")
(comment LevelOfColdSensation "The type of internal sensation or feeling of coldness. This unit is for describing how chilly somebody feels internally.")
(comment ChristianOrganization "The collection of all explicitly Christian organizations")
(comment SteppingOutOfBounds "Stepping out of bounds or leaving your lane during a sports event.")
(comment NuclearRadiologist "A nuclear radiologist is a doctor who specializes in using nuclear radiation to diagnose and treat patients.")
(comment Designing "The act of designing something, be it clothing, cars, computer chips or buildings. ")
(disjointWith Person TouristAttraction)
(comment Immunologist "Immunologists are doctors who specialize in the phenomena and causes of immunity.")
(comment QuickBurstSport "SportsEvents in which the competitors release quick bursts of energy.")
(comment AutoMaintenance "Fun things like pumping gas and changing oil; the collection of things people do to keep their automobiles running")
(comment SubLBoolean "The collection of #$SubLObjects whose value is either NIL or non-NIL.")
(disjointWith YardWork MakingWrittenMaterial)
(comment Dipping "Dipping something solid into a liquid.")
(comment InternetStandard "An internet standard is a kind of product specification, applicable to #$NetworkingPrograms, concerning how the product behaves in the #$Internet environment.")
(comment AddictionPsychiatrist "The collection of all addiction #$Psychiatrists.  An individual #$AddictionPsychiatrist is a #$Psychiatrist who has specialized in the management of patients with substance abuse disorders.  An #$AddictionPsychiatrist is versed in the fields of #$Psychiatry, pharmacology, general medicine, and psychology.")
(comment Acne "an inflammatory disease of the sebaceous glands, characterized by comedones and pimples, esp. on the face, back, and chest, and, in severe cases, by cysts and nodules resulting in scarring. Also called 'acne vulgaris.'")
(comment UnsportsmanlikeAction "Behavior that goes against the code of Sportsmanship.  This can include anything from not shaking hands after the game to blatant cheating.")
(comment BirdWatching "This is the collection of observings of birds for recreational purposes.  Thus, it is not simply casual noticing of birds, but deliberate observation.  #$BirdWatching usually includes an attempt to identify the species and sex of the birds, observe their behavior, and sometimes count the number of individuals.  Often called 'birding'.")
(comment CycLSetExpression "The collection of all non-atomic expressions in the CycL language that denote sets.  #$CycLSetExpression is a quoted-collection (see #$quotedCollection) that is a subcollection of #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm.  Each instance of #$CycLSetExpression denotes some instance of #$Set-Mathematical.  For example, the expression `(#$TheSetOf ?X (#$and (#$isa ?X #$Dog) (#$mainColorOfObject ?X #$BlackColor)))' denotes the set of all black dogs.  Note that all CycL set expressions do indeed denote, as those whose matrices are satisfied by nothing -- e.g. `(#$TheSetOf ?X (#$different ?X ?X))' -- still denote #$TheEmptySet.")
(comment Swim-100MeterButterfly "Swimming race - 100 meter butterfly stroke, not a huge insect.")
(comment Magician-Performer "A #$Collection of #$Persons.  A #$Magician-Performer performs actions that are intended to appear impossible without the use of #$Magic..")
(disjointWith TwoStoryBuilding Skyscraper)
(comment PropositionalInformationThing "A specialization of both #$InformationStore and #$Microtheory.  Each instance of #$PropositionalInformationThing (or \"PIT\") is an abstract object -- a chunk of information consisting of one or more propositions.  The propositional content of a PIT is not essentially encoded in any particular language, and it may be representable in many languages.  PITs are used to represent the informational contents of #$InformationBearingThings.  Objects or events which are instances of #$InformationBearingThing are linked to the abstract PIT contents they embody using the predicate #$containsInformation (see also the function #$PITOfIBTFn).  An instance of #$PropositionalInformationThing may be something as simple as the information content of a command to stop one's vehicle, expressed in a road sign or in a traffic officer's gesture, or it may be something as complex as the entire contemporary knowledge of #$Mathematics, embodied in many and various sources.")
(comment Appetizer "Food dishes which might be served as an appetizer.")
(comment dealerFor "The predicate #$dealerFor relates a retailer to the manufacturer(s) whose products are sold by that retailer.  (#$dealerFor RETAILER MANUF) means that the #$RetailOrganization RETAILER is a dealer for products made by the #$ManufacturingOrganization MANUF.  RETAILER may be only one of many dealers.  RETAIL sells MANUF's products to the final consumers.")
(comment MiddleweightFSWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of FSWrestlingSportsEvent")
(comment participatingProvider "ARG2 is a participating or `in-network' health care provider in ARG1.")
(comment IntravenousInfusionProcess "The process of introducing a solution into an animal's vein by means of a container connected to a needle by a flexible tube.")
(comment phoneNumberExchange "The prefix of the #$PhoneNumber of this #$ContactLocation")
(disjointWith RuralArea UrbanArea)
(comment Acronym "When the name of something consists of many words, often an acronym will be formed out of the first letter of each word in the name and this will be used to refer to the thing instead of the full name.  For example, the ''American Association for Artificial Intelligence'' is often referred to as AAAI.")
(comment Saturday "A collection of #$CalendarDays and an 
instance of #$DayOfWeekType.  #$Saturday is the collection of all 
(and only) saturdays.")
(comment averageRainFall "The average number of inches per year of precipitation falling as rain             in this geographical region.            This is the rate averaged over a long period of time, so that the            irregularity is averaged out.")
(comment Distress "Extremely troubled; mentally confused, distracted.")
(comment GraduateMedicalProgramOrganization "The class of graduate programs which specialize in medical training and research.")
(comment PositionPenalizing "A penalty of having the starting position of the next play being moved against your favor.")
(comment PediatricSurgeon "A pediatric surgeon is a doctor who specializes in performing surgery on children.")
(comment Thick "Thick")
(comment Ticket "The collection of hardcopy and electronic objects, used in an agreement between agents, entitling the bearer to some service or object. The common usage of 'ticket', for a thing which entitles the bearer to admission to movies, ball games, amusement parks, etc., is what is meant.")
(comment Epiphany-TheDay "Each of these is an annual one-day-long #$ChristianHoliday which is celebrated on January 6 and which commemorates either the coming of the Magi (Western Christianity) or the Baptism of Christ (Greek Orthodox).")
(comment Podiatrist "The collection of health professionals concerned with the care and treatment of the human foot.")
(comment EnduranceEvent "TrackSportsEvents in which it is necessary to be able to run long distances")
(comment Pruning "Cutting off branches from a tree or bush in order to improve the shape, growth, or production of flowers and/or fruit")
(comment Florist "the collection of all persons who arrange and try to sell flowers")
(comment SurfaceChemicalProcessing "Transforming something by chemical means applied only at and near the surface of the transformed object (e.g.:  etching or film processing).  This implies that the transformed object is a solid or liquid.")
(comment InternalBusinessNetwork "A computer network that is within a business.  All the computers on the network are controlled by the business that owns the network.")
(comment Counselor-Psychological "A collection of persons; a subset of #$Professional. Each element of #$Counselor-Psychological is a professional whose job is to counsel others on psychological, emotional or behavioral, issues.  Elements include members of the subsets #$Psychoanalyst, #$SocialWorker, #$CounselingPsychologist, etc.  This collection does NOT include other types of counselors or advisers.")
(comment Time-Quantity "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity.  Each instance of #$Time-Quantity is a physical quantity, corresponding to a certain \"amount of time\", that can be possessed by  #$TemporalThings.  The #$Time-Quantity had by a given thing represents the total amount of time that the thing exists, occurs over, or endures; see #$duration.  Consider a sentence of the form (#$duration TEMPTHING TIMEQUANT).  If TEMPTHING is a #$SomethingExisting, the sentence means that TEMPTHING exists for a lifetime that is TIMEQUANT in duration.  If TEMPTHING is an #$Event, the sentence means that TEMPTHING (fully) transpires over an interval of time that is TIMEQUANT in duration.  If TEMPTHING is itself a #$TimeInterval (q.v.), the sentence means that TEMPTHING has a duration of TIMEQUANT.  The standard unit of 

#$Time-Quantity in Cyc is #$SecondsDuration (q.v.); but there are other ways to specify an amount of time, e.g. with other instances of #$UnitOfMeasure (such as #$WeeksDuration and #$YearsDuration) or with instances of #$Time-Quantity (such as #$LongTime, #$Immediately, and #$AFewDecadesDuration).")
(comment (MedicalTreatmentFn Acne) "The collection of #$MedicalTreatmentEvents for #$Acne.")
(comment Record-ExtremeValue "Records are objects that record which object among a collection satisfies a particular extremal property.  All the records in the Guinness Book are instances of this collection.")
(comment FineDining "The collection of events in which one or more #$Persons eats a meal in            a formal and elegant setting, usually at a #$FineRestaurant.")
(comment networkAddresses "A list of addresses for this computer.  The CAR is a network name (string) the cdr a network address (a string)")
(comment Swim-400MeterIndivMedley "Swimming race - 400 meter individual medley.")
(comment Cuddling "Action where two creatures stay in physical contact because they like each other.  Cuddling is comforting and expresses affection.")
(disjointWith OneStoryBuilding TwoStoryBuilding)
(comment StayingAtCommercialLodging "Spending one or more days where one's residence is a hotel/motel room.  Includes at minimum an overnight stay.")
(comment Tar "the thick, sticky brown-black liquid made from various organic compounds like wood, coal, etc.")
(comment BeliefSystemType "The collection of all the kinds of #$BeliefSystems -- religious, philosophical, political, ethical, cultural, and scientific.  Some elements of this collection include #$Religion, #$PhilosophyBeliefs, etc.  The most general member of this set is #$BeliefSystems (qv).")
(comment viewpointOf-Spatial "ARG1 is the point from which ARG2 is viewed.")
(comment CostBreakdownSlot "A specialization of #$BinaryPredicate. Each instance of #$CostBreakdownSlot is a binary predicate used to describe some pecuniary aspect of an instance of #$Buying. The first argument to every #$CostBreakdownSlot is constrained to be an instance of #$Buying and the second argument is constrained to be an instance of #$MonetaryValue. Instances of #$CostBreakdownSlot include #$moneyTransferred, #$discount, #$salesTax, and #$salesCommission.")
(comment MedicalTesting "A specialization of #$MedicalCareEvent, #$InformationGathering and #$Evaluating.  Each instance of #$MedicalTesting is a test performed by some #$IntelligentAgent on a #$MedicalPatient (or, often, on a sample taken from the patient's body) in order to gather information about the patient's general state of health, in order to help in making a diagnosis, or in order to determine or monitor the severity of a known condition of the patient.  Instances of #$MedicalTesting include individual blood tests, as well as individual MRIs. See also #$MedicalDiagnosis.")
(comment LightFlyweightGRWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of GRWrestlingSportsEvent")
(comment StringConcatWithSpaces "Fields combined in this way will be string-concatenated with one or more spaces intervening between the fields.")
(comment LegalProcess "Each #$LegalProcess involves both mental processing and some physical recording, people doing things in the real world, etc., hence is a #$CompositePhysicalAndMentalEvent")
(comment phoneNumberCountryCode "The country code of the #$PhoneNumber of this #$ContactLocation")
(comment SpecifiedContentIT "The collection of all image types which specify a particular depicted content.  Rhino016InSandDiegoZoo would be an instance of this collection, but #$StillImage (no actual content specified) would not.")
(disjointWith UnitOfCurrent UnitOfPower)
(comment AMCNumber "Number given to a medical service provider by the American Medical Census Organization.")
(comment SafetyDevice "A collection of devices.  An instance of #$SafetyDevice is a device whose #$primaryFunction is to promote or ensure safety.  For example, a #$LifePreserver, a #$SafetySeatBelt.")
(comment Weak "not having much physical strength, delicate. ")
(comment ElectricalSupplyCompany "Companies which sell electrical parts and supplies, such as wiring, conduit, electrical fixtures, etc.")
(comment SportsPenalizing "An action taken by a sports official to reprimand a competitor or player for a sports infraction.")
(comment CardiovascularSurgeon "A cardiovascular surgeon is a doctor who specializes in performing surgical procedures on the  heart and blood vessels.")
(comment amountOfEnergyUsed "Events often require some energy. (#$amountOfEnergyUsed EVENT ENERGYAMOUNT) means that the event EVENT uses ENERGYAMOUNT of energy.")
(comment ActorUseTypeSlot "Instances of #$ActorUseTypeSlot are actor slots which give information about the fate of the actor - whether it is destroyed, unchanged, temporarily changed, etc. Which #$ActorUseTypeSlot an actor appears on affects whether or not the same actor will act in the same role in the same kind of event in the future. ")
(comment ChristmasSeason "Each #$ChristmasSeason is the annual event around the #$ChristmasHoliday where people observing this holiday perform related activities, such as displaying #$ChristmasDecorations, participating in related religious services, etc. ")
(comment Pathologist "Pathologists are doctors who are concerned with the causes or disease and the changes in structure and function produced in an organ or part of the body by disease.")
(comment CharSequenceOfMaximumLengthFn "Returns the datatype of character sequences no longer than ARG1.")
(comment SubLInteger "The collection of all integer-denoting expressions in the CycL language that are _not_ CycL constants or NATs, but are terms of SubL, the underlying implementation language of the Cyc system.  #$SubLIntegers  are numeric strings of the Arabic decimal system (including the negative-value symbol `-', but _not_ the decimal point or scientific notation) that denote integers.  Examples include the expressions `0', `12', and `-4' (which denote the integers 0, 12, and -4, respectively).  Non-examples include `4.012', `(#$Meter 6)', `(#$Unity 3.3)', `:34', and `#$PlusInfinity'.  Note that #$SubLInteger is a \"quoted-collection\" (see #$quotedCollection). Thus the sentence `(#$isa 12 #$SubLInteger)' means that the expression `12' (and not the number 12) is an instance of #$SubLInteger.  Similarly, the assertion `(#$genls #$SubLInteger #$Integer)' means (not that each SubL integer is an integer, but) that each  instance of #$SubLInteger _denotes_ an instance of #$Integer (see the shared #$NoteAboutUseVersusMention).")
(comment StandingDive "The collection of dives in which the diver stands at the edge of the board or plaform before take-off.")
(comment Laughing "Laughing process")
(comment CrewTeam "a team of rowers for competing in crew events")
(comment MassChemicalProcessing "Processing a mass of stuff; possibly even creating a new substance (e.g., steel) from the input materials.")
(comment ConjunctAdverb "Adverbials which are neither disjuncts nor subjuncts. #$ConjunctAdverbs can generally act as sentential modifiers, however, they cannot appear as the focus of a cleft sentence. Semantically, these conjuncts generally indicate how the speaker views the connection between two linguistic units.")
(comment PPTDosageFormFn "Returns collections which are PharmacyProductTypes intended to be administered in doses of the form ARG2, containing the substance ARG1.")
(comment OrganismInfectedWithFn "Returns the class of organisms which are instances of the first argument but which contains instances of the second arugument in their bodies.")
(comment recordScore "The score of the record performance of this record")
(comment CrossCountrySkiing "The #$SnowSkiing where one provides his/her own motive force for skiing on relatively flat snowy surfaces")
(comment CubicMeter "A function which returns an element of #$Volume.  One cubic meter (#$CubicMeter 1) equals about 35 cubic feet.")
(comment MiddleweightWeightliftingSportsEvent "A weight class of WeightliftingSportsEvent")
(comment NLSemanticPredicate "these are semantic predicates for CycL")
(comment Grazing "moving through the landscape eating parts of plants that grow there.")
(disjointWith ThreeStoryBuilding Skyscraper)
(comment Number-SP "The collection of all numbers used as words. This includes spelled-out numbers, like 'five', and digits, like '5'.")
(comment DollarsPerPound "The cost of something (in U.S.Dollars) per Pound.  For bananas, e.g., this would be about 0.45.  It can be used to describe the sale of a tangible object, or of a service (e.g. deliveries).")
(disjointWith Account-LegalAgreement License-LegalAgreement)
(comment HavingAMeal-Individual "An individual's part in a meal.")
(comment Continuously "Used to indicate that something is occurring at every instant in time.")
(comment ProductRepairDepartment "Each instance of #$ProductRepairDepartment consists of employees who are responsible for fixing items returned because they are faulty in some way.")
(disjointWith PreparingFoodOrDrink Meeting-SocialGathering)
(comment FlyingDutchmanSportsEvent "A class of YachtingSportsEvent")
(comment BodilyGoal "BodilyGoals are those that are shared by humans and pertain to physical appearance and physical well being.")
(disjointWith UnitOfCurrent UnitOfAngularSpeed)
(comment Lobbyist "A lobbyist is a Professional who attempts to influence Politicians.")
(comment LogFn "A unary #$EvaluatableFunction that returns the natural logarithm of the number taken as its argument.  (#$LogFn NUM) is the exponent to which e is raised to get NUM (where e is #$E-LogarithmBase). Its inverse (cf. #$inverseQuantFunctions-Nonsymmetric) is #$ExpFn.")
(comment RustCausingStuff "The collection of substances that eat away metal.  See oxidizing agent.")
(comment VeterinarySupplyCompany "Companies which sell supplies for caring for domesticated animals (pets and livestock) primarily to veterinarians.")
(disjointWith Competition SportsPenalizing)
(comment dependentMapping-Old "(#$dependentMapping TABLE LF1 VALUE LF2 MAP) means that the mapping MAP should be used to interpret the field LF2 on the table TABLE when the field LF1 has the value VALUE.")
(comment circumferenceOfObject "The distance around a circular object")
(comment contractorFor "The predicate #$contractorFor relates a particular contractor to one of its clients.  (#$contractorFor CONTR CLIENT) means that CONTR has a contract with CLIENT to supply some service to CLIENT.  This relationship holds from the inception to the completion of their contractual #$Agreement.  Either CONTR or CLIENT may be a person or an organization.  For example, a real estate agency may be a #$contractorFor an individual whose house they are selling; an individual graphic artist may be a #$contractorFor a company whose Web pages she designs; an aircraft manufacturer may be a #$contractorFor the U.S. Department of Defense, to supply jet fighters.")
(disjointWith HumanResidenceArea WildernessArea)
(comment Endocrinologist "Endocrinologists are doctors who specialize in treatment of disorders of the endocrine system.")
(comment CorrectnessOfPosture "Chest out, shoulders back, stomach in.")
(comment Accelerating-Rotational "#$Accelerating-Rotational occurs whenever the angular velocity of the #$objectMoving changes, e.g. spinning faster or slower or changing the axis along which spinning occurs.")
(comment Fan-Supporter "The collection of all people who are fans of some famous person in CYC's point of view.  Later should state rule like, instances of fans like a particular famous person or team (perhaps even Agent).  I feel a bit uneasy about such a unit, but it will probably get good use.  Plus it makes it easy to say io PerformerArtsEntertainment want to liked by lots of fans.  See that unit.")
(comment ProductionEvent "In the ManufacturingMt, every instance of ProductionEvent includes at least one instance of Manufacturing and all the ancillary events on which the instance of Manufacturing depends.  Scheduling, ordering raw materials, etc.")
(comment ImmunityConferringInfectionType "The collection of #$InfectionTypes which confer immunity to that type of #$Infection on those who contract them.  Many of these illnesses are `childhood illnesses'.")
(comment QualifyingTrial "A competition which is a precursor to another competition.  Only those who perform sufficiently well in a #$QualifyingTrial become competitors in the subsequent competition.")
(comment Quilting "The sewing together of patches of material to make a quilt.  This is NOT the creating of a finished quilt, but rather the sewing technique itself, and hence instances of #$Quilting should be #$subEvents of instances of (#$MakingFn Quilt).")
(comment lengthOfObject "(#$lengthOfObject OBJECT LENGTH) means that the length of OBJECT is LENGTH.  Which dimension of a given object counts as its length partly depends on such things as the type of object it is, its shape, and its spatial relations to other objects in its environment.  Length is normally  measured as the #$Distance from (what one intuitively thinks of as) one \"end\" of the object to its other \"end\", and often corresponds to the dimension of the object that has the greatest magnitude.  Some types of objects (e.g. trains and yachts) have front and back ends -- and thus lengths -- by virtue of having an intrinsic default orientation (see #$FrontAndBackSidedObject and the other specializations of #$BilateralObject).  For some other types of objects (e.g. shoelaces and hair strands), length is determined by that dimension that is of much greater magnitude, relatively speaking, than any of the object's other dimensions.  Still other objects have lengths by virtue of having orientations determined only in relation to their environments (e.g. the \"length\" of a row of adjacent buldings might be the distance across the side of the row that faces the street, whether or not that happens to be the row's dimension of greatest magnitude).  See also #$widthOfObject, #$heightOfObject, and #$depthOfObject.")
(comment WeightliftingSportsEvent "The collection of weight lifting sports competitions")
(disjointWith OneStoryBuilding ThreeStoryBuilding)
(comment PerUnitTime "A billing scheme in which charges are computed based on some unit of time.  This applies to car rentals, long-distance telephone service, etc.")
(comment holdsOver "This proposition becomes true during this time period.  For example, Liz drank three cups of coffee between 8 and 9 am.")
(comment Vomit "Vomit -- partially digested food emitted from the stomach out the mouth")
(comment quantityRequested "the quantity of the item or items requested.  Can be a number in the case of individual objects, or can be mass, volume, distance, killowatts, etc. depending on the type of the object")
(comment ExtraLightJudoSportsEvent "Judo matches for sport, in the ExtraLight weight class.")
(comment ExtractPhoneExchangeFn "This function returns the prefix of a phone number represented as a string.  For example, (#$ExtractPhoneExchangeFn ''512-338-3634'') will return 338.  If the prefix is not present in the phone number, the function returns NIL")
(comment spaceOfImage "ARG2 is the space depicted by the visual image ARG1.")
(disjointWith UnitOfMonetaryRate UnitOfCurrent)
(comment vandalismRate "Per capita frequency of acts of vandalism in an area.")
(comment TangibleObjectTypeBySide "This collection has just two instances: #$LeftObject, and #$RightObject.  It exists so that we can avoid axiom duplication in cases where we want an axiom to apply independently to both left things and right things.")
(disjointWith SportsPenalizing BiologicalDestructionEvent)
(comment DiabetesSpecialist "A diabetes specialist is a doctor who specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of diabetes.")
(comment recyclableActors "An object that requires some sort of reconditioning after each use in the event, before it can be used again in a similar event.  E.g., a gun which requires reloading.")
(comment MythologicalThing "The collection of all #$TemporalThings (beings, magical artifacts, spells, etc.) appearing in myths or legends but not extant in the world modeled by the KB in which something is asserted to be an instance of this.  This collection should have no instances in #$BaseKB or other general microtheories, but be restricted to microtheories dealing with the \"real world\" or some fictional world.  Note that stories about #$MythologicalThings are not themselves #$MythologicalThings.")
(comment Proctologist "Proctologists specialize in the branch of medicine dealing with the structure and diseases of the anus, rectum, and the sigmoid colon.")
(comment hasPhysicalPartTypes "(#$hasPhysicalPartTypes OBJ PART-TYPE) means that the object OBJ has at least one part of type PART-TYPE as a physical part. Use the predicate #$physicalPartTypes to state that every object of a given type has at least one part of PART-TYPE.")
(comment InformationStorageMedia "Items which can have (but don't necessarily have) information stored onto them that can be retrieved later.")
(comment ArmstandDive "The collection of dives in which the diver takes-off from a handstand position.")
(comment Mayor "city leader.")
(comment EntertainmentOrArtsAdministrator "Professionals not intimately involved in entertainment or the creation of art.  They are usually more on the administrative or business end of the artist's entreprise.")
(comment manufacturingSteps "The steps involved in a particular Manufacturing event.")
(comment SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType "A collection of collections which is being phased out. In most cases, instances of #$ConceptualWork should be used instead. Each instance of #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType is a subcollection of #$InformationBearingThing, all of whose instances are instantiations of the same #$ConceptualWork and share a primary media form. Instances of #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType can be created to refer to any instance of #$ConceptualWork. For example, the collection of all instances of #$BookCopy which are instantiations of #$WarAndPeace-TheNovel would be an instance of #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType, as would the collection of all instance of #$MovieShowing which are instantiations of #$Jaws-TheMovie (even though both the novel `War and Peace' and #$Jaws-TheMovie were issued in slightly different variants). Heterogeneous collections, however, such as those defined by `copies of books written by Mark Twain', or by `physical instantiations of the Jaws story in all its forms', are NOT subcollections of #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType, although they are subcollections of #$InformationBearingThing. Example of #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType: #$DimeCoin-US.")
(comment Tonsillitis "A collection of infections. Instances of #$Tonsillitis are inflamationtions of the tonsil.")
(comment TakingACourse "Enrolling and participating in a course for study. Groups can also take a course, for example, a class for couples.  A #$CourseOfStudy consists of many of these events.")
(comment areaOfRegion "This predicate relates a geographical region to its physical size or area. (#$areaOfRegion REGION AREA) means that the physical size of REGION is AREA.  Examples: (#$areaOfRegion #$LakeErie (#$SquareMile 9940)), (#$areaOfRegion #$Elba-Island-Italy (#$SquareMile 86)), (#$areaOfRegion #$VaticanCity (#$SquareMile 0.17)), (#$areaOfRegion #$China-PeoplesRepublic (#$SquareMile 3705390)).  For stating the areas of other (strictly or roughly \"two-dimensional\") sorts of objects, see the generalization #$areaOfObject; and see #$Area for ways of representing areas.")
(comment M500SpeedSkateSportsEvent "The 500M speed skating competition")
(disjointWith ThreeStoryBuilding TwoStoryBuilding)
(comment queryVarType "Objects bound to the variable ARG2 which occurs in the CycL expression ARG1 will be instances of the collection ARG3.")
(comment Electrolyzing "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$Electrolyzing, a liquid is subjected to the action of an electrical current passing through it.")
(disjointWith GeographicalRegion Particle)
(comment ProcessingStation "A processing station in an #$AssemblyLine.")
(comment Dream "Dreams -- mental fantasy visualizations during sleep")
(comment itemTypeRequested "the type of the item or items requested")
(disjointWith MakingAnOralSound PreparingFoodOrDrink)
(comment RacingSportsEvent "A sports event where the competitors attempt to travel as fast as possible over some distance.  They are typically constrained in the mode of travel and the course to be traveled.")
(comment levelOfCoverage "The insurance plan ARG1 covers the cost of the event ARG2 to the degree specified by ARG3.")
(comment SquareMile "The measurement function used in Cyc to represent the square mile used as a unit of measure for area, within the British (FPS) system.  See also #$FPSUnitOfMeasure, #$UnitOfMeasure.")
(comment faxNumberSuffix "The suffix of the #$faxNumber of this Contact Location")
(disjointWith UnitOfFlowRate UnitOfCurrent)
(comment Researcher "A subcollection of #$PersonWithOccupation each instance of which is a person who performs research as a significant part of his or her occupation.  This collection includes academicians, clinical investigators, experimental physicists, market researchers, industrial researchers, etc.")
(comment FixedStructure "#$FixedStructure is a specialization of #$ConstructionArtifact.  Each instance of #$FixedStructure is a human-constructed, freestanding object that exists in a fixed location.  Examples include buildings, pyramids, the Great Wall of China, dams, bridges, elevated roadways, and canals. Such structures may have parts which are also instances of #$FixedStructure (e.g. bridge pilings) and parts which are not freestanding (e.g. the span of a bridge, or a room in a building).")
(comment PublicEvent "The collection of #$Events which occur in front of, or in the contemporaneous awareness of, a large number of #$Persons -- #$ThePublic.  Usually these are intended to be public events, such as the Olympics, a public beheading, etc.")
(comment prepCollocation "(#$prepCollocation WORD POS PREP) means that WORD, when used with part-of-speech POS, often collocates with the preposition PREP. For example, (#$prepCollocation #$Covetous-TheWord #$Adjective #$Of-TheWord) means that the adjective 'covetous' has an affinity for the preposition 'of'.")
(disjointWith CommercialActivity SportsPenalizing)
(comment DiagnosticLabImmunologist "A diagnostic lab immunologist is a doctor whose specialty is diagnosing problems with the immune system through laboratory tests.")
(comment unchangedActors "(#$unchangedActors EVENT OBJ) means that the object OBJ is an actor (see the predicate #$actors) in the event EVENT, and that OBJ remains virtually unchanged by its participation in the event EVENT. (#$unchangedActors EVENT OBJ) implies that OBJ does not appreciably move, nor does it undergo some internal change in its properties, nor is it created or destroyed, in the course of EVENT.")
(comment PackagedObject "An object that is packaged together with its packaging. Packaging may serve to protect, identify, disguise (e.g., a wrapped present), physically control, ..., the object.")
(comment Urologist "Urologists are doctors who specialize in the branch of medicine dealing with the urinary or urogenital tract.")
(comment LinguisticObjectType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$LinguisticObjectType is a specialization of #$LinguisticObject (q.v.).")
(comment OfficialDocument "A specialization of #$HardcopyInformationBearingObject. Each instance of #$OfficialDocument is a document that can be used as the basis, proof, or support of some fact (such as a person's nationality, marital status, credit, or qualifications; or the ownership or transfer of property, etc.). #$OfficialDocuments are typically generated, issued, and/or certified by relevant institutions (as with #$Passports or #$StockCertificates), but they also include unique personal documents (such as wills) which meet certain standards to be accepted in support of facts. Instances of #$OfficialDocument include: #$BirthCertificates, #$TaxReturns, insurance policies, #$PostageStamps, receipts, #$PackingSlips and student ID cards. A notable specialization of this collection is #$LegalDocument. See also #$OfficialDocumentType.")
(comment SpeedOfReflexes "The ability to react quickly to stimuli.")
(comment CommunicationProtocol "The collection of #$CommunicationConventions which are actual standards or protocols; for example, #$TCP-IP.")
(comment FolkDance "A dance characteristic of a particular culture; generally originating in the rural past, sometimes the remnant of some ritual.  Examples: Square dancing; national dances; the Virginia Reel; the Irish Jig.  Folk dances are often performed in the clothing of the culture the dance is associated with.")
(comment LevelOfDizziness "The type of feeling or sensation of being dizzy.")
(comment Forester "The collection of professional foresters")
(comment ContinuousManufacturingProcess "A collection of events.  Each element of this collection is a continuous manufacturing process that can be kept going arbitrarily long (depending on, e.g., the availability of inputs, power, labor, etc.).  Product begins to be produced some time after the process is started and continues to be produced during the run.  A hallmark of continuous (vs. batch or run) manufacturing is that inputs are added continously or periodically, and outputs and byproducts are removed continously or periodically, during the process.")
(comment recordValueForType "(#$recordValueForType ?RECORD ?COLL) states that ?RECORD is relevant to all objects of the type ?COLL. For example, (#$recordValueForType TallestPersonRecord #$Person).")
(comment (LowAmountFn LevelOfPhysicalActivity) "Categorizes the level of physical activity required for everything from a physiological process occuring to sitting")
(comment TrapShootingSportsEvent "A marksmanship sports event in which the targets are clay pidgeons tossed into the air.")
(disjointWith TwoBedroomDwelling OneBedroomDwelling)
(comment temporallyIntersects-TypeType "A #$ComplexTemporalPredicate that is a type-level correlate of #$temporallyIntersects (q.v.).  This predicate is used to state that things of one given type always temporally intersect things of another given type.  (#$temporallyIntersects-TypeType TYPE1 TYPE2) means that for every instance INST1 of TYPE1, there is an instance INST2 of TYPE2 such that (#$temporallyIntersects INST1 INST2).  For example, (#$temporallyIntersects-TypeType #$January #$Wednesday) states (correctly) that each January overlaps some Wednesday.  Note that this predicate is _not_ symmetric; e.g. (#$temporallyIntersects-TypeType #$Wednesday #$January) does not hold.  Specializations of #$temporallyIntersects-TypeType include #$temporallySubsumes-TypeType and #$temporallySubsumedBy-TypeType.")
(comment FamilyMeal "A meal that occurs around a table in a family's house.  Not all those present need be members of the family.")
(comment paymentDueForRequest "The money which would be due from the buyer if the requested purchase transaction was completed.")
(disjointWith Manufacturing MakingAGesture)
(disjointWith RacingSportsEvent FreestyleSkiingSportsEvent)
(comment StudentHealthCenter "The collection of all student health centers (associated with some educational institution, such as a university).")
(comment Courageousness-Feeling "Braveness. Emotion of those who show undismayed resolution in presence of evil or danger.")
(comment Patrolling-LawEnforcement "The collection of all instances of 

patrolling done by law enforcement agencies and/or #$Vigilantes. See also

#$Patrolling-Military.")
(comment phoneNumberSuffix "(#$phoneNumberSuffix CONTACT_LOCATION NUM) means that NUM is the base phone number used at the #$ContactLocation CONTACT_LOCATION, ignoring the country code, area code, and exchange.  When calling from one phone in certain exchanges to other telephones in the same exchange (or occasionally an associated exchange, as in some corporate offices) only the #$phoneNumberSuffix needs to be used to reach the other line.")
(comment mtImageDepicts "The predicate #$mtImageDepicts is used to determine things represented in images, on the basis of the information content of the image.  For this purpose, the content of an image is represented as an abstract, propositional thing--an element of #$ImageMicrotheory (which is a subset of #$PropositionalInformationThing (q.v.)).   (#$mtImageDepicts IMT OBJ) means that the image(s) which have the information content IMT depict the object OBJ.  Those images may be still or moving images.  IMT is an element of #$ImageMicrotheory.  OBJ is an element of #$SpatialThing, which includes both tangible objects and physical events.  One usage of #$mtImageDepicts is for the description and representation of particular images; e.g., an image with the content `Roy Rogers is riding Trigger' depicts Roy Rogers and depicts Trigger.  Another usage of #$mtImageDepicts is in inference rules about the content of images.  For example, using a series of common sense inferences, we conclude that an image with the content `a cowboy [is] on his horse' probably also depicts some instance of #$OutdoorLocation.")
(comment recordCount "(#$recordCount TABLE N) indicates that physical table TABLE has N records. This information is used by DB-query applications in assessing cost of DB calls.  Assertions using this predicate are usually updated by code at application initialization time.")
(comment hasOwnershipIn "This predicate relates agents to things of which they have part or whole ownership.  (#$hasOwnershipIn AGENT THING) means that AGENT owns a part (or the whole) of THING.  For example, Ted Turner #$hasOwnershipIn Atlanta's Olympic Stadium; there may be other owners.  See also #$legalOwnerOf and #$ownsShare.")
(comment Drawing-Depiction "The collection of all drawings.  Instances

of drawing are #$StillImages which contain significant lines.  Some occur

on paper and may be made with pencil, ink (see #$PenOrPencilDrawing), etc.. Some occur on computers and are presented via a computer

monitor.  Some are artistic (see #$ArtObject) and some are not.  Thus, a

painting composed entirely of lines would be a #$Drawing-Depiction.  A

drawing produced by a drawing program which was saved in a computer file

and was viewable on a computer monitor would also be an example.  A 

painted image composed entirely of paint splotches would probably be a

negative example of a #$Drawing-Depiction.  Such an image with a tiny line

in the corner would also probably be a negative example of a

#$Drawing-Depiction since the tiny line would not be a ``significant''

line or a focal object in the image.  An image ``drawn'' with paint using a paintbrush is currently (Nov 98) considered an agnostic example.")
(disjointWith SportsPenalizing Collision)
(comment ObstetricianGynecologist "An OB/GYN is a doctor who specializes in the treatment of women during pregnancy and childbirth in addition to diagnosing and treating problems with women's reproductive organs.")
(comment Shallow "Shallow")
(comment optionsAvailable "With respect to Agent ARG1, the value of F(ARG2) can optionally assume the values v1, v2...")
(comment BeliefSystemMicrotheory "The collection of microtheories each of which contains the assertional content of the beliefs of some religion, creed, cult, social group, school of thought, political party, or other group that has shared beliefs or doctrines.  Example: #$ChristianityMt.")
(comment LocalGovernmentEmployee "A collection of persons; a subset of #$PublicSectorEmployee.  Each element of #$LocalGovernmentEmployee is a worker who is employed by a local government.  Examples include (for the United States) local tax collectors, sheriffs or local police, aldermen, firefighters, and public school teachers.")
(comment UnitOfArea "A specialization of #$UnitOfMeasure. Each instance of #$UnitOfArea is a function which returns an instance of #$Area (q.v.) when applied to a real number (see the collection #$SubLRealNumber) or a sequence of two real numbers. For instance, (#$SquareMeter 9) is an area of 9 square meters.  Instances of #$UnitOfArea include #$SquareMile, #$SquareMeter, and #$SquareInch.")
(disjointWith ApplyingAForce MoneyTransfer)
(comment meanOfNormalDistribution "What it says.")
(comment DrillingSomething "A collection of events involving a subevent of #$DrillBit spinning along a major axis while translating along that axis through #$SolidTangibleThing, thereby making a hole and removing part of that solid.  #$DrillingSomething, itself, is not a #$Movement-Rotation as it involves not-rotational acts such as translation of the drill's body.")
(comment FeelingOfCompetence "A feeling of self-confidence with respect to a certain kind of task or area of expertise.  This is a #$Collection --- for an explanation of that, see #$Happiness.")
(comment ElectionForOffice "An event in which many people state their choices for the person to take a particular office.")
(comment ForestRanger "The collection of professional forest rangers")
(comment ManufacturingASingleObject "A collection of events.  In each #$ManufacturingASingleObject event, manufacturing procedures are applied to only a single object or a single chunk of stuff.  This includes both one-off creation events such as carving a statue, and also can be a `slice' of a #$MassManufacturing event in which all that is considered is how one single small lump of stuff or set of parts gets acted on to become some new thing.  In the latter case, then, what is `produced' is one car, one can of Coke, etc., even though that is just one part or iteration of a mass manufacturing event taking place.")
(comment AIDS "Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome.")
(comment WinterOlympicsFn "A function which takes a year and returns the winter olympic games of that year")
(comment (MediumAmountFn LevelOfPhysicalActivity) "Categorizes the level of physical activity required for everything from standing to walking")
(comment Punishing "Elements of #$Punishing are events which one agent does to another agent in return for some offense.")
(comment StarSportsEvent "A class of YachtingSportsEvent")
(comment Foraging "Looking around for food in the wild and eating it when found.  This is the activity by which many wild animals get food.  Specializations include grazing and hunting.")
(disjointWith OneDiningRoomDwelling ZeroDiningRoomDwelling)
(comment CalendarSummer "A specialization of #$CalendarSeason.  Each instance of #$CalendarSummer is a time interval that begins on a day considered to begin a summer season, and ends on a day considered to end a summer season. For example, according to mainstream culture in the U.S.A., instances of this collection begin each year on the #$JuneSolstice (about June 21) and end on the #$AutumnalEquinox (about September 21st) (see #$CalendarSummer-US), whereas according to mainstram Australasian culture, instances of this collection begin December 1st and end on the last day of February (see #$CalendarSummer-Australasian).")
(comment CenterOfISFn "An IndividualDenotingFunction for referring to the center of the piece of space depicted/displayed in an image.")
(comment AbsoluteSportsEvent "Sports where the measurements of performance can be compared across competitions. Running, swimming, jumping, but not gymnastics or downhill skiing.  Sports in which its meaningfull to have a world record, an olympic record, etc.")
(comment associatedSale "Relates a #$ChargebackRequestDetail to the particular sale that the request detail corresponds to.")
(comment LocalPoliceOrganization "A collection of law enforcement organizations.  An element of #$LocalPoliceOrganization is a local police department, not state or national police organizations.")
(comment ExtractPhoneSuffixFn "This function returns the suffix of a phone number represented as a string.  For example, (#$ExtractPhoneSuffixFn ''512-338-3634'') will return 3634.  If the suffix is not present in the phone number, the function returns NIL")
(comment SortingE-MailMessages "The collection of all events in which E-MailMessages are sorted.  The assumption is that, in the #$DevicePerspectiveMt, some program is the performer.")
(comment XRayTest "The collection of all XRay tests that determine some property of the #$objectActedOn.")
(comment BenefitsManager "A manager working on employee benefits for an organization.")
(comment TopSide "The collection of all the entire top sides (as conventionally understood) of all objects that have distinct #$Sides, one of which faces up.")
(comment HumanInfant "A specialization of #$HomoSapiens, and an instance of #$HumanTypeByLifeStageType. Each instance of this collection is a human in the infant stage of life.  Functionally, this ends when the infant learns to walk (even just toddle) and/or talk (even a few words)... or, at latest, when the person's age greatly exceeds that at which most people develop those skills.  Generally, this means that it spans the period from birth to about 12 - 18 months old. A notable specialization of this collection is #$NewbornBaby.")
(comment UsedAutoDealership "Establishment that sells used cars. ")
(disjointWith TextualMaterial Drawing-Depiction)
(disjointWith SportsPenalizing SocialGathering)
(comment EmergencyMedicineSpecialist "Doctors who specialize in emergency medical treatment.")
(comment Soft "Soft")
(disjointWith SomethingExisting BeliefSystemMicrotheory)
(comment Psychiatrist "Psychiatrists are doctors who diagnose and treat mental disorders.")
(disjointWith SocialOccurrence ElectricalEvent)
(comment PromotionalEvent "The collection of occurrences or events held at least partly to promote some product or service, or to help some candidate get elected to public office.")
(comment NormalDistribution "This represents the most general normal distribution.")
(comment SISLogicalSchema "Instances represent the propositions that define the schema (not the actual content) of a structured information source.  For schemas for database tables, see the spec #$LogicalTableSchema.  The axioms for interpreting a structured information source are expressed as assertions involving instances of #$LogicalField, which serve as prototypes for the values in the fields of the info source.  The actual content of the info source, to the extent that this content is ever imported into the Cyc KB, is represented as assertions in some instance of #$PropositionalInformationThing.")
(comment RunningDive "The collection of dives in which the diver runs to the end of the board or platform before take-off.")
(comment Cheerfulness "The emotion characterized by having a spontaneous flow of good spirits as a result of feeling glad or happy or as a result of an equable disposition or of temperament")
(comment Hitchhiking "Getting from place to place by accepting rides from other people.")
(disjointWith BatchManufacturingEvent ContinuousManufacturingProcess)
(comment Tuberculosis "A collection of infections. Instances of #$Tuberculosis are infectious diseases caused by species of Mycobacterium. Those are diseases of man and animals. Any organ may be affected, in man it is primarily the lungs that are also the usual portal for the infection to reach other organs.")
(comment DayOfYearType "Instances are collections of calendar days having a common month and day. For example, the collections October22 (i.e., the collection of every October 22) , IdesOfMarch, and February29 would be instances of #$DayOfYearType.")
(comment (HighAmountFn LevelOfPhysicalActivity) "Categorizes the level of physical activity required for everything from jogging to running a marathon")
(comment Learning "The collection of all events, brief or extended, in which an agent is acquiring information or know-how.")
(comment DoubScullsRowingSportsEvent "The rowing sports events in which sculls are propelled by two rowers with two oars each.")
(comment NLPredicate "The collection of predicates which are used to make assertions in the Cyc lexicon. Many of these predicates are mentioned in the NLU and NLG code.")
(comment AlarmSignal "A signal intended to convey some kind of warning message (to people or to devices that understand its content).")
(disjointWith ZeroDiningRoomDwelling TwoDiningRoomDwelling)
(comment HotelReservation "Each #$HotelReservation is an agreement made between a provider of lodging and a customer, that the lodging provider will reserve lodging for the customer at the time he or she requests.  This collection includes reservations for all types of commerical lodging, including motels, bed-&-breakfasts, beach cabins, etc.")
(comment CyclicalSuccessiveIntervalGroupType "A specialization of #$MutuallyDisjointIntervalCollectionType (q.v.) and a collection of collections of collections of #$TimeIntervals.  Each instance CIGTYPE of #$CyclicalSuccessiveIntervalGroupType is a collection of interval-types whose instances recur in a set pattern throughout all of calendar history.  CIGTYPE must partition all of time: the instances of CIGTYPE must be mutually disjoint and, taken all together, _their_ instances must cover all time.  For example, CIGTYPE could be the collection of the seven calendar days of the week (see #$DayOfWeekType) or the collection of the twelve calendar months (see #$MonthOfYearType).  \"Recurring in a set pattern\" means here that the instances of CIGTYPE can be put into an order INTTYPE(1), ..., INTTYPE(n) such that each instance of INTTYPE(i) (for 1 <= i < n) is immediately followed by (see #$contiguousAfter) an instance of INTTYPE(i+1), and each instance of INTTYPE(n) is immediately followed by an instance of INTTYPE(1).  For example, if CIGTYPE is #$DayOfWeekType,  INTTYPE(1) might be #$Monday (the collection of all mondays), INTTYPE(2) #$Tuesday, and so on.")
(comment overrides "The binary predicate #$overrides (which relates two instances of #$CycLAssertion) is used to tell Cyc which rule to prefer when it encounters two conflicting rules while reasoning with default assertions.  (#$overrides FIRST SECOND) means that if the assertions FIRST and SECOND both appear in conflicting arguments for and against some proposition, the argument that contains FIRST is to be preferred.")
(comment fullnessOfContainer "U has the qualitative fullness v.")
(disjointWith MakingAnOralSound ManipulatingFoodOrDrink)
(comment CombatSportsEvent "Sports which involve constrained physical combat: boxing, judo, wrestling, karate, fencing.  Protective gear is often worn.  A veneer of scoring is added, but these are basically attempts for one individual to subdue another within a set of rules. ")
(comment ChargebackRequestDetail "A component of a #$ChargebackRequest that corresponds to a single sale by a wholesaler to an end-buyer.  In it, the wholesaler is requesting payment from the commercial organization for the difference between the contract price awarded to the end-buyer by the commercial organization, and the cost to the wholesaler to replace their stock shipped to the end-buyer.")
(comment eventKnown "The predicate #$eventKnown relates an act in which some agent becomes aware of a particular event to the event of which the agent becomes aware. (#$eventKnown AWARENESS EVENT) means that the doer of the act AWARENESS becomes aware of the event EVENT. The first argument to #$eventKnown must be an element of #$BecomingAwareOfAnEvent, while the second argument must be an element of #$Event.")
(comment EquityTrader "#$EquityTrader buys and sells stock.")
(comment Spokesman "People who are authorized by some organization to speak for that organization.")
(comment AttendingPhysician "Physician with primary responsibility for a patient.")
(comment AlwaysNegativeFunction "Function which is always negative")
(comment HoldingCompany "A collection of organizations; a subset of #$LegalAgent.  An element of #$HoldingCompany is an organization which exists primarily to own controlling interests in other #$Organizations.")
(disjointWith SportsPenalizing DecompositionProcess)
(comment CardiovascularSpecialist "A cardiovascular specialist is a doctor who specializes in diagnosing and treating problems with the heart and blood vessels.")
(comment Long "Long")
(comment Trial "The subcollection of #$LegalConflict events whose instances are heard and decided by a court and are officiated by a #$Judge.")
(comment interArgReln1-4 "A binary #$InterArgRelnPredicate (q.v.).  (#$interArgReln1-4 RELN BINPRED) means that a formula built from RELN (i.e. a \"GAF\" or \"NAT\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence and  #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm) is semantically well-formed only if BINPRED holds between the first and fourth arguments to RELN (in that order) in the GAF/NAT.  That is, a formula (RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ..) is semantically well-formed only if (BINPRED ARG1 ARG4) holds.  For further explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations. See also the more general quaternary predicate #$interArgReln, which has two argument-places for specifying the pair of RELN's arguments that must be related by BINPRED.")
(comment Gynecologist "Gynecologists are doctors who specialize in disorders of the female reproductive system.")
(comment Micron "This is a unit of length derived by dividing a meter by 1,000,000 - in the real world this is about the size of a bacteria.")
(comment SISContent "The class of microtheories which represent the information content of #$StructuredInformationSources.")
(comment HittingAHomeRun "Hitting a home run, in baseball.")
(comment PunchingSomething "The action of throwing a punch and striking something - serious punches only, not playful ones.")
(comment Listlessness "The attribute-type associated with the feeling of listlessness: the felt experience of having little or no interest in or concern for what is going on around one.  Note that a mere lack of interest in-itself is not a _feeling_, and thus is not sufficient for possessing an instance of 

#$Listlessness; one's lack of interest must be consciously experienced as such.  (For the rationale behind treating feelings in terms of types -- i.e. collections -- of attributes, see the comment on #$Happiness.)")
(comment LevelOfSharpPain "The type of internal sensation or feeling of a sharp pain.")
(comment Rebelliousness-Feeling "A feeling of opposition against authority or the status quo.")
(comment DoorMan "Someone who opens and closes a door (usually the outside entrance to a hotel, apartment bldg, or commercial building frequented by many people) as the main task of his/her job.")
(comment MiddleAgedHuman "Adults between 35 and 60 years of age.")
(comment notices "(#$notices AGT PROP) means that

AGT believes the proposition PROP because AGT has seen, heard,

smelled, etc. PROP via some instance of #$Perceiving.  Although

(#$notices AGT PROP) implies (#$beliefs AGT PROP) {via the assertion

(#$genlPreds #$notices #$beliefs)}, exceptions occur if AGT believes

they have been hallucinating or drugged, for example.  The predicate

#$beliefs, unlike #$notices, can include propositions gathered through

inferring, dreaming, intuiting.  The temporal extent of (#$notices AGT

PROP) is at least a 'short time' following the perceiving of PROP.

The extent of this time is a function of the type of fact perceived or 

noticed, when forgetting or other overriding information comes into

play.")
(comment StomachFlu "The common stomach flu where you throw up a lot.")
(comment SummerOlympicsFn "A function which takes a year and returns the summer olympic games of that year")
(comment (HighAmountFn LevelOfPhysicalActivity) "Categorizes the level of physical activity required for everything from jogging to runni
ng a marathon")
(comment LongHorseVaultSportsEvent "The collection of gymnastic vaulting events on the LongHorse.")
(comment AlarmSound "An audible warning.")
(disjointWith TwoBathDwelling OneAndAHalfBathDwelling)
(comment MoneyPerAreaRatio "How much something costs per unit of area.")
(comment StructuredInformationSource "A specialization of both #$InformationStore and #$PartiallyIntangibleIndividual.  Each instance of #$StructuredInformationSource is an #$InformationStore in which bits of information are represented as related in a systematic way that is easily characterized by some type of formal structure, including spatial or architectural terms (used metaphorically).  Examples include: a database organized in fields and values; a spreadsheet organized in rows and columns with entries; an organizational tree diagram with nodes and branches; a topographical map; a document written in HTML (hyper-text markup language).  Negative examples include computer programs, poems, and novels.")
(comment MutuallyDisjointIntervalCollectionType "A collection of collections of collections of time-intervals.  Each instance INTTYPETYPE of #$MutuallyDisjointIntervalCollectionType is a collection of interval-types INTTYPE(1), ..., INTTYPE(n) whose own instances are mutually temporally disjoint, in the sense that no instance of INTTYPE(i) temporally intersects any instance of INTTYPE(j) (for 1 <= i <= n; 1 <= j <= n; i =/ j).  For example, #$DayOfWeekType (whose instances are #$Monday, #$Tuesday, etc.) is a #$MutuallyDisjointIntervalCollectionType, as no monday temporally intersects any tuesday or wednesday or ..., no tuesday temporally intersects any monday or wednesday or ..., and so on.  An important specialization of #$MutuallyDisjointIntervalCollectionType is #$CyclicalSuccessiveIntervalGroupType (q.v.), each of whose instances is such that _its_ instances recur in a cyclic pattern that covers all of time.  (#$DayOfWeekType is also an instance of #$CyclicalSuccessiveIntervalGroupType.) See also #$TemporallyDisjointTemporalObjectType.")
(comment Shaved "An attribute for describing a level of hair coverage: in this case, none, because it has been shaved off.")
(comment Fullness "The collection of states of relative fullness/emptiness")
(comment UnderstoodReflexiveObjectFrame "This frame is used for words whose subject acts as an understood reflexive object. Examples: `I dressed.' `The man shaved.'")
(comment IndividualSportsCompetition "Sports competitions where the competitors are individual agents, not teams")
(comment SalesContract "A collection of agreements; a subset of #$LegalAgreement.  Each element of #$SalesContract is a legal agreement between a selling agent and a buying agent, stipulating the terms under which the seller will provide goods and/or services to the buyer.")
(comment BecomingAwareOfAnEvent "The act of gaining knowledge or awareness of a particular action.")
(comment ExtractAreaCodeFn "This function returns the area code of a phone number represented as a string.  For example, (#$ExtractAreaCodeFn ''512-338-3634'') will return 512.  If the area code is not present in the phone number, the function returns NIL")
(comment ForeignExchangeTrader "#$ForeignExchangeTrader buys and sells smth.")
(comment Optometrist "The collection of professionally trained healthcare providers who diagnose and treat conditions and diseases of the human eye.  This includes the writing of prescriptions for corrective lenses.")
(comment AnimalActivity "A specialization of #$Action.   Each instance of #$AnimalActivity is a spatially-localized action, each of whose \"doers\" (see #$doneBy) is either an #$Animal or a  group of animals (i.e. a #$Group all of whose members are #$Animals).")
(disjointWith AlwaysNegativeFunction AlwaysPositiveFunction)
(comment ThrowingADiscus "The collection of events in which an agent throws a discus while particpating in the discus throw sporting event")
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization NationalTaxAgency)
(comment InterferingWithOpponent "The interfering with your opponents performance in ways not allowed by the rules of the game.")
(comment ClinicalPharmacologist "The collection of pharmacologists who study the therapeutic properties of drugs.")
(comment Narrow "Narrow, as in minded.")
(comment countryPhoneCode "(#$countryPhoneCode PLACE CODE) means that CODE is a country telephone code number for the #$GeopoliticalEntity or #$GeographicalRegion PLACE.  Countries, colonies, even the #$ContinentOfAntarctica have \"country codes\".  A country normally has only one telephone country code number (exceptions may exist for a while if two countries join such as the two Germanies or the two Yemens, or a place (e.g. Hong Kong) is absorbed by a different country).  Several countries may share the same country code number, using different city/area codes.")
(comment hasOdorMagnitude "If arg1  (#$PartiallyTangible or #$PieceOfFreeSpace) has (vis a vis placeHasOdor or objectEmitsOdor) some #$Odor arg2, tells its  magnitude arg3. ")
(comment Orthopaedist "Orthopaedists are concerned with the correction and prevention of of skeletal deformities.")
(comment Field-LogicalOrPhysical "The class of all fields, physical or logical, in the schemas of structured information sources.")
(comment Minister "The leader of a Protestant church.")
(comment UnconsciousPhysicalActivityLevel "Categorizes the level of physical activity required for everything from a physiological process occuring to sitting")
(comment Contentment "Feeling of satisfaction with one's possessions, status, or situation. Appeasement to the point where one is not disquieted or disturbed by a desire for what s/he does not have")
(comment LevelOfBurningSensation "The type of internal feeling or sensation of burning .")
(comment HospitalCareEvent "What happens when you are in the hospital being treated for a disease like Cancer or Hepatitis or AIDS, or recovering from Surgery.  This is not just a #$MedicalCareEvent which happens in a hospital; it's the whole event meant by a hospital stay.  Also see #$HospitalRoomStay which only represents the stay in the room.")
(disjointWith MiddleAgedHuman OldHuman)
(comment Dirtiness "A specialization of #$ScalarInterval.  Each instance of the collection #$Dirtiness is a specific level of dirtiness (or, alternatively, cleanliness).  Instances of  #$Dirtiness include #$Dirty, #$ReallyDirty, #$ALittleDirty, #$Clean, and #$Sterile.  Indicate a particular object's #$Dirtiness with the predicate #$dirtinessOfObject (q.v.).")
(comment SocialSecurityNumber "A specialization of #$UniqueID and #$IDNumber.  Each instance of #$SocialSecurityNumber is a nine-digit unique identification number assigned by the #$SocialSecurityAdministration to a particular individual's #$SocialSecurityAccount.")
(comment SportsJacket "The collection of lightweight, single-breasted #$Jackets, worn for casual or sports events.")
(comment SocialAgreement "agreements that are endorsed by soceity but might not have any legal status")
(comment Swim-200MeterBreaststroke "Swimming race - 200 meter breaststroke.")
(comment SteeringWheelImmobilizer "A passive security device for preventing auto thefts.  A device that, when locked in place, prevents the steering wheel of a car from turning normally.  Some kinds stop the gas pedal, too.")
(disjointWith TwoBathDwelling ThreeBathDwelling)
(comment BillingScheme "Methods used for computing the price of in a Buying - see the instances for examples.")
(disjointWith BeliefSystem StructuredInformationSource)
(disjointWith TimePoint CalendarSeason)
(comment PartiallyHairy "An attribute for describing a body part which is partially, but not totally, covered with hair.")
(comment Empty "The state of being empty, with reference to any individual object considered as a container.")
(comment EstheticJudgedSportsEvent "Judged sports events where the esthetic opinions of the judges are supposed to be part of the evaluation process.  Ice Dancing as opposed to Platform Diving.  Its sometimes a thin line, but supposedly Platform Diving is evaluated according to purely tecnical guidelines")
(comment ChargebackRequest "The subevent of a chargeback in which a wholesaler requests payment from a commercial organization for the difference between contract prices awarded to an end-buyer by the commercial organization, and the cost to the wholesaler to replace their stock shipped to the end-buyer.  A single #$ChargebackRequest is composed of several #$ChargebackRequestDetails, each of which correspond to a single sale by the wholesaler to the end-buyer.  The amount requested in the #$ChargebackRequest is the sum of the amounts requested in its component #$ChargebackRequestDetails.")
(comment Speculum "The collection of all hand tools used to dialate an opening in the body cavity for medical examination.  Different types ofpecula are used for opening surgical incisions and natural cavities (e.g. for a gyneclogical examination).")
(comment ProgramCoordinator "An admistrator who manages a program, but not necessarily the head of an organization.")
(comment FunctionalSlot "A specialization of #$FunctionalPredicate each instance of which is a binary predicate that is functional in its second argument position.  More precisely, a binary predicate PRED is an instance of #$FunctionalSlot if, for any legal occupant THING1 of PRED's first (or \"arg1\") argument position, there is at most one legal occupant THING2 of PRED's second (or \"arg2\") argument position such that (PRED THING1 THING2) holds.  (The foregoing sufficient condition is not necessary in the case where the arg2 entry-format of PRED is #$intervalEntryFormatInArgs (q.v.) instead of #$singleEntryFormatInArgs; see the comment for #$FunctionalPredicate for that case. Cf. #$StrictlyFunctionalSlot.)  #$FunctionalSlot is thus the subcollection of the \"collection-intersection\" of #$BinaryPredicate and #$FunctionalPredicate containing those predicates whose second argument (at least) is functional.  Examples include #$latitude, #$countryOfAddress, and #$femaleParentActor.")
(comment FrontSide "The collection of all the entire front sides (as conventionally understood) of all objects that have distinct #$Sides, one of which faces in the frontwards direction.")
(comment DetachedHouse "Individual residence separated from others, typically surrounded by a yard.")
(comment WrestlingHold "The collection of events in which one agent uses a wrestling hold to physically manipulate another agent")
(comment AutoPartsStore "Each instance is a local organization (located at one site) that sells parts for automobiles and other motorized road vehicles.")
(disjointWith WeatherEvent AnimalSound)
(comment PointsPenalizing "A penalty of losing the points off your score.")
(comment Wide "Wide")
(comment Trial-Criminal "A trial in which a court determines whether the defendent is guilty as charged, and, if so, the punishment the defendent is to receive.")
(comment OdorLevel "Instances are scalars which indicate how powerful a particular odor or smell might be.  The higher the magnitude, the more noticeable the odor is.")
(comment hostOfEvent "(#$hostOfEvent GATHERING AGENT) means that AGENT is a host of the #$SocialGathering GATHERING.")
(comment Pediatrician "Pediatricians are doctors who specialize in the branch of medicine concerned with the care of children and the treatment of childhood diseases.")
(comment TimeOfDayType "A specialization of #$ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries-Disjoint (q.v.), containing every type TYPE of time intervals such that each calendar day intersects, indeed subsumes, exactly one member of TYPE; that is to say, the relation #$temporallySubsumes, when restricted to #$CalendarDay times TYPE, is a one-one function from #$CalendarDay to TYPE.  Examples include #$TimeOfDay-PM, #$TimeOfDay-9AM, and #$TimeOfDay-MidnightHour.")
(comment Priest "Person, usually male, who is the leader of a Catholic or Epicopalian church.")
(disjointWith Landing WeatherEvent)
(comment Depression-Feeling "An emotion marked by sadness, inactivity, difficulty in thinking and concentration, feelings of dejection and hopelessness; unhappiness, discouraged and without vigor")
(comment LevelOfSoreness "The type of internal sensation or feeling of being sore.")
(disjointWith BlueCollarWorker PublicOfficial)
(comment RealEstateAgent "The collection of all people who professionally represent sellers, buyers, landlords or tenants of real estate or apartments.  They often drive their potential buyers or tenants around and show them properties.  Most but not all are members of #$RealEstateFirms.")
(comment Manufacturing "A collection of events.  In each #$Manufacturing event, raw materials or component parts are combined to produce a product (whether by a #$ManufacturingOrganization or by an individual).  In a typical #$Manufacturing process, the motivation of the manufacturer is that the value of the #$outputs should exceed the value of the #$inputs.  #$Manufacturing does not include related or supportive processes such as transporting the raw materials to the manufacturing site, scheduling done ahead of time, etc. -- the concept #$ProductionEvent covers that bigger picture. A notable specialization of this collection is #$MassManufacturing.")
(comment SecureCommunication "A kind of communication where there exists a #$communicationTarget, and if an agent receives the communication, they are the target.")
(comment NonPositiveScalarInterval "For a measurable non-positive

quantity, the ordered sequence of possible values may be thought of as a

line. #$NonPositiveScalarIntervals are the line segments (or points)

on such a line, representing a range of consecutive values, all equal to

or less than 0. An important subcollection is #$NonPositiveNumber the  

instances of which correspond to the non-positive part of the Real Number

Line. Instances of #$NonPositiveNumber are either contiguous sets of

points there (i.e., a range of numbers) or just single points there (i.e.,

a number). Instances of #$NonPositiveScalarInterval for which there is

some unit of measure (e.g. volts, degrees fahrenheit) are not instances of

#$NonPositiveNumber.")
(comment hasAssociatedRitual "The instance of SpecialEvent U has the associated ritual events v1, v2, ... vN.")
(comment Weaving "The process by which filamentlike materials are woven.")
(comment Goal "Typically, this attribute characterizes relationships holding between Cyc formulas and a particular agent when the formula describes a state of affairs that the agent intends to take steps to actualize, i.e., when actualizing the state of affairs is a goal of the agent.  However, it might also be seen as an attribute of the relationship between the agent and the static situation depicted by that cyc formula (see #$StateFn).  This is the most general goal attribute and should be used only when one is unable to specify more exactly what kind of goal the relevant state of affairs is for an agent.")
(comment DoublesTableTennisGame "Games of Doubles Table-Tennis, or PingPong.")
(comment Tie-Clothing "The collection of ties that are worn around the neck.")
(comment SecurityDevice "A collection of physical devices.  An instance of #$SecurityDevice is any device designed to protect people or goods from being harmed (or stolen) intentionally.  Some instances of #$SecurityDevice accomplish this by keeping unauthorized or unwelcome intruders away from the people or materials in question (e.g., elements of #$AntiTheftDevice, #$PerimeterSensor).  Others are designed to make it impossible or difficult to remove goods (e.g., elements of #$Lock).  Compare with #$SafetyDevice, whose elements are designed to protect an object or animal against accidental harm.  Of course some devices play multiple roles --- a single fence may be a security device to keep burglars out, and may protect toddlers from wandering in and falling into a swimming pool.")
(disjointWith OneAndAHalfBathDwelling ThreeBathDwelling)
(comment Painter-Tradesperson "Someone who paints walls & other construction artifacts as a job.")
(comment secondPersonSg-Present "The relationship between an #$EnglishWord and its second person singular verb form.")
(disjointWith TimeOfDay CalendarSeason)
(comment SkinnyPhysicalBuild "Thin in proportion to one's bone structure.")
(comment Full "The state of being full, with reference to any individual object considered as a container")
(comment SymbolicObject "A specialization of both #$SymbolicThing and #$HumanAccessibleIBO. Each instance of #$SymbolicObject is a #$SymbolicThing 
that has some material part (i.e. is an instance of #$PartiallyTangible), and symbolizes some thing, event or achievement, without describing it propositionally in any detail.  Examples include national flags, military medals and ribbons, an Oscar, a Crucifix, a caduceus, and printed trademark logos of commercial brands.  Only some instances of #$SymbolicObject have the #$primaryFunction of serving as symbols (e.g. national flags, war memorials); others are symbolic in a secondary capacity (e.g. a gravestone symbolizes death but its primary function is as a marker), and/or acquire symbolic associations over time (e.g. Ellis Island).  Examples of #$SymbolicObject include the #$ArcDeTriomphe, the #$StatueOfLiberty, the #$PyramidOfCheops, a hangman's noose, a Menorah, a white dove.  Negative examples include #$NationalAnthems and #$Swastikas projected on walls, because these do not have a material part; for such symbols use the broader collection #$SymbolicThing.")
(disjointWith CommunicationAct-Single PerformanceTesting)
(comment SinglesFigureSkatingSportsEvent "The single person figure skating competition")
(comment Chargeback "A chargeback is a commercial activity in which a wholesaler submits a claim to a commercial organization for the difference between contract prices awarded to an end-buyer by the commercial organization, and the cost to the wholesaler to replace their stock shipped to the end-buyer.  The commercial organization then evaluates the wholesaler's claim, and either: 1.) accepts the claim, and thereby pays the wholesaler all, or part of, (or even more than) the amount claimed; or 2.) rejects the claim, giving the wholesaler reasons for the rejection.")
(comment PreservingOwnSpecies "This attribute characterizes situations in which biological objects (#$BiologicalLivingObject) pursue the preservation of their own species.  Often this will be attributed to relationships between agents and cyc formulas that describe states of affairs in which the agent is attempting to preserve one's own species.")
(comment commissionPercentage "The percent of each sale to be paid by the employer/seller to the comissioned salesperson/employee as (possibly partial) compensation for making the sale.")
(comment ContinuingEdProgramCoordinator "A person who administers a continuing education program.")
(comment HumanOccupationConstruct "A specialization of both #$ConstructionArtifact and #$HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject.  Each instance of #$HumanOccupationConstruct is a construction artifact whose primary function is to serve as a place where people perform certain activities.  Instances of #$HumanOccupationConstruct include instances of #$HumanShelterConstruction (e.g., houses), sub-regions within a #$HumanShelterConstruction which are intended for human use (e.g., rooms, shower stalls), and  regions in any transportation vehicle which are designed for human occupancy (e.g., a cockpit, a passenger compartment).  Note that some buildings which are not themselves instances of #$HumanOccupationConstruct, such as #$HooverDam, may have a sub-region which is a #$HumanOccupationConstruct (e.g., the control room at the top of the dam).  Note also that the collection #$HumanOccupationConstruct is broad enough to include tents, boiler rooms, elevator shafts, steam tunnels, and the space inside the #$LincolnMemorialInWashingtonDC.  Consequently, an instance of #$HumanOccupationConstruct need not be completely indoors (see #$Indoors-IsolatedFromOutside), although it cannot be purely outdoors (see #$OutdoorLocation).")
(comment forceCapacity "The slot describing the capability of an animal to exert force.")
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization FinancialOrganization)
(comment PhysicalInterferenceWithOpponent-Excessive "Physically interfering with an opponent outside of certain set limits.  For example, hitting below the belt in boxing.")
(comment ForensicPathologist "A forensic pathologist is a doctor who applies knowledge of pathology in the legal domain.")
(comment Short "Short")
(comment Internist "Internists are specialists in internal medicine, especially as distinguished from surgeons.")
(comment infinitive "This predicate relates #$LexicalWords (q.v.) to their corresponding infinitive verb forms.  (#$infinitive WORD STRING) means that STRING is an infinitive verb form of WORD.  But note that for the sake of convenience STRING does _not_ include the marker `to' that is commonly given at the beginning of an (English) infinitive.  For example, #$infinitive relates #$Hit-TheWord simply to the string `hit' (rather than `to hit').  Note also that, in the Knowledge Base (KB), the closed atomic sentences (i.e. \"GAF\"s) built with #$infinitive typically have #$SubLStrings (q.v.) as their second arguments, as indicated by a surrounding pair of double-quotation marks.  So the above example actually appears in the KB as `(#$infinitive #$Hit-TheWord \"hit\")'.")
(comment IncurringPhysicalDamage "A specialization of #$PhysicalEvent and #$IncurringDamage. Each instance of this collection is an event in which some sort of physical damage is incurred to an organism or material object. Notable specializations include #$IncurringBodilyHarm, #$IncurringEquipmentDamage and #$DegenerationEvent. For cases where the damage incurred is so extensive that the thing is destroyed, see the more specialized #$PhysicalDestructionEvent.")
(comment HarvestingAField "The collection of field harvesting events")
(comment Resolution-Emotion "Emotion of one who is firm of mind and purpose, capable of resisting temptations or surrender in face of opposition, danger or hardship")
(comment LevelOfDullThrobbingPain "The type of internal sensation or feeling of a dull, throbbing pain.")
(comment PublicOfficial "A subcollection of #$PublicSectorEmployee and an instance of #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg.  Each instance of #$PublicOfficial is a person who holds a position that is directly involved with some aspect of governing a country (or subregion of a country).  Many public offices in democratically governed countries are filled by election; some are filled by appointment.  In other countries, public offices are sometimes filled by succession or by military decree.  Note that public offices are represented in Cyc in terms of the collections of officials who hold those offices (e.g. #$Mayor and #$UnitedStatesPresident) together with axioms describing the responsibilities those offices entail.")
(comment TravelingSalesPerson "A #$SalesPerson who travels around selling things; by default, they have to have a car.")
(comment raceLength "The length of a race, the distance traveled by the competitors between the beginning and ending of the event.")
(comment Homogenizing "the class of events in which an object is homogenized")
(comment EnrollingInSchool "The enrolling of a student in an educational institution.")
(comment FreestyleSkiingSportsEvent "The alpine sports events in which competitors are judged rather than timed")
(comment PerimeterSensor "A security device that senses when a certain boundary has been crossed.  One method is with photovoltaic detectors; another is with wired electrical contacts.")
(disjointWith OneLivingRoomDwelling TwoLivingRoomDwelling)
(comment PPTByAdministrationRouteType "The collection of types of drug products which are specified as to administration route, and may be specified as to dosage form and type of preparation (the drug compound(s) contained).")
(comment Industry-Localized "Each element of the collection #$Industry-Localized is a particular #$Group of producers of a particular kind of good or service (usually in a defined geographic area).  For instance, the United States' automobile industry would be an element of #$Industry-Localized, and would have U.S. automobile manufacturers  like #$GeneralMotors, #$Daimler-ChryslerTheCompany, #$FordTheCompany etc. as #$groupMembers.  For major economic sectors consisting of many industries, use #$EconomicSector-Localized and #$EconomicSectorType, which refer to larger groups.  Thus, 'the world agriculture sector', or 'the technology sector in the United States' refer to instances of #$EconomicSector-Localized rather than instances of #$Industry-Localized.  'The U.S. Automobile Industry' should be considered a sub-industry (see #$subIndustries) of 'The U.S. Industrial Sector'.  Note that specific kinds of industry (#$IndustryTypes like #$MetallurgyIndustry) are #$Collections of particular (often geographically defined) industries; they are not individual industries (instances of #$Industry-Localized) in this scheme.  That is, there are several instances of #$MetallurgyIndustry, such as the German metallurgy industry, the Mexican metallurgy industry, etc.  There is also the worldwide metallurgy industry.  These may be described as (#$IndustryOfRegionFn #$MetallurgyIndustry #$Germany), etc.  Thus the collection #$MetallurgyIndustry is a specialization, not an instance, of #$Industry-Localized.  See also #$MtOfIndustryTypeFn and #$MtOfIndustryOfRegionFn which create microtheories for the types and the individuals, respectively.")
(comment UnderstoodReciprocalObjectFrame "This frame is used for words whose (plural) subject acts as an understood 

          reciprocal object. Example: `They were flirting the whole night.")
(comment StandardAutoMarketCategory "Car products typically found in department stores with automotive departments.")
(disjointWith CommunicationAct-Single Manufacturing)
(comment SkiJumpLargeSportsEvent "The large hill ski jump event")
(comment totalProjectedRxCountForOrgDuring "The organization ARG2 reported a projected total of ARG4  prescriptions dispensed/filled for the product type ARG1 during the time interval ARG3.")
(comment SubLForm "A collection of lists in the Cyc System.  Each element of #$SubLForm is a list that represents a function call, i.e., an expression that can be EVAL'ed by the CycL interpreter, or at least compiled by the CycL compiler.")
(comment ComputerHardwareIndustry "The collection of all computer hardware industries. (Each is an element of of #$Industry-Localized.)

Each element of the collection is a #$Group of manufacturers and/or

entrepreneurs whose output is related in some way to the manufacturing

and/or distributing of computer hardware; e.g., mainframes, CPUs, monitors, disk drives, chips, etc.  See also #$SoftwareIndustry and #$ComputerIndustry.")
(comment IndexFinger "The second #$Finger on the human hand, closest to the thumb.")
(comment restrictsMovement "arg1 restricts the movement of arg2")
(comment NewbornMedicalSpecialist "A newborn medical specialist is a doctor who specializes in the treatment of babies under one month old.")
(comment totalChromosomeNumber "The total number of chromosomes. Also expressed as 1N for haploid cells, 2N for diploid cells, etc., where N is numberOfChromosomesPerSet.")
(comment SoundPitch "The collection of attributes that describe the pitch of a sound.")
(comment Obstetrician "Obstetricians are doctors who specialize in the treatment of women during pregnancy and childbirth.")
(comment plural "(#$plural WORD STRING) means that the #$CharacterString STRING is the plural noun form of the #$LexicalWord WORD.  For example, the #$plural form of #$Hit-TheWord is `hits', and the plural form of #$Goose-TheWord is `geese'.  Note that this is the plural form corresponding to the #$CountNoun part of speech. See also #$pnPlural for #$ProperCountNoun forms, and #$agentive-Pl for #$AgentiveNoun forms.")
(comment CalendarDecade "An instance of #$CalendarCoveringType, and a specialization of #$Date.  Each instance of #$CalendarDecade is a decade on a particular calendar.  For the example, the nineteen eighties is an instance of #$CalendarDecade.")
(comment IncurringAnInjury "A collection of events.  An instance of #$IncurringAnInjury is an event in which an animal becomes injured.  In such events, the animal which is hurt is the #$bodilyActedOn in the event.  The condition which results of an instance of #$IncurringAnInjury would be an instance of #$InjuryCondition (q.v.).  Also see the comment on #$AilmentCondition.")
(comment PlantingAPlant "The collection of all events in which a (usually immature) plant is intentionally placed in or covered with soil")
(comment LevelOfPhysicalPleasure "The type of internal sensation or feeling of pleasure.")
(comment Love-Romantic "The subcollection of #$Love that is romantic love-- to be distinguished from love between parents and children or between people and their pets.")
(comment Potter "A person who works with clay and makes pots and ceramic dishes.")
(comment Command "A kind of illocutionary force associated with commanding.  When illocutionary act has this illocutionary force, then the speaker intends to have the listener either carry out the action described in the utterance and/or bring about the situation described in the utterance.  The speaker in any given instance of #$Ordering-CommunicationAct presupposes that s/he has the authority to command those s/he adresses.  `Speaker' and `listener' are broadly interpreted to mean, respectively, any #$senderOfInfo and #$recipientOfInfo.")
(comment NewYearsEveDay "Each of these is a one-day-long annual #$Holiday celebrating the ending of one calendar year, and presaging the beginning of the next.   Each of these occurs on December 31st, the last day of the year.")
(comment GumSurgery "Surgery on a patient's gums.")
(comment SmallRifleProneShootingSportsEvent "A marksmanship sports event in which small-ore rifles are used in a prone position.")
(comment Coaching "Instructing or training a performer or team of performers")
(comment BundleFn "#$BundleFn(TYPE) returns the collection of all bundles of things of type TYPE.  For instance, #$BundleFn(#$String-Textile) returns the collection of bundles of string, i.e., pieces of strings that are collected in a group, as opposed to arbitrary subsets of the #$Collection #$String-Textile.  Note that this function is more specific than #$GroupFn because the objects that make up the bundle are attached to each other or are in very close proximity, i.e., are bundles.")
(disjointWith ZeroFamilyRoomDwelling TwoFamilyRoomDwelling)
(disjointWith FiscalYear CalendarSeason)
(disjointWith TangibleStuffCompositionType TangibleStuffStateType)
(disjointWith CookingFood Sewing)
(comment CourtAndNetGame "Games where the competitors move an object back and forth between parts of the playing field.  Typically, each competitor has their side of the field and there is something akin to a net between them.  Points are scored when the object is not returned correctly.  Volleyball, Tennis, Badmintion, TableTennis, etc. Handball, Racketball, and Squash are quite similar, event though they are ab in some important respects, so they comprise a spec.")
(comment Hydrocortisone "The chemical compound which is a steroid.")
(comment RequestingToMakeAPurchase "Communicating, in some medium, a request to purchase goods or services; specifies which items the potential buyer is interested in purchasing. This implies an obligation on the part of the performer/requestor to participate in the buying as specified by the (possibly implicit) terms of the request if these terms are accepted by the recipient of the request (ergo this is a kind of offering).")
(comment averageProfit "The average bucks per unit time this business makes as profit.")
(disjointWith Water-Fresh Water-Saline)
(comment ClinicalInvestigator "A Medical Care Professional in clinical practice who is involved in research.")
(disjointWith Microtheory FieldOfStudy)
(comment PeoplePerSquareMile "The number of human inhabitants found in a square mile of area.")
(comment South-Generally "An instance of #$GeographicalDirection-General (q.v.).  From a given reference point, #$South-Generally comprises the wedge-shaped set of vectors that point within 22.5 degrees (in either horizontal direction) of #$South-Directly.")
(comment BenchPenalizing "A penalty in which the offending player must sit out for a period of the game, or even a period of the season.")
(comment JCAHAccreditation "A credential issued by the Joint Commission on Accreditation of Hospitals to hospitals that have been accredited in accordance with JCAH's rules and regulations.")
(comment inputSignals "The inputs of an electrical device.")
(comment Cardiologist "Cardiologists are doctors who specialize in the study and care of the heart, its actions and diseases.")
(comment Are-UnitOfArea "NOT ACRE! This is a metric unit of area which is equivalent to a square 10 meters on a side.")
(comment regularDegree "The relationship between an #$EnglishWord and its regular adjectival form.  Example: 'strong'.")
(comment StealingABase "When a runner on one of the bases runs to the next consecutive base when not during a hit, walk or error. Usually while the pitcher has the ball.")
(comment FlowerArranging "the act of arranging flowers for display")
(comment Awe "Emotion inspired by something which arouses one's deep respect, veneratioon and wonder. Implies a sense of being overwhelmed or overcome by great superiority or impressiveness.")
(comment LevelOfIrritationSensation "The type of internal feeling or sensation of being physically irritated.")
(comment choices "This predicate relates an act of making a selection (see  #$SelectingSomething) to each of the items that could be (or could have been) selected in that act.  (#$choices CHOOSING OPTION) means that in the event CHOOSING, OPTION is (was) one of the items that the chooser might choose (might have chosen).  Depending upon the type of CHOOSING, OPTION might be a person (e.g. a job applicant or political candidate), a product (e.g. a computer, automobile, or lipstick), a plan or course of action, a policy or belief, or something else.  Also depending upon the type of CHOOSING, one or more of the possible choices might ultimately be selected.")
(comment FamilyCohabitationUnit "The collection of family units (relatives) whose members live together.  A FamilyCohabitationUnit may include friends of the family, but it must include some members of one family (relativesByMarriage or biologicalRelatives) to be a FamilyCohabitationUnit")
(comment AntennaSocket "A socket located on the back of the television in which the antenna cord is plugged .")
(comment MetaKnowledgePredicate "A collection of predicates, each instance of which is used to state things about the Cyc system or the CycL language itself -- usually about a particular reified constant or assertion in the Knowledge Base.  Examples include #$myCreator, #$cyclistNotes, #$sharedNotes, #$salientAssertions, and #$assertionConclusionActionType.")
(comment GeneralSurgery "This is the kind of surgery which most surgeons are capable of - things like stitching a wound, appendectomy, etc.  Although, there are some cases of general surgery which can be done by non-surgeons, like stitching small wounds, these tasks are typically deferred to an available surgeon when possible.")
(comment PhilosophyBeliefs "The class of #$BeliefSystems that deal in rather abstract terms with what can be known, what is and what can be, and/or with what should be.  Sample elements of #$PhilosophyBeliefs include #$MilesianSchoolBeliefs, #$ThalesPhilosophy, etc.")
(comment FireArmSportsEvent "Marksman sports events, involving guns.")
(disjointWith ThreeBedroomDwelling TwoBedroomDwelling)
(comment MoneyPerDistanceRatio "How much something costs per linear distance.  The meaning may be different between, e.g., the cost of building a highway (per mile) and the cost of operating a car (per mile).")
(comment LocalAreaNetwork "A kind of network in which computers nearby to one another interconnect. Where the interconnection makes use of internet technology such as TCP/IP and web servers, see the more specialized #$Intranet.")
(comment CalendarWinter "A specialization of #$CalendarSeason. Each instance of #$CalendarWinter is a time interval that begins on a day considered to begin a winter season, and ends on a day considered to end a winter season.  For example, according to mainstream culture in the U.S.A., instances of this collection begin each year on the #$DecemberSolstice (about December 21) and end on the #$VernalEquinox (about March 21) each year (see #$CalendarWinter-US), whereas according to mainstram Australasian culture, instances of this collection begin June 1st and end August 31st (see #$CalendarWinter-Australasian).")
(comment StockyPhysicalBuild "The attribute of being bulky, `big-boned', `large-for-height', `solid' in physical build.  This is orthogonal to being fat.")
(comment ComputerDiskType "The collection of computer disk types")
(comment ApplicationContext "Contexts which are persistent yet contain knowledge specific to a certain application.  An example would be a context that contains all the meaning formulae and other descriptions of the tables in a certain database.")
(comment deliveryDate "the date on which the objects purchased in the buying are delivered to the buyer")
(disjointWith PhysiologicalProcess Meeting-SocialGathering)
(comment Ultravate "The chemical compound which is a steroid.")
(comment RationalNumber "A specialization of #$RealNumber.  A number NUM is an instance of #$RationalNumber just in case NUM can be expressed as the quotient of two integers.  For example, 3/4, 2 1/8, 0.3333333..., 11/5.")
(comment extraFourDigitsOfZip "The extra four digit portion of the zip code of this contact location represented as a number")
(disjointWith GaseousTangibleThing LiquidTangibleThing)
(comment HospitalSalesManager "A sales manager working for a hospital.")
(disjointWith HumanOccupationConstruct SheetOfSomeStuff)
(comment CulDeSac "A residential street that comes to an end - i.e., a dead end or a circle.")
(comment North-Generally "An instance of #$GeographicalDirection-General (q.v.).  From a given reference point, #$North-Generally comprises the wedge-shaped set of vectors that point within 22.5 degrees (in either horizontal direction) of #$North-Directly.")
(comment LossOfPossessionPenalizing "A penalty in which the ball or puck is turned over to your opponent's control.")
(comment Accreditation "A collection of abstract (intangible) objects consisting of information; a subset of #$Credential.  Each element of #$Accreditation is a credential, issued to an organization by the appropriate authority, that declares the issuer's approval of the quality of the recipient's activities.  For example, accreditation of an educational organization to offer a kind of degree or training; or accreditation of a hospital to offer medical services.")
(comment numberOfChromosomeSets "The number of sets of chromosomes.")
(comment interArgReln1-2 "A binary #$InterArgRelnPredicate (q.v.).  (#$interArgReln1-2 RELN BINPRED) means that a formula built from RELN (i.e. a \"GAF\" or \"NAT\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence and  #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm) is semantically well-formed only if BINPRED holds between the first and second arguments to RELN (in that order) in the GAF/NAT.  That is, a formula (RELN ARG1 ARG2 ..) is semantically well-formed only if (BINPRED ARG1 ARG2) holds.  For example, (#$interArgReln1-2 #$relativePosition #$cotemporal) means that the first and second arguments in #$relativePosition assertions must be cotemporal.  For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations. See also the more general quaternary predicate #$interArgReln, which has two argument-places for specifying the pair of RELN's arguments that must be related by BINPRED.")
(comment ColorScheme "Identifies colors that are grouped (e.g., the colors a decorator might choose for furnishing a room) or that have meaning together (e.g., the red, white and blue of the USA flag).")
(comment BuyingAnObject "A collection of events; a subset of #$Buying.  In an instance of #$BuyingAnObject, the thing purchased (i.e., the #$objectPaidFor) is a material object.  Cf. #$BuyingAService.")
(comment singular "(#$singular WORD STRING) means that STRING is the singular noun form of WORD.  For example, the #$singular form of #$Hit-TheWord is `hit'.")
(comment Perceiving "A specialization of both #$SingleDoerAction and #$InformationTransferPhysicalEvent.  Each instance of #$Perceiving is an event in which an agent (an instance of #$PerceptualAgent) acquires information through the exercise of its senses.")
(comment HittingAnOpponent "Hitting an opponent with the arms.")
(comment HarvestingACrop "The collection of field harvesting events")
(comment LexicalSlot "The collection #$LexicalSlot exists mainly to propagate values for threshold, aPrioriLikelihood, and defaultCF.  It is not clear to me that these slots are meaningful in this context, but the system forces me to include them.  If have tried to choose values reflecting the precise nature of the lexical enterprise.  That is, although any particular usage of the word `flower' may be ambiguous, it is nearly certain that in general, the objects which are in fact flowers are among the possible meanings of flower.  As for the threshold, we don't want lexical entries unless the lexicographer is quite certain he is right.  As for aPrioriLikelihood, it is highly unlikely that, for example, some arbitrarily choosen word will have among its possible meanings some arbitrarily choosen concept.  The number  .01 was choosen based on the estimated size of CYC's lexica for the forseeable future.        Another possible value of this unit is simply as an organizing concept allowing lexicographers quick access to the existing slots relevant to their interests.")
(comment LevelOfTingling "A collection of attributes representing different levels of an internal sensation or feeling of tingling.")
(comment TheGroupMemberFn "A TheTerm-forming function denoting any member of group ARG1")
(comment Carpenter "A person who constructs things or works with wood.")
(comment TangibleProductDistribution "A transfer of a TangibleProduct from one place to another as part of the overall transfer of the product from producer to consumer.")
(comment enforcementFor "(#$enforcementFor ?EF ?COC ?ROLE) means that ?EF is the script for enforcing ?ROLE's compliance with ?COC.")
(comment famousFor "ARG1 is famous to members of ARG2, for the role played in ARG3.  ARG3 should at least refer to ARG1, and probably should be propositionAbout that Agent.  Note that this assertion does not distinguish between fame and infamy - that should be stated elsewhere, e.g. in a likes/dislikes statement, or feelsTowardsEvent.")
(comment IssuingAPrescription "What doctors do when they write or call a pharmacy to say that a given patient should take a given drug according to some schedule.")
(comment GettingAJob "The activity of getting a job.  This unit should be fleshed out to include the stereotypical steps involved in getting a job.  These might include: responding to a notice, sending a resume, going for an interview, negotiating for a salary, etc.")
(comment LightHeavyweightWeightliftingSportsEvent "A weight class of WeightliftingSportsEvent")
(disjointWith ChainOrganization SingleSiteOrganization)
(comment WeatherTesting "Testing a product for its ability to stand up to severe weather conditions, for example, testing a car for its resistance to wind, rain, etc.")
(disjointWith ThreeBedroomDwelling OneBedroomDwelling)
(comment CommunicationsSecurityProtocol "#$CommunicationsSecurityProtocol is

the collection of instances of #$NetworkProtocol that are protocols for

secure transmission and reception of information.")
(comment CalendarSpring "A specialization of #$CalendarSeason.  Each instance of #$CalendarSpring is a time interval that begins on a day considered to begin a spring season, and ends on a day considered to end a spring season. For example, according to mainstream culture in the U.S.A., instances of this collection begin each year on the #$VernalEquinox (about March 21) and end on the #$JuneSolstice (about June 21st) (see #$CalendarSpring-US), whereas according to mainstream Australasian culture, instances of this collection begin September 1st and end November 30th (see #$CalendarSpring-Australasian).")
(comment CubicCentimeter "An instance of #$UnitOfVolume.  When applied to a number or a pair of numbers, #$CubicCentimeter returns an instance of #$Volume.  For example, (#$CubicCentimeter 10) is a volume of ten cubic centimeters.")
(comment Boiling "A collection of events and a specialization of #$StateOfMatterChangeEvent. In each instance of this collection some liquid matter is raised to its #$boilingPoint and is thereby changed from being in the #$Liquid-StateOfMatter to being in the #$Gaseous-StateOfMatter. (Note: this does not cover cases of heat or evacuation causing a solid to sublime directly into a gas.) See also #$BoilingFood, which is not a specialization of this collection since it is not the food itself which is being boiled but the water in which it is cooking.")
(disjointWith IndividualSportsCompetition TeamSportsCompetition)
(comment BeclomethasoneDipropionate "The chemical compound which is a cortico-steroid")
(comment NonNegativeInteger "#$NonNegativeInteger is the sub-collection of #$Integer that excludes the negative integers.  Each instance of #$NonNegativeInteger is a whole number greater than or equal to zero -- for example, 0, 1, 2, 3, ....")
(comment LawEnforcementActivity "The collection of all events performed with the purpose of enforcing laws, that are performed by people officially charged with this this duty. Includes most activities of law enforcement officials (such as police) including detection of crime, identification of offenders, and arrests.")
(comment ExtractZipExtra4DigitsFn "This function returns the extra four digit part of an American postal code (zip code) represented as a string.  For example, (#$ExtractZipExtra4DigitsFn ''78759-6509'') will return 6509.  If the extra 4 digits are not present in the postal code, the function returns NIL")
(comment StillImageMicrotheory "A collection microtheories; a subset of #$ImageMicrotheory.  Each element of #$StillImageMicrotheory is a context in which to state the propositional content of a particular (two-dimensional) still image, such as a photograph, painting, or drawing.")
(disjointWith GaseousTangibleThing Water-Saline)
(comment PharmacyTechnician "A Technician working in a Phamacy, assisting a Pharmacist.")
(disjointWith Microtheory BeliefSystem)
(comment Street-Private "A road in a residential area that is owned by the people who live on it. Usually only one or two homes.")
(comment West-Generally "An instance of #$GeographicalDirection-General (q.v.).  From a given reference point, #$West-Generally comprises the wedge-shaped set of vectors that point within 22.5 degrees (in either horizontal direction) of #$West-Directly.")
(comment BuyingGroup "The collection of buying groups (also known as group purchasing organizations, bid groups, or purchasing groups).  Each is a  group of independent instititutions (or a system of institutions) such as hospitals, nursing homes, or schools, that contracts with suppliers to get good deals in buying objects or services.  Buying groups typically charge membership fees.  Each member is an organization.  If a buying group enters into a sales contract with a manufacturer or supplier, then any member of the buying group can make purchases under that contract.")
(disjointWith Organism-Whole OrganismPart)
(comment Calmness "The attribute-type associated with the feeling of calmness or serenity, being free from disturbance. (For the rationale behind treating feelings as types -- i.e. collections -- of attributes, see #$FeelingAttribute and the comment on #$Happiness.)")
(comment GynecologicalOncologist "A gynecological oncologist is a doctor who specializes in diagnosing and treating tumors within the female reproductive system.")
(comment outputSignals "The outputs of an electrical device.")
(comment PrisonSentencePunishment "Punishments in which the agent punished is sentenced to be in prison for some amount of time.")
(comment Anesthesiologist "Anesthesiologists administer anesthesia.")
(comment TheTerm "A special kind of term that allows back-reference to any individual thing that satisfies the constraints on the #$TheTerm.  E.g., 'Suppose a cat walks into a fish store.  The cat is likely to get into a lot of trouble.'  'The cat' in the second sentence refers back to 'a cat' in the first; i.e., any cat that walks into a fish store.  In Cyc, the constraints for a #$TheTerm in a given context are given by use of the predicate #$theTermConstraints on the unit representing that context.  In lifting assertions out of that context, the constraints are added as antecedents.")
(comment SportsInfraction "An infraction of some sports rules, such as stepping out of bounds or interfering with your opponent.  Please note that these collections are not specs of this collection, since a particular act of #$SteppingOutOfBounds may or may not be a #$SportsInfraction.")
(comment PlantingATree "The collection of all events in which a (usually immature) tree is intentionally placed in soil")
(comment Entertained-Emotion "The emotion experienced when one is entertained or occupied in a light, playful, or pleasant manner. Not necessarily implies play or sport.")
(comment PositionSelection "The collection of #$SelectingSomething events in which the thing chosen is a #$Person to fill a position at some #$Organization (e.g., the event of selecting someone to be the new VP of Marketing for IBM.)")
(comment Roofer "A person who repairs or builds roofs.")
(comment resultMt "The predicate #$resultMt relates a thought process to its outcome.  The outcome is represented as a #$Microtheory.  (#$resultMt THOUGHT RESULT) means that the outcome of the #$Thinking process THOUGHT is the #$Microtheory represented by RESULT.  Typical results are instances of #$Plan, #$Schedule, #$Agreement, or another type of rational mental construct.")
(comment punishmentIssued "ARG1 is a #$Punishment (an mt), and ARG2 is a #$Punishing (may be an action, or more generally some type of #$Situation).  The agent that the punishment ARG1 is for is subject to the punishing ARG2.")
(comment StateOfMatterChangeEvent "#$StateOfMatterChangeEvent is the collection of events in which some piece of matter changes from one of the physical states of matter to another.  Such changes of state can be induced by changes in temperature (or the equivalent in the manipulation of kinetic energy).  Each particular instance of #$Boiling, #$Freezing, #$Evaporating, #$Condensing, #$Melting, etc. is an instance of #$StateOfMatterChangeEvent.  

Note: Most Cyc microtheories distinguish four states of matter, namely, #$Solid-StateOfMatter, #$Plasma-StateOfMatter, #$Liquid-StateOfMatter, #$Gaseous-StateOfMatter.  See #$MatterTypeByPhysicalState and its individual state constants.")
(comment DayOfMonthFn "(#$DayOfMonthFn ?N) denotes the collection of #$CalendarDays which are the Nth day of the calendar month in which they fall. For example, (#$DayOfMonthFn 4) is the collection of all #$CalendarDays which are the fourth day of some month.  Every July 4th is an instance of (#$DayOfMonthFn 4)")
(comment TradeAgreement "Agreements in which the parties involved agree to exchange equities, stocks, etc.")
(comment Swim-4By200MeterFreestyleRelay "Swimming race - 200 meter freestyle relay.")
(comment middleNameInitial "The first character of the #$middleName.")
(disjointWith TwoBathDwelling TwoAndAHalfBathDwelling)
(comment PossessiveMarker-Pl "The collection of all contracted possessive endings which attach to plural nouns. In English, this is only s', as in 'boys''.")
(comment DollarsPerYard "The cost of something (in U.S.Dollars) per linear yard.")
(comment Client-ServerSystem "A #$Client-ServerSystem is a network of computer programs which includes at least one #$ClientProgram and #$ServerProgram.  There is a #$CommunicationProtocol by which the #$ClientProgram requests information or processing from the #$ServerProgram, then when the information is found or the processing is complete, the #$ServerProgram sends the results to the #$ClientProgram.  There can be many programs operating at distant locations in the one #$Client-ServerSystem.")
(comment CalendarAutumn "A specialization of #$CalendarSeason.  Each instance of #$CalendarAutumn is a time interval that begins on a day considered to begin an autumn season, and ends on a day considered to end an autumn season. For example, according to mainstream culture in the U.S.A., instances of this collection begin each year on the #$AutumnalEquinox (about September 21) and end on the #$DecemberSolstice (about December 21st) (see #$CalendarAutumn-US), whereas according to mainstream Australasian culture, instances of this collection begin March 1st and end on the last day of May (see #$CalendarAutumn-Australasian).")
(comment TimesPerWeek "An instance of #$UnitOfFrequency.  When applied to a number or pair of numbers, #$TimesPerWeek returns an instance of #$Frequency as its value.  For example, (#$TimesPerWeek 3) is a frequency of three times per week.")
(comment headHairLength "arg1 has head hair which falls roughly in the length range specified by arg2.")
(comment Translation-LocationChange "A collection of translational motion events; thus a subcollection of #$Movement-TranslationEvent.  In each instance of #$Translation-LocationChange, the moving object (see #$objectMoving) ends up in a different place than it started from: the destination (see #$toLocation) is not the same as the origin (see #$fromLocation).  Thus, a round-trip travel event (see #$Translation-RoundTrip) is _not_ an instance of this collection.  Cf. #$Translation-NoLocationChange.")
(comment toughnessOfObject "Indicates the degree of toughness of an object (i.e. how well it can withstand impact forces).")
(comment Desonide "The chemical compound which is a steroid.")
(comment Cyclist "A specialization of #$IndividualAgent. Each instance of #$Cyclist is an agent (usually a person) entitled to inspect and modify the Cyc knowledge base.")
(comment objectTypeToAffect "The type of thing the goal expressed in the first argument concerns; i.e., the #$objectToAffect will be instances of that type.  Goals of changing, destroying, protecting, retaliating, preventing, etc. typically have some clear type of thing of which it is the goal to affect.")
(disjointWith Solid-StateOfMatter Mixture)
(comment ProperCountNoun "The collection of all proper count nouns. Proper nouns are usually capitalized, and they usually denote some particular person, place, or thing.  Many proper nouns cannot be preceded by a determiner, and many have no plural form.  Example: `Dallas'.  Although one might think that names for languages e.g. ``Cherokee'' are #$ProperCountNouns, they are actually #$MassNouns.  One test is to see if you can ``too much X'' or ``a lot of X'' without a distinct plural form.  For example ``too much Crest'' vs *``too much Q-tips'' and ``a lot of Coke'' vs *``a lot of Q-tip'' suggest that ``crest'' and ``coke'' are mass nouns, whereas ``Q-tip'' is a count noun.")
(comment East-Generally "An instance of #$GeographicalDirection-General (q.v.).  From a given reference point, #$East-Generally comprises the wedge-shaped set of vectors that point within 22.5 degrees (in either horizontal direction) of #$East-Directly.")
(comment HumanServicesOrganization "The collection of all organizations which provide  subsidized human services to financially disadvantages persons.")
(comment HeelOfPalm "The heel of a palm is a region close to the wrist, over a thick, fleshy part of the body of the hand.")
(comment NonCoopTeamSportsCompetition "A team event in which the players perform seperately, and only their scores are combined to decide the winning team.  SnowSkiing as opposed to Basketball.")
(comment FacialPlasticSurgeon "A facial plastic surgeon is a doctor who specializes in the restoration or improvement of facial features through surgery.")
(comment interArgReln1-5 "ARG2 Gives a relationship that holds between the first and fifth  arguments in assertions using ARG1.  An example using a similar predicate is as follows:  (#$interArgReln1-2 #$relativePosition cotemporal) means that in assertions using #$relativePosition, the first and second arguments must be cotemporal.")
(comment Litter-Garbage "Loose (unbagged) DomesticGarbage.  Litter is composed primarily of inorganic material.")
(comment ClericalWorker "employees who tally columns of numbers, do rote data entry, etc., for a living")
(comment Planet "A specialization of #$PlanetaryBody.  Each instance of #$Planet is a planet either in Earth's solar system or elsewhere in the universe.  Instances of #$Planet include #$PlanetEarth, #$PlanetJupiter, and #$PlanetVenus.")
(comment comparativeAdverb "The relationship between an #$EnglishWord and its comparative adverbial form. Example: 'better'.")
(comment Cell "The collection of living cells; a specialization of #$BiologicalLivingObject.  Each instance of #$Cell is one of the basic structural units of nearly all living things, consisting (at least) of cytoplasm bounded by a cell membrane. Only the living structures viruses, mitochondria, and plastids are not composed of cells.")
(comment MakingADoublePlay "Getting two members of the opposing team out, in the same play.")
(comment HikingEvent "Long walking for pleasure or exercise.")
(comment Delight "Live and obvious (and somewhat ephemeral) emotion found in the satisfaction or gratification induced by the possession, acquisition or expectation of something good or greatly desired.")
(comment chosenItem "The item or items chosen in selecting.")
(comment TreeSurgeon "A person who helps sick trees.")
(comment coworkers "Entries are the persons who work with ARG1 as members of a TaskGroup.")
(comment MonthOfYearFn "(#$MonthOfYearFn ?N) denotes the collection of #$CalendarMonths which are the Nth month of some year.  #$January, which is the set of all Januaries, is the same as the value of (#$MonthOfYearFn 1).")
(comment MakingAMedicalIncisionInABLO "The collection of events in which an incision is intentionally made in a BLO, usually as one of the first #$subEvents of a Surgery.")
(comment ThreeTimesDaily "Used to indicate that something happens regularly three times a day.")
(comment LugeSportsEvent "A luge sled is raced down a bobsled run")
(disjointWith OneAndAHalfBathDwelling TwoAndAHalfBathDwelling)
(comment TemporallyDisjointTemporalObjectType "A collection of collections and a specialization of #$TemporalObjectType. TYPE is an instance of #$TemporallyDisjointTemporalObjectType just in case any two distinct instances of TYPE are #$temporallyDisjoint.  For example, #$Wednesday is an instance of  #$TemporallyDisjointTemporalObjectType because no Wednesday can temporally intersect any Wednesday other than itself.")
(comment Cent-UnitedStates "An instance of #$UnitOfMoney.  When applied to a number or a pair of numbers, #$Cent-UnitedStates returns an instance of #$MonetaryValue.  For example, (#$Cent-UnitedStates 2) is two U.S. cents.  #$Cent-UnitedStates is the smallest unit of money used officially in the United States of America; it is one-hundredth of a #$Dollar-UnitedStates (q.v.).")
(comment RecoveringFromAilment "A collection of events.  In an instance of #$RecoveringFromAilment, some member of #$BiologicalLivingObject recovers from an #$AilmentCondition it has at the beginning of this recovery period.")
(comment AccountBetweenFn "This maps from two agents to a financial account of the net amount owed between agent1 and agent2; this is being limited to debts which can be expressed in money; other obligations must be treated seperately")
(comment SocialOccurrence "A specialization of both #$PurposefulAction  and #$CompositePhysicalAndMentalEvent.  Each instance of #$SocialOccurrence  is an action in which two or more agents take part.  In many cases,  #$SocialOccurrences involve communication among the participating agents.   Some instances of #$SocialOccurrence have very elaborate role structures  (e.g. a typical lawsuit), while others have fairly simple role structures  (e.g. greeting a colleague at work).")
(disjointWith AppropriatingSomething LosingUserRights)
(comment MometasoneFuroate "The chemical compound which is a steroid.")
(comment maximumDepth "The maximum depth of a geographical region.  This can be a canyon or an ocean.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentEvent LawEnforcementActivity)
(comment (LeftObjectOfPairFn Femur) "Left thigh bones")
(comment WarehouseChain "A collection of commercial service organizations; a subset of #$StorageOrganization.  An element of #$WarehouseChain is a #$CommercialServiceOrganization which stores goods in exchange for money.  Each element of #$WarehouseChain owns or controls (perhaps leases) several instances of #$Warehouse.")
(comment CooperativeTeamSportsCompetition "A team event in which the entire team plays at the same time, helping each other towards the goal of winning.  Hockey as opposed to Gymnastics.")
(comment Immunopathologist "An immunopathologist is a doctor who specializes in diagnosing diseases which affect the immune system, as evidenced in abnormal body tissues.")
(comment Saprophyte "The collection of heterotrophic plants, fungi, or bacteria that live and feed on dead organic matter.")
(comment HumidityPerception "Perception events where the thing perceived is the ambient humidity.")
(comment spendingRate "The rate at which this agent makes expenditures, in money-per-unit-time. ")
(comment Garbage-Domestic "Garbage that is thrown out from a domestic residence.")
(comment Accountant "The collection of persons who prepare and interpret the financial records of a person or organization")
(comment Daily "Used to indicate that something happens regularly on an at-least daily basis.")
(comment Fellow-FACC "This title is given to fellows of the American College of Cardiology.")
(comment WeddingEvent-Entire "A subcollection of #$SocialOccurrence.  Each instance of #$WeddingEvent-Entire is a complex event, usually discontinuous in time, consisting of all of the applicable  \"parts\" of the event of getting married.  These various parts will be #$subEvents of the #$WeddingEvent-Entire.  They minimally include a #$WeddingCeremony, and (depending on the culture, the wishes of the betrothed, etc.) might also include a #$WeddingReception and perhaps other social events (for one or both partners and their friends and family) before or after the actual ceremony.")
(comment ClothesIroningEvent "The collection of clothes ironing events -- events in which wrinkles are removed from an item of clothing.  You hold an iron, stroke the clothes with it, set it down, pick it up again after smoothing the clothes.  This is repeated a mob of times.")
(comment Boredom "The attribute-type associated with dissatisfaction, weariness, or restlessness accompanied by a felt lack of interest in what is going on around one.  A specialization of #$Listlessness.  (For the rationale behind treating feelings as types -- i.e. collections -- of attributes, see the comment on #$Happiness.)")
(comment awardFor "Awards people receive are usually for some action they performed.  Also, if a person has an award, there was some action they performed in the past for which they got the award. ")
(comment TelevisionCrew "A collection of groups of people.  An element of #$TelevisionCrew is a group of #$MediaProfessionals who work together to create, shoot, or broadcast particular television shows or scenes.")
(comment TradeWorker "A collection of persons; a subset of #$BlueCollarWorker.  Each element of #$TradeWorker is a worker who performs a skilled trade.  Such skills are typically acquired through practical training and do not require an academic or higher education, though some individuals working in a trade may have college degrees.  A large portion of #$TradeWorker includes various types of workers in the building trades, such as the members of its subsets #$Carpenter, #$Electrician, #$Plumber, #$Painter-Tradesperson, #$Roofer, etc.  Other subsets include workers who maintain or repair things, e.g., those included in #$Gardener, #$ShoeCobbler, #$ApplianceRepairPerson, #$CarMechanic, #$MaintenancePerson, etc.")
(comment ScriptSpecification "The collection of #$PropositionalInformationThings which contain assertions about instances of a #$SpecifiedMakingType concerned: order and type of steps in the process, durations, etc.  It is not necessary that every #$SpecifiedMakingType will have a reified #$ScriptSpecification.")
(comment Solemnity "Feeling of impressive gravity, as if weighed down by deep thought or important work. Not light or frivolous, but serious")
(comment ScrewedConnection "A rigid connection for which the fasteners are screws")
(comment FiveTimesDaily "Used to indicate that something happens regularly five times a day.")
(comment AlpineSkiingSportsEvent "The collection of downhill skiing sports competitions.")
(comment AstronomicalObservatory "The collection of all installations constructed for gathering data on celestial and astronomical phenomena.  Astronomical instruments are housed in observatories (and may even be a part of the structures).")
(disjointWith TwoAndAHalfBathDwelling ThreeBathDwelling)
(comment MoneyPerMassRatio "How much something costs per unit mass.")
(comment actualTextOfPIT "ARG2 is the #$TextualMaterial string that ARG1 represents.")
(comment CalendarSeasonType "A specialization of #$ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries-DisjointWithGaps and #$AnnualTemporalObjectType.  Each instance of  #$CalendarSeasonType is a specialization of #$CalendarSeason -- #$CalendarWinter, #$CalendarSpring, #$CalendarSummer, and #$CalendarAutumn.")
(comment overlapsStart "(#$overlapsStart FIRST SECOND) means that the #$TemporalThing SECOND starts during the #$TemporalThing FIRST, and FIRST ends during SECOND.  Consequently, the #$startingPoint of FIRST is before the #$startingPoint of SECOND, the #$endingPoint of FIRST is after the #$startingPoint of SECOND, and the #$endingPoint of FIRST is before the #$endingPoint of SECOND.")
(comment physicalBuild "arg1 is described by the physical build attribute arg2.")
(comment Lobby-Room "The collection of all lobbies -- entry rooms, usually of a business establishment, where people often stand around and wait ....")
(comment Translation-SingleTrajectory "A specialization of #$Movement-TranslationEvent.  Each instance of #$Translation-SingleTrajectory is a translational movement that involves exactly one #$trajectory-Complete.  One or more items might have the role of #$objectMoving in such an event.  Note that although there is a single #$trajectory-Complete, it does not follow that there is a unique place in the role of #$fromLocation or #$toLocation because that depends on our descriptions of these locations.  (E.g. the same single-trajectory movement can be described as from Texas to Pennsylvania, from Austin to Pittsburgh, or from northwest Austin to south Pittsburgh.)  However, the single #$trajectory-Complete connects one from-location and one to-location.  (Similarly, there may be a single existing #$motionPathway-Complete that the trajectory goes along, or a single #$Traversal of paths indicated by #$traverses-Complete.)  Note that a translational motion performed by a whole #$Group is likely to be a #$Translation-SingleTrajectory; e.g. a flock of birds flying together or a snarl of rush-hour traffic on the Beltway.  Non-examples include an opening break in a game of billiards and a group of water droplets coming together into one big drop. Contrast with #$Translation-MultiTrajectory.")
(comment QuickMaintenanceAutoMC "Car products which are readily available and typically used by the car's owner.")
(comment TwoManBobsledSportsEvent "The collection of two person bobsled competitions")
(comment reciprocalTransfers "(#$reciprocalTransfers T1 T2) means that T1 and T2 are transfers of possession done in exchange for each other.  They are part of some #$ExchangeOfUserRights.")
(comment ClobetasolPropionate "The chemical compound which is a steroid.")
(disjointWith PreparingFoodOrDrink LawEnforcementActivity)
(comment MillionDollars "A unit of measure equal to one million U.S. dollars

(see #$Dollar-UnitedStates).")
(comment mtImageSpace "Images with content represented in ARG1 depict the space ARG2.")
(disjointWith SeparationEvent Travel-TripEvent)
(disjointWith OrganismClassificationType SpatiallyDisjointRegionType)
(comment PoliticalParty "A specialization of #$PoliticalOrganization.  Each instance of #$PoliticalParty is an organization that primarily seeks to elect candidates to public office or have members continue holding public office, and which is identified as a party affiliation by persons holding or seeking public office.")
(disjointWith NonCoopTeamSportsCompetition CooperativeTeamSportsCompetition)
(comment AdolescentMedicineSpecialist "An adolescent medical specialist is a doctor who specializes in the treatment of adolescents.")
(comment Often "Often")
(comment PassengerAirplane "The collection of all airplanes designed and/or used for carrying passengers (transportees in addition to the pilot).")
(comment GeneralPractitioner "GeneralPractitioners are medical doctors who do not specialize in any one field.")
(comment Wetness "The collection of all degrees of wetness ")
(comment regularAdverb "The relationship between an #$EnglishWord and its regular adverbial form.  Example: 'strongly'.")
(comment MaintainingAHold "In judo or wrestling, placing a hold or lock on an opponent.")
(comment shelfLife "How long would this product remain useful for its intended purpose if it were kept under recommended storage conditions (temperature, humidity, etc.), if it were never used, and its packaging, if any, were never opened. (#$shelfLife PRODUCT INTERVAL) means that from (#$StartFn PRODUCT) for a period equal to INTERVAL, PRODUCT is predicted to be useful for its intended purpose. Note that the actual length of time an unused product stays useful may be longer or shorter than its shelflife. Freezing some perishable products increases how long they remain useable, and exposing some products to the atmosphere, heat, humidity, etc., can cause them to go bad in a time shorter than their shelf life. This predicate is intended for products that deteriorate significantly over a period of anywhere from less than a day to at most several years, including flowers, food, and pharmaceuticals. It does NOT denote the actual amount of time spent on a shelf.")
(comment Grief "Intense emotional suffering or poignant distress caused by or as if by bereavement")
(comment Landscaper "A person who does landscaping.")
(comment SpecifiedMakingType "Instances are classes of manufacturings to which Specifications apply (e.g. AcmeToyFiretruckProcess3B, *not* MakingToys or even MakingToyTrucks).  Many instances of these instances (e.g. AcmeFiretruckProcess3B-RunNumber252 ...-RunNumber253) occur regularly at manufacturing firms.  General collections such as Assembly and BatchManufacturing would not be instances of SpecifiedMakingType; only Manufacturings which have very specific requirements for inputs, outputs and/or script components.")
(comment Dressmaker-Professional "A worker whose job involves the making, altering, or repairing of dresses, skirts, and blouses.")
(disjointWith TemporalThing MathematicalOrComputationalThing)
(comment popularityOfActivity "Performing instances of ARG1 in role ARG2 is popular (to the degree ARG4) to instances of ARG3.")
(comment The "A function used in forming a non-atomic term (NAT).  The argument to #$The is a collection, and the resulting NAT is an instance of #$TheTerm, which must be constrained for a given microtheory by using the predicate #$theTermConstraints.")
(comment BiathlonSportsEvent "Cross country skiing and shooting")
(comment ElectromagneticRadiation "A specialization of #$WavePropagation (q.v.).  Each instance of #$ElectromagneticRadiation is an event that arises from the interaction of an electrical field and a magnetic field.  Specializations of  #$ElectromagneticRadiation include #$VisibleLight, #$RadioWaves, and #$XRays.")
(disjointWith ZeroFamilyRoomDwelling OneFamilyRoomDwelling)
(comment NewsOrganization "Any organization that produces #$News.")
(comment WeddingCeremony "This is the collection of actual wedding ceremonies. Use #$WeddingReception for the party afterwards and #$WeddingEvent-Entire for the whole shebang.")
(comment ChangingADiaper "What you do when you change a baby's dirty diaper for a clean one.  A dirty job, but someone has to do it.")
(comment marginOfVictory "The winner of this competition beat the runner up by ARG2")
(comment ritualInEvent "(#$ritualInEvent RITUAL EVENT) means that RITUAL is a ritual that is part of the larger event, EVENT.")
(comment FourManBobsledSportsEvent "The collection of four person bobsled competitions")
(comment Valisone "The chemical compound which is a steroid.")
(comment Dread "Each Dread is an intangible object which specifies some undesirable state or event (which, by the way, are also intangible objects)")
(comment CountyPoliceOrganization "A collection of law enforcement organizations.  An element of #$CountyPoliceOrganization is a county police force which is a sub-organization of the government of some #$County, with that county being in its jurisdictional territory for #$LawEnforcementActivity.")
(comment ImageSpaceFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction for denoting the space depicted in an image.  The content of the image is represented in the mt ARG1.")
(comment Biceps "The #$Collection of all instances of #$Biceps #$Muscle.  The #$Biceps is a #$Muscle with two heads which parallels the #$Humerus.  The two heads attach at differentparts of the Scapula, while the distal end attaches to the #$Radius-Bone.")
(comment UnitVectorInterval "The collection #$UnitVectorInterval is a subcollection of #$VectorInterval.  Each instance of #$UnitVectorInterval is a vector interval with a magnitude of 1.  The range of the endpoints of all the unit vectors  [#$UnitVector-Precise] form a contiguous curve (in 2 space), surface (in 3 space), volume (in 4 space), etc. depending upon the dimentionality of the vector.  One #$UnitVectorInterval differs from another only in range of direction, since the magnitude of every #$UnitVectorInterval is the same.  An instance of #$UnitVectorInterval may specify either a precise unit vector [#$UnitVector-Precise] or a generalized range of directions such as `in front of'.  The range of directions in 3-space may be quite irregular, such as the direction interval from #$Chile to #$Russia.")
(comment DanceClub "The collection of businesses which run places for recreational dancing to various kinds of music -- live bands or recordings -- increasingly popular in the late twentieth century")
(comment OlympicsOpeningCeremony "A ceremony used to officially `kick off' a series of Olympic Games.")
(comment MedicalMicrobiologist "A pathologist who specializes in the adverse effects of microorganisms on body tissues.")
(comment ScriptPerformanceAttributeType "A collection of collections.  Each #$ScriptPerformanceAttributeType is a type of attribute that can be used to describe the manner in which actions are performed.  Examples include: #$Competence, #$Precision, #$Dexterity, #$Gracefulness, #$Creativity, etc.  So, e.g., one may run a race with some measure of #$Gracefulness, some measure of #$Competence, etc.")
(comment groupPrototype "The predicate #$groupPrototype is used to identify the individual prototype for a particular group.  (#$groupPrototype GROUP PROTO) means that the prototype of GROUP is PROTO.  PROTO is an individual which is (or becomes), intentionally or unintentionally, the model for the #$groupMembers of GROUP, which share some feature(s) of the prototype.  A group may or may not have a prototype.  A group has only one prototype (if it has any).  A prototype exists prior to other members of the group; it may or may not itself be a member of the group (by default, Cyc assumes it is).  For example, the prototype for the class of Saturn V rockets; or, Casanova as the prototypical romantic adventurer.")
(comment MoneyModeExchange "The collection of events in which one form of money is exchanged for another - buying a money order, foreign currency exchange, or getting change for a large bill.")
(comment Nurse "The class of health professionals who provide various aspects of hands-on health care to patients.  Nurses do not usually diagnose or decide on treatments, but they administer medicines and treatments, perform medical tests, give regular care to hospitalized patients, etc.")
(disjointWith Travel-TripEvent OpeningSomething)
(comment massNumber "(#$massNumber WORD STRING) means that STRING is the mass noun form of WORD.  For example, \"paper\" is the mass noun form of #$Paper-TheWord.")
(comment RegionType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$RegionType is a subcollection of #$SpatialThing-Localized each of whose instances is an identifiable subregion of some object, but not itself an independent object.  Instances of #$RegionType include #$PalmOfHand, #$Doorway, #$Wall-GenericBarrier, #$WorkSurface, and #$Handle.")
(comment LieutenantCommander-Title "The prefix ''LCDR'' that may attach to a person's name.  Used as a title for Lieutenant Commanders.")
(comment Accelerating-Translational "#$Accelerating-Translational occurs whenever #$velocityOfObject changes, e.g. speeding up, slowing down, or changing direction of translation.")
(comment Love "Strong affection for another agent arising out of kinship or personal ties.  Love may be felt towards things, too: warm attachment, enthusiasm, or devotion.  This does not, however, mean something as specialized/metaphorical as `Fred loves to eat ice cream' or `Ethel loves to get her way.'  #$Love is a collection, as further explained under #$Happiness.  Specialized forms of #$Love are #$Love-Romantic, platonic love, maternal love, infatuation, agape, etc.")
(comment informationRetrievalOn "This info retrieval task is on retrieving info on arg2.")
(comment Debate "An exchange of opinions in which participants defend opposing beliefs, presumably on rational grounds.  By default, a #$Debate is assumed to be a spoken communication.  Debators are assumed to hold the beliefs they defend.")
(comment Runner-Messenger "a person who picks up and delivers documents, etc.")
(disjointWith ObjectSpecification ScriptSpecification)
(comment Tailor-Professional "A worker whose job involves the making, altering, or repairing of clothing items.")
(comment MonthOfYearType "A collection of #$Collections.

Instances of #$MonthOfYearType are the canonical subcollections of #$CalendarMonth.  There are twelve of these in the #$JulianCalendar; for example, #$September is the collection of all Septembers.")
(comment MathematicalOrComputationalThing "The collection of #$Intangible things that are intrinsically mathematical (see #$MathematicalThing) or computational (see #$ComputationalObject).  Instances of #$MathematicalOrComputationalThing are abstract in the very strong sense of being nonspatial, atemporal, and massless.  Examples include numbers, sets, collections, relations, algorithms, and abstract character strings.")
(comment FeatherweightGRWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of GRWrestlingSportsEvent")
(comment firstNameInitial "The first character of the #$firstName.")
(disjointWith TwoFamilyRoomDwelling OneFamilyRoomDwelling)
(comment MonthFn "An instance of #$DateDenotingFunction.  #$MonthFn returns an instance of #$CalendarMonth when applied to an instance of #$MonthOfYearType and an instance of #$CalendarYear. (#$MonthFn MONTH YEAR) denotes the month of type MONTH during YEAR.  For example, (#$MonthFn #$February (#$YearFn 1966)) denotes February of 1966.")
(comment temporallyFinishedBy "(#$temporallyFinishedBy PERIOD FINISH) means that PERIOD (an instance of #$TemporalThing) and FINISH (another instance of #$TemporalThing) end simultaneously (see #$temporallyCoterminal), and that FINISH starts within the bounds of PERIOD.   That is, the #$endingPoint of PERIOD and FINISH are the same instance of #$TimePoint (q.v.), and the #$startingPoint of FINISH is later than the #$startingPoint of PERIOD.")
(comment PetroleumJelly "A substance produced from petroleum for use in such things as preventing chapped lips and diaper rash")
(comment SchemaLF "RESULT is a #$LogicalField in the #$LogicalTableSchema ARG1, uniquely determined by the #$LogicalFieldAttribute ARG2.")
(comment quantitySold "ARG3 is the amount of #$ObjectType ARG2 sold in ARG1.  This is a kind of predicate slot since its interpretation depends on the object type and perhaps some additional context.")
(disjointWith CommunicationAct-Single PlayingABoardGame)
(comment JudgedSportsEvent "Judged sports event where judges provide the measurement of performance.  Of course, in many sports there are judges of some kind who interpret the rules.  The difference lies in the complexity of the rules, whether the judge is merely asked to verify a simple fact like a ball being inbounds at a certain time, or whether they are asked to evaluate one performance on many criteria and produce a particular score or scores.")
(comment processRunningOn "(#$processRunningOn PROC SYS) means that PROC is a #$ComputerProcessRunning that is occuring on computer hardware SYS.")
(comment IntangibleIndividual "The collection of wholly intangible 

individuals, a specialization of both #$Intangible and #$Individual.  

Instances of #$IntangibleIndividual are immaterial, and thus do not have mass, color, or other tangible qualities. Examples include mathematical objects (such as numbers, functions, and relations), attributes, time intervals, space regions, and events.  Excluded are sets and collections because, although intangible, they are not individuals.")
(disjointWith LawEnforcementOrganization FinancialOrganization)
(comment TextMarking "A collection of visual marks.  Each element of #$TextMarking is a visual artifact, a mark or configuration of marks recognizable as text in some writing system.  Examples of #$TextMarking include written words, written numbers, sentences, individual letters and numerals, all the text on a piece of paper or in a book, auxiliary marks like punctuation, etc.")
(comment Triceps "The #$Collection of all instances of #$Triceps #$Muscle.  The #$Triceps is athree headed muscle, the only muscle on the posterior #$UpperArm.")
(comment CoveredWithHair "An attribute for describing a high level of body hair, in general.  Note that a bald person may be quite hairy on other parts of his/her body.")
(comment NightClub "A collection of businesses.  An element of #$NightClub is a business that runs a nighttime social-gathering place where some form of entertainment (usually live music) is offered and alcoholic beverages are served.  Besides music, #$NightClub establishments may also have dance floors, DJs, go-go dancers, comedy acts, stage presentations, or sex shows.")
(comment TimePenalizing "A penalty of losing a certain amount of time off the clock, or of having it added, whichever is against your favor.")
(comment MedicareNumber "An ID number assigned by the federal government to hospitals that are medicare providers.")
(comment LogicLow "Logic Low signal.")
(comment Imprisoning "A situation where a person is held in a prison.")
(comment BuyingAMoneyOrder "A transaction in which one agent gives money to another, and the recipient then prints a money order of that amount, typically for a small fee.")
(comment Judge "A judge in a governmental legal system.  People who judge competitions or conflicts are elements of #$JudicialAgent, but are not elements of #$Judge.")
(comment CompositePhysicalAndMentalEvent "A specialization of #$AtLeastPartiallyMentalEvent.  Each instance of #$CompositePhysicalAndMentalEvent is an event that involves some mental event(s), as well as some interaction between physical objects. Each instance will thus have at least one #$PhysicalEvent as a sub-event. (It may or may not itself be an instance of #$PhysicalEvent, depending on whether it occurs at a specific spatial location.) Examples include a news broadcast program, a court trial, someone inheriting property, someone writing a letter, a physical examination, and a charity ball. Notable specializations of this collection include #$PurposefulPhysicalAction and #$SensoryEvent.")
(comment SocialWorkerCredential "This credential is given to certified social workers.")
(comment AtLeastPartiallyMentalEvent "A collection of events.  Each instance of #$AtLeastPartiallyMentalEvent is an event involving the mental functions of  a participant or group of participants (see #$actors) in that event.  The collection includes such things as dreaming, perceiving, sensing, theorizing about something, having a realization, making a decision, building something, designing something, and consciously carrying out a task.  Note that the above list includes both purposeful events and non-purposeful events that involve mental functions.  Note also that any event that has a mental component is also an instance of this collection, so that events like preparing lunch would be classified as instances of #$AtLeastPartiallyMentalEvent.  In entering knowledge, it is almost always possible and preferable to use one of the specializations of #$AtLeastPartiallyMentalEvent.  If an event seems mostly mental in nature, modulo neurons firing and related brain activity, use #$StrictlyMentalEvent or one of its specializations.  If it essentially involves both mental and physical activity, see #$CompositePhysicalAndMentalEvent or #$PurposefulPhysicalAction.  For mental events that are intentionally and purposefully performed, see the specialization #$PurposefulMentalActivity.")
(comment Lieutenant-Title "The prefix ''LT'' that may attach to a person's name.  Used as a title for Lieutenants.")
(comment BlockingAnOpponent "Placing yourself in front of an opponent, thereby getting in his  way and limiting his movements, e.g. in a race, or being screened in basketball.")
(comment Impatience "Emotion arising from the inability to bear some trial (as delay, opposition, discomfort, or stupidity), shown by mental and emotional unrest, and inability to keep still")
(disjointWith Hosting GoingToUniversity)
(disjointWith BuyingActivity AthleticActivity)
(comment Homemaker "People who take care of a home and family.")
(comment ObjectSpecification "ObjectSpecification instances will contain assertions about the physical characteristics (dimensions, color, density, etc.), and the behavior under certain tests, of the inputs or products of instances of the SpecifiedMakingType the specification is concerned with.  Each input and each output of a SpecifiedMakingType should have an ObjectSpecification mt.")
(comment CosmeticSurgery "Surgery which is done primarily for appearance's sake, rather than functional.")
(comment Clean "Clean")
(comment SolingSportsEvent "A class of YachtingSportsEvent")
(comment Angstrom "An instance of #$UnitOfDistance.  When applied to a number or pair of numbers, #$Angstrom returns an instance of #$Distance as its value.  For example, (#$Angstrom 212) is a length of 212 angstroms.  Note that 1 angstrom is equivalent to 1/10,000,000,000 (i.e., 10^-10) meter.")
(comment ZonedAirConditioningDwelling "Dwelling has central air, but different zones are controlled by different units.")
(comment ArrangementOfLikeObjects "A collection of groups of #$PartiallyTangibles. Each instance of #$ArrangementOfLikeObjects is a group of partially tangible objects, all of the same type (see #$arrangementObjectTypes and #$arrangementNearestObjectTypes), having a specified set of spatial relations holding among them (see #$arrangementPredicates and #$arrangementNearestPredicates). See also #$Group.")
(comment accountBalance "The predicate #$accountBalance is used to indicate the balance of a particular account.  (#$accountBalance ACCT BAL) means that the #$FinancialAccount ACCT has the balance BAL; BAL is the amount of #$MonetaryValue either owed by, or available to, the #$accountHolder (depending upon the type of account).")
(comment Tripping "Locomotion accident where the locomoter catches their foot on a protrusion of the pathway surface, losing their balance.")
(comment explicitFields "(#$explicitFields PIT L-FIELD) means that L-FIELD is explicitly present in the #$PropositionalInformationThing PIT. A PropositionalInformation thing is typically the content of some information source.  If something is an #$explicitFields of a source's PIT, we expect that the source has a binding for that field, such as a field in a datbase table.  There may be other objects which are implicitly referred to by the information source, but these are referred to with #$implicitFields.")
(disjointWith PlayingABoardGame BodyMovementEvent)
(comment JudgedSportsEvent "Measured sports event where judges provide the measurement of performance.  Of course, in many sports there are judges of some kind who interpret the rules.  The difference lies in the complexity of the rules, whether the judge is merely asked to verify a simple fact like a ball being inbounds at a certain time, or whether they are asked to evaluate one performance on many criteria and produce a particular score or scores.")
(comment PharmacyBenefitManagementOrganization "The collection of all Pharmacy Benefit Management Organizations (PBMs).  These organizations basically provide drug insurance to subscribers.  They get their revenue from fees paid on a per member/per month basis and from pharmacy claims processing fees. For some PBMs, drug manufacturer rebates and discounts are an important source of revenue and are usually passed to the payer.")
(comment NationalLawEnforcementOrganization "Instances are law enforcement organizations on the national level.")
(comment Numeral "A specialization of #$WritingSymbolCharacter instances of which are individual abstract characters used as symbols for numbers in  some numeric system or other.  Instances include the #$ArabicNumerals '0' through '9' and single-character Roman numerals. Numerals from a given numeric system can normally be combined according to the rules of that system to form numeric character-strings that serve as names of numbers.")
(comment mtImageFocusesOn "Images with their content represented in the image microtheory ARG1 have as a focal (main, important, noticeable) object ARG2.")
(comment Diaphragm-BodyPart "The #$Collection of all instances of #$Diaphragm-BodyPart.  The #$Diaphragm-BodyPart is a #$Muscle which separates the #$ChestCavity from the #$AbdominalCavity.  It changes shape as the #$ChestCavity expands and contracts during #$Breathing.  The diaphragm contracts during #$Inhaling and relaxes during #$Exhaling.  It has three major #$Portals: for the #$Aorta, #$InferiorVenaCava, and #$Esophagus.")
(comment TopRidgeOfPalm "The top ridge of a palm is the upper region, close to where the fingers attach.")
(comment GeneralPreventativeMedicalDoctor "A general preventative medicine specialist is a doctor who specializes in preventative medicine.")
(comment LogicHighImpedance "Logic HighImpedance signal.")
(comment Lecturing "A collection of communication actions, a subset of #$PublicSpeaking.

Each instance of this collection is an action where some 

primary actor(s) are mostly speaking and audience members 

are mostly listening.")
(comment thicknessOfObject "(#$thicknessOfObject OBJECT THICKNESS) means that THICKNESS is the thickness of OBJECT.  The dimension in question is the one that corresponds to the intuitive notion of thickness for the type of thing that OBJECT is.")
(comment systemMaintainers "The people who maintain the computer systems of this agent")
(comment Surgeon "Surgeons are doctors who specialize in the branch of medicine concerned with the diagnosis and treatment of injuries and pathological conditions requiring manual or instrumental operative procedures.")
(comment MaterialHandling "A specialization of #$ActionOnObject: the collection of all actions in which some sort of material (solid, liquid, or gas) is handled or moved around. This includes actions done with the use of tools or machinery (such as shovels, dump trucks, or cranes), and is therefore not restricted to the kind of \"handling\" that is done with one's hands (cf. #$HandlingAnObject).")
(comment MilitaryTitle "Titles that indicate military rank.")
(comment MakingAnAssist "Passing to someone who makes a successful shot.")
(comment imageDesired "(#$imageDesired PER ATTRIB) means that the #$Person PER wishes to project him/herself as having the #$PersonalityAttributeType ATTRIB to a positive degree.")
(comment Hate "An intense feeling of hostility and aversion, usually deriving from fear, anger, or a sense of injury, and usually coupled with enmity and malice.  This is a #$Collection --- for an explanation of that, see #$Happiness.")
(comment Hosting "The collection of events in which an agent plays host to (somehow looks after the wants of) visitors, guests, etc.")
(comment ObjectSpecification "#$ObjectSpecification instances are mts which contain assertions about the properties of some object or number of objects.  If an ObjectSepcification instance applies to a particular thing, the statements in the #$ObjectSpecification are true about the thing.  This has a more specific treatment in the #$ManufacturingMt.")
(comment AdhesiveConnection "Connections formed with an adhesive, such as glue or epoxy")
(comment dayOfTheMonth "Indicates the index of this calendar day in the current month. The standard numbering scheme for days of the month.")
(comment Dirty "Dirty")
(comment LightJudoSportsEvent "Judo matches for sport, in the Light weight class.")
(comment RoomHeatDwelling "Assuming the only kinds of heat a dwelling can have are Furnace (= Central) or Room heat.")
(comment DayFn "An instance of #$DateDenotingFunction.  When applied to an integer in the range 1 through 31 and an instance of #$CalendarMonth, #$DayFn returns an instance of #$CalendarDay.  (#$DayFn DAY MONTH) denotes day number DAY of MONTH.  For example, (#$DayFn 14 (#$MonthFn #$February (#$YearFn 1966))) denotes Feb. 14th, 1966.")
(comment FinancialAccount "A specialization of #$Account.  Each instance of #$FinancialAccount is an account which is denominated in units of #$MonetaryValue (q.v.).  Specializations of #$FinancialAccount include #$BankAccount, #$CreditCardAccount, and #$VendorAccount.")
(comment IndependenceDay-US "The #$Holiday commemorating the declaration of independence by the United States on July 4, 1776. Celebrated in the United States each July 4.")
(comment horizontalComponent "(#$horizontalComponent ?vec1 ?vec2) means that ?vec2 is the horizontal vector component of the vector ?vec1.")
(comment fields "(#$fields PIT L-FIELD) indicates that the logical field L-FIELD is present in PIT, either explicitly or implicitly. Typically, most GAFs involving #$fields are concluded from the more specific relations #$implicitFields and #$explicitFields. One can make a direct assertion in cases where it is unknown if L-FIELD is implicit or explicit.")
(comment shearStrengthOfObject "(#$shearStrengthOfObject OBJ DEGREE) means that the tangible object OBJ has a DEGREE amount of #$ShearStrength, i.e., resistance to shearing stress.")
(comment SalesRepresentative "The collection of all sales persons who operate by making sales visits to (old or prospective) clients.")
(comment CityPoliceOrganization "#$CityPoliceOrganization is a subOrganization of the government of some City.           They have that City as a territory for #$LawEnforcementActivity.")
(comment VisualImage "A specialization of #$InformationBearingWavePropagation.  Each instance of #$VisualImage is an event in which visible light is generated in a particular pattern, which (does or might) contain information for an observer.  Visual images may be produced by illuminating some tangible object -- a #$VisualInformationBearingThing (such as a photograph, movie film, or page of print), or by direct manipulation of light(s) to produce a pattern (e.g., nautical code lights).  Visual images may be instantaneous or extended in time.  Visual images may be classified (among other ways) by features of their appearance (e.g., #$ColorImage, #$BlackAndWhiteImage), by their origin (e.g., #$XRayImage, #$PenOrPencilDrawing, #$SatelliteImage), or by their content (e.g., #$LandscapeImage).")
(comment Hamstrings "The #$Collection of all #$Hamstrings.  The #$Hamstrings is comprised of three #$Muscles (BicepsFemoris, SemiTeninousus, and SemiMembranosus) which connect the #$PelvicBone to the#$Fibula.  The #$Hamstrings extend the #$Hip, flex the #$Knee, and rotate the #$Knee both laterally and medially.  Shortened #$Hamstrings prevents one from touching ones toes with knees straight (extended).  The BicepsFemoris also attaches to the #$Femur.")
(comment Research "A specialization of both #$InformationGathering and #$PurposefulAction.  Each instance of #$Research is an event in which an agent or group of agents gathers information about a particular subject, with the aim of learning things about that subject that the agent or agents did not previously know.  In some cases, the agents in question (e.g., professional scientists) aim to learn things that no one knows, in other cases the agents (e.g., high school students) merely aim to find published knowledge which they did not know before. In some cases research may involve doing experiments (see #$Experimenting) or building systems (see #$ResearchProject), in other cases it may involve strictly document search.")
(comment WakingHours "#$WakingHours is a set of time intervals.  The length of each of those, and its #$startingPoint and #$endingPoint, is defined by the bulk of a population being awake.  The schedule varies by context -- i.e. which group of people are being considered -- and the boundaries are fuzzy.")
(comment RailwayOrganization "The collection of rail transportation companies.  An element of #$RailwayOrganization is a particular #$TransportationCompany that operates trains to transport people or goods, or makes its tracks available for use by trains, in exchange for money.")
(comment LossOfAttemptPenalizing "A penalty in which you are not allowed to count the score on an attempt, and not allowed to repeat it for a score.")
(comment OccupationalMedicineSpecialist "An occupational medicine specialist is a doctor who works in a company setting.  They treat workplace-related injuries and conditions and are concerned with the health of the company's employees.")
(comment LogicUnknown "Logic signal which is undetermined (or floating).")
(comment FarmWorker "The collection of people who work as hired help on a farm to make a living")
(comment raisesLivingObject "U raises (cares for, brings up, provides for the needs of) v1, v2, ...")
(disjointWith AstronomicalObject StormAsObject)
(comment StateEmployee "A collection of persons; a subset of #$GovernmentEmployee.  Each element of #$StateEmployee is a worker who is on the payroll of a state government organization.  Note: In Cyc, `state' refers generically to a major geographical subdivision of a country; see #$State-Geopolitical.")
(comment Fellow-FACEP "This title is given to fellows of the American College of Emergency Physicians.")
(comment givenNames "(#$givenNames AGENT NAME) means that NAME is a given name (i.e. a first name or \"Christian name\") of AGENT.")
(comment Father-Title "The prefix ''Father'' that may attach to a man's name.  Usually used as a title for Catholic priests.")
(comment KnockingOut "In boxing, knocking down an opponent with such force that he can't get up within 10 seconds after falling.")
(comment Inspiration-Emotion "The seemingly involuntary element where intellect and emotions are clearer and quicker")
(comment SensoryEvent "A collection of events.  Each element of #$SensoryEvent is an event which elicits a direct sensory response from either its performer or its #$objectActedOn, when those predicates link the event to an instance of #$PerceptualAgent.  Examples include the elements of #$VoluntaryBodyMovement (such as leg and arm movements), #$PhysicalContactEvent (such as touches), #$HumidityPerception, #$TemperatureChangingProcess, etc., when there is a #$PerceptualAgent linked to those events in the appropriate way.")
(disjointWith MilitaryPerson Civilian)
(comment MilitaryPerson "A specialization of #$MilitaryAgent.  Each instance of #$MilitaryPerson is a person belonging to one of the national military services (see the collection #$BranchOfMilitaryService) of some instance of #$Country.  Notable specializations of #$MilitaryPerson include #$ArmyPersonnel, #$NavyPersonnel, and #$MarinePersonnel.")
(comment objectSpecificationFor "Instances of ARG2 have products-or-inputs which are instances of ARG3.  ARG1 is the ObjectSpecification for ARG3 - i.e. the mt which contains the specification info.")
(comment StitchingAWound "A collection of events.  In each #$StitchingAWound, a wound is sewed up, typically with a suture.  Notice that each taking of one single stitch is not a #$StitchingAWound, though it is one of the #$subEvents of the entire #$StitchingAWound event.")
(comment DaysWorkFn "The collection of #$DoingADaysWork where one is a ARG1. This is used to enable one to represent  tasks when the person has more than one job (e.g. one is both a student and an engineer).")
(comment WhiteBoard "A (usually rectangular) sheet of some plastic or other composite material, usually framed and supported by a stand or hung on a wall, for writing messages with impermanent markers.  Popular in business/corporate offices and school rooms.")
(comment UprightPiano "Collection of all instances of #$Piano-Acoustic in which the frame on which the piano strings are strung is vertical.")
(comment dirtinessOfObject "(#$dirtinessOfObject OBJ DEGREE) means that the tangible object OBJ has this DEGREE of #$Dirtiness.")
(comment MovingTargetShootingSportsEvent "A marksmanship sports event in which moving targets are used.")
(comment ExitingToSafety "Leaving a place quickly in order to escape a real or imagined danger.")
(disjointWith TwoFirePlaceDwelling OneFirePlaceDwelling)
(comment Dollar-UnitedStates "An instance of #$UnitOfMoney (q.v).  #$Dollar-UnitedStates is a function which returns an instance of #$MonetaryValue when applied to a real number (see the collection #$SubLRealNumber) or a sequence of two real numbers. (#$Dollar-UnitedStates 10) denotes the instance of #$MonetaryValue that is equivalent to 10 U.S. dollars.  One #$Dollar-UnitedStates is equivalent to 100 #$Cent-UnitedStates (q.v.).")
(comment Cleric "A specialization of both #$PersonWithOccupation and #$ReligiousPerson.  Each instance of #$Cleric is a religious leader, typically in charge of some congregation (for instance, a synagogue, temple, mosque, or church).  Notable specializations of #$Cleric include #$Rabbi, #$Priest, #$Mullah, and #$Minister.")
(comment ApplyingATorque "The event of applying a force which producs a torque")
(comment LosingOnesBalance "Losing one's balance. A precursor to falling.")
(comment BallAndGoalGame "Sports where the competitors attempt to put a designated object in a place designated as a goal, thereby scoring points")
(disjointWith GivingSomething UnintendedLossOfUserRights)
(comment DEANumber "An identification number assigned by the U.S. Drug Enforcement Agency to an organization that dispenses controlled substances.")
(comment CrimeDetection "A specialization of #$LawEnforcementActivity.  In each instance of #$CrimeDetection, an authorized law enforcement agent detects a crime (i.e., some instance of #$CriminalAct).")
(comment WrittenWord "A collection of text markings each instance of which is arranged to be recognizable as a written word in some system of writing.")
(comment Deltoid "The #$Collection of all instances of #$Deltoid #$Muscle.  The #$Deltoid #$Muscles, located in the #$Shoulder, connect the #$Humerus to the #$Scapula.  The anterior, lateral, and posteriorportions of the #$Deltoid #$Muscle move the #$Humerus in different manners.")
(comment KnowledgeBase "A specialization of #$Database-AbstractContent. Each instance of #$KnowledgeBase is a database (considered as an abstract repository of information rather than a physical storage device) containing knowledge about at least part of the world.  A notable specialization of #$KnowledgeBase is #$CycKB, the collection of all Cyc knowledge bases.")
(comment BeltedConnection "A connection between two or more rotating wheels where rotation is transfered vis a vis a belt.")
(comment MarchingBand "The collection of organizations whose members play music together while marching.")
(comment PhysicalAttackOnNonOpponent "The attacking of a spectator, official, or any other person who is not currently your opponent.")
(comment TraumaSurgeon "A surgeon who specializes in surgery to repair serious injuries.")
(comment LogicHigh "Logic High signal.")
(comment Title "The collection of all titles: proper nouns (noun phrases) that relate to a person's status and/or function/role in an organization.  E.g., #$SeniorVicePresident-Title, #$MemberOfTechnicalStaff-Title, #$Reverend-Title, #$Father-Title, #$Miss, etc.  Note that this concept is not (closely) related to the title of a book or work of art, nor to the nicknames for a place, etc.")
(comment PhysicalTherapy "A form of therapy involving exercise, massage, heat, cold and electrical stimulation. #$PhysicalTherapy is usually for treatment of muscle, joint and associated tissue problems, as well as neurological ailments.")
(comment Author "The kind of people that have written a composition, for example students, professional writers.  Authors are NOT necessary professionals (see #$Writer) as they don't necessarily do it for pay, or do it as a central job related activity.")
(comment RealNumber "The collection of real numbers; a specialization of both  #$IntervalOnNumberLine and #$ScalarPointValue (qq.v.).  Each  instance of #$RealNumber is a single point on the real number  line, which has no upper or lower bounds.  Specializations  of this collection include #$Integer, #$RationalNumber, and  #$NegativeNumber.  Note that #$RealNumber is also a specialization  of #$ComplexNumber (q.v.), and any instance of the former  constitutes a degenerate case of the latter, in that the value  along the real's \"imaginary axis\" is zero (cf. #$ImaginaryNumber).")
(comment Fellow-FICS "This title is given to fellows of the International College of Surgeons.")
(comment Sister-Title "The prefix ''Sister'' that may attach to a woman's name.  Usually used as a title for a member of a women's religious order.")
(comment TippingOver "Events in which an object turns over.  If the object is an open container, it can no longer support (all) its contents.  This turn involves an approximately 90 degree #$Turning around a horizontal #$IntrinsicAxisOfObject while remaining in contact with some supporting material (although other support may be lost).  This is an abnormal, normally unintended event.  Prior to #$TippingOver an object is normally (reasonably) #$RightSideUp.  After #$TippingOver, an object is not #$RightSideUp.")
(comment Irritation "Emotion of a person who is disturbed, nervously upset, without equanimity or patience as a result of being forced to endure something that s/he finds obnoxious, offensive, displeasing or distasteful")
(comment Civilian "Persons who are not members of military organizations.")
(comment hasPatients "The predicate #$hasPatients represents a relationship between a medical professional and a patient (including nonhuman animals).  (#$hasPatients MEDIC PATIENT) means that the #$MedicalCareProvider MEDIC is treating the recipient-of-care PATIENT.  PATIENT may be a human or a nonhuman animal.  An assertion using #$hasPatients holds only during the time that PATIENT has a condition that is being treated by MEDIC; it does not represent or imply a long term doctor-patient relationship.")
(comment CrowdOfPeople "A group of people all together for some purpose.")
(comment PPTByStrengthType "The collection of types of drug products which are specified as to strength, and may be specified as to administration route, dosage form, and type of preparation (the drug compounds(s) contained).")
(comment Blackboard "A (usually rectangular) sheet of some composite material (or in the old days, slate), usually framed and supported by a stand or hung on a wall, for writing messages with sticks of chalk.  Popular in business/corporate offices and school rooms.")
(comment DayOfMonthType "Types of numeric days of the month.  Example instances are The1stDayOfMonth and The31stDayOfMonth.  TheLastDayOfMonth is *not* allInstanceOf #$DayOfMonthType, because this is a SibDisCol, and the last day can be the 28th, 29th, 30th, or 31st")
(comment GrandPiano "Collection of all instances of #$Piano-Acoustic in which the frame in which the pianos strings are mounted is held horizontally, often with the strings fanning out.  Such pianos are often equipped with a lid which, when raised, amplifies the sound.")
(comment AlwaysPositiveFunction "Function which is always positive")
(comment NordicSkiingSportsEvent "The subset of SnowSkiingSportsEvents in which the skiers heel is not bound to the ski.  This includes cross country skiing and ski jumping")
(disjointWith OneBathDwelling OneAndAHalfBathDwelling)
(comment rankOfFluentValue "(#$rankOfFluentValue OBJ COLL F(X) N) states that OBJ has the Nth largest value for F(X) among objects in the collection COLL.  For example, (#$rankOfFluentValue #$Texas-State #$State-UnitedStates #$areaOfRegion 2) states that of the US states, Texas has the 2nd largest area.")
(comment SecondFn "An instance of #$DateDenotingFunction.  When applied to an integer in the range 0 through 59 and an instance of #$CalendarMinute, #$SecondFn returns an instance of #$CalendarSecond.  (#$SecondFn S MINUTE) denotes second number S of MINUTE.  For example, (#$SecondFn 59 (#$MinuteFn 12 (#$HourFn 18 (#$DayFn 14 (#$MonthFn #$February (#$YearFn 1966)))))) denotes 6:12:59pm Feb. 14th, 1966.")
(comment UnitOfMoney "A specialization of #$UnitOfMeasure. Each instance of #$UnitOfMoney is a function which returns an instance of #$MonetaryValue (q.v.) when applied to a real number (see the collection #$SubLRealNumber) or a sequence of two real numbers.  For instance, (#$Cent-UnitedStates 2) is 2 U.S. cents.  Instances of #$UnitOfMoney include #$Dollar-UnitedStates, #$Peso-Mexico, and #$Yen-Japan.")
(disjointWith BlueCollarWorker Cleric)
(comment Trajectory "The collection of all trajectories of moving objects: each instance of #$Trajectory is the individual spatial region consisting of the points in space through which an object passes during a #$Movement-TranslationEvent.  A trajectory may or may not follow some pre-existing or pre-defined path (#$Path-Generic).  If it does follow one or more such paths, it determines a #$Traversal of those paths.  A #$Trajectory is understood and defined as a spatial line with one of the two possible directions of motion along it.  It is considered as being a part of some stationary background space (thus, in most contexts, a #$Trajectory cannot itself 'move').  Unlike a #$Path-Generic, a #$Trajectory (or a #$Traversal) can cross itself any number of times, and go back along itself, cycle over and over again, etc.  If there is a #$Movement-TranslationEvent, then that event always has a #$Trajectory; it is linked to its #$Trajectory by the #$ActorSlots #$trajectory-Complete and possibly #$trajectory-Partial.  In most contexts, a #$Trajectory will be a line (or rather a one-manifold) through space as traced by some designated point within the moving object (e.g., the center of gravity), but the collection #$Trajectory-SweptSpace is available to represent the whole space (with space and thickness) swept through by a moving object.  Contrast #$Trajectory with #$Path-Generic and with #$Traversal.")
(comment BillTotaling "The class of bill totaling events")
(comment BendingBrake "A machine used to bend sheets of metal.")
(disjointWith Transaction UnintendedLossOfUserRights)
(comment IndividualCustomerSalesRepresentative "The collection of all sales persons who sell to (makes sales pitches to) individual product/service users and dispensers.  Their contacts are individuals, as distinct from being companies (and company reprsentatives, such as company purchasing agents).")
(comment ExecutingAContract "A contractor arranges for, and performs, some action for a client, in exchange for some consideration")
(comment UsingAnObject "The collection of all #$Actions of using an object.  This refers to actual acts of manipulating/using an object, not the general events of which such use would be #$subEvents.  If the object being used is a #$PhysicalDevice (see #$deviceUsed), employ the more specific collection #$UsingADevice.")
(comment WrittenCharacterSequence "A collection of text markings each instance of which is a physical series of one or more #$WrittenCharacters.  Note that it is _not_ necessary that the series spell out a word or phrase in some  actual language.")
(comment CalfMuscle "The #$Collection of all instances of #$CalfMuscle.  The #$CalfMuscle ('gasterocnemius'), located in the #$Calf-AnimalBodyPart, either provides plantar (downward) flexion of the #$Foot-AnimalBodyPart or assists flexion of the #$Knee depending on situation.  It can act on either the #$Knee or the #$Ankle, but not simultaneously.  It has two heads, one attaching to the medial epicondyle of the #$Femur and the other to the lateral epicondyle.  The #$CalfMuscle and #$Soleus taken together are called the 'triceps sural'.")
(comment ThesaurusInformation "This unit will become fleshed out once theories of information get flushed out.  Note that a whole book's worth of thesaurus info is an instance of ThesarausInformation just as is a pair of synonyms.")
(comment IndependentOrganization "#$IndependentOrganization is a specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$IndependentOrganization is an organization which is not affiliated with any instance of #$ChainOrganization (q.v.), and is not a sub-organization of any other #$Organization.  An independent organization is neither the top-level organization of a chain, nor a lower level organization in a chain, nor is it an instance of #$ChainOrganization.  Note, however, that an instance of #$IndependentOrganization may have several locations within a small geographical region; e.g., Texas French Bread (a single, independent business) has multiple locations in Austin, TX.")
(comment AwardsCeremony "A ceremony at which the focal participant(s) receives an award recognizing an accomplishment.  Sometimes they do not know beforehand that they will receive this award.")
(comment TherapeuticRadiologist "A therapeutic radiologist is a doctor who specializes in using ionizing radiation for treating malignant tumors.")
(comment SinkingEvent "Events in which an object sinks (loses buoyancy and becomes immersed in fluid).")
(comment List-Information "The collection of pieces of information in which the contents are discrete items, perhaps enumerated or in some other way ordered.")
(comment periodRightsGrantedFor "This predicate is used to state the period during which a temporary user right is in force, as given in a particular agreement.  (#$periodRightsGrantedFor AGR DUR) means that DUR is the #$TimeInterval for which rights are granted in the #$TemporaryUserRightsAgreement AGR.  This predicate is useful in expressing, e.g., China's lease of Hong Kong to the British, a landlord's lease of an apartment to a tenant, Avis giving someone the right to drive one of their cars for a week, etc.")
(comment financialPlanners "The people who perform financial planning for this agent")
(comment PhysicalTherapist "A health care worker whose job involves using the techniques of physical therapy to treat a condition.")
(comment UndergraduateStudent "The most ideal person type until the most ideal instance graduates in June of 1989.")
(comment InterExistingObjectPredicate "A specialization of both #$ObjectPredicate (q.v.) and #$BinaryPredicate.  Each instance of #$InterExistingObjectPredicate is a binary predicate that only relates pairs of #$SomethingExistings to each other.  Thus both argument-places of such a predicate are constrained to instances (see #$argIsa) of #$SomethingExisting or some specialization thereof.  Instances of #$InterExistingObjectPredicate include #$derivedFrom, #$cohabitants, #$capitalCity, and #$electricallyConnectedTo.")
(comment (LowAmountFn TidinessLevel) "Slovenly")
(comment Fellow-FACS "This title is given to fellows of the American College of Surgeons.")
(comment Honorable "The prefix ''Hon'' that may attach to a person's name.  Used as a title for judges.")
(comment GainingPossessionOfPlayingObject "In games with two opposing sides, this is when one side gains control of the playing object (ball, puck, etc.).  This includes rebounding in basketball.")
(comment Panic "Overmastering and unreasoning, often groundless, fear or fright")
(comment adheresToCodeOfConduct "Agent ARG1 fits the constraints on its behavior specified in the #$CodeOfConduct ARG2.")
(comment CamouflagePattern "Painted or dyed markings used on cloth or devices, usually by military forces, to hide personnel and equipment by blending them into the natural background of a geographical region.  The colors used in the pattern depend upon the region.  Typical colors are khaki, sand, jungle green.")
(comment MilitaryOfficer "A subcollection of #$MilitaryPerson. Each instance of this collection is a person who is a (commissioned or non-commissioned) officer in some #$MilitaryOrganization.")
(comment StandardServiceType "Instances are types of service events which are typically sold at a fixed price, and consist of a more-or-less fixed sequence of actions - that is, each service provider who performs one of these types of service charges every customer the same amount and gives them pretty much the same service")
(disjointWith LegalGovernmentOrganization RevoltOrganization)
(comment Dragon "Dragons - fictional monsters.  This collection should only  have instances in #$FictionalContexts")
(comment WaterColorPainting "WaterColorPaintings as representational art forms")
(comment Marathon "A specialization of #$RunningSportsEvent and #$IndividualSportsCompetition.  Each instance of #$Marathon is a cross-country footrace of 26 miles, 385 yards (41.3 kilometers).")
(comment HobbyActivity "An activity which is performed as a hobby.")
(comment SnowSkiingSportsEvent "The collection of snow skiing sports events, including alpine, nordic, and freestyle skiing")
(disjointWith OneBathDwelling ThreeBathDwelling)
(comment UnaryPredicate "A specialization of both #$UnaryRelation and #$Predicate.  #$UnaryPredicate is the collection of all predicates whose arity (see #$arity) is 1.")
(comment ContactLocationType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$ContactLocationType is a collection of places  at which a particular agent may be contacted. Instances of #$ContactLocationType may be characterized in several different ways, including the following: by method of contact (e.g., #$VoicePhoneLocation, #$FaxLocation); by purpose of contact (e.g., #$BillingLocation, #$ShippingLocation, #$EmergencyContact); by the agent's relationship to those places (e.g., #$HumanResidence, #$Workplace).  Note that a particular place may be an instance of two or more instances of #$ContactLocationType, since, for example, one person's home might be another's vacation location.")
(comment subBeliefSystem "This predicate relates belief systems to more specialized belief systems.  (#$subBeliefSystem BSYS SUB) indicates that SUB is a more specialized \"branch\" of belief system BSYS.  Thus the #$beliefStatements of SUB will be a superset of the #$beliefStatements of BSYS (sometimes with a few changes and deletions.)  Some examples of this are:  (#$subBeliefSystem #$Islam #$ShiiteIslam), which means that Shiite Islam is a specialized belief system with respect to Islam; (#$subBeliefSystem #$ProtestantReligion #$PresbyterianReligion), which means that Presbyterianism is a specialized form of Protestantism;  and (#$subBeliefSystem #$MilesianSchoolBeliefs #$AnaximandersPhilosophy), which means that Anaximander's philosophical beliefs comprise one variety of Milesian School belief.")
(comment JusticeOfThePeace "A collection of persons.  Each element of #$JusticeOfThePeace is a magistrate authorized to perform marriages, decide minor cases, commit persons to trial in a higher court, etc.")
(comment fieldDependsOn "The value of the #$LogicalField ARG1 depends on the value of the #$LogicalField ARG2.")
(comment CarDealerFn "Collection-forming function - takes a type of automobile as an argument, returns the class of auto dealership which is derived from instances of that type of automobile.")
(disjointWith Climbing SnowSkiing)
(comment DrugEvaluation "The collection of events in which the efficacy and/or safety of a drug or pharmaceutical substance/product is evaluated.  See also #$DrugTesting which refers to performing tests to perform on people to  determine if they have been taking drugs.")
(comment CrimeDetectionActivity "The collection of actions that can result in the detecting of a crime.")
(comment VisualMark "A specialization of #$VisualInformationBearingThing.  Each instance of #$VisualMark is a visible marking on some tangible object.  Visual markings may be applied to an object using ink, paint, or pencil; they may be engraved into or molded out of the object's material; they may be made of other objects affixed to or resting on the object (e.g., a plaque bearing a house number); or they may consist of contrasting areas of color or light level (e.g., markings on a computer screen). This collection is not to be confused with #$MarkingOnASurface, which is the collection of #$Events which consist, naturally, in making a mark on a surface. See also the predicates #$marks and #$markCreated.")
(comment GluteusMaximus "The #$Collection of all instances of #$GluteusMaximus #$Muscle.  The #$GluteusMaximus is located under the posterior surface of the #$Buttocks.  It controls extension of the #$Femur at the #$Hip.")
(comment QuotientFn "An instance of both #$BinaryFunction and #$EvaluatableFunction.  When applied to an instance DIVIDEND of #$ScalarInterval and an instance DIVISOR of #$ScalarInterval, #$QuotientFn returns an instance of #$ScalarInterval that is the result of dividing DIVIDEND by DIVISOR.  For example, (#$QuotientFn 24 6) is 4, (#$QuotientFn (#$Meter 3) (#$SecondsDuration 2)) is (#$MetersPerSecond 1.5) (i.e., 1.5 meters per second), and (#$QuotientFn (#$SecondsDuration 2) (#$Meter 3)) is ((#$PerFn #$SecondsDuration #$Meter) 0.6666666666666666) (i.e., 0.6666666666666666 seconds per meter).  Note that (#$QuotientFn DIVIDEND 0) is undefined for any instance DIVIDEND of #$ScalarInterval.")
(comment SpellingInformation "This unit will become fleshed out once theories of information get flushed out.    Note that a whole book's worth of thesaurus info is an instance of ThesarausInformation just as is a pair of synonyms.")
(comment ContactPointSubOrganization "#$ContactPointSubOrganization is a specialization of #$ServiceOrganization.  Each instance of #$ContactPointSubOrganization is an organization that is a #$subOrganizations of another #$Organization and is an important (within the larger #$Organization) contact point between the public and that #$Organization or between the #$Organization's #$clients and the #$Organization.")
(comment FreeShotPenalizing "A penalty in which your opponent is allowed one un-rushed, un-blocked kick, throw, or shot of the ball or puck.")
(comment AbdominalSurgeon "An abdominal surgeon is a doctor who specializes in performing surgical procedures on the abdomen.")
(comment HouseSized "Something that has the approximate volume of a house")
(comment MigrantFarmWorker "A farm worker who travels from state to state in search for work.")
(comment allowedAudience "entries are agents who are allowed to have access to this information bearing thing.")
(comment DayNursingEvent "A nursing care event which typically occurs outside of a medical facility.")
(comment Discoverer " the first person known --usually just the first European-- to have reached an unfamiliar place; Balboa discovered the Pacific, but Armstrong didn't discover the moon nor Marco Polo discover Cathay")
(disjointWith CalendarHour CalendarWeek)
(comment (MediumAmountFn LevelOfFitness) "The level of physical fitness of a moderately active person (or animal).")
(comment Fellow-FRCP "This title is given to fellows of the Royal College of Physicians (British).")
(comment BrigadierGeneral-Title "The prefix ''BG'' that may attach to a person's name.  Used as a title for Brigadier Generals.")
(comment CommittingAnError "Committing an error, in baseball.")
(comment SnowSkiing "The collection of all snow skiing events.  For now, this includes downhill and x-country.")
(comment Sympathy "A feeling of tenderness or respect induced by the suffering or distress of another")
(comment credibleToOn "(#$credibleToOn ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4) means that ARG2 has a credibility  of level ARG4 for the agent ARG1 with respect to an event ARG3 .")
(comment evaluee-Direct "The predicate #$evaluee-Direct relates a particular process of evaluation to the thing which is being evaluated in that process.  (#$evaluee-Direct EVAL OBJ) means that OBJ is both an input being considered (#$evaluationInput) during the instance of #$Evaluating, EVAL, and the thing about which information is concluded.  As examples: each contestant for Miss America 1996 is an #$evaluee-Direct in the 1996 Miss America Pageant; I am the #$evaluee-Direct in my annual employee review. A borderline example is an instance of #$PhysicalDevice being the #$evaluee-Direct in the research phase of an article for a Consumer Report article;  Although information about the specific device was determined, that device was being used as a prototype in order to determine information about a specific type of device.")
(comment perspectives "U, a third-person description, has V as one of it's perspective mts which results from an assertion of the form #$actorSlotOfMt(V U AS) where AS can be any #$ActorSlot.")
(comment RevoltOrganization "A specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$RevoltOrganization is an organization that is dedicated to the overthrow some established civil authority (be it monarchy, dictatorship, theocratic, or democratic). An important subcollection of #$RevoltOrganization is #$TerroristGroup, but #$RevoltOrganization also includes organizations that do not use terrorist tactics.  The designation of an organization as ``terrorist'' is often a political act, with opponents of the organization calling it such while supporters argue that the members are ``freedom fighters''.")
(comment LobsterBuoy "A buoy used to mark the location of an underwater lobster trap.")
(comment AcrylicPainting "AcrylicPaintings as representational art forms")
(comment DayOfYearFn "(#$DayOfYearFn ?MONTH ?N) denotes the collection of #$CalendarDays which are the Nth day of the month ?MONTH.  For example, (#$DayOfYearFn #$July 4) denotes the collection of each and every fourth of July -- including, of course, those that occured before the American Revolutionary War.")
(comment Remodeling "A collection of events. In each instance of #$Remodeling, an agent makes some significant structural change to a #$Building in an effort to improve it. Examples include replacing the roof, siding, flooring, cabinets, etc., building or removing walls, or building additional rooms, floors, or wings. Painting, cleaning, and repairing, are NOT specs of #$Remodeling, although instances of #$Remodeling often include subevents of painting or cleaning.")
(comment JudoSportsEvent "Judo matches for sport.")
(comment AirShow "#$AirShow is the collection of instances of #$EntertainmentEvent such that (#$PerformingFn #$AirShow) returns a collection of instances of #$Flying.")
(disjointWith OneBathDwelling TwoBathDwelling)
(comment Assembling "A collection of events.  In each #$Assembling event, physical objects are combined by fastening them together in some way to produce a new object.")
(disjointWith ContactLocationType OrganismClassificationType)
(comment MinuteFn "An instance of #$DateDenotingFunction.  When applied to an integer in the range 0 through 59 and an instance of #$CalendarHour, #$MinuteFn returns an instance of #$CalendarMinute.  (#$MinuteFn MINUTE HOUR) denotes minute number MINUTE of HOUR.  For example, (#$MinuteFn 12 (#$HourFn 18 (#$DayFn 14 (#$MonthFn #$February (#$YearFn 1966))))) is 6:12pm, Feb. 14th, 1966.")
(comment fieldCodedValues "The #$LogicalField ARG1 can have the value ARG2, which depends on a code entry in the physical table.")
(comment HandballCourt "A court where handball is played.")
(disjointWith Holiday ChangeInUserRights)
(comment freightRailTrafficRate "This measures the rate at which freight is shipped by rail

in some region. The most common rate measure for this is in

terms of billion net ton-kilometers per year.")
(disjointWith StoryTelling AnnouncingSomething)
(comment WrittenNumeralSequence "A specialization of #$WrittenCharacterSequence any instance of which is a

sequence of one or more #$WrittenNumerals (and possibly

also certain other #$WrittenCharacters such as decimal

points, etc.) that are arranged so as to denote a number

according to the conventions of some numeric system.")
(comment BreastExam "A #$BreastExam is a manual test to detect the presence of lumps in a breast.  A result of True means that a lump was detected.")
(comment exponentOfQuantity "In the equation for ARG1, the (mathematical) value of ARG2 has the exponent ARG3.  So, e.g. (#$exponentOfQuantity Area Distance 2).")
(comment VeterinaryHospital "#$VeterinaryHospital is a specialization of #$SingleSiteLocalOrganizationWithClients and #$MedicalCareOrganization.  Each instance of #$VeterinaryHospital a local organization that provides professional medical care to non-human animals.  Note that this is not a specialization of #$Hospital.  The names may be the same, but hospitals provide medical care to persons only.")
(comment BackOfHand "the whole back surface of a hand, including the outer surface of the fingers and thumb.")
(comment FinePenalizing "A penalty in which you are required to pay a monetary fine.")
(comment Rheumatologist "A rheumatologist is a doctor who specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of arthritis.")
(comment LycophytinaSubdivision "A subdivision in the plant kingdom which contains the club mosses and other lycopods.  Many are extinct.")
(comment Tribunal "A collection of organizations.  Each instance of #$Tribunal is a collective #$JudicialAgent, consisting of a group of people who are appointed, sometimes on a temporary basis (as opposed to the permanent nature of a #$Court-Judicial), to judge special matters and determine punishment or order restitution or other remedies.")
(comment DiningSet "A group of furniture consisting of a table and several chairs, which is intended to be used together for eating at.")
(comment Analyst "Analysts create work for others by pointing out problems and trends. They create the mountains of information that administrators supposedly act on.")
(comment Parsec "A very large unit of distance.  An object which is one parsec away from the earth will have a parallax of one arc second, which is 1/60 of a degree.  A parsec is 3.26 light-years")
(comment Fellow-FAAN "This title is given to fellows of the American Academy of Nursing.")
(comment MathematicalThing "A specialization of #$MathematicalOrComputationalThing.  Each instance of #$MathematicalThing is an atemporal, nonspatial, purely mathematical thing.  #$MathematicalThing is partitioned into two main specializations, #$MathematicalObject and #$SetOrCollection (qq.v).")
(comment RelayLeg "A single leg of a relay.")
(comment Tempering "A heating process and cooling process applied to a material to change its physical characteristics.")
(comment CommercialAircraft "This is the collection of all commercially owned or operated aircraft.  This collection includes both fixed and rotary wing commercial aircraft used primarily for the transportation of passengers or freight.")
(comment EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus "A collection of specializations of #$Employee.  Each instance of #$EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus is a classification commonly used by human resources departments to describe the status of workers on the company payroll.  Note that these collections classify a person's status in a job, rather than the position itself.  Examples of #$EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus include #$CommissionedWorker, #$HourlyWorker, #$FullTimeWorker, #$PartTimeWorker, #$TemporaryWorker. Also see #$employeeStatus.")
(comment PharmacyProductType-Level1 "The collection of types of drug products that may be specified as to dosage form and type of preparation (the drug product(s) contained), but are not specified as to administration route, strength or packaging.")
(comment TemperaPainting "The collection of paintings made using tempera, a mixture of dry pigment and egg yolks, among other materials.  Many instances of #$TemperaPainting were made using oil glazes in addition to tempera.")
(comment Tattooing "The process in which permanent marks are intentionally made on the skin (usually of a person).  Involves a subEvent of cutting the skin and (usually) inserting a pigment.")
(comment CycHLTruthValue "The truth/strength combinations used in the Cyc HL implementation of #$CycLAssertions and arguments.")
(comment MiddleJudoSportsEvent "Judo matches for sport, in the Middle weight class.")
(disjointWith OneBathDwelling TwoAndAHalfBathDwelling)
(disjointWith Assembling MakingAGesture)
(comment ContactLocation "A specialization of #$PartiallyTangible.   Each instance of #$ContactLocation is a location at which some particular agent (e.g. a person or a corporation) may be contacted by any of several means, for any of several purposes.  #$ContactLocations include any place to which one may direct one or more of the following: letters, packages, phone calls or voice messages, bills, email, faxes, pages, subpoenas.  Contact locations must be fairly specific -- e.g. my house or my office, but not simply my city of residence.")
(comment Bagging "In this context, putting purchased items into a bag.  Often done by a store employee.")
(comment MilitaryVeteran "A person who has served in the armed forces of a country.")
(disjointWith Translation-SingleTrajectory Translation-MultiTrajectory)
(disjointWith YardWork PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment TennisCourt "A court where tennis is played.")
(disjointWith ChangeInUserRights IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(comment codeMapping "(#$codeMapping MAP CODE DENOTATION) specifies one mapping for the reified mapping MAP.  When a table uses MAP to interpret some field, the value CODE in that field will be interpreted as DENOTATION. DENOTATION will typically be a Cyc constant, but it might be a string or a number.")
(comment ApplicationForm "A form containing questions about certain basic personal data, used when applying for something (typically, a job).  The physical instrument with which one applies for something.")
(comment Balancing "The situation in which something is supported in equilibrium (usually with gravity), such that if its position changes just a little bit then it will change quite a bit.")
(comment MentalInformation "A specialization of #$PropositionalInformationThing.  Each instance of #$MentalInformation is the propositional content of a specific mental state (for example, a memory or a sensory perception) of an individual person.")
(disjointWith TimePoint CalendarDay)
(comment TerrestrialDirection "A specialization of #$Direction (q.v.).  Each instance of #$TerrestrialDirection is a direction that characterizes the orientation of objects on or near the surface of the Earth.  An important specialization is #$GeographicalDirection (q.v.).")
(comment AirportOrganization "#$AirportOrganization is a specialization of #$TravelOrganization.  Each instance of #$AirportOrganization is an organization that manages and controls particular airports and their appurtenant facilities; e.g., #$LaGuardiaAirport-Organization.")
(comment SideOfIndexFinger "the side of the index finger facing the thumb.")
(comment AnimalAbuse "The mistreatment of an animal involved in the sports event.")
(comment RadioisotopicPathologist "A radiosotopic pathologist is a doctor who specializes in using radioactive isotopes to reveal the effects of a disease on body tissue.")
(comment PsilotophytinaSubdivision "A subdivision in the plant kingdom which contains the whisk ferns.")
(comment Manor "A piece of land owned by royalty.")
(comment userRightsConstraints "In instances of ARG1, entries on ARG2 must be in the user-rights relation ARG4 to entries on ARG3.  For example, (#$userRightsConstraints BUYING SELLER #$objectOfPossessionTransfer #$FullUseRights).")
(comment BedroomSuite "A group of furniture consisting of a bed, a dresser, and possibly a desk, smaller chest of drawers, or bedside stand.")
(comment ServiceManager "These folk have to deal with the tough cases, managing impossible customer schedules, testy customers, sharp-tongued service reps. Dog's life.")
(disjointWith CalendarSecond CalendarWeek)
(comment pnMassNumber "The relationship between an #$EnglishWord and its mass proper noun form.  Proper nouns often are names of individuals or organizations;they may also be product brand names.  Mass forms denote non-countable quantities.  Syntactically singular in form and agreement properties. Example: 'Coke'.")
(comment LieutenantColonel-Title "The prefix ''LTC'' that may attach to a person's name.  Used as a title for Lieutenant Colonels.")
(comment ChokingSomeone "The action of choking someone - constricting an agent around the neck in order to induce pain, injury, or death.")
(comment BlockingAnAttack "Preventing an opponent from hitting you.")
(comment contraryFeelings "(#$contraryFeelings EMOTYPE CONTTYPE) means that a feeling of the type EMOTYPE is contrary to a feeling of the type CONTTYPE.  One feeling is contrary to another if they are opposed in almost all their components.  See also #$contrastedFeelings.  It would be very rare for someone to feel both an EMOTYPE and CONTTYPE at the same time, especially about the same thing/event/situation.  E.g., (#$contraryFeelings #$Gloominess #$Cheerfulness), (#$contraryFeelings #$Respect #$Contempt), (#$contraryFeelings #$Shame #$Pride), and so on.")
(comment advisorToOn " (#$advisorToOn ARG1 ARG2 ARG3) means that ARG1 is the advisor of ARG2 in a matter ARG3 .")
(comment NonDisclosureAgreement "an agreement between a party that provides information and a party that receives information which states that the recipient of the information will not share the info they receive with anyone else.")
(comment GoingToWork "The event of going to work.")
(comment JobDescription "A kind of context whose instances should contain assertions that indicates the disjunction of tasks that an employee normally performs while he/she is at work. This is represented as assertions using performsInsAsJob. Some of the well-defined job decriptions will actually contain obligations (which would be a #$genlMt of the #$JobDescription) for the employee to perform a certain task.  It also may outline what their boss may ask them to do.  For example, a janitor's job description would include an obligation such that the janitor performs vacuuming, dusting, cleaning the bathroom, etc.  It may even be as specific to say that the janitor performs vacuuming on Thursdays and dusting on Fridays.")
(disjointWith EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus LanguageGroupingType)
(comment Buoy "A floating marker used to denote points of interest to boaters on a waterway.")
(comment averageLinearVelocity "The average velocity of the transportee(s) during this event.")
(comment ProtestMarch "A (usually large) group of people walking together in order to protest something.  Usually done at some relevant location (near government buildings, e.g.).  Often signs or placards are carried.")
(comment QueensGuardUniform "The uniforms worn by queens guards: tall, black fluffy hats, red jackets and black pants. The queens guards are the people who perform the 'changing of the guards.'")
(comment ToIncreaseProfits "Make more profit")
(comment Swim-50MeterFreestyle "Swimming race - 50 meter freestyle.")
(comment Piety "Strong religious feeling and devotion to religious practice.")
(comment groundsOfBuilding "The #$LotOfLand on which this building is located.")
(disjointWith BiologicalLivingObject ContactLocation)
(comment HourFn "An instance of #$DateDenotingFunction.  When applied to an integer in the range 0 through 23 and an instance of #$CalendarDay, #$HourFn returns an instance of #$CalendarHour.  (#$HourFn INTEGER DAY) denotes hour number INTEGER of DAY.  For example, (#$HourFn 18 (#$DayFn 14 (#$MonthFn #$February (#$YearFn 1966)))) denotes  the 60 minute interval lasting from 6:00:00pm on 14 February 1966 to 7:00:00pm on 14 February 1966.")
(comment Meter "An instance of #$UnitOfDistance.  When applied to a number or pair of numbers, #$Meter returns an instance of #$Distance as its value.  For example, (#$Meter 5) is a distance of five meters.")
(comment Diploma "The collection of abstract #$Credentials each of which is awarded to certify that a particular #$Student has attended school or training sessions of some particular kind.  A #$Diploma (the abstract #$Credential) is represented by a #$DiplomaDocument.")
(disjointWith PreparingFoodOrDrink MedicalTesting)
(comment VolleyballCourt "A court where volleyball is played.")
(comment ReifiedMapping "Instances of #$ReifiedMapping collect sets of code-denotation mappings, specified by assertions involving #$codeMapping. #$usesMapping can be used to specify an instance of #$ReifiedMapping to interpret a particular field in a physical table.")
(comment Real0-1 "A number between 0 and 1")
(comment Hiker "The collection of all people who engage in instances of #$HikingEvent as a hobby.")
(comment BooksAndMagazinesMarketCategory "The market category for published books, magazines, related materials.  What a shopper would find in BookStop, or in a well-stocked bookstore.")
(disjointWith Communicating Eavesdropping)
(comment CreationGoal "A goal attribute.  If a goal has this attribute for an agent then the goal involves bringing a new entity into being.")
(comment fixedObstacleWRT "OBJ1 is a fixed obstacle with respect to OBJ2, i.e in a collision between both objects, OBJ2 will stop OBJ1's movement")
(comment PossessiveMarker-Sg "The collection of all contracted possessive endings which attach to singular nouns. In English, this is only 's, as in 'boy's'.")
(comment ProhibitedSportsEquipmentUse "The use of prohibited equipment or the illegal altering of equipment, yours or your opponent's.")
(comment Nephrologist "A nephrologist is a doctor who specializes in diagnosing and treating kidney problems.")
(comment GuidingAMovingObject "A specialization of #$DirectedTranslation.  Each instance of #$GuidingAMovingObject is an event in which an agent guides or steers an object which is in translational (as opposed to rotational) motion.  Notable specializations of #$GuidingAMovingObject include #$PuttingSomethingSomewhere, #$GuidingAnAnimal, and #$SteeringADeviceByHand.")
(comment CustomerRep "The customer rep deals with customers and is usually cranky. Depending on the size of the company, they may do everything or just answer phones and enqueue assignments to others.")
(comment Fathom "A nautical unit of distance equal to 6 feet.  Often used to indicate water depths.")
(disjointWith CalendarMonth CalendarWeek)
(comment Fellow-FRCS "This title is given to fellows of the Royal College of Surgeons (British).")
(comment Organism-Whole "A specialization of #$BiologicalLivingObject.  Each instance of #$Organism-Whole is a biological living object (BLO) that is a whole, and not part of some other BLO.  Most instances of #$Organism-Whole are capable of existing and reproducing while physically separate from other organisms (with allowances for eating and mating).  Abnormal BLOs which are nonetheless considered to be instances of #$Organism-Whole include instances of #$Virus, as well as sterile hybrids and colony organisms, like those in slime molds or the instances of #$PortugueseManOfWar.")
(comment NLSyntacticPredicate "The predicates which make up the Cyc lexicon.")
(comment CoordinatingWithTeammates "Working together efficiently and smoothly with teammates.")
(comment contrastedFeelings "(#$contrastedFeelings EMOTYPE CONTTYPE) means that a feeling of the type EMOTYPE differs in enough components from a feeling of the type CONTTYPE that it is unlikely (but not virtually impossible, as in the case of #$contraryFeelings) that someone would simultaneously experience feelings of both types EMOTYPE and CONTTYPE, especially with respect to the same object. E.g., (#$contrastedFeelings #$Pride #$Remorse),  (#$contrastedFeelings #$Abhorrence #$Respect), (#$contrastedFeelings #$Entertained-Emotion #$Panic), etc.  That last assertion expresses the rule of thumb that one does not often feel both entertained and panicy at the same time, though those two emotions are clearly not each other's `opposite' by any means.")
(comment SubjectPronoun "The collection of all subject pronouns. Subject pronouns can replace the subject noun in a sentence, but not the direct object, indirect object, or oblique object noun. Example: 'he'.")
(comment Stationary "objects which have this velocity are not moving (i.e. have a velocity of 0) with respect to the current reference frame.  Note that you can be waving your arms about and still be stationary.  What matters is if your center of gravity moves substantially enough (what precisely is `substantially enough' is a fuzzy notion right now...we should only define this when forced to, probably in a highly context dependent way), not whether some part of you may be moving with respects to other parts of you.")
(comment ComingHomeFromWork "The event of returning home from work.")
(disjointWith EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus ContactLocationType)
(comment NavigationalBuoy "A buoy intended to demarcate navigational pathways on large bodies of water.")
(comment Sit-In "Sitting at a location in order to protest something.  Usually done in groups.")
(comment PlayingABrassInstrument "Playing any #$BrassInstrument: #$Trumpet, #$Tuba, French horn, etc.")
(comment subFields "(#$subFields FIELD SUBFIELD) means that SUBFIELD is a narrower #$FieldOfStudy than FIELD and is part of FIELD.")
(comment AirRifleShootingSportsEvent "A marksmanship sports event in which air rifles are used.")
(comment Defeatedness-Feeling "The feeling of despair and loss one feels when defeated or overthrown.")
(disjointWith TwoFirePlaceDwelling ZeroFirePlaceDwelling)
(disjointWith Turning Assembling)
(comment pointOfContact "This predicate is used for specifying locations, of various types, where particular agents can be contacted. (#$pointOfContact AGENT LOCTYPE LOC) means that AGENT has as its LOCTYPE (a #$ContactLocationType, such as #$Workplace, #$HumanResidence, or #$BillingLocation) the particular #$ContactLocation (q.v.) LOC.  Thus, AGENT can be contacted at LOC.  Typically, LOC will correspond to a specific street address, as opposed to being a more generic location like #$CityOfAustinTX.")
(comment satisfiesDescription "ARG1 is a list of things (item1, item2, ...) which, taken together, satisfy the descriptions in the MT ARG3 of the roles listed in ARG2 (role1, role2, ...).  For example, we might see (#$satisfiesDescription (Joe Jane) (TheHusband TheWife) #$HumanSocialLifeMt).")
(comment ObjectFromIDFn "The Thing denoted by ARG2 under the mapping ARG1.")
(comment commemoratesEvent "The event ARG1 commemorates, celebrates, or is somehow centered around the event ARG2. E.g. Each of Joe's birthdays commemorates his birth. A baby shower celebrates (is focused on) an upcoming birth.")
(comment CertificationOfCompetence "A collection of certifications.  Each element of #$CertificationOfCompetence is the (abstract) declaration, by an appropriate authority, that a person is competent to perform a certain kind of job or task.  Such a certification may be embodied in a written document, oral testimonial, or personal recommendation.")
(comment TransactionIDFn "a function that maps from an ID and an organization to some transaction that the organization has participated in")
(disjointWith AstronomicalObject HumanScaleObject)
(disjointWith PoundingDrivingSomething ChangeInUserRights)
(comment BillionDollars "A unit of measure equal to one billion dollars.

This is the unit in which nations measure their #$grossDomesticProduct.

Note that the dollars are U.S. dollars (#$Dollar-UnitedStates),

and that the billion is a U.S. billion (10^9, not 10^12).")
(comment hasLabels "v1, v2, ... vN are labels on/near U, and contain information about U.")
(comment SoftwareIndustry "The collection of all software industries.  Each instance is an instance of #$Industry-Localized.

Each element of the collection is a #$Group of manufacturers and/or

entrepreneurs whose output is related in some way to the manufacturing

and/or distribution of software, i.e., #$ComputerProgram-CWs.  See also

#$ComputerHardwareIndustry and #$ComputerIndustry.")
(comment Aux-Negated "The collection of all auxiliary verbs negated by contraction. Example: 'hadn't'.")
(comment pointingToward "(#$pointingToward OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 has a pointing axis and that its axis points toward OBJ2.  A pointing axis is ascribed to objects that have directionality (e.g., a gun, a projectile, an arrow, an extended finger).")
(comment UseOfProscribedDrugs "The use of certain drugs in certain circumstances, as described in the rules of the competition.")
(comment PediatricPulmonologist " A pediatric pulmonologist is a doctor who specializes in diagnosing and treating lung problems in children.")
(comment internalSignals "All internal node signal declarations.")
(comment examples-Positive "Used to aid in exemplifying appropriate use of a constant. In assertions of the form (#$examples-Positive FORT EXAMPLE COMMENT), EXAMPLE is english text describing a single example which is relevant to the meaning of the #$HLReifiedDenotationalTerm, FORT. COMMENT is optional commentary about that example.  If you choose not to include the commentary then use the null string as the value for the third argument. Some examples are classically prototypical.  Others are just barely positive and serve to illustrate boundary cases for using FORT.  See also #$examples-Negative, #$examples-Borderline.")
(comment affiliatedOrganizations "The predicate #$affiliatedOrganizations indicates the organizations which are concerned with a certain `thing'.  (#$affiliatedOrganizations THING ORG) means ORG is one of (presumably, a set or possible set of) #$Organizations that have THING as a major focus of interest or activity.  THING can be anything, from a particular person, organization, place, event, type of event, work of art, game, intellectual endeavor, etc.  E.g., (#$affiliatedOrganizations ProtectingHumanRights #$AmnestyInternational); (#$affiliatedOrganizations ProtectingHumanRights #$SouthernPovertyLawCenter).")
(comment FinancialAnalyst "These folk detect trends in the financial situation of a business. Woe is them.")
(disjointWith CalendarWeek CalendarDay)
(comment subcatFrame "(#$subcatFrame WORD PART INT FRAME) means that the part of speech PART of word WORD has the subcategorization frame FRAME, for word sense INT.")
(comment Captain-Title "The prefix ''CPT'' that may attach to a person's name.  Used as a title for Captains.")
(comment TableTennisMatch "The collection of table tennis matches. A match of table tennis is either won by winning one game, winning the best of three, or winning the best of five games.")
(comment Spelunking "Cave-exploring events.")
(comment Passion "Intense longing for somebody or something regarded as essential to one's well-being or happiness")
(comment ObjectPronoun "The collection of all object pronouns. Object pronouns can replace the direct object, indirect object, or oblique object noun in a sentence, but not the subject noun. Example: 'them'.")
(comment MovieStar "A successful movie actor or actress. They are famous and rich.")
(comment USFederalEmployee "A subcollection of #$NationalGovernmentEmployee.  Each instance of #$USFederalEmployee is a worker who is employed directly by the United States federal government.")
(comment numericFluentGTOrET "#$numericFluentGTOrET(OBJ F(X) G(X)) states that F(OBJ) >= G(OBJ)")
(disjointWith ElectricalDevice Rowboat)
(comment UnitOfForce "Units of force measure force.")
(comment SummerOlympicsYear "A year in which a summer olympics was or will be held")
(comment FirefighterUniform "A coat, hat and boots.")
(comment Theorizing "This is the collection of instances in which an intelligent

agent forms an hypothesis or engages in the sort of thought process typically intended

to culminate in the formation and propounding of an hypothesis.")
(comment Swim-400MeterFreestyle "Swimming race - 400 meter freestyle.")
(comment ReligiousHoliday "A specialization of both #$ReligiousEvent and #$Holiday.  Each instance of #$ReligiousHoliday is a holiday observed by some religious tradition.  Note that individuals may observe or otherwise participate in some instances of #$ReligiousHoliday even if they are not members of the associated #$Religion.  Notable specializations of #$ReligiousHoliday include #$ChristianHoliday, #$JewishHoliday, and #$IslamicHoliday.")
(disjointWith OneFirePlaceDwelling ZeroFirePlaceDwelling)
(comment AreaCode "The area code (also called `city code') part of a phone number.  In the US, this is a string of three numeric characters.")
(comment moreCanonicalID "ARG1 and ARG2 are allSpecSlots of #$identificationStrings.  If an #$Individual has entries on both ARG1 and ARG2, the ARG1 entry is a more canonical way to refer to the object.  This is used by Cyccess to move all the assertions about an individual to one term, even if the assertions refer to the term with syntactically different forms.")
(comment totalCharge "(#$totalCharge THING MONEY) means that the total charge for all goods, services, #$salesTax and other taxes, shipping and handling, delivery charges, discounts, etc., in order to buy the #$TemporalThing THING is the #$MonetaryValue MONEY. For the thing's price without such extra charges, see #$basicPrice. This predicate is not to be confused with #$totalCharge-Event, which is the total charge not for a (purchased) thing but for a given #$Buying event. See also #$cost.")
(comment Steroid "The collection of #$Hormones having a characteristic ring structure and formed in the body from cholesterol. It includes both corticosteroid #$Hormones produced by the #$AdrenalGlands and reproductive hormones such as #$Testosterone and #$Estrogen.")
(disjointWith YardWork Meeting-SocialGathering)
(disjointWith OrganicMaterial AstronomicalObject)
(disjointWith Collision ChangeInUserRights)
(comment HeavenlyBodyScaleObject "Tangible objects on the order of size of moons, planets, and stars")
(comment MarkTypeFn "Given a marking template, there is a single class to which all the marks it makes belong.  This function returns that class for any #$MarkingTemplate.")
(comment MinusFn "A #$UnaryFunction that changes the sign of the instance of #$ScalarInterval taken as its argument. (#$MinusFn NUM) returns -NUM, and (#$MinusFn -NUM) returns NUM. For representing subtraction in CycL, see #$DifferenceFn.")
(comment arg3Format "An instance of #$ArgFormatPredicate (q.v.) used to place a particular #$Format (q.v.) constraint on the third (or \"arg3\") argument-place of a given predicate.  (#$arg3Format PRED FORMAT) means that PRED's arg3 is constrained to FORMAT.  See the reified instances #$Format for

further details.")
(comment HIVTest "BloodTests which test for the presence of HIV.")
(comment Approaching "The collection of events in which some object is approaching another object or location.")
(comment firstPersonSg-Present "The relationship between an #$EnglishWord and its first person singular verb form. This predicate is only used for the auxiliary verbs 'be', 'have', and 'do'.  Example: 'am'.")
(comment accompaniedBy "The agent ARG1 is accompanied by the agent ARG2 in the event ARG3.")
(comment DoctorOfJurisprudenceDegree "Law degrees.  All Lawyers need to have one.")
(comment RedoPlayPenalizing "A penalty in which you are required to repeat a play or attempt, as if the original one had never occurred.")
(comment CriticalCareMedicineSpecialist "A critical-care medicine specialist is a doctor who specializes in the treatment of patients in intensive care situations.")
(comment NonNegativeNumber "#$NonNegativeNumber is the sub-collection of #$RealNumber that excludes the negative reals.  Each instance of #$NonNegativeNumber is a  number greater than or equal to zero -- for example, 0, 0.173, Pi, 4, and 101.  Quantities measured in units -- for example, (#$SecondsDuration 4) and (#$Mile 42) -- are not instances of #$NonNegativeNumber, but rather are instances of its super-collection #$NonNegativeScalarInterval.")
(comment examples-Negative "Used to make clear inappropriate uses of a given constant and the rational for why these are inappropriate.   In assertions of the form (#$examples-Negative CONSTANT EXAMPLE COMMENT), EXAMPLE is english text describing a single example. COMMENT is optional commentary about that example.  If you choose not to include the commentary then use the null string as the value for the third argument.   Of course, it would not be instructive to assert #$examples-Negative about patently clear non-exemplars of a constant.  E.g. It would be foolish to assert that Frankfurt is an #$examples-Negative of #$Dog.  Nonetheless, certain exclusion criteria may be more important or ``set in stone'' than others.  For example, it may felt that the rationale for a certain exclusion criterion's existence is based on an intuitive guess and may be removed without too much trouble from other facts in kb which depend on this criterion.  An assertion with the comment that the affiliated example is a boundary negative can help clue later knowledge enterers to the more negotiable aspects of a terms definition.")
(comment TemporaryUserRightsAgreement "An agreement in which user rights are temporarily affected.")
(disjointWith CalendarCentury CalendarWeek)
(comment perfect "(#$perfect WORD STRING) means that STRING is the perfect verb form (also known as the past participle) of WORD.  The regular perfect verb form is often the same as the past tense verb form. Verbs in the Cyc lexicon should have a #$perfect entry only if they are irregular, since regular forms are generated by the morphology component. Regular example: `helped'. Irregular example: `eaten'.")
(comment Reverend-Title "The prefix ''Reverend'' that may attach to a man's name.  Used as a title for reverends.")
(comment LocalTalkNetwork "A kind of network via which Macintosh computers may interconnect.")
(comment ScoringPoints "Scoring, winning a point.")
(comment RockClimbing "Rock climbing events.")
(comment Remorse "Regret, self-reproach, and suffering or guilt for past sins or wrongs.")
(comment ReflexivePronoun "The collection of all reflexive pronouns. Reflexive pronouns can replace nouns in the context of an action which one does to oneself. Example: 'himself'.")
(comment spaceOfImageType "ARG1 is the space depicted in the VisualImageType ARG2.")
(comment AimingAProjectileLauncher "Positioning a projectile launcher so that its missile will hit the intended target.  Or perhaps, positioning in the way the user *thinks* will strike the target.  May be done by a human user or by an automatic device (as in guided missiles).")
(comment WinterOlympicsYear "A year in which a winter olympics was or will be held")
(comment CarryingPiggyback "Carrying someone (typically a child) on one's back.  Often done as a way of amusing the child.")
(comment LogicSignal "Signals that take part in electronic circuits.")
(comment SinglesTennisMatch "Games of Singles Tennis.")
(disjointWith MLKHoliday ReligiousHoliday)
(comment HandicapAccessibleBuilding "Should say it has ramps, elevators, &c.")
(comment TelephoneCountryCode "The collection of codes (character strings) one must dial to place a call to a country different from the country you are in.  For calls within the U.S., this defaults to 1.")
(comment ConsultingAnExpert "The collection of events in which someone consults a professional in order to solve a problem within that professional's #$fieldsOfCompetence.  During the event, the professional gives some advice, which we expect the consultor to follow, and if they do, then we expect this to further some professional goal of the consultant (such as a doctor's goal of helping patients to be healthy).")
(comment Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure "An instance of #$UnitOfAngularDistance.  When applied to a number or pair of numbers, #$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure returns an instance of #$AngularDistance as its value.  For example, (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure 360) is an angular distance of 360 degrees.")
(comment birthDay "This maps a #$Person to his/her birthday (as a #$DayOfYearType).  To specify the #$Date, use #$birthDate.")
(comment SetDenotingFunction "The subcollection of #$Function-Denotational whose instances, when applied to any appropriate (sequence of) arguments, return instances of #$Set-Mathematical.  Examples include #$ThePartition, #$TheCovering, and #$PowerSetFn.  Cf. #$CollectionDenotingFunction, #$IndividualDenotingFunction, and #$FunctionDenotingFunction.")
(comment implicitFields "(#$implicitFields PIT LF) indicates that LF is implicitly present in PIT.  We we expect a binding for that field to exist, although the IBO whose meaning is represented by the PIT does not explicitly state what the binding is.  For example, in a database of employees, there are explicit fields for names of employees, but we represent the employee associated with each record by an implicit logical field.")
(comment Hormone "A substance formed in some organ of the body and carried by a body fluid to another organ or tissue where it has a specific effect.")
(disjointWith Fishing CommunicationAct-Single)
(disjointWith Secretion-Bodily AstronomicalObject)
(comment marksWithTemplate "ARG2 is a mark made by the marking template ARG1.")
(disjointWith RollingOnASurface Sliding-Generic)
(comment dateSubsumes "(#$dateSubsumes LARGEDATE SMALLDATE) means that SMALLDATE is temporally subsumed by LARGEDATE.  Either or both temporal ends of SMALLDATE may coincide with the corresponding temporal end of LARGEDATE.")
(disjointWith CalendarMonth TimePoint)
(comment OrganizationWithBusinessCustomers "#$OrganizationWithBusinessCustomers is a specialization of #$OrganizationWithBusinessClients.  An instance of #$OrganizationWithBusinessCustomers sells goods and/or services to #$customers, most of whom are businesses or other #$Organizations, rather than individual #$Persons.")
(comment DistractingOpponent "The intentional distraction of your opponent's attention during his/her performance.")
(comment PediatricAllergist "A pediatric allergist is a doctor who specializes in diagnosing and treating children with allergy problems.")
(comment lengthOfTopographicFeature "(#$lengthOfTopographicFeature FEAT LENGTH) means that the length of the #$TopographicalFeature FEAT is the #$Distance LENGTH.  Examples: (#$lengthOfTopographicFeature #$Pyrenees-Mountains (#$Mile 435)); (#$lengthOfTopographicFeature #$ChangJiangRiver (#$Mile 6378)); (#$lengthOfTopographicFeature #$Andes-Mountains (#$Mile 7200)); (#$lengthOfTopographicFeature #$ZambeziRiver (#$Mile 2740)); (#$lengthOfTopographicFeature #$GreatBarrierReef (#$Mile 1250)).")
(comment examples-Borderline "Used when knowledge enterers are

agnostic about whether a given case counts as an exemplar usage of the

constant.  In assertions of the form (#$examples-Borderline CONSTANT

EXAMPLE COMMENT), EXAMPLE is english text describing a single

example.  COMMENT is optional commentary about that example.  Why do

we allow ourselves to be undecided about certain cases?  Explicit

vagueness may help later users understand the amount of leeway they

have in tailoring a constant for a particular unforseen use.  For

example, User1 may reify ConstantA for usage X.  User2 may come along

ConstantA years later wanting to use it for usage Y.  Assume that

usage Y requires some fact to be true about ConstantA about which

User1 was agnostic.  #$examples-Borderline is useful for indicating

this agnosticism and not requiring the knowledge enterer to waste time

deciding on membership for every possible exemplar they can think

of.")
(comment MusicalConducting "A #$MusicalConductor conducts a group of musicians.")
(disjointWith CalendarWeek TimePoint)
(comment Major-Title "The prefix ''Maj'' that may attach to a person's name.  Used as a title for Majors.")
(comment CompletingAPass "Successfully transfering a game object over land, air or water, to another team member. i.e. not a hand-off. This includes throws in baseball.")
(comment Bathing "The collection of whole body washing events, such as #$TakingAShower and #$TakingABath.")
(comment Reverence "Emotion inspired by something sacred or inviolable which arouses one's deep respect or veneration")
(disjointWith DevelopingAProduct CharitableDonation)
(comment TechnologyUserType "A set of types to categorize a person according to the kinds of technologies s/he uses.  Note that it is NOT presumed that a person can build or even understand the workings of that technology.  Any such assumptions are stated explicitly.  Also, note the explicit (default) connections between technology user types.")
(comment DoingADaysWork "The event of doing a day's work.")
(comment numericFluentEquals "#$numericFluentEquals(OBJ F(X) G(X)) states that F(OBJ) = G(OBJ)")
(disjointWith EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus MicrotheoryType)
(comment WaterPoloTeam "An organization of athletes that play water polo as a team.")
(comment SpinningWool "Creating wool thread from a mass of wool.")
(comment memoryOf "The event that this memory records.")
(comment FreePistolShootingSportsEvent "A marksmanship sports event in which free pistols are used.")
(disjointWith ThreeCarGarage TwoCarGarage)
(disjointWith AreaCode TelephoneCountryCode)
(comment regularPersonalServiceProvider "ARG1 has a relationship with ARG3, such that if ARG1 needs to consult a professional of type ARG2, by default they will go to ARG3 first.")
(comment Renting "A specialization of both #$MonetaryExchangeOfUserRights and #$TemporaryChangeOfUserRights.  Each instance of #$Renting is an event during which one agent grants to another agent the use of an object (owned or controlled by the first agent) for a period of time, in exchange for some remuneration.  The schedule of payment may vary, depending upon the rental period, type of object involved, type of usage granted, and/or other considerations.  The agent providing the object to rent is related to the instance of #$Renting by the predicate #$fromPossessor (q.v.); the agent paying to use the object is related to the instance of #$Renting by the predicate #$toPossessor (q.v.).  Those agents enter into an #$Agreement (q.v.).  Examples of #$Renting might include:  Fred renting a particular apartment last year; Jane renting a car all this week; Jack renting a canoe on Saturday morning.")
(comment moneyTransferred "This predicate indicates the amount of money involved in a particular transfer of funds.  (#$moneyTransferred TRANSFER MONEY) means that the #$MonetaryValue MONEY is transferred in the money transfer event TRANSFER.  Note that MONEY is distinct from the physical #$TenderObjects (q.v.) used to accomplish TRANSFER (cf. #$objectTendered).  For example, the #$moneyTransferred in a car payment might be 400 U.S. dollars, while the #$objectTendered in the payment is an instance of #$Check-TenderObject (q.v.).")
(comment officiator "The predicate #$officiator points to the agent who performs official functions at an event. For example, it is used to indicate the person who plays the role of a priest or justice of the peace at a wedding; also, a master of ceremonies, a judge, a referee.  An #$officiator is one of the performers at the social event where s/he officiates, usually not the only one.")
(comment preferredEntry "The agent ARG1 prefers ARG3 over ARG4 on its ARG2 slot.")
(comment ColdTemperatureActivity "Activities/events which typically happen only in an ambient temperature range that is below the freezing point of water.  ColdTemperatureActivities generally happen in the cold because some aspect of the event (#$stuffUsed, #$deviceUsed, etc.) requires cold temperatures to exist or to achieve optimum conditions.")
(comment Gymnast "Someone who performs gymnastics, possibly in competition or for a living.")
(disjointWith YardWork ShootingAProjectileWeapon)
(disjointWith MicroscopicScaleObject AstronomicalObject)
(disjointWith Fishing ChangeInUserRights)
(comment InkStamping "Ink-stamping is the process of marking something with ink by transferring the ink from a pad or well on a pre-shaped object.")
(comment arg1Format "An instance of #$ArgFormatPredicate (q.v.) used to place a particular #$Format (q.v.) constraint on the first (or \"arg1\") argument-place of a given predicate.  (#$arg1Format PRED FORMAT) means that PRED's arg1 is constrained to FORMAT.  See the reified instances #$Format for

further details.")
(disjointWith ContactLocationType PersonTypeByPositionInOrg)
(comment relativePosition-Vectored "Rays drawn from some point in arg2 in the direction arg3 intersect with some point of arg1.  #$relativePosition-Vectored is analogous to #$relativePosition, but uses an instance of #$UnitVectorInterval where #$relativePosition cites an instance of #$RelativePositionAttribute.")
(comment SoleProprietorship "#$SoleProprietorship is a specialization of #$PrivatelyHeldOrganization and #$OrganizationOfPeopleOnly.  Each instance of #$SoleProprietorship is a business in which an individual #$Person (or a married couple) owns, operates, and assumes liability for the business.   A #$SoleProprietorship may or may not have employees.  It has no shareholders or partners.")
(comment PhysicalInterferenceWithOpponent "Physically interfering in any way with your opponents performance.")
(comment AllergyAndImmunologySpecialist "A allergy and immunology specialist is a doctor who specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of problems cause by allergies or by weaknesses in the immune system.")
(comment deviationOfNormalDistribution "what it says")
(comment DocumentationConstant "A collection of CycL constants whose purpose is to facilitate users in their understanding of the system, tracking knowledge representation work being done, noting cleanup work to be done, etc. Documentation constants are usually not involved in inference.  Instances may be excluded from versions of the knowledge base in which available memory is a premium without affecting the performance of applications.")
(comment Wave-Liquid "the bumps that form on the top surface of liquids of sufficient volume in response to wind impact or vibration. One doesn't see waves on raindrops mists or very thin films of water on your windshield, does one?.  One does see waves on anything from oceans to gas in a gas tank to cups of water.")
(comment CalendarYear "A subcollection of #$Date (q.v.) and an instance of #$CalendarCoveringType (q.v.).  Each instance of #$CalendarYear is a year in some particular calendar.  Examples include #$TheYear1972 and (#$YearFn 2001).  Note that (as with any instance of an instance of calendar-covering-type) a given calendar-year is a temporally-continuous individual that occurs only _once_; e.g. it is not something that recurs each century or each millenium.")
(comment Fellow-FACA "This title is given to fellows of the American College of Anesthesiologists.")
(comment UnitOfPressure "A specialization of #$UnitOfMeasure.  Each instance of #$UnitOfPressure is a function which returns an instance of #$Pressure (q.v.) when applied to a real number (see the collection #$SubLRealNumber) or a sequence of two real numbers. For instance, (#$PoundsPerSquareInch 500) is a pressure of 500 pounds per square inch.  Instances of #$UnitOfPressure include #$Bar-UnitOfPressure, #$Pascal-UnitOfPressure, and #$PoundsPerSquareInch.")
(comment LieutenantGeneral-Title "The prefix ''LTG'' that may attach to a person's name.  Used as a title for Lieutenant Generals.")
(comment representsAgentInEvent "(#$representsAgentInEvent

REPRESENTATIVE AGENT EVENT) means that REPRESENTATIVE is an agent who represents AGENT in the temporal situation EVENT.  It is not uncommon for the same REPRESENTATIVE to represent multiple agents in the same EVENT, e.g. when someone is appointed to represent the interests of a group.")
(comment Despair "Utter loss of hope")
(comment LogicalFieldAttribute "Instances of #$LogicalFieldAttribute are used as tags within the function #$SchemaLF to generate terms that stand for a #$LogicalField of a table.  There is an informal convention - not enforced in code - that the names of #$LogicalFieldAttributes should begin with 'LF'. Many #$LogicalFieldAttributes have rules associated with them that infer various kinds of information about the resulting #$LogicalFields.")
(comment License-IBTRights "The set of licenses conferring specific rights to the use of some #$InformationBearingThing.")
(disjointWith IndustrializedRegion UnderdevelopedRegion)
(comment Politician "An instance of #$PersonTypeByActivity.  Each instance of #$Politician is a person who is involved in politics.  Specializations of #$Politician include #$HeadOfState, #$ElectoralCandidate, and #$HeadOfPoliticalParty.")
(comment Store-Generic "Not a store as in a business.  A store of something, a clump of stored things amassed for future use.  Not just a place for storing, but the store itself.  The store doesn't change when its contents changes - I could remove a tablespoon of sugar from my store of sugar, then put one back.  The store is the same.  A store can even be empty! So a store is different from its contents and from the place it's located.  Also, this concept depends on the INTENT of the agent placing the something there - something being in a given place for a long time still is not necessarily a store.  A #$Store-Generic is also not necessarily in an enclosed area - a pile of clothing on my bedroom floor could be a #$Store-Generic if I think of that spot as being where my laundry belongs.")
(disjointWith EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus BeliefSystemType)
(comment hasPhysicalAttractiveness "The socially recognized physical attractiveness of a person.")
(comment SingleLugeSportsEvent "The one person luge event")
(comment Falling-Freefall "Elements of #$Falling-Freefall are events in which the #$objectMoving is accelerated downward by the force of gravity and is not supported by anything.  Usually such objects move straight down (#$Down-Directly) but the stronger the wind or more significant the horizontal velocity, the greater the horizontal component of its direction (#$directionOfTranslation-Throughout).")
(disjointWith TwoCarGarage OneCarGarage)
(comment rfdNumber "Gives the rural free delivery number of an address.  E.g., in R.F.D. 72-C, Eggersville, OK, the entry on this slot would be the string ``72-C''.")
(comment ConsultingAFn "This NAT returns the collection of events in which someone consults a professional of the type ARG1.")
(comment MoneyTransfer "A specialization of both #$ChangeInUserRights and #$PurposefulAction.  In each instance of #$MoneyTransfer, possession of some quantity of money is transferred from one agent to another.  The transfer in question may be done in exchange for some good(s) or service(s), according to some (implicit or explicit) agreement (in which case the transfer is an instance of #$MoneyTransaction, an important specialization of #$MoneyTransfer), but it need not be.  Notable specializations of #$MoneyTransfer include #$Buying, #$Renting, and #$Paying.")
(comment SaleByCreditCard "A specialization of #$Buying.  Each instance of #$SaleByCreditCard is a purchase in which the buyer (see the predicate #$buyer) pays by using some instance of #$CreditCard (q.v.).")
(disjointWith CommunicationAct-Single YardWork)
(disjointWith ChangeInUserRights PerformanceTesting)
(comment Caliber "unit used to measure diameter of the bore of a firearm")
(comment altitudeOfLowestPointIs "(#$altitudeOfLowestPointIs REG ALT) means that there is a place in REG which has the altitude (#$altitudeAboveSeaLevel) ALT and this ALT is less than or equal to the altitudes of all the places within REG.")
(comment spatialConstraints "ARG4 gives the spatial relationship which ARG2 must have in relation to ARG3 while an instance of ARG1 is occuring.")
(comment interArgFormat5-1 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat5-1 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the first argument-place of PRED when PRED's fifth argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ... ARGN) in which ARG5 is an instance of COL, 
PRED's arg1 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG1' in 
the preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its 
instances for further explanation.")
(comment IndividualFullMedicalInsurance "These insurance policies cover medical expenses for a single person only.")
(comment rentsFrom "(#$rentsFrom RENTER OBJECT OWNER) means that RENTER rents OBJECT from OWNER.")
(disjointWith TimePoint CalendarYear)
(comment TrainingFn "This function can be used to denote the set of events in which an agent gets trained for some occupation.")
(comment Hospital "#$Hospital is a specialization of #$MedicalCareInstitution and #$SingleSiteLocalOrganizationWithClients.  Each instance of #$Hospital is a local (at one site -- see #$HospitalBuilding) organization composed of physicians, support personnel, and usually administrators.  The main function of the organization is to provide medical care (short or long term) to a number of patients/clients, for a fee if the patient/client is able to pay.  A clinic services out-patients, while a hospital has in-patients.  A hospital may have a clinic as a sub-organization, though.")
(comment defnIff "A #$CycInferenceDescriptorPredicate.  (#$defnIff COL TEST) means 
that TEST is the name of a piece of code in the SubL implementation 
of Cyc that specifies, and tests for, a necessary and sufficient 
condition for a CycL term's denoting an instance of (see #$isa) the 
collection COL.  If and only if TEST returns `T' (for `True') when 
applied to a particular term can that term's denotatum be considered 
an instance of COL; all and only terms that denote instances of COL 
must fulfill TEST's requirements.  See also #$defnNecessary and 
#$defnSufficient.")
(comment Gastroenterologist "The collection of doctors who specialize in the diagnosis and treatment of stomach and intestinal disorders.")
(comment instGroupMemberTypeIsOneOf "All instances of ARG1 have group members which are instances of some ARG2.")
(comment ClothingConvention "ClothingConventions (instances of #$ClothingConvention) are microtheories containing assertions about what clothes are worn with what items in a given social context.")
(comment HeadOfPoliticalParty "The head of politicalParty of a nation")
(disjointWith NuclearEvent ElectricalEvent)
(comment Fellow-FAAP "This title is given to fellows of the American Academy of Pediatricians.")
(comment CarAccident "The collection of all vehicular accidents in which one of the things damaged (see #$damages) is an #$Automobile.")
(comment MajorGeneral-Title "The prefix ''MG'' that may attach to a person's name.  Used as a title for Major Generals.")
(comment stringInLanguage "The string ARG1 is recognized as a meaningful fragment of (or a possibly meaningless but valid proper name in) the language ARG2 by people fluent in the language ARG2.")
(comment BlockingAPunch "In boxing, preventing an opponent from striking you.")
(comment BatchManufacturingEvent "A collection of manufacturing events.  In each #$BatchManufacturingEvent, the product is produced in batches, with a batch produced at the end of each such event.  #$BatchManufacturingEvents can be applied over and over to similar inputs to produce similar batches.  Batches may consist of discrete objects or may be masses of some stuff.")
(comment Vanity "Unjustified self-esteem and superiority. Excessive desire to win the notice, approval or praise of anothers. See Pride")
(comment PersonFocusGroup "Organizations which have as their focus a particular person, such as fan clubs.")
(comment DimeCoin-US "The US dime -- ten cents, silvery, and, if minted after 1945, with FDR on it")
(comment BondsTrader "The collection of all persons who professionally buy and sell municipal or government bonds")
(comment FinishedProductStores "A store of completely finished products from a Manufacturing.")
(comment TradeUnion "An organization of workers formed to mutually benefit all of its members.  If an employer establishes itself as a union shop, then all of its employees must be members of that particular trade union.")
(comment Shingling "A roofing task in which shingles are applied to a roof.")
(comment Sensor "The collection of devices, biological or artificial, that gather information.  

Note:  If a well-known named part of such an entity does the data-gathering, then generally only those parts are considered sensors, not the whole entity.  E.g., even though a person gathers information, we generally do not consider them to be a sensor, but rather the sensors are their eyes, ears, skin, etc.  In a context such as an ophthalmology convention, `well-known part' has a different binding, and they would consider just certain parts of the eye to be sensors.")
(comment Swim-100MeterBreaststroke "Swimming race - 100 meter breaststroke.")
(disjointWith ThreeCarGarage OneCarGarage)
(comment TelephoneExchangeNumber "The code for an exchange, currently expressed as the first three digits after the area code, of a telephone number in the U.S. and perhaps in some other countries.  An exchange was originally a set of equipment to handle up to 10,000 telephone lines located in a single office.  It was referred to in the US by two letters (Q and Z excluded -- having no holes on the dial telephone) and a single digit.  The two letters were usually referred to in speech by a word which they started.  Toll-free numbers did not have a dialable exchange and had to be accessed through an operator, as a \"Quincy\" or \"Zenith\" number.")
(comment medicalProscriptionForBLO "It is medically recommended that the organism ARG1 *refrain* from playing the role ARG3 in some instance of ARG2, typically but not necessarily, in order to ameliorate some condition they are experiencing.")
(comment accountAdministrator "The predicate #$accountAdministrator identifies the agent who administers a particular account (i.e. recorded  obligation of some particular type between specified parties).  (#$accountAdministrator ACCT AGENT) means that the #$Account ACCT is administered by the individual or organization (often a bank) AGENT. See also #$AccountManager.")
(comment RadiansPerSecondPerSecond "An instance of #$UnitOfAngularAcceleration.  When applied to a number or pair of numbers, #$RadiansPerSecondPerSecond returns an instance of #$AngularAccelerationRate as its value.  For example (#$RadiansPerSecondPerSecond 60) is an angular acceleration rate of 60 radians per second per second.")
(comment CashAndCarrySale "A subset of #$BuyingAnObject. Each instance of #$CashAndCarrySale is a sale in which the buyer pays cash for the items purchased, and the seller provides no delivery service for the purchased items.")
(disjointWith Fishing LegalProceeding)
(comment Congratulating "The activity of congratulating someone")
(disjointWith Perceiving ChangeInUserRights)
(comment BiologicalGoal "This attribute typically characterizes relationships between agents and cyc formulas describing states of affairs that are biological goals of the agent.  Most of these states of affairs are instinctually pursued by living objects and often not consciously pursued.")
(comment policyForClaim "ARG1 is an insurance claim which is made against the insurance policy ARG2.")
(comment CharSequenceOfLength-MixedCaseFn "Returns the datatype of mixed-case character sequences of length ARG1.")
(comment ancestors "This predicate relates an organism to any of its ancestors.  (#$ancestors YOUNGER OLDER) means that OLDER is one of the biological ancestors of YOUNGER.  That is, OLDER is either one of YOUNGER's biological parents, one of its biological grandparents, one of its biological great-grandparents, or so on.  #$ancestors is thus the \"transitive closure\" of the inverse of the #$biologicalOffspring relation.")
(disjointWith CalendarHour TimePoint)
(comment TrainingATruckDriver "This is the process of training someone to drive a truck, whether the person is actually able to drive a truck at the end or not.  For instance, if I take one truck-driving lesson, then drop out, the lesson will be an instance of this collection.  Successful events of training a truck driver are instances of the specialization #$TeachingASkillTruckDriving.")
(comment NationalPostalService "#$NationalPostalService is a specialization of #$PostalService.  Each instance of #$NationalPostalService is a postal service managed by the national government of its particular country.  The United States Postal Service would be an example, but United Parcel Service, since it is a private business, wouldn't be.")
(comment TransitiveWhClauseFrame "This frame is used for transitive words that take exactly one

          complement which is a either finite or infinitival wh-clause, but do not take either a that-clause or a that-less and wh-less 'bare' finite clause. In HPSG terms:

          [COMPS  <S[wh-comp]>] Example: 'I asked whether he had eaten', 'I wonder why he left', but not 'I asked that he leaves' or 'I asked he leaves' (in the question sense of ask) Another example is 'wonder'.")
(comment OpeningCeremony "A ceremony used to officially `kick off' an event, such as a banquet before a conference or a ribbon-cutting ceremony for a building.")
(comment PediatricRadiologist "A pediatric radiologist is a doctor who uses radiation to diagnose and treat disease in children.")
(comment SpaceShuttle "A fuel-burning conveyance for orbiting the Earth and returning")
(comment hasAllegianceTo "The agents that U feels close to, or loyal to, at the level indicated in ARG3.")
(comment wornWithGarmentType "(#$wornWithGarmentType ?THING-TYPE ?GARMENT-TYPE) means that a person is wearing an instance of ?GARMENT-TYPE if that person is also wearing an instance o ?THING-TYPE.  For example, (#$wornWithGarmentType Belt Pants) says that people who are wearing belts are also wearing pants.")
(comment Premier-HeadOfPoliticalParty "The #$Premier-HeadOfPoliticalParty of a country.")
(comment temporallyStartedBy "A #$ComplexTemporalPredicate that is a specialization of both  #$temporallyCooriginating and #$endsAfterEndingOf (qq.v.).   (#$temporallyStartedBy TEMPTHING STARTER) means that TEMPTHING  and STARTER start to occur or exist at the same time point (see  #$startingPoint) and that TEMPTHING ends or ceases to exist (see #$endingPoint) after STARTER ends or ceases to exist.  For example, TEMPTHING might be a #$WeddingCeremony and STARTER might be the  bride's walk down the aisle.")
(comment Fellow-FRCSC "This title is given to fellows of the Royal College of Surgeons (#$Canada).")
(comment Colonel-Title "The prefix ''Col'' that may attach to a person's name.  Used as a title for Colonels.")
(comment There-Existential "The collection of all existential indicators. In English, this is only the word 'there'.")
(comment TakingAStrike "In baseball, having a strike called against you, either by swinging at a ball and missing or by hitting a foul ball (when one has fewer than 2 strikes).")
(comment PackagingEvent "Final pre-sale preparation of a product, including placing the product into a container and attaching labels to the product - the process that turns a products into finishedProducts.")
(comment Concern "Care for, preocupation, worry. Feeling of a person with his mind engrossed by something pertinent to himself or another, due to his responsibility, interest or affection")
(comment TangibleTypeFocusGroup "Organizations which have as their focus a type of tangible thing, like cats or wine or French food.")
(comment Bill-US "US paper bill currency of all amounts")
(comment Soldier "An instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation, and a specialization of #$MilitaryPerson.  Each instance of #$Soldier is a person who serves in some military organization that operates primarily or exclusively on land (as opposed to on the water or in the air).")
(comment Appointment "An agreement to do something (usually meet someone) at a specified time and place")
(disjointWith ManufacturingOrganization FinancialOrganization)
(comment profit "The profit made by this agent in this transaction")
(comment SportsmanlikeAction "An action that is particularly sportsmanlike, not just one that is not unsportsmanlike.")
(comment TransplantingAPlant "Transferring a plant (house plant, shrub, tree, bulb, etc.) from one location to another.")
(comment TwoSeatLugeSportsEvent "The two person luge event")
(comment PromotingSomeone "A specialization of #$MakingAnAgreement.  Each instance of #$PromotingSomeone is an event in which someone is reassigned to a higher position within a company or other organization, so that s/he has more authority or responsibility and, with it, typically greater prestige and higher pay.")
(comment streetNumber "Gives the number of the street of an address.  E.g., in 6372-A Royal Crest Lane, the entry on this slot would be the string ``6372-A''.")
(comment medicalRecommendationForBLO "It is medically recommended that the BLO ARG1 play the role ARG3 in some instance of ARG2, typically but not necessarily, in order to ameliorate some condition they are experiencing.")
(comment BankAccount "The collection of bank acounts.")
(disjointWith MovieShowingAtATheater FluidFlowEvent)
(comment WorldRecord "The collection of world's records.")
(disjointWith MusicalCommunicating Meeting-SocialGathering)
(comment Consoling "The activity of consoling someone")
(disjointWith YardWork ChangeInUserRights)
(comment importValue "The amount of money spent by a nation on imports in a year.")
(comment mtImageID "ARG3 is a non-negative integer indicating the catalogue number of the image ARG1.  ARG2 denotes the catalogue in which the visual image is grouped.")
(comment qualifications "the credentials required to engage in profession.")
(comment CharSequenceOfMaximumLength-lowercaseFn "Returns the datatype of lowercase character sequences no longer than ARG1.")
(disjointWith NonLeapYear LeapYear)
(comment TeachingASkillFn "This function can be used to denote the set of events in which an agent gets taught some skill, as opposed to training an agent.")
(disjointWith Department IndependentOrganization)
(comment ProjectileImpact "A specialization of #$Colliding.  Each instance of #$ProjectileImpact is an event in which a projectile (an instance of #$Projectile-Device) collides with another object.")
(comment InsultingSomeone "The collection of communication acts in which the performer insults the recipient.  Saying something bad about someone when they are not present is not an example of #$InsultingSomeone.")
(comment PediatricEndocrinologist "A #$PediatricEndocrinologist is a doctor who specializes in diagnosing and treating problems with the endocrine glands in children.")
(comment expectedValue "The expected value of this distribution. Not the mode or mean.")
(disjointWith InformationTransferEvent CharitableDonation)
(comment RollFn "This function denotes collections whose members are stores of sheetlike or cordlike stuff wound on some type of tube or core.")
(comment President-HeadOfPoliticalParty "The #$President-HeadOfPoliticalParty of a country.")
(comment Sunday "A collection of #$CalendarDays and an  instance of #$DayOfWeekType.  #$Sunday is the collection of all  (and only) sundays.")
(comment pnPlural "The relationship between an #$EnglishWord and its plural proper noun form. Proper nouns often are names of individuals or organizations. The regular form of the plural can usually be made by adding 's' to the singular form. Plural forms denote more than one. Example: 'Czechs'.")
(disjointWith MicroscopicScaleObject HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject)
(comment Sir "The prefix ''Sir'' that may attach to a man's name.  To address a man as ''sir'' shows respect.")
(comment TransitiveADJPFrame "This frame is used for transitive words that take exactly one

          complement which is an AdjP. In HPSG terms:

          [COMPS  <AdjP>] Example: 'He got sick'.")
(comment HittingAGrandSlam "Hitting a home run when the bases are loaded.")
(comment Ingratitude "Feeling of one that shows poor return for kindness received. Ungratefulness")
(comment FieldOfStudyFocusGroup "Organizations which have as their focus a particular field of study.")
(comment TwentyDollarBill-US "The US 20 dollar bill -- with Andrew Jackson on it")
(comment WorkingProcess "Human occupations")
(disjointWith ManufacturingOrganization PoliticalParty)
(comment HumidifyingAir "The collection of intrinsic state-change processes which increase the concentration of water vapor in some portion of air.")
(disjointWith RudeAction SportsmanlikeAction)
(comment SpeedSkatingSportsEvent "The collection of speed skating competitions")
(comment postSituation "(#$postSituation EVENT SIT) means that SIT is a #$StaticSituation that begins after the #$Event EVENT ends, and that SIT is directly (usually causally) related to EVENT.  See #$postEvents and #$preSituation for related predicates.")
(comment PhoneNumberPartType "Collection of the different collections used to divide phone numbers into different parts.")
(comment medicallyRecommended "It is medically recommended that the BLO with the condition ARG1 (note that it's a particular instance of a condition and not the condition type) play the role ARG3 in some instance of ARG2, in order to ameliorate the condition.")
(disjointWith Check-TenderObject CreditCard)
(comment PeaceAccord "The collection of international agreements which aim at the settlement of questions outstanding among nations so that peace may be restored.")
(disjointWith ShootingAProjectileWeapon FluidFlowEvent)
(comment OlympicRecord "The collection of records for some event in the Olympics.")
(disjointWith Cleaning ShootingAProjectileWeapon)
(comment GymHorse "The piece of gymnastic equipment used during a gymnastic vault, with one wide, thick, relatively short horizontal beam.")
(disjointWith MicrotheoryType PharmacyProductType)
(comment VisualMarkType "Instances are types of visual marks.  If a class of visual mark VM is an instance of this, the instances of VM all share (more or less) the same informational content.")
(comment VerifyConclusionSometime "If we have (P => Q) and P is asserted, this verifies that Q is true. If Q is later retracted, the system might not immediately signal a warning but will eventually do so. Use this instead of #$VerifyConclusionImmediate if this delay in warning you is acceptable (there is a big savings in storage overhead).")
(comment agentPhoneNumber "(#$agentPhoneNumber AGENT PHONE-NUMBER) means that AGENT can be contacted by telephone at PHONE-NUMBER.  Another way to state much the same information is to use  #$pointOfContactInfo (q.v.) with #$phoneNumberText (q.v.) as its third argument.")
(comment temporallyCooriginating "A #$ComplexTemporalPredicate (q.v.) that is a specialization of 
#$temporallyIntersects.  (#$temporallyCooriginating TEMP1 TEMP2) means 
that the point of time at which TEMP1 starts to exist or occur (see 
#$startingPoint) is the same as the point of time at which TEMP2 starts 
to exist or occur.  Equivalently, (#$simultaneousWith (#$StartFn TEMP1) 
(#$StartFn TEMP2)) holds.  (Note that #$simultaneousWith is a 
specialization of #$equals.)  Sharing the same starting point as they 
do, TEMP1 and TEMP2 thus intersect temporally.")
(comment NonLeapYear "The collection of #$CalendarYears which are not leap years; i.e., calendar years in which February has 28 days")
(comment TeachingASkillTruckDriving "This is the collection of successful instances of #$TrainingATruckDriver, that is, at the end of an instance of this collection, the trainee is able to drive a truck.  This is the 'event'-version of the process.")
(disjointWith MilitaryOrganization FinancialOrganization)
(comment TransitiveGerundPhraseFrame "This frame is used for transitive words that take exactly one

          complement which is a gerund phrase. In HPSG terms:

          [COMPS  <VP[gerund]>] Example: 'He started eating at noon'.")
(comment ClosingCeremony "A ceremony used to officially end an event, like the closing ceremonies of the Olympics.")
(comment PediatricNeurologist "A pediatric neurologist is a doctor who specializes in treating brain and nerve disorders in children.")
(comment FamilyStyleFoodService "The type of dining in which the food is delivered to the table in serving dishes and the diners take their individual portions from the common dishes.")
(comment SecretaryGeneral-HeadOfPoliticalParty "The #$SecretaryGeneral-HeadOfPoliticalParty of a country.")
(comment pnSingular "The relationship between an #$EnglishWord and its singular proper noun form.  Proper nouns often are names of individuals or organizations. Singular forms denote one instance of the proper noun.  Example: 'Mary'.")
(disjointWith HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject Particle)
(comment Sergeant-Title "The prefix ''Sgt'' that may attach to a person's name. ''Sgt.'' is an abbreviation for Sargeant.")
(comment LanguageDialect "Related languages, so closely related they are really parts of the same language")
(comment WinningAdvantage "In tennis, winning a point after a deuce.")
(comment voiceMailNumber "This predicate gives the different parts of the phone number of the voice mail at a given location.")
(comment EmotionalColdness "Absence of feeling; less than normal human sympathy, friendliness, sensitiveness or responsiveness")
(comment IntraOrganizationCommunication " The communication that occurs  between the different departments of an organization . ")
(comment CopyrightLicense "An exclusive right to produce or sell an informationBearingThingForm.   Each InformationBearingThingForm should have only one CopyrightLicense associated with it at any given time.")
(comment Epidemiologist "Epidemiologists are doctors who study the distribution and determinants of health-related states or events in specified populations. This knowledge is applied to control health problems. One important function they perform is to analyze health data from a sample population to determine risk factors for a specific #$AilmentCondition. Another important function is to investigate #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemics to determine the cicrumstances under which people have become infected by harmful #$Microorganisms.")
(comment MaterialStores "A store of input materials to a Manufacturing.")
(comment FoundationOrganization "An organization whose purpose is to fund activities aligned with their beliefs.")
(comment usesIn "The agent ARG1 uses the object ARG2 to perform the action ARG3.")
(comment Orienteering "The collection of all hiking events in which a major component of the hike is navigating across country (no trails or roads) using map and compass.  A rite of passage for some Boy Scouts and most Explorer troops.")
(comment eventTemporalLocality "The time period over which the effects of an event may be felt. This could be infinite for certain events, but for most events this is a much shorter period")
(comment SuperHeavyweightFSWrestlingSportsEvent "A weight class of FSWrestlingSportsEvent")
(comment sharedNotes "A predicate-denoting constant that is an instance of #$DocumentationPredicate.  It is sometimes useful to include the same piece of text in the documentation of two or more constants or other #$CycLIndexedTerms. Rather than actually duplicating text in the Knowledge Base, one can create a #$SharedNote (q.v.): a piece of text that is to serve as this shared documentation, and which is itself the comment (see #$comment) on the #$SharedNote's constant.  (Thus the constants for shared-notes actually denote their own comments.)  (#$sharedNotes TERM NOTE) means that NOTE is a string of text (see #$TextString) serving as shared documentation partly about TERM.  Since #$SharedNotes are typically _shared_, there are likely to be one or more other indexed terms having NOTE as their shared-note as well.")
(disjointWith BorderCheckEvent-Person BorderCheckEvent-Thing)
(comment suiteNumber "Gives the suite number of an address.  E.g., in 1000 Welch Road, Suite 204-B, the entry on this slot would be the string ``204-B''.")
(comment medicallyProscribed "It is medically recommended that the organism with the condition ARG1 (note that it's a particular instance of a condition and not the condition type) *refrain* from playing the role ARG3 in instances of ARG2, in order to ameliorate the condition.")
(comment FinancialAccountTenderObject "A specialization of #$TenderObject.  Each instance of #$FinancialAccountTenderObject is an object (e.g., a check or a credit card) that serves as a means for offering payment in funds drawn on an associated instance of #$FinancialAccount.  The liquidity of an instance of #$FinancialAccountTenderObject depends on the status of the associated financial account (see the predicates #$accountBalance and #$accountStatus).")
(comment Commemoration "An action that commemorates some event or person.")
(comment issuesCredential "The agent ARG1 issues the credential ARG2.")
(comment Translation-Periodic "A specialization of both #$Movement-TranslationEvent and #$Movement-Periodic.  Each instance of #$Translation-Periodic is a translational movement in which the moving object returns to a certain location repeatedly, and at more or less regular time intervals.  Instances of #$Translation-Periodic include a ball bouncing in place and a planet revolving around a star.  Note that a planet rotating on its axis or a top spinning in place would not count as an instance of #$Translation-Periodic, since these movements, although periodic, are rotations rather than translations.")
(comment WorldRecordInFn "NAT which, given a competition type, returns the (individual) world record in that type of competition.")
(disjointWith ComputerActivity YardWork)
(comment GymPommelHorse "The piece of gymnastic equipment used during a Pommel Horse gymnastic routine, with one wide, thick, relatively short beam with two large handles on top.")
(comment SubLFunction "A collection of pieces of CycL code.  Each element of #$SubLFunction is a function that can be run (FUNCALL'ed) by the CycL interpreter.")
(comment assertionConclusionActionType "Consider an axiom of the form (P -> Q). 

If P is true, we might want the system to go ahead and conclude Q. 

On the other hand, we might want it just to verify that Q is true and 

complain if it is not. If later Q is retracted, we might want the system 

to immediately complain, or to detect this at its leisure. 

All this is indicated by placing instances of the collection

#$AssertionConclusionType as the arg2 of

the predicate #$assertionConclusionActionType, with the rule

in question being the arg1. See the comments on the instances of the 

collection #$AssertionConclusionType for further details.")
(comment marketShare "Arg3 is the proportion out of total dollar sales in the market ARG2 that went to the agent Arg1.")
(comment LeavingAPlace "A specialization of both #$TransferOut and #$Translation-LocationChange.  Each instance of #$LeavingAPlace is an event in which the performer (see the predicate #$performedBy) moves, under its own control and often under its own power, from one location to another.  Notable specializations of #$LeavingAPlace include #$EvacuatingAPlace and #$ExitingAContainer.")
(comment MovementProcess "A specialization of #$MovementEvent and an instance of #$TemporalStuffType. Each instance MOTION of #$MovementProcess is a movement event that can be considered as a continuous motion.  That is, (i) motion happens without interruption throughout MOTION and thus (ii) every time-slice of MOTION is 
itself a #$MovementProcess.")
(disjointWith CalendarDecade TimePoint)
(comment SubLRealNumber "The collection of all number-denoting expressions in the CycL language that are _not_ CycL constants or NATs, but are terms of SubL, the underlying implementation language of the Cyc system. #$SubLRealNumbers are numeric strings of the Arabic decimal system, including the decimal point and scientific notation.  Examples include the terms `212' and `3.14159d0'.  Non-examples include the expressions `#$One', `(#$Meter 6)', `(#$Unity 3)', `:34', `#$PlusInfinity', and `Avogadro's number'.  Note that this collection, like most instances of #$CycLExpressionType, is \"quoted\" (see #$quotedCollection).")
(comment Swimmer "The collection of persons who are trained in swimming, and who do it cosistently and with dedication, possibly competitively.")
(disjointWith SupplyCompany FoodServiceOrganization)
(comment salientAssertions "(#$salientAssertions TERM ASSERTION) means that ASSERTION has been deemed one of the assertions most useful to examine when one is trying to figure out the intended meaning of TERM.  Thus, ASSERTION will normally contain TERM, and should be something that has been asserted on its own in the KB as well.  Statements using #$salientAssertions are primarily intended for human consumption, and are not normally used by the Cyc inference engine.")
(comment ForensicSpecialist "A forensic specialist is a doctor who specializes in applying medical knowledge to legal situations.")
(comment AwardPractice "A collection of intangibles.  Each instance of #$AwardPractice is a distinction bestowed upon someone or something by an appropriately authorized agent, generally in recognition of some accomplishment and often as a result of a competitive process.  Awards may be given to people, books, buildings, cities, etc.  Note that this collection represents the awards themselves rather than tangible symbols of awards, such as medals or Oscar statuettes.  Nor do its instances represent any money that might accompany an award.  See also #$SymbolicObject, #$Token-Physical.")
(comment and2-In0 "In0 for a two input and gate.")
(disjointWith ServingFoodOrDrink CourseDuringAMeal)
(comment Chairman-HeadOfGovernment "The #$Chairman-HeadOfGovernment of a country.")
(comment ConnectingTogether "A specialization of both #$AttachmentEvent  and #$ActionOnObject (q.v.).  In a #$ConnectingTogether event, two or more tangible things get physically connected together (attached) by means of some  sort of connector or fastener.  Specializations of this collection include #$Riveting, #$Splicing, and #$ChemicalBonding.  Note that a #$ConnectingTogether need not be a #$Movement-TranslationEvent, since the objects being connected may be already at rest with respect to each other.")
(comment comparativeDegree "The relationship between an #$EnglishWord and its comparative adjectival form. This is often formed by suffixing 'er' to the regular form. Example: 'stronger'.")
(disjointWith TenderObject HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject)
(comment General-Title "The prefix ''General'' that may attach to a person's name.  Used as a title for Generals.")
(comment LogographicWriting "originally pictorial characters, primarily representing whole words")
(comment TennisMatch "The collection of tennis matches. Men need to win three sets to win a match. Women need to win two sets to win a match.")
(comment phoneNumberPart "This predicate gives the different parts of the phone number at a given location.")
(comment Charm "Fascination, allurement, delight; physical grace with compelling attractiveness")
(comment Student "An instance of #$PersonTypeByActivity.  Each instance of #$Student is a person who studies at some educational institution.  This collection includes students at all levels of study in all types of educational institutions.  Notable specializations of #$Student include #$UniversityStudent, #$GraduateStudent, and #$HighSchoolStudent.")
(comment SpinningLaundry "How a clotheswasher removes water from clothes - by spinning.  A subEvent of washing.")
(comment Icicle "Unlike e.g. #$SnowFlake or #$SnowMob, some of my instances (espec those which hang from cars) are so disgustingly dirty that they do not deserve to have #$Water-Fresh as their genls.")
(comment eventTypeDurationOfEffects "The time period over which the effects of this type of event may be felt. This could be infinite for certain events (such as killing a person), but for most events this is a much shorter period.  E.g., some of the effects of swimming are being wet, being tired, being out of breath, etc. but those effect generally only persist for a period of minutes after the swimming ends.")
(comment FourShellWithCoxRowingSportsEvent "The rowing sports events in which shells are propelled by four rowers with one oar each (two row port, two starboard), directed by a coxswain.")
(comment apartmentNumber "Gives the apartment number in an address.  E.g., in 16 Cherry Tree Lane, Apt 15-B, the entry on this slot would be the string ``15-B''.")
(comment allergen "The allergic reaction ARG1 was caused by ARG2.")
(disjointWith Currency FinancialAccountTenderObject)
(comment defnSufficient "A #$CycInferenceDescriptorPredicate.  (#$defnSufficient COL TEST) means that TEST is the name of a piece of code in the SubL implementation of Cyc that specifies, and tests for, a sufficient condition for a CycL term's denoting an instance of (see #$isa) the collection COL.  If TEST returns `T' (for `True') when applied to a particular term, then that term's denotatum is considered to be an instance of COL.  Note that TEST isn't necessarily a necessary test for membership in COL; that is, not all instances of COL must pass the test, unless TEST is also a #$defnNecessary for COL.  See the related predicates #$defnNecessary and #$defnIff.")
(comment FoundingOfCountryCelebration "A celebration of the founding of a country.  May include parades, speeches, TV specials, etc.")
(comment componentFields "The value of the #$LogicalField ARG1 can be partly decomposed into the value of the #$LogicalField ARG2.")
(comment GymBalanceBeam "The piece of gymnastic equipment used during a balance beam routine, with one wide, thick, horizontal beam.")
(disjointWith ContactLocationType PharmacyProductType)
(comment averageDepth "The average depth, in feet, of geographical regions such as oceans and canyons.")
(comment VerifyConclusionImmediate "If we have (P => Q) and P is asserted, this verifies that Q is true. If Q is later retracted, the system will immediately signal a warning. Use  #$VerifyConclusionSometime instead of this if a  delay in warning the user is acceptable (there is a big savings in storage overhead).")
(comment FullMedicalInsurance "These insurance policies cover all types of medical expenses, including routine examinations.  Major medical and supplemental insurance do not belong in this collection.")
(disjointWith CalendarSecond TimePoint)
(comment Diver "The collection of persons who are trained in and practice the sport of diving.")
(comment Pharmacy "#$Pharmacy is a specialization of #$PharmaceuticalDispensingOrganization, #$CommercialServiceOrganization, and #$SingleSiteLocalOrganizationWithClients.  Each instance of #$Pharmacy is a  (local-level) organization which sells mainly prescription drugs, but usually also carries non-prescription drugs and other medical supplies that might be needed by a family or individual.  Sometimes these are free-standing stores, sometimes departments within other stores (like drugstores and supermarkets).")
(comment englishGloss "To be used to refer to the manual english rendering of an assertion or perhaps a constant but see also #$denotation.  #$englishGloss assertions may be used to enhance or supplement automatic nl generation results, serve as a training data set for a program which learns to generate NL from CycL, etc..  This predicate should not be used for commentary.  For commentary see #$comment or #$cyclistNotes.")
(comment PhysicalMedicineSpecialist "A doctor who specializes in rehabilitation and physical therapy.")
(comment and2-In1 "In1 for a two input and gate.")
(comment EMailAddress "A specialization of #$ContactInfoString.  Each instance of #$EMailAddress is a string that identifies an e-mail user's electronic mailbox.")
(comment Chancellor-HeadOfGovernment "The #$Chancellor-HeadOfGovernment of a country.")
(comment ControllingSomething "A specialization of #$PurposefulPhysicalAction (q.v.).  Each instance  of #$ControllingSomething is a purposeful physical action in which an  agent intentionally controls an object (i.e. instance of  #$SomethingExisting).  It is not necessary that the agent touch the  object being controlled (see #$objectControlled), only that s/he  exercise control over some of its movements, functioning, or  actions.  Specializations of #$ControllingSomething include  #$GuidingAMovingObject (some instances of which involve a  #$RemoteControlDevice), #$HandlingAnObject, #$Braking, #$SteeringADeviceByHand,  #$PlayingAMusicalInstrument, #$CuttingFabric, #$CarryingWhileLocomoting,  and #$FlushingAToilet.  When a #$ControlDevice (q.v.) is being used  by an agent for its primary function, a #$ControllingSomething event is  typically taking place.")
(comment Fellow-FRACS "This title is given to fellows of the Royal Australasian College of Surgeons.")
(comment CalendarCentury "An instance of #$CalendarCoveringType, and a specialization of #$Date.  Each instance of #$CalendarCentury is a century on a particular calendar.  Instances of #$CalendarCentury include #$TheNineteenthCenturyCE and #$TheTwentiethCenturyCE.")
(comment Admiral-Title "The prefix ''Admiral'' that may attach to a person's name.  Used as a title for Admirals.  An admiral is considered as a ''general'' of the Navy/Coast Guard.")
(comment SyllabicWriting "writing with characters primarily representing syllables")
(comment faxNumber "This predicate gives the different parts of the phone number of the fax machine at a given location.")
(comment Diffidence "Unsure of himself. Emotion of a person who feels hesitant, lacking self-confidence. Distrust in my own ability, opinions or powers")
(comment communicationStyleConventions " #$communicationStyleConventions ARG1 ARG2 means that ARG1 communicates (whether speaking, writing, or some other means) using style ARG2 .")
(comment FiftyDollarBill-US "The US 50 dollar bill -- with Ulysses Grant on it")
(disjointWith Student HumanInfant)
(comment finalSportsEvent "The one event (the game/race/round) whose winner determines the winner of the competition.  It may not be the temporally last event (the game for the silver might be played after the game for the gold), but it is the decisive event for the winner of the whole competition.  It may well be the case that the competition has only one event, in which case this is the Finals.")
(comment Unshaved "An attribute for describing the level of hair on a body part: in this case, the body part has not been shaved and has some hair.")
(comment HorizontalBarSportsEvent "The collection of gymnastic events on the HorizontalBar.")
(comment propertyTaxRate "There isn't necessarily a property tax on iO all the specs of this slot's entryIsA.")
(comment PhoneSuffix "The last four digits of a telephone number in the U.S. and perhaps some other countries.")
(comment LegalHoliday "The subcollection of #$Holidays which are typically declared to be #$Holidays by the governments of western countries, and which are therefore days on which most people governed by that government do not work and on which students do not attend classes.  Such #$Holidays may coincide with #$ReligiousHolidays, especially where there is a government-sanctioned religion.")
(comment (FruitFn GrapeVine) "The collection of individual Grapes.")
(comment usesSchema "(#$usesSchema ?CONTENT ?SCHEMA) means that CONTENT (a #$LogicalTable or other #$SISContent) is defined/structured according to the relations represented in the #$SISLogicalSchema SCHEMA.")
(comment documentID "A unique identifier for a document, usually a document which is associated with and identifies some agreement.")
(comment BidItem "A bid for a particular item.")
(comment GymHorizontalBar "The piece of gymnastic equipment used during a horizontal bar routine, with one long, thin, horizontal bar.")
(comment passengerRailTrafficRate "(#$passengerRailTrafficRate

?AREA ?RATE) means that the #$GeographicalRegion ?AREA has a

passenger rail traffic rate of ?RATE. 

A passenger rail traffic rate is a measure based on the 

total number of 'passenger-miles' travelled

within a certain area, e.g., such-and-so billion miles per year.")
(comment Fingerprint "A collection of visual marks.  Each element of #$Fingerprint is a mark made when pressure from a manual digit leaves traces of body oils (or ink) on a surface, showing the patterns on the skin of the finger(s) that made them.")
(comment AssertConclusion "An instance of #$AssertionConclusionType.

If we have a rule of the form (#$implies FORMULA1 FORMULA2), and

the #$assertionConclusionActionType is #$AssertConclusion, then

the system will assert the consequent (FORMULA2) when the 

antecedent (FORMULA1) obtains. This is the default setting

for #$assertionConclusionActionType, so that there isn't really 

any reason to assert this #$AssertionConclusionType of

assertions.")
(comment interArgFormat1-2 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat1-2 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the second argument-place of PRED when PRED's first argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ... ARGN) in which ARG1 is an instance of COL, PRED's arg2
position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG2' in the 
preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its instances 
for further explanation.")
(comment FamilyFullMedicalInsurance "These insurance policies cover medical expenses for all immediate members of a particular family.")
(disjointWith CalendarCentury TimePoint)
(comment physicalPartTypes "(#$physicalPartTypes OBJ-TYPE PART-TYPE) means that every instance of the collection OBJ-TYPE has at least one instance of the collection PART-TYPE as a physical part (see the predicate #$physicalParts).")
(disjointWith Pharmacy MedicalClinic)
(comment ChildPsychologist "A child psychologist is a psychologist who specializes in diagnosing and treating children with psychological disorders.")
(comment and-Out "Out for a two input and gate.")
(disjointWith AreaCode EMailAddress)
(comment accountRepresentatives "Entries will the person who is the account representative for the organization")
(comment MainCourse "The collection of events which are defined as subevents of multiple-course meals during which the main course is eaten.")
(disjointWith PrivateSectorEmployee PublicSectorEmployee)
(comment LightYear "A very large unit of distance.  The distance that light travels in one year in a vacuum.")
(comment PersonTypeByOccupation "A collection of collections and a specialization of #$PersonTypeByActivity (q.v.).  Each instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation is a collection of workers (see #$PersonWithOccupation) and is defined in terms of the kind of work done.  The various instances of #$PersonTypeByOccupation correspond to jobs of all kinds, and not just to those colloquially called \"professions\".  Examples include #$ComputerProgrammerProfessional, #$FoodServiceEmployee, #$MedicalCareProfessional, #$SalesRepresentative, #$Brewer, and many others.  See also #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg.")
(comment GeriatricDoctor "A doctor who specializes in treating the elderly.")
(comment Hieroglyph "pictorial characters used in ancient writing systems, esp. Egyptian")
(comment PlacingOpponentInDanger "In wrestling, placing opponent in danger of falling, in the air, with back facing down, and upper body resisting fall.")
(comment ImportExportEvent "The collection of events in which a #$Product is transferred from one #$IndependentCountry to another along a single pathway. Because its instances involve a single pathway, they are not

#$PhysicalDistributionEvents.  Rather, an #$ImportExportEvent may be part (#$subEvents) of a product distribution.")
(comment Indecision "Emotion of one who is wavering between two or more courses of action")
(comment StyleOfCommunication " This is the style used when communicating something. ")
(comment PersonTypeByActivity "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$PersonTypeByActivity is a collection of #$Persons that classifies people by some kind of activity that they do on a regular basis.  Examples include #$Student, #$Tourist, and #$HornPlayer.  If the differentiating activity is one that is normally done as a career or job, it is preferable to make the collection an instance of the more specific #$PersonTypeByOccupation (q.v.).")
(comment PennyCoin-US "The US penny -- one cent, copper, with Honest Abe on it")
(comment DollarsPerDay "The amount of currency in dollars earned/spent in a day.")
(comment Tetanus "A condition caused by the toxin of a bacterium, which causes the muscles (esp. jaw) to contract tightly.  It is frequently contracted through puncture wounds.")
(comment Coloring-OfDrawing "A common child's activity where crayons or other colored media are used to add color to previously black and white line drawings.")
(comment SkiJumpNormalSportsEvent "The normal hill ski jump event")
(comment CookingUtensil "A specialization of #$FoodUtensil and #$FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice.  Each instance of #$CookingUtensil is a utensil used to manipulate food while it is being prepared.")
(comment SoreThroat "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition. Each instance of this collection is a soreness of the #$Pharynx, making #$Swallowing painful (as opposed to cases of soreness of the external #$Throat, caused by blows or cuts to the neck, or ills of the #$Esophagus such as acid reflux).")
(comment ELRelation-OneWay "A specialization of #$ELRelation (q.v.) instances of which appear only when input at the \"epistemological level\" (or EL) of the Cyc system, and whose original EL form is thereafter irretrievable.  Each instance of #$ELRelation-OneWay is associated, via the #$expansion or #$expansionDefn relation, to a sentence template to which the former is essentially equivalent and for which the former serves as a convenient alternative.  More precisely: A GAF (see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence) whose main  functor (or \"0th argument\") is a term that denotes a one-way EL relation can  occur only at the EL, and not at the underlying HL (\"heuristic level\") of the system.  Thus, although one can use a one-way-EL-relation-based GAF to make an assertion to the system, the GAF that actually gets stored as an assertion in the Cyc Knowledge Base is a different (though logically  equivalent) one that is related to the first via the #$expansion assertion  on the EL relation.  Upon assertion, the first GAF is \"transformed into\" the second GAF by the #$CycCanonicalizer.  For example, #$lessThan is a one-way EL relation whose #$expansion correlate is the template (#$greaterThan :ARG2 :ARG1).  So if one makes an assertion using the sentence `(#$lessThan 1 2)', the assertion that actually shows up in the KB is `(#$greaterThan 2 1)'.  Note that terms for one-way EL relations _do_ appear in stored assertions in which  they occur in argument places other than the 0th; e.g. the sentence `(#$isa #$lessThan #$OrderingPredicate)' is in the KB.  One-way EL relations afford cyclists the convenience of having alternative forms of expression, while their expansions serve to minimize redundancy in the types of GAFs that the system has to store and reason with.")
(comment (UsingAForFn Spoon EatingAMorsel deviceUsed) "An instance of #$ScriptedEventType.  Each instance of (#$UsingAForFn #$Spoon #$EatingAMorsel #$deviceUsed) is an event in which a spoon is moved to a soup bowl, filled with soup, lifted to a mouth, and emptied into the mouth (whereupon the soup in the mouth is swallowed).  This script is itself an iterated scene in #$EatingABowlOfSoup (q.v.).")
(disjointWith SimpleRepairing Manufacturing)
(comment BramStoker "Bram (Abraham) Stoker was born November 8, 1847 in Dublin, Ireland. Stoker was a sickly child and spent a lot of time in bed. Growing up his mother told him a lot of horror stories. Stoker studied Math at Trinity College Dublin. After graduation he became a civil servant. At this time, he also worked as a free lance journalist, a drama critic and editor of the \"Evening Mail\". In 1876 he met Sir Henry Irving, a famous actor. Stoker accepted a job as a personal secretary to Irving and went to England in 1878. While working for Irving he met an aspiring actress named Florence Balcombe. They were married 1878 and had one son, Noel, born 1879. In England he also began writing a series of novels and short stories the first of which was \"The Snake's Pass\". Although best known for #$Dracula-TheNovel, Stoker wrote eighteen books before he died in 1912 of exhaustion")
