(comment Bronchodilator "Substances whihch cause the bronchia to open wider - frequently given to asthma sufferers.")
(comment across-UnderspecifiedRegion "(#$across-UnderspecifiedRegion ACT REGION) states that an abstract locational relation holds between ACT and REGION, where REGION is a #$Region-Underspecified crossed during ACT. #$across-UnderspecifiedRegion is an underspecified semantic representation that may be elaborated to represent either a spatial example of crossing (as in 'crossing the park') or a temporal use of crossing ('processions will be held across Easter') or a metaphorical use ('Smith's theory extends across science and religion').")
(comment InsulatingCover "The set of objects which function as insulators and thus protect against undesirable energy transfers.  Includes artificial as well as ``natural'' material such as hair, fat, down.")
(comment ComputeImplicitISObjectFn "An #$EvaluatableFunction that generates terms to represent the implicit objects denoted by data recorded in fields of database tables and other information sources.  (#$ComputeImplicitISObjectFn ?LTS ?KEYOBJ ?LF) denotes the particular object corresponding to the implicit field ?LF of the tuple identified by ?KEYOBJ.  Where possible, this term will evaluate to a #$DBEntryFn term which is a function of a collection, a type of unique identifier for that collection (see #$IDStringType), and a particular instance of that identifier type taken from the tuple identified by ?KEYOBJ.  When this is not possible, this term will evaluate to a term represented by an #$ImplicitISObjectFn expression.")
(comment Rags-ClothingItem "Ripped,  shabby clothes, typically worn by vagrants.")
(comment fixedRate "The predicate used to state the fixed rate of interest charged on the principle amount of some agreement, such as a #$Bond or a #$LoanAgreement.  (#$fixedRate AGREE RATE) means that RATE is the rate of interest on AGREE, set in the #$Agreement itself, and fixed at that RATE for the term of the #$Agreement.")
(comment OnlineVendor "The collection of #$Vendors who do some of their transactions online.")
(comment DagFn "(#$DagFn AVM) converts the AVM/Typed Feature Structure AVM into a directed acyclic graph (or Dag; essentially a Lisp list) that is amenable to efficient unification at the Lisp level.")
(comment Van "Vans are vehicles that can hold lotsa people or things (like drum sets). Can be adapted for mobility impaired people.")
(comment NucleosideTriphosphate "A collection of nucleotides. They consist of a #$NitrogenBase, such as #$Adenine-Base, linked with a sugar and three phosphates.")
(comment Jeep-Military "The collection of jeep-like vehicles used primarily by military organizations.")
(comment ProtectingABackupPowerSupply "A spec of #$ProtectingSomething where the #$objectActedOn is a #$BackupPowerSupply.")
(comment MineWarfareShip "The collection of ships intended for use in placing, detecting, or destroying underwater mines.")
(comment MassTranscriptionOfDNAToRNA "The event in #$GeneExpression which is itself composed of a series of  subevents in which a gene is replicated repeatedly to RNA.")
(comment interArgFormat4-4 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat4-4 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the fourth argument-place of PRED when PRED's fourth argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ... ARGN) in which ARG4 is an instance of COL, PRED's
arg4 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG4' in the 
preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its instances 
for further explanation.  Note that #$interArgFormat4-4 is one of several 
\"degenerate-case\" inter-argument format predicates, in which the specified 
condition and the corresponding format constraint both have to do with the 
_same_ argument-place of a given predicate.")
(comment GeneralDataMicrotheory "The collection of all instances of #$DataMicrotheory which are also instances of #$GeneralMicrotheory.  Because these are instances of #$GeneralMicrotheory, they have sets of rules that are used in many contexts.  Because they are instances of #$DataMicrotheory they have assertions about (normally #$PartiallyTangible) #$Individuals.  Unless the rules are about these #$Individuals, they should probably be separated out into

a more generic #$GeneralMicrotheory that could be used with different data, for example in a different century or in a fictional world.")
(comment Iodine "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of iodine in stuffeous form.")
(comment Artifact-Intangible "A specialization of both #$IntangibleIndividual and #$Artifact-Generic.  Each instance of #$Artifact-Intangible is an intangible thing intentionally created by an agent or agents.  Important specializations of #$Artifact-Intangible include #$ComputerLanguage, #$ConceptualWork, and #$Agreement.")
(comment FillingAToothCavity "Replacing decayed tooth material with an artificial substance, to prevent further tissue loss.")
(comment SkiArea "A collection of named, local geographic regions.  An element of #$SkiArea is located in a (partially, at least) developed mountainous area, where slopes are cleared for skiing and snowboarding, with lodges, ski-lifts, and other accompanying skiing-related facilities and businesses nearby.  Some #$SkiAreas include one or more entire towns. Examples:  Snowmass, Taos Ski Valley, Buttermilk, St. Moritz, Malbun.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (RightObjectOfPairFn NinthRib) Tuberosity) "")
(comment BallisticMissile-Minuteman1 "The collection of all Minuteman I missiles.

  The Minuteman I was an early type

 of #$MinutemanBallisticMissile developed

 by the U.S. during the early 1960's.")
(comment Grebe-Western "A swimming and diving bird that has a complex mating dance.  Found near calm waters.")
(comment UnitOfMeasureTypeBySystem "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$UnitOfMeasure whose instances are all of the same system.")
(comment Mixing "A collection of events: an instance of #$CreationTypeByMethod and a specialization of #$PhysicalCreationEvent, #$Incorporation-Physical and #$MaterialHandling. In each instance of this collection two or more substances are combined to form a #$Mixture. Notable specializations include #$Diluting and #$Aerosolizing.")
(comment TrafficJam "The type of traffic in which there are so many cars (or other vehicles) that the drivers are often stopped longer than they are moving")
(comment AutomobileBoatRack "This is the collection of boat racks which allow a person to attach

a canoe, kayak, or other small boat to the roof of their car.")
(comment GroundToGroundCommunicationsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile centers on           communication between ground-based platforms.")
(disjointWith Agent-Generic Place-NonAgent)
(comment typeBehaviorCapability "(#$typeBehaviorCapability COL SIT-TYPE ROLE SCALAR) means
that instances of COL are typically capable of playing the role ROLE
in situations of type, SITTYPE, at a level of aptitude LEVEL or
higher.  Note that this does not refer to the average \"aptitude\"
level but the level of aptitude above which nearly all instances (i.e., the
default assumption) of the collection will play the role. This is a version of #$typeBehaviorCapable that admits
of gradations.  Also compare with #$behaviorCapable and
#$behaviorCapability.")
(comment PasswordFile "#$PasswordFile is the collection of files used to store computer passwords.")
(disjointWith Gear LandTransportationWheel)
(comment SmallAnimalVeterinarian "Instances are veterinarians that specialize in the care of small animals kept as pets, such as dogs, cats and the occasional hamster or rat.")
(comment Membrane "This is the collection of membranes. It includes membranes which

grow as parts of living organisms (#$Membrane-Biological), as well as artifacts such as drum heads and

the plastic membranes used in osmotic laboratory procedures.")
(comment hasImmunityWithRespectToDisease "(#$hasImmunityWithRespectToDisease ORG IMM DISEASE-TYPE) means that ORG, an instance

of #$Organism-Whole, has the type of immunity IMM, an #$ImmunityAttribute,

with respect to diseases of the type DISEASE-TYPE. Org is also said

insusceptible to diseases of the type DISEASE-TYPE. See

#$immuneWithRespectToDisease. Contrast with #$hasImmunityWithRespectToOrg and

#$immuneWithRespectToPathogen.")
(comment Logician "The collection of all people whose work involves the study and development of formal logic.  Note that most logicians consider themselves either philosophers or mathematicians.")
(comment physicalCopies "(#$physicalCopies COPY1 COPY2) means that COPY1 and COPY2 are numerically distinct physical copies of the same thing or one is a copy of the other.  If they are information bearing objects, then they contained and conveyed the same information as the original at the time the copy was made. COPY1 and COPY2 are not necessarily physically (type) identical but might have changed in different ways.  For example, records or photographs may be scratched, a copy of a book may be missing a page, identical twins have developed differently so may be more or less similar in appearance at the present moment, etc.")
(disjointWith Facility-Construct Gateway)
(comment Bodybuilder "The collection of #$Athletes who lift weights in order to increase their muscle mass and who may participate in #$WeightliftingSportsEvents.")
(comment chainEnds-Set "(#$chainEnds-Set CORD {A,B}) means that A and B are the two ends of CORD, this predicate relates a chain to the set, or sets when the chain changes length over time, containing its chain ends.")
(comment IBTWithFullTextOfIBTTypeFn "#$IBTWithFullTextOfIBTTypeFn takes as argument any spec of #$InformationStore and returns the collection of IBTs that contain the full written text of any instance of that spec.  For example, (#$IBTWithFullTextOfIBTTypeFn #$TravelGuide) returns the collection of IBTs containing the full text of travel guides.")
(comment CruiseMissile-CSSN1 "A type of cruise missile.  According to the CSIS source document 'Creeping Proliferation Could Mean a Paradigm Shift

          in the Cost of War and Terrorism', Egypt is in possession of many of these cruise missiles and may use the missiles as delivery vehicles for weapons of mass destruction.")
(comment ProcaineHydrochloride "The chemical compound which is used as an anesthetic.")
(comment OverheadExpenseAccount "An account for the money which goes to pay for overhead expenses")
(disjointWith Train-TransportationDevice ArmoredVehicle-Light)
(comment ServiceEconomicSector "The collection of all groups of enterprises in which the enterprises in each such group define themselves primarily as providers of some type of service (see #$ServiceEvent), as opposed to devices or commodities, and each such group together forms the major service sector for that region.  An example would be the service sector of #$France.")
(comment nationalBudgetExpenditures "The total budget expenditures of a geopolitical entity. This is the planned amount of money that will be spent during the following #$CalendarYear. See also #$nationalBudgetRevenues. ")
(comment internalCodeTransducer-FunctionalRole "(#$internalCodeTransducer-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT)
means that AGENT is responsible for changing the encoding of instances
of #$InformationBearingObject originating within SYSTEM to a form
suitable for transmission and dissemination outside SYSTEM.")
(comment Rufiyaa-Maldives "Major unit of currency of #$Maldives")
(comment ApplicationLayerProtocol "The collection of all network protocols that implement an application layer. A user interacts directly with an instance of #$ApplicationLayerProtocol,  so it is the top layer in a #$NetworkProtocolStack. In an instance of #$OpenSystemInterconnectionReferenceModel, an #$ApplicationLayerProtocol communicates  with a #$PresentationLayerProtocol. In most other models, it communicates with a #$TransportLayerProtocol.")
(comment TollPathway "A collection; a specialization of #$Path-Customary.  An instance of #$TollPathway is a path for the privilege of traversing which a fee must be paid.")
(comment RelationExistsAllFn "The predicate #$relationExistsAll states that for every instance of a collection, some other term exists in a certain relationship.  An arbitrary such term is a function of the instance, the predicate, the collection, and the type of the other term.  (#$RelationExistsAllFn TERM PRED DEP-COL INDEP-COL) allows one to denote this `arbitrary such term that so exists' in a named fashion.")
(comment SesamePlant "Individual sesame plants.")
(comment M1A2AbramsTank "A newer version of #$M1A1AbramsTank.")
(disjointWith CloudOfH2O DrugSubstance)
(comment YZCrossSectionFn "This function maps three-dimensional objects to the arbitrarily thin slice of the object that defines a yz-cross section of the object as determined by the object's intrinsic axes.  See also #$yzCrossSection and #$IntrinsicAxisOfObjects.")
(comment Garden "A small plot of cultivated land within a yard used to grow plants, especially vegetables and flowers")
(comment MardiGras "Literally, `Fat Tuesday', also known in English as Shrove Tuesday. In the Christian liturgical year, each Mardi Gras is the Tuesday before  Ash Wednesday, which is the beginning of Lent, the 40-day period of fasting and penitence leading up to Easter.  Mardi Gras is thus celebrated as a time of ribald release and excess before the more serious Lenten period.  While Mardi Gras derives much of its significance from being the day before the beginning of Lent, in most countries it is not celebrated as a #$ReligiousHoliday.")
(comment PornographicMaterial-Legal "This is the subcollection of #$PornographicMaterial possession of which is

not explicitly illegal. See the comment on #$PornographicMaterial-Illegal.")
(comment Mitochondrion "An organelle found in all eukaryotic cells, that provides for an efficient apparatus for the production of ATP.")
(comment sponsorOfEvent "(#$sponsorOfEvent ?EVENT ?SPONSOR) means that Agent ?SPONSOR plays a sponsorship role in the #$SocialOccurrence ?EVENT.  Sponsorship roles include providing funding, materials, incentive, or other support for ?EVENT and its participants.  For example, (#$sponsorOfEvent AmericanAssociationfortheAdvancementOfScienceConference1998 SubaruOfAmericaInc) ")
(comment documentsRequiredOnTour "(#$documentsRequiredOnTour TOUR PERSON CREDENTIAL) means that PERSON is required to have some instance of CREDENTIAL issued to him/her in order to participate in the instance of #$TravelTour TOUR.")
(comment DecontaminationProcedure-Animal "The collection of all activities wherein one tries to decomtaminate #$NonPersonAniamls that have been exposed to something #$Toxic.")
(comment interArg5ResultGenls "A ternary #$MetaRelation predicate for stating that a certain kind of complex, partly #$genls based relationship holds between the fifth argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned. (#$interArg2ResultGenls FUNC INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the fifth argument to FUNC, then -- regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be -- the value (if any) of that function for those arguments is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is: if INST is a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 INST ...) = VALUE, then VALUE is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  Note that, unlike (e.g.) the #$InterArgTypePredicates, #$interArg5ResultGenls _cannot_ be used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on functions.  See also the similar but more flexible quaternary #$interArgResultGenl.")
(comment Serial-MediaProduct "This is the collection of all #$MediaProducts which tell a #$Narrative in more than one episode.  Subcollections include serial radio programs, serial movie shorts, serial animated cartoon film shorts, most #$SoapOperas, and other serial TV shows (#$TVSeriesProduct).  This collection does not include #$ConceptualWorks which are instantiated in print.")
(disjointWith InformationBearingThing PuttingSomethingSomewhere)
(comment AttackByComputerOperationTypeByDegreeOfSecrecy "#$AttackByComputerOperationTypeByDegreeOfSecrecy is a subset of #$AttackByComputerOperationType. Every instance of this collection is a collection of attacks whose degree of secrecy is significantly related to their potenital success. For example, some attacks must be conducted in such a way that discourages detection of the attack as the attack is occurring.  Obviously, all 'sensible' electronic attacks will be conducted by the attacker in a manner that is intended to disguise the source of the attack, who conducted it, and so on. What makes an electronic attack 'covert' is the additional principle stated above. For an attack that is 'highly covert', see #$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Espionage.")
(disjointWith LighterThanAirCraft Parachute)
(comment LunarPlain "The collection of small #$Plain-Topographicals which appear on the #$MoonOfEarth.")
(disjointWith Collision LookingForAThingOrTypeOfThing)
(comment negativelyDependsOn "(#$negativelyDependsOn ?SET ?DEP-SLOT ?INDEP-SLOT) means that the values for ?DEP-SLOT are negatively dependent on the values for ?INDEP-SLOT, for elements of ?SET.  In other words, if the value for ?INDEP-SLOT is high for an arbitrary element of ?SET, then the value for ?DEP-SLOT will be low (and vice versa: high if low). Unlike the more general #$negativelyCorrelatedWith, #$negativelyDependsOn means that there is some causal link from ?INDEP-SLOT affecting ?DEP-SLOT.")
(comment ScubaJacket "The collection of scuba jacket.")
(comment ZPU-4MachineGun "A large machine gun used for air defense.")
(comment Aluminum "A piece (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of aluminum; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment ProfessionalSportsTeam "The collection of #$SportsTeams whose members are paid a salary for being a member of that team. Typically, but not always, a member of a #$ProfessionalSportsTeam does not hold other jobs while he is a member of the team.")
(disjointWith LiquidTangibleThing Molecule)
(comment ExtractingNaturalGas "Extracting natural gas from the earth; one of the           #$industryActivityTypes of a #$GasIndustry.")
(disjointWith Incorporation-Physical Talking)
(comment Photosynthesis-Generic "A collection of events that include the organized capture of light energy and its transformation into usable chemical energy in the synthesis of organic compounds.  This collection includes #$Photosynthesis-Plant and #$Photosynthesis-Bacterial.")
(comment Colon-BodyPart "The collection of all colons, the major parts of large intestines in certain animals and in human beings. A member of #$Colon-BodyPart is the portion of a #$LargeIntestine which extends from the #$Cecum to the #$Rectum.")
(disjointWith Rubber Metal)
(comment populationGrowthRate "(#$populationGrowthRate PLACE NUM) means that the population of PLACE is growing at the rate of NUM per year. This growth includes new births as well as immigrants.")
(comment Disability "This is the collection of #$PhysiologicalConditionTypes which are defined in terms of an inability to perform a normal function.  For instance, there are many causes of #$Deafness, including several diseases, so #$Deafness itself is not an #$AilmentCondition, but a condition of impaired hearing that may result from an ailment.")
(comment nonSingular-Generic "This predicate is a generalization over the #$SpeechPartPredicates that do not express singular number: the spec-preds of #$plural-Generic and #$massNumber-Generic (q.v.).  This predicate is #$notAssertible, since it will always cash out as an assertion on a more specialized predicate")
(comment RaiseTariffs "The collection of events where one state raises the economic tariffs on imports.")
(comment KlebsiellaPneumoniae "A collection of #$Bacterium in the #$MoneranKingdom.  This #$BiologicalSpecies is present in the resiratory tract
and feces of 5% of normal individuals.  It can produce #$UrinaryTractInfection or #$Pneumonia.")
(disjointWith MovingImage StillImage)
(comment backupMediumFor "(#$backupMediumFor BACKUP COMPSYS) means that BACKUP is a backup for computational system COMPSYS.")
(comment MDMA-TheStimulant "methylene dioxymethamphetamine: an amphetamine derivative, C11H15NO2, that reduces inhibitions and that was used in psychotherapy until it was banned in the U.S. in 1985. It is currently used typically by young adults and adolescents at clubs, raves, and rock concerts.")
(comment MilitaryWithdrawal "The collection of all those instances of #$MilitaryOperation whose primary purpose is the withdrawal of some military personnel from a region. This includes, but is not restricted to, cases in which forces are withdrawn from a region that they have previously occupied in the course of some element of #$MilitaryAttack.")
(comment Foam "The collection of all foam.  Foam is a lightweight, opaque  semi-solid substance.")
(comment FalxCerebelli "The collection of all falx cerebellii.  An instance of #$FalxCerebelli is the part of the #$DuraMater which separates the two hemispheres of the Cerebellum.  It is a unique part of a #$Brain.")
(comment SportingGoodsManufacturer "The collection of all companies that manufacture and sell at least some instances of #$SportingGoodsMarketCategory like footballs, skis, athletic shoes etc.")
(disjointWith ConferenceSeminar GraduateSeminarSeries)
(comment MultiLevelMarketingOrganization "The collection of businesses that engage 

in #$MultiLevelMarketingActivity.")
(comment Chasm-Topographical "A deep cleft in the surface of a planet.")
(comment ControllableAutonomousActionType "The collection of all types of actions that are #$doneBy an #$Animal which are often done automatically, but could also be intentionally #$performedBy the animal.")
(comment Bazooka-B40 "The collection of B40 #$Bazookas.  This weapon fired  rocket-propelled grenades.  It was Soviet-made and used by the NVA in the  Vietnam War.")
(disjointWith Density ElectricalResistance)
(comment ObtainOperationalControl "A specialization of both #$GainingUserRights and #$PurposefulAction.  In each instance of #$ObtainOperationalControl, a military unit gains user rights over some resource.")
(disjointWith Dock BusStop)
(comment AnalogyCorrespondenceFn "(#$AnalogyCorrespondenceFn STRING) denotes the #$AnalogyCorrespondence which is referred to by the name STRING in the MAC-FAC analogy reasoning system.  See also #$hasCorrespondence, #$correspondenceBetween, and #$commonalities.")
(comment MonologueInDramaticPerformance "A #$MonologueInDramaticPerformance is a long speech by one character            in a play or film.")
(comment inputIndicatedProduct "(#$inputIndicatedProduct PRSN PROD-TYPE) means that because of customer input to the Cyc ProductAdvisor about her preferences of what type of item to purchase for the #$Person PRSN, it can be inferred that #$ProductType PROD-TYPE is positively indicated for PRSN. In contrast to (#$explicitlyIndicatedProduct PRSN STATED-TYPE), which represents a customer's stated preference for #$ProductType STATED-TYPE, (#$inputIndicatedProduct PRSN PROD-TYPE) represents a lesser degree of positive indication because PROD-TYPE is derived via #$genls from STATED-TYPE. For example, suppose a customer using the Cyc Product Advisor gives a positive response to a question of the form, 'Are you interested in toys?'. This response would result in the following assertion being provably true in #$TheSessionMt, (#$inputIndicatedProduct #$TheRecipient #$ActionFigure-Toy), because (#$genls #$ActionFigure-Toy #$Toy). Assertions using this predicate indicate a weaker degree of suitability than assertions using #$explicitlyIndicatedProduct. For example, from the fact that the customer states that she is interested in buying a #$Toy, it should follow that all subcollections of #$Toy have some positive indication, but she might not be interested in #$ActionFigure-Toy. So the degree to which #$ActionFigure-Toy is indicated should be less than the degree to which #$Toy is indicated.")
(disjointWith Running Walking-Generic)
(comment MaintenanceFn "This function can be used to denote the set of events in which an agent maintains something.")
(disjointWith Street-Residential Highway)
(comment groupResidesInRegion "(#$groupResidesInRegion GROUP REGION) means that the group of animals GROUP 
resides in the region REGION. In general, that means that all members of GROUP also reside
in REGION.")
(comment schoolSymbolName-Female "(#$schoolSymbolName-Female SCHOOL STRING) means that

  STRING is a common way to refer to all-women SCHOOL-affiliated

  #$SportsTeams, clubs, and other student organizations. 

   Accordingly, instances of STRING will be pluralized (e.g.

    'the Ohio State Lady Buckeyes').")
(comment Holonet "The collection of #$WebHosting events sold by #$InformationAccessTechnologiesInc as part of their 'Holonet' service.")
(comment Trimethobenzamide "The chemical compound which is an anti-emetic.")
(comment I-TheLetter "The letter I of the alphabet.  This is 'I' (or 'i') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.   As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterI and #$LatinSmallLetterI.")
(comment Dollar-Jamaica "Major unit of currency of #$Jamaica")
(comment BotanicalCellWall "Cell walls are the covering of botanical cells, external to the plasma membrane.  They are composed primarily of cellulose microfibrils, are somewhat rigid (but elastic due to their hydrated nature), and experience pressure from the cell contents. these characteristics provide some mechanical support to non-woody plant tissues.")
(disjointWith Electron Neutrino)
(comment PolitenessOfSpeech "Politeness attributes apply to individual word senses of words or phrases.")
(comment Tondar-68-Missile "A type of surface-to-surface missile.  According to the CSIS source document 'Creeping Proliferation Could Mean a Paradigm Shift

          in the Cost of War and Terrorism', Egypt developed and produced these missiles with Chinese assistance.  The two countries are in possession of many of these missiles and may use them as delivery vehicles for weapons of mass destruction.")
(comment flammabilityOfObject "(#$flammabilityOfObject SUBST DEGREE) means that the tangible SUBST has this DEGREE of #$Flammability.  A higher value of DEGREE describes objects that catch fire and burn more quickly and easily than those with a lower value.")
(comment HostsOnSubnetwork "The collection of groups of computers, 

where each group is a subnetwork of computers (computers are grouped by IPAddresses into a subnetwork on 

an internetwork).")
(comment hasAccess "(#$hasAccess AGENT OBJ) means that AGENT has access to the individual OBJ.  This predicate is true of AGENT and OBJ whenever AGENT can access OBJ.  It should be construed broadly enough to include the following senses of access: the access one has to physical objects in one's immediate vicinity or to a place the person may go to, the access to information or files one may gain with a remote computer connection, and the sort of access one has to other people (e.g. access to a telephone operator by picking up the phone).  Having access generally precedes possessing or controlling an object.  Note that AGENT may have access to OBJ even though he is not permitted to; that is, (#$hasAccess AGENT OBJ) may be true even though (#$not (#$groupMembers (#$AccessorFn OBJ) AGENT)).")
(comment Nitrococcus-Genus "A collection of all #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$BiologicalGenus #$Nitrococcus-Genus.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are CoccusBacterium that occur singly or in pairsss.  These are #$MotileBacterium eith one or two flagella; they are #$AreobicBacterium and oxidize nitrite to nitrate.  They are also obligate chemolithotrophs.")
(comment NosocomialInfection "A specialization of #$Infection.  Each instance of #$NosocomialInfection is an infection originating in the environment of some medical treatment facility (for example, a hospital).")
(comment ProperNamedObjectFn "The expression (#$ProperNamedObjectFn STRING TYPES ALTERNATES) denotes an object which has the proper name STRING, is instance of each collection in the list TYPES, and can also be called by any of the strings in ALTERNATES.  For example, (#$ProperNamedObjectFn \"Peter Frampton\" (#$TheList #$Musician) (#$TheList \"Frampton\")).")
(disjointWith HangGlider UnmannedAircraft)
(comment CelestialRegion "A collection of spatial regions of the celestial sphere.  Each element of #$CelestialRegion is a region of the sky that may be represented on a map of the sky as seen from a frame of reference which is fixed with respect to the stars.  In this sense, #$CelestialRegion is the 'sky' analog of #$GeographicalRegion.  A #$CelestialRegion may be intangible.")
(comment SwingAroundOnCord "The collection of all events in which an object (as #$primaryObjectMoving and #$supportedObject)  is swung around a central pivot, which it is attached to a via a cord (a #$CordlikeObject that plays the roles: #$deviceUsed, #$constrainingObject, #$objectMoving, and #$supportingObject).  This is a specialization of #$ConstrainedMultirevolutionRotation.")
(comment Stroke-PhysiologicalCondition "The collection of physiological conditions in which a blood vessel in the brain bursts or is plugged up, causing unconsciousness, paralysis, etc.")
(comment GelatinousEdema "A subset of #$AilmentCondition. In each case of #$GelatinousEdema, the affected animal has excessive fluid in its tissue .")
(comment InternationalCodeOfConductGoal "The attribute characterizing goals which are concerned with making, maintaining, and enforcing international agreements.")
(comment AssaultRifle-AK47 "The collection of all AK47 assault rifles, a type of assault rifle originally manufactured in Russia.")
(comment DataEntryPerson "Someone who does data entry into a computer as his/her job.")
(comment TransportOperationsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units that deal with any dimension           of transport operations.")
(comment instantiationOfWork "A #$BinaryPredicate which relates instances of #$InformationStore to instances of #$DevisedPracticeOrWork. (#$instantiationOfWork IS WORK) means that IS is an instantiation of the #$DevisedPracticeOrWork, WORK. Roughly, this is the relation that holds between any event or object (for instance, a particular copy of the novel _Moby_Dick_) and any #$DevisedPracticeOrWork \"embodied\" in this event or object (for instance, the novel _Moby_Dick_ considered qua artistic creation and independently of any printed copy of it). Examples of pairs to which this predicate applies include; any #$BookCopy and any #$Book-CW of which it is a copy; any #$GameEvent and any #$Game which the #$GameEvent is the playing of; any #$Medal-Physical and any #$AwardPractice (like an #$OlympicGoldMedal) which that #$Medal-Physical embodies. See also #$instantiationOfAIT.")
(disjointWith FreeSheet RealEstate)
(comment Terbium "The collection of all pieces (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of terbium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment DirectionDenotingFunction "The instances of this collection are functions which return as
results directions in a specified frame of reference.  It includes
both functions which take as arguments Cyc system numbers, i.e.,
HorizontalBearingFn and AltitudeFn, functions that take as
arguments #$HexalateralObjects, and functions that take as arguments
#$GeographicalRegions, the only requirement being that they return
directions or directional intervals in a reference frame.")
(comment USMarineSquad "#$USMarineSquad is the collection of all squads within the #$UnitedStatesMarineCorps which have the echelon of #$Squad-UnitDesignation.  They are usually composed of three fire squads and a staff sergeant or a sergeant in command.")
(comment ComputerThread "The collection of acts in which a computer executes a 'thread',
as defined in standard computer parlance, which is 'A portion of a process
that can run independently of and concurrently with other portions of
the process.'  A process might have only one thread, in which case it is
the entire portion.")
(disjointWith SeasonOfYear ImmediateWeatherProcess)
(comment Game "A specialization of #$DevisedStructuredActivity.  Each instance of #$Game is an abstraction of a game that is played according to a semi-rigid set of rules. Each instance includes both the rules (see #$GameRulesFn) and a specification of any physical components required for play (instances of #$GameBoard, #$Ball, etc.).  Neither #$Events of playing games (instances of #$PlayingAGame) nor any physical components required for play (e.g. #$GameBoards) are instances of #$Game.")
(comment keConsiderationPreds "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate (q.v.) and specialization of #$keRelevantPreds (q.v.) that relates a collection to a binary predicate.  (#$keConsiderationPreds COL BINPRED) means that for any reified instance INST of COL, it should be determined whether there is any thing THING such that BINPRED holds between THING and INST, and if so it is suggested that one consider asserting (BINPRED THING INST) in the Cyc Knowledge Base.  See also #$keConsiderationInverse.")
(comment EnglishPrefix "The set of lexical items which may attach to the beginning of
an English word. Example: 'un', as in 'unhappy'.")
(comment genericTestPred "Prototypical instance of #$BinaryPredicate, to be used for
testing purposes")
(comment TakingASample "The collection of events in which a portion of some substance which is to be tested is separated out from the larger mass of it.")
(comment preconditionFor-Events "The predicate #$preconditionFor-Events is used to state that one event is a necessary precondition for another.  (#$preconditionFor-Events COND OUTCOME) means that the #$Event COND precedes and is a necessary condition for the #$Event OUTCOME.")
(comment Smurf-CartoonCharacter "The collection of all Smurfs, cute blue cartoon charaters. Instances feature prominently in #$TheSmurfs-TheTVShow.")
(comment Spirillales-Order "A collection of #$Bacterium classified in the #$Spirillales-Order.  It includes the #$Vibrionaceae-Family.")
(comment collateral "The predicate used to relate a loan to the property pledged as security for its repayment, agreeing that the lender has the right to sell it for the purpose of liquidating the debt if the #$borrower fails to repay it at maturity.")
(comment PracticingFn "(#$PracticingFn SKILL-TYPE) denotes the collection of actions in which an agent practices the skilled activity SKILL-TYPE.  For example, (#$PracticingFn #$Juggling) is the collection of actions of practicing juggling.")
(comment portForProgramType "A predicate relating collections of #$ComputerProgram-CW with the port numbers (and transport layer protocols) with which they are conventionally associated. (#$portForProgramType PROGTYPE PROTOCOL PORT) means that, as a matter of custom, running copies of instances of PROGTYPE run on PORT on computers, listening for packets that conform to PROTOCOL.  For example, (#$portForProgramType #$FTPServerProgram #$TransmissionControlProtocol 21) means that copies of FTP programs usually run on TCP port 21. See also #$portForProgram.")
(comment ImipenemCilastatinSodium "A chemical compound which is used in injectable antibiotic products.")
(comment PhysicalLayerProtocol "The collection of all network protocols that implement a physical layer. An instance of #$PhysicalLayerProtocol is the  connector between nodes in a network,  or the medium through which data physically travels.")
(comment formsBorderBetween "A #$SpatialPredicate that relates a pair of bordering spatial 
things to parts of the border that separates them. 
(#$formsBorderBetween BORDER REG1 REG2) means that BORDER 
constitutes at least part of the border between REG1 and REG2.  
BORDER may be a surface separating two regions of space, or a 
curve separating two regions of a surface.  REG1 and REG2 may 
be physical objects, geographical regions, or intangible spatial
lines or regions.  Note that BORDER need not constitute the entire 
border between REG1 and REG2.  By contrast, the more specialized
predicate #$borderBetweenRegions relates a pair of 
#$GeographicalRegions to their entire shared border; see also
the corresponding function #$BorderBetweenFn.")
(comment On-linePromotionalOccurrence "This is the collection of instances of PromotionalOccurrence that occur on-line.")
(comment Emirate-Geopolitical "A kind of #$SystemOfGovernment, and hence a specialization of #$AttributeValue. Characteristic of certain kinds of Arab states and domestic political arrangements.")
(comment vulnerableToType "(#$vulnerableToType COLLECTION OBJECT SIT-TYPE) means that instances of COLLECTION are able to inflict harm of kind SIT-TYPE on OBJECT.")
(comment DataInjection "This is the collection of all events in which new data enters a computer network.")
(comment WearableConveyance "Instances are instruments in movement events which are 'worn' by an #$objectMoving in the #$MovementEvent.  Positive exemplars include ice skates, shoes, skiis, snow shoes, wings strapped on to a persons body.  We have not imagined any cases in which a #$WearableConveyance would be an instrument worn by a non-person, or at least a non-animal in some movment event.  The motivation for creating this collection was that it seemed strange to have collections like (#$TransportViaFn (#$PairFn #$IceSkate)) or assertions like (#$transporter JoeWalking SneakerInstance01).")
(comment mayAuthorize "The agent ARG1 may authorize (grant the authority for) the agent ARG2 to perform instances of the action type ARG3.")
(comment subjectOfReport-Prop "(#$subjectOfReport-Prop REPORT PROP) means that PROP describes the main focus and topic of REPORT.")
(comment PartialOrdering "The collection of all those #$MathematicalOrderings ORDER in which the ordering relation R is a reflexive, transitive and antisymmetric relation on the #$baseSet S of ORDER.  R is reflexive on S if and only if for each X in S, R(X X).  R is transitive on S if and only if for each X, Y and Z in S, R(X Y) and R(Y Z) imply R(X Z).  R is antisymmetric on S if and only if for each X and Y in S, R(X Y) and R(Y X) imply X = Y.  For example, if you take a set of #$Lists and take the #$subLists relation restricted to this set, then you have a #$PartialOrdering because the #$subLists relation is reflexive, transitive and antisymmetric.  Since the ordering relation in each #$PartialOrdering is reflexive and transitive, the collection #$PartialOrdering is a subcollection of #$QuasiOrdering. Subcollections of #$PartialOrdering include #$TreeOrdering, #$TotalOrdering and #$Lattice-LatticeTheoretic.  If you want a #$MathematicalOrdering in which the ordering relation is irreflexive, see #$PartialOrdering-Strict.")
(comment AutomaticFirearm-GasOperated "The collection of all #$AutomaticFirearms whose automatic chambering mechanism is powered by pressurized gasses from discharged ammunition.")
(comment SuburbanPopulationDensity "The population density of suburban areas.")
(disjointWith Fishing AcademicTesting)
(comment LentiformNucleus "The collection of all lentiform nuclei.  An individual #$LentiformNucleus (or 'lenticular nucleus') is a #$BasalNucleus which is a unique part of a #$CerebralHemisphere.")
(comment PageInAPublishedEdition-PIT "Each instance of this collection is the propositional informational content of some 'page' in an instance of #$PublishedEdition-PIT.  This concept of 'page' differs from the idea of a 'page' as a group of character strings and also from the idea of a collection of physical pages in the physical instances of a particular edition, i.e., the idea of a 'page' as a #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType.")
(comment AssessingEnemyPlan "A collection of processes, each of which is related by the
#$subEvents relation to some instance of #$AssessingEnemyCOA.  In each
instance of #$AssessingEnemyPlan, information is evaluated with the purpose of 
determining the enemy's plan for action.")
(comment OpticalMarketCategory "The market category for prescription and non-prescription retail optical supplies, such as eyeglasses, contact lenses, and the accessories needed to maintain them")
(comment ElectricalGround "The common reference point for electrical voltages.")
(comment HusbandryFn "This function can be used to denote the set of events in which an agent raises/grows some kind of animal or plant.")
(comment FoundingAnOrganization "The collection of all events in which some instance of
#$Organization is formally established.")
(disjointWith Indivisible Issue)
(comment indicatedDrug "(#$indicatedDrug AILMENT DRUG) means that DRUG is a standard type of #$DrugSubstance that is used to treat the kind of #$AilmentCondition AILMENT.")
(comment Play-Musical-CW "The collection of plays [#$Play-CW] intended to be instantiated in musical #$PlayPerformances [see #$PlayPerformance-Musical].")
(comment Mortar-120mm-Standard "A mortar which fires 120mm shells.")
(comment VeterinaryMedication "Medicines prepared for administration to animals - usually pets or livestock.  The drug(s) contained in such medications may be the same drugs used on people (particularly when the type of animal they are intended for is a mammal), but veterinary medications often differ from human medications in mode of delivery or purity. ")
(comment OpaqueCovering "The set of coverings which are opaque to visible light, and hence protect against the covered object from being seen")
(comment fullLexEntry "(#$fullLexEntry ?String ?AVM) states that the morphological
string variant ?String of some instance of #$LexicalWord is
represented fully, for unification purposes, by the hl-level
avm (or 'attribute-value-matrix') ?AVM. The underlying HL
implementation of #$fullLexEntry is responsible for performing a
morphological analysis of ?String to determine the correct
instance of #$LexicalWord. (#$fullLexEntry ?String ?Dag) works by
gathering together all partial lexical entries of ?String (via
#$partialLexEntry) and unifying (via unify) those partial
entries that belong together.")
(comment HangGlider "The collection of all #$Gliders from which the pilot is suspended below and steers by shifting forward and back and side to side.")
(comment CytidineTriphosphate "A collection of nucleotides that are activated precursors to

the synthesis of RNA.  They contain #$Cytosine-Base linked to

#$Ribose and three phosphates.")
(disjointWith Boiling ShreddingEvent)
(comment ManufacturingEconomicSector "The collection of all localized groups of manufacturing enterprises that each together (each group) forms the major manufacturing economic sector for the region.  An example instance would be the Manufacturing sector of #$Switzerland, or the worldwide manufacturing sector.")
(comment DomainName "A string of symbols that uniquely identifies a web server. Such strings are usually descriptive of the nature of the site and are used as a mnemonic aid in lieu of the actual numerical IP address of the server.")
(comment NuclearAircraftCarrier "The collection of #$AircraftCarriers which are nuclear-powered.")
(disjointWith SolidTangibleThing SemiSolidTangibleThing)
(comment (ListOfTypeFn PersonTypeByOccupation) "A specialization of #$List.  Each instance of (#$ListOfTypeFn #$PersonTypeByOccupation) is a list each of whose members (see the predicate #$listMembers) is an instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation.  An example of such a list is (#$TheList #$Scientist #$Doctor-Medical #$Soldier).")
(comment Gold "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of gold.")
(disjointWith PhysicalSeries (GroupFn Artifact-Intangible))
(comment BoneRepair "A collection of events.  In each #$BoneRepair event, a broken bone is repaired.  Typically, each such event has a sub-event of `setting' the bone.  The whole #$BoneRepair event goes far beyond this, however, probably lasting for weeks or months, during which time the bone heals; if the bone belongs to a civilized human being, they may wear a cast or be in traction to immobilize the broken place until the bone heals.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (RightObjectOfPairFn FifthRib) Tuberosity) "")
(comment Casino-Organization "The collection of all #$Organizations that operate individual casinos.  For example, the group of individuals that operates The Mirage in Las Vegas (and no other casinos) is an instance of #$Casino-Organization, while #$DonaldTrump's organization that operates casinos in Las Vegas and Atlantic City is not an instance of this collection (that organization would be an instance of #$EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization). #$Casino-Organizations make #$Gambling activities available to their #$customers and other visitors.  Instances of #$Casino-Organization operate out of #$Casino-Objects.")
(comment LGM-30A-MinutemanMissile "The collection of all

 #$LGM-30A-MinutemanMissiles, the

 first type of #$MinutemanBallisticMissile.")
(comment Swinger-Sexual "#$Swinger-Sexual denotes the collection of all people that
engage freely in promiscuous sex.  Compare with #$Swinger.")
(comment EarPlug "The collection of ear plugs. This collection includes swimming ear plugs,

plugs designed to reduce noise, and any other sort of ear plug.")
(comment HeavyAssaultUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units trained and equipped for           conducting assaults with 'heavy' weapons and artillery accompanied           by heavily armored units.")
(comment GangBang-Voluntary "This is the collection of events in which a group of males has sex,

sequentially and/or simultaneously, with a single person, usually but

not always female. Unlike #$GangRape, these acts are voluntary on the

part of all the participants.")
(comment ReferenceWebSite "The collection of all #$WorldWideWebSites that provide a more or less non-speculative, \"fact-oriented,\" comprehensive         description of some knowledge domain.")
(disjointWith WindPoweredDevice LandTransportationWheel)
(comment FoggyClimateCycle "The collection of climate cycles that have frequent cases of fog.")
(comment Book-CW "A specialization of #$PropositionalConceptualWork and #$BookGeneric-CW. Each instance of #$Book-CW is an abstract work intended to be instantiated as a book of some sort.  Instances of #$Book-CW may be intended to be instantiated in any book format: hardcopy (see #$BookCopy), electronic, audio tape, etc.  Instances of #$Book-CW are usually also instances of #$TextualPCW, but some may be comprised of mainly non-propositional information, such as images.  Note that books with no propositional information (such as certain coloring books) would not be instances of this specialization of #$BookGeneric-CW.")
(disjointWith GovernmentOfCountry USStateGovernment)
(comment VeterinarianByAnimalType "Instances of #$VeterinarianByAnimalType represent types of veterinarians characterized by the kinds of animals they care for.")
(comment (WaveEmissionFn VisibleLight) "A collection of events; a specialization of #$EmittingAWave. Each instance of (#$WaveEmissionFn #$VisibleLight) is an event in which an instance of #$VisibleLight is emitted from some #$waveSource. Examples: the burning of a candle; the shining of a light bulb; a firefly's glowing. Almost every instance of (#$WaveEmissionFn #$VisibleLight) will also emit instances of types of #$ElectromagneticRadiation other than #$VisibleLight.")
(comment SharedNoteOnAssignedQueries "The collection of instances of #$SharedNote pertaining to 
assigned HPKB queries.  This collection and the notes in it
were created to providereviewers with a convenient way of quickly
pulling together all rules pertaining to the inference path of a given
query.")
(disjointWith HandRail Facility-Construct)
(comment objectFound-DefiniteDeRe "The expression `(#$objectFound-DefiniteDeRe SEARCH SEEKER OBJECT)' 

is a \"third party perspective\" way of saying that the SEEKER has found

the object for which s/he was searching in SEARCH.  The arg3 position

not opaque. This is because we often don't know exactly how the searcher

conceived of the OBJECT which in fact uniquely satisfies their #$searchCriterion-Definite.

Compare to #$objectFound-Definite.")
(comment Prom "Each #$Prom is a formal #$Dance-Party held toward the end of the academic year for a graduating high school class.")
(comment EndOfNucleotideChain "The collection of all ends of nucleotide chains.  Nucleotide chains are naturally oriented according to their component nucleotides.")
(comment IronOre "Magnetite ore - macroscopic quantities of the same.")
(comment CompositionMovement "The collection of all individual movements that are part of #$Multi-MovementCompositions.")
(comment Antidepressant "Drugs which treat psychic depression.")
(comment PersonnelExpenseAccount "An account for the money which goes to pay for the employees' salary")
(comment Mullah "Mullah derives from the old Arabian word MAWLA, which denotes either the slave or the master (cf. http://www.usc.edu/dept/MSA/reference/glossary/term.MAWLA.html). In the extended sense, it means a Muslim teacher of religion, who has interpretive authority over the Qur'an, Hadith and the other bodies of Islam's religious knowledge. Notice that due to the intertwined relationship of religion, politics and social policy in Islam, the religious rulings of a Mullah can have massive socio-political consequences.")
(comment resistanceToCorrosion "(#$resistanceToCorrosion OBJ DEGREE) means that the tangible object OBJ has the stated DEGREE of #$CorrosionResistance.  The higher DEGREE is, the less readily OBJ will corrode.")
(comment AgriculturalEconomicSector "The collection of all localized groups of enterprises that together (each such group of enterprises together) form major agricultural economic sectors of regions.  The enterprises in each such group define themselves as producers of agricultural commodities or as supporting such producers (see #$AgriculturalCommodity).")
(comment Peso-Chile "The unit of currency for Chile-AtPresent.")
(comment movementHasLeaders "(#$movementHasLeaders

MOVE AGT) means that AGT is considered to by

 the participants of the movement MOVE to be

 a leader of MOVE.  It is important to keep in mind

  the difference between a movement, which

  is a collection of activities, and an

  #$Organization, which engages in activities.

 The predicate used to identify the 

   leaders of an organization is #$hasLeaders.")
(comment DataLinkLayerProtocol "The collection of all network protocols that implement a data link layer. An instance of #$DataLinkLayerProtocol is responsible for getting  data to the next node in the route to the data's destination.")
(comment GasTanker "The collection of tanker ships intended to be used for
replenishment of gasoline to other ships.")
(comment BeanPlant "Individual bean plants.")
(comment MultipleRocketLauncherSystem-MLRS "The collection of American-made multiple rocket launchers, similar to the Soviet #$MultipleRocketLauncher-122mmMRL, but much newer.")
(comment linesInside-Skinlike "(#$linesInside-Skinlike SKIN OBJ) means that SKIN is a skin-like covering of the inside the hollow object, cavity, or inner surface OBJ.")
(comment ComputerClipartFile "The collection of small image files meant to be pasted into document files, primarily as decoration. Some #$ComputerClipartFiles contain multiple images, any one of which can be selected and pasted into another file. Clipart images are generally in the public domain, so they can be used freely without violating copyright laws.")
(comment FinancialAdvisor "A specialization of #$PersonWithOccupation and an instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation. Instances are people who professionally advise other people or institutions on their finances.")
(comment protectsAgainstType "(#$protectsAgainstType PROTECTOR TYPE) says that

   PROTECTOR can provide protection against TYPE, where

  TYPE can be a spec of #$PartiallyTangible (e.g., 

   (#$GroupFn #$Mosquito)) or a spec of #$Event

 (e.g., (#$BitingByFn #$Mosquito)).  The main point

 of this predicate is to help with parsing; with it,

 we can write general templates to handle sentences

  (roughly) of the form, \"X is protection against Y\"

 without requiring us to assume what kind of things X

 and Y are.  KErs should use one of the more specific

  spec preds, when possible.")
(comment LittleJohnnyJoke "This subset of #$Joke-CW includes as instances all and only jokes about the antics           of a young boy whose name is Johnny.")
(comment AtmosphericLayer "Instances are spherical layers of a planet's atmosphere, demarcated by distinctive properties of temperature and pressure. Most such regions terminate in instances of #$AtmosphericBoundaryLayer which, while considered proper parts of the layers below them, exhibit special thermal properties, e.g., #$Stratopause-PlanetEarth.")
(comment JargonFn "`(#$JargonFn PROFESSION)' denotes that #$FormalityOfSpeech
attribute of being jargon used by members of PROFESSION.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperationTypeByMethod "#$AttackByComputerOperationTypeByMethod is a subset of #$AttackByComputerOperationType. Every instance of #$AttackByComputerOperationTypeByMethod is a collection of attacks instances of which are executed by similar methods. Examples include #$AttackByComputerOperation-Distributed, 

 #$AttackByComputerOperation-LogicBomb, and #$AttackByComputerOperation-TimeBomb.")
(disjointWith SubwayStation LaneOfRoadway)
(comment Lacus-Lunar "The collection of topographical features where each element is a a small plain on Earth's moon.")
(comment Sound-BodyOfWater "a long, broad inlet of the ocean, generally parallel to the coast; a long passage connecting 2 large bodies of water or passing between an island and the mainland")
(disjointWith MaintainingSomething LookingForAThingOrTypeOfThing)
(comment WhiteTailedDeer "A specification of #$Deer.  Their scientific name is Odocoileus virginianus.")
(comment GeneralEducationalDevelopmentCredential "The collection of all 'GED' credentials. Instances are awarded based on a student's scores on a series of standardized tests, and not on the completion of a high school curriculum, but are considered equivalent to #$HighSchoolDiplomas for purposes of college admission, employment, etc.")
(comment SportsEquipment "Equipment, generally manufactured, which is used in the performance of some sport.  This does not include playing fields, terrain (snow, turf), or other sports-related surroundings (like pool water).  It does include skis, golf clubs, catcher's masks, bows and arrows, etc.")
(comment M4T6FloatingBridge "Military bridges which use aluminum pontoons for flotation.")
(comment Lanthanum "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of lanthanum; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.  This unit could probably just as well be called Lanthanum or LanthanumStuff")
(disjointWith ChemicalObject Solution)
(comment CaspianCountry "The collection of nation-states bordering the Caspian Sea.")
(comment HepaticDuct "The collection of all hepatic ducts. Each instance of this collection is an #$AnatomicalVessel allowing #$BileTheSecretion to flow from the #$Liver to the #$CommonBileDuct.")
(comment Wet "Perhaps a good definition for this in #$NaivePhysicsMt is : The directed surface of an object contains water.  cf. P. Hayes 'Naive Physics I : Ontology For Liquids'.")
(comment lengthOfObjectPerimeter "This predicate relates objects to their perimeter lengths. (#$lengthOfObjectPerimeter OBJ PERIM) means that the length of OBJ's perimeter is PERIM.  Compare this with #$objectPerimeter.")
(comment testCyclistsResponsible "(#$testCyclistsResponsible TEST CYCLIST) means that CYCLIST is responsible for, interested in implementing the kb functionality to support TEST.  For example, they should receive email when TEST stops working.  In some cases, the work of CYCLIST is to be reviewed by #$testCyclistsReviewer.  The best place to assert (#$testCyclistsResponsible TEST CYCLIST) is in the mt TEST. If you see a need to do otherwise, please tell #$BillJ.")
(disjointWith SeparationEvent ChangeOfStatusEvent)
(comment chemicallyBonded "(#$chemicallyBonded OBJ1 OBJ2) means that there is a chemical bond between OBJ1 and OBJ2, two instances of #$ChemicalObject. For example, in a particular molecule of carbon monoxide, the atom of #$Carbon and that of #$Oxygen that compose the molecule are in such relationship.")
(comment InLineSkate "The #$Collection of all #$RollerSkates having #$Wheels arranged in a straight line mid-sole.  The term 'Roller Blade' (TM) is the name for one company's brand of this product.")
(comment CharacterStringMode-ElectroMagnetic "A specialization of #$CharacterStringMode each 
  instance of which is the collection of all of the 
  electromagnetically encoded tokens of some particular 
  character-string.  Examples include the collection of 
  all such tokens (see #$CharacterStringToken-ElectroMagnetic)
  of the string '10101010'.")
(comment Phentermine "A stimulant similar to #$Amphetamines used as a weight-loss aid, often in combination with fenfluramine. The combination is commonly referred to as 'fen/phen'.")
(disjointWith MilitaryOffensiveOperation MilitaryWithdrawal)
(comment AerosolThePowder "#$AerosolThePowder is a collection of aerosols that are powder suspended in gas.")
(disjointWith InformationBearingThing (LiquidFn Water))
(comment GayAndLesbianMagazineSeries "The collection of all #$MagazineSeries which are intened primarily for the gay community.  These magazines deal mostly with issues surrounding the gay and lesbian lifestyle, and do not contain pornographic material.")
(comment TentoriumCerebelli "The collection of all portions of #$DuraMater named 'tentorium cerebelli'.  An instance of #$TentoriumCerebelli is the part of the #$DuraMater which extends between the #$Cerebellum from the #$Cerebrum.  It is a unique part of a head which supports the #$OccipitalLobes.")
(comment CodingSequence-MolecularSegment "The collection of all molecular subcomponents of #$PolynucleotideMolecules that instantiate nucleotide sequences that contribute to the coding sequence that specifies protein-specifying amino acid sequences. For example, the part of the nucleotide sequence of a #$DNAMolecule that specifies only the first two amino acids for a given protein type would be an instance of this collection.  Instances of #$CodingSequence-MolecularSegment need not contain the entire nucleotide sequence required to specify a protein type. This collection includes as specs both the coding sequences of bacterial DNA and bacterial RNA and the coding sequences of eucaryotic DNA and eucaryotic RNA, called #$Exon-MolecularSegments. See also #$Exon-GIS.")
(comment eventUndermines "If there is a known propositional precondition PRECON for
SIT2 such that SIT1 causes the negation of PRECON to become true, then
(#$eventUndermines SIT1 SIT2).")
(comment Declining-CommunicationAct "An acknowledgement of a communication in which the performer declines the content of the communication.")
(comment OrganizationRepresentative "#$OrganizationRepresentative is a specialization of #$PersonWithOccupation. Each instance of #$OrganizationRepresentative is officially sanctioned to act on behalf of an organization during interactions with agents who are not part of that organization.  Such a person will often be a member of the organization (e.g., an employee), but need not be.")
(comment naturalResourcesInRegion "(#$naturalResourcesInRegion REG RES) means that a non-trivial quantity of the natural resource RES is found in the region REG. Natural resources are useful materials supplied by nature. See also #$regionStoredResourceAmount.")
(comment Bazooka-M72 "The collection of all M72-series LAW #$Bazookas.  It is a  lightweight, self-contained, antiarmor weapon consisting of a rocket packed  in a launcher. It is man-portable, may be fired from either shoulder, and is  issued as a round of ammunition. It requires little from the user--only a  visual inspection and some operator maintenance. The launcher, which consists  of two tubes, one inside the other, serves as a watertight packing container  for the rocket and houses a percussion-type firing mechanism that activates  the rocket.")
(comment SpanningDevice "Dummy constant for workaround phase of Battlespace.")
(disjointWith Dock Graveyard)
(comment PublicRecordInfo "Facts, data and knowledge officially available to the public.")
(comment SleetProcess "A form of precipitation like raining ice.  It is not hard chunks like hail, and it is not completely liquid, like rain.  It is somewhere in between.")
(comment Absorbency "A collection of attributes; a subset of #$PhysicalAttribute.  Each element of #$Absorbency is an attribute describing how readily some substance absorbs some liquid.  Different levels of #$Absorbency may be indicated qualitatively (e.g., #$WillAbsorb), or relatively, using #$GenericValueFunctions. A particular thing's absorbency is indicated with the predicate #$absorbencyOfSubstInSubst.")
(comment increases-Generic "(#$increases-Generic TEMP-THING THING SLOT)            means that the value of the predicate SLOT applied to THING (in the second argument position) is greater over some time period after the start of TEMP-THING. Compared with its value immediately before TEMP-THING, the value of SLOT applied to THING will be higher immediately following or some time after the start of TEMP-THING. This is the most generic of the #$SlotTrendPredicates relating to increasing of a given instance of #$QuantitySlot. The increase may be caused by TEMP-THING, but need not be. It may occur immediately, or over a period of time following TEMP-THING. For GAFs, or in the consequents of rules dealing with increased quantities, use the more specific predicates if possible. See #$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates for a map of related predicates.")
(comment InfectionType "A collection of collections. Each instance of #$InfectionType is a specialization of #$Infection. Instances include #$BubonicPlague, #$Leprosy, and #$Herpes.")
(comment SurfaceForceVector "Forces that act on bodies through the surface, contact forces etc.")
(comment contradictoryMt "(#$contradictoryMt MT-1 MT-2) means that at least some of the assertions of MT-1 (content assertions and/or domain assumptions) are inconsistent with assertions of MT-2, and no lifting can occur between MT-1 and MT-2 (i.e. assertions made in one microtheory should not be made visible to the other microtheory). For cases where it is specifically domain assumptions that are in conflict, the more specialized predicate #$negationMt should be used.")
(comment ShoreOfLakeFn "(#$ShoreOfLakeFn LAKE) denotes the shore of LAKE, an instance of #$Lake.")
(comment Brucellosis "A disease usually caused by contact with farm animals carrying the #$BrucellaBacterium.  May include mild flu-like symptoms, fever, chills, sweating, muscle aches, joint aches, and malaise.")
(comment MassEventOfTypeFn "(#$MassEventOfTypeFn EVTTYPE) is the collection of instances of EVTTYPE, the main #$subEvents and #$groupMembers of which are all also instances of EVTTYPE.  For example, (#$MassEventOfTypeFn SinglePhotoCopyingEvent) is the collection of 'mass' photocopying events, that is, events, the main #$subEvents and #$groupMembers of which are individual SinglePhotoCopyingEvents.")
(disjointWith SubLString JustificationTruth)
(comment Prochlorperazine "The chemical compound which is an anti-emetic.")
(comment J-TheLetter "The letter J of the alphabet.  This is 'J' (or 'j') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.   As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterJ and #$LatinSmallLetterJ.")
(comment Baht-Thailand "The unitOfCurrenty used in Thailand-AtPresent.")
(comment BiologicalMaturationEvent "A collection of events.  In each #$BiologicalMaturationEvent, a living thing undergoes biological processes and changes from its species' juvenile form to its species' mature form.  In humans, this means reaching puberty; i.e., #$Puberty is a subset of this collection.  Note that many episodes of maturation are accompanied by growth, but not all are (e.g., the final stages of seed maturation, during which the seed loses water and actually shrinks in size).")
(comment interArgIsa3-5 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  
(#$interArgIsa3-5 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, 
when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the third argument to RELN, 
a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the fifth argument 
must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is
an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then 
(RELN ARG1 ARG2 INST ARG4 ARG5 ... ARGN) is semantically 
well-formed only if ARG5 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation 
of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct 
specializations.")
(comment FighterPlane-F15 "The #$FighterPlane-F15 Eagle is an all-weather, extremely maneuverable, tactical fighter designed to gain and maintain air superiority in aerial combat. The Eagle's air superiority is achieved through a mixture of maneuverability and acceleration, range, weapons and avionics. The F-15 has electronic systems and weaponry to detect, acquire, track and attack enemy aircraft while operating in friendly or enemy-controlled airspace. Its weapons and flight control systems are designed so one person can safely and effectively perform air-to-air combat. It can penetrate enemy defense and outperform and outfight current or projected enemy aircraft.  The F-15's superior maneuverability and acceleration are achieved through high engine thrust-to-weight ratio and low wing loading. Low wing-loading (the ratio of aircraft weight to its wing area) is a vital factor in maneuverability and, combined with the high thrust-to-weight ratio, enables the aircraft to turn tightly without losing airspeed.")
(comment porosityOfObject "(#$porosityOfObject OBJ DEGREE) means that the tangible object OBJ has the degree of #$Porosity DEGREE.")
(comment MappingMicrotheory "A collection of microtheories.  An instance of #$MappingMicrotheory contains information about mappings between Cyc terms and terms in external representation systems.")
(comment Bacteremia "The collection of all bacterial bloodstream infections [see
#$CirculatorySystem]. #$Bacteremia allow bacteria to spread widely into the
host from #$PrimaryInfectionSite to #$SecondaryInfectionSites, where they
found more suitable conditions to multiply. #$Bacteremia can be transient
or persistent.")
(disjointWith PassengerAircraft UnmannedAircraft)
(comment Intron-MolecularSegment "The collection of all #$molecularSubComponents of

#$NucleicAcidMolecules that instantiate nucleotide sequences which do

not code for amino acid sequences.  The function of intron molecules

in protein production has not yet been fully elucidated: the final

step in mRNA production consists in excision of the intron-components

of the primary transcript RNA.")
(disjointWith HumanScaleObject CelestialRegion)
(comment nearnessForRolesInEventType "This predicate relates roles according to nearness

conventions associated with an event type.  (#$nearnessForRolesInEventType 

ROLE1 ROLE2 EVENTTYPE MAX-DISTANCE) means that things playing ROLE1 and 

ROLE2 respectively in an instance of EVENTTYPE are considered near each 

other according to the conventions for EVENTTYPE if the distance between 

them is less than or equal to MAX-DISTANCE.  See #$nearForRolesInEventType to express the fact that two objects are actually near each other according to the conventions articulated in this predicate.  Other nearness predicates include #$near, #$nearRelativeTo and #$nearToDegree.")
(comment Bass-Singer "Each #$Bass-Singer is a singer having an adult male voice which performs well in the lower registers.  Of all the male voices, a bass can sing the lowest.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-DataFloodingOSCrashing "#$AttackByComputerOperation-DataFloodingOSCrashing is a subset of both #$AttackByComputerOperation-DataFlooding and #$AttackByComputerOperation-OSCrashing.  Each instance of #$AttackByComputerOperation-DataFloodingOSCrashing is an electronic attack in which the objective of the attack is to flood a computer or #$ComputerNetwork with enough information to cause a #$ComputerCrashing.  Such attacks are typically instances of #$AttackByComputerOperation-Coordinated and #$AttackByComputerOperation-Distributed as well.")
(comment Vendor "The collection of all #$LegalAgents who specialize in selling at least one type of #$Product at the wholesale or retail level.")
(comment Papule-Condition "The collection of the conditions of having #$Papule-Objects, which are small, firm elevated nodules on the skin.")
(comment Conjunction "The collection of all coordinating and subordinating conjunctions")
(comment Banshee "The collection of all banshees. The #$Banshee is a supernatural being in Irish and other Celtic folklore whose mournful 'keening,' or wailing screaming or lamentation, at night was believed to foretell the death of a member of the family of the person who heard the spirit. The word 'banshee' is a phonetic spelling of the Irish 'bean sidhe'.")
(disjointWith PortableObject Place)
(comment Dysprosium "The collection of all pieces (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of dysprosium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment UpwardsFn "This function, applied to a #$TopAndBottomSidedObject, returns the
exact direction its top is facing in the implicit frame of reference
defined by the object.")
(comment Initiative "#$Initiative is the attribute of actions that are performed on the basis of an independent decision on the part of the performer.")
(comment processThreads "(#$processThreads PROCESS THREAD) means that THREAD is a thread
of the process PROCESS.")
(disjointWith BodyOfWater CircularWindSystem)
(comment BoatingSportsEvent "The collection of #$SportsEvents using human powered boats (#$Watercraft-Surface) normally held outdoors.")
(comment Quotation "The collection of all #$TextuallySpecificWorks consisting of a small number of sentences that are attributed to a specific individual.  Although many utterance or written #$Statement by a person may instantiate #$ConceptualWorks that may be used as a #$Quotation of that person, unless and until such a work is recorded and so attributed it is not an instance of the collection, #$Quotation.  Every #$Quotation has a #$TextString as an #$infoStructureOfCW.  The #$Quotation is neither the #$TextString nor the initially generated #$InformationBearingThing (#$AnimalUtterance-IBT or #$Statement), but is the #$ConceptualWork instantiated by that IBT.")
(comment arg6Format "An instance of #$ArgFormatPredicate (q.v.) used to place a particular #$Format (q.v.) constraint on the sixth (or \"arg6\") argument-place of a given predicate.  (#$arg6Format PRED FORMAT) means that PRED's arg6 is constrained to FORMAT.  See the reified instances #$Format for

further details.")
(comment (ClubRelatedFn PorscheCar) "The collection of Porsche car clubs.")
(comment AspectTenseModifier "A spec of #$ModalOperator. This is the collection of the sentential operators used to

represent tense and aspectual modification in natural language.")
(comment separatingConstituent "(#$separatingConstituent arg1 arg2) is true if after sometime (maybe several minutes to several hours) of just resting in normal physical conditions not being churned or stirred, the constituent arg2 would begin to separate out of the #$Mixture arg1.  Only the stuff that separates away/does not remain is a #$separatingConstituent.  For example, carbonation separates out of beer that has been standing in open air for a while.  Thus only the #$constituents alchohol and water remain--the beer is flat.  On the other hand, salad dressing separates into oil and vinegar and we wouldn't call either of those `the stuff that remains' thus *both* vinegar and oil are values on #$separatingConstituent.  Presumably then salad dressing undergoes a destruction event as separation happens.")
(comment Smurf-MoneyLaunderer "The collection of 'smurfs' - those who launder money by making small, frequent cash deposits.")
(comment Vibrionaceae-Family "A collection  of #$Bacterium in the #$MoneraKingdom classified as a #$BiologicalFamily.  It includes the #$BiologicalGenus #$Vibrio-Genus.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are #$GramNegativeBacterium and #$BacillusBacterium, either straight or curved.  They are motile bacterium with polar flagella.  They are chemoorganotrophs capable of both fermentative and respiratory metabolism.  Most are oxidase-positive.  All utilize D-glucose for a source of carbon and energy.  These are primarily aquatic organisms.")
(comment TVBiography-PartlyFictional "#$TVBiography-PartlyFictional is a collection of #$FictionalTVShow-CWs intended to present a biography as a semi-fictional #$Narrative. Each instance may contain some information that is known to its author to be false. If it is intended to be wholly factual, then it is an instance of #$TVBiography.")
(comment programOnPort "A predicate relating instances of #$SoftwareObject-Individual with ports on instances of #$Computer.  (#$programOnPort PROGRAM PROTOCOL PORT COMPUTER) means that a copy of PROGRAM is currently listening for packets conforming to PROTOCOL on PORT on COMPUTER.  (See #$NetworkPortNumber).")
(comment Hydrochlorothiazide "The chemical compound which is used to make products which help control high blood pressure .")
(comment interArgIsa1-5 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  
(#$interArgIsa1-5 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, 
when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the first argument to RELN, 
a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the fifth argument 
must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is
an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then 
(RELN INST ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ... ARGN) is semantically 
well-formed only if ARG5 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation 
of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct 
specializations.")
(comment FreeTourTimeInFn "(#$FreeTourTimeInFn PLACE) returns the collection of all

instances of #$SightSeeing that occur in PLACE as part of a tour, that

are not explicitly dictated by the tour itinerary.")
(comment ScheduleFn-EntertainmentPerformer "(#$ScheduleFn-EntertainmentPerformer ENT) returns the collection of all instances of #$Schedule that include information about EntertainmentEvents performed by ENT.  For example (#$ScheduleFn-EntertainmentPerformer #$Madonna) returns the collection of all schedules listing appearances, tour dates, etc., for the singer Madonna.")
(comment AikidoEvent "#$AikidoEvent is the collection of events in which one or more agents engage in the activity of aikido.")
(comment vulnerableToType "(#$vulnerableToType THREAT-OBJ-TYPE OBJECT HARM-TYPE) means that instances of the collection THREAT-OBJ-TYPE generally pose harm results of type HARM-TYPE to OBJECT.  The purpose of this predicate is to represent the knowledge that an entire class of things poses a certain kind of vulnerability to a particular object.  For restrictions on the use of HARM-TYPE see #$vulnerableTo.  Note that this is a type-level predicate in the first argument place and that care needs to be taken in developing rules that draw #$vulnerableTo conclusions from #$vulnerableToType GAFs so that we do not overpopulate the KB with potentially questionable #$vulnerableTo judgments.")
(comment Stretcher "A device which is used to carry medical patients, usually to a location where a medical procedure will be performed on them.")
(comment subjectOfReport-Sit "(#$subjectOfReport-Sit REPORT SIT) means that the #$Situation instance SIT is the main focus or topic of REPORT.")
(comment TotalOrdering "The collection of all those #$PartialOrdering ORDER in which the ordering relation R orders elements of the #$baseSet S of ORDER into a single line.  A #$TotalOrdering is sometimes called a 'linear ordering' or a 'chain'.  A #$PartialOrdering ORDER is a #$TotalOrdering if all elements of the #$baseSet S of ORDER are comparable by the ordering relation R of ORDER, i.e., for any X and Y in S, either R(X Y) or R(Y X).  For example, if you take a set of real numbers and the usual 'greater than or equal to' relation among these numbers, you have a #$TotalOrdering.  Note that if you want a 'strict line', i.e., if you want the ordering relation in a total ordering to be irreflexive, see #$TotalOrdering-Strict.")
(comment AutomaticFirearm-HopperFed "The collection of #$AutomaticFirearms that use a hopper feed system of gravity.")
(comment UnitOfCharge "A collection of functions and an instance of #$UnitOfMeasureTypeByTypeMeasured. Each function in this collection is used to denote instances of #$ElectricalCharge.  E.g., (#$Coulomb 3) denotes an electrical charge of 3 coulombs.")
(comment oilSupply "This predicate denotes the supply of oil available to a country (or other region).  For some countries, this quantity correlates with amount of oil production.  For others, it correlates with amount of oil import.")
(comment IndustrializedRegion "This is the subcollection of #$GeographicalRegions which are characterized by intensive development of industry and manufacturing.")
(disjointWith Perceiving AcademicTesting)
(comment AssessingEnemyStrength "A collection of processes.  Each element of #$AssessingEnemyStrength
is an instance of #$Evaluating in which what is evaluated is the military
strength of the enemy.")
(comment CurrentSource "A source of electrical current")
(comment USFederalGovernmentOrganization "A collection of government organizations.  An instance of #$USFederalGovernmentOrganization is an  instance of #$LegalGovernmentOrganization which is part of the #$UnitedStatesFederalGovernment. This collection includes the US military,  Federal courts, US Congress, US territorial governments, Federal departments  and independent agencies, and the city of Washington DC.  It does _not_  include US states, interstate compacts, and cities (other than Washington  DC).")
(disjointWith Covering-Object InanimateObject-Natural)
(comment CredentialTypeBySkill "Elements are kinds of credentials, characterized by certifying a particular skill or training.")
(comment ExpropriatingSomething "The collection of events in which one agent takes something previously belonging to another agent, without that agent's free consent.  Instances of #$ExpropriatingSomething differ from those of #$AppropriatingSomething because in the latter, we assume that the taking doesn't violate any other agent's rights.  Compensation may or may not be offered by the expropriating agent.  Examples of #$ExpropriatingSomething include a government takeover of oil companies (see #$NationalizingAnIndustry) or taking property by the right of eminent domain.")
(disjointWith ComputationalObject Issue)
(comment keGenlsWeakSuggestionInverse "(#$keGenlsWeakSuggestionInverse COL BIN-PRED) means that for every specialization SPEC-COL of COL, it is weakly
suggested that there exist some VALUE such that (BIN-PRED VALUE SPEC-COL) is known in the KB.")
(comment CityBlockFn "(#$CityBlockFn ST1 ST2 ST3 ST4) denotes the instance of #$CityBlock (if any) that is bounded by streets ST1 - ST4, such  that if one starts on ST1 and circles around the block making  only right-hand turns one will travel along ST1, ST2, ST3, and ST4, in that order.  The region immediately surrounding the  block must be an #$UrbanArea that has a #$GridStreetSystem running through it.  To have this function return a specific desired city BLOCK, one can fill its arg1 position with any  of the four streets that borders BLOCK, and then continue to fill in the remaining argument-places according to the order in which one would travel along the other three streets if one were circling BLOCK in a clockwise fashion (i.e. by  making only right-hand turns).  See also #$cityBlockBoundedBy, #$CityGridSectionFn, and #$CitySectionFn.")
(comment SuperBowlGame "The collection of the once-a-year season-final championship games of the #$NationalFootballLeague. Instances pit the champion of the #$AmericanConference-Football against the champion of the #$NationalConference-Football, and take place in late January.")
(comment SalesEconomicSector "The collection of all localized groups of enterprises that are chiefly concerned with sales, such that each group forms the major economic sales sector for the region.  Many enterprises are part of such sectors while at the same time being parts of other major economic sectors.  An example instance would be the sales sector of Illinois.")
(comment VeterinaryAnimalRestraint "The equipment used by vets to hold animals safely immobile during medical procedures.")
(comment up-UnderspecifiedPath "(#$up-UnderspecifiedPath ACT REGION) states that an abstract
locational relation holds between ACT and REGION, where REGION is a
#$Region-Underspecified crossed in an 'upwardly motion' during ACT.
#$up-UnderspecifiedPath is an underspecified semantic representation that
may be elaborated to represent either a spatial example of upward
motion (as in 'walking up the hill') or a temporal use of downward
'motion' ('bill's appointment was moved up to tomorrow') or a
metaphorical use ('Jones climbed up the corporate ladder').")
(comment PhysicalImpactBuffer "The set of objects which  act as buffers to protect against physical impact")
(comment interestRateCap-Periodic "The predicate used to state, for an adjustable-rate loan, the highest amount by which the interest rate can change during any single adjustment period.  (#$interestRateCap-Periodic LOAN PERIOD (#$Percent N)) means that the #$interestRate on LOAN cannot either increase or decrease by more than (#$Percent N) during PERIOD.  So if it is also the case that (#$interestRate LOAN RATE) where RATE is (#$PerFn (#$Percent M) DURATION) then RATE may not become more than (#$PerFn (#$Percent M + N) DURATION) during PERIOD, or less than (#$PerFn (#$Percent M - N) DURATION) during PERIOD.")
(comment MilitaryOrganization "A specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$MilitaryOrganization is an organization whose function (and expertise) is the use of armed force, or the threat of such use, against enemies, especially other organized, armed enemies.  A military organization includes its fighting forces and their command structure, together with dedicated support services controlled by that military command.  Typically, there are special conditions in the relationships between a #$MilitaryOrganization and its workers, going beyond what is expected in work agreements in civilian settings, including strict sanctions to enforce obedience.  This collection includes #$GovernmentMilitaryOrganizations such as the armies, navies, and air forces of the world's governments, and in addition private armies, rebel armies, and organized mercenary units.")
(comment GuanosineTriphosphate "A collection of nucleotides that are activated precursors to

the synthesis of RNA and are also involved in energy metabolism.

They contain #$Guanine-Base linked to #$Ribose and three phosphates.")
(disjointWith ShreddingEvent LosingALeaf)
(comment SupplyTruck "The collection of trucks used by a military to transport supplies.")
(comment SwingingOnASwing "The collection of events in which someone swings on a (playground, recreational equipment) swing")
(comment WebPublishedTypeFn "(#$WebPublishedTypeFn INFORMATIONTYPE) yields the collection of INFORMATIONTYPEs that are published on the web.  (#$WebPublishedTypeFn #$LovePoem), for example, represents the collection of love poems published on the web.")
(comment IDObjectFn "(#$IDObjectFn ID) returns the #$Individual associated with #$UniqueID ID.")
(comment BorreliaRecurrentis "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies in
the #$MoneraKingdom.  #$Infection leads to attacks of #$Fever.  ")
(comment NuclearGuidedMissileCruiser "The collection of #$Cruiser ships which are nuclear-powered, and which transport and launch #$GuidedMissiles.")
(disjointWith FluidTangibleThing SemiSolidTangibleThing)
(comment BudgetDescriptionDocument "The collection of all documents that describe the financial budget of some agent (an organization or person).")
(comment MarineExpeditionaryForce "A specialization of #$ModernMilitaryUnit-Deployable, each instance of which
  is one of the #$subOrganizations of the #$UnitedStatesMarineCorps.  The instances
  of #$MarineExpeditionaryForce (MEFs) are the Marine Corps' principal warfighting
  organizations, particularly for larger crises or contingencies, and are
  normally commanded by a lieutenant general.  An MEF can range in size from
  less than one to multiple infantry divisions and aircraft wings, together
  with supporting units.  An MEF is primarily a standing Marine Air-Ground
  Task Force, or MAGTF.  Currently, the Marine Corps is organized with three
  standing MEFs, each with a division, wing, and force service support group.")
(comment Fluorine "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of fluorine in stuffeous form (could be solid, liquid, gaseous, etc.).")
(disjointWith PlayingABoardGame CreatingAnArtifact)
(comment Malnutrition "A collection of physiological conditions caused by the lack of
essential #$Nutrients (usually vitamins, minerals or proteins).
Specialized forms of #$Malnutrition are: (1)
#$DietaryDeficiencyCondition, in which the necessary nutrients are
not ingested; and (2) #$Malnutrition-Secondary, in which the necessary
nutrients are not properly metabolized.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (RightObjectOfPairFn SixthRib) Tuberosity) "")
(comment standardEchelonSubstructure "(#$standardEchelonSubstructure COUNTRY BOS-TYPE ECHELON

SUB-ECHELON N) means that under ordinary circumstances, a military

unit of echelon ECHELON whose sovereign allegiance is COUNTRY and whose branch of service

is BOS-TYPE is expected to have N units of echelon SUB-ECHELON as

assigned sub-units.")
(comment Prostitution "Each instance of #$Prostitution is an event in which a #$Prostitute performs #$SexualBehavior with a client for money.")
(comment LGM-30B-MinutemanMissile "The collection of all

 #$LGM-30B-MinutemanMissiles, the

 second (and last) type of #$BallisticMissile-Minuteman1.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-DefacingAWebsite "#$AttackByComputerOperation-DefacingAWebsite is a subset of #$AttackByComputerOperation.  In every instance of this collection, some instance of           #$WorldWideWebSite is the object of some form of vandalism.")
(comment KneeSurgery "Surgery on a patient's knees.")
(comment NosePlug "The collection of nose plugs. These are usually

rubber and are designed to keep water out of a person's nose while

they are swimming.")
(comment HeavyFieldArtilleryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units trained and equipped for handling field           pieces with a bore greater than or equal to 200mm.")
(disjointWith CurrentFlowThruComponent WeatherEvent)
(comment InformationThingAboutFn "A Cyc function that is an element of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  (#$InformationThingAboutFn SUBJ) returns the collection of #$InformationBearingThings which contain information about the particular thing SUBJ.  That collection may include both objects (e.g., #$BookCopy, #$Photographs, physical documents) and intangibles such as singing events [#$Song-Sung] or even gestural communication.  See also #$containsInformationAbout.  To state the content of the information, see #$containsInformation.")
(comment CompletelyFlawed "This is the most severe flaw attribute.  If something has this attribute it is capable of performing none, or almost none, of the relevant functions for which it is intended or designed or functions which things of its type are typically expected to perform.")
(comment SurfaceLayer-TopSurfaceFn "(#$SurfaceLayer-TopSurfaceFn SPATIALTHING) returns the

contiguous #$SurfaceLayer-TopSurface that covers the top of SPATIALTHING.  We

remain agnostic about whether or not it is the case that

(#$physicalParts SPATIALTHING (#$SurfaceLayer-TopSurfaceFn

SPATIALTHING)), although this may be the case for instances of certain

classes of #$SpatialThing.  The 'top' surface is the highest-up surface of the uppermost parts of a #$SpatialThing when it is in its normal position; if the top is curved, like the back of a pig, the top surface includes the skin over the backbone and an indefinite amount of surrounding skin.  The top surface of a body of water (like a lake) is the surface exposed to the air.")
(disjointWith Flywheel LandTransportationWheel)
(comment PlayboyModel "The collection of all #$FemalePersons who have appeared as #$Nude or scantily-clad models in pictures in Playboy Magazine, an international men's magazine published in the late 20th century.")
(disjointWith ProfessionalSport CollegeSport)
(comment Spreadsheet "A specialization of #$HumanAccessibleIBT and #$StructuredInformationSource.  Each instance of #$Spreadsheet is an information-bearing thing that presents (usually numeric) data in a two-dimensional matrix of cells that are organized into rows and columns so that people can view it.  A spreadsheet may be produced by hand with pencil and paper or generated by a computer #$SpreadsheetProgram (q.v.) such as #$Lotus123 onto a computer screen or hardcopy device.  Associated with every spreadsheet are mathematical definitions of some of its cells as a function of other cells in that spreadsheet.  A database [see #$Database-Physical] that holds the information from which the spreadsheet is generated is not an instance of #$Spreadsheet.")
(disjointWith USStateGovernment CityGovernment)
(disjointWith UnitOfFrequency UnitOfPower)
(comment AncientTownSquare "the collection of town squares from ancient times")
(comment SpreadingASubstance "The collection of events in which a substance (instance of an #$ExistingStuffType) is spread out over a volume or area.  Important specializations of #$SpreadingASubstance are #$SpreadingStuffOntoSurface and #$SpreadingStuffOntoSurfaceWithTool.  This is distinct from spreading out something like a blanket for which the event type #$SpreadingSheetOntoSurface should be used.")
(comment DNAStrand-FivePrimeEnd "The ends of DNA strands deemed to be the 5' end because of the orientation of the component nucleotides.")
(comment topicOf "(#$topicOf CONCEPT TOPIC) means that TOPIC is in some way the topic of CONCEPT that distinguishes CONCEPT from one of its generalizations and from most, if not all, of its siblings.  For example (#$topicOf #$ApplianceStore #$HouseholdAppliance).")
(comment Pentobarbital "The chemical compound which is used as a sedative.")
(comment MovingExpenseAccount "An account for the money which goes to pay for moving expenses")
(comment travelLegs "(#$travelLegs TOUR PATH LOCFROM LOCTO) means that PATH
constitutes a 'leg' on the itinerary of TOUR from the location LOCFROM
to the location LOCTO.#$travelLegs are usually represented as running
between well-known locations, such as instances of #$City, and are
often composed of a single #$Path-Customary or several instances of
#$Path-Customary.  In a graphical representation of a #$TravelTour in
which #$tourDestinations and/or #$tourVisits are the nodes, the
instances of #$Path-Simple that are second arguments of the
#$travelLegs GAFs for the tour will be the links.")
(comment IndustrialEconomicSector "The collection of all localized groups of enterprises that are producers of industrial commodities, in which each such group together forms the major industrial sector for the region.  'Industrial commodities' includes #$MechanicalDevices and basic industrial materials.   Examples include 'the world industrial sector', the 'industrial sector of China'.  The Chinese water pump industry would not be an exemplar of #$IndustrialEconomicSector but would rather be a sub-industry (see #$subIndustries) of it.  On the other hand, chinese water pump manufacturers would be considered #$groupMembers of 'the industrial sector of China'.")
(disjointWith AudioClip VideoRecordedObject)
(comment NewPeso-Uruguay "The unit of currency for Uruguay-AtPresent.")
(comment HostToNetworkLayerProtocol "A #$HostToNetworkLayerProtocol is a combination of

a #$DataLinkLayerProtocol and a #$PhysicalLayerProtocol. A

#$HostToNetworkLayerProtocol would include both the software needed to

transport data between nodes (i.e. #$DataLinkLayerProtocol) and the physical

medium which connects nodes (i.e. #$PhysicalLayerProtocol). An example of

a #$HostToNetworkLayerProtocol is Ethernet.")
(comment TankerAircraft "The collection of aircraft used to transport liquid substances.")
(comment PeanutPod "The fruit of the peanut plant; contains edible seeds [peanuts].  Peanut pods are unusual in that the shoot bearing the pod elongates, pushing the pod underground as it starts  to form; the peanut pod then matures underground.")
(comment interArgReln3-4 "A binary #$InterArgRelnPredicate (q.v.).  (#$interArgReln3-4 RELN BINPRED) means that a formula built from RELN (i.e. a \"GAF\" or \"NAT\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence and  #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm) is semantically well-formed only if BINPRED holds between the third and fourth arguments to RELN (in that order) in the GAF/NAT.  That is, a formula (RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ..) is semantically well-formed only if (BINPRED ARG3 ARG4) holds.  For example, (#$interArgReln3-4 #$candidateEngagementAreaOfCOAForForces #$opponents) means that the arg3 and arg4 in a #$candidateEngagementAreaOfCOAForForces assertion must be opponents.  For further explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations. See also the more general quaternary predicate #$interArgReln, which has two argument-places for specifying the pair of RELN's arguments that must be related by BINPRED.")
(comment Campsite "The region where people have temporarily set up lodging in the form of tents, sleeping bags, campfires, etc..  Also includes military style encampments.  Some campsites are campsites for no longer than the duration the tent is set up there.  Other campsites remain campsites for years, e.g. #$Campground.")
(comment ThrowingADie "Throwing a die or dice, as part of a game")
(comment XFighting "A form of #$WrestlingSportsEvent which ends in the two male participants engaging in #$SexualBehavior with each other.")
(comment nearestTransitiveNeighbor "(#$nearestTransitiveNeighbor PRED TERM NEAR-TERM) relates any transitive binary predicate PRED and a TERM to those other NEAR-TERMs that are the nearest in the following sense: (PRED TERM NEAR-TERM) holds and there is no other instance BETWEEN distinct from TERM and  NEAR-TERM such that both (PRED TERM BETWEEN) and (PRED BETWEEN NEAR-TERM) hold. #$nearestTransitiveNeighbor generalizes the functionality of #$nearestGenls,  #$nearestGenlMt and others to any transitive binary predicate.  Note that this predicate is #$notAssertible, since it must be recomputed from the transitive hierarchy generated by PRED.")
(disjointWith ExistingStuffType HumanCapabilityType)
(comment HIVInfection "The precursor to AIDS.")
(comment recommendedTouristsVisit "(#$recommendedTouristsVisit REGION LANDMARK) means that it is recommended that a tourist, while in the instance of #$GeographicalRegion REGION, visits some instance of the #$ExistingObjectType LANDMARK.")
(comment HayFever "#$HayFever is the collection of all bouts of hay fever, which is an #$AllergicReaction to #$Ragweed pollen.")
(comment redundantAssertions "(#$redundantAssertions ASSN-1 ASSN-2) means that ASSN-1 and ASSN-2 entail each other.  Note that this is not currently a replacement for the [R] notation one sees automatically generated on redundant #$genls or #$isa assertions.  Rather, its primary purpose is to label pairs of assertions whose mutual entailment is hard for the system to automatically deduce.  It is much more likely that human #$Cyclists will notice the redundancies.  Although not currently (March 97) supported, #$redundantAssertions may help the system narrow search.  E.g. if ASSN-1 has already been used in an inference path, attempt to use ASSN-2 with the same priority that one would wish to re-use ASSN-1.  It also may be useful in helping us induce preferential synactic forms.  For example imagine two syntactic classes of assertions A and B.  Suppose there are a large number of assertions a in A and b in B such that (#$redundantAssertions a b) is true.  Further, suppose that assertions in A are used in inference paths 10 times more often than those in B in a suite of several thousand application related inferences.  This would indicate that knowledge enterers should prefer syntactic forms similar to those in A over syntactic forms to those in B.  For an assertion that is a special case of a more general assertion see #$assertionIsArgumentFor.")
(comment superTimeSliceType "(#$superTimeSliceType SHORTER-TYPE LONGER-TYPE) means that  for every instance X of SHORTER-TYPE, there is an instance Y of LONGER-TYPE such that (#$timeSlices Y X).  Examples: (#$superTimeSliceType #$Halloween #$October),  (#$superTimeSliceType #$October #$CalendarYear). See also the comments on #$timeSlices, #$subTimeSliceType.  Note that (#$superTimeSliceType SHORTER-TYPE LONGER-TYPE) does not necessarily entail (#$subTimeSliceType LONGER-TYPE SHORTER-TYPE).")
(disjointWith SubwayStation ParkingPlace)
(comment LunarStuff "A collection of tangible things.  Each element in #$LunarStuff is a portion of the stuff that the ground of Earth's moon Luna (at or near its land surface) is made of, including rocks, boulders, sand grains, rigolith, ice, etc., and mixtures of those things.")
(comment Strait "The collection of water passageways connecting two larger bodies of water.")
(comment Wolf-Gray "A collection of wolves.  Instances of #$Wolf-Gray are the largest of the           wolves and live in the Northern           Hemisphere.  Common names (sometimes referring to a subspecies) include Tundra           Wolf,  Arctic Wolf, Lobo Wolf, Plains Wolf and Buffalo Wolf and especially Timber           Wolf.  Their scientific name is Canis lupus.")
(comment EthernetNetwork "A coaxial cable local area network first described by Metcalfe & Boggs of Xerox PARC in 1976. Specified by DEC, Intel and XEROX (DIX) as IEEE 802.3 and now recognised as the industry standard. The bandwidth is about 10 Mbit/s. Disk-Ethernet-Disk transfer rate with TCP/IP is typically 30 kilobyte per second.")
(comment hasGlamour "Entries are U's glamor rating.  Glamor refers to a combination of social fascination, allure, popularity, and stylishness.")
(comment VolleyballBall "The ball manipulated in a volley-ball game.")
(comment BallisticMissile-MAR-290 "A type of ballistic missile.  According to the CSIS source document 'Creeping Proliferation Could Mean a Paradigm Shift

          in the Cost of War and Terrorism', Isreal is in possession of many of these missiles and may use them as delivery vehicles for weapons of mass destruction.")
(comment Osmium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of Osmium.")
(disjointWith MaghrebCountry CaspianCountry)
(disjointWith IDStringType MatterTypeByPhysicalState)
(comment InjuryUnderTreatment "The collection of all bodily injuries [#$Injury-Object] that are receiving medical treatment.  The treatment process has started, yet not yet finished.  An injury is still considered to be an #$InjuryUnderTreatment between active steps in the treatment process.")
(comment DefaultOnInternationalLoan "The collection of events where a state refuses to pay a loan given to them by another state(s) or an international bank(s).")
(comment Proteus-BacteriumGenus "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom.

These #$ProkaryoticCells are #$GramNegativeBacterium, rods whose natural

habitat is in the intestinal tract of humans and animals.  They produce

infection only when they leave the intestinal tract.  They are found

in #$UrinaryTractInfections.")
(comment ContactInfoFn "#$ContactInfoFn takes as argument any Agent and returns the collection of PropositionalInformationThings about how to contact that agent.  For example, (#$ContactInfoFn #$NASA) returns the collection of information about how to contact the National Aeronautics and Space Adminstration.")
(disjointWith IntrinsicStateChangeEvent ChangeOfStatusEvent)
(comment CombustionOfIndividualFn "#$CombustionOfIndividualFn is a function that takes as an argument an instance of

#$PartiallyTangible and returns the instance of #$CombustionProcess in

which the #$PartiallyTangible thing is destroyed.  That is,

(#$CombustionOfIndividualFn TANG) denotes the event in which TANG is destroyed in

an instance of #$CombustionProcess.")
(comment BirthControlDrug "Each instance of #$BirthControlDrug is some piece of a substance 
which can be used to regulate female fertility and prevent ovulation.")
(comment tourParticipants "This predicate relates travel tours to the tourists and guides taking part in the travel tour.")
(comment AerosolTheSolution "#$AerosolTheSolution is a collection of aerosols which have no solid component, and whose liquid component is a solution.")
(comment EducationalMagazineSeries "The collection of all #$MagazineSeries which have educational content.  These magazines are generally intended to be read for academic purposes, rather than purely for entertainment.")
(comment CodingPortionOfGene-MolecularSegment "#$CodingPortionOfGene-MolecularSegment is a collection of groups of #$CodingSequence-MolecularSegment. Each instance is an instance of (#$GroupFn #$CodingSequence-MolecularSegment) such that each member of the group is a molecular subcomponent of a single instance of #$Gene-HereditaryUnit. That is, each instance of #$CodingPortionOfGene-MolecularSegment is the coding portion of a single #$Gene-HereditaryUnit.")
(comment globalRequisiteFor "If PRECON is any known propositional precondition for SIT2
and (#$globalRequisiteFor SIT1 SIT2), then SIT1's 'obtaining' or
'happening' is a necessary precondition for PRECON becoming true.")
(comment Bleach "Chemical substance often used as a whitening agent for

removing dyes and other staining agents from cloth products.  It can

also be used as a topical disinfectant.")
(comment GrenadeLauncher-M79 "The collection of M79 #$GrenadeLaunchers.  This weapon first  appeared during the Vietnam war and closely resembled a large bore, single  barrel, sawn-off shotgun. The first M79 Grenade launchers were delivered to  the US Army in 1961. The M79 was designed as a close support weapon for the  infantry, and was intended to bridge the gap between the maximum throwing  distance of a hand grenade, and the lowest range of supporting mortar fire.   An area of between 50 and 300 meters.")
(disjointWith Pressure Volume)
(comment interArgCondIsa2-1 "(#$interArgCondIsa2-1  PRED INDEP-COL COND-COL DEP-COL) is shorthand for the class of rules that state the following: For every instance INDEP-INST of INDEP-COL, if there is some instance COND-INST of COND-COL such that (PRED COND-INST INDEP-INST) holds, COND-INST will also be an instance of DEP-COL.  For example, (#$interArgCondIsa2-1 #$anatomicalParts #$Head-Vertebrate #$Organism-Whole #$Vertebrate) -- if an element of #$Head-Vertebrate is an #$anatomicalParts of some #$Organism-Whole, that organism is a #$Vertebrate.")
(disjointWith Campsite Dock)
(comment AnalogyMappingFn "(#$AnalogyMappingFn STRING) denotes the #$AnalogyMapping which is referred to by the name STRING in the MAC-FAC analogy reasoning system.  See also #$bestMapping, #$hasCorrespondence, and #$commonalities.")
(comment CycLOpenNonAtomicTerm "The collection of denotational #$CycLNonAtomicTerms that have free variables. Examples: `(#$JuvenileFn ?X)', `(#$JuvenileFn ?X ?Y ?Z)'.  Counterexample: `(#$TheSetOf ?X (#$objectHasColor ?X #$GreenColor))'.")
(comment AmateurRadioOperator "An instance of #$AmateurRadioOperator is a person who operates           an instance of #$AmateurRadioEquipment.")
(comment Concentrating "A collection of processes; a subset of #$Thinking.  Each element of #$Concentrating is a mental process in which the doer's attention is fully or mostly absorbed by his or her thoughts.  Every process of mental concentration is also an element of #$PurposefulAction (q.v.)")
(comment inferenceIndicatedProduct "(#$inferenceIndicatedProduct PRSN PROD-TYPE) means that it can be inferred that instances of #$ProductType PROD-TYPE are positively indicated as a purchase for the #$Person PRSN. The inference might make use of general rules relating recipients to #$ProductTypes and specific information about a particular recipient. General rules which conclude that PROD-TYPE is indicated for a #$Person PRSN should use #$inferenceIndicatedProduct in the consequent, not #$defaultSuitableProduct.")
(comment completeTextOfIBT "(#$completeTextOfIBT IBT TEXT) means that the full text of the #$InformationBearingThing, IBT, is TEXT.")
(comment movesInDirection-Average "(#$movesInDirection-Average OBJ DIR) means that OBJ moves in the

average direction DIR.  In other words DIR is the direction from the

the location of OBJ at the 'start' to the location of OBJ at the

'end'.  The times 'start' and 'end' are determined by either the

beginning and end of either argument one of a #$holdsIn expression

that the #$movesInDirection-Average assertion is wrapped, or the

beginning and ending times of OBJ.  This predicate is useful when you

wish to make the statement about the overall direction of a moving

object in spite of short term deviations in time or in space from this

overall direction.  Consider such exemplar cases as a temporally

varying direction of a fluttering butterfly or the spatially varying

course of a winding river.  However, if you need to make inferences

about the direction of motion of a temporal or spatial slice of OBJ,

consider using the stronger #$movesInDirection-Throughout.  Related

predicates include #$directionOfTranslation-Avg and

#$directionOfTranslation-Throughout which relate a

#$Movement-TranslationEvent to a direction that all #$objectMovings of

that event move in.  #$movesInDirection-Average is to be preferred

over #$directionOfTranslation-Avg in situations where the

computational cost of reifying a movement event (see

#$Movement-TranslationEvent) is not warranted.")
(comment survivalRate "(#$survivalRate CONDITION PROPORTION) means that the proportion of #$Persons who have the #$AilmentCondition CONDITION but do not die from it is PROPORTION.  In the #$ModernWesternMedicineMt, and possibly in other contexts as well, #$survivalRates are usually 5-year survival rates; that is, 5 years free of symptoms after having had the condition.")
(comment Werewolf "A mythological creature which can change form between a human and a wolflike creature.")
(comment BodyForceVector "Body forces such as gravity, centrifugal force etc.")
(comment CycArgument "The collection of all individual arguments (sets of supports) which justify individual assertions in the Cyc knowledge base. Currently, a support for an assertion can be either another Cyc assertion, or a proposition or symbol produced by one of Cyc's HL (Heuristic Level) modules. (The latter are, in effect, `virtual' assertions).")
(comment terrainAccessLimited "(#$terrainAccessLimited REGION AGENT) means that AGENT will
find it difficult if not impossible to perform an
#$LocomotionEvent-Animal within the boundaries of PLACE.")
(comment initialSituation "In Workarounds problems, (initialSituation ?ProblemMt ?InitialMt) means that InitialMt is the initial state of the problem. It corresponds to what is true at T0. The ProblemMt argument

ensures that rules can be written about how information in the InitialMt is to be inherited by the ProblemMt. ")
(comment JustificationTruth "Instances of #$JustificationTruth are attribute values which indicate the provability status of a justification for an assertion in a context.  The two most important examples are #$True-JustificationTruth and #$False-JustificationTruth.  See also #$assertionTruth.")
(comment Cisapride "The chemical compound which is used to treat peptic acid problems.")
(comment semiTransparentSituationTypePredicate "A characteristic predicated of instances of #$SituationTypePredicate.  If (#$semiTransparentSituationTypePredicate PRED) and PRED is used to express a GAF where the second, \"situation type\" argument is expressed as (#$CollectionSubsetFn #$Situation (#$TheSetOf FORMULA)) and FORMULA provably entails ENTFORMULA in CycL, then an analogous GAF holds for PRED in which the other argument or arguments are the same as before, and the 'sit type' argument is (#$CollectionSubsetFn #$Situation (#$TheSetOf ENTAILEDFORMULA)).  More collocquially, if a situation type predicate is #$semiTransparentSituationTypePredicate and relates a #$SituationType with a certain definition to an argument or arguments, then it also relates any #$SituationType whose definition is a generalization of the first to the same argument or arguments.")
(comment BroadcastOfSportsTeamEventFn "#$BroadcastOfSportsTeamEventFn

        takes as argument an instance TEAM

        of #$SportsTeam or #$SportsLeague and

        returns the collection of events that

        are broadcasts (radio or television) of

        games in which TEAM participates.

        For instance,

        (#$BroadcastOfSportsTeamEventFn

        #$MinnesotaVikings) returns the

        collection of all (radio or television)

        broadcasts of Minnesota Vikings

        games.")
(comment K-TheLetter "The letter K of the alphabet.  This is 'K' (or 'k') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.   As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterK and #$LatinSmallLetterK.")
(comment Dollar-Liberia "The main standard monetary unit of #$Liberia.")
(comment LinearPolymer "The collection of instances of #$PolymerMolecule with a completely linear structure [#$LinearStructure-Polymer].  This collection excludes those polymers which connect back on themselves (and thus are ring-shaped) and those which branch.")
(comment BiologicalGrowthEvent "A collection of events.  In each element of #$BiologicalGrowthEvent, a living structure (not necessarily a whole organism) increases in size.")
(comment TornadoADV "A collection; a specialization of #$MilitaryAircraft.  The Tornado ADV (Air Defense Variant) is a fighter aircraft designed and built by a British, Italian, and German consortium.")
(comment tensileStrengthOfSubstance "(#$tensileStrengthOfSubstance OBJ DEGREE) indicates the relative force needed to pull the tangible OBJ apart.  A higher DEGREE of #$TensileStrength indicates more force is required to pull the object apart.")
(comment assertionIsArgumentFor "(#$assertionIsArgumentFor ASSN-1 ASSN-2) means that ASSN-1 is an argument for ASSN-2. In other words, ASSN-1 is one of the assertions used in a (potential) proof for ASSN-2. So if ASSN-1 is one of 5 assertions supporting ASSN-2, (#$assertionIsArgumentFor ASSN-1 ASSN-2) should be true. 

Although this predicate could conceivably be a meta-assertion on the assertion supports for any conclusion of the inference engine, the real intent of this predicate is for the kind of entailments that only a human #$Cyclist would notice.

In a sense #$assertionIsArgumentFor means that ASSN-2 is redundant. If ASSN-1 and ASSN-2 are arguments for each other or are at about the same level of generality, then use #$redundantAssertions. 

Although not currently (Feb 98) supported, #$assertionIsArgumentFor may help the system to narrow search.  E.g. if ASSN-2 has already been used unsuccesfully in an inference path, then attempting to use ASSN-1 is less likely to be succesful. 

In general, marking redundant assertions, rather than removing them, increases the robustness of the knowledge. It is possible, for instance, to release redundant assertions without having to release more powerful arguments.  See also #$subsumingAssertions.")
(comment userDocComment "A documentation predicate. (#$userDocComment CONSTANT STRING) means that the Cyc Constant CONSTANT is explained simply, for user documentation purposes, by the description STRING.  This is used for relatively untrained users.  A #$userDocComment should not use any undue precision or Cyc jargon that would confuse an ordinary user.  This is not a substitute for #$comment.  Every constant should have a #$comment, but only certain constants need a #$userDocComment, depending on likely applications.")
(comment LandPlatform-SelfPropelled "The collection of military land platforms which are self-propelled.")
(disjointWith Exon-MolecularSegment Intron-MolecularSegment)
(comment MayModeFn "(#$MayModeFn SCRIPTTYPE CONTEXT-MT) denotes the      subcollection of SCRIPTTYPE whose instances possess the modal property denoted by \"may\", from the perspective of CONTEXT-MT.")
(comment AirborneReconnaissanceUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of military reconnaissance units that are deployed by parachute drop.")
(comment Horizon "The collection of all horizons, each being the far-off region within a few degrees of the horizontal plane, where the sky appears to join the distant landscape.   The horizon is always relative to a particular point of observation.")
(comment nearToDegree "This predicate relates a pair of spatial things and a number

representing a degree of proximity between them.  (#$nearToDegree OBJ1 OBJ2 N)

means that the #$distanceBetween OBJ1 and OBJ2 is not greater than N times 

the largest dimension of the smaller of OBJ1 and OBJ2 (where the 'smaller

object' is the one having the smaller largest dimension).  Note that if A 

is equidistant from B and C, it may be the case that (#$nearToDegree A B NUM) 

but not (#$nearToDegree A C NUM) if C is smaller than B.  Also note that if

(#$nearToDegree OBJ1 OBJ2 NUM) and NUM2 is larger than NUM, then 

(#$nearToDegree OBJ1 OBJ2 NUM2).  If the third argument is 0, the objects 

are touching (see #$touches) each other.  Other predicates that specify nearness relations are #$near, #$nearRelativeTo, #$nearForRolesInEventType, #$nearnessForRolesInEventType.")
(comment Stomachache "The condition of having a stomach ache, the internal pain in the lower half of the torso which may be generalized or somewhat localized, but does not include, for example, the pain associated with a cut on your hip.")
(comment Baritone-Singer "Each #$Baritone-Singer is a singer having an adult male voice which performs well in the middle registers.  Baritones can't sing as high as tenors or as low as basses.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-Bonk "#$AttackByComputerOperation-Bonk is the collection of uses of instances of #$BonkProgram to overwhelm a computer with corrupt instances of #$Packet-UDP.")
(comment Vesicle-Condition "The physiological condition of having a small fluid filled cavity, blister-like lesion on the skin.")
(comment resultGenlFuncArgs "(#$resultGenlFuncArgs INDFUNC N DEPFUNC) means that the collection returned by the function INDFUNC must be a spec of the collection that results from applying DEPFUNC to the Nth argument of INDFUNC.")
(comment MeatSectionWorker "Collection of people who work in the meat section usually in a grocery store.")
(comment verbPrep-TransitiveTemplate "This predicate expresses a template for the relationship between collections denoted by transitive verbs, prepositions with which they co-occur, and the semantic interpretation of the verb and particle preposition together.")
(comment Holmium "The collection of all pieces (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of holmium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment RainProcess "A specialization of #$PrecipitationProcess.  Each instance of #$RainProcess is an event in which the condensed liquid water in one or more clouds forms droplets (or ice cystals which subsequently melt in mid-air) substantial enough to fall to the surface of the planet.")
(disjointWith ProkaryoticCell EukaryoticOrganism)
(comment keConsiderationInverse "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate (q.v.) and specialization of #$keRelevantInverse (q.v.) that relates a collection to a binary predicate.  (#$keConsiderationInverse COL BINPRED) means that for any reified instance INST of COL, it should be determined whether there is anything THING such that BINPRED holds between INST and THING, and if so it is suggested that one consider asserting (BINPRED INST THING) in the Cyc Knowledge Base.  See also #$keConsiderationPreds.")
(comment uncodedLogicalFields "(#$uncodedLogicalFields ?PT ?LF) means that ?LF is one of the logical fields on the #$PhysicalDBTable ?PT, and it is meant to be interpreted literally.  I.e., the literal value for that field on a row of the table (see #$cellValue) is the same as the represented value (see #$repValue).")
(comment ChamberOfCommerce "A collection of organizations.  Any instance of #$ChamberOfCommerce is an              association consisting of businesspersons from a local community.            The main purpose is to further the business-related interests of            this community.")
(comment GameShowHost "Each #$GameShowHost is the host of a #$TVGameShow.")
(comment Vibrio-Genus "The collection of all #$Bacterium classified in the #$Vibrio-Genus.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are #$BacillusBacterium and motile bacterium with polar flagella.  In liquid media, these are motile by monotrichous or multitrichous polar flagella enclosed in a sheath; however, on a solid media, they may synthesize numerous lateral flagella.  These are #$AnaerobicBacterium facultative.  These are among the most common #$Bacterium in surface waters.  Sodium ions are a stimulator for growth and for many species they are required.")
(comment CreditRatingService "The collection of #$CommercialServiceOrganizations that rate public, private, or consumer credit ratings.  See #$creditRating.  The primary credit rating companies for country and corporate ratings are DuffAndPhelpsCompany, #$Moodys, and #$StandardAndPoors.")
(comment Methodology-StudyOfFn "The term `(#$Methodology-StudyOfFn ?FIELD)' denotes the #$FieldOfStudy in which

the subject matter studied is the question of what the methodology of the #$FieldOfStudy ?FIELD is and what it should be. (Compare #$Methodology-ActualFn.) ")
(comment Droperidol "A chemical compound which is used in tranquilization and sedation.")
(disjointWith StaticSituation MovementOrShapeChangeEvent)
(comment MediaInterviewing "A collection of events; a subset of #$Interviewing.  Every instance of #$MediaInterviewing is done by a person who is a member of a #$MediaOrganization.  The purpose of the interview is to put the information gathered into a #$MediaProduct, which will then be distributed by the mass media.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn FifthRib) HeadOfBone) "")
(comment PriceQuoteForFn "(#$PriceQuoteForFn PRODUCTTYPE) denotes the collection of all #$PriceQuoteDocuments containing quotes for prices of products of type PRODUCTTYPE.--Baxter, Jan 6, 1999")
(comment mileageDriven "The distance this vehicle has been driven.")
(comment AutomaticFirearm-RecoilOperated "The collection of #$AutomaticFirearms that use the recoil system for automatic loading and firing.  Before firing, the breechblock and barrel are locked together and held forward by its own spring.  On firing, they are  driven back together by the rearward thrust in reaction to the forward motion of the bullet and then unlocked, the pressure in the barrel now being down to  atmospheric.  The breach block continues to the rear and the empty case is  ejected.")
(comment NobleGasElementType "A specialization of #$ElementStuffTypeByNumberOfProtons.  Each instance of #$NobleGasElementType is a type of element that does _not_ readily form compounds with other types of elements.  Instances of #$NobleGasElementType are highly stable, due to the fact that they have the maximum number of electrons possible in their outer shell.  The six instances of #$NobleGasElementType are #$Helium, #$Neon, #$Argon, #$Krypton, #$Xenon, and #$Radon.")
(comment ExurbiaPopulationDensity "The population density of exuburbian areas.")
(disjointWith DeviceRunning AcademicTesting)
(comment EndingRelations "A collection of events.

Each element of #$EndingRelations is an event in which two 

instances of #$IndependentCountry sever their formal diplomatic

ties. For further information, see #$EstablishingRelations.")
(comment CycLRepresentedTerm "The collection of all denotational terms that are represented in the CycL language, instead of being defined in SubL, the underlying implementation language used by Cyc.  That is, each instance of #$CycLRepresentedTerm is either (i) an atomic term, and thus also an instance of #$CycLRepresentedAtomicTerm (q.v.), or (ii) a non-atomic term (or \"NAT\"), and has a #$CycLRepresentedTerm as its arg0 functor (the other arguments in the NAT

need not be CycL represented terms).  Thus #$CycLRepresentedTerm has as instances all #$CycLConstants, all #$CycLVariables, and all #$CycLNonAtomicTerms.")
(comment PageRangeFn "If TEXT is a text with numbered pages that is not divided into subsections and is not itself a subsection of some larger text, (PageRangeFn TEXT N M) returns the informational contents of pages numbered N through M of TEXT.  If TEXT is divided into subsections and has as its #$PageNumberingSchema the #$SimpleSequentialSchema, then (#$PageRangeFn TEXT N M) also returns the informational contents of pages N through M of TEXT.  If TEXT is divided into subsections and has as its #$PageNumberingSchema the #$SequentialWithPriviledgedSubsectionsSchema, then (#$PageRangeFn TEXT N M) returns the informational content of pages with numbers N through M in the main body of the text, disregarding the priviledged subsection or subsections. If TEXT is itself a subsection of a larger autonomous text SUPERTEXT with the #$PageNumberingSchema of #$SimpleSequentialSchema then (#$PageRangeFn TEXT N M) returns (#$PageRangeFn SUPERTEXT N M). If TEXT is itself a subsection of a larger autonomous text SUPERTEXT with the #$PageNumberingSchema of #$RepetitionBySubsectionSchema then (#$PageRangeFn TEXT N M) returns the informational contents of pages number N through M in TEXT's own internal numbering schema. And if TEXT is itself a subsection of a larger autonomous text SUPERTEXT with the #$PageNumberingSchema of #$SequentialWithPriviledgedSubsectionsSchema, then (#$PageRangeFn TEXT N M) returns (#$PageRangeFn SUPERTEXT N M) unless TEXT is one of the 'priviledged' subsections, in which case (#$PageRangeFn TEXT N M) returns the informatational contents of pages with numbers N through M in TEXT's own internal numbering schema.  In any case the function returns an instance of #$PropositionalInformationThing, which means there will always be a #$genlMt access link between a given (#$PageRangeFn TEXT N M) and (#$PageFn TEXT K) where the function is defined and where N<K<M, and also a #$genlMt access link between a given TEXT and (#$PageRangeFn TEXT N M) where the function is defined.")
(comment BattlefieldAssessment "A collection of processes.  Each element of #$BattlefieldAssessment
is a process in which an agent mentally evaluates information relevant to
current or future battlefield conditions.")
(comment maxSpeed "(#$maxSpeed VEHICLE SPEED) states that VEHICLE can go at the maximum speed SPEED when traveling in forward direction along a \"normal\" pathway, all else being equal. For #$AirTransportationDevices this is through the air when cruising - not climbing or descending - in calm weather. For #$LandTransportationDevices this is on normal flat terrain and calm weather. ")
(comment VoltageSource "A source of electrical voltage")
(comment FederalCorrectionalFacility "The collection of all US federal correctional facilities: local organizations responsible for holding convicted criminals.")
(disjointWith SportsCompetition OrganizationalTransfer)
(comment PowderedFn "`(#$PowderedFn TYPE)' denotes the collection of instances (groups of
particles) which are a powdery substance derived from an instance or instances
of TYPE, where this derivation was via an action of crushing or grinding those
instances to a powdery consistency.")
(disjointWith TimeInterval Issue)
(comment holdsInTypeOfPlace-Somewhere "(#$holdsInTypeOfPlace-Somewhere MT PLACE-TYPE) means that assertions in MT hold at least somewhere in every place (spatial region) of type PLACE-TYPE.  See also #$holdsInTypeOfPlace-Everywhere.")
(disjointWith SeatingDevice RoadVehicle)
(comment TelecommutingEvent "The collection of all situations in which someone works at home, rather than commuting to a workplace, and interacts with people and/or machines at the workplace by means of telephones, computer hookups, etc.")
(comment linkedByPath "(#$linkedByPath LOC1 LOC2) means that there is some #$Path-Simple of which the spatial locations LOC1 and LOC2 are the termini.")
(comment HigherEducationDegree "Collection of degrees granted by #$HigherEducationInstitutions. Note that it is not the case that every instance of #$HigherEducationInstitution grants every kind of #$HigherEducationDegree; for example, some instances of #$College may not grant

#$GraduateDegrees.")
(comment VeterinaryMedicalSuppliesMC "Medical supplies for use with animals.")
(comment EnvelopingCovering "The collection of coverings which envelope closely the object being      covered")
(comment MathematicalLanguage "A #$MathematicalLanguage is formalized #$Language used in  mathematics to express mathematical notions. The language of set theory,  when formalized, is an example of a mathematical language. Usually  mathematical languages include a logical language together with some mathematical constants such as '+' or '0'.")
(comment interestRateCeiling "The predicate used to state the maxiumum #$interestRate that can be charged on an adjustable rate #$MortgageAgreement (see #$AdjustableRateLoan) during the life of that loan.  (#$interestRateCeiling LOAN RATE) means that RATE is the maximum allowed interest on the LOAN, anytime during its term.")
(comment NestedDagFn "(#$NestedDagFn ?Path ?Dag) returns the dag that recursively contains ?Dag within it, at a position dictated by ?Path. Effectively the inverse functionality of #$SubDagFn, so (#$SubDagFn ?Path (#$NestedDagFn ?Path ?Dag)) = ?Dag.")
(comment Street-Residential "A normal residential area with lots of homes and no businesses or traffic lights.")
(comment UridineTriphosphate "A collection of nucleotides that are an activated precursor

to RNA synthesis.  They contain #$Uracil-Base linked to #$Ribose and

three phosphates.")
(comment ShatteringEvent "A specialization of both #$PhysicalDestructionEvent and #$Separation-Complete.  In each instance of #$ShatteringEvent, something is destroyed by being broken into a large number of pieces.  Since the salient parts of the object destroyed must be brittle (see the constant #$Brittle) in order for this to happen, fluids (such as liquid water) and elastic stuff (such as rubber at room temperature) will generally not undergo any #$ShatteringEvents.  Items which can be an #$objectActedOn in shattering events are typically made of glass, pottery, bone, plaster, or other brittle material.  Many substances, particularly solid metals and alloys, are extremely difficult to shatter.")
(comment Bridge-Military "The collection of all bridges built (temporarily) for military purposes.  Sub-collections of this collection include #$FixedBridge-Military, #$FloatingBridge-Military, and #$BridgeWithArmoredVehicle etc.")
(comment ComicBookSeries "The collection of all #$MagazineSeries that tell a story using #$ComicStrips.")
(comment PatrolBoat "The collection of boats which are intended for use in patrolling.")
(comment MassTranslationOfRNAToProtein "The collection of events in which RNA provides instructions for the generation of a large number of protein molecules.")
(comment interArgFormat5-5 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat5-5 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the fifth argument-place of PRED when PRED's fifth argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ... ARGN) in which ARG5 is an instance of COL, 
PRED's arg5 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG5' 
in the preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its 
instances for further explanation.  Note that #$interArgFormat5-5 is one of 
several \"degenerate-case\" inter-argument format predicates, in which the 
specified condition and the corresponding constraint both have to do with 
the _same_ argument-place of a given predicate.")
(comment BusinessSectionOfPeriodical "The set of sections of a periodical which are dedicated to reporting news and information for the business communicty.")
(comment MarineExpeditionaryUnit "A specialization of #$ExpeditionaryUnit-MilitarySpecialty, each instance
  of which is one of the #$subOrganizations of the #$UnitedStatesMarineCorps.
  An instance of #$MarineExpeditionaryUnit (an MEU) consists of about 2,200 instances
  of #$MarinePersonnel, and comprises a reinforced battalion, a composite aircraft
  squadron, and an MEU Service Support group.  Commanded by a colonel, an MEU is
  employed to fulfill routine forward deployments with fleets in the Mediterranean,
  the Western Pacific, and periodically, the Atlantic and Indian Oceans.  An MEU is
  deployed on up to four Naval amphibious ships.  See also #$MarineExpeditionaryForce.")
(comment Cobalt "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of cobalt.")
(comment MentalRetardation "A condition in which a person doesn't develop mentally and has much lower intelligence than average.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (RightObjectOfPairFn TenthRib) Tuberosity) "")
(comment standardEchelonSpecialtySubstructure "(#$standardEchelonSpecialtySubstructure

ORG-TYPE-BY-EGB-SUPER MIL-ORG-COL ORG-TYPE-BY-EGB-SUB

SPECIALTY-TYPE N) means that ordinarily, a unit with the #$MilitaryEchelon,

#$sovereignAllegianceOfOrg, and #$BranchOfMilitaryService of

ORG-TYPE-BY-EGB-SUPER, of the military organization class

MIL-ORG-COL can be expected to have exactly N

#$subOrganizations with #$MilitaryUnitSpecialtyType

SPECIALTY-TYPE and with the #$MilitaryEchelon, #$sovereignAllegianceOfOrg, and

#$BranchOfMilitaryService of ORG-TYPE-BY-EGB-SUB.")
(disjointWith RemovingSomething Perceiving)
(comment RegulatingGasFlow "Controlling the flow of a gas by using a tap to either open or close 

to varying degrees a portal in the container which holds that gas.")
(comment fileCopyContainsVirus "(#$fileCopyContainsVirus FILECOPY VIRUS) means that the #$ComputerFileCopy FILECOPY is infected with the #$ComputerVirus VIRUS.  More precisely, it means that FILECOPY instantiates some instance of #$ComputerCode which is source or executable code for VIRUS.")
(comment CollegeSport "The collection of all #$Sports whose instantiations are performed by competing individuals or teams who represent #$HigherEducationInstitutions and whose rules are sanctioned by such institutions and (usually) by some overarching #$Organization to which the institutions belong, such as a conference or the #$NationalCollegiateAthleticAssociation.")
(comment VisualArtifact-CW "A specialization of #$VisualWork.  Each instance of #$VisualArtifact-CW is an abstract work intended to be instantiated as an instance of #$Artifact in a manner that would permit it to be viewed. Notable instances include paintings (instantiated as instances of #$Painting-ArtForm), photographs, drawings, engravings, and sculptures.")
(disjointWith CountyGovernment USStateGovernment)
(disjointWith UnitOfFrequency UnitOfAngularAcceleration)
(comment streetCornerOf "This predicate can be used to relate a lot of land,

a street intersection it is adjacent to, and a general direction from the latter to the former.  (#$streetCornerOf LOT XING DIR) means that LOT is adjacent to 

XING and the general direction from the center of XING to the center of LOT

is DIR.  See also #$StreetCornerFn.")
(comment DNAStrand-ThreePrimeEnd "The ends of DNA strands deemed to be the 3' end because of the nucleotide polarity.")
(disjointWith Lake Stream)
(comment CruiseMissile-SAQR80 "A type of cruise missile.  According to the CSIS source document 'Creeping Proliferation Could Mean a Paradigm Shift

          in the Cost of War and Terrorism', Egypt, Libya, and Iraq are possession of many of these cruise missiles and may use the missiles as delivery vehicles for weapons of mass destruction.")
(comment SoftwareExpenseAccount "An account for the money which goes to pay for software")
(comment travelLegFromLocation "(#$travelLegFromLocation PATH FROM) means that FROM is
represented as the the starting point of PATH in the itinerary of some
#$TravelTour.  This means, among other things, that FROM is expected
to be the #$fromLocation in the traversal of PATH that is the actual
instantiation of that leg of the tour.  See also #$TourTravelLegFn.")
(comment RussianFederalGovernmentOrganization "This constant is the backbone for modelling of the organizations of the Government of Russia.")
(comment EnergyEconomicSector "The collection of all localized major groups of enterprises in which the enterprises in each such group define themselves as producers of #$EnergyStuff, and together form a major economic energy sector for the region.  For example, one instance is the group of all electric power companies in #$ElSalvador. Important sub-sectors (see #$subIndustryTypes and #$subIndustries) include: #$OilIndustry, #$CoalIndustry, #$GasIndustry.")
(comment Experimental "An attribute that describes things, methods, actions which are not yet established as standard, which are still being evaluated.")
(comment Recommendation "A collection of abstract (intangible) objects which consist of information; a subset of #$Credential.  Each element of #$Recommendation consists of a statement by some agent about the qualities of another agent, product, program, or activity.  Examples: a letter of recommendation for graduate school; a reference letter for a jobseeker; or a product endorsement.")
(comment Rial-Iran "The main standard monetary unit of #$Iran.")
(comment NetworkLayerProtocol "The collection of all #$NetworkProtocols that implement a network layer. An instance of #$NetworkLayerProtocol is responsible for routing data  to its destination. An instance of #$NetworkLayerProtocol facilitates end-to-end  transmission, as opposed to transmission between adjacent computers.")
(comment OilTerminal "The collection of #$Terminal-TransferPoints where oil

is unloaded from one form of conveyance and transferred to another (or

possibly the same) form. It will normally have storage facilities.")
(comment SoybeanPod "The fruit of the soybean plant; contains edible seeds [soybeans].")
(comment objectsObserved "(#$objectsObserved INFORMING OBJECT) means that OBJECT is observed by the performer or performers of the #$InformationGathering

event INFORMING.  Use of this predicate entails that the information

being gathered relies on an observational or visual component:

however, the information-gathering may be mediated by instrumentalities, and it is perfectly permissable for the agent doing the observing to be an instance of #$Organization or #$Group.  Also, #$objectsObserved is used

to pick out the real-world 'target' of a real-world 'observation

event'.  It is not used to represent the subjective content of the

observation.")
(comment supportedBy-Contributing "A generalization of #$supportedBy.  (#$supportedBy-Contributing OBJECT SUPPORT) means that SUPPORT contributes  to the total amount of support holding OBJECT up and maintaining its vertical position.  If SUPPORT were to be removed, then (everything else being equal) OBJECT would have less support against falling down than before. (OBJECT might even actually fall, but not necessarily.)  For example, a bridge is  #$supportedBy-Contributing each individual pile underneath it, though it is unlikely to be crucially #$supportedBy any one of them.")
(comment DaytimeWorkingHours "A specialization of #$TimeOfDay.  Each instance of #$DaytimeWorkingHours is a time interval during which most members of a working population perform their daily jobs.  Instances of #$DaytimeWorkingHours will vary in their respective durations, starting points, and ending points (see the constants #$duration, #$startingPoint, and #$endingPoint), according to which group of workers is being considered.")
(comment connected-EntireEdge "(#$connected-EntireEdge SHEET OBJ2) means that the complete edge of a #$SheetOfSomeStuff, SHEET, is #$connectedTo OBJ2.")
(comment ListeriaMonocytogenes "A collection of #$Bacterium. Each instance is rod-shaped, aerobic, parasitic, and pathogenic for humans and non-human animals, causing #$Listeriosis.")
(comment ErythemaMultiforme "A collection of #$AilmentConditions characterized by the sudden eruption of crops of red or

 violet flat spots, wheals, papules (small solid elevations), and vesicles (blisters), the

 characteristic lesions often having a concentric, or target, pattern; the skin on the palm

 of the hand and the mucous surfaces, especially the mouth and eyelids, are commonly

 involved. Erythema multiforme is believed to be a symptom complex that is secondary to a

 wide variety of underlying disease states.  (Encyclopedia Britannica)")
(disjointWith UpperLip LowerLip)
(comment SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn "(#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn COLLECTION PREDICATE TYPE) specifies the collection of all instances INSTANCE of COLLECTION for which (PREDICATE INSTANCE THING) holds for some instance (THING) of TYPE.  For example, (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn #$VehicleAccident #$damages #$Airplane) refers to airplane accidents.")
(comment AnimalCapabilityType "This is the collection of types of action which can be #$doneBy all normal adult animals in typical circumstances.  They are animal capabilities in the sense that we expect any normal adult animal to be able to do them, as opposed to the sense that some animal can do them.  Also, this is not the collection of actions which must be done by an animal, for which see #$AnimalActivity.")
(disjointWith DecontaminationProcedure-Area DecontaminationProcedure-Animal)
(comment interArg4ResultGenls "A ternary #$MetaRelation predicate for stating that a certain kind of complex, partly #$genls based relationship holds between the fourth argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned. (#$interArg2ResultGenls FUNC INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the fourth argument to FUNC, then -- regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be -- the value (if any) of that function for those arguments is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is: if INST is a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 INST ...) = VALUE, then VALUE is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  Note that, unlike (e.g.) the #$InterArgTypePredicates, #$interArg4ResultGenls _cannot_ be used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on functions.  See also the similar but more flexible quaternary #$interArgResultGenl.")
(comment Blindness "Any ailment in which an animal suffers complete or near complete loss of vision.")
(disjointWith ModernHumanResidence SubwayStation)
(disjointWith PrescriptionDrugTherapy OTCDrugTherapy)
(comment permanentlyNorthwestOf "(#$permanentlyNorthwestOf REGION-1 REGION-2) means that the #$GeographicalRegion REGION-1 is to the northwest of the #$GeographicalRegion REGION-2, when viewed in the terrestrial frame of reference.  Note that REGION-2 is therefore southeast of REGION-1; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent `southeast of'.  Example: (#$northwestOf #$GreatBritain-TheIsland StraitOfDover).")
(comment Tiger-Bengal "A collection of tigers with habitats in India as well as Nepal, Bhutan and Myanmar.  Their scientific name is Panthera tigris tigris.")
(comment BPV-Microtheory "The collection of microtheories containing information specific to the CPOF Block Party V experiment.")
(comment SkaMusic "A modern style of vocalized Jamaican popular music, which emerged in the 1950s as a blend of African-Jamaican folk music, calypso, and American rhythm and blues, notable for its shuffling, scratchlike tempo and jazzlike horn riffs on the offbeat. Precursor to #$ReggaeMusic and rock steady.")
(comment sticksInto-2D "(#$sticksInto-2D OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1, has one end inside of OBJ2 in a 2 dimensional fashion, its other end is at the edge of or outside of OBJ2.  The end of OBJ2 inside of OBJ1 bordersOn OBJ1 and is surrounded by it in two dimensions (such as the #$IndianSubcontinent and the #$IndianOcean).")
(comment CensusGroupOfAsianOrPacificIslander "The collection of persons who identified with ethnic groups of or originally found in Asia or the Pacific Islands.  Abbreviated by the U.S. Census Bureau as API.")
(comment HandballBall "The ball manipulated in a game of handball.")
(comment CruiseMissile-SSC-1B "A type of cruise missile.  According to the CSIS source document 'Creeping Proliferation Could Mean a Paradigm Shift

          in the Cost of War and Terrorism', Syria is in possession of many of these cruise missiles and may use the missiles as delivery vehicles for weapons of mass destruction.")
(comment Actinium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of actinium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.  This unit could probably just as well be called Actinium or ActiniumStuff")
(disjointWith CaspianCountry LevantCountry)
(comment ImprovementEvent "The collection of actions in which something is improved by being changed.  The improvement is from the point of view of the performer.")
(disjointWith MatterTypeByPhysicalState RelationshipType)
(comment SortingPapersToFile "Events in which papers are sorted in preparation for being filed.")
(comment numberOfSurfaces "This predicate relates an instance of #$SpatialThing to the number of distinct surfaces that it has which serve as boundaries of the object.  In other words, while the xy cross section (see #$xyCrossSection) of an object might pick out a surface, this would not count as one of the surfaces of this object.")
(comment Fornix "The collection of all fornices.  An individual #$Fornix is a unique part of a #$Brain which connects each #$Hippocampus with other parts of the #$LimbicSystem.")
(comment HostileEconomicPolicy "The collection of events where a state changes its economic policy to one that the other state(s) in the event view as hostile.  ie. In USA-China negotiations the Chinese lack of copyright/patent enforcement could be viewed as a hostile economic policy.")
(disjointWith Perceiving ChangeOfStatusEvent)
(comment ArmoredReconCarrier-VBC90 "A French armored car that used mostly for reconnaissance missions.")
(comment EchinaceaDerivedDrug "The collection of drugs which are derived from the echinacea plant.  Popular especially in Germany as a treatment for the common cold.")
(disjointWith OfficialDocument SportsCard)
(comment Smoke "Particulate matter suspended in the atmosphere, resulting from oxidation (combustion).")
(disjointWith Collision InformationBearingThing)
(comment VAX "The set of DEC VAX machines.")
(comment SupportGroupFn-PhysiologicalCondition "#$SupportGroupFn-PhysiologicalCondition takes as argument any spec of #$PhysiologicalCondition and returns the collection of all support groups for persons who have or are currently experiencing that #$PhysiologicalCondition, or for persons who bear some special relation to someone experiencing that condition.")
(comment (LeftObjectOfPairFn MainBronchus) "This NAT is weird.")
(comment rolesTemporallyExclusiveInSystemType "(#$rolesTemporallyExclusiveInSystemType SYSTEM-TYPE ROLE1 ROLE2)

means that the expectation is that the same agent cannot play ROLE1 and ROLE2 in 

#$FunctionalSystems of type SYSTEM-TYPE simultaneously.  More specifically, if

(#$rolesTemporallyExclusiveInSystemType SYSTEM-TYPE ROLE1 ROLE2) and

(#$isa SYSTEM SYSTEM-TYPE), and it #$holdsIn any time interval TEMP

that (ROLE1 SYSTEM AGENT), then it should also hold in TEMP that

(unknownSentence (ROLE2 SYSTEM AGENT)).")
(comment globalRequisiteForAnti "If (#$globalRequisiteForAnti SIT1 SIT2) and PRECON is any know propositional precondition for SIT2, then SIT1's happening is a necessary precondition for the negation of PRECON becoming true.")
(comment massNumber-Generic "This predicate is a generalization over the #$SpeechPartPredicates that express mass number.  (#$massNumber-Generic WORD STRING) means that the #$EnglishWord WORD has STRING as a mass form: either #$massNumber (the form corresponding to the #$MassNoun part of speech), #$pnMassNumber (for #$ProperMassNoun forms), or #$agentive-Mass (for #$AgentiveNoun forms).  This predicate is #$notAssertible, since it will always cash out as an assertion on one of its spec-preds.")
(comment PullingAnObjectCloser "A collection of #$PullingAnObjectAlong events in which the the #$pullee is brought closer to the #$puller due to the pulling.")
(comment USMilitaryChemicalProtectiveMask "The class of all #$ProtectiveFiltrationMasks manufactured by

the US Army during the last decade of the 20th century and the first

decade of the 21st, and issued to US Army personnel for field use.")
(comment SpermProductionEvent "The process in which sperm cells are produced by the testicles.")
(comment SquareKilometer "A measurement function used to measure area, within the metric system.")
(comment gunTakesAmmunition "(#$gunTakesAmmunition GUN AMMUNITION) indicates what type of ammunition a gun uses.  This is more detailed than merely stating the caliber size of the  bullet or shell.  For example, a M-16 uses 5.56mm NATO bullets.  A #$Mortar  uses #$MortarShells.")
(disjointWith Volatility-Physical Pressure)
(comment AccountingUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military organizations whose purpose           is to perform accounting and bookkeeping functions.")
(disjointWith Dock Terrace-Topographical)
(comment Transcription-DNAToRNA "The process whereby a DNA molecule is unwound, opened, and used to generate a complementary strand of RNA (see #$RNAMolecule), via the intermediary action of RNA polymerase enzymes.  In the case of eucaryotic organisms, the output of transcription is referred to as a primary transcript (see #$PrimaryTranscript-RNAMolecule) which in turn undergoes the processing steps of capping, polyadenylation, and splicing to produce an instance of mRNA (see #$MessengerRNA) that is then used in protein production.")
(comment SubcollectionPerformedByTypeFn "(#$SubcollectionPerformedByTypeFn EVENTTYPE AGENTTYPE) describes the collection of all instances of EVENTTYPE which are #$performedBy instances of AGENTTYPE.")
(comment ModerateThunderstormArea "The weather attribute for a location of being stormy, having stormy weather.")
(comment Band-MusicGroup "A collection of music performance organizations.  An element of #$Band-MusicGroup is a (small or large) group of musicians who play non-Classical music together on either a regular or intermittent schedule.  For example, the #$RollingStones or the University of Texas marching band -- but not the Chicago Symphony Orchestra.")
(comment CycLCanonicalizerDirective "The subcollection of #$CycLAssertions which express instructions to
the #$CycCanonicalizer.  Even though the canonicalizer may treat these as
rules, they are GAFs in the KB.  Each #$CycLCanonicalizerDirective must
have a #$CanonicalizerDirectivePredicate as its predicate.
They are relevant in the microtheory in which they are
asserted, and in specMts of that microtheory unless overridden.")
(comment VicePresidentOfResearch-Title "The #$Title for the vice president of an organization who is in charge of managing or overseeing #$Research (and usually also #$DevelopingAProduct).")
(comment Monk "Essentially the set of scholarly thoughtful, introspective clerics, who         dedicate their lives to consideration of God/gods and scholarly         devotion.")
(comment VegetableMatter "A specialization of both #$NaturalTangibleStuff and #$OrganicStuff.  Each instance of #$VegetableMatter is a piece of stuff (solid, liquid, or, improbably but conceivably, gaseous) which is a piece of vegetable material.  Important specializations of #$VegetableMatter include #$Plant and #$PlantProduct.")
(comment MaritimeClaimFn "(MaritimeClaimFn ENT) picks out the belt of sea which forms the maritime claim of some coastal entity ENT. U.N. regulations specify how countries may figure their maritime claims. Typically, a country has control over the waters, ocean bed, and subsoil of its maritime claim region, as well as to the airspace over it.")
(comment Unicorn "A mythological creature with the general size and shape of a horse, but with a horn growing out of its forehead. Unicorns are usually white.")
(comment eventOverlaps "This predicate relates overlapping events. (#$eventOverlaps EVENT1 EVENT2) means that EVENT1 and EVENT2 share a common subevent.  That is, there is a SUBEVENT such that both (#$subEvents EVENT1 SUBEVENT) and (#$subEvents EVENT2 SUBEVENT) hold.")
(comment CentrifugalForceVector "the force acting on objects pushing them outwards when they are moving in a circle")
(comment DesiresContext "The collection of all contexts which contain assertions expressing the desires of some agent or group of agents.")
(disjointWith Conveying-Generic InformationBearingThing)
(comment LeftRiverbank "The collection of left bank of a river. See #$LeftBankFn.")
(comment MultiWordForStringPred "The specialization of #$MultiWordPhrasePredicate whose instances map phrases to strings. See also #$MultiWordForFormulaPred and #$MultiWordForConstantPred.")
(comment typicalOccupationDuties "(#$typicalOccupationDuties ACTTYPE OCCTYPE) means that under

normal circumstance the a person in the occupation represented by

OCCTYPE will be expected to perform actions of type ACTTYPE, in the

course of fulfilling his or her duties.")
(comment remainsForwardBecause "(#$remainsForwardBecause RULE COMMENT) means that it is essential that RULE remain forward.  RULE should not automatically be switched to backward as part of periodic KB housecleaning procedures. The motivation for such housecleaning is that assertions take longer and longer as the number of forward rules in the kb increases.  As the knowledge base grows and applications are developed, special purpose forward rules accumulate as a result of daily KE activity.  Many of these rules should not remain forward forever.  Rather they may need to remain forward for a short time (e.g. days to weeks) during an application development phase.  Such rules should not have a #$remainsForwardBecause meta-assertion and will be automatically switched backward at periodic (monthly?)  intervals as a form of housecleaning.  Clear exemplars of rules which should have #$remainsForwardBecause assertions include rules which conclude #$arity 2 based on (#$isa ?pred #$BinaryPredicate).  More borderline positive exemplars of a #$remainsForwardBecause rules are 'documentation updating' rules.  An example of such a rule is one which puts the #$SharedNote called #$DecidingWhichInstrumentPredicateToUse on every specialization of #$instrument-Generic.  Perhaps rules like this can be periodically repropagated rather than continually forward propagated (such functionality is not curently (June 1998) available).  It may be helpful to give uniform comments for different classes of #$remainsForwardBecause rules.  For example assertions for 'documentation updating' rules might all have the COMMENT 'automatic #$SharedNotes updating.' on them.  That way, as more fine grained control over forward inference is obtained, the uniformity of such comments will aid the semi-automatic assignment of such rules to the appropriate class of forward inference.")
(comment NuclearMagneticResonance "This is the collection of instances wherein the spin states

of atomic nuclei are affected by a magnetic field in such a way that they differentially give off

energy. These different spectra provide data about the atomic make-up of the sample. This

data can be used to create images, as in #$MagneticResonanceImaging.")
(comment Omeprazole "The chemical compound which is used to treat peptic acid problems.")
(comment Pascal-UnitOfPressure "The standard unit of pressure, equivalent to one Newton per square meter.")
(comment industryFractionOfGDP "(#$industryFractionOfGDP GE COL THING NR) means that NR is the quotient of the monetary value of the goods and services produced by the specialization of #$Industry-Localized COL within the #$GeopoliticalEntity GE during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING (as dividend) and the monetary value of GE's total domestic production of goods and services (its gross domestic product) during the temporal extent of THING (as divisor).  A country would be a typical instance of GE.  COL can range from a broad economic sector, such as agriculture, manufacturing, or services to a more specific segment of the economy such as the automobile industry.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  For example, to express the fact that services accounted for 41 percent of Saudi Arabia's gross domestic product for 1994, we can say (#$industryFractionOfGDP #$SaudiArabia #$ServiceEconomicSector (#$YearFn 1994) (#$Percent 41)).  See also #$grossDomesticProduct and #$productionValueOfIndustryDuring.")
(comment L-TheLetter "The letter L of the alphabet.  This is 'L' (or 'l') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.   As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterL and #$LatinSmallLetterL.")
(comment ShippingLane-International "The collection of shipping lanes that are commonly considered (under international law) to be freely available for marine traffic from all nations.  Such lanes are not subregions of (#$TerritorialSeaFn COUNTRY) for any instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity, COUNTRY.  See also #$InternationalOceanLawCOC.")
(comment PolynucleotideStrand "The collection of all sequentially linked chains of instances of
#$Nucleotide. The individual strands of a DNA helix-shaped molecule are
instances of this collection.")
(comment BiologicalAbsorptionEvent "The process in which objects are taken into some living structure across some membrane.")
(disjointWith BodyOfWater Frost)
(comment E-3-AWACS "The collection of E-3 AWACS aircraft.  The primary function of these aircraft is airborne surveillance and command, control and communications.")
(comment PrimaryInfectionSite "#$PrimaryInfectionSite is the attribute that describes first sites of

#$Infection. In a given instance of #$Infection, instances of #$OrganismPart where pathogenic organisms first establish

themselve shortly after their entry in the host's body will have this attribute. It is the usual process of an invasive infection that pathogens multiply in those first parts affected, and then spread into the body's host until they reach another part where to establish themselve, see #$SecondaryInfectionSite in this case. In instances of #$BacterialInfection, see also

#$Bacteremia, for the event during which bacteria are travelling the body's host.")
(comment ComputerGameProgram "An instance of #$ComputerProgramTypeByFunction. Each instance of #$ComputerGameProgram is a computer program which is such that one can play games (see #$Game) with running copies of it.")
(comment LandPlatform-Towed "The collection of military land platforms which are not self-propelled; they are usually towed into place by another vehicle.")
(comment Exon-MolecularSegment "The collection of all #$molecularSubComponents of

#$PolynucleotideMolecules that instantiate nucleotide sequences which

code for protein-specifying amino acid sequences when spliced together

in a #$MessengerRNA molecule.")
(comment IFVArmoredCavalryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of cavalry units equipped with Infantry Fighting Vehicles.")
(comment OvarianCyst "An abnormal sac-like growth in a mammal's ovary.")
(comment FractalRepresentation "A fractal representation is the result of applying a fractal function to some data (numbers) and displaying the results in a visual representation")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-CorruptionOfInformation "#$AttackByComputerOperation-CorruptionOfInformation is a subset of #$AttackByComputerOperation and #$AttackOnIBT.  It is the collection of all electronic attacks whose primary purpose is the corruption of the information of the #$ComputationalSystem under attack.")
(comment Pustule-Condition "A collection of the condition of having #$Pustule-Objects, which are collections of pus within or beneath the epidermis, most often in a hair follicle or sweat pore.")
(comment DayTrading "The collection of #$StockTrading activities in which the buyer sells stock held for a very short period of time - usually less than a day - in an effort to make a large profit very quickly.")
(comment ServiceStationAttendant "People who work in a gas station.")
(comment Morphologist "A #$Linguist specializing in #$Morphology")
(comment Erbium "The collection of all pieces (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of erbium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment DownwardsFn "This function, applied to a #$TopAndBottomSidedObject, returns the
exact direction its bottom is facing in the
implicit frame of reference defined by the object.")
(comment enables-ImpartsSkills "This predicate expresses the notion of 'enabling' in the sense of
furnishing to someone the skills she needs for the performance of a certain
type of action. This is the sense in which training or education may be
enabling factors in a person's life. Therefore, (#$enables-ImpartsSkills
SIT AGENT ACT_TYPE) means that SIT causes AGENT to have skills sufficient
for the successful performance of tokens of ACT_TYPE, assuming that the
circumstances of SIT are favorable. In essence, SIT causes AGENT to be
#$skillCapableOf ACT_TYPE: SIT cause AGENT to be in a certain state, the
state we can label as 'having skills sufficient for ACT_TYPE'. The
assumption that circumstances be favorable is necessary because even a
skilled agent would not be expected to perform successfully if the general
circumstances were unfavorable.")
(comment Snowflake "A specialization of #$PrecipitationParticle.  Each instance of #$Snowflake is a frozen water crystal emitted by a cloud during an instances of #$SnowProcess (q.v.).")
(comment AlternativeRockMusic "A specialization of #$RockMusic, #$AlternativeRockMusic covers a variety of styles through which it's hard to trace many common threads.  Named so as to distinguish itself from (at least) pop- and dance-oriented Rock, #$AlternativeRockMusic nevertheless made up a significant portion of the most popular #$RockMusic during the 1990s.")
(comment Carving "A collection of events.  In each #$Carving, the shape of an object is changed by removing pieces of it, usually with some kind of tool.  Some instances of #$Carving are also instances of #$IBOCreation (like carving a statue of someone), in which some image or information is encoded into the product; but not all are.")
(comment TalkShowHost "Each #$TalkShowHost is the host of a #$TVTalkShow or #$RadioTalkShow.")
(disjointWith CreditRatingService FinancialCompany)
(comment PassingAResolution "The collection of all events in which a governing body with nominally legislative powers passes an agreement resolving to take some kind of action. The body may be a formally empowered legislature, or an informal committee or group of agents, representing one or several interests.  Most legislative resolutions characterize themselves as such with formal language.")
(comment FourierTransform "This is the collection of Fourier Transforms of functions. A Fourier Transform of a function is a way of representing the function as an integral of particularly well-behaved functions based on trigonometric functions, or sometimes as a sum of such.")
(comment PrescriptionDrugSample "Instances are samples of prescription drugs.  Each instance will be #$isa some #$PrescriptionDrugSampleType (some fully-specified #$FormalProductType which has a #$NationalDrugCode, etc.), but this collection and its subsets are not necessarily PrescriptionDrugSampleTypes.")
(comment cohesivenessOfObject "(#$cohesivenessOfObject OBJ DEGREE) indicates how tightly a tangible object OBJ coheres.  A higher value of DEGREE means that it is harder to separate away chunks from the object. Degrees of #$Cohesiveness may be indicated using a #$GenericValueFunction (e.g. 

(#$MediumAmountFn #$Cohesiveness).")
(disjointWith MovementOrShapeChangeEvent StrictlyMentalEvent)
(comment ContactInfoString "A specialization of #$IDString.  Each instance of #$ContactInfoString is a character string that conveys information about how to contact an agent or a place (see #$ContactInformation).  Specializations include #$PostalCode, #$DomainName, and #$PhoneNumber.")
(comment CountryBorder "The collection of all borders and politically and socially significant border sections of all countries.  Note that this is a smaller class than #$GeopoliticalBorder, which includes the boundaries of other entities besides countries that are mandated by international treaty and law.")
(comment (RightObjectOfPairFn (PartTypeFn ThirdThoracicVertebra VertebralTransverseProcess)) "")
(comment RaidVehicle "The collection of vehicles intended to be used in military or police raids.")
(comment ProvincialPark-Canada "A collection of parks.  An element of #$ProvincialPark-Canada is a park which is managed by the government of the Canadian province in which it is located.")
(comment ListWithoutRepetition "A specialization of #$List.  An instance LIST of #$List is also an instance of #$ListWithoutRepetition just in case each of the members of LIST occurs in only one member-position in LIST.")
(disjointWith AngularDistance Volatility-Physical)
(comment Bun "A bread bun of some type.")
(comment FighterPlane-F16 "The collection of a type of aircraft, used widely and in a variety of combat  roles. Flown by U.S. AirForce, Air National Guard, Air Force Reserve.  Also flown by air  forces of a significant number of European, Asian, and South American countries.  Produced in U.S., #$Belgium, #$Netherlands, and #$Turkey.")
(comment TerritorialSeaFn "(#$TerritorialSeaFn GEO_ENTITY) picks out the region of the sea designated as the territorial sea of GEO_ENTITY, in accordance with U.N provisions. An entity's [see #$GeopoliticalEntity] territorial sea must be adjacent to its coastline, and cannot be more than 12 nautical miles wide (as of the late 20th Century). The territorial sea of an entity is not included as part of that entity's actual area.")
(disjointWith EmploymentTermination AcademicTesting)
(comment WithdrawingARepresentative "Events in which an organization or  individual withdraws  (one or more) of its/his/her representatives from another organization, conference, etc.  Examples:  a country calling home  its ambassador from another country, a company  ordering its representatives to leave a conference or a negotiating  session.  Instances of #$WithdrawingARepresentative frequently involve a #$Translation-LocationChange, as the ambassador leaves the country, the lawyer leaves the place of negotiations, etc.  (But sometimes merely having a representative refuse to show up to a meeting is sufficient.) Such events have the individual or organization being represented as their #$directingAgent. Unilateral decisions to leave by the representative herself/themselves are not  instances of #$WithdrawingARepresentative.")
(comment MilitaryThreatAnalysis "A collection of subevents of #$BattlefieldAssessment.  Each instance of 

#$MilitaryThreatAnalysis is an instance of #$Evaluating in which what is evaluated is the military threat posed by enemy forces. Subevents include #$AssessingEnemyStrength,

#$AssessingEnemyCOA, and #$AssessingEnemyPlan.")
(comment MissileLauncher-Manpack "The Manpack launching platform that is used to fire a #$AntiTankWeapon-M47Dragon")
(comment ElectricalComponent "A specialization of both #$ElectricalDevice and #$PhysicalPartOfObject.  Each instance of #$ElectricalComponent is an #$ElectricalDevice which is normally considered to be a part of some larger, more clearly distinguished #$PhysicalDevice (for example, clearly distinguished in the sense that it is sold or moved as a unit).  Each instance of  #$ElectricalComponent must be connected with other parts in order to perform its #$primaryFunction.")
(comment USCircuitCourtOfAppeals "The collection of all US Federal Appeals Courts, as defined by the United States Code.  Such courts are subOrganizations of the #$USJudicialBranch.")
(comment ancestorWritingSystem "Prior writing system which influenced the development of this one")
(comment SurfaceArea-TopSurfaceFn "This function denotes the total area of the top surface of an object (the surface area of the top, not of the sides and underside); it applies to 3-D objects and to 2-D objects.  If a 2-D object is deemed to have a top surface this function will refer to its area.  This function would be used to refer to the surface area of a lake, for example. (See also #$SurfaceArea-WholeSurfaceFn.)")
(disjointWith Nothing Nothing)
(comment IgneousRock "Frozen lava; i.e. solid volcanic rock.")
(comment PestControlLicense "a license issue by an appropriate local authority (often city or county) allowing the holder to work as a pest control worker.")
(disjointWith DiplomaticAction ViolentAction)
(disjointWith MathematicalObject Issue)
(comment keWeakSuggestionInverse "(#$keWeakSuggestionInverse COL BIN-PRED) means that for
every instance INST of COL, it is weakly suggested that there exist
some VALUE such that (BIN-PRED VALUE INST) is known in the KB.")
(disjointWith SeatingDevice AirTransportationDevice)
(comment SpaceMission "This is the collection of planned endeavors wherein a spacecraft of some sort is

sent either into Earth orbit or into interplanetary space. Often the same name

is used to refer both to the mission and to the craft involved in the mission.")
(comment MovieSoundtrack "The collection of all #$AudioConceptualWorks that distill either 1) all of the sound intended for a #$Movie-CW (an instantiation of which the audience at a MoviePerformance hears) or 2) are essentially identical in sonic content to all or part of soundtracks of type 1, such as is instantiated in a #$RecordedSoundProduct such as a CD.")
(comment KangarooShaped "#$KangarooShaped is the shape attribute defined by the typical shape of a kangaroo (#$Kangaroo).")
(comment CycIntegratedKnowledgeBase "#$CycIntegratedKnowledgeBase is a specialization of #$CycKB.  Each instance of #$CycIntegratedKnowledgeBase contains part of the information in the full Cyc knowledge base.")
(comment CollegeInUniversity-NonDegreeGranting "Collection of colleges that are named parts of universities which serve various academic, social, and administrative functions but which do not grant degrees.  Trinity College at Cambridge University is an example of such a college.")
(comment DietarySupplement "A manufactured substance people take to supplement their diets.  Not normally considered food.")
(comment Covering-Object "The collection of all objects designed or evolved to be used as coverings for other objects. The intended purpose could be to shelter or protect the covered object, or even just to serve a decorative function. Examples include paint, #$Tile, #$Wigs, #$Carpets, and #$Eyelids.")
(comment USDollarFn "A unary function, which takes an #$Integer NR as its argument, by means of which one can specify a United States dollar -- that is, a function belonging to the collection #$UnitOfMoney -- having the value of a dollar in the year NR.  For example, ((#$USDollarFn 1987) 20) denotes $20 in 1987 US dollars.  Because of inflation ((#$USDollarFn 1997) 20) is worth less than ((#$USDollarFn 1987) 20).  See also the more general #$CurrencyOfDateFn.")
(comment Resources "The collection of all #$Resources consists in things needed for carrying  a task or running a system. Resources include financial resources, energy resources, raw materials, information, infra-structure and so on.")
(comment Street-Urban "A typical busy street in an urban area.")
(comment Nucleoside "A collection of compounds obtained by the partial hydrolysis

of #$PolynucleotideMolecules.  These contain a purine or pyrimidine base linked

to either #$Ribose, and thus forming ribosides, or #$Deoxyribose, and

thus forming deoxyribosides.  Essentially, these compounds are

#$Nucleotides without the phosphorus group.")
(disjointWith ShatteringEvent LosingALeaf)
(comment (HobbyFn-Field Astronomy) "The collection of

     all instances of (#$PracticeFn #$Astronomy)

    that are also instances of #$HobbyActivity.  In

 other words, it is the collection of the events

 in which one studies and practices #$Astronomy

 as a hobby.")
(comment FixedBridge-Military "The collection of military bridges which are fixed, as opposed to floating.  Sub-collections of this collection include #$HeavyDrySupportBridge, #$M3MediumGirderBridge and #$BaileyBridge-Military, etc.")
(comment Advising "A collection of events, in which an #$IntelligentAgent A            tells another #$IntelligentAgent B what A thinks B should do,            especially when A knows more than B does about something.")
(comment Leptospirceae-Family "A collection of #$Bacterium in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These are flexible helical cells.  These #$Bacterium are motile, #$AerobicBacterium, chemoorganotrophs, and have two periplasmic flagella that do not overlap in the central region.  These utilize long chain fatty acids or alcohols instead of carbohydrates for carbon and energy.")
(comment PatrolBoat-River "The collection of boats which are intended for use in patrolling on rivers.")
(comment PersonnelDocumentation "The collection of all written material that has as it's primary informational component `personnel information': number of employees, their qualifications, their salaries, their performance reviews, etc.  This refers to the #$InformationBearingObjects.")
(comment InfrastructureIndustry "This collection includes those industries whose primary function is to make  #$InfrastructureProducts. Also, the overall product of some national industries,  e.g. a #$BankingIndustry or #$TelecommunicationsIndustry, constitutes an   #$InfrastructureProduct, hence these are InfrastructureIndustries.")
(comment Chlorine "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby 

molecules) of chlorine. Chlorine is normally found in gaseous form, and is often used

to purify water, and as a bleaching or disinfecting agent.")
(comment Asthma "A chronic disorder characterized by wheezing, coughing and difficulty in breathing.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn FifthRib) Tuberosity) "")
(comment AssistantChiefOfStaff-CivilMilitaryOperations "The collection of instances of  #$CoordinatingStaffMember-USArmy 
with responsibility for all matters concerning civil-military operations.")
(comment UnitOfMeasureTypeByPrefix "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$UnitOfMeasure whose instances are all of the same prefix.")
(disjointWith SeparationEvent FusionEvent)
(comment EyeProcedure-Surgical "Surgery on a patient's eyes.")
(comment Fin-Artifact "This is the collection of swimming and diving fins, rubber devices worn on

the feet to help propell a person through the water.")
(comment CanadianProvince "The collection of all the #$Provinces of #$Canada.")
(comment TrajectoryThroughWater "The collection of all trajectories of underwater motions (#$Movement-TranslationEvents that go entirely through water).   An #$objectMoving with such a #$Trajectory is immersed in, and supported by, the water.  Thus it excludes a #$SolidSurfaceTrajectoryThroughWater and a #$WaterSurfaceTrajectory.  For pre-designated or customary #$Path-Generics through water (e.g. submarine designated paths, sea lanes and corridors), use #$PathThroughWater.  For trajectories of objects floating on the surface, use #$WaterSurfaceTrajectory.")
(disjointWith UnitOfFrequency UnitOfAcceleration)
(comment assertionDirection "An #$AssertionDescriptorPredicate that 
is used to state that a given #$CycLAssertion has a certain inference 
\"direction\", which indicates something about how and when the assertion 
can be used in inferences by the Cyc system. (#$assertionDirection ASSERTION DIRECTION) means that ASSERTION has DIRECTION as its #$CycLAssertionDirection (q.v.).  DIRECTION is normally #$Backward-AssertionDirection (q.v.) when 
ASSERTION is a rule and #$Forward-AssertionDirection (q.v.) when ASSERTION is 
a ground atomic formula (or \"GAF\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence).  Note 
that a CycL sentence is given a direction at the time of its assertion to the 
Knowledge Base, and this fact _need_not_ in general be reflected in another, 
#$assertionDirection GAF's being asserted (as that would of course lead to an infinite regress).")
(comment Ripping "Generic ripping events, in which some tangible object is pulled apart in some way.")
(comment NuclearWeaponResearchFacility "The collection of instances of 

#$ResearchFacility 

(buildings or other type of construction) 

used to perform #$Research

 on #$NuclearWeapons technology.")
(comment NucleotideChain-FivePrimeEnd "This is the collection of all 5' chain ends of nucleotide chains as determined by the orientation of the component nucleotides, this nomenclature is typically applied to DNA strands and RNA strands.  Important specializations include the 5' ends of DNA strands and the 5' ends of various types of RNA-Molecules.")
(comment Iceberg "The stuff that floats in the ocean near the polar ice caps.  The water in icebergs in liquid form would have a slightly different salinity than #$Sea water.")
(comment natArgumentsEqual "(#$natArgumentsEqual NAT1 NAT2) means that the

arguments of NAT1 and NAT2 unify.  For example,  (#$natArgumentsEqual (#$FemaleFn #$Dog) (#$MaleFn #$Dog).  More precisely, (#$and (#$termOfUnit NAT1 (FUNCTION1 . ARGS)) (#$termOfUnit NAT2 (FUNCTION2 . ARGS))) implies  (#$natArgumentsEqual NAT1 NAT2).")
(comment CruiseMissile-SSN2 "A type of cruise missile.  According to the CSIS source document 'Creeping Proliferation Could Mean a Paradigm Shift

          in the Cost of War and Terrorism', Egypt, Libya, and Iraq are in possession of many of these cruise missiles and may use the missiles as delivery vehicles for weapons of mass destruction.")
(comment Diazepam "The chemical compound which is used as a sedative.")
(comment TaxExpenseAccount "An account for the money which goes for paying state taxes.")
(comment MediaTransferEvent "A collection of #$Events; a subset of #$MassCommunicating.  In every instance of #$MediaTransferEvent, a #$ConceptualWork is distributed to the public as a collection of #$InformationBearingThings (IBTs). Accordingly, every instance of #$MediaTransferEvent has two #$subEvents: (1) an instance of #$IBTGeneration-Replication, in which the IBTs are produced, and (2) an instance of #$TransferOut, in which the IBTs are distributed.  Important subsets of #$MediaTransferEvent are #$PrintCirculationEvent and #$MediaTransmitting.  In #$PrintCirculationEvents, the generated IBTs are #$HardcopyInformationBearingObjects, and the replication subEvent precedes the distribution subEvent.  In #$MediaTransmitting, the IBTs are #$InformationBearingWavePropagations, and the replication subEvent is the same as the distribution subEvent.  See also #$ConceptualWork and #$MediaProduct.")
(comment LeadersOfMovementFn "#$LeadersOfMovementFn takes as its argument

 some instance of #$ScriptType and returns the

  collection of

  #$Leaders of those involved in that #$ScriptType.")
(comment NetworkProtocol "#$NetworkProtocol is the collection of all protocols for communication over computer networks. Many of the protocols governing communication over the #$Internet find expression in so called \"Request For Comment\" documents (see #$RequestForComments-Internet).")
(comment OilTanker "The collection of tanker ships intended to be used for replenishment of petroleum products to other ships.")
(comment BlackPeppercorn "The single-seeded fruit of the black pepper vine. when dried, it can be ground up and used as a flavoring.")
(comment PolishingSomething "A specialization of #$Rubbing.  In each instance of #$PolishingSomething, a surface of an object is made smooth and glossy by rubbing that surface.")
(comment LivecamBroadcasting "A collection of events. In every instance of #$LivecamBroadcasting, a live visual image is recorded on electronic media and transmitted via the Internet.")
(comment Cytoplasm "The collection of all cytoplasm, material found in cells outside of the nucleus and within the plasma membrane.")
(comment sponsors "(#$sponsors SPONSOR BENEFICIARY) means that #$Agent-Generic SPONSOR sponsors #$Agent-Generic BENEFICIARY in some instance of #$Action.  For example, (#$sponsors SubaruOfAmericaInc RainbowEndowment), since SubaruOfAmericaInc provides funding for some of the RainbowEndowment's activities.")
(comment genQuestion "The Common Lisp format string ARG3 can be applied to the argument list ARG4 to generate a question for the Cyc Relation ARG1 when all the arguments are filled except the argument indicated by ARG2. For example, when applied to (#$movieActors #$DieHard-TheMovie :WHO) it can generate the question 'Who acted in Die Hard?'")
(comment MammalCapabilityType "This is the collection of types of action which can be done by any normal adult #$Mammal in typical circumstances, as opposed to types of action which can be done by only some mammals.  For example, #$Breathing is an instance, though #$Flying-FlappingWings is not, because all mammals breathe but only some fly.")
(comment MobileNetwork "#$MobileNetwork is a kind of communications network that connects mobile devices like #$CellularTelephone to 'fixed' communications networks.")
(comment tourTransits "(tourTransits TOUR MOVETYPE) means that a #$Movement-TranslationEvent of type MOVETYPE is supposed to occur as a #$subEvents of the TOUR.")
(comment freeSpaceContentAround "The slot equivalent of #$FreeSpaceContentAroundFn")
(comment DecontaminationProcedure-Area "The collection of all activities wherein one tries to decomtaminate #$GeographicalRegions that have been exposed to something #$Toxic.")
(comment Deafness "Any ailment in which an animal suffers complete or near complete loss of hearing.")
(comment contradictorySentence "A unary predicate which pertains to instances of #$CycLSentence. (#$contradictorySentence FORMULA) states that FORMULA is a CycL formula which although being both syntactically and semantically well-formed is known to be false because it contradicts existing knowledge.  Note that this is stronger than #$unknownSentence, which states that a formula is not currently known to be true.  For example, (#$contradictorySentence (#$isa #$Canada #$Person)).  See also #$trueSentence and #$rejectedSentence.")
(disjointWith PathArtifact SubwayStation)
(comment permanentlyNortheastOf "(#$northeastOf REGION-1 REGION-2) means that the #$GeographicalRegion REGION-1 is to the north-east of the #$GeographicalRegion REGION-2, when viewed in the terrestrial frame of reference.  Note that REGION-2 is therefore southwest of REGION-1; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent `southwest of'.  Example: (#$northeastOf #$LakeOntario #$LakeErie).  To refer to instances of #$SpatialThing-Localized that can move, use the more general #$northeastOf.")
(comment SewingNeedle "The collection of #$Needles used in instances of #$Sewing, including              instances of #$SewingByHand and #$SewingWithASewingMachine.")
(comment Tiger-Siberian "A collection of tigers with habitats in Siberia and Manchuria.  Their scientific name is Panthera tigris altaica.")
(comment BPV-QueryMtFn "(#$BPV-QueryMtFn REPORT-MT) is a microtheory useful as an mt in which to ask queries related to the CPOF Block Party V SALUTE report the content of which is represented in REPORT-MT. (#$BPV-QueryMtFn REPORT-MT) will be a spec-mt of the #$BPV-QueryMt, REPORT-MT, and any other SALUTE report mts concurrent with REPORT-MT (see #$bpv-ConcurrentMicrotheories).")
(comment CreditCardFraud "The collection of all events in which someone knowingly and intentionally buys something with a credit card or credit card number that does not legally belong to them.")
(comment ServingAirPassenger "This is the task performed by flight attendants. 

It overlaps with the task of waiters, ushers, etc.

One major difference is that flight attendants also give orders,

such as:  'Fasten your seatbelt'. ")
(comment Basketball-Ball "The ball used in playing Basketball (the game).")
(comment Su-20-Fighter "#$The collection of a type of Russian fighter plane.")
(comment Cesium "A piece (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of cesium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(disjointWith WesternEuropeanCountry CaspianCountry)
(comment MarineCorpsFn "(#$MarineCorpsFn COUNTRY) 

 denotes the instance of #$MarineCorps that belongs to COUNTRY.")
(disjointWith AnoxygenicPhotosynthesis OxygenicPhotosynthesis)
(comment Second-UnitOfAngularMeasure "A unit to measure the size of angles.  60 seconds = 1 minute (#$Minute-UnitOfAngularMeasure)")
(disjointWith MatterTypeByPhysicalState WavePropagationType)
(comment WaitingOnATable "Waiting on a table starts with the waitperson taking an order.  Next the meal is prepared (this is not one of the #$subEvents of #$WaitingOnATable).  Then the meal is served.  The last of the #$subEvents is paying.  Eating the meal is not a subEvent but starts after the meal is served.")
(comment suffrageAge "(#$suffrageAge PLACE AGE) means that #$citizens of PLACE are legally able to vote when they reach AGE.")
(disjointWith Injury-Object HaploidCell)
(comment ImplementEmbargo "The collection of events where the acting state begins an embargo against anothe state or group of states.")
(comment statusAffected "(#$statusAffected EVT AGT-1 AGT-2 RELN) means that in the #$ChangeOfStatusEvent EVT, the relation RELN between the agents AGT-1 and AGT-2 is changed somehow (depending on the kind of #$ChangeOfStatusEvent).")
(comment hydrogenBondBetween "(#$hydrogenBondBetween CHEMOBJ1 CHEMOBJ2) means that at least one hydrogen bond exists between CHEMOBJ1 and CHEMOBJ2.  If both CHEMOBJ1 and CHEMOBJ2 are atoms a single hydrogen bond exists between them.")
(comment Shroud-BoatPart "One of the lines leading usually in pairs from a ship's mastheads to give lateral support to the masts.")
(comment CharacterToken "The collection of physical representations of individual 

  abstract characters.  More precisely, #$CharacterToken is a collection 

  each of whose instances is a specific physical representation, within 

  some communication convention, of some particular instance of 

  #$Character-Abstract.  (Alternatively, each instance can be viewed 

  as representing an instance of #$CharacterString consisting of only 

  one character.)  Instances of #$CharacterToken come in at least 

  three basically different forms: #$CharacterToken-Inscribed 

  (e.g. shapes written down or printed on paper, drawn on a wall, carved 

  on a tree trunk, chiseled onto stone, displayed on a computer monitor, 

  or skywritten by airplanes), #$CharacterToken-Sounded (sound 

  events that might be produced by a human voice, loudspeaker, 

  or other apparatus), and #$CharacterToken-ElectroMagnetic 

  (which can be stored in RAM or on magnetic diskettes and can

  be transmitted via wires or as radio signals).  Abstract 

  characters are inherently neither inscriptional nor sonic nor

  electromagnetic, so the same character can be represented by 

  tokens of these different forms.  See also #$tokensCharacter.")
(comment MemorialDay-US "The instance of #$Holiday commemorating the sacrifices of American soldiers in defending the United States.")
(comment Zyban "The colleciton of drug products called #$Zyban designed to help users quit smoking.  Zyabn does not  control #$Nicotine.")
(comment suggestedTourDayActivities "(#$suggestedTourDayActivities TOUR DAY ACTIVITY) relates the

TOUR's suggested ACTIVITY to the DAY in which the participants have

free time.")
(comment LightTank "The collection of military vehicles that fall into the light tank category.")
(comment MushroomCloud "The collection of all mushroom-shaped dust clouds.  The mushroom cloud is the characteristic signature of a ground-level atomic blast, but can be caused by any blast of sufficient intensity.")
(disjointWith SportsPenalizing InformationBearingThing)
(comment BridalMagazineSeries "The collection of all #$MagazineSeries which contain information for planning a #$WeddingEvent-Generic.  These magazines generally include many pictures of #$BridalGowns.")
(comment BuyingADrink "A subset of #$Buying. In each instance of #$BuyingADrink, a person purchases one or more beverages. The purchased beverages usually come in open containers (such as drinking glasses, cups, or opened bottles), although they sometimes come in containers with lids (for instance, when one purchases a cup of coffee to go). Each instance of #$BuyingADrink includes a sub-event in which the beverage is served to the buyer. Examples include buying a cup of coffee at a coffee shop and buying a cocktail at a bar.")
(comment SeriesWithoutRepetition "A #$SeriesWithoutRepetition is a #$Series in which each member occurs only once.")
(comment preconditionFor-SitProp "#$preconditionFor-SitProp is used to state a situational precondition for a proposition's being veridical. (#$preconditionFor-SitProp SIT PROP) means that unless the situation SIT 'occurs' or 'obtains', the proposition PROP won't be true.")
(comment Braking "Braking, using either a hand brake, an emergency brake, or a foot brake.")
(comment InternalFertilizationEvent "fertilization of an egg by a sperm within the body of one of the parent actors, usually the female.")
(comment MachineGun-M60 "The collection of all M60 machine guns.  It fires the standard NATO  7.62 mm round and is used as a general support crew-served weapon. It has a  removable barrel which can be easily changed to prevent overheating. The  weapon has an integral, folding bipod and can also be mounted on a folding  tripod.")
(disjointWith Voltage Pressure)
(comment AdministrativeSupportUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military organizations dedicated to           providing support for administrative processes.")
(disjointWith Garden Dock)
(comment AnalogyMatchFn "(#$AnalogyMatchFn STRING) denotes the #$AnalogyMatch which is referred to by the name STRING in the MAC-FAC analogy reasoning system.  See also #$matchBetween and #$bestMapping.")
(comment DataMicrotheory "A specialization of #$DeclarativeContext (q.v.).
An instance of #$DataMicrotheory contains information about particular
#$Individuals of a certain kind (such as specific #$Persons, #$Organizations, 
#$GeographicalRegions, or #$ConceptualWorks).  Data microtheories thus 
typically contain mostly GAFs (see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence) and few
rules.  For example, #$PeopleDataMt contains lots of information about 
individual #$Persons, but no rules about persons generally.  Contrast with 
#$GeneralMicrotheory.")
(comment adjSemTrans "(#$adjSemTrans ADJ NUM FRAME TRANS) means that the translation of word sense number NUM of ADJ, appearing with subcategorization frame FRAME, is TRANS.")
(disjointWith Decrypting Transcription-DNAToRNA)
(comment turnRadius "(#$turnRadius VEHICLE RADIUS) is the minimum achievable radius of the circle that is partially traversed when VEHICLE is #$Turning. For #$AirTransportationDevices this is for turns in a horizontal plane; a vertical turn (as in a looping) is not expressed as a predicate. ")
(comment Advice-IBT "The collection of all #$InformationBearingThings whose information content is advice. An #$Advice-IBT is the #$communicationToken in any act of #$Advising.")
(comment DefaultMonotonicPredicate "A collection of predicates.  Each instance of #$DefaultMonotonicPredicate is a predicate whose use as the predicate of a locally asserted ground formula causes that formula to be entered, by default, as :MONOTONIC.  Examples: #$isa, #$genls, #$disjointWith, #$equals, #$arity, #$arg1Isa.")
(comment indicatedProduct "(#$indicatedProduct PRSN PROD-TYPE) means that #$ProductType PROD-TYPE is positively indicated as a purchase for the #$Person PRSN. In contrast to #$defaultSuitableProduct, which can be used to make assertions about a #$ProductType's suitability for a recipient in the absence of any positive evidence, #$indicatedProduct should be used only if there is some positive evidence for a #$ProductType's suitability. Thus, this predicate is a #$genlPreds of #$explicitlyIndicatedProduct, #$inputIndicatedProduct, and #$inferenceIndicatedProduct, but not of #$defaultSuitableProduct.")
(comment CycLReformulatorDirective "The subcollection of #$CycLAssertions which express rules or instructions to
the #$CycLReformulator.  Even though the reformulator may treat these as
rules, they are GAFs in the KB.  Each #$CycLReformulatorDirective must
have a #$ReformulatorDirectivePredicate as its predicate.
They are relevant in the microtheory in which they are
asserted, and in specMts of that microtheory unless overridden.
For meta-directives, the convention is that the #$CycLReformulatorDirective
argument comes last.")
(comment Gliding "The collection of all instances of #$Locomotion-Air in which the #$primaryObjectMoving does not expend significant energy to go faster or higher, although energy may be expended to maintain tautness of its wings, etc.. The movement of air particles under it slow its fall or even push it upwards, while the pull of gravity is translated into forward motion. Such flight generally cannot be sustained for arbitrary lengths of time. The #$primaryObjectMoving may be an animal or other natural object, or an #$Artifact.")
(comment CharacterMode-ElectroMagnetic "A specialization of #$CharacterMode each instance of    which is the collection of all of the electromagnetic character    tokens of a some particular abstract character.  Examples    include the collection of all electromagnetic tokens (see   #$CharacterToken-ElectroMagnetic) of the numeral '0'.")
(comment ChiefExecutiveOfficer "A collection of people (a subset of #$Person). The #$ChiefExecutiveOfficer is the head of a corporate organization (not necessarily a business, although Cyc's current representation tends to assume a business context).  The #$ChiefExecutiveOfficer may or may not be the same #$Person as the #$President-CorporateOfficer.")
(comment ReliefOperation "A specialization of #$HelpingAnAgent.  Each instance of #$ReliefOperation is an operation whose goal is to provide residents of a territory recently faced with disaster (either natural or man-made) with food, clothing, and other goods necessary for survival..")
(comment Merman "A mythological being
which lives in the sea and has the upper body of a man and the lower parts of a fish. The female counterpart is the #$Mermaid.")
(comment desires-Microtheory "(#$desires-Microtheory AGENT MT) means that AGENT's desires include all of the propositions in MT.")
(comment LibraryFile "A specialization of #$ComputerFile-CW. Each instance of this collection is a computer file designed to store software components which may be used by an arbitrary number of different programs. A good example of the use of such files is #$MSWindows, which is constructed from a core or \"kernel\" set of programs and a large number of \"DLLs\" (#$LibraryFiles).")
(disjointWith Thinking Conveying-Generic)
(comment denotatumArg "(#$denotatumArg PRED N) means that the Nth argument to the #$NLSemanticPredicate PRED is the denoted Cyc term.")
(comment RicinToxin "A #$Collection. #$RicinToxin is one of the main toxic proteins of the castor bean plant (ricinus communis). Ricin is a potent cytotoxin but a weak hemagglutinin.")
(comment PornographicWebsitePassword "The collection of #$Password-Computers that allow access to #$PornographicWebSites.")
(comment Famotidine "The chemical compound which is used to treat peptic acid problems.")
(comment eventTypeCallsForAttireType "(#$eventTypeCallsForAttireType EVENTTYPE ATTIRETYPE) means that in the social or cultural expectations of the assertion context, attire of type ATTIRETYPE is what social convention demands the #$socialParticipants in EVENTTYPE wear, on pain of opprobrium.  Compare with #$eventTypeAllowsForAttireType")
(comment Pieze-UnitOfPressure "A unit of pressure, equivalent to 0.01 bars (#$Bar-UnitOfPressure), 10 millibars, or 1000 pascals (#$Pascal-UnitOfPressure).")
(comment M-TheLetter "The letter M of the alphabet.  This is 'M' (or 'a') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.   As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterM and #$LatinSmallLetterM.")
(comment Dong-Vietnam "The unitOfCurrenty used in Vietnam-AtPresent.")
(comment UnderwaterTransportation "The collection of #$TransportationEvents in which the #$transporter is underwater.")
(comment HydrogenBonding "The collection of events that establish an #$HydrogenBond configuration between an instance of #$ChemicalObject and a hydrogen atom.")
(disjointWith BodyOfWater OrganicMaterial)
(comment interArgIsa4-3 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  
(#$interArgIsa4-3 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, 
when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the fourth argument to RELN, 
a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the third argument 
must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is
an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then 
(RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 INST ... ARGN) is semantically well-formed only 
if ARG3 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation of semantic 
well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations.")
(comment KE-3TankerPlane "The collection of E-3 derivative inflight refueling tanker aircraft.")
(comment BondageStory "The specialization of #$EroticStory whose elements contain the propositional content of an #$EroticStory in which an instance of #$Bondage-Sexual occurs.")
(comment Reeling "The #$Collection of events spooling something onto or off of a reel or spool by the #$AxisConstrainedMultirevolutionRotation of that spool.  Often when something is reeled off of one reel, it is reeled onto another one such that the amount of unreeled material remains about constant.  The #$motionPathway-Complete traversed by points on the #$objectMoving follows along the #$objectMoving.")
(comment OnlineChat "A specialization of #$InternetCommunication and #$MultiDirectionalCommunication, Each instance of this collection is an online conversation between two or more #$Persons logged in remotely to a #$ChatRoom. The program sends each participant's utterances more-or-less in real time in the order in which they were received to all clients connected to the #$ChatRoom. Typically, a user's utterance is identified by their username or graphical 'avatar'.")
(comment TrueContinent "A specialization of both #$LandBody and #$Continent (q.v.).  The  current instances of #$TrueContinent (on the #$PlanetEarth) are the  four main land masses on the surface of the earth that are surrounded  by water: #$EasternContinent (which includes Africa, Asia, and Europe),  #$WesternContinent (which includes North and South America),  #$ContinentOfAntarctica, and #$ContinentOfAustralia.")
(disjointWith SelfPoweredDevice LandPlatform-Towed)
(comment CheckingWhetherConditionObtains "A collection of events in which an agent evaluates whether or not some condition obtains. For example, checking whether it is raining outside, checking whether the door is locked.")
(comment unitsOfDrugPrescriptionsByDocPayerTypeDuring "(#$unitsOfDrugPrescriptionsByDocPayerTypeDuring DOC PRODUCT-TYPE RXFILLTYPE PAYER-TYPE PERIOD NUM) means that during the #$TimeInterval PERIOD, DOC has had NUM RXFILLTYPE #$DrugPrescriptions for PRODUCT-TYPE, that were paid for by a #$HealthCarePayer of type PAYER-TYPE, filled.  For TabletDrugs, the 'unit' is a single Tablet, while for fluids, creams, and inhalents, the 'unit' is mg of active ingredient.  For example, (#$unitsOfDrugPrescriptionsByDocPayerTypeDuring DrSmith #$ZoloftProduct #$StateMedicaidAdministrationOrganization #$FillingAPrescription-MailOrder (#$YearFn 1998) 270) means that DrSmith made prescriptions that were filled by mail-order and paid for by Medicaid for 270 units of Zoloft in 1998.")
(comment TransportationFromToByFn "(TransportationFromToByFn PLACE1 PLACE2 VEHICLETYPE) denotes the collection of instances of #$TransportationEvent which begin at PLACE1 and end at PLACE2 in which a vehicle of type VEHICLETYPE is used.")
(comment IFVArmoredReconnaissanceUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of armored reconnaissance units typically employing Infantry Fighting Vehicles.")
(comment ApplyingSomethingToSurface "A collection of events.  In each #$ApplyingSomethingToSurface event, something is applied to a surface.")
(comment RunnyNose "The physiological condition of having a runny nose.")
(comment Trivia "The collection of all items of trivia: individual facts about some detail about the world that people are not expected to know because they are insignificant for daily life.")
(comment ActionMovie "#$ActionMovie is a collection of instances of #$Movie-CW each of which relates a story characterized by fast-moving action such as car chases and kick-boxing.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-DestructionOfInformation "#$AttackByComputerOperation-DestructionOfInformation is a subset of #$AttackByComputerOperation-CorruptionOfInformation and an instance of #$AttackByComputerOperationTypeByPurpose. It is the collection of 

electtonic attacks that involve the destruction of information on their victim's #$ComputationalSystems. Like #$AttackByComputerOperation-Vandalism,

#$AttackByComputerOperation-DestructionOfInformation requires a deliberate,

malicious intention to corrupt information possessed by the victim.  

Unlike vandalism, all instances of destruction of information must

have as their primary purpose the willful destruction of that

information.  A website defacement where someone posted critical

information or unwanted images would not qualify, whereas an

attack where the primary purpose was the deleting of files would qualify.")
(comment MalignantPustule-Condition "A type of #$Pustule-Condition specifically associated with #$AnthraxInfection.  This is an intermediate stage in the #$Infection, next the infection site will become a #$NecroticUlcer.")
(comment Emphysema "The collection of all cases of emphysema, a devastating lung disease associated with cigarette smoking and chronic bronchitis and characterized by abnormal distension of the alveoli.")
(comment InventoryControlPerson "Someone who keeps track of a company's inventory.  This probably includes some security functions.")
(comment GroundsPerson "someone whose work primarily consists of maintaining the outdoor areas of some commercial site.")
(comment Thulium "The collection of all pieces (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of thulium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment softwareAgentCopies "(#$softwareAgentCopies AGENT COPY) means that COPY is a copy of the entire software agent AGENT.  If COPY does not contain all of the information that AGENT contains, it is not an copy of the entire agent. (i.e. it must contain all the code and all the data.)")
(comment SnowProcess "A specialization of #$PrecipitationProcess.  Each instance of #$SnowProcess is an event in which the condensed liquid water in one or more clouds freezes into ice crystals which become substantial enough to fall to the earth as snow.  See also #$Snowflake.")
(comment DynamicIndexedInfoSource "The collection of #$IndexedInformationSources for which the associated indexing may change over time. For each #$IndexedInformationSource, and for each time, there is a characteristic function associating index terms with the pieces of information indexed by that #$IndexedInformationSource (see #$comment on #$IndexedInformationSource). For any #$DynamicIndexedInfoSource, the indexing of information may change over time. Each #$DynamicIndexedInfoSource is such that it may have various characteristic functions over the course of its existence. This can happen in several ways: New information is added to the source and is indexed by some new terms; the index terms and information in the source remain the same, but the indexing changes; information or terms are removed from the source. The OED, considered as a single work that has been modified over time, is an example of an #$DynamicIndexedInfoSource -- the amount of information (the number of definintions) in this source has increased,  and the number of index terms (the number of words defined) has also increased. Another example is the #$WorldWideWeb-DynamicIndexedInfoSource. This #$DynamicIndexedInfoSource associates, at a given time, certain peices of information (web pages) with certain addresses (URLs). At a later time it may associate a new web page with a previously unused URL, or it may associate an existing web page with a URL previously used for a different web page.")
(comment Puzzle "The collection of #$DevisedStructuredActivity that test one's ingenuity.  See #$Puzzle-Generic for a broader sense of 'puzzle' and #$Puzzle-TangibleProduct for physicalObjects.")
(comment keGenlsConsiderationInverse "(#$keGenlsConsiderationInverse COL BIN-PRED) means that for every specialization SPEC-COL of COL, it should be considered whether there there exist some VALUE such that (BIN-PRED VALUE SPEC-COL) should be asserted in the KB.")
(comment otherCommonLanguageHere "The otherCommon language of a country.  This is also a legally recognized language, but is usually not used in official documents, and is not necessarily the most common language in the nation.")
(comment PunkMusic "A specialization of #$RockMusic whose heyday was the mid-to-late 1970s.

  #$PunkMusic tends to be loud and musically unsophisticated; the song lyrics

  are often angry and political in nature.  It was conceived in part as an antidote

  to the perceived pretentiousness and pomposity of #$ProgressiveRockMusic and other

  mainstream forms of #$RockMusic.  Influential practitioners of this style include

  the Ramones, the Sex Pistols, and the Clash.  (Note: the music of many mid-1960s

  garage bands is sometimes called Punk; that music, however apt the label might

  be for it, is not a specialization #$PunkMusic).")
(comment hangs-Picturelike "(#$hangs-Picturelike ?obj ?wall).  This is a very special purpose spatial relation.  So far confined to a thing which has a horizontal wire or hook on one side.  The wire rests on something which is #$in-Spiked ?wall.  OR it is #$stuckTo the wall in some way, e.g. with tape OR it is like a plaque #$weldedTo or #$boltedTo with the wall.")
(comment legalPreconditionFor "(#$legalPreconditionFor COND PROP) means that unless the legal condition expressed in COND is true, PROP does not hold.")
(comment RecruitingActivity-Military "The collection of activities in which a recruiting officer or other representative of a #$MilitaryOrganization attempts to persuade someone (typically a high school senior or recent graduate) to commit to joining that organization.")
(comment VibrioCholerae "A collection of #$Bacterium in the #$MoneraKingdom that causes #$CholeraInfection.  Transmission to humans is by contaminated food or water.  This species of Vibrio is negative for lateral flagella on solid medium.  They produce an enterotoxic toxin which is the cause for #$CholeraInfection.  The cells must reach the small intestine in a sufficent amount to multiply and colonize.")
(comment (PerformingFn EntertainmentEvent) "(#$PerformingFn #$EntertainmentEvent) is the collection of subevents of instances of #$EntertainmentEvent which subevents consist of activities performed in the production of an entertainment event. This might include acting in a play, working as a stage-hand, or being an usher. Note that (#$PerformingFn #$EntertainmentEvent) is a spec of #$ServiceEvent, whereas its complement, (#$AttendingFn #$EntertainmentEvent), is a spec of #$RecreationalActivity.")
(comment structureRelations "(#$structureRelations STRUCT REL) means that the situation or structure STRUCT has REL as one of its associated relations between its structure-members.  This is very general and it could be an abstract predicate, relation or function, defined on the structure-members.")
(comment InstanceWithRelationFromFn "'(#$InstanceWithRelationFromFn COLLECTION PREDICATE THING)' denotes the unique INSTANCE of COLLECTION such that (PREDICATE THING INSTANCE) holds.  So for example, (#$InstanceWithRelationFromFn #$FemaleAnimal #$biologicalMother #$JonC) is Jon Curtis' mother.  To guarantee a unique value, the predicate that occurs in the arg2 position must be #$SingleEntry in its arg2.")
(comment AntiPruritic "Drugs which reduce itching.")
(comment Incohesive "no cohesiveness at all-- will not spontaneously bead or clump")
(disjointWith Holiday MovementOrShapeChangeEvent)
(comment CrossingACountryBorder "The subset of the collection #$CrossingABorder where the border crossed is a #$CountryBorder.")
(disjointWith PersonTypeByActivity GeopoliticalEntityTypeByBasicCategory)
(comment ElectronicDocumentTemplate "This is the collection of all template files for electronic documents.  
    These files are used to store macros to be executed when the associated
    text file is opened by the appropriate application.")
(comment OverSnowVehicle "The collection of vehicles which are intended to travel easily over snow-covered terrain.")
(comment BuyingWrittenMaterial "A subset of #$BuyingAnObject. In each instance of #$BuyingWrittenMaterial, an agent buys textual material in a hardcopy form. Examples include a person buying the morning newspaper, or a scholar buying a weighty tome. Note that purchases of textual material which is not in hardcopy form are not included in this collection.")
(comment TreeOrdering "A specialization of #$PartialOrdering.  An instance ORDER of #$PartialOrdering is also an instance of #$TreeOrdering just in case  the ordering relation R of ORDER orders elements of the #$baseSet S of ORDER into a tree-like structure, so that each pair of elements of S has a common 'R-lower-bound' in S (i.e., for each X, Y in S, there is a Z in S such that R(Z X) and R(Z Y)), and the set of 'R-lower-bounds' of each X in S is ordered in a chain by R (i.e., {Y: Y is in S and R(Y X)} is a chain).  Note that an instance of #$TreeOrdering can itself be a chain, i.e., an instance of #$TotalOrdering.")
(comment hasDevices "(#$hasDevices COMP DEV) means that the computer COMP has the device DEV).")
(comment BasicInputOutputSystem "The #$ComputerProgram-CW which is the collection of low-level #$DeviceDriverPrograms that provide the interface to the hardware for the #$OperatingSystem.")
(comment (AttemptingFn ResolvingByMediation) "A collection of events in which one or more #$mediators try to resolve a conflict by some form of mediation between the opposing sides.  Mediation may take the form of negotiations, independent investigations, quasi-judicial proceedings, and other techniques.")
(comment ProductMadeOfFn "#$ProductMadeOfFn takes as argument any instance of #$TangibleStuffCompositionType and returns the collection of all products made from stuff of that type.  For example (#$ProductMadeOfFn #$Titanium) returns the collection of all products made out of titanium.")
(comment pipeAbuts-DeadEnd "(pipeAbuts-DeadEnd PIPE OBJECT) means that the generic pipe PIPE abuts and ends at OBJECT, but that any fluid flow is blocked at that point (effectively a dead end) and cannot pass through the junction to or from OBJECT.")
(comment typeMakesMoreVulnerableThan-Object "(#$typeMakesMoreVulnerableThan-Object THREAT-OBJ1 THREAT-OBJ2 OBJECT-TYPE HARM-TYPE) means that otherwise normal interactions of existing things of type THREAT-OBJ1 with existing things of type OBJECT-TYPE generally make the latter more vulnerable to hardships of type HARM-TYPE than do interactions with existing things of type THREAT-OBJ2.  This predicate provides a broad method to express that some classes of objects pose greater risks than others and should enable broad, comparative vulnerability knowledge representations.  For a similar, instance level predicate see #$makesMoreVulnerableThan-Object.")
(comment CycLProbabilityConstant "The collection of those Cyc constants (individuals, collections, predicates, functions, and non-atomic terms) created to enable probabilistic reasoning (of various kinds).")
(comment numberOfCrew "(#$numberOfCrew VEHICLE NR) states that the number of crew members that are needed to operate VEHICLE is NR. This number is often 1, for #$Automobile, but for many complicated #$WeaponSystems it is more. Crew includes the #$driverActor but not the #$passengers.")
(comment Antenna "The electrical component used to receive electromagnetic signals")
(comment FederalDistrictCourt "The collection of all US Federal District Courts, as defined by the United States Code.  Such courts are subOrganizations of the #$USJudicialBranch.")
(disjointWith RaisingLivingThings MovementOrShapeChangeEvent)
(comment WaterSolubleStuff "A collection of tangibles.  Each element of #$WaterSolubleStuff is a tangible thing that can dissolve in water.  For example, instances of the collections #$Soap-Personal, #$LaundryDetergent, #$Sugar-Table.")
(comment FreeSpaceContentAroundFn "(#$FreeSpaceContentAroundFn OBJECT) denotes the instance of #$FreeSpaceContent surrounding OBJECT.  If OBJECT is

a geographical region, this amounts to an #$OpenSpaceContent above OBJECT.")
(comment Stilton-Cheese "This the collection of all instances of Stilton, an

English cheese. It is one of the three great blue cheeses.")
(disjointWith Issue SpatialThing-Localized)
(comment keWeakSuggestionInverse "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate and specialization of #$keRelevantInverse that relates a collection to a binary predicate.  (#$keWeakSuggestionInverse COL BINPRED) means that for every known (i.e. Cyc-reified) instance INST of COL, it is weakly suggested that there be some reified THING such that (BINPRED THING INST) is known in the Knowledge Base.  See also #$keStrongSuggestionInverse and #$keWeakSuggestionPreds.")
(comment Aerobiologist "#$Aerobiologist is the collection of scientists who study  #$Aerobiology.")
(disjointWith SeatingDevice WaterTransportationDevice)
(comment ReggaeMusic "Jamaican popular music that developed in #$The1960s among Kingston's poor blacks, drawing on #$SoulMusic and traditional African and Jamaican folk music and #$SkaMusic. Many of its highly political songs proclaim the tenets of the Rastafarian religious movement. Instrumentation usually includes an ensemble of organ, piano, drums, and electric guitars, led by a #$BassGuitar-Electric played at high volume.  Springy, offbeat rhythm characterizes its sound. It is popular internationally and has influenced African music. Bob Marley and his group, the Wailers, and Toots and the Maytals are among the best-known performers.")
(comment ModalReasoningAuxiliaryMicrotheory "Instances of #$ModalReasoningAuxiliaryMicrotheory are
microtheories used in `modal reasoning via microtheories' for the
following purposes: (1) converting non-modal statements into modal
statements, (2) storing or inheriting common facts or rule for a set
of modal reasoning microtheories (see #$ModalReasoningMicrotheory),
(3) separating a certain set of modal reasoning microtheories from the
others.  For an example of how these microtheories are used in modal
reasoning via microtheories, see
#$NoteOnModalReasoningViaMicrotheories.")
(comment OverTheCounterDrug "The collection of drugs which are legally able to be sold without a doctor's prescription.")
(comment StateCapital "A specialization of #$CapitalCityOfRegion.  An instance of #$CapitalCityOfRegion is an instance of #$StateCapital just in case it is the capital city of some instance of #$State-Geopolitical (q.v.).  Instances of #$StateCapital include the capital cities of instances of #$State-UnitedStates, as well as the capital cities of instances of other specializations of #$State-Geopolitical, such as #$Prefecture and #$Province.")
(comment Milli "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10^-3")
(comment SubDagFn "(#$SubDagFn ?Path ?Dag) returns the sub-part (or nested Dag) within ?Dag that can be reached by following the sequence of attributes listed in ?Path.")
(comment JetPropelledAircraft "The collection of all aircraft propelled by #$JetEngines.")
(comment NucleosideType "A collection of collections.  Instances of #$NucleosideType
are types of instances of the collection #$Nucleoside.")
(comment subCharacterStrings "This predicate relates a given abstract character-string to the character-strings contained within it. (#$subCharacterStrings SUPER SUB) means that SUB is a substring

of SUPER.  That is, SUB is a list of abstract characters

<CHAR(1), ..., CHAR(N)> and there is some positive integer M such that the

Mth through (M+N)th members of SUPER are CHAR(1) through CHAR(N),

respectively.  For a similar but more restricted predicate that

relates instances of #$SubLString, see #$substring.")
(comment HeavyDrySupportBridge "Each #$HeavyDrySupportBridge (HDSB) is a modular bridge that can span a 40 meter gap in 90 minutes with 14 or fewer soldiers.  One bridge set provides either one 40 meter bridge or two 20 meter bridges.  The bridge will cross MLC 96W/70T traffic and allows the crossing of a Heavy Equipment Transporter carrying an M1A1 tank.  The HDSB is designed for transportation as a palletized load by a CommonBridgeTransporter, Palletized Load System (PLS) trailers or by service support units equipped with PLS trucks.  A bridge set will consist of no more than 9 PLS pallet loads and a launcher vehicle. (Source: Engineer Systems Handbook, 4/97)")
(comment Herb-HumanUse "#$Herb-HumanUse is the collection of all herbs that humans value for their flavoring/aromatherapeutic or medicinal qualities. For example, #$BayLeaf, #$Ginseng, and #$KavaPlant. See also #$Plant-NonWoody and #$Spice.")
(comment PatrolWatercraft "The collection of watercraft intended to be used for patrolling.")
(comment Interjection-SpeechPart "The collection of all interjections, also called 

exclamations. Interjections often serve a purely pragmatic or discourse function, 

and can often stand alone as utterances. Examples: 'ugh', 'abracadabra', and 'wow!'.")
(comment BudgetReportDocument "The collection of documents that contrast an agent's budget with their actual financial status and transactions.")
(comment personTakingTourMightParticularlyEnjoyObject "(#$personTakingTourMightParticularlyEnjoyObject TOUR PERSON

THING) means that an argument exists to the effect that, if PERSON

were to take TOUR, PERSON might particularly enjoy the

#$SomethingExisting THING connected with TOUR.")
(comment Blister "A raised bump on the skin, often containing liquid.")
(comment Prostitute "An instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation and a specialization of #$SexWorker.  Each instance of #$Prostitute is a person who earns at least part of his/her livelihood by performing sexual acts in exchange for money.")
(comment AssistantChiefOfStaff-Intelligence "A collection of instances of  #$CoordinatingStaffMember-USArmy 
with responsibility for the collection and use of military intelligence.")
(comment canPerformWithLevelOfEffectiveness "(#$canPerformWithLevelOfEffectiveness AGENTTYPE ACTIONTYPE LEVEL)

means that, other things being equal, the #$skillLevel with which a

given instance of AGENTTYPE can effectively perform an action of type

ACTIONTYPE is LEVEL.")
(comment minimizeExtentForArg "(#$minimizeExtentForArg PREDICATE THING N) means that if we can't prove some positive literal in which THING is the Nth arg to PREDICATE, there is a very weak argument -- an assumption --  for the negation of that literal.  Assumptions are weak arguments that lose against any other kind of argument.  See also #$minimizeExtent.")
(comment CultureMedium "Artificial medium that supplies the nutrients needed for a living material to grow in a controlled (typically, laboratory) environment.  For example, the agar-based mix used to grow bacteria or mold in petri dishes.")
(comment HorseSweats "This is the collection of what for horses is analogous to a sweat suit for

humans.")
(comment TreatmentProcedure "The collection of procedures during which some organism is treated with respect to some physiological condition affecting it or one of its part.")
(comment Cartoonist "Cartoonists are artists that produce #$Cartoons.")
(comment GamblingCardGame "All instances of gambling games played with playing cards")
(comment SubcollectionOfUsedForEventTypeFn "This is a specialization of the extremely general #$SubcollectionOfUsedForTypeFn. (#$SubcollectionOfUsedForEventTypeFn COL EVENTTYPE)

 is that spec of COL, all instances of which play the role of

#$instrument-Generic in instances of EVENTTYPE.")
(disjointWith UnitOfFrequency UnitOfAngularSpeed)
(comment TheTermDenotingFunction "Functions whose values are TheTerms.")
(comment NucleotideChain-ThreePrimeEnd "The collection of all 3' ends of nucleotide chains as determined by the orientation of the component nucleotides relevant to RNA molecules and DNA strands.")
(comment SkyFn "takes a place as an argument, and returns the sky over it.")
(comment signatories "The predicate #$signatories relates a particular agreement to the   agents who have signed the agreement.  (#$signatories AGR PARTY) does not   entail (#$agreeingAgents AGR PARTY), as in some cases an agreement does not   enter into force directly upon its being signed, but only after some   other action has occurred.  For example, the following is true of certain   international agreements: although a given country's leader or other   representative has signed the agreement on behalf of her country--   thus making the country a signatory--the country cannot be considered an   agreeing agent unless and until the country's government as a whole has   ratified the agreement.  Nor, of course, does entailment hold in the   opposite direction, due to the existence of verbal agreements.  Depending   on the nature of the agreement, a signatory might be a person who has   physically put his signature on a copy of the agreement, or (as in the   above example) might be a country or other instance of #$MultiIndividualAgent   for whom the actual signer is acting as representative.")
(comment FighterPlane-F16A "The collection of the original model of the #$FighterPlane-F16 aircraft.")
(comment travelLegToLocation "(#$travelLegToLocation PATH TO) means that TO is
represented as the the ending point of PATH in the itinerary of some
#$TravelTour.  This means, among other things, that TO is expected
to be the #$toLocation in the traversal of PATH that is the actual
instantiation of that leg of the tour.  See also #$TourTravelLegFn.")
(comment publishedWork "This predicate describes the relation between a collection of #$PublishedMaterial (see #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType) and the #$MediaTransferEvent event in which the instances of that type were published.")
(comment NetworkProtocolStack "#$NetworkProtocolStack is the collection of all protocol stacks. An instance of

           #$NetworkProtocolStack is a group (or stack) of instances of #$NetworkProtocols

(or more specifically, #$ProtocolStackLayers)  that define the software and

hardware which

           allow one machine to communicate with another in an instance of

           #$ComputerNetwork.")
(comment GasTerminal "A subset of #$Terminal-TransferPoint.  Each instance of #$GasTerminal is a terminal where gas

is transferred from conveyance to another (of the same or different type). It will normally have storage facilities for gas, as well.")
(comment CoconutMilk "A portion of the liquid from the inside of coconuts; the liquid in a single coconut forms part of its endosperm.")
(disjointWith ConductingMedium Organization)
(comment Backgammon-ComputerGameEvent "The set of events consisting of a complete game of #$Backgammon being played on a computer")
(comment Septum-Bacterium "The collection of all septums that develop in the process of bacterial cell division.  After DNA replication, part of the cell wall grows inward forming the septum to divide the bacterial cell into two new cells.")
(comment HumanCapabilityType "This is the collection of all types of action which can be performed in normal circumstances by any adult human being, that is, they are human capabilities in the sense that we expect a normal adult person to be able to do them in typical circumstances.  This is not the collection of types of action which can be done by some, but not all, persons.  For example, #$WalkingOnTwoLegs is an instance, but #$Juggling is not, because all normal people can walk but only some can juggle.")
(comment portalConnectsRegions "(#$portalConnectsRegions PORTAL HERE THERE) means that the regions HERE and THERE are connected via PORTAL, and that at least one of HERE and THERE contains PORTAL as a physical part.")
(comment GallStoneCondition "An ailment characterized by the build-up of gall-stones in the body.")
(disjointWith TimeInterval InformationStore)
(disjointWith LighterThanAirCraft Projectile-Device)
(comment HonorSociety "This is the collection of honor societies such as PhiBetaKappa and PiSigmaAlpha.")
(comment Tiger-Sumatran "A collection of tigers found only on the island of Sumatra. Their scientific name is Panthera tigris sumatrae.")
(comment BPV-SALUTE-ReportMicrotheory "The collection of microtheories the content of which captures information in a particular CPOF Block Party V SALUTE report.")
(comment nothingBetweenOfType "(#$nothingBetweenOfType REFERENT THING COL) means that there does not exist any instance of COL that is between THING and REFERENT.")
(comment MountainBike "A specialization of #$Bicycle.  Each instance of #$MountainBike is a sturdy bicycle designed to have fat, knobby tires installed in order to facilitate riding off-road or on trails.")
(comment BallisticMissile-IRAN130 "A type of ballistic missile.  According to the CSIS source document 'Creeping Proliferation Could Mean a Paradigm Shift

          in the Cost of War and Terrorism', Iran is in possession of many of these missiles and may use them as delivery vehicles for weapons of mass destruction.")
(comment Gallium "A piece (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of gallium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment SDBITestLogicalSchema "The collection of #$LogicalTableSchema instances which are  part of the #$SDBITestDB.")
(comment SetOfGroupMembersFn "`(#$SetOfGroupMembersFn GROUP)' denotes the set whose elements
are exactly the members of GROUP.")
(disjointWith MatterTypeByPhysicalState MicrotheoryType)
(comment WaitingOnATable "The server greets the seated people (recipients of service), takes their orders and brings them what they request.  Finally takes their payment.")
(comment numInhabitantsOfTypeInRegion "(#$numInhabitantsOfTypeInRegion PLACE TYPE INT) means that INT number of entities of TYPE reside in PLACE.")
(comment TerminalPhysiologicalCondition "A collection of ailments which are distinguished by the shared characteristic that they result in the death of the afflicted organism.")
(disjointWith InternalCombustionEngine ExternalCombustionEngine)
(comment TerminatingTradeRelations "The collection of events where the a state terminates all or some trade relations another state or group of states.")
(comment Providencia "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom.
These #$ProkaryoticCells are all members of the intestinal flora.  All may
cause #$UrinaryTractInfections.")
(disjointWith RearWindowWithDefroster AutomaticCarWindow)
(disjointWith MemorialDay-US ReligiousHoliday)
(disjointWith InterrogativeUtterance DeclarativeUtterance)
(comment suggestedTourDayActivities "(suggestedTourDayActivities TOUR DAY ACTIVITY) relates the
TOUR's suggested ACTIVITY to the DAY in which the participants have
free time.")
(comment DustCloud "Dust Clouds occur when moving air blows dirt into the air.  Usually their bottoms are on the ground.  They often occur during dust storms, sandstorms, tornados.  THe dirt particles suspended will separate out once the air stands still for a time.  Their transparency is dependent on whether one is experiencing such a cloud (#$AmbientConditionsMt), or describing one in the abstract (#$WeatherProcessMt).")
(disjointWith Perceiving InformationBearingThing)
(comment composerOfMusicalCW "(#$composerOfMusicalCW AGENT CW) means that AGENT

is the composer of CW (a #$MusicalComposition).")
(comment purposeOfScriptTypeInPlan "(#$purposeOfScriptTypeInPlan SCRIPTTYPE PLANMT GOAL) means
that within the #$Plan (i.e., the microtheoretic planning context)
PLAN, events of the type SCRIPTTYPE are ordinarily associated with a
purpose represented by GOAL.  In many but not all contexts this
entails that is an event of type SCRIPTTYPE is performed by someone,
that agent will have GOAL as a #$goals.  It is true generally that if
(#$purposeOfScriptTypeInPlan SCRIPTTYPE PLANMT GOAL) and it is true in
the PLANMT that (isa EVENT SCRIPTTYPE), it will be true in the PLANMT
that(#$purposeOfEvent EVENT GOAL).")
(comment HeavingAnObject "The type of actions in which an object is lifted, propelled, or thrown by the force of a body movement.  In particular, throwing movements performed with the shoulders or hindquarters, as a horse bucking someone off or a bull tossing someone.  (For hurling something using an arm movement, see #$ThrowingAnObject.)")
(comment ExternalFertilizationEvent "fertilization of an egg by a sperm outside the bodies of the parent actors, such as when fish spawn.")
(disjointWith AngularDistance Pressure)
(comment ProduceMarketCategory "Market category for the kinds of fresh fruits and vegetables typically sold in a grocery store produce department or at a farmers' market.  Associated items sometimes marketed with the main items include salad dressing and fresh fruit and vegetable juices.")
(comment AerialReconnaissanceUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units tasked with observing various           regions of airspace. This attribute should not be confused with           AirBasedReconnaissance-MilitarySpecialization. This latter           applies to reconnaissance carried out by means of air-based           platforms.")
(comment CycLAssertedAssertion "A specialization of #$CycLAssertion.  An instance ASSERT of #$CycLAssertion is also an instance of #$CycLAssertedAssertion  just in case ASSERT was explicitly asserted to the Cyc Knowledge Base by one of its users (see the collection #$Cyclist), as opposed to having been deduced by Cyc's inference engine (in which case it would be an instance of #$CycLDeducedAssertion (q.v.)).  Note that since a single assertion can be both explicitly asserted to the knowledge base and also deduced by the inference engine, the collections #$CycLAssertedAssertion and #$CycLDeducedAssertion are not disjoint.")
(comment Treaty "The collection of agreements that are formally concluded between two

or more geopolitical agents. Treaties are usually established in some

ceremony, although they may be concluded in secret, and are usually

instantiated in documents signed by the official representatives of

the agent states concluding the treaty.")
(comment PredicativeFrame "Frames for adjectives that can be used predicatively, like 'happy' in 'Chris is happy'.")
(comment StratusCloud "The collection of flat low clouds one sees on an overcast day.")
(comment CycLSimplifierDirective "The subcollection of #$CycLAssertions which express rules
or instructions to the #$CycLSimplifier.  Even though the simplifier
may treat these as rules, they are GAFs in the KB.  Each
#$CycLSimplifierDirective must have a #$SimplifierDirectivePredicate
as its predicate.  They are relevant in the microtheory in which they are
asserted, and in specMts of that microtheory unless overridden.")
(comment Locomotion-TwoLegged "The collection of all locomotion events in which the locomotor uses two feet or foot-like extremities to move along a solid surface. Examples include walking done by humans or birds, as well as locomotion by a dog, bear, etc., on its hind legs. Someone walking on their hands would be a borderline negative example.")
(comment CharacterMode "A collection of collections.  A character mode is a   collection of concrete character tokens that all represent the   same abstract character in the same way, e.g. by being    handwritten rather than printed or spoken.  That is, each    instance MODE-INST of #$CharacterMode is a specialization of   some instance TYPE-INST of #$CharacterType that includes all    elements of TYPE-INST -- i.e. all tokens of a particular abstract    character -- that are realized in a particular way (e.g. by being   inscribed, sounded, electromagnetically-encoded, or whatever).     For example, if TYPE-INST is the collection of all tokens of the    letter 'A', MODE-INST might be the collection of all _inscribed_    tokens of 'A'.  For other examples, see the specializations    #$CharacterMode-Inscribed, #$CharacterMode-Sounded, and    #$CharacterMode-ElectroMagnetic.  See also #$modeOfCharacterType for the relation between a given character type and each the various character modes it subsumes.")
(comment ChiefFinancialOfficer "A collection of people. The #$ChiefFinancialOfficer is the senior person in charge of the finances of a corporate organization (not necessarily a business, although Cyc's current representation tends to assume a business context).  The #$ChiefFinancialOfficer will probably be a member of the organization's board of directors.")
(disjointWith MakingAPrediction RequestingAction)
(comment PetFood "The collection of foods and beverages not only normally 

eaten by #$DomesticPets, but intended to be eaten by #$DomesticPets and marketed 

as such. A salient example is commercial #$DogFood, 

but this also includes food for more unusual pets like snakes or spiders.

It does not include commerical feed for non-pet domesticated animals like horses.")
(comment IdentityFn "An instance of both #$UnaryFunction and #$EvaluatableFunction.  When applied to an instance THING of #$Thing, #$IdentityFn returns THING as its value, so that (#$equals (#$IdentityFn THING) THING) holds.")
(comment Mermaid "A mythological being which lives in the sea and has the upper body of a woman and the lower parts of a fish. The male counterpart is the #$Merman.")
(comment KineticEnergy "Kinetic energy is energy due to an objects being in motion, can be calculated as 1/2*M*V**2; it is measured in Joules in the MKS system.")
(comment GoalsContext "The collection of all contexts which contain assertions expressing the goals of some agent or group of agents.")
(comment DigitalSignalProcessing "#$DigitalSignalProcessing (DSP) refers to manipulating information, such as representations of sound or images, that have been converted from analog into digital form.")
(disjointWith LocomotionEvent-Animal (TransportViaFn TransportationDevice-Vehicle))
(comment semTransArg "(#$semTransArg PRED N) means that the Nth argument to the #$NLSemanticPredicate PRED is the #$NLTemplateExpression in which the denoted Cyc term appears.")
(comment interArgReln2-3 "A binary #$InterArgRelnPredicate (q.v.).  (#$interArgReln2-3 RELN BINPRED) means that a formula built from RELN (i.e. a \"GAF\" or \"NAT\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence and  #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm) is semantically well-formed only if BINPRED holds between the second and third arguments to RELN (in that order) in the GAF/NAT.  That is, a formula (RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ..) is semantically well-formed only if (BINPRED ARG2 ARG3) holds.  For further explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations. See also the more general quaternary predicate #$interArgReln, which has two argument-places for specifying the pair of RELN's arguments that must be related by BINPRED.")
(comment BrucellaBacterium "A #$Collection.  Each instance is a portion of the #$Bacterium Brucella, which is responsible for the disease #$Brucellosis.")
(comment BlackHole "The collection of individual #$BlackHoles; singularities in spacetime caused by the collapse of very massive stars. The gravitational pull of a black hole is so strong that even light cannot escape, hence the term 'Black Hole'.")
(comment JamesBondMovie "This is the collection of all the movies featuring

#$JamesBond-FictionalCharacter.")
(comment DihydroergotamineMesylate "The chemical compound which is an anti-migraine drug.")
(comment Barye-UnitOfPressure "A unit of pressure, equivalent to 0.1 pascals (#$Pascal-UnitOfPressure) or 10^-6 bars (#$Bar-UnitOfPressure).  This unit is variously referred to as ``barie'', ``barye'', and ``baryl''.")
(comment N-TheLetter "The letter N of the alphabet.  This is 'N' (or 'n') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.   As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterN and #$LatinSmallLetterN.")
(comment Rupee-Mauritius "Major unit of currency of #$Mauritius")
(comment orgWithJobPosition "(#$orgWithJobPosition JOB ORG) means that #$Organization ORG has #$JobPosition JOB. The position may be either open or filled. See #$JobOpen and #$JobFilled.")
(comment WaterSurfaceTransportation "The collection of #$TransportationEvents in which the #$transporter is travelling while floating on the surface of some body of water.")
(comment PersonalIncomeTax "An instance of #$MicrotheoryType and a subset of both #$PersonalTax and #$IncomeTax. Each instance of #$PersonalIncomeTax places an obligation upon certain persons to pay a tax on their respective incomes.")
(comment BiologicalDevelopmentProcess "The biological process in which a living object or objects develop.")
(comment Evaporating "A specialization of #$StateOfMatterChangeEvent.  In each instance of #$Evaporating, something in liquid form (i.e., an instance of #$Liquid-StateOfMatter) is converted to vapor (and thus becomes an instance of #$Gaseous-StateOfMatter).")
(comment TornadoIDS "A collection; a specialization of #$MilitaryAircraft.  The Tornado IDS (Interdiction and Strike) is a ground attack aircraft designed and built by a British, Italian, and German consortium.")
(comment qaWebString "(#$qaWebString FORT STRING) means that STRING is a character string to be offered as an enhanced query string when other components of the QuA application have determined the query submitted by the user to be about FORT. Note that the #$arg2Format is #$SingleEntry, to ensure that at most one query string is offered for any given FORT.")
(comment relationInstanceExistsCount "(#$relationInstanceExistsCount PRED THING COL N) means there exist exactly N instances (INS_1, INS_2, ..., INS_N) of COL such that THING stands in relation PRED to each of them, i.e. (PRED THING INS_1), (PRED THING INS_2), ..., (PRED THING INS_N), all hold.  Thus it is equivalent to the more complex form (#$thereExistExactly NUM ?INST (#$and (#$isa ?INST COL) (PRED THING ?INST))).  So a ground atomic formula (or \"GAF\") built upon #$relationInstanceExistsCount is in effect shorthand (i.e. a \"macro\") for an equivalent rule with the more complex quantified form.  For example, (#$relationInstanceExistsCount #$geographicalSubRegions #$Iran #$OilField 3) means that Iran has exactly three oil fields. See the shared #$NoteAboutUseOfRuleMacroPredicates.")
(comment CompromisedDataSourceSending "This is a spec of #$DataSending in which the information sent comes from an   #$informationOrigin whose security has been compromised in some manner.  This  is often done to request secure documents or to issue directives which are   accepted as being from the compromised source.")
(comment Tenericutes-Division "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalDivision within the #$MoneraKingdom.  The #$Tenericutes-Division are #$ProcaryoticCells that are pliable and lack a cell wall.  They are instead bound by a plasma membrane.")
(comment ChatRoom "A collection of #$Events. Each #$ChatRoom is an event of a program running on a #$ComputerServer that accepts contributions to an #$OnlineChat from multiple users logged on remotely, sending their 'utterances' over the Internet. The program sends each participant's utterances more-or-less in real time in the order in which they were received to all clients connected to the chat room. Typically, a user's utterance is identified by their username or graphical 'avatar'.")
(comment SpacePlatform-Manned "The collection of manned military space platforms.")
(comment conditionEvaluated "(#$conditionEvaluated CHECK COND) means that in the #$CheckingWhetherConditionObtains event CHECK, the  ELSentence-Assertible COND is the condition being checked. That is, the agent performing CHECK is determining whether COND obtains or not.")
(comment MightModeFn "(#$MightModeFn SCRIPTTYPE CONTEXT-MT) denotes the      subcollection of SCRIPTTYPE whose instances possess the modal property denoted by \"might\", from the perspective of CONTEXT-MT.")
(comment LightCavalryReconnaissanceUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of lightly armed cavalry units dedicated to reconnaissance operations.")
(comment containerCapacity "How much stuff can be contained.  (#$containerCapacity ?CONT ?CAPACITY) means that the stuff contained in ?CONT cannot have a volume more than ?CAPACITY.")
(comment Depression-PsychologicalCondition "A psychological ailment characterized by sadness, inactivity, and altered sleeping and eating patterns.")
(comment ComedyMovie "#$ComedyMovie is a collection of instances of #$Movie-CW each of which relates a humorous story.")
(comment ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Espionage "#$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Espionage is the subset of 

#$AttackByComputerOperation whose instances are directed to enable the unauthorized collection of information, resulting in the decrease of value of the information to the victim and the availability, and hence increase in value, of the information to the attacker. #$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Espionage is distinct from  #$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-General by virtue of being highly covert. That is, performers of all instances of #$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Espionage must be engaged in (a) attempting to disguise the attack from the victim of the attack and others while the attack is in progress, and (b) attempting to disguise the results of the attack after the attack is completed.  For an electronic attack to be 'highly' covert,  both (a) and (b) are necessary, an attack that is covert requires that only condition (a) be met.")
(comment NecroticUlcer "This is the final stage of the #$AnthraxInfection at the lesion site.  From here, the #$Infection disseminates and may cause septicemia.")
(comment GroupOfMaxSizeFn "(#$GroupOfMaxSizeFn N TYPE) returns the collection of all

#$Groups composed of at most N instances of TYPE.")
(comment ComputerProgrammerProfessional "People who hack for a living.  Don't need certification.  Can work for huge corp to private consultant.")
(comment typicalArmamentOfUnitType "(#$typicalArmamentOfUnitType  UNITTYPE ARMSTYPE) means that individual military units of type UNITTYPE typically have one or more instances of ARMSTYPE as weapons or armaments.")
(comment performanceOfWork "(#$performanceOfWork ACT WORK) means that ACT is a performance of the #$DevisedPracticeOrWork, WORK.  For example: (#$performanceOfWork DaisyDaisySungByHAL-EventRecordedFor2001Movie  #$DaisyDaisy)")
(comment Tester-Professional "Someone whose job is to test products.")
(comment Ytterbium "The collection of all pieces (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of ytterbium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment ForwardsFn "This function, applied to a #$FrontAndBackSidedObject, returns the
exact direction the object's front is facing in the 
implicit frame of reference defined by the object.")
(comment softwareAgentProcesses "(#$softwareAgentProcesses AGENT PROCESS) means that PROCESS
is an agentive computer process of the software agent AGENT.
Associating a software agent with an instance of #$ComputerProcessRunning
in this way is analogous to associating an animal agent with an instance of
#$BiologicalEvent that is the event of its mental and physiological processes.")
(disjointWith AstronomicalObject CloudInSky)
(disjointWith OfficialDocument GreetingCard)
(comment Gendarmerie "The collection of all #$Groups of #$Gendarmes.")
(comment Sucrose "The disachharide (complex sugar) C12-H22-O11 in any state.")
(comment RecruitingActivity-Sports "The collection of activities in which a #$SportsCoach or other representative of a sports team (typically one affiliated with a #$University) attempts to persuade an athlete to commit to joining that team.")
(comment InhalantDrug "drugs which are inhaled")
(comment RigidlyCohesive "will stay together indefinitely until separated with much force (with a tool)")
(disjointWith MovementOrShapeChangeEvent AcademicTesting)
(comment WebDirectoryFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  (#$WebDirectoryFn CONTACT-INFO) takes a spec of #$ContactInfoString -- such as #$ZipCode, #$DomainName, or #$PhoneNumber -- and returns the collection of #$ReferenceWebSites that contain directories or listings of that type of information. (#$Kean 10/11/99)")
(comment IllegalImmigration "Instances are cases where a person attempts to gain illegal entry to a country by evading a border check, using false documents, etc.")
(comment (RightObjectOfPairFn (PartTypeFn EighthThoracicVertebra VertebralTransverseProcess)) "")
(disjointWith ContactLocation City)
(comment IndefiniteWait-ComputerPerformance "This is the collection of all attempts to run some process on a computer which
    leads to the computer getting caught in a pause which will continue indefinitely.")
(comment Bulldozer "The collection of vehicles generally used to move large amounts of earth and other materials for construction projects")
(comment QuasiOrdering "The collection of all those #$MathematicalOrderings ORDER in which the ordering relation R is a reflexive and transitive relation on the #$baseSet S of ORDER, i.e., for each X in S, R(X X) holds, and for each X, Y and Z in S, if R(X Y) and R(Y Z) then R(X Z).  For example, if you take the set of all people in the states today, and take the relation '__ is at least as tall as ...' (i.e., either __ is as tall as ...  or __ is taller than ...) on this set, you get a #$QuasiOrdering because this relation is reflexive and transitive on the set of all people in the states today.  Note that the #$QuasiOrdering in this example is neither a #$PartialOrdering nor a #$PartialOrdering-Strict.  Subcollections of #$QuasiOrdering include #$PartialOrdering, #$TreeOrdering, #$TotalOrdering and #$Lattice-LatticeTheoretic.")
(disjointWith Density Volatility-Physical)
(comment ComputerMonitor-VideoKind "Like the screen you are staring at.  Don't confuse with ComputerDisplay.")
(comment PowerSupply "A device which provides the power to an electrical device.")
(comment USStateGovernor "head of US States. Every US State has one-- usually a new one every 2 years.")
(disjointWith HandlingAnObject RaisingLivingThings)
(comment characterSetForWritingSystem "The predicate #$characterSetForWritingSystem links a particular system of writing to the specific set of characters used in that system.  (#$characterSetForWritingSystem WRIT CHACSET) means that the #$WritingSystem WRIT contains the characters in the set CHACSET.  For example, #$CyrillicWriting uses the characters in the set #$CyrillicLetter.  A character set may be used by more than one writing system, e.g., the #$ChineseCharacter set is used by both #$ChineseWriting and #$JapaneseKanamajiriWriting.")
(disjointWith Oil WaterSolubleStuff)
(comment surfaceAreaOfTopOfObject "(#$surfaceAreaOfTopOfObject OBJECT AREA) means that the top surface of OBJECT has area AREA.  This predicates relates an object to the area of its top surface, that is, the area of its top side; see #$SurfaceArea-TopSurfaceFn. This should be used for surfaces of lakes, tabletops, etc. (It does not refer to the whole surface of the object including sides and underside; for that, see #$surfaceAreaOfWholeObject and #$SurfaceArea-WholeSurfaceFn.)")
(comment MonochromeImage "A collection of visual images.  Each element of #$MonochromeImage is an all grey-scale or otherwise monochrome visual image.  #$BlackAndWhiteImage is a subset of #$MonochromeImage.  Some images, e.g. some infrared images, are in varying shades of red.  These would be elements of #$MonochromeImage but not #$BlackAndWhiteImage.")
(comment Monastery-Residence "This is the collection of monasteries. A monastery is a large communal

dwelling which is a home for monks.")
(comment BestialityStory "The subset of #$EroticStory whose elements contain the propositional content of an #$EroticStory in which there is at least a #$Person and at least a #$NonPersonAnimal participant.")
(comment DeglutitionMuscleSet "The collection of all instances of #$DeglutitionMuscleSet.  The #$DeglutitionMuscleSet consists of eight (or more depending on how one counts) #$Muscles on one side of the body connected to the #$Hyoid.  Suprahyoid muscles connect to the #$Jawbone, while Infrahyoid muscles connect to the #$Manubrium or #$Scapula.  They are used in opening the #$Jaw or in #$Swallowing.")
(disjointWith InternationalOrganizationOfCountries RegionalGovernment)
(comment AerosolPhysicist "#$AerosolPhysicist is the collection of scientists who study  #$AerosolPhysics.")
(disjointWith SeatingDevice Spacecraft)
(comment ModalReasoningMicrotheory "Instances of #$ModalReasoningMicrotheory are microtheories
accessible to (some) modal operators, in which modal reasoning via
rules concerning modal operators can be carried out.  They can also be
used in modal reasoning via microtheories, applying rules (outside)
about these microtheories.  General relations among these
microtheories, in addition to #$genlMt, include #$mtConverts-PlainOp
and #$mtConverts-OpPlain.  For an example of how these microtheories
are used in modal reasoning via microtheories, see
#$NoteOnModalReasoningViaMicrotheories.")
(comment PrescriptionDrugMarketCategory "The market category in which prescription drugs fall.  Also includes such things as hypodermic needles and the blood test kits that diabetics use.")
(comment down-UnderspecifiedPath "(#$down-UnderspecifiedPath ACT REGION) states that an abstract locational relation holds between ACT and REGION, where REGION is a #$Region-Underspecified crossed in a 'downwardly motion' during ACT.  #$down-UnderspecifiedPath is an underspecified semantic representation that may be elaborated to represent either a spatial example of downward motion (as in 'walking down the hill') or a temporal use of downward 'motion' ('down the ages Easter has become ...') or a metaphorical use ('Smith's theory fell down when presented with new data it could not explain.').  REGION may be an instance of #$Collection ('man decended from apes') as well as of #$Individual.")
(comment DiscoMusic "A specialization of #$RockMusic whose heyday was the mid-to-late 1970s.
  #$DiscoMusic was the main stlye of music played in discoteques at that time.
  #$DiscoMusic is characterized by strong rhythms and good-timey lyrics.
  Principle practitioners include Donna Summer, the Bee Gees, and Barry White.")
(comment interestRate-Periodic "The predicate used to state the periodic rate for some #$LoanAgreement.  (#$interestRate-Periodic LOAN RATE) means that RATE is the interest rate for the compounding period for LOAN.  The #$compoundingPeriod for a loan is a #$Time-Quantity for which interest is accumulated before being added to the principal for further interest caluculations.")
(comment Biplane "The collection of all airplanes which have two primary sets of wings.  Nowdays biplanes are used mostly for crop-dusting and aerobatics.")
(comment Deoxyribose "A collection of molecules. Instances of #$Deoxyribose are
molecules of a sugar that is a variation of #$Ribose, that has one more
oxygen atom.")
(comment MovieSeriesProduct "The collection of all movie series considered as #$ConceptualWorks. Each instance of #$MovieSeriesProduct has at least two instances of Movie-CW as #$episodes. ")
(comment BaileyBridge-Military "Each instance of #$BaileyBridge-Military is a through-truss bridge manually assembled by connecting panels end to end.  The roadway is formed by connecting stringers and decking between truss girders.  The main girders on each side of the bridge can be assembled in multiple widths and heights to provide added strength and/or length of span.  Components of the bridge can be assembled to form piers which are used as intermidiate supports for long spans.  The BaileyBridge system is highly labor-intensive but also highly versatile.  In some cases, because it can be assembled in multiple heights and widths, it is the only tactical bridge suitable for long spans and heavy loads.  The basic bridge set contains enough parts and equipment to install two 80-foot double-single bridges or one 130-foot double-double bridge.  The use of a Reinforcement Set will enable a unit to construct a triple-truss, single-story bridge (in any length from 100 to 180 feet) for Military Load Class 60 traffic.  (Source: Engineer Systems Handbook, 4/97)")
(comment HousewaresMarketCategory "Brooms, plastic bags, cupcake molds, potholders, eating utensils, plates, cups, bowls, silverware, and all the other miscellaneous household things you can get in grocery, drug, and some department stores")
(comment Leptospira "These #$ProkaryoticCells are tightly coiled, thin, flexible
spirochetes.  These are oxidase-positive as well as catalase- and/or peroxidase-positive #$Bacterium.")
(disjointWith PatrolWatercraft CargoShip)
(disjointWith PlantBLO AnimalBLO)
(comment equatable "(#$equatable TT1 TT2) indicates that the two #$TheTerms, TT1 and TT2, can bind to each other.  One case of this is when TT1 and TT2 are #$LogicalFields which are allowed to join due to a #$joinDependency.")
(comment BusinessPlanDocument "The collection of all documents that describe the plans of a business for products, marketing, management and finance.")
(comment Arsenic "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of arsenic; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form -- but not necessarily.")
(comment SubstanceAbuse "The collection of events which occur when someone takes a drug inappropriately, whether recreationally or by overdosing.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (RightObjectOfPairFn SeventhRib) Tuberosity) "")
(disjointWith Paper-IBO Tool)
(comment AssistantChiefOfStaff-Logistics "The collection of instances of #$CoordinatingStaffMember-USArmy
with responsibility for the logistics integration of supply, maintenance, transportation, 
and services.")
(comment BlowingAir "Expelling air from the lungs in a controlled manner, whether for playing a flute or extinguishing flames on a group of birthday candles.")
(comment Melioidosis-Infection "The collection of #$BacterialInfections caused by
Pseudomonas pseudomallei. #$Melioidosis-Infection occurs in Burma, Vietnam,
Guam, and the Philippines.  It is present in soil,
water, and plants.  Human infection probably occurs from any of these
sources, by contamination of skin abrasions and possibly by inhalation
or ingestion; person-to-person transmission is rare.  It may manifest as an acute or chronic lung disease.")
(disjointWith PulverizationEvent ConstructionProject)
(comment HorseBoot "This is the collection of boot-like objects designed for horses.

There are various types, each designed for a specific function. ")
(comment templateGene "(#$templateGene TRANSFER GENE) means that GENE plays the role of a template in TRANSFER.")
(comment securedBy "A generalization of #$supportedBy. (#$securedBy OBJECT HOLDER) means that HOLDER is at least partially responsible for holding OBJECT in its current position.  If HOLDER were to be removed, then (everything else being equal) either all or part of OBJECT would move in some direction or other

relative to its frame of reference.  (Only _part_ of OBJECT would move if (say)

OBJECT is also #$securedBy a second HOLDER2, in which case OBJECT might simply

pivot around some point were only HOLDER removed.)  If HOLDER were to be moved

(in concert with anything else that OBJECT might be directly #$securedBy), then (everything else being equal) OBJECT would move with it.  Examples: a golf ball is #$securedBy a tee on which it sits and a helium-filled balloon is #$securedBy a string attaching it to a child's wrist.  Note that OBJECT's being #$securedBy

HOLDER from moving in a particular direction does _not_ in itself preclude the possibility of OBJECT's moving (at least a little) in some other direction: a gust of wind might momentarily blow the secured balloon along an arc-like path

about the child's wrist.  If, like the golf tee, HOLDER provides crucial _vertical_ support to OBJECT, consider using #$supportedBy.  If HOLDER merely _contributes_ to OBJECT's being secured without being essential to it, use #$securedBy-Contributing.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperationTypeByProgram "#$AttackByComputerOperationTypeByProgram is a subset of #$AttackByComputerOperationType.  Every instance of  this collection is a collection of attacks, instances of which are executed through use of the same sort of program. Examples of #$AttackByComputerOperationTypeByProgram include #$AttackByComputerOperation-Virus and #$AttackByComputerOperation-Worm.")
(comment WebSiteFn-Reference "A #$Cyc function that is an element of #$CollectionDenotingFunction. (#$WebSiteFn-Reference SUBJ) returns the collection of #$ReferenceWebSites which contain non-speculative, 'fact-oriented,' information about the particular thing SUBJ. These sites can be structured in various ways, but typically they are indexed to allow the user to search for specific facts quickly.  For example,  (#$WebSiteFn-Reference #$ZipCode) would denote the collection of all #$ReferenceWebSites that provide #$ZipCode listings or directories (#$MWakoff 9/14/99).")
(comment Celebrity-Political "Instances of #$Celebrity-Political are people (actually, subabstractions of people) who are well-known due to their involvement, however tangential, in politics.")
(comment CanOfFn "'(#$CanOfFn EDIBLE)' denotes the collection of all cans containing the food or drink EDIBLE.")
(comment TemperateMarineClimateCycle "climate of coastal areas in temperate regions, such as Seattle. Warm summer, cool winter, precipitation throughout")
(comment eventTypeFallsOnNthDayTypeInMonth "(#$eventTypeFallsOnNthDayTypeInMonth EVENT MONTH DAY-TYPE

NUM) is used to say that a special event falls annually on a specified Nth day of the week DAY-TYPE during a certain month MONTH.  For example, to say that Mother's Day falls on the second Sunday of May: (#$eventTypeFallsOnNthDayTypeInMonth #$MothersDay #$May #$Sunday 2).")
(comment wetnessOfObject "The degree of #$Wetness of an object.  The object need not be wet with water, but could be wet with any liquid. The liquid is specified with #$wetWithLiquid.")
(disjointWith UnitOfMonetaryRate UnitOfFrequency)
(comment MobileElectronicsMC "The collection of #$ElectronicDevices and

accessories used 'on the go'.  #$PalmtopComputer, #$CellularTelephone, and #$Pager are positive examples.")
(comment clinicalFormMostCommonInOrgType-Infection "(#$clinicalFormMostCommonInOrgType-Infection INF-GEN-TYPE ORG-TYPE INF-SPEC-TYPE)

means that if an infection INF is known to be an instance of

INF-GEN-TYPE, and an instance of ORG-TYPE is known to be the #$bodilyDoer of INF, it is extremely likely, absent information to support

the conclusion (#$not (#$isa INF INF-SPEC-TYPE)), that (#$isa INF

INF-SPEC-TYPE).")
(comment SoakingWet "Something that is saturated with a liquid (see #$wetWithLiquid), but not overly so.")
(comment FileCopiesFn "(#$FileCopiesFn FILE-TYPE) is the collection of all copies of computer files of type FILE-TYPE.")
(comment YearBCE-JulianFn "(#$YearBCE-JulianFn N) denotes the calendar year that is Nth year before the start of the common era. Indeed, when translated to #$YearFn these are negative years, with the exception of (#$YearBCE-JulianFn 1), which corresponds to (#$YearFn 0). ")
(disjointWith NucleotideChain-FivePrimeEnd NucleotideChain-ThreePrimeEnd)
(comment TranscriptOfEventTypeFn "#$TranscriptOfEventTypeFn takes as argument any type of event and returns the collection of transcripts [#$TranscriptOfSpeech-CWIS] of any event of that type.  For example,(#$TranscriptOfEventTypeFn #$Sermon) returns the collection of transcripts of sermons. To represent the collection of transcripts of a particular event (for example, Lincoln's speech at Gettysburg) use #$TranscriptOfEventFn.  To represent the collection of transcripts of a type of a #$ConceptualWork use #$TranscriptOfCWTypeFn, e.g. use (#$TranscriptOfCWTypeFn #$TVShow-CW) for the collection of transcripts of TV shows.  To represent the collection of transcripts of a particular episode of a type of TV show (for example, The Trouble with Tribbles episode) use #$TranscriptOfCWFn.")
(comment Loam "A specialization of #$Soil-Generic.  Each instance of #$Loam is a portion of soil composed of a mixture of clay, silt, sand and organic matter.")
(comment witnesses-Legal "(#$witnesses-Legal DOC WITNESS) means that WITNESS attests by signing DOCUMENT that
  the (other, nonwitness) signature(s) on DOCUMENT is (are) authentic.")
(comment FighterPlane-F16C "Modified version of the #$FighterPlane-F16, used by the U.S. in the Persian Gulf.")
(comment PPTByPackageType "The collection of types of drug products which are specified as to packaging, and may be specified as to strength, administration route, dosage form, and type of preparation (the drug compounds(s) contained).")
(comment Cruzado-Brazil "The unit of currency for Brazil-AtPresent.")
(comment PresentationLayerProtocol "The collection of all network protocols which implement a presentation layer. The only instances of #$NetworkProtocolStack that generally includes instances of  #$PresentationLayerProtocol are instances of #$OpenSystemInterconnectionReferenceModel. An instance of #$PresentationLayerProtocol takes the responsibility for routine tasks from an #$ApplicationLayerProtocol, such as converting between character sets.")
(comment relationExistsSpecExistsSpec "(#$relationExistsSpecExistsSpec PRED COL1 COL2) means that there

exists a subcollection of COL1, SUBCOL1 and a subcollection of COL2,

SUBCOL2 such that (PRED SUBCOL1 SUBCOL2).")
(comment in-Spiked "(#$in-Spiked SPIKE OBJ) means that SPIKE, an object with at least one sharp end, is lodged in OBJ, so that (#$in-Lodged SPIKE OBJ) holds.  Moreover, SPIKE is lodged in OBJ because a sharp end of SPIKE has pierced OBJ.  For example, #$in-Spiked would hold between a tack lodged in a wall or a nail driven into a two-by-four.  Typically, the rigid connection between OBJ and SPIKE can support forces substantially greater than the weight of SPIKE.")
(comment ExogenousOxidizingAgent "An external agent used in bacterial respiration, see #$Respiration-Bacterium.  The oxidizing agent is metabolized with the substrate so that the substrate will undergo a net oxidization.  This provides the cell with more energy possible in fermentation, see #$Fermentation-Bacterium.")
(disjointWith MatterTypeByPhysicalState HumanCapabilityType)
(comment tourTransitsFromTo "(#$tourTransitsFromTo TOUR MOVETYPE FROM TO) means that,
according to its itinerary, TOUR is supposed to include a movement of
type MOVETYPE from the #$PartiallyTangible FROM, considered as a
#$fromLocation, to the #$PartiallyTangible TO, considered as
#$toLocation.")
(comment Necking "The collection of events in which two (usually not more) people engage in intimate kissing which is usually accompanied by close bodily contact (hugging at least).")
(comment Basin "A container with sides and bottom, but open at the top.  The sides and bottom of instances of #$Basin are usually impermeable to liquids.  Instances of #$Basin may be bowl-shaped, box-shaped, etc.")
(comment interArg3ResultGenls "A ternary #$MetaRelation predicate for stating that a certain kind of complex, partly #$genls based relationship holds between the third argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned. (#$interArg2ResultGenls FUNC INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the third argument to FUNC, then -- regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be -- the value (if any) of that function for those arguments is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is: if INST is a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC ARG1 ARG2 INST ...) = VALUE, then VALUE is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  Note that, unlike (e.g.) the #$InterArgTypePredicates, #$interArg3ResultGenls _cannot_ be used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on functions.  See also the similar but more flexible quaternary #$interArgResultGenl.")
(comment Coccidioidomycosis "A form of respiratory infection - either asymptomatic or flu-like. Has an inhaled and a disseminated form. In disseminated form (approx 0.1% of cases), the infection produces lesions in lungs and abscesses throughout the body, and is frequently fatal.")
(comment objectRotating "The predicate #$objectRotating is used to refer to an object which is rotating in a particular #$Movement-Rotation event. (#$objectRotating MOVE OBJECT) means that OBJECT is turning during MOVE around an axis that spatially intersects OBJECT (or goes through a 'hole' in it). The #$primaryObjectMoving in a #$Movement-Rotation is always an #$objectRotating.")
(comment MusicType "This is the collection of all music types. It includes not only types-by-style

(basically genres) but also types-by-instrumentation, -period, -region, etc.")
(comment GoldenEagle "A collection of large birds, a spec of #$BirdOfPrey, living throughout the Northern Hemisphere.  Their color is dark brown with gold on the back of the head and neck.  Their scientific name is Aquila chrysaetos.")
(comment ReflexologyMassage "#$ReflexologyMassage is the collection of events in which a therapist called a 'reflexologist' massages a person's foot or hand in an effort to reduce that person's stress and cause physiological changes in his or her body. It is based on the premise that there are zones and reflex areas in the feet and hands that correspond to all body parts.")
(comment Chute-SlopingPath "A sloping pathway along which materials can be made to descend easily. Examples

would include the part of a children's slide that is used for sliding, and a laundry chute in a multi-level building, where

the laundry slides down the chute and collects at some location on a lower level.  Elements do not have to be devices.  Thus, a sled path, or a canyon can be considered elements of #$Chute-SlopingPath as well.")
(comment Ghost "The collection of #$Agent-Intangibles (q.v.) who were formerly #$Persons but have since died (see #$Deceased), and (it is commonly believed) are bound (perhaps temporarily) to the locales where as #$Persons they lived and died.  Despite their intangiblity (see #$Intangible), ghosts are traditionally believed to be perceivable to humans, at least on occasion.  Seeing a ghost, reportedly, can be a very frightening experience.")
(comment BallisticMissile-Oghab "The collection of ballistic missiles with a range of 40 kilometers.")
(comment Potassium "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of potassium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment DualIndexedMortgage "The collection of #$AdjustableRateMortgages that are also dual indexed (#$DualIndexedLoan).")
(comment HL-EndFn "An #$HL-EndFn term represents the ending point of a #$TemporalThing in a data structure that facilitates temporal relations inference.")
(comment WaitingOnATable "The objects involved in #$WaitingOnATable are  instances of #$EdibleStuff, #$Drink, etc., and maybe an instance of #$Table-PieceOfFurniture, too. ")
(comment MilitaryOperationsSituationMicrotheory "Each instance of #$MilitaryOperationsSituationMicrotheory contains background information that is relevant to a particular group of #$MilitaryOperations. This collection is partitioned into #$MilitaryOperationsStaticSituationMicrotheory and #$MilitaryOperationsDynamicSituationMicrotheory.")
(disjointWith RearWindowWithDefroster ManualCarWindow)
(disjointWith CharacterMode-Inscribed CharacterMode-ElectroMagnetic)
(disjointWith InterrogativeUtterance ImperativeUtterance)
(comment drugTypeAdministered "This predicate relates a drug administration event to the type of drug administered in the event.")
(comment GangRape "A collection of events.  Each element of #$GangRape is a horrific violent action in which the performers force another person to undergo an act of sexual intercourse.  A #$GangRape is typically performed by many people against one victim, typically female.--Colvin, March 9. 1999")
(comment CloudOfH2O "A cloud of particles of liquid or solid water in the atmosphere covering a #$GeographicalRegion.")
(disjointWith Manufacturing InformationBearingThing)
(comment HandBraking "Using a hand instead of a foot to brake a vehicle.  Bikes are often braked in this fashion.")
(comment CesareanBirth "A birth event in which the child is removed through an incision in the mother's abdomen.")
(comment rateOfFire-Sustained "(rateOfFire-Sustained GUN RATE) indicates  the number of rounds per minute that can be fired at a sustained rate.  This is in contrast to the cyclic rate.  The sustained rate includes factors like reloading, recocking, and overheating.  It also assumes that the gun is being  used for a sustained period of time, i.e., for at least a few minutes.  The  unit of RATE to use is TimesPerMinute.")
(disjointWith Temperature Pressure)
(comment interArgGenl2-1 "(#$interArgGenl2-1 PRED INDEPENDENT-COL DEPENDENT-COL) means that for assertions using PRED, when the first argument to PRED is a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-COL, then the second argument to PRED must be a subcollection of DEPENDENT-COL.")
(comment AirAssaultUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all offensive units that are inserted into           combat from air vehicles (usually choppers) without parachute           drop.")
(disjointWith Dock ProvingGround)
(comment containingObject "(#$containingObject CONT OBJ) means that OBJ is the physical object which is acting as the container in the instance of #$ContainingSomething, CONT.  See also #$containedObject.")
(comment UnderwritingSecurities "The collection of #$Underwritings in which an #$IntelligentAgent (almost always an #$Organization) brings a new security issue (#$TradeableSecurity) to the investment public in an offering.  The #$Organization performing the underwriting is not identical to the #$Organization (a #$LegalCorporation) which issues the security.  In #$Underwriting securities, the underwriting #$Organization assumes the risk of bringing the new issue to market by buying the issue from the issuer and guaranteeing the sale of a certain number of shares to investors.")
(comment CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm "The collection of closed, non-atomic denotational terms of the CycL language.  Each instance of #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm is a CycL term that contains no free variables, is constructible from other CycL terms via the syntax of CycL, and can have a denotatum (this last requirement excludes closed CycL sentences from #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm).  Examples: `(#$JuvenileFn #$Platypus)', `(#$JuvenileFn #$isa #$genls)', and `(#$TheSetOf ?X (#$objectHasColor ?X #$GreenColor))'.  Non-example: `(#$JuvenileFn ?X)'.")
(comment AttributiveFrame "Frames for adjectives that can be used attributively, like 'happy' in 'a happy person'.")
(comment Regio-Planetary "A collection of topographical features.  Each element of #$Regio-Planetary is a large geographical region with a significantly different #$AlbedoFeature-Topographical than the surrounding terrain.")
(comment CirrusCloud "The collection of wispy high ice clouds that often preceed a warm front.")
(comment ReformulatorMode "The collection of modes of operation of the #$CycLReformulator.  This collection is user-extensible, and the behavior of the reformulator in each mode is determined by reformulator rules and #$reformulationDirectionInMode meta-assertions on those rules.  In #$ReformulatorMode-Simplify mode, the reformulator will also use the #$CycLSimplifier to simplify expressions.")
(disjointWith Locomotion-FourLegged Locomotion-TwoLegged)
(comment movesInDirection-Throughout "(#$movesInDirection-Throughout OBJ DIR) means that OBJ moves in the

direction DIR throughout all spatial and temporal slices of OBJ.

Since instances of #$Entity rarely move in one direction throughout their

entire existence, assertions involving #$movesInDirection-Throughout

will usually be qualified with a #$holdsIn.  This predicate is useful

for inheriting the direction of motion of an

object to its temporal or spatial parts.  If such an inference is too

strong see #$movesInDirection-Average.  Negative exemplar cases of the

relationship include a winding river whose different spatial slices

follow different directions, or a deflating balloon whose different

temporal slices move in different directions.  Positive exemplar

usages of #$movesInDirection-Throughout could relate a specific point

of the winding river to its direction, or could relate the deflating

balloon at particular instant in time to its direction.  Related

predicates include #$directionOfTranslation-Avg and

#$directionOfTranslation-Throughout which relate a

#$Movement-TranslationEvent to a direction that all #$objectMovings of

that event move in.  #$movesInDirection-Throughout is to be preferred

over #$directionOfTranslation-Throughout in situations where the

computational cost of reifying a movement event (see

#$Movement-TranslationEvent) is not warranted.")
(comment Sangha-ReligiousOrderMember "The order of monks established by #$Buddha.")
(comment connectedViaConnector "(#$connectedViaConnector OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are connected via a connector which is #$connectedTo each of them.  It is not necessarily the case that OBJ1 #$touches OBJ2, but neither is it prohibited.")
(comment SuitJacket "#$SuitJacket corresponds to the collection of blazers and jackets that are worn with suits.  Note that a #$SuitJacket doesn't  have to be part of a multi-piece suit, but it will have the same general cut as a jacket that is part of a suit.")
(comment mediaSeriesDistributed "This predicate expresses the relation between a type of media series (such as a #$NewspaperSeries or #$TVSeriesProduct) and an event in which instantiations of an episode/issue of this series are disseminated via the media.  For example, (#$mediaSeriesDistributed Event001 #$USAToday-TheNewspaper) means that some edition of USA Today was circulated in Event001.  The first argument to #$mediaSeriesDistributed must be a #$MediaTransferEvent; the second must be a #$MediaSeriesProduct.")
(comment casualtyCountByAilment "(#$casualtyCountByAilment EVT WHAT AILMENT NUM) means that as a result of the event EVT, the number of WHAT who are suffering with the physical condition AILMENT is NUM.  WHAT is a type of #$Organism-Whole, and AILMENT is a type of #$AilmentCondition.  The subsets of #$AilmentCondition cover injuries as well as illnesses, allergies, and psychological disorders.  Note that an organism that suffers from some instance of an ailment is the #$bodilyDoer of that ailment instance.  Examples:  #$casualtyCountByAilment may be used to state the number of persons who are afflicted by smoke inhalation in a particular fire, the number who contract food poisoning from a family picnic, or the number who suffer shell shock as a result of a particular battle.")
(comment SexWorker "A specialization of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each instance of #$SexWorker is a person whose job involves either engaging in sexual acts with others, or sexually stimulating others (without necessarily engaging in sexual acts with them).  Notable specializations of #$SexWorker include #$Prostitute, #$Stripper, and #$PornStar.")
(comment Martian "Mythical creatures who come from #$PlanetMars.")
(comment Damp "Damp")
(comment goals-Microtheory "(#$goals-Microtheory AGENT MT) means that AGENT's goals include all of the propositions in MT.")
(disjointWith StateOfMatterChangeEvent Conveying-Generic)
(comment energyDerivedFrom "The expression `(#$energyDerivedFrom ENERGYSTUFF SOURCE)' means that the 

instance or quantum of #$EnergyStuff ENERGYSTUFF had SOURCE as its proximal 

source. The proximal source of the heat from your fireplace, for example, is the wood that

is burning, though the energy that created that wood came from the sun.   ")
(comment interArgReln2-4 "A binary #$InterArgRelnPredicate (q.v.).  (#$interArgReln2-4 RELN BINPRED) means that a formula built from RELN (i.e. a \"GAF\" or \"NAT\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence and  #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm) is semantically well-formed only if BINPRED holds between the second and fourth arguments to RELN (in that order) in the GAF/NAT.  That is, a formula (RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ..) is semantically well-formed only if (BINPRED ARG2 ARG4) holds.  For further explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations. See also the more general quaternary predicate #$interArgReln, which has two argument-places for specifying the pair of RELN's arguments that must be related by BINPRED.")
(disjointWith HollowCylindricalObject SheetOfSomeStuff)
(comment GlobularCluster "A #$GlobularCluster is a #$StarCluster which has so many stars that they are all gathered into a very spherical grouping due to their collective gravity.  A good example is the cluster M13 in the constellation #$Hercules-Constellation.")
(comment AthleticAward "A distinction or honor given by some awarding agent to a deserving agent usually as the outcome of an athletic competition.")
(comment Nizatidine "The chemical compound which is used to treat peptic acid problems.")
(comment PoundsPerSquareInch "Air pressure for tires and atmospheres is often measured in PSI -- pounds per square inch")
(comment genericallyIsa "(#$genericallyIsa GENERIC COLLECTION) relates a generic instance GENERIC to the unique COLLECTION it represents.  For example, (#$genericallyIsa (#$GenericInstanceFn #$Dog) #$Dog)")
(comment O-TheLetter "The letter O of the alphabet.  This is 'O' (or 'o') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.  As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterO and #$LatinSmallLetterO.")
(comment personWithJobPosition "(#$personWithJobPosition JOB PERSON) means that #$Person PERSON has #$JobPosition JOB. When this relation holds between JOB and PERSON, the #$JobPosition is filled. See #$JobOpen and #$JobFilled.")
(comment CelestialEvent "The collection of events that involve heavenly

bodies, which may or may not be observable from earth.")
(comment SpyPlane "The collection of aircraft intended for use in reconnaisance. Such planes often carry #$Sensors, cameras, and other surveillance equipment.")
(comment Appraiser "The collection of instances of #$PersonWithOccupation whose job it is to determine the likely selling price of some object based upon an interpretation of disinterested facts and judgements.")
(comment objectChemicallyBonded "(#$objectChemicallyBonded BONDING OBJ) means that OBJ, an
instance of #$ChemicalObject, is one of the objects bonded by BONDING, an
instance of #$ChemicalBonding.")
(comment physicalPortions "(#$physicalPortions WHOLE PART) means that PART is a representative physical part of WHOLE, in the sense that the intrinsic physical properties of WHOLE are also properties of PART.  Physical parts of WHOLE which are not representative in this sense should not be related to WHOLE by #$physicalPortions, but rather by #$physicalParts or #$physicalDecompositions (qq.v.).  For example, the SpaghettiSauce001 which is part of SpaghettiDinner001 would not be related to SpaghettiDinner001 by #$physicalPortions, since SpaghettiSauce001 differs from SpaghettiDinner001 in its composition (the latter has constituents -- noodles, parmesan cheese, and so on -- that the former does not have).  On the other hand, a #$physicalPortions of the dinner would include parts of all the constituents of the dinner.")
(comment AgentiveRole "A subcollection of #$ActorSlot.  Each instance ROLE of #$AgentiveRole must be an #$ActorSlot that satisfies the following conditions: (i) ROLE specifies what an agent does (in the strict sense) in an #$Event rather than describing what happens to the agent in the #$Event.  That is to say, (ROLE AGT EVENT), when true, must describe agency rather than a mere happening.  Thus, each #$ActorSlot that does not describe agency, such as #$objectActedOn, #$victim, #$instrument-Generic, #$bodilyDoer, #$fromLocation and #$motionPathway-Partial etc., is not an instance of #$AgentiveRole.  (ii) ROLE must be specific enough to distinguish itself from other instances of #$AgentiveRole. This means, roughly, that if SLOT is a generalization of both SLOT1 and SLOT2, where SLOT1 is different from SLOT2, then SLOT is not an instance of #$AgentiveRole if both SLOT1 and SLOT2 are.  Thus, #$interviewee is an instance of #$AgentiveRole while #$socialParticipants is not.")
(comment underspecifiedExpressionOf "(#$underspecifiedExpressionOf EXP THING FEATURE) says that EXP, in some abstract or perhaps metaphorical way, is an \"expression\" by THING of some underspecified \"feature\" FEATURE of THING.  So for example, one might assert (#$underspecifiedExpressionOf BobSpraypaintingLousCar001 Bob Anger) to mean that Bob's spraypainting Lou's car is an expression of Bob's anger.")
(comment TransmissionPathInjection "This is a collection of events in which information is intercepted by some source  which is capable of altering the content before forwarding it to the intended  #$informationDestination.")
(comment fedByConfluenceOfRivers "A #$SpatialPredicate and specialization of #$tributaries (q.v.) that holds 
only between #$Rivers.  (#$fedByConfluenceOfRivers BIGRIVER SMALLRIVER) 
means that BIGRIVER is either formed by or increased in volume by a 
confluence of rivers that includes SMALLRIVER.  That is, there is some 
place where SMALLRIVER merges with one or more other rivers (besides 
BIGRIVER itself) to form or increase the volume of BIGRIVER.  Note that 
the #$fedByConfluenceOfRivers relation does _not_ hold in cases where a 
smaller river feeds all by itself into (and thereby increases the volume
of) a bigger river; for such cases use the more general #$tributaries.")
(comment SpacePlatform-Unmanned "The collection of unmanned military space platforms.")
(comment NucleolyticProofreading "A collection of events in which a #$NucleicAcidPolymerase checks whether the #$Nucleotide it has just added to a #$PolynucleotideStrand is correctly base-paired. #$DNAPolymerase performs #$NucleolyticProofreading during #$Replication-DNA events. #$RNAPolymerase is not capable of performing #$NucleolyticProofreading during #$Transcription-DNAToRNA events.")
(comment Sunburn "Too much ultra-violet radiation causes skin to burn.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-TearDrop "#$AttackByComputerOperation-TearDrop is a subset of #$AttackByComputerOperation-DataFloodingOSCrashing.  It is the collection of uses of instances of #$TearDrop-DenialOfServiceProgram to perform an instance of #$AttackByComputerOperation-DenialOfService on a computer by sending malformed instances of #$Packet-Internet to a victim's machine in order to flood the machine's memory and thereby cause an instance #$ComputerCrashing.")
(comment Homeopath "The collection of all practitioners of homeopathy, a system of medicine whose fundamental principle is the law of similars - that like is cured by like. A #$Homeopath will give a patient a tiny dose of a substance that produces in healthy people the same symptoms that the patient exhibits.")
(comment connected-EdgeAlongCylinder "(#$connected-EdgeAlongCylinder SHEET CYL) means that a #$SheetOfSomeStuff, SHEET, is #$connectedAlongEdge to the outside surface of #$LongAndThin object CYL along its length.")
(comment GroceryCart "#$GroceryCart is the collection of handcarts that are designed to hold groceries.")
(comment collectionRestrictsWhen "(#$collectionRestrictsWhen COL SPEC PRED) means that when INST is an instance of COL and bears a binary relation to some X in PRED (i.e. (PRED INST X) or (PRED X INST) holds) then INST is also an instance of SPEC.  Note that SPEC is a spec of COL.")
(comment UtilityUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all support units specialized for facilitated call-up           and rapid deployment.")
(comment specifiedIBTTypeOfPIT "(#$specifiedIBTTypeOfPIT PIT IBTTYPE) means that IBTTYPE is the collection of all #$InformationBearingThings of a certain form which instantiate the #$PropositionalInformationThing, PIT.")
(comment ArtistOrEntertainerRepresentative "Some who helps arts/entertainer professionals find work.  Actors, musicians,(performers generally) and writers often have them.  Demote this to a lower part in the spec/genl hierarchy when appropriate. (and change the english assertion asking you to do so!).")
(comment TourDayFn "(#$TourDayFn TOUR N) returns the Nth day of the #$TravelTour TOUR.")
(comment Lutetium "The collection of all pieces (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of lutetium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment DesertClimateCycle "A specialization of #$AnnualClimateCycle.  Each instance of #$DesertClimateCycle is a year-long event consisting of weather occurring (typically) within a desert region.  Characteristics of a desert climate cycle include wide temperature extremes (from very hot in the day to cold at night) and very little yearly precipitation.")
(comment keGenlsConsiderationPreds "(#$keGenlsConsiderationPreds COL BIN-PRED) means that for every specialization SPEC-COL of COL, it should be considered whether there is some VALUE such that (BIN-PRED SPEC-COL VALUE) is known in the KB.")
(comment Transubstantiation "The collection of events in #$Catholicism in 

which #$CommunionWafer(a sliver of bread) is transformed into the body 

of #$JesusChrist. #$Transubstantiation is one of the key issues of doctrine

that separates #$Catholicism and #$ProtestantReligion.")
(comment constituentMass "(#$constituentMass ?obj ?constituent ?mass) means ?obj has ?mass amount of ?constituent as a #$constituents.")
(comment stoplistWord "(#$stoplistWord ?THING ?WORD) means that for the purposes of ?THING, ?WORD should not be treated as a content item.")
(comment BillionBarrels "A function which returns an element of #$Volume.  One billion barrels -- (#$BillionBarrels 1) or (#$Barrel-UnitOfVolume 1000000000).")
(comment causalPreconditionFor "(#$causalPreconditionFor COND PROP) means that unless the causal condition expressed in COND is true, PROP does not hold.")
(comment NewsShowHost "Each #$NewsShowHost is the host of a #$NewsShow.")
(comment Clostridiales-Order "A collection of #$Bacterium. A #$BiologicalOrder formed in the
#$Firmicutes-Division of the #$MoneraKingdom.  An important subtaxon is the
Clostridiaceae-Family.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are #$SporeFormingBacterium.")
(comment hasLiability "The predicate used to express that a #$LoanAgreement or some other #$FinancialObligation is a current liability for a particular #$IntelligentAgent.  Use with #$holdsIn.  Also see #$currentLiabilities.")
(comment fileCopyCreated "(#$fileCopyCreated CREATION FILE) means that FILE            is the instance of #$ComputerFileCopy created in the instance            of #$CreatingAFile, CREATION.  ")
(comment IntravenousDrug "drugs which are injected.")
(comment HumanlySeparable "level beyond which it cannot be separated by humans without tools")
(disjointWith UnmannedAircraft Paraglider)
(comment CrossingACountryBorderWOBorderCheck-Thing "Instances are cases where a good (something owned) crosses a country border without going through a border checkpoint.  This is only illegal within the context of certain #$Laws.")
(comment enforcer-FunctionalRole "(#$enforcer-FunctionalRole SYSTEM ENFORCER) means that
ENFORCER is responsible for helping to insure that the edicts of the
#$executive-FunctionalRole of SYSTEM are carried out.  ENFORCER may
have this responsibility singly or in concert with other agents
playing the same role.")
(comment Consulate-TheMission "The collection of all consulates, the official diplomatic representations of a country A in a foreign country B. Not to be confused with the buildings in which such offices are hosted. See #$Consulate-TheBuilding.")
(comment macroCapable "An element of #$ComputerProgram-CW is #$macroCapable if it includes the ability to define macros within its functionality.  A macro

typically enables easy execution of a complex command by remapping

keystrokes or menu selections.")
(comment SpecialPurposeVehicle "The collection of vehicles which are built and/or adapted for a specific purpose (other than generic passenger and cargo transport.")
(disjointWith ColorElectronicDisplayDevice MonochromeElectronicDisplayDevice)
(comment CommunicatingUsingADevice "A subset of #$Communicating in which some instance of #$CommunicationDevice is used           deliberately by the #$senderOfInfo in the communication.            Examples include (#$UsingAFn #$Telephone),           #$InternetCommunication, two-way radio communication, using a microphone           on a stage, etc.")
(comment CC2CommonOntologyConstant "#$CC2CommonOntologyConstant a collection of constants that were designed by CC2

        program participants who do not work at Cycorp. It is intended to facilitate communication among

        technology developers in CC2, and so its contents are included in all IKB releases.  All instances of #$CC2CommonOntologyConstant should be located in the #$CC2CommonOntologyMt. Cycorp

        does not take credit or responsibility for instances of this collection. Cyclists from Cycorp are

        not discouraged from enriching the constants in this collection and then moving the enriched

        constants to more general microtheories.")
(comment roadSpeed "The maximum speed of a vehicle when travelling on a road. This is relevant for #$Tank-Vehicles that are meant to travel over all kinds of terrains, yet can only go at their #$roadSpeed when traveling on a road.")
(comment Fuse-ElectricalComponent "Device that prevents another electrical device from drawing too much electrical current.")
(comment Pitch-WhileTranslating "Turning along a lateral axis perpendicular to the front to back axis of a translating object (often a craft).  A boat may do this as it dives into the trough of a wave.  It also applies to air- and spacecraft.")
(comment USRepresentative "The collection of elected officials which serve in the United States House of Representatives.  Each state in the nation is represented by a number of representatives proportionate to the state's population.")
(comment subEchelonsInOrg "(#$subEchelonsInOrg SUPERLEVEL SUBLEVEL SCALE) means that the echelon  SUBLEVEL is the next strictly 'lower' (not as high as) echelon below SUPERLEVEL in the partially ordered echelon system represented by SCALE,  exactly one level lower (immediate successor) than SUPERLEVEL in the  same #$BranchOfMilitaryService.")
(disjointWith RaisingLivingThings SportsAction)
(comment BookCopy "A collection of #$InformationBearingObjects. A #$BookCopy is a physical object consisting of folded, cut, bound, and usually printed sheets.  Book copies are often contain #$TextualMaterial, but sometimes contain only images.  Instances of #$BookCopy are instantiations of instances of #$Book-CW (the #$ConceptualWorks).")
(comment HTST-Pasteurization "A specific method of
#$Pasteurization.  The object acted on in such events (e.g., milk) is
held for at least 15 seconds at a minumum temperature of
(#$DegreeCelsius 72).  This process will kill many pathogens of
milk-borne diseases such as Salmonellosis and #$Tuberculosis, and it
also kills #$Enzymes that may spoil the product.")
(comment notAssertibleCollection "A #$UnaryPredicate used for stating a certain restriction regarding the use of a given #$Collection in assertions to the Cyc Knowledge Base.  (#$notAssertibleCollection COL) means that no ground atomic formula (or \"GAF\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence) whose initial (or \"0th\" argument-place) term is `#$isa', and whose 2nd argument-place term denotes COL, can be asserted to the KB.  See also #$notAssertible, which constrains predicates in a similar fashion.")
(comment hides "ARG1 hides ARG2 from #$EnergyType ARG3")
(comment Monastery-Organization "This is the collection of monasteries

considered as organizations. A monastery in this sense

is a #$MultiIndividualAgent much like a company. (The main difference is that

many of the monks don't leave the building and go home after work.)")
(comment GayStory "The subset of #$EroticStory whose elements contain the propositional content of an #$EroticStory in which two or more instances of #$MalePerson engage in #$HomosexualBehavior-Male.")
(comment ExtraocularMuscleSet "The #$Collection of all instances of #$ExtraocularMuscleSet.  The #$ExtraocularMuscleSet consists of six #$Muscles which control #$Eye rotation.  The #$Muscles are the superior and inferior oblique and the superior, lateral, inferior, and medial rectus.")
(comment keFarthestGenlsStrongSuggestionInverse "(#$keFarthestGenlsStrongSuggestionPreds COL BIN-PRED) means that for
every specialization SPEC-COL of COL such that SPEC-COL is not known to have dependent specializations, it is strongly suggested that
there exist some VALUE such that (BIN-PRED VALUE SPEC-COL) is known in
the KB.")
(comment holdsInTypeOfTime-Always "(#$holdsInTypeOfTime-Always MT TYPE) means that the assertions in MT are true throughout the entire temporal extent of instances of TYPE.  See also #$holdsInTypeOfTime-Sometime.")
(disjointWith ControlledLand InternationalOrganizationOfCountries)
(comment IgnoringSomething "Intentionally paying no attention to something.  If someone ignores a thing, they do not look at it and do not listen to the sounds it makes.")
(disjointWith TransportationDevice MeasuringDevice)
(comment culturalRegionOfOrigin "(#$culturalRegionOfOrigin COL PLACE) means that COL (a spec of #$CulturalThing) originated in the #$GeographicalRegion PLACE.")
(comment OppositeAngleFn "This function denotes the angular measure of the interior angle that is across from the edge in arg1  in the triangular object that is arg 2, i.e. its opposite angle.")
(comment ReasoningWithTenseAuxiliaryMicrotheory "Instances of #$ReasoningWithTenseAuxiliaryMicrotheory are

microtheories used for the following purposes: For a particular

project or a part of it, if it requires reasoning with tenses and such

reasoning is supposed to be carried out by using microtheories with

#$mtPrecedes relation among them, instances of

#$ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheory will be used.  Let us call these

instances RWTmts.  These RWTmts are supposed to relate to each other,

within the project or the part of the project, through #$mtPrecedes,

forming an event ordering (interval ordering) in

#$ReasoningWithTense-InferenceMt and

#$ReasoningWithTense-InferenceMt-MixedDateSeries, and as a linear

ordering in #$ReasoningWithTense-InferenceMt-LinearTime and

#$ReasoningWithTense-InferenceMt-SingleDateSeries.  There are other

relations between RWTmts as well, like #$mtPrecedes-Metric,

#$mtPrecedes-NthDate-Forward etc.  (1) Whether the WRTmts for one

project are related to each other as an event ordering or a linear

ordering, an instance Mt-AUX of #$ReasoningWithTenseAuxiliaryMicrotheory

needs to be used to `separate' them from other WRTmts for other

projects, for otherwise #$mtPrecedes, #$mtPrecedes-Metric etc. may mix

up RWTmts for different projects.  Thus we require a relation

#$mtConverts-RWT-Aux between Mt-AUX and those WRTmts for the project

in order for the rules concerning event ordering or linear ordering to

fire.  (2) There are assertions in some microtheory, say Mt, whose

contents need to be used in all the RWTmts for a project in such a way

that if PROP holds in Mt, then PROP, (#$willAlwaysBe PROP) and

(#$hasAlwaysBeen PROP) etc. must hold in all RWTmts for the project.

In such cases, Mt-AUX can be used as a specMt of Mt, and the relation

(#$mtConverts-RWT-Aux Mt-AUX Mt-0) for each Mt-0 of

those WRTmts should be asserted.  For an example of how these

microtheories are used in modal reasoning via microtheories, see

#$NoteOnModalReasoningViaMicrotheories.")
(comment AntibioticCream "An ointment containing an antibiotic, which is intended to be used on wounds to prevent infection.")
(comment through-UnderspecifiedPortal "(#$through-UnderspecifiedPortal ACT PORTAL) states that an
abstract locational relation holds between ACT and PORTAL, where
Portal is a #$Portal-Underspecified passed through during ACT.
#$through-UnderspecifiedPortal is an underspecified semantic representation
that may be elaborated to represent either a spatial example of
'passing through' (as in 'cutting through the park') or a temporal use
of crossing ('through the centuries philosophers have argued about
...') or a metaphorical use ('Bill went through Jones to have his
proposal reviewed').  Note that #$through-UnderspecifiedPortal and
#$across-UnderspecifiedRegion are very similar, but differ in the
conceptualizations they demand of their arguments. One can go through
a door, and cross a threshold, but not cross a door.")
(comment (Milli Liter) "A (#$Milli #$Liter), or milliliter, is a unit of volume derived by dividing a liter by 1000 - in the real world this is about the size of a cubic pinhead.")
(comment UnifyFn "(#$UnifyFn A1 A2) unifies the Dags A1 and A2, each of which represents a typed-feature structure, to produce a new typed feature structure that contains all the information in A1 and A2. See also #$DagFn and #$dagOf.")
(comment Monoplane "The collection of all airplanes which have one primary set of wings.  Most modern airplanes are monoplanes, although some airplanes used for crop-dusting and aerobatics are biplanes.")
(comment MetabolicSubstrate "The collection of the substances, for
example a nutrient, used in #$MetabolicPathways and acted upon by
#$Enzymes. The substance is converted during metabolism to an
end-product. This end-product is normally a direct energy source for
the cell, like #$AdenosineTriphosphate.")
(comment TheSpec "#$TheSpec is a type-level version of #$TheInstance.  Where

 (#$TheInstance COL) returns an instance I of COL, (#$TheSpec

 COL) returns a collection C such that

 (#$genls C COL).")
(comment ShreddingEvent "A specialization of both #$PhysicalDestructionEvent and #$SeparationEvent.  In each instance of #$ShreddingEvent, some item or items are destroyed by a large number of ripping (see the collection #$Ripping) sub-events.  An example would be the tearing of office files into tiny pieces by a machine designed for that purpose. A shirt suddenly tearing due to pressure applied by the wearer's muscles would, however, not be an instance of #$ShreddingEvent, but only of #$Ripping.")
(comment M3MediumGirderBridge "Each   #$M3MediumGirderBridge  (MGB)  is a  hand-erectable, heavy-duty, prefabricated  deck  bridge consisting  of  high  strength components, which can  be  assembled into bridges of  varying lengths. The  key advantages of MGB  over #$BaileyBridge-Military are speed and ease of erection.  One MGB set contains enough components to construct 102 feet of Military  Load Class (MLC) 60 bridge.   With the use  of a Reinforcement Kit and two  sets of MGB, a 160-foot  span MLC 60 bridge can be constructed.  Although the MGB can withstand  MLC 70 loads, the effective life  of the bridge is  shortened from about 10,000 to 7,000 crossings.  The bridge set can also be used to  construct a variety of shorter span bridges.  The  rapid construction characteristics  of the MGB provide a capability which  can be used well  forward in the  main battle  area.  The MGB  and the #$BaileyBridge-Military are considered as   complementary systems,  each   satisfying  different  operational requirements.  The primary role of the MGB is for tactical bridging in the brigade area while  the #$BaileyBridge-Military is used  primarily as a   lines  of  communication  bridge.  As   the  tactical situation permits, MGB  would be removed and replaced  by Bailey, timber or steel bridges.  (Source: Engineer Systems Handbook, 4/97)")
(comment LeptospiraInterrogans "These #$ProkaryoticCells are often found in the urine and feces
of animals; human infection is accidental, following exposure to
contaminated water or other contaminated materials.")
(disjointWith LandTransportationDevice PatrolWatercraft)
(comment OrganizationPolicy "A specialization of #$Agreement.  Each instance of #$OrganizationPolicy is an agreement which contains the terms of some policy of a particular organization.  Instances of #$OrganizationPolicy would include U.S. Federal government hiring policies, a policy governing a corporation's charitable or political donations, or a school dress code.")
(comment InvestmentPortfolio-CW "A document [#$DocumentaryCW] which lists an agent's investments and their value.")
(comment personTakingTourMightParticularlyEnjoyEvent "(#$personTakingTourMightParticularlyEnjoyEvent TOUR PERSON

EVTTYPE) means that an argument exists to the effect that, if PERSON

were to take TOUR, PERSON might particularly enjoy an

event of type EVTTYPE.")
(comment Argon "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of argon in stuffeous form.")
(comment HigherEducationCOS "The collection of courses of study which are more advanced than high school, including undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn NinthRib) Tuberosity) "")
(comment TriathlonSportsEvent "Each #$TriathlonSportsEvent is a sports competition with three segments in which each competitor competes.  Very typically, the segments involve a foot race, a bicycle race, and a swimming race.")
(comment AssistantChiefOfStaff-Operations "The collection of instances of #$CoordinatingStaffMember-USArmy
with responsibility for all matters concerning training, operations and plans, and force 
development and modernization.")
(comment GloryHole "Elements of this collection are holes between two rooms (usually men's room stalls), used for #$Fellatio.")
(comment HardeningAWebsite "A specialization of both #$ComputerActivity and #$ProtectingSomething.  In each instance of #$HardeningAWebsite, some instance of a #$WorldWideWebSite is protected against instances of #$AttackByComputerOperation-DefacingAWebsite.")
(comment PepperPlant "Individual pepper plants.  This term generically covers green peppers, jalapeno peppers, and all the many other varieties.")
(comment EpidemicTyphus-NAmerica "A collection of #$BacterialInfections caused by Rickettsia canada.  These infections are severe febrile diseases transmitted by the tick.  This infection is similar to that caused by Rickettsia prowsecki, but it is limited to North America.")
(disjointWith DegenerationEvent Baking-Hardening)
(comment AerosolDeodorant "Aerosol deodorant: the stuff itself, not a package of it.")
(comment HorseGallopingBoot "This is the collection of #$HorseBoots which are designed to protect the cannon bones, splint bones, sesamoids, pastern, flexor and extensor tendons, suspensory ligaments and the fetlock area from injuries.")
(comment sequenceTranscribed "(#$sequenceTranscribed EVT SEQ) means that the coding sequence SEQ which is a molecular subcomponent of a #$DNAMolecule that codes for protein is the object transcribed in an instance of  #$Transcription-DNAToRNA EVT.")
(comment Torture "A collection of events. In an instance of #$Torture, an #$perpetrator intentionally inflicts physical or psychological distress on a #$Person or #$NonPersonAnimal in the #$perpetrator's control, either for pleasure or to get them to do something they would ordinarily be unwilling to do, especially give the #$perpetrator some information.")
(comment LetterToTheEditor " The collection of letters to the editor.")
(comment AssistedLiving "This is the collection of events in which persons, usually

elderly, live in arrangements wherein some of the tasks involved in everyday life

are taken care of for them. These tasks often include preparing meals and cleaning, and may include

personal hygiene, administering medications, and so on. Many retirement communities 

are built with the plan that many of their residents will be living in such arrangements.")
(comment Province "A specialization of #$State-Geopolitical.  Each instance of #$Province is a  major geopolitical subdivision of a country, corresponding closely to a U.S. state.  Instances of #$Province include #$VinhBinh-ProvinceVietnam, #$SoukAhras-ProvinceAlgeria, and #$Manitoba-CanadianProvince.")
(comment Film-FreeSheet "The collection of all films that are unattached along their surfaces.  Exemplars include #$PhotographicFilm, the surface of SoapBubbles, and #$PlasticWrap.  For instances of #$LiquidFilm which coat a surface use the sibling concept #$Film-Coating.")
(disjointWith UnitOfFlowRate UnitOfFrequency)
(comment AnimeTVShow "The collection of #$TVShow-CWs that use the anime style.  For a detailed explaination of this style see #$Anime.")
(comment streetSystemOfArea "(#$streetSystemOfArea SYSTEM AREA) means that SYSTEM is a street system that is maximally spread throughout much of (and possibly beyond) AREA.  SYSTEM's being \"maximally spread\" throughout AREA means that it must not be a proper #$subPathSystems of any other 

street system wholly in AREA and covering a larger 

portion of AREA.  (If there were such a larger system, 

presumably, _it_ would be related to AREA by #$streetSystemOfArea.)  See also #$StreetSystemOfAreaFn and #$transPathSystemTypeOfRegion.")
(comment Molding "A collection of events.  In each #$Molding, a mold is used to form a softened substance so that it hardens into (and retains) a specific shape.")
(comment RNAMolecule-FivePrimeEnd "The collection of 5 prime ends of all RNA molecules.")
(comment FROG7RocketLauncher "A collection of rocket launchers with a 40 kilometer range.")
(comment programRunBy "#$programRunBy is used to assert that an agent intentionally initiates a computer process.  #$programRunBy PROGRAM AGENT) means that the instance of #$IntelligentAgent, AGENT, runs the instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW, PROGRAM.")
(comment travelSubLegs "(#$travelSubLegs TOUR PATH SUBPATH) means that SUPATH is a
'subleg' of the leg of TOUR constituted by PATH.  This entails, among
other things, (#$subPaths PATH SUBPATH).  Also, if it is known that
PATH is the #$travelLegs of TOUR, and (#$subPaths PATH SUBPATH), then
(#$travelSubLegs TOUR PATH SUBPATH) will be inferred as the default.")
(comment Guilder-Suriname "The unit of currency for Suriname-AtPresent.")
(comment ProtocolStackLayer "#$ProtocolStackLayer is the collection of all #$NetworkProtocols which are classifed relative to their position in a #$NetworkProtocolStack.  An instance of #$ProtocolStackLayer is expected to provide certain services to other #$NetworkProtocols which are instances of different #$ProtocolStackLayers.")
(disjointWith Configuration RetainingUserRights)
(comment Hemp-Fiber "Quantities of fiber derived from the stems of  the hemp plant.")
(comment powerInRegion-Generic "#$powerInRegion-Generic specifies the degree of power or influence that some #$IntelligentAgent has in some #$GeographicalRegion. (#$powerInRegion-Generic AGENT REGION GENERIC-VALUE) means that AGENT's level of power or influence in REGION is GENERIC-VALUE.  To specify the exact type of power involved, see #$powerInRegion-Economic, #$powerInRegion-Military, #$powerInRegion-Geopolitical.")
(comment SlimeLayer-Bacterium "A collection of the thick layer of hydrophilic gel surrounding a bacterial cell.  It is transparent and not readily stainable.  If this layer is amorphous, it is a slime layer; however, if the layer is discrete, it is refered to as a capsule, see also #$Capsule-Bacterium.")
(disjointWith BiologicalLivingObject (SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromTypeFn Thing outputsCreated Boiling))
(comment problemWithIKB "(#$problemWithIKB CYC-TERM) means that the instance of #$CycLIndexedTerm, CYC-TERM, has assertions on it that may cause problems for an IKB build.")
(comment linkedByBodyOfWater "a smaller body of water such as a strait which joins two larger ones.  The order of this list is 1st- the larger body of water; 2nd- the linking body of water")
(comment SpecifiedPsychologicalTest "A specialization of #$DevisedPracticeOrWork.  Each instance of this collection is a psychological test, such as the Myers-Briggs Type Indicator test.")
(comment Shark-GreatWhite "A collection of large sharks of the mackerel family.  Often referred to simply as white sharks.  Their scientific name is Carcharodon carcharias.  Also known as the White Pointer or White Death.")
(comment SubLKeyword "The subcollection of #$SubLSymbol consisting of all SubL keywords.  Instances include the symbols `:KEYWORD', `:OBJECT', and `:PLURAL'.  Every instance of #$SubLKeyword satisfies (in the sense relevant to #$defnIff) `KEYWORDP'.  Note that #$SubLKeyword, like most instances of #$CycLExpressionType, is \"quoted\" (see #$quotedCollection).")
(comment GarbageCollecting "What garbage collectors, custodians, and maids do as part or all of their job.")
(comment MiG-29-Fighter "The collection of a type of Russian fighter aircraft.")
(comment Boron "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of boron; typically, these will be tightly bound into  form, but not necessarily.\")(\"All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of boron; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form -- but not necessarily")
(comment ImplicitISObjectFn "(#$ImplicitISObjectFn ?KEYOBJ ?LF) denotes the  object which is the value of the implicit field, ?LF, in the information-source tuple idenitified by ?KEYOBJ.  The most common sort of tuple may be a row in a physical database table.")
(comment President-HeadOfGovernmentOrHeadOfState "A collection of persons.  Each instance of #$President-HeadOfGovernmentOrHeadOfState is a person who holds the title of president of some #$Country, whether that title belongs to a position which is #$HeadOfState or #$HeadOfGovernment (or both). Examples: Boris Yeltsin, #$BillClinton, Jiang Zemin, Lee Dung-Hui.")
(comment TreeOrdering-Strict "The collection of all those #$MathematicalOrderings ORDER in which the ordering relation R is irreflexive and transitive on the #$baseSet S of ORDER, and in which every pair of different elements of S has a common 'R'-lower-bound' (where R'(X Y) iff R(X Y) or X = Y), and the set of 'R'-lower-bounds' of each X in S is ordered in a chain by R' (i.e., {Y: Y is in S and R'(Y X)} is a chain).  Note that the only difference between a #$TreeOrdering and a #$TreeOrdering-Strict is that the ordering relation of the former is reflexive while that of the latter is irreflexive.")
(comment equalStrings-CaseInsensitive "(#$equalStrings-CaseInsensitive STRING1 STRING2) means that the #$CharacterStrings STRING1 and STRING2 contain the same characters in the same order, although some of the characters in STRING1 may differ in case from some of the characters in STRING2.  For example, (#$equalStrings-CaseInsensitive \"Foo\" \"fOo\") holds.")
(comment Minute-UnitOfAngularMeasure "A unit to measure the size of angles; 60 minutes = 1 degree (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure)")
(comment AnalogyCaseFn "(#$AnalogyCaseFn EVENT) denotes the #$AnalogyCase which is based on the given EVENT.  This function is primarily used with #$matchBetween to state that an #$AnalogyMatch exists between two cases which are based on two events.")
(comment WaitingOnATable "The recipients of #$WaitingOnATable are the customers who sit at a table and who consume the #$EdibleStuff.")
(comment CommandVehicle "The subset of military vehicles which transport commanding officers.")
(comment MenageATrois "The collection of all instances of #$SexualBehavior with exactly three participants whom the behavior is #$performedBy.")
(comment CooperationEvent "A collection of all instances of #$SocialOccurrence that can be called 'cooperations'.  For each #$CooperationEvent COOP the following hold: (i) there are at least two #$IntelligentAgents AGT1 and AGT2 such that (#$partnersInCooperation AGT1 AGT2 COOP), (ii) AGT1 and AGT2 share a GOAL, (iii) there are subevents ACT1 and ACT2 of COOP, both of which are #$PurposefulActions, such that ACT1 is performed by AGT1 with the intent of furthering GOAL and ACT2 is performed by AGT2 with the intent of furthering GOAL, (iv) AGT1 believes that ACT2 furthers GOAL and AGT2 believes that ACT1 furthers GOAL, and (v) the fact ACT1 and ACT2 both further GOAL is not an unexpected coincidence: it was a part of AGT1's expectation that an act like (i.e. of the same kind as) ACT2, performed by AGT2, would further GOAL; and it was a part of AGT2's expectation that an act like ACT1, performed by AGT1, would further GOAL.")
(comment HarassingForeignBusiness "The collection of events where the a state actively discourages a foreign business to conduct trade within the state.")
(comment ProvidenciaRettgeri "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies under #$Providencia-Genus
in the #$MoneraKingdom.")
(comment typesHydrogenBondBetweenCapable "(#$typesHydrogenBondBetweenCapable COL1 COL2) means that
instances of COL1 can form hydrogen bonds with instances of COL2, where
'can' means that it is chemically possible.")
(disjointWith RearWindowWithDefroster Windshield)
(disjointWith CharacterMode-Sounded CharacterMode-ElectroMagnetic)
(disjointWith ImperativeUtterance DeclarativeUtterance)
(comment Fluconazole "The chemical compound which is an anti-fungal. #$Fluconazole is
used to treat #$Candida and other #$FungalInfections. It has less liver
toxicity than #$Ketoconazole.")
(comment MissilePatrolVessel "The collection of military vessels designed to patrol for #$Missiles.")
(disjointWith OpeningSomething InformationBearingThing)
(comment FillingANewPrescription "The collection of all events in which a #$DrugPrescription is filled for the first time.  This is a subset of the collection of #$FillingAPrescription which is disjoint from #$FillingARefillPrescription.")
(comment rolesTemporallyExclusiveInSystemType-Constraint "(#$rolesTemporallyExclusiveInSystemType-Constraint SYSTEM-TYPE ROLE1 ROLE2) means that it is not possible to assert to Cyc that the same agent plays ROLE1 and ROLE2 in a #$FunctionalSystem of type SYSTEM-TYPE at the same time.  That is, if Cyc knows that (#$isa SYS SYSTYPE) and (#$holdsIn TEMP (ROLE1 SYS AGENT), (#$holdsIn TEMP (ROLE2 SYS AGENT)) is semantically constrained to be an #$unknownSentence:  attempting to assert it will generate an error condition.")
(comment requisiteFor "If there is a propositional precondition PRECON for SIT2 such that SIT1's 'happening' is a precondition for PRECON becoming true, then (#$requisiteFor SIT1 SIT2).")
(disjointWith BeliefSystem GeneticInformationStructure)
(comment birthChild "(#$birthChild BIRTH ANIM) means that ANIM is the #$Animal that is born in the #$BirthEvent BIRTH.")
(disjointWith Density Pressure)
(comment AirBasedReconnaissanceUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units specialized for conducting           reconnaissance missions from airborne platforms: balloons,           airplanes, and helicopters. Orbital reconnaissance may constitute a           borderline case.")
(comment countryOfAddress "(#$countryOfAddress LOC COUNTRY) means that the #$ContactLocation LOC is located in the #$Country COUNTRY.  For example, the contact location for #$Cycorp is related by #$countryOfAddress to the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.  See also #$ContactLocation.")
(comment ArtificialLanguage-Formal "All elements of ArtificialLanguage that have a formally and explicitly specified syntax and/or semantics. Some examples are computer programming languages and languages of formal logic.")
(comment DiplomaticProtest "The collection of events in which one country or international organization uses diplomatic channels to protest the behavior of another country.  Instances of #$DiplomaticProtest are expressed by a representative from the protesting country and are typically delivered to a representative of the country whose action is protested.  Elements of #$DiplomaticProtest may also be elements of #$DiplomaticRequest.")
(comment RegularAdjFrame "Frames for adjectives that can be used both attributively and predicatively, like 'happy' in 'a happy person' and 'Chris is happy'.")
(comment Reticulum-Venusian "The collection of topographical features where each element is a net-like pattern on the planet Venus.")
(comment IceCloudstuff "This is the stuff that makes up the weather clouds that are very high and made of.")
(comment defaultReformulatorModePrecedence "(#$defaultReformulatorModePrecedence PRIMARY-MODE
SECONDARY-MODE TERTIARY-MODE ...), asserted in the microtheory MT,
means that in MT or a specMt thereof (unless overridden),
the #$CycLReformulator will use PRIMARY-MODE as its primary mode,
SECONDARY-MODE as its secondary mode, etc.  This helps the
reformulator establish precedence of #$CycLReformulatorDirectives.
Do not specify both tersify and verbosify.")
(comment Locomotion-FourLegged "The collection of all locomotion events in which the locomotor uses four feet or foot-like extremities to move along a solid surface.  Examples include instances of most locomotion events performed by the larger kinds of land animals such as lions, horses, and elephants.")
(disjointWith HomosexualHuman HeterosexualHuman)
(comment SatelliteTVBroadcasting "The collection of all #$TVBroadcasting events in which the signal is bounced off a satellite into a dish-shaped #$SatelliteTVAntenna connected directly to the #$TelevisionSet on which the images are displayed. Does not include 'satellite feeds' in which a signal is relayed via satellite from a television camera to the broadcast station, and broadcast traditionally from there.")
(comment solute "The predicate #$solute indicates a particular instance of #$PartiallyTangible in a #$Solution which is dissolved in the #$solvent of that #$Solution.")
(comment GeneralTenseReasoningConstant "This collection contains all constants for general tense 

reasoning in Cyc, created to make it easier to get all relevant notions.  

All but #$currentDate are metalanguage constants.  Note 

that tense operators and tense predicates are not included in this 

collection, but in #$TensePredicate.")
(comment SideEffectsFn "Denotes the physiological side-effects of a medical treatment. Note that side-effects are not always negative or unwanted, e.g., the side-effects of a blood-pressure treatment might include a remission of impotence (as with Viagra, originally intended to treat heart problems) or increased hair growth in bald men, and so on.")
(comment Politics "The collection of activities, methods, and tactics in furtherance of affecting governmental policies (or sometimes activities of other large institutions).")
(comment Dry "Dry")
(comment CallusOnSkin "The harsh and tough skin typically found on the surface of hands and feet.")
(disjointWith Cleaning (TransportViaFn TransportationDevice))
(comment LeftRiverbankFn "(#$LeftRiverbank RIVER) denotes the left riverbank of RIVER, an instance of #$River.")
(comment UnixShell "The collection of all Unix #$ShellPrograms - command interpreters that take textual commands from a user or program and execute them.")
(comment adjacentTo "(#$adjacentTo OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are touching, and that their region of contact is (at least for practical purposes, relative to the objects' dimensions and shapes) a line (i.e. the contact region is not a point, though the \"line\" of contact might actually have some height).   Moreover, OBJ1 is neither mostly above nor mostly below OBJ2.  Positive examples: adjacent squares on a chessboard, bordering countries, a connected pair of puzzle pieces.  Negative examples: diagonally touching squares on a chessboard, a geographical region and the air directly above it, one block stacked on top of another.")
(comment BinaryStarSystem "This is the collection of binary stars. Binary stars are

pairs of stars which are close enough to orbit about each other.")
(disjointWith NobelPrize AthleticAward)
(comment ErgotamineTartrate "The chemical compound which is an anti-migraine drug.")
(comment TechnicalWriter "A person who writes technical documents for a living.")
(comment MM-Hg "Millimeters of #$Mercury -- this strange unit is used to describe blood pressures and barometric pressures on earth.")
(comment exportDestinationFractionDuring "(#$exportDestinationFractionDuring REGION1 REGION2 THING NR) means that NR is the quotient of the monetary value of the exports by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION1 to the #$GeographicalRegion REGION2 during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING (as dividend) and the monetary value of REGION1's exports of all goods and services during the temporal extent of THING (as divisor).  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  For example, to express the fact that exports to the United States accounted for 6 percent of the total value of Oman's exports in 1995, we can say (#$exportDestinationFractionDuring #$Oman #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica (#$YearFn 1995) (#$Percent 6)).  See also #$exportAmountDuring.")
(comment P-TheLetter "The letter P of the alphabet.  This is 'P' (or 'p') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.  As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterP and #$LatinSmallLetterP.")
(comment jobPositionHasPositionType "(#$jobPositionHasPositionType JOB POS-TYPE) means that #$JobPosition JOB has the job duties and responsibilities normally associated with #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg POS-TYPE. Use #$JobPositionTypeFn to denote the collection of all #$JobPositions of a certain #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg.")
(disjointWith WeatherEvent CelestialEvent)
(comment SalvageShip "The collection of ships intended to be used in salvage operations.")
(comment romanticInterest "(#$romanticInterest PERS1 PERS2) indicates that PERS1 is interested, in a romantic way, in PERS2.  The two might actually be in a relationship, in which case a more specific predicate such as #$boyfriend, #$girlfriend, #$mate, etc. should probably be used.  However, it is possible for one person to have another as a #$romanticInterest where the second person doesn't even know the first.")
(comment Broker "Instances of the collection #$Broker are #$BusinessPersons who act as intermediaries between buyers (see #$buyer) and seller (see #$seller).  A #$Broker facilitates the finalization and conclusion of a #$SalesContract, and receives a fee for this service.  The #$Broker is therefore a #$providerOfService within and of the #$ServiceEvents, brokering.")
(comment InterArgGenlAttributeIsaPredicate "Those instances of #$InterArgConstraintPredicate used to specify conditional #$isa requirement of one argument (the dependent argument) of a #$Relation given the #$genlAttributes of another argument (the independent argument).  The arg1 is the Relation.  The arg2, the independent argument, is an instance of #$AttributeValue that defines the antecedent of the conditional constraint.  The arg3 is a #$Collection that must have the following property: if a spec attribute of the independent argument is used by the #$Relation, the dependent argument must be an instance of the arg3.  The name of the predicate derives from the dependency relation.  In this case a #$genlAttributes relationship constrains an #$isa.")
(comment LandAttackCruiseMissile "A specialization of #$CruiseMissile.  Instances have the capability
of overflying terrain as they approach an assigned land target.  Note
that this specialization is not necessarily exclusive of anti-ship
capability.")
(comment frictionalForce "(#$frictionalForce ?mov ?force) means that ?force is the (time averaged?) amount of frictional force acting on every object moving (#$objectMoving qv) in ?mov.  If ?force is greater than zero (which it is in any 'real world' context) then there is some #$FrictionProcess which happens as a #$subEvents in ?mov (the #$FrictionProcess is a #$cotemporalSubEvents if ?mov is a #$MovementProcess.  The direction of the friction force is opposite the #$directionOfTranslation-Throughout and/or #$axisOfRotation.  Air resistance is considered a frictional force as is the similar, but smaller resistance to motion caused by interplanetary/-stellar/-galactic particles.")
(comment COAMissionAnalysisProdsG2Microtheory "A collection of microtheories.  The information in each
instance will inherit to some instance of
#$COASpecificationMicrotheory, and in some cases, to multiple
instances.  Each instance of #$COAMissionAnalysisProdsG2Microtheory is used
to specify mission analysis products deriving from the G2, pursuant to the COAs
that appear among the #$genlMt dependents.")
(comment vehicleRange "(#$vehicleRange VEH DIST) means that DIST is the maximum distance that can be translated using the vehicle VEH, without intermediate refueling and assuming typical usage and normal operating parameters.  We intend this to be a very strict measure, an important thing to keep in mind since the vernacular sense of 'effective range' is much looser.  In point of fact, the #$vehicleRange is a key tool in calculating what the effective operating range of a fuel-powered vehicle is.  If, e.g., we are dealing with a case of a vehicle that operates from a fixed base of operations, such as a #$FighterPlane, the effective operating range will ordinarily be one-half the absolute #$vehicleRange, since ordinarily provision will be made for the plane's returning to base.  However, we may well want to consider special cases where this provision is not made.  Conversely, in cases where aerial refueling is a possibility, the actual effective operating range will be some multiple of the #$vehicleRange, or may even be indefinite.")
(comment Serotonin "The collection of all portions of serotonin. #$Serotonin has been shown to be in many representatives of the animal kingdom, in wasp, toad, and scorpion #$Venom, in various fruits, such as pineapples, bananas, and plums, and in various nuts. It has been estimated that an adult human contains about 5 to 10 mg of serotonin, 90% of which is in the intestine and the rest in blood platelets and the brain. It is concentrated in certain areas of the brain, especially the midbrain and the hypothalamus, and changes in its concentration are associated with several mood disorders. The hallucinogenic compound #$LSD may act by inhibiting the action of #$Serotonin.")
(comment MediaTechnician "A person with media-related technical skills which he/she uses in his/her job.")
(comment CatholicGift "An instance of #$GiftTypeByReligion.  The collection of all #$Gifts that are somehow associated with #$Catholicism.")
(comment WeaponsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units trained, equipped, and organized for           the handling of a particular kind of weapons system.")
(comment hotelInCity "(#$hotelInCity BLDG CITY) means that the #$HotelBuilding
BLDG is found in the #$City CITY.")
(comment Thallium "The element Thallium, atomic number 81.")
(comment BackwardsFn "This function, applied to a #$FrontAndBackSidedObject,returns the
exact direction the object's back is facing in the implicit
frameOfReference defined by the object.")
(comment favorableFor "(#$favorableFor CIRC AGENT ACT_TYPE) means that the situation CIRC is
a normally favorable circumstance for AGENT to perform an instance of
ACT_TYPE. For example, normal external circumstances for playing the piano
would be those in which one has access to a piano in reasonably good shape,
is awake, alert, lacking physical disabilities, not underwater, etc. The
idea is that this is the kind of situation in which a person skilled at
ACT-TYPE would have a good chance to perform succesfully an action of type
ACT_TYPE.")
(disjointWith CloudlessArea CloudyArea)
(comment BodyOfJesusChrist "The 'organic' body of #$JesusChrist

as perceived by instances of #$CatholicPerson (perhaps naively, in the sense that

this belief may contradict other beliefs, e.g., that the divine Christ is non-corporeal) to constitute

the #$CommunionWafer after #$Transubstantiation has occured.")
(comment crossSections "This predicate relates an object to one of its cross section. (#$crossSections THING SLICE) means that SLICE is an arbitrarily thin slice of THING found at one of its cross sections.  It is used to describe the shape of three dimensional objects.  See its #$specs.")
(comment percentPopulationInCities "The percentage of the population of this #$GeopoliticalEntity that lives in cities.")
(comment Shadow "A region of space having markedly less illumination than the area surrounding it, due to some object intervening between the light source and that region.  The shape of a shadow is related systematically to the shape of the object blocking the light source.")
(comment DeadSeaScroll "The collection of ancient leather and papyrus manuscripts discovered in caves and ruins near the #$DeadSea.")
(comment ProfessionalSportsEvent "#$ProfessionalSportsEvent is the collection of instances of #$SportsEvent which are deliberately carried out for the benefit of paying spectators. The fact that every instance of #$ProfessionalSportsEvent has as essential #$subEvents BOTH an instance of (#$PerformingFn #$ProfessionalSportsEvent) AND an instance of (#$AttendingFn #$ProfessionalSportsEvent) is what makes this collection a spec of #$EntertainmentEvent.")
(comment equivalentHosts "#$equivalentHosts relates one #$ComputationalSystem to another.             (#$equivalentHosts SYSTEM1 SYSTEM2)  means that the users (except users with root access)            of SYSTEM1 can access their accounts on SYSTEM2  without having to re-enter their #$Username or           #$Password-Computer. Usually host equivalency is configured by a system administrator using the           file /etc/hosts.equiv.  Compare this predicate to #$equivalentRoot.")
(comment ExfoliantScrub "Ointments containing tiny granules that scrub off the dry dead top layer of skin when applied to the face or body.  Used to improve the appearance and texture of the skin.")
(comment LiquidCohesiveness "beads or clumps together, but can be effortlessly separated")
(disjointWith MovementOrShapeChangeEvent BusinessRelationshipActivity)
(comment Paraglider "The collection of all combinations of #$Gliders and #$Parachutes.")
(comment CrossingACountryBorderWOBorderCheck-Person "Instances are cases where a person crosses a country border without going through a border checkpoint.  This is only illegal within the context of certain #$Laws.")
(comment (RightObjectOfPairFn (PartTypeFn FifthThoracicVertebra VertebralTransverseProcess)) "")
(comment PeopleFinderProgram "The collection of all #$SearchEngines designed to help users find information about #$Persons, such as their addresses and phone numbers.")
(comment ElectronicBoxBodiedVehicle "A collection. Electronic box bodied military vehicles.")
(comment translationOfAISFromTo "(#$translationOfAISFromTo AIS1 CC1 AIS2 CC2) means that the meaning attributed the #$AbstractInformationStructure AIS1, by #$CommunicationConvention CC1, is the same as the meaning attributed to AIS2 by CC2. Thus, if TEXT1 = 'Schnee ist weiss' and TEXT2 = 'Snow is white' then it would be true that (#$translationOfAISFromTo TEXT1 #$GermanLanguage TEXT2 #$EnglishLanguage).")
(comment AutomaticFirearm-StripFed "The collection of #$AutomaticFirearms that use a strip feed system, i.e., the bullets are held in a stiff metal clip.")
(disjointWith AngularDistance Voltage)
(comment UnitOfCPUSpeed "A specialization of #$UnitOfComputerResourceCapacity. Each instance of this collection represents a  unit (or \"benchmark\") used to measure CPU (central processing unit) power. Instances include #$MIPS (\"Millions of Instructions per Second\"), #$SPECfp, and #$TransactionsPerSecond.")
(comment priorProbability "A predicate used for probability statements.  (#$priorProbability PROPOSITION PROBNO) means that the a priori probability of the truth of the formula PROPOSITION, in the applicable #$Microtheory, is PROBNO (a real number between zero and one, where zero means certainly false and one means certainly true).  In most microtheories, generally, this refers to the probability that PROPOSITION, by itself, would be true if there were no further evidence in the #$Microtheory for or against it, nor knowledge of the truth of anything else other than the #$domainAssumptions of the #$Microtheory.  Contrast this with #$derivedProbability and with #$priorProbability-Range.  See also the function version of this predicate: #$PriorProbabilityFn.  A #$priorProbability may represent an absolute objective probability, a subjective assigned probability, a quantum probability, or an assigned probability based on some internal characteristic of PROPOSITION (including possibly a statement in it of the occurrence of a number of outcomes within a large number of trials).  This definition makes no presumption as to determinism versus nondeterminism, nor as to whether probability is only in the mind of some beholder.")
(comment SourceCitationSlot "A collection of #$BinaryPredicates used for citing sources of various kinds for CycL terms or stating information regarding the assertion of CycL assertions.")
(comment ReceivingAntenna "Devices for converting radio waves into electrical signals.  The signals may then be sent to a receiver.")
(comment USSenator "The collection of elected officials which serve in the United States Senate.  Each state of the nation is represented by two senators.")
(comment allSubEchelonsInOrg "(#$allSubEchelonsInOrg SUPERLEVEL SUBLEVEL SCALE) means that SUBLEVEL ranks somewhere below SUPERLEVEL in the partial ordering of the military echelon scheme represented by SCALE and that there is a directed path in the system from SUBLEVEL to SUPERLEVEL.")
(disjointWith RaisingLivingThings IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(comment BlankForm "A form which has not yet been filled out.")
(comment UTH-Pasteurization "A subcollection of #$Pasteurization.  In pasteurizations of this type the object acted on, e.g. milk, is held between heated plates for 3-4 seconds at a minumum temperature of (#$DegreeCelsius 141).")
(comment BlurryStreak "The collection of images depicting some object which appear as a blurry streak, usually because of quick movement.")
(comment IncestStory "The subset of #$EroticStory whose elements contain the propositional content of an erotic story in which one or more instances of #$Incest are described.")
(comment MasticationMuscleSet "The #$Collection of all instances of #$MasticationMuscleSet.  The #$MasticationMuscleSet consists of five symmetric pairs of muscles connected to the #$Jawbone (mandible) and the Orbicularis Oris which circles the lips.  The set includes the Temporalis, Masseter, Buccinator, Medial Pterygoid, and Lateral Pterygoid.")
(disjointWith County InternationalOrganizationOfCountries)
(disjointWith MilitaryWatercraft OceanLiner)
(comment QuadrupedBodyShaped "The body shape attribute which correspond to the body shapes held by quadrupeds.  That is they have four legs which support the body when in #$StandingOnAllLegsPosture.  By default, all four legs are used when the animal is walking upright (see #$UprightPosture).  Humans do not have this shape attribute.")
(comment ModalReasoningInferenceMicrotheory "This type of microtheories contains all and only those microtheories in which some particular instances of #$ModalReasoningMicrotheoryPredicate are defined.  Note that no instance of #$ModalReasoningLogicMicrotheory should have access to any instance of this collection.")
(comment Pill "A small object which is used to administer some substance that is to be ingested.")
(comment Coulomb "This is the basic unit of measure for charge in the metric system and in CYC.")
(comment CityGovernment "The collection of all #$City governments.")
(comment unifySchema "(#$unifySchema ?Dag1 ?SchematicTFS ?Dag2) causes the
typed-feature unification of the Lisp-level ?Dag1 (see #$dagOf) to
be unified with the EL-Level Typed feature structure
?SchematicTFS to produce the Lisp-level typed-feature structure
?Dag2. Essentially a version of unify where the second argument is
not a dag, but a more readable SubLList. The HL-level is
responsible for converting ?SchematicTFS into a Dag for the
unification to occur.")
(comment ThymineDeoxyribonucleotide "A collection of compounds consisting of a #$Thymine-Base and a phosphate group linked with #$Deoxyribose.  Its abbreviation is T, and it links with #$AdenineDeoxyribonucleotide or #$AdenineRibonucleotide, depending on the process.  This #$Nucleotide is specific to #$DNAMolecules, and its complement in #$RNAMolecules is #$UracilRibonucleotide.")
(comment MassSpectrometry "This is collection of events in which the #$ScientificTechnique of using

mass spectrometers is employed. Mass spectrometers use the difference in mass-to-charge ratio (m/e) of ionized atoms or molecules to separate them from each other. Mass

spectrometry is therefore useful for quantitation of atoms or molecules and also for determining chemical and structural information about molecules.

Molecules have distinctive fragmentation patterns that provide structural information to identify structural components.")
(disjointWith FixedBridge-Military FloatingBridge-Military)
(comment StealingInformation "#$StealingInformation is a collection of events in which a person obtains information that she is not commonly considered to be legally entitled to possess.  It  includes stealing credit card numbers from the internet, learning personal identification  numbers for ATM cards by spying on automatic teller machine users, and those forms of  corporate espionage that involve acquiring trade secrets.")
(comment Chlamydiales-Order "A collection of #$BiologicalFamilys in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These often are parasitic organism to humans and other mammals, and birds.")
(comment LawsInTerritoryFn "#$LawsInTerritoryFn takes as argument any instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity, and returns the collection of laws holding within that GeopoliticalEntity's legal sphere.  For example, (#$LawsInTerritoryFn #$BrooklynNY-Borough) returns the collection of all laws in place within the confines of Brooklyn, NY.")
(comment RepairShip "The collection of ships intended to be used in repairs.")
(disjointWith NonessentialAminoAcidType EssentialAminoAcidType)
(comment joinable "(#$joinable ?LF1 ?LF2) means the two fields, ?LF1 and ?LF2, can directly join.  Two fields representing IDs of the same type can directly join, as well as two fields which use the same #$ReifiedMapping for encoding their values.")
(comment personTakingTourMightDislikeObject "(#$personTakingTourMightDislikeObject TOUR PERSON OBJ) means
that if PERSON were to take TOUR, there is a better-than-even chance
they would dislike OBJECT, featured on TOUR.")
(comment AirDefenseArtilleryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of ground-based military units that are trained in handling certain classes of projectile weapons and are dedicated to protecting airspace regions.")
(comment Helium "A piece of helium as it coalesces in Nature -- usually in gaseous form, except near superconductors on Earth.")
(comment SkinBurn "Burned skin due to heat, acid, cold, or electric shock.  This unit is not a spec of #$Burnt because most skin burns do not actually involve combustion.  Third-degree burns would be both #$SkinBurn and #$Burnt.")
(comment K-Through-12COS "The course of studies, K-12, pursued by most North Americans from the ages 5-18.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (RightObjectOfPairFn ThirdRib) Tuberosity) "")
(comment (VeryLowAmountFn Glamour) "The attribute of lacking glamor, of being unglamorous.")
(comment footprintOfSatellite "(footprintOfSatellite SAT REG) indicates that the #$Satellite-Device SAT
orbiting #$PlanetEarth is capable of sending #$SatelliteTransmissions to
and receiving #$SatelliteTransmissions from 
#$SatelliteCommunicationsEquipment on the Earth's Surface in 
#$GeographicalRegion REG.")
(comment AssistantChiefOfStaff-Personnel "The collection of all instances of #$CoordinatingStaffMember-USArmy 
with assigned responsibility for personnel matters.")
(comment Escort-EntertainmentProvider "The collection of #$Persons that earn an income by offering their company  to those willing to pay for it. Their physical attractiveness is the main reason why their company is sought after. As a consequence, a border line negative example of this concept is a lady-in-waiting, whose company is sought after for the sparkle in her conversation or the propriety of her manners (or both).")
(comment posesGreaterVulnerabilityTo-Object "(#$posesGreaterVulnerabilityTo-Object OBJ TARGET1 TARGET2 HARM-TYPE) means that, all other things being equal, OBJ poses a greater potential harm of HARM-TYPE to TARGET1 than to TARGET2.  By implication this means that TARGET1 is at least vulnerable to OBJ (although TARGET2 may not be).  This is one of several comparative vulnerability predicates.  #$posesGreaterVulnerabilityTo-Object differs from #$makesMoreVulnerableThan-Object in that the former expresses a comparative difference in the things threatened (TARGET1 is more vulnerable than TARGET2), whereas the latter expresses a comparative difference in the threats.  As a rule you should use #$posesGreaterVulnerabilityTo-Object when comparing how one object threatens two distinct targets; use #$makesMoreVulnerableThan-Object when comparing two threats to one object.  See #$NoteAboutVulnerability for more on these distinctions.")
(comment DiploidCell "The collection of #$EukaryoticCells with paired chromosomes (two sets during the metaphase of mitosis).  This is the  standard arrangement for the cells in the bodies of adult multicellular organisms.")
(comment ResourceManagementAuthority "The collection of organizations that oversee specific resources, such as public water supplies, parks, etc.")
(comment PostPartumFever "A collection of a broad group of #$Infections that occur in the mother after the birth of offspring.  These infections have a variety of causes, for example #$EscherichiaColi or Mycoplasma hominis.")
(disjointWith PhysicalTransformationEvent Perceiving)
(comment CustomerAccount "An account decremented by payments from a customer who buys something from the vendor and incremented by selling something to the customer.")
(comment HorseShippingBoot "This is the collection of #$HorseBoots which are designed to protect a horse's hooves and ankles while it is being shipped in a horse trailer. ")
(comment LightAssaultUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units trained and equipped for           conducting assaults with 'light' weapons, usually hand-held, and           lightly- armored equipment.")
(comment FlawAttributeType "The collection of kinds of flaw attributes, i.e., kind vs. degree.")
(comment NewspaperTypeByName "Elements of #$NewspaperTypeByName are collections of all copies of all issues of particular named newspapers [#$NewspaperSeries].")
(comment CloudInSky "A specialization of #$CloudOfH2O.  Each instance of #$CloudInSky is a cloud located in the sky over some instance of #$GeographicalRegion.  Since #$CloudInSky is a specialization of #$CloudOfH2O, each instance of #$CloudInSky must be primarily composed of water particles.")
(comment FieldAppliedToFn "The term `(#$FieldAppliedToFn FIELD THING)' denotes the #$FieldOfStudy which

is the subfield of the #$FieldOfStudy FIELD constituted by the narrowing of

the topic of FIELD's study to THING. ")
(disjointWith UnitOfCurrent UnitOfFrequency)
(comment ClassicMovie "Classic movies are generally movies which have stood the test of time.  Instances of this collection are movies that are of outstanding quality and have had multiple theater re-releases with much success.")
(comment mtsConflict "(#$mtsConflict PROP MTPROVE MTDISPROVE) means that PROP is
provable in MTPROVE and that (#$not PROP) is provable in MTDISPROVE.")
(comment downtownOf "(#$downtownOf CITY DOWNTOWN) means that DOWNTOWN is the downtown region of CITY.")
(comment Stamping-Shaping "A collection of events.  In each #$Stamping-Shaping event, an image or form is pressed into a surface.  Typically done to sheets of metal, for example, but this also includes certain kinds of printing such as is done with currency, postage stamps, newspapers, etc., but not photocopying, laser printing, inkjet printing, writing by hand, etc.  A #$Stamping-Shaping is an inherently parallel process, with the transformation happening all at once, and it is an inherently `sympathetic' process, with the new `look' of the thing being mirror-imaged exactly in the shape of (part of) the device doing the #$Stamping-Shaping.")
(comment RNAMolecule-ThreePrimeEnd "The collection of 3' end of  RNA molecules.")
(comment Anthrax-BWBacterium "This is the spec of #$Anthrax-Bacterium consisting of those
anthrax bacteria of the type that would be used in a #$BiologicalWeapon.
These bacteria would be selected for their size and for their producing a
more slowly developing form of #$InhalationalAnthrax. The purpose of the
latter is to delay the possible use of antibiotics until it is too late
for them to be effective.")
(disjointWith LandBody Hill)
(comment Symphony "The collection of all symphonies - orchestral works in more than one movement, without soloists except those sitting as members of the orchestra. Unlike earlier suites and concerti grossi, most movements of a symphony are not based on dance forms. Notable examples include those of #$FranzJosephHaydn, #$GustavMahler, and many composers in between.")
(comment NuclearWeaponsTesting "The collection of all instances of #$WeaponsTesting in which the weapon   being tested is an instance of #$NuclearWeapon.")
(comment Mirage2000EMFighterPlane "A collection of a type of French #$FighterInterceptorPlane.")
(comment Injecting-Intramuscular "Injecting a fluid, usually containing a drug, into muscle tissue.")
(comment tourTravelLegTransport "(#$tourTravelLegTransport TOUR PATH TRAVELINGTYPE) means
that the leg of tour represented by PATH will involve a
#$TransportationEventByVehicleType of type TRAVELINGTYPE.")
(comment resistanceToRadiation "(#$resistanceToRadiation OBJ DEGREE) indicates how resistant a tangible object OBJ is to radiation.  A higher DEGREE of resistance means that an object is less penetrable by #$ElectromagneticRadiation.")
(comment SessionLayerProtocol "The collection of all network protocols that implement

a session layer. An instance of #$SessionLayerProtocol allows sessions to be established between two 

machines. A session facilitates processes that involve intensive data transfer

between two computers, such as transferring a large file.

Most instances of #$NetworkProtocolStack do not include an instance of #$SessionLayerProtocol.")
(comment CottonBoll "The fruit of the cotton plant; a capsule containing cottonseeds and the downy fibers in which they are embedded.")
(comment Playboy "Not the well-known magazine 'Playboy' published by #$HughHefner,  but the lifestyle exemplified by HughHefner, that of a party-going, easy-living, wealthy bon-vivant. In fictional terms, Bruce Wayne and Bertie Wooster played the role of a playboy also. Playboys are perhaps best described by their lifestyle choices -- typically they drive fast cars, party at exclusive clubs and drink champagne in copious amounts. The word derives from an originally derisive word for people who worked in traveling theatre groups and/or seemed to live a life free of social responsibility. Singe's play 'The playboy of the western world' exemplifies this original reading of the word.")
(comment PhysicalTransformationProcess "The collection of #$PhysicalTransformationEvents that also are instances of #$TemporalStuffType.  That is, each of their temporal parts is also a #$PhysicalTransformationEvent, in which something is destroyed and something created.  
Note:  It is often the case that a #$PhysicalTransformationEvent is NOT a #$PhysicalTransformationProcess --- e.g., there may be several preparation stages, and then at the end everything is brought together and the foaming starts, or the butterfly emerges, or whatever transformation occurs.  So #$PhysicalTransformationProcess is a small subcollection of #$PhysicalTransformationEvent (qv).")
(comment Capsule-Bacterium "A collection of the thick layer of hydrophilic gel that may surround bacterial cells.  It is transparent and not readily stainable.  If this layer forms a discrete layer around the bacterium, it is a capsule.  If it is amourphous in appearence, it is referred to as a slime layer.  See also #$SlimeLayer-Bacterium.")
(comment AntiArmorHandGrenade "A collection of grenades, a subset of #$HandGrenade. Each instance is a grenade designed to pierce

vehicular armor.")
(comment PositiveNumber "A specialization of #$RealNumber.  An instance NUMBER of #$RealNumber is also an instance of #$PositiveNumber just in case NUMBER is greater than zero.  Instances of #$PositiveNumber include 42 and 0.17, but not 0 or -5.")
(comment tourTransitsFrom "(#$tourTransitsFrom TOUR MOVETYPE FROM) means that,
according to its itinerary, TOUR is supposed to include a movement of
type MOVETYPE from the #$PartiallyTangible FROM, considered as a
#$fromLocation.")
(comment (TransportViaFn Tractor) "The collection of all tractor-driving events")
(comment argFormat "A ternary #$ArgFormatPredicate (q.v.) used to put #$Format (q.v.) constraints on a specified argument-place of a given predicate.  (#$argFormat PRED N FORMAT) means that the Nth argument of PRED has the format FORMAT.  See the reified instances of #$Format for further explanation.  Note that there are binary predicates that mean essentially the same thing as #$argFormat, but are restricted to some particular argument-place: #$arg1Format, #$arg2Format, etc.")
(comment superLocationType "(#$superLocationType SMALLER-TYPE LARGER-TYPE)  means that for every #$SpatialThing X of type SMALLER-TYPE, there is a #$SpatialThing Y of type LARGER-TYPE such that X is spatially contained in Y.  Examples: (#$superLocationType #$Kitchen #$Building), (#$superLocationType #$Downtown #$City).  See also #$subLocationType.  Note that (#$superLocationType X Y) does not necessarily entail (#$subLocationType Y X).")
(disjointWith MatterTypeByPhysicalState TransportationEventByVehicleType)
(comment Shark-Hammerhead "The collection of all sharks belonging to the biological family Sphyrnidae.         These sharks are medium-sized and have flattened heads.")
(comment SilkwormMissile "A collection of missiles,

a subset of #$AntiShipCruiseMissile. The silkworm missile is

a type of antiship cruise missile manufactured by the People's

Republic of China.")
(comment MilkingACow "The actual activity of milking a cow with or without a machine, but probably with.")
(comment programCopyUsedInElectronicAttack "A binary predicate that relates an instance of #$AttackByComputerOperation to an instance of #$ComputerProgramCopy.  (#$programCopyUsedInElectronicAttack ATTACK COPY) means that executing ATTACK involves running COPY.  See also #$programUsedInElectronicAttack.")
(comment Mirage-F1-Fighter "A collection of a type of French fighter plane, with variants used for air-to-ground, training,

close defense, #$and reconnaisance.")
(comment Rhodium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of Rhodium.")
(comment myReviewer "(#$myReviewer TERM CYCLIST) means that TERM has been reviewed by CYCLIST and is deemed ``okay''.  In other words, all assertions on CONSTANT that were made prior to the time prior to when #$myReviewer was asserted (see #$assertionAssertTime and #$assertionAssertSecond) have been checked over by CYCLIST.  Note, if CONSTANT has had assertions made on it since #$myReviewer was asserted, then, technically speaking the constant has not been completely reviewed and should be re-reviewed.")
(comment ConventionalMortgage "The collection of #$MortgageAgreements that are based on the credit of the #$borrower and the collateral for the loan.  Such loans are not insured by the HUD (#$USDepartmentOfHousingAndUrbanDevelopment) nor guaranteed by the Veteran's Administration (#$USVeteransAffairsDepartment).")
(comment HL-StartFn "An #$HL-StartFn term represents the starting point of a #$TemporalThing in a data structure that facilitates temporal relations inference.")
(comment Terrorist "A specialization of #$TerroristAgent and #$Person (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$Terrorist is a person who tries to achieve political ends by engaging in terrorist activities (see #$TerroristAct), such as bombing buildings, attacking civilians, etc. Instances of this collection include some, but not all, members of #$TerroristGroups such as the #$Contras, #$PalestineIslamicJihad, or the #$IrishRepublicanArmy, as well as individuals acting alone.")
(comment analogyCaseEvent "(#$analogyCaseEvent CASE EVENT) relates the #$AnalogyCase CASE to the EVENT upon which the case is focused.")
(comment M577A1CommandVehicle "A subset of command vehicles.")
(comment SyntaxSpecificationSymbol "The collection of all grammar symbols used in #$FormalGrammarSpecifications to represent structural units.  For example, in a #$ContextFreeGrammar, with the rule 'S --> VP+NP' meaning that a sentence S consists of a verb phrase VP followed by a noun phrase NP, all three symbols, S, VP and NP, are #$SyntaxSpecificationSymbols.")
(comment ConflictEvent "A collection of all events in #$SocialOccurrence that can be called 'conflicts'.  For each #$ConflictEvent CONF, there are at least two #$IntelligentAgents AGT1 and AGT2 such that (#$opponentsInConflict AGT1 AGT2 CONF) holds.  For each #$ConflictEvent CONF, there are subevents ACT1 and ACT2 of CONF, which are #$PurposefulActions, and there are GOAL1 and GOAL2 such that (#$purposeInEvent AGT1 ACT1 GOAL1), (#$purposeInEvent AGT2 ACT2 GOAL2), and GOAL1 and GOAL2 are in conflict, i.e., (#$and GOAL1 GOAL2) is not consistent (in the current #$Microtheory).")
(comment EconomicEspionage "The collection of events where the a state actively commits acts of espionage against another state(s) to gain an economic advantage.")
(comment Salmonella "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom.
These #$ProkaryoticCells are often pathogenic for humans and animals
when acquired by the oral route.")
(comment RadioBroadcastOfTypeFn "#$RadioBroadcastOfTypeFn takes as argument any content-defined spec of #$SoundInformationBearingThing (including specs of #$Music) and returns the collection of events that are radio broadcasts of instances of that spec.  For example, (#$RadioBroadcastOfTypeFn #$JazzMusic) returns the collection of radio broadcasts of Jazz, and (#$RadioBroadcastOfTypeFn PrarieHomeCompanion) would return the collection of radio broadcasts of that particular radio show.")
(disjointWith PowerBrakeSystem ManualBrakeSystem)
(disjointWith CharacterMode-Sounded CharacterMode-Inscribed)
(comment LaborDay-US "The instance of #$Holiday commemorating the contributions of the Americal labor force.")
(comment Ciprofloxacin "A kind of #$Cephalosporin. It helps treat lower respiratory infections (including #$InhalationalAnthrax), skin and skin structure infections (including  (#$CutaneousFormFn #$AnthraxInfection)), bone and joint infections, urinary tract infections and infectious diarrhea caused by E. coli bacteria.")
(comment ShoppingAtFn "(ShoppingAtFn LOCATIONTYPE) returns the collection of all instances of #$Shopping which occur within the general boundaries of some instance of LOCATIONTYPE.")
(comment MinisterOfForeignAffairs "The collection of upper (cabinet-) level government officials whose job it is to deal with foreign relations.")
(comment AerosolStuff "#$AerosolStuff is a collection of all aerosols.  Aerosols are suspensions of small particles in a gas.  Aerosols can be dispensed from aerosol cans, but can also occur naturally.")
(disjointWith Travel-TripEvent InformationBearingThing)
(disjointWith BuyingADrink FillingAPrescription)
(comment salientDifferenceBetween-Inverse "(#$salientDifferenceBetween-Inverse COL1 COL2 COL3 BINPRED) means that while COL1 and COL2 contain instances that are similar in many salient respects, they differ in the fact that for every instance, INS1, of COL1 there is an instance of COL3, INS3 such that (BINPRED INS3 INS1).  On the other hand, instances of COL2 do not bear the relation BINPRED to any instance of COL3.  The differences noted with this predicate should be salient ones, e.g., differences that one familiar with COL1 and COL2 might note if asked to compare and contrast COL1 and COL2.  See also the closely related predicates, #$salientDifferenceBetweenSiblings-Inverse and #$salientDifferenceBetween.")
(comment seriesLength "(#$seriesLength SER LEN) means that the series, SER, is LEN members long.  Note that some #$Series have an unknown or infinite number of members.")
(comment requisiteForAnti "If there is a known propositional precondition PRECON for

SIT2 such that SIT1's happening is a necessary precondition for the negation of PRECON becoming true, then (#$requisiteForAnti SIT1 SIT2).")
(disjointWith Microtheory GeneticInformationStructure)
(comment plural-Generic "This predicate is a generalization over the #$SpeechPartPredicates that express plural number.  (#$plural-Generic WORD STRING) means that the #$EnglishWord WORD has STRING as a plural form: either #$plural (the plural form corresponding to the #$CountNoun part of speech), #$pnPlural (for #$ProperCountNoun forms), or #$agentive-Pl (for #$AgentiveNoun forms).  This predicate is #$notAssertible, since it will always cash out as an assertion on one of its spec-preds.")
(comment Boring-Locomotion "Locomotion of an animal through a solid, whether chewing through wood or pushing through dirt.")
(comment BenignTumor "Tumors which are not cancerous.")
(comment ProtectiveEquipment-Human "This is the collection of artifacts designed to protect people

from harm when they engage in various activities. Some members were designed to

protect people from harm when engaging in very specific activities, such as

the mats used on gymnastic vaulting. Other members, like bullet-proof

vests, are designed to protect people from quite specific types of harm

but types of harm which may accompany a number of different activities.

Excluded from this collection are things like computer firewalls, which

are designed to protect computer systems directly, and only protect

persons from indirect harms that may result from computer attacks.")
(comment AirborneUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military or paramilitary forces that are           deployed by parachute drop.")
(comment CycLDeducedAssertion "The subcollection of semantically well-formed #$CycLAssertions that are supported by at least one argument which is a deduction by Cyc's inference engine, as opposed to having been explicitly asserted to Cyc. A given assertion can have more than one argument, and can therefore be both a #$CycLAssertedAssertion and a #$CycLDeducedAssertion.")
(comment NaturalResourceType "The collection of collections of things that are useful in nature.")
(comment TrustAgreement "The collection of #$TemporaryUserRightsAgreements in which property is given by one #$Person (called a 'donor' or 'settlor') to a #$Trustee, for the benefit of another person (who is the #$beneficiary in the relevant #$TemporaryChangeOfUserRights, which event is also a #$MakingLegalAgreement).  Like all #$Agreements, a #$TrustAgreement engenders certain #$Obligations upon the #$agreeingAgents.  One such agent is the #$Trustee; the other is the 'grantor' of the trust.  The #$TrustAgreement establishes a fiduciary relationship in which the #$Trustee holds title in property, subject to an equitable obligation to use it for the benefit of the #$beneficiary.")
(disjointWith ArtificialLanguage-Informal ArtificialLanguage-Formal)
(comment InspectingForWeapons "The collection of all events in which an agent, usually a

geographical agent acting through representatives, conducts an

inspection to determine whether or not certain types of weapons are

present in a particular location.")
(comment CycLNonAtomicReifiedTerm "The subcollection of #$CycLReifiableNonAtomicTerms that are reified in the KB. Example: (#$JuvenileFn #$Dog).  Counterexample: (#$JuvenileFn #$Platypus), because that term is not currently reified in the KB.  These are often called NARTs, which stands for 'non-atomic reified term'.")
(comment TransitivePPFrameType "Frames used for verbs, adjectives and nouns that have a single PP complement. Examples include 'depend on X', 'mad at X', 'picture of X'.")
(comment typeSoleFunction "(#$typeSoleFunction SE-TYPE SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that if INS is an instance of SE-TYPE then, (#$soleFunction INS SIT-TYPE ROLE): i.e., all instances of SE-TYPE have as their sole function playing role ROLE in situations of type SIT-TYPE, and this as the result of the design of some intelligent agent or user.")
(comment VenusianStuff "A collection of tangible things.  Each element in #$VenusianStuff is a portion of the stuff that the ground of the planet #$PlanetVenus (at or near its land surface) is made of, including rocks, boulders, sand grains, rigolith, magma, etc., and mixtures of those things.")
(comment StormAsObject "A large object, mostly gaseous, turbulent region where high winds occurs.   Often contains precipitation.  See also #$StormAsEvent.")
(comment kleenePlusOf "(#$kleenePlusOf SUPER SUB) means that (SUPER A B) means that one or more applications of (SUB U V) will transform A to B.  SUPER is necessarily a #$TransitiveBinaryPredicate.  If no iteration of SUB is needed, use #$kleeneStarOf.")
(comment explicitlyContraindicatedProduct "(#$explicitlyContraindicatedProduct PRSN PROD-TYPE) means that the customer using the CYC Product Advisor interface has explicitly indicated a negative interest in purchasing instances of the instance of #$ProductType PROD-TYPE for the #$Person PRSN. For example, a negative response to a question of the form, 'Are you interested in toys?' would result in the following assertion being made in #$TheSessionMt, (#$explicitlyContraindicatedProduct #$TheRecipient #$Toy). Assertions using this predicate are the strongest indication of the unsuitability of a #$ProductType and also represent that the justification for this assertion is that the customer has told us she is not interested in this #$ProductType.")
(comment defaultReformulationDirectionInModeForPred "If the #$CycLReformulator is operating in MT in the mode MODE, and it
encounters a reformulation rule with no #$reformulationDirectionInMode
meta-assertion for MODE stated in MT or a genlMt thereof, the extent of this
predicate will be used to determine the reformulation direction of the
rule.")
(disjointWith HeterosexualHuman BisexualHuman)
(comment tuition "The fees that an #$EducationalOrganization or private instructor charges students for teaching, evaluating, and official recognition or certification.")
(disjointWith StoneStuff EdibleStuff)
(comment ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheory-LinearTime "This is the sub-collection of

#$ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheory that contains all and only

those that take #$ReasoningWithTense-LogicMt-LinearTime as

#$genlMt.")
(comment infectionLocalizedIn "(#$infectionLocalizedIn ORG INFECTION PART-TYPE) means that in
the context of the assertion, INFECTION is localized in the part or
parts of ORG that are instances of PART-TYPE.")
(comment GenericSpeechPartPredicate "A collection of #$SpeechPartPredicates.  Each instance of #$GenericSpeechPartPredicate represents a syntactic generalization shared by a group of #$SpeechPartPredicates.  For instance, #$singular-Generic abstracts over #$singular, #$pnSingular, and #$agentive-Sg.  Note that instances of #$GenericSpeechPartPredicate are #$notAssertible, since they will always cash out as assertions on one of their spec-preds.")
(comment AbominableSnowman "A collection of large hairy humanoid mammals said to roam the #$HimalayaMountains.")
(comment DrippingWet "Something that is so saturated with water, that it would drip off it in streams.")
(comment mtAreaValue "(#$mtAreaValue MT INTERVAL) means that when reasoning in (or with) the context MT, objects with an area that falls within the range specified by INTERVAL should be attended to, or taken into account.  For example, (#$mtAreaValue MT (#$SquareMile 1 1000)) means that when reasoning proceeds using the knowledge in MT, only objects having an that measures greater than or equal to 1 square mile, and less than or equal to 1000 square mile, should be considered relevant.")
(comment SystemOfDevices "This collection involves instances which are #$Groups of #$PhysicalDevices which interact and are connected in some sort of network. Positive examples include a computer system, a telephone system, a plumbing system. Negative examples include instances of simple tools, such as a screwdriver or a hammer, which have discrete connected parts, but whose parts do not interact in any complicated way. Another negative example is a single instance of #$Telephone. In a context of naive familiarity with the device, the telephone is not a system because its parts do not form an obvious network. ")
(comment RightRiverbankFn "(#$RightRiverbank RIVER) denotes the right riverbank of RIVER, an instance of River.")
(disjointWith DustDevil StormAsObject)
(disjointWith WeaponOfMassDestruction ConventionalWeapon)
(comment VariableStar "This is the collection of variable stars. These

are stars which appear to vary in intensity over short periods of time. They are

a favorite object of amateur astronomers.")
(comment Sumitriptan "The chemical compound which is an anti-migraine drug.")
(comment GearShifting "What happens when a driver shifts gears in a car.  This is a subEvent of a DrivingEvent in the DriverPerspectiveMt:  Since performedBy transfersThro subEvents we only want GearShifting to be performedBy the Driver.  Thus a suEvent assertion should not be placed in a perspective neutral mt.")
(comment importOriginFractionDuring "(#$importOriginFractionDuring REGION1 REGION2 THING NR) means that NR is the quotient of the monetary value of the imports by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION1 from the #$GeographicalRegion REGION2 during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING (as dividend) and the monetary value of REGION1's imports of all goods and services during the temporal extent of THING (as divisor).  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  For example, to express the fact that imports to the United States accounted for 5 percent of the total value of Oman's imports in 1995, we can say (#$importOriginFractionDuring #$Oman #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica (#$YearFn 1995) (#$Percent 5)).  See also #$importAmountDuring.")
(comment Q-TheLetter "The letter Q of the alphabet.  This is 'Q' (or 'q') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.  As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterQ and #$LatinSmallLetterQ.")
(comment SubLStringConcatenationFn "This function takes one or more #$SubLStrings (q.v.) as argument(s) and returns the SubL string that is the concatenation of the former strings (in the order given by their respective argument-places, and with all resulting internal quotation marks removed).  For example, `(#$SubLStringConcatenationFn \"Hot\" \"Dog\")' denotes the 8-character string `\"HotDog\"'.  For a similar but more general function that is defined on any sequence of #$CharacterStrings, see #$ConcatenateStringsFn.")
(comment Dollar-Belize "The unit of currency for Belize-AtPresent.")
(comment hasJobPositionIn "(#$hasJobPositionIn PERSON ORG JOB) means that #$Person PERSON has #$JobPosition JOB in #$Organization ORG. Note that assertions using #$hasJobPositionIn should be properly time-constrained, for example, with #$holdsIn.")
(comment Prisoner-Legal "The collection of all people that are incarcerated in a #$Prison maintained by some law-enforcement authority.")
(comment Autogyro "The collection of aircraft whose lift is provided by unpowered rotating blades, but whose propulsion is provided by a propeller.")
(comment DynamicInfoSource "The collection of all abstract sources of information whose information content can change over time. Includes all intangible works that 'survive' modification or editing.")
(comment CruiseMissile-HarassmentDrone "A specialization of #$CruiseMissile, intended to function as drone
aircraft in attacks on enemy planes and helicopters.")
(comment Mollicutes-Class "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalClass in the #$MoneraKingdom.  Currently, all organisms in the #$Tenericutes-Division are under this #$BiologicalClass.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are usually #$Bacterium, but some species have gliding motility.  Most species require sterols and fatty acids for growth.")
(comment Username "A collection of #$IDStrings. Each #$Username is a #$CharacterString that represents a distinct user of a #$Computer or the #$agreeingServiceRecipient of a #$ComputerAccount.")
(disjointWith Lake Ocean)
(comment COAMissionAnalysisProdsG3Microtheory "A collection of microtheories.  The information in each
instance will inherit to some instance of
#$COASpecificationMicrotheory, and in some cases, to multiple
instances.  Each instance of #$COAMissionAnalysisProdsG3Microtheory is used
to specify mission analysis products deriving from the G3, pursuant to the COAs
that appear among the #$genlMt dependents.")
(comment MustModeFn "(#$MustModeFn SCRIPTTYPE CONTEXT-MT) denotes the      subcollection of SCRIPTTYPE whose instances possess the modal property denoted by \"must\", from the perspective of CONTEXT-MT.")
(comment unitsOfDrugPrescriptionsByDocTypeDuring "(#$unitsOfDrugPrescriptionsByDocTypeDuring DOC-TYPE DRUG-PROD PRESC-TYPE PERIOD NUM) means that, during the #$TimeInterval PERIOD, #$MedicalCareProfessionals of type, DOC-TYPE, had #$DrugPrescriptions for NUM  units of DRUG-PROD filled.")
(comment Syphilis "A sexually transmissible disease that, if undetected, can lead to insanity and death.")
(comment Sunset "Each #$Sunset is an #$Event in which, at a given location, the horizon occludes the #$Sun as it appears to set.  This event is construed to occur regardless of the visibility of the #$Sun due to obscuring objects such as clouds.  There is a #$Dusk which is #$contiguousAfter each #$Sunset.  Every #$DaytimeHours is #$temporallyFinishedBy a #$Sunset (unless it #$endsDuring a #$MidnightSun), as is every #$Afternoon.")
(comment Acrophobia "Fear of high places")
(comment RetaliationGoal "Typically, this attribute characterizes relationships between Cyc formulas and agents when the Cyc formula describes some state of affairs that the agent intends to actualize in order to retaliate against some other agent.")
(comment ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-General "#$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-General is the collection of all #$AttackByComputerOperation where the  primary purpose of the attack is to acquire information contained in an instance of #$ComputationalSystem.")
(comment alignedAlong "(#$alignedAlong OBJ1 OBJ2) means that the two objects are adjacent and aligned so as to be oriented in the same way.")
(comment PlantMaintenancePerson "That's plant as in 'production site', not as in 'botanical thing'.")
(comment TaoistGift "An instance of #$GiftTypeByReligion.  The collection of all #$Gifts that are somehow associated with #$Taoism.")
(comment AirDefenseArtilleryRADAR "A type of RADAR used to detect incoming artillery fire and to determine the position of the source of the fire.")
(comment collectionIntersection "A #$TaxonomicSlotForCollections (q.v.) that relates a set of collections to the collection whose extent (see #$extent) is by definition the intersection of the extents of all the collections in that set.  (#$collectionIntersection INTERSECT SET-OF-COLS) means that INTERSECT is the \"collection-intersection\" of SET-OF-COLS: any given thing THING is an instance of INTERSECT if and only if THING is an instance of every collection that is an element of SET-OF-COLS.  It follows that INTERSECT is itself a subcollection of every element of SET-OF-COLS.  Note that, since collections are supposed to be \"intensionally defined\", it is theoretically possible that there be more than one collection having exactly the extent (i.e. set of instances) characterized above.  But COL is to be thought of as the collection which _by_definition_ contains all and only the instances common to every collection in SET-OF-COLS.  In other words, the criterion for instanceship associated with INTERSECT (i.e. its \"intensional definition\") is in effect simply the conjunction of each of the criteria associated with the various members of SET-OF-COLS.  This is what justifies the above description of INTERSECT as _the_ collection-intersection corresponding to SET-OF-COLS, and what justifies #$collectionIntersection's being defined as a functional predicate.  See the corresponding function #$CollectionIntersectionFn; also see #$collectionUnion.")
(comment Technetium "The element Technetium, atomic number 43.")
(comment USMarinePlatoon "#$USMarinePlatoon is the collection of all platoons within the #$UnitedStatesMarineCorps.  It consists of four #$USMarineSquad, and is commanded by a Lieutenant with a Sergeant as a second-in-command.")
(disjointWith ClimateCycleType BeliefSystemType)
(comment derivedLiteraryWork "(#$derivedLiteraryWork WORK DERIVED) means that the literary work WORK is derived from the literary work DERIVED. There are no generally accepted criteria for when this relation obtains between two works. Nonetheless, there may be contexts in which there are criteria for the applciation of this predicate. Perhaps in a type of naive context, one literary work is not derived from another if, when the original contains fictional characters, the derived work does not have some character which is 'based on' some character in the original.")
(comment MoralPrecept "The moral equivalent of a #$Law, that is, a ruling or

guiding principle that has moral/religious force, but not (necessarily) legal force.

Note however that fundamentalist nations may well give full legal force to the moral precepts of the

national religion.")
(comment CalciumCarbonate "Chemical compound found naturally as limestone, calcite, and making up the shells of molluscs; also used as an antacid.")
(comment nationalityOfManufacturer "The country or other kind of geopolitical entity which is home to the agent that manufactured this object.  This doesn't necessarily mean the object was manufactured in this geopolitical entity - for example, #$Japan is home to the makers of Honda cars, but many Hondas are actually manufactured in the US.")
(comment SemelfactiveEventType "The collection of collections of events that occur momentarily. In set-theoretic terms, it includes the union of the range of #$SemelfactiveTypeFn. For every SLOT, (#$SemelfactiveTypeFn SLOT) is a spec of #$SemelfactiveEventType. Hence, an instance of #$SemelfactiveEventType is a spec of #$Event that is semelfactive with respect to at least one actor slot. It is a spec of #$AccomplishmentType because no cumulative event type can be semelfactive: any continuous proper segment of a process of type X is still a (another) process of type X.")
(comment UncoveringSomething "The set of actions in which an takes a covering off of something-- reveals it.")
(disjointWith DecoratingWithObjects DecoratingWithMarks)
(comment Abrasive "The attribute of being so #$Rough in texture that it wears material of something with which there is a #$TranslationAlongASurface.")
(comment Clostridium "A collection of #$Bacterium.  A #$BiologicalGenus formed in the

#$MoneraKingdom.  The #$Clostridium-Genus are large #$AnaerobicBacterium,

#$GramPositiveBacterium, #$BacillusBacterium.  These #$ProkaryoticCells cause

#$Botulism, #$Tetanus, gas gangrene, and pseudomembranous colitis.")
(comment DefaultingOnLoan "The collection of #$ScriptTypes in which some #$Organization or other #$IntelligentAgent fails to fulfill some legal obligation, such as by neglecting to pay back a #$LoanAgreement on schedule.")
(comment prospectiveBuyer "(#$prospectiveBuyer ACT AGENT) means that AGENT acts in the purchaser's, or potential purchaser's, role in the #$CommercialActivity ACT.")
(comment equivalentRoot "#$equivalentRoot relates one #$ComputationalSystem to           another.  (#$equivalentRoot SYSTEM1 SYSTEM2)  means that the root user           of SYSTEM1 can access the root account on SYSTEM2 without having to           re-enter their  #$Username or #$Password-Computer.")
(comment Ductile "has greater than #$NonDuctile Ductility")
(disjointWith HospitalCareEvent MovementOrShapeChangeEvent)
(comment TimeZoneBorder "The collection of all boundaries between international #$TimeZones.")
(comment (RightObjectOfPairFn (PartTypeFn FourthThoracicVertebra VertebralTransverseProcess)) "")
(comment proxyEnforcer-FunctionalRole "(#$proxyEnforcer-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT) means that there is a supersystem SUPER such that (#$subGroups SUPER SYSTEM) and (#$different SUPER SYSTEM) and such that (#$enforcer-FunctionalRole SUPER AGENT).  This predicate is applicable in cases of enforcement function where the executive whose edicts are being enforced is executive of a system that subsumes the system in which the enforcement is happening, and is the common generalization of a number of more specialized roles, such as #$politicalCommisar.")
(comment VelvetCloth "The collection of all velvet cloth.  Velvet was traditionally made of silk, but is now made of synthetic fiber or of cotton.")
(disjointWith Country FederalDistrict)
(comment ProgramSelfReplication "This is the collection of all events of programs replicating themselves.  It 

    includes the propagation of instances of #$ComputerWorm and

    #$ComputerVirus.")
(comment ElectronicCountermeasuresVehicle "The collection of vehicles intended for use in electronic countermeasure operations.")
(comment HTTPCookie "The collection of instances of

 #$ComputerFileCopy that, during

  server connections, are generated

 on the server side of the connection but 

 stored on the client's system, where they can

  be retrieved by the server's system.  

  #$HTTPCookies are used to store information 

  about the client and his/her system.")
(comment AutomaticWeaponTypeByOperationType "The three instances of #$AutomaticWeaponTypeByOperationType are  collections of #$AutomaticFirearms according to how bullets automatically reload.  There are three types: #$AutomaticFirearm-RecoilOperated, #$AutomaticFirearm-BlowbackOperated, and #$AutomaticFirearm-GasOperated.")
(disjointWith Temperature Voltage)
(disjointWith DefenseSystem StuffedToy)
(comment TreatmentOfInjuryFn "#$TreatmentOfInjuryFn is a #$CollectionDenotingFunction. (#$TreatmentFn INJURY) denotes the subset of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent whose elements are treatments of instances of the #$Injury-Object type, INJURY. For a specific #$Injury-Object type, the collection returned as the value of (#$TreatmentFn INJURY) may be a subset of some more general collection of medical procedures; e.g., standard processes of (#$TreatmentFn SunBurn) will also be elements of (#$TreatmentFn #$SkinBurn).")
(comment SpecialEvent "This is a collection of instances of #$Event-Organized. Membership criteria is a bit squishy. Instances might be EntertainmentEvent(s), PoliticalEvent(s), etc.")
(disjointWith CycLRepresentedAtomicTerm SubLAtomicTerm)
(disjointWith GovernmentMilitaryOrganization Militia)
(comment DNAStrand "The collection of all DNA strands or chains. A single instance of
#$DNAMolecule consists of two such complementary strands linked together in
a double-helix shape.")
(comment weaponArmorPenetration "The predicate #$weaponArmorPenetration

 indicates how thick an armor (average strength)

 a #$Weapon can penetrate if it hits it head on.

 This can be used to describe the penetration ability of

 an #$AntiTankWeapon

 as well as that of simpler weapons like #$Swords or #$Arrows.")
(comment ProtectionRacketeering "The collection of activities in which one agent extracts payment from another agent ostensibly for the first agent providing 'protection' services to the second. In protection rackets, there is usually no real threat that the victim needs protecting from, except the racketeer himself. The victim pays the racketeer because he knows that if he doesn't, the racketeer will arrange for some harmful action to occur to the victim's person, family, business, etc.")
(comment BroadcastAntenna "Devices for converting modulated electrical signals into information-bearing radio waves that are radiated from the antenna into space.")
(comment BeltedMotion "#$MultirevolutionRotation of a loop (e.g. #$Belt-Mechanical or #$Chain) driven by a non-attached #$Wheel/#$Gear/roller/....  Objects may ride on the #$Belt-Mechanical if the #$Belt-Mechanical is wide enough, slow enough, and at an appropriate orientation.  A #$Belt-Mechanical circumscribing several #$Wheel/#$Gear/...s can be used to drive those which are not providing power to the #$Belt-Mechanical.  The purpose of #$BeltedMotion may be to relay rotary motion between two locations, to carry something on the belt's surface, both, or to apply linear motion to the #$Belt-Mechanical.  The motion of a #$FanBelt or #$ConveyorBelt or the spinning of a #$Chain on a #$Bicycle, #$Motorcycle, or #$ChainSaw are examples of #$BeltedMotion.")
(comment USStateRepresentative "The collection of elected officials who serve in a state-level, as opposed to a national, House of Representatives.")
(disjointWith InformationTransferEvent RaisingLivingThings)
(comment WetClayTablet "Moist, soft substance composed of very fine particles of earth and, usually, water.")
(comment WorksOfArtPeriodFn "(#$WorksOfArtPeriodFn PERIOD) denotes the collection of objects
of art that belong to PERIOD, a certain period ofently noted by historian
of art.")
(comment Moonlight "The light that comes from the moon.")
(comment LesbianStory "The subset of #$EroticStory whose elements contain the propositional content of an  #$EroticStory in which two or more instances of #$FemalePerson engage in #$HomosexualBehavior-Female.")
(comment FacialMuscleSet "The #$Collection of all instances of #$FacialMuscleSet.  The #$FacialMuscleSet controls facial movement, including the #$Eyebrows, #$Eyelids, and some of the motions of the lips (#$Lip-AnimalBodyPart).  There are 18 facial muscles on each side.")
(comment keFarthestGenlsStrongSuggestionPreds "(#$keFarthestGenlsStrongSuggestionPreds COL BIN-PRED) means that for
every specialization SPEC-COL of COL such that SPEC-COL is not known to have dependent specializations, it is strongly suggested that
there exist some VALUE such that (BIN-PRED SPEC-COL VALUE) is known in
the KB.")
(disjointWith ModalReasoningMicrotheory ModalReasoningInferenceMicrotheory)
(comment Tranquilizer "Drugs which are used to calm patients with psychoses.  Milder versions are also used as anti-depressants.")
(comment around-UnderspecifiedRegion "(#$around-UnderspecifiedRegion ACT REGION) states that an
abstract locational relation holds between ACT and REGION, where
REGION is a #$Region-Underspecified circumvented or circumscribed during
ACT.  #$around-UnderspecifiedRegion is an underspecified semantic
representation that may be elaborated to represent either a spatial
example of 'go around' (as in 'walking around the park') or a temporal
use of crossing ('shall we meet around nine o'clock?') or a
metaphorical use ('Smith had to go around Bob to get the promotion he
wanted').")
(comment Meteorologist "The collection of all #$Scientists whose #$fieldsOfFormalEducation include #$Meteorology.")
(comment Volt "The basic unit of electrical potential in the MKS system.  It is defined as one watt per ampere.")
(comment GameRecordHoldersFn "#$GameRecordHoldersFn takes a spec of #$PurposefulAction as its argument and returns as its result the collection of all record-holders in that type of event. For example, (#$GameRecordHoldersFn #$CarRacing) returns the collection of all car racing record holders.")
(comment ParseMtFn "This function takes a string and returns an instance of #$ParsingContext.
#$ParseMtFn NATs are created in CYC-STRING-TO-CONSTITUENTS,
which is the LISP function hooked to #$StringParsingFn.  For all
STRING, (#$ParseMtFn STRING) is a spec-Mt of #$ParsingTestMt.")
(comment Kayak "The collection of kayaks.")
(comment MaterialSafetyDataSheet "This is the collection of individual concrete

#$InformationBearingThings which are required by law to be created by companies

which produce certain materials. The purpose of these sheets is to

provide information relevant to safety. There are sheets about many different

materials and are produced in conformity to ANSI standards.

There are many different MSDS types, and for some purposes it will be more useful

to talk about these types rather than about the members of this collection. See also

#$MaterialSafetyDataSheetCW.")
(comment FloatingBridge-Military "The collection of military bridges that are floating  rather than fixed. Sub-collections of this collection include #$RibbonBridge, #$AluminumFloatingFootBridge and #$LightTacticalRaft, etc.")
(comment StealingStorageSpace "#$StealingStorageSpace is a collection of events in which a person uses an information storage medium that she is not commonly considered to be legally entitled  to use. Almost always, the perpetrator is a #$Hacker, and the medium illictly  used is a #$HardDisk.")
(comment Chlamydia-Genus "A collection of #$Bacterium in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These are obligate parasites.  They are dependent on the host cell for energy generation and can not synthesize #$AdenosineTriphosphate.")
(comment AerialSupportUnit-MilitarySpecialty "Collection of all units that are specialized for air combat and dedicated to support of ground units.")
(comment Claremont-Mudd-ScrippsCollegesAthleticsProgram "This is the collection of all sports teams

    who compete under the banner of 'Claremont-Mudd-Scripps.'  Members of

     such teams are students at either #$ClaremontMcKennaCollege, #$HarveyMuddCollege,

     or #$ScrippsCollege -- three very small colleges with no

     sports teams of their very own.")
(comment ReplenishmentOiler "A collection. Underway replenishment oiler ships.")
(comment Tryptophan "A collection of organic compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.
These compounds are essential for optimal growth in infants as well as
maintaining nitrogen equilibrium in human adults.  These are a
precursor to serotonin.  Its abbreviations are Trp and W.")
(comment uniqueIDOfField "(#$uniqueIDOfField ?LF ?IDTYPE) indicates that ?LF is a logical field which, within its schema, denotes an instance of ?IDTYPE.")
(comment DomainOfFunctionFn "A #$SetDenotingFunction that relates a given function (see
#$Function-Denotational) to its set-theoretic domain (see
#$relationDomain).  (#$DomainOfFunctionFn FUNCTION) is the 
instance of #$Set-Mathematical consisting of all and only 
those things that FUNCTION maps to some (indeed, to exactly 
one) thing (see #$valueOfFunctionForArgs).  For each element 
D of FUNCTION's domain, there will be exactly one element R 
of FUNCTION's range (see #$relationRange and #$RangeOfFunctionFn) 
such that FUNCTION relates D to R.  Where the #$arity (q.v.)
of FUNCTION is N, D is an N-length instance of #$List, and 
applying FUNCTION to D is a matter of filling each successive 
argument-place in FUNCTION with the corresponding item in 
D.  Note that if FUNCTION is a #$VariableArityFunction (q.v.)
there will be no particular length N shared by each of the 
lists in its domain.")
(comment IFVAntiArmorUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of military units trained and equipped to fight armored vehicles and typically employing Infantry Fighting Vehilces. (See #$M2InfantryFightingVehicle.)")
(comment IDObject "A specialization of #$SubLAtom.  Each instance of #$IDObject is a token (such as a string or a number) that is used as an identifier for a distinct thing.  Instances of #$IDObject may be unique identifiers, in which case they are instances of the specialization #$UniqueID.")
(comment Fever "A condition characterized by a high core body temperature and other symptoms. Not all situations in which the core temp is hot are fevers - exertion, for example, produces high core temp")
(comment (PartTypeFn (RightObjectOfPairFn EighthRib) Tuberosity) "")
(comment (HighAmountFn Glamour) "The attribute of being considered highly glamorous.")
(comment AssistantChiefOfStaff-Signal "The collection of instances of  #$CoordinatingStaffMember-USArmy
with responsibility for all matters concerning signal operations, automation management, 
network management,and information security.")
(comment Escort-SexualEntertainmentProvider "The collection of #$Escort-EntertainmentProviders that provide company as well as #$SexualGratification.")
(comment verbClassDenotation "(#$verbClassDenotation VERB-CLASS DENOTATUM) indicates that
DENOTATUM serves as the default denotation for verbs in
VERB-CLASS. For example, (#$verbClassDenotation
#$SoundsMadeByAnimalsVerbClass (#$SubcollectionPerformedByTypeFn
#$EmittingSound #$SentientAnimal)) indicates that, by default, the verbs in
Levin Class 38 denote an event of a sound by emitted by an animal.")
(comment VendorAccount "An account decremented by payments to a vendor and incremented by buying something from the vendor.")
(comment HorseSplintBoot "This is the collection of #$HorseBoots which are designed to protect a horse's splint and fetlock areas.")
(comment LogisticsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units specialized for           providing logistical support to other military units.")
(comment TheOneOf "A function that results in a #$TheTerm that satisfis some #$ELSentence-Assertible. The first argument is a #$ELVariable that appears as a free variable in the second argument. For example, (#$TheOneOf ?X (#$and (#$isa ?X #$Dog) (#$colorOfObject ?X #$BlackColor))) denotes the (contextually salient) black dog.")
(comment IndoorSoccerTeam "the collection of #$SoccerTeams that play

  #$IndoorSoccer-CW.")
(comment Ecotourism "This is the collection of ecotourism events. Ecotourism

is an increasingly popular way of taking a vacation wherein the tourists stay in

environmentally friendly dwellings and, as a form of recreation, observe and learn

about the ambient ecosystem.")
(comment BookGeneric-CW "A specialization of #$ConceptualWork. Each instance of the collection #$BookGeneric-CW is an abstract work intended to be instantiated as a book of some sort (hardcopy, electronic, audio tape or compact disc, etc.).  An important specialization is #$Book-CW, instances of which are books that contain propositional information.")
(comment Porous "has greater than #$NoAmountFn Porosity")
(comment UnitOfFrequency "A specialization of #$UnitOfRate, and the collection of functions used to express how often something occurs during an interval of time.  Each instance of #$UnitOfFrequency is a function which returns an instance of #$Frequency when applied to a real number.  For example, (#$MegaHertz 89.5) returns a frequency of 89.5 MHz.")
(comment AttackTypeByTargetType "A collection of collections.  Instances of #$AttackTypeByTargetType are collections of #$AttackOnTangible organized by the intended target type of the attack (e.g., attacks aimed primarily against personnel, versus infrastructure, etc.).")
(comment TransmissionOfFromTypeToTypeFn "(#$TransmissionOfFromTypeToTypeFn AIL TYPE1 TYPE2)

 is the collection of all #$InfectionTransmissionEvents

 in which AIL is transmitted from instances of TYPE1

 to instances of TYPE2.  For example, 

 (#$TransmissionOfFromTypeToTypeFn #$AIDS #$Monkey #$Person)

  is the collection of all transmissions of AIDS

 from monkeys to humans.")
(comment mtsDisparate "(#$mtsDisparate PROP MTPROVE MTNOT) means that there are
well-defined inference parameters by which PROP can be proven in MT,
and that PROP cannot be proven in MTNOT using those same parameters.")
(comment Ablation "A collection of events.  In an #$Ablation, a (usually relatively thin) layer of material is removed from the surface of an object.")
(comment symptomInstanceOnsetRateInCondition "`(#$symptomInstanceOnsetRateInCondition SYM AIL RATE) means that

SYM is a subevent and symptom of AIL and it has/had an onset rate of RATE.")
(comment StandardsFn "#$StandardsFn takes as argument any spec of #$SomethingExisting and returns the collection of PropositionalInformationThings which describe standards for elements of that spec. These standards may be elements of #$ProductStandard, but they may also be standards in a broader sense.  For example, (#$StandardsFn #$RadioReceiver) returns the collection of PITs describing product standards for radio recievers, and (#$StandardsFn #$Poodle) returns the collection of PITs describing standards, probably breed and breeding standards, for poodles.")
(comment Gulf "A specialization of #$BodyOfWater-Large.  Each instance of #$Gulf is a part of a sea extending into a land mass.  Instances of #$Gulf include the #$SaronicGulf, #$GulfOfMexico, #$GulfOfArkangelsk, #$GulfOfCalifornia, and #$PersianGulf.")
(comment WeaponsTesting "The collection of all events that are instances of #$PerformanceTesting in
  which the #$objectTested is an instance of #$Weapon.")
(comment AudioRecordingEngineer "This is the collection of all persons who are skilled at audio recording

and who perform this activity professionally.")
(comment Mirage5E2FighterPlane "A collection of a type of French #$FighterInterceptorPlane.")
(comment PPTByDosageFormType "The collection of types of drug products that are specified as to dosage form, and may be specified as to type of preparation (the drug compounds(s) contained).")
(comment tourTravelSubLegTransport "(#$tourTravelSubLegTransport TOUR PATH TRAVELINGTYPE) means

that a subleg of the leg of tour represented by PATH will involve a

#$TransportationEventByVehicleType of type TRAVELINGTYPE.")
(comment intelligenceOfficer "A functional role that an agent plays with respect to a

military unit.  The #$intelligenceOfficer is responsible for making

sure that the #$unitCommander has access to the intelligence

information needed in order to make correct executive decisions.")
(comment ProfessionalFn "(#$ProfessionalFn PERSON-BY-ACTIV-TYPE) denotes the subcollection of both PERSON-BY-ACTIV-TYPE and #$PersonTypeByOccupation consisting of those people who perform the relevant activity professionally, i.e. for pay.  Compare #$AmateurFn.")
(comment Kwanza-Angola "The currency unit of Angola-1986")
(comment TransportLayerProtocol "The collection of all instances of network

protocol that implement a transport layer. An instance of #$TransportLayerProtocol 

is responsible for ensuring  that data arrives at the 

destination. A #$TransportLayerProtocol splits

a stream of data into #$TransportProtocolDataUnits.")
(comment SorghumPlant "Individual sorghum plants.")
(comment Dissolving "A specialization of #$PhysicalTransformationEvent.  In each instance of #$Dissolving, a solute dissolves in a solvent to form a solution.")
(comment JewishHoliday "The subset of #$ReligiousHolidays specified as part of the religion #$Judaism.")
(comment passwordForAccount "(#$passwordForAccount PASSWORD ACCOUNT) means that PASSWORD is a character string in the collection #$Password-Computer that, along with the use of a character string in the collection #$Username, is used to access ACCOUNT on a computerational system.")
(comment Landmark "Some tangible thing which is usually a topographic feature or a large construction artifact which is well-known in an area, often of interest to travelers.  Exactly what is a landmark is culture dependent, so assertions that X is a landmark should be in an mt which admits to its bias, like the western bias of the #$WorldGeographyMt")
(comment ManyFn "(#$ManyFn COL) denotes a term which represents an instance of COL which is a representative exemplar of many instances of COL.  This function is not a #$ReifiableFunction, since it primarily exists to support NL generation. See #$EveryFn and #$SomeFn for similar functions.")
(comment AntiArmorMine "The collection of #$LandMines that detonate when a heavy vehicle, such as a #$Tank-Vehicle or #$ArmoredPersonnelCarrier, rolls over   the ground above the #$LandMine.  #$AntiArmorMines usually have armor-piercing capability.")
(comment TypeCapableFn "#$TypeCapableFn takes an instance-level #$CapabilityPredicate, and returns a type-level version of that predicate.  In other words, if CAP-PRED is an instance-level #$CapabilityPredicate, then (#$TypeCapableFn CAP-PRED) is the corresponding type-level predicate. A member of #$CapabilityPredicate-InstanceLevel is a predicate which can be used to assert that an individual thing has the capability of playing a certain role in a type of event.  So, '(CAP-PRED INDIVIDUAL EVENT-TYPE ROLE)' means that INDIVIDUAL has the capability CAP-PRED of playing ROLE in EVENT-TYPE.  The corresponding type-level #$CapabilityPredicate, '(#$TypeCapableFn CAP-PRED)', allows one to say that a type of individual has the capability of playing a certain role in a type of event.  So, '((#$TypeCapableFn CAP-PRED) TYPE EVENT-TYPE ROLE)' means that TYPE has the capability CAP-PRED of playing ROLE in EVENT-TYPE.  To say that a type of thing has a capability means that a typical, or normal, individual of that type has the instance-level capability.")
(comment episodeType "(#$episodeType SERIES EPISODETYPE) means that each of the #$episodes of SERIES #$isa EPISODETYPE. Example: (#$episodeType #$Quake-TheGameSeries #$ComputerActionGame) means that every episode of the Quake game series is a computer action game.")
(comment SuccessorFn "A unary function that returns an instance of #$Integer when given an instance of #$Integer as an argument.  (#$SuccessorFn N) denotes the least #$Integer greater than N.  Thus (#$SuccessorFn 42) denotes 43, and (#$SuccessorFn -42) denotes -41.  This function is somewhat broader than the familiar \"successor\" function on natural numbers, since #$SuccessorFn applies to all instances of #$Integer.")
(comment interArg2ResultGenls "A ternary #$MetaRelation predicate for stating that a certain kind of complex, partly #$genls based relationship holds between the second argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned. (#$interArg2ResultGenls FUNC INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the second argument to FUNC, then -- regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be -- the value of that function for those arguments is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is: if INST is a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC ARG1 INST ...) = VALUE, then VALUE is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  Note that, unlike (e.g.) the #$InterArgTypePredicates, #$interArg2ResultGenls _cannot_ be used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on functions.  See also the similar but more flexible quaternary #$interArgResultGenl.")
(comment MusicalCharts "The collection of all published lists of song names ranked by some 'popularity measure'. This measure is typically the number of recordings sold of the songs, the number of votes for the songs of some audience.")
(comment translatesFromTo "(#$translatesFromTo MOTION OBJECT) means that OBJECT

undergoes place to place motion (technically referred to as

translation) such that it moves from the 'from' and to the 'to'

locations which are strongly associated with MOTION.  More formally, a

short time before MOTION starts, OBJECT is located at the

#$fromLocation of MOTION.  A short time after MOTION ends, OBJECT is

located at the #$toLocation of MOTION.  Given MOTION, all values on

#$fromLocation must spatially intersect.  Likewise, given MOTION, all

values on #$toLocation must spatially intersect.  This is because if

MOTION is an event in which there are multiple non-intersecting

#$toLocations (as is the case with scattering or distribution events)

then it would not make sense to use #$translatesFromTo.  Consider the

following examples.  It would be impossible for a plane to fly

(i.e. play the role of #$translatesFromTo) to both #$LaGuardiaAirport

and #$KennedyAirport.  However, it would be possible for both

#$LaGuardiaAirport and #$CityOfNewYorkNY to be #$toLocations since

#$LaGuardiaAirport spatially intersects with #$CityOfNewYorkNY.

Although #$toLocation and #$fromLocation must be spatially

intersecting, pathways (see #$motionPathway-Complete) may be

distinct.  Consider the event in which several flocks of birds migrate

from Alaska to Mexico.  Each flock may leave and arrive at the roughly

the same time.  Each flock may leave from and arrive at the same

general locations.  However, they probably take different pathways en

route.  #$translatesFromTo can be used to relate that single group

migration event to the several flocks, or even the numerous birds

participating in the event.")
(comment ArgFormatTernaryPredicate "The collection of ternary predicates used to specify the required #$Format (q.v.) for a given argument-place of a given #$Predicate.")
(comment Volcano "A collection of topographical features. Each element of #$Volcano is a mountain created by the outflow of lava. Elements of #$Volcano may or may not be active volcanoes.  Examples: #$Vesuvius-Volcano, #$MountFuji-Volcano, #$Popocatepetl-Volcano, #$Krakatoa-Volcano, #$MaunaKea-Volcano, #$MountSaintHelens-Volcano.")
(comment Simulation-Activity "This is the collection of simulations. A simulation in the

present sense is the deliberate creation of a situation (usually event) which resembles another

situation (usually event). The former is often referred to as a simulation or modelling.

The things used to effect such a simulation or modelling are also sometimes called

simulations or, less confusingly, models.

In the intended sense, a #$Simulation-Activity is the creation and use of simulations in

the sense of models, not the model itself. The purposes for which simulations

are created (performed) can be quite various, but each simulation is created for some fairly definite

purpose. An important spec of #$Simulation-Activity is #$ComputerModeling. The

predicate that relates a simulation to what it's a simulation of is 

#$objectOfSimulation.")
(comment Shark-Mackerel "A collection of large sharks; instances are  members of the family           Lamnidae.  These sharks are partly warm-blooded.  This collection includes           the white, porbeagle, and mako sharks.")
(disjointWith TranslationAlongASurface UnderwaterTransportation)
(comment DownwardLocationBySpecifity "This collection contains all collections that are asserted to subcollections of #$DownwardLocation-Underspecified.  Creation of this constant facilitates representation of instances of #$DownwardLocation-Underspecified as it allows us to take advantage of ke facilitation rules (see #$KEFacilitationPredicate) that consider the facets of a collection when an instance of a collection is created.")
(comment genKeyword "An #$NLGenerationPredicate that

relates a given CycL denotational term to the SubL keyword 

that is used to represent it in generating natural language 

from CycL.  (#$genKeyword CYCL-TERM KEYWORD) means that 

KEYWORD represents CYCL-TERM in the generation of natural 

language paraphrases of CycL expressions, e.g. in #$genFormat 

(q.v.) assertions.")
(disjointWith SelectingSomething MusicalPerformance)
(comment Tu-16-Bomber "A type of bomber plane owned by Iraq.")
(comment (GaseousFn Chloropicrin) "Poisonous gas which has effects similar to tear gas.  If ingested, the gas causes gastroenteritis.")
(comment topicOfBeliefSystem "(#$topicOfBeliefSystem BSYSTEM TOPIC) indicates that TOPIC is central to belief system BSYSTEM.")
(comment Magician "The collection of all people who act as intermediary between the natural and supernatural worlds, using #$Magic to cure illness, foretell the future, control spiritual forces, etc.")
(comment DateFromIntegerFn "(#$DateFromIntegerFn UNIVERSAL-DATE) converts the integer UNIVERSAL-DATE into the instance of #$Date which it encodes.  For example, (#$DateFromIntegerFn 19980921) denotes (#$DayFn 21 (#$MonthFn #$September (#$YearFn 1998))).")
(comment ClosingADoor "#$performedBy #$DoorMan, etc.")
(comment BattleTank-M60 "A subset of #$Tank-Vehicle.  The M60 was the main battle tank of the United States Army before it was replaced by the M1A1Abrams.")
(comment SupportGroupFn-Misc "#$SupportGroupFn-Misc takes as argument any spec of #$Event and returns the collection of all support groups for persons experiencing events of that type.  For example (#$SupportGroupFn-Misc #$Dieting) returns the collection of all dieting support groups.")
(comment FormalGrammar-CW "The collection of all formal grammars, each being a conceptual work containing a formal specification of the set of grammatically valid relational structures (often #$CharacterStrings) allowed by the formal specification.  The grammar is formal in that there is, in theory at least, a precise test (whether or not it is decidable or feasible) for compliance of a given structure with the specification.  Most #$FormalGrammar-CWs are #$StringGrammars, but there are also #$GraphGrammars and other kinds.  Often a candidate structure is tested against a #$FormalGrammar-CW with a computer program that parses the candidate into its constituent substructures. #$FormalGrammar-CWs have been used to specify #$ComputerLanguages and to describe #$NaturalLanguages.")
(disjointWith SocialGathering ConflictEvent)
(comment RepayInternationalLoans "The collection of events where a state repays a loan to another state(s) or an international bank(s).  Brazil has many loans of this sort that it is slowly repaying.")
(comment SalmonellaArizonae "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom.  It
causes bacteremia with focal lesions.  Following oral infection, there
is an early invasion of the bloodstream, but intestinal manifestations
are often absent.")
(comment InternetBroadcasting "A collection of events and a specialization of   #$MassCommunicating and #$InternetCommunication. In every instance of #$InternetBroadcasting, information is transmitted via the #$Internet and aimed at a great many agents.  For example, an internet transmission of footage of court testimony aimed at the general public is an instance of #$InternetBroadcasting.  A private email message is not.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentEvent MakingAPlan)
(comment Cephalexin "A commonly prescribed #$Cephalosporin.")
(comment Resin "The collection of all pieces of resin that are naturally occurring; generally             these come from plant secretions.  Resins are yellow to brown, translucent to            transparent, and vary in their physical state from semisolid to solid and             very hard.")
(comment Colloid "The collection of mixtures consisting of a medium and a substance dispersed in the medium in particles too fine to be seen with an ordinary light microscope but large enough to be unable to pass through a semipermeable membrane. This second property distinguishes #$Colloids from true #$Solutions.")
(comment EntertainmentIndustry "The collection of all entertainment industries. Each #$EntertainmentIndustry is an instance of #$Industry-Localized whose members are involved in the production of #$TVSeriesProducts, #$Movie-CWs, and other entertainment products.")
(comment PushingOff "Pushing with arms or legs to initiate movement.  For example, to start from a standing position in ice skating or to move away from the wall in swimming.")
(comment SetOrCollectionType "The #$Collection of all #$SetOrCollections of #$SetOrCollections.")
(comment MalignantTumor "Tumors which are cancerous.")
(disjointWith Volatility-Physical Volume)
(comment relationExpansion "ARG2 is a CycL expression which indicates the meaning of expressions in which the relation ARG1 is the operator (i.e., in which ARG1 is in the 0th argument position).  In ARG2, the variables ?arg1, ?arg2, ?arg3, ?arg4, and ?arg5 correspond to the objects in the argument positions 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5, respectively, in expressions which have ARG1 as the operator.")
(comment AirDefenseUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all ground-based military units dedicated to           protecting airspace regions.")
(disjointWith Pond InternationalWaters)
(comment ArtificialLanguage-Informal "All elements of ArtificialLanguage whose explicit syntax and semantics is informal, e.g. the constructed international languages like Esperanto and Ido .")
(comment ReconnaissancePlane "The collection of all airplanes used for surveying terrain for the

purpose of gathering information, usually for some military purpose.")
(comment DitransitivePPFrameType "Frames used for verbs that take an NP complement followed by a PP complement. Examples include 'make X out of Y', etc.")
(comment Contrail "The word `contrail' was coined in 1943 to refer to the CONdensation TRAIL (water vapor) left by a jet or rocket flying at high altitude")
(comment objectTypeInCommercialActivity "The predicate #$objectTypeInCommercialActivity is used to indicate the type of product involved in a particular commercial activity.  (#$objectTypeInCommercialActivity COMACT PRODTYP) means that in the instance COMACT of #$CommercialActivity, a central and focal `participant' is the #$ProductType PRODTYP (the type, not an instance of it).  This kind of information is important in such product-related commercial activities as advertising, specifying (e.g., for a bid), or recalling a product.")
(comment reformulationDirectionInMode "(#$reformulationDirectionInMode DIRECTION MODE RULE), when

asserted in the microtheory MT, tells the #$CycLReformulator whether to use RULE

in the forward (#$ReformulationForwardDirection) or backward

(#$ReformulationBackwardDirection) direction when reformulating

#$CycLExpressions in MT or a specMt thereof, and when operating in the mode MODE.

It will reformulate the 'from' arg into the 'to' arg,

based on DIRECTION.  #$ReformulationNeitherDirection

indicates the rule is not to be used at all in this mt.

This concept of direction has nothing to do with the forward vs. backward rule

distinction in inference.")
(disjointWith HomosexualHuman BisexualHuman)
(comment EquivalenceCollectionFn "Equivalence relations \"carve up\" sets or collections to which

they apply into equivalence classes.  Each member of the original set

or collection belongs to one and only one of the resulting equivalence

classes.  Given an equivalence relation and collection, which must be

a subcollection of the domain of the relation, and a member of the given collection, this function denotes the collection of other elements

of the collection that bear the equivalence relation to the

given thing.   See #$equivalenceCollectionWRT and the analogous

#$EquivalenceClassFn for further discussion.")
(comment genFormat "The Common Lisp format string ARG2 can be applied to the argument list ARG3 to generate pseudo-English for the #$Cyc #$Relation ARG1")
(comment ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheory-MixedDateSeries "This is the sub-collection of

#$ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheory that contains all and only

those that take #$ReasoningWithTense-LogicMt-MixedDateSeries as

#$genlMt.")
(comment Infection "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Each instance of #$Infection is an ailment condition in which microorganisms are abnormally present (or abnormally numerous) within an animal's body.  The microorganisms involved in an infection may be instances of the collections #$Bacterium, #$Virus, or #$ProtistaKingdom.  Specializations of #$Infection include #$Bronchitis, #$Tonsillitis, and #$SexuallyTransmittedInfection (which has further specializations).")
(comment initialSublists "(#$initialSublists LIST1 LIST2) means that LIST2 is an initial sublist of LIST1. That is, LIST1 begins with the sequence of elements in LIST2.  Note that, unlike the predicate #$sublists, the arguments #$initialSublists are not EL lists -- that is, they do not begin with #$TheList.")
(comment Giant "Legendary beings who are enormous in size. An example in American folklore is Paul Bunyan.")
(comment mtLinearDistanceValue "(#$mtLinearDistanceValue MT INTERVAL) means that when reasoning in (or with) the context MT, spatial objects for which the longest axis (longest linear dimension) falls within the range specified by INTERVAL should be attended to, or taken into account.  For example, (#$mtLinearDistanceValue MT (#$Meter 1 100)) means that when reasoning with the knowledge in MT, only objects for which the longest axis (length, width, height, diameter) measures greater than or equal to 1 meter, and less than or equal to 100 meters, should be considered relevant.")
(comment BridalShower "The collection of all parties [#$Party-Celebration] to bestow gifts upon a woman before her wedding [#$WeddingCeremony].")
(comment FindOrInstantiateFn "(#$FindOrInstantiateFn PREFIX MT SET) denotes a term which is an element of SET in MT, which is a #$SetOrCollection.  This is accomplished by first attempting to find any existing element of SET and using the first one found.  If none can be found, a new #$CycLConstant with a unique name that begins with the string PREFIX is created and asserted to be an element of SET.  See also #$InstantiateFn.")
(comment IcyPlanetaryBody "A collection of heavenly bodies.  Each element of #$IcyPlanetaryBody is a planetary body composed primarily of icy substances.")
(comment Tigan "The chemical compound which is an anti-emetic.")
(comment ImperceptiblePressure "Pressure in an amount below human sensitivity to pressure.  Humans do not detect pressures less than .85 g/mm.sq.")
(comment R-TheLetter "The letter R of the alphabet.  This is 'R' (or 'r') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.  As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterR and #$LatinSmallLetterR.")
(comment Dollar-Barbados "Major unit of currency of Barbados")
(comment UniversityEntryTest "The collection of #$AcademicTesting events that are designed to test the scholastic aptitude, and thus college eligibility, of a student. Such tests may attempt to discern either a school-leaver's aptitude for a primary college degree, or a college graduate's aptitude for post-graduate education.")
(comment UnmannedAircraft "The collection of #$AirTransportationDevices which are designed to travel without human #$driverActor. These craft may be steered by remote control.")
(comment CollegeFootballTeamFn "(#$CollegeFootballTeamFn COLLEGE) denotes the college football team for COLLEGE.  For example, (#$CollegeFootballTeamFn #$UniversityOfTexasAtAustin) denotes the University of Texas football team.")
(comment SeedCoat "The protective outercovering of the seed, developed from the ovule integuments.")
(comment interArgIsa5-1 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).   (#$interArgIsa5-1 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that,  when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the fifth argument to RELN,  a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the first argument  must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then  (RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 INST ... ARGN) is semantically  well-formed only if ARG1 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation  of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct  specializations.")
(comment OffshoreBankingIndustry "The collection of all geograpically defined offshore banking industries, each being an instance of #$Industry-Localized in a particular area, concerned primarily with handling foreign accounts, currency and securities.  Members are banks in that locale.  Offshore banks are attractive to certain customers because they offer very low tax rates and/or ways to avoid certain taxes that may be imposed by the  country of residence of the depositors and investors.  The banking industries of #$CuracaoIsland-NetherlandsAntilles and #$CaymanIslands-TheColony are examples.")
(comment CompleteAISOfIBTFn "A function taking an #$InformationBearingThing, IBT, as its argument and returning the maximal #$AbstractInformationStructure instantiated by IBT.  More precisely, (#$CompleteAISOfIBTFn IBT) is the #$AbstractInformationStructure such that for all ?AIS distinct from (#$CompleteAISOfIBTFn IBT), IBT instantiates ?AIS if and only if ?AIS is a #$subInfoStructures of (#$CompleteAISOfIBTFn IBT).")
(comment WaterPlatform-Subsurface "The collection of military water platforms meant to travel underwater.")
(comment COASupplementMicrotheory "A military Course Of Action (COA) sketch only outlines the
intended course of action at a certain level of specificity.  For
purposes of evaluating COAs, users may on occasion wish to supply
supplementary hypotheses, deriving in particular from the mission
analysis products.  These can be supplied in instances of
#$COASupplementMicrotheory.  Instances are microtheories that consist
of sets of assertions that posit specific hypotheses whose effect on a
proposed plan execution we wish to test.  Some of these hypotheses
might involve adjustments to critical background parameters--e.g.,
suppositions to the effect that it is raining heavily or that it is
nighttime--or they might involve further assumptions about the
friendly forces charged with carrying out the tasks represented in the
COA.  See also #$Plan, #$COASpecificationMicrotheory.")
(comment nucleotideSequenceOf "(#$nucleotideSequenceOf POLYNUC SEQUENCE) means that SEQUENCE is the nucleotide sequence of the #$Polynucleotide POLYNUC.  SEQUENCE is expressed as an abstract list of nuclear base symbols.  See #$Nucleotide-GIS.")
(comment unitsOfDrugPrescriptionsByDocTypePayerDuring "(#$unitsOfDrugPrescriptionsByDocTypePayerDuring DOCTYPE DRUGTYPE RXFILLTYPE PAYER PERIOD NUM) means that DOCTYPEs had NUM prescriptions of type RXFILLTYPE filled for DRUGTYPE and payed by PAYER during PERIOD.  RXFILLTYPE may be #$FillingAPrescription-Retail, #$FillingAPrescription-MailOrder, #$FillingANewPrescription, #$FillingARefillPrescription, intersections of these, or merely #$FillingAPrescription.")
(comment MakingAReferral "A communication act in which agent x directs agent y to agent z, so that agent z can do something for agent y.")
(comment FallingProcess "A moving process in which a non completely supported object moves downward under the force of gravity.  Since time slice is also a #$FallingProcess, the collision with the ground or some other object is not a necessary #$subEvents as it is with #$FallingEvent.")
(comment EthnicGroupOfCajuns "This is the group of people who are mostly Roman Catholic and live primarily in rural southern Louisiana. They are descendents of French settlers to the region.

They speak a dialect of French. ")
(comment MultipleSclerosis "Disorder of the nervous system resulting in partial or complete paralysis and muscle tremors")
(comment ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Information "#$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Information is the subset of #$AttackByComputerOperation whose instances are

defined by the kind of information that is the object of the attack.

'Kind of information' might be explicated in terms of the value of 

the information to the information-holder, it's value  to

the attacker, whether it is protected, whether it is classified,

whether and to what degree it is restricted, and others.

Examples of specific kinds of information that might become the object

of an #$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Information include

#$ProtectedInformation, #$RestrictedInformation,

#$Classification-US information, #$PublicInformation,

#$SecurityInformation, and perhaps others.")
(comment groupsOfMaxSize "The functional predicate corresponding to GroupsOfMaxSizeFn.  (#$groupsOfMaxSize relates a #$NonNegativeInteger N and a collection of #$TemporalThings TYPE to the collection of all #$Groups composed of at most N instances of TYPE.")
(comment FoodDeliveryPerson "The collection of people who deliver food to the END CONSUMER, not just to any buyer.")
(comment JewishGift "An instance of #$GiftTypeByReligion.  The collection of all #$Gifts that are somehow associated with #$Judaism.")
(comment AntiAircraftArtilleryGun "Large mounted guns used to bring down enemy aircraft.")
(comment Tantalum "The element Tantalum, atomic number 73.")
(comment LeftwardsFn "This function, applied to a #$LeftAndRightSidedObject,returns the
exact direction the object's left is facing in the 
implicit frame of reference defined by the object.")
(comment USMarineCompany "#$USMarineCompany is the collection of all companies within the #$UnitedStatesMarineCorps.  It consists of four #$USMarinePlatoon and a headquarters staff.  It is commanded by a captain.")
(comment keGenlsStrongConsiderationPreds "(#$keGenlsStrongConsiderationPreds COL BIN-PRED) means that for every specialization SPEC-COL of COL, it should be considered whether there is some VALUE such that (BIN-PRED SPEC-COL VALUE) holds, and if there is, it is strongly suggested that this relationship be made known in the KB.")
(comment ImmoralAct "Actions which are immoral and wrong with respect to a particular moral code of conduct.

 The moral analog of a #$CriminalAct (see #$HowToDescribeCrimes).")
(comment Studying "Looking over books, papers, notes, etc. and trying to learn and understand.")
(comment BrightFn "returns a bright version of the color arg1")
(comment Tutorial "A type of #$Instructions.  Tutorials (say, about ?X) are generally aimed at people who have never used ?X before, and provide an introduction about the basic kinds of things ?X can do.  They do not usually provide information about more complicated abilities or features of ?X.  Although the word \"tutorial\" is especially often used for tutorials of computer programs, one can imagine a tutorials for using a car, fixing a roof, etc.")
(comment programCopyAccessed-ReadOnly "(#$programCopyAccessed-ReadOnly EVENT PROGRAMCOPY) means that PROGRAMCOPY is            the instance of #$ComputerProgramCopy from which information is read in the instance            of #$FileOperation, EVENT.")
(comment Aflatoxin "A #$ToxicSubstance; a naturally occurring carcinogen")
(comment ExecutePermission "#$ExecutePermission is one of the three #$FilePermissions.           If an account has #$ExecutePermission for a file, it can legitimately           run that file.")
(comment Abortifacient "Class of substances that can be used to end pregnancy.")
(comment NonDuctile "not at all ductile")
(comment PartialFunction "A specialization of  #$Function-Denotational whose instances are partial functions: functions that do not have well-defined values for everything to which they can legally be applied.  More precisely,  an (N-ary) function F is partial if it is #$undefined  -- i.e. returns no value -- for one or more (length N sequences of) things that meet its (respective) argument-type constraints (see #$ArgTypePredicate).  An example of a #$PartialFunction is  #$TangentFn because although (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure 90)  and (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure 270) both meet its  argument-constraints, #$TangentFn is undefined for both.  Another  example of a #$PartialFunction is #$BorderBetweenFn.  As the  #$arg1Isa and #$arg2Isa for this binary function are both  #$GeographicalRegion (and there are no further-restricting arg[N]Genl  constraints on the function), #$BorderBetweenFn can be applied to any  pair of geographical regions whatsoever.  But of course not all pairs of  regions are such that they share a border.  Thus it is correct to assert, for  example, (#$undefined (#$BorderBetweenFn #$Albania #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica)). Instances of #$Function-Denotational that are not partial are #$TotalFunctions.")
(comment VehicleConversion "Conversion of a #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle into another type of #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle.  For example, conversion of an #$Automobile into a #$LowRiderCar.")
(comment HumanRegionalBorder "The collection of all boundaries, borders, lines of demarcation, etc., used to delineate territories that play a role in human civic, political, or economic affairs.  This includes #$GeopoliticalBorders like #$CountryBorders and #$TimeZoneBorders, the boundaries of other administrative districts like States, cities, and counties, statistics- and census-related boundaries, and boundaries relating to trade and business, like the borders of sales territories. It also includes politically or socially significant border sections, like the section of the German border that #$formsBorderBetween Germany and France")
(comment (RightObjectOfPairFn (PartTypeFn SeventhThoracicVertebra VertebralTransverseProcess)) "")
(comment ElectronicEquipmentVehicle "The collection of vehicles intended to be used for the transport of electronic equipment.")
(comment inStock "(#$inStock AGENT STOCKED_ITEMS) means that AGENT, an instance of #$LegalAgent, has STOCKED_ITEMS, an instance of the set of groups of instances of #$PartiallyTangible,in the storage area in which AGENT usually keeps the items AGENT intends to sell.")
(comment BattleRifle "The collection of #$Rifles that are used in military combat, but are different from #$AssaultRifles in that they are semi-automatic.  Assault  rifles have mostly replaced the #$BattleRifle.  #$BattleRifles are mostly  self-loading and gas-operated.")
(disjointWith Density Voltage)
(comment HealthFoodMarketCategory "Market category for food, herbs, vitamins, and beverages typically sold in health food stores (or health food departments of a grocery store).")
(comment HelpDesk-Organization "A specialization of #$CustomerServiceDepartment. Each instance of this collection is a department which provides customers with more or less immediate, personal telephone or e-mail service, especially with regard to computers or electronic devices.")
(comment priorProbability-Range "A predicate used for probability statements.  (#$priorProbability-Range PROPOSITION PROBRANGE) means that the a priori probability of the truth of the formula PROPOSITION, in the applicable #$Microtheory, is somewhere in range PROBRANGE (either a real number between zero and one, where zero means certainly false and one means certainly true, or an interval between two such numbers).  In most microtheories, generally, this refers to the range of probability that PROPOSITION, by itself, would be true if there were no further evidence in the #$Microtheory for or against it, nor knowledge of the truth of anything else other than the #$domainAssumptions of the #$Microtheory.  Contrast this with #$derivedProbability and #$priorProbability.  A #$priorProbability-Range may represent an absolute objective probability range, a subjective assigned probability range, a quantum probability range, or an assigned probability range based on some internal characteristic of PROPOSITION (including possibly a statement in it of the occurrence of a number of outcomes within a large number of trials).  This definition makes no presumption as to determinism versus nondeterminism, nor as to whether probability is only in the mind of some beholder.")
(comment PartwiseSymmetricObject "The collection  of things that consist of two
symmetrical parts -- not just any bilaterally symmetric object!")
(comment WorldWideWebPage-AIS "#$WorldWideWebPage-AIS is the collection of instances of #$WebPage-AIS that are #$subInformation of the #$WorldWideWeb-DynamicIndexedInfoSource.")
(comment MurderForHire "The collection of activities in which one agent pays another to #$Murder someone.")
(comment Transformer-Electric "a device that transfers electricity from one circuit to another, usually changing the voltage and amperage")
(comment NonConstrainedRotation "Rotation not constrained by a physical object or surface.  There may be boundaries to the space in which the object is moving, but while the object is not in contact with or affected by them, the motion is non-constrained.")
(comment USStateSenator "The collection of elected officials who serve in state-level senates.")
(disjointWith RemovingSomething RaisingLivingThings)
(comment CedingTerritory "The collection of events in which an agent gives up its claim to some geographical region that it controls.  The ceded territory is surrendered to another agent, who annexes it.  Note that formal cession and annexation need not occur in that temporal order, as there may be a period of dispute (see #$territoryDisputed). The territory ceded is the #$objectOfPossessionTransfer in the event, the ceding agent is the #$fromPossessor, and the annexing agent is the #$toPossessor.  See also #$AnnexingTerritory.")
(comment MovingImage "A collection of visual images.  Each element of #$MovingImage is a visual image which persists while changing over time.  Examples of #$MovingImage include shadows of trees swaying in the wind, meteors, film and video images; images produced by light reflected from moving physical objects; images produced directly by a changing pattern of lights (e.g., nautical beacons).")
(comment StarTrekMovie "This is the collection of all the Star Trek movies.")
(disjointWith Country InternationalOrganizationOfCountries)
(comment Scene-Dramatic "#$Scene-Dramatic is the collection of all major divisions (#$subProcesses) of instances of #$Act-Dramatic which are defined as \"scenes\".  An #$Act-Dramatic may have a single #$Scene-Dramatic which is a #$cotemporalSubEvents.")
(disjointWith SelfPoweredDevice Glider)
(comment Meteor "The collection of all streaks of light formed when #$Meteoroids pass through the atmosphere.")
(comment FlyShaped "#$FlyShaped is the instance of #$ShapeAttribute defined by the typical shape of a fly (insect).")
(comment ModalReasoningLogicMicrotheory "This type of microtheories contains all and only those microtheories in which some particular instances of #$ModalOperator are defined and their modality features are specified.  Note that no instance of this collection should have access to any instance of #$ModalReasoningInferenceMicrotheory.")
(comment IntegerToStringFn "(#$IntegerToStringFn INT) returns the integer INT as a string, i.e., wrapped in double quotes.")
(comment Barbiturate "An addictive family of drugs which are used as sedatives, hypnotics, and anti-spasmodics.")
(comment Genogram "The collection of all #$PropositionalInformationThings consisting of the information contained in a graphic representation of the personalities, genetic conditions and interplay of generations within a family, and used to identify repetitive patterns of behavior  or illness - a medical or psychological #$FamilyTree.")
(comment ElectricalCapacitance "#$ElectricalCapacitance is a physical quantity.  It is an amount of electricity.")
(comment DrunkDriving "The collection of all #$TransportInvolvingADriver events in which the #$driverActor involved in the event is #$LegallyDrunk.")
(comment consumptionAmountDuring "(#$consumptionAmountDuring PT PRODUCT-TYPE THING AMOUNT) means that the #$NonNegativeScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the amount of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE consumed by the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  PT might, for example, be a #$Country, a #$Business, or a household (#$CohabitationUnit).  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  If AMOUNT is a #$Rate, AMOUNT indicates the average rate of consumption of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE by PT during the temporal extent of THING.")
(comment CapsizingEvent "Events in which a container (often a boat) turns over and can no longer support its contents (e.g. people, cargo).  This involves at least a 90 degree turn around the horizontal major axis while remaining floating and in contact with a supporting liquid.  This is an abnormal, normally unintended event.")
(comment GuanineDeoxyribonucleotide "A collection of compounds consisting of a #$Guanine-Base and a phosphate group linked with #$Deoxyribose.  Its abbreviation is G, and it pairs with #$CytosineDeoxyribonucleotide or #$CytosineRibonucleotide, depending on the process.")
(comment Corrosion "This is the collection of events in which something

corrodes. Prime examples would include the action of various acids upon metals

and other substances.")
(comment difference-Propositional "(#$difference-Propositional THING1 THING2 SENT1 SENT2) means that SENT1 describes some important fact about THING1 and SENT2 describes some fact about THING2 and the fact that these sentences hold underscores a salient difference between THING1 and THING2.  See also #$similarity-Propositional and #$differWRTSet.")
(comment RibbonBridge "A Ribbon Bridge is a modular, aluminum alloy, continuous floating bridge system consisting of interior and ramp bays that are transported, launched and retrieved by a transporter/launcher vehicle. Bridge bays, which are carried in a folded position, automatically open upon entering the water to form a 22-foot section of bridge. Under certain raft/bridge designs and slower current velocities the M1 Abrams Tank can cross the Ribbon Bridge.  The Riboon Bridge provides task force lead elements with a dependable bridging capability, which can be emplaced rapidly under all conditions.  It facilitates the forward movement across wet gap barriers of wheeled and tracked vehicles in support of ground combat troops.  The bridge system accompanies armored, mechanized and motorized units and provides wet gap bridging as required.  The bridge bays and ramps are also helicopter tranportable.  (Source: Engineer Systems Handbook, 4/97)")
(comment Router-Network "Electronic devices which direct incoming and outgoing packets to specified IP addresses.")
(comment Rickettsiales-Order "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalOrder in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are mainly bacillus and coccus without flagella.  Biany fission is used by all members of this #$BiologicalOrder.  There are three #$BiologicalFamilys: #$Anaplasmataceae-Family, #$Rickettsiaceae-Family, and #$Bartonellaceae-Family.")
(comment subsumesTemplate "(#$subsumesTemplate PQ-WIDE PQ-NARROW) means that all of the fully specified queries that can be generated by the template PQ-NARROW can also be generated by the template PQ-WIDE, given the same definitions for the classes used with the templates.  Both templates are instances of #$HPKB-CM-PQ-Microtheory.")
(comment SubmarineTender "A collection. Military submarine tender ships.")
(comment Isoleucine "A collection of organic compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.
These compounds are essential for optimal growth in infants as well as
maintaining nitrogen equilibrium in human adults.  Its abbreviations
are Ile and I.")
(comment personTakingTourMightDislikeEvent "(#$personTakingTourMightDislikeEvent TOUR PERSON EVTTYPE) means
that if PERSON were to take TOUR, there is a better-than-even chance
they would dislike an event of type EVTTYPE, which is supposed to be a feature of TOUR.")
(comment IFVMechanizedUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of military units that employ Infantry Fighting Vehicles. (See M2InfantryFightingVehicle.)")
(comment DetachedRetina "An ailment that occurs when the retina pulls away from the back of the eyeball.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn FourthRib) Tuberosity) "")
(comment (VeryHighAmountFn Glamour) "The attribute of being considered very highly glamorous, appealing.  For some, Madonna, for others, Cary Grant.")
(comment CoordinatingStaffMember-USArmy "The collection of instances of  #$MilitaryOfficer that are
members of some #$CoordinatingStaff-USArmy.")
(comment Geisha "A Japanese variety of female #$Escort-EntertainmentProvider. #$Geishas may or may not provide #$SexualGratification. They are expected to be accomplished in the art of #$Conversation, #$Singing  and #$PlayingAMusicalInstrument.")
(comment Arthrogryposis "A collection of #$AilmentConditions in which one has crooked joints.")
(comment TyphusFeverGroup "A specialization of #$BacterialInfection.  The #$TyphusFeverGroup is a group of infections caused by several species of the #$Rickettsia genus.  This collection includes #$EpidemicTyphus-NAmerica as a specialization.")
(disjointWith ChangeInUserRights FluidFlowEvent)
(comment SpringBloomingPlant "A plant which typically flowers in the springtime.")
(comment HorseBellBoot "This is the collection of #$HorseBoots which are  designed to protect the lower                         pastern, coronet band and hoof from overreaching injuries. They are so named because part of the device is bell-shaped.")
(comment ClimateCycleType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$ClimateCycleType is a specialization of #$AnnualClimateCycle (q.v.), and thus is a collection of extended weather events of a certain type.  Instances of #$ClimateCycleType include #$TemperateClimateCycle and #$SteppeClimateCycle.")
(comment DBEntryFn "The result of applying #$DBEntryFn to its arguments is an instance of ARG1, which (usually) can be uniquely identified by the ID string ARG3 which is an ID of type ARG2.  This function is used to produce temporary DB entry objects (Cyc constants) which correspond to entities in database tables.")
(comment CWOfIBTFn "(#$CWOfIBTFn IBT) returns the #$ConceptualWork instantiated in that #$InformationBearingThing.  For example: if IBT is a particular printed copy of Psalm 23, then (#$CWOfIBTFn MyCopyOfPsalm23) refers to the abstract work Psalm 23.")
(comment PuzzleTypeByTangibility "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$Puzzle-Generic whose instances are all of the same tangibility.")
(comment TrajectoryThroughSolid "The collection of all tajectories of motions through solid material.  The trajectory traced by a burrowing animal, or a neutrino trajectory through the Earth, would be examples.  Boring into wood and burrowing through the earth are locomotions whose trajectories may or may not follow designated paths.  For a designated or pre-existing path through a solid, (not just a #$Trajectory of some motion), use #$PathThroughSolid.")
(comment PhysicalDistributionFn "This function can be used to denote the set of events in which objects (tangible or intangible) are distributed.")
(comment AquaticOperationsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all instances of
#$ModernMilitaryUnit-Deployable that are specialized for and capable
of carrying out operations that occur in close proximity to large
bodies of water, inclusive of operations occurring on or in those
bodies.  The default expectation is that an #$AquaticOperationsUnit-MilitarySpecialty will be able to perform #$MilitaryOperations that occur at or near a large body of water.")
(comment ElectroPlating "A collection of events.  In each #$ElectroPlating event, some metal is coated with a thin layer of another metal, with the aid of an electric current.  Some instances of #$Galvanizing will also be instances of this collection.")
(comment SystemicArtery "The collection of all arteries which provide #$OxygenatedBlood from the #$Heart to the body.  This includes every #$Artery except pulmonary arteries (#$PulmonaryArtery-Generic) which carry #$DeoxygenatedBlood.")
(comment LookingForSomething-Indefinite "This is the collection of lookings where the seeker has a

particular #$PossibleIdentificationCondition but does not believe that

exactly one thing satisfies it. It is not required that the seeker believe

that more than one thing satisfies it, although this will often be the

case. The agent might have consciously in mind one or more descriptions of

the sort of thing s/he is seeking or, if not, could at least be prompted to

produce such descriptions.  Some of these descriptions will express

properties the seeker would take to be criterial of success in the sense

that s/he could not conceive of a case in which both (i) s/he successfully

finds an object of that type and (ii) the object s/he finds lacks any of

those properties. The conjunction of these criterial properties will

correspond to the instance of #$PossibleIdentificationCondition that is

associated with the search (see #$searchCriterion-Indefinite). There are two

rather different varieties of this sort of looking. In the first sort, the

seeker is after just one thing and any thing that satisfies the

identification condition will minimally suffice. In the second sort, the

seeker is looking for multiple instances of some type of thing. See

#$LookingForSomething-IndefiniteSingle and

#$LookingForSomething-IndefiniteMultiple.")
(comment FivePrimeEndFn "(#$FivePrimeEndFn CHAIN) denotes the 5' end of the nucleotide chain, CHAIN.")
(disjointWith Sea Gulf)
(comment ContainerShapedObject "The collection of #$CavityOrContainers which have a distinct or clearly defined outside surface (see #$ClearlyDefinedEntireExternalSurface).  Unlike instances of the more specialized collection #$Container, instances of #$ContainerShapedObject do not necessarily contain things as their main function.  Examples of #$ContainerShapedObject include the cap of an #$Acorn, the flower of a #$Tulip-Plant, a #$RadioTelescope dish, or a table tennis ball. Negative examples include a #$Cave.  Although a cave is a #$CavityOrContainer it does not have clearly defined outside walls. However, the existence of clearly defined *inside* walls entails that any #$Cave is a #$CavityWithWalls (q.v.).")
(comment Magnification-Process "The collection of all instances in which the image of something is

magnified.")
(comment BuccalAdministration "Introducing something into the body by placing it in the mouth (without swallowing).")
(disjointWith StateGovernmentAgency USFederalGovernmentAgency)
(comment Dobra-SaoTomeAndPrincipe "Major unit of currency of SaoTome&Principe")
(comment ApplicationProtocolDataUnit "#$ApplicationProtocolDataUnit the collection of discrete blocks of

data that are composed by instances #$ApplicationLayerProtocol and passed

down to a #$PresentationLayerProtocol, #$SessionLayerProtocol, or 

#$TransportLayerProtocol. APDUs contain data generated by 

an application.")
(comment objectRetained "(#$objectRetained SIT OBJ) means that in SIT, user rights to OBJ are retained (by some agent).  See also #$agentRetaining and #$RetainingUserRights")
(comment MilletPlant "Individual millet plants. ")
(comment postalCodeOfAddress-NC "The predicate #$postalCodeOfAddress-NC maps a particular element of #$ContactLocation to a non-canonical #$PostalCode. The `NC' in the name stands for `non-canonical'.   (#$postalCodeOfAddress-NC LOCATION CODE) means that the #$ContactLocation LOCATION has the non-canonicalized #$PostalCode, CODE.  For example, one value  for #$postalCodeOfAddress-NC of the #$Cycorp #$MailingLocation is `78731'. Note that this postal code as printed does not conform to the US Postal Service's recommended standard for printed ZIP codes, and so relative to this standard it is not `canonical.' Non-canonical means that  CODE may not conform to the canonicalization scheme(s) used for other known postal codes for LOCATION.  These other (presumed canonical) postal codes should be related to LOCATION using the predicate #$postalCodeOfAddress. It really only makes sense to use #$postalCodeOfAddress-NC in contexts (such as the #$LogicalTableSchemas for certain database tables) where LOCATION may have both canonical and non-canonical postal codes entered for it.  In contexts where the differences between canonicalized and non-canonicalized postal codes is not an issue, just use #$postalCodeOfAddress.  See also #$ContactLocation.")
(comment ChlamydiaTrachomatisInfection "The #$SexuallyTransmittedInfection caused by the bacterium #$ChlamydiaTrachomatisBacterium.")
(comment Ribosome "#$Ribosome is the collection of small spherical organelles located in cells which serve as the site for protein synthesis.")
(comment AntiPersonnelMine "The collection of #$LandMines that are intended to work on #$ArmyPersonnel as opposed to #$Tank-Vehicles or other vehicles.")
(disjointWith MicrotheoryType HumanCapabilityType)
(comment Horoscope-Daily "The collection of #$Horoscope-AdviceOrPrediction instances which are intended to cover the time period of one day. ")
(comment tourTransitsTo "(#$tourTransitsTo TOUR MOVETYPE TO) means that,
according to its itinerary, TOUR is supposed to include a movement of
type MOVETYPE to the #$PartiallyTangible TO, considered as
#$toLocation.")
(disjointWith HalfBath FullBath)
(disjointWith DecontaminationProcedure-Area DecontaminationProcedure-Personnel)
(comment lastEruptionDate "year of latest eruption")
(comment SewingNeedle-Machine "The collection of #$Needles used in instances of #$SewingWithASewingMachine.           Unlike instances of #$SewingNeedle used in instances of #$SewingByHand (see           #$SewingNeedle-Hand) instances of #$SewingNeedle-Machine often have the point           of the needle very near the 'eye'")
(comment onPath-Alongside "This predicate relates customary paths such as 

roads and trails to things that are alongside them,

like buildings, towns, parks, and trees.  

(#$onPath-Alongside THING PATH) means that THING is located

right beside a portion of PATH (see #$alongsidePathSegment).

THING need not be touching PATH, but must be #$near PATH.

Thus a house set very far back from the street might fail to

be alongside it, while the lot on which the house sits _is_ 

alongside the street.  There should be no other object of the 

same type as THING, nor any object as large or larger than

THING, standing between THING and PATH.  THING might be on 

both sides of PATH at once (e.g. a road going through a park), 

and might even spatially contain a portion of PATH; but PATH 

must not terminate strictly inside of THING (e.g. the path 

must begin and end at least at the park's edges, if not 

outside them).")
(disjointWith ManipulatingFoodOrDrink MusicalPerformance)
(comment programUsedInElectronicAttack "A binary predicate that relates an instance of #$AttackByComputerOperation to an instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  (#$programUsedInElectronicAttack ATTACK PROGRAM) means that PROGRAM is used to execute ATTACK.  Compare this predicate to #$programCopyUsedInElectronicAttack.")
(comment Tu-22-Bomber "A type of bomber plane owned by Iraq.")
(comment Yttrium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of yttrium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.  This unit could probably just as well be called Yttrium or YttriumStuff")
(comment (GaseousFn Phosgene) "A colorless, highly poisonous gas.")
(comment LexicalStructureSchema "All HPSG lexical rules are reified as concepts, and represented as instances of #$LexicalStructureSchema.")
(comment FirstMortgage "The collection of #$MortgageAgreements which hold priority over the claims against the same property by any subsequent lender.  Such a mortgage engenders a #$Lien on the property that is less risky for the #$creditor, and therefore usually carries a lower #$interestRate.")
(comment compositionScoredForPerformerType "(#$compositionScoredForPerformerType COMP TYPE) means that the #$MusicalComposition COMP is scored for soloists or ensembles of type TYPE.")
(comment mtOfBeliefSystem "(#$mtOfBeliefSystem BELIEF-SYSTEM-MT BELIEF-SYSTEM) means that the propositions which make up BELIEF-SYSTEM are contained in BELIEF-SYSTEM-MT.  See also #$MtOfBeliefSystemFn.")
(comment retainTerm "(#$retainTerm TERM) states that TERM should remain defined in the system, even if it would otherwise appear that TERM could be

removed from the system. This is most useful when applied to

NATs, since NATs are functionally defined and added to the

system whenever they are used in some assertion. If the

assertions motivating the addition of the NAT are later removed

from the KB, there is no longer any a priori reason to retain the

NAT in the system. This predicate provides the means to state

the expectation that such a NAT should stay defined, even in

such cases.  When manually asserting, cyclists are encouraged to use #$retainTermBecause.")
(disjointWith MatterTypeByPhysicalState BeliefSystemType)
(comment ArmoredRecoveryVehicle "A type of armored vehicle which is capable of towing other large military vehicles.")
(comment ShallowPersonality "People with a #$ShallowPersonality are generally concerned only with the surface of things, and not with any deeper meaning or implications.  People with #$ShallowPersonalitys can frequently be identified by the fact that they are very interested in appearances, and are rather less interested in the actual characteristics of the object behind the appearance.")
(comment StringGrammar "The collection of all #$FormalGrammar-CWs (conceptual works) that specify sets of 'grammatically valid' #$CharacterStrings.  Most #$FormalGrammar-CWs are #$StringGrammars, but there are also #$GraphGrammars and other kinds.  Often a candidate #$CharacterString is tested against a #$StringGrammar with a computer program that parses the string into its constituent substructures. #$StringGrammars have been used to specify #$ComputerLanguages and to describe #$NaturalLanguages.")
(disjointWith SeparationEvent ConflictEvent)
(comment EconomicCoordination "The collection of events where one state participates in a common market or coordinates it's economy with other states.  Examples would be Germany participating in the EC and maybe even Quebec participating in Federal Canadian economic policies.")
(comment SalmonellaTyphimurium "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom.
This is the common cause of #$Salmonellosis.")
(disjointWith ShootingAProjectileWeapon MakingAPlan)
(comment CharacterType "A collection of collections.  A character type is a   collection of concrete character tokens (regardless of their    physical form: written, spoken, or whatever) that all represent    the same abstract character.  That is, each instance of    #$CharacterType is the collection of all the character tokens    that #$tokensCharacter some particular abstract character.     Examples include the collection of all tokens of the Arabic    numeral '1' and the collection of all tokens of the uppercase    Roman letter 'W'.  For more specialized collections that    correspond to particular physical forms, see #$CharacterMode   and its specializations.  Note that although instances of    #$CharacterType group character tokens according what abstract    characters they represent, character types are not to be    confused with the abstract characters themselves; see #$typeForCharacter.")
(comment Cephalosporin "A widely-used type of #$Antibiotic. Doctors use cephalosporins to treat a variety of bacterial infections, including respiratory system, urinary, bloodstream, and skin infections. Cephalosporins are also usefule for preventing infections following surgical procedures.  Cephalosporins are chemically similar to #$Penicillins, but cephalosporins fight more kinds of bacteria than penicillins.")
(comment Sewage "The collection of all #$Sewage, a #$Suspension containing #$Water and usually also #$Urine, #$Feces, #$CleaningSubstances, and any other stuff that is flushed down a toilet or drain.")
(disjointWith WholesaleBuying FillingAPrescription)
(comment Amphetamine "Drugs which are used to reduce the appetite while dieting and/or to treat colds or hay fever.")
(disjointWith Voltage Volume)
(comment AirMobileUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units which are           deployed on land from air vehicles, usually choppers.")
(comment TicketSeller "The collection of persons who give tickets in exchange for  money,i.e at the theatre, the circus, etc. ")
(comment BinarySignal "A collection of elements of DiscreteTimeSignal whose attributes have only one of two values, 0 and 1.")
(comment LiftingOfSanctions "The collection of all events where some pre-established sanction or

set of pre-established sanctions is lifted.  Each #$LiftingOfSanctions

is composed of both the legal edicts requisite to lift the sanction

and actual steps taken in recognition of those edicts, eg, the

resumption of trade.")
(comment CycLOpenFormula "A specialization of both #$CycLOpenExpression and #$CycLFormula (qq.v.).  The collection of compound CycL expressions that contain one or more free variables.")
(comment WebRing "Bidirected, connected path systems with ring structure.  Each system consists of a group of web sites that figure as nodes in the path system, connected by HTML links.  Nodes in a web ring typically have thematic unity of content.")
(comment mostRecentVaccinationFor "This predicate relates a pair consisting of an organism and disease type to the last vaccination event for that ailment.")
(comment AcidRainProcess "The process of acid rain falling.")
(comment Diplomat "A collection of persons; a subset of #$NationalGovernmentEmployee.  Each element of #$Diplomat is a person who officially represents his or her country's government in dealing with another government or an international organization.  The collection #$Diplomat includes ambassadors, foreign ministers, emissaries, and all others specially charged to represent their country in international dealings.")
(comment inferenceContraindicatedProduct "(#$inferenceContraindicatedProduct PRSN PROD-TYPE) means that it can be inferred that #$ProductType PROD-TYPE is not indicated as a purchase for the #$Person PRSN. The inference might make use of general rules relating recipients to #$ProductTypes and specific information about a particular recipient. General rules which conclude that PROD-TYPE is contraindicated for PRSN should use #$inferenceContraindicatedProduct in the consequent.")
(comment OrthopedicSurgeon-Reconstructive "The collection of all #$OrthopedicSurgeons who specialize in the reconstructive surgical treatment of the #$Hip, #$Knee, #$Ankle, foot (#$Foot-AnimalBodyPart), #$Shoulder, and #$Elbow.")
(comment BackboneNetwork "The collection of #$ComputerNetworks that connect instances of #$ComputerNetwork")
(comment suspendedPart "The predicate #$suspendedPart indicates an instance of #$Particle which is suspended in a particular instance of #$Suspension.  Thus, (#$suspendedPart SUS PART) means that PART is a #$Particle suspended in the #$suspendingFluid of the #$Suspension SUS.  Examples: in an instance of #$CloudOfH2O, the (typical) #$suspendedPart is a #$Particle of water; in muddy water, the (typical) #$suspendedPart is a #$Particle of soil.")
(disjointWith ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheory-SingleDateSeries ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheory-MixedDateSeries)
(comment BacterialInfection "An instance of #$InfectionTypeByPathogenType, and a specialization of #$Infection.  Each instance of #$BacterialInfection is an infection caused by bacteria (see the constant #$Bacterium).  Notable specializations of #$BacterialInfection include #$AnthraxInfection, #$Diphtheria, #$Acne, and #$Leprosy.")
(comment scientificName "Assertions using #$scientificName should be placed in a #$LexicalMicrotheory.  #$AnimalClassificationLexicalMt should be used for animals, #$PlantClassificationLexicalMt should be used for plants, #$OrganismClassificationLexicalMt should be used for other organisms (such as bacteria, viruses, etc.), #$AnimalAnatomyLexicalMt for English names for animal body parts, and #$Anatomy-LatinNameLexicalMt for Latin names of body parts. ")
(comment Lacerating "The process of cutting or tearing something roughly and/or deeply.  Not good to do to skin.")
(comment mtRelevantPhenomena "(#$mtRelevantPhenomena MT TERM) means that when reasoning in (or with) the context MT, the phenomenon indicated by TERM (or instances of TERM, if TERM is a #$Collection) should be attened to, or taken into account.")
(disjointWith OpeningAContainerArtifact TransportationEvent)
(disjointWith Bomb-RoadVehicleDelivered ConventionalWeapon)
(comment StarCluster "A #$StarCluster is a grouping of stars smaller than

a #$Galaxy but still gathered together into a group by their collective

gravity.")
(comment authenticationDeviceTypeFor "(#$authenticationDeviceTypeFor DEVICE_TYPE INDIVIDUAL) means that,            in order to access the instance of #$Individual INDIVIDUAL, one must            use an instance of DEVICE_TYPE, where DEVICE_TYPE is a subset of            #$AuthenticationDevice.")
(comment Sucralfate "The chemical compound which is used to treat peptic acid problems.")
(comment SubmittingSomething "This collection includes events where an agent submits something (often for the purpose of some type of evaluation) to another agent. Common examples of SubmittingSomething include students handing in term papers, writers submitting materials for publication, patients turning in urine samples to a lab for tests.")
(comment MediumPressure "Pressure in an amount that is noticeable but not painful on most parts of the human body; e.g., weight of a daypack or a heavy winter coat.")
(comment DateInSituationFn "Similar to #$DayFn, #$MonthFn, etc., #$DateInSituationFn returns the specified day or month or year, etc., of some event or temporal situation.  In contrast to #$DayFn et al., #$DateInSituationFn is ternary; its first argument specifies the type of calendar interval (day, month, etc.) being denoted.  Thus, (#$DateInSituationFn DATE-TYPE N SIT) returns the Nth DATE-TYPE of the temporal situation SIT.  E.g., to refer to the 24th day of the Iranian hostage crisis, we can use (#$DateInSituationFn #$CalendarDay 24 #$IranHostageCrisis).")
(comment S-TheLetter "The letter S of the alphabet.  This is 'S' (or 's') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.  As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterS and #$LatinSmallLetterS.")
(comment Lempira-Honduras "The unit of currency for Honduras-AtPresent.")
(disjointWith ResearchProject UniversityEntryTest)
(comment mediatesChemicalBonding "(#$mediatesChemicalBonding BONDING OBJ) means that OBJ mediates

the forming of a chemical bond during the #$ChemicalBonding BONDING. Note

that OBJ can be an instance of #$ChemicalObject as well as an Electron, for

this latter case see #$CovalentLinking.")
(comment AsexualReproductionEvent "A collection of events.  In each element of #$AsexualReproductionEvent, an organism produces offspring via asexual means.  E.g., mitotic division by instances of #$SingleCellOrganism; and budding, root-sprouting, etc., for (various) instances of #$Plant).")
(comment interArgIsa4-5 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  
(#$interArgIsa4-5 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, 
when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the fourth argument to RELN, 
a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the fifth argument 
must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is
an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then 
(RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 INST ARG5 ... ARGN) is semantically 
well-formed only if ARG5 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation 
of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct 
specializations.")
(comment GroundStamids "An instance of #$GroundStamids is a vehicle-mounted mine detection and marking system for use both on and off road.  It detects metallic and non-metallic mines, through use of multiple sensors, with a standoff capability to prevent mine detonation under the vehicle.  Possible detection sensors are metal detectors and ground penetrating radar.  Teleoperation, or semi-autonomous operation techniques, using the Army Standard Teleoperation System, will be used to provide increased soldier safety.  Mine detection, data processing and display, and mine marking are autonomous.  Mine information is displayed to the system operator, and the operator will disseminate this information through the appropriate channels.  A #$GroundStamids may be used for route clearance missions, leading convoys, detecting the leading edges of minefields, or reconnaissance missions by Engineers, Cavalry, scouts, Military Police, etc. (Source: Engineer Systems Handbook, 4/97)")
(comment flushSurfaces "(#$flushSurfaces ?SURF1 ?SURF2) means that ?SURF1 and ?SURF2 are in contact at all points of ?SURF1 and ?SURF2. Thus they have the same surface area.")
(comment HelpDeskOperator "The collection of all persons whose job it is to help others, via telephone or email, from desks or workstations at which they have access to a computerized information system set up to assist with helping their customers.  The persons helped may  include in-house persons needing help, in addition to outside customers.  Many #$HelpDeskOperators use Help Desk software or scripts, and they may use Knowledge Management tools.")
(comment Rim-Topographical "The uppermost edge of a deep topographical depression, such as the rim of a #$Crater, #$Canyon, #$Volcano, etc.")
(comment WaterPlatform-Surface "The collection of military water platforms meant to travel on the surface of a body of water.")
(comment PlanBackgroundContext-General "Instances are contexts used for reasoning about #$Plans. More specifically, #$PlanBackgroundContexts are used to store high-level information about resources, constraints, commitments, initial state and purpose that are applicable to a certain class or type of #$Plan, such as military COAs (see #$COASpecificationMicrotheory).  All #$Plans of the class in question will be established as specializations of the appropriate #$PlanBackgroundContext, so that they inherit these assumptions.")
(comment Goiter "Having an enlarged thyroid gland because of an iodine deficiency.")
(comment ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-ClassifiedUS "The collection of 

#$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Information where the

primary purpose of the attack is the acquisition of information having the 

attribute #$Classification-US.")
(comment TransportationEventByVehicleType "An instance of #$CollectionType which is a generic faceting

of #$TransportationEvent.  Each instance is a collection of

translation processes characterized by a single type of

vehicular #$transporter: #$Automobile, #$Train-TransportationDevice, #$Ship,

etc..  For reifying collections that are instances of this collection,

see #$TravelingByMeansOfFn.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-Vandalism "#$AttackByComputerOperation-Vandalism is a subset of #$Vandalism in which each the vandalism occurs through electronic means and damages, say, an instance of #$ComputerFileCopy or #$WorldWideWebSite.")
(comment RetailCashier "The collection of persons who ring up a customer's purchases on a cash register and receive payment for them, in a retail enterprise. A spec of cashier.")
(comment IslamicGift "An instance of #$GiftTypeByReligion.  The collection of all #$Gifts that are somehow associated with #$Islam.")
(comment AntiMineExplosives "The collection of explosive devices used to intentionally set off mines.")
(comment translationOfCWToISIn "(#$translationOfCWToISIn PCW TEXT LANGUAGE) means that TEXT is a translated text of the #$PropositionalConceptualWork, PCW, into LANGUAGE from the language of its original #$AbstractInformationStructure.")
(comment tourVisits "(#$tourVisits TOUR PLACE) means that PLACE is considered a 'stop' on the itinerary of TOUR.  PLACE may either be a #$GeographicalRegion or an #$Artifact of one sort or another, like the #$LouvrePalace.  See also #$tourDestinations.")
(comment CollectionIntersectionFn "(#$CollectionIntersectionFn SET-OF-COLS) is the collection that is by definition the \"collection-intersection\" (see #$collectionIntersection) of all of the collections that are elements of the set SET-OF-COLS.")
(comment Astatine "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of Astatine in stuffeous form. -- sorry, I couldn't resist leaving the copy of gaseous to stuffeous.")
(comment USMarineBattalion "#$USMarineBattalion is the collection of all battalions within the #$UnitedStatesMarineCorps.  It consists of four or more companies and has a Lieutenant Colonel in command.")
(comment WindProcess "A specialization of both #$ImmediateWeatherProcess and #$FluidFlow-Translation.  Each instance of #$WindProcess is an event in which the ambient air (or some significant part of the ambient air) at a #$GeographicalRegion is in motion.")
(comment relatedHobbyActivity "(#$relatedHobbyActivity THING ACT) means that the instance of #$ScriptType ACT is significantly related as a hobby activity to the instance of #$Thing THING. For example, (#$relatedHobbyActivity#$PostageStamp (#$CollectingFn #$PostageStamp)) means that the activity of collecting #$PostageStamps is significantly related as a hobby activity to #$PostageStamps. What counts as significantly related? Suppose someone reasonably answers the query, 'What is one of your hobbies?' by supplying the concept THING. Then the concept THING stands for one or more hobby activities that involve THING. These activities are the ones that are #$relatedHobbyActivitys to THING.")
(disjointWith DecompositionProcess Studying)
(disjointWith PersianGulfCountry LevantCountry)
(comment SemelfactiveTypeFn "Whenever SLOT is an instance of #$ActorSlot, (#$SemelfactiveTypeFn SLOT) denotes the collection of all event types that are semelfactive with respect to SLOT, i.e., can be instantiated only once with a given individual playing the role SLOT in the event. Positive example: #$Dying is an element of (#$SemelfactiveTypeFn #$bodilyDoer), since the formula (#$and (#$isa ?X #$Dying) (#$bodilyDoer ?X ?P)) cannot be satisfied more than once over time, once ?P is fixed. Negative example: #$BirthEvent is not an element of (#$SemelfactiveTypeFn #$birthParent) -- though of course it *is* an element of (#$SemelfactiveTypeFn #$birthChild). Observe that we have to define `semelfactive' in this somewhat counterintuive way because in the Davidsonian conception of events adopted in Cyc events are particular occurrences -- and all event *particulars*  can happen at most once!  My particular pressing of the SpaceBar key now cannot happen again: any later such pressing would be another event, not *this* one. Consequently, we can't simply define semelfactive event types as those the instances of which can happen only once, since *all* event types in Cyc would have that property. In Cyc, the following 2 claims are equivalent: (i) the formula (#$isa ?X #$Dying) is satisfied only once (over time), (ii) the formula (#$isa ?X #$Dying) is satisfied by only 1 object.")
(comment SmokeEmission "the emission of smoke, e.g., during combustion")
(comment PoliticalCartoon "A type of #$Cartoon used to make an often-satirical statement about current political events.  Political cartoons usually emphasize characature and appear on opinion pages of newspapers.")
(comment ClostridiumPerfringens "A #$BiologicalAgent, which can cause gangrene")
(comment unixFilePermissions "#$unixFilePermissions describes important security features of a file. (#$unixFilePermissions FILE ACCOUNT VALUE) means that a permission of file FILE for user account ACCOUNT is permission value VALUE.")
(comment Oxytocin "A #$Hormone secreted by the pituitary gland which stimulates uterine contractions. Pitocin is the trade name of a common commercial #$Oxytocin compound.")
(comment DenseAsStyrofoam "dense as styrofoam - not very dense at all")
(comment deviceTypeManipulates "(#$deviceTypeManipulates USER-DEV INPUT-DEV) means that instances of USER-DEV are designed to 'operate on' or manipulate instances of INPUT-DEV.  INPUT-DEVs are separate devices, not physical or functional components of USER-DEVs.  The manipulation (mechanical or electrical) of INPUT-DEVs is central to the operation of USER-DEVs. INPUT-DEVs are typically inserted into USER-DEVs.  Examples of the #$deviceTypeManipulates relationship include staplers and staples, guns and bullets, and media playing/recording devices and their media (e.g., CD players and CDs).  Note that INPUT-DEV must itself be a device of some sort -- cooking containers do not operate on food, or garden hoses on water, in this sense.  Also, devices and their remote-controllers are not examples.")
(comment (RightObjectOfPairFn (PartTypeFn SixthThoracicVertebra VertebralTransverseProcess)) "")
(comment militaryAttache-OrganizationalRole "(#$militaryAttache-OrganizationalRole ORG PERSON) means that

PERSON who has been 'attached' to the non-military #$Organization ORG.

Ordinarily, PERSON is a member of the armed forces of the

#$GeopoliticalEntity to whose government ORG is subordinated.  Responsibilities for military attaches vary with the organization to which they are subordinated, but may include providing security personal protection for members of the organization's staff, and various liason activities.")
(comment SystemOverload "This is the collection of all events in which a computer system suffers some
    kind of malfunction due to an excessive burden placed on its computing resources.")
(comment MaintenanceVehicle "The collection of vehicles intended for use in the maintenance of other objects.")
(comment omitFromProjectBroadsword "This predicate serves to exempt individual assertions or FORT's from inclusion in #$ProjectBroadsword releases.  One should only use this predicate in cases where the assertion in question would have been included by default.")
(comment CombatShotgun "The collection of #$Shotguns that have been designed for military  use.  They are used as a close-range assault weapon.")
(disjointWith Voltage IntervalOnNumberLine)
(comment ExampleInstanceFn "(#$ExampleInstanceFn COL PRED N) returns the NAT that is the
Nth instance of COL to be used in an example assertion involving PRED
and linked to PRED by #$examplePredSentences.  One of the constraints on
the use of the function is that the example assertion NOT be 
asserted in the KB, something which can be taken for granted if examples 
have to be reified for the example assertion.")
(comment TakingATest "The collection of actions in which someone submits to some sort of #$Evaluating such as an instance of #$MedicalTesting, of #$PsychologicalTesting, or of #$AcademicTesting.  If #$TakingATest is #$performedBy someone successfully, then they are said to have 'passed the test'.  This collection excludes tests taken by non-human animals.")
(comment SubLCharacter "The collection of all character-denoting terms in the CycL language that are #$SubLAtomicTerms (q.v.). (SubL, which subsumes CycL, is the underlying implementation language of the Cyc system.)  A given #$SubLCharacter CHAR-TERM is itself a string consisting of the hash-symbol (`#'), followed by the backslash (`\\'), followed (in most cases) by the character CHAR that CHAR-TERM denotes.  For example, the SubLCharacter `#\\A'

denotes the character `A'.  (An exception to the above is when CHAR is a non-printing or control character, in which case a specially-designated string

appears after the `#\\'.)")
(comment ComedyTeam "#$ComedyTeam is a collection of groups of #$Comedian(s). Each group is such that its members perform together regularly. Examples of instances of #$ComedyTeam include The Marx Brothers, Laurel and Hardy, Abbott and Costello, and Martin and Lewis.")
(comment weaponEffectiveRange "(#$weaponEffectiveRange WEAPON DISTANCE) means that #$Distance-Absolute DISTANCE is the effective range of #$ProjectileWeapon WEAPON. Thus DISTANCE is the range within which, other things being equal, if one aims at a target with WEAPON, one will be likely to hit the target.  Unlike #$weaponRange that gives values for the maximum distance, #$weaponEffectiveRange is a minimum and a maximum. Depending on the type of weapon this may be the minimum and maximum height at which a flying #$AirTransportationDevice can be effectively hit by a #$SurfaceToAirMissile. ")
(disjointWith CoilTightening CoilLoosening)
(comment USStateSecretaryOfState "The secretary of State is an appointed or elected official whose chief responsibilities include the processing and filing of public records including election records.")
(disjointWith RaisingLivingThings MedicalCareEvent)
(comment translationOfCWToAIS "(#$translationOfCWToAIS PCW TEXT) means that TEXT isa a translation of the #$PropositionalConceptualWork, PCW, into a language other than the original.")
(comment genMassNoun "(#$genMassNoun TERM) means that the #$CycLReifiableDenotationalTerm TERM should be treated as a mass noun when CycL formulae containing TERM are paraphrased into English.  See also the related predicate #$prettyName.")
(comment Reflection-Visual "A collection of visual images.  Each element of #$Reflection-Visual is a visual image produced by the reflection of light from a surface.")
(comment SupermanMovie "This is the collection of all the movies featuring

the character #$Superman.")
(comment keFarthestGenlsWeakSuggestionPreds "(#$keFarthestGenlsWeakSuggestionPreds COL BIN-PRED) means that for

every specialization SPEC-COL of COL such that SPEC-COL is not known to have any specializations other than itself, it is weakly suggested that

there exist some VALUE such that (BIN-PRED SPEC-COL VALUE) is known in

the KB.")
(comment holdsInTypeOfTime-Sometime "(#$holdsInTypeOfTime-Sometime MT TYPE) means that the assertions in MT are true sometime during the temporal extent of instances of TYPE.  See also #$holdsInTypeOfTime-Always.")
(disjointWith IndependentCountry CountrySubsidiary)
(disjointWith MechanicalDevice Parachute)
(comment Meteoroid "The collection of all meteoroids.  An instance of this collection is a rock (#$StoneObject-Natural) smaller than an #$Asteroid which is orbiting the #$Sun.")
(disjointWith ModalReasoningInferenceMicrotheory ModalReasoningLogicMicrotheory)
(comment Diuretic "Drugs which promote the loss of water and salt from the body. They typically lower blood pressure, too.")
(comment about-UnderspecifiedRegion "(#$about-UnderspecifiedRegion ACT REGION) states that an
abstract locational relation holds between ACT and REGION, where
REGION is a #$Region-Underspecified selectively 'traversed' during ACT.
#$about-UnderspecifiedRegion is an underspecified semantic representation
that may be elaborated to represent either a spatial example of
'go around' (as in 'pacing about the house')
or a metaphorical use ('Smith went about his business all morning.').
#$about-UnderspecifiedRegion differs from #$around-UnderspecifiedRegion inasmuch
as the latter suggests the center of the region was not traversed, while
the former suggests some kind of selective routing.")
(comment EgyptianSphinx "A mythical beast of #$AncientEgypt, symbolizing the #$Pharaoh-HeadOfState as an incarnation of the sun god Ra. An #$EgyptianSphinx has the head of a man, ram, or #$Hawk and the body of a lion. Cf. #$GreatSphinxOfGiza for the famous statue.")
(comment DegreeCelsius "The standard unit of temperature in much of the world and also in CYC.")
(comment consumptionCapacityDuring "(#$consumptionCapacityDuring PT PRODUCT-TYPE THING AMOUNT) means that the #$NonNegativeScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the greatest possible amount of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE that could be consumed by the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  PT might, for example, be a #$Country, a #$Business, or a household (#$CohabitationUnit).  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  If AMOUNT is a #$Rate, AMOUNT indicates what would be the average rate of consumption of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE by PT during the temporal extent of THING if PT were consuming PRODUCT-TYPE at the limit of its capacity.")
(comment GuanineRibonucleotide "A collection of compounds consisting of a #$Guanine-Base and

a phosphate group linked to #$Ribose.  Its abbreviation is G, and it

pairs with #$CytosineRibonucleotide or #$CytosineDeoxyribonucleotide,

depending on the process.")
(comment UnaffiliatedCollegeSportsTeam "This is the collection of college sports teams that have no conference affiliation.  A famous example of this is the Notre Dame football team, which remains unaffiliated, despite the school's membership in the Big East.")
(comment StrapOnDildo "#$Dildoes can be used in many different ways. Sometimes they are fitted into a #$Harness which is then strapped around the loins, so as not to require the use of hands. A #$StrapOnDildo is an object made of two components: the first one could often be used as a #$Dildo by itself used to keep the #$Dildo in place.")
(comment ImprovedRibbonBridge "The collection of bridges that will be employed in the same general manner as the standard Ribbon Bridge.  However, it will be able to cross faster water with higher MLCs and with banks that are up to two meters high.  The Improved Ribbon Bridge bays are modified ribbon bays.  The will posses better hydrodynamics, providing the capability of rafting or bridging MLC 70T traffic in currents up to 8 fps.  The bays can be connected in one minute and can be connected to the standard ribbon bays.  The bays will include postive floatation to increase the survivability of the system.  The ramp bays can be hydraulically articulated to two meters.  (Source: Engineer Systems Handbook, 4/97)")
(comment Enclave-Computer "The collection of groups of #$Computers of #$ComputerNetworks which are protected by a single #$FirewallProgram.")
(comment Index-PointerList "Elements of #$Index-PointerList are #$InformationBearingThings structured such that they have two main parts: referents, and lists of pointers.  An #$Index-PointerList may be thought of as list of such referent/pointer pairs.  The first element of each such pair contains a term.  The second element of each such pair contains a list of pointers to locations (not necessary spatial locations) which are related to that term in some way which is characteristic of the given index.  Some examples: At the back of many reference books one will find a Subject Index.  Such a subject index is comprised of a list of referent/pointer list pairs.  The referents are individual subjects. The pointer list associated with each subject is a list of page numbers which mention the subject.  The Cyc KB is full of indexes. For example, the constant #$Dog has an assertion index associated with it.  One of the referents in the index is called ''All GAFs''.  This referent has a list of pointers associated with it.  Each pointer points to a GAF which mentions #$Dog.  A #$Dictionary is an non-example of an index.  Although each word in the dictionary might correspond to a index referent, the items following each such word are not pointers but are definitions.")
(comment UnderwayReplenishmentShip "The collection of ships intended to be used to transport materiel to other ships which are engaged in some kind of operation.")
(comment Phenylalanine "A collection of organic compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.
These compounds are ingested and turned into other compounds for the
body's use.  Its abbreviations are Phe and F.")
(comment NegativeNumber "A specialization of #$RealNumber.  An instance REAL of #$RealNumber is also an instance of #$NegativeNumber just in case REAL is less than 0.")
(comment RangeOfFunctionFn "A #$SetDenotingFunction that associates each function 
(see #$Function-Denotational) to its set-theoretic range 
(see #$relationRange).  (#$RangeOfFunctionFn FUNCTION) 
is the instance of #$Set-Mathematical consisting of all 
and only those things to which FUNCTION maps at least 
one thing (see #$valueOfFunctionForArgs).  For each 
element R of FUNCTION's range, there will be at least 
one element D of FUNCTION's domain (see #$relationDomain 
and #$DomainOfFunctionFn) such that FUNCTION maps D to R 
(and only to R).  See also #$inRangeOf.")
(comment MechanizedAntiArmorUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of military units trained and equipped to fight armored vehicles and typically employing motorized track vehicles.")
(comment CoronaryBlockage "Blockage of blood flow in the #$CoronaryArtery.")
(comment LearnedInfoFn "This function maps a particular event of an agent learning some information to the information that the agent learns.  The result of the function is the set of information learned; in the case where a single fact is learned, this set will be a singleton.")
(comment (LowAmountFn Glamour) "The attribute of being undistinguished in style, glamor, allure.")
(comment BeefcakeModel "The collection of attractive #$MalePersons working as a #$Photographer's model.")
(comment RadioTalkShow "A collection of radio shows [#$RadioShow-CW], ones normally refered to as talk shows, e.g. 'Car Talk' [#$CarTalk-RadioSeries].")
(comment CellPart "The collection of structures which are typically found and formed as parts of #$Cells. This covers components of both #$EukaryoticCells and #$ProkaryoticCells.  It includes organelles, vesicles, cell walls, extracellular matrix, plasma membranes, receptors, cellular humours, microtubules, etc.")
(disjointWith Landing PhysicalTransformationEvent)
(comment PresidentialCandidate "A person running for the office of president")
(comment Binding-Device "This is the collection of bindings of the sort that are used to

bind one thing to another. Examples include the bindings used on

skis and snowboards. Something wrapped around a pipe to keep it

from breaking, though sometimes called a binding, would not be

a binding in this sense.")
(comment MaterialSupportUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units specialized for           providing material support to other military units.")
(comment CommutingFunctionSet "If (#$isa SET #$CommutingFunctionSet) then any #$UnaryFunction in SET commutes with any other in SET.")
(comment SeparationFromTypeFn "(#$SeparationFromTypeFn COL1 COL2) is the collection of instances of #$SeparationEvent in which instances of COL1 are separated from instances of COL2.")
(disjointWith SeparationEvent AnnualClimateCycle)
(comment cityPhoneCode "ARG2 is a city telephone code number (analogous to #$AreaCode in the US) for the city ARG1. A city may have more than one city telephone code number.")
(comment SurfaceWarfareUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all instances of #$ModernMilitaryUnit-Deployable which are trained and specialized for combat on and near the surface of the ocean.  The default expectation is that a #$SurfaceWarfareUnit-MilitarySpecialty will be able to perform #$MilitaryOperations that occur at the ocean's surface.")
(comment consumesPortion "(#$consumesPortion EV OBJ) means that a portion of the object OBJ is used up (consumed) in the event EV.  However, enough of OBJ remains at the end of EV for it to maintain its identity.  Thus #$consumesPortion would be appropriate for an apple that has a bite taken out of it in an eating event, but not for an apple that has been eaten to its core, since the latter is no longer an apple.")
(comment ObjectWithUse "A collection of tangible things that have clear intended behavior or purpose. An important subcollection is #$PhysicalDevice that consists of things made or modified for some particular purpose. #$ObjectWithUse, however, is meant to include the members of collections such as #$Horse (and some other subcollections of #$Animal) that are intended for transportation (at least in some contexts). Also, an #$ObjectWithUse need not have a relatively rigid, set shape, so #$GasolineFuel or #$AntiFreeze are subsets of #$ObjectWithUse.")
(comment LookingForSomething-IndefiniteSingle "This is the collection of lookings where the seeker has a particular
#$searchCriterion-Indefinite and does not believe that exactly one thing
satisfies it but the seeker is really after just one such thing, where any
thing satisfying the identification condition will at least minimally suffice.
For example, I might be looking for a screwdriver in the Cycorp offices. I have
no reason to believe that there is exactly one. If I come across two, I might
prefer one over the other, but were I to have only found either one I would
have considered it a success. For more about identification conditions, see
the comment on #$searchCriterion-Indefinite.")
(comment Sediment "Instances of #$Sediment are  mobs of small, solid materials from
the Earth's surface (of either organic or inorganic origin) that have
been transported by water, ice, wind, or gravity.  Examples include
gravel deposits left by streams, rock debris deposited by glaciers, and
windblown dust.  When compacted under high pressure, an instance of
#$Sediment will turn into an instance of #$SedimentaryRock.")
(disjointWith CompositionForSoloInstrument CompositionWithSoloistAndAccompaniment)
(comment (BuyingFn EntertainmentEvent) "A subset of #$BuyingAService. In each instance of #$BuyingEntertainmentEvent, an agent pays money for the right to attend an entertainment event. Examples include buying a ticket for a movie, paying a cover charge for a live musical performance at a night club, and buying a ticket to a football game.")
(comment PartyGift "An instance of #$GiftTypeByOccasion.  The collection of #$Gifts that 

are appropriate to bring to parties.")
(comment BombSubmunition "A military device, usually intended to strike a target or pierce through armor before the main munition is released.")
(comment PPTPackageFn "Uses are collections of drug products of type ARG1 packaged in a package of type ARG3, of size ARG2 when new.  Sizes may be measured as counts, as weights, as volumes, etc.  #$ScalarInterval is actually too broad for the arg2type because it admits many types of quantity that don't make sense for drug package sizes (like Money, Wetness, flow rates, etc.), but it is the least common genl of Integer and Mass, Volume, etc.")
(comment PairOfIdenticalTwins "The collection of pairs of identical twins, i.e., offspring who develop from a single egg that divided in the womb.")
(comment worksFoundInStructure "This predicate relates display objects to the building in which they are displayed or possibly stored.")
(comment IBOCirculationEvent "A collection of #$Events; a subset of #$MediaTransferEvent.  In every instance of #$IBOCirculationEvent, a collection of #$InformationBearingObjects (IBOs) is created and distributed to the public.  An important subset of #$IBOCirculationEvent is #$PrintCirculationEvent, the duplication and distribution of book copies [#$BookCopy], newspaper copies [#$NewspaperCopy], and hardcopy #$TextualMaterial in general. See also #$PublishedMaterial.")
(comment Substandard "An attribute to describe things, actions which are lower than normal in quality.")
(comment Sucre-Ecuador "The unit of currency for Ecuador-AtPresent.")
(comment MovieTypeBySeries "#$MovieTypeBySeries is a collection of collections.  Each element of #$MovieTypeBySeries is a collection of movies that either feature the same character(s), tell a continued story, or in some other way make up a series.  Example instances of this collection are #$JamesBondMovie, #$BatmanMovie, and #$SupermanMovie.")
(comment Frame-Network "#$Frame-Network is the collection of discrete blocks of data composed by a  #$DataLinkLayerProtocol and passed down to a #$PhysicalLayerProtocol.  An instance of #$Frame-Network consist of a header created and attached by a #$DataLinkLayerProtocol and an instance of #$Packet-Network received from a #$NetworkLayerProtocol.")
(comment transportThroughAmountDuring "(#$transportThroughAmountDuring PT1 COL PT2 THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the amount of instances of the #$Collection COL transported by the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT1 through the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT2 during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  PT1 might, for example, be a #$Country or a #$Business.  PT2 might, in the case of oil transport, for instance, be a #$GeographicalRegion or a #$Pipeline.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  In the case of oil transport, for example, AMOUNT might be a #$Volume (a number of barrels) indicating the total quantity of oil transported (by PT1 through PT2).  Alternatively, AMOUNT might be a #$Rate, characterizing the average rate of transport of instances of COL by PT1 through PT2 during the temporal extent of THING.  Oil transport, for example, might be expressed in terms of so many million barrels per day.")
(comment PacketSniffer "An object that examines packets of data sent over a network and extracts information from them. Used as a tool by webmasters, may be used in espionage. Generally, instances of #$PacketSniffer are either programs residing on some computer connected to the network, or they physical devices connected to some peice of hardware which is connected to, or part of, the network.")
(comment RicePlant "Individual rice plants.")
(comment LightCavalryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "Collection of lightly armed and armored cavalry units,
useful in rapid deployment. ")
(comment DecompositionProcess "A specialization of both #$SeparationEvent and #$PhysicalTransformationProcess.  Each instance of #$DecompositionProcess is an event in which some object's matter undergoes chemical reactions (sometimes mediated by microorganisms) that result in the object losing its shape and other material characteristics.")
(comment ColdSeason "A specialization of #$SeasonOfYear.  Each instance of #$ColdSeason is the cooler part of an annual climate cycle for a region (see #$AnnualClimateCycle).  If a place has a Winter (see #$WinterSeason), the cold season generally includes the Winter.  Note that #$WinterSeason is _not_ a specialization of #$CalendarSeason (q.v.).")
(comment UserAccount "A person or process with an instance of #$UserAccount is able to access storage space and CPU time on an instance of #$AccountSystem. Instances of #$UserAccount are normally held by typical users of account systems and have relatively low levels of privilege.  For example, on linux users cannot open raw socket connections, users of user accounts cannot sidestep permissions, and usually cannot edit initialization scripts for machines or network configuration files.")
(comment Tinnitus "A sensation of noise arising from a bodily condition, such as excessive earwax or a perforated tympanic membrane. Usually sounds like ringing or roaring.")
(comment IndexicalFirstOrderTerm "An element of #$IndexicalFirstOrderTerm is a term the denotation (referent) of which varies from context to context (or at least might so vary).  In addition, an element of this collection is not a predicate, formula, or function.  However, it may be a non-atomic term, in which case it will not contain free variables.  For example, at any moment during January 1, 1998, the denotation of the constant `#$Tomorrow-Indexical' is January 2, 1998.  [So it's the case that (#$holdsIn (#$DayFn 1 (#$MonthFn #$January (#$YearFn 1998))) (#$equals #$Tomorrow-Indexical (#$DayFn 2 (#$MonthFn #$January (#$YearFn 1998))))).]  But at any moment during January 2, 1998, the denotation of `#$Tomorrow-Indexical' is not January 2, 1998, but January 3, 1998.  As another example, at any moment in 1996, the denotation of `(PresidentFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica)' is #$BillClinton.  But at any moment in 1990, `(PresidentFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica)' denotes #$GeorgeHWBush.")
(comment InformationDissemination "An instance of #$InformationDissemination is an instance of
#$Communicating in which information is disseminated to a group of agents
by means of instances of #$InformationBearingObject.")
(comment CruiseMissile-SubmarineLaunched "A collection of

missiles, a subset of #$CruiseMissile.  Each instance is a cruise

missile designed to be launched from a submarine.")
(comment ProjectMicrotheory "The collection of microtheories related to created for instances of #$Cyc-BasedProject and not intended to be used outside that project.")
(disjointWith BidirectedPathSystem DirectedPathSystem)
(comment Horoscope-Monthly "The collection of #$Horoscope-AdviceOrPrediction instances which are intended to cover the time period of one month. ")
(comment FrenchWord "The collection of all lexical words in French; a subset of #$LexicalWord.            Different inflectional forms of a word do not count as different words.")
(comment KilometersPerHour "(#$KilometersPerHour NUMBER) returns a dimensionless rate or speed of NUMBER kilometers per hour.")
(comment Canoe "#$Canoe is a specialization of #$Watercraft-Small and #$Device-UserPowered.  Each instance of #$Canoe is a small and narrow watercraft powered by human paddling, poling, or by a small boat-engine.")
(comment highestPeakInThisGroup "The highest peak in a given group of mountains")
(comment Emu "The collection of all emus. A very large, flightless bird.")
(comment RifleGrenade "A specialization of #$ProjectileShellAssembly.  Each instance of #$RifleGrenade is a grenade designed to be launched with a #$GrenadeLauncher, as opposed to being thrown by hand.  Cf. #$HandGrenade.")
(disjointWith MusicalPerformance TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment SignStructureSchema "All HPSG sign-creation rules, whether of words or phrases, are reified as concepts, and represented as instances of #$SignStructureSchema.")
(comment FixedRateMortgage "The collection of #$MortgageAgreements which have a fixed #$interestRate for the term of the loan.")
(comment StringQuartetComposition-CW "The collection of all string quartet music compositions -- works usually scored for four solo string instruments, usually two violins, one viola and one cello.")
(comment retainTermBecause "(#$retainTermBecause NAT DOCUMENTED-REASON) means that for reasons specified in the english text DOCUMENTED-REASON the non-atomic term NAT will not be 'forgotten' during 'NAT forgetting KB cleanups'.  Such periodically performed KB cleanups automatically remove ('forget') references to non-atomic terms (NATs) unless a given NAT has something stated about it which is not concluded from its #$termOfUnit.  For example, a NAT which has no local assertions but does have a rule concluding something about it will be 'forgotten' when the cleanup function is run since that rule concluded via a #$termOfUnit literal which satisfied its antecedent.  However, a NAT which has a local assertion or which has (#$retainTermBecause NAT DOCUMENTED-REASON) asserted about it will not be forgotten.  See also #$ephemeralTerm.")
(comment biochemicalSynthesisOfMolecularType "(#$biochemicalSynthesisOfMolecularType BIO-SYNTH MOL-TYPE) means that BIO-SYNTH, a specialization of #$BiochemicalSynthesis, is the collection of

biochemical syntheses of molecules of the type MOL-TYPE. Note that this predicate relates a collection of molecules to a collection of events [See also #$BiochemicalSynthesisFn]. Given the current representation of chemical compounds in Cyc, one may use #$MoleculeFn to specify the appropriate argument when only the corresponding spec of #$MolecularStuff is reified.")
(comment M88ArmoredRecoveryVehicle "A type of armored recovery vehicle.")
(comment mtChangeEventRelativeTime "There exists some instance of Event, E, during which a change is made to the mt ARG1.  The following relationship holds: ARG2(E ARG3).")
(comment GraphGrammar "The collection of all #$FormalGrammar-CWs (conceptual works) that formally specify sets of 'grammatically valid' structures of #$Multigraphs or kinds of #$SimpleGraph-GraphTheoretic.  Often a candidate graph or multigraph is tested against a #$GraphGrammar with a computer program that recursively 'parses' the graph into its constituent substructures.  #$GraphGrammars have been used to specify classes of decorative patterns, physical shapes, networks, semantic networks, and biological growth patterns.  (#$StringGrammars are technically like a special case of #$GraphGrammars in which the described graphs are always directed chains corresponding to lists of characters (#$CharacterStrings)).")
(disjointWith CommunicationAct-Single ConflictEvent)
(comment GrantingTradeStatus "The collection of events where one state grants a positive trade status to another state.")
(comment SalmonellaTyphi "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies responsible for the
#$BacterialInfection #$TyphoidFever.")
(comment BroadcastOfEventFn "#$BroadcastOfEventFn takes as argument any organized, public event and returns the collection of events that are broadcasts (radio or television) of that organized, public event.  For example, (#$BroadcastOfEventFn Trial001) would return the collection of broadcasts of that particular trial.")
(disjointWith Surgery MakingAPlan)
(comment StateUniformMixture "A mixture in which all of the constituents have the same state.  E.g. sand is a mixture of various kinds of particles all of which are in the solid state.")
(comment subGIS "The binary predicate #$subGIS relates an abstract chemical structure to the abstract chemical structures it contains. (#$subGIS GIS SUB-GIS) means that GIS contains SUB-GIS as an intangible part, where both GIS and SUB-GIS are required to be instances of #$GeneticInformationStructure. Note that if (#$subGIS GIS SUB-GIS) holds, then any instance of #$ChemicalGeneticIBT that instantiates the structure GIS also instantiates the structure SUB-GIS. See #$instantiationOfGIS for a related predicate.")
(comment TransportationDevice-Unmanned "The collection of #$TransportationDevices that can operate without a driver (see #$driverActor) actually being in or on the device.  Examples include drone aircraft operated by remote control and #$WeatherBalloons.")
(comment Anorectic "Drugs which suppress the appetite.")
(disjointWith AngularDistance Volume)
(comment AirToAirCommunicationsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units trained and equipped for a           mission profile that centers around some aspect of communication           between air-based platforms.")
(disjointWith CycLRuleAssertion CycLGAFAssertion)
(disjointWith ProductTypeByBrand NaturalResourceType)
(comment AlcoholicBeverageBuyer "Collection of people who purchase alcoholic beverages to be sold at a retail store.")
(comment Translation-RNAToProtein "The process whereby a strand of messenger RNA attaches to a
ribosomal complex that assembles a long-chain polymer of amino acids,
based on the codon instructions stored in the RNA.  The released
polymer undergoes tertiary folding to become a functional protein
molecule, usually some kind of enzyme.")
(comment ContactInformation "The collection of information about how to contact (address, phone, specification of physical location) an agent or place.")
(comment ReincarnationBeliefSystems "The collection of belief systems in which

#$Reincarnation is a belief. These systems contain assertions pertaining to the

basic belief in the past lives of people. Among the beliefs in such systems is the axiom relating every 

person to a reincarnation event (i.e., every person has at least one past life).")
(comment ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheory-SingleDateSeries "This is the sub-collection of

#$ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheory that contains all and only

those that take #$ReasoningWithTense-LogicMt-SingleDateSeries as

#$genlMt.")
(comment AnthraxInfection "An instance of #$InfectionTypeByPathogenType, and a specialization of #$BacterialInfection.  Each instance of #$AnthraxInfection is an infection caused by the bacterium Bacillus anthracis (see the collection #$Anthrax-Bacterium).  Important specializations of #$AnthraxInfection include the collections #$InhalationalAnthrax and #$CutaneousAnthrax.")
(comment State-Australia "A collection of geopolitical sub-regions.  Each of the elements of #$State-Australia is a state in #$Australia, such as #$Victoria-StateAustralia.")
(comment AceticAcid "The colorless liquid acid CH3COOH which is found in vinegar and used in the production of plastics.")
(comment coversPartially "'(#$coversPartially COVER OBJECT)' means that COVER covers part of, but not all of, OBJECT.")
(comment Memorabilia "The collection of #$Artifacts that are 

produced or kept for the purpose of illiciting memories or 

thoughts about some object or event. Typically this object or event

 has importance to many people or to the person possessing the

 memorabilia.")
(comment analogousSituation "(#$analogousSituation ?Microtheory ?Agent ?Role ?Patient ?Description) detetermines the set of situations in ?Microtheory in which ?Agent plays the role ?Role, and in which ?Patient is somehow involved. A CycL description of the situation and involvement is then returned as a binding for ?Description. If more than one answer is available, multiple successive bindings are made to ?Description. If a list of roles, rather than a single role, is used as the value of ?Role, then all member values are considered in turn.")
(comment GoingSomewhereByTransportationDevice "This is the collection of #$GoingSomewhere events in which the performer is transported for the majority of the trip by some #$TransportationDevice.")
(comment Dyne "The #$Dyne is the basic unit of force in the CGS system.  It is the force that gives to a mass of one #$Gram an acceleration of one centimeter per second per second.  It is equal to 10^-5 #$Newtons, the basic unit of force in the MKS system.")
(disjointWith GaseousTangibleThing GranularFluid)
(comment CruiseMissile-GroundLaunched "The collection of #$CruiseMissiles whose instances are launched from either a #$LandPlatform-Towed or a #$LandPlatform-SelfPropelled.")
(comment EllipticalGalaxy "#$EllipticalGalaxy is the collection of all elliptical galaxies.")
(comment authenticationEventFor "(authenticationEventFor AUTH_EVENT INDIVIDUAL) means that, in            order to access the instance of #$Individual INDIVIDUAL, one must            perform  AUTH_EVENT, where AUTH_EVENT is an instance of            #$AuthenticationEvent.")
(comment Butalbital "The chemical compound which is used in anti-migraine drugs.")
(comment DisplayingArtGalleryHoldings "The collection of instances of #$DisplayingArtObject in which the items displayed are #$ArtObjects that are members of some museum's holdings and the display is controlled by an art gallery organization (#$Gallery-ArtDisplayOrganization).")
(comment Refunding "This collection includes events where money is returned to an individual. The amount refunded is generally the same as or less than the amount the individual originally paid.")
(comment LightPressure "Pressure in an amount not uncomfortable or painful to humans when felt on most body parts; e.g., pressure of clothing that fits, of a gentle touch, or of mild winds.")
(comment Hydrocarbon "A compound, or mixture of compounds, composed of only carbon and hydrogen atoms.  These are found in natural gas and crude oil.")
(comment T-TheLetter "The letter T of the alphabet.  This is 'T' (or 't') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.  As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterT and #$LatinSmallLetterT.")
(comment smuggledGoods "The predicate #$smuggledGoods is used to relate a #$Smuggling event to the goods smuggled. Thus (#$smuggledGoods EVENT OBJECT) means that OBJECT plays the role as one of perhaps multiple smuggled items. Since one may smuggle many things at once, there is no constraint on the number of different OBJECTs that can appear with a particular EVENT; similarly, one may smuggle the same goods more than once.  The object smuggled is also a #$primaryObjectMoving and an #$objectControlled in a given #$Smuggling event.  The smuggled goods are presumed to be central to the #$Smuggling event; they proceed from the #$fromLocation to the #$toLocation of the event; and the smuggled goods are controlled throughout the duration of the event.")
(comment Dinar-Jordan "The currency unit for Jordan.")
(comment GraduateRecordExamination "The collection of #$AcademicTesting events that are designed to test the scholastic aptitude of graduate students so they may be admitted to a post-graduate degree course. Also known as GRE testing , GRE test scores are used by universities and a primary selection criterion for new graduate student admittance.")
(comment Pollen "A mass of pollen grains.")
(comment HumanSelfControlStandard "#$HumanSelfControlStandard is a collection of standards having to do with maintaining self control.  Example instances include the standard that one does not trip, that one does not accidentally hit someone, that one maintains bowel control, etc, etc.  Some elements are standards about #$HumanSelfControlStandards.  For example, the standard that one not violate an element of #$HumanSelfControlStandard in public is a standard about standards. To fail to adhere to such a standard would cause #$Embarrassment.")
(comment HolderGripper "A specialization of#$SolidTangibleThing.  Each instance of #$HolderGripper is an object that can apply pressure to another object and thereby grip it in such a way that its motion is restricted.")
(comment InterimVehicleMountedMineDetector "A #$InterimVehicleMountedMineDetector (IVMMD) is used for route clearance missions and to precede convoys.  It is a vehicle-mounted mine detection and marking system for use on-road and is capable of being teleoperated.  It only detects metallic mines.  As a 'non-developmental item' system, it may have a lower probability of detection and higher false alarm rate than the objective #$GroundStamids system.  IVMMD is mounted on blast-resistant vehicles which are field repairable following a mine detonation.  It has low ground-pressure tires and the second detection vehicle tows proofing trailers to detonate mines which are missed by the metal detector sensors.  (Source: Engineer Systems Handbook, 4/97)")
(comment KanisaKnowledgeManagementProgram "The collection of all #$KnowledgeManagementPrograms made by #$KanisaInc.")
(disjointWith DirectFireWeapon IndirectFireWeapon)
(comment PlanContextRestrictionPredicate "A #$PlanContextRestrictionPredicate can be any relation
on a plan, planning problem, context or task that constrains the forms
of refinements of instantiations possible.")
(comment SkolemTerm "#$SkolemTerm is the collection of all CycL symbols introduced by the CycL system via the process of skolemization to denote some indeterminate object in the universe of discourse.  See also #$SkolemFunction and #$IndeterminateTerm.")
(disjointWith Configuration InterAgentSituation)
(comment LinuxOS "A specialization of #$UnixOS and #$OpenSourceComputerProgram. Each instance of #$LinuxOS is an operating system built around #$LinuxKernel-TheProgram (q.v).  Instances (known as \"distributions\") include #$Linux-RedHat, #$Linux-Caldera, #$Linux-YellowDog, etc.  See #$SharedNoteOnOperatingSystemsAndKernels.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-Smurfing "#$AttackByComputerOperation-Smurfing is the collection of electronic attacks in which the attacker sends a large stream of spoofed instances of ping  #$Packet-Internets to a broadcast address (an instance of #$IPAddress that services an instance of #$ComputerNetwork).  The packets have as their source IP address the spoofed address of the victim.  When the broadcast host relays the packets to all of the host computers on its network, the hosts reply to the victim, resulting in a multiplication of the information sent to the victim and, if successful, disabling the victim's machine. (These attacks have been referred to as \"smurf attacks\" because the name of one of the exploit programs attackers use to execute this attack is called \"smurf.\")")
(comment BaseballCenterFielder "The collection of all #$BaseballOutfielders who play the position of center field on a #$BaseballTeam.")
(comment RetailCashier "The collection of persons who ring up a customer's purchases on a cash register and receive payment for them.")
(comment Laminating "The collection of events in which a sheet of paper or plastic is fully covered in a skin-like enclosure of transparent plastic.")
(comment ARS-12DecontaminationTruck "A type of military decontamination vehicle.")
(comment specifiedIBTTypeOfAIS "(#$specifiedIBTTypeOfAIS INFO_STRUC IBTTYPE) means that IBTTYPE is the collection of all #$InformationBearingThings of a certain form which instantiate the #$AbstractInformationStructure, INFO_STRUC.")
(comment RightwardsFn "This function, applied to a #$LeftAndRightSidedObject,returns the
exact direction the object's right is facing in the implicit
frame of reference defined by the object.")
(comment USMarineBrigade "#$USMarineBrigade is the collection of all brigades within the #$UnitedStatesMarineCorps.  It consists of three or more battalions and is commanded by a colonel.")
(comment Letter-CW "The collection of all compositions created to be transmitted as letters.  Each #$Letter-CW is instantiated in one or more instances of #$LetterCopy.")
(comment GaseousFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  #$GaseousFn takes as an argument a collection COL, membership in which is based only on physical and/or chemical composition and not on any other property (see #$TangibleStuffCompositionType).  (#$GaseousFn COL) is the collection of elements of COL that are in gaseous form (i.e., are instances of #$GaseousTangibleThing) inluding objects having #$Gaseous-StateOfMatter as well as mixtures that behave like gasses.  For example, all the water vapor in the atmosphere is an instance of (#$GaseousFn #$Water).")
(comment WesternEuropeanCountry "The collection of nation-states in the Western region of Europe.")
(comment ElectricalPowerGeneration "A collection of events.  In each instance of this collection, electrical current is produced, by converting either mechanical or chemical energy to electrical energy.")
(comment BackChannelExchanges "The collection of events where a state secretly deals with another state.  These are usually to the detriment of the state and the benefit of the state representitives and are thus viewed negatively.")
(comment MilitaryBiologicalWeaponsProgram "The collection of organized research and development activities performed by military organizations for the purpose of creating #$BiologicalWeapons.")
(comment FilePermission "#$FilePermission is the collection of attributes that characterize the permissions of a #$ComputerFileCopy.")
(comment Norepinephrine "A #$Hormone secreted by the adrenal medulla It acts to constrict blood vessels, increasing blood pressure.")
(comment DenseAsLead "BTW, lead's specific gravity is 11.34")
(comment ScheduleFn-EntertainmentProvider "(#$ScheduleFn-EntertainmentProvider ENT) returns the collection of all instances of #$Schedule that include information about #$EntertainmentEvents provided (hosted, organized, broadcast, etc.) by that ENT .  For example (#$ScheduleFn-EntertainmentProvider #$CBS-TVNetwork) returns the collection of all schedules listing entertainment events broadcast or otherwise provided by CBS.")
(disjointWith ComputerImageFile ComputerTextFile)
(comment CommunicationVehicle "The collection of vehicles intended to transport communications equipment.")
(comment ProjectBroadswordConstant "This is the collection of all #$Cyc constants included in #$ProjectBroadsword releases.  Such constants should be explicitly tagged so as to ensure complete and accurate releases.")
(comment GrenadeLauncher-Automatic "Currently, the collection of #$GrenadeLaunchers that are automatic are also too heavy for one man to carry.  They are often mounted on a vehicle and act like small artillery.")
(disjointWith Distance AngularDistance)
(comment CurrencyExchangeCompany "A company that exists to perform instances of #$CurrencyExchange.")
(comment SecurityBreach "The collection of all events in which some sort of security  has been breached.  Examples include classified information transmitted to an unclassified destination, a person placing a classified document in an unclassified space, or simply a building being broken into.")
(comment SideOneFn "#$SideOneFn denotes one of the two symmetrical parts of an
instance of #$PartwiseSymmetricObject, individuated with respect to a plane
cutting through the object (cf. #$SideTwoFn). Example: a #$PhonographRecord
has 2 symmetric sides divided by a plane cutting longitudinally through it.")
(comment weaponRange "(#$weaponRange WEAPON DISTANCE) means that the maximum distance #$ProjectileWeapon WEAPON can travel in a #$ShootingAProjectileWeapon event is DISTANCE. This is something different than the #$weaponEffectiveRange that is never greater than #$weaponRange, but often quite a lot smaller. For #$IndirectFireWeapons the #$weaponRange is not the length of the trajectory it follows, but rather the maximum direct distance between the #$Gun and the place of impact of the #$ProjectileWeapon.")
(comment interArgResultGenl "A quaternary #$MetaRelation predicate for stating that a certain kind of complex, partly #$genls based relationship holds between a given argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned. (#$interArgResultGenls FUNC N INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the Nth argument to FUNC, then (regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be) the value (if any) of that function for those arguments is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is: if INST is a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC ARG(1) ... ARG(N-1) INST ...) = VALUE, then VALUE is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  Note that, unlike (e.g.) the #$InterArgTypePredicates, #$interArgResultGenl _cannot_ be used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on functions.  See also the similar but less flexible ternary #$interArg1ResultGenls et al.")
(comment clinicalFormMostCommon-Infection "(#$clinicalFormMostCommon-Infection INF-GEN-TYPE INF-SPEC-TYPE)

means that ifan infection INF is known to be an instance of

INF-GEN-TYPE, it is extremely likely, absent information to support

the conclusion (#$not (#$isa INF INF-SPEC-TYPE)), that (#$isa INF

INF-SPEC-TYPE).")
(comment ContraceptiveDevice "The collection of #$MedicalDevices that are used by instances of #$Person to prevent instances of #$ReproductiveFertilizationEvent")
(disjointWith Airplane Spacecraft)
(comment DarkSpot-Topographical "The collection of all topographical features noted for significantly lower albedo than surrounding terrain.")
(disjointWith ModalReasoningMicrotheory ModalReasoningLogicMicrotheory)
(comment Spermicide "Substances used to kill sperm, usually in order to prevent pregnancy from occurring.")
(comment DegreeFahrenheit "The unit of measure on the Fahrenheit scale; mainly used in the USA")
(comment AirForce "A subcollection of #$BranchOfMilitaryService.  Each instance of #$AirForce is a modern military organization composed mainly of airborne forces (such as bombers, fighters, torpedo planes, parachute troops, surveillance aircraft, etc.) and which has the function of defending or attacking air space, ships, or ground targets.")
(comment locationOfAsset "(#$locationOfAsset INV LOC) means that the primary location of the assets invested during the #$Investing INV is LOC.  For instance, the primary location of an investment in the #$StandardAndPoors500 would be #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, because most (all?) of the companies in that index are based in the US.  Similarly, the #$locationOfAsset of an investment in a painting would be wherever the painting happens to be (this is moot, however, because at present (3/2000) #$Investing doesn't allow investments in things like paintings).")
(comment OperatingAWheelchair "Events in which a person in a wheelchair pushes themselves under their own power.")
(comment CytosineRibonucleotide "A collection of compounds consisting of a #$Cytosine-Base

and a phosphate group linked to #$Ribose.  Its abbreviation is C, and

it pairs with #$GuanineRibonucleotide or #$GuanineDeoxyribonucleotide,

depending on the process.")
(comment constraint "(#$constraint RULE) labels a given RULE assertion as a constraint.  Constraints are typically used to verify that a given logical expectation is already true, rather than to deduce (and then add) a new formula which would satisfy the expectation.  In other words, if a rule (#$implies P(?X) Q(?X)) is labelled as a #$constraint, then when P(?X) is determined to be true, we verify that Q(?X) is already true rather than add a new argument for Q(?X) using the rule and P(?X) as justification.")
(comment differWRTSet "(#$differWRTSet 

THING1 THING2 SET) means that THING1 belongs to SET, 

while THING2 does not.  SET will often be an expression of the form 

(#$TheSetOf VAR FORMULA).  In such cases, the meaning of the overall

expression is that THING1 satisfies FORMULA (belongs to the set

of things which satisfy FORMULA), while THING2 does not.

This fact should be a salient difference between THING1 and THING2, 

i.e. a relevant point of comparison.")
(comment ExperiencingEmotionFn "#$ExperiencingEmotionFn is a unary denotational function for specifying the collection of events of feeling a particular kind of #$FeelingAttribute.  For example, (#$ExperiencingEmotionFn #$Happiness) is the collection of all events in which an agent experiences (see #$ExperiencingEmotion) happiness (see #$Happiness).")
(comment AluminumFloatingFootBridge "The collection of bridges which consist of an aluminum treadway suported by aluminum pontoons.  The bridge is assembled by feeding successive bays into the stream and connecting them.  One set provides up to 472.5 feet of bridge and is normally transported by two 2-1/2 ton trucks and two 2-1/2 ton pole trailers.  Such a bridge is deployed to provide a rapid means of crossing foot troops in an assault phase of a river crossing operation.  (Source: Engineer Systems Handbook, 4/97)")
(comment AirDefenseWeapon "A collection.  Each instance of #$AirDefenseWeapon is a weapon designed to defend against aerial military attack, either by #$MilitaryAircraft or by #$Weapons.")
(comment Leucine "A collection of organic compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.
These compounds are essential for protein synthesis and must be
ingested by the organism.  Its abbreviations are Leu and L.")
(comment TLAssertionFn "Denotes HL assertion terms at the TL (e.g., assertions appearing as terms within meta-assertions): arg1 is the mt of the assertion; arg2 is the formula of the assertion.")
(comment functionIntoSet "A #$MetaRelation predicate that relates a given function
to any set whose elements include all of the function's
values.  (#$functionIntoSet FUNCTION SET) means that 
FUNCTION is a mapping into SET.  That is, the value of 
FUNCTION for any element of (see #$elementOf) its domain 
taken as argument (see #$DomainOfFunctionFn and 
#$valueOfFunctionForArgs) is itself an element of SET.  
FUNCTION is a mapping into SET if and only if SET is a 
(proper or otherwise) superset of FUNCTION's range (see 
#$RangeOfFunctionFn).  See also the specialization 
#$functionOntoSet.")
(comment communicationTarget "The predicate #$communicationTarget is used to indicate an intended recipient in a communication act.  (#$communicationTarget COMM AGENT) means that the agent who originates the #$CommunicationAct-Single COMM intends the #$recipientOfInfo to be AGENT. Note that AGENT may or may not receive the information contained in COMM.  To indicate both that AGENT is an intended recipient of COMM, and that AGENT actually receives the information contained in COMM, use the more specialized predicate #$recipientOfInfo-Intended.")
(comment AviationReconUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of instances of ModernMilityUnit-Deployable that rely on the use of helicopters for reconnaissance operations to which they are dedicated.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn SecondRib) Tuberosity) "")
(comment (MediumAmountFn Glamour) "The attribute of being considered moderately glamorous, stylish, socially appealing.")
(comment ComplementOfInFn "(#$ComplementOfInFn SUBCOL COL) denotes the #$Collection of instances of COL that are not instances of SUBCOL, where SUBCOL is a specialization of COL. See #$complementOfIn, and contrast with the more general #$CollectionDifferenceFn that does not require subsumption of one argument by the other.")
(comment CheesecakeModel "The collection of attractive #$FemalePersons working as a #$Photographer's model.")
(comment vulnerabilityCascades "(#$vulnerabilityCascades SOURCE-TYPE OBJ-TYPE RESULT-TYPE) means that in cases where an instance of SOURCE-TYPE makes an instance of OBJ-TYPE vulnerable to results of type RESULT-TYPE, the vulnerability transfers across other instances of SOURCE-TYPE and OBJ-TYPE.  In practical terms this means that every instance of OBJ-TYPE will be vulnerable to (or in) every instance of SOURCE-TYPE.  It also means that one should take *extreme* care in making assertions with #$vulnerabilityCascades.  Typical examples will be conceptually true.")
(comment BroadcastSeriesProduct "The collection of all broadcast series considered as #$ConceptualWorks.  Each instance of #$BroadcastSeriesProduct has a (large) number of instances of #$MediaProduct designed for broadcast as #$subWorks.")
(comment Straw "the dried stems of grasses.")
(comment StrengthConditioning "The collection of all #$Exercising events designed to increase the strength of particular muscle groups.")
(comment MechanizedUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units typically           employing vehicles that run on motorized tracks or treads. Such units are usually partially           equipped for the maintainance of such vehicles.")
(comment averageSnowFall "The average number of inches per year of precipitation falling as snow             in this geographical region.  Divide by 10 to get its contribution to             #$averagePrecipitation            This is the rate averaged over a long period of time, so that the            irregularity is averaged out.")
(comment constantName "(#$constantName CONSTANT STRING) means that the #$SubLString STRING is the \"name\" for the #$CycLConstant CONSTANT.  That is, STRING is the string of characters that make up CONSTANT, minus the initial \"#\" and the following \"$\".")
(disjointWith SeasonOfYear SeparationEvent)
(comment Oatmeal "The processed (e.g., rolled or cut) but uncooked grain of the oat, from which is made hot cereal, cookies, oatcakes, haggis, etc.  A food ingredient.")
(disjointWith Country County)
(comment intendedAttackTargets "(#$intendedAttackTargets  ACTION THING) means that any agent who is the #$directingAgent of ACTION intends  for ACTION to result in damage to THING.")
(comment ExtraterritorialRegion "A collection of geographical regions.  Each instance of #$ExtraterritorialRegion is a geographical region located within the boundaries of one country but administered by officials of a foreign country.  Most commonly, extraterritoriality is extended to the grounds of diplomatic missions, including the living quarters of ambassadors.  In some cases, it has been extended to larger areas, as to the former European concessions in Shanghai that were granted by the Treaty of Nanking.  Authorities of the surrounding country cannot enter or search within an extraterritorial region without permission from the foreign authorities who administer that region (generally, the head of the diplomatic mission).")
(comment SubmarineUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all instances of #$ModernMilitaryUnit-Deployable which are specialized for military operations involving submarines. The default expectation is that a #$SubmarineUnit-MilitarySpecialty will be able to perform #$MilitaryOperations that occur in an underwater environment.")
(comment Piercing "A forming process where a smooth hole is formed without removing any material from the original object.")
(comment LookingForSomething-IndefiniteMultiple "This is the collection of lookings where the seeker has a
particular #$searchCriterion-Indefinite, does not believe that
exactly one thing satisfies it, and the seeker is looking for multiple
things that satisfy it. An example would be looking for metal objects
on a beach with a metal detector.  With this sort of search, success is incremental
(contrast this with #$LookingForSomething-IndefiniteSingle). For more about
identification conditions, see the comment on
#$searchCriterion-Indefinite.")
(comment ThreePrimeEndFn "(#$ThreePrimeEndFn CHAIN) denotes the 3' end of the nucleotide chain, CHAIN.")
(comment ArchaicSpeech "Word senses of words or phrases which are considered archaic. Archaic speech tends to sound formal.")
(comment Lava "molten rock which comes out of active volcanoes.")
(comment Concerto "The collection of all concertos, a common form of #$ClassicalMusic in which one or more soloists is accompanied by an #$Orchestra.")
(comment Marriage-Agreement "The collection of all marriages. An instance of #$Marriage-Agreement is an agreement (in many cultures an instance of #$LegalAgreement) between two #$Persons to be each other's spouse (almost always husband and wife). It is started by a #$WeddingEvent-Entire and ended either by #$Divorce, annulment, or by one of the spouses #$Dying. During a #$Marriage-Agreement, the two #$agreeingAgents are #$Married (to each other) and are #$spouses of one another.")
(comment ConfucianGift "An instance of #$GiftTypeByReligion.  The collection of all #$Gifts that are somehow associated with #$Confucianism.")
(comment MortarShell "The collection of a type of #$ArtilleryShell which is launched from a #$Mortar.")
(comment TicarcillinDiSodium "A chemical compound which is used in injectable antibiotic products.")
(comment TestDrive "The collection of all actions wherein a person drives a vehicle not owned by that person in order to evaluate the vehicle's performance.")
(comment UniformResourceLocator "A specialization of #$ContactInfoString.  Instances of this collection are commonly called \"web addresses\".  Each instance of #$UniformResourceLocator (often abbreviated \"URL\") is a string that can be used to specify an object on the #$Internet, such as a #$WebPage-CW or #$InternetNewsgroup. The first part of a URL is the name of a particular #$InternetProtocol, such as http, ftp, news, telnet, or mailto, and is followed by a colon. The part immediately following the first colon is different for each protocol, but generally is a string of characters identifying a file location, a username, and/or a password. Some URLs have a third part, consisting of '?'  or '#' followed by a query string or the name of a location within a web page. Examples include ftp://ftp.downlodes.com/pub/stuff/file.zip, http://www.myorg.org/index.html, news:alt.hypertext, mailto:santa@northpole.com.")
(comment Kina-PapuaNewGuinea "Unit of currency in #$PapuaNewGuinea")
(comment IPAddress "A specialization of #$UniqueID and #$IDString. Each instance of #$IPAddress is a string that is a unique address of a computer that is used in communications over the #$Internet that conform to #$InternetProtocol. Every instance of #$Packet-Internet includes both the #$IPAddress of the machine that sent it and the #$IPAddress of the machine to receive it. To relate #$Computers to their IP addresses, see the predicate #$computerIP.")
(comment keSuggestion-MultipleChoice "(#$keSuggestion-MultipleChoice TERM FORMULA SET) states an expectation that FORMULA should be known about TERM, where the possible values for the free variable of FORMULA are the elements of SET.")
(comment Halo-Symbolic "The collection of all symbolic halos.  A halo is a depicted circle of light above or behind an agent's head.  A symbolic halo is usually a religious symbol, indicating saintliness or divinity.")
(comment WheatPlant "Individual wheat plants.")
(comment Flaw "Each element of this collection is a state of affairs that some Agent prefers would NOT hold. Often, flaws are perceived goal violations (see #$Goal). A chipped cup is flawed from the perspective of someone who wishes to drink from it, but may not be deemed intrinsically flawed. However, things may be deemed to be intrinsically flawed.  See also #$flaws.")
(disjointWith WarmSeason ColdSeason)
(comment usernameForAccount "(#$usernameForAccount USERNAME ACCOUNT) means that USERNAME is a character string in the collection #$Username that, typically along with the use of a character string in the collection #$Password-Computer, enables access to ACCOUNT on a computational system.")
(comment StringToIntegerFn "(#$StringToIntegerFn NUMSTRING) denotes the integer (if any) that is represented by NUMSTRING in the Arabic numeral system. That is: if NUMSTRING consists entirely of #$ArabicNumerals, then the above non-atomic term (or \"NAT\") denotes whichever integer NUMSTRING represents in the Arabic system; otherwise the NAT is #$undefined (q.v.).")
(comment HomecamBroadcasting "A spec of WebcamBroadcasting. In every instance of #$HomecamBroadcasting, a visual image is transmitted via the Internet and aimed at a great many agents. The idea behind HomecamBroadcasting is that the images are supposed to be of someone in their private home or office.")
(disjointWith GeneralMicrotheory ProjectMicrotheory)
(comment tourTransitUsesPath "(#$tourTransitUsesPath TOUR MOVETYPE PATH) means that TOUR
is expected to include a #$TransportationEvent of type MOVETYPE that
has PATH as it's #$motionPathway-Partial, according to the itinerary.")
(comment intendedTargetTypeOfAttack "(#$intendedTargetTypeOfAttack ATTACK TYPE) says that during ATTACK, instances of TYPE are being targeted.  For example, (#$intendedTargetTypeOfAttack TodaysAttackOnTelAviv #$IsraeliPerson), says that Israelis were targeted during today's attack on Tel Aviv.")
(disjointWith PedalBoat RowingShell)
(comment highestVolcanoInThisArea "The highest volcano in a region")
(comment SewingNeedle-Hand "The collection of #$Needles used in instances of #$SewingByHand.  Unlike            instances of #$SewingNeedle used by instances of #$SewingMachine (see           #$SewingNeedle-Machine) instances of #$SewingNeedle-Hand have the eye           of the needle and the point on opposite ends. ")
(comment BrownRecluseSpider "A collection of very shy spiders common in the U.S., especially in   the Midwest, particularly          around the Mississippi River Valley.  They are medium-sized, very   poisonous and have a violin-shaped mark on their bodies.  They are also referred to as   fiddlebacks or violin spiders.  Their scientific name is Loxosceles   reclusa. They are members of the Loxascelidae family.")
(comment IntelligenceGathering "A collection of #$InformationGathering events, in which the gathering is done in secret.  Most commonly known as 'spying', though the intelligence gathering need not be visual.")
(comment FashionIndustry "The collection of all fashion industries. Each #$FashionIndustry is an instance of #$Industry-Localized (i.e., a #$Group of #$Organizations) whose members design, produce, and market designer clothing.")
(comment JokeTelling "Telling a joke.")
(comment SightseeingOfFn "The collection of all instances of #$SightSeeing specifically targeted toward some #$Artifact, such as the #$StatueOfLiberty or the #$EiffelTower.")
(comment AntiShipMissile "A subset of #$Missile comprising missiles that are designed to attack instances of #$ModernNavalShip.")
(comment tableKeyObject "Test vocab for SDBI.  (#$tableKeyObject ?PT ?KEYOBJ) means that  ?KEYOBJ is one of the key objects identifying a particular row of ?PT.")
(comment FictionalPCW "The collection of all #$PropositionalConceptualWorks that are fictional.")
(comment MtOfBeliefSystemFn "#$MtOfBeliefSystemFn is a function which relates a particular belief system (see #$BeliefSystem) to the microtheory which contains the beliefs of that belief system (see instances of #$BeliefSystemMicrotheory).  Thus, if someone has a particular belief system BELIEF-SYSTEM, it is likely that they believe any given assertion in (#$MtOfBeliefSystemFn BELIEF-SYSTEM)--unless, of course, they are ignorant of some particular aspect of that belief system. Note that currently (Jun 99), certain elements of #$BeliefSystemMicrotheory are atomic-terms which are redundant with their non-atomic counterparts.  For example, the atomic #$ChristianityMt should refer to the same microtheory as the non-atomic (#$MtOfBeliefSystemFn #$Christianity).  See also #$mtOfBeliefSystem.")
(comment independentArg "A #$MetaPredicate that is used to state, of a given

(ternary) #$InterArgConstraintPredicate, that it is (always) used to constrain a relation in such a way that a certain specified argument-place of the relation is for the \"independent\" argument (with respect to that constraint).  (#$independentArg INT-ARG-PRED N) means that any sentence of the form (INT-ARG-PRED RELN ...) constrains RELN in some way that treats RELN's Nth argument as independent.  For example, (#$independentArg #$interArgIsa3-4 3) holds.  See the comment on #$InterArgConstraintPredicate for an explanation of what it means to be an \"independent\" argument in this sense.  Note that #$independentArg is contrained to apply only to _ternary_ inter-argument constraint predicates, as only they have already-fixed positions for the corresponding independent and dependent arguments; thus it cannot (on pain of semantic malformedness) be applied to the quintary inter-argument constraint predicates, such as #$interArgIsa.")
(comment catalyst-TypeType "(#$catalyst-TypeType REACTION OBJECT) means that instances
of OBJECT are the chemical substance that catalyze instances of the
#$ChemicalReaction REACTION.  See also #$catalyst for the instance
level predicate.")
(comment GenocideCampaign "A collection of complex events.  An instance of #$GenocideCampaign involves the systematic killing of many or all members of some racial, ethnic, or cultural group.  In most cases, the extermination of the relevant group is a fundamental goal of the genocide campaign.")
(comment MilitaryEngineeringEquipment "The subset of military hardware that is used for support tasks such as building bridges, clearing mines, clearing rubble, and earth-moving.")
(comment ProductProviderFn-Seller "#$ProductProviderFn-Seller takes as argument any spec of #$SpatialThing-Localized and returns the collection of agents who sell things of that type.  For example, (#$ProductProviderFn-Seller #$OperatingSystem) returns the collection of all sellers of operating systems, and (#$ProductProviderFn-Seller #$LegalCounsellingService) returns the collection of all sellers of legal counselling.  See also #$sellsProductType.")
(comment ContextFreeGrammar "The collection of all #$FormalGrammar-CWs (conceptual works) that specify sets of 'grammatically valid' structures by substitution of multiple #$SyntaxSpecificationSymbols for a single one, without regard to the specifics of the surrounding parts of the relevant structure (the 'context' of the symbol).  Most #$ContextFreeGrammars are #$StringGrammars, but there are also #$GraphGrammars and other kinds.  Often a candidate #$CharacterString is tested against a #$ContextFreeGrammar with a computer program that uses a push-down stack to help parse the string into nested constituent substructures.  #$ContextFreeGrammars are often used to specify #$ComputerLanguages, and they have been used to describe some #$NaturalLanguages.  See also #$ContextSensitiveGrammar and #$RegularExpressionGrammar.")
(disjointWith MoneyTransfer ConflictEvent)
(comment ImplementingProtectionistPolicies "The collection of events where one state attempts to protect its own economy from what are perceived to be threats.  This is considered positive because a state can only implement protectionist policies upon itself, and would be viewed as positive by the directingAgent of the event; namely the state.")
(comment Shigella "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom.  Its
natural habitat is limited to the intestinal tract of humans and other
primates.  They are slender #$GramNegativeBacterium rods.")
(comment modeOfStringType "This predicate relates a type of character-string 
  token to certain specializations within that type. 
  (#$modeOfStringType MODE TYPE) means that MODE is a
  specialization of TYPE whose instances all realize the
  corresponding character-string in the same general way, 
  e.g. as inscriptions, or as sounds, or as electromagnetic 
  encodings.  For example, if MODE is an instance of 
  #$CharacterStringMode-Sounded and TYPE corresponds to 
  the string 'hello', then MODE is the collection of all 
  sounded tokens of 'hello'.")
(comment Enema-DosageForm "The collection of all enemas.  An enema is the fluid used for injection into the rectum.")
(comment Water-Ingestible "This is #$Water which is sufficiently pure that people can drink it, eat it and not get sick.")
(disjointWith FillingAPrescription (BuyingFn EntertainmentEvent))
(comment MilitaryOrgTypeByGeoAndBOS "This type-level collection forms an important partition on

#$ModernMilitaryOrganization. For each possible combination of a

#$GeographicalAgent instance (e.g. #$France) and a #$BranchOfMilitaryService

spec (#$Army-BranchOfService, #$Navy, #$AirForce, etc.),

#$MilitaryOrgTypeByGeoAndBOS has an instance, comprising all and only

those #$ModernMilitaryOrganizations which are #$subOrganizations of an instance of the #$BranchOfMilitaryService spec that has the #$GeographicalAgent instance as #$sovereignAllegianceOfOrg.  E.g.,  collection of all French army units.  See also #$OrgTypeByGeoAndBOSFn.")
(comment Nucleotide-GIS "An instance of #$ObjectType and a subset of #$GeneticInformationStructure. Each element of #$Nucleotide-GIS is an abstract chemical structure that is instantiated by all instances of some proper subset of #$Nucleotide. Instances of #$Nucleotide-GIS include #$Adenine-GIS.")
(comment singular-Generic "This predicate is a generalization over the #$SpeechPartPredicates that express singular number.  (#$singular-Generic WORD STRING) means that the #$EnglishWord WORD has STRING as a singular form: either #$singular (the singular form corresponding to the #$CountNoun part of speech), #$pnSingular (for #$ProperCountNoun forms), or #$agentive-Sg (for #$AgentiveNoun forms).  This predicate is #$notAssertible, since it will always cash out as an assertion on one of its spec-preds.")
(comment TransportingPeople "A specialization of #$TransportationEvent.  Each instance of #$TransportingPeople is a transportation event in which at least one instance of #$Person is among the main transportees (see the predicate #$transportees).  Note that this collection excludes events in which people are merely conveyed (as, for example, by a moving sidewalk), rather than travelling with their transporting device.  Note that the notion of 'transportees' is interpreted broadly: even the driver (#$driverActor) of the transportation device counts among the transportees.")
(comment Platelet "There are a mob of these in #$Blood.")
(disjointWith Temperature Volume)
(comment AirToAirMissileUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile centers on missiles           that are fired from an airborne weapons platform at a target that is           also airborne.")
(comment UbiquitousResourceType "The collection of natural resources (see #$NaturalResourceType) whose instances are found in abundance on #$PlanetEarth.  Examples include #$Air, #$Dirt, and #$Water.  Non-examples include #$Diamond-Gems and #$Petroleum-CrudeOil.")
(comment compoundingPeriod "The predicate used to state the period of time over which interest on a #$LoanAgreement is accumulated before being added to the principal of the loan for further interest calculations.  (#$compoundingPeriod LOAN TIME) means that every TIME, the interest accumulated on LOAN is added to the #$principal for this purpose.")
(comment AttemptingFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction from types of actions to collections of attempts to perform them.  (#$AttemptingFn ACTION-TYPE) is the collection of all attempts to perform an action of form ACTION-TYPE.  For example, (#$AttemptingFn #$FollowingInstructions) is the collection of all attempts at following instructions, whether successful (and thus resulting in actual instruction-followings) or not.")
(comment contraindicatedProduct "(#$contraindicatedProduct PRSN PROD-TYPE) means that the instance of #$ProductType PROD-TYPE is contraindicated as a purchase for the #$Person PRSN. This predicate is a #$genlPreds of #$explicitlyContraindicatedProduct and #$inferenceContraindicatedProduct.")
(comment HardcopyOfIBTTypeFn "A function that maps collections of #$InformationBearingThings onto their hardcopy subcollections. For example, (#$HardcopyOfIBTTypeFn #$StillImage) is the collection of all hardcopy still images, e.g., physical slides [#$Slide-Photograph] would be elements of this collection while the projected #$StillImages generated from the slides would not. See #$HardcopyOfCWFn for specifying hardcopies of #$ConceptualWorks, #$HardcopyOfInformationTypeFn for specifying hardcopies of types of #$ConceptualWorks, and #$ElectronicFn for electronic copies.")
(comment StringConcatWithHyphens "Fields combined in this way will be string-concatenated with one or more hyphens intervening between the fields.")
(comment Reincarnation "The act of being reborn, whereby the spiritual essence

that previously occupied (a now dead) body (or technically, #$Organism-Whole) now occupies

a new #$Organism-Whole from its inception onwards.

The concept of #$Reincarnation adopted here assumes that the connection between an entity and

a 'past-life' is the spiritual being (i.e., #$DivineBeing) of which the new and past lives

are physical incarnations (see #$IncarnationPhysicalFn).")
(comment Malleability "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity.  Each instance of #$Malleability is a specific capacity of a physical material to be shaped or formed.  Different degrees of malleability may be designated using a #$GenericValueFunction.  Malleability of objects is indicated with the predicate #$malleabilityOfObject (q.v.).")
(comment ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheorySet "Each instance SET of #$ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheorySet 

is a set of microtheories that are instances of 

#$ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheory, and are related through #$mtPrecedes as 

an event ordering (interval ordering) in #$ReasoningWithTense-InferenceMt, 

as a linear ordering in #$ReasoningWithTense-InferenceMt-LinearTime, and 

as a discrete linear ordering in 

#$ReasoningWithTense-InferenceMt-SingleDateSeries.  Such 

a SET `isolates' its members from other instances of 

#$ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheory, and avoids undesired 

#$mtPrecedes link to microtheories outside SET that could be inferred in 

the absence of SET.  Thus, instances of 

#$ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheorySet should be used for particular 

projects or parts of them if they require reasoning with tenses and 

such reasoning is supposed to be carried out by using microtheories 

with #$mtPrecedes relation among them.")
(comment CommercialFishing "Fishing done for subsistence or financial gain.")
(comment productionRateOfRegion "(#$productionRateOfRegion REGION PRODUCT-TYPE RATE) means that

PRODUCT-TYPE is produced within REGION at the rate of RATE.")
(comment PhysicalContactEvent "A collection of physical events in which two or more objects are in physical contact (see #$touches) for at least part of the event's duration. Note that, although most #$PhysicalEvents involve some kind of touching, only those for which contact is salient should be instances of #$PhysicalContactEvent.  For events involving continuous contact and events in which contact is made, respectively, see the specializations #$ContinuousPhysicalContactEvent and #$PhysicalContactMakingEvent.")
(disjointWith ConstructionArtifact Memorabilia)
(comment mtVolumeValue "(#$mtVolumeValue MT INTERVAL) means that when reasoning in (or with) the context MT, spatial objects with a volume that falls within the range specified by INTERVAL should be attended to, or taken into account.  For example, (#$mtVolumeValue MT (#$CubicMeter 1 100)) means that when reasoning proceeds using the knowledge in MT, only objects having a volume that measures greater than or equal to 1 cubic meter, and less than or equal to 100 cubic meters, should be considered relevant.")
(comment AnalogousVersionFn "(#$AnalogousVersionFn ?Situation ?Source ?Target) denotes the set of analogous situations that pertain to some target domain entity ?Target rather than the given source domain entity. For instance, while #Y1Stage2-TerroristAttacks denotes the terrorist attacks by Iran on #SaudiArabia, (#AnalogousVersionFn #Y1Stage2-TerroristAttacks #SaudiArabia #Azerbaijan) denotes the analogous set of terrorist acts that might potentially be perpetrated by #$Iran on #Azerbaijan instead of #SaudiArabia.")
(disjointWith LiquidTangibleThing GranularFluid)
(comment BattleTank-M60A3 "A kind of battle tank.")
(comment SpiralGalaxy "#$SpiralGalaxy is the collection of all spiral galaxies.")
(comment Promethazine "The chemical compound which is an anti-emetic.")
(comment HeavyPressure "Pressure in an amount that is at least uncomfortable and eventually painful to humans.")
(comment DiplomaticSupport "#$DiplomaticSupport is a collection of attributes representing the different generic levels of diplomatic support that one country can give to another. Attributes in this collection represent the general commitment of one diplomatic agent (e.g., a country or organization of   countries) to provide diplomatic support to another agent, as evidenced by pledges and/or present or previous behavior. For example, (#$givesSupportToAgent #$GreatBritain-TheIsland #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica (#$HighAmountFn #$DiplomaticSupport)). Note that such relationships are liable to change and, therefore, assertions about them should have a temporal qualification (see #$holdsIn).  Diplomatic support is intangible but significant, in that it may affect actions in international organizations, it may influence third parties,   and it may imply or include economic or military support. (See also #$MilitarySupport and #$EconomicSupport.)  To represent actual events in which support is given, see #$ShowingSupportForSomeone and #$HelpingAnAgent.--Lupher, June 23, 1998")
(comment CollectionVsPredicateNoteFn "(#$CollectionVsPredicateNoteFn TERM) denotes a #$SharedNote which concerns itself with the subject of whether TERM should be represented in the Cyc KB as an element of #$Collection or an element of #$Predicate.  In contentious cases KE-ers may be encouraged to add their opinions on #$cyclistNotes for (#$CollectionVsPredicateNoteFn TERM).  Once a more or less final or official decision has been made regarding the predicatehood or collectionhood of TERM has been made, all appropriate #$cyclistNotes assertions should be digestified and promoted to a #$comment on the #$SharedNote called (#$CollectionVsPredicateNoteFn TERM).  As cases of (#$CollectionVsPredicateNoteFn TERM-1), (#$CollectionVsPredicateNoteFn TERM-2) ...(#$CollectionVsPredicateNoteFn TERM-n) accumulate, we can inductively look for generalizations and positively contribute to the perenial 'collections vs predicates' debate.")
(comment totalBudgetExpenditures "(#$totalBudgetExpenditures ORG THING MONEY) means that MONEY is a measure of the amount of money spent by the #$Organization ORG during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  ORG might, for example, be a #$Business, a #$LegalGovernmentOrganization, or a #$Country.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.")
(comment U-TheLetter "The letter U of the alphabet.  This is 'U' (or 'u') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.  As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterU and #$LatinSmallLetterU.")
(comment NewDollar-Taiwan "Major unit of currency of Taiwan")
(comment ScholasticAptitudeTest "The collection of #$AcademicTesting events that are designed to test the scholastic aptitude, and thus college eligibility, of a student. Also known as SAT testing, SAT test scores are used by universities and a primary selection criterion for new student admittance.")
(comment mediatorConfigured-ChemBond "(#$mediatorConfigured-ChemBond BOND OBJ) means that OBJ is
configured as the mediating object in the #$ChemicalBond  BOND. OBJ can be
an instance of #$ChemicalObject or an Electron when BOND is a
#$CovalentBond.")
(comment FlowerBud "A stage of an immature flower, developed enough that it can be recognized (with careful observation) as a flower and not an apical meristem.")
(comment agentBelievesInObligation "#$agentBelievesInObligation is a binary predicate which relates agents to the obligations that they ``believe in'', ``support'', or ``honor''.  This predicate is often important when to reasoning about agent's emotions.  For example, emotions such as pride, shame, reproach, or admiration often involve some standard or value (i.e. some #$Obligation) being upheld or violated.  Typically, a given agent must support or believe in the upheld/violated #$Obligation in order for such an emotion to be warranted.")
(comment connectionJoins "(#$connectionJoins CONN OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are joined in the #$Connection-Physical, CONN.  This predicate handles the common case where a connection joins 2 things.")
(comment PlanSupplementMicrotheory "In representing a #$Plan, many of the background constraints
and assumptions specific to the #$Plan instance will be represented in
the #$PlanBackgroundContext.  However, in certain circumstances it may
be necessary to represent additional hypotheses in a context distinct
from the background, either because these are to be varied, or because
they need to be sequestered for some other reason.  For such purposes
we use instances of #$PlanSupplementMicrotheory. Instances are
microtheories that consist of sets of assertions that posit specific
hypotheses whose effect on a proposed plan execution we wish to
test.")
(comment Intron-GIS "A nucleotide sequence separating two
#$Exon-GIS's.  #$Intron-GIS's do not code
for proteins, in whole or in part, and serve to separate coding
sequences which, when joined together in an RNA molecule, code for a
specific protein type.")
(comment Biscuit "Collection of American-style biscuits: a soft wheat-flour shortbread, typically served at breakfast.  Served as soon as possible after baking.  Not to be confused with English wafer biscuits.")
(comment Rifling-Nonconstrained "Moving forward in #$ProjectileMotion along a trajectory while spinning along the front-back axis.  Examples are a rifle bullet and #$Football-American.")
(comment SYNFlooderProgram "#$SYNFlooderProgram is the specialization of #$MaliciousComputerProgram, instances of which are designed to facilitate the performance of instances of #$AttackByComputerOperation-SYNFlooding.")
(comment Ferry "#$Ferry is a specialization of #$Ship and #$PublicTransportationDevice.  Each instance of #$Ferry is a ferryboat, i.e., boats that are used to carry people, goods or vehicles across rivers, lakes, canals or channels etc. or even from one side of a harbor to another, but normally not used to cross oceans.  #$Ferry is disjoint with #$OceanLiner.")
(comment SwollenBodyPartCondition "The collection of all #$AilmentConditions that are characterized by swollen body parts.")
(comment RedCrossSociety-National "A collection of organizations. Instances of this collection are Red Cross or Red Crescent societies of specific countries, for example, the American Red Cross. Each national society is a member of the InternationalFederationOfRedCrossAndRedCrescentSocieties.")
(comment BaseballFirstBaseman "The collection of all #$BaseballPlayers who play the position of first base on a #$BaseballTeam.")
(comment connectedAtSpot "(#$connectedAtSpot OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 is #$connectedTo OBJ2 at a localized spot.  To indicate multiple spot connections between two objects, the connections themselves must be reified.")
(comment NegativeInteger "A specialization of #$Integer.  An instance INT of #$Integer is also an instance of #$NegativeInteger if and only if INT is less than zero.")
(comment HinduGift "An instance of #$GiftTypeByReligion.  The collection of all #$Gifts that are somehow associated with #$Hinduism.")
(comment CounterArtilleryRADAR "A type of RADAR used to detect and destroy incoming artillery fire.")
(comment tourDestinations "(#$tourDestinations TOUR REGION) means that REGION is a place
where the itinerary of TOUR specifies TOUR is supposed to 'stop':
i.e., one of the sites that TOUR is specifically identified as
covering.  If a tour were represented as a graph or a #$PathSystem,
#$tourDestinations would most reasonably be represented as nodes.")
(comment Ununnilium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is a RadioactiveObject of #$Ununnilium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment USMarineDivision "#$USMarineDivision is the collection of all divisions within the #$UnitedStatesMarineCorps.  It consists of two or three brigades and is commanded by a general.")
(comment EccentricSubculture "Instances of #$EccentricSubculture are #$HumanCultures, that, among other things, have a small number of participants relative to a larger #$HumanCulture of which these members are also in some sense a part.  Additionally, #$EccentricSubcultures involve activities and beliefs that are, from the perspective of the larger culture, eccentric; usually their participants embrace such activities and beliefs for that very reason.  Examples include punk culture and gothic culture.  Non-examples include suburbanite culture, farm culture, and cultures practiced by ethnic groups who happen to be minority groups.")
(disjointWith InformationTransferEvent WeatherEvent)
(comment SupportGroup "This is the collection of support groups (individuals, not types). A support group is a loosely organized group of people who share some sort of problem and

get together to support each other psychologically.")
(comment VisualInformationGeneratingAct "A specialization of #$IBTGeneration (q.v.).  Each instance of #$VisualInformationGeneratingAct is an action that generates visual information (i.e. information of a kind typically accessed via the sense of sight).  Specializations of this collection include #$MakingAGesture, #$DisplayingSomething, and #$Writing.  If a given visual-information-generating act also involves conveying the information to another agent (i.e. if it is a #$Communicating), then it is also a #$VisualCommunicating (q.v.).  Or a visual-information-generating act might be a proper sub-event of a visual-communicating act.")
(comment keStrongConsiderationPreds "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate (q.v.) and specialization of #$keConsiderationPreds (q.v.) that relates a collection to a binary predicate.  (#$keStrongConsiderationPreds COL BINPRED) means that for any reified instance INST of COL, it should be determined whether there is any thing THING such that BINPRED holds between THING and INST, and if so it is strongly suggested that (BINPRED THING INST) be asserted in the Cyc Knowledge Base.  See also #$keStrongConsiderationInverse.")
(comment MusicTypeByMajorGenre "Instances are collections representing different styles of music.  The instances of #$MusicTypeByMajorGenre divides music up by style as opposed to by composer or by geographic region, although it's certainly true that particular styles originate in different regions. Notably, no instance of this collection is a sub-genre of any other genre.")
(comment Melting "A collection of events.  In each instance of this collection, an object is heated to (and then above) its #$freezingPoint and is thereby changed from a #$Solid-StateOfMatter to a #$Liquid-StateOfMatter.")
(comment HeightFn "(#$HeightFn OBJ) denotes the height of OBJ.")
(comment VicePresident-GovernmentOfficial "A collection of persons.  Each element of #$VicePresident-GovernmentOfficial is a person who holds the title of vice president of some element of #$Country. Often, the vice president of a country is first in the line of succession to the presidency. Examples: Al Gore, Dan Quayle.")
(comment TerminatingDiplomaticRelations "The collection of events where a state officially terminates all diplomatics relations with another state.")
(comment prospectiveSeller "(#$prospectiveSeller ACT AGENT) means that AGENT acts in the seller's, or potential seller's, role in the #$CommercialActivity ACT.")
(comment MilitaryChemicalWeaponsProgram "The collection of organized research and development activities performed by military organizations for the purpose of creating #$ChemicalWeapons.")
(comment processRunBy "(#$processAccessedBy PROCESS AGENT) means that agent AGENT interacts with computer process PROCESS.  For example, a user of an ATM, a participant in an IRC chat room, or a person joining a #$MUDGame.  If AGENT initiates PROCESS as well, use the more specific predicate, #$processRunBy.")
(comment Cortisone "A #$Glucocorticoid synthesized in the adrenal cortex May also be prepared synthetically.")
(comment DenseAsAluminum "BTW, #$Aluminum's specific gravity is 2.7")
(comment makesMoreVulnerableThan-Object "(#$makesMoreVulnerableThan-Object THREAT-OBJ1 THREAT-OBJ2 OBJECT HARM-TYPE) means that THREAT-OBJ1 increases the vulnerability of OBJECT to results of type HARM-TYPE more than THREAT-OBJ2 does. OBJECT is presumably vulnerable to both THREAT-OBJ1 and THREAT-OBJ2.  Note also that this is an instance level predicate, although the last argument is a type of situation.  For restrictions on HARM-TYPE see #$vulnerableTo.")
(comment TimeDelay-ComputerPerformance "This is the collection of all events in which a computer experiences a 
    time delay during some computer process.  Any instance of
    #$ComputerProcessRunning in which there is a significant delay, usually due to
    some external factor will be included here.")
(comment OperativeAgentOfFn "(#$OperativeAgentOfFn ORG) is the collection of all officers or field agents of the #$LawEnforcementOrganization ORG who are charged with carrying out ORG's law enforcement activities in the field.  Thus, for example, (#$OperativeAgentOfFn #$INTERPOL) returns the collection of all of #$INTERPOL's agents.")
(comment Robin-American "The American robin")
(comment GrenadeLauncher-Portable "The collection of #$GrenadeLaunchers that are carried by a single infantryman.")
(disjointWith Distance Temperature)
(comment StringReplaceSubstringFn "StringReplaceSubstringFn is an evaluatable function that takes three strings as its arguments. (StringReplaceSubstringFn STRING SUBSTRING NEWSTRING) tests to make sure that the n tokens in SUBSTRING exactly match a substring of STRING. If this condition is met, the function will then replace all occurrences of SUBSTRING in STRING with NEWSTRING, returning the resulting string. Otherwise the function will simply return STRING. For example, (StringReplaceSubstringFn 'I like to bicycle' 'like' 'hate') returns 'I hate to bicycle'. However, (StringReplaceSubstringFn 'I like to bicycle' 'likes' 'hate') would return 'I like to bicycle'.")
(comment ManagementConsulting "A constant on which to hang the phrase 'management consulting' for HotBot.")
(comment derivedProbability "A predicate used for probability statements.  (#$derivedProbability PROPOSITION PROBNO) means that, in the applicable #$Microtheory, the a posteriori probability of the truth of the formula PROPOSITION, given (and depending on) the current state of knowledge of all other assertions, is PROBNO (a real number between zero and one, where zero means certainly false and one means certainly true).  In most microtheories, generally, this refers to the derived probability that PROPOSITION is true given the probabilities of the other #$CycLAssertions and #$domainAssumptions of the #$Microtheory.   Contrast this with #$priorProbability and #$derivedProbability-Range.  See also the function version of this: #$DerivedProbabilityFn.  A #$derivedProbability depends at least partially on, and is in some manner derived from or affected by, the probabilities of some or all of the other #$CycLAssertions in the #$Microtheory (whether prior, derived or conditional) along with the #$domainAssumptions.  See also #$conditionalProbability.  This definition makes no presumption as to determinism versus nondeterminism, nor as to whether probability is only in the mind of some beholder.  The definition allows for any of several different systems of deriving the probability of one assertion from the probabilities of, or conditional probabilities relating, other assertions.")
(comment DiscoveringOfWeaknessInNetwork "The activity of identifying aspects of computer system or network for the purpose of tailoring an electronic
attack to inflict damage on the system or network.")
(comment Amplifier "A collection of devices; a subset of   ElectronicComponent. Each instance of Amplifier is a device used for   increasing the amplitude of a signal passing through it.")
(comment IndianHealthServiceFacility "A medical care organization/facility operated under the direction of the Indian Health Service.")
(comment muchLessThan "(#$muchLessThan SMALL LARGE) says that the #$ScalarInterval SMALL is

 much less than the #$ScalarInterval LARGE.  It is important to keep in 

mind that the notion of \"much\" is relative to some scale, and

 so assertions using this predicate should be carefully placed in the right 

context.  See also #$muchLessThanWRTScale.  #$muchLessThan was introduced primarily to facilitate parsing NL, in which speakers make comparative

 claims often without specifying the relevant scale.")
(comment Article-PCW "The collection of all nonfiction literary compositions intended to be published as a subdivision of some #$PublishedMaterial.")
(comment WorksOfArtFromFn "(#$WorksOfArtFromFn GEO-THING) denotes the collection of objects of

art that come from GEOO-THING, an instance of #$GeographicalThing.")
(disjointWith UnintendedLossOfUserRights CedingTerritory)
(comment UnitOfCapacitance "A specialization of #$UnitOfMeasure. Each instance of #$UnitOfCapacitance is a function which returns an instance of #$ElectricalCapacitance (q.v.) when applied to a real number (see the collection #$SubLRealNumber) or a sequence of two real numbers. For instance, (#$Farad 20) is a capacitance of 20 farads.")
(disjointWith MeasuringDevice ContraceptiveDevice)
(comment keFarthestGenlsWeakSuggestionInverse "(#$keFarthestGenlsWeakSuggestionPreds COL BIN-PRED) means that for
every specialization SPEC-COL of COL such that SPEC-COL is not known to have dependent specializations, it is weakly suggested that
there exist some VALUE such that (BIN-PRED VALUE SPEC-COL) is known in
the KB.")
(disjointWith InternationalOrganizationOfCountries CountrySubsidiary)
(disjointWith WaterTransportationDevice IntraBuildingTransportationDevice)
(comment IBTSeriesOfEditionsType "A collection of collections. Each instance of #$IBTSeriesOfEditionsType is a collection of InformationBearingThings which are all editions of the same work.  These InformationBearingThings share substantially the same information, and typically share the same name, but don't share exactly the same information because they are not all from the same edition.  For example, #$MSWindows has many versions (or editions), so it is an instance of IBTSeriesOfEditionsType.  Any particular instance of #$MSWindows would also be an instance of some particular edition of #$MSWindows; e.g., #$MSWindows95.  Collections of IBTs which are all from the same edition, such as #$MSWindows95, would be instances of #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType.  The relationship between an instance of IBTSeriesOfEditionsType (such as MSWindows) and the SpecifiedInformationBearingThingTypes that are its editions (such as #$MSWindows95) is #$genls.")
(comment AntiInflammatory "Drugs which reduce inflammation.")
(comment along-UnderspecifiedPath "(#$along-UnderspecifiedPath ACT PATH) states that an abstract
locational relation holds between ACT and PATH, where PATH is a
#$Path-Underspecified 'moved along' during ACT.  #$along-UnderspecifiedPath is an
underspecified semantic representation that may be elaborated to
represent either a spatial example of 'going along' (as in 'walking
along the footpath') or a metaphorical use ('Smith has to go along
with Jones' plan, for now ...').")
(comment primeRate-US "The predicate used to state the interest rate that commercial banks in the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica are charging their most creditworthy borrowers, such as large corporations.")
(comment CountrySubsidiary "A specialization of #$GeopoliticalEntity.  Each instance of #$CountrySubsidiary is a political region that is a direct subsidiary of some country.  This collection includes states, provinces, territories, and some special districts such as Washington, D.C.")
(comment Dinghy "small one or two-person rowboat.")
(comment CytosineDeoxyribonucleotide "A collection of compounds consisting of a #$Cytosine-Base and a phosphate group linked with #$Deoxyribose.  Its abbreviation is C, and it pairs with #$GuanineDeoxyribonucleotide or #$GuanineRibonucleotide, depending on the process.")
(comment BridgeWithArmoredVehicle "A collection of military bridges that are physically supported underneath by an armored vehicle such as a modified tank chassis.")
(comment AccessorFn "A function which returns the group of people who have official access to some   individual.  Thus, e.g. any object whose #$levelOfSecurity is #$OpenAccess will  be accessible by all instances of #$Person.")
(comment Orientia-Genus "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom.
These are small #$Bacterium that are transmitted to humans by
arthropods.  Some #$BiologicalSpecies are transmitted transovarially in the arthrpod, which serves as a vector and reservoir.")
(comment AircraftWeaponPylon "The collection of #$Containers attached to #$MilitaryAircraft, usually under the wing, used for holding #$Weapons.")
(disjointWith LandBody Shoreline)
(comment Lysine "A collection of organic compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.
These compounds are essential for protein synthesis and must be
ingested by the organism.  Its abbreviations are Lys and K.")
(comment VulnerableToPhysicalDamage "The the attribute of being vulnerable, which, if exploited, would result in physical damage to the victim.  A computer's being #$VulnerableToPhysicalDamage, for instance, could arise when its position is directly under a water sprinkler.  This attribute does not apply to things by virtue of their being vulnerable to unauthorized access (see #$VulnerableToPhysicalBreachOfSecurity).")
(comment ReplyingToAQuestion "Answering a question that someone or something has posed to you.")
(comment CasualWear "The collection of all clothing items that are casual wear, e.g. turtlenecks.")
(comment DismountedAntiArmorUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of military units trained and equipped to fight armored vehicles while on foot.")
(comment LearningByObserving "This is the kind of #$Learning in which one either gathers information by #$Perceiving, or perceives 
how to do something.  Observation includes all of the senses, not just sight.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn TenthRib) Tuberosity) "")
(comment Glamour "The collection of attributes that describe some combination of a person's socially recognized charm, appealingness, fascination, allure, popularity, stylishness, and sexiness.")
(comment PinupModel "The collection of attractive #$Persons working as a #$Photographer's model.")
(comment BroadcastMediaProduct "A collection of #$ConceptualWorks created for the purposes of #$Broadcasting.")
(comment SpinachPlant "The green leafy plant from which the food spinach is obtained.")
(comment functionCommutesWith "Used to assert that the order

of application of two functions is irrelevant, and that the

functions commute with each other.  This information is used

to canonicalize terms involving these functions.  For instance,

if (#$functionCommutesWith FOO BAR) is asserted, then the two

terms (FOO (BAR X)) and (BAR (FOO X)) will canonicalize to the

same thing.")
(comment dailyLowTemperature "(#$dailyLowTemperature PLACE TEMP) means that the #$Temperature TEMP is the low temperature for a day at the #$GeographicalRegion PLACE.  #$dailyLowTemperature is typically used for a specified period of time (e.g., a particular day or a specific season); it may be used with generic temperature ranges as well as precise temperatures.")
(comment NationalSportsTeam "The collection of #$SportsTeams

 who represent a country during 

#$InternationalSportsCompetitions.  #$OlympicTeams

 are a celebrated special case of this.")
(comment Hypoglycemia "#$Hypoglycemia is an #$AilmentCondition involving an abnormal decrease of sugar in the bloodstream.")
(comment LightningEvent "A specialization of both #$Emission and #$ImmediateWeatherProcess.  In each instance of #$LightningEvent, a flashing of light is produced by the discharge of atmospheric electricity.")
(disjointWith County City)
(comment UnderdevelopedRegion "The collection of geographical regions whose economy is characterized by having (1) very little industrialization; (2) a lack of capital; (3) low annual incomes and material poverty for most residents; and (4) low annual GNP.  See also #$TheDevelopingWorld.")
(comment ColdForming "Changing the shape of a substance at a temperature lower than its recrystallization point. This process alters the internal structure of the substance.")
(comment searchCriterion-Indefinite "`(#$searchCriterion-Indefinite SEARCH CRITERION)' means that

CRITERION is the search criterion for the #$LookingForSomething-Indefinite

SEARCH.  The agent might have consciously in mind one or more descriptions

of the sort of thing s/he is seeking or, if not, could at least be prompted

to produce such descriptions.  Some of these descriptions will express

properties the seeker would take to be criterial of success in the sense

that s/he could not conceive of a case in which both (i) s/he successfully

finds an object of that type and (ii) the object s/he finds lacks any of

those properties. The conjunction of these criterial properties will

correspond to the instance of #$PossibleIdentificationCondition that is

associated with the search.")
(disjointWith LightningEvent VolcanicEruption)
(comment BallisticMissile-ICBM "The collection of #$BallisticMissiles used against strategic targets, such as cities, and with a range of 3,438 miles and above.")
(comment ChristianGift "An instance of #$GiftTypeByReligion.  The collection of all #$Gifts that are somehow associated with #$Christianity.")
(comment Cefoperazone "A chemical compound which is used in injectable antibiotic products.")
(comment tourRoutes "(#$tourRoutes TOUR ROUTE) means that the #$Path-Simple ROUTE is a route taken by TOUR, according to the tour itinerary.")
(comment Traditional "An attribute used to describe those things, activities, methods of doing things which are typical of the past, and/or which are viewed as conventional and well-established.")
(comment nationalBudget "The government budget of a nation given in billions of dollars if it is not broken down into revenues and expenditures")
(comment Cheating "The collection of all actions in which one agent breaks some rule without being penalized or otherwise adversely affected. This generally entails that at least one other agent is deceived into thinking that the cheater has abided by the rules. If the cheater is discovered and penalized for the #$Cheating, then the action is an instance not of #$Cheating, but of (#$AttemptingFn #$Cheating).")
(comment Escudo-Portugal "The standard UnitOfCurrency in #$Portugal")
(comment rejectedSentence "A unary predicate which pertains to instances of #$CycLSentence. (#$rejectedSentence FORMULA) states that FORMULA is a CycL formula which although syntactically well-formed is not semantically well-formed with respect to argument constraints only.  For example, (#$rejectedSentence (#$bordersOn #$Canada #$Country)).  See also #$admittedSentence.")
(comment Packet-Internet "#$Packet-Internet is the collection of instances of #$Packet-Network which adhere to the specifications set by #$InternetProtocol. An instance of #$Packet-Internet consists of 

a #$Header-Packet and data which is received from the #$TransportLayerProtocol.

A #$Packet-Internet contains information which allows it to be routed to its

destination on the #$Internet.")
(comment paStereotypicProductTopic "(#$paStereotypicProductTopic PERS COL) means that due to minimal information available about PERS, we might expect that products related to COL might be at least worth asking about.")
(comment Grass-Plant "Individual plants which are part of a mass of turf grass.")
(comment flaws "(flaws ?NOTION ?F) means that the situation/thing/whatever is flawed by virtue of possessing the detrimental state-of-affairs (#$Flaw) ?F. Note that Flaw is a subjective attribution, and so flaws should only be used within the context of a propositional attribute predicate such as #$beliefs or #$biases.")
(comment WarmSeason "A specialization of #$SeasonOfYear.  Each instance of #$WarmSeason is the warmer time of the seasonal cycle at a particular region.  In most places on Earth, an instance of #$WarmSeason temporally subsumes anb instance of #$SummerSeason.  Each instance of #$WarmSeason is a weather season that is part of an annual cliomate cycle (see #$AnnualClimateCycle).  Note that #$WarmSeason is _not_ a specialization of #$CalendarSeason.")
(comment AidingAllies "This attribute characterizes goals which involve aiding one's allies.")
(comment hasHeadquartersInCountry "The predicate #$hasHeadquartersInCountry identifies a country in which a particular organization has one of its headquarters.  (#$hasHeadquartersInCountry ORG COUNTRY) means that the #$Organization ORG has one of its headquarters and places of primary central control in the #$Country COUNTRY.")
(comment Hypothyroidism "Deficient activity of the thyroid gland.  Produces lowered metabolic rate and general lack of vigor.")
(comment RescuingSomeone "The collection of events in which a person is removed from a dangerous situation. Examples would include rescuing someone who is lost in the wilderness, as well as rescuing someone who is being held captive.")
(disjointWith Thinking Travel-TripEvent)
(comment Corporal-Title "This Cyc constant denotes the term of address used for someone holding the rank-attribute of #$Corporal-Rank in an  instance of #$ModernMilitaryOrganization.")
(comment Bore "Each #$Bore is a walled cavity which is mostly cylindrical in shape. It may or may not be open on both ends.")
(disjointWith Water Mineral)
(comment FighterUnit-MilitarySpecialty "A specialization of #$AviationUnit-MilitarySpecialty.
Instances are units equipped primarily with fighter aircraft,
specializing in missions that employ fighter aircraft.")
(comment StorageFacility "The collection of all #$ConstructionArtifacts,

 one major function of which is to hold

  large amounts of products.  A #$Warehouse is

  a good example, though StorageFacilities

  need not be restricted to buildings; parts

  of a #$StorageFacility can include the grounds

  surrounding a #$Warehouse.  In the case of

  military StorageFacilities, there will often

 be several #$Warehouses or similar structures

  located at one facility.")
(disjointWith Kayak RowingShell)
(comment mostNotableEruptionDate "year of best known big eruption")
(comment ChlamydiaTrachomatisBacterium "The class of bacteria that are responsible for the venereal disease Chlamydia.")
(comment vaccinationEffectiveAgainstInfectionType "#$vaccinationEffectiveAgainstInfectionType is used to link a particular class of #$Infection with the collection of all vaccines that are effective against the type of #$Microorganism that causes the infection.")
(comment Witchcraft "The collection of all #$ParanormalEvents performed by #$Witches. Includes things like casting spells and flying on #$WitchBroomsticks.")
(comment alongsidePathSegment "This predicate relates an object that is alongside a

customary path to the precise segment of the path that the 

object is strictly alongside.  The path segment will have

the same length as whichever dimension (if any) of the object

is aligned with the path.  More precisely, 

(#$alongsidePathSegment THING SEGMENT) means that SEGMENT is 

a #$subPaths of some PATH that THING is #$onPath-Alongside, 

and SEGMENT is the longest portion of PATH lying between two 

planes that both intersect THING and are both perpendicular 

to the centerline of PATH.  For example, a 100-foot-wide 

building standing alongside and facing a street is 

#$alongsidePathSegment the corresponding 100-foot-long 

segment of the street.")
(comment BasketballCourt "Any area used to play basketball on -- a school gym, a driveway, or a 'real' basketball court.")
(comment Posing "arranging the body in a particular way, so as to created a certain effect, as in posing for a picture.")
(comment multiWordSemTrans "This pred allows the use of a #$SubcategorizationFrame with a multi word string.  The first three args function as in #$multiWordString.  When the string produced appears with the arg4 #$SubcategorizationFrame, it is translated into CycL with the arg5 #$NLTemplateExpression.")
(comment repValue "(#$repValue ?PT ?KEYOBJ ?LF ?VAL) means that ?VAL is the meaning of the contents of the field ?LF in the physical table ?PT, in the tuple identified by ?KEYOBJ.  #$repValue is similar to #$cellValue, but #$cellValue states actual cell contents, while the fourth argument of #$repValue has been translated into the meaning of the contents. ")
(comment PluralsConstant "Every constant introduced as part of the plurals proposal is in
this collection. For a full, satisfying helping of documentation on Cyc's
handling of plurals, inspect
http://localhost/cycdoc/sigs/plurals/plural-maindoc.html.")
(comment (FreeThingOfTypeFn OnlineGameProgram) "The collection of  free online games.")
(comment dependentFields "(#$dependentFields ?LTS ?DF) means that ?DF is a logical field of the schema ?LTS, which may or may not have a value for a particular row.  Whether it does depends on some other field; if this controlling field has the right value, then ?DF takes the value of a third, explicit field.  See #$fieldValueDependsOn.")
(comment ContextSensitiveGrammar "The collection of all #$FormalGrammar-CWs (conceptual works) that specify sets of 'grammatically valid' structures by substitution of multiple #$SyntaxSpecificationSymbols for a single or multiple ones possibly restricted to those that are surrounded by certain kinds of parts of the relevant structure (the 'context' of the symbol).  Most #$ContextSensitiveGrammars are #$StringGrammars, but there are also #$GraphGrammars and other kinds, often with special substitution and attachment-frontier conditions.  Often a candidate structure is tested against a #$ContextSensitiveGrammar with a computer program that uses a general algorithm (like a general Turing Machine) to help parse the string into nested constituent substructures.  #$ContextSensitiveGrammars are often used to specify #$ComputerLanguages, and they have been used to describe some #$NaturalLanguages.  See also #$ContextFreeGrammar and #$RegularExpressionGrammar.")
(disjointWith YardWork ConflictEvent)
(comment EncouragingForeignInvestment "The collection of events where one state actively attempts to increase the amount of foreign investment it is receiving.")
(comment holdsAfter "(#$holdsAfter ?THING ?PRED ?OBJ ?VAL) means that (?PRED ?OBJ ?VAL) is true after the temporal extent of ?THING ends.")
(comment EmbassyMissionFn "(#$EmbassyMissionFn COUNTRY CITY) returns the #$Organization that is the #$Embassy-TheMission of COUNTRY in CITY.")
(comment FillingAPrescription-Institutional "The collection of #$FillingAPrescription events in which an animal (normally a person) while being cared for in a facility of a #$MedicalCareInstitution receives prescribed medicines from the health care workers of that facility.  In most such cases a charge for the medicine will appear on the patient's bill.  This collection is disjoint both from #$FillingAPrescription-Retail, in which the patient or a representative goes to a pharmacy to obtain the medicine, and from #$FillingAPrescription-MailOrder, in which the patient requests that the medicines be delivered by the postal service or similar organization.")
(comment toFacilitateInSit-Prop "(#$toFacilitateInSit-Prop SIT PROP) means that SIT is a

#$Situation whose success in a planning context is contingent upon its

making PROP true.")
(comment NucleicAcidSequence-GIS "An instance of #$StuffType and a subset of #$GeneticInformationStructure. Each instance of #$NucleicAcidSequence-GIS is an abstract chemical structure consisting of a sequence of nucleotides; each such sequence is represented as an instance of #$List, each of whose members is an instance of #$Nucleotide-GIS.")
(disjointWith HeatingDevice TransportationDevice)
(comment Tonsillectomy "the surgical procedure in which the tonsils are removed.")
(disjointWith Density Volume)
(comment AirToGroundCommunicationsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units trained and equipped for a           mission profile that centers around some aspect of communication           from air-based platforms to ground-based platforms.")
(comment CycLClosedFormula "A specialization of both #$CycLFormula and #$CycLClosedExpression.  The collection of compound expressions of CycL that contain no free variables.")
(comment AchieveFn "Allows us to convert from the passive (#$Goal) to the active (#$GoalAction) form")
(disjointWith AwardPractice ConceptualWork)
(comment LitFuseDetonatingDevice "The collection of #$ExplosiveDevices that detonate when their lit fuse is exhausted.")
(comment Tsunami "A wave or set of waves in a body of water caused by seismic activity.")
(comment Ambassador "A collection of persons; a subset of #$Diplomat.  Each element of #$Ambassador is a person who is the officially appointed chief representative of a country's government in dealing with another government or an international organization.  For example, the collection #$Ambassador includes the U.S. ambassadors to #$Japan, #$Russia, #$China-PeoplesRepublic, and other countries, and also the U.S. ambassador to the #$UnitedNationsOrganization.  A country sends an ambassador to another country only if it officially recognizes that country's sovereign status; e.g., currently there is no U.S. ambassador to #$Taiwan-RepublicOfChina.")
(comment ReformulatorRuleProperty "The collection of intrinsic properties of reformulator rules,
e.g. which of their arguments is more terse, whether they are truth-
preserving, reversible, etc.")
(comment assertionID "A predicate which relates each Cyc assertion to an internal identification number for it. This number is unique within any given image, though not necessarily across images. (#$assertionID ASSERTION ID) states that the #$NonNegativeInteger ID is the unique internal id for the #$CycLAssertion ASSERTION. For obvious reasons, this predicate is #$notAssertible.")
(comment streetNameSuffixText "ARG2 is the street suffix (typically this indicates a type of street or roadway) for the #$ContactLocation ARG1.  This can include #$Abbreviations.  Examples: `RD', `WAY', `BLVD' `STREET', etc.")
(comment ElectroMagneticRadiationSensor "A subcollection of #$Sensor, namely those sensors that detect #$ElectromagneticRadiation.")
(comment GallStone "The collection of objects formed by buildup of minerals in the gall bladder.")
(comment Grinding "A collection of events.  In each #$Grinding event, a substance is broken or torn into smaller pieces through the steady application of force, typically in a circular motion.")
(disjointWith DefenseSystem Memorabilia)
(comment formulaRefersTo "(#$formulaRefersTo FORMULA FORT) is a goal

which succeeds if the formula FORMULA contains the fort FORT at some level. For

instance, (#$formulaRefersTo #$Dog (#$isa #$Dog #$CanineAnimal)) succeeds, but

(#$formulaRefersTo #$Cat (#$isa #$Dog #$CanineAnimal)) fails. In essence, #$formulaRefersTo is a recursive list-membership test for formulae.")
(comment BloodAgentStuff "The collection of #$ToxicSubstances designed to cause swift death when inhaled. They operate by interfering with oxygen use at the cellular level.")
(comment Quasar "This is the collection of quasars. Quasars are intensely bright, almost

stellar objects of tiny volume embedded in a very complex and diffuse galactic medium. 

They are all at least 1 billion light-years from the Earth. 

Although they aren't much bigger than the Earth's solar system, Quasars produce 100 times as much light as a galaxy comprised of tens of billions of

stars. ")
(comment Cimetidine "The chemical compound which is used to treat peptic acid problems.")
(comment FracturingPressure "Pressure in an amount that would fracture human bone; e.g., pressure of a hard blow, collision, or explosion.")
(comment MythologicalHero "This collection is a subset of #$FictionalCharacter and #$MythologicalThing.  Instances of #$MythologicalHero are such heros #$Odysseus and Achilles.")
(comment V-TheLetter "The letter V of the alphabet.  This is 'V' (or 'v') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.  As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterV and #$LatinSmallLetterV.")
(comment Balboa-Panama "The unit of currency for Panama-AtPresent.")
(comment jobAgreement "(#$jobAgreement REL AGREE) means that the job agreement for #$HasPositionRelationship REL is #$WorkAgreement AGREE. Each #$HasPositionRelationship is an employer-employee relationship between a #$Person and an #$Organization. Part of the expected relationship is made explicit by the #$WorkAgreement between the #$Person and the #$Organization. The predicate #$jobAgreement enables us to write axioms that relate #$HasPositionRelationships to the job duties (#$duties and #$dutiesOfAgentInJob) defined in their associated #$WorkAgreements. See also #$versionOfJobPosition that relates #$JobPositions to #$HasPositionRelationships.")
(disjointWith StockTypeByIssuerAndClass PersonTypeByCulture)
(comment ChemicalInteractionFn "The term `(#$ChemicalInteractionFn CHEM1 CHEM2)' denotes the spec of #$ChemicalInteraction consisting of interactions between sets of molecules of

types CHEM1 and CHEM2.")
(comment FreewareProviderFn "This function takes as its argument any instance of #$Freeware, and returns the collection of agents that provide the software for free.  For example, (#$FreewareProviderFn #$GnuEmacs) returns the collection of all providers of Gnu Emacs.")
(comment Cotyledon "The first leaf (leaves) of seed plants; plays an important role in nurturing the developing embryo and seedling.")
(disjointWith Path-Cyclic ConvexTangibleObject)
(comment underspecifiedTypeExpressionOf "(#$underspecifiedTypeExpressionOf EXPTYPE THING FEATURE) says that instances of EXPTYPE, when in some sense \"done\" by THING, are, in some abstract or perhaps metaphorical way,  

\"expressions\" by THING of some underspecified \"feature\" FEATURE of THING.  So for example, one might assert (#$underspecifiedTypeExpressionOf 

#$Singing BarryManilow #$Sadness) to mean that singing events by Barry Manilow are an expression of his feelings of sadness.")
(comment Mycoplasmatales-Order "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalOrder in the #$MoneraKingdom.  It contains the #$Mycoplasmataceae-Family.")
(comment purposeOfPlan "(purposeOfPlan PLAN GOAL) means that in a higher-level instance of #$PlanBackgroundContext or #$PlanSelectionContext, the purpose of the #$Plan PLAN is the goal expressed in GOAL. What this implies will vary from context to context: however there will often be the entailment that Agents in the context who are tasked with carrying out PLAN will themselves have GOAL as a goals. For the present, we remain agnostic as to how a #$Plan may inherit a 'purpose', apart from stipulating that (intentInPlan AGENT PLAN GOAL) implies (purposeOfPlan PLAN GOAL). However, it seems fairly certain that (purposeOfPlan PLAN GOAL) implies that there is an Agent either developing or executing PLAN who has GOAL as a purpose.")
(comment eventTypeAllowsForAttireType "(#$eventTypeAllowsForAttireType EVENTTYPE ATTIRETYPE) means that in the social or cultural expectations of the assertion context, it would be acceptable to wear attire of type ATTIRETYPE.  It is acceptable but not necessarily required.  A stronger relation is #$eventTypeCallsForAttireType.")
(disjointWith SportsPlayingArea GeoculturalRegion)
(comment connectedToInside "(#$connectedToInside OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 is #$connectedTo the inside of OBJ2.")
(comment atPeace "This relationship exists between two multiindividual agents if there is no ConflictEvent in which both are involved and have inconsistent goals.  Typically, this relationship is most meaningfully asserted about countries that could wage war.")
(comment Alto-Singer "Each #$Alto-Singer is a singer having an adult female voice which performs well singing lower notes.  Altos usually aren't required to sing much higher than E at the top space of the treble cleff, and are comfortable singing down to F or G below the treble cleff.  The alto voice is usually richer and deeper than the soprano voice.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-SYNFlooding "#$AttackByComputerOperation-SYNFlooding is a specialization of #$AttackByComputerOperation-DenialOfService. Each instance of #$AttackByComputerOperation-SYNFlooding is an attack in which the attacker sends SYN #$Packet-Internets with phony return #$IPAddresses, resulting in the target server staying open while it waits for the return or ACK packet to complete the handshake (to establish a connection with a remote computer -- see #$InternetPacketExchange).  While the target computer stays open, it is vulnerable to bombardment by additional phony packets, leaving no room to establish a legitimate connection.")
(comment Helicopter "#$Helicopter is a specialization of #$RotaryWingAircraft and #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle.  Each instance of #$Helicopter is a self-powered mechanical device that hovers in the air using a rotary wing.")
(comment BaseballLeftFielder "The collection of all #$BaseballOutfielders who play the position of left field on a #$BaseballTeam.")
(comment BettaSplendens "A collection of tropical fish.  Each element of #$BettaSplendens is a tropical fish of the kind commonly known as `Siamese fighting fish'.  Bettas are native to swampy areas of Southeast Asia.  In captivity, they have been bred for brilliant color and long flowing fins.  Distinctive characteristics are a labyrinth organ, which allows the fish to breathe air at the surface (an auxiliary mechanism to its gills), and a fiercely territorial temperament.  Fry are tended by the male.")
(comment Lipid "The collection of all lipids - greasy, non-water-soluble organic compounds found in all living cells.")
(comment Prolactin "A #$Hormone which promotes lactation.")
(comment CraneVehicle "Large wheeled vehicles mounted with cranes for mounting equipment on other vehicles.")
(comment Crop "#$Crop is the collection of things that are harvested. Most

crops are cultivated and are harvested for food, but there are exceptions. For example,

wild mushrooms brought in from the forest can be considered a crop. Mushrooms are

also an example of a crop which is not part of a plant. Crops such as cotton

have no culinary use, while other crops, such as (#$FruitFn #$CacaoTree), are turned into food products

only after considerable processing.")
(comment tourNightLocation "(#$tourNightLocation TOUR DAY REGION) means that TOUR spends
the night in REGION on the #$CalendarDay DAY.")
(comment eventTypeUsesDeviceType "This predicate is used to relate two collections. (#$eventTypeUsesDeviceType EVENT-TYPE DEVICE-TYPE) means that, by default, equipment of type DEVICE-TYPE is a #$deviceUsed in any #$Event of type EVENT-TYPE. This predicate is a specialization of #$conceptuallyRelated, so it should only be used when the event type is conceptually related to the equipment type. Thus (#$eventTypeUsesDeviceType (#$InstrumentPlayingFn #$Cello) #$BowForStringInstrument), but probably not (#$eventTypeUsesDeviceType (#$InstrumentPlayingFn #$Cello) #$Chair-PieceOfFurniture)")
(comment Beryllium "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of beryllium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment cyclistPrimaryProject "(#$cyclistPrimaryProject CYCLIST PROJECT) relates a human CYCLIST to the Cyc-based PROJECT on which they are primarily working.")
(disjointWith WeatherEvent ChangingDeviceState)
(disjointWith SortingPhysicalObjects Emission)
(comment equivalentAssertions "(#$equivalentAssertions ASSN-1 ASSN-2) means that ASSN-1 and ASSN-2 are two different assertions which are equivalent formalizations of the same knowledge.")
(comment infoPathway-Complete "This predicate can be used to indicate that the instance of #$InformationBearingThing transferred in  some instance of #$InformationTransferEvent follows, throughout the entire transfer, some part (perhaps the whole) of an instance of #$Path-Spatial. (#$infoPathway-Complete TRANS PATH) means that the entire \"route\" of TRANS is spatial and follows PATH. By definition, any #$infoPathway-Complete of an instance ITE of #$InformationTransferEvent connects the \"starting\" and \"stopping\" points (the #$informationOrigin and #$informationDestination) of all of ITE (See #$pathConnects). See also #$infoPathway-Partial.")
(comment LengthFn "(#$LengthFn OBJ) denotes the length of OBJ.")
(comment MiddleEasternCountry "The collection of countries in southwest Asia or, in the case of Egypt, northeast Africa, in the vicinity of the eastern Mediterranean or the Persian Gulf.  Admittedly, a certain amount of arbitrariness is inevitable in specifying which countries are Middle Eastern; still, we've sought a serviceable delimitation based on geography and common usage.  Specifically, the members of this collection are Bahrain, Cyprus, Egypt, Iran, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Kuwait, Lebanon, Oman, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, Syria, the United Arab Emirates, and Yemen.")
(comment MilitarySupportQuantity "A collection of attributes denoting various gradations of logistical

and/or material aid whose purpose is to facilitate the operations of

an agent's military organizations in some fashion.")
(comment Respiration-Bacterium "#$Respiration by #$Bacterium, specifically
#$Chemoorganotrophs, in which the substrate is metabolized with the
involvment of an exogenous oxidizing agent.  This type of
#$Respiration may occur in #$AerobicBacterium or #$AnaerobicBacterium.
Other #$Chemoorganotrophs use #$Fermentation-Bacterium for their
#$BiologicalMetabolismEvent.")
(comment programCopyCreated "(#$programCopyCreated CREATION PROGRAM) means that PROGRAM is            the instance of #$ComputerProgramCopy created in the instance            of #$CreatingAFile, CREATION.")
(comment CruiseMissile-AirLaunched "The collection of #$CruiseMissiles which are deployed from #$MilitaryAircraft.")
(comment MilitaryNuclearWeaponsProgram "The collection of organized research and development activities performed by military organizations for the purpose of creating #$NuclearWeapons.")
(comment processRunBy "#$processRunBy is used to assert that an agent intentionally initiates a computer process.          (#$processRunBy PROCESS AGENT) means that agent AGENT initiates computer process PROCESS.")
(comment Bupropion "A #$PharmaceuticalType which is a subcategory of #$AntiDepressant.")
(comment DenseAsIron "BTW, #$Iron's specific gravity is 7.86")
(comment chairperson-OrganizationalRole "(#$chairperson-OrganizationalRole ORG CHAIR) means that CHAIR

presides over the proceedings or deliberations of ORG in the capacity

of a #$Chairman.  As a rule, an organization can have only one chairperson.")
(comment ApplicationVirus "This is the collection of all elements of #$ComputerVirus which infect an 
    application program and are therefore activated at some point during the use
    of that application.")
(comment vehicleCargoCapacity-Volume "(#$vehicleCargoCapacity-Volume ?VEH ?VOL) means that ?VOL is the volume of material that can be transported in the cargo-carrying region of ?VEH (a vehicle).")
(disjointWith Distance IntervalOnNumberLine)
(comment UnitOfBandwidth "A specialization of  #$UnitOfComputerResourceCapacity. Each instance of this collection represents a standard unit of computer bandwidth (the maximum speed at which data can be transmitted between computers in a network).")
(comment MovingCompany "The collection of companies that provide transportation of goods, in particular household or business furnishings being transported because of the relocation of the owner of the goods.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperationActionType "The collection of all action types which are typically involved in electronic attack. At present, this collection is
extensionally defined.")
(comment SideTwoFn "#$SideTwoFn denotes one of the two symmetrical parts of an
instance of #$PartwiseSymmetricObject. Cf #$SideOneFn. Example: a
#$PhonographRecord has 2 symmetric sides divided by a plane cutting
longitudinally through it.")
(comment weaponRounds "The number of #$ProjectileSlug-Bullets that can be fired consecutively without reloading. For most #$MachineGuns this is a large number > 100, whereas for most #$Pistols it is somewhere between 1 and 6.")
(comment Leftward "From the perspective of a specified observer, A is #$Leftward of B if from the observer's perspective B is located further toward the positive end of the Cartesian x axis than is A.")
(comment Climbing-Recreational "This is the collection of #$Climbing

events which are performed for recreation or as a sport.")
(comment textParagraph "(#$textParagraph TEXTMT N STRING) means that STRING is the Nth paragraph in the text of TEXTMT.")
(comment (LowAmountFn ThermalConductivity) "A measurable physical attribute.  This is the element of #$ThermalConductivity that represents the level of thermal conductivity in an object that conducts virtually no heat.")
(comment AncientEgypt-LouvreCollection "The collection of Egyptian object of art exposed in the Louvre.")
(comment Neutron "A specialization of #$Nucleon.  Each instance of #$Neutron is a nucleon with an electrical charge of 0.")
(comment OralHerpes "A contagious disease which is caused by the herpes simplex virus, type 1 (HSV-1).  This virus is related to HSV-2, the virus which causes #$GenitalHerpes.   #$OralHerpes usually results in recurring cold sores on the mouth, but the carrier may be asymptomatic for long periods of time (or forever).  This disease is transmittable by skin to skin contact, and currently has no cure.")
(comment kePredArgStrongSuggestionPreds "(#$kePredArgStrongSuggestionPreds PRED N BINPRED) means that
if the relation expression (PRED . ARGS) is known, and ARGN appears as
the Nth argument in (PRED . ARGS) it is strongly suggested that Cyc
know there exists a THING such that (BINPRED ARGN THING).")
(disjointWith WaterTransportationDevice Train-TransportationDevice)
(comment BactericidalAntibiotic "The strongest kind of #$Antibiotics, capable of killing bacteria,
used in most severe #$BacterialInfections. This kind of drug is also used
when the host's #$ImmuneSystem is impaired.")
(comment IBTSeriesType "A collection of collections.  Instances of #$IBTSeriesType are collections of InformationBearingThings belonging to a single, named series.  The sense of series here is not the broad one which includes the production order of multiple copies, but rather a narrower notion.  Each series element (e.g., a particular issue of the New York Times) is not an IBTSeriesType but is instead an instance of #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType, because all instances (particular copies) of a single series element will have identical information.  For example, (#$isa #$StarTrek-Classic #$IBTSeriesType), but (#$MediaSeriesNthFn #$StarTrek-Classic 17) is not.  (#$isa #$USAToday-TheNewspaper #IBTSeriesType), but (#$MediaSeriesByDateFn #$USAToday-TheNewspaper (#$DayFn 2 (#$MonthFn #$May (#$YearFn 1998)))) is not.  The information content of that set of copies will be substantially different from the information content of another element of the same series.  For example, all copies of the May 2, 1998 USA Today share the same information, but only a small amount of information is shared between the May 2 and May 3 issues of any year.")
(comment Play-CW "The collection of #$Narratives intended to be instantiated in #$PlayPerformances.")
(comment Antihistamine "Drugs which are used to alleviate the symptoms associated with allergies.")
(comment UnitOfTemperature "The collection of functions which return elements of #$Temperature.  E.g., (#$DegreeFahrenheit 451) denotes a #$Temperature of 451 F.")
(comment productionCapacityDuring "(#$productionCapacityDuring PT PRODUCT-TYPE THING AMOUNT) means that the #$NonNegativeScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the greatest possible amount of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE that could be produced by the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  PT might, for example, be a #$Country or a #$Business.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  If AMOUNT is a #$Rate, AMOUNT indicates what would be the average rate of production of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE by PT during the temporal extent of THING if PT were producing PRODUCT-TYPE at the limit of its capacity.")
(comment FederalTaxReturn "The collection of all #$TaxReturns for taxes owed to the U.S. federal government.")
(comment CountryFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction for referring to the country of a person (when you don't know what that might be).")
(comment (Milli Meter) "This is a unit of length derived by dividing a meter by 1000 - in the real world this is about the size of half a pin head.")
(comment InstantFoodOrDrink "A collection of stuff normally eaten or drunk by humans. Instances of #$InstantFood are instances of (#$FoodOrDrinkForFn #$Person) that are made from an instance of #$InstantFoodMix by adding other ingredients, mixing ingredients together, and/or heating or chilling. An instance of #$InstantFoodMix can be converted into an instance of #$InstantFood in a short amount of time, with a small amount of effort, equipment and expertise, and with the addition of only staple food items such as water, milk, eggs, etc. Examples include reconstituted frozen concentrated fruit juice, ramen noodles, and jello. Not included are foods that require only unwrapping or washing before eating. Something must be added, mixed together, and/or heated or chilled.")
(comment AdenineDeoxyribonucleotide "A collection of compounds consisting of a #$Adenine-Base and a phosphate group linked with #$Deoxyribose.  Its abbreviation is A, and it pairs with #$ThymineDeoxyribonucleotide or #$UracilRibonucleotide, depending on the process.")
(comment GrassFamily "All individual plants from the order of Grasses, which includes cereal grains, bamboo, turf grass, etc.")
(comment cavityInteriorRegionOf "(#$cavityInteriorRegionOf INT OBJ) means that INT is all of the interior space (see #$CavityInteriorRegion) within the cavity or cavities (possibly discontinuous chambers, passages, pockets, bubbles, etc.) that occur inside of the #$PartiallyTangible OBJ.  Note that INT does not include the walls of the cavity or cavities that occur inside of OBJ, just the interior space itself. See also #$CavityInteriorRegionFn.")
(comment ArmoredVehicleLaunchedBridge "The #$ArmoredVehicleLaunchedBridge (AVLB) launcher is a standard M60 or M48 tank chssis modified to transport, launch and retrieve the 60-foot span, Military Load Class (MLC) 60 AVLB.  The tank chassis is modified by the removal of the turret and weapons, a special basket assembly is fitted into the turret will and reinforcement beams are welded to the inside of the hull. A bridge carrying rack on the hull rear provides the necessary support for the bridge during transport.  The bridge is capable of carrying MLC 60 track loads across a 17.4 meter (57 foot) gap with unprepared abutments and 18.3 meter (60 foot) gap with prepared abutments.  The AVLB launcher can launch and retrieve the AVLB on slopes up to 15% and on side slopes up to 8%.  System mobility is compatible with the supported combat vehicles.  The AVLB travels with maneuvering Tank and Mechanized Infantry formations.  The assault launcher can launch the bridge without exposing bridge personnel to enemy fire and can retrieve the bridge from either end.  (Source: Engineer Systems Handbook, 4/97)")
(comment fileCopyModifiedInPlace "(#$fileCopyModifiedInPlace EVENT COPY) means that COPY is the ComputerProgramCopy modified in place in the event EVENT. The low-level properties of COPY like its size and location are not changed by EVENT.")
(disjointWith Isthmus LandBody)
(comment Methionine "A collection of organic compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.
These compounds are an essential component of the diet and furnishes
both methyl groups and sulfur necessary for metabolism.  Its
abbreviations are Met and M.")
(comment TLReifiedNatFn "Denotes a reified nat term at the TL: arg1 is the formula of the nat.")
(comment Inviting-CommunicationAct "Issuing an invitation to someone.  The host suggesting that someone attend or participate in a specific event.")
(comment HeavyAttackHelicopterUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of heavily armed military units that rely on the use of attack helicopters for closing with and engaging the enemy.")
(comment Flying "The collection of all events of sustainable locomotion of an object through the air or other piece of free space. The #$providerOfMotiveForce must be able to remain aloft as long as it doesn't tire out or exhaust its fuel supply. Thus jumping and falling do not count.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (RightObjectOfPairFn FourthRib) Tuberosity) "")
(comment ObjectDenotedByFn "This is a parser-generated stub the sole purpose of which is to
remind those of us in the Logical Form group of the enormity of the task.")
(comment WetTShirtContest "A kind of beauty contest featuring #$FemalePersons wearing #$Wet #$T-Shirts")
(comment TradeAssociation "#$TradeAssociation is a collection of #$Organizations. Each element of #$TradeAssociation is an organization whose main function is to serve as an advocate for the commercial interests of either a set of member organizations or a particular industry. An example of the first is the #$EuropeanFreeTradeAssociation and an example of the second is the #$MotionPictureAssociationOfAmerica.")
(comment WheatKernel "Individual wheat kernels, which are the fruits of the wheat plant.")
(disjointWith Landing SocialGathering)
(comment FuturesOptionsTrader "The collection of all #$Traders that buy and sell futures and options.")
(comment MedicalSupportUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile is centered on           providing some kind of medical support.")
(comment levelOfEfficiency "(#$levelOfEfficiency SYSTEM LEVEL) says that SYSTEM

has a LEVEL level of efficiency.  For example,

 (#$levelOfEfficiency MySprinklerSystem 

 (#$VeryLowAmountFn #$Efficiency)) says that my

sprinkler system is inefficient.  Note, however, that

to be \"efficient\" or \"highly efficient,\" etc. is

 to be such with respect to some activity.  Thus

  #$levelOfEfficiency is a #$PresuppositionPredicate

 that should be used primarily for parsing or in the context

 of an RKF-type interaction with Cyc.  Where the relevant kind of 

#$Event is known, the ke-er should use #$levelOfEfficiencyWithRespectTo.

Where it is unknown, the ke-er might wish to

 do some research and find out, so as to be

 able to use the more informative predicate.")
(comment CollegeAndUniversitySportsEvent "The collection of all sports events whose 

participants are college or university students 

 who compete as sanctioned representatives of their

   respective schools.")
(comment MedicalProcedure "The collection of medical procedures.")
(comment NationalSoccerTeam "the collection of #$SoccerTeams who represent

 countries at #$InternationalSoccerCompetitions, such as 

 the World Cup.")
(comment DateOfNthDayTypeInMonthFn "#$DateOfNthDayTypeInMonthFn is an evaluatable function used to return a particular calendar date from a specified year, month, and nth day-of-the-week in that month.  For example, (#$DateOfNthDayTypeInMonthFn (#$YearFn 2000) #$June #$Friday 2) denotes Friday, June 9, 2000.  That is, it evaluates to (#$DayFn 9 (#$MonthFn #$June (#$YearFn 2000))).")
(disjointWith USCity Country)
(comment Film-SheetOrCoating "The collection of all films that are either instances of #$FreeSheet or liquid coating (#$Film-Coating). Elements are thin (less than 5 millimeters in thickness) flexible sheets (see #$SheetOfSomeStuff).  Some films are removable from objects that they touch (see #$Film-FreeSheet) such as #$PlasticWrap, or a section of motion picture film (see #$PhotographicFilm-Exposed) on a roll.  Others are liquid coatings, such as films of grease or wet #$Paint (see #$Film-Coating).  Dried paint is a negative exemplar of #$Film-SheetOrCoating.--Foxvog, Oct 16, 1998")
(comment Roadside "A long and thin region that is along and #$adjacentTo the side of the road.")
(comment NewsAgency "The collection of organizations that collect and transmit information about current events of regional or worldwide interest.  Elements of #$NewsAgency may be either independent, commercial companies or state-run organizations.")
(comment soleActorOfTypeInEvent "'(#$soleActorOfTypeInEvent OBJECT TYPE EVENT)' means that
OBJECT is the only actor of type TYPE which plays a role in the
#$Event EVENT.")
(comment BuddhistGift "An instance of #$GiftTypeByReligion.  The collection of all #$Gifts that are somehow associated with #$Buddhism.")
(comment Cefotaxime "A chemical compound which is used in injectable antibiotic products.")
(comment rigidityOfObject "(#$rigidityOfObject OBJ DEGREE) means that the tangible object OBJ has this DEGREE of #$Rigidity.  A higher DEGREE of #$Rigidity means more force is required to change the shape of OBJ than for a lower DEGREE.")
(comment logisticsOfficer "A functional role that an agent plays with respect to a
military unit.  The #$logisticsOfficer is responsible for assisting
the #$unitCommander in matters of planning and logistics.")
(comment Marijuana "The collection of all harvested (and possibly dried and shredded) psychoactive leaves and flowers of instances of #$HempPlant (often with seeds and stems included). #$Marijuana is a recreational #$IllegalDrug in the #$NaiveUSLawCOC microtheory, and is also used to relieve intraocular pressure in glaucoma, to relieve nausea in chemotherapy patients, to enhance appetite, and for other medical purposes.")
(comment Pula-Botswana "The unit of currency used in Botswana-1986")
(comment Packet-Network "#$Packet-Network is the collection of discrete blocks of data which
are transported over a network. A #$Packet-Network must contain sufficient
information to be routed from the source machine to the destination
machine.")
(comment Heliport-Physical "An area specifically designated for the takeoff and landing of helicopters.")
(comment paCustomerIndicatedTopic "(#$paCustomerIndicatedTopic PRSN TOPIC) means that in the Product Advisor interface, #$TheCustomer has stated she is interested in gift suggestions for #$Person PRSN related to TOPIC. This predicate is used to track #$TheCustomer's stated preference about which aspect of PRSN's life is to serve as a jumping off point for clarificatory questions. These followup questions aim at learning more about PRSN in order to make relevant gift suggestions. For example, (#$paCustomerIndicatedTopic #$TheRecipient #$HobbyActivity) means that #$TheCustomer has stated she is interested in gift suggestions related to #$TheRecipient's #$HobbyActivitys. In contrast, use #$explicitlyIndicatedProduct to assert that #$TheCustomer has stated she is interested in suggestions about an instance of #$ProductType.")
(comment CornPlant "Individual corn plants.")
(comment Fructose "Fructose, an organic sweetening agent used in soft drinks and other prepared foods.  Chemical formula: C6H12O6.  An isomer of #$Glucose.")
(comment Median "(#$Median ?SET ?FUNCTION) computes the #$Median ?FUNCTION value over the domain, ?SET.  The #$Median is the value of ?FUNCTION at the element of ?SET which lies in the center of ?SET when the elements of ?SET are ordered in according to their ?FUNCTION values.")
(comment CitySkyline "The kind of horizon view found in a city - buildings next to sky.")
(comment JobBank "The collection of all job banks. Each instance of this collection involves a set of employment advertisements and may be a database accessible on a single computer system, or through the internet. ")
(comment FirstLieutenant-Title "This Cyc constant denotes the term of address used for someone holding the rank-attribute of #$FirstLieutenant-Rank in an  instance of #$ModernMilitaryOrganization. May be abbreviated as 1st LT or Fst.Lt. in text.")
(comment containsInfoStructure-CW "(#$containsInfoStructure-CW WORK STRUCTURE) means that WORK contains the information structure STRUCTURE. For example, a #$TextuallySpecificWork (such as a certain of edition of #$MobyDickNovel which is written in English) contains the #$AbstractInformationStructure 'Ahab', as well as the entire abstract sequences of characters that were used in the writing of this edition of #$MobyDickNovel. This predicate allows us to make assertions about the information structures used in a particular work without reference to any instantiation of that work.")
(disjointWith StormAsObject Mineral)
(comment intendedTargetTypeOfWeapon "(#$intendedTargetTypeOfWeapon WEAPON ATTACK TYPE) says that during ATTACK, WEAPON is being directed at instances of TYPE.  For example, (#$intendedTargetTypeOfWeapon Gun001 TodaysAttackInWashingtonDC #$Politician) says that Gun001 was fired at politicians during today's attack in Washington.  To say that a weapon *type* is generally used to target things of a given type, use #$intendedTargetTypeOfWeaponType.")
(comment (TransportViaFn Animal) "Transportation in which an animal provides the force for movement.  Includes horses and other animals carrying people and objects, people carrying objects and other people, etc.")
(comment BomberUnit-MilitarySpecialty "A specialization of #$AviationUnit-MilitarySpecialty.  Instances are units equipped primarily with bomber aircraft, specializing in #$BombingMission.")
(comment SponsorFn-Event "#$SponsorFn-Event takes as argument any instance of #$Event-Organized and returns the collection of all agents sponsoring that event.  For example, (#$SponsorFn-Event Superbowl1999) would return the collection of agents sponsoring the 1999 Superbowl.")
(comment StorageOfSomethingDangerous "The collection of all #$Situations in which

 dangerous things are in storage.")
(disjointWith Kayak PedalBoat)
(comment ProductRecall "A collection of events; a subset of #$BusinessEvent.  Each instance of #$ProductRecall is an official recall of some or all instances of a #$ProductType by the manufacturer and/or distributor who made or sold them.  Products are recalled because after the date of sale, the maker/seller is (or could be) held legally responsible for a discovered failure of the products to meet some #$ProductStandard or other safety #$Specification.  To indicate the #$ProductType involved in a particular instance of #$ProductRecall, use #$objectTypeInCommercialActivity.")
(comment CirrostratusCloud "A collection of veil-like clouds that often cover the sky, causing the appearance of halos around the #$Sun and Moon.")
(comment Mach-UnitOfSpeed "The speed of sound on earth at sea level.  344.4 m/s")
(comment ConfigurationOfComplexObject "The collection of #$Situations in which some complex object, i.e. one with distinguishable parts, is configured in some static manner.  It is in virtue of these distinguishable parts that this collection is a specialization of #$Configuration since a #$Configuration must involve two or more objects.  (When all of the configured objects in a #$Configuration are part of some larger object then the configuration might be deemed to be a #$ConfigurationOfComplexObject.)  Note that a configuration is an instance only if a single object is the thing configured in the configuration.  Hence, the configuration of eleven different chairs in the room would not likely be an instance, but a configuration of a network of telephone poles insofar as the network is an object, having the telephone poles as parts, might be.")
(comment objectHasVisualMarks "A #$BinaryPredicate which relates instances of #$PartiallyTangible to instances of #$VisualMark. (#$objectHasVisualMarks OBJ VIS-MARK) means that the object OBJ has the marking VIS-MARK inscribed on it, which is visible to the naked eye under normal conditions. See also #$objectMarked (which relates a marked object to the event of marking it), #$marks (which relates a marked object to the agent who marks it) and #$markCreated.")
(comment PhysicalContactSituation "The collection of all temporal situations in which two or more tangible objects are touching (see #$touches) for at least part of the situation's duration.  This includes an object's rubbing against another, objects colliding, as well as static touching configurations.  Note that, although most types of #$PhysicalEvents involve some kind of touching, only those types for which contact is salient should be subcollections of  #$PhysicalContactSituation.")
(disjointWith MedicalCareEvent ConflictEvent)
(comment LiftingTariffs "The collection of events where one state reduces the tariffs on imports into the state.")
(comment ShigellaFlexneri " A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom.")
(comment BroadcastOfEventTypeFn "#$BroadcastOfEventTypeFn takes as argument any type of organized, public event and returns the collection of events that are broadcasts (radio or television) of instances of that type.  For example, (#$BroadcastOfEventTypeFn Trial) would return the collection of broadcasts of trials.")
(comment EvenNumber "A specialization of #$Integer.  An instance INT of #$Integer is also an instance of #$EvenNumber if and only if INT is divisible (without remainder) by two.")
(comment holdsBefore "(#$holdsBefore ?THING ?PRED ?OBJ ?VAL) means that (?PRED ?OBJ ?VAL) is true before the temporal extent of ?THING begins.")
(comment PathSystem-Communications "The collection of #$PathSystems each of which is capable of supporting instances              of #$InformationTransferEvents among all its nodes.  Note that many of the links              and nodes of any #$PathSystem-Communications may not have as their               #$primaryFunction supporting instances of #$InformationTransferEvents, but              may still be capable of supporting such instances.  For instance, a #$PathForWheeledVehicles              is not constructed primarily to support communications but can be used for              such purposes.")
(comment Courier-Diplomatic "A member of the diplomatic corps charged with carrying sensitive messages or material.")
(disjointWith FillingAPrescription-MailOrder FillingAPrescription-Institutional)
(comment toInsureInEvent-SitType "(#$toInsureInEvent-SitType SIT SITTYPE) means that SIT isa

a #$Situation whose success in a planning context is contingent on a

situation of type SITTYPE 'happening'.")
(comment RemovalOfUniqueBodyPart "A #$RemovalSurgery in which the person has only one of the thing removed, like an Appendectomy.")
(comment Hostile "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being hostile. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment AmphibiousUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all land units which are trained and           equipped to move to their places of deployment by water vehicles.")
(comment CycLRuleAssertion "The subcollection of semantically well-formed #$CycLAssertions whose formulas are rules.
More precisely, the formulas are not
GAFs (see #$CycLGAFAssertion), so they either have more than one literal (and therefore are
non-atomic) or they quantify over some free variables (and therefore are non-ground).
Any free variables are implicitly universally quantified.")
(comment keIrrelevantTerm "(#$keIrrelevantTerm TERM) means that printed representations of TERM (for example, via #$preferredGenUnit) should not show up in any RKF-based interface. (#$keIrrelevantTerm TERM) does not entail that inferences involving TERM will be ignored.  This is a general predicate and has several spec preds which should be used in order to separate different categories of ke irrelevance.  This separation will aid in controlling which terms should be seen in different types of KFD/UIA interactions and which terms should be used in inferences based upon ke irrelevance.  For upper ontology terms use #$keIrrelevantTerm-UpperOntologyConcept, for internal terms use #$keIrrelevantTerm-InternalCycTerm, for general experimental terms use #$keIrrelevantTerm-ExperimentalVocabulary and for terms created in the attribute cleanup use #$keIrrelevantTerm-AttributeCleanupVocabulary.")
(comment actionEpiphenomena "(#$actionEpiphenomena Action Event) asserts that the event was 'caused by' the Action, but not necessarily on
         purpose. E.g. 'it is raining so my car got wet', describes an event of the car getting wet, which is
         epiphenominal to the raining 'action'. Typically this is used with #$GenericPurposefulAction to distinguish side
         effects from the intended result. Note that the Action can really be an #$Event in Cyc terms; that is, it is
         not something necessarily #$doneBy an agent (other than the weather), though we may think it has. A
         counterexample is 'My sister hit me so my arm hurts', since the hurting arm was presumably on purpose. But 'My
         sister hit me so I'm in a bad mood' is more likely epiphenominal.")
(disjointWith DevisedStructuredActivity ConceptualWork)
(comment PointDetonatingWeapon "The collection of #$ExplosiveDevices which detonate upon impact.")
(comment HailStormProcess "A storm which is also a precipitation process during which the objects falling are #$HailStone(s).")
(comment NationalGovernmentEmployee "A specialization of #$GovernmentEmployee.  Each instance of #$NationalGovernmentEmployee is a person who is employed by the national government of some instance of #$Country.  Instances of #$NationalGovernmentEmployee would include, among others, heads of national governments, diplomats, and members of a nation's armed forces.")
(comment unitTypeText "ARG2 is a #$CharacterString (possibly an #$Abbreviation)  indicating the type of unit for the #$Address-LocationDesignator for the #$ContactLocation ARG1.  Examples: `BLDG', `APT', `SUITE', `DEPT', etc.")
(comment Ductility "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity.  Each instance of #$Ductility is a specific capacity of a physical material to be stretched, drawn, or hammered thin without breaking.  Different degrees of ductility may be represented using a #$GenericValueFunction.  Ductilities of objects are indicated with the predicate #$ductilityOfObject.")
(comment AirDefenseGun "A collection.  Each instance of #$AirDefenseGun is a #$Gun designed
to defend against aerial military attack by #$MilitaryAircraft.")
(comment KidneyStone "The collection of objects formed by buildup of minerals in the kidney.")
(comment typeConnotes "When an abstract agent perceives or thinks about an instance of ARG1, this causes the agent to think of ARG2 with a strength of assocation indicated by ARG3.  See also #$connotes.")
(comment negationMt "(#$negationMt MT-1 MT-2) means that the domain assumptions of the #$Microtheory MT-1 are inconsistent with those of the #$Microtheory MT-2, and no lifting can occur between MT-1 and MT-2 (i.e. assertions made in one microtheory should not be made visible to the other microtheory). For cases where two microtheories differ not in domain assumptions but purely in content (assertions made within those microtheories), see the less specialized #$contradictoryMt.")
(disjointWith SteeringADeviceByHand CreatingAnArtifact)
(comment BotulinumToxin "A #$ToxicSubstance produced by the bacterium Clostridium botulinum. Causes #$Botulism when ingested in sufficient amounts.")
(comment DwarfStar "There are essentially two sorts of histories of stars

which involve dwarf stages. Red dwarfs burn for around 30 billion years before

their conversion of hydrogen into helium halts. They then become brown dwarfs

and finally black dwarfs, when they stop cooling. Stars like our sun will become

red giants before becoming white dwarfs, when their conversion of hydrogen into helium

stops. Finally they too will become black dwarfs when they stop cooling.")
(comment UlcerMedication "Drugs which are used to treat stomach ulcers and related conditions. ")
(comment ArtGalleryHoldings "The collection of groups of art objects that constitute the holdings of a particular art gallery.")
(comment BruisingPressure "Pressure in an amount that would quickly bruise a human being; e.g., pressure of a blow or of a very heavy weight.")
(comment W-TheLetter "The letter W of the alphabet.  This is 'W' (or 'w') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.  As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterW and #$LatinSmallLetterW.")
(comment Dollar-TrinidadAndTobago "The unit of currency for Trinidad&Tobago-AtPresent.")
(disjointWith StockTypeByIssuerAndClass SpatialThingTypeByShape)
(comment Ozone "A triatomic allotropic form of the chemical element #$Oxygen, O3. Pure #$Ozone is an unstable, faintly bluish gas with a characteristic fresh, penetrating odor. Below its boiling point (-112 C) ozone is a dark blue liquid a blue-black crystalline solid. It is formed in the #$OzoneLayer-PlanetEarth (part of #$Stratosphere-PlanetEarth) by the action of solar ultraviolet light on #$Oxygen.")
(comment Wildfire "This is the collection of wildfires. A wildfire is

an uncontrolled large-scale fire in a wilderness area. Many wildfires are

#$NaturalHazards because they are started by lightning or some other

natural phenomenon. Other wildfires are the result of human activity.")
(comment Autotroph "The collection of organisms capable of manufacturing organic nutrients from inorganic raw materials.  Photosynthetic plants fall into this category, as do certain bacteria.  See #$Photosynthesis-Generic.  Cf. #$Heterotroph.")
(comment PenisEnlargement-Surgical "A collection of #$Surgery #$Events in which a #$Penis of a #$MalePerson is enlarged.             Sometimes referred to as 'enhancement phalloplasty'.  #$PenisEnlargement-NonSurgical refers to nonsurgical procedures with the same goal.")
(comment PlayingPinball "The collection of all events of playing pinball, a game played on a            #$PinballMachine, with a sloping board down which a ball rolls, which            the player has to prevent reaching the bottom.")
(comment CentralPeakUpliftOfCrater "A topographical peak within the #$CraterBasin of an #$ImpactCrater.")
(comment ArbitraryUnion "An #$ArbitraryUnion is a collection whose extent is the arbitrary agglomeration of two or more other collections.  Merely being a union of two other collections is not sufficient -- the union must be an arbitrary one in which it is difficult to state any interesting property about the union other than the specification of the collections which together make up its extent.  For example, a concept like CoyoteOrRoadRunner would likely be an #$ArbitraryUnion, whereas #$Person, which is the union of #$MalePerson and #$FemalePerson is definitely not.")
(comment AntiAircraftWeapon "A collection.  Each instance is a ground-based #$Weapon designed to attack and bring down aircraft.  Those #$AntiAircraftWeapons that are not designated as #$AntiAircraftGuns, such as #$Missiles, will be classified simply as #$AntiAircraftWeapons.")
(comment Exon-GIS "A nucleic acid sequence that appears in a
#$NucleicAcidMolecule, either DNA or RNA, in a eukeriotic cell.  An
exon is a fragment of a coding sequence which, when joined together
with other exons as expressed in a molecule of messenger RNA, codes
for a protein.")
(comment numberOfPrescriptionsByDocTypePayerDuring "(#$numberOfPrescriptionsByDocTypePayerDuring DOCTYPE DRUGTYPE RXFILLTYPE PAYER PERIOD NUM) means that DOCTYPEs had NUM prescriptions of type RXFILLTYPE filled for DRUGTYPE and paid by PAYER during PERIOD.  RXFILLTYPE may be #$FillingAPrescription-Retail, #$FillingAPrescription-MailOrder, #$FillingANewPrescription, #$FillingARefillPrescription, intersections of these, or merely #$FillingAPrescription.")
(comment FloorPlan "The collection of information bearing objects that contain information about the layout (spatial configuration) of the interior space of a construction artifact.")
(comment ThingConformingToKosherDietaryLaws "This is the attribute of being kosher. Being kosher means conforming

to Jewish laws dealing with food. The attribute can apply to anthing

related to food: kitchens, slaughtering techniques, diets, food items.")
(comment Soprano-Singer "Each #$Soprano-Singer is a singer having an adult female voice which performs well in the upper registers.  Every decent soprano can sing comfortably up to the G above the treble cleff, and often higher.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-UDPPacketStorm "#$AttackByComputerOperation-UDPPacketStorm is a subset of #$AttackByComputerOperation-DataFloodingOSCrashing.   It is the collection of instances of UDP packet storming attacks.  In this kind of attack, the attacker floods the victim's machine with UDP #$Packet-Internets.  Unlike other versions of UDP packet electronic attacks, such as those involving the use of a #$BonkProgram, the UDP packets may not be corrupt or malformed. Instances of #$AttackByComputerOperation-UDPPacketStorm are successful when they congest the victim's computer until it cannot handle the incoming data and fails or undergoes an instance of #$ComputerCrashing.")
(comment InflatableBoat "#$InflatableBoat is a specialization of #$Watercraft-Small. Each instance of #$InflatableBoat is composed of some fabric or membrane, which is inflated with air to give it buoyancy on water.")
(comment OperaPerformance "#$OperaPerformance is the collection of events which are performed in a theatre, for an audience, and are characterized as follows: a drama in which the actors, including soloists, ensembles and choral singers, sing their parts, in the form of arias, recitatives and choruses, which are generally accompanied by an orchestra. Also characteristic of opera are elaborate, and even extravagant, stage sets and costumes.")
(comment BaseballPlayerTypeByPosition "#$BaseballPlayerTypeByPosition is a collection of collections. Each element is a collection of #$BaseballPlayers who play the same position on a #$BaseballTeam. An example is #$BaseballCatcher. The motivation for creating this collection is to make use of a faceting of #$BaseballPlayer to generate English questions to aid classification. See #$NoteAboutHowFacetAssertionsAreUsed.")
(comment MillionBarrelsPerDay "A function which returns an element of #$FlowRate, that is, a volume per unit of time.  One million barrels per day -- (#$MillionBarrelsPerDay 1) or (#$BarrelsPerDay 1000000) -- is about 158.97 million #$Liters per day.")
(comment EightPersonInflatableBoat "The collection of military inflatable boats that can accommodate eight people.")
(comment Flyfishing "A specialization of #$Fishing. #$Flyfishing employs real or artificial flies or other insects as lures. The lure is attached to the end of the fishing line, and the fisher attempts to cast the lure in such a way so that the fish will think that an insect has just alighted on the surface of the water. To achieve this effect, the flyfisher sometimes waves the lure back and forth overhead several times in the process of casting, so that the lure will touch the surface of the water before any part of the line does. Cf. #$FishingLine.")
(comment Neptunium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of neptunium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.  This unit could probably just as well be called Neptunium or NeptuniumStuff")
(comment agreementMaturity "The predicate that relates an #$Agreement, such as a #$Bond or a #$LoanAgreement to the #$Date at which it matures or becomes due and payable to the purchaser (the investor) or #$creditor.")
(disjointWith MicroPhysicalEvent WeatherEvent)
(comment definingTimeUnit "(#$definingTimeUnit ?CALENDAR-INTERVAL-TYPE ?TIME-UNIT) means that the #$CalendarCoveringType, ?CALENDAR-INTERVAL-TYPE, and the unit of time, ?TIME-UNIT, are defined in terms of each other.  For example, (#$definingTimeUnit #$CalendarDay #$DaysDuration).")
(comment subsumingAssertions "(#$subsumingAssertions SPEC-ASSN GENL-ASSN) means that GENL-ASSN is a more general assertion which trivially subsumes the more specific assertion SPEC-ASSN.  For example, (#$subsumingAssertions (#$isa #$AbrahamLincoln #$Person)) (#$isa #$AbrahamLincoln #$MalePerson)). In effect, this predicate states that SPEC-ASSN is known to be redundant, since GENL-ASSN trivially implies it.  This is useful for flagging intentional redundancies in the knowledge base.")
(comment RockMusicTypeByStyle "Instances divide up #$RockMusic by style, rather than by geographic region.  Note that this is NOT a spec of #$MusicTypeByGenre.")
(comment boilingPoint "(#$boilingPoint STUFF TEMP) means that TEMP is the temperature at which the substance STUFF changes from having the attribute #$Liquid-StateOfMatter to #$Gaseous-StateOfMatter (when sufficient energy is input to raise STUFF's temperature through that point).  Note that the boiling point of most substances is context-dependent; on a mountaintop in Tibet the boiling point of water is much lower than it is in New York City.")
(disjointWith WesternEuropeanCountry MiddleEasternCountry)
(comment preconditionFor-EventTypeEventType "(#$preconditionFor-EventTypeEventType LATER-TYPE EARLY-TYPE) means that every instance of LATER-TYPE requires an instance of EARLY-TYPE to precede it.")
(comment EconomicSupport "A collection of attributes denoting various gradations of logistical

and/or material aid whose purpose is to stimulate the economy of some

agent.")
(comment RecallingAmbassador "The collection of events where a state officially recalls their foreign ambassador from another state.")
(comment DemolitionWeapon "A collection.  Each instance is an #$ExplosiveDevice placed to achieve very specific results.  These #$Weapons are command-detonated devices as opposed to #$ProximityTriggeredWeapons (like #$Mine-Weapons.")
(comment GrossRegisterTon "One Gross Register Ton is equal to (#$CubicFoot 100). It is used to describe the capacity of a vessel, usually a #$Ship, of the spaces within the hull and of the enclosed spaces above the main deck available for cargo, stores, and crew.")
(comment ReadPermission "#$ReadPermission is one of the three #$FilePermissions.  If an account has #$ReadPermission for a file, it can legitimately access the information on that file.")
(comment Fluvoxamine "A #$PharmaceuticalType which is a subcategory of #$AntiDepressant.")
(comment tourMealsTotal "(#$tourMealsTotal TOUR MEALTYPE N) means that TOUR provides a total of N meals of type MEALTYPE for the tour participants, these having
already been paid for in advance by the participants as part of the
tour package.")
(comment DenseAsWater "Specific Gravity of 1 - as dense as water")
(comment ScheduleFn-Sports "(#$ScheduleFn-Sports ARG1) returns the collection of all instances of #$Schedule that include schedule information for #$SportsCompetitions featuring ARG1, (or by members of ARG1, if ARG1 is an organization such as a #$SportsLeague).")
(comment EnteringAContainer "The collection of events in which an object enters a container.")
(comment Bondage-Sexual "This is the collection of instances of ConstrainingEvent in which one or more agents constains one or more other agents for the purpose of sexual pleasure.")
(comment IndependentCountry "A collection of geopolitical entities and a specialization of #$Country.  Each instance of #$IndependentCountry is a distinct, independent geopolitical entity generally recognized by the international community.  An independent country typically has a relatively stable government, enforced borders, its own currency, laws, and culture.  Examples include #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, #$Germany, #$Liberia, #$Mongolia, #$India, #$Taiwan-RepublicOfChina, and #$Honduras.")
(comment NonPersonAnimalAbuse "A spec of #$AnimalAbuse.  This is the collection of all events where people mistreat or abuse animals.  The abuse is either overtly physical or a form of neglect which endangers the welfare of the animal.")
(comment BootVirus "This is the collection of all elements of #$ComputerVirus that infect the 
    boot sector of a disk.")
(comment vehicleCargoCapacity-Mass "(#$vehicleCargoCapacity-Mass ?VEH ?MASS) means that ?MASS is the mass of material that can safely be transported in the cargo-carrying region of ?VEH (a vehicle).")
(disjointWith MarchingBand HeavyMetalBand)
(disjointWith Temperature AngularDistance)
(disjointWith TextEditing SportsCompetition)
(disjointWith ExistingObjectType AttackByComputerOperationActionType)
(comment Fellatio "The collection involving events of oral stimulation of the penis.")
(comment ElectricalPotentialDifferenceFn "The measure of electrical potential difference, measured in #$Volts.")
(comment PositiveScalarInterval "For a measurable positive (> 0) quantity, the ordered sequence of possible values may be thought of as a line. #$PositiveScalarIntervals are the line segments (or points) on such a line,  representing a range of consecutive values, all greater than 0.  The most common case is where the line is just the positive part of the Real Number Line, and in fact where the #$PositiveScalarInterval is either a contiguous set of points there (i.e., a range of numbers) or just a single point there (i.e., a number). Another common case is where the line has some unit of measure marked off, such as meters.")
(comment exposedObjects "If an object is located in some geographical region, and has the same open air around it as does the geographical region then this object is considered to be exposed to weather.  This allows the effect of certain weather attributes to be propagated to the things outside.  Without this slot, if-then rules would be required to encode statements like, `If it is rainy, the things exposed get wet.'")
(comment muchGreaterThan "(#$muchGreaterThan LARGE SMALL) says that the #$ScalarInterval LARGE is

 much greater than the #$ScalarInterval SMALL.  It is important to keep in 

mind that the notion of \"much\" is relative to some scale, and

 so assertions using this predicate should be carefully placed in the right 

context.  See also #$muchGreaterThanWRTScale. #$muchGreaterThan was introduced primarily to facilitate parsing NL, in which speakers often make

 comparisions without specifying any scale.")
(comment (MediumAmountFn ThermalConductivity) "An element of #$ThermalConductivity, which represents the level of thermal conductivity in an object which conducts heat, but slowly. Examples include #$Asphalt and #$Milk.")
(comment in-Floating "(#$in-Floating OBJ LIQUID) means that the #$SolidTangibleThing OBJ is floating on the surface of the #$LiquidTangibleThing LIQUID.  Thus, (#$in-Floating OBJ LIQUID) implies that OBJ is buoyant and that OBJ is partly immersed (see the predicate #$in-ImmersedPartly) in LIQUID.")
(comment kePredArgStrongSuggestionInverse "(#$kePredArgStrongSuggestionInverse PRED N BINPRED) means that if a #$CycLFormula of the form (PRED ARG1 ... ARGK) is known, and ARGN (where N is #$greaterThanOrEqualTo 1 and #$lessThanOrEqualTo K) appears as the Nth argument in (PRED ARG1 ... ARGK), it is strongly suggested that there exists a THING such that (BINPRED THING ARGN) is known in the Knowledge Base.")
(disjointWith WaterTransportationDevice Wagon)
(comment BacteriostaticAntibiotic "The most common kind of #$Antibiotics, merely preventing
bacterial multiplication, the body, the host's #$ImmuneSystem, is left in charge of elimination of bacteria.")
(comment IBTFormatType "A collection of collections.  Instances of #$IBTFormatType are collections of things which store or encode

information.

  Each IBTFormatType is distinguished primarily by the physical format of 

its instances.  For example, #$CompactDisc-Generic, #$HardcopyInformationBearingObject, and #$VideoTape are all instances of #$IBTFormatType.  Non-examples include #$JazzMusic and #$StarTrek-TNG, since these are distinguished primarily by the kind of information contained, rather than physical format. (edited

ABelasco)")
(comment unitMovesHardwareWithVehicleType "(#$unitMovesHardwareWithVehicleType UNIT EQUIPMENTTYPE VEHICLETYPE) means that the military unit UNIT under typical circumstances uses one or more instances of VEHICLETYPE to transport one or more instances of EQUIPMENTTYPE.  The equipment in question may merely be carried, or it may be mounted on the vehicle that is carrying it.  (unitMovesHardwareWithVehicleType UNIT EQUIPMENTTYPE VEHICLETYPE) defeasibly implies that UNIT possesses at least one instance of VEHICLETYPE and at least one instance of EQUIPMENTTYPE also defeasibly implies that instances of VEHICLETYPE are #$behaviorCapable of transporting instances of EQUIPMENTTYPE.")
(comment genlMt-Vocabulary "A specialization of #$genlMt, which relates Cyc microtheories to their corresponding \"vocabulary microtheories\" (which define terms used in those microtheories). (#$genlMt-Vocabulary MT VOCAB_MT) means that VOCAB_MT is the #$VocabularyMicrotheory which contains the definitional information for Cyc terms used in no more general #$Microtheory than MT. For example, (#$genlMt-Vocabulary #$InformationGMt #$InformationGVocabularyMt).")
(comment KnickKnackMarketCategory "A collection of items one might find in those stores (see #$KnickKnackStore) that sell a variety of generally useless things. Some examples are lava lamps, bumper stickers, trick devices, and coffee mugs with pictures and/or text on them.")
(comment Antipyretic "Drugs which reduce fever.")
(comment into-UnderspecifiedContainer "An #$UnderspecifiedPredicate used for generating initial semantics for 'X is into Y' constructions.")
(comment UnitOfCurrent "The collection of functions which return elements of #$ElectricalCurrentLevel.  E.g., (#$Ampere 2) denotes an instance of #$ElectricalCurrentLevel that would measure two amps.")
(comment demandAmountDuring "(#$demandAmountDuring PT PRODUCT-TYPE THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the demand for instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE by the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  In a general economic context, PT will often be an instance of (#$GroupFn #$IntelligentAgent).  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  If AMOUNT is a #$Rate, AMOUNT indicates the average rate of demand for instances of PRODUCT-TYPE by PT during the temporal extent of THING.")
(comment MinorityPerson "The collection of people who are members of an ethnic group which is considered a minority group in the country in which they reside.  This means that there is some other ethnic group in that country which the person is not in, which has more people than the person's ethnic group and is not considerd a minority ethnicity.")
(comment MetricUnitPrefix "Non-atomic term functions, like #$Kilo, which take a basic unit of measure, such as #$Gram, and add a metric prefix to it, creating a new derived unit of measure, such as #$Kilogram")
(comment InstantFoodMix "A collection of stuff edible by humans, but not normally eaten by humans. Instances of #$InstantFoodMix are the primary ingredients from which instances of #$InstantFood are made, and do not include any packaging. For a package of #$InstantFood, use #$PackageFn.")
(comment AdenineRibonucleotide "A collection of compounds consisting of a #$Adenine-Base and

a phosphate group linked to #$Ribose.  Its abbreviation is A, and it pairs with #$UracilRibonucleotide.")
(comment argElementOf "A #$MetaRelation predicate for stating a quite general sort of argument-type constraint on a specified argument-place of a specified relation, where the constraint is membership (see #$elementOf) in a given #$SetOrCollection (q.v.).  (#$argElementOf REL N SETORCOLL) means that semantic well-formedness requires that anything given as the Nth argument to REL be an element of SETORCOLL.  (An exception to this is when N is 0: (#$argElementOf REL 0 SETORCOLL) means that _any_ argument to REL, regardless of argument place, must be an element of SETORCOLL.) #$argElementOf is useful for stating constraints that are specified with the use of set-theoretical relations such as #$TheSetOf or #$TheSet. For cases where a constraint can be specified strictly in terms of membership in a certain #$Collection, consider the more specialized predicate #$argIsa.")
(comment Yucca "A plant that is a member of the lily family found in desert regions of the southwest #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica and #$Mexico.  It depends on the yucca moth for polination.")
(comment LowerCaseLetter "The collection of all lowercase or  letters in an alphabetic system.")
(comment LightTacticalRaft "The collection of aluminum rafts which are used in ground military operations to span a wet gap.  Rafts are joined together and an aluminum roadway is laid atop the rafts to form a floating bridge.")
(comment InfusionFn "#$InfusionFn is a Cyc function, specifically a #$CollectionDenotingFunction, which is used to denote various types infusions (see #$InfusionDrink).  #$InfusionFn takes a herb collection as its argument and returns the collection of infusions made with that type of herb.  (#$InfusionFn HERBTYPE) denotes the collection of all infusions made from the elements of HERBTYPE.")
(comment Bartonellaceae-Family "A collection of all #$Bacterium in the #$BiologicalGenus #$Bartonella-Genus and #$Grahamella-Genus.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are vertebrate #$Pathogens.")
(comment MentalHealthNurse "The collection of #$Nurses who provide mental health care.")
(comment IntroductionToFn "The term `(#$IntroductionToFn THING)' denotes the collection of #$PropositionalConceptualWorks which are intended to be introductions to the

topic THING. ")
(disjointWith Cliff LandBody)
(comment Threonine "A collection of organic compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.
These compounds are essential for optimal infant growth and for
nitrogen equilibrium in adults.  Its abbreviations are Thr and T.")
(comment SalesPerson "A specialization of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each instance of #$SalesPerson is someone whose principal job activity is negotiating with potential buyers, finding out what they want, describing what is available, taking orders, etc.  This collection includes door-to-door salespeople, Avon reprentatives, new and used car salespeople, sales representatives for the product lines of large industrial companies, and store clerks working on a sales commission.")
(comment TaxForm-1040 "The document through which a person subject to United States income tax determines/informs the government how much money s/he owes in taxes.")
(comment HeavyLiftHelicopterUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of heavily armed military units that are responsible for airlifting troops to the combat areas.")
(comment CoolingAir "A collection of events, and a subset of #$CoolingProcess.  During each #$CoolingAir event, the #$objectOfStateChange is some piece of air which is cooled.  Every time the thermostat in an office building clicks on, in the summer, and the building air conditioner kicks in, and blowers run to circulate the air to the offices, etc., there is a new instance of this collection (namely one subevent of that whole process --- the subevent in which the air conditioner actually cools the air that passes by it, for a few minutes).")
(comment ProfessionalSchooling "This is the collection of events in which someone attends a professional school, that is, a law 
school, medical school, etc.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn FirstRib) Tuberosity) "")
(comment RidingPants "The collection of #$LongPants constructed expecially to be worn while riding #$Horses.  #$RidingPants may be worn by men, women, or children, and are typically worn for English style riding.  They are typically made of stretchy material with #$Leather or leather-like patches at areas where they will be in contact with the saddle.")
(comment PastFn "(#$PastFn SCRIPTTYPE CONTEXT-TIME) denotes the         subcollection of SCRIPTTYPE whose instances start before the starting of CONTEXT-TIME.")
(comment RemovalSurgery "Surgery in which something is removed from the body.  The removed thing may be part of the body (like the appendix), or something more-or-less foreign, like a tumor or gallstones, etc.")
(comment intermediateGoals "(#$intermediateGoals AGT 

CYCFORMULA1 CYCFORMULA2) means

agent has CYCFORMULA1 as one of her #$goals, but for the sake of achieving

her goal CYCFORMULA2. This doesn't preclude AGT from having

CYCFORMULA1 as an intermediate goal for some further goal

also or also as a final goal.")
(comment WashingInFn "(#$WashingInFn STUFFTYPE) returns the collection of all
instances of #$Washing in which an instance of STUFFTYPE is the fluid
medium used for cleaning purposes.")
(disjointWith Landing IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(comment EarthScience "This is a collection of scientific disciplines 

having to do primarily with large-scale features of the earth. It includes

#$AtmosphericChemistry, #$Geology, #$Meteorology, and #$Oceanography.")
(comment raininessOfRegion "(#$raininessOfRegion LOC DEGREE) indicates the intensity with which it is raining at the #$OutdoorLocation LOC.  (If it is not raining at LOC, it will be the case that (#$raininessOfRegion LOC (#$NoAmountFn #$Raininess)).)")
(comment Form-AIS "The collection of all #$CWInfoStructures which comprise the complete structure of a specific type of #$BlankForms. Every instance of #$Form-AIS has instantiations which are instances of #$Form-StandardizedIBO.")
(comment subjectOfInfo "(#$subjectOfInfo INFO ABOUT) means that ABOUT is a major subject of INFO.")
(comment HumidClimateCycle "A specialization of #$AnnualClimateCycle.  Each instance of #$HumidClimateCycle is a year-long event consisting of weather occurring (typically) in various continental and subtropical regions.  Characteristics of a humid climate include copious precipitation and high humidity.")
(comment gameEquipmentType "(#$gameEquipmentType GAME EQUIPMENT_TYPE) means that at least one instance of EQUIPMENT_TYPE is likely to be used in a playing of GAME.")
(comment SolidSurfaceTrajectoryThroughWater "The collection of all trajectories of motions that pass through water but along a solid surface.  Any #$objectMoving following such a #$Trajectory (see #$trajectory-Partial) is immersed in water but supported by the solid surface.  Examples: the trajectory of a crab walking along the sea bottom, or of an undersea exploration robot, or of a snail crawling up inside the glass of an aquarium.  For designated or pre-existing #$Path-Generics that are situated in water along a solid, use #$SolidSurfacePathThroughWater.")
(comment mtsDisparate-Assert "(#$mtsDisparate-Assert PROP MTASSERTED MTNOTASSERTED) means
that PROPis asserted (in the sense of being locally cached) in
MTASSERTED and is not asserted in MTNOTASSERTED.  It is thus like an
extremely weak version of mts-Disparate.  Weak as it is, it is
anticipated that the predicate may be of some use for certain simple
conformity-checks.")
(comment DemilitarizedZone "The collection of geographical regions declared to be off-limits to military operations. Typically, a demilitarized zone will be situated on the border between two political entities which have been at war with one another.")
(comment HotForming "Forming done at a temperature greater than the substance's recrystallization point.")
(comment ActorOfTypeInEventFn "'(#$ActorOfTypeInEventFn TYPE EVENT)' picks out the unique
object of TYPE that plays a role in the #$Event EVENT.")
(comment Ceftriaxone "A chemical compound which is used in injectable antibiotic products.")
(comment Doublet "The collection of #$Jackets primarily worn in Western cultures beginning in the 15th century and ending in the 18th century.  Typically doublets had a close fitting waist with a skirt-like section below, and were fastened in the front by buttons.")
(comment redundantSentence "(#$redundantSentence FORMULA) indicates that the given FORMULA is redundant with Cyc's existing knowledge.  In other words, FORMULA can already be proven from the current state of the knowledge base.  This is a specialization of #$trueSentence, primarily for reasons of focus.")
(comment (PerFn MillionBarrels YearsDuration) "Compositional version")
(comment TransportProtocolDataUnit "A #$TransportProtocolDataUnit is a discrete block of data
composed by a #$TransportLayerProtocol and passed down to a 
#$NetworkLayerProtocol. #$TransportProtocolDataUnits consist of a header
created and attached by the #$TransportLayerProtocol and data received
from an #$ApplicationLayerProtocol.")
(comment PaddlingABoat "The collection of all instances of #$Boating in which the boat is propelled partially or wholly by means of repeatedly dipping a #$Paddle-Water into the water, pushing or pulling the paddle against the water, and removing the paddle.")
(comment appropriateRecipientForOccasionType "(#$appropriateRecipientForOccasionType PERSON OCCASION-TYPE) means that the individual PERSON has characteristics that make him or her an appropriate candidate to receive a gift on an occasion of the kind OCCASION-TYPE.  For example, someone who has just graduated is an appropriate gift recipient for an instance of #$GraduationCeremony.")
(comment (FruitFn MangoTree) "The collection of individual mangos.")
(comment TVShow-CW "A collection of objects; a subset of #$TVMediaProduct.  Every #$TVShow-CW is a #$ConceptualWork, usually with some sort of #$News or #$Narrative content.  There are two major specializations of #$TVShow-CW:  #$TVShow-SingleCW and #$TVSeriesProduct.  ``Seinfeld'' would be a #$TVSeriesProduct and an individual episode of ``Seinfeld'' would be an instance of #$TVShow-SingleCW, but both would be instances of #$TVShow-CW.")
(comment RyePlant "Individual rye plants.")
(comment RunningVersionFn "(#$RunningVersionFn ?PROG-COPY) denotes the collection of individual running computer processes that arise from the execution of the #$ComputerProgramCopy ?PROG-COPY. For example, if you are viewing this definition via a browser such as Netscape Communicator, then the copy of Communicator on disk which you are executing is ?PROG-COPY, and the real-time process with with you are interacting is an instance of (#$RunningVersionFn ?PROG-COPY). Many trial programs limit the size of the collection denoted by (#$RunningVersionFn ?PROG), in an effort to get one to licence/buy the unlimited version.")
(comment MilitaryAirplane "#$MilitaryAirplane is a specialization of #$Airplane and #$MilitaryAircraft.  Each instance of #$MilitaryAirplane is an airplane typically used by the military.")
(comment oilPriceCharged "This predicate denotes the price that a country charges for the oil it
exports.  As with other global commodity types, this price is determined
by the world market.  A country's revenue from oil (see #$oilRevenue)
is equal to this quantity times #$oilExport.")
(comment ResumeBank "The collection of all resume banks. Each instance of this collection involves a set of resumes, often in electronic format so they may be accessible in a database on a single computer system, or through the internet. ")
(comment RibosomalRNA "#$RibosomalRNA is the collection of #$RNAMolecules that form the core of a cell's #$Ribosome, the site of protein synthesis during #$Translation-RNAToProtein.")
(comment CriminalInfringerOfCopyright "The collection of all persons who infringe copyright to such a degree that they are subject to criminal penalties (as opposed to civil remedies by lawsuit).")
(comment TimeZoneMicrotheory "This is the collection of all microtheories involved in reasoning about 

time zones.  It was created because it is useful to be able to generalize 

over all microtheories of this type in making certain assertions.  This 

collection should not be confused with #$TimeZoneMt, which is the microtheory

containing the most general rules concerning time zones.")
(comment GeneralOfTheArmy-Title "This Cyc constant denotes the term of address used for someone holding the rank-attribute of #$ArmyGroupGeneral-Rank in an  instance of #$ModernMilitaryOrganization.  In the USA during wartime this title is used for five-star generals.")
(comment tourTransitTransporterType "(#$tourTransitTransporterType TOUR MOVETYPE TRANSPORTERTYPE) means that TOUR is supposed to include a #$TransportationEvent of type MOVETYPE using a #$transporter of type TRANSPORTERTYPE.")
(comment (TransportViaFn RoadVehicle) "The collection of transportion events in which a (more or less conventional) road vehicle (see #$RoadVehicle) is the transportation device (see #$transporter and #$vehicle).")
(comment GroundAttackAircraftUnit-MilitarySpecialty "A specialization of #$AviationUnit-MilitarySpecialty.  Instances are constitutionally structured for mounting instances of #$AerialAttackOnGroundForces.")
(comment Knot-Speed "A unit of speed equal to one #$NauticalMile per hour (#$HoursDuration).  This unit is usually only used in nautical references.  One knot is equal to about 1.15 #$MilesPerHour.")
(disjointWith Lifeboat RowingShell)
(comment FissionWeapon "The subset of #$MilitaryWeapons that result in a #$NuclearFission-Uncontrolled                 event when they detonate.")
(comment BodyPartPiercing "The collection of all events of #$Piercing an #$ExternalAnatomicalPart of a #$Person so that an item of #$Jewelry can be inserted through the resulting hole. The collection of all ear-piercing events would be a specialization of #$BodyPartPiercing.")
(comment oppositeOnPath "This predicate relates a customary path such
as a street to two objects that are on opposite sides 
of the path, whether or not the objects are anywhere near 
each other.  (#$oppositeOnPath OBJ1 OBJ2 PATH) means that 
OBJ1 and OBJ2 are both #$onPath-Alongside PATH, but are 
located on opposite sides of PATH.  For more specific 
predicates that imply that the objects are nearer to
each other, see #$oppositeOnPath-Generally and 
#$oppositeOnPath-Directly.")
(disjointWith FinancialOrganization WorkersOrganization)
(comment PrimaryTranscript-RNAMolecule "The type of RNA (see #$RNAMolecule) that is the immediate
product of the #$PrimaryTranscriptProductionProcess in eukaryotic organisms,
prior to capping, polyadenylation, and RNA splicing.")
(comment tourNightLocationTotal "(#$tourNightLocationTotal TOUR REGION N) means that TOUR is slated to spend a total of N nights in REGION, according to its itinerary.")
(comment uncodedFields "(#$uncodedFields ?PTS ?PF) means the #$PhysicalField ?PF is not a coded field of ?PTS.  Values of this field need no interpretation.")
(comment EconomyFn "A function, applied to a #$MultiIndividualAgent (such as a #$GeographicalAgent), returns the economy of that #$MultiIndividualAgent.  For example, (#$EconomyFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica) denotes the economy of the United States, while (#$EconomyFn #$Texas-State) denotes the economy of Texas.")
(comment GraduatedPaymentMortgage "The collection of #$MortgageAgreements whose payments are increased according to a schedule specified by the agreement.  #$GraduatedPaymentMortgages are intended to be used for home buyers whose incomes are expected to increase over time.  They may be either #$FixedRateLoans or #$AdjustableRateLoans.")
(comment loadCapacity-Conveyance "(#$loadCapacity-Conveyance CONVEYANCE MASS) 

 says that MASS is the greatest mass that

   CONVEYANCE can carry before damage

    results to CONVEYANCE.  For example,

  (#$loadCapacity-Conveyance ABSM10Hovercraft0023

  (#$MetricTon 10.5)) says that this particular

   hovercraft can safely carry up to 10.5 #$MetricTons.")
(comment TotalOrdering-Strict "A specialization of #$TreeOrdering-Strict.  Each instance of #$TotalOrdering-Strict is an ordering in which the ordering relation R orders elements of the #$baseSet S into a strict line.  An instance ORDER of #$PartialOrdering-Strict is an instance of #$TotalOrdering-Strict just in case all elements of the #$baseSet S of ORDER are comparable by the ordering relation R of ORDER; i.e., if X and Y are elements of S, then either R(X Y) or X = Y or R(Y X).  One example of a #$TotalOrdering-Strict is the set of real numbers with the usual 'smaller than' relation on those numbers.")
(comment salientDifferenceBetween "(#$salientDifferenceBetween COL1 COL2 COL3 BINPRED) means that while COL1 and COL2 contain instances that are similar in many salient respects, they differ in the fact that for every instance, INS1, of COL1 there is an instance of COL3, INS3 such that (BINPRED INS1 INS3).  On the other hand, instances of COL2 do not bear the relation BINPRED to any instance of COL3.  The differences noted with this predicate should be salient ones, e.g., differences that one familiar with COL1 and COL2 might note if asked to compare and contrast COL1 and COL2.  See #$salientDifferenceBetweenSiblings and #$salientDifferenceBetween-Inverse for closely related predicates.")
(comment keRequirement "(#$keRequirement OBJ FORMULA) states a strong expectation for the term OBJ that FORMULA must be known to be true.  This can be used in rules to state KE constraints and invariants that should be encouraged or enforced.  It can also be used in tools that look for KB omissions that explicitly violate these expectations.  See also #$keStrongSuggestion, #$keWeakSuggestion, #$keRequirementPreds.")
(comment Nucleon "A specialization of #$SubAtomicParticle.  Each instance of #$Nucleon is a subatomic particle found in some atomic nucleus (see the collection #$AtomicNucleus).   #$Nucleon has two subcollections, #$Proton and #$Neutron.  Every instance of #$AtomicNucleus is composed of some number of #$Nucleons.")
(comment EntertainmentPerformance "A specialization of #$EntertainmentEvent. Each instance of this collection is a public or private performance with artistic or entertainment value (#$performedBy instances of #$Artist-Performer) arranged in order for some audience to witness and enjoy it. Examples include #$PlayPerformances, street performances, #$BalletDancePerformances, #$MovieShowings.  Note:  Movies are included even though the performers aren't performing at the same point in space-time as the performance is occurring. But  still photographs are not included, since one would not generally call the viewing of a photograph an instance of #$EntertainmentEvent.")
(comment AreaFn "This function denotes the Area of an object, it applies to 2-D objects.")
(comment EMailAccount "A collection of #$ComputerAccounts. Each #$EMailAccount is an arrangement in which a client has the right to use resources made available by a #$EMailServiceProvider-WebBased.")
(comment ProductProviderFn-NoCost "#$ProductProviderFn-NoCost takes as argument any instance of #$ProductType and returns the collection of agents who provide products of that type for free.  For example, (#$ProductProviderFn-NoCost #$LegalCounsellingService) returns the collection of all providers of free legal counselling, and (#$ProductProviderFn-NoCost #$OperatingSystem) returns the collection of all providers of free operating system software.")
(comment PromotingExports "The collection of events where one state economically promotes exporting its products.")
(comment InternetBroadcastFn-Event "#$InternetBroadcastFn-Event takes as argument any organized, public event and returns the collection of events that are broadcasts over the #$Internet of that organized, public event.  For example, (#$InternetBroadcastFn-Event Trial001) would return the collection of Internet broadcasts of that particular trial.")
(comment changesSlot "(#$changesSlot EVENT PRED) means that the #$objectOfStateChange in EVENT has a different value for the slot PRED after EVENT than it did before EVENT.")
(comment Courier-Generic "#$Courier-Generic differs from its genl #$DeliveryPerson in that couriers typically deliver #$InformationBearingObjects which  either contain sensitive material or are required in HardcopyInformationBearingObject form (or both).")
(comment FillingAPrescription-MailOrder "The collection of all events in which a #$DrugPrescription is filled by a #$MailOrderPharmacy; a subset of #$FillingAPrescription.  This collection is a subset of the collection of all #$MailOrderSales.")
(comment OrgTypeByGeoAndBOSFn "This function enables us to refer to instances of the
#$ModernMilitaryOrganization partition #$MilitaryOrgTypeByGeoAndBOS.
More specifically, (#$OrgTypeByGeoAndBOSFn GEO-AGENT BOS) returns the
collection of all #$ModernMilitaryOrganizations that are
#$subOrganizations of the instance of BOS that has GEO-AGENT as the
#$sovereignAllegianceOfOrg.  Thus, e.g., (#$OrgTypeByGeoAndBOSFn
#$France #$Army-BranchOfService) returns the collection of all French
army units.")
(comment findAnalog "(#$findAnalog ?Src-Mt ?Src ?Tgt-Mt ?Tgt) causes ?Tgt to become bound to the best analog (according to structure-mapping metrics) for the source concept ?Src as defined source domain microtheory ?Src-Mt in the target domain ?Tgt-Mt. That is, find the ?Tgt-Mt equivalent of ?Src as it is defined in ?Src-Mt.  Example: (#$findAnalog #$Iraq #$DesertShieldMt #$Y1Phase2-AllStagesMt ?What) should cause ?What to be bound to #$Iran. See also #$structureMaps and #$structureDiffs.")
(comment MotorcycleTypeByBodyStyle "A collection of collections, each element of #$MotorcycleTypeByBodyStyle is a collection of motorcycles which share a particular body style, e.g., dirt bikes, choppers, panheads.")
(comment Hardwood "includes wood from many deciduous broadleaved temperate trees, including oak, ash, maple, etc.  These trees have wood that is much harder that that of most conifers (pine, etc.) and is used for building furniture, finishing floors...")
(disjointWith Volatility-Physical Voltage)
(comment AntiAircraftUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all ground-based military units dedicated to           defending airspace regions against incursions by choppers and           fixed-wing aircraft.")
(comment GrammyAward "The collection of all awards (#$AwardPractice) designated \"Grammy Awards\".")
(comment GeoculturalRegion "A specialization of #$GeographicalRegion. Each instance of #$GeoculturalRegion is a region united by economic, cultural, political, or religious ties. The exact boundaries for such regions are sometimes difficult to determine, and sometimes it is unclear whether a region ought to count as one. Instances of #$GeoculturalRegion include the #$CaribbeanRegion and #$Scandinavia.  Non-examples of #$GeoculturalRegion include #$NorthernHemisphere-Region, where there is only a geographical commonality shared by the areas subsumed by the region, and the area of #$Nicaragua and #$CostaRica combined, which does not by itself form a natural grouping, but is subsumed by the #$GeoculturalRegion #$CentralAmerica.  Another non-example of #$GeoculturalRegion would be 'Spanish-speaking countries,' which are too geographically scattered to form a #$GeoculturalRegion.  Note that one country may be subsumed by more than one #$GeoculturalRegion : for example, #$Norway is in both #$WesternEurope and #$Scandinavia.")
(comment actionIntendedEpiphenomena "(#$actionIntendedEpiphenomena GPAction Event) asserts that the event was 'caused by' the Action, and it was on
         purpose, but it is not the primary reason for the action. These are usually related to the #$subpurposeInEvent,
         but the latter is more a desire of the agent, and the #$actionIntendedEpiphenomena relates actual
         events (where the agent may be yet unknown). Example, if I hit my sister to make her apologize, and her
         arm is bruised, then I did cause the action, and it was a purposeful action, and the bruising of the arm is in
         any real sense intentional, but the actual goal was to get her to apologize, not to bruise her arm (assuming I would
         have been just as happy if the arm were not bruised). So the bruising is ephiphenomenal to (this particular)
         hitting action, but it is intended rather than some other specs of #$actionEpiphenomena where the outcome was
         accidentally related. Perhaps a better example is if I need to sprinkle my lawn. I may know that the driveway
         getting wet is epiphonminal (not what I'm intending to do). Now let's say the neighbor's kid keeps leaving his
         bike on my driveway. So I decide to do some sprinkling (heh heh). In other words, this action is going to be
         executed not for the primary purpose of the action but in order to bring about the epiphenomena.")
(disjointWith ImmediateWeatherProcess AnnualClimateCycle)
(comment ProductIndicationPredicate "The collection of #$BinaryPredicates used in the Cyc Product Advisor application to represent whether an instance of #$ProductType is positively or negatively indicated as a purchase for the recipient of the purchase. In the Cyc Gift Advisor application, (see #$GiftAdvisorMt) these predicates are used to represent whether an instance of #$ProductType is positively or negatively indicated as a gift to be purchased by #$TheCustomer and given as #$TheGift to #$TheRecipient.")
(comment reformulatorRuleProperties "(#$reformulatorRuleProperties PROP RULE) means that RULE has
the property PROP.  Most reformulator directives express an assertion
of the form 'The reformulator should do X', for some X.  In contrast,
#$reformulatorRuleProperties assertions are stronger, in that they
express intrinsic properties of reformulator rules, and it is a
consequence that the reformulator should do X in order to be
correct.  For example, a reformulator directive could say 'For this
reformulator rule, if in tersification mode, the reformulator should reformulate
the second argument into the first argument.', whereas a reformulator
rule property could say 'This reformulator rule's first argument is
more terse than its second argument.'  The latter implies the former.")
(comment streetNameDirectionalSuffix "ARG2 is the directional suffix for the street address of  the #$ContactLocation ARG1.  This includes #$CharacterStrings such as `NORTH' and #$Abbreviations such as `SW'.")
(comment Pacifier "The collection of all pacifiers.  A #$Pacifier is a device that is used by a #$HumanInfant or #$HumanToddler.  The child holds the #$Pacifier in his or her mouth and sucks on it.  This often has a soothing affect on the child, and may also ease the pain of teething.")
(comment AntiRadarMissile "The collection of #$Missiles intended for use against radar.")
(comment ApplyingAColdPack "Holding something very cold against the skin, in order to relieve an injury.")
(comment holySite "(#$holySite RELIGION PLACE) means that the #$Place PLACE is a holy site in the #$Religion RELIGION, e.g., (#$holySite #$HomericReligion #$MountOlympus).")
(disjointWith TimeOfDayType AccomplishmentType)
(comment ThermalEnergy "The transfer of energy into or out of an object either through
a change in its #$KineticEnergy (which likewise produces a change in its #$Temperature)
or a change in its potential energy.")
(comment PersistenceDistribution "#$PersistenceDistribution is a collection of objects, each of which consists of parameters that together indicate the probability distribution (likelihood of being true) for an assertion or set of assertions.  The parameters for a #$PersistenceDistribution pertain to the `shape' (graph contour) and temporal or spatial characteristics of the probability distribution.")
(comment TransitiveBareInfinitiveFrame "This frame is used for words that take a bare infinitive phrase (e.g., 'eat cookies') as a complement. In HPSG terms: [COMPS <VP[bse]>]")
(disjointWith ProjectilePropelling SteeringADeviceByHand)
(comment ChokingAgentStuff "The collection of #$ToxicSubstances designed to cause hemorrhage in the blood vessels of the lungs, effectively causing the victim to choke to death.")
(comment NeutronStar "This is the collection of neutron stars. A neutron star is the massive object

left after a supernova is created. It typically has a mass about 1.4 times that 

of the sun, but with a radius of only 5 miles. If the neutron star started as a

massive enough sun, it will end up being too dense to support itself and will

collapse, becoming a black hole.")
(comment Antiasthmatic "Drugs which are used to reduce the symptoms of asthma.")
(comment Gallery-ArtDisplayOrganization "The collection of organizations that administer art galleries. Compare with #$Museum-Organization.  Also see #$Gallery-ArtDisplayStructure.")
(comment realGNPGrowthRateDuring "(#$realGNPGrowthRateDuring GE THING NR) means that NR is the growth rate of the #$GeopoliticalEntity GE's real (adjusted for inflation) gross national product during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  (THING will often be a calendar time period.)  That is, NR is the quotient of the difference between GE's gross national product for the temporal extent of THING and GE's gross national product for the time interval immediately preceding, and of the same duration as, THING (as dividend) and GE's gross national product for the time interval immediately preceding, and of the same duration as, THING (as divisor).  For example, to express the fact that Oman's real gross national product growth rate for 1997 was 5.9%, we can say (#$realGNPGrowthRateDuring #$Oman (#$YearFn 1997) .059).  See also #$grossNationalProduct.")
(comment X-TheLetter "The letter X of the alphabet.  This is 'X' (or 'x') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.  As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterX and #$LatinSmallLetterX.")
(comment Tala-WesternSamoa "Local unit of currency")
(disjointWith OrganismTypeByHabitat StockTypeByIssuerAndClass)
(comment objectConfiguredInChemicalBond "(#$objectConfiguredInChemicalBond BOND OBJ) means that OBJ, an instance of #$ChemicalObject, is one of the objects bonded in BOND, an instance of #$ChemicalBond.")
(comment Expedition "This is the collection of expeditions. An expedition is

a planned trip to somewhere for some definite purpose. Expeditions are often

#$Explorations, though they need not be. Unlike purely recreational journeys, 

expeditions can always aptly be said to succeed or fail. An expedition, in the present sense,

may be carried out by a agent-surrogate, such as an unmanned space probe.")
(comment Epicotyl "Part of an angiosperm shoot system; in embyos it is the apical end of the axis of the embryo above the cotyledon(s), which gives rise to the stem and associated organs.")
(comment TactileSensor "A specialization of #$Sensor.  Each instance of #$TactileSensor is a sensor that operates by coming into physical contact with the object being perceived.  Instances of #$TactileSensor are usually capable of perceiving properties such as texture, hardness, and roughness.")
(comment interArgIsa5-2 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).   (#$interArgIsa5-2 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that,  when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the fifth argument to RELN,  a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the second argument  must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then  (RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 INST ... ARGN) is semantically well-formed  only if ARG2 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation of semantic  well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations.")
(disjointWith NetIncreasingFunction NetUnchangingFunction)
(comment subArrangements "This predicate is a 

specialization of #$subGroups that 

relates an instance of #$ArrangementOfLikeObjects to all 

sub-arrangements within it.  (#$subArrangements SUPER SUB) 

means that (i) all #$groupMembers of SUB are also 

#$groupMembers of SUPER and (ii) if SUB is distinct from 

SUPER, then the members of SUB constitute an 

#$ArrangementOfLikeObjects in their own right, over and 

above their being members of SUPER.  That is, either (iia)

the members of SUB stand in certain spatial relations to 

each other that they don't stand in with any other objects

(including any non-SUB members of SUPER) or (iib) the members 

of SUB are instances of a certain #$ExistingObjectType that 

no non-SUB members of SUPER are instances of.  For example, 

a row of corn plants might be a #$subArrangements of a 

cornfield, and the arrangement of dinner plates on a 

nicely-set table would be a #$subArrangements of the 

arrangement of all the items (including silverware, 

glasses, etc.) on the table.")
(comment ClassABaseballLeague "This is the collection of all minor baseball leagues that

  are commonly described as 'Class A.'")
(comment COACommandIntentMicrotheory "A collection of microtheories.  The information in each
instance will inherit to some instance of
#$COASpecificationMicrotheory, and in some cases, to multiple
instances.  Each instance of #$COACommandIntentMicrotheory is used to
specify the commander's intent for the overall purpose of the instance
or instances of #$COASpecificationMicrotheory that appear among its
#$genlMt dependents.")
(disjointWith Exon-GIS Intron-GIS)
(comment TheIntendedOneOfFn "A function used by the HPSG parser system to represent ambiguity. (#$TheIntendedOneOfFn STRING SET) denotes that item in SET which the speaker intended STRING to denote.")
(comment transporterExclusiveToPath-Complete "(#$transporterExclusiveToPath-Complete TRANSPORTER PATH) means that there is an expectation to the effect that the primaryObjectMoving in any complete motion along path from beginning to end will be TRANSPORTER.")
(comment PullingWithoutTranslation "Applying force upon an object (#$pullee) to tend the object to move towards the #$puller, but without causing motion by either the #$puller or #$pullee.")
(comment Nursery-BabysRoom "The collection of rooms in which objects used to take care of a #$HumanInfant are kept.  Changing tables, #$Cribs, and #$Cradles are just a few of the items one might find in a #$Nursery-BabysRoom")
(comment Myeloma "The collection of #$Cancers involving #$MalignantTumors made up of cells in the bone #$Marrow.")
(comment Tenor-Singer "Each #$Tenor-Singer is a singer having an adult male voice which performs well in the upper registers.  Tenors can sing comfortably in full voice (as opposed to falsetto) up to F or G above the bass clef.")
(comment Motorboat "#$Motorboat is the specialization of #$Watercraft-Surface and #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle.  Each instance of #$Motorboat is usually powered by motors (including in-board and out-board motors).  If a boat is primarily a #$Sailboat, but has a back-up motor to use when becalmed or piloting, that is not enough to make it a #$Motorboat.  To be more precise, this collection is the intersection of #$Watercraft-Surface, #$InternalCombustionPoweredDevice and #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle.")
(comment OperaSinger "#$OperaSinger is the collection of persons who make a living as opera singers.")
(comment ComputerBasedTraining "A specialization of #$Training and #$ComputerActivity. Each instance of this collection is a training event in which the primary instructional content, practice exercises, evaluations, etc., are contained in computer files and accessed via computer. There may or may not be a 'live' instructor and/or other 'off-line' aspects of the training as well.")
(comment EmergencyWorker "paramedics, firemen, etc - people whose job it is to help victims of accidents, fires, disasters.")
(comment EndTrayRADAR "A type of RADAR used to find and destroy short-range ballistic missiles.")
(comment TextAboutFn "#$TextAboutFn takes as argument any thing and returns the collection of all texts (i.e. #$PropositionalCWText) about that thing.  For example, (#$TextAboutFn #$JohnKennedy) returns the collection of all written texts on the subject of John F. Kennedy, and (#$TextAboutFn #$Dog) returns the collection of all written texts on the subject of dogs. To refer to collections of physical objects use #$TextualMaterialAboutFn.")
(comment tourHighlights "(#$tourHighlights TOUR EVTTYPE) means that an event of type
EVTTYPE is advertised as being one of the 'highlights' of TOUR.")
(comment ArmWrestling "The collection of all athletic #$Competitions in which the #$competingAgents sit facing each other across a table, place their (typically) right elbows on the table, clasp each other's (again,           typically) right hand, and try to force each other's forearm down so that it touches the top of the table.")
(comment Hassium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is a RadioactiveObject of #$Hassium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment RoadAtlasFn "#$RoadAtlasFn takes as argument any instance of #$GeographicalRegion and returns the collection of all #$InformationBearingThings that are road atlases of that  #$GeographicalRegion.  For example, (#$RoadAtlasFn #$RockyMountainStates-USRegion) denotes the collection of all paper, computerized and other road atlases of the Rocky Mountain States.")
(disjointWith NuclearEvent WeatherEvent)
(disjointWith StoringSomething DisplayingSomething)
(comment InternationalWaters "A specialization of #$BodyOfWater.  Each instance of #$InternationalWaters is a body of water that is considered to be accessible to international maritime traffic and trade.  International waters may be subject to the customs and laws of a particular country, or of the international community.  Examples include instances of #$ShippingLane-International, the #$HighSeas, and, ordinarily, territorial waters like (#$TerritorialSeaFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica), unless these have been closed to shipping in a particular context.")
(comment incorporatedIn " (incorporated Arg1 Arg2) means that the business company Arg1 is legally incorporated in the country Arg2")
(comment IdeologicalSupport "#$IdeologicalSupport is a collection of attributes representing the generic levels of ideological support that one group of agents gives to another.  For example, the Christian Right typically offers a high degree of #$IdeologicalSupport to anti-abortion groups.")
(comment RejectingDiplomaticCredentials "The collection of events where a state officially rejects another states diplomatic credentials.")
(comment Chemolithotroph "The collection of all #$Chemotrophs that process inorganic compounds, for example #$Ammonia and #$Hydrogen, for energy.")
(comment denotesOpposite "The predicate #$denotesOpposite is used to relate English words to concepts that are negatively related to their meanings.  For instance, both #$Private-TheWord and #$Public-TheWord are semantically connected to #$ThePublic, but the two words are opposite in meaning. If (#$denotesOpposite #$Private-TheWord #$Adjective 0 #$ThePublic), we can conclude that the phrase 'not private' refers to #$ThePublic. Note that #$denotesOpposite is a placeholder predicate, signaling the need for further KE to represent the opposite concept.")
(comment programCopyInstalled "(#$programCopyInstalled INSTALLATION PROGRAM) means that PROGRAM is the instance of #$ComputerProgramCopy installed in the instance of #$InstallingAProgramCopy, INSTALLATION.  Compare this predicate to      #$programCopyCreated, which is used to assert that instances of #$ComputerProgramCopy are created, but are not necessarily installed, since installations are instances of #$ProgramAction-HumanInitiated.")
(comment CruiseMissile-SeaLaunched "A collection of

missiles, a subset of #$CruiseMissile.  Each instance is a cruise

missile designed to be launched from a seaborne weapons platform.")
(comment PersonFitForMilitaryService "The set of all people physically capable of modern military service, but not necessarily currently serving. See also #$PersonLegallyCapableOfMilitaryService.")
(comment Nefazodone "A #$PharmaceuticalType which is a subcategory of #$AntiDepressant.")
(comment SnackFoodMarketCategory "Market category for foodstuffs whose primary function is to satisfy cravings for something to eat, usually between meals, usually very sweet or salty.  Typically sold at many outlets, from grocery stores to discount department stores to vending machines and sports events.")
(comment MoneyBackGuarantee "A promise made by a selling agent that the buying agent will be refunded the money paid for a product or service if the buying agent is unsatisified with the product or the product is defective.")
(comment DenseAsOil "slightly less dense than water - floatable")
(comment PeepHole "A small hole big enough to see through.  This unit can be used in the descriptions of periscopes, telescopes, cameras, etc.")
(comment secretary-OrganizationalRole "(#$secretary-OrganizationalRole ORG SECRETARY) means that
SECRETARY plays a secretarial role with respect to ORG, which in most
cases entails secretarial responsibilities that include maintaining
records and files.  However, this role also contains among its
specializations the role of #$secretary-Executive-OrganizationalRole,
which may entail broader responsibilities.")
(comment (ProfessionalFn FigureSkater) "The collection of professional figure skaters.")
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization CountrySubsidiary)
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-OSCrashing "#$AttackByComputerOperation-OSCrashing is the subset of #$AttackByComputerOperation-DenialOfService whose instances are intended to crash computers.")
(comment transporterTypeTransportsType "(#$transporterTypeTransportsType TRANSPORTERTYPE

 TRANSPORTEETYPE) says that a intended function

  of instances of TRANSPORTERTYPE is to 

  play the role of #$transporter in the

   transportation of things of TRANSPORTEETYPE.

   For example, (#$transporterTypeTransportsType

 SchoolBus SchoolChildren) says that one of the

 intended 

  functions of school busses is to transport

  school children.")
(comment AnimalBreeder-Business "Each instance of #$AnimalBreeder-Business is a business that cares for animals, usually of a certain type, allows them to produce offspring, and sells those offspring.")
(comment GettingBids "A specialization of #$CommercialActivity. Each instance of this collection is an activity whereby an agent obtains bids (or price quotes, cf. #$BidOnSale) for items to be purchased. See also #$Bidding.")
(comment derivedProbability-Range "A predicate used for probability statements.  (#$derivedProbability-Range PROPOSITION PROBRANGE) means that, in the applicable #$Microtheory, the a posteriori probability of the truth of the formula PROPOSITION, given (and depending on) the current state of knowledge of all other assertions, is somewhere in the range PROBRANGE (either a real number between zero and one, where zero means certainly false and one means certainly true, or an interval between two such numbers).  In most microtheories, generally, this refers to the derived range of derived probability that PROPOSITION is true given the probabilities (or probability ranges) of the other #$CycLAssertions and #$domainAssumptions of the #$Microtheory.   Contrast this with #$priorProbability-Range and with #$derivedProbability.  A #$derivedProbability-Range depends at least partially on, and is in some manner derived from or affected by, the probabilities of some or all of the other #$CycLAssertions in the #$Microtheory (whether prior, derived or conditional) along with the #$domainAssumptions.  This definition makes no presumption as to determinism versus nondeterminism, nor as to whether probability is only in the mind of some beholder.  The definition allows for any of several different systems of deriving the probability of one assertion from the probabilities of, or conditional probabilities relating, other assertions.")
(comment FontType "A collection of collections. Each instance of #$FontType is a collection of all #$WritingSymbolCharacters that belong to a defined typeface and size. For example, the collection of all 10-point Arial characters is an instance of #$FontType. See also #$Font-ComputerTypeface.")
(comment ditchWidth "(#$ditchWidth VEHICLE HEIGHT) indicates the widest ditch that can be crossed by VEHICLE")
(comment LoanSharking "The collection of activities in which one agent lends money to another at a very high (usually illegal) rate of interest. Often, failure to repay a loan shark in a timely manner results in some sort of harm to the borrower.")
(comment ElectricalPotentialDifferenceFn "An operator in the equation template language.  It takes two arguments, which must be electrical terminal units.  It returns the variables that represent the potential difference between the two terminals.  If none exists, one is created.")
(comment shoppingsAt "#$shoppingsAt relates an instance of #$Place to the collection of all instances of #$Shopping that occur there.")
(disjointWith Proton Neutron)
(comment kePredArgWeakSuggestionPreds "(#$kePredArgWeakSuggestionPreds PRED N BINPRED) means that
if the relation expression (PRED . ARGS) is known, and ARGN appears as
the Nth argument in (PRED . ARGS) it is weakly suggested that Cyc
know there exists a THING such that (BINPRED ARGN THING).")
(disjointWith Trailer Wheelbarrow)
(comment Mare-Lunar "The collection of topographical features where each element is a large circular plain on Earth's moon.")
(comment SubTopicFunction "A collection of functions.  Instances of #$SubTopicFunction are functions which take as argument some topic and return a collection which is a subtopic of the argument given. Examples of instances of #$SubTopicFunction include #$DesignForObjectTypeFn and #$CareAndFeedingFn.")
(comment BodyOfWater-Large "Bodies of water which are substantial in some sense. For example, a #$Puddle or a small #$Creek are not substantial bodies of water, but #$Oceans and many #$Lakes are. A #$BodyOfWater-Large tends to be permanent, not seasonal (though there are exceptions). Large bodies of water count as water area in geographical calculations, while non-large bodies of water do not.")
(comment pathCapacity "(#$pathCapacity PATH RATE) means that the #$Path-Customary PATH has a capacity of RATE, e.g.,  (#$pathCapacity Bridge001 (#$VehiclesPerHour 500)) means that 500 vehicles an hour can pass over Bridge001. #$pathCapacity can also be used to specify other types of flow capacities for paths, e.g., bytes per second over a modem line.")
(comment KnickKnackStore "The collection of stores that sell knickknacks.  See #$KnickKnackMarketCategory for examples of the kinds of things one might find in such stores.")
(comment Ointment "Ointments")
(comment outOf-UnderspecifiedContainer "(#$outOf-UnderspecifiedContainer ACT CONT) states that an
abstract containment exiting relation (and a from/origin relation) holds
between ACT and CONT, where ?Cont is the abstract container employed by the
action ACT.  See also #$in-UnderspecifiedContainer, which is an even more
underspecified version of #$into-UnderspecifiedContainer.")
(comment CruiseMissile-AS7Kerry "The collection of AS-7 missiles. These are short-range

air-to-surface missiles developed in #$Russia, and deployed

in about 30 countries worldwide.")
(comment Education "A specialization of #$ServiceEvent. Each instance of this collection is an event in which some #$Person receives some considerable quantity of knowledge which they did not have before. Any given #$Education event  typically consists of many sub-events of #$Learning and #$Teaching. #$Education events differ from #$Training events in their typically longer duration, and in the fact that one may be 'trained' in practical skills rather than intellectual knowledge.")
(comment BeetPlant "Individual beet plants")
(disjointWith UpperCaseLetter LowerCaseLetter)
(comment DrugTrafficking "A specialization of #$CommercialActivity. Instances are actions undertaken as part of an illicit business seeking to profit from the buying, selling, manufacture, transport, etc., of illegal drugs.")
(comment ReceivingAnObject "#$ReceivingAnObject is a specialization of #$Receiving.  An instance of #$ReceivingAnObject is an event in which there is some #$PartiallyTangible which is the #$objectMoving, i.e., the thing which \"comes in\" to the receiver (the #$toLocation).  For example, the #$objectMoving on an occasion when Lynn Swann received a pass from Terry Bradshaw during a Steelers' game would be a football (i.e., some instance of #$Football-American) and the passing/receiving event itself would be an instance of #$ReceivingAnObject.")
(comment BloodBank "The collection of all #$Organizations that collect, process, type and store whole #$Blood and #$Blood products.")
(comment MentalHealthProfessional "A collection of professional people who provide mental health services such as diagnosis and treatment of mental disorders, counselling, etc. Examples include #$MentalHealthNurses, #$Psychoanalysts, #$CounselingPsychologists.")
(comment Valine "A collection of compounds and a spec of#$AminoAcid.  These
compounds are essential for optimal growth in infants and for nitrogen
equilibrium in human adults.  Its abbreviations are Val and V.")
(comment ScientificFieldOfStudy "A specialization of #$FieldOfStudy.  Each instance of #$ScientificFieldOfStudy is a specialized body of knowledge, theory, hypotheses, observations, and problems, which together constitute the informational content of a systematic endeavor to explain (some part of) the natural world by rational (and frequently, quantifiable) methods, including, but not limited to, induction, falsifiable hypotheses tested by repeatable physical experiments, and deductive proof.  Instances of #$ScientificFieldOfStudy include the traditional hard sciences (e.g., #$Physics, #$Chemistry), the life sciences (e.g., #$Biology, #$Genetics, #$Toxicology), and #$Mathematics.")
(comment TLVariableFn "Denotes HL variables at the TL: arg1 is the HL index of the variable; arg2 is the EL string name of the variable.")
(comment functionOntoSet "A #$MetaRelation predicate 
and specialization of #$functionIntoSet that relates a 
given function to a set whose elements include all of and 
only the function's values.  (#$functionOntoSet FUNCTION SET) 
means that FUNCTION is a mapping onto SET.  That is, 
something is an element of SET if and only if it is the 
value of FUNCTION for some element of FUNCTION's 
domain taken as argument (see #$DomainOfFunctionFn and 
#$valueOfFunctionForArgs).  Such a function is sometimes 
called a _surjection_ with respect to such a set, and if 
the function is also an instance of #$OneToOneFunction,
it is called a _bijection_.  FUNCTION is a mapping onto 
SET if and only if SET is identical to FUNCTION's range 
(see #$RangeOfFunctionFn and #$relationRange).")
(comment LegalPad "The collection of all legal pads: pads of writing paper specially ruled for writing legal notes and briefs.")
(comment LightAttackHelicopterUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of lightly armed military units that rely on the use of attack helicopters for closing with and engaging the enemy.")
(comment Fossil "The collection of all instances of remains or imprints of #$Plants or #$Animals preserved from prehistoric times by the operation of natural conditions. #$Fossils are found in sedimentary rock, asphalt deposits, and #$Coal and sometimes in #$Amber and certain other materials.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn EighthRib) Tuberosity) "")
(comment BlackTie "#$BlackTie is the subset of #$BowTie whose instances are narrow and black and are typically worn with instances of #$Tuxedo.")
(comment MudWrestling "A form of #$WrestlingSportsEvent in which two or more #$Persons wrestle  covered with #$Mud.")
(comment hardshipPropagatesViaRelation "(#$hardshipPropagatesViaRelation OBJ-TYPE1 OBJ-TYPE2 PRED SIT-TYPE) means that when an INST1 of OBJ-TYPE1 is related via the binary predicate PRED to some second instance INST2 of OBJ-TYPE2, hardships of type SIT-TYPE propagate from INST1 to INST2.  Note that INST1 and INST2 do not have to be the same kind of thing, although in many cases they are.  For instance, security weaknesses generally propagate through connected computer systems linked in certain ways, that is, if one computer is vulnerable to being attacked in a certain way so are others connected to it.  We would represent one version of this as (#$hardshipPropagatesViaRelation #$ComputationalSystem #$ComputationalSystem #$equivalentHosts #$Cracking-CompromisingSecurity).  A variant in which INST1 and INST2 would be different is (#$hardshipPropagatesViaRelation #$Computer #$ComputerNetwork #$parts #$Cracking-CompromisingSecurity).")
(comment Poultry "The collection of all domesticated farm birds bred and kept for meat or eggs.  The collection #$Poultry includes members of its subsets #$Chicken, #$Turkey, #$Duck, #$Goose-Bird, etc.")
(comment rationalIntermediateGoals "(#$rationalIntermediateGoals AGT 

CYCFORMULA1 CYCFORMULA2)

means that, 

given the agent's overall beliefs and goals, it would be rational for the

agent to adopt CYCFORMULA1 as an #$intermediateGoals

in order to achieve CYCFORMULA2.

Note that the sense of 'rationality' used here

is merely 'economic' rationality; i.e., rationality

relative to attaining ones goals, given one's beliefs. No

evaluation of the rationality of the ends, or of the beliefs

of the agent, is presumed here. Note also that, as a default,

Cyc assumes that agents act rationally, i.e., that they adopt

as #$intermediateGoals their #$rationalIntermediateGoals.")
(disjointWith LiquidFlowAlongConduit ElectricalConduction)
(comment HolidayGiftBasket "An instance of #$GiftBasketTypeByOccasion.  The collection of #$GiftBaskets that are appropriate for a #$Holiday.")
(comment EnvironmentalStudies "This is a fairly broad collection of scientific and quasi-scientific disciplines 

having in common a concern about the state of the environment. This collection would include #$Ecology,

#$Ecotoxicology, #$SustainableAgriculture, the study of energy consumption and conservation, 

and the study of climate change.")
(comment Phonetician "A #$Linguist specializing in #$Phonetics")
(comment GuitarTablatureText "The collection of all instances of #$MusicalText that are written in #$GuitarTablatureNotation. #$GuitarTablatureNotation is a notation used to describe how a sequence of musical notes is to be played on a guitar.")
(comment ExceptionPredicate "A collection of mathematical objects, which are the #$LogicalConnectives used to express exceptions to rules.  Elements include #$exceptWhen and #$exceptFor.")
(comment SteppeClimateCycle "A specialization of #$TemperateClimateCycle.  Each instance of #$SteppeClimateCycle is a year-long event consisting of weather characteristic of the steppes (i.e., temperate zone semiarid plains).  Characteristics of a steppe climate include: little precipitation, but wetter than a desert; wide temperature extremes, from very hot in the day to cold at night.")
(comment USCity "A specialization of #$City each instance of which is a city, town, or village in the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.  Instances of #$USCity include #$CityOfAustinTX, #$CityOfGainesvilleFL, and #$CityOfLongBeachCA.")
(comment EdemaToPapuleEvent "The collection of events in which an edema turns into a #$Papule-Object, for example in the #$BacterialInfection #$CutaneousAnthrax.")
(comment ProvingGround "A tract of land used by a military organization for the testing and

development of various kinds of military hardware and weapons

systems.")
(comment Trimming "Cutting small pieces that aren't wanted off of an object.")
(comment BinaryFunction "A specialization of both #$BinaryRelation and #$Function-Denotational.  An instance of #$Function-Denotational FUNC is an instance of #$BinaryFunction if and only if FUNC has an #$arity of 2.")
(comment objectFound-Indefinite "The expression `#$objectFound-Indefinite (SEARCH SEEKER

OBJECT)' means that a #$LookingForSomething-Indefinite has succeeded,

partially or totally. It says that SEEKER, the #$performedBy in the SEARCH, has

come across an OBJECT of the type that  was sought

(in whatever sense of coming across the SEEKER thinks is required for

having found it) and that SEEKER #$notices that OBJECT satisfies the

#$searchCriterion-Indefinite associated with the search. Since the arg2 of

#$notices is opaque, it is required that the term in the OBJECT place

match the way SEEKER conceives of the OBJECT. This is why the arg3 of this

predicate is opaque.")
(comment featuredSoloistType "(#$featuredSoloistType COMP SOL) means that the #$MusicalComposition COMP features a single soloist of the type SOL. For example, (#$featuredSoloistType BrahmsViolinConcerto 
 (#$PlayerOfInstrumentFn #$Violin)) means that the Brahms violin concerto features a single violin soloist.")
(comment LocalAnesthetic "Drugs which numb the body to pain and other sensation, but only in the area of the body where they are administered.")
(comment NavalMine-Deployed "Instances are

 #$NavalMines that have been successfully

planted undersea.")
(comment PrintCirculationEvent "A collection of #$Events; a subset of #$PublishingWrittenMaterial. In every instance of #$PrintCirculationEvent, a group of #$HardcopyInformationBearingObjects instantiating the same #$ConceptualWork (e.g., instances of #$BookCopy or #$NewspaperCopy) is created and distributed via the media.  See also #$PublishedMaterial, #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType.")
(comment BroadcastSeriesType "Every instance of this collection is a broadcast series, either a television or radio show.  Each

instance is a broadcast which appears in multiple episodes, usually at regular intervals.  Examples include: 

#$StarTrek-Classic and #$TheShadow-RadioSeries.  A particular episode of a television or radio show will be 

an element of an element of #$BroadcastSeriesType.")
(comment BomberJacket "The collection of #$Jackets extending just to the waist, where they are gathered into a band, commonly made of leather or leather-like material.")
(comment Dollar-Brunei "Major unit of currency of #$Brunei")
(comment (PerFn MillionBarrels YearsDuration) "compositional version")
(comment Parachute "The collection of parachutes. I.e., those large, roundish sheets of fabric which are attached by cords to a harness worn on the back by persons jumping from airplanes or helicopters. Parachutes can also be used for transporting inanimate objects from the air to the ground.")
(comment appropriatelyRelatedRecipientForOccasionType "(#$appropriatelyRelatedRecipientForOccasionType GIVER RECIPIENT OCCASION-TYPE) means that the individual GIVER is related to RECIPIENT in some way that makes it appropriate for RECIPIENT to receive a gift from GIVER on an occasion of the kind OCCASION-TYPE. For example, if RECIPIENT is a #$romanticInterest of GIVER, then it is appropriate for GIVER to give RECIPIENT a #$ValentinesDay gift.")
(comment LandSurveying "This is the determination of the shape of the

earth's surface in limited areas using optical techniques.")
(comment Rye-TheGrain "Individual rye grains, which are the fruits of the rye plant.")
(comment NetworkTraffic "#$NetworkTraffic is the collection of measures of how much traffic individual networks are experiencing.  This can include any kind of network; specs of this collection will refer to particular kinds of networks (e.g. computer network, phone network, communications network, network of safehouses) where the traffic is understood as being whatever moves through the network.  Note that traffic is not cumulative in the following sense: the fact that one network has high traffic does not mean that any larger networks of which it is part do.")
(comment Flaw-Intermittent "A situation in which something has a flaw (see #$hasFlawAttributes, or, perhaps, #$malfunctionAffects) that does not always make itself apparent. In software, an intermittent bug is a bug (#$Malfunction) that does not affect every execution of the software program, but which seems to occur 'every now and then'. Such bugs make related instances of #$DebuggingAComputerProgram harder rather than easier. Sometimes programmers just live with such bugs, rather than fixing them, if they strike infrequently.")
(comment Propelling "A collection of all processes of applying a force which results in translational motion.  Examples include a boy sitting still propelling a toy car by giving it a push across the floor.  Another example; an airplane propeller propels an airplane through the air.  Negative examples include a fan motor rotationally propelling fan blades (#$Propelling is a specialization of #$CausingAnotherObjectsTranslationalMotion and rotation is not translation).  Another negative example is a wagon full of groceries coasting downhill.  Even though the wagon may propel (in a general sense of the term \"propel\") groceries *up* the hill, the strictly downhill timeslice of the motion does not involve the wagon propelling the groceries, since no appreciable force is applied to them.  Note, however, that the wagon coasting downhill is a positive example of #$TransportationEvent.  Another negative example is dropping something (see #$Dropping) because no force is applied.  However, dropping something would still be an instance of #$CausingAnotherObjectsTranslationalMotion.")
(disjointWith AnnualTemporalObjectType WeeklyTemporalObjectType)
(comment instantiatesToRuleMacro "Suppose PRED is a #$BinaryPredicate that is type-level in at least one argument position, and that INST-PRED is an 'instance-level analog' of PRED that is instance-level in at least one argument position in which PRED is type-level.  (#$instantiatesToRuleMacro MACRO PRED INST-PRED) means that if (PRED ARG1COL ARG2COL) is known to be true, (MACRO INST-PRED ARG1COL ARG2COL) is known to be true.  For example, suppose we decide that in a certain reasoning context (#$colorOfType COL COLOR) means that, for every instance INST of COL, (#$mainColorOfObject INST COLOR), i.e., that (#$relationAllInstance #$mainColorOfObject COL COLOR).  We would express this by asserting (#$instantiatesToRuleMacro #$relationAllInstance #$colorOfType #$mainColorOfObject).")
(comment FootwearMarketCategory "The general market category for shoes and boots, accessories like shoelaces and heel taps, shoe polish and brushes, all the usual merchandise of a shoe store or department store shoe department.")
(comment Oktoberfest-Holiday "Each of these is an annual #$Holiday  celebrated for a period of about three weeks during the autumn. The tradition originated in Bavaria in 1810 to commemorate the wedding of Crown Prince Ludwig. Today, Oktoberfest is celebrated as a large festival with food, beer, and music. Some towns in the U.S. that were settled by people from Germany also have Oktoberfest celebrations.")
(comment AreaCodeFinder "The collection of all #$SearchEngines designed to help users find information about telephone #$AreaCode, such as listings by city, number, etc.")
(comment TransferRNA "#$TransferRNA is the collection of #$RNAMolecules that select the required #$AminoAcids and fasten them to the cell's #$Ribosome during protein synthesis (#$Translation-RNAToProtein).")
(comment AnimatedMovie "The collection of animated moving images with sound that people watch on their television screens, or on the movie screen at a theater. Please see #$Movie-CW for a more detailed explanation.")
(comment MasterSergeant-Title "This Cyc constant denotes the term of address used for someone holding the rank-attribute of #$MasterSergeant-Rank in an  instance of #$ModernMilitaryOrganization.")
(comment editionOfBook "This predicate is intended to express the relation typically attributed to a pair of objects by phrases of the form: book x is an edition of the book y -- where x and y refer to #$ConceptualWorks, and to not to any particular copies of those works. Given enough information about the content of two books (including what is written prior to the bodies of the books), and information about their origins (publisher, author et al), it is typically easy to determine whether or not this relation obtains between two books. Typically when (#$editionOfBook EDITION LATEREDITION), EDITION and LATEREDITION will have a common title and author (or at east some common author -- an author might be added -- and at least some part of the title in common), and LATEREDITION will be asserted to be an edition of 2nd or higher order somewhere in the text preceding its body. There will few circumstances in which these criteria will not be satisfied in which (#$editionOfBook EDITION LATEREDITION) is true.")
(comment usedInWPDemoInferencing "(#$usedInWPDemoInferencing FORMULA) says

  that FORMULA is cited by Cyc when asked to 

justify some conclusion drawn in response to

  an ASK during the WPDemo.  This predicate is

   used by the NL team to test English

  generation.")
(comment (TransportViaFn Spacecraft) "The collection of all events in which vehicles, manned or unmanned, leave the atmosphere of earth to orbit around it or travel to other regions of the universe.")
(comment Saxitoxin "A #$Collection. #$Saxitoxin is 

a poisonous substance, C10H17N7O4.2HCI, 

found in certain species of #$Mollusks.")
(disjointWith PedalBoat Lifeboat)
(disjointWith Teaching GameOfChance-Event)
(comment AtomicBomb "The collection of all bombs that derive their explosive force from fission, the energy released by the splitting apart of atoms (usually of plutonium or enriched uranium)")
(comment keStrongConsiderationInverse "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate (q.v.) and specialization of #$keConsiderationInverse (q.v.) that relates a collection to a binary predicate.  (#$keStrongConsiderationInverse COL BINPRED) means that for any reified instance INST of COL, it should be determined whether there is any thing THING such that BINPRED holds between INST and THING, and if so it is strongly suggested that (BINPRED INST THING) be asserted in the Cyc Knowledge Base.  See also #$keStrongConsiderationPreds.")
(comment ProfessionalSport "The collection of all professional #$Sports.")
(comment CirrocumulusCloud "A collection of thin, white, patchy clouds, said to resemble fish scales.")
(comment AnthraxSprayer-PortableWeapon "A collection of weapons.  Each instance of #$AnthraxSprayer-PortableWeapon is a spraying device designed to be carried by a single person and used to contaminate an area with anthrax.")
(comment orbits "(#$orbits SMALL LARGE) means that the object SMALL orbits around the larger object LARGE.")
(comment E-LogarithmBase "#$E-LogarithmBase is the mathematical constant 'e', which is defined to be the base of the natural logarithms. Although #$E-LogarithmBase is an instance of  #$IrrationalNumber, a reasonable rational approximation is 2.7182817.")
(comment GrowingEquityMortgage "The collection of #$GraduatedPaymentMortgages whose payment increases are applied directly to principal reduction.")
(comment WellOrdering "The collection of all those linear #$MathematicalOrderings that are called 'well-orderings' because they (and their subsets) have 'first' or 'smallest' members.  Let ORDER be a #$TotalOrdering-Strict, and let S be the #$baseSet of ORDER and R the ordering relation.  ORDER is a #$WellOrdering if every nonempty subset SUBSET of S has its 'R-smallest' member, i.e., there is an X in SUBSET such that R(X Y) for all Y in SUBSET except X.  For example, if you take the set of all natural numbers and the usual less-than relation among these numbers then you have a #$WellOrdering because there is a lowest natural number, while if you take the set of all integers (including negative ones) and the usual less-than relation among these numbers then you have a #$TotalOrdering that is not a #$WellOrdering because there is no lowest negative number.")
(comment placeName-LocalLongForm "(placeName-LongForm PLACE NAME) means that NAME is a long-form name of the #$GeographicalThing PLACE used by people who live in or near PLACE.")
(disjointWith AnimalActivity Photosynthesis-Generic)
(disjointWith EntertainmentPerformance ChangeInUserRights)
(comment VolumeFn "This function denotes the volume of an object.")
(comment EMailServiceEvent "The Collection of #$ServiceEvent in which an #$Agent is using the services of a #$EmailServiceProvider-WebBased in order to read or write #$EMailMessageTexts.")
(comment barrier "(#$barrier BLOCKAGE BLOCK) means that BLOCK serves as a barrier in

the #$BarrierSituation BLOCKAGE.  See also #$blockedPath.")
(comment keStrongSuggestion "(#$keStrongSuggestion TERM FORMULA) states a strong suggestion that FORMULA should be known to be true about TERM.  This is most useful at expressing suggestions or expectations about TERM which can then be used by tools that look for KB omissions, or conditions that explicitly violate these expectations.  See also #$keWeakSuggestion, #$keRequirement, #$keStrongSuggestionPreds.")
(comment ShigellaBoydii "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom.")
(comment increasesSlot "(#$increasesSlot EVENT PRED) means that the #$objectOfStateChange in EVENT has a higher value for PRED after EVENT than before EVENT.")
(comment tokensCharacter "This predicate is a specialization of #$instantiationOfAIS that relates an instance of    #$CharacterToken to the instance of #$Character-Abstract it    tokens.  (#$tokensCharacter TOKEN CHAR) means that TOKEN    is a physical token or representation or realization of the   abstract character CHAR.  By definition, any character token   #$tokensCharacter exactly one character; conversely, a given    character might be tokened by various distinct character tokens.    Character tokens come in the form of inscriptions, sounds, or    electromagnetic encodings.  See also #$tokensString.")
(comment BrandNamePharmacyProductType "Each element of #$BrandNamePharmacyProductType is a trade name drug product, such as #$ZoloftProduct.")
(comment ProperNamePredicateForNPParser "The collection of all name predicates that are consulted in order
to build the lexical trie on which the Noun Phrase parser is presently 
(September 6, 2000) based")
(comment Courier-Military "(DOD) A messenger (usually a commissioned or warrant officer) responsible for the secure physical transmission and delivery of documents and material. Generally referred to as a command or local courier.")
(comment Codon-GIS "An instance of #$ObjectType and a specialization of #$RibonucleotideSequence-GIS. Each instance of #$Codon-GIS is an abstract chemical structure consisting of a sequence of 3 instances of #$Nucleotide-GIS. Instances of #$Codon-GIS are instantiated by instances of #$Codon-MolecularSegment, which have three instances of #$Ribonucleotide available for pairing.")
(comment Stalk "the stem or main section of a non-woody plant....(we never say tree stalks do we?, but we do say corn stalk or stalk of wild grass.")
(comment in-ImmersedFully "A specialization of #$in-ImmersedGeneric, #$objectFoundInLocation, and (via #$genlInverse) #$surroundsCompletely.  (#$in-ImmersedFully OBJ FLUID) means that FLUID is a body of fluid in which OBJ is completely immersed.  Thus (as a default assumption) every outside surface region of OBJ #$touches FLUID.  For example, fish are normally fully immersed in water, and people are normally fully immersed in air (even though the bottoms of their feet touch the ground and not the air).  Note that a fluid might be fully immersed in another fluid; consider air bubbles in water and mercury globules in air.  See also the specialization #$suspendedIn.")
(comment AntiArmorUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units that are trained,           equipped and organized to fight armored vehicles.")
(comment AuthenticationDevice "#$AuthenticationDevice is the collection of physical devices that play the role of #$deviceUsed in instances of #$AuthenticationEvent.  Note that such a device is not required for an instance of #$AuthenticationEvent.")
(disjointWith Beach GeoculturalRegion)
(comment relationExistsSpecMinAll "(#$relationExistsSpecMinAll SLOT COL1 COL2 NUM) means that, for every instance of COL2 (INS2) there are at least NUM subcollections of COL1 (SUBCOL1, SUBCOL3, ...) such that (SLOT SUBCOL1 INS2), (SLOT SUBCOL3             INS2), ..., hold.")
(comment OnlineListingsFn-Product "#$OnlineListingsFn-Product takes as argument any instance of #$ProductType and returns the collection of all web pages featuring online listings of available items of that type.  For example, (#$OnlineListingsFn-Product #$RoadVehicle) returns the collection of all web pages featuring online listings of cars, motorcycles or other road vehicles. (#$Vizedom 2/2/99)")
(comment ProximityTriggeredWeapon "A specialixzation  of #$Weapon.  Each instance of #$ProximityTriggeredWeapon is a weapon whose destructive power   is unleashed when something gets within a certain range of it.")
(comment SleetyArea "The current condition of having some sleet.")
(comment TersifyForward "A property of reformulator rules which says that in this rule,
the terse argument comes after the verbose argument.")
(comment Glossary "This is the collection of glossaries. A glossary is a kind of mini-dictionary, generally listing vocabulary relevant to a particular field, or vocabulary

used in a particle text, together with definitions of these terms.")
(comment acknowledgedAct "(#$acknowledgedAct ACKACT COMACT) means that the #$CommunicationAct-Single COMACT is acknowledged and replied-to by the responsive #$Acknowledging-CommunicationAct ACKACT.   Particular acceptances or rejections of a particular project proposal would involve examples of this predicate, as would a person responding to a wedding invitation, or a court responding to a motion.  See also #$acknowledgementOf which refers to the abstract content of the communication.")
(comment streetNameText "ARG2 is the base name of the street (minus the street number and directional prefixes or suffixes) for the #$ContactLocation ARG1.")
(comment WaveEmissionFn "#$WaveEmissionFn is a Cyc function, specifically a #$CollectionDenotingFunction. (#$WaveEmissionFn WAVETYPE) denotes a collection of events which is a subcollection of #$EmittingAWave; each instance of (#$WaveEmissionFn WAVETYPE) is an event in which an instance of #$WavePropagation of the type WAVETYPE is emitted at a #$fromLocation. For example, (#$WaveEmissionFn #$VisibleLight) denotes the collection of events in which visible light waves are emitted.")
(comment boss "(#$boss SUPERVISEE SUPERVISOR) means that SUPERVISOR is an immediate boss or supervisor of SUPERVISEE.")
(comment Teether "The collection of #$PhysicalDevices which are used to make the teething process of #$HumanInfants and #$HumanToddlers less painful.  #$Teethers are generally made of #$Plastic or some similar material.")
(comment Corvette-Ship "A collection of #$MilitaryWatercraft.  Every instance of #$Corvette-Ship is a ship smaller than a destroyer, armed with antisubmarine and anti-aircraft guns and depth charges, and equipped with detection devices.  (The car was named after the ship, not the other way around.)")
(comment FrugalAction "The collection of #$GoalActions,

 the goals or motives of which are at least partially to save money.")
(comment PropositionalAttitudeContext "The collection of all contexts (all instances of #$Microtheory, q.v.)  which contain assertions expressing the propositional attitudes (beliefs, desires, intentions) of some agent or group of agents.")
(comment DitransitiveNP-GenericFrameType "This frame is used for words that take exactly two complements,            the first of which is always -- in the case of English, at least --           an NP. In HPSG terms: [COMPS  <NP, synsem>]")
(disjointWith SteeringADeviceByHand LocomotionEvent-Animal)
(comment FreedomOfAction "#$FreedomOfAction is the ability of an agent to decide among alternatives, to act with an aim goal or desire that arises from within itself and not due to some external compulsion or restraint imposed by nature, society, or some diety.")
(comment NLPragmaticPredicate-New "This collection has as its instances the ``new'' pragmatic           predicates that take as their first argument either an instance of #$CycLNLAssertion and as their second argument an instance           of something which will indicate the pragmatic force of the assertion. See the different instances of this collection to see the possibilities. These are the only pragmatic predicates            that are used in the NL Trie.")
(comment Supernova "This is the collection of supernovae. A supernova is the explosion created when

stars of a certain mass collapse. They could be considered to be either objects or events. ")
(comment Ceftazidime "The chemical compound which is used in antibiotic products.")
(comment memberOfOrgsHoldings "This constant relates an object to the organization that has it in its holdings.  (#$memberOfOrgsHoldings THING ORG) means that THING is one of the items in ORGS's holding (see #$Holdings).")
(comment MicrowaveRadiation "A collection of events; a subset of #$ElectromagneticRadiation.  Each element

of #$MicrowaveRadiation is an instance of electromagnetic radiation 

having a wavelength in the range from approximately .01 centimeters

(1X10^6 #$Angstrom) to 10 centimeters (1X10^9 #$Angstrom), and a frequency 

of approximately 3X10^9 #$Hertz to 3X10^12 #$Hertz.  This includes

transmissions of super high frequency (SHF) including #$Microwave-SBand,

#$Microwave-CBand, #$Microwave-XBand, #$Microwave-KuBand, #$Microwave-KaBand.")
(comment Y-TheLetter "The letter Y of the alphabet.  This is 'Y' (or 'y') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.  As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterY and #$LatinSmallLetterY.")
(comment Micro "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10^-6")
(comment PropertyManagementCompany "A company which manages the affairs of real-estate properties.")
(comment NitrogenBase "A collection of #$MolecularRadicals. Instances of #$NitrogenBase are radicals of which the structure is based on #$Nitrogen entering in the constitution of #$Nucleotides, themselves basic elements of #$DNAMolecules or #$RNAMolecules. There are five natural types of these (four used in #$Ribonucleotides and four used in #$Deoxyribonucleotides, see #$NitrogenBaseType.")
(comment Dendrochronology "Dendrochronology is the

     dating of past events (climatic changes)

     through study of tree ring growth.

   The technique was developed 

     by A.E. Douglass from the University of

     Arizona, who noted that the wide rings of

     certain species of trees were produced

     during wet years and, inversely, narrow

     rings during dry seasons.")
(comment FlowerOpeningEvent "The process in which a flower bud opens and becomes a receptive flower.")
(comment relationExistsSpecAllSpecs "(#$relationExistsSpecAllSpecs PRED COL1 COL2) means that for

all subcollection SUBCOL2 of COL2, there exists a subcollection of COL1,

say SUBCOL1, such that (PRED SUBCOL1 SUBCOL2) holds. This assumes that PRED

is a type level predicate.")
(disjointWith NetUnchangingFunction NetDecreasingFunction)
(comment relationInstanceExistsMin "(#$relationInstanceExistsMin PRED THING COL NUM) means that there exist at least NUM instances (INS_1, INS_2, ..., INS_NUM) of COL such that THING stands in relation PRED to them, i.e., such that (PRED THING INS_1), (PRED THING INS_2), ..., (PRED THING INS_NUM),hold. (#$relationInstanceExistsMin PRED THING COL NUM) is thus is equivalent to the more complex form (#$thereExistAtLeast NUM ?INST (#$and (isa ?INST COL) (PRED THING ?INST))). So a ground atomic formula (or \"GAF\") built upon

#$relationInstanceExistsMin is in effect shorthand (i.e. a \"macro\") for an equivalent rule with the more complex quantified form. For example, (#$relationInstanceExistsMin #$geographicalSubRegions #$Iran

#$OilField 3) means Iraq has at least 3 oil fields. See the shared #$NoteAboutUseOfRuleMacroPredicates.")
(comment MycoplasmaPneumoniae "A collection of #$Bacterium.  These #$ProkaryoticCells cause #$Pneumonia in humans and is
transmitted by means of infected respiratory secretions.")
(comment COADeepOpsGuidanceMicrotheory "A collection of microtheories.  The information in each
instance will inherit to some instance of
#$COASpecificationMicrotheory, and in some cases, to multiple
instances.  Each instance of #$COADeepOpsGuidanceMicrotheory is used
to specify the commander's guidance for deep operations in the COAs
that appear among the #$genlMt dependents.")
(comment TourTravelLegFn "(#$TourTravelLegFn TOUR LOCFROM LOCTO) returns the 'travel leg' that TOUR takes from LOCFROM to LOCTO, considered as an instance of #$Path-Customary")
(comment Translator "Someone who translates written or oral material from one spoken language to another.")
(comment BiologicalWeapon-Fungal "The collection of all #$BiologicalWeapons that make use of fungi.")
(comment Lymphoma-Malignant "The collection of #$Cancers involving #$MalignantTumors made up of cells in the lymphatic system.")
(comment Kennel-Organization "The collection of all #$Organizations which provide temporary (long-term or short-term) lodging for pets.  Instances of the collection could include a that part of a veterinarian's office that boards pets while owners are out of town, an animal shelter, and a commercial enterprise whose business is to care for pets on a temporary basis in its own facilities.")
(comment Watercraft-Small "#$Watercraft-Small is a specialization of #$Watercraft-Surface.  Each instance of #$Watercraft-Small is a watercraft so small that the usual posture of a person in the boat is sitting, since standing in a small watercraft may capsize it or one may fall out of the boat.  A few examples are #$Raft, #$Canoe, and #$Lifeboat.  This collection is disjoint with #$Watercraft-Subsurface.")
(comment HydrogenCyanide "The collection of all hydrogen cyanide, whether in gaseous form or in solution as hydrocyanic acid [#$HydrocyanicAcid].")
(comment BaseballRightFielder "The collection of all #$BaseballOutfielders who play the position of right field on a #$BaseballTeam.")
(comment TheCoordinationSet "A piece of NL-CycL scaffolding vocab, used to coordinate reformulations in the initial incarnation of SMART.")
(comment connected-EdgeToSurface "(#$connected-EdgeToSurface SHEET OBJ2) means that a #$SheetOfSomeStuff, SHEET, is #$connectedAlongEdge to a surface of OBJ2.")
(comment UrinaryTractInfection "An infection that causes urination to be painful.  See #$BladderInfection.")
(comment FiveTonTruck "A type of military supply truck.")
(comment eventTypeSuggestsOccurrenceOfIn "(#$eventTypeSuggestsOccurrenceOfIn FLAG NONOBVIOUS MAIN) means that in events of type MAIN, an event of type FLAG provides evidence that an event of type NONOBVIOUS has occurred.  For instance, (#$eventTypeSuggestsOccurrenceOfIn SirenSounding #$CarAccident #$Traffic) means that if a siren sounding occurs during a traffic event an observer's evidence for the existence of a #$CarAccident is increased.")
(comment Iridium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of Iridium.")
(comment FeminineDominance "The kind of #$SexualServitude in which a woman plays the role of the master.")
(comment TextByAgentTypeFn "#$TextByAgentTypeFn takes as argument any spec of #$IntelligentAgent and returns the collection of all texts authored by (or in the name of) agents of that type.  For example, (#$TextByAgentTypeFn #$HeadOfGovernment) returns the set of all texts written by the head of any government.")
(comment PoliceTVShow "Instances of this collection are #$FictionalTVShow-CWs in which #$LawEnforcementActivity is the main focus. Only fictional shows are included.  Use (#$SubcollectionOfAboutFn #$InformativeTVShow #$LawEnforcementActivity) for #$TVShow-CWs intended to be wholly factual.")
(disjointWith ChemicalReaction WeatherEvent)
(disjointWith Requesting-CommunicationAct Rejecting-CommunicationAct)
(comment doesBusinessWith "(#$doesBusinessWith AGENT1 AGENT2) means that AGENT1 does some business with AGENT2.  Minimally, (#$doesBusinessWith AGENT1 AGENT2) implies that AGENT1 and AGENT2 at least occasionally negotiate to buy or sell products or services from one other. The two agents may or may not complete the sale or purchase, or enter into any actual contracts.")
(comment TOWMissile "A collection missiles, a specialization of
#$GuidedMissile. 'TOW' stands for 'Tube-launched, Optically-tracked,
Wire-guided.' These missiles can be launched from tripods, vehicles
such as Humvees and tanks, and helicopters, and are especially effective against tanks.  Successive versions of the TOW include the specializations #$BasicTOWMissile, #$ImprovedTOWMissile, and #$TOW2Missile.")
(comment FengShui "#$FengShui is a set of beliefs that has its origins in the Orient. Feng Shui is concerned with living harmoniously with the energy of the surrounding environment. It encompasses the art of placement, not only of buildings, but of everything within them. Feng Shui has recently become popular in the West, and the business of feng shui consulating, book-publishing, etc. is generating large profits for many people.")
(comment Artist "A specialization of #$Person. Each instance of this collection is a person who produces or performs works of art.  This includes performing artists (whose works are transitory unless recorded) as well as visual artists, literary writers, and composers (whose works are intended to last for a significant length of time and be viewed or otherwise appreciated after the artist finishes them). A notable specialization of this collection is #$Artist-Visual. See also #$ArtObject, #$artisticWorksCreated.")
(comment SurfaceToSurfaceMissile-Ballistic "A collection.  Each instance is a #$Missile propelled from a surface #$Platform-Military (located on land or on water) into the upper atmosphere by rockets.  The #$Missile uses gravitational pull to make its high-speed return to the surface--either land or water surface--where it detonates on contact with the target.")
(comment PersonLegallyCapableOfMilitaryService "The set of all people legally capable of modern military service, but not necessarily currently serving. See also #$PersonFitForMilitaryService.")
(comment RootAccessFn "#$RootAccessFn is a function which returns the group of users who            have root access to a system.             (#$hasMembers (#$RootAccessFn SYSTEM) ComputerSecurityPerson001) means that           ComputerSecurityPerson001  has root access to the system SYSTEM.           People with root access to a system have uncontrolled access  to the           files on the system.")
(comment AlimonyPayment "The collection of all events of paying alimony, court-ordered payments to a spouse for his or her support, after a divorce or dissolution of marriage.")
(comment GaseousDensity "A measurable physical attribute.  The element of #$Density that represents the physical attribute typical of gases.  Density lower than that of most liquids.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn SeventhRib) HeadOfBone) "")
(comment secretary-Executive-OrganizationalRole "(#$secretary-Executive-OrganizationalRole ORG EXEC) means
that while EXEC carries out or may carry out a more conventionally
'secretarial' function, EXEC also maintains broad and sweeping
executive power within ORG.  'Secretary' in this sense may carry the
older etymological connotation of someone within the organization who
knows where the secrets are kept.  Examples include the General
Secretary of the #$UnitedNationsOrganization, and the General
Secretary of the communist party of the #$PeoplesRepublicOfChina.")
(comment FigureSkater "This is the collection of persons who engage in figure skating, either professionally, or as an amateur who is very serious about the sport - e.g., Olympic skaters.")
(comment Monitoring "A specialization of #$PurposefulAction.  Each instance of #$Monitoring is an event in which one or more agents keep track of some ongoing situation, such as the movement of a storm, a military operation, or a series of related crimes.  Each instance of #$Monitoring has sub-events of two different types (see the predicate #$subEventTypes): the first type of sub-event is the establishment of communication links with relevant information sources, while the second type of sub-event is the gathering of information (see the collection #$InformationGathering) from these sources.  Instances of these two types of event can occur any number of times in a given instance of #$Monitoring, although the first instance of the latter type must always be preceded by an instance of the former type.  For example, in monitoring the movement of a storm, some agent may establish some communication link with a    weather station acquiring information about the storm, and then gather information about the storm from the station.  This could be repeated with different weather stations in the same instance of #$Monitoring, as long as the information gathered concerns the same storm.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-Coordinated "#$AttackByComputerOperation-Coordinated is a subset of #$AttackByComputerOperation-Distributed.  In fact, very few instances of #$AttackByComputerOperation-Distributed are not instances of this collection.  Each instance of #$AttackByComputerOperation-Coordinated is timed so that all distributed tools perform their tasks simultaneously.")
(comment AnimalBreeding "An activity in which an agent cares for animals, encourages their reproduction, and cares for the offspring they produce.  Usually #$AnimalBreeding is performed with the intention of selling the offspring. ")
(comment MachineGun-AirCooled "The collection of #$MachineGuns that use an air-cooling system to  keep the machine gun from overheating.")
(disjointWith Temperature IntervalOnNumberLine)
(comment MilitaryFn "This function takes any #$Country and   returns the collection of  #$GovernmentMilitaryOrganizations that    represent that country.")
(comment FashionModel "The collection of #$Persons whose job it is to model fashion items, especially clothes but also instances of #$ClothingAccessory, #$Jewelry, etc. #$FashionModels may appear on runways in fashion shows, in #$Advertisement-Commercial-IBT, or in a #$SalesCatalog. A few #$FashionModels who become celebrities are members of the collection #$Supermodel.")
(comment TaxEvasion "The collection of activities in which one agent purposely avoids paying taxes that he knows he is legally required to pay. This would include both avoiding tax payment altogether, as well as underpaying.")
(comment ElectricalWire "Wire used as an electrical conductor, usually housed in insulation of some sort.")
(comment NonNegativeScalarInterval "A specialization of #$ScalarInterval.  An instance INTERVAL of #$ScalarInterval is also an instance of #$NonNegativeScalarInterval just in case INTERVAL is a non-negative number or quantity.  Instances of #$NonNegativeScalarInterval include all instances of #$NonNegativeNumber (q.v.), as well as non-negative quantities such as (#$Meter 212), (#$Kilogram 5), and (#$SecondsDuration 0).")
(comment Infestation "The collection of infestations, events in which a large group of unwelcome animals, generally insects, congregates in a particular location. It is important in infestations that there be a fairly high density, in the sense of number of animals per area or volume. The proportion of volume taken up by the animals doesn't matter: a dozen elephants might virtually fill one's house, but the house is not thereby infested with elephants.")
(comment kePredArgWeakSuggestionInverse "(#$kePredArgWeakSuggestionInverse PRED N BINPRED) means that
if the relation expression (PRED . ARGS) is known, and ARGN appears as
the Nth argument in (PRED . ARGS) it is weakly suggested that Cyc
know there exists a THING such that (BINPRED THING ARGN).")
(disjointWith Wheelbarrow WaterTransportationDevice)
(comment Sidewinder-Missile "The AIM-9 #$Sidewinder-Missile is a supersonic, heat-seeking, air-to-air missile carried by fighter aircraft. It has a high-explosive warhead and an active infrared guidance system..")
(comment TimePointAtDistanceAfterEndOf "(#$TimePointAtDistanceAfterEndOf INT EVT) is the  #$TimePoint that is exactly INT after the ending of  EVT.  For example, (#$TimePointAtDistanceAfterEndOf     (#$DecadesDuration 3) TheAssassinationOfLincoln)  is the #$TimePoint that is exactly 30 years after  the (end of the) assassination of Abraham Lincoln.")
(comment Constellation "A collection of instances of #$CelestialRegion which are normally distinguished by a particular asterism that is intended to depict

some object.  The celestial sphere is completely covered with #$Constellations,

which do not overlap.  This is the more formal notion of 'constellation' used

by astronomers.  Examples include #$UrsaMajor-Constellation and #$Orion-Constellation.  See also #$Asterism, which is the more informal notion of 'constellation'.")
(comment JustificationStrength "Instances of #$JustificationStrength are attribute values which indicate the argumentational strength of a justification for an assertion in a context.  The two most important examples are #$Monotonic-JustificationStrength and #$Default-JustificationStrength.  See also #$assertionStrength.")
(comment Expectorant "Drugs which are used to help a patient bring up phlegm, by increasing the amount of mucus produced.")
(comment KilowattHour "A unit of measure of electrical energy equal a power demand of 1,000 watts for one hour. The equivalent of 3,600,000 Joules. Power company utility rates are typically expressed in cents per kilowatt-hour.")
(comment Kilo "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10^3")
(comment PreparedInstantFoodFn "A function to be used in referring to the 

collection of ready-to-eat, prepared forms of a spec of #$InstantFoodMix. 

For example, (#$PreparedInstantFoodFn #$MacaroniAndCheeseMix) is the collection of 

prepared instances of #$MacaroniAndCheese.")
(comment NitrogenBaseType "A collection of #$Collections. Instances of #$NitrogenBaseType are types of nitrogen bases. This collection has 5 chemically specific instances forming two disjoint specs: #$Adenine-Base and #$Guanine-Base being types of #$Purine-Base and #$Cytosine-Base, #$Thymine-Base, and #$Uracil-Base being types of #$Pyrimide-Base. These bases become constituents of nucleotides that are as basic monomers of DNA and RNA molecules. See #$NitrogenBase, #$Nucleotides, #$DNAMolecule, #$RNAMolecule.")
(comment Fern "An instance of #$BiologicalClass, and a subset of #$Plant. Instances of #$Fern are vascular plants that lack flowers, have characteristic fronds, and reproduce sexually via spores.")
(comment Letter-Alphabetic "A specialization of #$WritingSymbolCharacter

whose instances are all graphemic characters from any system of 

#$AlphabeticWriting.  Specializations of #$Letter-Alphabetic include 

#$RomanLetter, #$CyrillicLetter, and #$UpperCaseLetter.")
(comment SeaWater "A specialization of #$Water-Saline.  Each instance of #$SeaWater is a portion of salt water with the kind of mineral concentrations found in oceans (see the collection #$Ocean) --including the oceans themselves.")
(disjointWith MedicalCareInstitution BloodBank)
(comment PsychologicalTesting "A collection of processes which involve the #$Evaluating of the mental or emotional state of the subject")
(comment introductionTo "The expression `(#$introductionTo INTRO THING)' means that the #$PropositionalConceptualWork INTRO is intended to be an introduction to

the topic THING.")
(comment Histidine "A collection of compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.  These
compounds are essential for optimal growth in infants and obtainable
from proteins by the action of sulfuric acid and water.  Its
abbreviations are His and H.")
(comment TLRelation "A specialization of #$ELRelation such that instances are only permitted at the TL (transcript level; a specialization of the epistemological level); that is, the canonicalizer will transform expressions that

reference instances of #$TLRelation into equivalent expressions that do not

reference instances of #$TLRelation; this transformation is guided by the

value (arg2) of #$expansionDefn for each #$TLRelation")
(disjointWith Path-Simple Path-Cyclic)
(comment AnnualDocument "Documents which are issued on a yearly basis and which report the status and activites of the topics for the year covered.  Corporate AnnualReports, Almanacs, etc.")
(comment SkolemFuncNFn "#$SkolemFuncNFn is used by the #$CycCanonicalizer and should rarely

(if ever) need to be seen by users or referenced in assertions entered

at the EL level.  It is used by the canonicalizer to denote a skolem

function before it is reified, when the skolem is derived from a formula

asserted at the EL level that uses #$thereExistAtLeast,

#$thereExistAtMost, or #$thereExistExactly.  Its arity is 4: the first

argument is a list of the term variable arguments of the denoted skolem function,

(term variables which are in the scope of the bounded existential).

The second argument is a variable which uniquely identifies the

existentially quantified variable by which the denoted skolem will

be represented in the canonical version of the formula.

The third is a sequence variable if there is a sequence variable

argument of the denoted skolem function (which there will be iff there

is a sequence variable in the scope of the bounded existential), and NIL otherwise.

The fourth is an interval specifying the number of things which may satisfy the formula.")
(comment LightLiftHelicopterUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of lightly armed military units that are responsible for airlifting troops to the combat areas.")
(disjointWith Drink ToiletrySubstance)
(comment seriesOrderedByInverse "(#$seriesOrderedByInverse SER PRED) means that PRED is the relation that imposes an order on the members of SER.  Each member of the series stands in the relation PRED to the series members that come before it.  For example, if SER is a line of cars driving south, the ordering relation might be #$northOf (or ''behind'').  See also #$seriesOrderedBy.")
(comment OilWrestling "A form of #$WrestlingSportsEvent in which two or more #$Persons wrestle  covered with #$Oil.")
(comment Dorsum-Planetary "A collection of topographical features.  Each element of #$Dorsum-Planetary is an elongated topographical region on an extraterrestrial planetary body of significantly higher elevation than its surrounding area.")
(comment MeatFn "Collection-forming function - takes a type of animal as an argument, returns the class of meat which is derived from instances of that type of animal.")
(comment ColorTypeByMetallicness "A collection of collections of collections. Each instance is a specialization of #$Color such that all the instances of the collection union of the set of the instances of the specialization have the same metallicness in their coloring.")
(comment multiWordString "(#$multiWordString STRINGS WORD PART TERM) means that the translation of the multi-word phrase containing STRINGS and WORD, with part of speech PART, is TERM.  TERM must be an element of either #$Collection or #$Individual.  If TERM is a collection, the semantic meaning of TERM is (#$isa :noun TERM).  If TERM is an individual object, the semantic meaning of TERM is (#$equals :noun TERM).  See also #$multiWordSemTrans.")
(comment ScientificTechnique "This is the collection of types of actions which

are specific to the pursuit of scientific fields of study. The collection includes (at least) laboratory techniques, techniques used to gather data in the field, 

and those involved in the use of any #$ScientificInstrument for any scientific purpose.")
(comment TablatureText-StringedInstruments "The collection of all instances of #$MusicalText that are written in #$TablatureNotation. #$TablatureNotation is a notation used to describe how a sequence of musical notes is to be played on a stringed instrument.")
(comment subjectOfMedicalProcedure "(#$subjectOfMedicalProcedure PROCEDURE SUBJECT) means that SUBJECT is the instance of #$Organism-Whole which is the affected target of the instance of #$MedicalProcedure PROCEDURE.")
(comment PicturesOfTypeFn "#$PicturesOfTypeFn takes as argument any spec of #$SpatialThing-Localized and returns the collection of all VisualInformationSources depicting instances of that spec.  For example (#$PicturesOfTypeFn #$EgyptianPyramid) returns the collection of all VisualInformationSource depicting any Egyptian pyramid.")
(comment Form-CW "The collection of all #$ConceptualWorks instantiated by instances of #$Form-StandardizedIBO.  Some forms may change over time, in which case the general form is an instance of #$ConceptualWorkSeries.")
(comment OccasionInYearFn "An instance of #$IndividualDenotingFunction, #$OccasionInYearFn is a binary function that is used to denote a particular calendar-based event in a given year.  For example, (#$OccasionInYearFn #$FathersDay (#$YearFn 2000)) denotes Father's Day of 2000, occurring on June 19, 2000.  Events denoted by this function may happen annually or at multiple-year intervals, so long as they are calendar-based.")
(disjointWith ClimateCycleType LanguageGroupingType)
(comment processPowerConsumption "the power consumed by this process. ")
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization Court-Judicial)
(comment DifficultBreathing "This is the collection of instances of labored or difficult breathing
as a result of some #$PhysiologicalCondition.")
(comment mtsIncommensurate "(#$mtsIncommensurate MTNOT MTPROVE) means that there is some

proposition that is provable in MTPROVE and not provable (to the

extent of some well-specified finite limit) in MTNOT.")
(comment IrrigatedLand "The collection of land which is artificially watered, using fresh water from rivers and lakes or from underground. Irrigation is necessary for agriculture in many areas.")
(comment Flame "A flame in a #$CombustionProcess.")
(comment UnaryRelation "The collection of all fixed-arity relations of arity 1 (see #$arity).  The most notable specializations of #$UnaryRelation are #$UnaryPredicate and #$UnaryFunction (qq.v.).")
(comment capableOfDoing "#$capableOfDoing is similar to #$capableOf except that the second argument is an instance of #$Situation. Thus, (#$capableOfDoing AGENT SIT ROLE) means that AGENT is capable of performing the ROLE in some particular SIT. This predicate can be used to express that some agent would be capable of doing some action, even if he does not actually participate in that event.")
(comment Warhead-BallisticMissile "A #$Warhead designed to be used with a #$BallisticMissile.")
(comment GeneralAnesthetic "Drugs which eliminate pain or other sensation everywhere on the body, usually by making the patient unconscious.")
(comment FastNeutron "The fast neutrons are neutrons that have kinetic energy above 100 KeV.")
(comment SurfaceToAirMissileLauncher "The collection of all #$MissileLaunchers

 that fire #$SurfaceToAirMissiles.")
(comment TVTransmitting "A collection of #$Events; a subset of #$MediaTransmitting.  In every #$TVTransmitting event, an intangible #$InformationBearingThing (usually a #$MovingImageWithSound) is transmitted to a #$TelevisionSet.  This transmission may be via coaxial cable, in which case it is a #$CableTVTransmitting event.  Or it may be via a #$BroadcastAntenna, in which case it is a #$TVBroadcasting event.  See also #$TVMediaProduct.")
(comment ArchiveOfPeriodicalFn "This function takes any instance of #$PeriodicalSeries and returns the collection of all archives [#$ArchiveHoldings] of that type.  For example, (#$ArchiveOfPeriodicalFn

#$TheShadow-ThePulpMagazine) returns the collection of all archives, in any format, of the pulp magazine 'The Shadow'.")
(comment PeaJacket "The collection of heavy woolen double-breasted #$Jackets, traditionally worn by sailors.")
(comment PATR-Specification "The collection of instances of #$SubLList that are well-formed and well-typed attribute-value-matrices according to the type hierarchy (see #$GrammarHierarchySort).")
(comment SeasonalGiftGivingOccasionType "A specialization of #$GiftGivingOccasionType and of #$CalendarBasedTemporalObjectType. #$SeasonalGiftGivingOccasionType is the collection of kinds of gift-giving occasions that are tied to certain dates in the calendar year.  It is #$disjointWith #$NonSeasonalGiftGivingOccasionType.")
(comment DataProcessing "This is the group of techniques for extracting

useful information from batches of raw data. It includes statistical analysis

of data and computational techniques, among others.")
(comment ComputerNetworkTraffic "#$ComputerNetworkTraffic is the collection of measures of
network traffic on computer networks. More specifically, for a given
computer network an instance of #$ComputerNetworkTraffic is the
measure of how much information is being transferred among the
computers on the network.")
(comment JobFn "(#$JobFn POSITION) denotes the #$WorkAgreement in which a person obeys the duties and responsibilities, and is rewarded by the compensations, associated with PositionType POSITION. For example, (#$JobFn #$ComputerProgrammer) denotes the job (i.e., #$WorkAgreement) of #$ComputerProgrammer (while #$ComputerProgrammer itself denotes the subclass of people who are computer programmers). See also #$duties.")
(comment ImpureCompound "A collection of tangible stuffs. Each instance of #$ImpureCompound is a chemically impure           portion of stuff belonging to some particular #$ChemicalSubstanceType (e.g., #$Carbon,           #$Water, #$Cellulose).  `Chemically impure' applies to a piece of stuff which has enough of           some sub-portion failing to conform to the chemical composition of           its (single) #$ChemicalSubstanceType.  What counts as `enough of a           sub-portion' is determined by context.           Most common portions of a #$ChemicalSubstanceType will, in many contexts, be instances           of #$ImpureCompound.  For example, since pencil lead is not pure carbon           and ordinary tap water contains           many impurities, pieces of pencil lead           and portions of tap water will, in most contexts, be instances.  Portions of           pencil lead and tap water will contain many sub-portions           failing to conform to the ChemicalSubstanceType of either carbon or water respectively.            Some instances of #$ChemicalSubstanceType will be #$genls of #$ImpureCompound only           in specialized contexts.           For example, in domestic contexts, ordinary distilled water would not           have enough impurities to be considered `impure' ( but see #$PureSubstance).  However, in a           context with much higher purity standards such as that of a microchip           manufacturing clean room, ordinary distilled water would be           considered an instance of #$ImpureCompound.           To refer to some impure portion of a STUFF, one can use (#$ImpureFn STUFF) which has           ImpureCompound as a #$resultGenl.  See also #$PureSubstance.")
(comment AnnualTemporalObjectType "A collection of collections. Each instance of #$AnnualTemporalObjectType is a specialization of #$TemporalThing, instances of which occur once per year according to some calendar. Furthermore, the occurrence of instances of each such type of event is tied to a specific time (for example, a specific date) in the calendar year. For example, #$ChristmasHoliday is an instance of #$AnnualTemporalObjectType, because one occurs on a specific date (namely, December 25) each year.")
(comment instantiatesToGenerics-Binary "Suppose that PRED is a #$BinaryPredicate that is type-level in the first and second argument positions. (#$instantiatesToGenerics-Binary PRED) means that if it is asserted that (PRED COL1 COL2), the instance level analog of PRED, (#$InstantiationInstanceFn PRED (#$TheSet 1 2)) holds between (#$GenericInstanceFn COL1) and (#$GenericInstanceFn COL2).")
(comment numberOfPrescriptionsByDocPayerTypeDuring "(#$numberOfPrescriptionsByDocPayerTypeDuring ?DOC ?PRODUCT-TYPE ?PAYER-TYPE ?TIME ?NUM) means that during the time interval ?TIME, there were ?NUM prescriptions for ?PRODUCT-TYPE made by ?DOC, which were paid for by a #$HealthCarePayer of type ?PAYER-TYPE.  For example, (#$numberOfPrescriptionsByDocPayerTypeDuring DrSmith #$ZoloftProduct #$StateMedicaidAdministrationOrganization (#$YearFn 1998) 27) means that DrSmith made 27 prescriptions for Zoloft in 1998 which were paid for by Medicaid.")
(comment LanguageArea "A specialization of #$GeographicalRegion.  Each instance of #$LanguageArea is a geographical region whose extent and boundaries  are determined by the dominant languages or language groups that are indigenous to, or imported into, that region.")
(comment CurrencyExchange "A specialization of #$MoneyModeExchange. Each instance of this collection is a transaction in which currency is exchanged for the same value in another type of currency.  A surcharge usually applies.")
(comment WebstersDictionary "The collection of all instances of #$Dictionary in the format described by #$NoahWebster.")
(comment EukaryoticGeneExpression "The collection of gene expression events in which eukaryotic cells supply the genetic information.")
(comment DramaticPerformanceTypeByName "A collection of collections. Every element of #$DramaticPerformanceTypeByName is a collection of performances of some named dramatic work. Given a named dramatic work, such as 'Hamlet', the collection of all performances of that work will be an instance of this class.  The work may be a play, an opera, or a ballet. For example, the collection of all performances of the ballet, 'Swan Lake,' is an element of DramaticPerformanceType, as is the class of all performances of e.g., 'Hamlet', 'West Side Story', and 'The Magic Flute'. (See #$DramaticPerformance for an explanation of the criteria for being a DramaticPerformance. Although all plays and operas are instances of #$DramaticPerformance, not all ballets are.)")
(comment officialUSCodeName "(#$officialUSCodeName DEVICE STRING) means that STRING is an officially recognized code name for DEVICE, where DEVICE is typically a weapon or military vehicle.")
(comment Private-Title "This Cyc constant denotes the term of address used for someone holding the rank-attribute of #$Private-Rank in an instance of #$ModernMilitaryOrganization.  This is usually the lowest rank in a land-based armed service.  The title is often abbreviated as PVT in text.  This refers to a 'buck private', and excludes the higher-ranked #$PrivateFirstClass-Title.")
(comment NonfictionalPCW "The collection of all #$PropositionalConceptualWorks that are nonfictional.")
(disjointWith VisualInformationBearingThing Sound)
(comment SponsorFn-EventType "#$SponsorFn-EventType takes as argument any spec of #$Event-Organized and returns the collection of all agents sponsoring some event of that type.  For example, (#$SponsorFn-EventType #$Debate) returns the collection of all agents playing a sponsorship role in any instance of #$Debate, and (#$SponsorFn-EventType OlympicGames) returns the collection of all agents playing a sponsorship role in any Olympics.")
(disjointWith UnitOfFlowRate UnitOfSpeed)
(comment PornographicMaterial-Illegal "This is the collection of pornographic material which is explicitly illegal to

possess.

An example of an explicit standard would be that the picture is both sexually

explicit and depicts someone under a particular age. A vague standard such as

being obscene and having no redeeming social value would not be considered an

explicit standard. Since the legal standards in force vary between countries and

even within countries, this collection should be considered implicitly indexical: it consists of those instances of pornographic material which are

explicitly illegal around here. ")
(disjointWith Kayak Lifeboat)
(comment Howitzer "A collection.  Each instance is a large #$Weapon too large for one person to carry and used for indirect shooting.  A #$Howitzer has a caliber larger than 15mm and fires projectiles at medium muzzle speed with a trajectory over 45 degrees.")
(comment VulnerableToBufferOverflow "#$VulnerableToBufferOverflow is an attribute of some instances of #$Computer.  A computer has the vulnerability #$VulnerableToBufferOverflow if it uses a buffer with a configuration that can be exploited in an #$AttackByComputerOperation-BufferOverflow.")
(comment SpringBreak "The collection of spring breaks - week-long academic vacations observed every spring by colleges and universities in the U.S.")
(comment oppositeOnPath-Generally "This predicate relates a customary path such as a 
street to two objects that are generally across the path from 
each other.  (#$oppositeOnPath-Generally OBJ1 OBJ2 PATH) means 
that some part of OBJ1 is directly across PATH from some part
of OBJ2.  In other words, OBJ1 and OBJ2 are #$onPath-Alongside 
opposite sides of PATH, and the two segments of PATH that OBJ1 
and OBJ2 are respectively related to by #$alongsidePathSegment 
spatially intersect.  More precisely: there is some vertical 
plane perpendicular to the vertical ''plane'' defined by the 
centerline of PATH (or, even more precisely, by the centerline
of the portion of PATH common to the two segments of PATH 
mentioned above) that passes through both OBJ1 and OBJ2.  For 
a specialization of this predicate that implies that the 
objects are more directly across the path from each other, 
see #$oppositeOnPath-Directly.")
(comment StratocumulusCloud "A collection of dark, gray clouds that often cover the sky, but may have sky-revealing breaks in them.")
(comment WorkingAdultAmericanWoman "A type of #$AdultMiddleClassAmerican who is female.  ")
(comment EmittingSound "A specialization of #$EmittingAWave.  Each instance of #$EmittingSound is an event in which some instance of #$Sound is emitted from some wave source (see the predicate #$waveSource).  Examples of #$EmittingSound include an explosion generating a sound wave, a plucked violin string resonating, a baby crying, and a person saying `Hello'.")
(comment Pi-Number "#$Pi-Number is the mathematical constant 'pi', which is defined to be the ratio of a circle's circumference to its diameter.  Although #$Pi-Number is an instance of #$IrrationalNumber, a reasonable rational approximation is 3.1415927.")
(comment powderedFormOfType "`(#$powderedFormOfType POWDER TYPE)' means that POWDER is an instance
(group or mob of grains) of the powdered form of TYPE, that POWDER was derived
from some instance of instances of TYPE by a #$ReducingToPowder.")
(comment HomeMortgage "The collection of #$MortgageAgreements which are #$HomeLoans.")
(comment structureFunctions "(#$structureFunctions STRUCT FUNCT) means that FUNCT is an operation on the #$baseSet of STRUCT.  An n-ary operation on a set SET is a function whose domain is SETx...xSET (n times), and whose range is SET.")
(comment TextMining "Text mining takes unstructured textual information and 

examines it in an attempt to discover structure and implicit meanings

buried in the text. By identifying this structure and meaning, text mining

can impose relevant indexing on textual data. Once a useful index is built, information

can be retrieved through search technology.")
(comment Cloning "The collection of #$Events in which a #$Cell from an #$Organism-Whole is collected and appropriately manipulated so as to turn it into a second #$Organism-Whole which is #$geneticallyIdentical to the first one.")
(comment SparselyHairy "An attribute for describing a body part which has a few strands of hair scattered over its surface.")
(comment fieldValueDependsOn "(#$fieldValueDependsOn ?LF ?VAL-LF ?DEP-LF ?VALUE) means that whether ?LF has a value for a particular record depends on the what the represented value of ?DEP-LF is.  If ?DEP-LF has ?VALUE, then ?LF takes on the represented value of ?VAL-LF. See also #$dependentFields. ")
(comment Knight "The collection of all (often mounted) soldiers serving directly under a feudal superior in the Middle Ages. Does not include modern honorary knights such as #$SirEdmundHillary.")
(comment terminalSyntaxSymbols "The predicate (#$terminalSyntaxSymbols SYSTEM SYMBOL) relates a #$SyntaxSpecificationSystem (such as a #$FormalGrammar-CW) to one of its grammar symbols that is 'terminal' in that it does not represent any further combinations of #$SyntaxSpecificationSymbols but rather stands for a final text or segment or 'surface element' of the (parsed or generated) structure.  For example, in a #$ContextFreeGrammar, with the rules S --> VP + YF; YF --> ''you fool!'' meaning that a sentence S consists of a verb phrase VP followed by the phrase ''you fool!''. YF acts as a #$terminalSyntaxSymbols for this grammar  (because YF here  stands directly for surface text) whereas symbols S and VP, act as #$nonterminalSyntaxSymbols.")
(comment conflictLevel "(#$conflictLevel CONF LEVEL) means that the conflict level of the ConlictEvent CONF IS as described in LEVEL.  Here IS emphasize the time when the sentence (#$conflictLevel CONF LEVEL) is evaluated since the level of the conflict may change during the temporal extension of CONF.  Note that the LEVEL only has a relative value in the sense that only the comparison of different values (rather than the values themselves) has real meanings.  For example, a CONF may start from a radom shooting on the border between two countries, followed by some threats of using military force, which in turn is followed by a small battle at the border, which eventually results in a war.  The level of conflict increases in this example from each stage to the next.")
(disjointWith Bar-Place Facility-Construct)
(comment AmateurRadioBroadcasting "The collection of all radio broadcasts which are made by a non-professional for recreation, usually using homemade equipment.  This practice is commonly known in the United States (and perhaps other places) as 'ham radio'.")
(comment InternetBroadcastFn-EventType "#$InternetBroadcastFn-EventType takes as argument any type of organized, public event and returns the collection of events that are broadcasts over the #$Internet of instances of that type.  For example, (#$InternetBroadcastFn-EventType Trial) would return the collection of Internet broadcasts of trials.")
(comment TraversingARoad "Collection of #$Translation-LocationChange   events in which an actor moves completely along a stretch of #$Roadway, from one designated endpoint to the other.")
(comment PrescriptionDrugSampleType "These are formal product types which have NationalDrugCodes and which are made for the purpose of giving as samples.")
(comment prototypicalPathMediumTypeForTransportationDeviceType "(#$prototypicalPathMediumTypeForTransportationDeviceType PATHTYPE CRAFTTYPE) says that PATHTYPE is *the* #$PathType that defines instances of

 CRAFTTYPE as said instances.  I.e., a vehicle VEH is an instance of 

CRAFTTYPE insofar as VEH is designed primarily to follow instances of

 PATHTYPE during #$TransportationEvents in which VEH plays the role of #$transporter.  #$prototypicalPathMediumTypeForTransportationDeviceType is thus used to link types of #$TransportationDevices to their defining #$PathTypes.")
(comment CombatAircraft "A specialization of #$MilitaryAircraft.  Each instance of #$CombatAircraft is an aircraft designed for use in combat, rather than (for example) for transport or reconnaissance.")
(comment CarbonDioxide "#$CarbonDioxide is the collection of all macroscopic portions of the organic compound CO_2.")
(comment toPreventInPlan-Prop "(#$toPreventInPlan-Prop PLAN PROP) means that the success of

the plan represented by the #$SupposedToBeMicrotheory PLAN is

contingent upon PROP not becoming true in the course of the plan.")
(comment Genome-GIS "A collection of groups of
#$GeneticInformationStructure. Each instance of #$Genome-GIS is a group
made of the abstract structures of each piece that pertains to the genome
of an individual BLO. Each member of an instance of #$Genome-GIS is in
correspondence with one member of an instance of #$Genome via
#$instantiationOfGIS and one member of an instance of #$Genome-GenInfo.")
(comment structureDiffs "Like (#$structureMaps ?Src ?Src-Mt ?Tgt ?Tgt-Mt ?Src-Desc ?Tgt-Desc), except (#$structureDiffs ?Src ?Src-Mt ?Tgt ?Tgt-Mt ?Src-Desc ?Tgt-Desc) returns axioms that are structurally isomorphic but differ in at least one argument position. structureDiffs thus implements the theory of 'alignable differences'. See also #$structureMaps.")
(comment FluidFlow-Complete "Instances of #$FluidFlow-Complete represent the motion of a piece of fluid from being entirely `at' (see #$objectFoundInLocation) the #$fromLocation to entirely `at' the #$toLocation.  Thus when we say, `The river flowed from West Egg to East Egg' we don't mean the same thing as `The entire river left West Egg and went to East Egg'.  Therefore, #$FluidFlow-Complete is not the correct motion event to use.  Instead, #$FluidFlow-Translation is.  However, if we wish to say, `Joe pumped all the water out of the bilge and into the ocean' we do mean the same thing that #$FluidFlow-Complete entails.")
(disjointWith GeoculturalRegion Shipyard)
(comment topicPattern-Relevant "A predicate used in text searching to classify texts by relevant topic.  It is used with #$regexStringMatch (or #$regexFileMatch) to find terms within a text that match a pattern template (a #$RegularExpression), and to associate the text with a particular Cyc term as its topic because of the matching.  (#$topicPattern-Relevant THING REGEX) means that a text containing any substring that matches REGEX is likely to be relevant to the topic of THING.  This predicate is used to associate #$RegularExpression templates with certain topics.  See also #$topicPattern-Irrelevant.  For example (#$topicPattern-Relevant #$TaxiCab ''((\\<taxi(cab)?(s)?)|(cab(s)?)|(cabbie(s)?)) '') provides a #$RegularExpression template to match 'taxicabs' or 'cab', etc. and connects this pattern to the concept #$TaxiCab.")
(comment OccursFn "Allows us to convert from the active (#$GoalAction) to the formula which expresses the state of affairs pursued in the action.")
(comment TimedDetonatingDevice "The collection of #$ExplosiveDevices which use #$Timers to control detonation.")
(comment ForestFire "A specialization of #$CombustionProcess. Each instance of #$ForestFire is a fire that damages some instance of #$WoodedArea.")
(comment SubLDescriptorPredicate "The collection of predicates which describe the internal data structures of the Cyc KB.")
(comment ElectronicFn "A function that maps collections of #$InformationStores onto computer informtion structures [#$ComputerAIS] which contain their structured information. For example, (#$ElectronicFn #$Map) is the collection of all #$Map structures in computer format. See also #$HardcopyOfIBTTypeFn, #$HardcopyOfCWFn, and #$HardcopyOfInformationTypeFn.")
(comment streetNameDirectionalPrefix "ARG2 is the directional prefix for the street address of  the #$ContactLocation ARG1.  This includes #$CharacterStrings such as `NORTH' and #$Abbreviations such as `SW'.")
(comment ThermalConductivity "A collection of attributes; a subcollection of #$PhysicalAttribute. Each instance of #$ThermalConductivity represents a specific ability of some physical object to conduct heat. An individual object's #$ThermalConductivity is indicated with the predicate #$thermalConductivityOfObject.")
(comment AirlineCompany "#$AirlineCompany is a specialization of #$TransportationCompany-Provider, #$CommercialServiceOrganization, and #$Business.  Each instance of #$AirlineCompany is a business that operates airplanes to transport goods or people in exchange for money.")
(comment DigitalSubscriberLine "DSL (Digital Subscriber Line) is a general technology which brings high-bandwidth information (soon up to 6.1 megabits/second) over normal copper telephone wire, which enables the transmission of motion video and audio. DSL has several variations: #$AsymmetricDigitalSubscriberLine (ADSL), HDSL, and RADSL. DSL is expected to replace ISDN in the near future.")
(comment Ramp-PersistenceDistribution "Each instance of this collection is an object consisting of parameters which together indicate the probability of an assertion or set of assertions being true.  The parameters define a ramp-like distribution contour (graph).  The parameters are specified using the predicates #$rampStartLocation, #$rampEndLocation, #$rampInitialValue, and #$rampFinalValue.")
(comment fundsOrganization "(#$fundsOrganization AGENT ORG N) means that AGENT provides N x 100

percent of the total funding for the organization ORG, throughout the

duration of ORG.  Embedding an assertion of this form in a 'holdsIn T'

context, generates an assertion which states that AGENT provides N x 100

percent of the total funding for ORG, in T, of the total funding for ORG

in T. So if a corporation has a total of 1 million dollars in funding for 

1999, and .5 million dollars of all of its funding for 1999 comes from 

AGENT01, then (#$holdsIn 1999 (#$fundsOrganization AGENT01 CORPORATION .5)).")
(disjointWith LocomotionEvent-Animal Incorporation-Physical)
(comment Cyclosarin "A #$NerveAgentType that is extremely lethal when inhaled.")
(comment OpenCluster "An #$OpenCluster is a #$StarCluster which has relatively few stars and is therefore very loosely arranged.  A good example is the #$Pleiades.")
(comment LabetalolHydrochloride "The chemical compound which is used to make cardiovascular drug products.")
(comment containsWorkBy "This predicate relates buildings like art galleries and museums to creators of objects whose works are displayed therein.")
(comment importExpenditureFractionDuring "(#$importExpenditureFractionDuring REGION PRODUCT-TYPE THING NR) means that NR is the quotient of the monetary value of imports of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING (as dividend) and the monetary value of REGION's imports of all goods and services during the temporal extent of THING (as divisor).  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  For example, to express the fact that Oman's oil imports accounted for 80 percent of the total value of its imports in 1997, we can say (#$importExpenditureFractionDuring #$Oman #$PetroleumProduct (#$YearFn 1997) (#$Percent 80)).  See also #$importAmountDuring.")
(comment Z-TheLetter "The letter Z of the alphabet.  This is 'Z' (or 'z') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.  As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterZ and #$LatinSmallLetterZ.")
(comment intendedBeneficiary "(#$intendedBeneficiary ACTION AGENT) means that any agent
who is the #$directingAgent of ACTION intends that AGENT be the
#$beneficiary of ACTION.")
(comment Guarani-Paraguay "The unit of currency for Paraguay-AtPresent.")
(comment (Micro Gram) "A microgram is a unit of mass derived by dividing a gram by 1,000,000.")
(comment Dwarf-Mythical "The mythical race of stocky, warrior-like beings described in such works as #$LordOfTheRings-Trilogy, and employed as characters in #$DungeonsAndDragons the #$RolePlayingGame.")
(comment FriendlySociety "A #$FriendlySociety is a mutual benefit organization in which all profits are put toward members' benefits; certain

tax benefits may apply.")
(comment Lecithin "#$Lecithin is a complex, naturally-occurring mixture of phospholipids            that most often comes from soybean oil. Phospholipids are a part of            almost all biological membranes. Phospholipids are the surface-active portion            of #$Lecithin, the part that gives lecithin most of its functional properties.")
(comment FlowerDevelopmentEvent "The process in which a shoot apical meristem develops into a receptive flower.")
(comment DozenOfObjects "The collection of dozens of objects")
(comment ComputerCardGameEvent "The collection of events consisting of a card game
(e.g. Poker) being played in its entirety on a computer.")
(comment hangsAttached "(#$hangsAttached HUNG HANGER) means that HUNG #$touches HANGER, is #$supportedBy it, and attached to it.  Unlike the more general #$hangsFrom, #$hangsAttached is not transitive.  For example, a weight attached to a fishing line #$hangsFrom both the fishing line and the fishing rod that the line hang from, but is #$hangsAttached only to the line.")
(comment ArityRelationFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction that maps a given integer 
to the collection of all relations having that integer
as their arity.  (#$ArityRelationFn INT) is the 
#$RelationshipTypeByArity whose instances are all and 
only those #$Relations RELN such that (#$arity RELN INT).
For example, (#$ArityRelationFn 2) is the collection
#$BinaryRelation.")
(comment arrangementObjectTypes "This predicate relates an arrangement of like
objects to a type of object under which all of its members
fall.  (#$arrangementObjectTypes GROUP OBJTYPE) means that
OBJTYPE is an instance of #$ExistingObjectType that all 
#$groupMembers of GROUP are instances of.  For example, if 
the members of GROUP are the trees in a palm grove, then
OBJTYPE could be #$PalmTree.  OBJTYPE need not be one of the 
maximally specific types under which all of GROUP's members 
fall: the grove can still be described as an arrangement of
#$PalmTrees even if all of the members happen to be instances 
of #$DatePalm.  Each instance of #$ArrangementOfLikeObjects 
should have at least one such corresponding object type.  For 
a more specific predicate see #$arrangementNearestObjectTypes.")
(comment Masquerading-Deceiving "#$Masquerading-Deceiving is the collection of events in which an agent pretends to be someone other than who he or she really is, and does so with the intent to deceive someone. The deception, in the case of #$Masquerading-Deceiving specifically involves the identity of the perpertrator, which is what makes this collection more specialized than the collection, #$Deceiving.")
(comment filterCollections "The predicate indicating that all instances of a collection should be filtered from   remote operations whenever the associated instance of #$TranscriptFilter is active.   (filterCollections FILTER COLLECTION) means that adding FILTER to the active    transcript filters will effectively add COLLECTION to the collections being    filtered.")
(comment giftGivingOccasion "(#$giftGivingOccasion GIVING OCCASION-TYPE) means that the instance of #$GiftGivingOccasionType, OCCASION-TYPE is the occasion for the instance of #$GiftGiving, GIVING. For example, (#$giftGivingOccasion GiftGiving01 #$MothersDay) means that #$MothersDay is the occasion for the instance of #$GiftGiving, GiftGiving01.")
(comment Publicist "A person who works for a company, either as an employee or a contractor, and performs #$PublicRelationsActivity.")
(comment PlayPerformance-Musical "#$PlayPerformance-Musical is the collection of events which meet all of the following conditions: it consists predominantly of singing, dancing and acting events which taken together as a whole tell a story.--Huffer, Oct. 27, 1998")
(comment ChemicalSubstanceFn "(#$ChemicalSubstanceFn OBJ) denotes  a collection of portions of stuff-like substances chemically composed of instances of OBJ, a specialization of #$ChemicalObject.  The returned collection is an instance of #$ChemicalSubstanceType.")
(comment BaseballSecondBaseman "The collection of all #$BaseballPlayers who play the position of second base on a #$BaseballTeam.")
(comment Cone-AnimalBodyPart "The collection of all cone cells in #$Vertebrate #$Retinas.  Cone cells are sensitive to color, but are not as sensitive to light as rod cells (#$Rod-AnimalBodyPart).")
(comment protrudesInto "(#$protrudesInto OBJ1 OBJ2) means that a #$Protrusion of OBJ1, has one end inside of OBJ2, while much of it is outside of OBJ2.")
(comment ProduceSectionWorker "Collection of people who work in the produce section usually in a grocery store")
(comment HammerForThrowing "The kind of hammer one throws in the Olympic #$HammerThrowSportsEvent.")
(comment FlapWheelRADAR "A type of RADAR used with heavy caliber anti-aircraft artillery guns for target acquisition.")
(comment possessiveRelation "(#$possessiveRelation OWNER CONTENT) captures a very underspecified possessive relationship between OWNER and CONTENT. This possession may be inalienable, as in 'Paula's big nose', or alienable, as in 'Clinton's cigars', relational as in 'Caesar's wife', situational as in' 'Monica's death by chocolate' or 'Hillary's running for office', or  just downright ambiguous as in 'DuMaurier's death in venice'. The idea is that such precise relationships (all of which are in some sense 'possessive', metaphoric or otherwise) are the products or situated reasoning and common-sense knowledge; these relationships cannot be inferred by lexical or grammatical means during language analysis.")
(comment Chromium "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of chromium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment ReproductiveHormone "The collection of #$Steroids produced normally by the #$Glands of the #$ReproductiveSystem of an animal. However, this collection also includes synthetic forms of these chemical compounds.")
(comment Index-IndicatorOrMeasure "A collection of measures derived from a set of observations taken at the same time.  Instance predicates are used to indicate the condition or overall status of some complex system phenomenon at a given point in time.  An example specialization is #$EconomicIndexPredicate, instances include #$consumerPriceIndex-USA and #$stockIndexValue.")
(disjointWith Accident WeatherEvent)
(comment ArgFormatBinaryPredicate "The collection of binary predicates used to specify the required #$Format (q.v.) for a particular argument-place of a given #$Predicate.")
(comment ElectroMagneticIBT "The collection of information bearing objects that exist (i.e., are stored and displayed) by means of electro-mechanical devices such as computers.  This might also include holography, telephone signals, radio transmissions (while they exist as radio waves, not when they exist as sound), etc.  See also #$Signal and #$InformationBearingWavePropagation.")
(comment resourceInEvent "(#$resourceInEvent EVENT RESOURCE) means that, in any #$Plan in which the assertion holds, if AGENT is to be the #$performedBy in EVENT (i.e., if (#$performedBy EVENT AGENT) is asserted in PLAN), then it is a precondition for EVENT being #$successfulForAgents that AGENT #$controls RESOURCE. The precise meaning of #$controls will vary depending upon the thing playing the role of 'resource' in the context.--Rode, April 2, 1999")
(comment Sarin "An instance of #$NerveAgentType.")
(comment Impeachment "The collection of events involving the charging of a public official before a competent tribunal with misconduct in office.")
(comment HostingStateDelegation "The collection of events where a state hosts a delegation of officials from a foreign state.")
(comment BacteriumTypeByTemperature "A collection of collections and a division of #$Bacterium
according to the differences in temperature needed for optimum growth.
This collection divides the #$ProkaryoticCells into several
collections: #$ThermophilicBacterium, #$ThermoduricBacterium,
#$MesophilicBacterium, #$PsychrophilicBacterium, and
#$PsychotrophicBacterium.  The best growth occurs between a range of
temperatures for each division, but no growth will occur beyond the
maximum and minimum temperatures.")
(comment denotationRelatedTo "The predicate #$denotationRelatedTo is used to link English words with concepts indirectly related to their meanings.  For instance, both #$Wife-TheWord and #$Husband-TheWord are semantically connected to the predicate #$wife, but the two words do not denote the same relation.  If (#$denotationRelatedTo #$Husband-TheWord #$CountNoun 0 #$wife), we know that the word 'husband' somehow relates to #$wife, but should not be taken to denote it.")
(comment programCopyInstalledBy "(#$programCopyInstalledBy INSTALLATION AGENT) means that the instance of #$IntelligentAgent, AGENT, performs the instance of #$InstallingAProgramCopy, INSTALLATION.")
(comment ServingInTheMilitaryAgreement "The agreement between a #$PersonLegallyCapableOfMilitaryService and a #$MilitaryOrganization governing a #$ServingInTheMilitary event in which the person and organization are actors.")
(comment WritePermission "#$WritePermission is one of the three #$FilePermissions.  If an account has #$WritePermission for a file, it can legitimately alter the information on that file.")
(comment Venlafaxine "A #$PharmaceuticalType which is a subcategory of #$AntiDepressant.")
(comment EquivalenceClassFn "Equivalence relations \"carve up\" sets or collections to which

they apply into equivalence classes.  Each member of the original set

or collection belongs to one and only one of the resulting equivalence

classes.  Given an equivalence relation and set or collection which is

a subset of the domain of the relation, this function maps

elements of the set or collection to their equivalence

class under the equivalence relation, i.e. the things in the

collection to which they bear the equivalence relation.  

For

instance, #$levelWith is an equivalence relation.  Consider the 

collection which contains all and only those things in Cycorp office

space, call it \"CycorpOfficeStuff\", and a constant,

LargeConferenceRoomTable, that denoted the tallest

table in Cycorp's large conference room, then (#$EquivalenceClassFn

LargeConferenceRoomTable #$levelWith CycorpOfficeStuff) returns the

set of things at Cycorp that are level with the top of the

tallest table in the large conference room.  This function is useful

because equivalence relations partition collections and often we are

interested in discussing the abstractions resulting from such

partitionings rather than the original class itself.  This function

allows us to specify a specific abstraction that results from the

application of an equivalence relation. See also

#$EquivalencePartitionFn and #$EquivalenceCollectionFn.  Also note that if a collection, COL, is not

a subset of a relation's (ER) domain, then (EquivalenceClassFn

SETORCOL ER THING) is undefined.")
(comment HistoricallySignificantEvent "This is the collection of events which are somehow historically significant.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-DataFlooding "#$AttackByComputerOperation-DataFlooding is a subset of #$AttackByComputerOperation-DenialOfService.  It is the collection of electronic attacks in which an instance of #$ComputationalSystem is

    flooded with data with the aim of denying service to the system.")
(comment GermanWord "The collection of all lexical words in German; a subset of #$LexicalWord.            Different inflectional forms of a word do not count as different words.")
(comment MaterialsExchange "A materials exchange is an operation that enables

industrial process wastes, by-products, surplusses, or off-specification

materials to be transferred to another company where they are used

as a process input.")
(comment Salivating "A collection of events.  In each #$Salivating event, an #$Animal secretes #$Saliva from its #$SalivaryGlands.  #$Salivating is a natural bodily function, occurring in the #$Mouth.")
(comment MachineGun-GeneralPurpose "The collection of #$MachineGuns that could serve as a portable infantry weapon, usually when held with or without a bipod.  However, it is powerful enough to perform like a #$MachineGun-Heavy and at a sustainable rate  when it uses a tripod.")
(comment MFLOPS "A function, and an instance of #$UnitOfCPUCapacity. It is used to represent a unit (or \"benchmark\") of computer processor speed, representing the number (in millions) of \"full word-size floating-point multiply operations\" that can be performed per  second. It is thus similar to the #$MIPS benchmark. It has been argued that these benchmarks are misleading due to questions such as: What workload is being referred to? What counts as a floating point operations (loads, stores, intermediate steps, etc.)?")
(comment ChildrenPretending "Where children are #$Masquerading, or

roleplaying, as someone or something other than themselves.  For example,

children playing house, or doctor, or cops and robbers.")
(comment Buyer-Professional "Someone who works as a buyer for a company.")
(comment Ammonia "The collection of all volumes of ammonia gas, NH3.  This collection does not refer to the household product called ammonia, which is a solution or #$Ammonia in #$Water.")
(comment SubLNonVariableSymbol "The collection of all #$SubLSymbols except #$SubLVariables (qq.v.); a subcollection of #$CycLClosedAtomicTerm.  Note that `symbol' has a very specific, technical meaning in SubL; #$SubLNonVariableSymbols are rarely used in CycL assertions, except within those built with certain #$CycInferenceDescriptorPredicates like #$defnIff and those whose arguments are #$KeywordVariableTemplates (qq.v.). Examples of SubL non-variable symbols include the symbols `GENLS', `:ARG1', and `CYC-SYSTEM-NON-VARIABLE-SYMBOL-P'.  Note that this collection, like most instances of #$CycLExpressionType, is \"quoted\" (see #$quotedCollection).")
(comment fordingDepth "(#$fordingDepth VEHICLE HEIGHT) indicates the deepest waterlevel that can be crossed by VEHICLE.  Remember - if a vehicle is amphibious, then the fording depth is unlimited.")
(comment MoneyLaundering "A specialization of #$ActsCommonlyConsideredCriminal.  Each instance of #$MoneyLaundering is an activity in which the source of some money is obscured, typically by distributing the money over many accounts or repositories of money. Normally, such an activity occurs in cases where an agent has acquired some money illegally, and needs to hide that fact in order to avoid prosecution or to avoid paying taxes.")
(comment electricallyConnectedTo "(#$electricallyConnectedTo ARG1 ARG2) means that electrical current can flow freely from ARG1 to ARG2")
(comment FrictionlessMotion "In elements of #$FrictionlessMotion the #$frictionalForce is 0.  Frictionless motion although practically never occurring in the `real world' (maybe it happens in cases such as superconductivity, I don't know) is a useful concept with which to explain elementary physics.")
(comment headMedialString "(headMedialString STRINGS1 WORD STRINGS2 POS TERM) means that the TERM is denoted with POS part of speech by the concatenation of STRING1, WORD, and STRING2.  If TERM is a collection, the semantic meaning of TERM is (#$isa :noun TERM).  If TERM is an individual object, the semantic meaning of TERM is (#$equals :noun TERM).  See also #$multiWordSemTrans.")
(comment muchLessThanWRTScale "(#$muchLessThanWRTScale SMALL LARGE SCALE) says that the #$ScalarInterval SMALL is

 much less than the #$ScalarInterval LARGE, in so far as the standard by 

which we make the comparison is SCALE.  For example, (#$muchLessThanWRTScale

 (#$Foot-UnitOfMeasure 4) (#$Foot-UnitOfMeasure 7) HeightOfPerson) says that 

 4 feet is much less than 7 feet where heights of people are concerned.")
(comment EvaluatingFn "This is a function that, applied to a collection (type)  of object or services, denotes the collection of all events in which one or more objects or services of the specified type are evaluated by someone. (#$EvaluatingFn FOO) denotes the collection of all events in which instances of the collection FOO are evaluated.")
(comment CoolingProcess "A specialization of #$TemperatureChangingProcess.  Each instance of #$CoolingProcess is an event in which the temperature of some object (related to the instance of #$CoolingProcess by #$objectOfStateChange) is lowered.")
(disjointWith Automobile Weapon)
(comment treatmentAppliedToCondition "(#$treatmentAppliedToCondition TREATMENT CONDITION) means that TREATMENT  is the treatment applied to the person suffering from the #$AilmentCondition CONDITION.")
(comment Caisson-MilitaryPlatform "the collection of two-wheeled military vehicles used to transport ammunition.")
(comment Monotonic-JustificationStrength "The strength of a monotonic justification.")
(comment CoughDrop "A small object which, when sucked on, helps relieve coughing, often by coating the throat.")
(comment outside-UnderspecifiedRegion "(#$outside-UnderspecifiedRegion ACT REGION) states that an
abstract regional relation holds between ACT and REGION, where
REGION is the abstract region against which the action ACT is
specified.")
(comment ElectronVolt "Unit of energy equal to 1.6E-19 Joules.  Usually used in atomic or nuclear physics.")
(comment budgetExpenditures "(#$budgetExpenditures ORG COL THING MONEY) means that MONEY is a measure of the amount of money spent by the #$Organization ORG on instances of the specialization of #$SpatialThing-Localized COL during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  ORG might, for example, be a #$Business, a #$LegalGovernmentOrganization, or a #$Country.  COL might be any type of thing on or for which budget expenditures are made; for example, goods, services, institutions (such as government agencies or military organizations), or debt service.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.")
(comment Snowmobile "Motorized device for conveying one or two people across snow")
(comment Uracil-Base "A collection of molecules.  #$Uracil-Base is a pyramidine and one of four used in #$UracilRibonucleotide.  #$Uracil-Base is the

only #$NitrogenBase specific to RNA.  Its abbreviation is U.")
(comment Mushroom-Broadly "The collection of all mushrooms (a kind of #$Fungus) including puffballs, toadstools, bark ears, morels, etc.")
(comment CropPlant "#$CropPlant is a specialization of #$Plant.  Each instance of #$CropPlant is a plant that has been or is commonly grown and harvested as crops, e.g. #$TobaccoPlant, #$CornPlant, #$OrangeTree, etc.")
(comment Mixture "A specialization of #$PartiallyTangible.  Each instance of #$Mixture is a homogeneous partially tangible thing composed of two or more different constituents (see the predicate #$constituents) which have been mixed.  The  inputs to this mixing do not form chemical bonds among themselves, and at a later time the mixture may be separated back out into these inputs.  Specializations of #$Mixture include #$Blood, #$Mud, #$Air, and #$CarbonatedBeverage.  Note that each instance of #$Mixture has a composition but not a structure; thus, the following are _not_ instances of #$Mixture, since all have some structure: a wet sponge, a person, or a portion of plywood.")
(disjointWith State-UnitedStates FederalDistrict)
(comment SpermBank "The collection of sites for collecting and storing sperm (see #$Semen, #$SpermCell).")
(comment BusNetwork "#$BusNetwork is the collection of all instances of #$ComputerNetwork that have a bus topology. Ethernet networks are generally bus networks. In an instance of  #$BusNetwork, all computers attach to a central cable, called a bus or backbone.")
(comment RorschachTest "The collection of RorschachTests include the personality and intelligence tests in which a subject interprets inkblot designs. The interpretations are taken to be indicators of the emotional and mental state of the subject.")
(comment Alanine "A collection of compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.  These
compounds are essential for protein synthesis and are synthesized by
the body from pyruvate.  Its abbreviations are Ala and A.")
(comment expansionDefn "(#$expansionDefn <Relation> <Symbol>) denotes that during canonicalization

the subl function definition of <Symbol> is used to transform an EL expression

(<Relation> . <args>) into the appropriate HL formula.")
(comment DiacriticMark "The set of marks which can be added to letters or characters, usually indicating that the pronunciation of that character is different from what it normally would be.")
(comment MediumLiftHelicopterUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of moderately armed military units that are responsible for airlifting troops to the combat areas.")
(disjointWith MakeupBase Drink)
(comment StringTie "#$StringTie is the collection, a subset of #$Tie-Clothing, whose instances are very thin neck ties, worn around the neck and hanging down the front of the wearer's shirt.")
(comment BrightSpot-Topographical "The collection of all topographical features noted for significantly higher albedo than surrounding terrain.")
(comment ColorTypeByChromaticity "A collection of collections of collections. Each instance is a specialization of #$Color such that all the instances of the collection union of the set of instances of the specialization have the same chromaticness in their coloring.")
(disjointWith AutomaticCarWindow ManualCarWindow)
(comment GiftBasketTypeByContent "A collection of collection.  Each instance of #$GiftBasketTypeByContent is a collection of instances of #$GiftBaskets that have similar contents.")
(comment MotorizedUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all motorized military units. A 'motorized' unit employs           motorized vehicles for transport and/or combat.")
(comment RoadAtlas "The collection of all road atlases: documents that consist primarily of a large number of #$RoadMaps, all unified by a theme.")
(comment HumidSubtropicalClimateCycle "A specialization of both #$HumidClimateCycle and #$TemperateClimateCycle.  Each instance of #$HumidSubtropicalClimateCycle is a year-long event consisting of weather occurring (typically) within a temperate climate zone.  Characteristics of a humid subtropical climate cycle include a hot summer and a cool winter, with precipitation and moist air throughout.  Cycles of this kind occur closer to the equator than do instances of #$HumidContinentalClimateCycle (q.v.).  For instance, the Southeastern United States is a good example of a region whose annual climate cycles are instances of #$HumidSubtropicalClimateCycle.")
(comment centralReferencePoint "(#$centralReferencePoint OBJECT REFERENCE) means that REFERENCE serves as a reference point from which distance or remoteness is typically measured.  For example (#$centralReferencePoint #$CityOfMexicoCityMexico Zocalo) says that the Zocalo serves as the commonly agreed-on center of Mexico City, and that the relative remoteness of two locations in Mexico City will be judged with respect to their distances from the Zocalo.  As another example (#$centralReferencePoint FredsArm FredsTorso) says that the distance (along Fred's arm) to Fred's torso determines which parts of his arm are #$distalTo other parts.  Note that in this case, the #$centralReferencePoint of OBJECT is not within OBJECT.")
(comment mandatoryGameEquipmentType "(#$mandatoryGameEquipmentType GAME EQUIPMENT_TYPE) means that at least one instance of EQUIPMENT_TYPE must be used in any playing of GAME.")
(comment AMAHospitalID "The collection of all American Medical Association #$IDStrings used to identify hospitals.")
(comment CollectionUnionFn "(#$CollectionUnionFn SET-OF-COLS) is the collection that is by definition the \"collection-union\" (see #$collectionUnion) of all of the collections in the set SET-OF-COLS.")
(comment waveSource "The predicate #$waveSource is used to indicate that a type of wave is travelling between a source and a reception point.  (#$waveSource SOURCE ENDPOINT WAVETYPE) means that there is a #$WavePropagation of type WAVETYPE propagating between the #$fromLocation SOURCE and the #$toLocation ENDPOINT.  For example, (#$waveSource VoiceOfAmerica-Seoul #$CityOfBeijingChina #$RadioWave).")
(comment Court-Judicial "#$Court-Judicial is a specialization of  #$Organization, #$GovernmentAgency, and #$JudicialAgent.  Each instance of #$Court-Judicial is an established judicial court, i.e., an enduring governmental organization whose primary function is to settle disputes by means of legal reasoning by one or more #$Judges (q.v.).  Typically, a court's orders are enforced by some other agency belonging to the government of which that court is a part.  The collection #$Court-Judicial includes federal, state, county, and municipal courts, appellate and chancery courts, tax courts, courts of claims, courts-martial (if non-temporary), admiralty courts, courts of chivalry, American Indian tribal courts, and the Permanent Court of International Justice.  It excludes Gypsy/Rom Kris courts, nonjudicial administrative county courts, stannaries, and temporary #$Tribunals (q.v.).")
(comment AilmentConditionTypeBySyndrome "The collection of types of abnormal medical or psychological conditions indicated by a collection of symptoms, but not attributed to a single infecting organism.")
(comment ArableLand "The collection of land areas which are suitable for farming, whether or not they are actually in use for crop production at any given moment.")
(comment FAQFn "#$FAQFn takes as argument any instance of #$Thing and returns the collection of InformationBearingObjects containing answers to frequently asked questions about that thing (FAQs about that thing).  For example, (#$FAQFn #$Snoopy) returns the collection of all FAQs about the #$FictionalCharacter #$Snoopy, and (#$FAQFn #$UnitedStatesCoastGuard) returns the collection of all FAQs about the US Coast Guard.")
(comment objectFound-IndefiniteDeRe "This is the \"third-party perspective\" way of saying that a
#$LookingForSomething-Indefinite has succeeded, incrementally or totally
(cf #$objectFound-Indefinite). `(#$objectFound-IndefiniteDeRe SEARCH
SEEKER OBJECT)' means that SEEKER has found OBJECT in SEARCH and
that OBJECT is an instance of the type of thing for which they were
looking. This predicate is useful in cases where we don't know how
the searcher conceives of the sort of object sought. Compare this
to #$objectFound-Indefinite, whose third argument position is opaque.")
(comment MountainRange "A specialization of #$LandTopographicalFeature.  Each instance of #$MountainRange is a natural group of mountains.  Instances of #$MountainRange include the #$RockyMountains, #$Andes-Mountains, and #$Alps-Mountains.")
(comment compositionFeaturesSoloistTypeCount "(#$compositionFeaturesSoloistTypeCount COMP TYPE INT) means that the #$MusicalComposition COMP features INT solists of type TYPE. For instance, (#$compositionFeaturesSoloistTypeCount BachDoubleViolinConcerto (#$PlayerOfInstrumentFn #$Violin) 2) means that the Bach double violin concerto features two violin soloists.")
(comment MassCommunicating "Communication actions in which a great many agents are the targets of the communication. This is not necessarily limited to communications which use broadcast media such as television or radio -- it also includes mass communications accomplished by print media, by telephoning lots of people, by individually telling many people the same message, or by using a combination of media. Examples: an ad campaign, a ``get out the vote'' effort, or a smear campaign.")
(comment ParaphilicSexualBehavior "The collection of #$ParaphilicSexualBehaviors includes activities or behaviors which are experienced by those so-oriented as erotic or sexually stimulating. #$ParaphilicSexualBehaviors are those behaviors considered non-erotic, deviant, or repugnant to the general populace. For example, the activities included in Pedophilia are experienced as erotic to someone with pedophilic proclivities.")
(comment Warhead-CruiseMissile "A #$Warhead designed to be used with a #$CruiseMissile.")
(comment Vasodilator "A substance which causes the blood vessels of someone taking it to dilate.")
(comment Graphite "A soft, black, lustrous form of carbon.")
(comment ArchiveOfBroadcastSeriesFn "This function takes any instance of #$BroadcastSeriesProduct and returns the collection of all archives [#$ArchiveHoldings] of that type.  For example, (#$ArchiveOfBroadcastSeriesFn

#$TheShadow-RadioSeries) returns the collection of all archives, in any format, of the radio show 'The Shadow'.")
(comment SmokingJacket "The collection of soft, belted #$Jackets that were, in recent modern Western culture, worn by men, at home.")
(comment Franc-Luxembourg "The monitary unit in #$Luxembourg.")
(comment keWeakSuggestion "(#$keWeakSuggestion TERM FORMULA) states a weak suggestion that FORMULA should possibly be known to be true about TERM.  This is most useful at expressing weak suggestions or expectations about TERM which can then be used by tools that look for KB omissions, or conditions that explicitly violate these expectations.  See also #$keRequirements, #$keStrongSuggestion, #$kePlausibleConsideration, #$keStrongConsideration.")
(comment PhraseStructureSchema "All HPSG phrase structure rules are reified as concepts, and represented as instances of #$PhraseStructureSchema.")
(comment PullingAnObjectAlongWith "A collection of #$PullingAnObjectAlong events in which the the #$pullee follows the motion of the #$puller due to the pulling.")
(disjointWith SeasonalGiftGivingOccasionType NonSeasonalGiftGivingOccasionType)
(comment Anemia "The collection of instances of the condition in which   the red cells of the blood (erythrocytes) are reduced in number or  volume or are deficient in hemoglobin, their oxygen-carrying pigment.  There are close to 100 different varieties of anemia, distinguished  by the cause, the size and hemoglobin content of the abnormal cells, and the symptoms.")
(comment Barley-TheGrain "Individual barley kernels, which are the fruits of the barley plant.")
(comment NetworkTraffic-SingleLAN "#$NetworkTraffic-SingleLAN is the collection of measures of network traffic on individual instances of #$LocalAreaNetwork.  This refers to the network traffic within the LAN.  To refer more generally to this traffic as well as that external to the individual LAN use #$ComputerNetworkTraffic.")
(comment PureSubstanceType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection.  Each instance of #$PureSubstanceType is both a specialization of #$PureSubstance (q.v.) and a specialization of some instance of #$ChemicalSubstanceType (q.v.).  Each instance of #$PureSubstanceType is characterized by the properties of the instance of #$ChemicalSubstanceType of which it is a specialization, and by the fact that each of its instances is chemically pure.")
(comment GroundBattle "The collection of all #$Battles that have significant ground forces opposing one another.  An air raid on a city is not a #$GroundBattle, but a #$GroundBattle can include air attacks and naval bombardment.")
(comment MassageTherapy "The collection of all #$ServiceEvents where #$Massaging is used to  soothe or cure some physical ailment.  Not a #$MedicalCareEvent, since it is not always performed by medical professionals.")
(comment ZipCodeFinder "The collection of all #$SearchEngines designed to help users find information about postal #$ZipCode.")
(comment SpecifiedPlay-DramaticType "A collection of collections, each element of #$SpecifiedPlay-DramaticType is a collection of performances of some dramatic work such as 'Hamlet'. So, all performances of 'Hamlet constitute a collection of performances of a particular dramatic work, and this collection would be an element of #$SpecifiedPlay-DramaticType.")
(comment PrivateFirstClass-Title "This Cyc constant denotes the term of address used for someone holding the rank-attribute of #$PrivateFirstClass-Rank in an  instance of #$ModernMilitaryOrganization.  Often abbreviated as PFC in text.  This ranks above #$Private-Title or 'buck private'.")
(disjointWith Sound ElectromagneticRadiation)
(comment keWeakSuggestionPreds "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate (q.v.) and specialization of #$keRelevantPreds that relates a collection to a binary predicate.  (#$keWeakSuggestionPreds COL BINPRED) means that for every known (i.e. Cyc-reified) instance INST of COL, it is weakly suggested that there be some reified THING such that (BINPRED INST THING) is known in the Knowledge Base.  See also #$keStrongSuggestionPreds and #$keWeakSuggestionInverse.")
(disjointWith UnitOfFrequency UnitOfSpeed)
(disjointWith Raft RowingShell)
(comment geneticallyIdentical "(#$geneticallyIdentical IND1 IND2) is true iff IND1 and IND2 have exactly the same genetic makeup,  as is the case with monozygotic #$twins")
(comment VulnerableToComputerVirusInfiltration "An attribute applying to instances of #$ComputationalSystem.  A computational system has the attribute #$VulnerableToComputerVirusInfiltration if it is configured in such a way as to allow a known instance of #$ComputerVirus to infiltrate the system.")
(comment LessonPlan "The collection of all lesson plans - #$Plans made by or for #$Teachers about how to conduct one or more lessons or classes.")
(comment Movie-CW "A specialization of #$VideoConceptualWork.  Each instance of #$Movie-CW is an abstract work whose performances are instances of #$MovieShowing.  Notable instances are #$CitizenKane-TheMovie and #$StarWars-TheMovie.")
(comment MRNAProductionProcess "The process whereby messenger RNA (mRNA) is generated from

information encoded in DNA molecules.  In the present CycL

representation we take it that mRNA production consists in the stages

of RNA Transcription that follow the production of the

#$PrimaryTranscript-RNAMolecule and which result in the production of a

mRNA molecule (see #$MessengerRNA).  Substages include the #$CappingProcess-ChemicalReaction, the

#$PolyadenylationProcess, and intron excision

(see #$RNASplicingProcess)")
(comment tourNightLodging "(#$tourNightLodging TOUR DAY BLDG) means that on DAY, the
participants in TOUR will spend the night at BLDG.")
(comment PortalCovering "A specialization of #$SolidTangibleThing.  Each instance of #$PortalCovering is a solid tangible object that covers a portal.  Instances of #$PortalCovering may be either flexible or rigid, and they may be either fixed in place or removable.  Examples include windows (in buildings or automobiles), doors, shutters, screens, draperies, window blinds, convertible tops, lids, and corks.")
(comment Lattice-LatticeTheoretic "The collection of all mathmetical structures called 'lattices' in Lattice Theory (this is not the same concept as the crystalline or grid lattices studied in Crystallography and Group Theory).  A #$Lattice-LatticeTheoretic is often defined in different but equivalent ways.  To define a lattice using ordering relation, it is a #$PartialOrdering ORDER in which each pair of elements of the #$baseSet S of ORDER has an R-smallest upper bound and an R-greatest lower bound, where R is the ordering relation on S.  To define a lattice using operations, it is a mathematical structure with two operations MEET and JOIN on the #$baseSet S of the structure that satisfy the commutative laws, the associative laws, the idempotent laws and the absorption laws.  Note that the correspondence of these two different ways of defining lattices is characterized by the following: for all X, Y in S, Y = (JOIN X Y) <=> R(X Y) <=> X = (MEET X Y).  See #$meetFunctionOnLattice and #$joinFunctionOnLattice.")
(comment placeName-LocalShortForm "(#$placeName-LocalShortForm PLACE NAME) means that NAME is a short-form name of the #$GeographicalThing PLACE used by people who live in or near PLACE.")
(comment Horse-Gelding "The collection of male #$Horses that have been castrated.  Most domesticated male horses used for riding or for any purposes other than breeding are geldings.")
(comment DataMining "Also known as knowledge discovery in databases and information archeology, this is the semi-automated discovery of trends and patterns across very large datasets, usually for the purposes of decision-making.")
(comment RNASplicingProcess "The process where by intron sequences are excised from a #$PrimaryTranscript-RNAMolecule in the #$MRNAProductionProcess.")
(comment outboundLegOfRoundTrip "(#$outboundLegOfRoundTrip TRIP OUTBOUND) means that the translational movement OUTBOUND is the initial portion of the round-trip translation event TRIP.  During the OUTBOUND leg, the object moving in TRIP (see the predicate #$objectMoving) travels from the origin of TRIP (see the predicate #$origin-RoundTrip) to its destination (see the predicate #$destination-RoundTrip).  Note that the starting point for OUTBOUND (related to OUTBOUND by #$fromLocation) is the same as the starting point for TRIP, and the ending point for OUTBOUND (related to OUTBOUND by #$toLocation) is the same as the destination for TRIP (related to TRIP by #$destination-RoundTrip).")
(comment decileIn "(#$decileIn DECILE_STRUCTURE VALUE N) means that VALUE appears in the Nth decile of DECILE_STRUCTURE.")
(comment Barcode "a series of printed parallel lines or bars used on products in stores, addresses on envelopes, etc to encode information.")
(comment cooperationLevel "(#$cooperationLevel COOP LEVEL) means that the cooperation level of the CooperationEvent COOP IS as described in LEVEL.  Here IS emphasize the time when the sentence (#$cooperationLevel COOP LEVEL) is evaluated since the level of the cooperation may change during the temporal extension of COOP.  Note that the LEVEL only has a relative value in the sense that only the comparison of different values (rather than the values themselves) has real meanings.  For example, a COOP may start from a small trade between two countries, followed by some official agreement of cooperation on some econimic projects, which in turn is followed by some military cooperation.  The level of cooperation increases in such an example from each stage to the next.")
(comment MicrotheorySpindle "The collection of all structures of microtheories consisting of a single common #$genlMt (the mtSpindleHead), a single common specMt (the mtSpindleCollector), and a significant number of other mts which mutually are neither #$genlMts or specMts, but are #$mtSpindleMembers of the #$MicrotheorySpindle.")
(comment ShigellaSonnei " A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom.")
(comment AcademyAward "A specialization of #$AwardPractice.  Each instance of #$AcademyAward is given by the #$AcademyOfMotionPictureArtsAndSciences.  Note that the award is an intangible.  Multiple Oscar statuettes may be given for one award, when there are collaborators, or on the rare occasions of a tie.")
(comment RequestForSanctions "The collection of actions in which one agent asks a third party for sanctions against another agent.")
(comment ProteinMolecule "The collection of molecules of proteins. Instances are defined

chemically as polymers made up of amino acids. Compare with

#$ProteinStuff.")
(comment SystemOfDevices-Communications "A subcollection of #$SystemOfDevices.  The collection           #$SystemOfDevices-Communications consists of those instances of           #$SystemOfDevices constructed at least in part to be a #$deviceUsed for           or in instances of #$Communicating.  They may have other intended           uses as well.  For example, an instance of #$SystemOfDevices consisting of           instances of #$Computer would be an instance of           #$SystemOfDevices-Communications if part of the purpose in           constructing the system of computers were to allow communication           among users of them or if communication           among users of them via the system were necessary to fulfill           the primary function of the system.  The system,           however, would probably have other purposes as well.           Note that some #$groupMembers of any instance of           #$SystemOfDevices-Communications will be instances of           #$CommunicationDevice (often of the same type) and all 'links' among these           members will allow the transfer of information appropriate to the type(s) of           communication devices.  For instance, any instance of           #$TelephoneSystem will have as #$groupMembers instances of            #$Telephone and, of course, these instances may be connected by           instances of #$TelephoneLine.")
(comment NationalDrugCode "Aka: NDC. A unique ID assigned to each prescription drug product on the US market.  This ID encodes information about who manufactures the product, the dosage form and strength, package size and compound used; however, we probably won't bother looking 'inside' an NDC to get this information.")
(comment TourGuide "A person who guides travel tour.")
(disjointWith CombatAircraft TransportAircraft)
(comment GourmetFood "The collection of all food or drink considered to be ``gormet'' food.  Specs of this collection vary with time, location, and culture.")
(comment toPreventInPlan-SitType "(#$toPreventInPlan-SitType PLAN SITTYPE) means that the

success of the plan represented by the #$SupposedToBeMicrotheory PLAN

is contingent upon a situation of type SITTYPE not 'happening' in the

course of the plan.")
(comment Succulent-Plant "The collection of all succulent #$Plants (of various #$BiologicalSpecies).")
(comment FluidFlowEvent "A specialization of #$MovementOrShapeChangeEvent.  Each instance of #$FluidFlowEvent is an event in which a fluid moves (or a group of particles collectively moves).  The spatial extent of the fluid may change (i.e. expansion or contraction, see #$ShapingSomething) and/or they may undergo a #$MovementEvent such as rotation (e.g. a whirlpool or a tornado) and/or translation.  If the fluid undergoes translation, then the event is also an instance of #$FluidFlow-Translation.  Examples of #$FluidFlow-Translation include `partial' motions such as occurs in rivers flowing, or jets of air blowing.  Another kind of example of #$FluidFlow-Translation is #$FluidFlow-Complete, in which the fluid moves entirely from the #$fromLocation and to the
#$toLocation.")
(comment AuthenticationEvent "#$AuthenticationEvent is the collection of events in which some sort of authentication or certification takes place.  For example, this includes certifying a person's identity, the authenticity  of a document, or the security of a computer login.")
(comment IsotopeFn "(IsotopeFn ?ELT ?NUMBER) denotes the collection of pieces of #$ElementStuff ?ELT which have a mass number of ?NUMBER. ?ELT and (IsotopeFn ?ELT ?NUMBER) will be forms of the same chemical element, but with different numbers of neutrons. For example, (IsotopeFn Uranium 235) picks out the collection of pieces of #$Uranium whose atoms have 92 #$Protons and 143 #$Neutrons.")
(comment subpurposeInEvent "(#$subpurposeInEvent Agent Event Goal) says that the Goal is not the real purpose of the Event, but it's a
          desired #$actionIntendedEpiphenomena. by the Agent. These can be considered a 'soft' purpose, rather than the
          'hard' purpose of #$purposeInEvent. For instance, my main purpose may be to inform someone of something. If I
          can also get a humorous dig in edgewise, in a passive agressive fashion, that would be a subpurpose. Note that
          I can achieve my goal with an action that does not acheive the #$actionIntendedEpiphenomena specified by
          #$subpurposeInEvent.")
(comment WildWeasel "The collection of F-4G #$MilitaryAircraft used mostly by the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica during Desert Storm to suppress enemy air defense systems. These aircraft are modified #$F-4E-Fighters with their cannons replaced with electronic warfare equipment which detects and counteracts enemy ground radar systems.")
(comment CumulusCloud "The collection of bumpy low-level clouds (#$CloudInSky) with flat dark bases (because of their thickness) and light tops.")
(comment TersifyBackward "A property of reformulator rules which says that in this rule,
the terse argument comes before the verbose argument.")
(comment decontextualizedPredicate "(#$decontextualizedPredicate PRED) states that PRED is a predicate which is context-independent.  In effect, any use of PRED can be lifted into any microtheory.  Predicates which are labelled with #$decontextualizedPredicate typically have an argument which either implicitly or explicitly provides the implied context.  A good example of such a predicate is #$ist.")
(disjointWith ProjectileWeapon BladedWeapon-NonProjectile)
(comment EmittingAWave "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$Emission.  Each instance is an event in which a wave is emitted at a #$fromLocation.  For example, Themistocles ordering his fleet to withdraw; Miles Davis playing the trumpet; an emergency flare burning by the side of the road.  See also #$WavePropagation.")
(comment LivestockFarm "The collection of all farms that raise some kind of animal.  This need not be restricted to traditional farm animals -- catfish and worm farms are also livestock farms.")
(comment CharacterSet "A collection of collections.

Each instance of #$CharacterSet is a collection of abstract

characters (i.e. a specialization of #$Character-Abstract).

Instances include #$UpperCaseLetter, #$Hieroglyph, and 

#$AuxiliaryWritingSymbol.  For a more specialized 

collection-type, any instance of which is the set of characters

used in some _particular_ writing system, see 

#$WritingSymbolCharacterSet.")
(comment MissileSystem "A collection of #$WeaponSystems.  Instances of #$MissileSystem
are designed to detect and destroy incoming missiles.")
(comment ProxyServer-Network "#$ProxyServer-Network is a specialization of #$ComputerServer.  Instances of this collection provide caches of items available on other servers which are presumably slower or more expensive to access.")
(comment rampEndLocation "(#$rampEndLocation RAMP LOCATION) means that the ramp-shaped #$PersistenceDistribution RAMP ends at LOCATION (a specified time or place).  For example, the LOCATION used to specify a temporal ramp persistence distribution might be (#$YearFn 1970), meaning that for the assertion or assertions to which the ramp distribution pertains, the changing likelihood of being true would reach a high (low) point (the ramp would end) at the year 1970.")
(comment AspergersSyndrome "The collection of #$AilmentConditions in which there is a pervasive developmental disorder characterized by an inability to understand how to interact socially.  Other features include clumsy and uncoordinated motor movements, extreme egocentricity, non-verbal communication problems, etc.  The boundary between this condition and #$Autism is fuzzy.")
(disjointWith Communicating SteeringADeviceByHand)
(comment HomeStudy "A collection of events. Each instance of #$HomeStudy one #$Person going through a #$CourseOfStudy at home, independently, using a set of course materials, but with no human teacher or tutor in the home. The student may correspond with a human teacher or tutor, however.")
(comment WideAreaNetwork "A subcollection of #$ComputerNetwork in which computers
separated by substantial distances interconnect.  Because
of the substantial distances involved, the connections will
often involve telephone lines, underground cables or satellites.
Contrast this
collection with #$LocalAreaNetwork (LAN).  Often, the computers
in an LAN will all be in the same building whereas those
in a wide area network (WAN) will always span more than one
building.")
(comment FluidPlanetaryBody "A collection of heavenly bodies.  Each element of #$FluidPlanetaryBody is a planetary body composed primarily of fluid (gas or liquid) substances.")
(comment ImitationOfIndividualFn "(#$ImitationOfIndividualFn ORIGINAL) returns a collection that is a            subset of #$ImitationOfIndividual. The subset of  #$ImitationOfIndividual            returned by (#$ImitationOfIndividualFn ORIGINAL)            is the collection of the instances of #$TemporalThing that have been            designed by someone to seem similar to the instance of #$TemporalThing,            ORIGINAL. For example, (#$ImitationOfIndividualFn #$StatueOfLiberty) is            the subset of #$ImitationOfIndividual whose instances are only every            imitation of the Statue of Liberty. Compare this function to            #$ImitationOfCollectionFn.")
(comment CefuroximeSodium "The chemical compound which is an antibiotic.")
(comment DisplayStructure "The collection of structures used to house objects that are being displayed to the public for their enjoyment and edification.")
(comment 1-TheDigit "The numeral 1 of the Arabic Number system.  This is '1' as a #$Character-Abstract rather than the physical #$WrittenCharacter or the abstract mathematical #$Number-General (see #$One).")
(comment Franc-Vanuatu "one of the Units of currency in Vanuatu")
(comment Elf "The mythical race of slender, magical beings described in such works as #$LordOfTheRings-Trilogy, and employed as characters in #$DungeonsAndDragons the #$RolePlayingGame.")
(comment SecuritiesUnderwriter "A specialization of #$CommercialOrganization.  Each instance of #$SecuritiesUnderwriter is an organization which brings new tradeable securities (see the collection #$TradeableSecurity) to the investment public through offerings.")
(comment IsopropylAlcohol "Rubbing alcohol-- a topical solution used on skin to prevent infection, etc.")
(comment ReproductiveFertilizationEvent "A collection of events.  In each element of #$ReproductiveFertilizationEvent, gametes fuse to form a zygote.")
(comment ComputerGameEvent "The collection of events consisting of a game (e.g. #$DungeonsAndDragons) being played in its entirety on a #$Computer.")
(comment TrickOrTreating "TrickOrTreating is a collection of events which take place on Halloween children dress in costumes on the Halloween evening, and go from house to house collecting candy.")
(comment filterTerms "The predicate indicating that a term should be filtered whenever the associated   instance of #$TranscriptFilter is active.  (filterTerms FILTER TERM) means that   adding FILTER to the transcript filters being filtered from remote operations will   effectively add TERM to the terms being filtered.")
(comment nearestCommonGenlMt "(#$nearestCommonGenlMt MT-1 MT-2 NEAR-MT) relates microtheories MT-1 and MT-2 to the nearest unsubsumed microtheories NEAR-MT of which both are spec microtheories.  This predicate is #$notAssertible, since it must always be recomputed from the current state of the #$genlMt hierarchy.")
(comment GiftGivingOccasionType "The collection of all occasion types for which it is appropriate (relative to some social norm) to give a gift to a person. Each instance is a collection of events of a certain type. Some instances are such that gifts are given on that occasion to recipients who participate in the event merely as a celebrant (see #$socialParticipants), e.g., #$ChristmasHoliday. Other instances are such that gifts are given on that occasion only to recipients who play the role of #$performedBy in the event, e.g., #$GraduatingEvent.")
(comment WindowWasher "Someone who washes windows as a job.")
(comment GeneticallyEngineeredVirus "The collection of all instances of #$Virus

   that have been genetically altered to serve

    some (usually medical) purpose.")
(comment Superpower "The collection of the world's most dominant countries.  Each  instance of #$Superpower is very powerful both politically and militarily around the world.  Throughout history countries have tended to align  themselves with a superpower.")
(comment PublicTransportationDevice "#$PublicTransportationDevice is a specialization of #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle and #$HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject.  Each instance of #$PublicTransportationDevice is a vehicle used for mass public transportation. Examples include

#$Bus-RoadVehicle, #$Train-TransportationDevice, #$Ferry. #$TaxiCab is

a non example.")
(comment chemicalProducts-TypeType "(#$chemicalProducts-TypeType REACTION-TYPE PRODUCT-TYPE) means that instances of the #$ChemicalSubstanceType PRODUCT-TYPE are produced in instances of REACTION-TYPE. The products are those chemicals that are formed by a reaction.")
(comment BaseballShortstop "The collection of all #$BaseballPlayers who play the position of shortstop on a #$BaseballTeam. The position is played between second and third base.")
(comment Rod-AnimalBodyPart "The collection of all rod cells in #$Vertebrate #$Retinas.  Rod cells are sensitive to dimmer light than cone cells (#$Cone-AnimalBodyPart), but do not detect color.")
(comment aligned-LengthAlongSurface "(#$aligned-LengthAlongSurface OBJ1 OBJ2) means that #$LongAndThin OBJ1 is #$alignedAlong the surface of OBJ2 along (most of) the whole length of OBJ1.")
(comment EscortingSomeone "These are escorting events relating to security procedures, rather than to entertainment.")
(comment Hurdle "The collection of hurdles that runners jump over in HurdleSportsEvents.")
(comment Hawk-SAMVehicle "A type of SAM Vehicle.")
(comment Bohrium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is a RadioactiveObject of #$Bohrium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment trajectory-Partial "(#$trajectory-Partial MOVE TRAJ) means that the #$Movement-TranslationEvent MOVE has at least part of its entire trajectory, i.e., the line or curve in space traced out by the whole motion, in common with a sub-trajectory of the #$Trajectory TRAJ where the motion along the shared segment moves in the same direction as TRAJ goes.  See also #$trajectory-Complete.  Contrast #$trajectory-Partial with #$motionPathway-Partial and with #$traverses-Partial.  The trajectory of the motion may cross itself, zig-zag back and forth along the same path, repeat several cycles, etc., (like a #$Traversal and unlike a #$Path-Generic), and the trajectory need not be confined to any pre-existing #$Path-Generics or #$Traversals of paths.")
(comment InterArgFormatPredicate "The subcollection of both #$InterArgConstraintPredicate and #$ArgFormatPredicate (qq.v.) whose instances are used to specify, for a given predicate PRED, a certain #$Format requirement on one of PRED's arguments (the \"dependent\" one), contingent upon one (usually, but not always, a different one) of PRED's arguments (the \"independent\" one) being an instance of (#$isa) a certain collection.  Currently, each instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate is ternary, where its first argument (or \"arg1\") is the predicate PRED upon which the constraint is being placed, its arg2 the collection serving as the #$isa condition on PRED's independent argument, and its arg3 the #$Format that PRED's dependent argument is (conditionally) constrained to have.  The (numerically-specified) identities of the arguments of PRED's that are to serve as the independent and dependent arguments are fixed for each instance of 

#$InterArgFormatPredicate.")
(comment agentResourceInEvent "(#$agentResourceInEvent ACT AGENT) means that for ACT to be #$successfulForAgents for any performing agent, it must be the case that AGENT is #$behaviorCapable of playing the role of #$assistingAgent in any specialization of #$Event of which ACT is an instance.--Rode, April 2, 1999")
(comment Solution "An instance of #$ExistingStuffType, and a specialization of #$Mixture.  Each instance of #$Solution is a mixture of two or more chemically distinct substances.  Instances of #$Solution are homogeneous, meaning that the composition at any one point in a given instance is the same as that at any other point.  In contrast, instances of #$Suspension are mixtures in which small discontinuous particles are surrounded by a continuous fluid.  The #$solvent of every #$Solution has the #$stateOfMatter #$Liquid-StateOfMatter.  Thus #$Solutions also normally exhibit the properties of a liquid, since #$solvents are #$mainConstituents.   Examples of #$Solutions include a sample of seawater, a cup of coffee, a tincture of iodine, some vanilla extract.")
(comment InterviewQuestion "Questions asked at interviews.")
(comment ProvidingDiplomaticAssistance "The collection of events where a state provides diplomatic assistance to another state.")
(comment ThermophilicBacterium "A collection of #$Bacterium with an optimum growth
temperature of greater than (#$DegreeCelsius 45).  These
#$ProkaryoticCells occur in #$Habitats such as composts, hot springs
and hydrothermal vents on the ocean floor.")
(comment Atlas "The collection of all atlases: documents that consist primarily of a large number of #$Maps, all unified by a theme. The #$Maps in an atlas usually combine to represent different aspects of a single geographical region or different subregions of a large region.")
(comment HumanAccessibleIBT "A collection of #$InformationBearingThings, each of which contains information, for a #$Person who understands how to interpret it.  Examples include a copy of the novel _Moby Dick_, a signal buoy, a #$Photograph, a #$Flag, an elevator sign in Braille, a map, a US dollar bill, a word in #$AmericanSignLanguage and a musical performance.  #$InformationBearingThings that must be processed by some device (movie reels, #$PhonographRecords, #$DVD-Disks, etc.) are not included in this collection. An important specialization of this collection is #$HumanAccessibleIBO, composed of #$HumanAccessibleIBTs that are also objects (i.e,. instances of #$PartiallyTangible). Thus the copy of _Moby Dick_, the buoy, the photograph and the flag mentioned above are also #$HumanAccessibleIBOs -- but not the word in #$AmericanSignLanguage, nor the musical performance.")
(comment CardiovascularAgent "Drugs commonly used to treat diseases and conditions of the circulatory system.")
(comment ScheduleFn-TransportationProvider "(#$ScheduleFn-TransportationProvider TRANCO) returns the collection of all instances of #$Schedule that include information on times and dates of transportation services provided by TRANCO.  For example (#$ScheduleFn-TransportationProvider Amtrak-TransportationCompany) returns the collection of all schedules that include timetables or other information on the times and dates of Amtrak rail services.")
(comment (RightObjectOfPairFn (PartTypeFn NinthThoracicVertebra VertebralTransverseProcess)) "")
(comment informationChannel-FunctionalRole "(#$informationChannel-FunctionalRole SYSTEM CHANNEL) means that CHANNEL is responsible for facilitating transmission of #$InformationBearingThings from one location to another within SYSTEM.  It may be assumed to entail that there is a level of graphical abstraction according to which CHANNEL may be represented as a #$Path-Simple within SYSTEM, along which information travels.")
(comment kePossibleRelation "(#$kePossibleRelation TERM1 TERM2 FORMULA) states that FORMULA would be a semantically well-formed way of relating the two terms TERM1 and TERM2.  For example, (#$kePossibleRelation #$Canada #$France (#$bordersOn #$Canada #$France)) states that one way of possible relating #$Canada to #$France would be to say that they border on each other.  Note that the FORMULA is not restricted to being known true, or even not known to be false, merely not trivially rejected by argument constraints.  See also #$admittedSentence.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-Distributed "#$AttackByComputerOperation-Distributed is a subset of #$AttackByComputerOperation.  It is the collection of electronic attacks which are initiated from  multiple sources. These attacks typically involve the use of tools  which have been placed on various clients and set to attack a single host or network at some later time. Usually all the distributed tools are set to attack simultaneously (see #$AttackByComputerOperation-Coordinated).")
(comment Convoy "The collection of all convoys of vehicles.  Each instance of #$Convoy is a composite object (a #$Group) that has various #$TransportationDevices as #$groupMembers.  In a #$Convoy, the member vehicles travel together in a line and close together, one behind the other.  #$Convoys of #$Ships and #$Trucks are often used in military operations.")
(comment Sweating "The excretion of sweat from the skin. It is an animal activity")
(comment MachineGun-Light "The collection of #$MachineGuns that are light enough to be carried  by one man, who would be expected to keep pace with the riflemen and give  them instant fire support.  They are not expected to sustain their rates of  fire for long without overheating.  Most use magazines as being better suited to mobility than belts.")
(disjointWith Time-Quantity ElectricalCharge)
(comment WorkingACashRegister "the collection of events in which a cashier works a cash register.")
(comment IATenseLogicTestConstant "#$IATenseLogicTestConstant is the collection of constants created to permit testing of  tense logic for the purposes of the IA scenario.")
(comment GapInPathArtifact "The collection of all #$SpatialThings that are located where a portion of a #$PathArtifact ''should'' be.  This includes: a #$PieceOfFreeSpace forming a gap where a section of #$Bridge used to be, or a strech of #$Street-Generic blocked by a pile of rocks.")
(comment complementaryDNAStrands "Two instances of #$DNAStrand stand in this relation to each other
if their bases can be paired***. Each DNA molecule consists of two
complementary strands.")
(comment StatingSomething "#$StatingSomething means declaring, asserting, setting forth an #$InformationBearingThing, in particular, a #$Statement.  The #$Statement is by default propositional.")
(comment Marble-Stone "All pieces of marble, which is a form of limestone that has been crystallized")
(comment Investigation "Collection of all instances of human inquiry where what is being sought is a deeper understanding of the nature of some #$Thing.  The subject of investigation could in principle be any one of a wide variety of entities: a philosophical problem, a criminal act, a natural phenomenon, etc..  The phenomenon under investigation may be actual or merely putative within the context of the representation. Also, the nature of the thing being investigated may be substantially different from what the #$investigatingAgent believes it to be.")
(disjointWith TransportationDevice NavigationDevice)
(comment Course-Online "This is the collection of courses which are taught online. These are a modern twist on the idea of correspondence courses.")
(comment ApeShaped "#$ApeShaped is the instance of #$ShapeAttribute defined by the typical shape of an ape.")
(comment VehiclesPerHour "A #$UnitOfRate. It is used in order to get the #$Rate, in vehicles per hour, at which vehciles pass through some path or the capacity of some path to allow vehicles to pass.")
(comment Default-JustificationStrength "The strength of a default (i.e. not monotonic) justification.")
(comment Antiviral "Drugs which are used to prevent or fight infections caused by viruses.")
(comment Kilocalorie "Amount of energy expressed in kilocalories. One kilocalorie is the    amount of heat needed to raise one kilogram of water one degree    centigrade, (from 14.5 to 15.5 degrees C). This is the unit    standardly used in measuring the caloric content of food, and is    sometimes called Calorie, large calorie, great calorie, or kilogram    calorie. Not to be confused with calorie, small calorie, or gram    calorie, which is the amount of heat needed to raise one GRAM of    water one degree centigrade.    See #$caloricContent and #$caloricContentOfFood for ways to express    the caloric content of substances.")
(comment laborForceDuring "(#$laborForceDuring REGION THING NR) means that NR is average labor force of the #$GeographicalRegion REGION during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING, where the labor force of a region at point in time is the sum of the number of employed and unemployed persons in the region.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.")
(comment NationalEconomyGoal "The attribute characterizing goals which are concerned with maintaining or increasing the strength of a nation's economy.  This encompasses controlling inflation and unemployment, decreasing international trade imbalances, maintaining a strong currency in the international market.")
(comment SlimeMold "The collection of slime molds, peculiar creatures that exist in multiple phases, sometimes as scattered cells, sometimes as macroscopic colony-creatures able to move slowly, with vaguely fungal mechanisms.  The class of slime molds is treated in many classification systems as an instance of #$BiologicalDivision, called Myxomycota, under the #$ProtistaKingdom.  See also #$TrueSlimeMold and #$CellularSlimeMold.")
(comment MathematicalCharacter "A written symbol used in mathematical representation.")
(disjointWith Fern CropPlant)
(comment Suspension "A collection of tangible stuffs; a subcollection of #$Mixture.  Each instance of #$Suspension is a mixture which has exactly one #$suspendingFluid and at least one kind of #$suspendedPart.  Each of the #$suspendedParts is an instance of #$Particle, and there are a mob of them.  Some suspensions are fairly stable (e.g., mayonnaise), while others tend to separate quickly (e.g., sugar stirred into cold lemonade).  Other examples of #$Suspension include a #$CloudInSky, a spray of aerosol deodorant.")
(comment shortTimeIntervalAfter "(shortTimeIntervalAfter INTER TEMP-OBJ) means that the instance of #$TimeInterval
INTER is the short time interval after the instance of #$TemporalThing TEMP-OBJ.")
(disjointWith MedicalCareInstitution SpermBank)
(comment RingNetwork "#$RingNetwork is the collection of all instances of #$ComputerNetwork that have a ring topology. In an instance of #$RingNetwork, each computer attaches to two other computers, forming a ring of computers.")
(comment MysteryWriter "The collection of writers who write mystery novels or stories")
(disjointWith Sunrise Twilight)
(comment majorCityInState "A specialization of #$cityInState (q.v.).
(#$majorCityInState CITY STATE) means that CITY is generally considered 
to be a major (i.e. highly-populated or important) city in STATE.")
(comment Real1-Infinity "#$Real1-Infinity is the subcollection of #$RealNumber that excludes numbers less than 1.  Each instance of #$Real1-Infinity is a number greater than or equal to 1.")
(comment ArtisticWorkOfDisplayedInFn "(#$ArtisticWorkOfDisplayedInFn ARTIST PLACE) denotes the group of objects of which ARTIST is the creator that are displayed in PLACE.")
(comment AirAssaultEngineeringUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of offensive military units that are inserted into combat (usually by helicopter) from the air and are also equipped to provide engineering support.")
(comment HeatingAir "A collection of events.  Each instance of this collection is a #$HeatingProcess event in which the #$objectOfStateChange is some piece of air which is heated.  Every time your thermostat clicks at home, and the heater fires up, and the blower runs, there is a new instance of this collection (namely one subevent of that whole process --- the subevent in which the heater actually heats the air for a few minutes).")
(disjointWith Drink Enema-DosageForm)
(comment seriesOrderedBy "This predicate relates series to relations that order them linearly.  (#$seriesOrderedBy SERIES PRED) means that PRED is a relation that imposes a linear, or total, ordering (see #$TotalOrdering) on the #$seriesMembers of SERIES.  PRED is both a #$TransitiveBinaryPredicate and an #$AntiSymmetricBinaryPredicate, and each member of SERIES stands in the relation PRED to all of the succeeding members.  For example, if SERIES is a line of cars driving north, it might be ordered by #$northOf (and perhaps also by \"ahead of\").")
(comment complementOfIn "(#$complementOfIn SUBCOL1 SUBCOL2 COL) means that SUBCOL1 is the complement of SUBCOL2 in COL.  I.e. (#$partitionedInto COL (#$ThePartition SUBCOL1 SUBCOL2)). Instances of SUBCOL1 are all the instances of COL which are not instances of SUBCOL2, where SUBCOL2 is a specialization of

COL. For example, #$Thing is partitioned into #$PartiallyTangible

and #$Intangible, therefore (#$complementOfIn #$PartiallyTangible #$Intangible #$Thing) holds. See also #$ComplementOfInFn.")
(comment ConceptualWorkSeries "The collection of all #$ConceptualWorks that appear as a series of individual freestanding #$ConceptualWorks.  This would include a novel [#$Novel-CW] whose chapters appear in consecutive #$PeriodicalIssues, the story told for 1001 nights by Scheherazade to her husband, or a #$TVSeriesProduct even though the individual episodes were not part of the same #$Narrative, and a #$TaxForm-CW which has somewhat different format and content each year.")
(comment BirdOfPrey "The collection of all raptors, commonly known as #$Birds of prey.")
(comment CitizenSafetyGoal "The attribute characterizing goals which are concerned with preserving the safety of a country's citizens both abroad and within the country.")
(comment washingsIn "#$washingsIn relates a spec of #$LiquidTangibleThing to the
collection of #$Washings that take place using instances of that
collection as the cleaning medium.")
(comment atRestWRT "OBJ1 is at rest with respect to OBJ2")
(comment MiddleFinger "The third #$Finger, found between the #$IndexFinger and the #$RingFinger on the human hand.")
(comment NonBallisticMissileUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile centers on rocket           propelled weapons that do not travel along ballistic trajectories: e.g., surface-to-air missiles, cruise missiles, etc..")
(comment Society "#$Society is not the thing debutantes are introduced to at coming out parties (\"high society\") but rather what is referred to by the term \"society\" in expressions such as \"the effect of violent movies on society\". The English term

is often used as an implicit indexical. Note that #$Society is quite different

from #$SocialOrganization.")
(comment mixtureComponents "(#$mixtureComponents MIXTURE COMPONENT) means that MIXTURE has COMPONENT as one of its mixed-in components.")
(comment DomainNameSearchEngine "The collection of all #$SearchEngines designed to help users find information about internet networks, including registered #$DomainNames.")
(comment HealthOfficial "The collection

of #$Persons who represent government agencies that oversee health issues.

Instances of this collection work for government health agencies and have

decision making power regarding the application and development of laws

regarding medical issues.")
(comment TemperateClimateCycle "A specialization of #$AnnualClimateCycle.  Each instance of #$TemperateClimateCycle is a year-long event consisting of weather occurring (typically) in terrestrial regions between (roughly) the Tropic of Cancer and the Arctic Circle in the Northern Hemisphere, and between the Tropic of Capricorn and the Antarctic Circle in the Southern Hemisphere.  Characteristics of a temperate climate include: four distinguishable seasons, Spring, Summer, Fall, and Winter, with variations in temperature and precipitation; overall moderate precipitation.")
(comment timelyOccasionTypeWRTDate "#$timelyOccasionTypeWRTDate is used to relate a particular date to the types of occasions that are coming up soon after it.")
(comment Paper-IBO "A specialization of #$InformationBearingObject. Each instance of this collection is an artifact in the form of one or more sheets of #$Paper, containing markings (see #$VisualMark) that may be interpreted as encoding information.  #$Paper-IBOs are often textual (i.e instances of #$TextualMaterial) but not always (c.f. #$MapCopy, for instance).  When they consist of more than one sheet of paper, these are often bound together, as in a #$BookCopy or #$MagazineCopy.")
(comment AttackTypeByTargetTypeFn "(#$AttackTypeByTargetTypeFn takes as its 

first argument any spec ATTK of #$AttackOnTangible

  and as its second argument any spec SPEC of

   #$SomethingExisting, and returns the 

 subcollection of ATTK where the 

   #$intendedTargetTypeOfAttack is SPEC.

   For example, (#$AttackTypeByTargetTypeFn

   #$TerroristAttack #$Monument) is the

   collection of terrorist attacks on 

   monuments.")
(comment InfectionDisseminationEvent "The collection of events that occur when #$Infection spreads from the original site of infection to other parts of the body, usually via the blood stream.  The #$objectMoving during an instance of this collection is the #$Microorganisms or their toxins.")
(comment FunctionRuleTemplateFn "(#$FunctionRuleTemplateFn FUNC) denotes the rule template unique to the function FUNC.")
(comment Hedge "A group of bushes in a line that have been made to grow together into a single long barrier.")
(comment DirectionsFn "#$DirectionsFn takes as argument any instance of #$SpatialThing-Localized and returns the collection of all pieces of information about how to get to that thing.  For example, (#$DirectionsFn #$CapeCod) returns the collection of pieces of information about getting to Cape Cod in Massachusetts.")
(comment PunchingAHole "A process where holes are punched out of some material.")
(comment BinaryRelation "The collection of all fixed-arity relations of arity 2 (see #$arity).  The most notable specializations of #$BinaryRelation are #$BinaryPredicate and #$BinaryFunction (qq.v.).")
(comment compositionScoredForInstrumentType-Count "(#$compositionScoredForInstrumentType-Count COMP TYPE INT) means that the scoring for the #$MusicalComposition COMP includes INT instruments, voices, or ensembles of type TYPE. For instance (#$compositionScoredForInstrumentType-Count DeathAndTheMaiden-StringQuartet #$Cello 1) means that the scoring for Schubert's 'Death and the Maiden' string quartet includes a single cello.")
(comment PropagandaCampaign "A #$MassCommunicating which is intended to shape public opinion about some agent or issue.")
(comment SulfaDrug "AKA Sulfonamide. A group of antibacterial drugs whose action is a result of their interference with enzyme systems necessary for normal growth and reproduction.")
(comment ClassicalMusic-Baroque "A specialization of Western #$ClassicalMusic whose #$genreHeyday lasted from about 1600 to 1750. Representative composers include J.S. Bach, Vivaldi, and Handel.")
(comment ChlorineGas "A greenish-yellow, poisonous gas which is sometimes used as a chemical weapon.")
(comment Packet-NIPRNet "#$Packet-NIPRNet is the collection of instances of #$Packet-Internet which adhere to the specifications set by #$NIPRNetProtocol.    A #$Packet-NIPRNet contains information which constrains it to be routed to its destination on machines on the #$NIPRNet-PathSystem.")
(comment exportValue "The annual value of items exported from a nation.")
(comment Gallery-ArtDisplayStructure "The collection of all rooms, series of rooms, and buildings designed or used for the exhibition (and often the sale) of #$ArtObjects.")
(comment NewKip-Laos "The unitOfCurrenty used in Laos-AtPresent.")
(comment Kite-TheDevice "The collection of all wind-powered aircraft restrained by a towline and deriving lift from the aerodynamic action of the wind flowing across their surface. Commonly the kite consists of a light framework upon which paper, silk, or other thin material is stretched. Kites are used both for meteorological and other scientific research, and also as toys.")
(comment NonSeasonalGiftGivingOccasionType "A specialization of #$GiftGivingOccasionType. #$SeasonalGiftGivingOccasionType is the collection of kinds of gift-giving occasions that are tied to certain dates in the calendar year.  It is #$disjointWith #$NonSeasonalGiftGivingOccasionType.")
(comment Oat-TheGrain "Individual oat grains, which are the fruits of the oat plant.")
(comment PureFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  (#$PureFn X) denotes the subcollection of the #$ChemicalSubstanceType X whose instances are chemically pure.  Note that #$PureFn can be applied only to instances of #$ChemicalSubstanceType (such as #$Fructose or #$Water), but not to mixtures (such as #$Air).  See also #$PureSubstance.")
(comment FlowerArrangementTypeByOccasion "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$FlowerArrangementTypeByOccasion is a collection of instances of #$FlowerArrangements that have something in common which makes them all appropriate for a particular occasion.  An instance of this collection is #$BirthdayFlowerArrangement.")
(comment PortCity "A specialization of #$City.  Each instance of #$PortCity is a city that borders on some instance of #$Harbor (q.v.).  Each instance of #$PortCity will contain at least one instance of #$Seaport (q.v.).")
(comment MicrosoftCertifiedDataBaseAdministrator "The collection of #$EducationalDegrees earned by taking a 'Microsoft Authorized Academic Training Program'.  Such degrees are considered industry-wide standards of database administration competence.")
(comment covers-Sheetlike "(#$covers-Sheetlike SHEET OBJ) means that SHEET, a #$SheetOfSomeStuff, covers OBJ like a sheet.  It may be resting on top (#$covers-Ruglike), draped over, or wrapped around the object.  #$covers-Baglike is a restricted form of this.")
(comment HostingASocialGathering "The class of events in which one or more people prepare for and then host some sort of social gathering intended to entertain their guests -- birthday parties, dinner parties, weddings, etc.")
(comment SpecifiedOperaType "A collection of collections, each element of #$SpecifiedOperaType is a collection of performances of some particular opera. For example, performances of 'The Magic Flute' constitute a collection which is an element of OperaType.")
(comment SecondLieutenant-Title "This Cyc constant denotes the term of address used for someone holding the rank-attribute of #$SecondLieutenant-Rank in an  instance of #$ModernMilitaryOrganization.  May be abbreviated as 2nd LT or Sec.Lt. in text.")
(comment WrittenCharacter "The collection of all markings which are intended to represent some instance of #$Character-Abstract.")
(comment exposureOfObjectToSubstanceType "(#$exposureOfObjectToSubstanceType EXPOSURE OBJECT

CONTAMINANT-TYPE) means that during EXPOSURE, OBJECT is exposed to

substance of the type CONTAMINANT-TYPE.")
(comment Translocation "A subcollection of #$MovementEvent.  Each instance of #$Translocation is a movement across a distance; thus there is both a location that it is a movement \"from\" (see #$fromLocation) and a location that it is a movement \"to\" (see #$toLocation).  (These two locations might or might not be distinct, considering round-trips.)  Note that instances of #$Translocation might or might not involve a salient moving object (see #$objectMoving); for those that do see the specialization #$Movement-TranslationEvent; for some that don't see #$WavePropagation.")
(comment (TransportViaFn WaterTransportationDevice) "A collection of events.  An instance of (#$TransportViaFn #$WaterTransportationDevice) is a transportation event in which a #$vehicle designed to float on or travel through water is used.  Examples include instances of #$Sailing in boats, #$WaterSkiing, and (#$TransportViaFn #$Windsurfer).  Note: This collection does not include swimming, which is a #$LocomotionProcess-Animal (q.v.), not a form of transportation as defined (intended and axiomatized) in Cyc.")
(disjointWith UnitOfPower UnitOfSpeed)
(comment Rickettsiosis "The collection of #$ParasiticInfections caused

  by #$Rickettsia.")
(disjointWith PedalBoat Raft)
(comment Deforestation "The collection of all events of a forested #$GeographicalRegion being made less so. Involves destruction of habitat and removal of trees.")
(comment BiologicalBomb "The collection of #$Bomb devices which use an explosive charge to release and disperse biologically active chemicals or pathogens. The chemicals or pathogens may be designed to contaminate animal or plant life.  In particular humans, domesticated animals, and agricultural plants are possible intended targets of #$BiologicalBombs.")
(comment VulnerableToDenialOfService "#$VulnerableToDenialOfService is an attribute of some instances of #$Computer.  A computer has the attribute #$VulnerableToDenialOfService if it is configured to receive data in a way that enables an #$AttackByComputerOperation-DenialOfService to be performed on it.  One common way for a computer to be configured in this way would be for it to be running a program that has a #$DenialOfServiceFault.")
(comment Coupon "The collection of all coupons - pieces of paper (or their electronic equivalent) that allow a consumer to purchase a product for less than would otherwise be charged.")
(comment oppositeOnPath-Directly "This predicate relates a customary path such as a 

street to two objects such that one is directly across the 

path from the other.  (#$oppositeOnPath-Directly OBJ1 OBJ2 PATH) 

means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are #$onPath-Alongside opposite sides 

of PATH, and the middle of OBJ1 is directly across PATH from 

some part of OBJ2.  More precisely: a vertical plane passing 

through the volumetric center of OBJ1 and perpendicular to the 

vertical ''plane'' defined by the centerline of PATH (or, 

even more precisely, by the centerline of the segment of PATH 

that OBJ1 is related to by #$alongsidePathSegment) would pass 

through some point in OBJ2.  Note that #$oppositeOnPath-Directly

is _not_ #$commutativeInArgs with respect to its arg1 and arg2 

positions, for if OBJ1 is narrower than OBJ2, it can happen that 

OBJ1 is directly opposite OBJ2 but not vice versa.  For a 

generalization of this predicate that allows the objects to 

be less directly across the path from each other, see 

#$oppositeOnPath-Generally.")
(comment MusicalScore "The collection of all abstract #$MusicalText which specifies the score for a piece of music.")
(comment PrimaryTranscriptProductionProcess "The process whereby a #$PrimaryTranscript-RNAMolecule is
generated from a DNA template in a eucaryotic organism.")
(comment UnderspecifiedObjectType "A collection of collections. Each element of #$UnderspecifiedObjectType is a collection of objects that may bridge any of the domains of literality and metaphoricity, space and time, or physical and intangible. Each type of underspecified object is intensionally neutral with regard to such issues; the type exists to allow underspecification to occur at the relational level, thus releasing Natural Language (NL) semantics from the need to specify precise semantic structures when such a responsibility is essentially post-NL (i.e., one of real-world reasoning).  For a more complete explanation of underspecification, please see the #$comment on #$UnderspecifiedCollectionType.")
(comment militaryManpower-Active "(militaryManpower-Active ?ORGANIZATION ?NUMBER) means that ?NUMBER is the number of members on active duty in the military forces of ?ORGANIZATION.")
(comment WholeOrganizationFn "(#$WholeOrganizationFn ?GROUP) returns the #$Organization which includes not only members of ?GROUP, but all the affiliated agents who form the core ?GROUP's support staff. For example, the Austin Symphony consists of musiscians, but (#$WholeOrganizationFn AustinSymphony) would also include the administrators, fundraising staff, and so on. Members of the #$DallasCowboys are football, but the (#$WholeOrganizationFn #$DallasCowboys) includes coaches, play coordinaters, trainers, and so on. A (#$WholeOrganizationFn ?GROUP) may or may not be a legal organization.")
(disjointWith NonconformingMortgage ConformingMortgage)
(comment Consciousness "This is the collection of all conscious mental events.

One could also represent consciousness as an attribute, either of mental events

or of sentient beings (the latter presumably being derivative of the former). The present collection seems to better correlate with the

notion in common parlance of the \"phenomenon of consciousness\".")
(comment TaxBracket "The collection of tax brackets, each of which is a collection of #$SocialBeings, grouped according to the rate they will be required to pay according to a certain #$IncomeTax (such as #$USIncomeTax) which rate is calculated as the percentage of their final dollar of taxable income that year.  A #$SocialBeing is assigned to a #$TaxBracket for various reasons, usually having to do with various social factors such as income level, whether it is a some special type of #$Organization or not, and the like.  So when (#$holdsIn YEAR (#$taxRate PER1 #$USIncomeTax RATE2)) and (#$holdsIn YEAR (#$taxRate PER2 #$USIncomeTax RATE2)), PER1 and PER2 are members of the same #$TaxBracket (in this case some US income tax bracket, represented by an instance of #$TaxBracket) if and only if RATE1 is equal to RATE2.")
(comment FreeEmailServiceProvider "The collection of #$EmailServiceProvider-WebBased that offer  (FreeThingOfTypeFn EmailAccount).")
(comment Brothel "A #$Building in which #$Prostitutes engage in #$SexualBehavior with clients for money.")
(disjointWith AthleticAward AcademyAward)
(comment F-4D-Fighter "A collection. The F-4D is an American all-weather attack fighterplane.")
(comment SchemaMicrotheory "Instances of #$SchemaMicrotheory are microtheories that combine the content of several #$LogicalTableSchemas.")
(comment PrescriptionDrugTradeType "These are formal product types which have NationalDrugCodes and which are made for the purpose of selling them.")
(disjointWith PassengerAircraft CombatAircraft)
(comment geneticTemplateFrom "(#$geneticTemplateFrom TRANSFER OBJ) means that OBJ results from a genetic template in TRANSFER. See also #$geneticTemplateFor.")
(disjointWith Water ChemicalGeneticIBT)
(comment PurposefulPhysicalAction "The collection of #$CompositePhysicalAndMentalEvents that are performed purposively (see #$performedBy).  This collection is the collection-intersection of #$PurposefulAction and #$CompositePhysicalAndMentalEvent.  Since each instance of #$PurposefulPhysicalAction is also an instance of #$CompositePhysicalAndMentalEvent, each instance has both a mental and a physical component. Driving a car would be an instance of #$PurposefulPhysicalAction since it involves mental and physical functioning on the part of the performing agent and is done purposively.  Crashing a car, conversely, would not normally be an instance (unless the driver purposefully caused the crash).")
(comment structureMap "(#$structureMap ?Src ?Src-Mt ?Tgt ?Tgt-Mt ?Src-Desc ?Tgt-Desc) returns a structure-mapping of the formulae in ?Src-Mt pertaining to the source concept ?Src that are isomorphic with formulae in ?Tgt-Mt that pertain to the target domain concept ?Tgt. The mappings are condensed as formulae, so ?Src-Desc becomes bound to an #$and of all the matching formulae in the source domain, while ?Tgt-Desc becomes bound to an #$and of all the matching formulae in the target domain. see also #$structureMaps.")
(comment RoadVehicleTypeByBodyStyle "A collection of collections, each element of

#$RoadVehicleTypeByBodyStyle is a collection of road vehicles

categorized by body style. For example, the collection of sedans, and

the collection of pickup trucks, would be elements of

#$RoadVehicleTypeByBodyStyle.")
(comment RadioShow-CW "A collection of objects; a subset of #$RadioMediaProduct. Every #$RadioShow-CW is a #$ConceptualWork.  An individual #$RadioMediaProduct may be either a series or an individual show.  ``Car Talk'' is a #$RadioShow-CW, the output of an individual radio [#$RadioReceiver] tuned to a broadcast of ``Car Talk'' is an instance of #$RadioShow-IBT.")
(comment FrontAndBackSidedObject "A #$FrontAndBackSidedObject is

a object with an intrinsic #$FrontSide and an intrinsic #$BackSide.

By 'intrinsic' we mean simply that there exists an estabilshed

convention according to which one side is considered 'Front' and the

other side is considered 'Back'.  Usually the two sides in question can be reliably

distinguished.  Notice that a conventionally

distinguishable front and back do not necessarily imply a bottom and

top, or a left and right: a #$Worm has a clear-cut front end and a

clear-cut back end according to biological convention, but it makes

little sense to talk of top, bottom, left or right.  However, see also

the comment for #$HexalateralObject.  Notice also--and this is crucial

to the whole conception-- that while a #$FrontAndBackSidedObject may well

have a preferred orientation and direction of motion, changing either

does not change what counts as the 'front' and what counts as the

'back': while I am backing my car out of the driveway in the morning,

its back end does not become its front end and vice versa. If an

entity does not obey this rule then it does not, generally speaking

count as having a distinguishable front and back--example: a dolley,

such as is used to transport crates, or some skateboards.")
(comment MotorizedInfantryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all motorized infantry military units. Such units employs motorized vehicles for transport, but fight on foot.")
(comment NaturalDisaster "The collection of all #$NaturalHazard events, such as tornadoes (see #$TornadoAsEvent) #$Mudslides, natural #$Famines, or #$Earthquakes, which actually inflict extensive property damage or injury.  #$NaturalDisasters are distinguished from #$ManMadeDisasters.")
(comment ArmoredUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units that employ motorized vehicles engineered to resist           penetration by explosives and projectile weapons. In modern armed           forces, it usually entails the presence of tanks and heavy artillery.")
(comment BiometricAuthenticationDevice "#$BiometricAuthenticationDevice is a collection of devices.  Individuals in the collection           are used to implement biometric methods of authenticating a person's right to access           some individual.")
(comment LaunchGuidedProjectile "The collection of #$Projectile-Devices which have paths that cannot be altered after the projectile leaves the #$ProjectileLauncher.")
(comment NimboStratusCloud "The collection of widespread middle level clouds (#$CloudInSky) which produce persistant rain")
(comment AssertionDescriptorPredicate "The collection of predicates which describe the internal Cyc #$CycLAssertion data structures.")
(comment Voltage "A specialization of #$ScalarInterval.  Each instance of #$Voltage is the electric potential of an electric force, measured in terms of the amount of work it takes the force to move a charge from one place to another.  The standard unit of measure (see the collection #$UnitOfMeasure) for #$Voltage is the volt (see the constant #$Volt).")
(comment MultipleRocketLauncher "The collection of #$MissileLaunchers capable of launching multiple
rocket-propelled missiles.")
(comment ExogenousInfection "A specialization of #$Infection. Each instance 

of #$ExogenousInfection is an invasion of an infectious pathogen from outside 

the infected organism via the skin or through the mucous membranes, 

including respiratory, digestive and genital tracts. See for instance the 

specialization #$GastroIntestinalInfection. Contrast with #$EndogenousInfection.")
(comment OilField-Developed "The collection of regions which are naturally rich in deposits of petroleum (crude oil) and have been developed to the point of producing petroleum (crude oil) commercially.  A developed oil field has production facilities located on the field, such as an oil well or an off-shore platform.  There will also be means for transporting the petroleum once it has been brought to the surface (by oil tanker or oil pipeline for example). #$JulieF 12/98")
(comment Drying "A collection of events in which involves a reduction in the moistness of something -- either its water content or its surface wetness -- by evaporation, absorption (e.g. with towels), or some other process.  Typical objects of a #$Drying event include instances of: paint, food, dishes, clothes, humans.  The event of a clothes dryer running is a #$Drying.")
(comment SpatialPersistenceDistribution "#$SpatialPersistenceDistribution is a collection of objects, each of which consists of parameters that together indicate the probability distribution (likelihood of being true) for an assertion or set of assertions over some spatial region.")
(comment evidentialSupportForPhenomena-AgentUnspecified "(#$evidentialSupportForPhenomena-AgentUnspecified

    PHENOM AMOUNT) allows us to say that there is

  AMOUNT of evidence supporting the existence of

  PHENOM, without requiring us to specifiy who has

 this evidence.  This is useful for parsing English 

 sentences, which frequently omit references to

  the \"whoever\" that has the evidence.  See also

  #$evidentialSupportForPhenomena and #$evidentialSupportForBelief.")
(comment DarwinAwards-Event-Organized "This is an online contest in which people nominate people who have managed to kill themselves in very stupid ways.")
(disjointWith ConveyingMaterials CreatingAnArtifact)
(comment HomeSchooling "A collection of events. Each instance of #$HomeSchooling involves one #$HumanChild (the #$recipientOfInfo) going through a #$CourseOfStudy at home rather than in a school, under the tutelage of his or her parents and/or private tutors (who play the #$performedBy role).")
(comment AirForceBase-Grounds "A subcollection of #$MilitaryBase-Grounds;
each is controlled by a #$subOrganizations of an
air force and is the #$orgFacilities of some
#$AirForceBase-MilitaryOrganization.")
(comment Soman "A #$NerveAgentType that is extremely lethal when inhaled.")
(comment PlanetaryNebula "After a star with an initial mass of less than about eight solar masses has completed its core hydrogen burning it becomes a red giant: The star brightens by a factor of between 1,000 and 10,000. The outer, hydrogen-rich envelope swells to enormous size.  A strong wind begins to blow from the star's surface and, in the course of the star's red giant life, carries away most of the hydrogen envelope surrounding the star's central core. The envelope material ejected by the star forms an expanding shell of gas that is known as a #$PlanetaryNebula.")
(comment Intrusion "A subset of #$PurposefulAction and #$ActionOnObject, #$Intrusion is the            collection of actions in which an agent purposefully and illicitly            accesses an individual.  Objects that can be the foci of instances of            #$Intrusion include only objects that have a #$levelOfSecurity           that is a specialization of the attribute #$LimitedAccess.")
(comment AntiHeadacheAgent "Don't get this confused with #$AntiMigraineAgent, as migraine drugs aren't usually used to treat normal headaches, and vice versa.")
(disjointWith DisplayStructure Facility-Construct)
(comment HittingAGolfBall "Hitting a #$GolfBall with a #$GolfClub.")
(comment groundOf "(#$groundOf OBJ GROUND) means that GROUND is the stationary surface on which OBJ is located and possibly supported.")
(comment consumptionQuotaDuring "(#$consumptionQuotaDuring PT PRODUCT-TYPE THING AMOUNT) means that the #$NonNegativeScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the consumption quota (or ration) of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE for the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  (Of course, the  existence of consumption quotas is the exception rather than the rule.)  PT might, for example, be a #$Country, a #$Business, or a household (#$CohabitationUnit).  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.")
(comment 2-TheDigit "The numeral 2 of the Arabic Number system.  This is '2' as a #$Character-Abstract rather than the physical #$WrittenCharacter or the abstract mathematical #$Number-General.")
(comment optionAvailableToAgent "This instance of #$TernaryPredicate is used to specify the
salient characteristics of a particular kind of option available to an
agent in a specific context.  Specifically, (#$optionAvailableToAgent
AGENT (#$TheSetOf ?VAR PROP1(?VAR)...PROPN(?VAR)) ROLE) means that
playing the role ROLE in an event which satisfies the conditions PROP1
through PROPN is an option available to AGENT in the context in which
the assertion is made.  Ordinarily GAFs which use this predicate will
be asserted in fairly constrained contexts in which a limited number
of contingent options exist.  The second argument must be an instance
of #$Set-Mathematical, not an instance of #$Collection.  This is
because there is no a priori reason that a set of propositions
describing the 'situational type' of an option should happen to
characterize a natural kind, such as a specialization of #$Event or
#$Situation.  The fact that arg3 is an instance of #$ActorSlot
presupposes that the set identified in the arg2 position is a subset
of the collection #$Event.")
(comment Lek-Albania "The currency unit for Albania.")
(comment GamesMaster "The referee in a #$RolePlayingGame, the #$GamesMaster is both the creative impetus of the game, and the ruling judge in contentious matters of game play. The #$GamesMaster controls the #$RPG-NonPlayerCharacters of a game in a way that makes the game as realistic as possible to the players who control the #$RPG-PlayerCharacters. In effect, the #$GamesMaster is god in such games, deciding (via rolls of Die-TheCube usually) the course of events, how much damage is inflicted on #$RPG-PlayerCharacters in a fight/trap etc., and how #$RPG-NonPlayerCharacters react to the actions of #$RPG-PlayerCharacters.")
(comment suppliedWith "(#$suppliedWith PT COL) means that the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT is supplied with instances of the #$Collection COL.  This is a very general predicate.  PT might, for example, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion.  The range of possible supplies is similarly broad.  These supplies may be 'domestic'; that is, PT may own or contain within itself or produce the supplies.  Alternately, the supplies may be provided from without.  Or some mix of both may prevail.")
(comment Alcohol-Compound "The collection of all macroscopic portions of organic compounds classified as alcohols.  Alcohol is one of a class of organic compounds made of molecules having one or more hydroxyl groups [-OH] attached to an alkyl group [made of carbon and hydrogen atoms].")
(comment interArgIsa3-4 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  
(#$interArgIsa3-4 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, 
when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the third argument to RELN, 
a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the fourth argument 
must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is
an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then 
(RELN ARG1 ARG2 INST ARG4 ... ARGN) is semantically well-formed only 
if ARG4 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation of semantic 
well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations.")
(comment CrossStitchingEvent "The collection of cross stitching events The peformer uses a 
needle and fine yarn, and makes decorative stiches, in the shape of X's, 
in a piece of fabric.")
(comment Anaeroplasmatales-Order "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalOrder in the #$MoneraKingdom.  It contains the Anaeroplasmataceae-Family.")
(comment DramaticActing "This is the collection of events in which a person portrays someone or something other than himself as part of a dramatic performance - either for film or television, or in a live theater production. It is thus distinguished from #$Masquerading, which is also a spec of #$Acting.--Huffer, Dec 2, 1998")
(comment TranscriptFilter "#$TranscriptFilters are used for filtering remote operations.  Use the predicates   #$filterTerms and #$filterCollections to associate other constants with a particular   transcript filter.  These can be added to the current filtering state of a running   image using the TranscriptFilter field on the Remote Operation Filtering page. This page can be found by clicking on \"Comm\" and then \"Edit Remote Operation Filters\". 

 All   collections and terms associated with the filter will be filtered exactly as if they   had been entered separately in the Collection and Term fields on the same page.")
(comment ReconnaissanceHelicopter "The collection of #$Helicopters used for reconnaissance and information gathering in a military context.")
(comment nearestCommonGenlPreds "(#$nearestCommonGenlPreds PRED-1 PRED-2 NEAR-PRED) means that NEAR-PRED is a \"nearest\" predicate of which both PRED-1 and PRED-2 are specializations.  That is, both (#$genlPreds PRED-1 NEAR-PRED) and (#$genlPreds PRED-2 NEAR-PRED) hold, and there is no reified #$Predicate NEARER-PRED distinct from NEAR-PRED such that (#$genlPreds PRED-1 NEARER-PRED), (#$genlPreds PRED-2 NEARER-PRED), and (#$genlPreds NEARER-PRED NEAR-PRED) all hold.  Note that this predicate is non-assertible (see #$notAssertible), since its extension at any given time depends upon (and so must be computed from) the current state of the #$genlPreds hierarchy in the Cyc Knowledge Base.")
(comment numberOfPrescriptionsByDocTypePayerTypeDuring "(#$numberOfPrescriptionsByDocTypePayerTypeDuring DOCTYPE DRUGTYPE RXFILLTYPE PAYERTYPE PERIOD NUM) means that DOCTYPEs had NUM prescriptions of type RXFILLTYPE filled for DRUGTYPE and paid by PAYERTYPEs during PERIOD.  RXFILLTYPE may be #$FillingAPrescription-Retail, #$FillingAPrescription-MailOrder, #$FillingANewPrescription, #$FillingARefillPrescription, intersections of these, or merely #$FillingAPrescription.")
(comment Manuscript "An unpublished piece of text that could serve as the basis for a published piece of text")
(comment FluLikeSymptoms "Flu-like symptoms include fever, chills, aches.  This collection treats such symptoms as a syndrome, which may not in fact be caused by #$Influenza.")
(comment ParticipateOpportunityFn "#$ParticipateOpportunityFn takes as its argument any type of activity, and returns the collection of all opportunities to participate in that activity.  For example, (#$ParticipateOpportunityFn #$SprintingRace) is the collection of all opportunities to participate in a sprint, and (#$ParticipateOpportunityFn #$Election) is the collection of all opportunities to vote.")
(comment BalletDancePerformance "#$BalletDancePerformance is the collection of instances of

DancePerformance such that (PerformanceFn Ballet)

returns a collection of instances of BalletDancing.")
(comment chemicalReactants-TypeType "(#$chemicalReactants-TypeType REACTION-TYPE REACTANT-TYPE) means that instances of the #$ChemicalSubstanceType REACTANT-TYPE are reactants in instances of REACTION-TYPE, a spec of #$ChemicalReaction. The reactants are those chemicals that react with other reactants to form the products of the reaction.")
(comment BaseballThirdBaseman "The collection of all #$BaseballPlayers who play the position of third base on a #$BaseballTeam.")
(comment BloodCell "The collection of all living #$Cells that form part of the #$Blood.  This collection includes #$RedBloodCells, #$WhiteBloodCells, and #$Platelets.  #$Cells from infecting organisms or freefloating #$Cancer #$Cells in the #$Blood are not members of this collection.  #$BloodCells are #$AnimalBLOs and #$anatomicalParts of #$Animals whose #$CirculatorySystem they are in.  #$BloodCells in a #$CirculatorySystem are #$AnimalBodyParts, but outside such a system (e.g. in a BloodBank or #$DigestiveSystem) they are not.")
(comment weaponTypeArmorPenetration "The predicate #$weaponTypeArmorPenetration

 indicates how thick an armor (average strength)

 a #$Weapon of the given type can penetrate if it hits it head on.  (#$weaponTypeArmorPenetration WEAPONTYPE DIST) means that a typical weapon of type WEAPONTYPE can penetrate armor to the distance DIST.")
(comment FootFetish "The collection of all fetish-related sexual behavior in which the fetish object is a #$Foot-AnimalBodyPart.")
(comment PoleForPoleVaulting "The collection of poles used in PoleVaultSportsEvents.")
(comment HAWKTransporterErectorLauncher "The collection of military vehicles used for transporting, erecting and launching Hawk missiles.")
(comment Zirconium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of Zirconium.")
(comment ShortPhysicalBuild "The attribute of being below average height.")
(comment Trajectory-SweptSpace "The collection of all spatial regions that are defined as the precise regions swept through by trajectories of moving objects: each instance of #$Trajectory-SweptSpace is the individual spatial region consisting of all the points in space through which an object (or any part of it) passes during a #$Movement-TranslationEvent.  A #$Trajectory-SweptSpace may or may not follow some pre-existing or pre-defined path (#$Path-Generic).  If it does follow one or more such paths, it determines a #$Traversal of those paths.  A #$Trajectory-SweptSpace is understood and defined as a spatial region (often long, thin and 'worm'-shaped) with one of the two possible directions of motion along it.  It is considered as being a part of some stationary background space (thus, in most contexts, a #$Trajectory-SweptSpace cannot itself 'move').  Unlike a #$Path-Generic, a #$Trajectory-SweptSpace (or a #$Traversal) can cross itself any number of times, intersect itself, go back along itself, cycle over and over again, etc.  If there is a #$Movement-TranslationEvent, then that event always has a #$Trajectory-SweptSpace; it contains within it the linear #$Trajectory of the motion, (indicated using #$trajectory-Complete or possibly #$trajectory-Partial).  In most contexts, a #$Trajectory will be a line (or rather a one-manifold) through space as traced by some designated point within the moving object (e.g., the center of gravity), but the #$Trajectory-SweptSpace is available to represent the whole space (with space and thickness) swept through by a moving object.  Contrast #$Trajectory-SweptSpace with #$Path-Generic and with #$Traversal.")
(comment BattleTank-T80 "A type of battle tank.")
(comment businessContacts "(#$businessContacts PERS1 PERS2) states that PERS1 and PERS2 are acquainted and at least part of the basis for their acquaintance is due to interaction at the workplace or in some other business context.  It is possible for one's #$businessContacts to also be acquainted in other ways, e.g., as friends or relatives.  Note that relationships like #$customers and #$clients don't imply #$businessContacts, because they don't necessarily imply acquaintance, even when the related agents are both people.")
(comment ArgFormatPredicate "The collection of those #$ArgConstraintPredicates used to specify an entry-format for a certain argument-place of a given #$Predicate.  An argument entry-format is a kind of restriction on a predicate regarding how many things, or the range of things, that the predicate holds of with respect to a given one of its argument-places.  More precisely: given any particular way of fixing the arguments in the rest of  the predicate's argument-places, the entry-format tells us something about  the number of different things, or the range of things, that can occupy the  given argument-place such that the relation holds of those arguments.  That is, supposing the given argument-place is the Nth, the entry-format tells us  something about the number or range of different sequences of arguments  of which the predicate holds and that differ from each other only in their Nth items.  Two important specializations of #$ArgFormatPredicate are #$SpecificEntryFormatPredicate and #$GeneralEntryFormatPredicate  (qq.v.).  Instances of #$SpecificEntryFormatPredicate each have to do with a specific format (see e.g. #$singleEntryFormatInArgs).  Instances of #$GeneralEntryFormatPredicate are comparatively \"higher-order\", and are used to relate any given #$SpecificEntryFormatPredicate to a (fixed or given) argument-place of a given predicate (see e.g. #$arg1Format and #$argFormat).  Note that in some of the later cases the specified format constraint will be an \"inter-argument\" one that depends in some way upon one of the predicate's other argument-places (or upon another, non-format, feature of the same argument-place); see #$InterArgFormatPredicate.  Note also that, in contrast with what #$ArgTypePredicates (q.v.) are used for, specifying an argument entry-format for a predicate does _not_ impose any sort of necessary condition for semantic well-formedness.  A violation of a legitimate entry-format constraint necessarily involves two or more statements, and at least one them must be _untrue_; but there is no implication that any of them  is malformed.")
(comment actionResourceQuantForTime "(#$actionResourceQuantForTime ACT THING QUANT TEMP) means that in ACT, a quantity QUANT of THING is a required resource for the duration of TEMP, in the sense that the agent performing ACT must have 'access' to a QUANT amount of THING for TEMP in order for ACT to be #$successfulForAgents.")
(comment meanOfDistribution "What it says -- only for all distributions, especially non-normal ones or ones not assumed to be normal.")
(comment HomeDecorating "The activity of making houses, apartments, etc. look           nicer by adding ornaments.")
(comment PinealBody "The collection of all pineal bodies (or 'pineal glands').  An individual #$PinealBody forms the dorsal tip of the #$Epithalamus in the #$Brain.  The #$Epithalamus contains and controls the #$PinealBody.  The #$PinealBody secretes the hormone #$Melatonin.")
(comment DiplomaticRecognitionOfGovernment "The collection of events where a state officially recognizes the government of another state where the goverment is in flux.")
(comment ThermoduricBacterium "A collection of #$Bacterium that may survive, but not
necessarily grow, at higher temperatures that would kill other
#$Bacterium.  These #$ProkaryoticCells will survive
#$Pasteurization.")
(comment InternetServiceProvider "A collection of service-providing organizations. Each #$InternetServiceProvider, or ISP, provides its clients with access to the #$Internet. An ISP typically charges a monthly or annual fee for this service, although some do not charge for the service. Access may be provided via a telephone number for the client's modem to connect to a modem at the ISP, a dedicated high-speed line, cable modem, cellular or sattelite connection, or more modern technologies. The ISP may or may not provide software or a modem for the client's computer, email service, website hosting, and online 'content' such as news, weather, magazines, chatrooms, etc. Some ISPs are national or international, like #$AmericaOnlineInc, and others are local.")
(comment Sustainability "This is the collection of degrees of ecological sustainability, attributes which should

be applied to kinds of events. A certain type of activity's having a high degree

of sustainability in this sense means that carrying it out does not delete 

non-renewable resources and does no environmental harm. ")
(disjointWith Sled WheeledTransportationDevice)
(comment MarkingExtentOfMineField "A collection of events.  A subcollection of #$MeasuringSomething in which the #$thingEvaluated is a #$MineField, and its extent is determined by some #$MilitaryOrganization, for the purpose of clearing a lane through it.")
(comment BetaBlockerWithDiuretic "Elements are drug formulations which include both a #$BetaBlocker and a #$Diuretic.")
(comment equivalenceClassWRT "This predicate relates things to their equivalence class

with respect to some collection and some equivalence relation.

(#$equivalenceClassWRT COL REL THING SUBCOL) means that SUBCOL is the

collection or set of elements of COL that bear the relation REL to THING.

For instance, (#$equivalenceClassWRT #$CanadianPerson #$cotemporal

#$JeanChretien CANADIANSCOTEMPORALWITHJC) means that #$JeanChretien is

cotemporal with all the Canadians that are elements of the set

CANADIANSCOTEMPORALCWITHJC.")
(comment typicalArmamentOfMilitaryPlatformType "(#$typicalArmamentOfMilitaryPlatformType  PLATFORMTTYPE ARMSTYPE) means that individual military platforms of type PLATFORMTYPE typically have one or more instances of ARMSTYPE as weapons or armaments.")
(comment (FemaleFn RaceCarDriver) "The collection of female race car drivers.")
(comment keAbstractCollection "(#$keAbstractCollection COLLECTION) states that COLLECTION is considered abstract for KE purposes.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation "A specialization of #$AttackOnObject, #$ActsCommonlyConsideredCriminal and #$ComputerActivity.  Each instance of #$AttackByComputerOperation an attack executed using computer operations as weapons.  Commonly, instances of this collection are called \"electronic attacks\" or \"cyber attacks\". This collection includes as specializations #$AttackByComputerOperation-DenialOfService, #$AttackByComputerOperation-CorruptionOfInformation and many others.  Note that #$AttackByComputerOperation is not a specialization of #$AttackOnIBT, because many instances of #$AttackByComputerOperation do not involve an attempt to change the information content of their targets.")
(comment TransportationDevice "A specialization of both #$Conveyance and #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$TransportationDevice is an artifact designed to move an object from one location to another, by (for example) carrying, pulling, or pushing the transported object.  Instances of this collection may or may not have their own power source (see #$SelfPoweredDevice).  Those that do, such as automobiles and speedboats, constitute the specialization #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle.  Other transportation devices (for example, instances of #$Wheelbarrow or #$Bicycle) require an external motive force.  Because #$transporter and #$transportees are specializations of #$objectMoving, it follows that any object in the role of #$transporter moves as a whole with those objects playing the role of #$transportees.  Consequently, since any instance of #$TransportationDevice has playing the role of #$transporter as its intended function, stationary objects which cause motion, such as conveyor belts, escalators, rocket launchers, and slingshots, are excluded from the collection #$TransportationDevice. Although they facilitate travel, ice skates, shoes, skis and other instances of #$WearableConveyance are also excluded from the collection #$TransportationDevice, since they are devices which are worn rather than ridden on, ridden with, or ridden in.")
(comment MachineGun-WaterCooled "The collection of #$MachineGuns that use a water-cooling system to  keep the machine gun from overheating.")
(disjointWith Time-Quantity Pressure)
(comment CarRacingFacility "The collection of all permanent facilities that serve as the locations for #$ProfessionalCarRaceEventTypes.  Ordinarily, instances of CarRacingFacility include a #$CarRaceTrack, concession stands, bleachers and/or a stadium, and parking facilities.")
(comment objectsPerArea "For example, (objectsPerArea PT Mine 4 (SquareMeter 1)) means that PT has 4 mines per square meter.")
(comment containsProposition-CW "(#$containsProposition-CW WORK PROPOSITION) means that PROPOSITION is part of the information content of the #$PropositionalConceptualWork. An analogue of #$containsInfoPropositional-IBT. The latter can be used to assert that a certain concrete instantiation of a #$PropositionalConceptualWork contains a certain piece of information. For example we can assert that a certain copy of #$MobyDickNovel contains the information that Captain Ahab is a ship captain: (#$containsInfoPropositional-IBT Copy787OfMobyDick (#$isa #$CaptainAhab #$ShipCaptain)), whereas #$containsProposition-CW can be used to assert that the abstract work -- #$MobyDickNovel --  which this copy instantiates, contains the same information: (#$containsProposition-CW #$MobyDickNovel (#$isa #$CaptainAhab #$ShipCaptain)). Note that we assert as a default rule that any information contained in #$PropositionalConceptualWork is contained in any instantiation of that work. For an explanation of why this rule is not monotonic, and of why we do not assert the converse, see the note on #$ContextOfPCWFn.")
(comment maxReverseSpeed "(#$maxReverseSpeed CAR SPEED) states that CAR can go at the maximum speed SPEED when traveling in reverse direction along a 'normal' pathway. This is especially relevant for #$LandTransportationDevices and #$WaterTransportationDevices")
(comment objectPowerDissipation "The power, typically measured in watts or milliwatts, that a physical device dissipates during its operation.  This power is usually converted to heat, although it could be converted to light, etc.")
(comment StoneObject-Natural "Instances are individual rocks, pebbles, boulders etc..")
(comment nonExistent "(#$nonExistent TERM) states the assumption that TERM does not exist.  This predicate is primarily used for reasoning in hypothetical contexts about the ramifications of some existing term not actually existing.")
(comment PumpingFluid "Pumping-induced pressure differential that causes a fluid to flow.")
(comment GasField "The collection of regions which are naturally

rich in deposits of #$NaturalGas.  Once a #$GasField is producing

#$NaturalGas, it ought to be considered a #$GasField-Developed. #$JulieF.")
(comment MagneticResonanceImaging "This is the technique of producing cross-sectional images of the body, especially of soft tissue, with a device that employs #$NuclearMagneticResonance. ")
(comment Patrolling "The collection of all instances of patrolling done 

either by law enforcement agencies, #$Vigilantes or military units.")
(comment OrientationFn "(#$OrientationFn AXIS1 DIR1 AXIS2 DIR2) denotes a particular orientation of an object OBJ.  AXIS1 and AXIS2 refer to different axes of OBJ.  DIR1 and DIR2 refer to the directions which AXIS1 and  AXIS2 point respectively.")
(comment vehicleLoadClass "(#$vehicleLoadClass V-TYPE MLC) means that the vehicle type V-TYPE is of the military load class MLC.")
(comment LunarEclipse "The subclass of #$Eclipse-CelestialEvent in which the #$Sun is obscured from view on #$MoonOfEarth by #$PlanetEarth. Realistically, this means that the #$PlanetEarth casts a visible #$Shadow across the surface of the #$MoonOfEarth. See also #$SolarEclipse.")
(comment Unknown-JustificationStrength "The strength of a justification in which the resulting truth cannot be determined, and is therefore unknown.")
(comment AntihypertensiveDrugSubstance "Drugs which are used to reduce high blood pressure.")
(comment on-UnderspecifiedSurface "(#$on-UnderspecifiedSurface ACT LOC) states that an abstract
locational relation holds between ACT and LOC, where LOC is an
#$SurfaceRegion-Underspecified. Only things which can be conceptualized as
surfaces are thus allowable as the second argument to an 'on'
relation. While we can say 'At IBM I wore a suit everyday' (since
#$IBMInc can be conceptualized as a #$Location-Underspecified), we cannot say
'On IBM I wore a suit'. However, we can say 'While on IBM's premises I
never used the bathroom'.")
(comment ConsumerGoodsGoal "The attribute characterizing goals which are concerned with maintaining or increasing the availability of consumer goods in a country.  This includes both domestic production of such goods and international trade relations enabling the acquisition of such goods.")
(comment Lifeboat "Smaller boats carried on a ship to provide a means of escape if the ship is in danger of sinking.")
(comment InstantFoodMixFn "A function to be used in referring to the pre-mixed form(s) of an #$InstantFood as sold in a #$GroceryStore. Instances of (#$InstantFoodMixFn FOOD) are instances of #$InstantFoodMix, and as such do not include packaging. A package of macaroni and cheese would be (#$PackageFn (#$InstantFoodMixFn #$MacaroniAndCheese)).")
(comment Calcitonin "A #$Hormone produced in the #$Thyroid gland. It is important for bone and calcium metabolism.")
(comment Algae-LikeProtist "The collection of protists (organisms classed in the #$ProtistaKingdom) that are said to be algae-like, such as golden algae or diatoms.")
(disjointWith SpanishMoss CropPlant)
(comment increasesCausally "(#$increasesCausally TEMP-THING THING SLOT) means that TEMP-THING causes the value of the predicate SLOT applied to THING (in the first argument position) to increase over some time period after the start of TEMP-THING.  This is defined in terms of #$increasesCausallyOverPeriod (see also).  Compared with its value immediately before TEMP-THING, the value of SLOT applied to THING is guaranteed to be higher immediately following or some time after TEMP-THING.  This net increase need not be monotonic.  See #$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates for a map of related predicates.")
(comment StarNetwork "#$StarNetwork is the collection of all instances of #$ComputerNetwork that have a star topology. In an instance of #$StarNetwork, all computers attach to a central computer, called a hub.")
(comment Anaplasmataceae-Family "A collection of all #$BiologicalGenus in the #$Anaplasmataceae-Family which includes #$Anaplasma-Genus #$Aegyptianella-Genus and #$Haemobartonella-Genus.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are pleomorphic, appearing as rods, cocci, or ring-shapes.  They reproduce by binary fission.  They are transmitted by arthropods, but may or may not cause disease.  Growth is slowed by tetracycline compounds, but not penicillin or streptomycin.")
(comment RomanceWriter "The collection of writers who write Romance stories or novels.")
(comment Asparagine "A collection of compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.  These
compounds are essential for protein synthesis.  Its abbreviations are
Asn and N.")
(comment HockeySkate "The collection of all skates used for playing hockey.

Unlike figure skates, hockey skates have no teeth at the toe end.")
(comment Approval-CommunicationAct "A collection of communication acts.  In each element of #$Approval-CommunicationAct, an agent expresses an approval.  Such approvals include: approving a loan application, endorsing a product, seconding or voting for a resolution proposed before an official body, condoning another agent's course of action.  Note: Acts communicating some kind of approval do not entail subjective feelings of approval by the agent (cf. #$Approval).  Also see #$Requesting-CommunicationAct.")
(comment AirborneEngineeringUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of military engineering units that are deployed by parachute drop.")
(disjointWith FoodGroup ElementStuffType)
(comment Dieting-LowCarbohydrate "The collection of dieting events whose primary emphasis is on decreasing the proportion of carbohydrates in the diet. The Atkins diet is an example, and the Zone diet is considered one by many.")
(comment MovieTypeByMPAAAdvisoryRating "#$MovieTypeByMPAAAdvisoryRating is a collection of collections. Each element is a collection of #$Movie-CWs having the same #$MPAAAdvisoryClassification-Film. The motivation for creating this collection is to make use of a faceting of #$Movie-CW to generate English questions to aid classification. See #$NoteAboutHowFacetAssertionsAreUsed.")
(comment RingFinger "The fourth #$Finger, located between the #$MiddleFinger and the #$LittleFinger on the human #$Hand.")
(comment WaterTreatment "This is the collection of events in which water is treated so as to

become ingestible or more healthful.")
(comment NuclearWeaponsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military unit organized, equipped, and trained for           operations involving handling, employment, and/or containment of           nuclear weapons.")
(comment SocialScienceType "This is a collection of fields of study which have to

do with the behavior of social groups. It includes #$Sociology, #$Economics, #$Anthropology, and

#$PoliticalScience.")
(comment PleasantWeatherArea "Attribute for generally nice or pleasant weather.  This will imply lots of specific things about the humidity, temp, wind, cloud cover")
(comment Production-Generic "The collection of instances of #$CreationEvent, each of which is a production event, regardless of whether it is a commercial production, a biological production, or something that involves both.  The

 distinction between #$Production-Generic and #$CreationEvent is suble; one

 can create a mess, but not produce one. More precisely, a production event appears to require that the activity be directed, in some sense, by a 'telos,'s or 'end' (nym).")
(comment MedicalDictionary "a collection of #$Dictionarys. Each element of #$MedicalDictionary provides lexical information about technical medical terms.")
(comment FamilyHoliday "A specialization of #$Holiday whose instances are such that, in cultures in which they are celebrated (see #$holidayCelebratedByCulture) families tend to celebrate them together at home.")
(comment TreeHouse "The subcollection of all instances of children's #$PlayhouseClubhouse built above the ground in trees.")
(comment HumidContinentalClimateCycle "A specialization of both #$HumidClimateCycle and #$TemperateClimateCycle.  Each instance of #$HumidContinentalClimateCycle is a year-long event consisting of weather occurring (typically) in continental interiors within a temperate climate zone.  Characteristics of a humid continental climate cycle include a warm summer and cold winter, with precipitation throughout.  A good example of a region whose annual climate cycles are instances of #$HumidContinentalClimateCycle is the American Midwest.  Cf. #$HumidSubtropicalClimateCycle.")
(comment NewReleaseMovie "The collection of #$Movie-CWs that have been released recently.  This is a collection which has different instances every week, as new movies are always being released.")
(comment Shock-PhysiologicalCondition "This is the collection of instances of shock. This is a condition
characterized by greatly decreased blood pressure and circulation.")
(comment numberOfPerformersScoredFor "(#$numberOfPerformersScoredFor COMP INT) means that the #$MusicalComposition COMP is scored for INT number of performers. For instance, (#$relationAllInstance #$numberOfPerformersScoredFor      #$StringQuartet-Composition 4) means that all string quartets are scored for four performers.")
(comment Su-24-Bomber "The collection of Su-24 aircraft. They are Russian-made attack aircraft. They are often called 'FENCERS'.")
(comment Voyeurism "This collection includes acts of viewing others (often surreptitiously) who are naked or undressing, or who are engaged in some sexual behavior. The viewer's goal is sexual titilation.")
(comment ChemicalWeaponFn "(#$ChemicalWeaponFn CHEMAGENT-TYPE) designates the subset of #$ChemicalWeapon whose elements are chemical weapons armed with the type of chemical agent CHEMAGENT-TYPE.")
(comment TetracyclineAntibiotic "Class of broad-spectrum antibiotic which includes tetracycline. ")
(comment ReconnaissanceWatercraft "The collection of aircraft used for reconnaissance and information gathering in a military context.")
(comment BookReviewFn "This function takes as argument any instance of #$Book-CW and returns the collection of all reviews of that book.  For example, (#$ReviewFn #$2001-ASpaceOdyssey-TheBook) returns the collection of all reviews of #$ArthurCClarke's novel.")
(disjointWith UnintendedLossOfUserRights PrivatizingAnIndustry)
(comment DisplayingArtObject "The collection of all instances of #$DisplayingSomething in which the items displayed are #$ArtObjects.")
(comment Dollar-Guyana "The unit of currency for Guyana-AtPresent.")
(comment BankingTurn "A Turn made by a vehicle that leans into a supporting medium to provide sufficient centrifugal force for the vehicle to remain on course.  #$RaceCars caroming around bends in a #$RaceTrack employ #$BankingTurns on the sloped corners of the #$RaceTrack to obtain a sling-shot effect as they come out of the turn. #$BankingTurns require a supporting medium to provide the #$CentrifugalForceVector. Thus, aircraft can make #$BankingTurns in the air, but spacecraft cannot make banking turns in the emptiness of #$OuterSpace. Nonethless, the distinctive sound of an aircraft entering a #$BankingTurn often accompanies images of spacecraft in #$ScienceFictionMovies (e.g., StarWars).")
(comment TranscriptOfCWTypeFn "#$TranscriptOfCWTypeFn takes as argument any spec of #$ConceptualWork and returns the collection of transcripts [#$TranscriptOfSpeech-CWIS] of the words to any #$ConceptualWork of that type.  For example,(#$TranscriptOfCWTypeFn #$TVShow-CW) returns the collection of transcripts of television shows.  To represent the collection of transcripts of a particular episode of a type of TV show (for example, The Trouble with Tribbles episode) use #$TranscriptOfCWFn.  Use #$TranscriptOfEventFn and #$TranscriptOfEventTypeFn for transcripts of specific events or classes of event.")
(comment OatPlant "Individual oat plants.")
(comment PureSubstance "A collection of tangible stuffs. Each instance of #$PureSubstance is a chemically pure portion of stuff belonging to some particular #$ChemicalSubstanceType (e.g. #$Water or #$Cellulose). `Chemically pure' applies to a piece of stuff which has no sub-portions that fail to conform to the chemical composition of its (single) #$ChemicalSubstanceType. In typical contexts, most common portions of a #$ChemicalSubstanceType will not be instances of #$PureSubstance . For example, a piece of pencil lead, though mostly carbon, will not be an instance since it is not pure carbon and any portion of ordinary tap water will contain too many impurities. Many sub-portions of either a piece of pencil lead or portion of tap water will fail to conform to the chemical composition of either carbon or water. Some instances of #$ChemicalSubstanceType are subcollections of #$PureSubstance in most contexts but not in all. In typical domestic contexts, for example, a piece of ordinary distilled water would be an instance of #$PureSubstance . However, in a clean room or microchip manufacturing context, ordinary distilled water would probably be considerd impure (see #$ImpureCompound). In general, to refer to a pure instance of a substance one can use the function #$PureFn, e.g. (#$PureFn #$Carbon). Note that #$PureFn has #$PureSubstance as a #$resultGenl . Since this kind of purity is relative to specified chemical composition only, #$PureSubstance (and #$PureFn) does not pertain to mixtures in Cyc (such as #$Air). Cf. #$Mixture, #$ChemicalSubstanceType. See also #$PureSubstanceType and #$ImpureCompound.")
(comment MicrosoftCertifiedSystemsEngineer "The collection of #$EducationalDegrees earned by taking a 'Microsoft Authorized Academic Training Program'.  Such degrees are considered industry-wide standards of systems engineering competence.")
(comment SpecifiedPlay-MusicalPerformanceType "A collection of collections, each element of #$SpecifiedPlay-MusicalPerformanceType is a collection of performances of a musical/dramatic work. For example, performances of 'West Side Story' constitute a collection which is an element of #$SpecifiedPlay-MusicalPerformanceType.")
(comment SergeantFirstClass-Title "This Cyc constant denotes the term of address used for someone holding the rank-attribute of #$SergeantFirstClass-Rank in an  instance of #$ModernMilitaryOrganization.  Often abbreviated as SGT in text.")
(comment WrittenCharacterFn "(#$WrittenCharacterFn ABSTRACT_CHARACTER) denotes the collection of instances of #$WrittenCharacter which instantiate the #AbstractCharacter ABSTRACT_CHARACTER.")
(comment suggestedSubEventTypesOnTour "(#$suggestedSubEventTypesOnTour TOUR EVENTTYPE SUBEVENTTYPE PLACE)

means that within the context of TOUR, a tour participant (see #$tourParticipants) in TOUR might be advised to consider performing an instance of SUBEVENTTYPE during the course of an event of type EVENTTYPE occuring at PLACE during the tour.")
(comment Wrinkle "The collection of ridges or furrows in non-rigid objects.")
(comment WavePropagationType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$WavePropagationType is a specialization of #$WavePropagation (q.v).  Instances of  #$WavePropagationType include the collections #$ElectromagneticRadiation, #$Sound, #$VisibleLight, and #$XRay.")
(comment keGenlsStrongSuggestionPreds "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate and a specialization of #$keGenlsRelevantPreds.
(#$keGenlsStrongSuggestionPreds COL BINPRED) means that for every known 
(i.e. reified-in-the-KB) specialization SPEC of COL, it is strongly suggested 
that there be some THING such that (BINPRED SPEC THING) is known in the Knowledge Base.")
(disjointWith UnitOfAngularSpeed UnitOfSpeed)
(disjointWith Kayak Raft)
(comment Hallucinogen "The collection of substances that can cause hallucinations. Also known as 'psychedelic drugs'.")
(comment MachineGun "A specialization of #$FullyAutomaticFirearm.  Each instance of #$MachineGun is an automatic firearm capable of sustained fire over relatively long periods.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseHasWeakPassword "An attribute of some instances of #$ComputationalSystem.  A computational system is #$VulnerableBecauseHasWeakPassword if the #$Password-Computer for an account on it is a #$Password-Weak.")
(comment groupMembersFoundInLocation "(#$groupMembersFoundInLocation GROUP LOCATION) means that the members of GROUP, an instance of #$Group, are all found within the bounds of LOCATION.")
(comment (FreeThingOfTypeFn MusicalTextCopy) "The collection of free sheet music.")
(comment Location-Underspecified "The collection of locations, tangible or otherwise, which are typically conceptualized by human beings for purposes of common-sense reasoning as locations. This collection thus includes tangible Places such as #$Ireland-TheIsland, as well as metaphoric locations. For instance, many states-of-being are conceptualized as abstract locations, such as Trouble ('he saw trouble ahead'), Depression ('she fell into a ...'), #$Happiness ('they found bliss together').")
(comment placeName-ShortForm "(#$placeName-ShortForm PLACE NAME) means that NAME is a common short-form name of PLACE that is used in English. See also #$placeName-LocalShortForm.")
(comment ConfiguringEvent "The collection of events in which at least two spatially distinct objects become spatially configured relative to each other, producing an instance of #$Configuration.")
(comment LandscapeImage "The collection of visual images which depict mainly geographical or topographical regions.  The depicted region itself is the focal object of the image.")
(disjointWith TemporalObjectType TaxBracket)
(disjointWith Wax Tar)
(comment decileRange "(#$decileRange DECILE_STRUCTURE N INTERVAL) means that the Nth decile in DECILE_STRUCTURE spans INTERVAL.")
(comment Yersinia "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom.  This genus contains several #$BiologicalSpecies that are pathogenic for humans, including #$Plague-Bacterium.   #$Yersinia-Genus are short,
pleomorphic, #$GramNegativeBacterium, rods.  They do not form spores.")
(disjointWith NobelPrize AcademyAward)
(comment F-5E-Fighter "A collection. The F-5E is an American light tactical fighter plane.")
(comment programTypeFoundOnComputer "A predicate relating instances of #$ComputationalSystem with collections of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  (#$programTypeFoundOnComputer PROGRAMTYPE COMPUTER) means that a copy of an instance of PROGRAMTYPE is installed on COMPUTER.")
(comment TableContentMicrotheory "Instances of #$SchemaMicrotheory are microtheories that combine the content of several #$LogicalTables.")
(comment InjectableLiquid-Medical "A fluid which is suitable and intended for injecting into the blood stream (or muscular system) of a patient.")
(disjointWith FillingAPrescription-Retail FillingAPrescription-Institutional)
(comment MilitaryOrgTypeByEchelonGeoAndBOS "This type-level collection forms an important partition on
#$ModernMilitaryOrganization. For each possible combination of a #$MilitaryUnitTypeByEchelon instance (e.g. #$Platoon-UnitDesignation), a
#$GeographicalAgent instance (e.g. #$France) and a #$BranchOfMilitaryService
spec (#$Army-BranchOfService, #$Navy, #$AirForce, etc.),
#$MilitaryOrgTypeByEchelonGeoAndBOS has an instance, comprising all and only
those #$ModernMilitaryOrganizations of the level of the #$MilitaryUnitTypeByEchelon instance which are #$subOrganizations of an instance of the #$BranchOfMilitaryService spec that has the #$GeographicalAgent instance as #$sovereignAllegianceOfOrg.  E.g.,  collection of all Iranian air force squadrons.  See also #$OrgTypeByEchelonGeoAndBOSFn.")
(comment toPreventInSit-Prop "(#$toPreventInSit-Prop SIT PROP) means that SIT is a

#$Situation whose success in a planning context is contingent upon

PROP not becoming true.")
(comment Codon-MolecularSegment "An instance of #$ObjectType and a specialization of #$PolynucleotideStrand. Each instance of #$Codon-MolecularSegment is an instance of #$MolecularComponent which is a physical series of three instances of #$Nucleotide and part of a longer #$PolynucleotideStrand.")
(comment passengers "(#$passengers MOVE PERSON) means that the instance of #$Person PERSON is a passenger in the instance of #$TransportationEvent MOVE.  (#$passengers MOVE PERSON) implies (i) that PERSON is transported in MOVE, so that (#$transportees MOVE PERSON) also holds, and (ii) PERSON does not control the transporter in MOVE, or in any sub-event (see the predicate #$subEvents) of MOVE, so that (#$not (#$driverActor SUB-MOVE PERSON)) holds for any sub-event SUB-MOVE of MOVE.")
(comment patientInCareEvent "#$ActorSlot that relates an instance of a  #$MedicalCareEvent to the #$MedicalPatient in that event.")
(comment MallardDuck "Common North American duck. Both wild and domesticated populations exist. Males have distinctive emerald-green heads.")
(comment LightMechanizedUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units lightly equipped with vehicles that run on motorized tracks or treads.")
(comment termDependsOn "(#$termDependsOn DEP-TERM INDEP-TERM) states that the reason for the existence of the term DEP-TERM in the Cyc knowledge base is completely dependent on the continued existence of the term INDEP-TERM.  Thus, if INDEP-TERM should ever be removed from the knowledge base, then DEP-TERM should also be immediately removed.  This relationship is automatically maintained between reified non-atomic terms (NATs) and the terms from which they are constructed.")
(comment MidcourseGuidedProjectile "A collection.  Instances have paths which can be altered in flight, either using on-board equipment or a #$RemoteControlDevice.  Subsets include #$CruiseMissiles and some types of #$AirToSurfaceMissiles and #$SurfaceToSurfaceMissiles.")
(comment AltoCumulusCloud "The collection of middle level clouds (#$CloudInSky) that
appear bumpy, whether in a limited region of the sky or covering a
wide area.  #$AltoCumulusClouds do not form continuous sheets, but always
have gaps between individual parts.")
(comment CustomarySystemOfLinks-Comm "The collection of all customary or conventional network systems consisting of interconnected           links (instances of #$Path-Customary) and nodes intended primarily to be capable for use           in instances of #$InformationTransferEvents.")
(comment IrregularFunction "This is the collection of all irregular functions.  For example, the flow rate of a dribbling faucet is an irregular function.  A periodic nor a monotonically increasing function are negative examplars of irregular functions.")
(comment Elasticity "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity.  Each instance of #$Elasticity is a specific ability of a physical material to quickly and completely return to its original shape after deformation that does not induce breakage, without permanent change to its original dimensions.  For example, billiard balls have a high degree of elasticity in this sense.  Elasticities of objects are indicated with the predicate #$elasticityOfObject.")
(comment ProfessionalAssociation "A collection of organizations.  Each element of #$ProfessionalOrganization is a group consisting of professionally trained, white-collar workers as members.  Usually, the members of a particular professional organization belong to a single profession (or a related group of professions).  Examples: #$AmericanMedicalAssociation, #$AmericanOsteopathyAssociation.")
(comment SingletonStringFn "(#$SingletonStringFn CHAR) denotes the STRING of length 1 

that has CHAR as its only member.  Though of course intimately 

related, CHAR and STRING are distinct individuals.  The purpose 

of applying this function is so the result can be used as an

argument to #$ConcatenateStringsFn.")
(comment NavalAircraft "A collection of #$MilitaryAircraft.  Every instance of
#$NavalAircraft is used or equipped to be used by some country's
#$Navy.")
(comment ProtozoanInfection "A specialization of #$Infection.  Each instance of #$ProtozoanInfection is an infection caused by protozoa (see the collection #$Protozoan).  Notable specializations of #$ProtozoanInfection include #$Giardiasis and #$Malaria.")
(disjointWith ChildrensProductMarketCategory SexualProductOrServiceEvent)
(comment BouncingAnObject "The event in which an agent bounces an object off of a surface by throwing it")
(disjointWith (TransportViaFn LandTransportationDevice) (TransportViaFn AirTransportationDevice))
(comment BuildingMaintenance "A collection of events. Each instance of #$BuildingMaintenance is an event of maintaining a #$Building over time. This includes maintaining not only walls, roof, and floors, etc., but also systems like the electrical system, plumbing, heating and air conditioning, etc. Like all instances of #$MaintainingSomething, an event of #$BuildingMaintenance is intended to keep something the same, to prevent it from deviating too much from its original condition, not to change it. Thus collections like #$Remodeling are NOT specs of #$BuildingMaintenance.")
(comment ArmyBase-Grounds "A subcollection of #$MilitaryBase-Grounds;
each is controlled by a #$subOrganizations of some
instance of an #$Army-BranchOfService
and is the #$orgFacilities of some
#$ArmyBase-MilitaryOrganization.")
(comment Tabun "A #$NerveAgentType that is extremely lethal when inhaled.")
(comment ReflectionNebula "A type of nebula that shines by reflected light. Bright stars near reflection nebulae emit light into the region that is reflected by the large amount of dust there. The size of the dust grains causes blue light to be reflected more efficiently than red light, so these reflection nebulae frequently appear blue in color.")
(disjointWith HorseRacingEvent GreyhoundRacingEvent)
(comment TelevisionNetwork "A subset of #$CommunicationsOrganization.  Elements of #$TelevisionNetwork are organizations that produce television programs and distribute them either directly to the public or through intermediaries (see also #$TelevisionStation).")
(comment Queen-HeadOfGovernment "The Queen of a country and the #$HeadOfGovernment of that country")
(comment 3-TheDigit "The numeral 3 of the Arabic Number system.  This is '3' as a #$Character-Abstract rather than the physical #$WrittenCharacter or the abstract mathematical #$Number-General.")
(comment Lira-Italy "The unit of currency used by both Italy and #$SanMarino.")
(comment AutomaticFirearm-ClipFed "the collection of #$AutomaticFirearms that

    draw ammunition from a gun clip.")
(comment FinancialStatement "The collection of all presentations of financial data which show the financial position and the results of financial operations of a company, a fund, a group of accounts, or an entire governmental unit for a particular accounting period.")
(comment MethylAlcohol "CH3OH. An alcohol which is used to make formaldehyde, and is used as an antifreeze.")
(disjointWith FluidTangibleThing CornerOnObject)
(comment CrosswordGameEvent "All events of solving a puzzle in which words corresponding to numbered clues are to be found and written in to squares in the puzzle")
(comment Anaeroplasmataceae-Family "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalFamily in the #$MoneraKingdom that includes the #$BiologicalGenus of #$Anaeroplasma-Genus and #$Asteroleplasma-Genus.")
(comment DramaticActingForFilm "This is the collection of events in which a person portrays someone or soemthing other than himself as part of the production of a film, either for television or the movies. DramaticActingForFilm is thus distinct from DramaticActing-Live, which is acting in an instance of live DramaticPerformance.")
(comment AttackHelicopter "The collection of #$Helicopters used for attacking ground or water targets in a military context.")
(comment TheOccasion "The instance of #$GiftGivingOccasionType which is the occasion for #$TheGiftGiving.")
(comment VariableArityFunction "A specialization of both #$Function-Denotational
and #$VariableArityRelation (qq.v.).  Each instance 
of #$VariableArityFunction is a function that can 
take a variable number of arguments. The degree 
of variability for a given such function can 
be constrained using the predicates #$arityMin 
and #$arityMax.  Examples of #$VariableArityFunctions 
include #$JoinListsFn and #$PlusFn.  Thus 
`(#$PlusFn 1 2)' and `(#$PlusFn 1 2 3)' are 
both well-formed.  Cf. #$FixedArityFunction.")
(comment (BuyingFn Manuscript) "A subset of #$BuyingAnObject. In each instance of (#$BuyingFn #$Manuscript), an agent buys an unpublished written work, along with the rights to use, and control the use of, the content of that work. An example would be a publishing house buying the manuscript of a novel from an author.")
(comment connected-AbutsSurface "(#$connected-AbutsSurface OBJ1 OBJ2) means that an end of #$LongAndThin OBJ1 contacts the surface of and is #$connectedTo OBJ2.")
(comment Dysmenorrhea "A physiological condition in which the patient experiences painful menstrual periods.")
(comment purposeInEvent-GoalType "This predicate relates agents and events in which they play some role to the kind of purpose that it has for the agent.  For instance, (#$purposeInEvent-GoalType #$WayneGretzky-Athlete EatingBreakfast001 #$SelfPreservationGoal) means that Wayne Gretzky eats breakfast001 with the explicit purpose of pursuing self preservation.  See also #$purposeInEvent.")
(disjointWith CargoShip Ferry)
(comment totalValueOfAssets "The total value of all assets owned by the agent.")
(comment moleculesOfCompoundType "This predicate relates instances of #$ChemicalSubstanceType to the collection of molecules of that type.  (#$moleculesOfCompoundType STUFF STUFF-MOC) means that STUFF-MOC is the collection of molecules of STUFF. It is not required that the stuff type in the 1st argument be an instance of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies, since this predicate may apply to chemical compounds that are not identified solely by their chemical composition, cf. e.g. #$PolymerType.")
(comment ScreeningOut "#$ScreeningOut refers to the collection of all screening actions in which some elements of a list (or set) are removed from the list according to a particular set of (possibly arbitrary) selection criteria.")
(comment Maximum "A #$NumericQuantifier.  Used to denote the maximum quantity which results from applying the function specified in the second argument to all of the elements of the set expression which appears in the first argument.--Rode 3/15/98")
(comment TabooAct "The collection of all #$Actions prohibited in a given context by a taboo. A taboo is placed on objects, places, words, etc., in some cultures when it is believed to have powers above the ordinary. If someone utters a taboo word or touches a taboo object, that is typically cause for punishment or a purification ceremony.")
(comment BoxingHeadgear "The kind of protection that one normally wears on one's head while boxing.")
(comment HeavyEquipmentTransport "The collection of military trailer trucks used to transport heavy equipment, such as #$EarthMovingEquipment-Military.")
(comment typesCorrectlyBasePairedDuring "(#$typesCorrectlyBasePairedDuring N-TYPE1 N-TYPE2 EVT-TYPE) means that during instances of #$GeneticInformationTransferEvent, EVT-TYPE, instances of the two instances of #$NucleotideType, N-TYPE1 and N-TYPE2 stand in the relation of being base-paired correctly. Hydrogen bonds between some #$Nucleotides are more stable than others -- the stable ones are correctly base-paired. They are considered correctly base-paired with respect to the goal or norm of transmitting a cell's genes without alteration during a #$GeneticInformationTransferEvent.")
(comment Seaborgium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is a RadioactiveObject of #$Seaborgium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment extraditionFor "ARG1 is an extradition action, and ARG2 is an action that the person extradited is believed to have performed, is believed to be a criminal act, and the reason why the person is being extradited is so that s/he can be tried for the accused crime by the country s/he is being extradited to.")
(comment Gendarme "A Collection.  In some countries on the #$ContinentOfEurope (especially #$France) or in Asia Minor,           #$Gendarmes are #$Soldiers acting as #$LawEnforcementOfficers.")
(comment ColorImage "A collection of visual images.  Each element of #$ColorImage is an image 'in color', i.e., it is not monochromatic but is composed of several colors.  Any 'in color' movie being shown on a 'color television' is a #$ColorImage.  Presumably, a nighttime sequence viewed on such a television would still be an element of #$ColorImage since the context was 'in color' and subtle blues as well as greys would be depicted.  An image consisting solely of varying shades of green, such as that seen on many monochromatic oscilloscopes, would be an element of #$MonochromeImage not #$ColorImage nor #$BlackAndWhiteImage.")
(comment Stereogram "A diagram or picture representing a solid form on            a plane surface.")
(comment AppointingAmbassador "The collection of events where a state appoints an ambassador to another state.")
(comment MesophilicBacterium "A collection of #$Bacterium that grow optimumally at
temperatures between (#$DegreeCelsius 15 45).  These
#$ProkaryoticCells have a wide range of habitats and include the
pathogens for humans and other animals.")
(comment baseRateForOngoingService "This predicate relates an #$AgreementForOngoingService to the amount of money that the #$agreeingServiceRecipient is obligated to pay to the #$agreeingServiceProvider every month or year, etc., throughout the term of the agreement, regardless of the amount of service actually provided. For example, (#$baseRateForOngoingService AGR (DollarsPerYear 50)) means that there is an annual fee of $50 for the service agreed to in AGR.")
(comment ArmoredC2ReconVehicle "The collection of armored C2 reconnaisance vehicles.")
(comment SBHLPredicate "#$SBHLPredicate is the collection of all Cyc predicates which have special SBHL module support.")
(comment CalciumChannelBlocker "Each #$CalciumChannelBlocker is a #$CardiovascularAgent that inhibits the flow of calcium into the heart and smooth muscle cells.")
(comment SaltingFood "A specialization of #$PreservingFood: each instance of this collection is an event in which food is soaked in salt to prevent it from rotting.")
(comment armedWithProjectile "(#$armedWithProjectile PLATFORM PROJECTILE)   says that PLATFORM is carrying PROJECTILE and    has the right sort of #$ProjectileLauncher with which to use PROJECTILE.  It is important to time-index most assertions using this predicate, for though it might be true right now that, say (#$relationInstanceExistsCount #$armedWithProjectile PLATFORM #$Missile 5), two seconds from now, when one of the #$Missiles is fired,  the assertion will become false.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn SixthRib) HeadOfBone) "")
(comment politicalInstructor "(#$politicalInstructor ORG AGENT) means that AGENT serves as a channel disseminating political information and propoganda within ORG.")
(comment RaceCarDriver "This is the collection of persons who earn their livings by racing cars.")
(comment ForeignPolicyGoal "This attribute characterizes goals which are foreign policy goals.")
(disjointWith AttackByComputerOperation AttackOnTangible)
(comment Tornado-FighterPlane "A brand of #$FighterPlane manufactured in 

  Europe.")
(comment SeaBattle "The collection of events that are battles at sea (or on some other body of water).")
(comment FattyTissue "The collection of all #$FattyTissue found in the body of an #$Animal. See #$EdibleFat for the fat that one eats.")
(comment DebuggingAComputerProgram "A collection of events, and a specialization of #$SimpleRepairing.  In each #$DebuggingAComputerProgram event,  a computer program is tested, analyzed, and modified (perhaps repeatedly) in order to remove unwanted features, restore intended functionality, etc.  This is more of a #$TemporalStuffType than a #$TemporalObjectType (i.e., more substance-like than object-like), since each `portion' of the total #$DebuggingAComputerProgram event is itself a small #$DebuggingAComputerProgram event.")
(comment LeftStrandFn "A specialized form of #$SideOneFn and #$SideTwoFn that applies
only to instances of #$DNAMolecule and designates either one of the
symmetric strands constituting such molecules.")
(comment FactionalConflict "A specialization of #$ConflictEvent.  Each instance of #$FactionalConflict is a conflict in which two agents within an organization struggle for control of the group's administration, agenda, or ideology.  The struggle may be between two factional agents or between a faction and those who currently hold power in the group.  Factional conflicts may or may not be violent.")
(comment Review-CW "The collection of all reviews of #$Events or #$ConceptualWorks intended to be published as a subdivision of some #$PublishedMaterial.")
(comment TectonicPlate "The collection of massive, irregularly shaped slabs of solid rock.  The size of these plates varies greatly, from a few hundred to thousands of kilometers across.  Some are as thick as 200km and others are less than 15km thick.  According to the assumptions of #$PlateTectonics, the Earth's outermost layer is composed of #$TectonicPlates, floating above the inner surface of the planet and moving relative to each other.")
(comment UniquePartFn "(#$UniquePartFn OBJ UNIQUEPARTTYPE) returns the unique part of OBJ that is of type UNIQUEPARTTYPE.")
(disjointWith Submarine LandTransportationDevice)
(disjointWith ChangeInUserRights Patrolling)
(comment SolarEclipse "The subclass of #$Eclipse-CelestialEvent in which the #$Sun is obscured from view on #$PlanetEarth by the #$MoonOfEarth. When the #$MoonOfEarth is aligned between the #$Sun and #$PlanetEarth, the moon partially or fully obscures the view of the #$Sun from some parts of #$PlanetEarth. Such eclipses could be predicted by the Ancients (e.g., the #$AncientRomanPersons) and were considered to have divine providence.  Full #$SolarEclipses, in which the moon obscures the entire solar disk, allow #$Astronomers to view the #$Sun's corona. See also #$LunarEclipse.")
(comment Sedative "Drugs which are used to treat anxiety and insomnia.  In higher doses, these are often used as sleeping pills.")
(comment CycLReifiableNonAtomicTerm "A collection of Cyc terms that are NATs (#$CycLNonAtomicTerms; see
#$Function-Denotational) whose functor is an instance of
#$ReifiableFunction. E.g., since #$GovernmentFn is an instance of
#$ReifiableFunction, it is true that (#$GovernmentFn #$France) is a
#$CycLReifiableNonAtomicTerm.")
(comment Kilowatt "1000 X Watt.  Unit for measuring power.")
(comment TypedSubcollectionFn "(#$TypedSubcollectionFn COL-TYPE COL) denotes the collection of
subcollections of COL that are also instances of COL-TYPE. For instance,
(#$TypedSubcollectionFn #$BiologicalTaxon #$Bacterium) is the collection of
specs of #$Bacterium that are biological taxa, for example
#$Anthrax-Bacterium, an instance of #$BiologicalSpecies and a spec of
#$Bacterium, is an instance of that collection. In the mean time, the
(#$SubcollectionByRegionFn #$Anthrax-Bacterium (#$LeftRiverbankFn
#$SeineRiver)) is not, yet, an instance of such collection.")
(comment EvacuatingAPlace "A collection of actions.  In each instance of #$EvacuatingAPlace, some person, animal, or organization leaves the place it had been 'occupying' (e.g., a house, office, geographical region) in response to some perceived danger.  In English, 'evacuating' is used mostly to denote flight prompted by a systematic threat to agents of a certain type or in a certain place. In this sense, leaving your home in response to an approaching hurricane or enemy army counts as 'evacuating,' while leaving your home to avoid an angry rival may not.  The Cyc collection #$EvacuatingAPlace includes both cases.  Note that the performer of an  #$EvacuatingAPlace may be evacuating herself or another agent or both.  If an intelligent agent is evacuating herself from a place, she is both the #$primaryObjectMoving in and the performer of that action.  If an intelligent agent is evacuating another agent(s) from a place (the latter agents need not be intelligent), those being moved are the #$primaryObjectMovings, while those doing the moving are the performers and may or may not also be #$primaryObjectMovings.")
(comment FoodSupplyGoal "The attribute characterizing goals which are concerned with maintaining an adequate supply of food to feed a nation's population.  Depending upon the country, this goal is supported by domestic agriculture or by importing food.")
(comment Seaport "The collection of seaports.  The entire area, including land area and man-made structures, where boats dock and water traffic is handled.  A single seaport contains at least one instance of #$PortFacility.  Developed seaports in industrial countries are typically under the jurisdiction of the port authority of the city in which the seaport is located.  See also #$PortCity.")
(comment FreshFoodOrDrink "The collection of all instances of #$FoodOrDrink whose nutritional or gustatory quality is acceptable but deteriorating rapidly and must be eaten within a fairly short period (usually a few days or less) to be healthful and/or palatable. In other words, instances of #$FreshFoodOrDrink have a fairly short #$shelfLife. Instances of #$FreshFoodOrDrink have not yet undergone an instance of #$Spoiling and are still edible, but if they are not eaten they undergo #$Spoiling and become instances of #$SpoiledFood.")
(comment Secretin "A #$Hormone that inhibits acid secretion in the stomach.")
(comment TomatoPlant "Individual tomato plants")
(comment SexualGratification "The states of #$SexualGratification; such a state is ordinarily achieved after an #$UrgeToHaveSex has been satisfied.")
(comment requiredArg2Pred "A #$MetaPredicate for stating that every  instance of a given collection is related (as the \"arg2\") to some  thing or things by a given predicate.  (#$requiredArg2Pred COL PRED)  means that for every instance INST of COL, there exists some sequence  <X1, X3, ..., Xn> of such that (PRED X1 INST X3 ... Xn) holds.  For  example, (#$requiredArg2Pred #$Side #$objectSides) means that every  side is the side of at least one object.  See also #$requiredArg1Pred.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfWeaklyEncryptedPasswordFile "A vulnerability attribute of some computers.  A computer is

#$VulnerableBecauseOfWeaklyEncryptedPasswordFile if it is

running a program that uses a weak encryption algorithm to store passwords in a

file on the computer.  This means that someone who acquires the

encrypted passwords can decode them without knowing the encryption

algorithm or the encryption key.")
(comment DegreeOfDamage "A collection of attributes which are scalar indices of damage done in

a particular kind of context.  This is a useful collection to have,

since it is common to see damage represented on a numeric scale in

situations where the kind, source, and subject of the damage of the

damage is already known.")
(comment VaccineForAgainstFn "(#$VaccineForAgainstFn FOR AGAINST) is the colllection

 of #$Vaccines used to protect instances of 

  creature-type FOR against #$InfectionType AGAINST.

 For example, (#$VaccineForAgainstFn #$Cattle-Domestic

 #$AnthraxInfection) is the collection of bovine anthrax

 vaccines.")
(comment Anaplasma-Genus "A collection of all #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$Anaplasma-Genus that includes obligate parasites of vertebrates, mostly cattle.")
(comment ScienceFictionWriter "The collection of writers who write Science Fiction")
(comment AsparticAcid "A collection of compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.  This

#$NonessentialAminoAcidType is also an excitory neurotransmitter in the

central nervous system.  Its abbreviations are Asp and D.")
(comment DismountedCombatEngineeringUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of dismounted military units that are equipped for both combat operations and engineering operations.")
(disjointWith Drink GargleSolution)
(comment valueOfLiabilities "The total value of all liabilities owed by the agent.")
(comment SpanishWord "The collection of all lexical words in Spanish; a subset of #$LexicalWord.            Different inflectional forms of a word do not count as different words.")
(comment PlayingACardGame "Playing a game involving a deck of cards.")
(comment Prednisone "A #$Corticosteroid with effects similar to those of #$Cortisone.")
(comment CampingStove "The collection of camping stoves.

A camping stove is a relatively light device which uses propane

or other fuel that comes is small tanks. It is supposed to be

quite portable. Some camping stoves are less portable and intended

for RV-type camping. Others are much more portable and intended

for real camping.")
(comment ObservationUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units that are dedicated to observation.  They are intended to perform observatory functions only, and are not trained, equipped, or intended to engage the enemy.")
(comment supportsActivity " The expression `(#$supportsActivity AGENT SCRIPT-TYPE)' means that the agent AGENT provides 

direct or

indirect economic support for SCRIPT-TYPE , thereby enabling, furthering, or sustaining it. This is to be distinguished from political support. Each

case of (#$supportsActivity AGENT SCRIPT-TYPE) will involve direct economic support by the

AGENT of some AGENT2, but the goal of this support will be the enabling or sustaining of SCRIPT-TYPE. Economic support could include the purchasing of goods, the volunteering of labor, or the giving of money. Examples of (#$supportsActivity AGENT SCRIPT-TYPE) would include parents supporting

their child's training on a musical instrument by paying for lessons and a community 

supporting local organic farming by purchasing the produce produced.")
(comment DreamDictionary "a collection of #$Dictionarys. Each element of #$DreamDictionary provides symbolic interpretations of words used to report #$Dreams.")
(comment Whipping "The collection of #$Whippings, which involve the hitting of a person with #$Whip.")
(comment primaryPracticeType "A Listwright constant created for relating a physician to one of the medical practice types reflected in the Listwright categorization, in this case the type of the physician's primary practice.")
(disjointWith SurfaceOnTangibleObject FreeSheet)
(comment AreaResourceIBTFn "#$AreaResourceIBTFn takes as argument any instance of #$SpatialThing-Localized and returns the collection of all InformationBearingThings designed to provide information about a broad range of resources available in the area of that thing.  The prototypical example is a website or brochure put together by a chamber of commerce and aimed at the average tourist or newcomer to an area. For example, (#$AreaResourceIBTFn #$CityOfAustinTX) returns the collection of all IBTs designed to offer information, conveniently assembled in one place, about a broad range of resources available in the Austin area (such as www.austin360.com).")
(disjointWith ChamberMusicComposition CompositionWithSoloistAndAccompaniment)
(comment BiologicalAttack "The collection of events in which a biological weapon is used against a #$PartiallyTangible target.")
(comment Analgesic "Drugs which are used to reduce or relieve pain.")
(comment ClassicalMusic-Romantic "A specialization of Western #$ClassicalMusic whose #$genreHeyday was #$TheNineteenthCenturyAD. Romanticism in music was characterized by an emphasis on emotion and great freedom of form. Representative composers include Berlioz, Mendelssohn, Schumann, Chopin, Liszt, and Wagner.")
(comment Packet-SIPRNet "#$Packet-SIPRNet is the collection of instances of #$Packet-Internet which adhere to the specifications set by #$SIPRNetProtocol.    A #$Packet-SIPRNet contains information which constrains it to be routed to its destination on machines on the #$SIPRNet-PathSystem.")
(comment MovieReviewFn "This function takes as argument any instance of #$SpecifiedMovieType and returns the collection of all reviews of that movie.  For example, (#$ReviewFn #$2001-ASpaceOdyssey-TheMovie) returns the collection of all reviews of #$StanleyKubrick-MovieDirector's movie.")
(comment PartTypeFn "(#$PartTypeFn OBTYPE PARTTYPE) yields the collection of instances of PARTTYPE that are physical parts of instances of OBJECTTYPE.  For example, (#$PartTypeFn #$Chimpanzee #$Heart) is the collection of chimpanzee hearts.")
(comment interpreter "A functional role that an agent plays with respect to an
organization.  The agent who is the #$interpreter for an instance of
#$Organization is supposed to make sure that that communications and
information relevant to the overall goals of the #$Organization
instance are translated into a language that the members of the
organization can understand.")
(comment internationalOrganizationMemberCountries "This predicate relates international organizations to countries that belong to them.  (#$internationalOrganizationMemberCountries ORG NATION) means that NATION (as represented by its national government or other legally designated body) is a member of the #$InternationalOrganizationOfCountries ORG.  For example, #$Bahrain is an #$internationalOrganizationMemberCountries of the #$LeagueOfArabStates and of the #$UnitedNationsOrganization, and #$China-PeoplesRepublic is a #$internationalOrganizationMemberCountries of the #$UnitedNationsOrganization but #$Taiwan-RepublicOfChina is not.")
(comment Glider "The collection of all unpowered steerable aircraft with lift surfaces designed for extended periods of gliding.")
(comment CalendarBasedTemporalObjectType "#$CalendarBasedTemporalObjectType  s a collection of collections and a specialization of #$TemporallyDisjointTemporalObjectType.  Each instance of #$CalendarBasedTemporalObjectType is a collection of instances of #$TemporalThing.  Each instance of an instance of #$CalendarBasedTemporalObjectType is a temporal thing that is co-temporal with a specific time in a calendar year. The calendar references may be to any sort of calendar -- lunar, Gregorian, Julian, etc.  Example instances of #$CalendarBasedTemporalObjectType include #$October, #$ChristmasHoliday, #$Equinox, and #$SuperBowlGame.")
(comment prevents-SitProp "(#$prevents-SitProp SIT PROP) means that SIT prevents PROP from    becoming true.")
(comment Corn-SingleGrain "The harvested fruit of the corn plant.")
(comment coRewriteOf "(#$coRewriteOf FORM1 FORM2) is the symmetric verison of #$rewriteOf. ie assertions in the KB will be propagated in both directions. That means that an assertion of the form (... FORM1 ...) will be replicated as (... FORM2 ...) and vice versa. ")
(comment MicrosoftCertifiedSolutionsDeveloper "The collection of #$EducationalDegrees earned by taking a 'Microsoft Authorized Academic Training Program'.  Such degrees are considered industry-wide standards of programming competence.")
(comment PleonasticFrameType "A collection of frames which require their subject to be an expletive 'it', as in 'it seems that John went to the party', 'it is bad that nobody came', 'it is bad for John that Mary left'.")
(disjointWith TimeInterval (GroupFn Situation))
(comment GeneExpressionByCellType "This collection of collections facets gene expression according to the type of cell containing the relevant genetic information, i.e. prokaryotic or bacterial, versus eukaryotic.")
(comment Oceanus-Lunar "The collection of topographical features where each element is a very large dark area on Earth's moon.")
(comment Cracking-CompromisingSecurity "#$Cracking-CompromisingSecurity is a subset of #$PurposefulAction and #$SecurityBreach.  It is the collection of actions that occurs whenever the security measures of some individual are circumvented by some unauthorized agent.  A wide variety of events may be elements of this collection.  For example, if one blows a safe open with dynamite one is said to ''crack the safe''.  Also, if one guesses the combination to a safe (in this case one also performs an instance of #$UnlockingALock), one compromises its security.  If someone cracks a password protected computer system (see #$PenetratingAComputerNetwork), one either circumvents the password access protocol or has otherwise determined the password to the system without appropriate permission.  Take care in distinguishing #$Cracking-CompromisingSecurity from #$SecurityBreach: the collection #$Cracking-CompromisingSecurity is a specialization of #$PurposefulAction, whereas the more general collection, #$SecurityBreach, is a specialization of #$Action.  Instances of #$SecurityBreach occur whenever security is breached, whether or not it was intentionally cracked, but all and only purposefully executed breaches of security are instances of #$Cracking-CompromisingSecurity.")
(comment aminoAcidSequenceOf "(#$aminoAcidSequenceOf PROTEIN LIST) means that the instance

of #$ProteinMolecule PROTEIN exhibts the amino acid sequence given by the list

of amino-acid types LIST.")
(comment MilitaryRankType "The collection of all military rank systems, each being an ordered collection (system) of rank attributes for a particular country and military organization.  This is a 'type', or collection of collections.  For example, (#$rank-Military JohnSmith #$Corporal-Rank), (#$isa #$Corporal-Rank #$USArmyRank) and (#$isa #$USArmyRank #$MilitaryRankType).")
(comment WrittenNumeral "A specialization of #$WrittenCharacter

any instance of which is a marking intended to represent some instance 

of #$Numeral.  #$WrittenNumerals are single characters; for multi-character 

sequences, see #$WrittenNumeralSequence.")
(comment PublisherOfIndOrSeriesFn "This function takes any instance of

an individual published work or periodical series and returns its

publisher. Note that these things have single publishers, unlike the

arguments of the function #$PublisherOfPublicationTypeFn.")
(comment interArg1ResultGenls "A ternary #$MetaRelation predicate for stating that a certain kind of complex, partly #$genls based relationship holds between the first argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned. (#$interArg1ResultGenls FUNC INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when a subcollection of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the first argument to FUNC, then -- regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be -- the value of that function for those arguments is a subcollection of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL. That is: if INST is an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC INST ...) = VALUE, then VALUE is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  Note that, unlike (e.g.) the #$InterArgTypePredicates, #$interArg1ResultGenls _cannot_ be used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on functions.  See also the similar but more flexible quaternary #$interArgResultGenl.")
(comment GameChampionsFn "#$GameChampionsFn takes as argument any spec of either #$PlayingAGame or #$GameEvent and returns the collection of all champions and other acknowledged masters of that type of game.  For example, (#$GameChampionsFn #$PlayingChess) returns the collection of all chess champions.")
(disjointWith UnitOfAcceleration UnitOfSpeed)
(comment subTimeSliceType "(#$subTimeSliceType LONGER-TYPE SHORTER-TYPE) means that  for every instance X of LONGER-TYPE, there is an instance Y of SHORTER-TYPE such that (#$timeSlices X Y).  Examples: (#$subTimeSliceType #$October #$Halloween),  (#$subTimeSliceType #$CalendarYear #$October). See also the comments on #$timeSlices, #$subTimeSliceType.  Note that (#$subTimeSliceType LONGER-TYPE SHORTER-TYPE) does not necessarily entail (#$superTimeSliceType SHORTER-TYPE LONGER-TYPE).")
(disjointWith Raft Lifeboat)
(comment PsilocybinMushroom "The collection of all mushrooms that contain the #$Hallucinogen #$Psilocybin. These mushrooms are used in religious ceremonies by Indians of Mexico, and were considered sacred by the Aztecs.")
(comment NuclearBomb "A specialization of #$Bomb.  Each instance of #$NuclearBomb is a bomb that derives its explosive force from energy released during nuclear fission or fusion.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseHasDictionaryPassword "An attribute applying to instances of #$Computer.  A computer system is #$VulnerableBecauseHasDictionaryPassword if an account accessible from it has a  #$Password-Computer that is a word found in a standard dictionary.

This is a vulnerability because several computer hacking programs work

by trying to login in using dictionary terms.")
(comment Hydroponics "This is the collection of activities in which plants

are grown in nutrient-enriched water.")
(comment importsThrough "(#$importsThrough REGION PRODUCT-TYPE PT) means that the #$GeographicalRegion REGION imports significant amounts of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE through the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT on their way from their origin.  PT might, in the case of oil imports, for example, be a #$GeographicalRegion or a #$Pipeline.")
(comment meetFunctionOnLattice "(#$meetFunctionOnLattice LATTICE MEET) means that MEET is the 'meet' function in the #$Lattice-LatticeTheoretic LATTICE.  This binary operation on the #$baseSet S of LATTICE is commutative, associative and satisfies the following properties: for each a in S, (MEET X X) = X (the idempotent laws), and for each a and b in S, (JOIN a (MEET a b)) = (MEET a (JOIN a b)) = a (the absorption laws), where JOIN is the 'join' function in LATTICE (i.e., (#$joinFunctionOnLattice LATTICE JOIN) holds).")
(comment EconomicEvent "#$EconomicEvent is the most general collection of events having an economic character, such as buying and selling, inflation and recession, and economic policy-making.")
(comment Charisma "Performing an activity with charisma.")
(comment nonterminalSyntaxSymbols "The predicate (#$nonterminalSyntaxSymbols SYSTEM SYMBOL) relates a #$SyntaxSpecificationSystem (such as a #$FormalGrammar-CW) to one of its grammar symbols that is 'non-terminal' in that it represents further combinations of #$SyntaxSpecificationSymbols rather than standing for a final text or segment or 'surface element' of the (parsed or generated) structure.  For example, in a #$ContextFreeGrammar, with the rules S --> VP + YF; YF --> ''you fool!'' meaning that a sentence S consists of a verb phrase VP followed by the phrase ''you fool!''. YF acts as #$terminalSyntaxSymbols for this grammar  (because YF here  stands directly for surface text) whereas symbols S and VP, act as #$nonterminalSyntaxSymbols.")
(comment YersiniaEnterocolitica "A collection of #$Bacterium forming a #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom
found in the intestinal tract of many animals.  They may be
transmittable to humans and produce a wide variety of clinical symptoms.")
(comment F-4E-Fighter "A collection. The F-4E is an American fighter-bomber plane.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseTransmitsInPlaintext "A vulnerability attribute of some instances of #$ComputationalSystem.  (#$hasVulnerability COMP #$VulnerableBecauseTransmitsInPlaintext) means that there is some #$NetworkingProgram on COMP which does not encrypt data before sending it over a network.")
(comment WorkaroundsSite "The collections of geographical features and fixed structures relevant to the Battlespace Workarounds project.")
(disjointWith FillingAPrescription-MailOrder FillingAPrescription-Retail)
(comment toPreventInSit-SitType "(#$toPreventInSit-SitType SIT SITTYPE) means that SIT is a

situation whose success in a planning context is contingent upon a situaion of  SITTYPE not 'happening' in the course of the plan.")
(comment structureMaps "(#$structureMaps ?Src ?Src-Mt ?Tgt ?Tgt-Mt ?Src-Desc ?Tgt-Desc) returns individual structure-mappings of the formulae in ?Src-Mt pertaining to the source concept ?Src that are isomorphic with formulae in ?Tgt-Mt that pertain to the target domain concept ?Tgt. The mappings are not condensed as #$and formulae as they are when you use structureMap each isomorphic axiom is returned as a distinct binding.")
(comment MigratoryBird "Members of bird species that change their residence on a seasonal basis.")
(comment LeftAndRightSidedObject "A #$LeftAndRightSidedObject is an object with an intrinsic left side and an intrinsic right side.  By 'intrinsic' we mean simply that there exists an established convention according to which one side is considered 'Left' and the other side is considered 'Right'.  Usually, the two sides can be reliably distinguished from one another.  Notice that a conventionally distinguishable left and right do not necessarily imply a bottom and top, or a front and back.  Interestingly, it has proved impossible so far to find instances of objects with a left and right but no top, bottom, front or back.  It is unclear why this should be so, but it apparently pertains to human psychology in reasoning about directions. However, if an object has a conventionally distinguished top, bottom, front, and back, then these suffice to determine an intrinsic left and an intrinsic right.  Notice also--and this is crucial to the whole conception--that while a #$LeftAndRightSidedObject may well have a preferred orientation, changing this orientation does not change what counts as 'left' and what counts as 'right': if you turn me upside down my left side does not become my right side and my right side my left. If an entity does not obey this rule then it does not, generally speaking, count as having a distinguishable left and right--example: a houseplant.")
(comment BallisticMissileUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile centers on missiles           that travel along ballistic trajectories.")
(comment AuthenticationSource "#$AuthenticationSource, a subset of #$TemporalThing, is the collection of sources which can be used for authentication events. Notable subsets include #$Fingerprint and #$Retina.")
(comment topicPattern-Irrelevant "A predicate used in text searching to classify texts by indicating which texts include terms irrelevant to a topic.  It is used with #$regexStringMatch (or #$regexFileMatch) to find terms within a text that match a pattern template (a #$RegularExpression), and to disassociate the text from a particular Cyc term as its topic, because of the matching.  (#$topicPattern-Irrelevant THING REGEX) means that a text containing any substring that matches REGEX is unlikely to be relevant to the topic of THING.  This predicate is used to allow #$RegularExpression templates to help exclude documents from relevance to certain topics.  See also #$topicPattern-Relevant.  For example (#$topicPattern-Irrelevant #$Riverbank ''((\\<financ(ial|e)(s)?)|(account(s)?)|(lend(ing)?)) '') provides a #$RegularExpression template to match 'finances' or 'lending', etc. and marks this pattern as indicating irrelevance to the concept #$Riverbank.")
(comment TerminalGuidedProjectile "The collection of #$PhysicalDevices which have guidance systems in use during the terminal phase of the flight. Subsets include some types of #$AirToSurfaceMissiles and #$SurfaceToSurfaceMissiles.")
(comment AltoStratusCloud "The collection of middle level clouds (#$CloudInSky) that appear as flat smooth dark grey sheets.")
(comment StillImage "A collection of visual images.  Each element of #$StillImage is a static visual image.  Such images are typically images reflected from, or generated by, objects that don't change in time, e.g. an illuminated photograph.  Other examples: images from maps, x-rays, drawings, labels, or any constant projection of light.")
(comment NoTerseArgument "A property of reformulator rules which says that in this rule,
neither argument is more terse or more verbose than the other.")
(disjointWith MonotonicallyDecreasingFunction IrregularFunction)
(comment ShavingSomething "A collection of events. In each #$ShavingSomething event, thin pieces of material on an object's surface are removed. An example would be someone whittling a wooden spoon, someone using a lathe to make a table leg, someone scraping the top layer of mold and cheese off a brick of cheese that was left in the refrigerator just a little too long, etc. WARNING: an event in which someone ``shaves'' their body hair (a #$ShavingBody event) from one's face, legs, etc. with a shaver or razor is NOT a #$ShavingSomething event; rather, it is an instance of the collection #$CuttingSomething.")
(comment employeeStatus "#$employeeStatus relates a person to an instance of #$EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus. For example (#$employeeStatus WORKER #$FullTimeWorker) means that WORKER has a full time job.")
(comment ReconnaissanceAircraft "The collection of aircraft used for reconnaissance and information gathering in a military context.")
(comment RelievingPain "Relieving pain by taking an AnalgesicDrug.  This covers the period during which the drug is taking its effect as well as the ingesting.")
(comment Empire "The collection of all instances of geopolitical entities that are ruled by an emperor or an emperess.")
(comment AbradingSomething "A collection of events.  In an #$AbradingSomething event, the surface of some object is gradually worn away by scraping or similar physical contact involving friction.  Devices used in elements of #$AbradingSomething include files and sand paper; elements of #$AbradingSomething would include the event in which Howard Hughes sanded down the Spruce Goose for the last time, the event in which Lucy Ricardo filed her fingernails just before her singing debut at Rickie's club, etc.")
(disjointWith DisputeEvent Conveying-Generic)
(comment HomeMaintenance "A collection of events. Each instance of #$HomeMaintenance is an event of maintaining a #$House-Modern over time. This includes maintaining not only walls, roof, and floors, etc., but also systems like the electrical system, plumbing, heating and air conditioning, etc.")
(comment SportsLeagueChampionsFn "#$SportsLeagueChampionsFn takes any instance

 of #$SportsLeague as its argument and returns as 

 its value the collection of all winners of league championships, regardless of

 the sport or year. For example, (#$SportsLeagueChampionsFn #$BigEastConference) 

 returns the collection of all Big East Conference champions.")
(comment Howitzer-152mmTowed "The collection of towed 152mm #$Howitzers.")
(comment EmissionNebula "An emission nebula is a cloud of gas and dust, the atoms of which give off light from being excited      by massive hot stars within the nebula itself. These nebulae are often red in color due to the fact       that they are made almost entirely of hydrogen, and hydrogen when excited gives off light, red                                light being the strongest of this emission.")
(comment BallAndStickGame "The collection of #$BallAndGoalGames in which the competitors, usually members of #$SportsTeams, use sticks to manipulate an object (usually a #$Ball or puck), in order to put the object into the opponent's goal, and to prevent the object from entering one's own goal.")
(comment TelevisionStation "A subset of #$CommunicationsOrganization.  Elements of #$TelevisionStation are organizations that disseminate television programming to the public by broadcast or cable.")
(comment 4-TheDigit "The numeral 4 of the Arabic Number system.  This is '4' as a #$Character-Abstract rather than the physical #$WrittenCharacter or the abstract mathematical #$Number-General.")
(disjointWith AutomaticFirearm-BeltFed AutomaticFirearm-ClipFed)
(comment Giga "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10^9")
(comment RPG-NonPlayerCharacter "The collection of characters in a #$RolePlayingGame that are not 'acted' by game participants, but by the games master who controls the game. The actions of #$RPG-NonPlayerCharacters are usually controlled by dice-rolls and pre-set rules, with a great deal of discretion given to the desires of the #$GamesMaster. See also #$RPG-PlayerCharacter.")
(comment suppliedWithFrom "(#$suppliedWithFrom PT1 COL PT2) means that the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT1 is supplied with instances of the #$Collection COL from the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT2.  Like the predicate #$suppliedWith (q.v.), #$suppliedWithFrom is very general.  In various assertions PT1 might, for instance, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion; and likewise for PT2.  The range of possible supplies is similarly broad.")
(comment H2O2Decomposition "The collection of events in which the enzyme #$Catalase decomposes molecules of hydrogen peroxide [#$HydrogenPeroxideMolecule] into water and free oxygen. This process removes the high quantities of hydrogen peroxide produced during cell metabolism.")
(comment BubonicPlague "A collection of ailments characterized by very high fever, chills, prostration, delirium, and enlarged, painful lymph nodes (buboes), which suppurate and may discharge. The most well known epidemic of #$BubonicPlague, the #$BlackDeath-Plague, occurred in Europe, wiping out a third of the population, as well as millions more in China and India.")
(comment KaraokeEvent "The collection of karaoke singing events. During such events
people typically take turns singing popular songs at a microphone,
often reading the words they are singing off a screen that is
syncronized with the sound base of the song itself.")
(comment MythologicalPlace "This collection includes all places, such as #$Atlantis and #$Valhalla, that are fictional and are introduced in some mythology.")
(comment Anaeroplasma-Genus "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom.")
(comment arrangementNearestObjectTypes "This predicate relates an arrangement of like objects 
to the maximally specific types of object under which all of 
its members fall.  
(#$arrangementNearestObjectTypes GROUP OBJTYPE) means that
(i) OBJTYPE is an instance of #$ExistingObjectType that all 
#$groupMembers of GROUP are instances of and (ii) there is 
no reified instance of #$ExistingObjectType that is a proper 
specialization of OBJTYPE and such that all members of GROUP 
are instances of it.  For example, if the members of GROUP 
are the trees in a date palm grove, then OBJTYPE might be 
#$DatePalm, but would not be the more general #$PalmTree.  
Each instance of #$ArrangementOfLikeObjects should have at 
least one such maximally specific corresponding object type.  
For a more general predicate see #$arrangementObjectTypes.")
(comment JazzDancePerformance "JazzDancePerformance is the collection of instances of DancePerformance such that (PerformanceFn JazzDancePerformance) returns a collection of instances of JazzDancing.")
(comment RescueHelicopter "The collection of #$Helicopters used for entering enemy territory in order to rescue personnel. These aircraft are usually heavily armored.")
(comment nearestCommonSpecMt "(#$nearestCommonSpecMt MT-1 MT-2 NEAR-MT) means that NEAR-MT is a \"nearest\" microtheory of which both #$Microtheory MT-1 and #$Microtheory MT-2 are generalizations.  That is, NEAR-MT is not identical to either MT-1 or MT-2, both (#$genlMt NEAR-MT MT-1) and (#$genlMt NEAR-MT MT-2) hold, and there is no reified #$Microtheory NEARER-MT distinct from MT-1, MT-2, and NEAR-MT such that (#$genlMt NEARER-MT MT-1), (#$genlMt NEARER-MT MT-2), and (#$genlMt NEAR-MT NEARER-MT) all hold.  Note that #$nearestCommonSpecMt is #$notAssertible, since it must always be recomputed from the current state of the #$genlMt hierarchy. For comparison, see also #$nearestGenlMt and #$nearestCommonGenlMt.")
(comment BoatMaintenance "Where a #$MaintainingSomething is

performed on a boat or some other #$Watercraft-Surface.")
(comment PicturesFromFn "#$PicturesFromFn, when applied to an instance of <IBTType>, gives the collection of all pictures that can in some sense be extracted from <IBTType>.  So, for example, (#$PicturesFromFn TimeMagazine) is the collection of all pictures ('types' not 'tokens' - i.e., it's the collection that includes 'the picture' of John-John saluting, rather than each and every copy of that picture) (ever) published in Time Magazine. (#$PicturesFromFn #$Terminator-TheMovie) is the collection of all stills from the movie, Terminator.")
(comment relationRange "A #$MetaRelation predicate that associates a given #$Relation 
with its set-theoretic range: the set of all and only things 
to which the relation relates something.  For example, the 
range of #$likesAsFriend is the set of sentient animals who 
are liked by some sentient animal or other, and the range of 
#$DifferenceFn is the set of all instances of #$ScalarInterval 
(since each scalar interval is the result of subtracting some 
scalar interval from some scalar interval).
(#$relationRange RELATION RANGE) means that the range of 
RELATION is RANGE.  More precisely (and following standard 
mathematical practice): if the #$relationalArity (q.v.) of 
RELATION is N (for N > 1), RANGE is the set of all the 
Nth-members of the N-length instances of #$List that are 
in the #$relationExtension (q.v.) of RELATION; if RELATION 
is unary it has no range, and #$relationRange is undefined 
for such a RELATION.  (Note that if FUNCTION is a 
#$VariableArityFunction (q.v.) there will be no particular 
length N shared by each of the lists in its extension.)
Though defined for polyadic relations generally, RANGE will 
normally be of particular interest only when RELATION is a 
function (see #$Function-Denotational), in which case RELATION 
relates each element of its #$relationDomain (q.v.) DOMAIN 
to exactly one element of RANGE, and each element of RANGE 
is related by RELATION to at least one element of DOMAIN.
See also #$RangeOfFunctionFn and #$inRangeOf.")
(comment Pianist "The collection of people who play the piano.")
(comment Ivory "The substance derived from elephant tusks.")
(comment BipolarDisorder "A type of #$Depression-PsychologicalCondition which involves cycles of depression and mania. Patients' mood swings are usually gradual.  Bipolar disorder encompasses a range of more specific disorders including Cyclothymia (which involves rapid mood cycling), Bipolar I and Bipolar II.")
(comment NetDecreasingFunction "#$NetDecreasingFunction is function which shows a net decrease in its value from 'start' to 'finish'.  Such functions may take on any intermediate values so long as the net change in value from 'start' to 'finish' is negative.  More formally, let x denote an element in the domain of some #$NetIncreasingFunction, F.  Thus F(x) denotes an element in the range of F.  Let x1 denote the lower bound on x.  Let x2 denote the upper bound on x.  F is an #$NetDecreasingFunction if and only if F(x1) > F(x2).  See #$NetIncreasingFunction.  See also #$MonotonicallyDecreasingFunction whose elements show an increase (technically, a non-decrease) for each successive range element.")
(disjointWith WaterTransportationDevice Spacecraft)
(comment BondIssuedByFn "#$BondIssuedByFn is a Cyc function, specifically a #$CollectionDenotingFunction. It is used to represent a collection of bonds issued by a particular company.  (#$BondIssuedByFn COMPANY) applied to a #$LegalCorporation COMPANY returns the collection of all #$Bonds issued by that corporation.")
(comment ArcheryGlove "The collection of gloves one often wears while using a bow and arrow.")
(comment MachineGun-Heavy "A large, mounted machine gun, usually used for air defense.")
(comment Dubnium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is a RadioactiveObject of #$Dubnium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment OnlineLottery "This is the spec of #$Lottery consisting of those lotteries which are operated

through a #$WorldWideWebSite.")
(comment InfectionTypeByOriginType "A collection of #$Collections. Instances of

#$InfectionTypeByOriginType are specs of #$Infection

of which instances share the common property of being

caused by the same type of event. See

#$InfectingEvent.")
(comment stateOfMatter "The predicate #$stateOfMatter is used to indicate the physical state of a tangible thing.  (#$stateOfMatter THING STATE) means that the #$PartiallyTangible THING is in the physical state STATE, where STATE is an instance of #$MatterTypeByPhysicalState.")
(comment exampleSentences "(#$exampleSentences TERM FORMULA) means that FORMULA is

considered to be a good example usage of TERM.  Note that FORMULA here refers to an instance of #$CycLFormula:  i.e., it can either be a #$CycLNonAtomicTerm or a #$CycLSentence.  This expression is intended to serve as the common generalization of #$examplePredSentences, which is used to cite sentences as example usages, and #$exampleNATs, which is used to cite non-atomic terms.")
(comment TolePainting "A kind of craft activity that typically involves decorative painting of useful household items, like furniture, watering cans, and so on.")
(comment Hypothalamus "The collection of all hypothalami.  An individual #$Hypothalamus is situated inferior to the #$Thalamus in the #$Diencephalon in the center of a #$Brain and borders on the #$ThirdVentricle.  The #$Hypothalamus controls the autonomic nervous system, emotions, hunger, thirst, sleep-wake cycles, body temperature, and secretions by the attached #$PituitaryGland.")
(comment ClosingBorders "The collection of events where one state formally restricts citizens from another state from entering their territory.")
(comment PsychrophilicBacterium "A collection of #$Bacterium that optimally grow at or below
(#$DegreeCelsius 15).  Bacteria of this type do not grow at
temperatures above (DegreeCelsius 20) or below (DegreeCelsius 0).
These #$ProkaryoticCells generally occur in the polar seas.")
(comment ArmoredFightingVehicle "A collection of military vehicles used for transport and protection of infantry.  These vehicles are equipped with armor and arms, enabling it to fight like a tank, but not against tanks.")
(comment HLPredicate "#$HLPredicate is the collection of all Cyc predicates which have special HL support.")
(comment CrimeMovie "An instance of #$MovieTypeByGenre; #$CrimeMovies
 are a type of film focusing on the lives of criminals. The
 stylistic approach ranges from grittily realistic portrayals
 of real-life criminal figures to the far-fetched evil doings
 of an imaginary arch-villain.  #$GangsterMovies are a popular spec
of this type of movie.  Criminal acts are almost always glorified in
 these movies.  However, this genre is distinguished from
#$MysteryMovie.")
(comment ScheduleFn-MovieType "#$ScheduleFn-MovieType takes as argument any #$SpecifiedMovieType and returns the collection of all instances of #$Schedule that include schedule information for showings of that type.  For example, (#$ScheduleFn-MovieType #$CitizenKane-TheMovie) returns the collection of #$Schedule listing showings of Citizen Kane.")
(comment RadioShow-IBT "A collection of objects; a subset of RadioMediaProduct. Every #$RadioShow-IBT is a #$SoundInformationBearingThing, an actual broadcast. Note that, e.g., 'The Rush Limbaugh Show' is not a RadioShow but a #$SpecifiedRadioSeriesType, a collection of RadioShows.")
(comment government "The predicate #$government identifies a government with the political entity which it has governing authority over.  (#$government GEOPOL GOV) means that the #$RegionalGovernment GOV is the government of the #$GeopoliticalEntity GEOPOL.  That is, GOV claims to be the government of GEOPOL, is recognized as such at least informally, and effectively functions as such (by administering the internal and external affairs of GEOPOL), whether or not GOV has formal diplomatic recognition.  Effectively functioning as a #$government includes having the power to settle disputes, collect revenue, and provide services.  Note that the US government is the #$government of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, but not that of #$Ohio-State.")
(comment ChangeOfConveyance "A collection of events in which the #$objectMoving transfers from one #$Conveyance to another; a subset of #$Translation-Complete and #$DirectedTranslation.  Every #$ChangeOfConveyance is also a subevent of some larger #$DirectedTranslation involving these two #$Conveyances.  Examples include: a traveller changing planes in an airport, oil being transferred from a pipeline to a tanker, and a railroad car unhooked from one train and hooked up to another.  A borderline negative example is a passenger on a train that is rolled onto a ferry for transport across water (because the passenger may not leave the train); the mode of conveyances changes so a #$ChangeOfConveyance does not necessarily occur.")
(comment NetworkPortNumber "#$NetworkPortNumber is the collection of #$NonNegativeIntegers from 0 to 65535.  Packets coming in to a computer are indexed by an instance of #$NetworkPortNumber, and the operating system on the computer directs the packet to the program assigned the same port number (see #$programCopyOnPort).  For instance,  packets sent to the Sendmail program on a computer contain information that they are bound for port 25, since this is the port on which Sendmail listens.")
(comment AtomFn "An instance of both #$CollectionDenotingFunction and #$ReifiableFunction.  When applied to an instance ELEMENT-TYPE of #$ElementStuffType, #$AtomFn returns the collection of all atoms (see #$Atom) of ELEMENT-TYPE.  Each instance of the collection (#$AtomFn ELEMENT-TYPE) is an atom with N protons in its atomic nucleus, where N is the #$atomicNumber (q.v.) of ELEMENT-TYPE.  For example, (#$AtomFn #$Carbon) is the collection of all carbon atoms, each of which has 6 protons in its nucleus. Additionally, each atom has a #$massNumberOfAtom (which need not be same for all atoms of the same #$ElementStuffType : see #$IsotopeFn).")
(comment Blubber "The fat of sea mammals and cetaceans, often used as fuel")
(disjointWith Time-Quantity Voltage)
(comment verticalClimb "(#$verticalClimb VEHICLE HEIGHT) indicates the highest vertical climb that VEHICLE can make. ")
(comment coGenlMts "(#$coGenlMts MT1 MT2) means that

MT1 and MT2 are extensionally equivalent, and should have the

same #$genlMts and specMts.")
(comment ShoppingAtPlaceFn "(#$ShoppingAtPlaceFn PLACE) returns the collection of all instances of #$Shopping which occur within the general boundaries of PLACE.")
(comment UnitOfVoltage "A specialization of #$UnitOfMeasure. Each instance of #$UnitOfVoltage is a function which returns an instance of #$Voltage (q.v.) when applied to a real number (see the collection #$SubLRealNumber) or a sequence of two real numbers. For instance, (#$Volt 500) is a voltage of 500 volts.")
(comment SelfLimitingCondition "These conditions will eventually clear up without additional treatments - a normally healthy body is able to deal with these conditions on its own.")
(comment ButtonDownCollar "The collection of shirt collars having buttonholes in their points, by which the collar is fastened to small buttons on the upper shirt front.  Especially characteristic of Oxford-style shirts.")
(disjointWith LightingDevice TransportationDevice)
(disjointWith GameEvent Patrolling)
(comment bridgeLoadCapacity "(#$bridgeLoadCapacity BRIDGE MLC) means that BRIDGE can support vehicles of the military load class MLC or lower.")
(comment computeRelevantSubcollection "(#$computeRelevantSubcollection COL)  means that it makes sense
to compute the relevant subcollection of COL.  Making a 
#$computeRelevantSubcollection assertion will cause
certain forward rules to fire and thereby the KB will might know
what SUBCOL is such that (#$relevantSubcollection COL SUBCOL) and
some of the ELEMENT such that (#$isaRelevantInstance ELEMENT COL).")
(comment TransdermalPatch "The collection of adhesive patches which contain a substance that can be absorbed through the skin.")
(comment unemploymentRateDuring "(#$unemploymentRateDuring REGION THING NR) means that NR is the average unemployment rate of the #$GeographicalRegion REGION during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING, where the unemployment rate of a region at a point in time is the quotient of the number of unemployed persons in the region and the region's labor force (that is, the sum of the number of employed and unemployed persons in the region).  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  For example, to express the fact that the United States' unemployment rate in 1996 was 5.4%, we can say (#$unemploymentRateDuring #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica (#$YearFn 1996) .054).")
(disjointWith CreditCounselingService FinancialCompany)
(comment StrategicNationalInterest "The attribute that characterizes goals which are crucial interests of nations.  #$StrategicNationalInterest has as its specializations #$ForeignPolicyGoal, #$NationalDefenseGoal, etc.")
(comment Dreadnought "A 20th century battleship")
(comment DNAStuff "The collection of all instances of DNA, the chemical compound composed of individual #$DNAMolecules.")
(comment CarrotPlant "Individual carrot plants")
(comment VQFFile "The set of #$ComputerSoundFiles that have been encoded using the format VQF.")
(disjointWith Cavity ConvexTangibleObject)
(comment WeakPasswordStorageEncryptionFault "#$WeakPasswordStorageEncryptionFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has a #$WeakPasswordStorageEncryptionFault if it
 uses a weak encryption algorithm to store passwords in a file.")
(comment amountOfDamageDone "#$BinaryPredicate used to relate a particular #$Situation to the

#$DegreeOfDamage done in that #$Situation.  The fact that a

#$DegreeOfDamage is cited almost always means that a particular source

and object of damage are presupposed; very often a particular kind of

damage is presupposed as well.")
(comment busInNetwork "(#$busInNetwork BUS NETWORK) means that BUS is a cable which is the main path, or bus, in NETWORK. Therefore, all computers in NETWORK must have a path to BUS.")
(comment Aegyptianella-Genus "A collection of all #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$Aegyptianella-Genus.  These ProkaryoticCells are obligate parasites of birds and are transmitted by arthropods.")
(comment predicateRuleEquivalent "(#$predicateRuleEquivalent PRED PRED-FORMULA RULE-FORMULA) states that for a rule macro predicate PRED, each use of the predicate which unifies with PRED-FORMULA will result in the addition to the system of a rule of the form RULE-FORMULA.  For example, one could implement #$genlInverse via : (#$predicateRuleEquivalent   #$genlInverse   (#$genlInverse ?SPEC-PRED ?GENL-PRED)   (#$implies      (?SPEC-PRED ?ARG1 ?ARG2)      (?GENL-PRED ?ARG2 ?ARG1))).")
(comment Cysteine "A collection of compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.  It is
easily oxidized into cystine, is sometimes found in urine, and has
limited detoxification properties.  Its abbreviations are Cys and C.")
(comment MechanizedCombatEngineeringUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of military combat units typically employing motorized tracked vehicles.")
(disjointWith FoodGroup TangibleStuffStateType)
(comment valueOfLiabilities "The sum of the value of all liabilities (loans, taxes due, payables, etc).")
(comment MillionBarrelsPerYear "A function which returns an element of #$FlowRate, that is, a volume per unit of time.  One million barrels per year -- (#$MillionBarrelsPerYear 1) or (#$BarrelsPerYear 1000000) -- is about 158.97 million #$Liters per year.")
(comment SleepingBag "The collection of sleeping bags. A sleeping bag is an insulated bag

which zips open to allow easier access and is intended to keep one

warm when sleeping outside.")
(comment OffensiveOperationsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units that deal with any dimension           of offensive operations.")
(comment HazyArea "A current condition where the air is full of haze and the visibility is moderate.")
(comment ProductionOfFn "(#$ProductionOfFn TYPE) returns the collection of all

#$Production-Generic Events whose #$outputsCreateds are instances of

TYPE.  When possible, Cyclists should use the more

 specific functions, #$ProductionOfArtifactFn and

  #$BiologicalProductionOfFn")
(comment Babying "This is the collection of behaviors in which something is treated in 

an exaggerated version of the way one treats babies. ")
(comment SlangDictionary "a collection of #$Dictionarys. Each element of #$SlangDictionary provides lexical information about words that are part of #$SlangSpeech.")
(comment TextByAgentFn "#$TextByAgentFn takes as argument any instance of #$IntelligentAgent and returns the collection of all texts authored by (or in the name of) that agent.  For example, (#$TextByAgentFn VaclavHavel) would return the collection of all texts written by the Czech president (such as `The Garden Party' and `Disturbing the Peace').  (#$TextByAgentFn #$WorldHealthOrganization) would return the collection of all texts authored by (or in the name of) that organization.")
(comment assertionAssertBy "(#$assertionAssertBy ASSERTION CYCLIST) means that ASSERTION was made by CYCLIST.  More precisely, it entails that the #$CycLAssertion ASSERTION was an #$infoTransferred in an #$AssertingAnAssertionToACycKB that was #$performedBy CYCLIST.")
(comment Token-Physical "A collection of small symbolic items, normally made of metal.  The collection includes medals (#$Medal-Physical) and coins (#$Coin-Currency) as well as privately issued #$Currency substitutes and similar objects.")
(comment TaxFormIBO "Forms which are designed and created in order to be to be filled out and returned to a a tax agency such as the IRS. When appropriately filled out, they are instances of #$TaxReturn.")
(comment salesRepresentatives "Entries are the people who are the sales representatives for this organization")
(comment constrainsArgs "(#$constrainsArgs INTER-ARG-PRED M N) means that the #$InterArgConstraintPredicate (q.v.) INTER-ARG-PRED can be used to place an inter-argument type or format constraint on the Nth argument of a relation to which it is applied, conditional upon the relation's corresponding Mth argument.")
(comment constrainsArg "A #$MetaRelation predicate for stating that a given meta-relation is used to put an argument-type or format constraint (see e.g. #$ArgConstraintPredicate) on a given argument-place of a relation. (#$constrainsArg METARELN N) means that METARELN is always used to put a constraint on a relation's Nth argument-place.  For example, (#$constrainsArg #$arg2Isa 2) holds.  A slight deviation from the above occurs when N is 0: we take (#$constrainsArg METARELN 0) to mean that METARELN is used to constrain _all_ of a relation's argument-places; see e.g. #$argsIsa and #$argsGenl.")
(comment rivetedTo "(#$rivetedTo ?obj1 ?obj2) means that ?obj1 is rigidly connected to ?obj2 by means of Rivets.")
(comment 125MMSmoothBoreCannon "A kind of #$Cannon

 common on Chinese Tanks.")
(comment Magic "Elements of #$Magic are ritualized #$Actions which are believed by some to effect change in human affairs or in the natural world by drawing on some mystical force outside ordinary human experience.  'Magic tricks' can be distinguished from #$Magic since sleights of hand rather than mystical forces are what enables them.  Historians and anthropologists have debated the manner and degree to which #$Magic and religion are similar.  See #$BlackMagic and #$WhiteMagic.")
(comment ChamberMusicComposition "The collection of all chamber music compositions - works for between 2 and about 8 instruments, each with its own part.")
(comment Sitophilia "The events in this collection include sexual behaviors involving the use of food items (e.g. vegetables).")
(disjointWith MaghrebCountry LevantCountry)
(comment Antiseptic "Drug product which is intended to kill germs.  Nearly always used topically.")
(comment Meditating "A collection of activities involving concentration and certain kinds of bodily positioning. In each instance of #$Meditating, the performer concentrates on something for spiritual or religious purposes, e.g. to achieve a higher degree of #$TranscendentEnlightenment.")
(comment MediumAccessControlSublayerProtocol "An instance of #$MediumAccessControlSublayerProtocol is a sublayer of an

instance of #$DataLinkLayerProtocol. A #$MediumAccessControlSublayerProtocol is used in 

broadcast networks to prevent collisions. Collisions occur when two or 

more machines attempt to send data at the same time.")
(comment grossNationalProduct "(#$grossNationalProduct GE THING MONEY) means that the instance of #$MonetaryValue MONEY is a measure of the value of all the goods and services produced by the citizens and resident corporations of the #$GeopoliticalEntity GE during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  These goods and services include those produced in foreign commercial activities.  A country would be a typical instance of GE.  THING will often be a time period -- for example, a calendar year such as (#$YearFn 1997) or a calendar quarter such as (#$QuarterFn 4 (#$YearFn 1997)); but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  See also #$grossDomesticProduct.")
(comment BoneStructure "A #$BoneStructure is a structure within a body composed of one or more #$Bone-BodyPart s or #$BoneSubPart s.")
(comment DatingAnObject "The collection of all events of estimating the age of an object. Examples include carbon dating of fossils, counting the rings in the trunk of a tree to find out how old it is, or estimating the age of an #$ArtObject by the materials and techniques used to create it.")
(comment Minister-Diplomatic "A collection of government officials who are entrusted with the management of their country's affairs abroad.  Ministers accredited to heads of state have a diplomatic rank below ambassadors and above charges d'affaires")
(comment Landsailor-Device "Collection of three-wheeled land vehicles powered mainly by lift or push from wind passing over or into their sails.")
(comment TranscriptOfCWFn "#$TranscriptOfCWFn takes as argument any instance of #$ConceptualWork and returns the collection of transcripts [#$TranscriptOfSpeech-CWIS] of that work.  For example,(#$TranscriptOfCWTypeFn #$2001-ASpaceOdyssey-TheMovie) returns the collection of transcripts of the movie (#$Movie-CW) 2001-A Space Odyssey.  To represent the collection of transcripts of a particular type of #$ConceptualWork (for example, #$TVShow-CW) use #$TranscriptOfCWTypeFn.  Use #$TranscriptOfEventFn and #$TranscriptOfEventTypeFn for transcripts of specific events or classes of event.")
(comment Rice-SingleGrain "Individual rice kernels, which are the harvested fruits of the rice plant.")
(comment Plutonium "An instance of #$ElementStuffTypeByNumberOfProtons and a specialization of #$UnalloyedMetal.  Each instance of #$Plutonium is a piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of plutonium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment hasSocialPower "'(#$hasSocialPower AGENT DEGREE)' means that AGENT has the degree of social power DEGREE in the society to which AGENT belongs.")
(comment (VersusFn coRewriteOf rewriteOf) "#$coRewriteOf is useful for equations which do not yield a normal form and thus do not have a natural canonical representative for each equivalence class.")
(comment AirspaceRegion "A region of space above a portion of the Earth's surface, inclusive

at least of the lower layers of the atmosphere and possibly extending

as far as near Earth orbit, and such that military and civilian

flights through it are regulated by a central administrative authority

or authorities.  Typically, this authority will be some

suborganization of the government of the terrestrial region which

serves to demarcate the #$AirspaceRegion in question, and if more than

one authority has immediate responsibility for air traffic in the same

#$AirspaceRegion, they will be related suborganizations of the same

parent organization.  There are some notable exceptions, however: eg,

the #$SouthernIraqiNoFlyZone.")
(comment AccessNumber "A specialization of #$PhoneNumber. Each instance of #$AccessNumber is a string that a user with #$Internet connections uses to connect to his/her #$InternetServiceProvider.")
(comment FormalGrammarSpecification "The collection of all formal grammar texts, each being an actual text (not necesarily a conceptual work) containing a formal specification of the set of 'grammatically valid' relational structures (often #$CharacterStrings) allowed by the formal specification.  The grammar is formal in that there is, in theory at least, a precise test (whether or not it is decidable or feasible) for compliance of a given structure with the specification.  See also #$FormalGrammar-CW.")
(comment ProkaryoticGeneExpression "The collection of gene expression events in which prokaryotic cells, or bacteria, provide the genetic information.")
(comment Crater-Lunar "A circular depression in the surrounding terrain of the Earth's moon.")
(comment CompletionOfMembership "The collection of events in which a member of some organization completes its term in an acceptable way (e.g., by finishing a fixed term or by voluntary retirement) and thereafter is no longer a current member of that organization.  See also #$EmeritusMember.")
(comment QuestionTemplate "This template category covers all syntactic questions.")
(comment cWIllocutionaryForce "(#$cWIllocutionaryForce CONCEPTUAL_WORK IF) is used to specify the illocutionary force of a #$PropositionalConceptualWork -- that is, how the #$creatorOfCW wants the apprehender of an instantiation of the work to apprehend and respond to the work.   For example, a news article may have #$IllocutionaryForce: #$Inform while an op-ed piece may have #$IllocutionaryForce: #$Threat.")
(comment transferInSubEvent "The Cyc predicate #$transferInSubEvent indicates the final stage of a particular #$GeneralizedTransfer in which the #$transferredThing reaches the destination.  For example, (#$transferInSubEvent COMM LISTENING) means that LISTENING is the final stage (see #$lastSubEvents) of the #$CommunicationAct-Single COMM.")
(comment ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Agent "#$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Agent is the subset of #$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-General whose instances are defined by the agent responsible for the attack. Examples include #$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Military, #$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Corporate, and #$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Personal.")
(comment pathogenWithRespectTo "(#$pathogenWithRespectTo PATHTYPE ORGTYPE) means that if a
sufficient concentration of organisms of PATHTYPE are present in an
instance of ORGTYPE those instances of PATHTYPE will normally be the
cause of an infectious disease.")
(comment GameRulesFn "(#$GameRulesFn GAME) denotes the collection of sets of rules for GAME.  For example, (#$GameRulesFn #$Bingo) returns the collection of all rule-sets for Bingo.")
(disjointWith UnitOfAngularAcceleration UnitOfSpeed)
(disjointWith Dinghy RowingShell)
(comment FlyAgaricMushroom "The collection of mushrooms of the species Amanita muscaria, which contain the hallucinogenic toxin muscimole. Used in Europe as fly poison, hence the name.")
(comment Livestock "This is the collection of animals, excluding pets, that are owned and

used for economic purposes. For example, livestock may provide labor, or may be used for their hair, milk, or meat.")
(comment Trajector-Underspecified "This is a very broad classification, encompassing all those concepts that can be seen, in a cognitive-linguistic sense, to be trajectors relative to a given background or landmark in  an event or a relation. A #$Trajector-Underspecified is the foregrounded element of an underspecified relation that relates in some way to a #$Landmark-Underspecified. When one says that 'the cat is in the cradle', an underspecified 'in' relation (#$in-UnderspecifiedContainer) connects the trajector, #$Cat, to the landmark #$Cradle (which happens to be a container). If I kick the cradle across the floor, the #$Cradle now becomes the trajector of this action (and the room becomes the landmark).")
(comment AircraftEngine "the collection of all #$Engines designed

   for use in #$Airplanes")
(comment OrganicFood "The collection of foods and beverages derived from animals or plants grown or raised without chemical hormones, fertilizers, herbicides, or pesticides, and processed only with like ingredients through mechanical and cooking processes.  Instances of #$OrganicFood (also called \"natural food\") have not had any chemically extracted additives added to them during processing and that not been treated with ionizing radiation.")
(comment deciles "(#$deciles BINARYPREDICATE TYPE DECILE_STRUCTURE) means that the set of instances of TYPE for which BINARYPREDICATE applies can be broken down into the #$NTupleInterval DECILE_STRUCTURE.")
(comment mtSpindle "(#$mtSpindle MICROTHEORY_SPINDLE HEAD_MT SPINDLE_COLLECTOR_MT) means that  MICROTHEORY_SPINDLE (an instance of #$MicrotheorySpindle) has HEAD_MT as its common #$genlMt and SPINDLE_COLLECTOR_MT as its common specMt.")
(comment Actinobacteria-Class "A collection of #$Bacterium forming a #$BiologicalClass in the #$MoneraKingdom that includes the #$BiologicalOrders such as #$Actinomycetales-Order.")
(comment MotionPictureAwardCategory "A collection of attributes that represent categories in which awards are given for achievement in motion pictures.  See #$AcademyAwardCategory for those that pertain to the Academy Awards.")
(comment AmmunitionShip "The collection of military ships intended for use in ammunition re-supply.")
(comment CosecantFn "(#$CosecantFn ANGLE) yields the cosecant of that angle.")
(comment PrescriptionDrug "A specialization of #$DrugProduct. The collection of drugs that require a doctor's permission before obtaining or consuming them. See also #$DrugPrescription, #$prescribedDrug, #$prescriptionFilled and #$prescriptionFor.")
(comment BlowableParticle "Particles which can be blown around in the air by wind but will settle out quickly otherwise.")
(comment FillingAPrescription-Retail "The collection of all events in which a #$DrugPrescription is filled in a #$Pharmacy which is either a #$RetailStore or a #$Department of a #$RetailStore; a subset of #$FillingAPrescription.")
(comment OrgTypeByEchelonGeoAndBOSFn "This function enables us to refer to instances of the
#$ModernMilitaryOrganization partition #$MilitaryOrgTypeByEchelonGeoAndBOS.
More specifically, (#$OrgTypeByGeoAndBOSFn ECHELON GEO-AGENT BOS) returns the
collection of all #$ModernMilitaryOrganizations that have #$echelonOfUnit ECHELON and that are#$subOrganizations of the instance of BOS that has GEO-AGENT as the
#$sovereignAllegianceOfOrg.  Thus, e.g., (#$OrgTypeByEchelonGeoAndBOSFn
#$Platoon-UnitDesignation #$France #$Army-BranchOfService) returns the collection of all French army units.")
(comment instantiationOfGIS "(#$instantiationOfGIS CGIBT GIS) means that CGIBT is an instance of #$ChemicalGeneticIBT which instantiates GIS, an instance of #$GeneticInformationStructure.  An instance of #$ChemicalObject not only instantiates the structure of the whole object (see #$completeGISOfChem) but also is said to instantiate (using this predicate) any #$subGIS of that #$GeneticInformationStructure.")
(disjointWith ApplyingAForce StrictlyMentalEvent)
(comment Airport-Physical "A specialization of both #$FixedStructure and #$TransportFacility.  Each instance of #$Airport-Physical is a facility which includes at least one runway where airplanes can take off and land.  Instances of #$Airport-Physical may also have terminals and an air control tower, in addition to having a runway.  See also the related collection #$AirportOrganization.")
(comment Nectar "Sweet liquid produced in the nectar glands (nectaries) of a flower.  Its sweetening agent is sucrose.")
(comment RemovingSomething-Translational "A specialization of both #$RemovingSomething and #$CausingAnotherObjectsTranslationalMotion (qq.v.).  During a #$RemovingSomething-Translational event, the #$objectRemoved is moved out of the object or configuration to which it belonged prior to the removal event.  The #$objectRemoved is not destroyed by the removal event.  Examples include unwrapping a present, undressing, digging up a root, and removing an appendix.")
(comment BiologicalWeaponsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units organized, equipped, and trained for           operations involving handling, employment, and/or containment of           biological weapons.")
(comment actionApplicabilityConditions "(#$actionApplicabilityConditions GENERICPURPOSEFULACTION CYCFORMULA) asserts that an instance of the
GENERICPURPOSEFULACTION is reasonable to plan to do within a particular #$Situation only if CYCFORMULA is known to be
true (in that situation). This is a constraint from the planning literature. Note that applicability conditions differ 
from preconditions - we can't try to plan to achive an applicability condition.")
(comment Rumor-CW "#$Rumor-CW is the collection of all            instances of #$PropositionalConceptualWork which            contain information with little or no justification,            and which are often designed to mislead others and            to be propagated with the intent to surreptitiously            achieve an objective.  (Cf. #$Rumor-IBT, which is the            collection of written or uttered rumors, and            #$RumorPropagation, the collection of instances of            transmissions of instances of #$Rumor-CW.)")
(comment TsunamiLandfall "The collection of all events in which a #$Tsunami makes contact with the shore.")
(disjointWith ColorImage MonochromeImage)
(comment SimplifyForward "A property of reformulator rules which says that in this rule,
the simpler argument comes after the verbose argument.")
(disjointWith CollegeSportsTeam HighSchoolSportsTeam)
(comment quantityChangeFunction "(#$quantityChangeFunction TIME THING QUANTITY-SLOT FUNCTION-TYPE) means that during TIME the value of QUANTITY-SLOT for successive instantaneous time slices of THING varies as instances of FUNCTION-TYPE vary.  Thus to say that 'during 1998 Fred had a net weight gain' we could say (#$quantityChangeFunction (#$YearFn 1998) Fred #$massOfObject #$NetIncreasingFunction).  This would mean that the value of #$massOfObject of Fred shows a net increase over 1998.  To say that the #$speedOfFlow is irregular throughout DribblingEvent01 one would write (#$quantityChangeFunction DribblingEvent01 DribblingEvent01 #$speedOfFlow #$IrregularFunction).  The thickness of the previously mentioned instantaneous time slices are determined by the temporal granule size of the #$Microtheory in which the statement is made.  Thus flow rate over time for a dribbling faucet would be smoother for large temporal grained contexts.  The slot in arg2 is assumed to be functional in arg3, unless e.g. #$FunctionToArg is used appropriately.  See also #$quantityInfluenceFunction for representing factors which influence but do not necessarily result in some particular kind of change in a quantity.  See #$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates for other important quantity change related predicates.")
(comment Density "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity.  Each instance of #$Density is a measure of an aspect of a tangible object, namely, its mass per volume.  Instances of #$Density include #$DenseAsOil, #$GaseousDensity, and #$SolidDensity.  See also the predicate #$densityOfObject, which relates an object to its density.")
(comment ReconnaissanceDevice "The collection of all devices, such as radar, sonar and night vision goggles, which aid in the gathering of information.")
(comment Resort-Attraction "A collection of objects, a spec of both #$TouristAttraction and #$Place.  Each instance of #$Resort-Attraction is a place which draws visitors, typically vacationers who stay there for one or more nights.")
(comment SlicingSomething "To cut as if with a knife; the process of cutting something with a slicing tool, using a slicing motion; cutting which breaks one object into two pieces.")
(comment northernRegion "(#$northernRegion SUPER SUB) means that SUB is the `northern region' of SUPER.  What counts as the `northern region' is contextually determined. Some of the factors  influencing the determination may be local geography, cultural identity, and political  considerations.")
(comment InformationGatheredFromFn "(#$InformationGatheredFromFn INFOGATHERING) takes

 any instance of #$InformationGathering and returns

 the PIT that is the information gathered from that gathering.")
(comment VG-NerveAgent "A kind of #$NerveAgent which is extremely lethal when inhaled.")
(disjointWith CourtAndNetGame BallAndStickGame)
(comment Troche "The colleciton of all troches.  A troche is a tablet or lozenge which dissolves slowly in the mouth.  It is typically used to relieve throat discomfort.")
(comment countriesVisitedOnTour "(#$countriesVisitedOnTour TOUR COUNTRY) means that COUNTRY is an
#$IndependentCountry which TOUR is scheduled to visit on its
itinerary.")
(comment productionQuotaDuring "(#$productionQuotaDuring PT PRODUCT-TYPE THING AMOUNT) means that the #$NonNegativeScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the production quota of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE for the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  (Of course, the existence of production quotas is the exception rather than the rule.)  PT will most commonly be a #$Country.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  For example, to express the fact that Algeria's 1997 crude oil production quota was 750,000 barrels per day, we can say (#$productionQuotaDuring #$Algeria #$Petroleum-CrudeOil (#$YearFn 1997) (#$BarrelsPerDay 750000)).")
(comment 5-TheDigit "The numeral 5 of the Arabic Number system.  This is '5' as a #$Character-Abstract rather than the physical #$WrittenCharacter or the abstract mathematical #$Number-General.")
(comment (SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn LoadingAProjectileWeapon toLocation MissileLauncher) "The collection of all events in which

  a #$MissileLauncher is loaded.")
(comment RPG-PlayerCharacter "The collection of characters in a #$RolePlayingGame that are 'acted' by game participants, and not by the GamesMaster. Contrasts with #$RPG-NonPlayerCharacter. The sets #$RPG-NonPlayerCharacter and #$RPG-PlayerCharacter are not disjoint however when a human player's #$RPG-PlayerCharacter is 'killed' in the course of the game, the player assumes control of a #$RPG-NonPlayerCharacter as a gaming convenience game.")
(comment OptionTransactionAgreement "Each instance is an #$OwnershipAgreement giving one or more parties an optional right to take some action related to ownership, such as a ChangeInUserRights or a MoneyTransfer.  While there may be certain conditions which are required to exist before the action will be allowed, in no case will the possessor of the right be forced to take the action.  The option to perform the action may expire on a certain date, expire upon the occurence of a described event, or else may be perpetual.")
(comment PhosphodiesterBond "The collection of covalent bonds between an instance of #$PhosphateRadical and another complex #$ChemicalObject. The phosphate radical or a chemical object containing it is bonded via an instance of #$PhosphodiesterBond to the second chemical object, an instance of #$MolecularComponent.")
(comment SeedGerminationEvent "The process of seed germination after the embryo begins to grow.")
(comment InformalSpeech "Word senses of words or phrases which are considered informal. One usually uses informal language when speaking to acquaintances or to people younger than oneself.")
(comment BreastEnhancement "The collection of all surgical events in which the appearance of a woman's breasts is improved.           Includes breast implants and mastoplexy but excludes reconstructive breast surgery done after a mastectomy.  For that type of #$Surgery see #$ReconstructiveBreastSurgery.")
(comment Anaeroplasma-Genus "A collection of #$Bacterium forming a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom.")
(comment arrangementPredicates "This predicate relates an arrangement of like objects 

to a spatial relationship that holds of or among its members.  

(#$arrangementPredicates GROUP PRED) means that either (i) PRED 

is a unary instance of #$SpatialPredicate that holds of all 

#$groupMembers of GROUP or (ii) PRED is an N-ary (for N > 1) 

spatial predicate that \"connects\" all of the members of 

GROUP; that is, for each MEMBER of GROUP, PRED holds among 

MEMBER (in any one of PRED's argument-positions) and some N-1 

members of GROUP.  For example, many arrangements of like 

objects have members that are all #$spatiallyContinuous, and 

proximally-grouped arrangments (such as a grove of trees) are 

likely to be connected by #$near or #$nextToLikeObjects.  

See also #$arrangementNearestPredicates")
(comment ModernDancePerformance "ModernDancePerformance is the collection of instances of DancePerformance such that (PerformingFn ModernDancePerformance) returns a collection of instances of ModernDancing.")
(disjointWith SensoryMotorNerve SensoryNerve)
(comment nearestCommonSpecPreds "(#$nearestCommonSpecPreds PRED-1 PRED-2 NEAR-PRED) relates predicates PRED-1 and PRED-2 to the nearest unsubsumed predicates NEAR-PRED which are spec predicates of both PRED-1 and PRED-2. #$nearestCommonSpecPreds is #$notAssertible, since it must always be recomputed from the current state of the #$genlPreds hierarchy.  For comparison, see also #$nearestGenlPreds and #$nearestCommonGenlPreds.")
(comment CompactDiscCover "The collection of all first pages of printed material that is included with a #$CompactDisc-Generic and usually found inside the disk's plastic cover. A #$CompactDiscCover is typically made up of a #$Photograph or artwork on which the name of the artist and the title of the CD is printed. An entire booklet with extensive liner notes or instructions does not count as a #$CompactDiscCover, only its visible (first) page.")
(comment HavingTheChills "The script an orgnism or body part is bodilyInvolved in when it has chills.")
(comment FluidWaveBreaking "The event in which a wave breaks under the force of gravity, losing its smooth curving surface and becoming disorganized.")
(comment PostPartumDepression "A type of depression which can occur after a woman gives birth.")
(disjointWith Trawler CargoShip)
(comment HydrogenPeroxideMolecule "A collection of #$HydrogenPeroxideMolecules. Each instance is one piece of the chemical compound H2O2.  This #$ChemicalObject is a highly reactive oxidizing agent and is produced in considerable quantities in the metabolic activities of cells.  (#$LiquidFn #$HydrogenPeroxideMolecule) is used in a diluted state as a disinfectant, or in a concentrated form as rocket fuel.")
(comment targetOfShooting "(#$targetOfShooting SHOOTING TARGET) means that TARGET is the #$target and the #$objectActedOn in SHOOTING. That is, TARGET is the thing being successfully shot at. Note that the shooting need not be an instance of #$ConflictEvent. TARGET could be just a target, as in those used in target practice.")
(disjointWith Gun-Portable MachineGun-Heavy)
(comment Rutherfordium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is a RadioactiveObject of #$Rutherfordium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment rolePlayerMaintainsCondition "(#$rolePlayerMaintainsCondition ROLE COND) means that if an
actor that plays ROLE in a #$FunctionalSystem, for the duration of the
time that the actor plays ROLE the actor's actions will be directed
toward making sure that COND remains true for the extent of the time
that ROLE is played.  At a minimum, this means that the default
#$purposeOfEvent of any action the actor does while playing ROLE will
be that COND holds for the duration of the role-playing.  Also, if the
actor is an #$IntelligentAgent,the default #$purposeInEvent that the
actor has for any action he, she, or it performs will be that COND
holds for the duration of the role-playing.")
(comment ToleranceFn "(#$ToleranceFn QUANTITY FRACTION) denotes a quantity which is an approximation of QUANTITY constructed by decreasing its mininum and increasing its maximum by (#$TimesFn QUANTITY FRACTION).  For example, (#$ToleranceFn (#$Mile 100) 0.01) denotes (#$Mile 99 101).")
(comment CycUniversalDate "A collection of integers which represent #$CalendarDays expressed as an integer of the form YYYYMMDD.  For example, 19690720 was the day of the Apollo 11 moon landing, July 20 1969, expressed as a #$CycUniversalDate.")
(comment GastroIntestinalInfection "A collection of infections. Instances of #$GastroIntestinalInfection are infections acquired by ingestion of pathogen. Do not confuse with food poisoning caused by bacterial toxins.")
(comment bestMapping "#$bestMapping is used to identify which mapping is the best #$AnalogyMapping of all those associated with a given #$AnalogyMatch.")
(comment Star "A self-luminous gaseous astronomical object, including the sun.")
(comment Muzzle-GunPart "The collection of open, discharging ends of #$Guns.")
(comment Thalamus "The collection of all thalami.  The #$Thalamus forms the major part of a #$Diencephalon in the center of a #$Brain.  All nerve signals entering the #$Cerebrum, whether sensory or from another part of the #$Brain, are relayed by the #$Thalamus.  The #$Thalamus is almost split in two parts, which are connected by the 'intermediate mass', but it is normally considered a single structure instead of a pair of structures.")
(comment UnderminingStatus "The collection of events where one state undermines another states status in some region; possibly globally.")
(comment PsychotrophicBacterium "A collection of #$Bacterium that have the ability to grow at
exceedingly low temperatures, between (#$DegreeCelsius 0 5).  The
optimum growth temperature for bacteria of this type is about (#$DegreeCelsius
15) with an upper growth limit of (#$IntervalMaxFn (#$DegreeCelsius
20)).")
(comment agreeingServiceProvider "The agent that agrees to provide an ongoing service in an #$AgreementForOngoingService. Examples include ISPs, utility companies, insurance companies, lawyers.")
(disjointWith TrainEngine ArmoredFightingVehicle)
(comment SBHLTimePredicate "#$SBHLTimePredicate is the collection of all Cyc predicates which have special SBHL-time module support.")
(comment FormulaArgSetFn "(#$FormulaArgSetFn RELATION-EXPRESSION) denotes

a set of the arguments of the given #$CycLFormula RELATION-EXPRESSION.  For example, (#$FormulaArgSetFn (#$genls #$Dog #$Animal)) denotes (#$TheSet #$Dog #$Animal).  See also #$FormulaArgFn and #$FormulaArityFn.")
(comment AllowsAnonymousLogin "A program on a computer has this attribute if it allows users to login anonymously.  This is common on computers running #$Ftpd-TheProgram (see the more specialized #$VulnerableBecauseAllowsAnonymousFTP). It can also be the case if, for example, the computer is a #$WindowsMachine which permits so-called \"null sessions\" (see the more specialized #$AllowsNullSessions).")
(comment HumanAccessibleIBO "A specialization of both #$HumanAccessibleIBT and #$InformationBearingObject.   Each instance of #$HumanAccessibleIBO is an object (i.e. an instance of #$PartiallyTangible) that can be interpreted by a #$Person to yield information. Examples include street signs, product wrappings and roulette wheels. #$InformationBearingObjects requiring a device to convert them into human understandable form (such as DVDs) are not included. Most instances of #$HumanAccessibleIBO are also instances of #$StillImageSource. Objects such as Braille book copies, however, are not (since they are not interpreted visually). Objects that are instances of #$HumanAccessibleIBT, #$StillImageSource and #$Artifact fall into the collection defined as the intersection of these three -- #$HardcopyInformationBearingObject.")
(comment ACEInhibitorWithDiuretic "Elements are drug formulations which include both an #$ACEInhibitor and a #$Diuretic.")
(comment DarkComedyMovie "A spec of #$ComedyMovie.  This genre usually has a wicked sense of humor -- often dark, cynical and edgy -- that makes fun of such supposedly serious subjects as death, illness, murder, or war. Black comedy uses humor as a defense mechanism, a way to explore and cope with the modern world's absurd, unbearable complexities. Nothing is sacred from attack in black comedy, and all taboos are welcome, in fact, are encouraged by the style.")
(comment Container-PressureBarrier "A container which when closed does not necessarily have the same ambient pressure as that which surrounds it.")
(comment (RightObjectOfPairFn (PartTypeFn TenthThoracicVertebra VertebralTransverseProcess)) "")
(comment politicalCommissar "(#$politicalCommissar ORG AGENT) means that AGENT has the
responsibility of enforcing the edicts of a political party and 'party
discipline' within the membership of ORG.")
(comment Dance-Party "Each #$Dance-Party is a social event involving all the normal actions at a party, but also necessarily involving the playing of music and dancing of the attendees to at least some of this music.")
(comment programCopyOnPort "(#$programCopyOnPort PROGRAM PORT) means that instance of #$ComputerProgramCopy PROGRAM receives packets addressed to instance of #$NetworkPortNumber PORT.")
(comment ChemicalBonding "The collection of events in which two separate chemical objects form a #$ChemicalBond.")
(comment EvaluatableRelation "A specialization of #$Relation.  Each instance of #$EvaluatableRelation is
a function or predicate for which there is some piece of system code that 
can be invoked to evaluate (i.e. to determine the denotation or truth-value
of) a closed expression built from that function or predicate (i.e. a closed 
expression that has the constant that denotes that function or predicate in 
its initial or \"0th\" argument-place).  An evaluation of this sort is carried 
out, for example, when the system is queried using an #$evaluate (q.v.) 
sentence.  As one might expect, most evaluatable relations are mathematical 
or syntactic in nature; for numbers, sets, lists, and strings are the sorts 
of things that are related in various ways that can be calculated 
algorithmically.  Examples include #$PlusFn, #$greaterThan, #$JoinListsFn, 
and #$substring.  In the case of a function that is evaluatable (see 
#$EvaluatableFunction), the practical result of evaluating the relevant 
expression is another _term_ -- one that has the same denotatum as the 
original expression, but that is syntactically simpler and constitutes a 
more straightforward way of referring to that denotatum.  For example, 
the term `(#$PlusFn (#$Inch 3) (#$Inch 1))', when evaluated, results in 
the term `(#$Inch 4)'.  So if a query using the open sentence
`(#$evaluate ?X (#$PlusFn (#$Inch 3) (#$Inch 1)))' is asked, the answer 
(or \"binding\" for the variable `?X') returned will be the term `(#$Inch 4)'.  
Evaluating a sentence built from (a constant that denotes) an 
#$EvaluatablePredicate, on the other hand, yields a _truth-value_.  For 
example, the sentence `(#$greaterThan (#$Inch 3) (#$Inch 1))' evaluates 
to (and so if used to ask a query will return the answer) `#$True'.  The 
predicate #$evaluationDefn (q.v.) is used to specify the name of the piece 
of system code used to evaluate expressions formed with a given 
evaluatable relation.")
(disjointWith Distance Time-Quantity)
(disjointWith CordlikeObject Concrete)
(comment networkAttackedBy "(#$networkAttackedBy Network1 Attack1) means that Network is

an object attacked as a consequence of the occurrence of Attack1.")
(comment RightStrandFn "A specialized form of #$SideOneFn and #$SideTwoFn that applies
only to instances of #$DNAMolecule and designates either one of the
symmetric strands constituting such molecules.")
(comment BankingIndustry "The collection of all banking industries:  each member of this collection            is a #$Group of #$Organizations  (an instance of #$Industry-Localized)            each #$groupMembers of which is in the business of providing banking services.")
(comment AntiArmorWeapon "The collection of #$Weapons that are designed to be used against #$ArmoredVehicles.")
(comment TermMacroFunction "Instances of #$TermMacroFunction are functions that have, implicit in their definition, the schema for a class of   terms. A use of one of these functions is in fact shorthand  for a term fitting this schema. For example, #$SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromTypeFn is a #$TermMacroFunction and its implicit schema would be (#$CollectionSubsetFn :ARG1    (#$TheSetOf ?X  (#$thereExists ?Y   (#$and  (#$isa ?Y :ARG3)  (:ARG2 ?Y ?X))))).   Therefore, (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromTypeFn #$Dog #$likesAsFriend #$Cyclist)  is shorthand for the term  (#$CollectionSubsetFn Dog                (#$TheSetOf ?X   (#$thereExists ?Y   (#$and  (#$isa ?Y #$Cyclist)                             (#$likesAsFriend ?Y ?X))))), namely, the set of             dogs liked by a cyclist.")
(comment AncientRome-LouvreCollection "The collection of Roman object of art exposed in the Louvre.")
(comment Glucose "Glucose, also called \"dextrose\", is an organic sweetening agent used in soft drinks and other prepared foods.  Chemical formula: C6-H12-O6. This is a dextrorotatory form.  The levorotatory form is called #$Fructose or \"levulose\".")
(comment interArgGenls "(#$interArgGenls PRED INDEPENDENT-ARG INDEPENDENT-COL DEPENDENT-ARG DEPENDENT-COL) means that, when a subset of INDEPENDENT-COL appears as argument # INDEPENDENT-ARG to PRED, argument # DEPENDENT-ARG in that assertion is constrained to be a subset of DEPENDENT-COL.")
(comment typesSimilarWRTPartType "(#$typesSimilarWRTPartType TYPE1 TYPE2 PART-TYPE) means that instances of TYPE1 and TYPE2 will be related to PART-TYPE via the relationship #$similarWRTPartType.")
(comment nonExistent-Specified "(#$nonExistent-Specified TERM) states the assumption that TERM has been explicitly stated to not exist.  This predicate is primarily used for reasoning in hypothetical contexts about the ramifications of some existing term not actually existing.  See also #$nonExistent and #$nonExistentSpecification")
(disjointWith Watercraft Water)
(comment patientTreated "(#$patientTreated TREATMENT PATIENT) means that PATIENT, an instance of #$Animal, is an instance of #$MedicalPatient during TREATMENT (an instance of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent) and is treated by that TREATMENT. ")
(comment Explanation "A collection of individual #$PropositionalInformationThings, each of which gives an explanation of something.  Note that individual explanations and the things which they explain may be related by using membership in collections created using the Cyc function #$ExplanationFn.")
(comment Vigilante "#$Vigilantes are people who take law into their own hands, by seeking out, and often punishing, perceived wrong-doers without the full force of the law on their side. #$Vigilantes are often perceived as #$Criminals in their own right.")
(comment storiesInBridge "(#$storiesInBridge BRIDGE NUM) means that BRIDGE is composed of NUM storiess.")
(comment assertionStrength "(#$assertionStrength ASSERTION STRENGTH) states that argumentation has determined that the arguments supporting ASSERTION indicate that STRENGTH is the justification strength of ASSERTION.  In other words, STRENGTH indicates how strongly the truth of ASSERTION is justified. The three possible justification strengths are #$Default-JustificationStrength,   #$Monotonic-JustificationStrength and #$Unknown-JustificationStrength. See also #$assertionTruth, #$assertionMt.")
(comment AntiEmetic "Drugs which prevent or reduce nausea and vomitting.")
(disjointWith CollectionAgency FinancialCompany)
(comment SpoiledFn "(#$SpoiledFn FOOD) relates collections of #$FreshFoodOrDrink to the  corresponding collections of #$SpoiledFood. It denotes the collection  of spoiled objects which used to be instances of the fresh food  collection FOOD.  Thus a rotten orange is an instance of (#$SpoiledFn  (#$FruitFn #$OrangeTree)). Note: Spoiled food is inedible, and food is edible, so anything in the denotation of #$SpoiledFn is no longer an instance of #$Food. See #$SpoiledFood, #$FreshFoodOrDrink, #$Spoiling.")
(comment PotatoPlant "The plant that gives us the Potato, the crop that every country exports and none imports.")
(comment CursorGUIComponent "Members of #$CursorGUIComponent are standard components of a #$GraphicalUserInterfaceProgram. Their position on a #$ComputerMonitor-VideoKind can be changed by skillful manipulation of a #$ComputerMouse. A #$CursorGUIComponent can be used to perform various kind of operations specified by the particular  #$GraphicalUserInterfaceProgram it is a component of.")
(comment MineralOre "A specialization of #$LandStuff.  Each instance of #$MineralOre is a piece of substance from which some instance(s) of #$Mineral (q.v.) can be extracted.  Specializations of #$MineralOre include #$IronOre, #$BauxiteOre, and #$CopperOre.")
(comment VulnerableToFileOverwriteSymlinkAttack "A vulnerability of some instances of #$Computer.  A computer
 is #$VulnerableToFileOverwriteSymlinkAttack if it is running a program that allows 
 a user to create symlinks to and then overwrite arbitrary files on the computer, including
 files for which the user does not have authorized access.")
(comment Haemobartonella-Genus "The collection of all 34BiologicalSpecies classified under the #$ Haemobartonella-Genus.  These are #$CoccusBacterium or #$BacillusBacterium that are parasitic to many vertebrate species, excluding humans.")
(comment Hovercraft "The collection of vehicles which ride above the surface of the water on a cushion of air, usually provided by fans.")
(comment GlutamicAcid "A collection of compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.  These
compounds also serve as a neurotransmitter in all areas of the central
nervous system.  Its abbreviations are Glu and E.")
(comment RugbyCleats-Shoe "The collection of #$Cleats-Shoes 

intended for use in playing rugby.")
(comment Tera "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10^12")
(comment TextualMaterialAboutFn "#$TextualMaterialAboutFn takes as argument any thing and returns the collection of all written texts (i.e. objects) about that thing.  For example, (#$TextualMaterialAboutFn #$JohnKennedy) returns the collection of all written texts on the subject of John F. Kennedy, and (#$TextualMaterialAboutFn #$Dog) returns the collection of all written texts on the subject of dogs. To refer to the conceptual texts (as opposed to physical objects) use #$TextAboutFn.")
(comment LightEngineeringUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of lightly armed instances of #$EngineeringUnit-MilitarySpecialty.")
(disjointWith Cheese Drink)
(comment Lien "A collection of #$TemporaryUserRightsAgreements. Each #$Lien is a charge against property making it security for the payment of a debt, judgment, mortgage, or taxes.  A #$Lien may be entered into voluntarily (as when taking out a loan, or one may be imposed by a government body, such as the #$InternalRevenueService.")
(comment colonyOf "(#$colonyOf COLONY ENTITY) means that the geographical region COLONY is a colony of ENTITY, which could be a country or a city-state.  Typically a group of people from ENTITY have distantly settled in COLONY but remain under the political jurisdiction of ENTITY.")
(comment Norethindrone "A #$Steroid which is similar to #$Progesterone. It can be used in #$BirthControlPills.")
(comment SleepingPad "The collection of sleeping pads. A sleeping pad

is a flat cushion-like object generally intended to be placed under

a sleeping bag.")
(comment RadioCommunicationsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile deals with radio           communications.")
(comment Community "#$Community is the collection of communities, which are to be distinguished from

#$Neighborhoods, the latter being geographical regions. Elements of #$Community

are groups of people. Many are distinguished by their inhabiting a particular #$Neighborhood, but what ties others together might be communication in cyberspace or some other less tangible factor. ")
(comment Semanticist "A #$Linguist specializing in #$Semantics")
(comment AttachmentEvent "The collection of events in which one object becomes attached to another.  This may involve fasteners of some sort in which case one should use the specialization #$ConnectingTogether or processes in which no fasteners are used, e.g. magnets moving together, two objects rusting together, chemical bonding.")
(comment MasochisticSexualBehavior "This is the collection of sexual behaviors in which the subject is

subjected to pain or other forms of subjugation, where these are a source

of arousal.")
(comment RhymingDictionary "a collection of #$Dictionarys.  Each element of #$RhymingDictionary provides information about words that rhyme with each other. For each word listed in a #$RhymingDictionary, the #$RhymingDictionary lists other words that rhyme with it.")
(comment QuarterEagleCoin-US "The collection of all US quarter eagle gold coins.  The face value is $2.50.")
(comment PartiallyCloudCoveredArea "An instance of #$DegreeOfCloudiness and a specialization of #$OutdoorLocation. Each instance is an #$OutdoorLocation having some cloud cover but not enough to completely block out all direct sunlight.  Direct sunlight comes and goes as clouds occluding the sun pass.")
(disjointWith Spreadsheet Database-Physical)
(comment boltedTo "(#$boltedTo OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 is #$fastenedTo OBJ2 such that at least one #$Bolt is a fastener.  The #$Bolt is passes through holes in OBJ1 and OBJ2.  The #$Bolt is #$screwedIn to either OBJ2 or a nut (#$Nut-TheDevice).")
(comment 105MMRifledBoreCannon "A kind of #$Cannon

 common on #$Tank-Vehicles.")
(comment TernaryRelation "The collection of all fixed-arity relations of arity 3 (see #$arity).  The most notable specializations of #$TernaryRelation are #$TernaryPredicate and #$TernaryFunction (qq.v.).")
(comment COASpecificationMicrotheory "A #$COASpecificationMicrotheory is a plan for achieving a particular military combat goal. The plan contains assertions about what actions are to be performed by what friendly units, as well as assertions about the anticipated actions of the enemy units.")
(comment Fetishism "A spec of ParaphilicSexualBehavior in which sexuoerotic arousal and facilitation or attainment of orgasm are responsive to, and contingent on a particular talisman or fetish object, substance, or part of the body belonging to the partner. Common objects of fetishistic behavior include feet, latex or rubber, and manekins.")
(disjointWith WesternEuropeanCountry MaghrebCountry)
(comment Anticonvulsant "Drugs that reduce or prevent convulsions.")
(comment adverbSemTrans "This predicate expresses the relationship between an adverb, a word sense, a subcategorization frame, and a CycL expression used to denote the adverb.")
(comment Villa "Large many-roomed residences set in rural settings, often with extensive gardens, fountains, and outdoor #$Sculptures.")
(comment TranscendentEnlightenment "A subclass of #$SacredPractice. Each element of TranscendentEnlightenment is a situation in which a person gains and maintains a transcendental understanding of the nature of existence, etc.")
(comment Armor "#$Armor is generically something used to protect an
object from damage. There are many kinds of armor and they protect the
objects they are attached to to various degrees and from various
deleterious effects.  Armor can be both intrinsic in an object (as
with #$Tank-Vehicle or #$Beetle) or added on to an object (as with
#$ReactiveArmor modules.)")
(comment grossDomesticProduct "(#$grossDomesticProduct GE THING MONEY) means that the instance of #$MonetaryValue MONEY is a measure of the value of the #$GeopoliticalEntity GE's total domestic production of goods and services during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  A country would be a typical instance of GE.  THING will often be a time period -- for example, a calendar year such as (#$YearFn 1997) or a calendar quarter such as (#$QuarterFn 4 (#$YearFn 1997)); but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  MONEY will sometimes be specified using the function #$USDollarFn, which returns a #$UnitOfMoney denominated in US dollars of a particular year; for example, to express the fact that the gross domestic product of the United Arab Emirates for 1997 was $35,930,000,000 in 1990 U.S. dollars, we can say (#$grossDomesticProduct #$UnitedArabEmirates (#$YearFn 1997) ((#$USDollarFn 1990) 3.593e+10)).  See also #$grossDomesticProduct-Nominal and #$grossNationalProduct.")
(comment Creatine "A substance present in muscle tissue and blood that facilitates the reconversion of adenosine diphosphate (ADP) into adenosine triphosphate (ATP) during muscle contraction. Some athletes take supplements of creatine monohydrate or creatine pyruvate to increase their creatine levels, which may provide them with greater energy and help them build muscles.")
(comment Envoy-Diplomatic "A collection of diplomatic officials, each of which is empowered to represent his or her government to another government. Envoys are appointed and used as needed for temporary assignments. Envoys are accredited to heads of state, but they rank below ambassadors.")
(comment PedalBoat "A small boat with a paddle wheel that is turned by pedaling.  Also called a 'paddle boat'.  For large paddle wheel boats, see #$RiverBoat.")
(comment agentRetaining "(#$agentRetaining SIT AGENT) means that in SIT, user rights to some object are retained by AGENT. See also #$objectRetained and #$RetainingUserRights.")
(comment Sorghum-TheGrain "Individual sorghum grains, which are the fruits of the sorghum plant.")
(comment TrafficSourceFn "(TrafficSourceFn THING PLACE TEMPTHING) is the measure of traffic directed at THING from PLACE during TEMPTHING averaged over the duration of TEMPTHING.  This function assumes PLACE is the source and not an intermediary for the traffic.")
(comment AnnexingTerritory "The collection of events in which an agent adds some geographical region to the territory it controls.  The annexed territory may have previously belonged to another agent, or it may have been unclaimed.  The territory annexed is the #$objectOfPossessionTransfer in the event, and the annexing agent is the #$toPossessor.  See also #$CedingTerritory, #$ExpropriatingSomething, and #$AppropriatingSomething.")
(comment Internship "The collection of typically unpaid job positions 
that are temporary and are sought for the experience of working
 in a particular field.")
(comment TemporaryJobPosition "The collection of #$JobPositions which are temporary, which last for a short duration of time.")
(comment TrigonometricFunction "A collection of the mathematical trigonometric functions.  Examples: #$SineFn, #$CosineFn, #$ArcTangentFn.")
(comment IntermediateTranscriptionTranslationPhase "The collection of events that might be described as an intermediate phase between transcription and translation.  This depicts the series of events in which RNA receive additional processing before leaving the cell nucleus.")
(disjointWith QualifyingTrial ChampionshipCompetition)
(disjointWith CommunicationDevice Tool)
(comment aminoAcidSequenceOfType "(#$aminoAcidSequenceOfType PROTEINTYPE LIST) means that

instances of the class of #$ProteinMolecule PROTEINTYPE all exhibit the

characteristic amino-acid sequence LIST, expressed as a list of amino

acid types.")
(comment Encoding "The collection of events where some data in an #$InformationBearingThing are tranformed from a more 'raw' or natural format to a more compressed/complex format.")
(comment hasDegreeInField "(#$hasDegreeInField PERSON DEGREETYPE FIELD) means that person has an #$educationalDegrees DEGREETYPE in the #$FieldOfStudy FIELD.")
(comment WordNetKnowledgeBase "The collection of all versions of WordNet, including the now defunct WordNet-1995Version and #$WordNet-1997Version.")
(comment in-ImmersedPartly "(#$in-ImmersedPartly OBJ FLUID) means that a portion of OBJ is immersed in FLUID, but OBJ is not completely surrounded by FLUID.")
(comment CulturedGrowthFn "This function can be used to denote the set of events in which an agent grows some kind of living material in an artificial medium; for example, growth of some bacteria in a petri dish.")
(comment ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Military "#$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Military is a subset of #$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Agent.  It is the collection of all electronic attacks perpetrated on instances of #$ComputationalSystem by a military agent.")
(disjointWith UnitOfMonetaryRate UnitOfSpeed)
(disjointWith PedalBoat Dinghy)
(comment VenomSecretionEvent "The collection of all events in which a #$VenomousAnimal secretes #$Venom.")
(comment HandGrenade "A specialization of #$ConventionalWeapon.  Each instance of #$HandGrenade is a grenade (i.e., a small explosive device) designed to be thrown by its user, as opposed to being projected by a grenade launcher.  Cf. #$RifleGrenade.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseHasSameUsernameAndPassword "#$VulnerableBecauseHasSameUsernameAndPassword is an attribute that applies to some instances of #$Computer as well as accounts on such systems.  An
 account accessible from a computer is #$VulnerableBecauseHasSameUsernameAndPassword if the #$Password-Computer for that account is the same as the #$Username for that account.")
(disjointWith DomesticPet Livestock)
(comment OrientedLocation-Underspecified "The collection of locations, tangible or otherwise, which are
typically conceptualized by human beings for purposes of common-sense
reasoning as possessing some sense of 'vertical orientation'. Language is
permeated with metaphors based on such oriented states/abstract-locations,
as in 'He is high', 'I'm down', 'his spirits rose', 'mine fell', 'Ishtar
nose-dived', etc.  These states are thus very important for many inference
tasks that must reason about affective states.  Orientation metaphors are
amongst the most pervasive in any language, e.g.: Up = More = Good =
Desirable, Down = Less = Bad = Undesirable.")
(comment rationalApproximation "(#$rationalApproximation IRRATIONAL RATIONAL) means that RATIONAL can be used as a reasonable rational approximation for IRRATIONAL, which is an instance of #$IrrationalNumber.   For example:  (#$rationalApproximation #$Pi-Number 3.1415927)")
(comment Cryonics "The collection of #$MedicalTreatmentEvents that use cold for therapeutic purposes, such as reducing a #$LevelOfPain with ice.")
(comment JumboMortgage "The collection of #$NonconformingMortgages which are #$JumboLoans.")
(comment ModifyingAFile "A collection of actions done by computers on files. In each instance of #$ModifyingAFile, a computer reads a file, modifies it, creates a new file with the new contents in a different location, and then deletes the original file.  It is possible that no information from the original file survives in the modified copy.")
(comment FitnessModel "The collection of #$FashionModels whose job is to model skimpy apparel, exposing their muscular bodies")
(comment toConfiguration "(#$toConfiguration EV CONF) means that CONF, an instance of

#$Configuration, is a state of affairs that results from EV, an instance of

#$ConfiguringEvent.")
(comment DecileStructure "The collection of all mathematical tuples representing deciles.  Instances have 10 values,  each being a ScalarInterval representing one tenth of the values of the domain of the associated predicate applied to all the members of the associated #$Collection.")
(comment (CollectionIntersection2Fn Helicopter MilitaryAircraft) "the collection of all 

helicopters used for military purposes")
(comment FormalMetaGrammar "The collection of all formal meta-grammars (such as #$BackusNaurForm), each being a textual formal specification of #$CharacterStrings that are themselves #$FormalGrammarSpecifications in forms allowed by the said specification in meta-grammar .  The meta-grammar specifies a class of grammars, each of which specifies its own class of complying structures.  Both the meta-grammar and the resulting grammars are formal in that there are, in theory at least, precise tests (whether or not decidable or feasible) for compliance of a given structure with its specification.  Most #$FormalMetaGrammars are #$StringGrammars defining classes of #$StringGrammars, but they could also specify #$GraphGrammars and other kinds.   #$FormalMetaGrammars like that for DTDs in the #$XML-MarkupLanguage 

are used to specify document formats which are themselves #$FormalGrammarSpecifications of actual document structure.")
(comment Actinomycetales-Order "A collection of #$Bacterium forming a #$BiologicalOrder in the #$MoneraKingdom that contains the #$BiologicalFamilys Actinomycetaceae-Family.")
(comment Oscar-Statuette "A collection of objects.  Each instance of #$Oscar-Statuette is a small gold-colored statuette, based on the design of Cedric Gibbons and used by the #$AcademyOfMotionPictureArtsAndSciences to symbolize the awards it gives for achievement in motion pictures.")
(comment AmphibiousCommandShip "A collection. Amphibious command military watercraft, which are intended to provide command and control in major amphibious operations.")
(comment RNAPolymerase "The collection of #$Enzymes that catalyze the polymerization reaction that produces #$RNAMolecules.")
(comment SecantFn "(#$SecantFn ANGLE) yields the secant of that angle.")
(comment DeletingFromSystemOfDevicesFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction used to denote the collection of           #$PurposefulActions in which some instance of a type of #$PhysicalDevice           is deleted from or taken out of some instance of #$SystemOfDevices.             (#$DeletingFromSystemOfDevicesFn SYS DEVTYPE)           denotes the subcollection of #$Actions in which some           instance of DEVTYPE is taken out of           from SYS.  What kind of #$Actions this subcollection           contains depends of course on what the type of #$SystemOfDevices SYS is.             If, for instance, SYS consists of instances of #$RadioTransmitter and           #$RadioReceiver, then the #$Actions that consist in deleting from SYS may involve           no more than destroying some instance of #$RadioTransmitter or taking it           out of range of all the instances of #$RadioReceiver in SYS.            If SYS is an instance of #$TelephoneSystem, then the #$Actions that consist           in deleting from SYS may be as simple as unplugging the telephone           or as complicated as whatever a telephone company does when it cuts           off someone's telephone service.")
(comment OralDrug "A specialization of #$DrugProduct.  Each instance of #$OralDrug is a drug which are intended to be adminstered orally.  Examples include cough syrup, throat lozenges, and birth control pills.")
(disjointWith DistributionEvent StrictlyMentalEvent)
(comment structureCorrespondences "(#$structureCorrespondences ?Src ?Src-Mt ?Tgt ?Tgt-Mt ?Src-Corr ?Tgt-Corr)

returns, via multiple successive bindings of the variables ?Src-Corr and 

?Tgt-Corr, corresponding entities in the analogy between ?Src and ?Tgt.")
(disjointWith Conveyance Airport-Physical)
(comment Mural "The collection of all mural paintings [#$Painting-ArtForm] as a representational art form.")
(comment Discretion "The quality of being discreet or circumspect. Having good judgement.")
(comment patient-Generic "(#$patient-Generic EVENT PATIENT) means that PATIENT plays a patient role in EVENT. PATIENT need not exist prior to EVENT (use #$objectActedOn for PATIENTS that pre-exist EVENT). Note that this is a very general predicate; in almost all representation cases you should be using a specPred of #$patient-GenericDirect. Example: in a #$GivingSomething event where Sally gives Fred a book, the book is playing a #$patient-GenericDirect role (namely #$objectOfPossessionTransfer), Sally is playing a #$doneBy role (namely #$fromPossessor and therefore #$deliberateActors) and Fred is playing a #$patient-GenericIndirect role (namely #$toPossessor).")
(comment CombustionProcess "A collection of events, and a specialization of #$EnergyConversionProcess and #$DecompositionProcess. Each #$CombustionProcess  is an event in which rapid oxidation is taking place.  These always have heat as an output and often involve emission of light as well (typically, #$Flames).  The #$objectActedOn in a #$CombustionProcess is at least partly consumed.  See also #$Flammability.")
(comment CavalryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units that are capable of covering           large distances in a wide variety of terrains, and to quickly engage           and disengage with the enemy, often in advance of the main force.           Historically and etymologically, 'cavalry' implies mounted units           however, in modern times the term has come to refer almost           exclusively to certain kinds of motorized armored unit.")
(comment definingMt "(#$definingMt TERM MT) states that TERM only begins to have semantic meaning in microtheory MT. In microtheories in which MT is not  accessible, TERM is #$undefined. Additionally,  (#$termDependsOn TERM MT).")
(comment Switch-Network "A computer that accepts, routes, and forwards elements of Packet-Network.")
(disjointWith Rumor-CW ComputerProgram-CW)
(comment objectsInRelativeMotion "(#$objectsInRelativeMotion EVT OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 move relative to each other during EVT. In other words, the vector from one object to the other is not a constant throughout EVT.")
(comment MaterialStrengthType "A collection of collections. Each instance of #$MaterialStrengthType is a specific collection of attributes used in determining the strength of a material. Examples: #$Hardness, #$Malleability, #$Ductility, #$Elasticity.")
(comment SupportHelicopter "The collection of #$Helicopters intended to provide support
for military combat.")
(comment Phobia "A collection of #$PsychologicalAilments characterized by a persistent, abnormal, and irrational fear of a specific thing or situation that compels one to avoid it, despite       the awareness and reassurance that it is not dangerous.")
(comment SwimStrokeType "The collection of those subsets of #$Swimming-Surface that represent standardized strokes such as those used in swimming competitions. Instances include #$ButterflySwimStroke and #$Breaststroke.")
(comment ChoppingSomething "The process of cutting something with a chopping tool, using a chopping motion.")
(disjointWith PeriodicalSeries BookGeneric-CW)
(disjointWith PhysicalTransformationEvent TransportationEvent)
(comment SetExtentFn "(#$SetExtentFn SETORCOL) returns a set of the form (#$TheSet ...) which is the currently represented extent of SETORCOL.")
(comment RodShapedObject "A #$ThreeDimensionalShapeType and a specialization of #$Cylinder.  Each instance of #$RodShapedObject is a solid cylinder whose height is much greater than the radius of its base.  Examples include spatially localized objects, such reactor rods, logs, and bacilli, as well as some abstract cylinders.")
(comment VK-NerveAgent "A kind of #$NerveAgent which is extremely lethal when inhaled.")
(disjointWith SportsStick Racket-SportsEquipment)
(comment Lozenge "the collection of all lozenges.  A Lozenge is a medicated candy which dissolves in the mouth.")
(comment exhibitedInMuseum "(#$exhibitedInMuseum MUSEUM ARTIFACT) means that ARTIFACT is on

exhibit in MUSEUM in the context of the assertion.")
(comment DrivingAGolfBall "A subcollection of #$HittingAGolfBall. In every instance of #$DrivingAGolfBall, a #$GolfBall is hit from a tee, usually with a #$Driver-GolfClub. Instances can occur either on a golf course or a driving range.")
(comment importQuotaDuring "(#$importQuotaDuring REGION PRODUCT-TYPE THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the import quota of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE for the #$GeographicalRegion REGION during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  (Of course, the existence of import quotas is the exception rather than the rule.)  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  In the case of automobile imports, for example, AMOUNT might be an #$Integer indicating the number of cars that may be imported.  In the case of oil imports, AMOUNT might be a #$Volume (a number of barrels) indicating the total quantity of oil REGION is allowed to import.  Alternatively, AMOUNT might be a #$Rate, characterizing the average rate of import, under the quota, of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE by REGION during the temporal extent of THING.  Oil imports, for example, might be expressed in terms of so many million barrels per day.")
(comment 6-TheDigit "The numeral 6 of the Arabic Number system.  This is '6' as a #$Character-Abstract rather than the physical #$WrittenCharacter or the abstract mathematical #$Number-General.")
(comment natFunction "(#$natFunction NAT FUNCTION) states that FUNCTION is the function used in the non-atomic term NAT.  For example,  (#$natFunction (#$JuvenileFn #$Dog) #$JuvenileFn).  More precisely, (#$termOfUnit NAT (FUNCTION ...)) implies  (#$natFunction NAT FUNCTION).")
(comment Lilangeni-Swaziland "The unit of currency used in Swaziland-1986")
(disjointWith ProjectilePropelling LoadingAProjectileWeapon)
(comment supplyRate "(#$supplyRate PT COL RATE) means that the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT is supplied with instances of the #$Collection COL at the #$Rate RATE.  Like the predicate #$suppliedWith (q.v.), #$supplyRate is very general.  PT might, for example, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion; and the range of possible supplies is similarly broad.")
(comment LoanAgreement "A collection of #$TemporaryUserRightsAgreements. In each #$Agreement, one party will give something of value (usually money) to a second party, and the second party will pay the money back, often paying interest as well.  Among other options, the parties can agree that there will be repeating #$Paying events, with the same amount paid each time; or they may agree that all the money will be paid back all at once.")
(comment PhosphodiesterBonding "A specialization of #$ChemicalBonding. Instances of #$PhosphodiesterBonding are events that establish an instance of

#$CovalentBond between an instance of #$PhosphateRadical and another complex chemical object. The phosphate radical, or a chemical object containing it, is bonded via an instance of #$PhosphodiesterBond to the second chemical object.")
(comment Algae "One of many different aquatic photosynthetic organisms, often one-celled but sometimes filamentous or parenchymatous, both prokaryotic and eukaryotic.")
(comment fastenedTo "(#$fastenedTo OBJ1 OBJ2) means that there is an assembly consisting of OBJ1, OBJ2, and one or more fasteners configured so that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are rigidly connected.  The fasteners in question may be (among other things) screws, nails, rivets, nuts and bolts, or staples.  The fasteners penetrate all the way through at least one of the objects (either OBJ1 or OBJ2) and may or may not go all the way through the other object.  Examples: a utility shelf screwed into the wall; paper notices stapled to a bulletin board; shingles nailed to the roof of a house.")
(comment BabyTalk "This attribute applies to word senses of words or phrases typically used when talking to babies or young children.")
(comment CycInferenceDescriptorPredicate "The collection of predicates which describe the internal inference mechanisms of the Cyc theorem prover.")
(comment BreastEnlargement "The collection of #$Events in which a procedure is undertaken to enlarge the          #$Breasts of an #$AdultFemalePerson.")
(comment Asteroplasma-Genus "A collection of #$Bacterium forming a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom.")
(comment TapDancePerformance "TapDancePerformance is the collection of instances of DancePerformance such that (PerformingFn TapDancePerformance) returns a collection of instances of TapDancing.")
(comment Cough-AilmentCondition "The collection of instances of the condition in which one suffers from regular instances of the collection #$Coughing.")
(disjointWith SensoryMotorNerve MotorNerve)
(comment JokeAboutFn "#$JokeAboutFn takes as an argument any instance of #$Thing and returns the           collection of all jokes about that thing.  For example, (#$JokeAboutFn #$Chicken)           would return the collection of all funny propositions about chickens.  See also #$Prank.")
(comment BacterialPneumonia "A bacterial infection of the lungs.  Viral pneumonia also exists but is not treated in this unit.  Causes coughing, sputum and difficulty in breathing.")
(comment SeasonalAffectiveDisorder "A type of depression in which depressive symptoms tend to worsen during the winter
months. Phototherapy is often useful for patients suffering from this disorder.")
(comment MilitaryAdministrativeRegion "The collection of all instances of #$CountrySubsidiary that are administered by some sub-organization (see the predicate #$subOrganizations) of a country's military, for purposes of military organization and control.  Generally, but not always, an instance of #$MilitaryAdministrativeRegion will be a part (see the predicate #$geographicalSubRegions) of the country whose military administers it.

The borders of a country's #$MilitaryAdministrativeRegions may or may

not parallel the borders of such provinces and subsidiaries as may be

administered by civilian governmental authority: there is, in most

cases, a correlation between this congruence of borders and the extent

to which military and civil authorities are intermingled within the

country.")
(comment Schedule "special kinds of Plans which deal with WHEN things are supposed to happen. For the hard-copy record of a schedule, see #$ScheduleDocument.")
(comment atomicComposition "(#$atomicComposition CHEM ELEM N) means that molecules of CHEM contain N atoms of ELEM.  For instance, (#$atomicComposition #$Water #$Hydrogen 2) means that every molecule of water contains two atoms of hydrogen.  See #$completeAtomicComposition-List to express the chemical formula for a  #$ChemicalSubstanceType.")
(comment issuedOnExchange "(#$issuedOnExchange SEC EXCH) relates a security SEC to the #$FinancialExchange EXCH on which it was originally issued and is thereafter traded.")
(disjointWith MensSportsTeam CoedSportsTeam)
(comment SwimmingGoggles "The Collection of all #$SwimmingGoggles, protective eyegear worn while swimming.")
(comment Howitzer-M101 "A type of howitzer.")
(comment UltimateFightingEvent "The collection of all staged events in which two #$competingAgents fight in a caged, octogonal ring until one surrenders or loses consciousness, or the referee calls the fight. The only rules are no eye-gouging and no biting. Illegal in eight states as of August 1997.")
(comment Indium "A piece (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of indium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment CycUniversalSecond "A collection of integers which represent #$CalendarSeconds within their #$CalendarDay expressed as an integer of the form HHMMSS. For example, 130759 represents 1:07:59 pm expressed as a #$CycUniversalSecond.")
(comment League-Distance "A unit of distance whose length is the same as 3 #$Miles.")
(comment VicePresident-CorporateOfficer "A collection of people.  An instance of #$VicePresident-CorporateOfficer is a member of the management of a company, designated as 'Vice President' on the official records of the company.  Most companies have one or more instances of #$VicePresident-CorporateOfficer; a small company usually has only one, whereas a large National Bank may have hundreds of Vice Presidents.  The primary Vice President (possibly a #$SeniorVicePresident-Title) is often empowered to direct the company in case of the death or incapacity of the #$President-CorporateOfficer.")
(comment Salmonellosis "A collection of infections. Instances of #$Salmonellosis are infectious diseases due to pathogen belonging to the Salmonelleae genus. They can be manifested as food poisoning or as typhoid or paratyphoid fever, symptoms related are more serious in immunocompromised victims.")
(comment Resurrection "The collection of events in which a dead human being

is raised from the dead. Examples from #$Christianity include the #$Resurrection

of #$JesusOfNazareth after the #$CrucifixionOfJesus, or the resurrection of 

Lazarus by #$JesusOfNazareth in the new testament. Currently, this concept is

defined relative to the religious (i.e., #$Christianity) interpretation of

#$Resurrection, and should probably not be used in non-religious contexts 

(e.g., a doctor resurrecting a patient who 'died' twenty-seconds ago). However,

fictional/mythological contexts that are in part informed by religious thought

(e.g., #$Vampire, zombies, etc.) could conceivably employ this event.")
(comment examplePredSentences "(#$examplePredSentences PRED EXPRESSION) means that the

#$CycLFormula EXPRESSION represents a good example usage of the

#$Predicate PRED.")
(comment AsynchronousTransferModeEvent "The collection of 

events in which data is transmitted over a #$ComputerNetwork using the Asynchronous Transfer Mode technology.  Such data transfers are

characterized by the following: 

(i) a single logical channel between sending and receiving points, (ii) data transferred in fixed-length, relatively small, packets.")
(comment Diencephalon "The collection of all diencephalons.  An individual #$Diencephalon is a central part of a #$Brain which connects the #$BrainStem to the #$Cerebrum.  A #$Diencephalon is comprised of a #$Thalamus, #$Hypothalamus, and #$Epithalamus.  The #$PituitaryGland is attached to the #$Hypothalamus, and thus the #$Diencephalon.")
(comment SupportingRevolutionaries "The collection of events where one state supports or sponsors revolutionary activities in a foreign state.")
(comment ArmoredPersonnelCarrier "A collection of armored military vehicles used for the transport and protection of infantry.  Unlike #$ArmoredFightingVehicles, #$ArmoredPersonnelCarriers have no armament other than #$SmallArm-Weapons.")
(comment LocalMagazineSeries "The collection of #$MagazineSeries that

deal with local matters. Austin, for example, has several magazines that

deal with goings-on in Austin.")
(comment Diltiazem "A #$PharmaceuticalType which is a subcategory of #$CalciumChannelBlocker.  Diltiazem is used in treating heart disease.")
(disjointWith PreservingFood CourseDuringAMeal)
(comment FrontPortal "The front portal region of a tangible object considered as a container")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn EleventhRib) HeadOfBone) "")
(comment Ball-FormalDance "Each instance of #$Ball-FormalDance is a fancy, special-occasion dance party to which the guests wear formal clothes.")
(disjointWith Navy Army-BranchOfService)
(comment AttackByComputerOperationType "This is the collection of all types of electronic attacks.  These are divided

    according to the program that initiates the attack, or

    according to the kind of damage done, etc.")
(disjointWith FixedStructure TransportationDevice)
(comment MoleculeFn "A function that takes as an argument an instance CHEM-TYPE of #$ChemicalSubstanceType and returns the collection of all molecules of CHEM-TYPE.  For example, (#$MoleculeFn #$Water) is the collection of all water molecules.")
(comment BambooWood "The woody substance derived from bamboo plants.")
(comment ArgIsaPredicate "The collection of #$ArgTypePredicates (q.v.) that specify argument-types directly (by referencing certain collections) and impose constraints that require a thing's being an instance of a collection thus specified.  More precisely, each instance of #$ArgIsaPredicate PRED takes a #$Relation RELN as its first argument (or \"arg1\"), and has at least one other argument-place (say the Mth) for specifying an argument-type for one of RELN's argument-places (say the Nth).  (The value of N might be fixed or might be given by yet another of PRED's arguments.)  Suppose M=2 and N=1.  PRED then takes a #$Collection as its second argument, and a closed atomic sentence (or \"GAF\") of the form (PRED RELN COL ..) puts an \"#$isa\" constraint on RELN's first argument-place that is based on COL.  If PRED is a \"single-argument\" constraint predicate, the GAF entails that a closed formula of the form (RELN ARG1 ..) is semantically well-formed only if ARG1 is an instance of (i.e. #$isa) COL.  If PRED is an \"inter-argument\" constraint predicate, the GAF expresses a slightly more complicated, conditional #$isa constraint on a pair of RELN's argument-places (see #$InterArgIsaPredicate).")
(comment ProjectileShellTypeByLoadingMechanism "The three instances of #$ProjectileShellTypeByLoadingMechanism are  collections of #$ProjectileShellAssembly according to how the parts are  loaded into the gun.  For example, #$ProjectileShell-SemiFixedLoading  requires that the shell and the metal case containing the primer and charge  be loaded separately.  #$ProjectileShell-FixedLoading, on the other hand,  requires no separate loading, e.g., in the case of #$BulletAssembly.")
(disjointWith Time-Quantity AngularDistance)
(comment regularFrequencyOfActionType "(#$regularFrequencyOfActionType EVENTTYPE ACTORTYPE ROLE FREQ) means that instances ACTOR of ACTORTYPE  typically play role ROLE in events of type EVENTTYPE with frequency FREQ. For instance, (#$regularFrequencyOfActionType #$ShavingBody #$AdultMalePerson #$performedBy #$Daily) means that men who shave regularly, typically shave daily. Thus this predicate is useful for ACTORTYPEs of which it cannot be said that typical instances regularly play role ROLE in events of type EVENTTYPE. For cases where that *can* be said, use the more specific predicate #$frequencyOfActionType.")
(comment covers-Generic "(#$covers-Generic COVER THING) means that COVER physically covers THING.  This is the most

general predicate referring to covering.  More specific predicates

include #$covers-Sheetlike, #$covers-Paintlike, #$covers-Hairlike, and so forth.")
(comment PenetratingAComputerNetwork "A specialization of #$Cracking-CompromisingSecurity. Each instance of this collection is an event in which unauthorized access to a #$ComputerNetwork occurs. See also #$Hacker, #$AttackByComputerOperationActionType.")
(disjointWith SpacePlatform-Manned TransportationDevice-Unmanned)
(comment targetOfContention "(#$targetOfContention CONFLICT THING) means that THING is what the opponents in the #$ConflictEvent CONFLICT are contending to control.  One of the #$opponentsInConflict may already control it, or neither may.")
(comment HeadMedialMultiWordForConstantPred "The specialization MultiWordForConstantPred that maps from head-medial lexical items to Cyc constnts.")
(comment Erosion "This is the collection of events in which some part of the earth's surface erodes due to the effects of wind or water.")
(comment AncientGreece-LouvreCollection "The collection of ancient Greek object of art exposed in the Louvre.")
(comment PharmaceuticalCompany "Instances are companies which develop and produce drugs and other pharmaceutical products, such as medical devices. ")
(disjointWith LandTransportationDevice TallShip)
(comment Commuting "A specialization of #$TransportingPeople and #$Translation-RoundTrip.  Each instance of #$Commuting are the events in which one or more persons travels from home to work via a transporter (#$Automobile, #$Train-TransportationDevice, etc.) and back home again.")
(disjointWith Sunset MidnightSun)
(comment TimePointAtDistanceAfterStartOf "(#$TimePointAtDistanceAfterStartOf INT EVT) is the  #$TimePoint that is exactly INT after the start of  EVT.  For example, (#$TimePointAtDistanceAfterStartOf     (#$YearsDuration 2.5) #$WorldWarII)  is the #$TimePoint that is exactly two and a half years  into #$WorldWarII.")
(comment Superhero "The class of fictitious people who perform superhuman feats of strength, bravery or daring. Often such heroes possess special, non-human powers, such as x-ray vision or powers of unassisted flight. In some cases no such superpowers are necessary, as in the case of #$Batman. In their general conception, #$Superheroes are conceived of as #$Vigilante crime-fighters")
(comment AntiDiarrheal "Drugs which relieve diarrhea.")
(disjointWith Lingerie SwimWear)
(comment DisplayingMuseumHoldings "A #$DisplayingSomething in which the things displayed are museum holdings.")
(comment legalSystem "The predicate #$legalSystem indicates what kinds of legal system a #$GeopoliticalEntity has. (#$legalSystem REGION LEGSYSTEM) means that the #$GeopoliticalEntity REGION has as part of its legal structure the instance LEGSYSTEM of #$LegalSystemType.")
(comment CabbagePlant "Cabbage: a vegetable shaped like a round head of lettuce, eaten either raw in a salad or cooked.")
(comment SeparatingAMixture "A specialization of #$Separation-Complete.  In each instance of #$SeparatingAMixture, an instance of #$Mixture is separated into two or more of its constituents (see the predicate #$constituents).")
(comment ElevatedPrivilegeFault "#$ElevatedPrivilegeFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has an #$ElevatedPrivilegeFault when it allows a (authorized or unauthorized) user to attain privileges distinct from the user's ordinary privileges.  See also the important specializations, #$ElevatedPrivilegeFault-Root and #$ElevatedPrivilegeFault-User.")
(comment BudgetaryInformation "The collection of all pieces of information that have as their content the financial budget of some agent (organization or person).")
(comment shortTimeIntervalBefore "(shortTimeIntervalBefore INTER TEMP-OBJ) means that the instance of #$TimeInterval
INTER is the short time interval before the instance of #$TemporalThing TEMP-OBJ.")
(comment Haemobartonella-Genus "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom.  It is currently unclassified in term of a #$BiologicalOrder and #$BiologicalFamily.")
(comment Lyric-WordsToSong "A collection of #$PoeticWorks. Each instance of #$Lyric-WordsToSong is a #$PoeticWork that

is intended to be, or has been, sung set to music.")
(comment AmphibiousAssaultShip "The collection of amphibious craft 

intended to be used as primary landing ships in an amphibious attack.")
(comment Glutamine "A collection of compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.  These
are the monoamide of #$GlutamicAcid and are an important carrier of
urinary ammonia.  They are broken down in the kidneys by the enzyme
glutaminase.  Its abbreviations are Gln and Q.")
(comment FootballCleats-Shoe "The collection of #$Cleats-Shoes 

intended for use in playing football.")
(comment manageableSubEventTypesOnTour "(#$manageableSubEventTypesOnTour TOUR EVENTTYPE SUBEVENTTYPE)

means that within the context of TOUR, a #$tourParticipants in TOUR

can generally manage to perform an instance of SUBEVENTTYPE during the

course of an event of type EVENTTYPE that occurs as part of the tour.")
(comment LightInfantryMortarUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of lightly armed infantry units employing mortar-type weapons. (See #$Mortar.).")
(comment in-Lodged "(#$in-Lodged LODGER LODGEE) means that LODGER is lodged in LODGEE.  In particular, LODGER has been forced into LODGEE and is not a part of LODGEE.  There is a rigid connection between LODGEE and LODGER.  In typical cases, the outside end of LODGER is at the surface of LODGEE, or LODGER extends partially outside of LODGEE (see #$sticksInto).  However, in certain exceptional cases, such as schrapnel deep in flesh, LODGEE in some cases may be lodged wholly inside of LODGER.")
(disjointWith ManipulatingFoodOrDrink PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment CycLIndexedTerm "The collection of indexed or indexable terms in the CycL language.
This includes reified HL terms as well as reifiable EL NATs and assertions.")
(comment BarrelsPerYear "This is a unit of volume movement equalling one #$Barrel-UnitOfVolume or 158.97 #$Liters in one #$YearsDuration.")
(comment FirstAidKit "The collection of first aid kits.

A first aid kit is a portable kit containing various bandages and

medications which might be needed for first aid.")
(comment CWInfoStructure "The collection of all #$AbstractInformationStructures that define the complete structure for a specific version [see #$infoStructureOfCW] of a #$ConceptualWork.")
(comment LevelOfPollutedness "This is the collection of degrees of pollution.")
(disjointWith Bronchiole SegmentalBronchus)
(comment objectOfAttachment "This object is one of the objects in an #$AttachmentEvent. If the adhering objects in an #$AttachmentEvent are of roughly the same size, or if there is no clear \"attached\" \"attachee\" then they are both related to the attachment event by the relation #$objectOfAttachment.  However, also consider the more specific predicates #$objectAttached and #$objectAdheredTo.")
(comment SadismAndMasochism "This is the collection of sexual activities in which one or more persons engage

in #$SadisticSexualBehavior while one or more other persons engages in

#$MasochisticSexualBehavior, the relationship between these being obvious.")
(comment NonPositiveNumber "A specialization of #$RealNumber.  An instance REAL of #$RealNumber is also an instance of #$NonPositiveNumber just in case REAL is less than or equal to zero.")
(comment ComputerDictionary "a collection of #$Dictionarys. Each element of #$ComputerDictionary provides lexical information about words commonly used in the field of computers and computing.")
(comment assertionAssertSecond "(#$assertionAssertSecond ASSERTION SECOND) means that the #$CycLAssertion ASSERTION was made precisely at SECOND within the day it was asserted.  SECOND is not, however, an instance of #$Date.  This assertion is not intended for inference, only for documentation, so the format is a simple one, designed for human readability and for use by internal Cyc functions.  The format of SECOND is HHMMSS, so for example, midnight is 000000 (or simply 0), noon is 120000, 3:42:59 pm is 154259, and 11:59:59 pm is 235959.  For the day ASSERTION was made see #$assertionAssertTime.  See also #$myCreationSecond.")
(comment HalfEagleCoin-US "The collection of all US half eagle gold coins.  The face value is $5.00.")
(comment SportsCoach "The collection of persons who instruct or train athletes (individually or in teams) in the performance of some sport.")
(comment DevisedStructuredActivity "A specialization of #$DevisedPracticeOrWork.  Each instance of #$DevisedStructuredActivity is an abstraction of a largely rule-governed activity.  Major specializations of this collection include #$Game and #$Sport -- instances of these collections are abstractions of activities that are obviously rule-governed.")
(comment Requesting-CommunicationAct "A specialization of #$CommunicationAct-Single.  Each instance of #$Requesting-CommunicationAct is a communication act in which one agent requests something of one or more other agents.  Requests are typically followed by responses.")
(comment xor "The #$LogicalConnective that represents exclusive-or in #$CycL. Unlike #$or, which is a #$VariableArityRelation, #$xor takes two arguments, which must be instances of #$ELSentence-Assertible. (#$xor P Q) means  one but not both of P and Q is true. (An EL formula that mentions 
  #$xor is translated during canonicalization into an equivalent, less compact, formula that mentions #$or, #$and, and #$not).")
(comment quotedArgument "The main (longer) comment on this predicate was written to explain the role of #$quotedArgument in an earlier approach for referring to CycL expressions in the CycL language that is currently (April 2002) being phased out in favor of a new approach.  Whereas the earlier approach enabled self-reference only by means of a sort of \"implicit quotation\", the new approach involves a mechanism for explicitly quoting CycL expressions (by putting them inside something analogous to quotation marks).  #$quotedArgument, unlike #$quotedCollection (q.v.), still has a role to play with respect to the new approach, and its main comment will soon revised to better explain that role.  For an explanation of the new approach to quoting, see the shared #$NoteAboutQuotingInCycL and the constants that share that note.")
(comment GeneticCondition "A specialization of #$PhysiologicalCondition.  Each instance of #$GeneticCondition is an abnormal physiological condition which developed in a particular organism due to that organism's genetic configuration.  Such conditions are not contagious as infections are, but they may be hereditary.  Specializations of #$GeneticCondition include #$DownsSyndrome, #$Hemophilia, and #$SickleCellAnemia.")
(comment typeOfMine "The type of mineral associated with the mine: e.g. oil or copper ore.")
(comment keGenlsStrongSuggestionInverse "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate and a specialization of #$keGenlsRelevantInverse.
(#$keGenlsStrongSuggestionInverse COL BINPRED) means that for every known 
(i.e. reified-in-the-KB) specialization SPEC of COL, it is strongly suggested 
that there be some THING such that (BINPRED THING SPEC) is known in the 
Knowledge Base.  See also #$keGenlsStrongSuggestionPreds.")
(comment 85MMSmoothBoreCannon "A kind of #$Cannon

 common on #$Tank-Vehicles.")
(comment Recitative "The collection of all operatic recitatives, represented as #$ConceptualWorks.")
(comment Necrophilia "The collection of behaviors which involve erotic interest in and stimulation by dead bodies.")
(disjointWith MaghrebCountry PersianGulfCountry)
(comment DermatologicalDrugProduct "Drug products intended to be used on the skin.")
(comment interArgIsa2-3 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  
(#$interArgIsa2-3 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, 
when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the second argument to RELN, 
a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the third argument 
must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is
an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then 
(RELN ARG1 INST ARG3 ... ARGN) is semantically well-formed only 
if ARG3 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation of semantic 
well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations.")
(comment Shaman "In #$Shamanism, a person who acts as intermediary between the natural and supernatural worlds, using #$Magic to cure illness, foretell the future, control spiritual forces, etc.")
(comment Armor-ExtrinsicToObject "#$Armor which is added to an object. A #$Vest-Bulletproof is
an example of #$Armor-ExtrinsicToObject.")
(disjointWith Music Tariff)
(comment subSeries "(#$subSeries SERIES SUBSERIES) means that SUBSERIES is a sub-series of SERIES.  This means that all the members of SUBSERIES are series-members (see the predicate #$seriesMembers) of SERIES, that SERIES and SUBSERIES share the same ordering principle, and that, if the first member of SUBSERIES is the Mth member of SERIES, the Nth member of SUBSERIES is the (N + M - 1)th member of SERIES.")
(comment defendsAgainst "(#$defendsAgainst SHIELD OBJECT SITUATION) means that instance of #$ProtectiveSystem SHIELD is able to lower OBJECT's vulnerability or its #$DegreeOfDamage during the instance of #$AttackOnObject SITUATION, in which OBJECT is under attacked. This predicate is similar to #$protectsFromAction, except it refers to a particular attack rather than a type of attack.")
(comment DramaticActing-Live "This is the collection of events in which a person portrays someone or something other than himself in the context of an instance of either a live DramaticPerformance, or a rehearsal for such a

performance. DramaticActing-Live is thus distinct from (1) DramaticActingForFilm, which is a collection of instances of dramatic

acting in front of a camera (or rehearsing for such dramatic acting),

and (2) #$Masquerading, which is the collection of events in which a

person pretends to be someone or something other than himself outside

the context of a dramatic performance. E. g., dressing up for a

halloween party, or Mardi Gras would constitute an instance of

#$Masquerading, but not DramaticActing-Live.")
(comment CarobPod "The fruit of the carob tree; contains harb brown seeds and a sweet edible pulp [from which the chocolate substitute is derived??]")
(comment Lubricant "The set of coverings that lubricate, and thus protects against damage resulting from physical contact")
(comment connectedTo-SemiRigidly "A #$ConnectionPredicate and thus a specialization of #$connectedTo.  
(#$connectedTo-SemiRigidly OBJ1 OBJ2) means that there is a physical 
connection between OBJ1 and OBJ2 that is flexibile enough to permit 
limited (and only limited) movement of OBJ1 and/or OBJ2 around the 
point of connection.  Positive examples include a front cover hinged 
to the spine of a book (see #$flapHingedTo) and the gall bladder's 
attachment to the liver.  Negative examples include a wheel's connection
to its axle and a door hinged to a door frame; in both cases the freedom 
of movement derives from geometrical or mechanical properties of the 
objects and their connectors, rather than from the flexibity of the 
connected objects.  Note that all flexible connections place some limit 
on the freedom of relative motion they allow.  An extreme example (in 
the \"more free\" direction) is the connection between the propeller 
and fuselage of a rubberband-powered toy airplane.")
(comment LittleFinger "The 5th #$Finger the smallest finger on the human hand, furthest away from the thumb.")
(comment OnceEveryKBDump "#$OnceEveryKBDump is a #$Frequency.  Events that happen at this frequency happen once during every #$CycKBDump.")
(comment genWithGloss "(#$genWithGloss PRED) means that the english for any rules beginning with PRED will be generated using an #$englishGloss assertion if there is one. If there isn't, english will be generated in the usual way using #$genFormats etc..")
(comment ResidentialRealEstate "The collection of real estate properties which are intended for residential occupancy.")
(comment ChampionshipCompetition "Elements are #$Competitions in which the #$winner-First is considered the ''best'' or the ''champion'' with respect to the contextually relevant group of competing individuals.  Thus, the ''world heavyweight championship'' would be a heavweight boxing competition such that the winner would be considered the ''world heavyweight champion''.  Not all championships are sports competitions.  Success at a #$QualifyingTrial is sometimes a requirement for being a #$competingAgents in a #$ChampionshipCompetition.  But no #$QualifyingTrial is also a #$ChampionshipCompetition.")
(comment Decoding "The collection of events where some data in an #$InformationBearingThing are transformed from a complex/compressed format to a more usable or natural format.")
(comment TheatreDistrict "An area with many #$Theater-PhysicalStructures.")
(comment (FemaleFn EthnicGroupOfBlacks) "The group of women that share  cultural features  common to Blacks.")
(comment ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Corporate "#$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Corporate is a subset of #$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Agent. It is the collection of all electronic attacks perpetrated on instances of #$ComputationalSystem by agents acting in the interests of some instance of #$LegalCorporation.")
(comment UnitOfSpeed "A specialization of #$UnitOfRate. Each instance of #$UnitOfSpeed is a function which returns an instance of #$Speed (q.v.) when applied to a real number (see the collection #$SubLRealNumber) or a sequence of two real numbers. For instance, (#$MilesPerHour 212) is a speed of 212 miles per hour. Instances of #$UnitOfSpeed include #$MilesPerHour, #$MetersPerSecond, and #$Mach-UnitOfSpeed.")
(comment StorageFn "The function that  returns collections of situations in which instances of ARG1 are stored.")
(disjointWith Kayak Dinghy)
(comment Kite-TheBird "The collection of all members of any of several types of small birds of the hawk family (see #$AccipitrineFamily) that have long, pointed wings, feed on insects, carrion, reptiles, rodents, and birds, and are noted for their graceful, gliding flight.")
(comment HydrogenBomb "A specialization of #$NuclearBomb and #$FusionWeapon.  Each instance of #$HydrogenBomb is a bomb that derives its explosive force from the energy released when atoms of hydrogen are fused to form helium.")
(comment NudeBeach "The collection of all #$Beaches where it is permitted for people to be #$Nude.")
(comment inFrontOf-Generally "(#$inFrontOf-Generally FORE AFT) means that FORE is in front of the tangible object AFT.  More precisely, the intrinsic back-to-front axis of AFT is within 45 degrees of some line intersecting both FORE and AFT.  Note that FORE may be an intangible spatial object, such as an image projected onto a screen.")
(comment UpwardLocation-Underspecified "The collection of all abstract locations that are perceived to
have some innate 'upward directionality'. For instance, many emotions are
organized according to an up/down dichotomy: #$Happiness is up, #$Sadness is
down. Likewise for #$GreatWealth (i.e., rich is up, poor is down).")
(comment RockMusic "A specialization of #$Music.  A very broad category of popular music that began
  in the mid-1950s and continues up to the present day (1999), and that encompasses a variety
  of submovements and styles.  Essentially a youth-oriented music.  #$RockMusic is usually 
  played on electrically-amplified instruments (esp. the electric guitar), often in a loud
  and aggressive manner.  The lyrics of#$RockMusic songs (in addition to the common popular 
  music themes of romantic love, sexual desire, and loneliness) often express
  rebellion and independence.")
(comment ambientRelativeHumidity "(#$ambientRelativeHumidity LOC DEGREE) indicates the DEGREE to which the water vapor content of the air at LOC approaches the total possible saturation (at that temperature).")
(comment PermanentMortgage "The collection of #$MortgageAgreements that are not #$ConstructionLoans, that is, dedicated for use in construction.  Such mortgages are designed to refinance or 'take out' an interim, short-term construction loan.")
(comment joinFunctionOnLattice "(#$joinFunctionOnLattice LATTICE JOIN) means that JOIN is the 'join' function in the #$Lattice-LatticeTheoretic LATTICE.  This binary operation on the #$baseSet S of LATTICE is commutative, associative and satisfies the following properties: for each a in S, (JOIN X X) = X (the idempotent laws), and for each a and b in S, (JOIN a (MEET a b)) = (MEET a (JOIN a b)) = a (the absorption laws), where MEET is the 'meet' function in LATTICE (i.e., (#$meetFunctionOnLattice LATTICE MEET) holds).")
(disjointWith MatterTypeByPhysicalState PhysiologicalConditionType)
(comment ASN1SyntaxSpecification "The ASN.1 Standard language for specifying the syntax of a message, file or document.")
(comment mtSpindleIsSpindleMember "(#$mtSpindleIsSpindleMember INNERSPINDLE OUTERSPINDLE) means that #$MicrotheorySpindle INNERSPINDLE is a spindle that appears inside of the #$MicrotheorySpindle MICROTHEORYSPINDLE.")
(comment Actinomycetaceae-Family "An collection of #$Bacterium comprising a #$BiologicalFamily in the #$MoneraKingdom that contains Actinomyces-Genus.")
(comment AttackAircraftCarrier "The collection of #$AircraftCarriers intended for use in transporting attack aircraft.")
(comment VectorFromToFn "(#$VectorFromToFn OBJ1 OBJ2) may be

colloquially thought of as denoting the range of directions which

point from OBJ1 to OBJ2.  More formally, (#$VectorFromToFn OBJ1 OBJ2)

is a set of #$UnitVectorIntervals.  This set, UNIT-VECTOR-SET, is

constructed as follows: A set of vectors is constructed such that for

every point P1 in OBJ1 and every point P2 in OBJ2 there is a vector (see #$Vector-Precise) with its origin at P1 and its terminus at P2.  For every vector in this

set, there is a parallel unit vector in UNIT-VECTOR-SET.  For example,

`the ball rolled towards Mecca' could be represented as

(#$directionOfTranslation-Throughout BallRolling01 (#$VectorFromToFn

Ball01 Mecca)).  `a ball rolling away from Mecca' would be represented

as (#$directionOfTranslation-Throughout BallRolling (#$VectorFromToFn

Mecca Ball)).   Note that the \"interval\" includes vectors which don't point in what is intuitively \"the\" direction in which the ball is rolling, since, for example, some vectors point from spots on the left side of the ball to spots on right side of Mecca.

Note further that (#$VectorFromToFn OBJ REF) assumes that OBJ does not

#$spatiallyIntersects REF.  See also #$directionBetweenObjects which

is roughly interchangeable with #$VectorFromToFn.

#$directionBetweenObjects has the advantage that an arbitrarily

precise direction may be specified.  #$VectorFromToFn saves the user

from doing the labor involved with reifying and from having to know

the direction between OBJ1 and OBJ2.). ")
(comment CotangentFn "(#$CotangentFn ANGLE) yields the cotangent of that angle.")
(disjointWith PrescriptionDrug OverTheCounterDrug)
(disjointWith Milk VeganCuisine)
(comment revenueFromEvent "The amount of money specified in ARG3 accrues to an account owned/controlled by ARG1 as a result of the action ARG2.")
(comment Pollutant "Collection of individuals that, in their current state, act as polluting agents.  At the moment, PollutionProcess does not allow for a more metaphorical use of the concept pollution as in ``the ideas polluted her mind''.")
(disjointWith Railway Airport-Physical)
(comment FungalBioAgent "The collection of #$BiologicalAgents whose instances are also instances of #$Fungus.  A partition cell in #$BiologicalAgentType.")
(comment Hummingbird "The collection of all hummingbirds, i.e. members of the #$BiologicalFamily Trochilidae.  The smallest birds are hummingbirds.  Hummingbirds have a diet that is mainly nectar from flowers.")
(comment AnIndefiniteAmountOfTime "Duration of an infinitesimal to a very large amount of time")
(disjointWith Motion-SolidAgainstSolid WavePropagation)
(comment PerformanceLevelQuantity "The most general type of attribute describing the manner in which an actor performs an action; specializations of this include #$CorrectnessOfPosture, #$Competence, #$Precision, #$Dexterity, #$Gracefulness, #$Creativity, etc.  The elements of #$Precision, e.g., represent the various qualitative levels such as high precision, low precision, etc.")
(comment ChemicalWeaponsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military unit that has been organized, equipped,           and trained for operations involving the handling, employment,           and/or containment of chemical weapons.")
(comment FingerprintScanner "#$FingerprintScanner is a subset of #$BiometricAuthenticationDevice.  Individuals in the collection           #$FingerprintScanner scan a finger and attempt to match its fingerprint with a stored representation of it.")
(comment citySectionBoundedBy "(#$citySectionBoundedBy SECTION ST(1)...ST(N)) means that SECTION is an urban region that is  completely bounded by parts of each of the streets ST(1) - ST(N).   The relative order (but not the absolute position) of the 2nd and higher arguments here is important:  it should be physically possible to circle SECTION completely once in a generally clockwise fashion by starting  along ST(1) and turning, successively, onto ST(2), ST(3), ...,  ST(N), and finally back onto ST(1).  In practice, the number  of streets N will usually be between 3 and 5 (and the shape  of the region returned roughly an N-gon), though N can be as  small as 1 if ST(1) is a loop.  To have this predicate correctly relate  a given street-bounded city section SECTION to the N streets that border  it, one can fill its second argument-place with any of these N streets,  and then continue to fill in the other argument-places  according to the order in which one would travel along the  other N-1 streets if one were circling SECTION in a generally clockwise fashion (i.e. by making mostly right-hand turns).   See also #$CitySectionFn, #$cityGridSectionBoundedBy, and #$cityBlockBoundedBy.")
(comment actionEffects "(#$actionEffects ACTION SITUATION) states that if some instance of the ACTION is executed and the #$actionPreconditions hold,

then we can expect that some instance of the SITUATION will arise. More specifially, the effect should be #$contiguousAfter the ACTION.")
(comment Rumor-IBT "#$Rumor-IBT is the collection of all           instances of #$InformationBearingThing whose information          content is a rumor.")
(comment TemperatureInversionEvent "The collection of #$WeatherEvents in which a warm air mass is resting on top of a cold air mass without relative motion between the air masses.  Such an event keeps the cold air mass from rising along with any particulate matter or pollutants in the cold air mass.")
(comment SimplifyBackward "A property of reformulator rules which says that in this rule,
the simpler argument comes before the verbose argument.")
(comment salesTerritoryOfAddress "This Listwright constant was created to link a particular #$ContactLocation with the Listwright sales force territory in which it is found, in order to support various profile queries.  It was modeled on #$stateOfAddress, #$countryOfAddress, etc..")
(comment TensileStrength "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity.  Each instance of #$TensileStrength describes a specific capacity of a physical object to withstand a force pulling it apart.  The higher the tensile strength of the object, the higher the force required to pull the object apart.  Different tensile strengths may be represented using a #$GenericValueFunction.  Tensile strengths of objects are indicated with the predicate #$tensileStrengthOfSubstance.")
(comment MegaHertz "The measurement function used in Cyc to represent the common unit of frequency.     See also #$UnitOfFrequency, #$UnitOfMeasure.")
(comment DisneyComicStrip "The collection of all #$ComicStrips published by #$WaltDisney-CommercialOrganization.")
(comment SurfaceToSurfaceMissileLauncher "A subset of #$MissileLaunchers that are situated on the surface of the land or water and that launch #$SurfaceToSurfaceMissiles.")
(comment infectingOccursAt "(#$infectingOccursAt INFECTING REGION) means that the #$InfectingEvent INFECTING occurs at the #$AnimalBodyRegion REGION. REGION is the place on the body of the infected #$Animal where the pathogen causing the #$Infection enters.")
(comment SweepingAnArea "The collection of sweeping-an-area-clean-with-a-broom events.")
(disjointWith BookGeneric-CW BusinessSectionOfPeriodical)
(comment HumanlyDecidableCollection "This is the collection of all collections that are such that actual humans

can comprehend their membership criteria and can, at least in favorable circumstances,

determine, for things which are in fact members of the collection, that these things

are members. Such collections cannot, for example, contain infinitely complex things

or even things of such great finite complexity that no actual human could comprehend

them or decide whether they belonged to the collection.")
(disjointWith Landing Conveying-Stationary)
(comment Zepto "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10^-21")
(comment southernRegion "(#$southernRegion SUPER SUB) means that SUB is the `souhern region' of SUPER.  What counts as the `southern region' is contextually determined. Some of the factors  influencing the determination may be local geography, cultural identity, and political  considerations.")
(comment VM-NerveAgent "An extremely lethal #$NerveAgentType.")
(comment LacrosseStick "The stick with which the ball is manipulated in a lacrosse game.")
(comment TabletEntericCoated "The collection of all enteric-coated tablets.  These tablets, when ingested, remain intact until they reach the intestines.")
(comment 7-TheDigit "The numeral 7 of the Arabic Number system.  This is '7' as a #$Character-Abstract rather than the physical #$WrittenCharacter or the abstract mathematical #$Number-General.")
(comment Escudo-CapeVerde "Major unit of currency of #$CapeVerde")
(disjointWith MovingEarth LoadingAProjectileWeapon)
(comment suppliedWithThrough "(#$suppliedWithThrough PT1 COL PT2) means that the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT1 is supplied with instances of the #$Collection COL through the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT2 (on their way from their origin to PT1).  Like the predicate #$suppliedWith (q.v.), #$suppliedWithThrough is very general.  In various assertions PT1 might, for instance, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion; and PT3 might, for example, be a #$Hose, a #$Railway, a #$GeographicalRegion, or a #$BloodVessel.  The range of possible supplies is similarly broad.")
(comment EnteringIntoAMortgageAgreement "The collection of #$MakingAnAgreement events in which money is borrowed and a claim against the borrower's property is given to secure the loan.  See #$MortgageAgreement.")
(comment ChemicalBond "The collection of configurations in which two #$ChemicalObjects are held together by a chemical bond. An instance of #$ChemicalBond relates three objects: two #$Atoms and a #$Molecule in which the two atoms are bound together.  The bond can be considered to bind together two molecular components (atoms, radicals, etc.) within some larger molecular component, as well as merely two atoms within a molecule.  Important specializations of #$ChemicalBond are #$CovalentBond (for cases in which electrons are shared), ionic bond, and #$HydrogenBond (qqv).  Variations on the type and the structure of the mediator of a bond are the main motivation for the specialization of this collection.  See #$objectConfiguredInChemicalBond and #$mediatorConfigured-ChemBond.")
(comment EggFertilizationEvent "The process in which a sperm cell fertilizes an egg cell.")
(comment LocalizationSequence "A collection of collections.  Every instance of #$LocalizationSequence is a collection consisting of a set of #$Intangible instances of #$SpatialThing-Localized plus one #$PhysicalReferent which will be an instance of either #$PartiallyTangible or of #$Event.  It may be assumed that the predicate #$physicallyLocalizes forms a partial order on the instances of the collection, such that the #$PhysicalReferent is the first element in the ordering, with the implication being that it is the location of the #$PhysicalReferent which serves to determine the location of all the elements in the sequence, with each element in the sequence serving in turn to #$physicallyLocalize the next.")
(comment in-ContGeneric "(#$in-ContGeneric OBJ CONT) means that OBJ is contained, confined, or held in CONT. OBJ is not a part of CONT.  CONT has a cavity (see #$CavityWithWalls) and OBJ is at least partly within (see #$spatiallyIntersects) the interior of this cavity. If CONT moves, OBJ is, by default, caused to move so as to remain within that cavity (see #$movesWith). If OBJ leaves the confines of CONT, then either OBJ passes through some appropriately sized portal of CONT, or OBJ breaks into smaller pieces that themselves pass through appropriately sized portals of CONT, or OBJ breaks through a wall of CONT.  CONT may function as an open or closed container with respect to objects of the size of OBJ. If CONT is closed with respect to OBJ, then #$in-ContClosed is the preferred more specific predicate. If CONT is open with respect to OBJ, #$in-ContOpen is preferred. If OBJ is a fluid which completely fills CONT (for example, a cup of coffee brimming over) then #$in-ContFullOf is more precise.")
(comment StoringWrittenMaterial "The collection of events in which written material is stored or filed.")
(comment vulnerabilityEnablesAttack "(#$vulnerabilityEnablesAttack VULNERABILITY ATTACK-TYPE) means that ATTACK-TYPE capitalizes on VULNERABILTY. There can be many vulnerabilities associated with an attack, and many attacks associated with a vulnerability.")
(comment OrnamentalSewing "The collection of all sewing events that result in the
production of some ornamental object. Examples are #$EmbroideringEvent and
#$CrossStitchingEvent. A non-example is #$StitchingAWound.")
(comment CycInferenceHeuristicPredicate "The collection of predicates which describe the heuristic mechanisms available in the internal inference mechanisms of the Cyc theorem prover.")
(comment Eperythrozoon-Genus "A collection of #$Bacterium forming a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom that is currently unclassified in terms of a #$BiologicalOrder or #$BiologicalFamily.")
(comment arrangementNearestPredicates "This predicate relates an arrangement of like objects 

to the maximally specific spatial relationships that hold of 

or among its members.  

(#$arrangementNearestPredicates GROUP PRED) means that PRED

is an #$arrangementPredicates (q.v.) of GROUP and no reified proper

specialization of PRED is an #$arrangementPredicates of GROUP.")
(comment Sneezing-AilmentCondition "The collection of instances of the condition in which one suffers from regular instances of the collection #$Sneezing.")
(comment unitsOfDrugPrescriptionsByDocTypePayerTypeDuring "(#$unitsOfDrugPrescriptionsByDocTypePayerDuring DOCTYPE DRUGTYPE RXFILLTYPE PAYER PERIOD NUM) means that DOCTYPEs had drug prescriptions of type RXFILLTYPE filled for NUM units of DRUGTYPE and paid by PAYER during PERIOD.  RXFILLTYPE may be #$FillingAPrescription-Retail, #$FillingAPrescription-MailOrder, #$FillingANewPrescription, #$FillingARefillPrescription, intersections of these, or merely #$FillingAPrescription.")
(comment AprilFoolsJoke "A subset of #$Joke-CW, #$AprilFoolsJoke is the collection           of jokes made on April Fool's Day that involve tricking someone          into believing that so-and-so is the case, and then revealing the           trickery as trickery by saying 'April Fool's!' or 'April Fool!'.            See also #$Prank.")
(comment Rubella "Epidemic, viral infection. Acquired by direct contact with person infected. One attack of rubella apparently confers lasting immunity. Rubella would be of little concern if it were not for the fact that it causes birth defects if a pregnant woman becomes infected.")
(comment Dyslexia "#$Dyslexia is the collection of instances of #$PhysiologicalCondition which adversely affect a person's ability to read.")
(comment administersMilitaryRegion "(#$administersMilitaryRegion COUNTRY REGION) means that the #$MilitaryAdministrativeRegion REGION is controlled by the (#$ArmedForcesFn COUNTRY) as a matter of jurisdiction.")
(comment CargoShip "#$CargoShip is a specialization of #$Ship.  Each instance of #$CargoShip is a ship that is designed to transport a large amount of goods.  See also #$TankerShip.")
(comment Salt-ChemicalSubstance "An instance of this collection is a quantity of stuff that decomposes in charged ions when dissolved in water. The instances of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies that are specializations of this collection are formed in neutralization reactions, when the hydrogen of an acid is replaced by a #$Cation, typically a metal cation.  E.g. #$Salt-NaCl, #$AmmoniumChloride. ")
(comment MusicalInstrumentPlayerTypeByMusicalInstrument "#$MusicalInstrumentPlayerTypeByMusicalInstrument is a collection of collections. Each element is a collection of #$MusicalInstrumentPlayers who play the same #$MusicalInstrument . An example is (#$PlayerOfInstrumentFn #$Cello). The motivation for creating this collection is to make use of a faceting of #$MusicalInstrumentPlayer to generate English questions to aid classification. See #$NoteAboutHowFacetAssertionsAreUsed.")
(disjointWith WomensSportsTeam CoedSportsTeam)
(comment IceHockeyPads "The collection of body pads worn by  IceHockey players")
(comment Howitzer-M101 "The #$Howitzer-M101 is a general purpose, light field artillery weapon consisting of a cannon, 105mm howitzer (M2A2); recoil mechanism, M2 series; and carriage, 105mm Howitzer, M2A2. It can be used for direct or indirect fire.")
(comment FlamencoDancePerformance "The collection of all #$DancePerformances such that (#$PerformingFn #$FlamencoDancePerformance) is the collection of all instances of flamenco dancing for an audience. Flamenco dancing is of Spanish origin, and is associated with the gypsies, or gitano. It is characterized by flamboyant costumes, clapping and stomping, and erotic movements. It is accompanied by flamenco music, generally played on a guitar.")
(comment Rhenium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of Rhenium.")
(comment IllegalDrugActivity "A collection of #$Events; a subset of #$CriminalAct.

Every instance of #$IllegalDrugActivity is an action involving some

instance of #$IllegalDrug.  This action may also be an instance of #$Ingesting,  #$BuyingActivity, #$ConveyingMaterials, and/or #$CreationEvent.")
(comment rolePlayerImplementsCondition "(#$rolePlayerImplementsCondition ROLE COND) means that if an
actor that plays ROLE in a #$FunctionalSystem, the actor's actions
will be directed toward making sure that COND becomes true sometime
during the duration of the time that the actor plays ROLE.  At a
minimum, this means that the default #$purposeOfEvent of any action
the actor does while playing ROLE will be that COND holds sometime
during the duration of the role-playing.  Also, if the actor is an
#$IntelligentAgent,the default #$purposeInEvent that the actor has for
any action he, she, or it performs will be that COND holds sometime
during the duration of the role-playing.")
(disjointWith SyntheticCloth NaturalFiberCloth)
(comment ViralPneumonia "A collection of infections. Instances of #$ViralPneumonia are pneumonia caused by a virus. Most common pathogen responsible for this kind of diseases are influenza, parainfluenza and varicella viri.")
(comment JudaicMoralCode "The moral code of conduct one normally associates

 with Old Testament thinking (as codified in the Ten Commandments say).")
(comment WernickesArea "The collection of all parts of human #$Brains called \"Wernicke's area\".  Such a region intersects the #$TemporalLobe and the #$ParietalLobe of the left #$CerebralHemisphere with the apparent function of the recognition of words.")
(comment SupportingTerrorists "The collection of events where one state supports or sponsors terrorist actions by a terrorist group.")
(comment agreeingServiceRecipient "The agent that agrees to pay a set base rate and/or per-use fee to receive an ongoing service in an #$AgreementForOngoingService. Examples include clients or customers of ISPs, utility companies, insurance companies, lawyers.")
(comment ArmoredReconCarrier "A collection. Armored reconnaisance vehicles.")
(comment RegionalMagazineSeries "The collection of #$MagazineSeries

that deal with regional matters.")
(comment Tsar-HeadOfState "Usually the ruler of Russia.")
(comment CollectorMicrotheory "The collection of all microtheories which collect as #$genlMts a (possibly large) set of other microtheories, but do not have any (non-derived) assertions of their own.  A #$CollectorMicrotheory may collect as #$genlMts a set of VocabularyMicrotheories, TopicMicrotheories, or DataMicrotheories, but should not have a mixture of these types as direct #$genlMts.")
(comment Felodipine "A #$PharmaceuticalType which is a subcategory of #$CalciumChannelBlocker.  Felodipine is used in treating heart disease.")
(disjointWith MedicalCareEvent PreservingFood)
(comment ExperimentalMovie "An instance of #$MovieTypeByGenre.  
In cinema, experimental, or avant-garde, refers to a series of
 filmmakers who experiment with non-traditional form and content,
 often completely discarding standard narrative structure to
 explore the possibilities of the medium as an art form. Surrealism, 
abstract studies of light and form, Dadaism, and impressionistic
 studies of people and things figure heavily in early works of the
 genre. More recently, #$ExperimentalMovie has expanded to include
 underground film, so-called 'trash' cinema, and even some
 non-traditional documentaries.")
(comment director-OrganizationalRole "(#$director-OrganizationalRole ORG PERSON) means that PERSON has the task of serving as the director of ORG, entailing the responsibility of making executive decisions. An organization may have more than one director.")
(comment Knitting "In instances of #$Knitting, a fiber (usually #$Yarn) is formed into a row of a series of loops, then back along the same row making loops through the last set of loops, and so on to form a piece of fabric.  When performed non-professionally, usually #$KnittingNeedles are used.")
(disjointWith Navy AirForce)
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-EMailBomb "#$AttackByComputerOperation-EMailBomb is a subset of #$AttackByComputerOperation-DenialOfService.  In each instance of #$AttackByComputerOperation-EMailBomb, a great

    deal of e-mail is sent to a target, usually jamming the target's incoming e-mail 

    box.")
(comment PhosphoricAcid "The collection of samples of phosphoric acid.  Its instances are moderately strong acids.  The formula for this type is H3PO4.")
(comment SexualCopulation "In the #$BaseKB, this refers to the act of two animals engaged in sexual copulation.  See #$HumanActivitiesMt (and related Mts) for assertions about this activity by #$Persons.")
(comment InterArgIsaPredicate "The subcollection of both #$InterArgTypePredicate and #$ArgIsaPredicate (qq.v.) whose instances are used to put conditional #$isa based argument-type constraints on polyadic relations in regards to two of their argument-places.  Each instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate specifies, with respect to a given #$Relation, that one of its arguments (the \"dependent\" one) must be an instance of (#$isa) a certain collection, contingent upon another of its argument's (the \"independent\" one's) being an instance of a certain (possibly different) collection.  An inter-argument-isa predicate PRED has argument-places for designating the relation and the two collections serving as argument-types; the (numerically-specified) identities of the relation's corresponding dependent and independent arguments is in most cases fixed (as in #$interArgIsa1-2), but is in some cases variable and specified via two additional argument-places of PRED's (as in #$interArgIsa).  In cases of the former sort, where the relation's argument-places are fixed, PRED is a #$TernaryPredicate that takes as it first argument (or \"arg1\") a relation, as its arg2 the type specified for the relation's independent argument, and as its arg3 the type specified (contingently) for the dependent argument.")
(comment ProjectileShellTypeByPurpose "Every instance of #$ProjectileShellTypeByPurpose is a collection of #$ProjectileShellAssembly according to the purpose and filler of the  projectile.  For example, a #$ProjectileShell-Blast depends on the explosion  of hot gas to destroy its target.  #$ProjectileShell-Illumination is used to  see the enemy more clearly in the dark.  Typical bullets belong to the  collection of #$ProjectileShell-Pierce.")
(disjointWith Time-Quantity Temperature)
(comment UrbanPopulationDensity "The population density of urban areas.")
(comment PlacementOfResidualMaliciousProgram "Collection of all activities of a placement of programs which are
instances of ResidueOfAttack.")
(comment PhysicalPortionsOfFn "(#$PhysicalPortionsOfFn OBJ) denotes the collection of all
parts of OBJ that have all the relevant intrinsic properties of OBJ itself,
ie., all those X such that (#$physicalPortions OBJ X) holds.")
(comment Promontorium-Lunar "A collection of topographical features.  Each element of #$Promontorium-Lunar is a prominent mass of land overlooking or projecting into a lunar lowland.  This collection is restricted to promontories on Earth's Moon only.")
(disjointWith ElectricalComponent Weapon)
(comment HeadInitialMultiWordForConstantPred "The specialization MultiWordForConstantPred that maps from head-initial lexical items to Cyc constnts.")
(comment CompostingProcess "This is the collection of events in which organic refuse is composted. Composting is a process in which what would otherwise be thrown away is turned into organic fertilizer.")
(comment tourDayLocations "This predicate relates travel tours and calendar days to the geographical regions that the tour visits, i.e. stops in, on the relevant day.  (tourDayLocations TOUR DAY CITY) means that tour participants in tour will visit some part of CITY on DAY.")
(comment MapFn-Individual "#$MapFn-Individual takes as argument any instance of #$Individual and returns the collection of all #$InformationBearingThings that are maps (in any format) of that #$Individual.  For example, (#$MapFn-Individual #$CityOfAustinTX) returns the collection of all paper, computerized, and other maps of Austin.")
(comment nonExistentSpecification "(#$nonExistentSpecification SET) states the assumption that every element of the given SET has been explicitly stated to not exist.  This predicate is primarily used for reasoning in hypothetical contexts about the ramifications of some existing term not actually existing.  See also #$nonExistent and #$nonExistent-Specified")
(disjointWith AirTransportationDevice Water)
(comment receivesTreatmentFor "(#$receivesTreatmentFor ORGANISM TREATMENT AILMENT) means that
ORGANISM, an instance of #$Organism-Whole, receives the TREATMENT, an
instance of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent, for AILMENT, an instance of
#$AilmentCondition, that it is the #$bodilyDoer of..")
(disjointWith Sunrise MidnightSun)
(comment Batman-AideDeCamp "The collection of assistants / aide-de-camps that are traditionally known as 'batmen' (probably a cricket term). Typically used to describe military assistants of #$Lieutenant-Title to people of #$Captain-Rank.")
(comment isaRelevantInstance "(#$isaRelevantInstance INST COL ) means INST is a relevant
instance of COL.")
(comment BirthControlPill "The collection of pills which are used to regulate a woman's fertility, making her virtually infertile during the time which it is taken.")
(comment inflationRateDuring "(#$inflationRateDuring GE THING NR) means that NR is the inflation rate of the #$GeopoliticalEntity GE's economy during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  (THING will often be a calendar time period.)  That is, NR is the quotient of the difference between the price level in GE's economy at the end of the temporal extent of THING and the price level at the start of the temporal extent of THING (as dividend) and the price level at the start of the temporal extent of THING (as divisor).  For example, to express the fact that Oman's inflation rate for 1997 was 1.1%, we can say (#$inflationRateDuring #$Oman (#$YearFn 1997) .011).")
(comment MultiLevelMarketingActivity "A kind of #$MarketingActivity. Each instance of #$MultiLevelMarketingActivity is part of a system in which a company recruits individuals to be independent representatives, who not only sell the product, but also recruit other independent representatives. The group of people recruited by one independent representative, together with all the people they recruited and so on ad infinitum, is that representative's 'downline' (cf. #$MLMDownline). A representative receives a commission not only for products he or she sells, but also for products sold by marketers in his or her #$MLMDownline, for up to about seven recruiting 'generations'. A negative example is a 'pyramid scheme', which is a fraudulent investment scheme, and has no product.")
(disjointWith EdibleStuff SpoiledFood)
(comment Latex-Stuff "This is the collection of all instances of latex. Latex is a synthetic

rubber-like material that is used to make surgical and Platex gloves as well as clothing.

In the latter case, it is generally very shiny.")
(comment HardcopyOfInformationTypeFn "A function that maps types of

#$ConceptualWorks or #$CWInfoStructures onto the collection of hardcopy instantiations of instances of that type of work. For example, (#$HardcopyOfInformationTypeFn #$Map) is the collection of all hardcopies of #$Maps, i.e., those that are readable by humans without the aid of any #$Computer or other man-made device. See #$HardcopyOfCWFn for hard copies of specific #$ConceptualWorks and #$HardcopyOfIBTTypeFn for collection intersection of IBT types with #$HardcopyInformationBearingObject.  Also see #$ElectronicFn.")
(comment TobaccoPlant "Individual tobacco plants.")
(disjointWith SeparatingAMixture LosingALeaf)
(comment PuttingMoneyIntoAMachine "The act of manually inserting currency into a machine, e.g. a soft drink machine, a parking meter, a slot machine.")
(comment Nanny "A #$Nanny is a person whose job is to take care of the           children in a family, usually in the children's own home.           Unlike a #$BabySitter, a #$Nanny usually lives in the home            of the people that they are taking care of.  Also they work            for several days at a time, rather than several hours at a            time like #$BabySitters do.")
(comment HourlyWorker "An instance of #$EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus and a specialization of #$Employee. Each instance of #$HourlyWorker is a worker who is paid an hourly rate for work done. See also #$SalariedWorker and #$CommissionedWorker.")
(comment kindOfDamageDone "A predicate used to relate a particular #$Situation, usually an #$ActionOnObject, to the qualitative damage done in that #$Situation.  See also #$NoteAboutDamage.")
(comment Lyric-WordsToSong "The collection of all words of songs [#$Song-CW].")
(comment AmphibiousCargoShip "The collection of amphibious craft intended for use in cargo transport.")
(comment BaseballCleats-Shoe "The collection of #$Cleats-Shoes 

intended for use in playing baseball.")
(comment Horoscope-AdviceOrPrediction "The collection of #$InformationBearingThings containing advice or predictions based on a person's #$ZodiacSign. Not the diagram used for generating such predictions or advice.")
(comment Bookstall-Construct "The collection of bookstalls. Typically, tables or small shops
open at the front where books, magazines are shown for sale. Instances are
construct and do not represent the instances of #$BookStore that are
operating there business at bookstalls.")
(comment LightInfantryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of lightly armed infantry units.")
(disjointWith ManipulatingFoodOrDrink BiologicalEvent)
(comment SkyDiving "The collection of actions in which a person jumps from a high altitude using a parachute to retard his velocity toward the earth.")
(comment CutaneousInfection "The subcollection of #$Infection that is acquired by touching the pathogen responsible for #$Infection.")
(comment HumanGrowthHormone "A #$Hormone necessary for normal human growth. Secreted by the anterior pituitary.")
(comment BicycleBag "The collection of bike bags. A bike bag is

a storage device, usually zippered, that attaches to a bike.")
(comment ReconnaissanceUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all task-dedicated military units whose purpose is to survey territory in order to           gain information.")
(comment ambientWindSpeed "(#$ambientWindSpeed X SPEED) means that in the vicinity of X the wind is blowing with the speed SPEED.")
(disjointWith SegmentalBronchus LobarBronchus)
(comment enables-MakesComplCapable "#$enables-MakesComplCapable expresses the notion that an agent is rendered completely capable (in the sense of #$capableOf) of doing something by a certain state of affairs -- a situation, that is, or, perhaps more frequently, an event. 'Being completely capable' implies that, were one to attempt to do something, one would in fact succeed. More accurately, (#$enables-MakesComplCapable SIT AGENT ACT_TYPE) is true iff SIT obtains, AGENT is completely capable of performing actions of type ACT_TYPE, and SIT is in fact what causes AGENT to be completely capable of performing a token of ACT_TYPE. An example: a military unit's clearing and securing a given area makes another unit completely capable of advancing through that area; short of extremely unlikely accident, the second unit would pass through, were it to attempt. An example in which this predicate does NOT apply: merely giving an ax to someone of ordinary physical build and skills does not amount to making him completely capable of chopping down a tree, for even with the ax he may lack the strength, training, etc., necessary to ensure that he would succeed were he to try. The 'enabling' in this case consists in the removal of a preventing factor, namely the lack of a proper tool -- see #$enables-RemovesDisablingFactors.")
(comment TradingCardGame "#$TradingCardGame is a collection of card games.  The cards used to play are collectible.")
(comment transmissionEventsForInfectionType "This predicate relates an infection type to the collection

of events in which instances of that disease are transmitted. (#$transmissionEventsForInfectionType INF-TYPE EVENT-TYPE) means that EVENT-TYPE, a specialization of #$InfectingEvent, is the collection of events during which an instance of INF-TYPE is transmitted to an host. Every type of infection has a corresponding collection of transmission.")
(comment EagleCoin-US "The collection of all US eagle gold coins.  The face value is $10.00.")
(comment cloudinessOfRegion "(#$cloudinessOfRegion LOC DEGREE) means that the #$OutdoorLocation LOC is characterized by DEGREE of cloud cover.")
(comment wordsOfIBT "(#$wordsOfIBT IBT STRING) means that IBT contains #$TextualMaterial

of which STRING represents one of the #$subTexts.")
(comment secondaryPracticeType "This binary predicate was created to link instances of #$Doctor-Medical to instances of the AMA secondary type-of-medical-group-practice in the LTS of lw_profile in the Listwright database.  It provides support for several of the Listwright profile comparison queries")
(comment ExercisingEminentDomain "The collection of events in which a government takes property from a private agent, presumably to use it for the public good.")
(comment bondedTo "(#$bondedTo OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 is #$connectedTo-Rigidly OBJ2 vis a vis some bonding substance such as glue, welding material.  Note: use #$stuckTo when the bonding substance is part of OBJ1 or OBJ2.")
(comment 76MMRifledBoreCannon "A kind of #$Cannon

 common on #$Tank-Vehicles.")
(comment PreventiveCareEvent "The subcollection of #$MedicalCareEvents that are conducted in order

to prevent or diminish the maleficiary effects of an anticipated event.")
(comment DeathMetalMusic "An especially dark, rather underground, specialization of #$HeavyMetalMusic whose heyday was during the 1990s.

  The music is generally very hard and heavy; the lyrics contain frequent references to violence, death, hatred, and Satan; the vocals often screamed in a hoarse baritone.  Influential practitioners of this style include Deicide.")
(comment SadisticSexualBehavior "The collection of all #$SexualBehavior in which the performer gains sexual gratification through causing pain or degradation to another #$SentientAnimal.")
(comment StrategicTarget "A #$StrategicTarget is one which is large and immobile, for example:  #$CityOfLosAngelesCA, #$OilRefinery, #$Railway")
(comment AntiDiabeticDrug "Class of drugs normally used to combat diabetes.")
(comment tourIsOfRegion "(#$tourIsOfRegion TOUR REGION) says that TOUR is a

 a #$TravelTour of REGION.  For example, (#$tourIsOfRegion

 MyVacationTourOfMexico #$Mexico) says that MyVacationTourOfMexico is a tour of #$Mexico.")
(comment Survivalist "a collection of #$Persons who make preparations to survive a widespread catastrophe, as an atomic war or anarchy, esp. by storing food and weapons in a safe place.")
(comment thermalConductivityOfObject "(#$thermalConductivityOfObject OBJ DEGREE) means that the tangible object OBJ has the #$ThermalConductivity attribute DEGREE.  Objects with higher values of DEGREE conduct heat faster and better (i.e., with less heat loss) than those with a lower #$ThermalConductivity.")
(comment Armor-IntrinsicToObject "#$Armor that is 'built into' an object.  #$Beetles have
#$Armor-IntrinsicToObject for example.")
(comment executive-FunctionalRole "(#$executive-FunctionalRole SYSTEM EXEC) means that EXEC
is the subsystem of SYSTEM which is capable of receiving information
inputs from all other subsystems in SYSTEM, and which is capable of
transmitting to them information outputs that control SYSTEM.")
(comment GovernmentOfCountry "A specialization of #$RegionalGovernment.  Each instance of #$GovernmentOfCountry is the government of some instance of #$Country.  A notable instance of #$GovernmentOfCountry is #$UnitedStatesFederalGovernment.")
(disjointWith EdibleStuffComposite DefenseSystem)
(comment infoTransferred-Prop "This predicate relates an information transfer event to a

sentence that expresses some or all of the propositional content of

that information transfer event.  Note that this is more specific than

#$infoTransferred insofar as it relates communication events to

propositional content alone and not to all the information

communicated in the event, i.e. propositions and illocutionary

force, which might be the case with #$infoTransferred.")
(comment Opium "The dried milky juice from the unripe seed pods of the opium poppy plant; has narcotic properties.")
(disjointWith Event AspatialInformationStore)
(comment in-ImmersedGeneric "A #$SpatialPredicate that is a specialization of #$touches and (via 
#$genlInverse) #$surroundsHorizontally.  (#$in-ImmersedGeneric OBJ FLUID) 
means that OBJ is immersed in FLUID.  OBJ might be completely or partially 
immersed in FLUID, but FLUID must touch OBJ and must conform to a 
significant portion of the surface of OBJ.   See also the specializations
#$in-ImmersedFully and #$in-ImmersedPartly.")
(comment AssertionForwardPeriodicallyFn "#$AssertionForwardPeriodicallyFn is a #$Function-Denotational.  The term (#$AssertionForwardPeriodicallyFn FREQUENCY) denotes an element #$CycLAssertionDirection which indicates how frequently an assertion should be automatically forward propagated.   It is particularly useful for keeping the consequences of rules somewhat up to date with the state of the KB, without incurring the agenda slowing computational burden of #$Forward-AssertionDirection.  For more information please see (#$AssertionForwardPeriodicallyFn #$OnceEveryKBDump)).")
(comment CommercialRealEstate "The collection of real estate property which is usually intended for commercial, as opposed to residential, habitation.")
(comment Legend "A story which has been passed down from previous generations.  They are often popularly considered to be historical, but may be hard to verify.  See also #$Fable and #$UrbanLegend.")
(comment TVDrama "A collection of television shows [#$TVShow-CW].  Instances of #$TVDrama usually tell a story involving human conflict.")
(comment EncryptedCode "A spec of #$CommunicationCode.  #$EncryptedCode is the collection of #$CommunicationCodes that are scrambled, or #$Encrypted, for the sake of securing the transmission of information from one source to another.")
(comment ShoppingDistrict "An area with shops and stores.")
(comment PhysicalReferent "This is the collection of every entity that functions as the foundation-point of a localization sequence serving to localize some #$Intangible instance of #$SpatialThing-Localized in the empirically observable universe. Instances may be #$PartiallyTangible, like the #$RoyalObservatory-Greenwich, or they may be #$Intangible #$Events, like the #$RotationOfEarth (which serves to localize the #$AxisOfRotation-Earth). ")
(comment ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Personal "#$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Personal is a subset of #$ElectronicIntelligenceAttack-Agent.  It is the collection of electronic attacks directed at instances of #$ComputationalSystem by agents having no direct affiliation with any government or any corporation.  The agent is 'personal' because he or she does not act directly on behalf of any such organization.")
(comment TarotCardReading "A specialization of #$Divination. Instances of #$TarotCardReading are events in which the doer foretells another person's future by turning over cards from a special deck.")
(disjointWith Dinghy Lifeboat)
(comment FusionWeapon "A specialization of #$NuclearWeapon.  Each instance of #$FusionWeapon is a nuclear weapon that derives its destructive power from the energy released by an instance of #$NuclearFusionProcess.")
(comment MutualFund "The collection of all mutual funds. A #$MutualFund is a #$LegalAgent that buys and sells instances of #$TradeableSecurity and other investments, using money invested in the fund by individual investors. The individual investors receive regular distributions of any profits made by the fund, and may sell their shares in the fund, or buy more shares, at any time, at a price determined by the current value of the investments held by the fund. Each #$MutualFund has a #$MutualFundManager who generally works for an #$InvestmentFirm and is ultimately responsible for making investment decisions for the fund. See also #$MutualFundShare, #$MutualFundManager.")
(comment CentralRegionFn "(#$CentralRegionFn ?REG) specifies, roughly the central area of some particular #$GeographicalRegion. For example, (#$CentralRegionFn #$Texas-State) would be an area including Austin and the Hill Country.")
(comment DownwardLocation-Underspecified "The collection of all abstract locations that are perceived
to have some innate 'downward directionality'. For instance, many
emotions are organized according to an up/down dichotomy: #$Sadness is
down while #$Happiness is up. Likewise for #$GreatWealth (i.e., poor
is down, rich is up).")
(comment GothicMusic "A specialization of #$RockMusic and a spin-off of #$PostPunkMusic.  A long-
  lasting (if decidedly fringe) movement, #$GothicMusic had its heyday from the mid 1980s
  to the late 1990s.  The music is somber, and the song lyrics contain frequent 
  references to death and the supernatural.  Influential practitioners of this style
  include Siouxsie and the Banshees, Bauhaus, Christian Death, and the Sex Gang Children.")
(comment Valve "The collection of all #$Valves, whether biological or manufactured.  Each instance of this collection consists of a section of #$FluidConduit with at least one moving part which can limit the volume or direction of flow within a system depending upon how it is situated or simply the moving parts within the #$FluidConduit which perform this action.")
(comment PavingARoad "Covering a pathway with material which forms a hard surface which can be used for travel.")
(comment PledgeAccountMortgage "The collection of #$MortgageAgreements secured by either a savings account or a #$CertificateOfDeposit belonging to a relative, pledged as collateral.  Typically, the amount that is pledged is at least ten percent of the purchase price or of the appraised value of the real estate that is mortgaged.")
(comment ModularLattice "The subcollection of #$Lattice-LatticeTheoretic that contains all those lattices called 'modular lattices' by the lattice theorists.  A #$Lattice-LatticeTheoretic LATTICE (with the #$baseSet S, ordering relation R, meet operation MEET and join operation JOIN) is a #$ModularLattice if the following condition holds: for each X, Y and Z in S, if R(Z X) then (MEET X (JOIN Y Z)) = (JOIN (MEET X Y) (MEET X Z)).  Note that there are many conditions equivalent to the one above, one of which is the condition that for each X, Y and Z in S, if R(Z X) then (JOIN X (MEET Y Z)) = (MEET (JOIN X Y) (MEET X Z)). (Other equivalent conditions may be found by browsing the rules for #$ModularLattice.)  Note also that a #$DistributiveLattice satisfies this condition automatically, and therefore is a #$ModularLattice.")
(comment GeneticallyEngineeredOrganism "The specialization of #$BiologicalLivingObject whose instances have a genetic makeup that was developed by some instance of #$GeneticEngineer.")
(disjointWith MatterTypeByPhysicalState TemporalObjectType)
(comment BackusNaurForm "The BNF (Backus-Naur Form, or Backus Normal Form) format, which is a #$FormalMetaGrammar for specifying a #$FormalGrammarSpecification.  BNF itself is used to specify a phrase structure grammar consisting of a list of replacement or production rules.  (It's possible to specify BNF itself in BNF.)")
(comment mtSpindleMember "(mtSpindleMember MICROTHEORYSPINDLE MT) means that #$Microtheory MT isa a member of #$MicrotheorySpindle MICROTHEORYSPINDLE.")
(comment sentenceEquiv "(#$sentenceEquiv FORMULA-1 FORMULA-2) means that  the #$ELSentence-Assertible FORMULA-1 is logically equivalent to the #$ELSentence-Assertible FORMULA-2.  This predicate is very similar to #$equiv, but #$equiv is an instance of #$LogicalConnective, while #$sentenceEquiv is an instance of #$Predicate.  #$sentenceEquiv is primarily intended to be used for rules that quantify over CycL formulas.")
(comment CoastalPatrolCraft "A collection. Boats meant to be used in coastal patrol operations.")
(comment TangentFn "(#$TangentFn ANGLE) yields the tangent of that angle.")
(comment PortugueseWord "The collection of all lexical words in Portuguese; a subset of #$LexicalWord.            Different inflectional forms of a word do not count as different words.")
(disjointWith OpeningSomething StrictlyMentalEvent)
(comment LawSchoolAdmissionTest "The collection of #$AcademicTesting events that are required for admission to all 196 law schools that are members of the Law School Admission Council.")
(disjointWith Airport-Physical Dock)
(comment BreederFn "(#$BreederFn AN-TYPE) denotes the collection of animal breeders (instances of the class #$AnimalBreeder-Business) which breed animals of the type AN-TYPE.  A given instance of (#$BreederFn AN-TYPE) might also breed animals of some other type. ")
(comment WaterSnake "Snakes which live near water, are often in the water, and which feed on aquatic animals.")
(disjointWith EmittingAnObject WavePropagation)
(comment CitySectionFn "(#$CitySectionFn ST(1)...ST(N)) denotes the unique urban region (if any) that is completely bounded by parts of  each of the streets ST(1) - ST(N).  The relative order (but  not the absolute position) of the arguments here is important:  it should be physically possible to circle completely the  bounded area once in a generally clockwise fashion by starting  along ST(1) and turning, successively, onto ST(2), ST(3), ...,  ST(N), and finally back onto ST(1).  In practice, the number  of streets N will usually be between 3 and 5 (and the shape  of the region returned roughly an N-gon), though N can be as  small as 1 if ST(1) is a loop.  To have this function return  a given street-bounded city section SECTION, one can fill its  first argument-place with any of the N streets that borders  SECTION, and then continue to fill in the other argument-places  according to the order in which one would travel along the  other N-1 streets if one were circling SECTION in a generally clockwise fashion (i.e. by making mostly right-hand turns).   See also #$citySectionBoundedBy, #$CityGridSectionFn and #$CityBlockFn.")
(comment Chauffeur "Person whose job is to drive important people/people with bucks around in big cars.")
(comment RumorPropagation "The specialization of #$Communicating whose instances           consist of the use of instances of #$Rumor-IBT to transmit           the information contained in instances of #$Rumor-CW.")
(comment WarmFrontEvent "The collection of all #$AirFrontEvents in which a large atmospheric air mass warmer than the ambient air moves into a region pushing under the cooler air.  This causes precipitation and often storm (see #$StormAsEvent), although the storms are not as severe as those generally produced by #$ColdFrontEvents.  The edge of the warm air mass is the the locus of the #$WarmFrontEvent.  In the #$NorthernHemisphere-Region, warm fronts generally move northward (#$North-Generally), while in the #$SouthernHemisphere-Region they normally move southward (#$South-Generally).")
(comment WinampSkin "Winamp skins are alternative interfaces for #$Winamp-TheProgram.")
(comment ElectricalResistance "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity.  Each instance of #$ElectricalResistance is a measure of the resistance to electrical flow through an object.  Instances of #$ElectricalResistance include #$InsulatorResistance, #$ConductorResistance, #$SemiconductorResistance, and #$SuperconductorResistance.")
(comment NationalLottery "Official lotteries that are regularly held across many states.")
(comment infectingActsOn "(#$infectingActsOn INFECTING OBJECT) means that as a

result of #$InfectingEvent INFECTING, the #$Organism-Whole OBJECT will carry the type of #$Infection conveyed by

INFECTING.")
(comment PornographicPicture "#$PornographicPicture is a collection of instances of #$VisualImage each of which depicts #$SexualBehavior in a graphic manner that is judged by some sectors of a particular community to be obscene.")
(comment BouncingTrajectory "A bouncing trajectory")
(disjointWith Joke-CW BookGeneric-CW)
(comment AirplaneTrip "The collection of journeys of instances of #$Airplane, each including subevents of an #$AirplaneTakeOff and an #$AirplaneLanding.  This is not the collection of trips taken by airplane passengers.")
(comment DispersionOfStuff "This is the collection of dispersion events. These are events in which some

member of an #$ExistingStuffType becomes dispersed in some other instance

of an #$ExistingStuffType. This would include cream mixing into coffee, radioactive fallout spreading over a large area, a powdery substance blowing away in the wind, sarin gas being released in the Tokyo subway. One can also speak of groups of large objects such as people dispersing into a crowd. While obviously related to the present notion, such events would not fall under

#$DispersionOfStuff. ")
(comment Howitzer-122mmTowed "The collection of towed 122mm #$Howitzers.")
(comment PeriodicalSubscription "The collection of all subscriptions to 
 periodicals.  Because subscriptions
 can be bought and sold, this collection
 is an instance of #$ProductType.")
(comment VR-55-NerveAgent "A kind of #$NerveAgent which is extremely lethal when inhaled.")
(disjointWith GlobularCluster OpenCluster)
(comment TabletTimeRelease "The collection of all tablets with time-release properties.  The contents of these  capsules are released into the body over measured intervals of time. 'CR' stands for 'controlled release.'")
(comment hardnessOfObject "(#$hardnessOfObject OBJ DEGREE) means that the instance of #$SolidTangibleThing OBJ has this DEGREE of #$Hardness.")
(comment exportQuotaDuring "(#$exportQuotaDuring REGION PRODUCT-TYPE THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the export quota of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE for the #$GeographicalRegion REGION during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  (Of course, the existence of export quotas is the exception rather than the rule.)  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  In the case of oil exports, for example, AMOUNT might be a #$Volume (a number of barrels) indicating the total quantity of oil REGION is allowed to export.  Alternatively, AMOUNT might be a #$Rate, characterizing the average rate of export, under the quota, of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE by REGION during the temporal extent of THING.  Oil exports, for example, might be expressed in terms of so many million barrels per day.")
(comment 8-TheDigit "The numeral 8 of the Arabic Number system.  This is '8' as a #$Character-Abstract rather than the physical #$WrittenCharacter or the abstract mathematical #$Number-General.")
(comment Underwriter-Person "The collection of employees of various corporate underwriters (such as #$SecuritiesUnderwriter) who decide whether or not their company should assume any particular #$Underwriting or risk.")
(comment Rupee-Seychelles "Major unit of currency of #$Seychelles")
(disjointWith FluidFlowEvent LoadingAProjectileWeapon)
(comment BiologicalDegenerationEvent "Those #$DegenerationEvents in which the object degenerating is a living biological structure.")
(comment relationAllSpecsExistsSpec "(#$relationAllSpecsExistsSpec PRED COL1 COL2) means that for

all subcollection SUBCOL1 of COL1, there exists a subcollection of COL2,

say SUBCOL2, such that (PRED SUBCOL1 SUBCOL2) holds. This assumes that PRED

is a type level predicate.")
(comment advertisedThing "ARG1 contains propositional content about the advertised thing ARG2.  ARG2 is the general focus of the propositional content of ARG1.")
(comment CyberVulnerabilityExploit "Collection of computer programs designed for performing an #$AttackByComputerOperation, as well as instructions for entering code by hand to perform an #$AttackByComputerOperation.  Thus, this collection includes #$MaliciousComputerProgram as well #$SoftwareCracks, but all the instances of #$CyberVulnerabilityExploit are not exhausted by them.")
(comment CholeraInfection "The collection of all Cholera infections. An instance of #$CholeraInfection is an infection of the small intestine caused by the bacterium Vibrio cholerae.")
(comment PlayingOf-Yo-Yo "The collection of Yo-Yo playing events")
(comment Acholeplasmatales-Order "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalOrder in the #$MoneraKingdom.  It includes the #$BiologicalFamily #$Acholeplasmataceae-Family. ")
(comment AlternativeMedicineHealthCareEvent "#$AlternativeMedicineHealthCareEvent is the collection of #$HealthCare events in which one of the healing modalities which are included in #$AlternativeMedicine is used. For example, an instance of #$Acupuncture is an instance of #$AlternativeMedicineHealthCareEvent.")
(comment nearestDifferentGenlMt "(#$nearestDifferentGenlMt  MT-1 MT-2 NEAR-DIFF) means that NEAR-DIFF is a \"nearest\" microtheory of which MT-1 is a specialization, but MT-2 is not. That is, (#$genlMt MT-1 NEAR-DIFF) holds, (#$genlMt MT-2 NEAR-DIFF) does not hold, MT-1 and NEAR-DIFF are not identical, and there is no reified #$Microtheory NEARER-DIFF distinct from NEAR-DIFF and MT-1 such that (#$genlMt MT-1 NEARER-DIFF) holds, (#$genlMt MT-2 NEARER-DIFF) does not hold, and (#$genlMt NEARER-DIFF NEAR-DIFF) holds. Note that this predicate is #$notAssertible, since it must always be recomputed from the current state of the #$genlMt hierarchy.")
(comment CleanJoke "A subset of #$Joke-CW, #$CleanJoke is the collection of all jokes           that are not likely to be offensive to anyone.  Note that #$CleanJoke is disjoint with the collection #$JokeOffensiveToSome.")
(disjointWith GeopoliticalEntityTypeByBasicCategory PersonTypeByCulture)
(comment TyphoidFever "A collection of infections. Instances of #$TyphoidFever are acute infections picked up from water, milk or food handlers contaminated with some pathogen, a few only of the Salmonellae, responsible for this type of diseases.")
(comment LearningDisability "#$LearningDisability is the collection of instances of #$PhysiologicalConditions which tend to inhibit the ability to learn. #$Dyslexia is an example.")
(comment ScheduleFn-Individual "#$ScheduleFn-Individual takes as argument any instance of #$TemporalThing and returns the collection of all instances of #$Schedule that include schedule information for that thing.  For example, (#$ScheduleFn-Individual #$Madonna) returns the collection of all schedules, including lists of appearances, for the singer Madonna.  (#$ScheduleFn-Individual #$UniversityOfTexasAtAustin) returns the collection of all schedules for the main branch of the University of Texas.")
(comment Submarine "#$Submarine is a specialization of #$Watercraft-Subsurface, #$Container-PressureBarrier, and #$ModernNavalShip.  Each instance of #$Submarine is a pressurized vessel designed to travel underwater.")
(comment ChemicalDecomposition "A collection of events in which a #$ChemicalObject is broken down into other instances of a different type.  In a simple decomposition, one #$ChemicalObject breaks down into two simpler substances, for example, #$Water decomposes into #$Hydrogen and #$Oxygen.  In a double decomposition, two compounds recombine to form two different compound types.")
(comment CoedSportsTeam "the collection of all #$SportsTeams whose members include both #$MalePersons and #$FemalePersons.")
(comment alignedAlongSurface "(#$alignedAlongSurface OBJ1 OBJ2) means that the surface of OBJ1 #$touches OBJ2 over a significant extent of OBJ2 (either area-wise or linearly).")
(comment WeightLiftingBelt "The collection of the (special) belts worn by weight lifters while lifting weights")
(comment M109SelfPropelledArtilleryVehicle "The collection of self-propelled artillery vehicles that carry a 155-mm howitzer.")
(comment CompiledConceptualWork "The collection of all #$ConceptualWorks which are composed of a group of pieces often by different authors or artists.  Examples are #$NewspaperIssues, art exhibits, and #$ShortStory collections.")
(comment Bismuth "BismuthStuff.  A piece (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of bismuth; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment HempCloth "The collection of cloth made from #$Hemp-Fiber.")
(comment Cubit "An ancient unit of distance whose length is the distance between the elbow and tip of the middle finger (often of the local ruler).  A cubit varies between 17 and 22 inches depending upon locale and year.")
(comment FoodPoisoning "A collection of ailment conditions. Instances of #$FoodPoisoning are poisoning resulting from ingestion of food contaminated with toxic substances.")
(comment Amber "The collection of all pieces of amber, a fossil resin that is often found in            decorative items.  Amber is yellow to brown in color.")
(comment exampleNATs "(#$exampleNATs FN NAT) means that the #$CycLNonAtomicTerm NAT

represents a good example of the use of the #$Function-Denotational FN.")
(comment BrocasArea "The collection of all parts of human #$Brains called \"Broca's area\".  Such a region is in the #$FrontalLobe of the left #$CerebralHemisphere with the apparent function of preplanning voluntary movements including speech.")
(comment PoliticalEspionage "The collection of events where one agent conducts acts that would be commonly considered acts of espionage against the political system of another agent.")
(comment AxialFilament "The #$AxialFilament is comprised of several filaments which spiral around the #$Bacterium under the outer sheath of the cell wall. The #$Spirochetes have #$AxialFilaments. #$AxialFilaments are not the same as either #$Flagellum-Eucaryotic or #$Flagellum-Prokaryotic, although they are very similar. The #$AxialFilaments attach at either end of the cell and move the #$Bacterium like a corkscrew.")
